COLLDATA("ibnhibban","en",[[1,"The delegation of ‘Abd al-Qays came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and said, “O Messenger of Allah, we are this tribe from Rabi‘a. The disbelievers of Mudar have come between us and you, and we cannot reach you except in a sacred month. So command us with a matter that we may act upon and call to it those behind us.” He said, “I command you with four: faith in Allah — the testimony that there is no god but Allah and that Muhammad is the Messenger of Allah — establishing prayer, giving zakah, and that you give a fifth of what you gain as booty. I forbid you from gourds, glazed jars, wooden vessels, and pitch-coated vessels.”"],[2,"\"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: 'Whoever attributes to me something that I have not said, let him take his place in Hell.\" (Using translation from Ibn Mājah 34)"],[3,"I said, \"O Abu Abdullah al-Rahman, referring to Ibn Umar, there are people who claim that there is no fate (predestination). He said: Do we have anyone among us like them? I said, No. He said: Then convey to them from me that when you meet them, indeed Ibn Umar disassociates himself from you and you disassociate yourselves from him.\" Umar ibn al-Khattab narrated to us that while we were sitting with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ , a man came who had no signs of travel nor was he from the people of the city. He came and sat in front of the Messenger of Allah. He said, \"O Muhammad, what is Islam? He said, \"Islam is that you bear witness that there is no deity worthy of worship except Allah and that Muhammad is the Messenger of Allah, and you establish prayer, give zakah, perform Hajj, perform Umrah, cleanse yourself from major impurity, complete ablution, and fast during Ramadan.\" He said, \"If I do all of that, would I be a Muslim?\" He said, \"Yes.\" He said, \"You have spoken the truth.\" He asked, \"O Muhammad, what is faith (imaan)?\" He said, \"Faith is that you believe in Allah, His angels, His books, His messengers, and you believe in the Day of Judgment, and you believe in fate, its good and its evil.\" He said, \"If I do all of that, would I be a believer (mu'min)?\" He said, \"Yes.\" He said, \"You have spoken the truth.\" He asked, \"O Muhammad, what is excellence (ihsan)?\" He said, \"Excellence is that you worship Allah as if you see Him, and even though you do not see Him, He sees you.\" He asked, \"If I do that, would I be excellent (muhsin)?\" He said, \"Yes.\" He said, \"You have spoken the truth.\" He asked, \"O Muhammad, when is the Hour (Day of Judgment)?\" He said, \"Glory be to Allah, the one who is asked about it knows no more than the questioner, but if you wish, I will inform you about its signs.\" He said, \"Yes.\" He said, \"When you see barefoot, naked, destitute shepherds competing in constructing tall buildings and when you see women giving birth to their mistresses, that is among the signs of the Hour.\" He said, \"You have spoken the truth.\" Then the man left, and the Prophet ﷺ said, \"O Umar, do you know who this man was?\" We said, \"Allah and His Messenger know best.\" He said, \"This was Gabriel who came to teach you your religion.\""],[4,"I have been commanded to fight the people until they say, \"There is no god but Allah.\" If they bear witness that there is no god but Allah and believe in me and in what I have brought, they have protected their blood and their wealth from me, except by its right, and their reckoning is upon Allah."],[5,"I have been commanded to fight the people until they bear witness that there is no god but Allah and that I am the Messenger of Allah, and they establish prayer and give zakat. If they do that, they have protected their blood and their wealth from me, except by the right of Islam, and their reckoning is upon Allah."],[6,"\"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: 'Whoever attributes to me something that I have not said, let him take his place in Hell.\" (Using translation from Ibn Mājah 34)"],[7,"\"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: 'Whoever attributes to me something that I have not said, let him take his place in Hell.\" (Using translation from Ibn Mājah 34)"],[8,"Faith has seventy or seventy-two branches, the highest of which is 'There is no god but Allah' and the lowest of which is removing harm from the road, and modesty is a branch of faith."],[9,"I said, “O Messenger of Allah, which deed is best?” He said, “Faith in Allah and striving in His cause.”"],[10,"A man asked the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, saying, “O Messenger of Allah, which deed is best?” He said, “Faith in Allah.” He said, “Then what?” He said, “Then striving in the cause of Allah.” He said, “Then what?” He said, “Then an accepted Hajj.”"],[11,"\"The Messenger of Allah said: 'Adhere to righteousness even though you will not be able to do all acts of virtue. Know that the best of your deeds is Salat (prayer) and that no one maintains his ablution except a believer.'\" (Using translation from Ibn Mājah 277)"],[12,"Shall I not inform you of that by which Allah erases sins and raises ranks? Perfecting ablution despite difficulties, taking many steps to the mosques, and waiting for prayer after prayer. That is the ribat; that is the ribat; that is the ribat."],[13,"Shall I not guide you to that by which Allah erases sins and expiates misdeeds? They said: Yes, O Messenger of Allah. He said: Perfecting ablution in adverse conditions, taking many steps to the mosques, and waiting for prayer after prayer. That is the ribat."],[14,"When a Muslim or believing servant performs ablution and washes his face, every sin that his eyes looked upon leaves his face with the water or with the last drop of water. When he washes his hands, every sin that his hands committed leaves his hands with the water or with the last drop of water, until he emerges cleansed of sins."],[15,"Uthman b. Affan sat on the benches, and the muezzin came and announced the afternoon prayer. He called for water and performed ablution, then said: I will narrate to you a hadith that, were it not for a verse in the Book of Allah, I would not have narrated to you. Then he said: I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: There is no person who performs ablution and perfects it, then prays a prayer, except that he is forgiven for what is between it and the next prayer until he prays it."],[16,"They raided the campaign of al-Salasil, and the enemy slipped away from them, so they stayed on guard, then returned to Mu'awiyah, and with him were Abu Ayyub and Uqbah b. Amir. Asim said: O Abu Ayyub, the enemy slipped away from us this year, and…"],[17,"Whoever completes ablution as Allah, Mighty and Exalted, commanded him, the five prayers are an expiation for what is between them."],[18,"I was with Uthman b. Affan, and he called for water for purification and said: I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: There is no Muslim person for whom the prescribed prayer arrives, and he perfects its ablution, bowing, and humility, except that it is an expiation for the sins before it, as long as he does not commit a major sin, and that for all time."],[19,"The adornment of the people of Paradise reaches as far as the ablution reaches."],[20,"“Peace be upon you, abode of believing people. We will join you soon, if Allah wills.” Then he said: “Would that we could see our brothers.” They said: “O Messenger of Allah, are we not your brothers?” He said: “You are my Companions. My brothers are those who will come after me. I will reach the Cistern ahead of you.” They said: “O Messenger of Allah, how will you recognize those of your nation who have not yet come?” He said: “If a man has a horse with a blaze on its forehead and white feet, don’t you think that he will recognize it among horses that are deep black in color?” They said: “Of course.” He said: “On the Day of Resurrection they will come with radiant faces, hands, and feet, because of the traces of ablution.” He said: “I will reach the Cistern ahead of you.” Then he said: “Men will be driven away from my Cistern just as stray camels are driven away. And I will call to them: ‘Come here!’ But it will be said: ‘They changed after you were gone, and they kept turning on their heels.’ So I will say: “Be off with you!” (Using translation from Ibn Mājah 4306)"],[21,"You will come with white blazes and white marks from ablution, a distinguishing mark of my community that no one else has."],[22,"He saw Abu Hurayrah performing ablution, washing his face and hands until he almost reached the shoulders, then washing his feet up to the shins, then said: I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: My community on the Day of Resurrection will have white blazes and white marks from the traces of ablution. So whoever among you can extend his blaze, let him do so."],[23,"We were with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ as servants of ourselves, taking turns grazing our camels. I was on camel-grazing duty, and I brought them back in the evening. I caught up with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ while he was addressing the people, and I heard him say: 'There is none of you who performs ablution and perfects it, then stands and performs two rak'ahs, turning to them with his heart and face, but that it becomes obligatory [for him to enter Paradise].' He said: So I said, 'How excellent is this!' A man said, 'The one before it is more excellent.' I looked, and there was Umar b. al-Khattab. I said, 'What is it, O Abu Hafs?' He said, 'He said just now, before you came: \"There is no one who performs ablution and perfects it, then says when he finishes his ablution: 'I bear witness that there is no god but Allah alone, with no partner, and that Muhammad is His servant and Messenger,' but that the eight gates of Paradise are opened for him, and he may enter from whichever of them he wishes.\"'\""],[24,"The siwak is a purification for the mouth and a cause of the Lord's pleasure."],[25,"“If people knew what is in the call to prayer and the first row, and they found no way to it except by drawing lots, they would draw lots. If they knew what is in going early, they would race to it. And if they knew what is in the late evening prayer and the dawn prayer, they would come to them even crawling.”"],[26,"“I see that you love sheep and the desert. When you are with your sheep and in your desert and you call the adhan for prayer, raise your voice with the call, for no jinn, human, or thing hears the extent of the muezzin’s voice except that it will testify for him on the Day of Resurrection.”"],[27,"\"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: 'Whoever attributes to me something that I have not said, let him take his place in Hell.\" (Using translation from Ibn Mājah 34)"],[28,"“When the call to prayer is given, Satan retreats, passing wind, so that he does not hear the adhan. When the adhan is completed, he returns. When the iqamah is called, he retreats until it is completed, then he returns, whispering between a person and his soul, saying, ‘Remember such and such, remember such and such,’ about things he had not remembered before, until a man does not know how many rakʿahs he has prayed.”"],[29,"«Indeed, when Satan hears the call to prayer, he goes off until he is at the distance of al-Rawḥāʾ.»"],[30,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ heard a man while he was walking and saying \"Allah is the Greatest, Allah is the Greatest\". The Prophet ﷺ said, \"According to our innate nature (Fitrah)\". Then he said, \"I bear witness that there is no god but Allah\" and the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, \"He is forbidden from Hell\". So we rushed to catch up with him, and when the prayer reached him, he called out with it."],[31,"«The muezzin is forgiven as far as his voice reaches, and every moist and dry thing bears witness for him, and the one who attends the prayer is credited with twenty-five good deeds and expiated for what is between them.»"],[32,"We were with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ at Talaʿāt al-Nakhl when Bilal stood up to give the call. When he fell silent, the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: «Whoever says the like of what this one said with certainty will enter Paradise.»"],[33,"A man came to the Prophet ﷺ and said: O Messenger of Allah, my mount has perished, so give me a mount. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: «I do not have one.» Then a man said: I will guide him to someone who can carry him. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: «Whoever guides to good has the like of the reward of its doer.»"],[34,"«The muezzins will have the longest necks of people on the Day of Resurrection.»"],[35,"\"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: 'Whoever attributes to me something that I have not said, let him take his place in Hell.\" (Using translation from Ibn Mājah 34)"],[36,"«The imam is a guarantor and the muezzin is entrusted; may Allah guide the imams and pardon the muezzins.»"],[37,"\"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: 'Whoever attributes to me something that I have not said, let him take his place in Hell.\" (Using translation from Ibn Mājah 34)"],[38,"\"Whoever builds a mosque in which the name of Allah is remembered, Allah builds for him a house in Paradise.\""],[39,"\"Whoever builds a mosque, Allah builds for him the like of it in Paradise.\""],[40,"\"Whoever builds a mosque for Allah, even if like the scrape of a sandgrouse, Allah builds for him a house in Paradise.\""],[41,"\"Whoever builds a mosque for Allah, even if like the scrape of a sandgrouse, Allah builds for him a house in Paradise.\""],[42,"A man asked the Prophet ﷺ, 'Which places are the worst?' He said, 'I do not know until I ask Gabriel.' He asked Gabriel, who said, 'I do not know until I ask Michael.' He came and said, 'The best of places are the mosques and the worst are the markets.'"],[43,"The most beloved of lands to Allah are their mosques, and the most hated of lands to Allah are their markets."],[44,"«In a human being there are three hundred and sixty joints; he must give charity for each joint of his.» They said: \"Who can do that, O Messenger of Allah?\" He said: \"Bury sputum that you see in the mosque, or remove something from the road. If you do not find anything, then the two rakʿahs of Ḍuḥā will suffice you.\""],[45,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ commanded the building of mosques in residential areas and that they be perfumed and cleaned."],[46,"Sulayman b. Dawud asked Allah, Blessed and Exalted, for three things, and He granted him two, and I hope He granted him the third. He asked Him for a kingdom that would not befit anyone after him, and He granted it to him. He asked Him for a judgment that would coincide with His judgment, and He granted it to him. He asked Him that whoever comes to this House—meaning the Holy House (Jerusalem)—intending only to pray in it, that he would come out of it as on the day his mother gave birth to him.' The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, 'And I hope that He granted him the third.'"],[47,"A man from the people of Najd came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ with disheveled hair; the murmur of his voice could be heard but what he was saying could not be understood until he came near to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and it turned out he was asking about Islam. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to him, “Five prayers in the day and night.” He said, “Are there any others due on me?” He said, “No, unless you do voluntary ones.” He said: And the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, “And fasting the month of Ramadan.” He said, “Is there any other due on me?” He said, “No, unless you do voluntary ones.” He said: And the Messenger of Allah ﷺ mentioned zakah to him. He said, “Is there any other due on me?” He said, “No, unless you do voluntary ones.” He said: The man turned away saying, “By Allah, I will not add to this nor subtract from it anything.” The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, “He will succeed if he is truthful.”"],[48,"\"Muḥammad ﷺ saw his Lord.\""],[49,"I heard Abu Muhammad Al-Ansari say, \"Witr prayer is obligatory.\" Ubada said, \"Abu Muhammad is lying. I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say, 'Allah has made five prayers obligatory upon His servants. Whoever fulfills them, completing and not diminishing them out of neglecting their rights, Allah will have a covenant with him to enter Paradise. And whoever fulfills them but diminishes them out of neglecting their rights, Allah will not have a covenant with him. He may either punish him or show him mercy.'\""],[50,"He asked the Prophet ﷺ, 'Which deeds are most beloved to Allah?' He said, 'The prayer at its time.' He said, 'Then which?' He said, 'Dutifulness to parents.' He said, 'Then which?' He said, 'Jihad in the path of Allah.' He said, 'He singled me out with these, and had I asked for more, he would have added more.'"],[51,"I asked the Prophet ﷺ, 'Which deed is best?' He said, 'The prayer at its time.'"],[52,"I said, 'O Messenger of Allah, which deeds are best?' He said, 'The prayer at the beginning of its time.'"],[53,"We complained to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ about the heat burning our feet, but he did not respond to our complaint."],[54,"“The likeness of the prescribed prayers is that of a flowing river at the door of one of you, in which he bathes five times every day.”"],[55,"“Do you think that if there were a river at the door of one of you in which he bathed five times every day, would any of his dirt remain?” They said, “No dirt of his would remain.” He said, “That is the likeness of the five prayers: through them Allah erases sins.”"],[56,"\"Whoever conceals knowledge, Allah will bridle him on the Day of Resurrection with a bridle of fire.\""],[57,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: Five prayers and from one Friday prayer to (the next) Friday prayer is an expiation (of the sins committed in between their intervals) if major sins are not committed. (Using translation from Muslim 233a)"],[58,"“O Kaab b. Ujrah, I seek refuge for you with Allah from the rule of fools. There will be rulers: whoever enters upon them, helps them in their wrongdoing, and confirms their lies is not of me, and I am not of him, and he will not come to me at the pond. Whoever does not enter upon them, does not help them in their wrongdoing, and does not confirm their lies is of me, and I am of him, and he will come to me at the pond. O Kaab b. Ujrah, prayer is an offering, fasting is a shield, and charity extinguishes sin just as water extinguishes fire. People go out in the morning: one sells himself and sets his soul free, or one destroys it. O Kaab b. Ujrah, no flesh that grew from ill-gotten gain will enter Paradise.”"],[59,"That he asked the Messenger of Allah ﷺ about praying while sitting. The Prophet ﷺ said: 'Pray standing, for that is better. Whoever prays sitting gets half the reward of one who stands, and whoever prays lying down gets half the reward of one who sits.'"],[60,"The excellence of the prayer of a person in congregation over the prayer of a man alone is twenty-five degrees."],[61,"Congregational prayer is superior to the prayer of one alone by twenty-seven degrees."],[62,"A man's prayer in congregation exceeds his prayer alone by twenty-five degrees. If he prays it in a barren land, perfecting its ablution, its bowing, and its prostration, his prayer is recorded as fifty degrees."],[63,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ led us in the morning prayer and said: \"Is so-and-so present?\" They said: No. He said: \"Is so-and-so present?\" They said: No. He said: \"These two prayers are the heaviest prayers for the hypocrites. If they knew the virtue in them, they would come to them even crawling. The first row is like the row of the angels. If you knew its virtue, you would race to it. A man's prayer with two men is purer than his prayer with one man, and the more (the number), the more beloved to Allah.\""],[64,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ delayed the 'Isha' prayer until half the night had passed. Then he came and said, 'The people have prayed and slept, but you have remained in prayer since you began waiting.' Anas said, 'It is as if I am looking at the glint of his ring.'"],[65,"Whoever is in a mosque waiting for the prayer, he is in prayer."],[66,"Whoever waits for the prayer is in prayer as long as he does not nullify it."],[67,"The angels send blessings upon one of you as long as he remains in his prayer place where he prayed, as long as he does not nullify it: 'O Allah, forgive him; O Allah, have mercy on him.'"],[68,"\"A man does not settle in the mosque for prayer or for the remembrance of Allah except that Allah rejoices in him, just as the family of an absent person rejoices when their absent one returns to them.\""],[69,"We wanted to move near the mosque, and the areas around the mosque were empty. That reached the Prophet ﷺ, and he came to us in our home and said: \"O Banu Salimah, it has reached me that you want to move near the mosque.\" They said: O Messenger of Allah, the mosque has become far for us, and the areas around it are empty. He said: \"O Banu Salimah, stay in your homes, stay in your homes, so that your footsteps are recorded.\" He said: We did not wish that we were near the mosque after the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said what he said."],[70,"A man's prayer in congregation exceeds his prayer in his house and his prayer in his market by twenty-five degrees. That is because when one of them performs ablution and does it well, then comes to the mosque intending only the prayer, he does not take a step except that Allah raises him a degree by it and removes from him a sin by it until he enters the mosque. When he enters the mosque, he is in prayer as long as the prayer holds him there."],[71,"Whoever purifies himself in his house, then walks to one of the houses of Allah to fulfill an obligation from the obligations of Allah, his two steps are: one of them removes a sin and the other raises a degree."],[72,"When a man purifies himself, then comes to the mosque to guard the prayer, his two recording angels write for him ten good deeds for every step he takes toward the mosque."],[73,"Whoever goes early to the mosque or returns, Allah prepares for him a place of hospitality in Paradise each time he goes early or returns."],[74,"Whoever walks through the darkness of the night to the mosques, Allah will give him light on the Day of Resurrection."],[75,"She came to the Prophet ﷺ and said: “O Messenger of Allah, I love to pray with you.” He said: “I know that you love to pray with me, but your prayer in your private room is better than your prayer in your courtyard, and your prayer in your courtyard is better than your prayer in your house, and your prayer in your house is better than your prayer in the mosque of your people, and your prayer in the mosque of your people is better than your prayer in my mosque.” He said: So she ordered, and a prayer place was built for her in the farthest and darkest part of her house, and she used to pray there until she met Allah, may He be glorified and exalted."],[76,"“When you see a man frequenting the mosque, bear witness to his faith.” Allah, Mighty and Exalted, said: {Only those who believe in Allah and the Last Day maintain the mosques of Allah}"],[77,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to come to us and wipe our shoulders and chests, saying, “Do not differ in your rows, lest your hearts differ. Indeed, Allah and His angels send blessings upon the first row.”"],[78,"He used to “send blessings upon the first, foremost row three times, and upon the second once.”"],[79,"“The Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to send blessings upon the foremost row three times and upon the second once.”"],[80,"“Indeed, Allah and His angels send blessings upon the right sides of the rows.”"],[81,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to wipe our shoulders and chests, saying, “Do not differ, lest your hearts differ. Indeed, Allah and His angels send blessings upon the front rows.”"],[82,"«Allah and His angels send blessings upon those who join the rows.»"],[83,"«Allah and His angels send blessings upon those who join the rows.»"],[84,"A man came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and said, 'O Messenger of Allah, which prayer is best?' He said, 'Length of qunut.'"],[85,"When the son of Ādam recites a prostration verse and prostrates, Satan withdraws weeping and says: “Woe to him! The son of Ādam was commanded to prostrate and he prostrated, so he will have Paradise, but I was commanded to prostrate and I refused, so I will have the Fire.”"],[86,"ʿAbd Allāh b. ʿUmar saw a young man while he was praying—he had lengthened his prayer and prolonged it—and said: “Who knows this one?” A man said: “I do.” ʿAbd Allāh said: “If I knew him, I would have commanded him to lengthen the bowing and the prostration, for I heard the Prophet ﷺ say: ‘When a servant stands to pray, his sins are brought and placed upon his head or his shoulder, and every time he bows or prostrates, they fall away from him.’”"],[87,"I met Thawbān, the freed slave of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and said to him: “Narrate to me a ḥadīth that perhaps Allah will benefit me by.” He said: “You must prostrate, for I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: ‘There is no servant who prostrates to Allah a single prostration except that Allah raises him a degree by it and removes from him a sin by it.’”"],[88,"“The closest a servant is to his Lord is when he is prostrating, so increase supplication.”"],[89,"“When a servant prostrates, seven parts prostrate with him: his face, his knees, his palms, and his feet.”"],[90,"The one who sits waiting for the prayer is like the one in constant devotion, and he is written among those who pray from the time he leaves his house until he returns to his house."],[91,"Whoever goes to a mosque for congregational prayer, his two steps are: a step that erases a bad deed and a step that records a good deed, going and returning."],[92,"“No one will enter the Fire who prayed before sunrise and before sunset.”"],[93,"Whoever prays the ‘Ishā’ and the morning prayer in congregation, it is as if he stood the night in prayer."],[94,"Whoever prays the ‘Ishā’ and Fajr in congregation, it is like standing the night in prayer."],[95,"‘Uthmān b. ‘Affān entered the mosque after the Maghrib prayer and sat alone, and I sat with him. He said, ‘O son of my brother, I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: “Whoever prays the ‘Ishā’ in congregation, it is as if he stood half the night in prayer, and whoever prays the morning prayer in congregation, it is as if he prayed the entire night.”’"],[96,"“Angels succeed one another among you: angels at night and angels by day, and they gather at the dawn prayer and the afternoon prayer. Then those who spent the night among you ascend, and He asks them—though He is most knowing—‘How did you leave My servants?’ They say: ‘We left them while they were praying, and we came to them while they were praying.’”"],[97,"They take turns among you: when the Fajr prayer is due, the angels of the day descend and attend the prayer with you all, while the angels of the night ascend. The angels of the day remain with you, and their Lord asks them—though He is most knowing—‘What did you leave My servants doing?’ They say, ‘We came to them while they were praying, and we left them while they were praying.’ He [the narrator] said, ‘I think they say, “So forgive them on the Day of Judgment.”’"],[98,"“Whoever prays the morning prayer is under Allah’s protection, so beware, O son of Ādam, that Allah should demand from you anything of His protection.”"],[99,"A man came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and said, “O Messenger of Allah, I have committed a punishable offense, so carry out the punishment on me.” He turned away from him. Then he said, “O Messenger of Allah, I have committed a punishable offense, so carry out the punishment on me,” and he turned away from him. Then the prayer was begun, and when he had said the salam, he said, “O Messenger of Allah, I have committed a punishable offense, so carry out the punishment on me.” The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, “Did you perform ablution when you came?” He said, “Yes.” He said, “Did you pray with us?” He said, “Yes.” He said, “Then go, for Allah has forgiven you.”"],[100,"\"A man came to the Prophet ﷺ and said, 'I had relations with a woman in the garden, and I did everything except getting married to her. So, do with me whatever you wish.' The Prophet ﷺ remained silent. Then he called the man and recited the following verse to him: \"Perform the prayer at the two ends of the day and at the approach of the night. Indeed, good deeds remove bad deeds.\""],[101,"“And perform prayers at the two ends of the day and in some hours of the night. Verily, the good deeds remove the evil deeds. That is a reminder for the mindful.” [11:114] The man said: “O Messenger of Allah, is this (the Verse) just for me?” He said: “It is for whoever acts upon it among my nation.” (Using translation from Ibn Mājah 4254)"],[102,"A man said, \"O Messenger of Allah, I met a woman in the garden, and I embraced her, kissed her, engaged in foreplay with her, and did everything with her except for intercourse.\" The Messenger of Allah remained silent, so Allah revealed, \"Establish prayer at the two ends of the day and at the approach of the night. Indeed, good deeds do away with misdeeds. That is a reminder for those who remember.\" The Messenger of Allah called him and recited it to him, then Umar asked, \"O Messenger of Allah, is this verse specific to him?\" The Messenger of Allah said, \"No, it is for all people.\""],[103,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ led us in the afternoon prayer, then said: “This prayer was presented to those before you, but they neglected it and abandoned it. Whoever among them prays it will have his reward doubled twice, and there is no prayer after it until the witness is seen”—and the witness is the star."],[104,"“Whoever prays the two cool prayers will enter Paradise.”"],[105,"“Never will enter the Fire one who prays before sunrise and before sunset.” A man from the people said: “Did you hear this ḥadīth from the Messenger of Allah ﷺ?” He said: “Yes.”"],[106,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ made a small enclosure with a mat in Ramadan and prayed in it for some nights. Some of his companions prayed following his prayer. When he learned of them, he began to stay seated. Then he came out to them and said, \"I recognized what I saw of your doing. O people, pray in your houses, for the best prayer of a person is in his house except the obligatory.\""],[107,"This is a Hadith from the Prophet Muhammad ﷺ . It says: \"The sun does not rise or set on a day better than Friday. Every creature is in a state of panic on the day of Friday except for these two: jinn and humans.\""],[108,"At every gate of the mosque there are two angels, writing down the first, then the next. Thus, one is like one who brings a she-camel, one is like one who brings a cow, one is like one who brings a sheep, one is like one who brings a bird, and one is like one who brings an egg. When the imam sits, the scrolls are folded up."],[109,"Whoever bathes on Friday with the bath of janabah, then goes early, it is as if he sacrificed a she-camel. Whoever goes in the second hour, it is as if he sacrificed a cow. Whoever goes in the third hour, it is as if he sacrificed a ram. Whoever goes in the fourth hour, it is as if he sacrificed a chicken. Whoever goes in the fifth hour, it is as if he sacrificed an egg. When the imam comes out, the angels attend to listen to the remembrance."],[110,"“Part of the fitrah of Islam is bathing on the day of Jumu'ah, using the tooth-stick, trimming the moustache, and letting the beard grow; for the Magians let their moustaches grow and shave their beards. So differ from them: trim your moustaches and let your beards grow.”"],[111,"Abu Qatadah came to me while I was bathing on Friday and said, “Is this bath of yours due to janabah?” I said, “Yes.” He said, “Perform another bath, for I heard the Prophet ﷺ say, ‘Whoever bathes on Friday remains pure until the next Friday.’”"],[112,"Whoever bathes on Friday and purifies himself as much as he can, then anoints himself with his oil or the perfume of his house, then goes to Friday prayer, and does not separate between two people, then prays as much as is decreed for him, then when the imam comes out, he listens silently, he will be forgiven what is between that Friday and the next Friday."],[113,"Whoever bathes on Friday, uses the siwak, touches perfume if he has any, wears his finest garments, then comes to the mosque without stepping over people's necks, then prays as much as Allah wills, then listens silently when his imam comes out until he prays, it will be an expiation for what is between that Friday and the Friday before it."],[114,"Whoever performs wudu and does it well, then comes to Friday prayer, and listens and remains silent, he will be forgiven what is between that Friday and the next Friday plus three days; and whoever touches the pebbles has engaged in idle talk."],[115,"Whoever bathes on Friday and does his bathing well, wears his best clothes, and touches the perfume or oil of his house, he will be forgiven what is between that Friday and the next Friday plus three days of the one after it."],[116,"Whoever washes on Friday and bathes, then comes early and is early, walks, draws near, listens, remains silent, and does not engage in idle talk, Allah will write for him for every step he takes the worship of a year, its fasting and its standing in prayer."],[117,"I said to Ibn Abbas, 'They claim that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: Bathe on Friday and wash your heads, unless you are in a state of janabah, and touch perfume.'"],[118,"He said, \"I went out to At-Tur and met Ka'b Al-Ahbar, so I sat with him and he told me about the Torah. I also told him about the Messenger of Allah ﷺ . In what he narrated, I said, 'The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, 'The best day on which the sun has risen is Friday; on it, Adam was created, on it he entered Paradise, on it he was expelled, on it he died, on it the Trumpet will be blown, and on it all creatures will swoon. Every beast is on the lookout from the time the sun rises until it has risen, fearing the coming of the Hour, except the Jinn and humans. There is an hour on Friday that no Muslim slave stands when praying and asks Allah for anything but He will give it to him.'\" Ka'b said, \"That happens every year on a day.\" I said, \"No, but every Friday.\" Ka`b said, \"So I read the Torah and he (i.e., the Prophet) said, 'The Messenger of Allah has spoken the truth.'\""],[119,"“In Friday there is an hour in which no Muslim standing praying asks Allah for good except that He gives it to him.”"],[120,"\"That the Prophet of Allah ﷺ was not more persistent in any of the supererogatory prayers than he was in the two rak'ahs before Fajr.\""],[121,"\"I did not see the Messenger of Allah ﷺ hasten to anything of the supererogatory prayers faster than he did to the two rak'ahs before Fajr, nor to any booty he might gain.\""],[122,"\"The two rak'ahs before Fajr are dearer to me than the world and all it contains.\""],[123,"\"I observed the Prophet ﷺ for a month, and he used to recite in the two rak'ahs before Fajr: 'Say, O disbelievers' and 'Say, He is Allah, the One.'\""],[124,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to say, “What excellent two surahs they are, which are recited in the two rak'ahs before Fajr: Say: O disbelievers and Say: He is Allah, the One.”"],[125,"A man stood and prayed the two rak'ahs of Fajr. In the first rak'ah he recited {Say: O disbelievers} until he completed the surah. The Prophet ﷺ said, “This is a servant who has known his Lord.” In the second he recited {Say: He is Allah, the One} until he completed the surah. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, “This is a servant who has believed in his Lord.” Talhah said, “I prefer to recite these two surahs in these two rak'ahs.”"],[126,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ dispatched a military expedition, and they deemed the spoils to be great and were swift in their return. A man said, \"O Messenger of Allah, we have not seen an expedition of people swifter in return nor greater in spoils than this expedition.\" He ﷺ said, \"Shall I not inform you of one swifter in return and greater in spoils than this expedition? A man who performs wudu' in his house and perfects his wudu', then carries himself to the mosque and prays the dawn prayer in it, then follows it with the Duha prayer. He has indeed been swift in return and great in spoils.\""],[127,"\"My dearest friend advised me (to do) three things: 'To sleep after praying Witr, to fast three days each month, and to pray two rak'ahs of Fajr.'\" (Using translation from Nasāʾī 1677)"],[128,"O son of Adam, pray four rak'ahs for Me at the beginning of the day, and I will suffice you at its end."],[129,"I saw the Messenger of Allah ﷺ in the year of the conquest. I said, \"O Messenger of Allah, I have granted protection to my two brothers-in-law, but the son of my mother—meaning 'Ali—claims that he will kill him.\" She said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, \"We have granted protection to whomever you have granted protection, O Umm Hani'.\" She said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ poured water and performed ghusl, then wrapped himself in a garment and crossed its two ends, and prayed the Duha prayer with eight rak'ahs."],[130,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ recited the morning (Duha) prayer and I couldn't find anyone to inform me about it except for Umm Hani bint Abi Talib, who informed me that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ performed it after the day had risen on the day of the conquest. He ordered for a garment to be brought to cover him, then he performed ablution and stood up and performed eight units of prayer. I do not know whether his standing or his bowing or his prostration was longer in duration. All of that was performed consecutively. She said: \"I did not see him reciting anything before or after it.\""],[131,"He saw some people praying Duha in the mosque of Quba' and said, \"They knew that prayer at a time other than this is better. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, 'The prayer of the oft-returning is when the young camels feel the heat.'\""],[132,"\"In a human being there are three hundred and sixty joints; for each joint a charity is due.\" They said, \"O Messenger of Allah, who can do that?\" He said, \"You remove something harmful, or if not, then two rak'ahs of Duha.\""],[133,"O son of Adam, pray four rak'ahs for Me at the beginning of the day, and I will suffice you at its end."],[134,"\"May Allah have mercy on a person who prays four (rak'ahs) before Asr.\""],[135,"\"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: 'Whoever prays twelve rak'ahs in a day apart from the obligatory prayers, Allah (SWT) will build for him, or there will be built for him, a house in Paradise.'\" (Using translation from Nasāʾī 1808)"],[136,"From the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, he said: \"Whoever prays twelve rak'ahs in a day, Allah builds for him a house in Paradise: four rak'ahs before Zuhr, two rak'ahs before Asr, two rak'ahs after Maghrib, and two rak'ahs before Fajr.\""],[137,"Whoever believes in Allah and His Messenger, establishes the prayer, and fasts Ramadan, it is incumbent upon Allah to admit him to Paradise, whether he emigrated in the path of Allah or remained in the land where his mother gave birth to him."],[138,"He sat on the pulpit and then said, 'By the One in Whose Hand is my soul,' three times, then fell silent. Every man among us bowed his head weeping in sorrow at the oath of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. Then he said, 'There is no servant who performs the five prayers, fasts Ramadan, and avoids the seven major sins except that the eight gates of Paradise will be opened for him on the Day of Resurrection, such that they will clatter.' Then he recited: {If you avoid the major sins which you are forbidden, We will expiate from you your evil deeds}."],[139,"\"Whoever fasts Ramadan out of faith and seeking reward, his previous sins will be forgiven.\""],[140,"Messenger of Allah ﷺ was asked about the offspring of the pagans. He said, \"Allah knows what they would have done (were they to live).\" (Using translation from Bukhārī 6598)"],[141,"\"When the first night of the month of Ramadan comes, the rebellious devils among the jinn are chained, the gates of the Fire are closed so that no gate among them is opened, the gates of Paradise are opened so that no gate among them is closed, and a caller calls out: 'O seeker of good, come forward! O seeker of evil, desist!' And Allah has those freed from the Fire, and that is every night.\""],[142,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ was the most generous of people in goodness, and he was most generous in the month of Ramadan. Jibril used to meet him every night of Ramadan until it ended, reviewing the Qur'an with him. When Jibril met him, the Messenger of Allah ﷺ was more generous in goodness than the sent wind."],[143,"\"Every deed of the son of Adam is for him except fasting; fasting is for Me and I reward it. The changed breath of the fasting person is more pleasant to Allah than the scent of musk.\""],[144,"Every deed of the son of Adam is for him except fasting, for it is for Me and I reward it. By the One in whose hand is the soul of Muhammad, the changed breath of the fasting person is more pleasant to Allah on the Day of Resurrection than the scent of musk. The fasting person has two joys: when he breaks his fast he rejoices in his breaking it, and when he meets Allah he rejoices in his fasting."],[145,"On the authority of the Prophet ﷺ, he said: \"Every good deed that the son of Adam performs is multiplied from ten good deeds up to seven hundredfold. Allah says: 'Except for fasting, for it is Mine and I shall reward it. He gives up his food for My sake, his drink for My sake, and his desire for My sake, and I shall reward it. The fasting person has two joys: a joy when he breaks his fast and a joy when he meets his Lord. And the changed breath of the mouth of the fasting person when it changes due to food is more pleasant to Allah than the scent of musk.'\""],[146,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ prepared an army, so I came to him and said: O Messenger of Allah, supplicate to Allah for martyrdom for me. He said: \"O Allah, grant them safety and spoils.\" So we went on a military expedition and we were safe and obtained spoils, until he mentioned that three times. He said: Then I came to him and said: O Messenger of Allah, I came to you repeatedly three times asking you to supplicate for martyrdom for me, and you said: \"O Allah, grant them safety and spoils,\" and we were safe and obtained spoils. O Messenger of Allah, so command me with a deed by which I may enter Paradise. He said: \"You must fast, for there is nothing like it.\" He said: So Abu Umamah would never be seen with smoke in his house during the day unless a guest came to them. When they saw smoke during the day, they knew that a guest had come upon them."],[147,"\"Fasting is a shield.\""],[148,"Whoever does not abandon false speech and acting upon it, and ignorance, Allah has no need for him to give up his food and drink."],[149,"\"Whoever fasts Ramadan and knows its limits and guards what should be guarded, it will expiate what came before it.\""],[150,"\"Whoever spends a pair of anything in the way of Allah is called from the gates of Paradise: 'O servant of Allah, this is good.' Paradise has gates. Whoever is from the people of prayer is called from the gate of prayer. Whoever is from the people of jihad is called from the gate of jihad. Whoever is from the people of charity is called from the gate of charity. Whoever is from the people of fasting is called from the gate of al-Rayyan.\" He said: Abu Bakr said, \"O Messenger of Allah, no one is under any compulsion in which of them he is called from; will everyone be called from all of them, O Messenger of Allah?\" He said, \"Yes, and I hope you will be among them.\""],[151,"A man asked the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, saying, “O Messenger of Allah, which deed is best?” He said, “Faith in Allah.” He said, “Then what?” He said, “Then striving in the cause of Allah.” He said, “Then what?” He said, “Then an accepted Hajj.”"],[152,"In Paradise there is a gate which is called Rayyan through which only the people who fast would enter on the Day on Resurrection. None else would enter along with them. It would be proclaimed: Where are the people who fast that they should be admitted into it? And when the last of them would enter, it would be closed and no one would enter it. (Using translation from Muslim 1152)"],[153,"Indeed Allah and His angels send blessings upon those who take the pre-dawn meal."],[154,"«It is the blessed morning meal,» meaning the pre-dawn meal (sahur)."],[155,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ entered upon her, and she called for food for him. He said: \"Come and eat.\" She said: I am fasting. He said: \"When food is eaten in the presence of a fasting person, the angels send blessings upon him.\""],[156,"People will continue to be upon good as long as they hasten the breaking of the fast."],[157,"The most beloved of My servants to Me is the one who is quickest in breaking the fast."],[158,"\"Three people's supplications are not rejected: the fasting person until he breaks his fast, the just ruler, and the supplication of the oppressed.\""],[159,"\"Whoever gives a fasting person something to break his fast with, the like of his reward is written for him, without diminishing anything from the fasting person's reward.\""],[160,"\"When one of you breaks his fast, let him break it with dates; if he does not find any, let him sip a sip of water.\""],[161,"ʿUthmān b. Abī al-ʿĀṣ called for milk to offer it, and Muṭarrif said, \"I am fasting.\" ʿUthmān said, \"I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say, 'Fasting is a shield, like the shield of any one of you in battle.'\""],[162,"\"A Bedouin came to the Prophet with a rabbit that he had grilled it and placed it in front of him. The Messenger of Allah refrained from eating, but he told the people to eat. The Bedouin also refrained, and the Prophet said to him: 'What is keeping you from eating?' He said: 'I fast three days of the month.' He said: 'If you was to fast, fast the shining days.\"' (Using translation from Nasāʾī 2421)"],[163,"The Prophet ﷺ used to command them to fast the white days (ayyām al-bīḍ), and he would say, \"They are the fast of a lifetime.\""],[164,"Fasting three days of every month is fasting a lifetime and its standing [in prayer]."],[165,"Fasting three days of every month is fasting a lifetime and its breaking [of the fast]."],[166,"I said to 'A'ishah, \"Did the Prophet ﷺ fast three days of the month?\" She said, \"Yes.\" I said, \"In which part of it?\" She said, \"He did not mind in which part of it he fasted.\""],[167,"Whoever fasts Ramadan and follows it with six from Shawwal, that is fasting the entire lifetime."],[168,"Whoever fasts Ramadan and six from Shawwal has fasted the year."],[169,"The best fasting after the month of Ramadan is the month of Allah, Muharram, and the best prayer after the obligatory prayer is the night prayer."],[170,"I came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and asked him about fasting. He said, \"Fast one day of every month, and you will have the reward of the rest.\" I said, \"I can bear more than that.\" He said, \"Fast two days of every month, and you will have the reward of the rest.\" I said, \"I can bear more than that.\" He said, \"Fast three days of every month, and you will have the reward of the rest.\" I said, \"I can bear more than that.\" He said, \"Indeed, the most beloved fasting to Allah is the fast of Dawud. He used to fast one day and break his fast one day.\""],[171,"Abu Hurayrah was on a journey. When they stopped and the food was laid out, they sent for him while he was praying. He said, \"I am fasting.\" When they had almost finished, he came and began to eat. The people looked at their messenger, and he said, \"Why are you looking at me? By Allah, he had [said he was fasting].\""],[172,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ was informed that I said, \"By Allah, I will fast the day and stand in prayer at night as long as I live.\" I said to him, \"I said it, O Messenger of Allah.\" He said, \"Indeed, you will not be able to do that. Fast and break your fast, sleep and stand in prayer, and fast three days of the month, for a good deed is multiplied by ten, and that is like fasting a lifetime.\""],[173,"I came to ʿĀʾishah to ask her about the fasting of the Prophet ﷺ, and she said, \"The Prophet ﷺ used to fast until we would say, 'He has fasted,' then he would break his fast until we would say, 'He has broken his fast.' And I never saw him fast more in any month after Ramadan than he did in Shaʿbān; he used to fast all of it except a little.\""],[174,"A man came to the Prophet ﷺ and said, \"O Prophet of Allah, how do you fast?\" He said: The Prophet ﷺ became angry. When ʿUmar saw that, he said, \"We are content with Allah as Lord, with Islam as religion, and with Muhammad ﷺ as Prophet. We seek refuge in Allah from the anger of Allah and the anger of His Messenger,\" and he kept repeating it until the Prophet's ﷺ anger subsided. Then he said, \"O Prophet of Allah, how about one who fasts two days and breaks his fast one day?\" He said, \"Can anyone bear that?\" He said, \"Then how about one who fasts one day and breaks his fast one day?\" He said, \"That is the fast of my brother Dāwūd.\" He said, \"Then how about one who fasts one day and breaks his fast two days?\" He said, \"I wish I were given the strength for that.\""],[175,"A Bedouin man asked the Prophet صلى الله عليه وسلم about fasting for a lifetime. The Prophet صلى الله عليه وسلم replied, \"He neither fasts nor breaks his fast.\" Another person stood up and asked, \"O Messenger of Allah, what do you think about a man who fasts three days every month?\" The Prophet صلى الله عليه وسلم replied, \"That is the fasting for a lifetime.\" The person then asked, \"What do you think about a man who fasts on Mondays?\" The Prophet صلى الله عليه وسلم said, \"That is the day I was born and the day in which revelation was sent to me.\" The person asked again, \"What do you think about a man who fasts one day and breaks his fast the next day?\" The Prophet صلى الله عليه وسلم replied, \"That is the fasting of my brother Dawood (David).\""],[176,"\"The gates of Paradise are opened every Monday and Thursday, and the deeds are presented every Monday and Thursday.\""],[177,"“The gates of Paradise are opened on Monday and Thursday, and Allah forgives every Muslim servant who does not associate anything with Allah, except a man between whom and his brother there is enmity. It is said, ‘Delay these two until they reconcile. Delay these two until they reconcile.’”"],[178,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ sent on the morning of Ashura to the villages of the Ansar around Madinah: Whoever has begun the day fasting, let him complete his fast, and whoever has begun the day not fasting, let him fast the rest of that day. She said: So we used to fast it and make our young children fast, and we would take them to the mosque and make for them a toy of wool, and if one of them cried for food, we would give it to him until it was time to break the fast."],[179,"A man asked the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, \"O Messenger of Allah, what do you think about a man who fasts on the day of Ashura?\" He said, \"That is the fasting of a Sunnah.\" The man asked, \"And what about a man who fasts on the day of Arafah?\" He said, \"It expiates the sins of the previous year and the coming year.\""],[180,"Fasting the day of Arafah: I count on Allah that it expiates the year before it and the year after it. And fasting the day of Ashura: I count on Allah that it expiates the year before it."],[181,"I came to Ibn Abbas while he was reclining on his cloak at Zamzam, so I sat with him, and what an excellent companion he was. I asked him about Ashura. He sat up straight and said, \"About which aspect of it are you asking?\" I said, \"About its fasting: which day do we fast?\" He said, \"When you see the crescent of Muharram, count, then begin the ninth day fasting.\" I said, \"Is that how Muhammad ﷺ used to fast?\" He said, \"Yes.\""],[182,"“Fasting is not merely from eating and drinking; rather, fasting is from vain talk and obscenity. If someone insults you or acts ignorantly towards you, say, ‘I am fasting.’”"],[183,"\"The eater who is thankful is of the station of the fasting one who is patient.\""],[184,"I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say about Ramadan: \"Whoever stands in it out of faith and seeking reward, his previous sins will be forgiven for him.\""],[185,"When the ten days entered, the Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to keep the night alive, tighten his waist-wrapper, and wake his family."],[186,"A man came to the Prophet ﷺ and said, 'O Messenger of Allah, tell me: if I testify that there is no god but Allah and that you are the Messenger of Allah, perform the five prayers, give zakat, fast Ramadan, and stand in prayer during it, then among whom am I?' He said, 'Among the truthful and the martyrs.'"],[187,"We fasted with the Prophet ﷺ in Ramadan, and he did not lead us in prayer on the sixth night, but he led us on the fifth until he went to wait for the night. We said, \"O Messenger of Allah, if only you would lead us in supererogatory prayer for the rest of this night of ours.\" He said, \"Whoever stands with the imam until he departs, the standing of a whole night is recorded for him.\" Then he did not pray with us until three days of the month remained. He led us on the third night and gathered his family and his women, and he led us until we feared that we would miss the time of the pre-dawn meal."],[188,"We mentioned the Night of Decree in the presence of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, so the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “How much of the month has passed?” We said, “Twenty-two days have passed and eight remain.” Then he ﷺ said: “No, rather twenty-two days have passed and seven remain; the month is twenty-nine days, so seek it tonight.”"],[189,"Whoever spends the night in a state of purity, an angel spends the night in his garment, and he does not awaken except that the angel says: 'O Allah, forgive Your servant so-and-so, for he spent the night in a state of purity.'"],[190,"“Satan ties three knots at the nape of one of your heads when he sleeps. He strikes the place of each knot saying: ‘You have a long night, so sleep.’ If he wakes up and remembers Allah, one knot is undone. If he performs ablution, one knot is undone. If he prays, one knot is undone. Then he enters the morning energetic and pleasant in spirit; otherwise he enters the morning foul in spirit and lazy.”"],[191,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to me: “There is no male or female except that there is a tied rope on his head when he sleeps. If he wakes up and remembers Allah, one knot is undone. Then if he gets up, performs ablution, and prays, the knots are undone.”"],[192,"“There is no Muslim, male or female, who sleeps except that there is a tied rope upon him. If he wakes up and remembers Allah, one knot is undone. If he performs ablution then stands for prayer, he enters the morning energetic, having attained good, and all his knots are undone. But if he enters the morning without remembering Allah, he enters the morning with his knots upon him, heavy, lazy, and having attained no good.”"],[193,"And I heard the Prophet ﷺ say: 'A man from my community gets up at night, striving against himself to purify himself, while there are knots upon you. When he washes his hands, a knot is undone; when he washes his face, a knot is undone; when he wipes his head, a knot is undone; when he washes his feet, a knot is undone. Then Allah, Mighty and Exalted, says to those behind the veil: \"Look at this servant of Mine, striving against himself. Whatever My servant asks Me, it is his; whatever My servant asks Me, it is his.\"'\""],[194,"“Our Lord wonders at two men: a man who rises from his bed and cover, from between his beloved and his family, to his prayer. Allah, Mighty and Exalted, says to His angels: ‘Look at My servant, he rises from his bed and cover, from between his beloved and his family, to his prayer, out of desire for what is with Me and fear of what is with Me.’ And a man who fights in the path of Allah, and his companions flee, but he knows what is upon him in fleeing and what is for him in returning, so he returns until his blood is shed. Allah says to His angels: ‘Look at My servant, he returned hoping for what is with Me and fearing what is with Me, until his blood was shed.’”"],[195,"I said, \"O Messenger of Allah, whenever I see you, my soul becomes content and my eyes become tranquil. Inform me about everything.\" He said, \"Everything was created from water.\" So, I said, \"Tell me something that if I do, I will enter Paradise.\" He said, \"Feed the hungry, spread peace, maintain family ties, and pray during the night while people are asleep. You will enter Paradise in peace.\""],[196,"\"There is to be no envy except for two: A man to whom Allah grants wealth and he spends from it during the hours of the night and the hours of the day. And a man to whom Allah grants (memorization of) the Quran so he stands with it (in prayer) during the hours of the night and the hours of the day.\" (Using translation from Tirmidhī 1936)"],[197,"Envy is not justified but in case of two persons only: one who, having been given (knowledge of) the Qur'an by Allah, recites it during the night and during the day (and acts upon it), and the person who, having been given wealth by God, gives it in charity during the night and the day. (Using translation from Muslim 815b)"],[198,"It was said, “O Messenger of Allah, so-and-so prays through the night, but when morning comes he steals.” He said, “What you mention (i.e., his prayer) will soon stop him.”"],[199,"A man asked the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, “Which prayer is best after the obligatory prayer?” He said, “Prayer in the middle of the night.” He said, “Which fast is best after the month of Ramadan?” He said, “The month of Allah which they call al-Muḥarram.”"],[200,"I asked Abū Dharr, “Which night prayer is best?” Abū Dharr said, “I asked the Messenger of Allah ﷺ just as you asked me,” and he said, “The middle of the night or the depths of the night.”"],[201,"“Whoever among you fears that he will not get up at the end of the night, let him perform witr at the beginning of the night. Whoever among you hopes to get up at the end of the night, let him perform witr at the end of the night, for the recitation at the end of the night is witnessed, and that is better.”"],[202,"“May Allah have mercy on a man who gets up at night to pray and wakes his wife; if she refuses, he sprinkles water on her face. And may Allah have mercy on a woman who gets up at night and wakes her husband; if he refuses, she sprinkles water on his face.”"],[203,"“Whoever wakes up at night and wakes his family, and they both get up and pray two rakʿahs, they will be recorded among the men and women who remember Allah much.”"],[204,"“When a man wakes up at night and wakes his wife, and they both pray two rakʿahs, they are recorded among the men and women who remember Allah much.”"],[205,"“During the night there is an hour in which no Muslim man happens to ask Allah for good of this world or the Hereafter but He gives it to him.”"],[206,"“Whoever stands in prayer during Ramadan and fasts it out of faith and seeking reward, his past sins will be forgiven; and whoever stands in prayer on Laylat al-Qadr out of faith and seeking reward, his past sins will be forgiven.”"],[207,"He said to Ubayy b. Kaʿb: Ibn Masʿūd says that whoever stands in prayer the whole year will attain Laylat al-Qadr. Ubayy said: By Allah, besides whom there is no god, it is indeed in the month of Ramadan, and he swore without making any exception. By Allah, I know that Laylat al-Qadr is this night which the Messenger of Allah ﷺ commanded us to stand in prayer, the morning of the twenty-seventh. Its sign is that the sun rises on the morning of that day white, without rays, as if it were a basin."],[208,"Tell me, for it pleases me to see you, and I have come only to meet you. So tell me about the Night of Qadr, as Ibn Mas'ud says: \"Whoever stands (in prayer) during the whole year will be affected by it or will attain it.\" He knew that it is in the month of Ramadan, but he preferred not to specify it for you. It is the twenty-seventh night, according to the verse that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ informed us about. So we memorized it and recognized it. It was a clear night until the last moments before dawn. He would ascend the minaret, look at the rising of the sun, and say, \"It rises without any rays until it rises high.\""],[209,"Whoever stands with ten verses will not be recorded among the heedless; and whoever stands with a hundred verses will be recorded among the devoutly obedient; and whoever stands with a thousand verses will be recorded among those receiving qintars."],[210,"A qintar is twelve thousand uqiyyas; each uqiyya is better than what is between heaven and earth."],[211,"Whoever recites Yasin in a night seeking Allah's countenance will be forgiven."],[212,"Whoever recites the two verses from the end of Surat al-Baqarah in a night, they will suffice him."],[213,"Would any of you be unable to recite a third of the Quran every night?\" They said, \"And who can bear that, O Messenger of Allah?\" He said, \"{Say: He is Allah, [who is] One}.\""],[214,"\"Allah has not permitted for anything what He has permitted for a prophet to chant the Qur'an.\""],[215,"\"Allah does not listen to anything as He listens to one who chants the Qur'an aloud.\""],[216,"I saw the Messenger of Allah ﷺ praying and a sound came from his breast like the rumbling of a mill owing to weeping. (Using translation from Abū Dāʾūd 904)"],[217,"\"Allah listens more intently to a man with a good voice reciting the Qur'an than the owner of a singing-girl listens to his singing-girl.\""],[218,"\"Beautify the Qur'an with your voices.\""],[219,"\"Beautify the Qur'an with your voices.\""],[220,"\"No servant talks to himself about standing for an hour of the night then sleeps through it except that his sleep is a charity Allah bestows upon him, and the reward of what he intended is written for him.\""],[221,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ, when he did a deed, he would make it a habit. And when he slept through the night or was ill, he would pray twelve rak'ahs during the day."],[222,"Whoever sleeps through his portion or part of it, then recites it between the dawn prayer and the noon prayer, it will be recorded for him as if he recited it at night."],[223,"A man came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and said, 'Tell me of a deed that will admit me to Paradise.' The Prophet ﷺ said, 'Worship Allah and do not associate anything with Him, establish the prayer, give the zakat, and maintain ties of kinship. Leave it at that.'"],[224,"'O Prophet of Allah, tell me of a deed that will admit me to Paradise.' The people said, 'What is with him? What is with him?' The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, 'He has a need. What is with him?' The Messenger of Allah said, 'Worship Allah and do not associate anything with Him, establish the prayer, give the zakat, and maintain ties of kinship. Leave it at that.' He said, as if he was on his mount."],[225,"There is no servant who worships Allah and does not associate anything with Him, establishes the prayer, gives the zakat, fasts Ramadan, and avoids major sins, except that he will enter Paradise."],[226,"A bedouin asked the Messenger of Allah ﷺ about emigration. He said, 'Woe to you! The matter of emigration is severe. Do you have camels?' He said, 'Yes.' He said, 'Do you pay their zakat?' He said, 'Yes.' He said, 'Then work beyond the seas, for Allah will not deprive you of any of your deeds.'"],[227,"Charity does not decrease wealth, and Allah does not increase a servant through pardoning except in honor, and no one humbles himself for Allah except that Allah raises him."],[228,"Charity extinguishes the wrath of the Lord and repels an evil death."],[229,"Every person will be in the shade of his charity until judgment is passed between people.\" Or he said: \"until judgment is rendered between people."],[230,"An angel at one of the gates of Paradise says, 'Whoever lends today will be repaid tomorrow,' and an angel at another gate says, 'O Allah, give the spender a replacement and give the withholder destruction.'"],[231,"Whoever is able to protect himself from the Fire, even with half a date, let him do so."],[232,"\"O Messenger of Allah, which charity is best?\" He said, \"The effort of one with little, and begin with those you support.\""],[233,"\"The best charity is that given from surplus wealth. Begin with those you support.\""],[234,"“The best charity is that given out of surplus wealth, and the upper hand is better than the lower hand. Let one of you begin with those he supports: his wife says, ‘Spend on me,’ and the mother of his child says, ‘To whom are you leaving me?’ and his slave says, ‘Feed me and employ me.’”"],[235,"“The upper hand is better than the lower hand. The upper hand is the one that spends, and the lower hand is the one that begs.”"],[236,"She freed a slave-girl during the time of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and mentioned that to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. He said, \"Had you given her to your maternal uncles, it would have been greater for your reward.\""],[237,"\"Charity to a poor person is charity, and to a relative it is two: charity and maintaining ties.\""],[238,"One day he said to his companions, \"Give charity.\" A man said, \"O Messenger of Allah, I have a dinar.\" He said, \"Spend it on yourself.\" He said, \"I have another.\" He said, \"Spend it on your wife.\" He said, \"I have another.\" He said, \"Spend it on your child.\" He said, \"I have another.\" He said, \"Spend it on your servant.\" He said, \"I have another.\" He said, \"You know best.\""],[239,"One day the Messenger of Allah ﷺ urged charity, and a man said: O Messenger of Allah, I have a dinar. He said: “Give it in charity on yourself.” He said: I have another. He said: “Give it in charity on your child.” He said: I have another. He said: “Give it in charity on your wife.” He said: I have another. He said: “Give it in charity on your servant.” He said: I have another. He said: “You know better.”"],[240,"The best charity is that which is given from a state of sufficient means, and the upper hand is better than the lower hand, and begin with those you support."],[241,"\"A dirham has surpassed a hundred thousand.\" A man said, \"How is that, O Messenger of Allah?\" He said, \"A man who has much wealth takes from its side a hundred thousand and gives it in charity, and a man who has only two dirhams takes one of them and gives it in charity.\""],[242,"Ibn Umar entered upon Ibn Amir to visit him. He said, “O Ibn Umar, will you not supplicate for me?” Ibn Umar said, “I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say, ‘No prayer is accepted without purification, and no charity from misappropriated wealth.’ And you were in charge of Basra.”"],[243,"\"If you pay the zakah of your wealth, you have fulfilled what is due from it. Whoever gathers unlawful wealth and then gives charity from it will have no reward for it, and its burden will be upon him.\""],[244,"'Three Allah loves, and three Allah hates. He loves a man who was among a people and a beggar came to them asking them by the face of Allah, not asking them for kinship between them and him, and they were miserly, so he followed them at their heels where no one saw him except Allah and the one he gave; and a man who was in a battalion and they were exposed, so he said the takbir and fought until Allah granted him victory or he was killed; and a man who was among a people and they traveled at night, and their night journey was long, so they alighted and sleep was dearer to them than anything they might equate with it, so they slept and he stood reciting My verses and appealing to Me. And He hates the adulterous old man, the miserly arrogant one'—and he mentioned the third."],[245,"A man came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and said: 'O Messenger of Allah, which charity is greatest?' He said: 'That you give charity while you are healthy and miserly, fearing poverty and hoping for wealth, and not delay until it reaches the throat and you say: For so-and-so is such and such, and for so-and-so is such and such, although it has already been for so-and-so.'"],[246,"The example of the one who spends and the miser is like two men who have two coats of mail from their collarbones to their chests. As for the one who spends, when he wants to spend, it expands and widens over him until it reaches his feet and covers his traces. As for the miser, when he wants to spend, each ring takes its place and clings, so he tries to widen it but it does not widen; he tries to widen it but it does not widen."],[247,"The wives of the Prophet ﷺ gathered with him, not one of them was absent. She said: I said: 'O Messenger of Allah, which of us will catch up with you soonest?' He said: 'The one among you with the longest hand.' She said: They took a reed and measured with it. Sawdah bint Zam'ah died, and she was very charitable, so we thought that he meant the one with the longest hand in charity."],[248,"No Muslim servant gives charity from good earnings, and Allah accepts only what is good, except that Allah takes it with His right hand and nurtures it for him as one of you nurtures his foal or his young camel, until a date becomes like Uhud."],[249,"Indeed, Allah nurtures for one of you the date and the morsel as one of you nurtures his foal or his young camel, until it becomes like Uhud."],[250,"I said to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ: Do I have any reward in (caring for) the children of Abu Salamah? For I spend on them, and they are only my sons, and I am not about to leave them like this and like that—she said: Will I have a reward or not? The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"Yes, you have a reward in them for what you spend on them.\""],[251,"'When a woman gives charity from her husband's house without causing corruption, she has her reward, her husband has the reward for what he earned, she has the reward for what she intended, and the storekeeper has the like of that.'"],[252,"'The trustworthy Muslim storekeeper who spends'—and sometimes he said, 'gives what he is commanded, giving it complete, full, with a willing heart, and passes it to the one to whom he is commanded—is one of the givers of charity.'"],[253,"'The poor person is not the one who is turned away by a date or two, or a morsel or two; rather, the poor person is the one who has nothing to suffice himself, and his need is not known so that charity might be given to him. That is the deprived one.'"],[254,"'The poor person is not this one who goes around among the people and is turned away by a morsel or two, or a date or two.' They said, 'Then who is the poor person, O Messenger of Allah?' He said, 'The one who finds no wealth to suffice him, and is not noticed so that charity might be given to him, and does not stand up asking people.'"],[255,"For a person to give charity during his life and health of one dirham is better for him than giving one hundred dirhams at his death."],[256,"Forty good deeds, the highest of which is the gift of a she-goat. No servant does one of them hoping for its reward and believing in its promise but that Allah will admit him to Paradise."],[257,"Whoever grants a gift of a milch animal or gives milk to drink or offers a small gift, it is like freeing a slave."],[258,"“There is no person among the descendants of Adam but that charity is due from him every day the sun rises.” It was said: \"O Messenger of Allah, from where can we get charity to give?\" He said: \"Indeed, the doors of good are many: glorifying Allah (tasbīḥ), praising Allah (taḥmīd), declaring Allah's greatness (takbīr), declaring Allah's oneness (tahlīl), enjoining good, forbidding evil, removing harm from the road, making the deaf hear, guiding the blind, directing the seeker to what he needs, hastening with the strength of your legs to the distressed one who calls for help, and carrying with the strength of your arms for the weak. All of this is charity from you for yourself.\""],[259,"“He does not thank Allah who does not thank people.”"],[260,"«Fear the Fire, even with half a date; and if you cannot find it, then with a good word.»"],[261,"The Prophet ﷺ stood and said, \"Guard yourselves from the Fire.\" Then he turned away and looked aside. Then he said, \"Guard yourselves from the Fire.\" Then he turned away and looked aside, until we thought he was seeing it. Then he said, \"Guard yourselves from the Fire, even with half a date; and if you cannot find that, then with a good word.\""],[262,"He entered upon Umm Mubashshir al-Ansariyyah in a palm grove of hers. The Prophet ﷺ said to her, “Who planted these palm trees? A Muslim or a disbeliever?” She said, “Rather, a Muslim.” He ﷺ said, “No Muslim plants a tree or sows a crop, and a human, an animal, or anything eats from it, except that it is charity for him.”"],[263,"“No Muslim plants a tree, and a beast, a bird, or anything eats from it, except that he has a reward for it.”"],[264,"I asked Abu Dharr: \"Guide me to a deed which, if a servant does it, he will enter Paradise.\" He said: \"I asked the Messenger of Allah ﷺ about that, and he said: 'He believes in Allah.'\" I said, \"O Messenger of Allah, is there any action with faith?\" He said: \"He gives from what Allah has provided him.\" I said, \"Even if he is destitute and has nothing?\" He said: \"He says something good with his tongue.\" I said, \"Even if he is tongue-tied and cannot express himself?\" He said: \"He helps someone who is overcome.\" I said, \"Even if he is weak and has no ability?\" He said: \"Let him make something for an unskilled person.\" I said, \"Even if he is unskilled?\" He said: Then he turned to me and said: \"Do you want to leave any good in your companion? Let him refrain from harming people.\" I said, \"O Messenger of Allah, these are easy words?\" He ﷺ said: \"By the One in whose hand is my soul, there is no servant who practices one of these traits, seeking thereby what is with Allah, except that it will take him by the hand on the Day of Resurrection until it enters him into Paradise.\""],[265,"A woman was punished because of a cat she tied up and did not feed, nor did she let it eat from the vermin of the earth."],[266,"“Every act of kindness is charity.”"],[267,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"Allah created every human being from the children of Adam with three hundred and sixty joints. Whoever declares Allah's greatness (takbīr), praises Him (taḥmīd), declares His oneness (tahlīl), glorifies Him (tasbīḥ), seeks His forgiveness (istighfār), removes a bone from people's path, removes a stone from their path, enjoins good, and forbids evil to the number of those three hundred and sixty, he will end that day having distanced himself from the Fire.\""],[268,"“The delegations to Allah are three: the pilgrim performing Hajj, the one performing Umrah, and the warrior in battle.”"],[269,"“Whoever performs Hajj and does not engage in obscenity or wickedness will return as on the day his mother gave birth to him.”"],[270,"“Perform Hajj and Umrah consecutively, for they remove poverty and sins just as the bellows removes the dross of iron, gold, and silver. And there is no reward for an accepted Hajj except Paradise.”"],[271,"“An accepted Hajj has no reward except Paradise, and one Umrah to the next expiates what is between them.”"],[272,"“One Umrah to the next expiates what is between them, and an accepted Hajj has no reward except Paradise.”"],[273,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ as saying: There is no virtue more to the liking of Allah in any day than in these days, that is, the first ten days of Dhu al-Hijjah. They (the Companions) asked: Messenger of Allah, not even the struggle in the path of Allah (Jihad) ? He said: (Yes), not even the struggle in the path of Allah, except a man who goes out (in the path of Allah) with his life and property, and does not return with any of them. (Using translation from Abū Dāʾūd 2438)"],[274,"“I saw the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, when he was on his she-camel, standing in Al-Hazwarah* saying: ‘By Allah, you are the best land of Allah, and the dearest of the land of Allah to me. By Allah, had I not been expelled from you I would never have left.’” *A place in Makkah. (Using translation from Ibn Mājah 3108)"],[275,"How good you are as a land, and how beloved you are to me! Were it not that my people expelled me from you, I would not have dwelt elsewhere.\""],[276,"When the Prophet ﷺ arrived in al-Madinah, Abu Bakr and Bilal fell ill. She said: I went in to them and said: O my father, how do you find yourself? And O Bilal, how do you find yourself? She said: When fever would seize Abu Bakr ؓ he would say:"],[277,"“O Allah, bless us in our mudd and our ṣāʿ, and place with the blessing two blessings.”"],[278,"“No one endures the hardship of Madinah and its toil except that I will be an intercessor or witness for him.”"],[279,"“Whoever among you is able to die in Madinah, let him die in Madinah, for I will intercede for the one who dies there.”"],[280,"“Whoever among you is able not to die except in Madinah, let him die there, for whoever dies there, she will intercede for him and testify for him.”"],[281,"No one leaves it—meaning al-Madinah—out of aversion for it except that Allah will replace him with one better for it than him. And al-Madinah is better for them, if they only knew."],[282,"A Bedouin gave allegiance to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ upon Islam. Then the Bedouin was afflicted with a fever in al-Madinah, so he left. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"Al-Madinah is only like a bellows: it expels its impurity and its goodness shines forth.\""],[283,"I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ name al-Madinah Tabah."],[284,"“The legs of the pulpit are fixed in Paradise.”"],[285,"“Between my house and my pulpit is a garden from the gardens of Paradise, and my pulpit is upon my cistern.”"],[286,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ bade farewell to a man and said, 'Where do you intend to go?' He said, 'I intend to go to the Holy House.' The Prophet ﷺ said, 'A prayer in this mosque is better than a hundred prayers in any other except the Sacred Mosque.'"],[287,"“A Muslim eats in one intestine, and a disbeliever eats in seven intestines.”"],[288,"Two men disagreed about the mosque founded on piety. One of them said it is the mosque of Madinah, and the other said it is the mosque of Quba. They came to the Prophet ﷺ, and he said, \"It is this mosque of mine.\""],[289,"From the time one of you leaves his house to my mosque, one step writes a good deed for him and another step erases a bad deed, until he returns."],[290,"Indeed, faith will retreat to al-Madinah just as a snake retreats to its hole."],[291,"A man from Banu Amr b. Auf and a man from Banu Khudrah disputed about the mosque founded on piety. The Khudri said, 'It is the mosque of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ,' and the Umari said, 'It is the mosque of Quba.' He said, so they went out until they came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and asked him about that. He said, 'It is this mosque, the mosque of the Messenger of Allah, and in that there is much good.'"],[292,"He witnessed a funeral at al-Awsat in the house of Sa'd b. 'Ubadah, then he set out walking to Banu 'Amr b. 'Awf at the courtyard of Banu al-Harith b. al-Khazraj. It was said to him, 'Where are you heading, O Abu 'Abd al-Rahman?' He said, 'I am heading to this mosque in Banu 'Amr b. 'Awf, for I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: \"Whoever prays in it is like the reward of an 'Umrah.\"'"],[293,"He used to visit Quba walking and riding."],[294,"Rejoice, O assembly of Muslims! The Dajjal will not enter it."],[295,"A prayer in this mosque of mine is better than a thousand prayers in any other except the Sacred Mosque, and a prayer in that one is better than a hundred prayers in this one."],[296,"Whoever circumambulates the House seven times, not placing a foot down nor lifting the other except that Allah removes from him a sin for it, and writes for him a good deed for it, and raises for him a rank for it.\""],[297,"Wiping the Stone and the Yemeni Corner removes sins completely.\""],[298,"I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say while leaning his back against the Ka'bah, \"The Corner and the Station are two rubies from the rubies of Paradise. Were it not that Allah has obscured their light, they would illuminate all that is between the east and the west.\""],[299,"Indeed this Stone has a tongue and two lips; it will testify on the Day of Resurrection for the one who touches it in truth."],[300,"Allah will surely resurrect this Corner on the Day of Resurrection with two eyes with which it sees and a tongue with which it speaks; it will testify for the one who touches it in truth."],[301,"\"Indeed Allah boasts to the angels of the inhabitants of the heaven about the people of Arafat, saying: Look at My servants, they have come to Me disheveled and dusty.\""],[302,"\"There are no days better in the sight of Allah than the ten days of Dhu al-Hijjah.\" A man said: \"O Messenger of Allah, are they better or an equivalent number of days spent in jihad in the path of Allah?\" He said: \"They are better than an equivalent number of days spent in jihad in the path of Allah.\" \"And there is no day better in the sight of Allah than the Day of Arafah. Allah descends to the lowest heaven and boasts to the inhabitants of the earth about the inhabitants of the heaven, saying: Look at My servants, disheveled, dusty, and sun-scorched, coming from every deep mountain pass, hoping for My mercy and not having seen My punishment. And no day is seen with more people freed from the Fire than the Day of Arafah.\""],[303,"The best of days in the sight of Allah is the Day of Sacrifice (Yawm al-Naḥr) and the Day of Rest (Yawm al-Qarr)."],[304,"Umm Sulaym came to the Prophet ﷺ and said, \"Abu Talhah and his son performed Hajj and left me behind.\" He said, \"O Umm Sulaym, an Umrah in Ramadan equals a Hajj.\""],[305,"“ ‘Umrah during Ramadan is equivalent to Hajj (i.e. in reward).” (Using translation from Ibn Mājah 2991)"],[306,"Whoever enters ihram for Umrah from al-Masjid al-Aqsa, his past sins will be forgiven.\" He said, so Umm Hakim rode to Jerusalem until she entered ihram from it for Umrah."],[307,"I sat among a group of the companions of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and said, ‘Which of you will go to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and ask him which deeds are most beloved to Allah?’ He said: But we were too awed for any of us to ask him. He said: Then the Messenger of Allah ﷺ sent for us, singling us out one by one, so that no one else remained. When we gathered before him, some of us gestured to others, ‘Why has he sent for us?’ We were alarmed that something had been revealed about us. He said: «The Messenger of Allah ﷺ recited to us: {Whatever is in the heavens and whatever is on the earth exalts Allah, and He is the Exalted in Might, the Wise. O you who have believed, why do you say what you do not do?}» He said: He recited from its beginning to its end."],[308,"He was asked, ‘Which deeds are best?’ He said: «Faith in Allah and His Messenger.» Then which? He said: «Jihad in the cause of Allah is the summit of deeds.» Then which? He said: «An accepted hajj.»"],[309,"While we were with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, he heard the people saying, ‘Which deeds are best, O Messenger of Allah?’ The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: «Faith in Allah and His Messenger, jihad in His cause, and an accepted hajj.» Then he heard a call in the valley saying, ‘I bear witness that there is no god but Allah and that Muhammad is the Messenger of Allah ﷺ.’ The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: «And I bear witness, and I bear witness that no one bears witness to it except that he is free from shirk.»"],[310,"I said, ‘O Messenger of Allah, which deed is best?’ He said: «Faith in Allah and jihad in His cause.» I said, ‘Which slaves are best?’ He said: «The most precious to their owners and the highest in price.» I said, ‘What if I do not do that?’ He said: «You help a craftsman or make something for an unskilled person.» I said, ‘What if I am too weak for that?’ He said: «Then refrain from evil, for it is a charity you give to yourself.»"],[311,"«The best deeds in the sight of Allah are faith without doubt, a military expedition without misappropriation of spoils, and an accepted hajj.»"],[312,"The mujahid is one who strives against his own self for the sake of Allah."],[313,"Blessing is in the forelocks of horses."],[314,"Horses are three kinds: for one man a reward, for another a covering, and for another a burden."],[315,"Horses have good tied to their forelocks until the Day of Resurrection."],[316,"Horses have good tied to their forelocks until the Day of Resurrection—the reward and the spoils."],[317,"The example of the one who spends on horses is like the one who spreads his hand in charity."],[318,"Horses are for one man a reward, for another a covering, and for another a burden. As for the one for whom they are a reward, he is a man who ties them in the way of Allah and gives them a long rope in a meadow or garden. Whatever they eat within the length of their rope from that meadow or garden becomes good deeds for him. And if they break their rope and run a height or two, their tracks and dung become good deeds for him. If they pass by a river and drink from it, even if he did not intend to water them, that becomes good deeds for him. So they are a reward for him for that. And a man who ties them to be self-sufficient and to refrain from begging, and does not forget Allah's right upon their necks and their backs, then they are a covering for him for that. And a man who ties them out of pride, showing off, and enmity against the people of Islam, then they are a burden on him for that.\" The Messenger of Allah ﷺ was asked about donkeys and said: \"Nothing has been revealed to me about them except this comprehensive and unique verse: 'So whoever does an atom's weight of good will see it, and whoever does an atom's weight of evil will see it.'\" (Quran 99:7-8)"],[319,"Good is knotted in the forelocks of horses, their people are assisted with them, and the one who spends on them is like the one who extends his hand in charity."],[320,"A man came to the Prophet ﷺ and said, ‘O Messenger of Allah, which people are best?’ He said: «A man who wages jihad in the cause of Allah with his wealth and his life; then a believer in one of the mountain passes who worships Allah and leaves people safe from his evil.»"],[321,"«There will come upon the people a time when the best of people in station will be a man who takes hold of his horse’s rein in the cause of Allah. Whenever he hears a call to battle, he mounts its back, then seeks death wherever it is expected. And a man in one of these mountain passes who establishes prayer, gives zakat, and leaves people except for good from him.»"],[322,"The best of horses is the black one with a white blaze on the forehead, a white upper lip, and white on three legs, with the right foreleg unrestrained."],[323,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ was once prominent among the people when a man came to him walking and said, \"O Muhammad, what is faith?\" He said, \"To believe in Allah, His angels, His messengers, and the Day of Judgement, and to believe in the resurrection after death.\" The man asked, \"O Messenger of Allah, what is Islam?\" He said, \"To worship Allah alone and not associate anything with Him, to establish the obligatory prayers, to pay the obligatory charity, and to fast during the month of Ramadan.\" The man then asked, \"O Muhammad, what is excellence (ihsan)?\" He said, \"To worship Allah as if you see Him, and if you cannot see Him, then know that He sees you.\" Finally, the man asked, \"O Muhammad, when will the Hour (the Day of Judgement) occur?\" He replied, \"The one being asked about it knows no more than the questioner, but I will inform you of its signs. When the servant girl gives birth to her master, and you see the barefooted, naked, destitute shepherds competing in the construction of tall buildings, that is among its signs. The knowledge of the Hour belongs only to Allah {Indeed, Allah [alone] has knowledge of the Hour} [Quran 31:34].\" Then the man left, and the Prophet ﷺ said, \"That was Gabriel who came to teach the people their religion.\""],[324,"Whoever withholds a horse in the way of Allah, believing in Allah and affirming His promise, its satiety, its thirst-quenching, and its dung will be good deeds in his balance on the Day of Resurrection."],[325,"\"The best dinar is a dinar that a man spends on his dependents, a dinar he spends on his horse in the cause of Allah, and a dinar a man spends on his companions in the cause of Allah.\""],[326,"From the Prophet ﷺ, he said: \"Whoever spends an expenditure in the cause of Allah, seven hundred fold is written for him.\""],[327,"When {The example of those who spend their wealth in the cause of Allah is like that of a grain that sprouts seven ears, in each ear a hundred grains, and Allah multiplies for whom He wills. And Allah is all-encompassing and knowing} was revealed, the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"Lord, increase my community.\" Then {Who is it that would loan Allah a goodly loan so He may multiply it for him many times over?} was revealed. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"Lord, increase my community.\" Then {Indeed, the patient will be given their reward without account} was revealed."],[328,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"For it on the Day of Resurrection you will have seven hundred she-camels, all of them bridled.\""],[329,"A man gave charity of a bridled she-camel in the cause of Allah, so the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"On the Day of Resurrection you will surely come with seven hundred bridled she-camels.\""],[330,"I came to Abu Dharr at al-Rabadha and said, 'O Abu Dharr, what is your wealth?' He said, 'My wealth is my deeds.' I said, 'Narrate to us a hadith from the Messenger of Allah ﷺ that you heard from him.' He said, 'I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say, \"There are no two Muslims who have three children die before reaching puberty but that Allah admits them to Paradise by the virtue of His mercy toward them.\"'"],[331,"I met Abu Dharr at al-Rabadhah while he had brought his riding camels to water, so he gave them to drink, then he brought them back. He had hung a water skin on the neck of one of his riding camels to drink from it and to give his companions drink. That is a trait from the traits of the Arabs. I said: O Abu Dharr, what is your wealth? He said: My wealth is my deeds. I said: O Abu Dharr, what did you hear the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say? He said: I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: \"Whoever spends a pair from his wealth, the gatekeepers of Paradise hasten to him.\" I said: O Abu Dharr, what are these two pairs? He said: If they are men, then two men; if they are horses, then two horses; if they are camels, then two camels, until he enumerated all types of wealth. I said: Tell me more, O Abu Dharr. He said: I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: \"There are no two Muslims for whom three children die but that Allah admits them into Paradise by His abundant mercy.\""],[332,"«The sanctity of the wives of the mujahidin upon those who remain behind is like that of their mothers. And no man among those who remain behind stays behind for a man among the mujahidin except that it is set up for him on the Day of Resurrection, and it is said: O so-and-so, this is so-and-so, so take from his good deeds whatever you wish.» Then he turned to his companions and said, «What do you think? I do not think he will leave anything of his good deeds.»"],[333,"«The sanctity of the wives of the mujahidin upon those who remain behind is like the sanctity of their mothers. And no one who remains behind stays behind for a mujahid in his family with evil except that it is set up for him on the Day of Resurrection, and it is said to him: This is the one you stayed behind for in his family with evil, so take from his good deeds.»"],[334,"«Whoever equips a warrior in the path of Allah has indeed fought, and whoever stays behind with his family in good has indeed fought.»"],[335,"«Whoever equips a warrior has the like of his reward, and whoever stays behind for a warrior in his family has the like of his reward.»"],[336,"«Whoever equips a warrior in the path of Allah or stays behind with his family, the like of his reward is recorded for him, except that nothing is decreased from his reward. And whoever provides iftar for a fasting person, the like of his reward is recorded for him, nothing being decreased from his reward.»"],[337,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ sent an expedition to Banu Lihyan and said, \"Let one of every two men volunteer, and the reward is between them both.\""],[338,"A young man from Aslam said, \"O Messenger of Allah, I wish to go on jihad but I have nothing to equip myself with.\" He said, \"Go to so-and-so the Ansari, for he had equipped himself. Tell him that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ sends you greetings and says to you: Give me what you prepared for the expedition.\" He went to him, and the man said to his wife, \"Do not hide anything from him. By Allah, do not hide anything from him, and you will be blessed through it.\""],[339,"Seek out your weak ones for me, for you are provided with sustenance and granted victory only because of your weak ones."],[340,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ slept one day near me, then woke up smiling. I said, “O Messenger of Allah, what made you laugh?” He said, “People of my community were shown to me riding on the back of this green sea like kings upon thrones.” She said, “Supplicate Allah to make me one of them.” He supplicated for her. Then he slept a second time and did the like, and she said the like of her words, and he answered her with the like of his first words. She said, “Supplicate Allah to make me one of them.” He said, “You are among the first.” She went out with her husband ʿUbādah b. al-Ṣāmit as a warrior the first time the Muslims rode the sea with Muʿāwiyah. When they returned from their expedition, her mount was brought near for her to ride, but she fell and died."],[341,"«A morning or an evening spent in the cause of Allah is better than the world and all that it contains.»"],[342,"ʿUthmān said in the mosque of al-Khayf at Minā: O people, I heard a hadith from the Messenger of Allah ﷺ that I had concealed from you out of concern for you, but it has occurred to me to disclose it as sincere counsel for Allah and for you. I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say, “A day in the way of Allah is better than a thousand days in anything else, so let every man among you look to himself.”"],[343,"He was at a frontier post, and they were alarmed and rushed to the coast. Then it was said, ‘No danger,’ and the people returned, but Abu Hurayrah remained standing. A person passed by him and said, ‘What keeps you standing, O Abu Hurayrah?’ He said, ‘I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: “Standing for an hour in the cause of Allah is better than praying on Laylat al-Qadr at the Black Stone.”’"],[344,"While we were traveling in the land of the Byzantines in a detachment commanded by Malik b. Abd Allah al-Khath‘ami, Malik passed by Jabir b. Abd Allah as he was walking, leading a mule of his. Malik said to him, ‘O Abu Abd Allah, ride, for Allah has given you a mount.’ Jabir said, ‘I am tending my mount and sparing my people, and I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: “Whoever’s feet become dusty in the cause of Allah, Allah has forbidden him to the Fire.”’ Malik admired his words, and he went on until he reached a place where his voice could be heard, then called out to him at the top of his voice, ‘O Abu Abd Allah, ride, for Allah has given you a mount.’ Jabir understood what he intended by raising his voice, and said, ‘I am tending my mount and sparing my people, and I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: “Whoever’s feet become dusty in the cause of Allah, Allah has forbidden him to the Fire.”’ Then the people jumped down from their mounts, and we did not see a day with more people walking than that day."],[345,"ʿAbāyah b. Rifāʿah b. Rāfiʿ b. Khadīj overtook me while I was walking to Friday prayer and said: I heard Abū ʿAbs say: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, “Whoever's feet become dusty in the way of Allah, Allah will forbid them to the Fire.”"],[346,"“Dust in the way of Allah and the hot breath of Hell will not come together in the belly of a believing servant, and faith and envy will not come together in the belly of a servant.”"],[347,"“The smoke of Hell and dust in the way of Allah will not come together in the nostrils of a Muslim.”"],[348,"Umar b. al-Khattab addressed us and said, \"Indeed, do not be excessive in the dowries of women, for if it were a source of honor in this world or piety in the sight of Allah, Muhammad ﷺ would have been the foremost and most deserving of you in it. He never gave any of his wives or his daughters a dowry exceeding twelve uqiyyahs. And another thing you say: 'Whoever is killed in your battles, so-and-so died a martyr.' Do not say that, but say as the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, or as Muhammad ﷺ said: 'Whoever is killed in the way of Allah or dies in the way of Allah is in Paradise.'\""],[349,"\"The example of the one who strives in the way of Allah is like the one who fasts and stands in prayer, not slackening from fasting and prayer until he returns.\""],[350,"\"The example of the one who strives in the way of Allah is like the one who is devoutly obedient, fasting, and does not slacken in prayer or fasting until Allah returns him to his family with whatever He returns him, whether spoils or reward, or takes him in death and admits him to Paradise.\""],[351,"They said, \"O Messenger of Allah, tell us of an action that equals jihad in the way of Allah.\" He said, \"You will not be able to do it.\" They said, \"O Messenger of Allah, tell us, perhaps we will be able to do it.\" He said, \"The example of the one who strives in the way of Allah is like the one who fasts, stands in prayer, and is devoutly obedient to the verses of Allah, not slackening from fasting or charity until the one who strives returns to his family.\""],[352,"“A Muslim eats in one intestine, and a disbeliever eats in seven intestines.”"],[353,"From 'Amr b. Malik al-Janbi that he heard Fadalah b. 'Ubayd al-Ansari saying: I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say, \"I am a guarantor, and the guarantor is the one who bears responsibility, for the one who believes in me, submits, and emigrates, of a house in the outskirts of Paradise and a house in the middle of Paradise. And I am a guarantor for the one who believes in me, submits, and strives in the way of Allah, of a house in the outskirts of Paradise, a house in the middle of Paradise, and a house in the highest chambers of Paradise. Whoever does that, he leaves no avenue for good unattained and no escape from evil unattained; he may die wherever he wishes to die.\""],[354,"\"Whoever shades the head of a warrior, Allah will shade him on the Day of Resurrection. And whoever equips a warrior in the way of Allah for his jihad will have the like of his reward. And whoever builds a mosque in which the name of Allah is remembered, Allah will build for him a house in Paradise.\""],[355,"That the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"Whoever develops some gray hair in the cause of Allah, it shall be a light for him in the Day of Judgement. (Using translation from Tirmidhī 1635)"],[356,"\"No servant fasts one day in the way of Allah except that Allah distances his face from the Fire by that day seventy autumns.\""],[357,"A man said: O Messenger of Allah, which jihad is best? He said: «That your horse be hamstrung and your blood be spilled.»"],[358,"A man came to the Prophet ﷺ while he was leading us in prayer, and when he reached the row he said: O Allah, give me the best of what You give Your righteous servants. When the Prophet ﷺ finished the prayer, he said: «Who was the one speaking just now?» The man said: I, O Messenger of Allah. The Prophet ﷺ said: «Then your horse will be hamstrung and you will be martyred in the path of Allah.»"],[359,"\"Indeed, the gates of Paradise are beneath the shades of the swords.\" Then a man of disheveled appearance stood up and said, \"O Abu Musa, did you hear the Prophet ﷺ say that?\" He said, \"Yes.\" He said, \"Then he went to his companions and said, 'I bid you farewell.' Then he broke the scabbard of his sword and threw it away, and advanced with his sword, striking with it until he was killed."],[360,"A man said to the Prophet ﷺ on the day of Uhud: \"Tell me, if I fight in the cause of Allah and am killed, O Messenger of Allah, where will I be?\" He said: \"In Paradise.\" He said: So he threw away some dates in his hand, then advanced and fought until he was killed."],[361,"A man came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and said: \"O Messenger of Allah, tell me, if I am killed in the cause of Allah, patient and seeking reward, advancing and not retreating, will Allah expiate my sins?\" The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"Yes.\" When he turned away, the Messenger of Allah ﷺ called him, or ordered someone to call him, and said: \"What did you say?\" He repeated his words, so the Prophet ﷺ said: \"Yes, except for debt. Thus Gabriel ﷺ said to me.\""],[362,"“In Paradise there are one hundred degrees which Allah has prepared for the mujāhidīn in His way. Between each two degrees is like what is between the heaven and the earth. So when you ask Allah, ask Him for al-Firdaws, for it is the middle of Paradise and the highest part of Paradise, and above it is the Throne, and from it the rivers of Paradise gush forth.”"],[363,"“O Abū Saʿīd, whoever is content with Allah as Lord, with Islam as religion, and with Muhammad as Prophet, Paradise is guaranteed for him.” Abū Saʿīd was amazed at this and said, “Repeat it to me, O Messenger of Allah.” He did so. Then the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, “And another matter by which the servant is raised one hundred degrees, between each two degrees being like what is between the heaven and the earth.” He said, “What is it, O Messenger of Allah?” He said, “Jihad in the way of Allah ﷻ.”"],[364,"“Whoever shoots an arrow in the way of Allah is like one who frees a slave.”"],[365,"We besieged al-Ṭāʾif with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say, “Whoever reaches the enemy with an arrow in the way of Allah, it is a degree for him in Paradise.” He said, “That day it reached sixteen arrows.”"],[366,"“Whoever reaches the enemy with an arrow, Allah raises him a degree by it.” ʿAbd al-Raḥmān b. al-Naḥḥām said to him, “O Messenger of Allah, what is the degree?” He said, “Indeed it is not your mother’s threshold. Between each two degrees is one hundred years.”"],[367,"Of jealousy there is some that Allah hates and some that Allah loves; and of pride there is some that Allah loves and some that Allah hates. The jealousy that Allah loves is jealousy in religion; the jealousy that Allah hates is jealousy in other than His religion. The pride that Allah loves is a man's pride in himself at the time of fighting and at the time of charity; and the pride that Allah hates is pride in falsehood."],[368,"When the Messenger of Allah ﷺ prayed the morning prayer, he would turn his face toward us and say, 'Did any of you see a dream last night?' One day he asked us and then said, 'Last night I was shown two men who came to me, took me by the hand, and ascended with me into a tree. They brought me into a house the like of which I have never seen more beautiful. They said, \"As for this house, it is the house of the martyrs.\"'"],[369,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, \"Whoever fights in the cause of Allah, having faith, with perseverance, the reward of Paradise is guaranteed for him.\""],[370,"\"The martyr does not feel the pain of being killed except like one of you feels the pain of a pinch.\""],[371,"\"The first three to enter Paradise: the martyr, a slave who is sincere to his master and perfects worship of his Lord, and a poor person who abstains from asking. The first three to enter the Fire: a tyrannical ruler, a wealthy person who does not pay Allah's right in his wealth, and a boastful poor person.\""],[372,"“A Muslim eats in one intestine, and a disbeliever eats in seven intestines.”"],[373,"«Whoever is wounded with a wound in the way of Allah will come on the Day of Resurrection bleeding, with the color the color of blood and the fragrance the fragrance of musk. And whoever is wounded in the way of Allah is stamped with the seal of the martyrs»"],[374,"We entered upon Umm al-Darda' while we were young orphans. She wiped our heads and said, 'Rejoice, O my sons, for I hope that you will be in the intercession of your father, for I heard Abu al-Darda' say: I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say, \"The martyr will intercede for seventy members of his household.\"'"],[375,"The soul of the believer is a bird that hangs in the trees of Paradise until Allah returns it to his body on the Day of Resurrection."],[376,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, \"The martyrs are on the banks of a flowing river near the gate of Paradise, in a green dome. Their provision comes to them from Paradise in the morning and evening.\""],[377,"There is no one who enters Paradise who would be pleased to return to this world except the martyr, for he would love to return and be killed once again."],[378,"There is no one who enters Paradise who would love to return to this world even if he had everything on earth, except the martyr, for he wishes to return to this world and be killed ten times because of the honor he sees."],[379,"The slain are of three types: a believing man who strives with his soul and wealth in the path of Allah, and when he meets the enemy he fights them until he is killed—that is the tested martyr in the tent of Allah beneath His Throne, and the prophets do not surpass him except by the rank of prophethood. A believing man who has brought sins and errors upon himself, who strives with his soul and wealth in the path of Allah, and when he meets the enemy he fights until he is killed—that is a purification that wipes away his sins and errors. Indeed the sword erases errors, and he will be admitted from whichever of the gates of Paradise he wishes, for it has eight gates, and Hell has seven gates, and some are better than others. And a hypocritical man who strives with his soul and wealth in the path of Allah, and when he meets the enemy he fights until he is killed—that one is in the Fire. Indeed the sword does not erase hypocrisy."],[380,"Three people Allah loves: A man who came to a people and asked them by Allah, not by kinship between them and him, and a man lagged behind them and gave him secretly, no one knowing of his gift except Allah and the one to whom he gave; and a people who traveled at night until sleep was dearer to them, so they dismounted and laid down their heads, but he stood flattering Me and reciting My verses; and a man who was in a raiding party and they met the enemy and were defeated, but he advanced with his chest until he was killed or victory was granted to them."],[381,"Harithah, the son of my paternal aunt, went as a spectator on the day of Badr, not for fighting. An arrow struck him and killed him. My aunt, his mother, came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and said, 'O Messenger of Allah, my son Harithah—if he is in Paradise, I will be patient and seek reward; otherwise, you will see what I do.' The Prophet ﷺ said, 'O mother of Harithah, there are many Gardens, and Harithah is in the highest Firdaws.'"],[382,"I have been commanded to fight the people until they say, \"There is no god but Allah.\" If they bear witness that there is no god but Allah and believe in me and in what I have brought, they have protected their blood and their wealth from me, except by its right, and their reckoning is upon Allah."],[383,"Allah laughs at two men, one of whom kills the other, and both are in Paradise."],[384,"Indeed Allah laughs at two men, one of whom kills the other, and both will enter Paradise: this one fights in the path of Allah and is killed, then Allah accepts the repentance of the killer, and he fights in the path of Allah and is martyred."],[385,"«Whoever is wounded with a wound in the way of Allah will come on the Day of Resurrection with his fragrance like the fragrance of musk, his color the color of saffron, and upon him the seal of the martyrs. And whoever asks Allah for martyrdom sincerely, Allah will give him the reward of a martyr even if he dies on his bed»"],[386,"«Whoever asks Allah for martyrdom with sincerity, Allah will convey him to the ranks of the martyrs even if he dies on his bed»"],[387,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ came to visit 'Abd Allah b. Thabit and found that he had been overcome. He called out to him, but he did not answer. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, \"We belong to Allah and to Him we return,\" and said, «We have been overcome concerning you, O Abu al-Rabi'.» The women cried out and wept, and Ibn 'Atik began to silence them. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, «Leave them. When it becomes obligatory, no weeping woman should weep.» They said, \"What is the obligation, O Messenger of Allah?\" He said, «When he dies.» His daughter said, \"By Allah, I had hoped that you would be a martyr, for you had prepared your equipment.\" The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, «Indeed Allah has placed his reward according to his intention. What do you consider martyrdom?» They said, \"Being killed in the way of Allah.\" The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, «Martyrdom is seven besides being killed in the way of Allah: the one who dies of a stomach disease is a martyr, the one who drowns is a martyr, the one with pleurisy is a martyr, the one who dies in the plague is a martyr, the one who burns is a martyr, the one who dies under a collapsed building is a martyr, and a woman who dies in childbirth is a martyr»"],[388,"«Whoever is killed defending his wealth is a martyr»"],[389,"“Whoever usurps a span of land, Allah will collar him on the Day of Resurrection with it from seven earths.”"],[390,"“The warrior in the way of Allah, the pilgrim to the House of Allah, and the one performing ʿUmrah are the delegation of Allah. He called them and they answered Him.”"],[391,"We were on a military expedition when the Prophet ﷺ said, “There are people in Madinah who have accompanied you, held back by illness.”"],[392,"When the Messenger of Allah ﷺ returned from the expedition of Tabuk and approached Madinah, he said, \"In Madinah there are people who, whatever distance you traveled and whatever valley you crossed, were with you in it.\" They said, \"O Messenger of Allah, while they are in Madinah?\" He said, \"Yes, an excuse detained them.\""],[393,"A man came to the Prophet ﷺ asking his permission for jihad. He said, \"Are your parents alive?\" He said, \"Yes.\" He said, \"Then strive in them.\""],[394,"A man said, \"O Messenger of Allah, do you permit me to go on jihad?\" He said, \"Do you have parents?\" He said, \"Yes.\" He said, \"Go and be dutiful to them.\" So he went, threading his way through the riding camels."],[395,"A man emigrated to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ from Yemen and said, “O Messenger of Allah, I have emigrated.” The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, “You have left polytheism behind, but what about jihad? Do you have anyone in Yemen?” He said, “My parents.” He said, “Did they give you permission?” He said, “No.” He said, “Go back and ask their permission. If they permit you, then fight; otherwise, be dutiful to them.”"],[396,"O Messenger of Allah, may we not go out and strive in jihad with you, for I do not see any deed in the Quran more virtuous than jihad.\" He said, \"No, but for you women the best jihad is Hajj of the House, a righteous Hajj.\""],[397,"Salman passed by [Shurahbil] while he was stationed for guarding and asked, \"What are you doing here, Shurahabil?\" Shurahabil replied, \"I am performing ribat (guarding) in the cause of Allah.\" Salman said, \"I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say, 'The act of guarding for a day or a night is better than fasting and praying for an entire month.'\""],[398,"\"Every deceased person's deeds are sealed, except the one who died standing guard in the way of Allah, for his deeds will continue to grow for him until the Day of Resurrection and he will be safe from the trial of the grave.\""],[399,"\"Whoever dies standing guard in the way of Allah will be protected from the punishment of the grave, and his reward will continue to grow for him until the Day of Resurrection.\""],[400,"Salman passed by him while he was standing guard and said, \"I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say, 'Whoever dies standing guard, the deeds he used to perform will continue to be recorded for him, and he will be protected from the two tempters, and his provision will continue to come to him.'\""],[401,"“The best of you are those who learn the Qurʾān and teach it.”"],[402,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, \"Learn the Quran and keep it with you, for by the One in whose hand is my soul, it is more intricate than the separation of the placenta in the womb.\""],[403,"“The example of one who is given the Qurʾān and faith is that of a citron: pleasant in taste and pleasant in smell. The example of one who is not given the Qurʾān nor faith is that of a colocynth: bitter in taste and no smell. The example of one who is given faith but not the Qurʾān is that of a date: pleasant in taste but no smell. The example of one who is given the Qurʾān but not faith is that of sweet basil: bitter in taste but pleasant in smell.”"],[404,"From the Prophet ﷺ: “The Qurʾān is an intercessor whose intercession is accepted, and a disputant whose argument is believed. Whoever places it before him, it will lead him to Paradise; and whoever puts it behind his back, it will drive him to the Fire.”"],[405,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ sent out an expedition of a group of men. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ called them and said, 'How much of the Quran do you have with you?' He examined them until he came to a man among them who was the youngest of them. He said, 'What do you have with you, O so-and-so?' He said, 'I have such-and-such and Surah al-Baqarah.' He said, 'You have Surah al-Baqarah?' He said, 'Yes.' He said, 'Go, for you are their commander.' A man from among their nobles said, 'By the One who is such-and-such, O Messenger of Allah, nothing prevented me from learning the Quran except the fear that I would not be able to uphold it.' The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, 'Learn the Quran, recite it, and sleep. For the example of the Quran for the one who learns it, recites it, and upholds it is like a leather bag filled with musk, whose fragrance spreads everywhere. And the one who learns it and sleeps while it is in his heart is like a leather bag tied over musk.'"],[406,"We entered upon him and said to him, \"You have indeed witnessed good, accompanied the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and prayed behind him.\" He replied, \"Yes, indeed he ﷺ delivered a sermon to us and said, 'I am leaving among you the Qur'an, it is the rope of Allah, whoever holds onto it will be upon guidance, and whoever abandons it will be upon misguidance.'\""],[407,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, \"It will be said to the companion of the Qur'an on the Day of Resurrection, 'Recite and ascend, and recite with tarteel as you used to recite with tarteel in the abode of the world, for your station will be at the last verse you used to recite.'\""],[408,"“The one who recites the Qur’an aloud is like the one who gives charity openly, and the one who recites it silently is like the one who gives charity secretly.”"],[409,"\"The parable of the one who recites the Qur'an while he is skilled in it is with the noble, righteous scribes (angels). And the one who recites it while it is difficult for him will have two rewards.\""],[410,"\"The parable of the companion of the Qur'an is like the owner of hobbled camels; if he keeps them hobbled, he retains them, and if he sets them free, they go away.\""],[411,"\"The parable of the believer who recites the Qur'an is like the citron: its taste is good and its fragrance is good. The parable of the believer who does not recite the Qur'an is like the date: its taste is good but it has no fragrance. The parable of the wicked person who recites the Qur'an is like the sweet basil: its fragrance is good but its taste is bitter. The parable of the wicked person who does not recite the Qur'an is like the colocynth: its taste is bitter and it has no fragrance.\""],[412,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ came out to us while we were in the shaded portico (al-ṣuffa) and said: “Which of you would love to go out every morning to Buṭḥān or al-ʿAqīq and bring back two large-humped, fat she-camels, taking them without committing any sin or severing ties of kinship?” They said: “All of us, O Messenger of Allah, would love that.” The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “If one of you goes to the mosque and learns two verses from the Book of Allah, that is better for him than two she-camels; three verses are better than three; and four verses are better than the same number of camels.”"],[413,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ came out to us and said: “Rejoice, rejoice! Do you not testify that there is no god but Allah and that I am the Messenger of Allah?” They said: “Yes.” He said: “This Qurʾān is a rope, one end of it is in the hand of Allah and the other end is in your hands. Hold fast to it, for you will never go astray nor perish after it, ever.”"],[414,"The Prophet ﷺ was on a journey and dismounted. A man from his companions walked beside him, so he turned to him and said, \"Shall I not tell you of the best of the Quran?\" He said: So he recited to him, \"{Praise be to Allah, Lord of the worlds}.\""],[415,"\"There is nothing in the Torah or the Gospel like the Mother of the Quran, which is the seven oft-repeated verses, and it is divided between Me and My servant, and My servant shall have what he asks.\""],[416,"\"Whoever prays a prayer in which he does not recite the Opening of the Book, it is deficient, it is deficient, not complete.\""],[417,"They had a drying-place for dates, and he used to check it and find it decreasing. One night he guarded it, and behold, there was a creature like a boy who had reached puberty. He said: I greeted it, and it returned the greeting. I said, \"What are you, a jinn or a human?\" It said, \"A jinn.\" I said, \"Give me your hand.\" Its hand was like a dog's paw with dog's hair. I said, \"Is this how jinn are created?\" It said, \"The jinn know that there is none among them stronger than I.\" I said, \"What made you do what you did?\" It said, \"I heard that you are a man who loves charity, so I wanted to get some of your food.\" I said, \"What protects us from you?\" It said, \"This verse, Ayat al-Kursi.\" He said: I left it, and in the morning my father went to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and told him. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, \"The wicked one spoke the truth.\""],[418,"\"O Messenger of Allah, while I was reciting Surah al-Baqarah last night, I heard a thud behind me and thought my horse had run off.\" The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, \"Recite, O Abu 'Atik.\" I turned around and saw something like a lamp hanging between heaven and earth, and the Messenger of Allah ﷺ was saying, \"Recite, O Abu 'Atik.\" He said, \"O Messenger of Allah, I could not continue.\" The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, \"Those were angels who descended to listen to the recitation of Surah al-Baqarah. If you had continued, you would have seen wonders.\""],[419,"\"Everything has a hump, and the hump of the Quran is Surah al-Baqarah. Whoever recites it in his house at night, Satan will not enter his house for three nights, and whoever recites it during the day, Satan will not enter his house for three days.\""],[420,"I met Abu Mas'ud during tawaf and asked him about it. He narrated to me that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, \"Whoever recites the two verses from the end of Surah al-Baqarah in a night, they will suffice him.\""],[421,"\"The two verses with which Surah al-Baqarah is concluded are not recited in a house for three nights without Satan coming near it.\""],[422,"\"Do not make your houses into graveyards. Pray in them, for Satan flees from a house in which he hears Surah al-Baqarah being recited.\""],[423,"While Gabriel was sitting with the Prophet ﷺ, he heard a creaking sound from above him. He raised his head and said, \"A gate of heaven has been opened that has never been opened before.\" Then an angel came to him and said, \"Rejoice in two surahs that you have been given and no prophet before you was given: the Opening of the Book and the closing verses of Surah al-Baqarah. You will not recite a letter from them except that you will be given it.\""],[424,"A man was reciting Surat al-Kahf while his mount was hobbled, and it began to shy as if seeing a fog or cloud that had enveloped him. He came to the Prophet ﷺ and mentioned that to him, and he said, \"Recite, O so-and-so; that was the tranquility (sakinah) sent down with the Qur'an or for the Qur'an.\""],[425,"Whoever recites ten verses from Surah al-Kahf will be protected from the trial of the Dajjal."],[426,"Whoever recites ten verses from the end of al-Kahf will be protected from the Dajjal."],[427,"Indeed, a surah in the Quran with thirty verses intercedes for its reciter until he is forgiven: {Tabarak alladhi biyadihi al-mulk}."],[428,"A man heard another man reciting {Qul huwa Allahu ahad}, repeating it. When morning came, he went to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and mentioned that to him, and the man seemed to belittle it. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to him, “By the One in whose hand is my soul, it is equal to a third of the Quran.”"],[429,"A man said, “O Messenger of Allah, I love Qul huwa Allahu ahad.” The Prophet ﷺ said, “Your love for it will admit you to Paradise.”"],[430,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ sent a man as commander of a military expedition, and he used to recite for his companions in their prayers Qul huwa Allahu ahad. When they returned, they mentioned that to the Prophet ﷺ, and he said, “Ask him why he did this.” They asked him, and he said, “I love to recite it.” The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, “Tell him that Allah loves him.”"],[431,"A man used to persist in reciting {Qul huwa Allahu ahad} in prayer along with every surah, and he was leading his companions. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to him about it, and he said, “I love it.” He said, “Love for it will admit you to Paradise.”"],[432,"I followed the Prophet ﷺ one day while he was riding, and I placed my hand on his hand and said, “O Messenger of Allah, teach me to recite from Surah Hud and from Surah Yusuf.” The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, “You will never recite anything more effective with Allah than Qul a'udhu bi-rabb al-falaq.”"],[433,"I followed the Messenger of Allah ﷺ while he was riding, and I placed my hand on his foot and said: O Messenger of Allah, teach me to recite either from Surat Hud or from Surat Yusuf. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “O ‘Uqbah b. ‘Amir, you will never recite a surah more beloved to Allah, nor more effective in His sight, than that you recite: ‘Say: I seek refuge in the Lord of the dawn.’ So if you can avoid missing it in any prayer, do so.”"],[434,"He said, “Recite, O Jabir.” I said, “What shall I recite, may my father and mother be your ransom?” He said, “{Qul a'udhu bi-rabb al-falaq} and {Qul a'udhu bi-rabb al-nas}.” So I recited them, and he ﷺ said, “Recite with them, and you will never recite anything like them.”"],[435,"Nafi' b. 'Abd al-Harith met 'Umar b. al-Khattab at 'Usfan. Nafi' was 'Umar's governor over Makkah. 'Umar said, \"Whom did you appoint as your successor over the people of the valley, meaning the people of Makkah?\" He said, \"Ibn Abza.\" 'Umar said, \"And who is Ibn Abza?\" He said, \"A man from the mawali.\" 'Umar said, \"You appointed over them a freed slave?\" He said, \"He is a reciter of the Book of Allah.\" 'Umar said, \"Indeed, your Prophet ﷺ said, 'Allah elevates some peoples by this Qur'an and lowers others by it.'\""],[436,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, \"No group of people gathers in a mosque, reciting the Book of Allah and studying it among themselves, except that tranquility descends upon them, mercy enfolds them, the angels surround them, and Allah mentions them to those in His presence. And whoever is slow in their actions will not be expedited by their lineage.\""],[437,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ was traveling on the road to Makkah when he passed by a mountain called Jumdan. He said, 'Move on, this is Jumdan. The mufarridun have gone ahead, the mufarridun have gone ahead.' They said, 'O Messenger of Allah, who are the mufarridun?' He said, 'Those men and women who remember Allah much.'"],[438,"I heard Abu Hurayrah in the house of Umm al-Darda' narrating from the Prophet ﷺ that he said: \"Allah, Blessed and Exalted, said: 'I am with My servant as long as he remembers Me and his lips move with My mention.'\""],[439,"Mu'awiyah b. Abi Sufyan came out upon a circle in the mosque and said: \"What makes you sit?\" They said: \"We have sat to remember Allah.\" He said: \"By Allah, has nothing made you sit except that?\" They said: \"By Allah, nothing has made us sit except that.\" He said: \"Indeed, the Messenger of Allah ﷺ came out upon a circle of his Companions and said: 'What makes you sit?' They said: 'We have sat to remember Allah and to praise Him for having guided us to Islam and bestowed it upon us as a favor.' He said: 'By Allah, has nothing made you sit except that?' They said: 'By Allah, nothing has made us sit except that.' He said: 'Indeed, I did not make you swear because I suspected you, but Jibril came to me and informed me that Allah is boasting of you to the angels.'\""],[440,"Indeed Allah has angels who are extra beyond the recorders of people's deeds. They walk along the roads seeking out remembrance. When they see people remembering Allah, Blessed and Exalted, they call to one another, 'Come to what you seek!' They surround them with their wings up to the sky. Then their Lord, Majestic and Exalted, asks them, though He knows best about them, 'My servants, what are they saying?' They say, 'O Lord, they are glorifying You, praising You, and magnifying You.' He says, 'Have they seen Me?' They say, 'No.' He says, 'How would it be if they saw Me?' They say, 'If they saw You, they would be even more intense in glorifying, extolling, magnifying, and praising You.' He says, 'What are they asking for?' They say, 'They ask You, O Lord, for Paradise.' He says, 'Have they seen it?' They say, 'No.' He says, 'How would it be if they saw it?' They say, 'If they saw it, they would be even more eager and more desirous of it.' He says, 'From what are they seeking refuge?' They say, 'They seek refuge with You from the Fire.' He says, 'Have they seen it?' They say, 'No.' He says, 'How would it be if they saw it?' They say, 'If they saw it, they would be even more earnest in seeking refuge from it.' He says, 'I call you to witness that I have forgiven them.'"],[441,"From the Messenger of Allahﷺ he said: \"Allah, Glorious and Exalted, says: 'The people of the gathering today will be recognized as the people of honor.' So it was said: 'Who are the people of honor, O Messenger of Allah?' He said: 'The people who gather for remembrance of Allah in the mosques.'\""],[442,"The best remembrance is the hidden one, and the best provision - or livelihood - is what suffices."],[443,"No people sit in a gathering without remembering Allah therein except that it will be a source of regret for them on the Day of Resurrection. No one walks a path without remembering Allah therein except that it will be a source of regret for him. No one retires to his bed without remembering Allah therein except that it will be a source of regret for him."],[444,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"Allah, Blessed and Exalted, said: 'I am as My servant thinks of Me, and I am with him wherever he remembers Me. If he remembers Me within himself, I remember him within Myself; and if he remembers Me in an assembly, I remember him in an assembly better than them. If he draws near to Me a handspan, I draw near to him an arm's length; and if he comes to Me walking, I come to him at speed.'\""],[445,"He bears witness, from Abu Hurairah and Abu Sa’eed Al-Khudri, that they bear witness, from the Messenger of Allah, that he said: “There is no group that remembers Allah, except that the angels encompass them, mercy covers them, and tranquility descends upon them: and Allah remembers (mentions) them before those who are with Him.” (Using translation from Tirmidhī 3378)"],[446,"Two Arab Bedouins came to the Prophet ﷺ and one of them said, \"O Messenger of Allah, tell me something that I can cling to.\" He said, \"Keep your tongue moist with the remembrance of Allah.\""],[447,"Indeed Allah has angels who are extra beyond the recorders of people's deeds. They roam the roads seeking out the people of remembrance. When they find a group remembering Allah, they call to one another, 'Come to what you seek!' They surround them with their wings up to the nearest heaven. Then their Lord asks them, though He knows better than them, 'What are My servants saying?' They say, 'They magnify You, extol You, glorify You, and praise You.' He says, 'Have they seen Me?' They say, 'No.' He says, 'How would it be if they saw Me?' They say, 'If they saw You, they would worship You even more intensely, and glorify, praise, and extol You even more.' He says, 'What are they asking of Me?' They say, 'They ask You for Paradise.' He says, 'Have they seen it?' They say, 'No, by Allah, O Lord.' He says, 'How would it be if they saw it?' They say, 'If they saw it, they would be even more eager for it, more desirous of it, and greater in their longing for it.' He says, 'From what are they seeking refuge?' They say, 'From the Fire.' He says, 'Have they seen it?' They say, 'No, by Allah, O Lord.' He says, 'How would it be if they saw it?' They say, 'If they saw it, they would flee from it even more, run from it even more, and fear it even more.' Then Allah says to His angels, 'I call you to witness that I have forgiven them.' One of the angels said, 'Among them is so-and-so, who is not one of them; he only came for some need.' He said, 'They are the companions; the one who sits with them will not be wretched.'"],[448,"Increase in remembrance of Allah until they say you are mad."],[449,"I asked the Messenger of Allah ﷺ: 'Which deeds are most beloved to Allah?' He said: 'That you die while your tongue is moist with the remembrance of Allah.'"],[450,"The example of the house in which Allah is remembered and the house in which Allah is not remembered is like the living and the dead."],[451,"No people gather in a gathering and then disperse without mentioning Allah and sending blessings upon the Prophet ﷺ except that it will be a regret for them on the Day of Resurrection."],[452,"No people sit in a sitting where they do not mention Allah and send blessings upon the Prophet except that it will be a regret for them on the Day of Resurrection, even if they are admitted to Paradise as a reward."],[453,"Whoever sends prayers upon me once, ten good deeds are recorded for him."],[454,"Whoever sends prayers upon me once, Allah sends prayers upon him ten times."],[455,"\"The Prophet (PBUH) ascended the pulpit and said, 'Ameen, Ameen, Ameen.' It was asked, 'O Messenger of Allah, when you ascended the pulpit, you said 'Ameen, Ameen, Ameen.' He said, 'Gabriel came to me and said, 'Whoever reaches the month of Ramadan and does not have his sins forgiven, and therefore enters Hell, then may Allah distance him. Say ameen.' So, I said 'ameen.' Then Gabriel said, 'Whoever's parents or one of them reaches old age and they do not earn Paradise by being dutiful towards them, then may Allah distance him. Say ameen.' So, I said 'ameen.' Then Gabriel said, 'Whoever hears your name mentioned and does not send blessings upon you, then may Allah distance him. Say ameen.' So, I said 'ameen.\""],[456,"May his nose be rubbed in dust: a man in whose presence I am mentioned and he does not send prayers upon me. May his nose be rubbed in dust: a man who attains his parents in old age and they do not cause him to enter Paradise. May his nose be rubbed in dust: a man in whose presence the month of Ramadan enters and then it slips away before he is forgiven."],[457,"“Indeed, the miser is the one in whose presence I am mentioned and he does not invoke blessings upon me.”"],[458,"“Indeed, one of the most excellent of your days is Friday: on it Allah created Adam, on it he was taken, on it is the blast, and on it is the thunderclap. So increase in invoking blessings upon me on it, for your blessings are presented to me.” They said, “How are our blessings presented to you when you have decayed?” He said, “Indeed Allah, Mighty and Exalted, has forbidden the earth to consume our bodies.”"],[459,"“Indeed, the closest of people to me on the Day of Resurrection will be the one who invoked blessings upon me the most.”"],[460,"\"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"Whoever sends salah upon me once, Allah (SWT) will send salah upon him tenfold, and will erase ten sins from him, and will raise him ten degrees in status.\" (Using translation from Nasāʾī 1297)"],[461,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ came out while he was joyful and said, “Indeed, the angel came to me and said, ‘O Muhammad, Allah says: Are you not pleased that no servant of My servants invokes blessings upon you but I bless him ten times for it, and no one greets you with one greeting of peace but I greet him with ten?’ I said, ‘Yes, O Lord.’”"],[462,"“Indeed, Allah has angels who roam the earth, conveying to me the greetings of peace from my nation.”"],[463,"“Do not be too weak to supplicate, for no one perishes with supplication.”"],[464,"“There is nothing more honorable to Allah than supplication.”"],[465,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, \"Indeed, Allah, the Exalted and High, feels shy from the servant to raise his hands to Him and return them empty.\""],[466,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, \"The servant's supplication continues to be answered as long as he does not supplicate for sin or severing ties of kinship, and as long as he does not hasten.\" It was said, \"O Messenger of Allah, how does he hasten?\" He said, \"He says, 'I have supplicated and I have not been answered,' so he gives up at that point and abandons supplication.\""],[467,"\"When one of you asks, let him ask abundantly, for he is asking his Lord.\""],[468,"“One of you should ask his Lord for all his needs, even the strap of his sandal when it breaks.”"],[469,"The translation of the given phrase in English is: \"Indeed the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, 'When one of you supplicates, let him have great desire and hope, for indeed there is nothing too great for Allah.'\""],[470,"\"When the muezzin says: 'Allahu akbar, Allahu akbar,' and one of you says: 'Allahu akbar, Allahu akbar'; then he says: 'Ashhadu an la ilaha illa Allah,' and he says: 'Ashhadu an la ilaha illa Allah'; then he says: 'Ashhadu anna Muhammadan rasul Allah,' and he says: 'Ashhadu anna Muhammadan rasul Allah'; then he says: 'Hayya 'ala al-salah,' and he says: 'La hawla wa la quwwata illa billah'; then he says: 'Hayya 'ala al-falah,' and he says: 'La hawla wa la quwwata illa billah'; then he says: 'Allahu akbar, Allahu akbar,' and he says: 'Allahu akbar, Allahu akbar'; then he says: 'La ilaha illa Allah,' and he says: 'La ilaha illa Allah' – he will enter Paradise.\""],[471,"A man said: 'O Messenger of Allah, the muezzins surpass us.' The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: 'Say as they say, and when you finish, ask, and you will be given.'"],[472,"\"When you hear the muezzin, say the like of what he says, then invoke blessings upon me, for whoever invokes blessings upon me once, Allah will bless him ten times. Then ask Allah for the means for me, for it is a station in Paradise that befits only one of Allah's servants, and I hope that I am he. Whoever asks Allah for the means for me, intercession will be assured for him.\""],[473,"\"When you hear the muezzin, say as he says, and invoke blessings upon me, for there is no one who invokes blessings upon me once except that Allah blesses him ten times. And ask for the means for me, for the means is a station in Paradise, and it is not fitting except for one of Allah's servants, and I hope that I am he. Whoever asks it for me, my intercession will be assured for him on the Day of Resurrection.\""],[474,"When you hear the muezzin, say what he says, then invoke blessings upon me, for whoever invokes blessings upon me once, Allah will bless him ten times. Then ask Allah to grant me al-wasilah, for it is a station in Paradise that is not befitting except for one of Allah’s servants, and I hope that I am he. Whoever asks Allah for al-wasilah for me, intercession becomes permitted for him."],[475,"Whoever says when he hears the muezzin: 'And I testify that there is no god but Allah alone, with no partner, and I testify that Muhammad is His servant and Messenger. I am pleased with Allah as Lord, with Islam as religion, and with Muhammad ﷺ as Messenger,' his previous sins will be forgiven."],[476,"He has tasted the flavor of faith who is pleased with Allah as Lord, with Islam as religion, and with Muhammad ﷺ as Prophet."],[477,"\"Whoever says upon hearing the call: 'O Allah, Lord of this perfect call and the established prayer, grant Muhammad the means and the excellence, and raise him to the praiseworthy station which You promised him' – intercession will be assured for him on the Day of Resurrection.\""],[478,"Supplication between the adhan and the iqamah is answered, so supplicate."],[479,"“Two hours in which the gates of heaven are opened: at the time of the prayer and when standing in ranks in the path of Allah.”"],[480,"Two times when the supplication of a supplicant is not rejected: when the prayer is called and when in the ranks in the cause of Allah."],[481,"When one of you enters the mosque, let him greet the Prophet ﷺ and say: O Allah, open for me the gates of Your mercy. And when he leaves, let him greet the Prophet ﷺ and say: O Allah, protect me from the accursed Shayṭān."],[482,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ was praying with them when a man came, out of breath, and said: “Praise be to Allah, abundant, good, and blessed praise.” When the Messenger of Allah ﷺ finished his prayer, he said: “Which of you said those words?” The people remained silent. He said: “Which of you said those words? He did not say anything wrong.” The man said: “I did, O Messenger of Allah. I came out of breath and I said them.” He said: “I saw twelve angels rushing to see which of them would raise it.”"],[483,"When the imam says, \"not of those who have incurred wrath nor of those who are astray,\" then say, \"Amin,\" for the angels say, \"Amin,\" and the imam says, \"Amin.\" And whoever's saying of Amin coincides with the angels' saying of Amin, his previous sins are forgiven."],[484,"When the imam says 'Allah hears the one who praises Him,' then say: 'O Allah, our Lord, and to You be praise,' for whoever's saying coincides with the saying of the angels, his previous sins are forgiven."],[485,"One day we were praying behind the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and when he raised his head from the rak'ah and said: 'Allah hears the one who praises Him,' a man behind him said: 'Our Lord, and to You be praise, much good and blessed praise therein.' When the Messenger of Allah ﷺ finished, he said: 'Who was the one speaking just now?' A man said: 'I, O Messenger of Allah.' The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: 'I saw thirty-some angels rushing to it, each vying to be the first to write it down.'"],[486,"The poor people came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and said, \"The wealthy have gone with their abundant wealth to the higher levels and constant blessings. They pray as we pray, fast as we fast, and they have extra wealth with which they perform Hajj, Umrah, strive in the cause of Allah, and give in charity.\" He ﷺ said, \"Shall I not inform you of something through which you will surpass those who preceded you and those who will come after you, and no one can exceed you except someone who does the same as you do?\" They said, \"Yes, Messenger of Allah.\" He ﷺ said, \"You should say Tahmid (saying 'Al-hamdu lillah'), Tahlil (saying 'La ilaha illallah'), and Tasbih (saying 'Subhanallah') thirty-three times after every Salah (prayer).\""],[487,"Abū Dharr said: \"O Messenger of Allah, the wealthy have gone with the reward, praying as we pray, fasting as we fast, and they have surplus wealth with which they give charity.\" The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"O Abū Dharr, shall I not teach you words by which you may catch up with those who have preceded you, and none after you will catch up with you except one who does the like of your deed?\" He said: \"Yes, O Messenger of Allah.\" He said: \"Magnify Allah after every prayer thirty-three times, praise Him thirty-three times, glorify Him thirty-three times, and conclude them with 'There is no god but Allah alone, with no partner. His is the dominion and His is the praise, and He is over all things competent.'\""],[488,"\"Whoever glorifies Allah after every prayer thirty-three times, praises Him thirty-three times, and magnifies Him thirty-three times—that is ninety-nine—and says to complete one hundred: 'There is no god but Allah alone, with no partner. His is the dominion and His is the praise, and He is over all things competent,' his sins will be forgiven, even if they are like the foam of the sea.\""],[489,"\"We were commanded to glorify Allah after every prayer thirty-three times, praise Him thirty-three times, and magnify Him thirty-four times.\" Then a man was visited in his sleep and it was said to him: \"Did Muḥammad ﷺ command you to glorify Allah after every prayer thirty-three times, praise Him thirty-three times, and magnify Him thirty-four times?\" He said: \"Yes.\" He said: \"Make them twenty-five each, and include the tahlīl in them.\" When he woke up, he went to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and told him, and the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"Do it.\""],[490,"\"Two qualities no servant keeps count of except that he enters Paradise, and they are easy, but few are those who act upon them. One of you glorifies Allah after every prayer ten times, praises Him ten times, and magnifies Him ten times—that is one hundred and fifty on the tongue and one thousand five hundred in the Balance. When he retires to his bed, he glorifies thirty-three times, praises thirty-three times, and magnifies thirty-four times—that is one hundred on the tongue and one thousand in the Balance.\" The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"Which of you would commit two thousand five hundred sins in a day and night?\" ʿAbd Allāh b. ʿAmr said: \"I saw the Messenger of Allah ﷺ counting them with his hand.\" He said: \"It was said: 'O Messenger of Allah, how can one not keep count of them?' He said: 'Satan comes to one of you while he is in his prayer and says: \"Remember such-and-such, remember such-and-such,\" and he comes to him at his sleep and makes him sleep.'\""],[491,"The Prophet said: “There are Mu’aqqibat, he who says them shall not be miserable. Glorify Allah at the end of every prayer thirty-three times, and praise him thirty-three times, and extol His greatness thirty-four times.” (Using translation from Tirmidhī 3412)"],[492,"That the Messenger of Allah ﷺ took Muʿādh by the hand and said: \"O Muʿādh, by Allah, I love you.\" Muʿādh said: \"May my father and mother be your ransom; by Allah, I love you.\" He said: \"O Muʿādh, I exhort you never to fail, after every prayer, to say: O Allah, help me to remember You, thank You, and worship You well.\""],[493,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ sent us on a military expedition. When we reached the raiding place, I urged my horse on and outstripped my companions. The tribe met me with wailing, so I said, \"Say: There is no god but Allah, and you will be protected.\" They said it, and my companions blamed me, saying, \"You deprived us of the spoils after they had been within our grasp.\" When we came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, they told him what I had done. He called me and commended what I had done, and said, \"Indeed, Allah has recorded for you for each person of them such and such.\""],[494,"'Whoever asks Allah for Paradise three times, Paradise says: O Allah, admit him to Paradise. And whoever seeks refuge from the Fire three times, the Fire says: O Allah, protect him from the Fire.'"],[495,"\"Whoever says when he reaches the morning: 'There is no god but Allah alone, with no partner; His is the dominion and His is the praise, and He is capable of everything' ten times, ten good deeds are recorded for him by them, ten evil deeds are erased from him by them, he is raised ten degrees by them, and they are for him equivalent to manumitting four slaves, and they are for him a guard from Satan until he reaches the evening. And whoever says them when he prays the sunset prayer, after his prayer, then the like of that until he reaches the morning.\""],[496,"Whoever says in the morning, 'Glory be to Allah the Magnificent and praise be to Him' one hundred times, and in the evening likewise, no one among creation will come on the Day of Resurrection with the like of what he comes with."],[497,"Whoever says in the morning, 'Glory be to Allah and praise be to Him' one hundred times, and in the evening one hundred times, his sins will be forgiven even if they are more than the foam of the sea."],[498,"The Prophet ﷺ said: If anyone says in the morning: \"O Allah! whatever favour has come to me, it comes from Thee alone Who has no partner; to Thee praise is due and thanksgiving,'! he will have expressed full thanksgiving for the day; and if anyone says the same in the evening, he will have expressed full thanksgiving for the night. (Using translation from Abū Dāʾūd 5073)"],[499,"The Prophet ﷺ said, \"Indeed, if you were to say, when you enter the evening, 'I seek refuge in the perfect words of Allah from the evil of what He has created, [then] nothing would harm you.'\""],[500,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: 'If you had said when evening came: Aʿūdhu bi-kalimāti llāhi t-tāmmāti min sharri mā khalaq (I seek refuge in the perfect words of Allah from the evil of what He has created), it would not have harmed you, if Allah wills.'"],[501,"'Whoever says when evening comes: Aʿūdhu bi-kalimāti llāhi t-tāmmāti min sharri mā khalaq (I seek refuge in the perfect words of Allah from the evil of what He has created) three times, no snake will harm him until morning.' He said: When one of his family was stung, he would say: Did he not say the words?*!"],[502,"Whoever says in the morning, 'In the name of Allah with Whose name nothing on earth or in heaven can cause harm, and He is the All-Hearing, the All-Knowing' three times, no sudden calamity will befall him until evening. And if he says it in the evening, no sudden calamity will befall him until morning."],[503,"Whoever says in the morning three times, 'In the name of Allah with Whose name nothing on earth or in heaven can cause harm, and He is the All-Hearing, the All-Knowing,' no sudden calamity will befall him until evening. And whoever says it in the evening, no sudden calamity will befall him until morning."],[504,"Whoever says: O Allah, You are my Lord, there is no god but You. You created me and I am Your servant, and I abide by Your covenant and promise as best I can. I seek refuge in You from the evil of what I have done. I acknowledge Your favor upon me and I acknowledge my sin, so forgive me, for none forgives sins except You. Then he dies that day or night, he will enter Paradise."],[505,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ commanded a man, when he took to his bed—and Ibn Kathir said: he enjoined a man—to say: 'O Allah, I have submitted myself to You, and turned my face to You, and entrusted my back to You, and delegated my affair to You, out of desire and fear of You. There is no refuge and no escape from You except to You. I believe in Your Book which You have sent down, and in Your Prophet whom You have sent.' Then if he dies, he dies upon the fitrah."],[506,"from the Prophet ﷺ, who said: \"Whoever says when he retires to his bed: (There is no god but Allah alone, with no partner. To Him belongs dominion, and to Him belongs praise, and He has power over all things. There is no might and no power except through Allah. Glory be to Allah, praise be to Allah, there is no god but Allah, and Allah is greatest) Allah will forgive his sins or his misdeeds\", Misar was uncertain, \"even if they are like the foam of the sea.\""],[507,"That Fatimah came to the Prophet ﷺ and used to serve him, so he said ﷺ , \"Shall I not guide you or teach you something that is better for you than that? When you go to your bed, say 'SubhanAllah', 'Allahu Akbar', and 'Alhamdulillah', thirty-three times each.\" Ali (may Allah be pleased with him) said, \"I have not left saying it since I heard it from the Prophet ﷺ .\" They said, \"Not even during the night of Siffin?\" He said, \"Not even during the night of Siffin.\""],[508,"\"Whoever wakes up at night and says when he awakens: 'There is no god but Allah alone with no partner; His is the dominion and His is the praise, and He is able to do all things. Glory be to Allah, praise be to Allah, there is no god but Allah, and Allah is greatest. There is no might and no power except with Allah. My Lord, forgive me,' he will be forgiven. And if he stands, performs ablution, and prays, his prayer will be accepted.\""],[509,"When a man retires to his bed, an angel and a devil come to him. The angel says: 'Seal with good,' and the devil says: 'Seal with evil.' If he remembers Allah and then sleeps, the angels spend the night guarding him. If he wakes up, the angel says: 'Open with good,' and the devil says: 'Open with evil.' Then if he says: 'Praise be to Allah who returned my soul to me and did not cause it to die in its sleep. Praise be to Allah who holds the heavens and the earth lest they cease to exist'—until the end of the verse—'Praise be to Allah who holds the heaven lest it fall upon the earth except by His permission,' then if he falls from his bed and dies, he will enter Paradise."],[510,"Indeed, Allah has ninety-nine names, one hundred less one; whoever enumerates them enters Paradise."],[511,"“Indeed, Allah has ninety-nine Names, one hundred less one, whoever counts them shall enter Paradise. He is Allah, the one whom there is none worthy of worship except for Him (Allāhu Lā Ilāha Illā Huwa), the Most Merciful (to the creation) (Ar-Raḥmān), the Most Beneficent (to the believers) (Ar-Raḥīm), the King (Al-Malik), the Free of Deficiencies (Al-Quddūs), the Granter of Safety (As-Salām), the Granter of Security (Al-Mu’min), the Watcher (Al-Muhaimin), the Mighty (Al-ʿAzīz), the Compeller (Al-Jabbār), the Supreme (Al-Mutakabbir), the Creator (Al-Khāliq), the Originator (Al-Bāri’), the Fashioner (Al-Muṣawwir), the Pardoner (Al-Ghaffār), the Overwhelming (Al-Qahhār), the Giving (Al-Wahhāb), the Provider (Ar-Razzāq), the Opener (Al-Fattāḥ), the Knowing (Al-ʿAlīm), the Taker (Al-Qābiḍ), the Giver (Al-Bāsiṭ), the Abaser (Al-Khāfiḍ), the Exalter (Ar-Rāfiʿ), the One who grants honor (Al-Muʿizz), the One who humiliates (Al-Mudhil), the Hearing (As-Samīʿ), the Seeing (Al-Baṣīr), the Judge (Al-Ḥakam), the Just (Al-ʿAdl), the Kind (Al-Laṭīf), the Aware (Al-Khabīr), the Forbearing (Al-Ḥalīm), the Magnificent (Al-ʿAẓīm), the Oft-Forgiving (Al-Ghafūr), the Grateful (Ash-Shakūr), the Most High (Al-ʿAliyy), the Great (Al-Kabīr), the Guardian (Al-Ḥafīẓ), the Powerful (Al-Muqīt), the Reckoner (Al-Ḥasīb), the Glorious (Al-Jalīl), the Generous (Al-Karīm), the Watcher (Ar-Raqīb), the Responder (Al-Mujīb), the Liberal Giver (Al-Wāsiʿ), the Wise (Al-Ḥakīm), the Loving (Al-Wadūd), the Majestic (Al-Majīd), the Reviver (Al-Bāʿith), the Witness (Ash-Shahīd), the Truth (Al-Ḥaqq), the Guarantor (Al-Wakīl), the Strong (Al-Qawiyy), the Firm (Al-Matīn), the One Who Aids (Al-Waliyy), the Praiseworthy (Al-Ḥamīd), the Encompasser (Al-Muḥṣi), the One Who Begins things (Al-Mubdi’), the One Who brings things back (Al-Muʿīd), the One Who gives life (Al-Muḥyi), the One Who causes death (Al-Mumīt), the Living (Al-Ḥayyu), the Self-Sufficient (Al-Qayyūm), the One Who brings into existence (Al-Wājid), the Illustrious (Al-Mājid), the One (Al-Wāḥid), the Master (Aṣ-Ṣamad), the Able (Al-Qādir), the Powerful (Al-Muqtadir), the One who hastens (Al-Muqaddim), the One who delays (Al-Mu’akhkhir), the First (Al-Awwal), the Last (Al-Ākhir), the Apparent (Aẓ-Ẓāhir), the Inner (Al-Bāṭin), the Owner (Al-Wāli), the Exalted (Al-Mutaʿāli), the Doer of Good (Al-Barr), the Acceptor of repentance (At-Tawwāb), the Avenger (Al-Muntaqim), the Pardoning (Al-ʿAfuww), the Kind (Ar-Ra’ūf), the Owner of Dominion (Mālikul-Mulk), the Possessor of Glory and Generosity (Dhul Jalāli wal Ikrām), the One who does justice (Al-Muqsiṭ), the Gatherer (Al-Jāmiʿ), the Rich (Al-Ghaniyy), the Enricher (Al-Mughni), the Preventer (Al-Māniʿ), the Harmer (Aḍ-Ḍār), the One who benefits (An-Nāfiʿ), the Light (An-Nūr), the Guide (Al-Hādi), the Originator (Al-Badīʿ), the Lasting (Al-Bāqi), the Inheritor (Al-Wārith), the Guide (Ar-Rashīd), the Tolerant (Aṣ-Ṣabūr).” (Using translation from Tirmidhī 3507)"],[512,"That Ibn Masʿūd was standing praying, and when he reached the hundredth verse of al-Nisāʾ he began to supplicate. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Ask, you will be given,” three times. He said: “O Allah, I ask You for faith that does not turn back, and bliss that does not run out, and the companionship of Muḥammad ﷺ in the highest garden of eternal residence.”"],[513,"\"Supplication is worship.\" Then he recited this verse: {Call upon Me, I will respond to you. Indeed, those who disdain My worship will enter Hell in humiliation.}"],[514,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ heard a man saying: O Allah, I ask Thee, I bear witness that there is no god but Thou, the One, He to Whom men repair, Who has not begotten, and has not been begotten, and to Whom no one is equal, and he said: You have supplicated Allah using His Greatest Name, when asked with this name He gives, and when supplicated by this name he answers. (Using translation from Abū Dāʾūd 1493)"],[515,"He entered the mosque with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ , and there was a man praying, supplicating and saying, \"O Allah, I ask You by virtue of the fact that I bear witness that there is no god but You, the One, the Eternal, who begets not nor was He begotten, and there is none comparable unto Him.\" The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, \"By the One in whose hand is my soul, he has asked Allah by His greatest name, which if He is called upon using it, He answers, and if He is asked by it, He gives.\" And when a man was reciting in a corner of the mosque, the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, \"He has been given a melodious voice from among the melodious voices of the family of Dawood (David).\" The man said, \"O Messenger of Allah, shall I inform him?\" He said, \"Yes, inform him.\" So I informed Abu Musa, and he said, \"He will always be my friend.\""],[516,"I was sitting with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ in the circle, and a man was standing praying. When he bowed and prostrated and recited the tashahhud, he supplicated. In his supplication he said: 'O Allah, I ask You by the fact that Yours is all praise; there is no god but You, the Bestower of Favors, the Ever-Giving, Originator of the heavens and the earth; O Possessor of Majesty and Honor, O Ever-Living, O Self-Subsisting. O Allah, I ask You.' The Prophet ﷺ said: 'Do you know what he has supplicated with?' They said: 'Allah and His Messenger know best.' He said: 'By the One in Whose hand is my soul, he has supplicated by His Great Name, which when one supplicates by it He answers, and when one asks by it He gives.'"],[517,"There is no forbearing person but one who has stumbled, and no wise person but one with experience."],[518,"Whoever says, 'I am pleased with Allah as Lord, with Islam as religion, and with Muhammad ﷺ as Prophet,' Paradise becomes obligatory for him."],[519,"Jibril came to the Prophet ﷺ and said: 'Allah commands you to supplicate with these words, for I will grant you one of them.' He said: 'O Allah, I ask You for the hastening of Your well-being, or patience upon Your affliction, or departure from this world to Your mercy.'"],[520,"When he goes out from his house and says: 'In the name of Allah, I have put my trust in Allah; there is no might and no power except with Allah,' it will be said to him: 'You are sufficed, protected, and guided.' Then Satan meets another Satan and says to him: 'How can you get to a man who has been sufficed, guided, and protected?'"],[521,"The Prophet ﷺ gathered his household and said, \"If any one of you experiences sadness or distress, let them say 'Allah, Allah, my Lord, I do not associate anything with Him.'\""],[522,"\"The supplications of the distressed: O Allah, Your mercy I hope for, so do not entrust me to myself for the blink of an eye, and set right all my affairs. There is no god but You.\""],[523,"He came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. Uthman said, \"I had a pain that nearly destroyed me.\" The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to him, \"Wipe with your right hand seven times and say: I seek refuge in the might of Allah and His power from the evil of what I find.\" He said, \"I said that and Allah removed what was in me, and I have kept commanding my family and others to do it.\""],[524,"When the Messenger of Allah ﷺ visited a sick person, he would sit at his head and then say seven times: “I ask Allah the Almighty, Lord of the Mighty Throne, to heal you.” If there was a delay in his appointed time, he would be cured of that pain of his."],[525,"None of you should wish for death because of harm that befalls him in this world, but let him say: O Allah, keep me alive as long as life is better for me, and take me when death is better and more virtuous for me."],[526,"Ibn ‘Abbas reported the Prophet ﷺ as saying “If anyone who means to have intercourse with his wife says “In the name of Allaah, O Allaah, keep us away from the devil and keep the devil away from what You hast provided us.” It will be ordained that no devil will ever harm the child born to them. (Using translation from Abū Dāʾūd 2161)"],[527,"Words that no one speaks in a gathering of idle talk or a gathering of falsehood upon his rising three times except that they expiate it for him, and he does not say them in a gathering of good and a gathering of remembrance except that it is sealed for him with them as a seal is placed upon a page: 'Glory be to You, O Allah, and with Your praise. There is no deity except You. I seek Your forgiveness and I repent to You.'"],[528,"Whoever sits in a gathering in which there is much noise and then says before he stands: 'Glory be to You, O Allah, our Lord, and with Your praise. There is no deity except You. I seek Your forgiveness and I repent to You,' except that he is forgiven for what occurred in that gathering of his."],[529,"The most complete of the Muslims in Islam is one from whose tongue and hand the Muslims are safe."],[530,"I set out to Iraq with a man who was with me, and 'Abdullah b. 'Umar saw us off. When he was about to part from us, he said: I do not have anything with me to give you two, but I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: “When Allah is entrusted with something, He preserves it. I entrust Allah with your religion, your trust, and the seal of your deeds.”"],[531,"“There is no Muslim who supplicates for his brother in his absence except that the angel says, 'And for you the like.' And for you the like.”"],[532,"“Three supplications are answered without doubt: the supplication of the wronged, the supplication of the traveler, and the supplication of a parent against his child.”"],[533,"“When one of you stops at a place, let him say: I seek refuge in the perfect words of Allah from the evil of what He has created, for nothing will harm him until he departs from it.”"],[534,"the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, \"Whoever some good was done to him, and he says: 'May Allah reward you in goodness' then he has done the most that he can of praise.\" (Using translation from Tirmidhī 2035)"],[535,"We were sitting with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ when he said, 'Is any one of you unable to earn a thousand good deeds every day?' A group of his companions asked him, 'How can any of us earn a thousand good deeds every day, O Messenger of Allah?' He said, 'He glorifies Allah one hundred times, and Allah writes for him a thousand good deeds and erases from him a thousand sins.'"],[536,"While a man was walking on a road, he found a thorny branch on the path, so he took it, and Allah thanked him and forgave him."],[537,"Whoever says, 'Glory be to Allah and praise be to Him,' a palm tree is planted for him thereby in the Garden."],[538,"Whoever says, 'Glory be to Allah, the Magnificent,' a tree is planted for him in the Garden."],[539,"that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ passed by him while he was moving his lips. He said: \"What are you saying, Abu Umamah?\" He said: I am remembering my Lord. He said: \"Shall I not inform you of something more—or better—than your remembrance through the night along with the day and the day along with the night? It is that you say: Glory be to Allah by the number of what He has created; glory be to Allah filling what He has created; glory be to Allah by the number of what is in the earth and the heaven; glory be to Allah filling what is in the earth and the heaven; glory be to Allah by the number of what His Book has enumerated; glory be to Allah by the number of everything; glory be to Allah filling everything. And you say: praise be to Allah in the same manner.\""],[540,"Two words are light on the tongue, beloved to the Most Merciful, heavy on the scale: 'Glory be to Allah and praise be to Him; glory be to Allah, the Magnificent.'"],[541,"The Prophet ﷺ went out for the dawn prayer while Juwayriyyah was sitting in the mosque, and he returned when the day had advanced and said, 'Have you remained seated since I left?' She said, 'Yes.' He said, 'I have said four words which, if weighed against them, would outweigh them: Glory be to Allah and praise be to Him by the number of His creation, by the ink of His words, by the contentment of Himself, and by the weight of His Throne.'"],[542,"\"Performing ablution thoroughly is half of faith, Al-hamdu lillah fills the scale, tasbih and takbir fill the heavens and the earth, prayer is light, zakah is proof, charity is radiance, and the Qur'an is a proof for you or against you. All people go out in the morning and sell themselves, either freeing themselves or destroying themselves.\""],[543,"I was sitting with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ in a circle when a man came and greeted the Prophet ﷺ and the people, saying, 'As-salamu 'alaykum.' The Prophet ﷺ said, 'Wa 'alaykum as-salam wa rahmat Allah wa barakatuh (And upon you be peace and the mercy of Allah and His blessings).' When he sat down, he said, 'Al-hamdu lillah hamdan kathiran tayyiban mubarakan fihi kama yuhibbu rabbuna wa yarda (Praise be to Allah, much good and blessed praise as our Lord loves and is pleased with).' The Prophet ﷺ said to him, 'What did you say?' He repeated to the Prophet ﷺ what he had said. The Prophet ﷺ said, 'By Him in whose hand is my soul, ten angels raced to it, each eager to write it down, but they did not know how to write it. So they referred it to the Possessor of Might, may His mention be exalted, and He said: Write it as My servant said.'"],[544,"\"The best remembrance is La ilaha illa Allah, and the best supplication is Al-hamdu lillah.\""],[545,"While a man was walking on a road, he found a thorny branch on the path, so he took it, and Allah thanked him and forgave him."],[546,"Whoever says, 'There is no god but Allah alone, with no partner; His is the dominion and His is the praise; He gives life and causes death; and He is over all things powerful' ten times, it is like the reward of freeing a slave or a soul."],[547,"I was walking behind the Prophet ﷺ and he said: 'O Abu Dharr, shall I not direct you to a treasure from the treasures of Paradise?' I said: 'Yes, O Messenger of Allah.' He said: 'There is no might and no power except with Allah.'"],[548,"Abu Ayoub, the companion of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ , narrated to me that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ passed by Prophet Ibrahim, the beloved friend of the Most Merciful, on the night of his Ascension. Ibrahim said to Jibril, \"Who is with you, O Jibril?\" Jibril replied, \"This is Muhammad ﷺ .\" Ibrahim then said, \"O Muhammad, tell your Ummah (nation) to increase the cultivation of Paradise, as its soil is good and its land is spacious.\" The Messenger of Allah ﷺ asked Ibrahim, \"What is the cultivation of Paradise?\" Ibrahim replied, \"There is no power or strength except with Allah.\""],[549,"'Excellent! Excellent!' and he gestured with his hand, holding five fingers: 'How heavy they are on the scale: Glory be to Allah, praise be to Allah, there is no god but Allah, and Allah is greatest; and a righteous child who dies for a Muslim man and he seeks reward for him.'"],[550,"For me to say, 'Glory be to Allah, praise be to Allah, there is no god but Allah, and Allah is greatest' is more beloved to me than all that the sun has risen upon."],[551,"\"The best of speech are four, and it does not matter which of them you begin with: Subhan Allah (Glory be to Allah), Al-hamdu lillah (Praise be to Allah), La ilaha illa Allah (There is no god but Allah), and Allahu akbar (Allah is most great).\""],[552,"\"Increase in the enduring righteous deeds.\" It was said, \"And what are they, O Messenger of Allah?\" He said, \"Takbir, tahlil, tasbih, praise be to Allah, and there is no might nor power except with Allah.\""],[553,"Some people from the companions of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to the Prophet ﷺ, 'O Messenger of Allah, the wealthy have gone with the reward. They pray as we pray, they fast as we fast, and they give charity from the surplus of their wealth.' He ﷺ said, 'Has Allah not given you that which you may give in charity? Every tasbihah is a charity, every takbirah is a charity, every tahmidah is a charity, every tahlilah is a charity, commanding good is a charity, and forbidding evil is a charity.'"],[554,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to us, \"You must do tasbih, tahlil, and taqdis, and count them on your fingers, for they will be questioned and made to speak.\""],[555,"\"I saw the Messenger of Allah ﷺ counting tasbih with his hand.\""],[556,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, “No Muslim man asks Allah for Paradise three times except that Paradise says, ‘O Allah, admit him to Paradise.’ And no Muslim seeks refuge from the Fire three times except that the Fire says, ‘O Allah, grant him refuge from me.’”"],[557,"I said to Ubayy b. Ka'b, 'Ibn Mas'ud does not write the two Mu'awwidhat in his mushaf.' He said, 'The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to me, \"Jibril said to me, {Say: I seek refuge in the Lord of the daybreak}, and I said it, and he said to me, {Say: I seek refuge in the Lord of mankind}, and I said it.\" So we say what the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said.'"],[558,"When he traveled and came at dawn, he would say, “A hearer has heard with the praise of Allah and His good favor. Our Lord, accompany us and bestow favor upon us, seeking refuge in Allah from the Fire.”"],[559,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: 'The master of seeking forgiveness is for the servant to say: \"O Allah, You are my Lord, there is no god but You. You created me, and I am Your servant, upon Your covenant and Your promise as much as I am able. I acknowledge Your favor, and I acknowledge my sin, so forgive me, for none forgives sins but You.\" If he says it after entering the morning, being certain of it, and then dies, he will be among the people of Paradise. And if he says it after entering the evening, being certain of it, he will be among the people of Paradise.'"],[560,"“Among those before you there was a man who killed ninety-nine souls. He asked about the most learned person on earth and was directed to a monk. He came to him and said: He has killed ninety-nine souls—is there any repentance for him? The monk said: No. So he killed him and completed a hundred with him. Then he asked about the most learned person on earth and was directed to a man. He said: He has killed a hundred souls—is there any repentance for him? The man said: Yes, who can stand between you and repentance? Go to such-and-such a land, for there are people there who worship Allah. Worship Allah with them and do not return to your land, for it is an evil land. So he set out until, when he was halfway along the road, death came to him. The angels of mercy and the angels of punishment disputed over him. The angels of mercy said: He came to us repentant, turning his heart to Allah, Mighty and Exalted. The angels of punishment said: He has never done any good at all. An angel came in the form of a human being and they made him judge between them. He said: Measure the distance between the two lands; to whichever he is closer, he belongs to it. So they measured and found him closer to the land he was heading for, and the angels of mercy took him.”"],[561,"“Remorse is repentance?” He said: Yes."],[562,"I said to Anas b. Malik, “Did the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say, ‘Remorse is repentance’?” He said, “Yes.”"],[563,"“My servant committed a sin and said, ‘O Lord, I have sinned.’ He said, ‘My servant committed a sin and knew that Allah forgives sins and takes to account for sins.’ Then he returned and sinned. He said, ‘O Lord, I have sinned.’ He said, ‘My servant sinned and knew that his Lord forgives sin and takes to account for sin. Do as you wish, for I have forgiven you.’”"],[564,"“Indeed, Allah forgives His servant as long as the veil has not fallen.” It was said, “And what is the falling of the veil?” He said, “That the soul dies while it is an associator.”"],[565,"“Indeed, Allah forgives His servant as long as the veil has not fallen.” They said, “O Messenger of Allah, and what is the falling of the veil?” He said, “That the soul dies while it is an associator.”"],[566,"“Indeed, Allah, Blessed and Exalted, accepts the repentance of the servant as long as he has not reached the death rattle.”"],[567,"“Whoever repents before the sun rises from its west, Allah will turn to him.”"],[568,"No fatigue, illness, worry, sorrow, grief, or harm befalls a believer, even a thorn that pricks him, except that Allah expiates some of his sins thereby."],[569,"\"There is no illness or pain that befalls a believer except that it is an expiation for his sin, even a thorn that pricks him or a misfortune that befalls him.\""],[570,"O Messenger of Allah, how can there be well-being after this verse: {Whoever does evil will be recompensed for it}? He said, \"May Allah have mercy on you, O Abu Bakr. Do you not fall ill? Do you not tire? Do you not suffer hardship? That is what you are recompensed for.\""],[571,"If I take away the two precious things of My servant and he is patient and seeks reward, I will not be satisfied with any reward for him less than Paradise.\""],[572,"Ayyub, the Prophet of Allah ﷺ, remained in his affliction for eighteen years. The near and the far shunned him except two men from among his brothers, who were of his closest brothers. They would come to him morning and evening. One of them said to his companion, 'You know, by Allah, Ayyub committed a sin that no one in the worlds has committed.' His companion said, 'What is that?' He said, 'For eighteen years Allah has not shown him mercy and removed his affliction.' When they came to him in the evening, the man could not restrain himself until he mentioned that to him. Ayyub said, 'I do not know what you are saying, but Allah knows that I used to pass by two men disputing and mentioning Allah, and I would return to my house and make expiation for them, disliking that Allah be mentioned except in truth.' He said, 'He used to go out to relieve himself, and when he finished, his wife would take him by the hand. One day he was delayed. Allah revealed to Ayyub in his place, \"Strike with your foot; this is a cool bathing place and a drink.\" She found him late and reached him. He came to her, Allah having removed from him the affliction, and he was in the best condition. When she saw him, she said, 'May Allah bless you. Have you seen the Prophet of Allah, this afflicted one? By Allah, I have seen no one more resembling him than you when he was healthy.' He said, 'I am he.' He had two threshing floors: one for wheat and one for barley. Allah sent two clouds. When one of them was over the wheat floor, it poured gold into it until it overflowed, and the other poured silver onto the barley floor until it overflowed.'"],[573,"No Muslim is pricked by a thorn or anything more than that except that Allah raises him a degree and wipes away a sin thereby."],[574,"Whomever Allah intends good for, He afflicts him."],[575,"A man may have a rank with Allah that he does not attain by deeds, and Allah will keep testing him with what he dislikes until He brings him to it."],[576,"The Prophet ﷺ was struck by pain, and he began to complain and toss on his bed. Aisha said to him, 'If one of us did that, you would be upset with him.' The Prophet ﷺ said, 'The righteous are indeed tested severely. No believer is afflicted by a thorn or something greater but that a sin is removed and a degree raised.'"],[577,"O Messenger of Allah, who are the people most severely tested? He said, \"The prophets, then the next best and the next best. A servant is tested according to his religion. Thus, it does not cease to afflict the servant until he walks upon the earth with no sin upon him.\""],[578,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ was asked, 'Which people have the most severe affliction?' He said, 'The prophets, then the next best, then the next best. People are tested according to their religion. Whoever's religion is firm, his affliction is severe; whoever's religion is weak, his affliction is light. A man may be afflicted until he walks among people with no sin upon him.'"],[579,"Calamity keeps befalling the believing man and woman in body, wealth, and self until they meet Allah with no sin upon them."],[580,"A daughter of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ was dying, so he took her and placed her before him, then he embraced her while she was breathing her last until her soul departed, and he was weeping. Then he laid her down, and Umm Ayman cried out. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, 'Do not weep.' She said, 'Do I not see the Messenger of Allah ﷺ weeping?' He said, 'I weep, but it is only mercy. The believer is in all good: his soul departs from between his sides while he praises Allah.'"],[581,"A man came to the Prophet ﷺ and said, \"By Allah, O Messenger of Allah, I love you.\" The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to him, \"Calamities hasten to the one who loves me faster than a flood to its end.\""],[582,"The world is the believer's prison and the disbeliever's paradise."],[583,"A woman came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ with a touch of madness and said, 'O Messenger of Allah, supplicate Allah to cure me.' He said, 'If you wish, I will supplicate Allah for you and He will cure you, and if you wish, be patient and there will be no reckoning upon you.' She said, 'Rather, I will be patient and there will be no reckoning upon me.'"],[584,"\"No believer, male or female, Muslim, male or female, falls ill except that Allah sheds their sins thereby, just as a leaf falls from a tree.\""],[585,"\"If I seize the two precious things of My servant while he is attached to them, and he praises Me for them, I will not be satisfied with any reward for him less than Paradise.\""],[586,"\"Allah does not take away the two beloved things of a servant and he is patient and seeks reward except that Allah will admit him to Paradise.\""],[587,"Fever came to the Prophet ﷺ and sought permission to enter upon him. He said, 'Who are you?' It said, 'I am Umm Mildam.' He said, 'Go to Quba and come to them.' It went to them and they became feverish, or they experienced severity from it. They said, 'O Messenger of Allah, do you not see what we have encountered from the fever?' He said, 'If you wish, I will supplicate to Allah and He will remove it from you, and if you wish, it will be a purification.' They said, 'Rather, let it be a purification.'"],[588,"A man among the Muslims said, \"O Messenger of Allah, what is our reward for these illnesses that afflict us?\" He said, \"They are expiations.\" He said, \"O Messenger of Allah, even if they are few?\" He said, \"Even a thorn or anything above it.\" He said, \"Then he called upon himself that fever would not leave him until he died, and that it would not distract him from Hajj, Umrah, jihad in the path of Allah, or prescribed prayer in congregation.\" He said, \"No person touched his body except that he found its heat, until he died.\""],[589,"When the believer falls ill, that purifies him just as the bellows removes the dross of iron."],[590,"I entered upon the Prophet ﷺ and touched him, and I said, 'O Messenger of Allah, you are suffering a severe fever.' He said, 'Yes, I suffer fever as much as two men of you.' I said, 'You will have two rewards.' The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, 'Yes.' Then the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, 'By the One in Whose hand is my soul, there is no Muslim on earth afflicted with harm from illness or anything else but that Allah removes his sins from him just as a tree sheds its leaves.'"],[591,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ entered upon Umm al-Sa'ib or Umm al-Musayyab while she was shivering. He said, 'What is the matter with you, O Umm al-Sa'ib or O Umm al-Musayyab, that you are shivering?' She said, 'The fever, may Allah not bless it.' He ﷺ said, 'Do not revile the fever, for it removes the sins of the son of Adam just as the bellows removes the dross of iron.'"],[592,"\"When a person travels or falls ill, Allah records for him the like of what he used to do when he was resident and healthy.\""],[593,"the Messenger of Allāh ﷺ said, \"[How] wondrous is the affair of a believer: for there is good in every affair of his, while that is not the case with anyone else except in the case of a believer: [i.e.,] if times of ease strike him, he is grateful which is good for him; and if times of distress strike him, he is patient, which is [also] good for him.\" (Using translation from Muslim 2999)"],[595,"They both learned that a man died of a stomach ailment, so one of them said, 'Has it not reached you that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, \"Whoever is killed by his stomach will not be punished in his grave\"?'"],[596,"'Amr b. Hurayth visited al-Hasan b. 'Ali, and 'Ali b. Abi Talib said to him, \"O 'Amr, do you visit Hasan while there is in the soul what there is?\" He said, \"Yes, O 'Ali, you are not the lord of my heart to turn it wherever you wish.\" 'Ali said, \"Indeed, that does not prevent me from giving you sincere advice. I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: 'There is no Muslim person who visits a Muslim person except that Allah dispatches seventy thousand angels who pray for him in whatever hours of the day it is, until evening, and in whatever hours of the night it is, until morning.'\""],[597,"\"Whoever visits a sick person continues to wade through mercy until he sits down; and when he sits down, he is immersed in it.\""],[598,"\"When a Muslim visits his sick Muslim brother, he remains in the harvest of Paradise until he returns.\""],[599,"'There is no Muslim who dies and four households of his closest neighbors testify that they know nothing but good of him except that God, Majestic and Exalted, says, \"I have accepted your knowledge of him and have forgiven him for what you do not know.\"'"],[600,"«Whoever attends the funeral until the prayer is offered over it will have a qirat, and whoever attends it until it is buried will have two qirats.» It was said: O Messenger of God, what are two qirats? He said: «Like two great mountains.»"],[601,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ heard saying: \"Whoever follows a funeral from the house until they pray over it, and then follows it until it is buried, will have two Qirats, with each Qirat similar to the size of Mount Uhud. And whoever goes back after praying over it and does not follow it, will have one Qirat similar to the size of Mount Uhud.\""],[602,"«Whoever follows the funeral of a Muslim out of faith and seeking reward until he prays over it, then sits until it is placed in its grave, will return with two qirats of reward, each like Uhud. Whoever prays over it and then returns before it is placed in the grave will have one qirat.»"],[603,"«There is no one who dies and a group of Muslims reaching one hundred pray over him and intercede for him except that their intercession is accepted for him.»"],[604,"A son of his died at Qudayd or at 'Usfan, and he said: O Kurayb, see how many people have gathered for him. He said: I went out and found that people had gathered, and I informed him. He said: Are they forty? I said: Yes. He said: Take him out, for I heard the Messenger of God ﷺ say: «There is no Muslim who dies and forty men who do not associate anything with God stand over his funeral except that God grants them intercession for him.»"],[605,"A funeral was brought past the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and it was praised with good qualities of virtue. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, “It is affirmed. You are Allah’s witnesses on the earth.”"],[606,"I came to Madinah when a disease had struck it, and people were dying rapidly. I sat with Umar b. al-Khattab, and a funeral procession passed by him and its owner was praised with good, so Umar said, 'It has become incumbent.' Then another was brought and its owner was spoken of with evil, so Umar said, 'It has become incumbent.' Abu al-Aswad said, 'What has become incumbent, O Commander of the Believers?' He said, 'As the Messenger of God ﷺ said, \"Any Muslim for whom four people testify to good, God will surely admit him to Paradise.\"' He said, 'We said, \"And three?\" He said, \"And three.\"' He said, 'Then we said, \"And two?\" He said, \"And two.\" And we did not ask him about one.'"],[607,"No Muslim has three children die but that the Fire will not touch him except for the fulfillment of the oath."],[608,"Whoever seeks reward for three of his own offspring will enter Paradise."],[609,"The women said, 'The men have overtaken you, O Messenger of Allah, so appoint for us a day.' He promised them a day, and they came. He admonished them, and among what he said to them was: 'There is no woman among you who sends forth three of her children but that they will be a screen for her from the Fire.' A woman said, 'O Messenger of Allah, and two?' Two of hers had died. The Prophet ﷺ said to her, 'And two.'"],[610,"\"There is no man whose two daughters reach the age of puberty and he treats them kindly for the time they are together, but they will gain him admittance to Paradise.\" (Using translation from Ibn Mājah 3670)"],[611,"I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say, \"Whoever has three children and they pass away, will enter paradise.\" They asked, \"O Messenger of Allah, what about two sons?\" He replied, \"And two sons.\""],[612,"A man used to frequent the Prophet ﷺ with a young son of his, and the Prophet ﷺ missed him. They said, \"He died, O Messenger of Allah.\" So the Prophet ﷺ said to his father, \"Would it not please you that you will not come to any gate of the gates of Paradise except that you find him waiting for you?\""],[613,"I buried my son while Abu Talha al-Khawlani was with me at the edge of the grave. When I wanted to leave, he took my hand and brought me out, saying, \"Shall I give you glad tidings? Al-Dahhak b. 'Abd al-Rahman b. 'Arzab narrated to me from Abu Musa al-Ash'ari that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: 'When the child of a believing servant dies, Allah says to the angels: You have taken the child of My servant?' They say: 'Yes.'\""],[614,"A woman entered upon her with her two daughters begging for food. She said, 'I found nothing but a single date, so I gave it to her. She took it and split it between her two daughters and did not eat any of it herself.' She said, 'Then she got up and left, and the Messenger of Allah ﷺ entered upon me, so I told him her story.' He ﷺ said, 'Whoever is tried with any of these daughters and treats them well, they will be a screen for him from the Fire.'"],[615,"I came to Abu Dharr at al-Rabadha and said, 'O Abu Dharr, what is your wealth?' He said, 'My wealth is my deeds.' I said, 'Narrate to us a hadith from the Messenger of Allah ﷺ that you heard from him.' He said, 'I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say, \"There are no two Muslims who have three children die before reaching puberty but that Allah admits them to Paradise by the virtue of His mercy toward them.\"'"],[616,"Some women of the Ansar said to him, 'O Messenger of Allah, we cannot come to you with the men.' The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, 'Your appointment is at the house of so-and-so.' He came and spoke with them, then said, 'If any one of you has three children die and she seeks reward for that, she will enter Paradise.' A woman among them said, 'And two, O Messenger of Allah?' He said, 'And two.'"],[617,"the Messenger of Allah said: \"Whoever has three daughters, or three sisters, or two daughters, or two sisters and he keeps good company with them and fears Allah regarding them, then Paradise is for him. (Using translation from Tirmidhī 1916)"],[618,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Whoever provides for two daughters, or two sisters, or three, or two sisters, or three, until they become independent or he dies leaving them, he and I will be in Paradise like these two,” and he gestured with his middle finger and the one next to it."],[619,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “I and the one who sponsors an orphan will be in Paradise like this,” and he indicated with his index and middle fingers."],[620,"\"The one who strives for the widow and the poor is like the one who strives in the way of Allah.\" And I think he said: \"Like the one who fasts without breaking it, and like the one who stands in prayer without sleeping.\""],[621,"“If a woman prays her five prayers, fasts her month, guards her private part, and obeys her husband, she will enter from any gate of Paradise she wishes.”"],[622,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ entered a garden from among the gardens of the Ansar, and there were two camels in it that were fighting and bellowing. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ drew near to them, and they placed their necks on the ground. Those with him said: They have prostrated to him. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: It is not appropriate for anyone to prostrate to anyone. If it were appropriate for anyone to prostrate to anyone, I would have commanded the woman to prostrate to her husband because of the greatness of the right Allah has placed upon her for him."],[623,"When Mu‘adh b. Jabal came from Syria, he prostrated to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, “What is this?” He said, “O Messenger of Allah, I came to Syria and saw them prostrating to their patricians and bishops, so I wanted to do that for you.” He said, “Do not do it. If I were to command anything to prostrate to anything, I would command a woman to prostrate to her husband. By the One in Whose hand is my soul, a woman does not fulfill the right of her Lord until she fulfills the right of her husband, such that if he were to ask her for herself while she is on a camel saddle, she would not refuse him.”"],[624,"A man came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ with a daughter of his and said: O Messenger of Allah, this is my daughter; she refuses to marry. The Prophet ﷺ said to her: “Obey your father.” She said: By the One who sent you with the truth, I will not marry until you tell me what the right of the husband is over his wife. The Prophet ﷺ said: “The right of the husband over his wife is that if there were a sore on him and she licked it, she would not have fulfilled his right.” She said: By the One who sent you with the truth, I will never marry. The Prophet ﷺ said: “Do not marry them except with the permission of their families.”"],[625,"“When a Muslim spends on his family, it is charity for him.”"],[626,"“When a man spends on his family while seeking reward for it, it is charity for him.”"],[627,"ʿUthmān b. ʿAffān or ʿAbd al-Raḥmān b. ʿAwf passed by a woollen cloak and found it too expensive. Then ʿAmr b. Umayyah passed by it and bought it, and clothed his wife Sukhaylah bt. ʿUbaydah b. al-Ḥārith b. al-Muṭṭalib with it. Then ʿUthmān or ʿAbd al-Raḥmān passed by him and said: What happened to the cloak you bought? ʿAmr said: I gave it in charity to Sukhaylah bt. ʿUbaydah b. al-Ḥārith. He said: Is everything you do for your family charity? ʿAmr said: I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say that. What ʿAmr said was mentioned to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and he ﷺ said: “ʿAmr has spoken the truth. Whatever you do for your family is charity for them.”"],[628,"On the authority of Raytah, the wife of 'Abd Allah b. Mas'ud and mother of his child, who was a skilled craftswoman. 'Abd Allah b. Mas'ud had no wealth, and she used to spend on him and his child from the proceeds of her craft. She said: By Allah, you and your child have preoccupied me from charity, so I am not able to give charity along with you. He said: I would not like you to do it if there is no reward for you in that. So he and she asked the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. She said: O Messenger of Allah, I am a woman with a craft from which I sell, and I have nothing, nor does my husband, nor does my child, and they preoccupied me, so I do not give charity. Do I have any reward in spending on them? He said: \"You have a reward in that for what you spend on them, so spend on them.\""],[629,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ addressed us and said: \"O assembly of women, give charity even from your jewelry, for you will be the majority of the inhabitants of Hell on the Day of Resurrection.\" She said: 'Abd Allah was a man of light means, so she said: Ask the Messenger of Allah ﷺ for me whether spending on my husband and orphans in my care would suffice me as charity. She said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ had been invested with awe, so he said: No, you ask him yourself. She said: So I went, and at the door was a woman from the Ansar whose need was the same as mine, her name was Zaynab. She said: Bilal came out to us, so I said to him: Ask the Messenger of Allah ﷺ for us whether spending on our husbands and orphans in our care would suffice us as charity. She said: Bilal entered and said: O Messenger of Allah, at the door are Zaynab—the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"Which Zaynab?\" He said: Zaynab the wife of 'Abd Allah, and Zaynab a woman from the Ansar, both asking about spending on their husbands and orphans in their care, whether that would suffice them as charity. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"Yes, they have two rewards: the reward of kinship and the reward of charity.\""],[630,"I fell ill in Makkah in the year of the conquest with an illness that brought me close to death. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ visited me, so I said to him: O Messenger of Allah, I have abundant wealth and no one inherits from me except my daughter. Shall I bequeath two-thirds of my wealth? He said: \"No.\" I said: Half? He said: \"No.\" I said: A third? He said: \"A third, and a third is much. If you leave your heirs wealthy, it is better than leaving them poor, begging from people. You will never spend an expenditure seeking thereby the face of Allah except that you will be rewarded for it, even the morsel you raise to your wife's mouth.\" I said: O Messenger of Allah, will I be left behind after my emigration? He said: \"You will not be left behind after me and then do a deed seeking thereby the face of Allah except that you will increase in elevation and degree. Perhaps you will be left behind after me until some people benefit by you and others are harmed by you. O Allah, carry out for my companions their emigration and do not turn them back on their heels. But the unfortunate one is Sa'd b. Khawlah—the Messenger of Allah ﷺ grieved for him because he died in Makkah.\""],[631,"Three persons are all guaranteed by Allah: if he lives, he is provided for and sufficed, and if he dies, Allah will admit him to Paradise. One who enters his house and gives the greeting of peace is guaranteed by Allah; one who goes out to the mosque is guaranteed by Allah; and one who goes out in the path of Allah is guaranteed by Allah."],[632,"Whatever you lighten from your servant's work, it will be a reward for you in your scales."],[633,"“In the private relations of one of you there is charity.” They said: O Messenger of Allah, if one of us fulfills his desire, will he have a reward for it? He said: “Do you think that if he were to put it in what is forbidden, there would be a sin upon him? Likewise, if he puts it in what is lawful, there is a reward for him.”"],[634,"“The most complete of the believers in faith are those with the best character, and the best of you are those who are best to their wives.”"],[635,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “The best of you is the one who is best to his family, and I am the best of you to my family; and when your companion dies, then leave him.”"],[636,"“Any man who earns wealth from lawful means and feeds himself or clothes himself, or anyone below him among Allah’s creation, it is purification for him.”"],[637,"I was walking with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ on the lava field of Madinah in the evening, and Uhud met us. He said, \"O Abu Dharr, I would not love to have Uhud in gold and spend a third night while I have a dinar of it, except a dinar which I set aside for a debt — unless I say about it regarding the servants of Allah like this and like this,\" meaning from in front of him, behind him, to his right, and to his left. Then he said, \"O Abu Dharr, indeed the wealthy are the fewest on the Day of Resurrection.\" Then he said to me, \"Do not leave until I come to you.\" He went off, then came in the darkness of night, and I heard a sound. I feared it might be harm to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, so I intended to leave. Then I remembered his words, so I sat until he came. I said to him, \"I wanted to come to you, O Messenger of Allah, then I remembered your words to me, and I heard a sound.\" He said, \"That was Jibril. He came to me and informed me that whoever of my community dies without associating anything with Allah will enter Paradise.\" I said, \"Even if he commits adultery and steals?\" He said, \"Even if he commits adultery and steals.\""],[638,"I came to the Prophet ﷺ while he was reciting: \"Competition for more distracts you\" (al-Takathur, 102:1). He said, \"The son of Adam says, 'My wealth, my wealth' but do you have any of your wealth except what you ate and consumed, or wore and wore out, or gave in charity and sent ahead?\""],[639,"Al-Aswad b. Yazid used to borrow from a merchant, and when his stipend came out he would pay him back. Al-Aswad said, 'If you wish I will delay it on your behalf, for we have claims in this stipend.' The merchant said to him, 'You will not do that.' Then al-Aswad gave him five hundred dirhams in cash. When he received it, the merchant said to him, 'Here it is, take it.' Al-Aswad said to him, 'I asked you for this and you refused.' The merchant said, 'I heard you narrate to us from Abd Allah b. Mas'ud that the Prophet of Allah ﷺ used to say, \"Whoever lends to Allah twice, he will have the like of the reward of one of them had he given it as charity.\"'"],[640,"I was sitting in Ariha when Wathila b. al-Asqapassed by me, leaning onAbd Allah b. al-Daylami. He seated him, then came to me and said, 'I wondered about...'"],[641,"Whoever frees a believing slave, Allah will free from the Fire a limb of his for every limb of the slave."],[642,"We besieged al-Ta'if with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: 'Any Muslim man who frees a Muslim man, Allah, Mighty and Exalted, will make each bone of the freed man's bones a shield for his bones from the Fire; and any Muslim woman who frees a Muslim woman, Allah, Mighty and Exalted, will make each bone of the freed woman's bones a shield for her bones from the Fire.'"],[643,"I said, 'O Prophet of Allah, which deed is best?' He said, 'Faith in Allah and jihad in His path.' He said, 'I said, which slaves are best, O Prophet of Allah?' He said, 'The most precious to their owners and the highest in price.' He said, 'I said, what if I do not do that?' He said, 'You help a weak person or make something for an unskilled person.' He said, 'I said, what if I am too weak?' He said, 'Refrain from harming people, for it is charity from you to yourself.'"],[644,"“There was a merchant who used to lend to people, and when he saw the insolvency of an insolvent person,” he would say to his servant, “Overlook it, perhaps Allah will overlook us.” The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, “So he met Allah, and He overlooked him.”"],[645,"The Prophet ﷺ said: A man never did a good deed but removed a thorny branch from the road; it was either in the tree and someone cut it and threw it on the road, or it was lying in it, he removed it. Allah accepted this good deed of his and brought him into Paradise. (Using translation from Abū Dāʾūd 5245)"],[646,"I and my father went out seeking knowledge among this tribe of the Ansar before they perished. The first person we met was Abu al-Yasar, the Companion of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and with him was a servant of his. On Abu al-Yasar was a burdah and a Ma'afiri garment, and on his servant was a burdah and a Ma'afiri garment. My father said to him, 'I see in your face something of anger.' He said, 'Yes, I had money owed to me by so-and-so son of so-and-so al-Harami. I came to his family and said, \"Is he there?\" They said, \"No.\" Then a son of his came out to me, and I said, \"Where is your father?\" He said, \"He heard your voice and went inside.\" I said, \"Come out to me, for I know where you are.\" So he came out to me, and I said, \"What made you hide?\" He said, \"By Allah, I will tell you and then not lie to you. I feared, by Allah, that if I spoke to you I would lie to you, and if I promised you I would break my promise. You are a Companion of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and I was, by Allah, insolvent.\" I said, \"By Allah?\" He said, \"By Allah.\" I said, \"By Allah?\" He said, \"By Allah.\" Then he took his document and erased it, and said, \"If you find a way to pay, then pay; otherwise, you are released.\" I bear witness—my two eyes saw this and my heart understood it, and he pointed to the aorta of his heart—I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say, \"Whoever grants respite to an insolvent person or remits for him, Allah will shade him in His shade.\""],[647,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"May Allah have mercy on a servant who is easygoing when he sells, easygoing when he buys, easygoing when he demands payment, and easygoing when he pays.\""],[648,"Whoever is easy with (a debtor) who is in difficulty, Allah will be easy with him in this world and in the Hereafter.” (Using translation from Ibn Mājah 2417)"],[649,"'Whoever conceals his Muslim brother, Allah will conceal him in this world and the Hereafter; and whoever relieves a Muslim of a distress, Allah will relieve him of a distress from the distresses of the Day of Resurrection; and Allah is in the aid of the servant as long as the servant is in the aid of his brother.'"],[650,"'The Muslim is the brother of the Muslim: he does not wrong him nor does he hand him over. Whoever is in the need of his brother, Allah is in his need; and whoever relieves a Muslim of a distress, Allah will relieve him of a distress from the distresses of the Day of Resurrection; and whoever conceals a Muslim, Allah will conceal him on the Day of Resurrection.'"],[651,"'Whoever is a means for his Muslim brother to reach one in authority in the amount of a kindness or the easing of a hardship, Allah will grant him passage over the bridge on the Day of Resurrection when feet slip.'"],[652,"“Whoever releases a Muslim from his stumble, Allah will release his stumble on the Day of Resurrection.”"],[653,"“Whoever releases a remorseful person from his sale, Allah will release his stumble on the Day of Resurrection.”"],[654,"“Treating people with kindness is charity.”"],[655,"“Every joint of a person has charity due from him every day the sun rises: judging justly between two people is charity, helping a man with his mount and lifting him onto it or raising his belongings onto it for him is charity, and removing harm from the road is charity.”"],[656,"Whoever revives dead land, he has a reward in it, and whatever the grazing animals eat from it is charity for him."],[657,"I said, 'O Messenger of Allah, which charity is best?' He ﷺ said, 'Giving water to drink.'"],[658,"O Messenger of Allah, a stray animal comes to my watering trough; is there a reward for me if I give it water? He said, 'Give it water, for in every living, thirsty creature there is a reward.'"],[659,"A man approached a well and went down and drank from it. There was a dog on the well panting, and he had mercy on it, so he removed one of his leather socks, scooped for it, and gave it water. Allah thanked him and admitted him to Paradise."],[660,"“Shall I not tell you who are the best among you?” They said: “Yes, O Messenger of Allah.” He said: “The best among you are those who live longest and have the best deeds.”"],[661,"Two men from Bali came to the Prophet ﷺ, and their Islam was together as one. One of them was more diligent in worship than the other. The diligent one went on a military campaign and was martyred. The other lived for a year until he fasted Ramadan, then died. Talhah b. Ubayd Allah saw a person coming out of Paradise. He gave permission to the one who died last of the two; then he came out again and gave permission to the one who was martyred; then he returned to Talhah and said: “Go back, for your time has not yet come.” In the morning, Talhah began telling the people about it. That reached the Prophet ﷺ, so they related the account to him and were amazed. They said: “O Messenger of Allah, the first of the two men was more diligent in worship and was martyred in the path of Allah, yet this one entered Paradise before him.” The Prophet ﷺ said: “Did this one not remain after him for a year?” They said: “Yes.”"],[662,"I heard the Prophet ﷺ say three days before his death: “Whoever among you is able not to die except while his thought of Allah is good, let him do so.”"],[663,"I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say, from Allah, Majestic and Exalted, who said: “I am with My servant’s thought of Me, so let him think of Me as he wishes.”"],[664,"From the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, he said: “Indeed Allah, Mighty and Majestic, says: I am as My servant thinks of Me. If he thinks good, then for him is good; and if he thinks evil, then for him is evil.”"],[665,"“By My might, I will not combine for My servant two fears or two securities: if he fears Me in this world, I will make him secure on the Day of Resurrection; and if he feels secure from Me in this world, I will make him fear on the Day of Resurrection.”"],[666,"“Good thoughts are from the goodness of worship.”"],[667,"“No Muslim man dies except that Allah enters the Fire in his place a Jew or a Christian.”"],[668,"When My servant intends a good deed but does not do it, I write it for him as a good deed. If he does it, I write it for him as ten good deeds. And if My servant intends an evil deed but does not do it, I do not write it against him. If he does it, I write it as one."],[669,"On the authority of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, from Allah, Mighty and Exalted, who said: \"Whoever intends a good deed but does not do it, I write for him a good deed. If he does it, I write it as ten times its like up to seven hundred. And whoever intends an evil deed but does not do it, I do not write it against him. If he does it, I write it against him as one evil deed.\""],[670,"When My servant intends an evil deed but does not do it, write it for him as a good deed. If he does it, write it for him as an evil deed. If he repents from it, erase it from him. And when My servant intends a good deed but does not do it, write it for him as a good deed. If he does it, write it for him as ten times its like up to seven hundred fold."],[671,"A man said: \"O Messenger of Allah, a man does a deed and keeps it secret, but when it is discovered, he is pleased?\" He said: \"He has two rewards: the reward of the secret and the reward of the public.\""],[672,"\"Indeed, when Allah loves a servant, He calls Jibril: 'I have loved so-and-so, so love him.' He said: Then Jibril says to the inhabitants of heaven: 'Your Lord has loved so-and-so, so love him.' Then the inhabitants of heaven love him. He said: And acceptance is placed for him on earth. And when He hates a servant, it is similar to that.\""],[673,"Abu Dhar said, \"O Messenger of Allah, a man works for himself and people love him?\" He (the Prophet) said, \"That is the glad tidings of a believer.\""],[674,"\"Indeed, when Allah loves a servant, He praises him with seven times the good he has not done; and when He is displeased with a servant, He criticizes him with seven times the evil he has not done.\""],[675,"A man died, and they brought his funeral procession past the Prophet ﷺ, and they praised him with evil, so the Prophet ﷺ said, 'It has become incumbent.' And they brought another, and they praised her with good, so the Prophet ﷺ said, 'It has become incumbent.' Umar asked him about that, so he said, 'You are the witnesses of God on earth.'"],[676,"It was said to Messenger of Allah ﷺ: What is your opinion about the person who has done good deeds and the people praise him? He said: It is glad tidings for a believer (which he has received in this mortal world). (Using translation from Muslim 2642a)"],[677,"None of you believes in Allah until he loves for his brother what he loves for himself."],[678,"A servant does not attain the reality of faith until he loves for people the good that he loves for himself."],[679,"Three things: whoever has them finds the sweetness of faith — for Allah and His Messenger to be more beloved to him than anything besides them; for a man to love a people, loving them only for Allah's sake; and for a man to prefer being thrown into the Fire over returning to Judaism or Christianity."],[680,"A man came to the Prophet ﷺ and said in a loud voice, 'O Muḥammad.' We said, 'Woe to you, lower your voice, for you have been forbidden from this.' He said, 'No, by Allah, not until he hears me.' The Prophet ﷺ beckoned with his hand and said, 'Here I am.' He said, 'What do you think of a man who loves a people but has not yet caught up with them?' He said, 'That is with the one he loves.'"],[681,"A man said: O Messenger of Allah, when is the Hour? He said: \"What have you prepared for it?\" He said: I love Allah and His Messenger. He said: \"You will be with the one you love.\""],[682,"A man said: O Prophet of Allah, when is the Hour? He said: \"Indeed it is coming, so what have you prepared for it?\" He said: I have not prepared for it much action except that I love Allah and His Messenger. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"You will be with the one you love, and you will have what you have hoped for.\""],[683,"\"No two people love each other for Allah's sake except the better of them is the one who has greater love for his companion.\""],[684,"\"The example of a good companion is that of a perfume seller: even if you do not get any from him, his fragrance reaches you. And the example of a bad companion is that of a blacksmith: even if his sparks do not burn you, some of his smell clings to you.\""],[685,"While I was sitting with the Prophet ﷺ, a man came and greeted him, then turned away. I said: O Messenger of Allah, I love this man for Allah's sake. He said: \"Have you informed him of that?\" I said: No. He said: \"Then inform your brother.\" So I followed him and caught up with him, grabbed his shoulder, greeted him, and said: By Allah, I love you for Allah's sake. He said: By Allah, I love you for Allah's sake. I said: If the Prophet ﷺ had not commanded me to inform you, I would not have done so."],[686,"I was sitting with the Prophet ﷺ when a man passed by. A man from the group said: O Messenger of Allah, I love this man. He said: \"Have you informed him of that?\" He said: No. He said: \"Stand and inform him.\" So he stood and went to him and said: O you, by Allah, I love you. He said: May the one for whose sake you love me love you."],[687,"\"Where are those who love one another for My glory? Today I will shade them in My shade on a day when there is no shade but My shade.\""],[688,"\"A man visited a brother of his in another village. Allah sent an angel to wait for him on his path. When he came to him, the angel said: Where do you intend to go? He said: I intend to visit a brother of mine in this village. The angel said: Does he owe you any favor that you seek? He said: No, except that I love him for Allah's sake. The angel said: I am Allah's messenger to you: Allah, Mighty and Majestic, has loved you as you loved him for His sake.\""],[689,"\"Among Allah's servants are servants who are not prophets, yet the prophets and martyrs envy them. It was said: Who are they, perhaps we may love them? He said: They are a people who love one another by Allah's light, without kinship or lineage. Their faces are light, upon pulpits of light. They do not fear when people fear, and they do not grieve when people grieve.\" Then he recited: {Verily, the friends of Allah have no fear, nor do they grieve.}"],[690,"I entered the mosque of Damascus, and there was a young man with gleaming front teeth, and the people were with him; when they differed about something, they referred it to him and accepted his opinion. I asked about him and was told: This is Mu'adh b. Jabal. The next day I went early (to the mosque), and I found that he had preceded me in going early, and I found him praying. He said: So I waited for him until he finished his prayer, then I came to him from before his face, greeted him, and said: By Allah, I love you for the sake of Allah. He said: By Allah? I said: By Allah. So he took hold of the gathered end of my cloak, pulled me towards him, and said: Rejoice, for I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: \"Allah, Blessed and Exalted, said: My love is due to those who love one another for My sake, sit together for My sake, and visit one another for My sake.\""],[691,"\"That I should be afflicted by it, nor any relationship between me and you.\" He said, \"For what reason?\" I said, \"For the sake of Allah.\" He said, \"Then He would draw my shoulder [closer to him] and say, 'Rejoice! If you are truthful, then I have heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say, 'Those who love one another for the sake of Allah will be in the shade of the Throne on the Day when there will be no shade except His shade. The prophets and martyrs will envy them for their position.'\" Then he said, \"So I went out and came to 'Ubada bin As-Samit and told him about the hadith of Mu'adh. 'Ubada bin As-Samit said, 'I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say, 'My love is guaranteed for those who love one another for my sake, for those who advise one another for my sake, for those who visit one another for my sake, and for those who spend on one another for my sake, while they are upon pulpits of light. The prophets and the truthful ones will envy them for their position.'\""],[692,"By the One in Whose hand is my soul, you will not enter Paradise until you believe, and you will not believe until you love one another. Shall I not guide you to something that, if you do it, you will love one another? Spread salam among yourselves."],[693,"The Prophet ﷺ said, \"When a Muslim visits his brother Muslim, or visits him, Allah the Almighty says, 'You have done well and behaved righteously. May your footsteps be blessed, and your place in Paradise be prepared.'\""],[694,"“Do not belittle any good deed. If you cannot find anything, then meet people with a cheerful face.”"],[695,"«Your smiling in the face of your brother is charity.»"],[696,"Do not deem any good deed insignificant, even if it is meeting your brother with a cheerful face. When you make broth, increase its water and ladle some of it for your neighbors."],[697,"“A good word is charity, and every step you take to the mosque is charity.”"],[698,"'Your smiling in the face of your brother is charity for you, and your commanding good and forbidding evil is charity, and your guiding a man in the land of error is charity for you, and your seeing for a man with bad eyesight is charity for you, and your removing a stone, thorn, or bone from the road is charity for you, and your pouring from your bucket into your brother's bucket is charity for you.'"],[699,"I said to 'Uqbah b. 'Amir, 'We have neighbors who drink wine, and I am going to call the police to seize them.' 'Uqbah said, 'Woe to you! Do not do that. Rather, admonish them and warn them.' He said, 'I forbade them but they did not stop, and I am going to call the police to seize them.' 'Uqbah said, 'Woe to you! Do not do that, for I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: \"Whoever conceals the fault of a believer, it is as if he brought back to life a girl buried alive in her grave.\"'"],[700,"We were with the Prophet ﷺ when a messenger from one of his daughters came and said: “O Messenger of Allah, your daughter sends word that you come to her, for a child of hers is dying.” He said: “Go to her and tell her: ‘To Allah belongs what He takes, and to Him belongs what He gives, and everything with Him has an appointed term. So let her be patient and seek reward.’” He said: It was not long before he returned and said, “O Messenger of Allah, she implores you to come to her.” So the Messenger of Allah ﷺ stood up, and a group of the Ansar stood with him. We entered, and the child was brought to him; his soul was rattling in his chest, and his eyes overflowed. Sa‘d b. ‘Ubadah said to him, “What is this, O Messenger of Allah?” He said: “It is mercy that Allah has placed in the hearts of His servants. Indeed, Allah shows mercy to those of His servants who are merciful.”"],[701,"“Mercy is not removed except from a wretched person.”"],[702,"“The Fire is forbidden only for every gentle, lenient, approachable, and easy-going person.”"],[703,"“Shall I tell you for whom the Fire is forbidden?” They said, “Yes, O Messenger of Allah.” He said: “For every gentle, lenient, approachable, and easy-going person.”"],[704,"“The likeness of the believer is the likeness of the bee: it does not eat except what is good, and it does not put except what is good.”"],[705,"The emigrant is one who abandons evil deeds, and the Muslim is one from whose tongue and hand the Muslims are safe."],[706,"The most complete of the Muslims in Islam is one from whose tongue and hand the Muslims are safe."],[707,"'Shall I inform you of the best of you from the worst of you?' A man said: Yes, O Messenger of Allah. He said: 'The best of you is the one whose good is hoped for and whose evil is safe, and the worst of you is the one whose good is not hoped for and whose evil is not safe.'"],[708,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ came out to them while they were sitting in a gathering and said: “Shall I inform you of the best of people in station?” We said: Yes, O Messenger of Allah. He said: “A man holding the head of his horse in the cause of Allah until it is hamstrung or he is killed. Shall I inform you of the one who comes after him?” We said: Yes, O Messenger of Allah. He said: “A man who secludes himself in a mountain pass, establishing prayer and giving zakah, and keeping away from the evils of people. Shall I inform you of the worst of people?” We said: Yes, O Messenger of Allah. He said: “The one who is asked by Allah and does not give by Him.”"],[709,"“A man will continue to be truthful and to seek out truthfulness until he is written with Allah as a truthful one (ṣiddīq), and a man will continue to lie and to seek out lying until he is written with Allah as a liar.”"],[710,"“Indeed, truthfulness guides to righteousness, and righteousness guides to Paradise. A man will continue to be truthful until he is written with Allah as a truthful one (ṣiddīq). And indeed, lying guides to wickedness, and wickedness guides to the Fire. A man will continue to lie until he is written with Allah as a liar.”"],[711,"I said: O Messenger of Allah, tell me something I can hold fast to. He said, \"Say: My Lord is Allah, then remain upright.\" I said, O Messenger of Allah, what is the most frightening thing you fear for me? He took hold of his own tongue and said, \"This.\""],[712,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ came out to us while we were nine—five and four—one of the two groups was from the Arabs and the other from the non-Arabs. He said: “Listen, or have you heard? Indeed, there will be rulers after me. Whoever enters upon them and confirms their lies and helps them in their wrongdoing is not of me, and I am not of him, and he will not come to me at the Basin. And whoever does not confirm their lies and does not help them in their wrongdoing is of me, and I am of him, and he will come to me at the Basin.”"],[713,"A man from the people of Madinah who had nobility passed by him while he was sitting in the market of Madinah. Then ʿAlqamah said: “O so-and-so, you have sanctity and you have a right. I have seen you entering upon these rulers and speaking before them. I heard Bilāl b. al-Ḥārith al-Muzanī, the Companion of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, say: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: ‘Indeed, one of you speaks a word that is pleasing to Allah, not expecting it to reach what it reaches, and Allah writes for him His pleasure until the day he meets Him. And indeed, one of you speaks a word that is displeasing to Allah, not expecting it to reach what it reaches, and Allah writes for him His displeasure until the Day of Resurrection.’”"],[714,"“Modesty is from faith, and faith is in Paradise; and obscenity is from harshness, and harshness is in the Fire.”"],[715,"I said, 'O Messenger of Allah, what will protect me from Allah's anger?' He said, 'Do not become angry.'"],[716,"“Whoever seeks the pleasure of Allah by the displeasure of people ؓ, Allah will be pleased with him and will make people pleased with him. And whoever seeks the pleasure of people by the displeasure of Allah, Allah will be displeased with him and will make people displeased with him.*”"],[717,"«The just ones on the Day of Resurrection will be on pulpits of light at the right hand of the Most Merciful — and both His hands are right: those who are just in their rulings, their families, and whatever they are given authority over.»"],[718,"The Prophet ﷺ said, \"Seven people will be shaded by Allah under His shade on the day when there will be no shade except His. They are: (1) a just ruler; (2) a young man who has been brought up in the worship of Allah, (i.e. worship Allah (Alone) sincerely from his childhood), (3) a man whose heart is attached to the mosque (who offers the five compulsory congregational prayers in the mosque); (4) two persons who love each other only for Allah's sake and they meet and part in Allah's cause only; (5) a man who refuses the call of a charming woman of noble birth for an illegal sexual intercourse with her and says: I am afraid of Allah; (6) a person who practices charity so secretly that his left hand does not know what his right hand has given (i.e. nobody knows how much he has given in charity). (7) a person who remembers Allah in seclusion and his eyes get flooded with tears.\" (Using translation from Bukhārī 1423)"],[719,"\"When a judge rules and strives and is correct, he has two rewards; and when he rules and strives and errs, he has one reward.\""],[720,"\"When a judge rules and strives and is correct, he has two rewards; and when he rules and strives and errs, he has one reward.\""],[721,"“Allah is with the judge so long as he is not unjust, but if he rules unjustly, He entrusts him to himself.” (Using translation from Ibn Mājah 2312)"],[722,"Indeed, Allah, exalted is He, loves gentleness in every matter."],[723,"Whoever is deprived of gentleness is deprived of good."],[724,"Indeed Allah is gentle and loves gentleness, and He gives for gentleness what He does not give for harshness."],[725,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ went out to these hills and said to me, 'O ʿĀʾishah, gentleness was never in anything but it adorned it, and it was never removed from anything but it disfigured it.'"],[726,"The Prophet ﷺ was asked: \"What most admits people into Paradise?\" He said: \"Fear of Allah and good character.\" It was said: \"And what most admits people into the Fire?\" He said: \"The two hollow ones: the mouth and the private parts.\""],[727,"Whoever is protected from the evil of what is between his jaws and his legs will enter Paradise."],[728,"Indeed the Messenger of Allah ﷺ was neither foul-mouthed nor one who deliberately uttered obscenities, and he used to say: \"The best of you are those with the best character.\""],[729,"They said: \"O Messenger of Allah, what is the best thing given to a Muslim person?\" He said: \"Good character.\""],[730,"“Modesty is from faith, and faith is in Paradise; and obscenity is from harshness, and harshness is in the Fire.”"],[731,"«Indeed a believer may attain, by his good character, the rank of one who fasts by day and stands in prayer at night.»"],[732,"«The heaviest thing in the Scales is good character.»"],[733,"«Indeed the most beloved of you to Allah and the closest of you to me are those with the best character, and indeed the most hateful of you to Allah and the furthest of you from me are the talkative, the boastful, and the long-winded.»"],[734,"«A person's nobility is his religion, his manliness is his intellect, and his lineage is his character.»"],[735,"O Messenger of Allah, tell me something that will make Paradise obligatory for me. He said, “You must have good speech and extending greetings of peace.”"],[736,"When Hāniʾ came as a delegate to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ with his people, he heard them calling Hāniʾ by the kunya Abū al-Ḥakam. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ called him and said, \"Allah is al-Ḥakam (the Judge), and to Him belongs judgment. So why are you called Abū al-Ḥakam?\" He said, \"When my people differ over something, they accept me as a judge (ḥakam), and I judge between them.\" He said, \"That is indeed good. What children do you have?\" He said, \"Shurayḥ, ʿAbd Allāh, and Muslim.\" He said, \"Which of them is the eldest?\" He said, \"Shurayḥ.\" He said, \"Then you are Abū Shurayḥ.\" Then he supplicated for him and his children. When the people wanted to return to their lands, he gave each man of them land wherever he wished in his country. Abū Shurayḥ said, \"O Messenger of Allah...\""],[737,"Worship the Most Merciful, spread peace, and feed food, and you will enter the gardens. *"],[738,"A man asked the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, \"Which [aspect] of Islam is best?\" He said, \"Feeding food and greeting with salam those you know and those you do not know.\""],[739,"A man passed by the Messenger of Allah ﷺ while he was in a gathering and said, “Peace be upon you.” He said, “Ten good deeds.” Then another man passed by and said, “Peace be upon you and the mercy of Allah.” He said, “Twenty good deeds.” Then another man passed by and said, “Peace be upon you and the mercy of Allah and His blessings.” He said, “Thirty good deeds.” Then a man got up from the gathering and did not greet. The Prophet ﷺ said, “How quickly your companion forgot! When one of you comes to a gathering, let him greet; and if he decides to sit, let him sit; and if he gets up, let him greet. The first is not more deserving than the last.”"],[740,"Whoever believes in Allah and the Last Day, let him honor his guest; whoever believes in Allah and the Last Day, let him not harm his neighbor; and whoever believes in Allah and the Last Day, let him say what is good or remain silent."],[741,"In Paradise there are rooms whose outside can be seen from inside and whose inside can be seen from outside. Allah has prepared them for those who feed food, spread salam, and pray at night while people are asleep."],[742,"Abu Talhah saw the Messenger of Allah ﷺ hungry and came to Umm Sulaym and said, \"Do you have anything?\" She said, \"We have nothing but about a mudd of barley flour.\" He said, \"Knead it and prepare it. Perhaps we can invite the Prophet ﷺ to eat with us.\" He said: So she kneaded it and baked it, and it came as a loaf. He said, \"Invite the Prophet ﷺ for me.\" He said: I went to the Prophet ﷺ, and with him were some people - Mubarak b. Fadalah said, I think about eighty-some. I said, \"O Messenger of Allah, Abu Talhah invites you.\" He said to his companions, \"Respond to Abu Talhah.\" I hurried back to tell him that he and his companions had come. Bakr said: He scolded me severely. Thabit said: Abu Talhah said, \"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ knows better what is in my house than I do.\" The two narrators said from Anas: Abu Talhah met him and said, \"O Messenger of Allah, we have nothing but a loaf. I saw you hungry, so I ordered Umm Sulaym to make that loaf.\" He said: He asked for the loaf and asked for a large platter and placed it in it, and said, \"Is there any ghee?\" Abu Talhah said: There was something in the small skin. He brought it, and the Prophet ﷺ and Abu Talhah squeezed it until something came out. The Prophet ﷺ wiped his forefinger with it and then wiped the loaf, and it swelled. He said, \"In the name of Allah.\" The loaf swelled, and he kept doing that while the loaf swelled until I saw the loaf in the platter melting. Then he said, \"Invite ten of my companions.\" I invited ten for him. He said: The Prophet ﷺ placed his hand in the middle of the loaf and said, \"Eat, in the name of Allah.\" They ate from around the loaf until they were full. Then he said, \"Invite ten more.\" He kept inviting ten at a time, and they ate from that loaf until eighty-some people ate from around the loaf and were full, while the middle of the loaf, where the Messenger of Allah ﷺ placed his hand, remained as it was."],[743,"I said, \"O Messenger of Allah, inform me about something that if I do it or act upon it, I will enter Paradise.\" He said, \"Spread peace, feed others, maintain family ties, and pray at night while people are asleep, and you will enter Paradise in peace.\""],[744,"Do not accompany anyone but a believer, and let no one eat your food but a pious person."],[745,"A man came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and said, \"I am exhausted [from hunger].\" He sent to one of his wives, and she said, \"By the One who sent you with the truth as a prophet, I have nothing but water.\" Then he sent to another, and she said the same, until all of them said the same. He said, \"Who will host this man tonight? May Allah have mercy on him.\" A man from the Ansar stood up and said, \"I will, O Messenger of Allah.\" He took him to his family and said to his wife, \"Do you have anything?\" She said, \"No, except the food of my children.\" He said, \"Distract them with something. When our guest enters, light the lamp and show him that we are eating. When he reaches to eat, get up to the lamp and extinguish it.\" He said: They sat down, and the guest ate. In the morning, he went to the Prophet ﷺ, and the Prophet ﷺ said, \"Allah marveled at what you two did last night.\""],[746,"Allah created the womb until when He finished creating it, the womb stood up and said, 'This is the standing of one seeking refuge from severance?' He said, 'Yes. Are you not pleased that I join whoever joins you and cut off whoever cuts you off?' It said, 'Yes.' He said, 'Then that is yours.' The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, 'And recite if you wish: {So would you perhaps, if you turned away, cause corruption on earth and sever your ties of kinship? Those are the ones whom Allah has cursed, so He made them deaf and blinded their sight.}'"],[747,"The womb is a branch of the Most Merciful, suspended from the Throne, saying, 'O Lord, I have been severed, I have been mistreated.' Its Lord answers it, 'Are you not pleased that I cut off whoever cuts you off and join whoever joins you?'"],[748,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, 'Allah, Blessed and Exalted, said: I am the Most Merciful. I created the womb and derived for it a name from My name. Whoever joins it, I join him, and whoever cuts it off, I cut him off.'"],[749,"The womb is a branch of the Most Merciful. When the Day of Resurrection comes, it says, 'O Lord, I have been wronged, I have been mistreated, I have been severed.' He said, 'Then its Lord answers it, \"Are you not pleased that I cut off whoever cuts you off and join whoever joins you?\"'"],[750,"The womb is suspended from the Throne. The maintainer is not the one who reciprocates, but the maintainer is the one who, when his kinship ties are severed, joins them."],[751,"“There is no sin more deserving that Allah hasten its punishment for its perpetrator in this world, along with what He stores up for him in the Hereafter, than injustice and severing kinship ties.”"],[752,"A bedouin intercepted the Prophet ﷺ and took hold of the rein of his she-camel and said, 'O Messenger of Allah'"],[753,"My close friend ﷺ enjoined upon me certain qualities of goodness. He enjoined me “not to look to those above me, but to look to those below me; to love the poor and be close to them; to maintain my kinship ties even if they turn away; not to fear, for the sake of Allah, the blame of any critic; to speak the truth even if it is bitter; and to say often ‘There is no might nor power except with Allah,’ for it is a treasure from the treasures of Paradise.”"],[754,"A man came and said, “O Messenger of Allah, I have relatives whom I maintain ties with, but they cut me off; they mistreat me, but I treat them well; they act ignorantly toward me, but I forbear with them.” The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “If you are as you say, then it is as if you are feeding them hot ashes, and a supporter from Allah will remain with you as long as you continue in that.”"],[755,"A man came and said, “O Messenger of Allah, I have relatives whom I maintain ties with, but they cut me off; they mistreat me, but I treat them well; they act ignorantly toward me, but I forbear with them.” The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “If you are as you say, then it is as if you are feeding them hot ashes, and a supporter from Allah will remain with you as long as you continue in that.”"],[756,"The deeds of people are presented twice every week: on Monday and on Thursday. Every believer is forgiven except a servant between whom and his brother there is enmity. It is said: Leave these two until they reconcile."],[757,"It is not lawful for a Muslim to boycott his brother for more than three nights. They meet, and this one turns away and that one turns away, and the better of them is the one who initiates the greeting of peace."],[758,"“Spread peace and you will be safe.”"],[759,"The rider should greet the walker, the walker the one sitting, and when two walkers meet, whichever of them begins is better."],[760,"Whoever loves to have his lifespan extended and his provision expanded, let him maintain his kinship ties."],[761,"Whoever loves to have his provision expanded and his lifespan extended, let him fear Allah and maintain his kinship ties."],[762,"The swiftest act of obedience in reward is maintaining kinship ties, so much so that the members of a household may be wicked, yet their wealth grows and their number increases when they maintain ties with one another. And there is no household whose members maintain ties with one another that will be in need."],[763,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ came across a man from the tribe of Salimah while I was with him. The man said, \"O Messenger of Allah, both my parents have passed away. Is there anything left for me to do in their favor after their death?\" The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, \"Yes, offer prayers for them, seek forgiveness for them, fulfill their covenants after their death, honor their close friends, and maintain good relations with their relatives, for there is no kinship for you except through them.\" The man said, \"O Messenger of Allah, this is abundant and pleasant. What should I do?\" The Prophet ﷺ replied, \"Act upon this.\""],[764,"A man came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and said, \"O Messenger of Allah, should I go on jihad?\" He said, \"Do you have parents?\" He said, \"Yes.\" He said, \"Then strive in serving them.\""],[765,"A man came and said, \"O Messenger of Allah, I want to pledge allegiance to you for emigration, but I have left my parents weeping.\" He said, \"Return to them and make them laugh as you made them weep.\""],[766,"A man came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and said, 'O Messenger of Allah, I have committed a great sin. Is there any repentance for me?' The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to him, 'Do you have parents?' He said, 'No.' He said, 'Do you have a maternal aunt?' He said, 'Yes.' He said, 'Then be dutiful to her.'"],[767,"“A child cannot repay his parent unless he finds him a slave, buys him, and sets him free.”"],[768,"A man came to Abu al-Darda' and said, “My father kept at me until I married, and now he commands me to divorce her.” He said, “I am not one to command you to disobey your father, nor am I one to command you to divorce your wife. But if you wish, I will tell you what I heard from the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. I heard him say, ‘The parent is the middle gate of Paradise, so guard that gate if you wish, or leave it.’”"],[769,"My father married a woman whom Umar disliked, so he ordered him to divorce her. He mentioned that to the Prophet ﷺ, who said, “Obey your father.”"],[770,"I had a wife whom I loved, and my father disliked her and ordered me to divorce her, but I refused. Umar mentioned that to the Prophet ﷺ, and the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, “O Abdullah, divorce her.”"],[771,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ passed by Abdullah b. Ubayy b. Salul while he was in the shade of a thicket and said, “Ibn Abi Kabsha has filled us with dust.” His son Abdullah b. Abdullah said, “By the One who honored you and sent down the Book to you, if you wish, I will bring you his head.” The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, “No, but be dutiful to your father and keep good company with him.”"],[772,"“Allah’s pleasure lies in the parent’s pleasure, and Allah’s wrath lies in the parent’s wrath.”"],[773,"A man came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and said, 'Who is most deserving of my good companionship?' He said, 'Your mother.' He said, 'Then who?' He said, 'Your mother.' He said, 'Then who?' He said, 'Your mother.' He said, 'Then who?' He said, 'Your father.'"],[774,"A man from Banu 'Udhrah freed a slave of his upon his death. The Prophet ﷺ sent for it, sold it, and handed him its price, and said, \"Begin with yourself and give charity to it, then to your parents, then to your relatives, then thus, then thus.\""],[776,"“The most dutiful act is that a man maintains ties with his father’s loved ones after he passes away.”"],[777,"I came to Madinah, and Abdullah b. Umar came to me and said, “Do you know why I came to you?” I said, “No.” He said, “I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say, ‘Whoever wishes to maintain ties with his father in his grave, let him maintain ties with his father’s brothers after him.’ There was brotherhood and affection between my father Umar and your father, so I wished to maintain that.”"],[778,"Jibril kept urging me to be good to the neighbor until I thought he would make him an heir."],[779,"A man came to the Prophet ﷺ and complained to him about a neighbor of his. The Prophet ﷺ said three times, 'Be patient.' Then he said to him on the fourth or the third time, 'Put your belongings out on the road.' So he did. He said: People began to pass by him and say, 'What is wrong with you?' He would say, 'His neighbor is harming him.' They began to say, 'May Allah curse him.' Then his neighbor came to him and said, 'Take back your belongings. By Allah, I will never harm you again.'"],[780,"The believer is one from whom people are safe; the Muslim is one from whose tongue and hand Muslims are safe; the emigrant (muhājir) is one who emigrates from evil; and by the One in whose hand is my soul, a servant whose neighbor does not feel safe from his harms will not enter Paradise."],[781,"The best of companions in the sight of Allah is the one who is best to his companion, and the best of neighbors in the sight of Allah is the one who is best to his neighbor."],[782,"I said, 'O Messenger of Allah, guide me to a deed from which I may benefit.' He said, 'Remove harm from the path of Muslims.'"],[783,"While a man was walking on a road, he found a thorny branch on the path, so he took it, and Allah thanked him and forgave him."],[784,"The Prophet ﷺ said: A man never did a good deed but removed a thorny branch from the road; it was either in the tree and someone cut it and threw it on the road, or it was lying in it, he removed it. Allah accepted this good deed of his and brought him into Paradise. (Using translation from Abū Dāʾūd 5245)"],[785,"“Among the people who came before you was a man whom Allah blessed with wealth and children. When death came to him, he gathered his sons and said: ‘What kind of father was I to you?’ They said: ‘The best of fathers.’ He said: ‘Indeed, by Allah, I have never stored up any good with Allah. His Lord will punish him. So when I die, burn me, then crush me, then scatter me in a violent wind.’ Allah said: ‘Be,’ and behold, he was a man standing. He said: ‘What made you do what you did?’ He said: ‘Fear of You.’ He said: ‘By the One in whose hand is my soul, if he meets nothing else, he will be forgiven.’”"],[786,"Three have a right upon God to help them: the one striving in the path of God, the one marrying seeking chastity, and the slave in a contract of emancipation who intends to pay."],[787,"Whoever comes on the Day of Resurrection free of three things will enter Paradise: arrogance, misappropriation of spoils, and debt."],[788,"He came to him and said: 'Lend me your stallion, for I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: Whoever lends a stallion and it sires offspring, he will have the reward of seventy horses that were ridden in the way of Allah; and if it does not sire, he will have the reward of one horse ridden in the way of Allah.'"],[790,"“When a man disciplines his slave woman and disciplines her well, and teaches her and teaches her well, then frees her and marries her, he has two rewards. And when a man believes in Jesus then believes in me, he has two rewards. And a slave, when he fears his Lord and obeys his masters, has two rewards.”"],[791,"from the Prophet ﷺ who said, \"Allah [audits] His creation on the middle night of Shaʿbān and He forgives all of His creation, except for an idolater or one filled with malice.\""],[792,"Every joint of a person owes charity every day. A man from the people said, 'Who can bear that?' He said, 'Enjoining good is charity, forbidding wrong is charity, helping the weak is charity, and every step one takes to prayer is charity.'"],[793,"From his grandfather, he said:"],[794,"“Whoever kills a snake will have seven good deeds, and whoever kills a gecko will have one good deed.”"],[795,"“O Mother of the Believers, what do you do with this?” She said: “We kill these house lizards with it, for the Prophet of Allah ﷺ told us that when Ibrahim was thrown into the fire, there was no beast on earth that did not try to put it out, apart from the house lizard that blew on it. So the Messenger of Allah ﷺ commanded that they should be killed.” (Using translation from Ibn Mājah 3231)"],[796,"Maymunah used to incur debt. Her family spoke to her about that and were upset with her, but she said, 'I will not stop, for I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say, \"There is no one who incurs a debt, knowing that Allah knows he intends to repay it, except that Allah will repay it on his behalf in this world.\"'"],[797,"«Shall I not inform you of the best of witnesses? He is the one who brings his testimony or speaks it before he is asked for it.»"],[798,"Whoever guarantees for me what is between his jaws, I will guarantee for him Paradise."],[799,"Glad tidings to the one who is guided to Islam, whose livelihood is sufficient, and whom Allah makes content with it."],[800,"\"Worship during turmoil is like emigration to me.\""],[801,"I came to Abu Tha'labah al-Khushani and said: O Abu Tha'labah, what do you say about this verse: {Those who have gone astray will not harm you if you are guided}? He said: By Allah, you have asked one who knows about it. I asked the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and he said: \"Rather, enjoin what is right and forbid what is wrong, until when you see miserliness obeyed, desire followed, this world preferred, and every person with an opinion admiring his own opinion, then upon you is yourself, and leave the affair of the common people. For behind you are days in which patience is like holding onto embers. For the one who acts in them is the reward of fifty men who do the like of his deed.\""],[802,"“Whoever grows a grey hair in the path of Allah, it will be light for him on the Day of Resurrection.”"],[803,"«Do not pluck grey hairs, for it is light on the Day of Resurrection. Whoever grows a grey hair in Islam, a good deed is recorded for him thereby, a misdeed is erased from him thereby, and a rank is raised for him thereby.»"],[804,"Blessing is with your elders."],[805,"A bedouin came to the Prophet ﷺ and said: \"O Messenger of Allah, teach me a deed that will admit me to Paradise.\" He said: \"Though you have shortened the speech, you have broadened the question. Free the slave, and release the neck.\" He said: \"Are they not the same?\" He said: \"No, freeing the slave is that you alone free him, and releasing the neck is that you contribute to his price. And the abundant gift, and the return to a relative who cuts off ties. If you cannot do that, then feed the hungry, give water to the thirsty, enjoin good, and forbid evil. If you cannot do that, then restrain your tongue except from good.\""],[806,"\"Whoever strives in the path of Allah is guaranteed by Allah. Whoever visits a sick person is guaranteed by Allah. Whoever goes early to a mosque or returns is guaranteed by Allah. Whoever enters upon a ruler to honor him is guaranteed by Allah. Whoever sits in his house and does not backbite anyone is guaranteed by Allah.\""],[807,"I entered the mosque, and there was the Messenger of Allah ﷺ sitting alone. He said: \"O Abu Dharr, the mosque has a greeting, and its greeting is two rakahs, so stand and pray them.\" He said: So I stood and prayed them, then I returned and sat with him. I said: O Messenger of Allah, you have commanded me to pray, so what is prayer? He said: \"A good thing that has been set forth; do much of it or little.\" He said: I said: O Messenger of Allah, which deed is best? He said: \"Faith in Allah and jihad in the path of Allah.\" He said: I said: O Messenger of Allah, which of the believers is most complete in faith? He said: \"The best of them in character.\" I said: O Messenger of Allah, which of the believers is safest in submission? He said: \"The one from whose tongue and hand people are safe.\" He said: I said: O Messenger of Allah, which prayer is best? He said: \"Lengthy devotion.\" He said: I said: O Messenger of Allah, which migration is best? He said: \"The one who abandons evil deeds.\" He said: I said: O Messenger of Allah, what of fasting? He said: \"An obligatory duty that suffices, and with Allah are many multiples of reward.\" He said: I said: O Messenger of Allah, which jihad is best? He said: \"The one whose steed is hamstrung and whose blood is shed.\" He said: I said: O Messenger of Allah, which charity is best? He said: \"The effort of one of little means, given quietly to a poor person.\" I said: O Messenger of Allah, which of what Allah has sent down to you is greatest? He said: \"Ayat al-Kursi.\" Then he said: \"O Abu Dharr, the seven heavens in relation to the Kursi are only like a ring cast in a vast open land, and the superiority of the Throne over the Kursi is like the superiority of that open land over the ring.\" He said: I said: O Messenger of Allah, how many prophets were there? He said: \"One hundred and twenty thousand.\" I said: O Messenger of Allah, how many messengers were among them? He said: \"Three hundred and thirteen, a great multitude.\" He said: I said: O Messenger of Allah, who was the first of them? He said: \"Adam.\" I said: O Messenger of Allah, was he a prophet sent as a messenger? He said: \"Yes. Allah created him with His hand, breathed into him of His spirit, and spoke to him directly.\" Then he said: \"O Abu Dharr, four were Syriac: Adam, Sheeth, Akhnukh—who is Idris and was the first to write with the pen—and Nuh; and four were Arabs: Hud, Shuayb, Salih, and your prophet Muhammad ﷺ.\" I said: O Messenger of Allah, how many books did Allah send down? He said: \"One hundred books and four books: fifty scrolls were sent down to Sheeth, thirty scrolls were sent down to Akhnukh, ten scrolls were sent down to Ibrahim, ten scrolls were sent down to Musa before the Tawrah, and the Tawrah, the Injil, the Zabur, and the Quran were sent down.\" He said: I said: O Messenger of Allah, what was in the scroll of Ibrahim? He said: \"It was all parables: O empowered king, afflicted and deluded, I did not send you to pile up this world, one part upon another; rather, I sent you to turn back from Me the supplication of the oppressed, for I do not reject it even if it comes from a disbeliever. The intelligent person, so long as his mind is not overcome, should have periods: a period in which he privately calls upon his Lord; a period in which he takes himself to account; a period in which he reflects on the work of Allah; and a period in which he withdraws for his needs of food and drink. The intelligent person should not set out except for three things: provision for the return, repair of livelihood, or pleasure that is not unlawful. The intelligent person should be aware of his time, attentive to his own affair, and guarding his tongue. Whoever counts his speech as part of his deeds, his speech will be little except in what concerns him.\" I said: O Messenger of Allah, what was in the scrolls of Musa? He said: \"They were all lessons: I am amazed at one who is certain of death, yet he rejoices; I am amazed at one who is certain of the Fire, yet he laughs; I am amazed at one who is certain of divine decree, yet he exhausts himself; I am amazed at one who sees the world and how it turns upon its people, yet he feels secure with it; and I am amazed at one who is certain of the reckoning tomorrow, yet does not act.\" I said: O Messenger of Allah, counsel me. He said: \"I counsel you to fear Allah, for it is the head of the whole matter.\" I said: O Messenger of Allah, give me more. He said: \"Hold fast to reciting the Quran and remembering Allah, for it is a light for you on earth and a treasure for you in heaven.\" I said: O Messenger of Allah, give me more. He said: \"Beware of excessive laughter, for it kills the heart and takes away the light of the face.\" I said: O Messenger of Allah, give me more. He said: \"Hold fast to silence except from good, for it drives Satan away from you and is a help for you in the matter of your religion.\" I said: O Messenger of Allah, give me more. He said: \"Hold fast to jihad, for it is the monasticism of my community.\" I said: O Messenger of Allah, give me more. He said: \"Love the poor and sit with them.\" I said: O Messenger of Allah, give me more. He said: \"Look to those beneath you and do not look to those above you, for that is more likely that you will not look down upon Allah's blessing with you.\" I said: O Messenger of Allah, give me more. He said: \"Speak the truth, even if it is bitter.\" I said: O Messenger of Allah, give me more. He said: \"Let what you know of yourself restrain you from people, and do not find fault with them for what you yourself do. It is enough as a fault in you that you recognize in people what you are ignorant of in yourself, or that you find fault with them for what you yourself do.\" Then he struck my chest with his hand and said: \"O Abu Dharr, there is no intelligence like careful planning, no piety like restraint, and no nobility like good character.\""],[808,"that He heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say, \"There are five actions that if done in a day, Allah will write the person from the people of Paradise: (1) visiting a sick person, (2) attending a funeral, (3) fasting for a day, (3) going to Jumuah prayer, and (5) freeing a slave.\""],[809,"\"Three men from among those before you set out seeking provision for their families. Rain overtook them, so they sought refuge in a mountain. A rock fell upon them, blocking their way. Then one of them said to the others, 'The trail has been obliterated and the rock has fallen, and none knows your place except Allah. Call upon Allah by the most trustworthy of your deeds.'\""],[810,"A man came to the Prophet ﷺ and asked him, and he said: \"I have nothing to give you, but go to so-and-so.\" He said: So the man went to that person and he gave him. Then the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"Whoever points to a good deed has the like of the reward of its doer or its performer.\""],[811,"While we were on a journey with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, those who were in front of him sat down and those who were behind him caught up until they gathered. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"Whoever bears witness that there is no god but Allah, Allah has forbidden him to the Fire and made Paradise obligatory for him.\""],[812,"When death approached Mu'adh, he said: \"Uncover the curtain of the tent from me. I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: 'Whoever bears witness that there is no god but Allah, sincerely from his heart, will enter Paradise.'\""],[813,"Whoever dies knowing that there is no god but Allah will enter Paradise."],[814,"I entered upon Ubadah b. al-Samit while he was dying, and I wept. He said to me, \"Wait, why do you weep? By Allah, if I am martyred, I will surely testify for you; and if I am granted intercession, I will surely intercede for you; and if I am able, I will surely benefit you.\" Then he said, \"By Allah, there is no hadith I heard from the Messenger of Allah ﷺ in which there is good for you except that I have narrated it to you, except one hadith, and I will narrate it to you today, now that my soul is about to depart. I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: 'Whoever bears witness that there is no god but Allah and that Muhammad is the Messenger of Allah, Allah has forbidden him to the Fire.'\""],[815,"«There is no soul on the earth that dies without associating anything with Allah and bears witness that I am the Messenger of Allah, that returning to a certain heart, except that it will be forgiven.»"],[816,"«I certainly know a word that no servant says truly from his heart and then dies upon that except that Allah forbids him from the Fire: 'There is no god but Allah.'»"],[817,"'Umar b. al-Khattab passed by Talha after the death of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and said, \"What is the matter with you, looking distressed? Did the leadership of your cousin's son displease you?\" He said, \"No, but I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: 'I certainly know a word that no servant says at his death except that it becomes a light for his record, and his body and soul will find rest through it at the moment of death.' He passed away and I did not ask him about it.\" 'Umar said, \"I know it only as the word he wanted his uncle to say; and if he had known of anything that would save him more than it, he would have commanded him with it.\""],[818,"The Prophet ﷺ said, \"When a believer testifies that there is no deity except Allah and acknowledges Muhammad as the Messenger of Allah ﷺ in his grave, then this is the saying of Allah, the Exalted, 'Allah keeps firm those who believe, with the firm word, in worldly life and in the Hereafter.'\""],[819,"«Whoever bears witness that there is no god but Allah alone with no partner, and that Muhammad is His servant and Messenger, and that Jesus is the servant of Allah and His Messenger and His word which He cast to Mary and a spirit from Him, and that Paradise and Hell are true, Allah will admit him through whichever of the eight gates of Paradise He wills.»"],[820,"«The people of Paradise will see the people of the upper chambers as you see the shining star that remains on the horizon from the east and the west, because of the difference in virtue between them.» They said, \"O Messenger of Allah, those are the stations of the Prophets that no one else can reach?\" He said, \"Yes, by the One in whose hand is my soul, men who believed in Allah and affirmed the Messengers.\""],[821,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, \"What is the right of Allah upon His servants?\" They replied, \"Allah and His Messenger know best.\" He said, \"That they worship Him alone and do not associate anything with Him.\" He asked, \"What is their right upon Allah if they do that?\" They replied, \"Allah and His Messenger know best.\" He said, \"That He forgives them and does not punish them.\""],[822,"From the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, he said: “Indeed Allah, Mighty and Majestic, says: I am as My servant thinks of Me. If he thinks good, then for him is good; and if he thinks evil, then for him is evil.”"],[823,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ made a halt with us one night, and each man among us spread out the foreleg of his mount. He said: I woke up during part of the night, and the she-camel of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ had no one in front of it. I set off looking for the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and found Mu'adh b. Jabal and 'Abd Allah b. Qays standing. I said, \"Where is the Messenger of Allah ﷺ?\" They said, \"We do not know, except that we heard a sound at the top of the valley like the rumbling of a mill.\" He said: We waited a short while, then the Messenger of Allah ﷺ came to us and said, \"A messenger came to me from my Lord and gave me the choice between half of my nation entering Paradise and intercession, and I chose intercession.\" They said, \"O Messenger of Allah, we adjure you by Allah and by companionship to make us among the people of your intercession.\" He said, \"You are among the people of my intercession.\" When they mounted, he said, \"I call to witness those present that my intercession is for whoever dies not associating anything with Allah from my nation.\""],[824,"By the One in whose hand is my soul, you will all enter Paradise except the one who refuses and flees from Allah as a camel flees. They said: O Messenger of Allah, who refuses to enter Paradise? He said: Whoever obeys me enters Paradise, and whoever disobeys me has refused."],[825,"I saw a man from Khurasan come to him and say, \"O Abu 'Amr, those among us from Khurasan say that when a man frees his slave woman and then marries her, he is like one who mounts his own sacrificial camel.\" Al-Sha'bi said, \"Abu Burdah narrated to me from his father that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: «Three people will be given their reward twice: a man from the People of the Book who believed in his prophet and then lived to see the Prophet ﷺ and believed in him and followed him, so he will have two rewards; a slave who fulfills the right of Allah, Glorified and Exalted, upon him and the right of his master upon him, so he will have two rewards; and a man who had a slave woman and fed her well and disciplined her well, then freed her and married her, so he will have two rewards.»\""],[826,"\"Whoever treads a path seeking knowledge therein, Allah will make easy for him thereby a path to one of the paths of Paradise. And whoever is slowed down by his deeds will not be hastened forward by his lineage.\""],[827,"I came to Safwan b. 'Assal al-Muradi and he said, \"What brings you?\" I said, \"I have come to seek knowledge.\" He said, \"I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: 'No one goes out from his house seeking knowledge except that the angels lower their wings in approval of what he does.'\" He said, \"I came to ask you about wiping over the two khuffs.\" He said, \"Yes. We were in the army that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ sent, and he commanded us to wipe over the two khuffs if we had put them on in a state of purity: for three days when traveling, and not to remove them for defecation or urination.\""],[828,"While the Messenger of Allah ﷺ was sitting in the mosque with the people around him, three persons came. Two came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and one went away. When the two stood before the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, they greeted. One of them saw a gap in the circle and sat in it, while the other sat behind them. As for the third, he turned and went away. When the Messenger of Allah ﷺ finished, he said: \"Shall I inform you about the three persons? As for one of them, he sought refuge with Allah, so Allah gave him refuge. As for the other, he was shy, so Allah was shy of him. As for the other, he turned away, so Allah turned away from him.\""],[829,"\"Whoever enters this mosque of ours to learn good or to teach it is like a warrior in the path of Allah. And whoever enters for other than that is like one who looks at what does not belong to him.\""],[830,"I was sitting with Abu al-Darda' in the mosque of Damascus when a man came to him and said, 'O Abu al-Darda', I have come to you from the City of the Messenger ﷺ concerning a hadith which I was told you narrate from the Messenger of Allah ﷺ.' Abu al-Darda' said, 'You have not come for any need, nor for trade; you have come only for this hadith?' He said, 'Yes.' He said, 'Indeed I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: \"Whoever travels a path seeking knowledge therein, Allah will make him travel a path from the paths of Paradise. The angels lower their wings in approval for the seeker of knowledge. Indeed the scholar is asked forgiveness for by whoever is in the heavens and whoever is on earth, and the fish in the water. The superiority of the scholar over the worshipper is like the superiority of the moon on the night of the full moon over all the other stars. Indeed the scholars are the heirs of the prophets. The prophets did not leave behind a dinar or a dirham; they left behind knowledge. So whoever takes it has taken an abundant share.\"'"],[831,"\"Whomever Allah wills good for, He gives him understanding in the religion.\""],[832,"“There is no (permissible) envy except in two cases: A man whom Allah has given wealth and caused him to dispose of it in a proper manner, and a man to whom Allah has given wisdom, and he acts in accordance with it and teaches it (to others).” (Using translation from Ibn Mājah 4208)"],[833,"\"The best of you are those with the best character when they attain understanding.\""],[834,"Zayd b. Thabit came out from Marwan's presence near midday. I said: He only sent for him to ask him about something. I went to him and asked him. He said: Yes, he asked us about things we heard from the Messenger of Allah ﷺ: \"May Allah have mercy on a person who hears a hadith from me, memorizes it, and conveys it to others. Perhaps a carrier of fiqh delivers it to one more insightful than himself, and perhaps a carrier of fiqh is not a faqih. Three qualities: the heart of a Muslim does not harbor rancor against them: sincerity of action for Allah, sincere counsel to those in authority, and adhering to the community, for their supplication encompasses those behind them.\""],[835,"\"The Messenger of Allah, peace be upon him, said, 'May Allah have mercy on the one who hears a hadith from me and conveys it as he heard it, for perhaps the one who conveys it understands it better than the one who hears it.'\""],[836,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, \"May Allah brighten the face of the individual who hears something from us and conveys it exactly as he heard it. There are times when the one who conveys something is more mindful of it than the one who hears it.\""],[837,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"A group of my Ummah will continue to prevail and they will never be harmed by those who forsake them, until the Hour begins.\" (Using translation from Ibn Mājah 6)"],[838,"\"The best of what a man leaves behind after him are three: a righteous child who supplicates for him, an ongoing charity whose reward reaches him, and knowledge from which benefit is derived after him.\""],[839,"We were forbidden to ask the Messenger of Allah ﷺ about anything. It pleased us when a man from the desert came and asked him while we listened. A man from them came to him and said, “O Muhammad, your messenger came to us and claimed that you claim that Allah has sent you.” He said, “He spoke the truth.” He said, “Who created the sky?” He said, “Allah.” He said, “Who created the earth?” He said, “Allah.” He said, “Who erected these mountains?” He said, “Allah.” He said, “Who placed these benefits in them?” He said, “Allah.” He said, “Then by the One who created the sky and the earth, erected the mountains, and placed these benefits in them, did Allah send you?” He said, “Yes.” He said, “Your messenger claimed that we owe five prayers in our day and night.” He said, “He spoke the truth.” He said, “By the One who sent you, did Allah command you with this?” He said, “Yes.” He said, “Your messenger claimed that we owe charity from our wealth.” He said, “He spoke the truth.” He said, “By the One who sent you, did Allah command you with this?” He said, “Yes.” He said, “Your messenger claimed that we owe fasting a month in our year.” He said, “He spoke the truth.” He said, “By the One who sent you, did Allah command you with this?” He said, “Yes.” He said, “Your messenger claimed that we owe pilgrimage to the House for whoever is able to find a way.” He said, “He spoke the truth.” He said, “By the One who sent you, did Allah command you with this?” He said, “Yes.” He said, “By the One who sent you with the truth, I will not add to them nor subtract from them anything.” When he turned away, the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, “If he is truthful, he will surely enter Paradise.”"],[840,"When the Messenger of Allah ﷺ sent Mu‘adh to Yemen, he said, “You will come upon a people from the People of the Book. Let the first thing to which you call them be worship of Allah. When they acknowledge Allah, inform them that Allah has obligated upon them five prayers in their day and night. When they do them, inform them that Allah has obligated upon them charity taken from their wealth and returned to their poor. When they obey this, take from them and avoid the best properties of the people.”"],[841,"The Prophet ﷺ fell from a horse and injured his right side. When it was time for prayer, he prayed with us sitting. When he finished his prayer, he said: 'The imam is only appointed to be followed. When he says the takbir, say the takbir; when he bows, bow; when he rises, rise; when he says “Allah hears the one who praises Him,” say “Our Lord, and to You belongs praise”; and when he prays sitting, all of you pray sitting.'"],[842,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ rode a horse and was thrown, meaning he injured his right side. He prayed one of the prayers sitting, and we prayed behind him sitting. When he finished, he said: 'The imam is only appointed to be followed. When he prays standing, pray standing; when he bows, bow; when he rises, rise; when he says “Allah hears the one who praises Him,” say “Our Lord, and to You belongs praise”; and when he prays sitting, all of you pray sitting.'"],[843,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ prayed in his house while he was ill, sitting. A group prayed behind him standing. He gestured to them to sit down. When the Messenger of Allah ﷺ finished, he said: 'The imam is only appointed to be followed. When he bows, bow; when he rises, rise; and when he prays sitting, pray sitting.'"],[844,"Leave me with what I have left you, for those before you were destroyed only by their questioning and their disagreement with their prophets. So when I forbid you from something, avoid it, and when I command you with something, do of it what you are able."],[845,"Leave me with what I have left you. Those before you were destroyed only by their excessive questioning and their disagreement with their prophets. Whatever I command you to do, do as much of it as you can, and whatever I forbid you, abstain from it."],[846,"The imam is only appointed to be followed, so do not differ from him. When he says the takbir, say the takbir; when he bows, bow; when he says “Allah hears the one who praises Him,” say “O Allah, our Lord, to You belongs praise”; and when he prays sitting, all of you pray sitting."],[847,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ rode a horse and was thrown from it, and his right side was scraped. Anas said: He prayed one of the prayers for us that day while seated, and we prayed behind him seated. Then, when he said the taslim, he said: “The imam is only appointed to be followed. So when the imam prays standing, then pray standing; when he bows, then bow; when he rises, then rise; when he prostrates, then prostrate; and when he says, ‘Allah hears the one who praises Him,’ then say, ‘Our Lord, and to You belongs praise.’ And when he prays seated, then pray seated, all of you.”"],[848,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ was among a group of his companions and said: “Do you not know that I am the Messenger of Allah to you?” They said: “Yes, we bear witness that you are the Messenger of Allah.” He said: “Do you not know that whoever obeys me has obeyed Allah, and that obedience to Allah includes obedience to me?” They said: “Yes, we bear witness that whoever obeys you has obeyed Allah, and that obedience to Allah includes obedience to you.” He said: “Then it is part of obedience to Allah that you obey me, and part of obedience to me that you obey your leaders. So if they pray seated, then pray seated.”"],[849,"The Prophet ﷺ was approached by some people, and the prayer time arrived. He led them in prayer while seated, and they were standing. When the next prayer time arrived, they started to stand, and he said: “Follow your imam. If he prays seated, then pray seated; and if he prays standing, then pray standing.”"],[850,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ rode a horse in Medina. It threw him off at the root of a date-palm. His foot was injured. We visited him to inquire about his illness. We found him praying sitting in the apartment of Aisha. We, therefore, stood, (praying) behind him. He kept silent. We again visited him to inquire about his illness. He offered the obligatory prayer sitting. We, therefore, stood (praying) behind him; he made a sign to us and we sat down. When he finished the prayer, he said: When the imam prays sitting, pray sitting; and when the imam prays standing, pray standing, and do not act as the people of Persia used to act with their chiefs (i.e. the people stood and they were sitting). (Using translation from Abū Dāʾūd 602)"],[851,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ fell from a horse and was injured, so he prayed with us while seated, and we prayed with him seated. Then he finished and said: “The imam is only to be followed. So when he says the takbir, then say the takbir; when he bows, then bow; when he rises, then rise; when he says, ‘Allah hears the one who praises Him,’ then say, ‘Our Lord, and to You belongs praise’; when he prostrates, then prostrate; and when he prays seated, then pray seated, all of you.”"],[852,"The Prophet ﷺ was thrown from a horse of his and fell onto a palm stump, dislocating his foot. We entered upon him to visit him while he was praying in a room of Aisha's, seated. We prayed along with his prayer while we were standing. Then we entered upon him another time while he was praying seated, and we prayed along with his prayer while standing. He gestured to us to sit down. When he finished praying, he said: “The imam is only appointed to be followed. So if he prays standing, then pray standing; and if he prays seated, then pray seated. Do not stand while he is seated, as the Persians do with their leaders.”"],[853,"From the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, he said: “Indeed Allah, Mighty and Majestic, says: I am as My servant thinks of Me. If he thinks good, then for him is good; and if he thinks evil, then for him is evil.”"],[854,"\"I entered upon Aisha and said: 'Will you not tell me about the sickness of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ?' She said: 'When the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, became seriously ill, he said: \"Have the people prayed?\" We said: \"No, they are waiting for you, 0 Messenger of Allah ﷺ\" He said: \"Put some water in a tub for me.\" We did that and he performed Ghusl, then he tried to get up but he fainted. Then he came to us and said: \"Have the people prayed?\" We said: \"No, they are waiting for you, 0 Messenger of Allah ﷺ.\" He said: \"Put some water in a tub for me.\" We did that and he performed Ghusl, then he tried to get up but he fainted. Then for the third time he said the same thing. She said: The people were in the Masjid, waiting for the Messenger of Allah ﷺ to lead the prayer. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ sent word to Abu Bakr, telling him to lead the people in prayer, so the messenger came to him and said: \"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ is telling you to lead the people in prayer.\" Abu Bakr was a tenderhearted man, he said: \"0 'Umar. lead the in prayer.\" But ('Umar) said: \"You have more right to that.\" So Abu Bakr led them in prayer during those days. When the Messenger of Allah ﷺ felt a little better, he came with the help of two men, one of whom was Al-'Abbas, to pray Zuhr. When Abu Bakr saw him, he wanted to step back, but the Messenger of Allah ﷺ gestured to him not to step back. He told them (the two men) to seat him beside Abu Bakr, and Abu Bakr started to pray standing. The people were following the prayer of Abu Bakr and the Messenger of Allah ﷺ was praying sitting.\"' \"I ('Ubaidullah) entered upon Ibn Abbas and said 'Shall I not tell you what Aisha narrated to me about the sickness of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ?' He said: 'Yes.' So I told him and he did not deny any of it, but he said: 'Did she tell you the name of the man who was with Al-'Abbas?' I said: 'No.' He said: 'That was Ali, may Allah honor his face.\"' (Using translation from Nasāʾī 834)"],[855,"“Abu Bakr led the people in prayer, and the Messenger of Allah ﷺ was in the row behind him.”"],[856,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ lost consciousness, then regained it and said: “Have the people prayed?” We said: “No.” He said: “Tell Abu Bakr to lead the people in prayer.” I said: “O Messenger of Allah, Abu Bakr is a tender-hearted man. If he stands in your place, he will not be able to lead the people in prayer.” Asim said: “Al-asif means tender and compassionate.” He said: “Tell Abu Bakr to lead the people in prayer.” He said that three times, and each time I responded to him. She said: So Abu Bakr led the people in prayer. Then the Messenger of Allah ﷺ felt some relief and came out supported between Barirah and Nubah. I could see his sandals making lines in the pebbles, and I could see the soles of his feet. He said to them: “Seat me beside Abu Bakr.” When Abu Bakr saw him, he started to step back, but he gestured to him to stay in his place. So they seated him beside Abu Bakr. She said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ was praying while seated, and Abu Bakr was standing, praying following the prayer of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and the people were praying following the prayer of Abu Bakr."],[857,"“The Messenger of Allah ﷺ prayed during his final illness behind Abu Bakr, seated.”"],[858,"When the Prophet ﷺ fell ill with his final illness, Bilal came to inform him of the prayer. He said: “Tell Abu Bakr to lead the people in prayer.” We said: “O Messenger of Allah, Abu Bakr is a tender-hearted man. Whenever he stands in your place, he weeps. If only you would command Umar to lead the people in prayer.” He said: “Tell Abu Bakr to lead the people in prayer” three times, then said: “You are like the women of Joseph.” She said: So we sent word to Abu Bakr, and he led the people in prayer. Then the Prophet ﷺ felt some relief and came out supported between two men, his feet making lines on the ground. When Abu Bakr sensed him, he started to step back, but the Prophet ﷺ gestured to him to stay in his place. So the Prophet ﷺ came and sat beside Abu Bakr. Abu Bakr followed the prayer of the Prophet ﷺ, and the people followed the prayer of Abu Bakr."],[859,"When the Messenger of Allah ﷺ felt some relief, he came and sat to the left of Abu Bakr. The Prophet ﷺ was leading the people in prayer while seated, and Abu Bakr was standing."],[860,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ was ill, so we prayed behind him while he was seated. Abu Bakr was saying the takbir, making his takbir audible to the people. He said: He turned toward us and saw us standing, so he gestured to us, and we sat down and prayed following his prayer, seated. When he said the taslim, he said: “You were about to do what the Persians and Romans do: they stand before their kings while the kings are seated. Do not do that. Follow your imam. If he prays standing, then pray standing; and if he prays seated, then pray seated.”"],[861,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ led us in the Zuhr prayer while he was sitting, with Abu Bakr behind him. When the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said the takbir, Abu Bakr said the takbir so that we could hear him. He (the narrator) said: We looked, standing, and he said, 'Sit down,' gesturing that to them. He said: So we sat down. When he finished the prayer, he said, 'You almost did what the Persians and Romans do with their great ones: stand before them while they sit. Follow your imams. If they pray sitting, then pray sitting; and if they pray standing, then pray standing.'"],[862,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ fell unconscious. When he regained consciousness, he said, 'Has the call to prayer been given?' We said, 'No.' He said, 'Tell Bilal to hasten the call to prayer and let Abu Bakr lead the people in prayer.' She said: I said, 'O Messenger of Allah, Abu Bakr is a tender-hearted man; he cannot stand in your place without weeping.' She said: He looked at me when I finished speaking, then he fell unconscious again. When he regained consciousness, he said, 'Has the call to prayer been given?' She said: I said, 'No.' He said, 'Tell Bilal to give the call to prayer and let Abu Bakr lead the people in prayer.' She said: So I gestured to Hafsah, who said, 'O Prophet of Allah, Abu Bakr is a soft-hearted man; he cannot recite without weeping.' He said: He looked at her when she finished speaking, then the Messenger of Allah ﷺ fell unconscious again. When he regained consciousness, he said, 'Has the call to prayer been given?' She said: I said, 'No.' He said, 'Tell Bilal to give the call to prayer and let Abu Bakr lead the people in prayer, for you are like the companions of Yusuf.' Then the Messenger of Allah ﷺ fell unconscious again. She said: So Bilal gave the iqamah and Abu Bakr led the people in prayer. Then the Messenger of Allah ﷺ regained consciousness and came supported by Nubah and Barirah, who carried him. Aishah said: It is as if I can see the toes of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ dragging on the ground. She said: When Abu Bakr felt the Prophet ﷺ coming, he wanted to step back, but he gestured to him to stay in place. She said: Then the Prophet of Allah ﷺ was brought and placed in line next to Abu Bakr in the row."],[863,"\"In the last prayer that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ prayed with the people, he prayed wrapped up in a single garment, behind Abu Bakr.\" (Using translation from Nasāʾī 785)"],[864,"Ibn Umm Maktūm came to the Prophet ﷺ and said, ‘O Messenger of Allah, I am blind and live far away.’ He spoke to him about the prayer, asking him to excuse him from praying in his home. He said, ‘Do you hear the adhān?’ He replied, ‘Yes.’ He said, ‘Then come to it, even if crawling.’"],[865,"Whoever hears the call and does not respond, there is no prayer for him except from an excuse."],[866,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ did not come out to us for three [days]. The prayer was about to be established, and Abū Bakr went forward to lead. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ lifted the curtain, and when the whiteness of the Prophet’s face appeared to us, we had never seen a sight more beloved to us than the face of the Prophet of Allah ﷺ when it appeared to us. He said, ‘The Prophet of Allah ﷺ gestured with his hand to Abū Bakr to go forward.’ He said, ‘The Messenger of Allah ﷺ lowered the curtain, and he was not able to [come out] until he died ﷺ.’"],[867,"When the evening meal is served and the prayer is due, begin with it before the Maghrib prayer, and do not hurry away from your dinner."],[868,"When the sun had set and night became clear to him, Ibn ‘Umar would sometimes have his evening meal brought forward while he was fasting, while the muezzin was calling the adhān and then the iqāmah, and he could hear it. He would not leave his dinner nor hurry until he finished his dinner, then he would go out and pray. He said, ‘The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Do not hurry away from your dinner when it is served to you.”’"],[869,"When the prayer is established and one of you is fasting, let him begin with the evening meal before the Maghrib prayer, and do not hurry away from your dinner."],[870,"'If you knew what I know, you would laugh little and weep much.'"],[871,"A man from the Anṣār, who was corpulent, said to the Prophet ﷺ, “I am not able to pray with you, so if you would come to my house and pray in it so that I may follow you.” The man prepared food for him and invited him to his house, and he spread for him an edge of a mat they had, and he prayed two rakʿahs on it. He said: Fulān b. al-Jārūd said to Anas, “Would the Prophet ﷺ pray al-ḍuḥā?” He said, “I never saw him pray it except on that day.”"],[872,"ʿAbd Allāh b. al-Arqam used to lead his companions in prayer. One day the prayer became due, so he went to relieve himself and then returned, and he said: I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say, “When one of you feels the need to defecate, let him attend to it before the prayer.”"],[873,"“None of you should pray while he is resisting the two impure things.”"],[874,"“None of you should stand up to pray when food is present, nor while he is resisting the two impure things: defecation and urination.”"],[875,"ʿItbān b. Mālik, who was one of the Anṣār and who had been present at Badr, came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and said, “O Messenger of Allah, I have noticed my eyesight has become weak, and I lead my people in prayer. When it rains, the valley between me and them floods, and I am not able to come to their mosque to lead them in prayer. I wish you, O Messenger of Allah, would come and pray in my house so that I may take it as a place of prayer.” He said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, “I will do it.” ʿItbān said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ set out early with Abū Bakr al-Ṣiddīq when the day had risen, and the Messenger of Allah ﷺ asked permission, so I gave him permission. He did not sit when he entered the house, then he said, “Where would you like me to pray in your house?” He said: So I pointed to a corner of the house, and the Messenger of Allah ﷺ stood and said the takbīr, and we stood behind him, and he prayed two rakʿahs, then he said the salām. He said: “And we detained him for a khazīrah we had prepared for him.”"],[876,"One night he found the cold to be severe, so he gave permission to those who were with him, and they prayed in their dwellings, and he said: I saw the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, when it was like this, command the people to “pray in their dwellings.”"],[877,"He gave the call to prayer on a night of cold and wind and said, “Indeed, pray in the dwellings.” Then he said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to command the muezzin, when it was a night of cold and rain, to say, “Indeed, pray in the dwellings.”"],[878,"that he called the adhān at Ḍajnān on a cold night and said to his companions: Pray in your dwellings, for the Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to instruct the mu’adhdhin to give the adhān on a rainy or cold night, and he would instruct his companions: \"Pray in your dwellings.\""],[879,"Rain fell on us at Ḥunayn, and the caller of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ called out, “Pray in the dwellings.”"],[880,"We were with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ on a journey, and we were rained upon, so he said, “Whoever wishes among you may pray in his dwelling.”"],[881,"We were with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ during the time of Hudaybiyah. Suddenly, we were hit by a rain that did not touch the ground beneath our sandals. So the Messenger of Allah ﷺ commanded his caller to announce, \"Pray in your garments.\""],[882,"When we were with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ on a journey, and it was a dark night or a rainy night, the mu'adhdhin of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ would call the adhan, or his caller would announce: 'Pray in your dwellings.'"],[883,"Garlic and onions were mentioned in the presence of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and it was said, 'O Messenger of Allah, the strongest of all that is garlic. Shall we deem it forbidden?' The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: 'Eat it, but whoever of you eats it should not come near this mosque until its odor goes away.'"],[884,"We used not to eat onions and leeks, but need overcame us and we ate them. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: 'Whoever eats of this offensive plant should not come near our mosque, for the angels are offended by what offends people.'"],[885,"He used to prohibit eating leeks and onions.'"],[886,"'Whoever eats of this plant should not come to the mosque.'"],[887,"'Whoever eats of this vegetable should not come near us in our mosques.'"],[888,"We used not to eat onions and leeks, but need overcame us and we ate them. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: 'Whoever eats of this offensive plant should not come near our mosque, for the angels are offended by what offends people.'"],[889,"'Umar b. al-Khattab gave a sermon and said: 'I saw in a dream as if a red rooster pecked me once or twice, and I think that only means the approach of my term. If my matter is hastened, then consultation is to those six men with whom the Messenger of Allah ﷺ was pleased when he died. I know that some people will criticize this matter; I fought them with this hand of mine for Islam. If they do so, then those are the enemies of Allah, the disbelievers, the misguided. I bear witness concerning the governors of the garrison towns, for I sent them only to teach the people their religion and the sunnah of their Prophet ﷺ and to distribute among them the booty. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ was never harsh with me about anything, or I never argued with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ about anything, like the verse of kalalah, until he struck my chest and said: \"The verse of summer that was revealed at the end of Surat al-Nisa' should suffice you: {They ask you for a ruling. Say: Allah gives you a ruling concerning kalalah.}\" I shall decide concerning it with a decision that whoever reads will know: it is what excludes the father. O people, you eat of two plants that I consider nothing but foul: onions and garlic. Indeed, the Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to order that a man found with their odor be sent out to al-Baqi'. Whoever must eat them should kill their odor by cooking.'"],[890,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ sent him food with vegetables including onion or leek. He did not see the trace of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ in it, so he refused to eat it. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to him: 'What prevented you from eating?' He said: 'I did not see your trace in it, O Messenger of Allah.' The Prophet ﷺ said: 'I feel shy before the angels of Allah, though it is not forbidden.'"],[891,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ stopped by us, and we prepared food for him containing some vegetables. He said to his companions: 'Eat, for I am not like any of you; I fear that I may offend my companion.'"],[892,"A bowl of tharid containing garlic was brought to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and he did not eat from it. He sent for Abu Ayyub. Abu Ayyub used to place his hand where he saw the hand of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. He placed his hand, but when he did not see the trace of the hand of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, he did not eat. He came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and said: 'I did not see the trace of your hand in it.' The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: 'It has the odor of garlic, and with me is an angel.'"],[893,"I ate garlic, then I came to the place of prayer of the Prophet ﷺ and found that he had preceded me by one rak'ah. When I stood to make it up, he noticed the odor of garlic and said: 'Whoever eats of this vegetable should not come near our mosque until its odor goes away.' Al-Mughirah said: 'When I finished the prayer, I came to him and said: O Messenger of Allah, I have an excuse. Give me your hand.' He gave me his hand, and I found it, by Allah, smooth. I put it inside my sleeve up to my chest, and he found it bandaged. He said: 'You have an excuse.'"],[894,"Worship the Most Merciful, spread peace, and feed food, and you will enter the gardens. *"],[895,"Fudayk came to the Prophet ﷺ and said, “O Messenger of Allah, they claim that whoever has not migrated is ruined.” The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, “O Fudayk, establish the prayer, avoid evil, and dwell wherever you wish in the land of your people.”"],[897,"“Convey from me even if it is a verse. And narrate from the Children of Israel, and there is no blame. And whoever lies about me deliberately, let him take his seat in the Fire.”"],[898,"While he was sitting with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, a man from the Jews came and said, “Does this funeral speak?” The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, “Allah knows best.” The Jew said, “I bear witness that it speaks.” The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, “Whatever the People of the Book narrate to you, do not believe them and do not reject them, and say: ‘We believe in Allah and His angels and His books and His messengers.’ For if it is true, you will not have rejected them, and if it is false, you will not have believed them.” And he said, “May Allah fight the Jews! They were given knowledge.”"],[899,"I said, \"Tell me of a deed that will admit me to Paradise.\" He said, \"Excellent, excellent. You have asked about a great matter, and it is easy for the one for whom Allah makes it easy: you establish the obligatory prayer, give the obligatory zakat, and do not associate anything with Allah.\""],[900,"I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ addressing us during the Farewell Pilgrimage while he was on his she-camel al-Jad'a', and he stretched up in the stirrup of the saddle and said: 'O people.' A man at the back of the people said: What are you saying or what do you want? He said: 'Do you not hear? Obey your Lord, pray your five prayers, pay the zakat of your wealth, and obey your rulers, and you will enter the Paradise of your Lord.' I said to Abu Umamah: How old were you on that day when you heard this? He said: 'I heard it when I was thirty years old.'"],[901,"I performed the Farewell Pilgrimage with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. I saw Usamah or Bilal leading the she-camel of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ by its halter, and the other raising his garment to shade him from the heat, until he threw the pebbles at Jamrat al-'Aqabah. Then he left and people stood. He had placed his garment under his right armpit over his left shoulder. He said: I saw under his right cartilage something like a fist. Then he mentioned much speech. Among what he said ﷺ was: 'If a mutilated black slave is appointed over you and leads you by the Book of Allah, then hear and obey.' Then he said: 'Have I conveyed?'"],[902,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ sent an army and placed a man in command over them. He lit a fire and said, \"Enter it.\" Some people wanted to enter it, while others said, \"We have fled from it.\" That was mentioned to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. To those who wanted to enter it, he said, \"Had you entered it, you would have remained in it until the Day of Resurrection,\" or he said, \"forever.\" To the others, he said, \"Good,\" and he said, \"You have done well. There is no obedience in disobedience to Allah; obedience is only in what is right.\""],[903,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ would pledge allegiance with us upon hearing and obedience, then he would instruct us: 'In what you are able.'"],[904,"\"O 'Ubadah.\" I said, \"At your service.\" He said, \"Listen and obey in your hardship and ease, in what you dislike, and when others are given preference over you, even if they consume your wealth and strike your back, unless it is open disobedience to Allah.\""],[905,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to his companions: \"Will you not pledge allegiance to me?\" They said: \"O Messenger of Allah, we have already pledged allegiance to you once. Upon what shall we pledge allegiance to you?\" He said: \"Pledge allegiance to me upon that you will not associate anything with Allah, that you will establish prayer, and give zakāh.\" Then he followed that with a light word: \"Upon that you will not ask people for anything.\""],[906,"Al-Hajjaj said to him: 'What prevented you from asking me?' He replied: 'Samurah b. Jundub said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"Indeed, this asking is a wound with which a man disfigures his face. So whoever wishes may preserve his face, and whoever wishes may leave it, except one who asks a person of authority, or who is faced with a matter from which he finds no alternative.\"\""],[907,"I was with Qabisah b. al-Mukhariq when a group of his people sought his help for the marriage of a man from his people, but he refused to give them anything. They left him. Kinanah said: I said to him, “You are the chief of your people, and they came to you asking, but you gave them nothing.” He said, “As for this, I will not give anything. I will tell you about that: I incurred a blood money obligation among my people, so I came to the Prophet ﷺ and told him, asking him to help me. He said, ‘Rather we will carry it on your behalf, O Qabisah, and pay it to them from the zakah camels.’ Then he said, ‘Asking is not lawful except for three: a man who has incurred a blood money obligation, for whom it is lawful until he pays it; or a man struck by a calamity that destroyed his wealth, for whom it is lawful until he obtains a sufficiency of livelihood or a means of livelihood; or a man stricken by poverty, for whom three from among the wise of his people testify that asking is lawful for him, so it is lawful for him until he obtains a sufficiency of livelihood or a means of livelihood. Asking other than that, O Qabisah, is suht.’”"],[908,"\"Indeed, asking is a wound with which a man disfigures his face. So whoever wishes may preserve his face, and whoever wishes may leave it, except one who asks a person of authority, or in a matter from which he finds no alternative.\""],[910,"\"Whoever asks while he has an uqiya, then he is importunate.\" He said: I said: 'The ruby of my camel is better than an uqiya.' He said: 'An uqiya is forty dirhams.'"],[911,"Umar b. al-Khattab gave Ibn al-Sa'di a thousand dinars, but he refused to accept them and said: I am self-sufficient from it. Umar said to him: I will tell you what the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to me: “When Allah brings you provision without your asking or coveting, take it, for Allah has given it to you.”"],[912,"I asked the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and he gave me. Then I asked him again, and he gave me. Then he said: “This wealth is sweet and green. Whoever takes it with a good soul, it will be blessed for him in it; and whoever takes it with greed of the soul, it will not be blessed for him in it, and he will be like one who eats but does not become full. The upper hand is better than the lower hand.”"],[913,"\"I came to the Prophet ﷺ with a cousin of mine\" - on an another occasion he said: \"with a companion of mine\" - \"and he said: 'When the two of you travel, call the Adhan and the Iqamah, and let the older of you lead the prayer.'\" (Using translation from Nasāʾī 634)"],[914,"The Prophet ﷺ said to me and a companion of mine, 'When you two go out, let one of you give the adhan, let him perform the iqamah, and let the older of you lead you in prayer.'"],[915,"If you are three on a journey, let one of you lead you in prayer. The one most entitled to lead you is the one among you with the most Quran."],[916,"The Prophet ﷺ commanded Sahlah, the wife of Abu Hudhayfah, to breastfeed Salim, the freed slave of Abu Hudhayfah, so that Abu Hudhayfah's jealousy would go away. She breastfed him while he was a man. Rabi'ah said: \"That was a concession for Salim.\""],[917,"Sahlah bint Suhayl came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and said: \"O Messenger of Allah, Salim is called [the son] of Abu Hudhayfah and he stays with him and enters upon me and sees me in a state of undress, while we are in a cramped house. And Allah has said: 'Call them by their fathers; it is more just in the sight of Allah' [33:5].\" He ﷺ said: \"Breastfeed him, and you will become forbidden to him.\""],[918,"Abu Hudhayfah b. 'Utbah b. Rabi'ah was one of the companions of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and had witnessed Badr. He had adopted Salim, who was called Salim the freed slave of Abu Hudhayfah, just as the Messenger of Allah ﷺ had adopted Zayd b. Harithah. Abu Hudhayfah married Salim—considering him his son—to his brother's daughter, Fatimah bint al-Walid b. 'Utbah b. Rabi'ah, who at that time was among the first of the emigrant women, and she was the best of the widowed women of Quraysh. When Allah sent down regarding Zayd b. Harithah what He sent down, He said: \"Call them by their fathers; it is more just in the sight of Allah. But if you do not know their fathers, then they are your brothers in religion and your freed slaves\" [33:5], each one who had been adopted was traced back to his father, and if his father was not known, he was traced back to his mawla. Then Sahlah bint Suhayl, the wife of Abu Hudhayfah, from Banu 'Amir b. Lu'ayy, came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and said: \"O Messenger of Allah, we used to regard Salim as a son. He used to enter upon me, and we have only one house. What do you think about his affair?\" The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"Breastfeed him with five sucklings, and he will become forbidden by your milk.\""],[919,"While I and Ibn Mas'ud were walking in the city, Uthman ibn Affan met us and took Ibn Mas'ud's hand. So they both stood up and I stepped aside. When Abdullah saw that he had no need for me to accompany him, he said, \"Come, O Alqamah.\" I then approached him while he was saying, \"Should we not marry you, Abdullah, to a girl who may remind you of what you have missed?\" Abdullah replied, \"If you say that, then indeed we were young with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ , and he said to us, 'Whoever is able to marry, let him marry, for it will help him lower his gaze and guard his chastity. And whoever is unable to marry, let him fast, for it will be a shield for him.\" And this is the Islamic castration."],[920,"I came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and embraced Islam, and he taught me the five prayers at their times. He said: I said to him: “These are hours in which I am busy, so command me with something comprehensive.” He said: “If you are busy, then do not be distracted from the two afternoon prayers.” I said: “What are the two afternoon prayers?” He said: “The morning prayer and the afternoon prayer.”"],[921,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ taught us, and among what he taught us he said: “Guard the prayers, and guard the two afternoon prayers.” I said: “O Messenger of Allah, what are the two afternoon prayers?” He said: “A prayer before sunrise and a prayer before sunset.”"],[922,"A man came to the Prophet ﷺ and asked him about found property. He said: \"Note its covering and its tie, then announce it for a year. If its owner comes, give it to him; otherwise, do as you wish with it.\" He asked about stray sheep, and he said: \"They are for you, or for your brother, or for the wolf.\" He asked about stray camels, and he said: \"What do you have to do with them? They have their own water-skins and shoes; they drink water and eat trees until their owner meets them.\""],[923,"A man came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ while I was with him and asked him about lost property. He said, \"Know its container and its tying string, then announce it for a year.\" He said, \"If no one claims it, then spend it.\" He asked about stray sheep. He said, \"It is for you, or your brother, or the wolf.\" He asked about stray camels. He said, \"They have their water-skin and their shoes; they go to water and eat trees until their owner finds them.\""],[924,"I went out with Zayd b. Ṣūḥān and Salmān b. Rabīʿah, and I picked up a whip. They said, \"Leave it.\" I said, \"By Allah, I will not leave it for wild animals to eat. I will make use of it.\" Then I came to Madinah and met Ubayy b. Kaʿb. He said, \"You did well. I once found a purse containing dinars and brought it to the Prophet ﷺ and told him. He said, 'Announce it for a year.' I did not find anyone, so I announced it for three years. Then I came to him, and he said, 'Memorize its container, its tying string, and its number. If someone comes and informs you, give it to him; otherwise, make use of it.'\""],[925,"I went out with Salmān b. Rabīʿah and Zayd b. Ṣūḥān, and I picked up a whip at al-ʿUdhayb. They said, \"Leave it.\" I said, \"I will not leave it for wild animals to eat.\" Then I came to Ubayy b. Kaʿb and told him the story. He said, \"You did well, you did well. I found a hundred dinars during the time of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and brought them to him. He said, 'Announce it.' I announced it for a year, then came to him. He said, 'Announce it.' I announced it for a year, then came to him. He said, 'Announce it.' I announced it for a year, then came to him. He said, 'Know its number, its container, and its tying string. If someone comes and informs you of its number, container, and tying string, give it to him; otherwise, make use of it.'\""],[926,"A man asked the Messenger of Allah ﷺ about stray camels. He said: \"What do you have to do with them? They have their own water-skins and shoes; leave them to eat trees and drink water until their owner finds them.\" He also asked him about stray sheep, and the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"They are for you, or for your brother, or for the wolf.\" Then he asked him about found property, and the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"Note its number, its container, and its tie. If its owner comes and knows its number, its container, and its tie, give it to him; otherwise, it is yours.\""],[927,"\"Whoever picks up a found item, let him call to witness two just persons, then he should not conceal it or alter it. If its owner comes, he has more right to it; otherwise, it is God's wealth which He gives to whomever He wills.\""],[928,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ was asked about found property. He said: \"Announce it for a year. If you do not find its owner, note its covering and its tie, then consume it; if its owner comes, return it to him.\""],[929,"“I asked the Messenger of Allah ﷺ about the sudden glance, and he commanded me to avert my gaze.”"],[930,"\"We used not to know what we should say in each rak'ah apart from glorifying, magnifying and praising our Lord. But Muhammad ﷺ taught us everything about what is good. He said: \"When you sit following every two rak'ahs, then say: At-tahiyyatu lillahi was-salawatu wat-tayyibat, as-salamu 'alaika ayyuhan-Nabiyyu wa rahmatAllahi wa baraktuhu. As-salamu 'alaina wa 'ala 'ibad illahis-salihin, ashahdu an la illaha ill-Allah wa ashhadu anna Muhammadan 'abduhu wa rasuluhu (Allah compliments, prayers and pure words are due to Allah. Peace be upon you, O Prophet, and the mercy of Allah (SWT) and his blessings. Peace be upon us and upon the righteous slaves of Allah (SWT). I bear witness that none has the right to be worshipped except Allah and I bear witness that Muhammad is His slave and Messenger), then choose any supplication that you like and call upon Allah the Mighty and Sublime with it.'\" (Using translation from Nasāʾī 1163)"],[931,"when we (prayed and) sat up during prayer along the Messenger of Allah (may peach be upon him), we said: “Peace be to Allah before it is supplicated for His servants; peace be to so and so. “The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: Do not say “Peace be to Allah ,”for Allah Himself is peace. When one of you sits(during the prayer), he should say: The adoration of the tongue are due to Allah, and acts of worship and all good things. Peace be upon you, O Prophet, and Allah’s mercy and His blessings. Peace be upon us and upon Allah’s upright servants. When you say that, it reaches every upright servant in heavens and earth or between heavens and earth. I testify that there is no god but Allah, and I testify that Muhammad is His servant and apostle. Then he may choose any supplication which pleases him and offer it. (Using translation from Abū Dāʾūd 968)"],[932,"«The Messenger of Allah ﷺ stood up from the noon prayer while he still had sitting (due). When he completed his prayer, he prostrated twice while sitting before saying the salam, and the people prostrated with him in place of the sitting he had forgotten.»"],[933,"A man said: O Messenger of Allah, how many prayers has Allah obligated upon His servants? He said: \"Five prayers.\" He said: Is there anything before them or after them? He said: \"Allah has obligated upon His servants five prayers.\" He said: Is there anything before them or after them? He said: \"Allah has obligated upon His servants five prayers.\" The man then swore by Allah that he would not add to them nor subtract from them. The Prophet ﷺ said: \"If he is truthful, he will enter Paradise.\""],[934,"He was sitting at the door of 'Umar b. 'Abd al-'Aziz during his governorship of Madinah, and with him was 'Urwah. 'Umar delayed the 'Asr prayer somewhat, so 'Urwah said to him: Indeed, Jibril descended and prayed before the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. 'Umar said: I know what you say, O 'Urwah. He said: I heard Bashir b. Abi Mas'ud say: I heard Abu Mas'ud say: I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: \"Jibril descended and prayed, so I prayed with him, then I prayed with him, then I prayed with him, then I prayed with him, then I prayed with him.\" And he counted with his fingers five prayers."],[935,"“The prayer was enjoined as two rakʿahs, two rakʿahs, in residence and in travel. Then the prayer of travel was kept as it was, and an increase was made in the prayer of residence.”"],[936,"“The first time the prayer was enjoined, in residence and in travel, it was two rakʿahs. Then an increase was made in the prayer of residence, and the prayer of travel was kept as it was.”"],[937,"\"The prayers for traveling and residing were prescribed as two units. However, when the Messenger of Allah ﷺ established the prayer, he prayed four units. The Fajr prayer was left behind due to the lengthy recitation, and the Maghrib prayer was left behind because it is the odd prayer of the day.\""],[938,"I said to ʿUmar b. al-Khaṭṭāb: “The saying of Allah, Mighty and Exalted: {There is no blame upon you} that you shorten the prayer if you fear—now the people are secure.” ʿUmar said: “I wondered at what you wondered at, so I asked the Messenger of Allah ﷺ about that. He ﷺ said: ‘A charity that Allah has given as charity to you, so accept the charity of Allah.’”"],[939,"I said to ʿUmar b. al-Khaṭṭāb: “I wonder at the people and their shortening of the prayer, when Allah has said: {There is no blame upon you} that you shorten the prayer if you fear that those who disbelieve may put you to trial. That has now passed away.” ʿUmar said: “I wondered at what you wondered at, so I mentioned that to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. He said: ‘It is a charity that Allah has given as charity to you, so accept His concession.’”"],[940,"that he said to ʿAbdullāh b. ʿUmar: \"Indeed, we find the prayer of the resident and the prayer of fear in the Quran, but we do not find the prayer of travel in the Quran?\" So ʿAbdullāh said to him: \"O son of my brother, indeed Allah sent Muhammad ﷺ to us and we do not know anything, so we only do as we have seen him do.\""],[941,"In every prayer there is recitation. Whatever the Messenger of Allah ﷺ made us hear, we make you hear, and whatever he concealed from us, we conceal from you."],[942,"There is no prayer for one who does not recite the Opening of the Book."],[943,"I was praying in the mosque when the Messenger of Allah ﷺ called me, but I did not answer him. I said, \"O Messenger of Allah, I was praying.\" He said, \"Did not Allah say, {Respond to Allah and to the Messenger when he calls you}?\" Then he said, \"Shall I not teach you a surah that is the greatest surah in the Quran?\" I said, \"Yes.\" He said, \"{Praise be to Allah, Lord of the worlds}. It is the seven oft-repeated verses and the Quran that I was given.\""],[944,"\"And the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, 'When one of you stands for prayer, let him not spit in front of him, for he is conversing with his Lord as long as he is in his prayer. Nor to his right, for there is an angel to his right. Instead, let him spit to his left or under his foot and bury it.\""],[945,"If anyone observes a prayer in which he does not recite Umm al-Qur’an, it is incomplete, it is incomplete, it is incomplete, and deficient. (The narrator said) I said: Abu Hurairah, sometime I pray behind the imam(then what should I do)? Pressing my hand he replied: O Persian, recite it inwardly, for I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ as saying that Allah, Most High, has said: I have Me and the Half for my servant and My servant will receive what he asks. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: Recite. When the servant says: “praise be to Allah, the Lord of the Universe,” Allah, Most High says: “My servant has praised me.” When the servant says: “ The Compassionate, the merciful, “Allah Most High says: “My servant has lauded me.” When the servant says: “Owner of the Day of Judgment,” Allah, Most High, says: “My servant has glorified Me” When the servant says: “ Thee do we worship and of thee we ask help. “ (Allah says) “This is between Me and My servant, and My servant will receive what he asks.” When the servant says: “ Guide us to the Straight Path, the path of those whom thou hast favoured, not ( the path) of those who earn thine anger nor of those who go astray,”(Allah says: ) “This is for My servant, and My servant will receive what he asks.” (Using translation from Abū Dāʾūd 821)"],[946,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ led us in the dawn prayer, and the recitation became heavy on him. When he finished, he said, 'I see that you are reciting behind your imam.' We said, 'Yes, O Messenger of Allah, this is so.' He said, 'Do not do so, except with the Mother of the Book, for there is no prayer for one who does not recite it.'"],[947,"There is no prayer for one who does not recite the Mother of the Qur'an and more."],[948,"A man came while the Messenger of Allah ﷺ was in the mosque, and he prayed near him. Then he went to him and greeted him. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to him, 'Repeat your prayer, for you have not prayed.' He returned and prayed as he had prayed before, then came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to him, 'Repeat your prayer, for you have not prayed.' The man said, 'O Messenger of Allah, how should I do?' He said, 'When you face the qiblah, say takbir, then recite the Mother of the Qur'an, then recite whatever you wish. When you bow, place your palms on your knees and stretch your back. When you raise your head, straighten your spine until the bones return to their joints. When you prostrate, make your prostration firm. When you raise your head, sit on your left thigh. Then do that in every rak'ah.'"],[949,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ finished a prayer in which he had recited aloud and said: “Did any of you recite just now?” A man said: Yes, I did, O Messenger of Allah. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “I say: What is the matter with me that I am contended with regarding the Qur’an?” Then the people stopped reciting in the prayers in which the Messenger of Allah ﷺ recited aloud, when they heard that from the Messenger of Allah ﷺ."],[950,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ prayed a prayer in which he recited aloud, and some people recited along with him. When he said the salam, he said: “Did any of you recite?” They said: Yes, O Messenger of Allah. He said: “I say: What is the matter with me that I am contended with regarding the Qur’an?” He said: “So the Muslims took admonition from that, and they would not recite.”"],[951,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ led us in a prayer in which he recited aloud. When he said the salam, he said: “Did any of you recite with me just now?” They said: Yes, O Messenger of Allah. He said: “I say: What is the matter with me that I am contended with regarding the Qur’an?”"],[952,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ prayed with his companions, and when he finished his prayer he turned to face them and said: “Do you recite in your prayer behind the imam while the imam is reciting?” They remained silent. He said it three times. Then a man or men said: We do. He said: “Do not do so; let each of you recite the Fatihah of the Book silently to himself.”"],[953,"“In every prayer there is recitation.” Whatever the Messenger of Allah ﷺ made us hear, we make you hear; and whatever he concealed from us, we conceal from you."],[954,"Every prayer in which the Opening of the Book is not recited is deficient. Every prayer in which the Opening of the Book is not recited is deficient. Every prayer in which the Opening of the Book is not recited is deficient."],[955,"A prayer in which the Opening of the Book is not recited is not valid.' I said, 'Even if I am behind the imam?' He took my hand and said, 'Recite it to yourself.'"],[956,"I heard Abu Humayd al-Sa'idi among ten of the Companions of the Prophet ﷺ, among them Abu Qatadah. Abu Humayd said, 'I am the most knowledgeable among you concerning the prayer of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ.' They said, 'Why? By Allah, you were not the most frequent of us in following him, nor the earliest of us in his companionship.' He said, 'Yes, I was.' They said, 'Then describe it.' He said, 'When the Messenger of Allah ﷺ stood for prayer, he said takbir and raised his hands until they were level with his shoulders, and kept every bone in its position. Then he recited. Then he raised his hands until they were level with his shoulders. Then he bowed and placed his palms on his knees, straight, not lowering his head nor drawing it in. He said, \"Allah hears those who praise Him,\" and raised his hands until they were level with his shoulders, until every bone returned to its position. Then he went down to the ground and kept his hands away from his sides. Then he raised his head and folded his leg and sat on it, and spread the toes of his feet when he prostrated. Then he prostrated. Then he said takbir and sat on his left leg until every bone returned to its position. Then he stood up and did the same in the other rak'ah. Then when he stood up from the two rak'ahs, he raised his hands until they were level with his shoulders, just as he did at the beginning of the prayer. Then he prayed the rest of his prayer in this way, until when he was in the prostration in which there is the taslim, he brought out his legs and sat on his left side, mutawarrikan.' They said, 'You have spoken the truth. This is how the Prophet ﷺ used to pray.'"],[957,"\"Ka'b bin Ujrah said to me: 'Shall I not give you a gift?' We said: \"O Messenger of Allah ﷺ, we know about sending salams upon you, but how should we send salah upon you?\" He said: 'Say: Alahumma salli 'ala Muhammad wa 'ala ali Muhammad, kama sallaita 'ala Ibrahima wa barik 'ala Muhammad kama barakta 'ala ali Ibrahim fil-'alamin, innaka hamidun majid (O Allah, send salah upon Muhammad and upon the family of Muhammad, as You sent salah upon the family of Ibrahim, and send blessings upon Muhammad and upon the family of Muhammad as You sent blessings upon the family of Ibrahim among the nations. You are indeed Worthy of praise, Full of glory.)'\" (Using translation from Nasāʾī 1289)"],[958,"Whoever sends prayers upon me once, ten good deeds are recorded for him."],[959,"\"We used to not know what to say in prayer until the Prophet ﷺ taught us to say, 'Peace be upon Allah, peace be upon Jibril, peace be upon Mika'il.' Then he taught us to say, 'The greetings are for Allah, and the prayers and good deeds. Peace be upon you, O Prophet, and the mercy of Allah and His blessings. Peace be upon us and upon the righteous servants of Allah.' Abu Wail reported in his hadith from Abdullah that the Prophet ﷺ said, 'When you say it, it reaches every righteous servant in the heavens and on the earth.' And Abu Ishaq reported in his hadith from Abdullah that the Prophet ﷺ said, 'When you say it, it reaches every near and distant servant, prophetic messenger, or righteous servant. I bear witness that there is no god but Allah, and I bear witness that Muhammad is His servant and messenger.'\""],[960,"His father said: \"We said: 'O Messenger of Allah, how should we send salah upon you?' He said: 'Say: Alahumma salli 'ala Muhammad wa 'ala ali Muhammad, kama sallaita 'ala Ibrahima wa barik 'ala Muhammad kama barakta 'ala ali Ibrahim fil-'alamin, innaka hamidun majid (O Allah, send salah upon Muhammad and upon the family of Muhammad, as You sent salah upon the family of Ibrahim, and send blessings upon Muhammad and upon the family of Muhammad as You sent blessings upon the family of Ibrahim among the nations. You are indeed Worthy of praise, Full of glory.)'\" (Using translation from Nasāʾī 1290)"],[961,"\"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ came to us in the Majlis of Sa'd bin 'Ubadah and Bashir bin Sa'd said to him: 'Allah has commanded us to send Salah upon you, O Messenger of Allah; so how should we send salah upon you?' The Messenger of Allah ﷺ remained silent until we wished that he had not asked him. Then he said: 'Say: 'Alahumma salli 'ala Muhammad wa 'ala ali Muhammad, kama sallaita 'ala Ibrahima wa barik 'ala Muhammad kama barakta 'ala ali Ibrahim fil-'alamin, innaka hamidun majid (O Allah, send salah upon Muhammad and upon the family of Muhammad, as You sent salah upon the family of Ibrahim, and send blessings upon Muhammad and upon the family of Muhammad as You sent blessings upon the family of Ibrahim among the nations. You are indeed Worthy of praise, Full of glory.)\" And the salam is as you know.'\" (Using translation from Nasāʾī 1285)"],[962,"Narrated Abu Mas'ud:A man came and sat in front of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and said, \"O Messenger of Allah, we know how to send greetings upon you, but how should we pray for you when we are already praying in our own prayers? Allah sends His blessings upon you, so how should we send blessings upon you?\" The Prophet ﷺ remained silent until we wished that the man had not asked him. Then he said, \"When you pray, say: 'O Allah, send blessings upon Muhammad, the Prophet who cannot read or write, and upon the family of Muhammad, as You sent blessings upon Ibrahim, and upon the family of Ibrahim. And bless Muhammad, the Prophet who cannot read or write, and the family of Muhammad, as You blessed Ibrahim and the family of Ibrahim. Verily, You are full of praise and majesty.'\" Source: Sunan Ibn Majah 927"],[963,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ heard a man supplicating in his prayer without praising Allah or sending prayers upon the Prophet ﷺ. The Prophet ﷺ said, 'This one has been hasty.' Then he called him and said to him, 'When one of you prays, let him begin with praising Allah and extolling Him, then let him send prayers upon the Prophet ﷺ, then let him supplicate after that with whatever he wishes.'"],[964,"\"And indeed the Prophet ﷺ took the hand of Abdullah and taught him the tashahhud in prayer: 'All greetings, blessings and good things are due to Allah. Peace be upon you, O Prophet, and the mercy of Allah and His blessings. Peace be upon us and upon the righteous servants of Allah. Zuhayr said, 'I memorized it from Al-Hasan's handwriting and he narrated it from his memory. I bear witness that there is no god but Allah, and I bear witness that Muhammad is His servant and messenger.' Zuhayr said, 'Then I went back to my own memorization and said, 'When you say this, you have completed your prayer. If you want to stand up, then stand up, and if you want to sit, then sit.'\""],[965,"'Alqamah took my hand, and Ibn Mas'ud took 'Alqamah's hand, and the Prophet ﷺ took Ibn Mas'ud's hand and taught him the tashahhud: 'All compliments, prayers, and good things are due to Allah. Peace be upon you, O Prophet, and the mercy of Allah and His blessings. Peace be upon us and upon the righteous servants of Allah. I bear witness that there is no god but Allah, and I bear witness that Muhammad is His servant and Messenger.' 'Abd Allah b. Mas'ud said, 'When you have completed this, you have completed your prayer. If you wish, remain seated, and if you wish, depart.'"],[966,"'Alqamah b. Qays took my hand and said: 'Abd Allah b. Mas'ud took my hand and said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ took my hand and taught me the tashahhud: 'All compliments, prayers, and good things are due to Allah. Peace be upon you, O Prophet, and the mercy of Allah and His blessings. Peace be upon us and upon the righteous servants of Allah. I bear witness that there is no god but Allah, and I bear witness that Muhammad is His servant and Messenger.'"],[967,"There is no charity on less than five camels, nor on less than five uqiyyahs of silver, nor on less than five awsuq of grains or dates."],[968,"There is no ṣadaqah on grains or dates below five wasqs, no ṣadaqah on what is below five camels, and no ṣadaqah on what is below five ounces."],[969,"No zakāh is due on wheat or dates until it reaches five wasqs, no zakāh is due on silver until it reaches five ounces, and no zakāh is due on camels until it reaches five camels."],[970,"“The Messenger of Allah ﷺ made obligatory a tenth on what the sky, rivers, and springs water, or what is athari; and half a tenth on what is irrigated by nadih.”"],[971,"When Abu Bakr al-Siddiq was appointed caliph, he wrote this letter for him when he sent him to Yemen: 'In the name of Allah, the Most Gracious, the Most Merciful. This is the obligatory charity that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ imposed upon the Muslims, which Allah commanded His Messenger. Whoever is asked for it among the Muslims in its proper manner should give it, and whoever is asked for more than that should not give it. For twenty-four camels or less, the zakah is sheep: one sheep for every five. When they reach twenty-five to thirty-five, a one-year-old female camel (bint makhad) is due. If there is no bint makhad, then a two-year-old male camel (ibn labun). When they reach thirty-six to forty-five, a two-year-old female camel (bint labun) is due. When they reach forty-six to sixty, a three-year-old female camel (hiqqah) that can be mounted by a male camel is due. When they reach sixty-one to seventy-five, a four-year-old female camel (jadha'ah) is due. When they reach seventy-six to ninety, two bint labun are due. When they reach ninety-one to one hundred and twenty, two hiqqah are due. If they exceed one hundred and twenty, then for every forty, one bint labun, and for every fifty, one hiqqah. And whoever has camels that reach the age for jadha'ah as zakah, but he does not have a jadha'ah and has a hiqqah, the hiqqah will be accepted from him, and he should add two sheep or twenty dirhams. And whoever has camels that reach the age for hiqqah as zakah, but he does not have a hiqqah and has a jadha'ah, the jadha'ah will be accepted from him, and the collector should give him twenty dirhams or two sheep. And whoever has camels that reach the age for hiqqah as zakah, but he only has a bint labun, it will be accepted from him, and he should give two sheep or twenty dirhams. And whoever has camels that reach the age for bint labun as zakah, but he only has a hiqqah, the hiqqah will be accepted from him, and the collector should give him twenty dirhams or two sheep. And whoever has camels that reach the age for bint labun as zakah, but he does not have it, a bint makhad will be accepted from him, and he should add twenty dirhams or two sheep. And whoever has camels that reach the age for bint makhad as zakah, but he does not have it and has a bint labun, the bint labun will be accepted from him, and the collector should give him twenty dirhams or two sheep. And whoever does not have a bint makhad but has an ibn labun, it will be accepted from him, and nothing else is required. And whoever has only four camels, there is no charity on them unless their owner wishes. When they reach five camels, one sheep is due. The charity on sheep: for every forty pasturing sheep up to one hundred and twenty, one sheep is due. If they exceed one hundred and twenty up to two hundred, two sheep are due. If they exceed two hundred up to three hundred, three sheep are due. If they exceed three hundred, then for every hundred, one sheep is due. No old, defective, or male goat is to be taken as charity unless the collector wishes. Separate herds should not be combined, and combined herds should not be separated for fear of charity. If two partners have mixed livestock, they should share the charity equally between them. If a man's pasturing sheep are forty minus one, there is no charity on them unless their owner wishes. On silver, one-quarter of one-tenth is due. If there is only one hundred and ninety dirhams, there is no charity on them unless their owner wishes.'"],[972,"I used to perfume the Messenger of Allah ﷺ for his ihram before he entered ihram, and for his exit from ihram before he circumambulated the House."],[973,"It is as if I am looking at the glisten of perfume on the head of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ while he was in ihram."],[974,"It is as if I am looking at the glisten of musk in the parting of the hair of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ while he was in ihram."],[975,"I perfumed the Messenger of Allah ﷺ before he entered ihram and on the Day of Sacrifice before he circumambulated the House, with perfume containing musk."],[976,"The Prophet of Allah ﷺ, when he reached Dhū al-Ḥulayfah, marked the sacrificial animal on the right side of its hump, then wiped away the blood and garlanded it with his two sandals. Then he mounted his riding camel, and when it stood upright with him at al-Baydāʾ, he entered iḥrām and pronounced the talbiyah for Hajj."],[977,"The Prophet ﷺ said to Duba'ah, \"Perform Hajj and stipulate, 'My place of exiting ihram is wherever You restrain me.'\""],[978,"The Prophet ﷺ entered upon Duba'ah bt. al-Zubayr b. 'Abd al-Muttalib while she was ill and said to her, \"Perform Hajj and stipulate, 'My place of exiting ihram is wherever You restrain me.'\""],[979,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ resided in Madinah for nine years without performing ḥajj. Then he announced to the people to set out. When he reached Dhū al-Ḥulayfah, he prayed at Dhū al-Ḥulayfah, and Asmāʾ bt. ʿUmays gave birth to Muḥammad b. Abī Bakr. She sent a message to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Bathe, wrap yourself with a cloth, and assume iḥrām.” He said: “She did so. When the chest of the Messenger of Allah’s ﷺ riding camel settled upon the open desert, he assumed iḥrām and we too assumed iḥrām, knowing nothing but ḥajj—for that we had set out—while the Messenger of Allah ﷺ was among us and the Qurʾān was being sent down upon him, and he knew its interpretation, and he only did what he was commanded.” Jābir said: “I looked in front of me, behind me, to my right, and to my left as far as my sight could reach, and the people were on foot and riding. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ began to say the talbiyah: ‘Labbayka allāhumma labbayka, labbayka lā sharīka laka labbayka, inna al-ḥamda wa al-niʿmata laka wa al-mulka lā sharīka laka.’ When we arrived in Makkah, he began by touching the corner, then he hastened in three circuits and walked in four. When he finished his ṭawāf, he went to the Maqām and said: ‘Allah said: “And take the Station of Ibrāhīm as a place of prayer.”’ Then he prayed two rakʿahs behind the Station of Ibrāhīm, then he went to the corner and touched it, then he went to al-Ṣafā and said: ‘We begin with what Allah began with: “Indeed, al-Ṣafā and al-Marwah are among the symbols of Allah.”’ He climbed al-Ṣafā until the House appeared to him, and he said the takbīr three times and said: ‘There is no god but Allah alone, with no partner; His is the dominion and His is the praise; He gives life and death; in His hand is all good, and He has power over all things’ three times. Then he supplicated. Then he descended from al-Ṣafā and walked until, when his feet went down into the bottom of the watercourse, he hastened; then when his feet climbed out of the watercourse, he walked to al-Marwah. He climbed al-Marwah until the House appeared to him, and he said the like of what he had said on al-Ṣafā. He performed seven rounds and said: ‘Whoever does not have a sacrificial animal, let him exit iḥrām; whoever has a sacrificial animal, let him remain in his iḥrām. Were it not that I have a sacrificial animal, I would have exited iḥrām; and had I known beforehand what came later, I would have assumed iḥrām for ʿumrah.’” He said: “ʿAlī arrived from Yemen, and the Prophet ﷺ said to him: ‘With what did you assume iḥrām, O ʿAlī?’ He said: ‘I said: O Allah, I assume iḥrām with what Your Messenger has assumed iḥrām.’ He said: ‘I have a sacrificial animal, so do not exit iḥrām.’” ʿAlī said: “I entered upon Fāṭimah, and she had applied kohl and worn dyed clothes. I said: ‘Who ordered you to do this?’ She said: ‘My father ﷺ ordered me.’” He said: “ʿAlī used to say in Iraq: I went to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, angry with Fāṭimah, seeking to verify what she had said. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: ‘She has spoken truth; I ordered her.’” He said: “The Messenger of Allah ﷺ slaughtered one hundred camels; with his own hand he slaughtered sixty-three, and ʿAlī slaughtered the rest. Then he took a piece from each camel and cooked them all together, and they both ate of the meat and drank of the broth. Then Surāqah b. Mālik b. Juʿshum said: ‘Is this for this year of ours or forever?’ He said: ‘No, rather forever; the ʿumrah has entered into the ḥajj.’”"],[980,"The hand of a thief is not amputated except for a quarter dinar or more."],[981,"We were informed by Al-Qa'nabi, who said that Malik narrated from Nafi' who narrated from Ibn Umar, who said, \"The Prophet ﷺ cut a male camel that was worth three dirhams.\""],[982,"We went out with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ in the year of Hunayn. When we met, the Muslims had a turn of flight. He said: I saw a man of the polytheists mount a man of the Muslims. He said: So I turned my back until I came at him from behind, and struck him on the vein of his shoulder with a blow that cut the armor from him. He said: He faced me and squeezed me in a squeeze in which I found the smell of death; then death overtook him, so he released me. I caught up with Umar b. al-Khattab and said to him: 'What is the matter with the people?' He said: 'The command of Allah.' He said: Then the people returned. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: 'Whoever kills a slain man and has proof for him, his spoil is his.' Abu Qatada said: I stood up, then said: 'Who will testify for me?' Then I sat down. Then the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: 'Whoever kills a slain man and has proof for him, his spoil is his.' I stood up, then said: 'Who will testify for me?' Then I sat down. Then he said it a third time, so I stood up. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: 'What is the matter with you, O Abu Qatada?' So I related the story to him. A man of the people said: 'He has spoken the truth, O Messenger of Allah, and the spoil of that slain man is with me; so satisfy him from me.' Abu Bakr said: 'No, by Allah, then a lion of the lions of Allah who fights for Allah and His Messenger would not intend to give you his spoil.' The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: 'Give it to him.' Abu Qatada said: So he gave it to me. I sold the armor and bought from it a garden in the Banu Salama, and it was the first wealth I acquired in Islam."],[983,"We raided with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ against Hawazin. While we were sitting taking our midday rest, a man on a red camel drew out a leather strap from the camel’s saddle and tied his camel with it. Then he came and sat with us to eat lunch. He looked at the faces of the people, and their backs were thin and most of them were on foot. When he looked at the faces of the people, he went out running until he came to his camel and sat on it, urging it on, and he was a scout for the disbelievers. A man from us of Aslam followed him on a grayish-brown she-camel. Iyas said: My father said: I followed him running, and I drew my sword and struck his head. Then I came with his she-camel, leading it, and on it were his spoils. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ met me with the people and said: «Who killed the man?» Ibn al-Akwa‘ said: “I did.” He said: «All his spoils are yours.»"],[984,"We came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ while we were young men close in age, and we stayed with him for twenty nights. He thought that we had missed our families, so he asked us about whom we had left among our families, and we told him. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ was compassionate and gentle, so he said, “Return to your families, teach them, command them, and pray as you have seen me pray. When the prayer time arrives, let one of you call the adhan, and let the oldest of you lead you.”"],[985,"Abdullah ibn AbuBakr reported that he heard Urwah say: I entered upon Marwan ibn al-Hakam. We mentioned things that render the ablution void. Marwan said: Does it become void by touching the penis? Urwah replied: This I do not know. Marwan said: Busrah daughter of Safwan reported to me that she heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: He who touches his penis should perform ablution. (Using translation from Abū Dāʾūd 181)"],[986,"She said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “When one of you touches his penis, let him perform wudu’.”"],[987,"She said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Whoever touches his private part, let him perform wudu’.”"],[988,"She said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Whoever touches his private part, let him repeat the wudu’.”"],[989,"She said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Whoever touches his penis, let him perform wudu’ as he does for prayer.”"],[990,"She said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “When one of you touches his private part, let him perform wudu’, and the woman is like that.”"],[991,"She said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “When one of you brings his hand to his private part with no cover or barrier between them, let him perform wudu’.”"],[992,"He said: We went out as a delegation to the Prophet ﷺ, and a man came and said: “O Prophet of Allah, what do you say about a man touching his penis after he has performed wudu’?” He said: “Is it but a morsel or a piece of him?”"],[993,"He said: We were with the Prophet ﷺ when a Bedouin came to him and said: “O Messenger of Allah, one of us may be in prayer and scratch himself, and his hand touches his penis.” The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Is it but a piece of you or a morsel of you?”"],[994,"He said: I asked the Prophet ﷺ about a man touching his penis while he is in prayer. He said: “There is no harm in it; it is but a part of your body.”"],[995,"He said: I built the mosque of Madinah with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and he would say: “Bring the Yamami forward with the clay, for he is the best of you at handling it.”*"],[997,"The intensity of fever is from the heat of Hell, so cool it with water."],[998,"Fever is from the heat of Hell, so extinguish it with water."],[999,"I used to keep people away from Ibn Abbas. I was detained for some days, and he said: 'What detained you?' I said: 'Fever.' He said: 'The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"Fever is from the heat of Hell, so cool it with Zamzam water.\"\""],[1000,"Accept the feast, when you are invited. (Using translation from Muslim 1429d)"],[1002,"\"When one of you is invited, let him accept; then if he wishes, he may eat, and if he wishes, he may leave.\""],[1003,"\"The worst food is the wedding feast to which the rich are invited and the poor are left out. Whoever does not accept the invitation has disobeyed Allah and His Messenger.\""],[1004,"\"The worst food is the wedding feast to which the rich are invited and the poor are left out. Whoever does not accept the invitation has disobeyed Allah and His Messenger.\""],[1005,"\"When one of you is invited, let him accept. If he is fasting, let him pray; if he is not fasting, let him eat.\""],[1006,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ entered upon us while the people were raising their hands. The narrator Zubair said: I think( they were raising the hands) during prayer. He (the prophet) said: What is the matter, I see you raising your hands as if they are the tails of restive horses! Maintain tranquility during prayer. (Using translation from Abū Dāʾūd 1000)"],[1007,"He entered the mosque and saw people raising their hands. He said, 'They have raised them as if they were the tails of restless horses. Be still in prayer.'"],[1008,"When we prayed behind the Prophet ﷺ, we used to gesture with our hands, saying 'Peace be upon you' to the right and to the left. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, 'What is wrong with me, seeing your hands as if they were the tails of restless horses? It is enough for one of you to place his hands on his thigh, then say taslim to his right and to his left.'"],[1009,"When we were with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, one of us would raise his hand to the right and to the left. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"What is the matter with me that I see you raising your hands as if they were tails of restive horses? Is it not enough for one of you to place his hand on his thigh and then give the greeting of peace to the one on his right and the one on his left?\""],[1010,"\"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ commanded that Zakat al-Fitr be a saʿ of dates or a saʿ of barley.\" ʿAbd Allah b. ʿUmar said: People made its equivalent two mudds of wheat."],[1011,"\"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ made Zakat al-Fitr of Ramadan obligatory upon the people: a saʿ of dates or a saʿ of barley upon every free person and slave, male and female, among the Muslims.\""],[1012,"\"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ made Zakat al-Fitr of Ramadan obligatory upon every Muslim soul, free or slave, male or female, young or old: a saʿ of dates or a saʿ of barley.\""],[1013,"\"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ made Zakat al-Fitr obligatory: a saʿ of dates or a saʿ of barley upon the free and the slave, the male and the female among the Muslims, and he commanded that it be given before the people go out to the prayer.\""],[1014,"\"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ commanded Zakat al-Fitr: a saʿ of dates or a saʿ of barley for every Muslim, young or old, free or slave.\" Ibn ʿUmar said: \"Then people made its equivalent two mudds of wheat.\""],[1015,"Abu Hurairah reported the Apostle of Allaah ﷺ as saying There are five(creatures) the killing of which is lawful in the sacred territory. The Snake, the Scorpion, the Kite, the Rat and the biting Dog. (Using translation from Abū Dāʾūd 1847)"],[1016,"“Five harmful creatures are to be killed in the sacred and the non-sacred precincts: the scorpion, the kite, the pied crow, the mouse, and the vicious dog.”"],[1017,"The sun eclipsed during the time of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ on the day Ibrahim died. The people said, “The sun eclipsed only because of Ibrahim’s death.” The Prophet ﷺ said, “The sun and the moon are two signs among the signs of Allah. They do not eclipse because of anyone’s death or life. So when you see that, supplicate and pray until it clears.”"],[1018,"On the day the sun eclipsed, the Messenger of Allah ﷺ prayed four rak‘ahs in two rak‘ahs and four prostrations."],[1019,"The sun eclipsed during the time of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ prayed, and the people with him. He stood for a long time, about the length of Surat al-Baqarah. Then he bowed for a long time. Then he rose and stood for a long time, but less than the first standing. Then he bowed for a long time, but less than the first bowing. Then he prostrated. Then he stood for a long time, but less than the first standing. Then he bowed for a long time, but less than the first bowing. Then he rose and stood for a long time, but less than the first standing. Then he bowed for a long time, but less than the first bowing. Then he prostrated. Then he finished, and the sun had cleared. He said, “The sun and the moon are two signs among the signs of Allah. They do not eclipse because of anyone’s death or life. So when you see that, remember Allah.” They said, “O Messenger of Allah, we saw you reach for something in your standing place, then we saw you step back.” He said, “I saw Paradise—or Paradise was shown to me—and I reached for a bunch of grapes. Had I taken it, you would have eaten from it as long as the world remains. And I saw the Fire, and I have never seen a sight like today. I saw that most of its inhabitants were women.” They said, “Why, O Messenger of Allah?” He said, “Because of their ingratitude.” It was said, “Do they disbelieve in Allah?” He said, “They are ungrateful to their husbands and ungrateful for kindness. If you were to treat one of them kindly for a lifetime, then she saw something from you, she would say, ‘By Allah, I have never seen any good from you.’”"],[1020,"\"When you hear the muezzin, say the like of what he says.\""],[1021,"I was with Mu'awiyah, and the muezzin said: \"Allahu akbar, Allahu akbar,\" and Mu'awiyah said: \"Allahu akbar, Allahu akbar.\" Then he said: \"Ashhadu an la ilaha illa Allah,\" and Mu'awiyah said: \"Ashhadu an la ilaha illa Allah.\" Then he said: \"Ashhadu anna Muhammadan rasul Allah,\" and Mu'awiyah said: \"Ashhadu anna Muhammadan rasul Allah.\" Then he said: \"Hayya 'ala al-salah,\" and Mu'awiyah said: \"La hawla wa la quwwata illa billah.\" Then he said: \"Hayya 'ala al-falah,\" and Mu'awiyah said: \"La hawla wa la quwwata illa billah.\" Then he said: \"Allahu akbar, Allahu akbar, la ilaha illa Allah,\" and Mu'awiyah said: \"Allahu akbar, Allahu akbar, la ilaha illa Allah.\" Then he said: \"Thus the Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to say.\""],[1022,"Remove both or wear both. When you put on clothes, start with the right, and when you take them off, start with the left."],[1023,"'When one of you prays and removes his sandals, let him not harm anyone with them. Let him place them between his feet, or let him pray in them.'"],[1024,"\"The Qur'an was revealed in seven modes, and disputing about the Qur'an is disbelief\" – three times. \"Whatever of it you know, act upon it; and whatever of it you are ignorant of, refer it to its knower.\""],[1025,"\"The Quran was sent down in seven ahruf. For every verse of it there is an outward and an inward meaning.\""],[1026,"Do not face the Qiblah with urine or feces, nor turn your backs to it, but rather face east or west."],[1027,"I climbed to the top of Hafsah's house and saw the Prophet ﷺ sitting on his backside, facing the Qiblah with his back toward Syria (i.e., relieving himself)."],[1028,"Some of our men had surplus lands that they used to rent out for one-third, one-fourth, or one-half [of the produce]. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, “Whoever has surplus land, let him cultivate it himself or let him give it to his brother to cultivate. If he refuses, let him retain his land.”"],[1029,"“Whoever has land, let him cultivate it. If he is unable to do so, let him grant it to his brother.”"],[1030,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ forbade us from something that was convenient for us. I said, “Whatever the Messenger of Allah ﷺ says is true.” He said, “What do you do with your cultivated fields?” We said, “We rent them out for one-third, one-fourth, and certain measures of wheat and barley.” He said, “Do not do that. Cultivate them yourselves or let them be cultivated.”"],[1031,"Allah loves sneezing and dislikes yawning. When one of you yawns, let him suppress it as much as he can, or let him place his hand over his mouth. For when he yawns and says 'aah', it is only Satan laughing from inside him."],[1032,"\"We went out with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ on one of his journeys, and when we were in Al-Baida' or Dhat Al-Jaish, a necklace of mine broke and fell. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ stayed there looking for it and the people stayed with him. There was no water near them, and they did not have water with them. The people came to Abu Bakr, may Allah be pleased with him, and said: 'Do you see what 'Aishah has done? She has made the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and the people stop and they are not near any water and they do not have water with them.' Abu Bakr, may Allah be pleased with him, came while the Messenger of Allah ﷺ was resting his head on my thigh and had gone to sleep. He said: 'You have detained the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and the people, and they are not near any water and they do not have any water with them.'\" 'Aishah said: \"Abu Bakr rebuked me and said whatever Allah willed he would say. He started poking me on my hip, and the only thing that prevented me from moving was the fact that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ was resting on my thigh. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ slept until morning when he woke up without any water. Then Allah, the Mighty and Sublime revealed the verse of Tayammum. Usaid bin Hudair said: 'This is not the first time we have been blessed because of you, O family of Abu Bakr!'\" She said: \"Then we made the camel that I had been riding stand up, and we found the necklace beneath it.\" (Using translation from Nasāʾī 310)"],[1033,"\"What prevented you, O so-and-so, from praying with the people?\" He said, \"O Messenger of Allah, I was afflicted by major ritual impurity and there is no water.\" The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, \"Use clean earth, for it suffices you.\" Then the Messenger of Allah ﷺ traveled on, and the people complained to him of thirst. He said: So he dismounted and summoned so-and-so—Abu Raja' used to name him but 'Awf forgot it—and summoned 'Ali, and said, \"Go and search for water for us.\" They met a woman between two water skins, or two flat leather water bags, full of water on a camel of hers. They said to her, \"Where is water?\" She said, \"My last sighting of water was yesterday at this hour, and our men have gone out to seek water.\" He said: So they said to her, \"Come with us, then.\" She said, \"To where?\" They said, \"To the Messenger of Allah ﷺ.\" She said, \"This one who is called the Sabian?\" They said, \"He is the one you mean; so come with us, then.\" They brought her to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and related the story to him. He said: So they made her dismount from her camel, and the Messenger of Allah ﷺ called for a vessel, into which he poured from the mouths of the two water skins, or the two flat leather water bags. He tied their mouths and loosened the spouts, and it was announced among the people: \"Draw water and give water.\" He said: So he gave drink to whom he wished, and drew water for whom he wished. The last of that was that the one who had been afflicted by major ritual impurity was given a vessel of water, and he said, \"Go and pour it over yourself.\" He said: And she was standing watching what was being done with her water. He said: By Allah, when it was lifted from her, it seemed to us that it was more full than when it was first started with. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, \"Gather food for her.\" He said: So they gathered for her from pressed dates, flour, and barley meal until they had gathered much food for her. They placed it in a cloth and mounted her on her camel, and put the cloth before her. He said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to her, \"Do you know that, by Allah, we did not diminish anything from your water? But it was Allah who gave us to drink.\" He said: So she came to her people, having been detained from them. They said, \"What detained you, O so-and-so?\" She said, \"The wonder: two men met me and took me to this one who is called the Sabian, and he did such and such with me. By Allah, he is either the greatest sorcerer between this and this, or he is truly the Messenger of Allah ﷺ.\" He said: After that, the Muslims used to raid the polytheists around her, but they would not strike the small group of tents in which she was. She said to her people, \"By Allah, these people are deliberately leaving you alone. Would you accept Islam?\" They obeyed her and entered Islam."],[1034,"Some sheep from the zakāt gathered with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. He said, “Go out, O Abū Dharr.” I went out with them to al-Rabadha. Five or six days would pass over me while I was junub, and I found unease in myself. I came to the Prophet ﷺ while he was leaning his back against the room. When he saw me, he said, “What is wrong with you, O Abū Dharr?” I sat down. He said, “What is wrong with you, O Abū Dharr? May your mother be bereaved of you.” I said, “O Messenger of Allah, I am junub.” He commanded a black slave girl, and she came with a vessel containing water. I screened myself with the camel and a cloth and washed. It was as if a mountain had been lifted from me. He said, “Come close. Clean earth is the ablution of a Muslim, even if for ten years. When he finds water, let him apply water to his skin.”"],[1035,"\"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: 'Clean earth is the Wudu' of the Muslim, even if he does not find water for ten years.'\" (Using translation from Nasāʾī 322)"],[1036,"I asked the Prophet ﷺ about tayammum, and he commanded me to do the face and the palms with one strike."],[1037,"I was sitting with 'Abdullah and Abu Musa, and Abu Musa said, \"O Abu 'Abd al-Rahman, a man becomes junub and does not find water—should he pray?\" He said, \"No.\" He said, \"Do you not remember what 'Ammar said to 'Umar: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ sent me and you, and I became junub, so I rolled in the dust, then came to the Prophet ﷺ and mentioned that to him. He said, 'It would have sufficed you to do like this,' and he struck the ground with his hand, then wiped his face and palms.\" He said, \"I did not see 'Umar satisfied with that.\" He said, \"What do you do with this verse: {And if you do not find water, then perform tayammum with clean earth}?\" He said, \"Indeed, if we granted them this concession, one of them would, when he found the water cold, perform tayammum with clean earth.\" Ya'la added: Al-A'mash said: I said to Shaqiq, \"This was only because of that.\""],[1038,"A man asked 'Umar: \"I became junub and found no water.\" He said: \"Do not pray.\" 'Ammar said: \"Do you not remember when you and I were on an expedition during the time of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ?\" He mentioned that to him, and he ﷺ said: \"It would have been enough for you,\" and he struck the ground with his hand once, blew into his palms, and wiped his face and his palms."],[1039,"We performed tayammum with the Prophet ﷺ up to the shoulders."],[1040,"While we were with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ on a journey, a woman was on a she-camel of hers. She became impatient and cursed it, so the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: «Take your belongings off it and let it go, for it is cursed.» He said: So they did. It is as if I can see it now, a dark grey she-camel."],[1041,"While the Messenger of Allah ﷺ was on one of his journeys, he heard a curse, and said: «Who is this?» It was said: «This is so-and-so, she cursed her mount.» The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: «Unload it, for it is cursed.» He said: So it was unloaded. 'Imran said: «It is as if I can see it now, a dark grey she-camel.»"],[1042,"We travelled with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ while he was seeking Majdi b. 'Amr al-Juhani. The water-carrying camel would be ridden in turns by five, six, or seven of us. The turn of a man from the Ansar came near, so he made his camel kneel and mounted it, then he urged it on. It balked under him somewhat, so he said: «Shah! May Allah curse you.» The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: «Who is this cursing his camel?» He said: «I am, O Messenger of Allah.» He said: «Dismount from it. Do not accompany us with one cursed. Do not pray against yourselves, nor against your children, nor against your property. Lest you coincide with an hour when He answers you.»"],[1043,"A slave girl, while she was on a camel or a mount carrying the people's luggage between two mountains, the mountain pass became narrow for her, and the Messenger of Allah ﷺ came upon her. When she saw him, she began to say: «Hal! O Allah, curse it. O Allah, curse it.» The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: «No mount with a curse from Allah upon it will accompany us.»"],[1044,"“Whoever receives a kindness from his brother without asking or coveting, let him accept it and not reject it, for it is only provision that Allah has brought to him.”"],[1045,"\"The Messenger of God ﷺ saw a man praying alone behind the rows, so the Prophet ﷺ ordered him to repeat the prayer.\""],[1046,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ saw a man praying alone behind the row, so he commanded him, and he repeated the prayer."],[1047,"A man prayed alone behind the Prophet ﷺ, not connecting with anyone, so he commanded him to repeat the prayer."],[1048,"A man prayed alone behind the row, so the Prophet ﷺ commanded him to repeat the prayer."],[1049,"We came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and prayed behind the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. When the Messenger of Allah ﷺ finished his prayer, there was a man standing alone. The Prophet of Allah ﷺ stood by him until the man finished his prayer, then the Prophet of Allah ﷺ said to him: \"Repeat your prayer, for there is no prayer for one standing alone behind the row.\""],[1050,"You prayed behind the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. When the Messenger of Allah ﷺ finished his prayer, he looked at a man alone behind the row and the Prophet ﷺ said: \"Did you pray like this?\" He said: \"Yes.\" He said: \"Then repeat your prayer, for there is no prayer for one alone behind the row.\""],[1051,"Abū Bakrah entered the mosque while the Prophet ﷺ was bowing, so he bowed [alone], then walked until he joined the row. The Prophet ﷺ said to him: \"May God increase you in keenness, but do not repeat it.\""],[1052,"He entered the mosque while the Prophet ﷺ was bowing. He said: \"So I bowed before [joining] the row.\" The Messenger of God ﷺ said: \"May God increase you in keenness, but do not repeat it.\""],[1053,"I prayed beside the Prophet ﷺ, and Aisha was behind us praying with us, while I was beside the Prophet ﷺ praying with him."],[1054,"His grandmother Mulaykah invited the Messenger of Allah ﷺ to a meal she had prepared, and he ate from it. Then he said: \"Stand up, so I may lead you in prayer.\" Anas said: I went to a mat of mine that had turned black from long use, sprinkled it with water, and the Messenger of Allah ﷺ stood on it. I and the orphan lined up behind him, and the old woman behind us. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ led us in two rak'ahs, then left."],[1055,"He, the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, his mother, and his maternal aunt were together, and the Messenger of Allah ﷺ led them in prayer. He placed Anas on his right and his mother and maternal aunt behind them."],[1056,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ led us in prayer on a carpet. He placed me on his right, and Umm Sulaym and Umm Haram stood behind us."],[1057,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ prayed with us a prayer in which he added or omitted something. When he finished, we said: \"O Messenger of Allah, has something new occurred in the prayer?\" He said, then he folded his leg and prostrated twice, then said: \"If something new had occurred in the prayer, I would have informed you of it. But I am only a human being; I forget as you forget. So when I forget, remind me. And if one of you doubts in his prayer, let him seek what is correct and build upon it, then let him prostrate twice.\""],[1058,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ prayed and added or omitted something. It was said to him: \"O Messenger of Allah, has something new occurred in the prayer?\" He said: \"If something had occurred, I would have informed you of it. But I am only a human being; I forget as you forget. So whoever of you doubts in his prayer, let him look for what is most likely correct and complete upon it, then stand and prostrate twice.\""],[1059,"He prayed Zuhr as five (rak'ahs), so it was said, 'Has something been added to the prayer?' The Prophet ﷺ said, 'And what is that?' They said, 'You prayed five.' So he prostrated two prostrations after he had given the salutation."],[1060,"When one of you doubts in his prayer, let him strive for what is correct, then give the salutation, then prostrate two prostrations."],[1061,"«The Messenger of Allah ﷺ stood up from the noon prayer while he still had sitting (due). When he completed his prayer, he prostrated twice while sitting before saying the salam, and the people prostrated with him in place of the sitting he had forgotten.»"],[1062,"'Abd Allah (said): The Messenger of Allah ﷺ prayed a prayer. Ibrahim said: I do not know whether he added or omitted. When he gave the salutation, it was said to him, 'O Messenger of Allah, has something occurred in the prayer?' He said, 'No, and what is that?' They said, 'You prayed such and such.' He said, 'So he folded his leg, faced the qiblah, prostrated two prostrations, then gave the salutation. When he turned his face to us, he said, 'If something had occurred in the prayer, I would have informed you of it, but I am only a human being like you; I forget as you forget. So when I forget, remind me, and when one of you doubts in his prayer, let him strive for what is correct, complete it accordingly, then give the salutation, then prostrate two prostrations.'"],[1063,"When one of you prays and does not know whether he prayed three or four (rak'ahs), let him pray one rak'ah and prostrate two prostrations before the salutation. If it was the third, the two prostrations make it even; and if it was the fourth, the two prostrations are a humiliation for Satan."],[1064,"When one of you doubts in his prayer, let him cast aside the doubt and build upon certainty. If he becomes certain of completion, he prostrates two prostrations. If his prayer was complete, the rak'ah is voluntary and the two prostrations are voluntary; and if it was deficient, the rak'ah completes his prayer and the two prostrations humiliate Satan's nose."],[1065,"“Every Muslim must bathe once every seven days, and that is the day of Jumu'ah.”"],[1066,"When the wind blew, that would be known from his face ﷺ. *"],[1067,"“Whoever attends Jumu'ah must bathe.”"],[1068,"“Whoever goes early to Jumu'ah must bathe.”"],[1069,"“Whoever attends Jumu'ah, men and women, must bathe.”"],[1070,"“Bathing on the day of Jumu'ah is obligatory on every adult male and on every adult female.”"],[1071,"“Bathing on the day of Jumu'ah is obligatory on every adult male.”"],[1072,"The bathing on the day of Jumu'ah is obligatory upon every muḥtalim, like the bathing from janābah."],[1073,"What is this hour (for attending the prayer)? He said: I was busy today and I did not return to my house when I heard the call (to Friday prayer), and I did no more but performed ablution only. Upon this Umar said: just ablution! You know that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ commanded (us) to take a bath (on Friday). (Using translation from Muslim 845a)"],[1074,"Whoever performs wuḍūʾ on the day of Jumu'ah and perfects the wuḍūʾ, then comes to Jumu'ah and draws near and listens attentively, Allah forgives him what is between that Jumu'ah and the next Jumu'ah, and an additional three days."],[1075,"Indeed, Allah has a right upon every Muslim to bathe one day every seven days; and if he has perfume, he should touch some of it. *"],[1076,"Bathing on the day of Jumu'ah is upon every muḥtalim, and the siwāk, and touching perfume as much as he is able."],[1077,"A right upon every Muslim to bathe every seven days, and to touch perfume if he finds it."],[1078,"I saw us while we were with our Prophet ﷺ, and if a rain shower had struck us, you would have smelled from us the odor of sheep."],[1079,"The people were negligent of themselves; they used to go to Jumu'ah in their usual appearance, so it was said to them: 'If only you bathed.'"],[1080,"The people used to come to Jumu'ah from their dwellings in the ʿAwālī, and they would come in woolen cloaks, and dust and sweat would afflict them, and an odor would emanate from them. A man from among them came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ while he was with me, and the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: 'If only you would purify yourselves for this day of yours.'"],[1081,"We used to go on military campaigns with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and we had no women with us. They said: O Messenger of Allah, should we not castrate ourselves? He forbade us from that and commanded us to marry a woman for a garment. Then Abdullah recited this verse: {O you who believe, do not forbid the good things which Allah has made lawful for you}."],[1082,"We used to go on military campaigns with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and we had no women with us. We said: O Messenger of Allah, should we not castrate ourselves? He forbade us from that and permitted us to marry a woman for a garment for a fixed period. Then he recited: {O you who believe, do not forbid the good things which Allah has made lawful for you, and do not transgress. Indeed, Allah does not love the transgressors}."],[1083,"He forbade mut'a with women on the day of Khaybar and the eating of the flesh of domesticated donkeys."],[1084,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ permitted us mut'a in the year of the Conquest. So I and another man went to a young woman, like a long-necked young she-camel, to enjoy her. We sat before her, he wearing a striped cloak and I wearing a striped cloak. We spoke to her and gave her our two cloaks as her dower. I was more youthful than him, and his cloak was better than mine. She began looking at me once and at his cloak once, then she chose me and I married her. I stayed with her for three [days]. Then the Messenger of Allah ﷺ forbade it, and I left her."],[1085,"That his father went on a military expedition with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. He said: I and a man of my people, over whom I had superiority in beauty while he was close to ugliness, each of us had a cloak. My cloak was worn out, while the cloak of my cousin was new and fresh. When we were in lower Makkah or in its upper part, we met a young woman like a young she-camel. We said, 'Will you allow us to enjoy you?' She said, 'What will you give?' Each of us spread out his cloak. She began to look at the man. When the man saw her looking at me, he turned aside. He said, 'This one's cloak is worn out, and my cloak is new and fresh.' She would say, 'This one's cloak is not bad.' Then I enjoyed her. We had not left before the Messenger of Allah ﷺ forbade it."],[1086,"When the Prophet ﷺ left, he stayed at the Thaniyyah Al-Wada'a and saw some lamps and heard women crying. He asked, \"What is this?\" They replied, \"O Messenger of Allah, these are the women who were enjoying their time with their husbands.\" The Messenger of Allah ﷺ then said, \"He has abolished or prohibited temporary marriage, divorce, waiting period after divorce, and inheritance.\""],[1087,"He forbade mut'a and said: 'It is forbidden from this day of yours until the Day of Resurrection. Whoever gave anything, let him not take it back.'"],[1088,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ permitted us mut'a in the year of Awtas for three [days], then he forbade us from it."],[1089,"A man broke his fast during Ramadan, so the Prophet ﷺ commanded him to expiate by freeing a slave, or fasting two months, or feeding sixty poor people. He said: I cannot find. Then the Prophet ﷺ was brought a basket of dates and said: \"Take this and give it in charity.\" He said: O Messenger of Allah, I find no one more in need than myself. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ laughed until his canine teeth showed, then said: \"Eat it.\""],[1090,"A man came to the Prophet ﷺ and said: I am destroyed. He said: \"What is your matter?\" He said: I fell upon my wife. He said: \"Can you find a slave to free?\" He said: No. He said: \"Can you fast two consecutive months?\" He said: No. He said: \"Can you feed sixty poor people?\" He said: No. He said: \"Sit.\" Then a large basket (ʿaraq) containing dates was brought, and it is the huge container (miktal). He said: \"Take this and give it in charity to sixty poor people.\" He said: There is no household between its two lava tracts poorer than us. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ laughed until his canine teeth showed and said: \"Take it and feed your dependents.\""],[1091,"A man came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and informed him that he had fallen upon his wife during Ramadan. He said: \"Can you find a slave?\" He said: No. He said: \"Can you fast two months?\" He said: No. He said: \"Feed sixty poor people?\" He said: I cannot find. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ gave him dates and commanded him to give them in charity. He said: Then he mentioned his need to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, so he commanded him to take it himself."],[1092,"A man said: O Messenger of Allah, I am destroyed. He said: \"Woe to you, what is that?\" He said: I fell upon my wife on a day in the month of Ramadan. He said: \"Free a slave.\" He said: I cannot find. He said: \"Fast two consecutive months.\" He said: I cannot. He said: \"Feed sixty poor people.\" He said: I cannot find. Then the Messenger of Allah ﷺ was brought a basket containing fifteen saʿs of dates. He said to him: \"Give it in charity.\" He said: On those poorer than my family? There is no one between the two lava tracts of Madinah more in need than my family. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ laughed until his canine teeth showed and said: \"Take it, seek Allah's forgiveness, and feed it to your family.\""],[1093,"When one of you prays, let him place something in front of his face. If he cannot find anything, let him set up a stick. If he cannot find a stick, let him draw a line, then nothing that passes in front of him will harm him."],[1094,"The first one to begin the sermon before the prayer on the day of Eid was Marwan b. al-Hakam. A man stood up to him and said: 'The prayer is before the sermon,' raising his voice. So [Marwan] said: 'Leave that, O Abu so-and-so.' Then Abu Sa'id al-Khudri said: 'As for this one, he has fulfilled what was upon him. I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: \"Whoever sees a wrong, let him change it with his hand; if he cannot, then with his tongue; if he cannot, then with his heart, and that is the weakest of faith.\"'"],[1096,"I said: O Messenger of Allah, I have embraced Islam while I have two sisters as wives. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: 'Divorce whichever of them you wish.'"],[1097,"That Ghaylan b. Salamah al-Thaqafi embraced Islam while he had ten wives. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to him: 'Choose four of them.' Later, during the caliphate of 'Umar, he divorced his wives and divided his wealth among his sons. That reached 'Umar, so he met him and said: 'I think Satan, in what he steals by hearing, heard of your death and cast it into your mind. Perhaps you will not remain but a little while. By Allah, you will take back your wives and return to your wealth, or I will make them inherit from you and order your grave to be stoned as the grave of Abu Righal was stoned.'"],[1098,"Ghaylan al-Thaqafi accepted Islam while he had ten wives, so the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Keep four, and separate from the rest.”"],[1099,"Ghaylan b. Salamah al-Thaqafi accepted Islam while he had ten wives, so the Messenger of Allah ﷺ ordered him to choose four of them and leave the rest."],[1100,"from Ka'b bin 'Ujrah who said: \"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ came to me while I was lighting a fire under a pot, and lice were falling on my face, or on my eye-brows. He said: 'Are your lice bothering you?'\" [He said:] \"I said: 'Yes.' He said: 'Then shave your head and offer a sacrifice, or fast three days, or feed six needy people.'\" Ayyub said: \"I do not know which of them he started with.\" (Using translation from Tirmidhī 2974)"],[1101,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ passed by him at the time of al-Hudaybiyyah and said, “Have the vermin of your head harmed you?” He said, “Yes.” The Prophet ﷺ said, “Shave, then slaughter a sheep as a sacrifice, or fast three days, or feed three sa‘s of dates among six poor persons.”"],[1102,"I sat with Ka‘b b. ‘Ujrah and asked him about the saying of Allah, Mighty and Exalted: {A ransom of fasting, or charity, or sacrifice}. He said: I was carried to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ while lice were falling on my face. He said, “I did not think that hardship had reached you to the extent I see. Can you find a sheep?” I said, “No.” He said, “Then fast three days, or feed six poor persons, for each poor person half a sa‘.” He said: It was revealed concerning me specifically, but it is for you all generally."],[1103,"I heard Hishām b. Ḥakīm b. Ḥizām reciting Sūrat al-Furqān differently from how I recite it, and the Messenger of Allah ﷺ had taught it to me. I almost rushed at him, but then I gave him time until he finished. Then I grabbed him by his cloak and brought him to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and said, “I heard this one reciting Sūrat al-Furqān differently from how you taught it to me.” The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to him, “Recite.” He recited the recitation I had heard. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, “Thus it was revealed.” Then he said to me, “Recite.” I recited, and he said, “Thus it was revealed. This Qur’an was revealed on seven ahruf, so recite whatever of it is easy.”"],[1104,"I heard a man reciting a verse that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ had taught me differently from the way he recited it, so I went to the Prophet ﷺ while he was conversing privately with 'Ali and mentioned that to him. 'Ali turned to us and said, 'The Messenger of Allah ﷺ commands you to recite as you have been taught.'"],[1105,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ taught me Surah al-Rahman. I went out to the mosque in the evening, and a group of people sat with me. I said to a man, 'Recite to me,' and he recited in ways that I did not recite. I said, 'Who taught you?' He said, 'The Messenger of Allah ﷺ taught me.' So we went until we stood before the Prophet ﷺ. I said, 'We have differed in our recitation.' The face of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ showed a change, and he felt something within himself when I mentioned the difference. He said, 'Those before you were destroyed only by differing.' Then he commanded 'Ali, who said, 'The Messenger of Allah ﷺ commands that each man among you recite as he has been taught, for those before you were destroyed only by differing.' He said, 'So we left, each man of us reciting a way that his companion did not recite.'"],[1106,"On the authority of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ , he said, \"Witr (an odd number of units of prayer) is a right (obligatory). So whoever wishes to perform Witr with five (units of prayer), let them do so. And whoever wishes to perform Witr with three (units), let them do so. And whoever wishes to perform Witr with one (unit), let them do so. And whoever finds it difficult, let them gesture with their head.\""],[1107,"Abu Musa sought permission to enter upon Umar three times, but permission was not granted to him, so he turned back. That reached Umar, who said, \"What made you go back?\" He said, \"I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say, 'When one of you asks permission three times and is not granted permission, let him return.'\" He said, \"Bring me proof of this, or else...\" Hammad said, \"He threatened him.\" He said, \"So he went away and entered the mosque, came to the gathering of the Ansar and told them the story of what he had said to Umar and what Umar had said to him. They said, 'None will stand with you except the youngest of us.' So Abu Sa'id al-Khudri stood with him and testified. Umar said to him, 'We do not suspect you, but the hadith of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ is a serious matter.'"],[1108,"Abu Musa sought permission to enter upon Umar three times, but permission was not granted to him, and it was as if Umar was busy. Abu Musa returned. When Umar was free, he said, \"Did I not hear the voice of Abdullah b. Qays? Grant him permission.\" It was said, \"He has already left.\" So he summoned him and said, \"We were commanded to do that.\" He said, \"You must bring me proof of that.\" So he went to the gathering of the Ansar and asked them. They said, \"None will testify for you except the youngest of us, Abu Sa'id al-Khudri.\" So he took Abu Sa'id and he testified for him. He said, \"This was hidden from me of the affair of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ; the haggling in the markets distracted me. But greet as you wish.\""],[1109,"The Messenger of God ﷺ entered upon us while we were washing his daughter, and he said, 'Wash her three times, or five times, or more than that if you see fit, with water and lote-tree leaves, and put camphor or something of camphor in the last. When you are finished, inform me.' She said, 'When we finished, we informed him.' She said, 'He threw his waist-wrapper to us and said, \"Wrap her in it as an inner garment.\"'"],[1110,"A daughter of the Messenger of God ﷺ died, and he said, 'Wash her with water and lote-tree leaves three times, or five times, or more than that if you see fit, and put something of camphor in the last of them. When you are finished, inform me.' So we informed him, and he threw his waist-wrapper to us and said, 'Wrap her in it as an inner garment.'"],[1111,"\"Make the Fajr prayer bright, for it is greater for the reward.\""],[1112,"\"Perform the Subh prayer in the morning light, for whenever you perform it in the morning light, it is greater for your rewards, or for its reward.\""],[1113,"\"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to pray Subh, and the women would leave wrapped in their cloaks, not being recognized from the darkness.\""],[1114,"A man came to the Prophet ﷺ and asked him about the time of prayer. He said, \"Pray with us these two times.\" When the sun declined, he prayed Zuhr, then he prayed Asr while the sun was high, white, and living, and he prayed Maghrib when the sun set, and he prayed Isha when the twilight disappeared, and he prayed Fajr in darkness. On the next day, he ordered Bilal and he delayed Zuhr until it was cool, and he made it very cool. He ordered him and he established Asr while the sun was living, delaying it beyond what it had been the first time. He ordered him and he established Maghrib before the twilight disappeared, and he ordered him and he established Isha after a third of the night had passed, and he ordered him and he established Fajr and made it bright. Then he said, \"Where is the one who asked about the time of prayer?\" He said, \"I am, O Messenger of Allah.\" He said, \"The time of your prayer is between what you have seen.\""],[1115,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ prayed Subh with us in darkness, then he prayed the morning prayer the next day and made it bright. Then he said, \"Where is the one who asked about the time of the morning prayer? It is between my prayer yesterday and today.\""],[1116,"That ʿUmar b. ʿAbd al-ʿAzīz was sitting on the pulpit and delayed the prayer somewhat. So ʿUrwah b. al-Zubayr said: “Indeed Jibrīl informed Muḥammad ﷺ of the time of prayer.” ʿUmar said to him: “Know what you are saying.” ʿUrwah said: “I heard Bashīr b. Abī Masʿūd say: I heard Abū Masʿūd al-Anṣārī say: I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: ‘Jibrīl descended and informed me of the time of prayer, so I prayed with him, then I prayed with him, then I prayed with him, then I prayed with him, then I prayed with him’—and he counted with his fingers five prayers—‘and I saw the Messenger of Allah ﷺ pray ẓuhr when the sun declines, and sometimes he delayed it when the heat became intense. And I saw him pray ʿaṣr while the sun was high and white before yellowness entered it, so that a man would leave after the prayer and reach Dhū al-Ḥulayfah before sunset. And he prayed maghrib when the sun set, and he prayed ʿishāʾ when the horizon became dark, and sometimes he delayed it until people gathered. And he prayed ṣubḥ once in darkness, and he prayed another time and let it brighten. Then his prayer after that was in darkness until he died ﷺ, not returning to letting it brighten.’”"],[1117,"Our Prophet ﷺ commanded us to recite the Opening of the Book (Fatihat al-Kitab) and whatever is easy [of the Quran]."],[1118,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ heard a man saying, “Labbayk on behalf of Shubrumah.” The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, “Who is Shubrumah?” He said, “A brother of mine, or a relative.” He said, “Have you ever performed Hajj?” He said, “No.” He said, “Then make this one for yourself, then perform Hajj on behalf of Shubrumah.”"],[1119,"'I command you with three things and I forbid you from three things. I command you to worship Allah and not associate anything with Him, to hold fast to the rope of Allah all together and not be divided, and to obey the one whom Allah has placed in authority over your affairs. I forbid you from he said/she said, excessive questioning, and wasting wealth.'"],[1120,"When we pledged allegiance to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ upon hearing and obedience, he would say to us: 'In what you are able.'"],[1121,"'Hear and obey in your hardship and ease, in your energy and weariness, and even when others are preferred over you, and even if they consume your wealth and strike your back, unless it is disobedience.'"],[1122,"Umar b. al-Khattab mentioned to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ that he becomes junub at night, so the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, 'Perform ablution and wash your private part, then sleep.'"],[1123,"I asked the Messenger of Allah ﷺ about menstrual blood that gets on a garment. He said, \"Wash it with water and sidr, and rub it with a rib (of a palm leaf).\""],[1124,"A woman came to the Prophet ﷺ and asked him about the ghusl of menstruation. He ordered her to bathe with water and sidr, and to take a piece of cloth, perform wudu' with it, and purify herself with it. She said: How do I purify myself with it? He said: \"Purify yourself with it.\" She said: How do I purify myself with it? The Prophet ﷺ covered himself with his hand and said: \"Glory be to Allah, purify yourself with it.\" A'ishah said: So I pulled the woman aside and said: You follow the trace of blood with it."],[1125,"A woman asked the Messenger of Allah ﷺ about menstruation: how should she bathe from it? He said: \"Take a piece of cloth perfumed with musk and perform wudu' with it.\" She said: How do I perform wudu' with it? The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"Perform wudu' with it.\" She said: How do I perform wudu' with it? The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"Perform wudu' with it.\" A'ishah said: I knew what he meant, so I pulled her to me and taught her."],[1126,"A woman asked the Messenger of Allah ﷺ about menstrual blood. He said, \"Scrape it off, then rub it with water, then sprinkle it and pray in it.\""],[1127,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ was asked about a garment that gets menstrual blood on it, and he said: \"Let her scrape it off, then rub it with water, then sprinkle it, and then she may pray in it.\""],[1128,"A woman said, \"O Messenger of Allah, what should I do about menstrual blood that gets on my garment?\" He said, \"Scrape it off, then rub it with water, and sprinkle the area around it.\""],[1129,"Whoever performs wudu' should draw water into his nose and expel it, and whoever cleanses himself with stones should make it an odd number."],[1130,"When one of you performs wudu', let him place water in his nose, then expel it, and whoever cleanses himself with stones, let him make it an odd number."],[1131,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ observed i'tikaf during the middle ten days of Ramadan, seeking Laylat al-Qadr. Then he ordered that a structure be built, but it was dismantled. Then it was made clear to him that it was in the last ten days, so he ordered that it be rebuilt. He came out to us and said, \"Laylat al-Qadr was made clear to me, and I came out to make it clear to you, but two men argued and I was made to forget it. So seek it in the ninth, the seventh, and the fifth.\" I said, \"O Abu Sa'id, you know numbers better than us. Which night is the ninth, the seventh, and the fifth?\" He said, \"When it is the twenty-first night, then skip a night; the one after it is the seventh. Then skip a night, and the one after it is the fifth.\""],[1132,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ entered upon her while a woman was treating her or incanting over her, and he said: 'Treat her with the Book of Allah.'"],[1133,"When the Prophet ﷺ was brought a sick person, he would supplicate and say: 'Remove the affliction, O Lord of mankind; heal, for You are the Healer; there is no healing except Your healing, a healing that leaves no illness.'"],[1134,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ forbade incantations. It was said: O Messenger of Allah, you have forbidden incantations? The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: 'Whoever of you can benefit his brother, let him do so.'"],[1135,"\"When one of you comes upon a camel herder, let him call out three times, 'O camel herder!' If he answers him, then fine; otherwise, let him milk and drink, but he must not carry away any. And when one of you comes upon a walled garden, let him call out three times, 'O owners of the garden!' If they answer him, then fine; otherwise, let him eat, but he must not carry away any.\""],[1136,"\"Let no one milk the livestock of another without his permission. Would any of you like his storeroom to be entered, his cupboard broken, and his food taken? The udders of their livestock and their food are indeed like that. So let no one milk the livestock of another without his permission.\""],[1137,"When one of you wakes up from his sleep, let him wash his hands before putting them into his ablution water, for one of you does not know where his hand spent the night."],[1138,"When one of you wakes up from his sleep, let him not dip his hand into the vessel until he washes it three times."],[1139,"When one of you wakes up from his sleep, let him not dip his hand into the vessel until he washes it three times, for he does not know where his hand spent the night from him."],[1140,"I was a slave, and I used to give charity from the meat of my master. I asked the Prophet ﷺ, and he said, “Give charity, and the reward is between you two, half and half.”"],[1141,"Whoever washes a dead person should perform ghusl, and whoever carries him should perform ablution."],[1143,"“Guarantee me six things and I will guarantee you Paradise: speak the truth when you speak, fulfill your promises when you promise, return trusts when you are entrusted, guard your private parts, lower your gazes, and restrain your hands.”"],[1144,"«The Messenger of Allah ﷺ commanded us to follow funerals, visit the sick, respond to the sneezer, fulfill the oath of the one who swears, help the oppressed, spread peace, and accept the invitation of the one who invites.»"],[1145,"“The sun and the moon do not eclipse because of anyone’s death or life, but they are two signs among the signs of Allah. So when you see them, pray.”"],[1146,"The sun eclipsed during the time of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, “The sun and the moon do not eclipse because of anyone’s death or life. So when you see any of that, pray until it clears or Allah brings about a new matter.”"],[1147,"The Prophet ﷺ entered upon Juwayriyah bt. al-Harith on Friday while she was fasting. He said, \"Did you fast yesterday?\" She said, \"No.\" He said, \"Do you intend to fast tomorrow?\" She said, \"No.\" He said, \"Then break your fast.\""],[1148,"We set out with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ toward Khaybar. A man from the people, 'Amir, said: 'If only you would entertain us with some of your songs.' So he began to chant for them, mentioning Allah and reciting poetry that I did not memorize. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: 'Who is this driver?' They said: ''Amir b. al-Akwa'.' He said: 'May Allah have mercy on him.' A man from the people said: 'O Messenger of Allah, if only you would let us enjoy his company longer.' When they encountered the enemy, they fought them, and 'Amir was struck. When evening came, they lit a great fire. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: 'What is this fire? What is it being lit for?' They said: 'For the meat of domestic donkeys.' He said: 'Pour out what is in them and break the pots.' A man said: 'O Messenger of Allah, should we not pour out what is in them and wash them?' He said: 'Do that.'"],[1149,"If women ask your permission to go to the mosques, grant them permission."],[1151,"Grant permission to women to go to the mosques at night."],[1152,"Do not prevent the female slaves of Allah from the mosques of Allah, and let them go out unperfumed."],[1153,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to her: “When you go out for the ʿishāʾ, do not touch perfume.”"],[1154,"I stayed with Abu Hashim b. 'Utbah b. Rabi'ah while he was ill with plague. Mu'awiyah came to visit him, and Abu Hashim wept. Mu'awiyah said, \"What makes you weep, O uncle? Is it pain, or is it over this world? Its clear enjoyment has departed.\" He said, \"Not over any of that. But the Messenger of Allah ﷺ gave me a charge, and I wish I had followed it. He said: 'Perhaps you will attain wealth that is distributed among people, and it will suffice you from that a servant and a mount in the way of Allah.' I attained it and gathered [wealth].\""],[1155,"When Salman al-Khayr was on his deathbed, they noticed some anxiety in him. They said, \"What distresses you, O Abu ʿAbdillāh, when you have such an outstanding record of good? You witnessed with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ noble expeditions and great conquests.\" He said, \"What distresses me is that when our beloved ﷺ parted from us, he made a covenant with us, saying, 'Let the worldly portion of one of you be only as much as a traveler's provision.'\""],[1156,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ passed by a man standing in prayer on a rock. He went toward Makkah and stayed for a long time, then returned and found the man still in his state, praying. He clasped his hands and said, “O people, be moderate. O people, be moderate, for Allah does not tire until you tire.”"],[1157,"“The Qur’an was revealed on seven ahruf.”"],[1158,"from the Prophet ﷺ, he said: Frequently remember the destroyer of pleasures (death), for whenever a servant mentions it while in difficulty, it [gives him relief], and whenever he mentions it while in ease, it gives him [self-restraint.]"],[1159,"I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ saying: \"Create a barrier of lawful (halal) things between you and what is prohibited (haram). Whoever does so has protected his honor and religion. And whoever allows himself to indulge in what is forbidden, it is as if he is standing on the edge of a precipice, about to fall into it. Certainly, every king has territories that he safeguards, and the territories of Allah on the earth are His prohibitions.\""],[1160,"from the Prophet ﷺ who said: Do not associate with anyone other than a believer not let anyone other than a God-fearing person eat from the meal [you serve.]"],[1161,"I came to the Prophet ﷺ, and he said, “Do the camels of your people produce healthy offspring with their ears, and then you take a razor and cut their ears, saying, ‘These are buhur,’ or you slit their hides and say, ‘These are surum,’ thereby forbidding them to yourself and your family?” He said: I said, “Yes.” He said, “Then whatever Allah gives you is lawful for you. Allah’s arm is stronger than your arm, and Allah’s razor is sharper than your razor.”"],[1162,"‘Umar passed by Ḥassān b. Thābit while he was reciting poetry in the mosque, so he glanced at him. He (Ḥassān) said, “I used to recite it while there was in it one better than you.” Then he turned to Abū Hurayrah and said, “I implore you by Allah, did you hear the Prophet ﷺ say, ‘Answer on my behalf: O Allah, support him with the Holy Spirit’?” He said, “Yes.”"],[1163,"When one of you prays and does not know whether he prayed three or four (rak'ahs), let him prostrate two prostrations while he is sitting. And when Satan comes to one of you and says, 'You have broken your ablution,' let him say, 'You lied,' unless he hears a sound with his ear or smells an odor with his nose."],[1164,"When Satan comes to one of you and says, 'You have broken your ablution,' let him say within himself, 'You lied,' until he hears a sound with his ear or smells an odor with his nose."],[1165,"From the Prophet ﷺ: \"When one of you is fasting, he should not behave obscenely or ignorantly; if someone behaves ignorantly toward him, let him say: I am a fasting person.\""],[1166,"Do not engage in mutual abuse while you are fasting. If someone abuses you, say, 'I am fasting,' and if you were standing, sit down."],[1167,"“If any one of you is insulted while he is fasting, let him say, 'I am fasting.'”"],[1168,"“Whoever asks by Allah, give him; whoever seeks refuge by Allah, grant him refuge; and whoever invites you, respond to him.”"],[1169,"“Whoever seeks refuge with you by Allah, grant him refuge; whoever asks you by Allah, give him; whoever invites you, accept his invitation; and whoever does you a kindness, reward him. If you do not find what to reward him with, then supplicate to Allah for him until you see that you have rewarded him.”"],[1170,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to go out on the day of Eid al-Fitr and Eid al-Adha to perform two units of prayer, then he would say the salaam and go to the people while he was standing in his prayer area. Then he would sit and face them and say to the people, \"Give charity.\" Most of those who would give charity were women, who would give their earrings and bracelets. If he had any need, he would send someone to the people, otherwise he would leave."],[1171,"Ibn Abbas witnessed that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ prayed on the day of Eid, then delivered a sermon, and then went to the women and commanded them to give charity."],[1172,"From the Prophet ﷺ, it is narrated that he said to the women, \"Give charity, for indeed you are the majority of the inhabitants of Hell.\" A woman who was not from a high-class background asked, \"Why is that so, O Messenger of Allah?\" He replied, \"You curse frequently and are ungrateful to your husbands.\" Abdullah said, \"The deficiency in intelligence and religion is most prevalent among men who have authority over their women.\" It was asked, \"And what is the deficiency in her intelligence and religion?\" He said, \"As for the deficiency in her intelligence, the testimony of two women is equal to the testimony of one man. And as for the deficiency in her religion, it is that on some days, she does not offer a single prayer.\""],[1173,"\"The parable of the companion of the Qur'an is like the parable of the owner of hobbled camels; if he keeps them hobbled, he holds them, and if he sets them free, they go away.\""],[1174,"\"Respond to the one who asks even with a sheep's foot.\" According to the narration of Harun: \"With a sheep's burned foot.\" (Using translation from Nasāʾī 2565)"],[1175,"She said to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ: \"A beggar stands at my door, and I cannot find anything to give him.\" The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to her: \"If you find nothing to give him except a burnt hoof, then place it in his hand.\""],[1176,"Whoever receives a favor from his brother without asking or coveting, let him accept it and not reject it."],[1177,"When you cook a pot, increase its broth, for it is more accommodating for the family and the neighbors."],[1178,"When you make broth, increase its water, then look to a household among your neighbors and give them a ladleful of it with kindness."],[1179,"When she prepared tharid, she would cover it until its steam subsided, then say, 'I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: \"It is greater in blessing.\"'"],[1180,"\"The best charity is that given from surplus wealth. Begin with those you support.\""],[1183,"A slave is entitled to his food and clothing, and should not be burdened except with what he can bear. If you burden them, then help them, and do not torment Allah's servants, creatures like yourselves."],[1184,"I and my father went out seeking knowledge among this tribe of the Ansar before they perished. The first person we met was Abu al-Yasar, the Companion of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and with him was a servant of his. On Abu al-Yasar was a burdah and a Ma'afiri garment, and on his servant was a burdah and a Ma'afiri garment. My father said to him, 'I see in your face something of anger.' He said, 'Yes, I had money owed to me by so-and-so son of so-and-so al-Harami. I came to his family and said, \"Is he there?\" They said, \"No.\" Then a son of his came out to me, and I said, \"Where is your father?\" He said, \"He heard your voice and went inside.\" I said, \"Come out to me, for I know where you are.\" So he came out to me, and I said, \"What made you hide?\" He said, \"By Allah, I will tell you and then not lie to you. I feared, by Allah, that if I spoke to you I would lie to you, and if I promised you I would break my promise. You are a Companion of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and I was, by Allah, insolvent.\" I said, \"By Allah?\" He said, \"By Allah.\" I said, \"By Allah?\" He said, \"By Allah.\" Then he took his document and erased it, and said, \"If you find a way to pay, then pay; otherwise, you are released.\" I bear witness—my two eyes saw this and my heart understood it, and he pointed to the aorta of his heart—I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say, \"Whoever grants respite to an insolvent person or remits for him, Allah will shade him in His shade.\""],[1185,"the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, \"Feed the hungry, visit the sick, and free the ʿānī (captive). Sufyān said: ʿānī means captive."],[1186,"“The Messenger of Allah ﷺ commanded for the mosque, from every wall, a bunch of dates.”"],[1187,"“The Messenger of Allah ﷺ commanded that from every jadd of ten wasqs of dates, a bunch be hung in the mosque for the poor.”"],[1188,"I came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ with a disheveled appearance. He said: 'Do you have any wealth?' I said: 'Yes.' He said: 'What kind of wealth?' I said: 'Of every kind; Allah has given me camels, slaves, and sheep.' He said: 'If Allah gives you wealth, let it be seen on you.' I said: 'O Messenger of Allah, do you think that if a man whom I visited did not honor me or host me, and then he visits me, should I repay him for what he did?' He said: 'No, rather host him.'"],[1190,"While we were traveling with the Prophet ﷺ , a man came on his riding animal and started striking right and left. The Prophet ﷺ said, \"Whoever has extra provisions, should count them for those who do not have any provisions. And whoever has extra belongings, should count them for those who do not have any belongings.\" Then he mentioned various types of wealth until we realized that none of us had any surplus."],[1191,"“We were with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ on a journey, and he said, ‘Indeed, this journey is difficult and burdensome. So, when someone among you wants to rest, let him perform two units of prayer, for if he wakes up, they will be for him.’”"],[1192,"I had a debt owed by the Prophet ﷺ, and he repaid me and gave me more. Then I entered upon him in the mosque, and he said to me, “Pray two rakʿahs.”"],[1193,"“When one of you comes to the mosque, let him pray two prostrations before sitting.”"],[1194,"“When one of you enters the mosque, let him perform two Rak’ah before he sits down.” (Using translation from Ibn Mājah 1013)"],[1195,"“When one of you enters the mosque, let him bow two rakʿahs before sitting or asking.”"],[1196,"“Sulayk al-Ghaṭafānī entered the mosque while the Prophet ﷺ was delivering the sermon, and he ordered him to pray two rakʿahs.”"],[1197,"A man entered the mosque while the Prophet ﷺ was delivering the sermon on Friday, and he said to him, “Pray two light rakʿahs before you sit.”"],[1198,"“A man entered the mosque on Friday while the Prophet ﷺ was on the pulpit. He called him and ordered him to pray two rakʿahs. Then he entered on the second Friday while he was on the pulpit, and he called him and ordered him to pray two rakʿahs. Then he entered on the third Friday while the Messenger of Allah ﷺ was on the pulpit, and he called him and ordered him to pray two rakʿahs.”"],[1199,"«When one of you prays Jumu'ah, let him pray four [rak'ahs] after it»"],[1200,"Messenger of Allah said: \"Whoever among you is to pray after the Friday prayer, then let him pray four.\" (Using translation from Tirmidhī 523)"],[1201,"«The prayer of night and day is two [rak'ahs] by two»"],[1202,"\"Whoever of you wants to pray after Jumu'ah, let him pray four; and if he has some business, then two rak'ahs in the mosque and two rak'ahs in the house.\""],[1204,"We were with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ on a journey. He said: “When he came to Madinah, the Prophet ﷺ commanded him to go to the mosque and pray two rak'ahs.”"],[1205,"When one of you rises at night, let him begin with two light rakʿahs."],[1206,"\"When one of you finishes his prayer in his mosque, let him allot a share for his house, for Allah will place good in his house from his prayer.\""],[1207,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ commanded us to fast the thirteenth, fourteenth, and fifteenth."],[1208,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ commanded us to fast three days of the month, the white days: the thirteenth, fourteenth, and fifteenth."],[1209,"Hafsah and I woke up fasting voluntarily. Food was given to us as a gift, so we broke our fast. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, 'Fast another day in its place.'"],[1210,"\"O ʿAbd Allāh b. ʿAmr, it has reached me that you fast during the day and stand in prayer at night. Do not do that, for your body has a right over you, and your soul has a right over you. Fast and break your fast; from every month, three days: that is the fast of a lifetime.\" He said: I said, \"O Messenger of Allah, I find strength.\" He said, \"Fast the fast of Dāwūd: fast one day and break your fast one day.\" He said: And ʿAbd Allāh b. ʿAmr used to say, \"Would that I had taken the concession.\""],[1211,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ arrived and found the Jews fasting on the day of Ashura. He said to them, \"What is this?\" They said, \"A great day on which Allah saved Moses and drowned the people of Pharaoh, so Moses fasted it in gratitude to Allah.\" The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, \"I am more entitled to Moses and more deserving of fasting it than you.\" So he fasted it and commanded fasting it."],[1212,"Mu'awiya gave a sermon in Madinah upon his arrival there on the day of Ashura and said, \"Where are your scholars, O people of Madinah? I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say, 'This is the day of Ashura, and fasting it has not been prescribed for you. I am fasting, so whoever wishes to fast, let him fast.'\""],[1213,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ sent a man from Aslam to announce among the people: Today is the day of Ashura. So whoever has eaten, let him not eat anything for the rest of his day, and whoever has not eaten or drunk, let him fast."],[1214,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ came out to us on the day of Ashura and said: Has any of you eaten today? They said: Some of us have eaten and some of us have not eaten. He said: Whoever of you has not eaten, let him fast, and whoever has eaten, let him complete the rest of his day. And inform the people of the rural regions to complete the rest of their day."],[1215,"A woman is married for four things: her beauty, her lineage, her wealth, and her religion. Choose the one with religion, may your hands be dusty."],[1216,"A woman is married for her wealth, a woman is married for her beauty, and a woman is married for her religion. Take the one with religion and character, may your right hand be dusty."],[1217,"'Abd al-Rahman b. 'Awf came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ with a trace of yellow perfume. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ asked him, and he informed him that he had married a woman from the Ansar. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to him, “How much did you give her as a dowry?” He said, “The weight of a date pit of gold.” The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to him, “Hold a wedding feast, even with a sheep.”"],[1218,"The Prophet ﷺ held a wedding feast for Safiyyah with sawiq and dates."],[1219,"The Prophet ﷺ passed by a gathering of the Ansar and said, \"If you insist on sitting, then guide the way, return the greeting, and help the distressed.\""],[1220,"When you assess, take and leave a third; if you do not leave a third, then leave a quarter."],[1221,"Whoever swears by al-Lat and al-‘Uzza, let him say, “There is no god but Allah.” And whoever says to his companion, “Come, let me gamble with you,” let him give something in charity."],[1222,"I swore by al-Lat and al-Uzza. My companions said: You have spoken an evil word. So I went to the Prophet ﷺ and said: O Messenger of Allah, the covenant was recent, and I swore by al-Lat and al-Uzza. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"Say: There is no god but Allah alone, three times, then spit to your left three times, and seek refuge in Allah from the accursed Satan, and do not repeat it.\""],[1223,"«A fire will emerge upon you at the end of time from Hadramawt, gathering the people.» He said: We said, \"What do you command us, O Messenger of God?\" He said, \"You must go to Al-Sham.\""],[1224,"When the people of Sham become corrupt, there is no good in you."],[1225,"Help your brother, whether he is an oppressor or oppressed. They said: O Messenger of Allah, this one we help when he is oppressed, but how do we help him when he is an oppressor? He said: 'You restrain him from oppression.'"],[1226,"'I am approached and asked, and needs are sought from me while you are with me, so intercede and you will be rewarded, and Allah will decree on the tongue of His Prophet what He loves or what He wills.'"],[1227,"\"Allah has prescribed excellence in everything. So when you kill, kill well; and when you slaughter, slaughter well. Let each of you sharpen his blade and spare suffering to the animal he slaughters.\""],[1228,"that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"When one of you arrives at the gathering, then give the Salam, and if he is given a place to sit, then let him sit. Then when he stands, let him give the Salam, the first is more worthy than the last.\" (Using translation from Tirmidhī 2706)"],[1229,"The Prophet ﷺ “used to command the manumission of slaves during the eclipse prayer.”"],[1230,"The Prophet ﷺ said: \"It is not right for any one of you to say: 'I have forgotten such and such a verse.' Rather, he has been caused to forget. Study the Qur'an, for it escapes from the heart of man faster than a camel escapes from its fetter. \" (Using translation from Nasāʾī 943)"],[1231,"None of you will be saved by his deeds.” A man said to him, “Not even you, O Messenger of Allah?” He said, “Not even me, unless Allah envelops me in His mercy. But aim for correctness.”"],[1232,"A man heard another man reciting {Qul huwa Allahu ahad}, repeating it. When morning came, he went to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and mentioned that to him, and the man seemed to belittle it. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to him, “By the One in whose hand is my soul, it is equal to a third of the Quran.”"],[1233,"Aim for correctness and near-correctness, and none of you will be saved by his deeds.” We said, “Not even you, O Messenger of Allah?” He said, “Not even me, unless Allah envelops me in mercy from Him.”"],[1234,"This religion is easy, and no one overburdens himself in the religion but that it overcomes him. So aim for correctness, be near-correct, and receive good tidings. Seek help in the morning, the afternoon, and some part of the night.”"],[1235,"He ﷺ used, when invited, to go to the inviter; if he was fasting, he would supplicate for blessing and then leave, and if he was not fasting, he would sit and eat."],[1236,"Whoever misses Friday, let him give a dinar in charity; if he cannot find that, half a dinar."],[1237,"Whoever abandons Friday without excuse, let him give a dinar in charity; if he cannot find that, half a dinar."],[1238,"“Indeed Bilal calls the adhan at night, so eat and drink until Ibn Umm Maktum calls the adhan.” Ibn Shihab said: “Ibn Umm Maktum was a blind man; he would not call the adhan until it was said to him, ‘It is morning, it is morning.’”"],[1239,"While a man was driving a garlanded camel, the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to him, “Ride it.” He said, “It is a sacrificial camel, O Messenger of Allah.” He said, “Ride it, woe to you.”"],[1240,"“Ride the sacrificial animals in a reasonable manner until you find another mount.”"],[1241,"A wolf bit a sheep, so they slaughtered it with a sharp stone. They asked the Prophet ﷺ and he ordered them to eat it, so they ate."],[1242,"We were with the Prophet ﷺ at Dhu al-Hulayfah. The people were afflicted by hunger, and we had captured camels and sheep. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ was in the rear of the people, so they hastened and slaughtered and set up cooking pots. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ returned to them and ordered that the pots be overturned. Then he distributed and considered ten sheep equal to one camel. One of the camels bolted, and there were a few horses among the people, so they chased it but it tired them. A man aimed at it with an arrow and stopped it. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"These beasts have wild tendencies like wild animals, so if any of them bolts from you, do with it like this.\" My grandfather said: We hope to meet the enemy tomorrow, and we have no knives, so we slaughter with sharp sticks. He ﷺ said: \"Whatever lets the blood flow and the name of Allah is mentioned over it, eat it, except the tooth and the nail. I will tell you about that: as for the tooth, it is bone; and as for the nail, it is the knife of the Abyssinians.\""],[1243,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ stood in Minā during the Farewell Pilgrimage for the people to ask him questions. A man came to him and said, \"O Messenger of Allah, I was not aware, so I shaved before I slaughtered.\" The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, \"Slaughter, and there is no harm.\" Then another man came and said, \"O Messenger of Allah, I was not aware, so I sacrificed before I stoned.\" He said, \"Stone, and there is no harm.\" The Messenger of Allah ﷺ was not asked about anything that was done earlier or later except that he said, \"Do it, and there is no harm.\""],[1244,"We slaughtered seventy camels on the day of al-Ḥudaybiyyah, one camel for seven people. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, \"A group may share in one sacrificial animal.\""],[1245,"Sa'd b. 'Ubadah sought a ruling from the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, saying, 'My mother died with an unfulfilled vow.' The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, 'Fulfill it on her behalf.'"],[1246,"She sought permission from the Messenger of Allah ﷺ regarding killing geckos, and he commanded her to kill them."],[1247,"The Prophet ﷺ said: Kill the two black things during prayer, the snake and scorpion. (Using translation from Abū Dāʾūd 921)"],[1248,"Ibn ʿUmar stopped at Ḍajnān on a cold night and ordered them to pray in their dwellings, and he told us that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, when he stopped at a place on a cold night, “would order them to pray in their dwellings.”"],[1249,"We were with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ at the time of al-Ḥudaybiyah, and rain fell on us that did not even wet the soles of our sandals, and the caller of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ called out, “Pray in your dwellings.”"],[1250,"Al-Fadl b. ‘Abbas was riding behind the Messenger of Allah ﷺ when a woman from Khath‘am came to ask him for a ruling. Al-Fadl began looking at her and she at him. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ began turning al-Fadl’s face to the other side. She said, “O Messenger of Allah, Allah’s obligation upon His servants regarding Hajj has found my father an old man who cannot remain mounted on a riding beast. Should I perform Hajj on his behalf?” He said, “Yes.” That was during the Farewell Pilgrimage."],[1251,"A man asked Sulaymān b. Yasār about a woman who wanted to free a slave on behalf of her mother. Sulaymān said: ʿAbd Allāh b. ʿAbbās told me that a man asked the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, saying: O Messenger of Allah, my father entered Islam as an old man. If I tie him onto my riding camel, I fear I may kill him, and if I do not tie him, he will not stay on it. Should I perform Hajj on his behalf? The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"Consider, if your father owed a debt and you paid it on his behalf, would that suffice him?\" He said: Yes. He said: \"Then perform Hajj on behalf of your father.\""],[1252,"O Messenger of Allah, my father is an old man who is not able to perform Hajj or ʿUmrah or to travel. He said: \"Perform Hajj on behalf of your father and perform ʿUmrah for him.\""],[1253,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ passed by a man being supported by two others. He asked about him, and they said, 'He vowed to walk'—meaning to the Kaaba. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, 'Indeed Allah is in no need of this man's tormenting himself,' and he ordered him to ride."],[1254,"“The Messenger of Allah ﷺ commanded the killing of geckos and called them fuwaysiq (a small transgressor).”"],[1255,"«The gecko is a little transgressor.»"],[1256,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ commanded us to eat horse meat and forbade us the meat of domestic donkeys."],[1257,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to command her to seek ruqya against the evil eye."],[1258,"O Messenger of Allah, what do you think of a medicine we treat ourselves with, incantations we seek healing with, and things we do—do they repel any of Allah's decree? He said: 'O Ka'b, rather they are part of Allah's decree.'"],[1259,"I heard Usamah b. Sharik say: I witnessed the Prophet ﷺ while the bedouins were asking him, 'O Messenger of Allah, is there any blame on us in such-and-such?' twice. He said: 'Servants of Allah, Allah has removed hardship, except a man who borrows something from his brother's honor—that is the one who is in hardship.' They said: 'O Messenger of Allah, is there any blame on us if we seek medical treatment?' He said: 'Seek medical treatment, O servants of Allah, for Allah has not placed any disease except that He has placed for it a cure.' They said: 'O Messenger of Allah, what is the best thing given to a servant?' He said: 'Good character.' Sufyan said: 'There is no chain of narration on the face of the earth today better than this.'"],[1260,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, \"Treat yourselves, for indeed Allah has not sent down any disease except that He has also sent down its cure, except for old age and death.\""],[1261,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ came out upon a group from Aslam shooting arrows in the market. He said, 'Shoot, Banī Ismāʿīl, for your father was an archer, and I am with Banū so-and-so'—one of the two groups. They lowered their hands. He said, 'What is wrong with you? Shoot.' They said, 'How can we shoot when you are with Banū so-and-so?' He said, 'Shoot, and I am with all of you.'"],[1262,"O Banu Bayada, give Abu Hind in marriage and marry into his family.\" And he was a cupper."],[1263,"Umm Salamah asked the Messenger of Allah ﷺ for permission to undergo cupping, so the Prophet ﷺ ordered Abu Taybah to cup her, and he said—I think he said that he was her foster brother or a boy who had not reached puberty."],[1264,"I came to Ṣafwān b. ʿAssāl al-Murādī, and he said, “What brought you?” I said, “Seeking knowledge.” He said, “The angels lower their wings for the seeker of knowledge, out of pleasure at what he seeks.” I said, “There is something itching in my mind about wiping over the two khuffs after defecation and urination, and you were one of the companions of the Prophet ﷺ, so I came to ask you: did you hear anything from him about that?” He said, “Yes. He would command us, when we were travelling or on a journey, not to remove our khuffs for three days and their nights, except for janabah, but not for defecation, urination, or sleep.”"],[1265,"I came to Safwan b. 'Assal al-Muradi and he said, \"What brings you?\" I said, \"I have come to seek knowledge.\" He said, \"I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: 'No one goes out from his house seeking knowledge except that the angels lower their wings in approval of what he does.'\" He said, \"I came to ask you about wiping over the two khuffs.\" He said, \"Yes. We were in the army that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ sent, and he commanded us to wipe over the two khuffs if we had put them on in a state of purity: for three days when traveling, and not to remove them for defecation or urination.\""],[1266,"He was asked about wiping over the two khuffs and said, «Three for the traveler, and for the resident one day.»"],[1267,"About wiping over the two khuffs, he said, «For the traveler, three days and their nights; and for the resident, a day and a night.»"],[1268,"«The Messenger of Allah ﷺ granted us a concession to wipe over the two khuffs: three days for the traveler and a day and a night for the resident.»"],[1269,"that he performed wudu and wiped over the two khuffs, and said, “I saw the Messenger of Allah ﷺ doing it.”"],[1270,"I saw Jarir b. Abdullah urinate, then perform wudu and wipe over his two khuffs, then stand and pray. He was asked about that, and he said, “I saw the Prophet ﷺ do the same as this.”"],[1271,"I said to ʿUmar: “The people’s shortening of the prayer—Allah, Mighty and Exalted, only said: {If you fear that those who disbelieve may put you to trial}. That has now passed away.” He said: “I wondered at it, until I asked the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. He said: ‘It is a charity that Allah has given as charity to you, so accept His charity.’”"],[1272,"“Allah loves that His concessions be taken, just as He hates that disobedience be done to Him.”"],[1273,"Hind said to the Prophet ﷺ, \"Abu Sufyan is a stingy man, and I have nothing except what he brings in to me.\" He said, \"Take what suffices you and your child in a reasonable manner.\""],[1274,"The sun eclipsed during the time of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. He stood up and we stood with him. Then he said, “O people, the sun and the moon are two signs among the signs of Allah. So when one of them eclipses, hasten to the mosques.”"],[1275,"“Among what people have found from the words of the earlier prophethood: If you feel no shame, then do as you wish.”"],[1276,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ passed by a man who was admonishing his brother about modesty, and he said: “Leave him, for modesty is from faith.”"],[1277,"He said while on the pulpit, 'Let people stop abandoning the Fridays, or Allah will seal their hearts, and they will be among the heedless.'"],[1278,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to straighten the row until he made it like an arrow shaft or a spear, then he saw a man's chest protruding and the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: «Servants of Allah, straighten your rows or Allah will certainly cause discord among your faces.»"],[1279,"«Close up your rows, bring them near together, and align the shoulders, for by Him in whose hand is my soul, I see the devil entering through the gaps in the row as if they were small black sheep.»"],[1280,"He came to the Prophet ﷺ and then returned from him, and he passed by a people who had a man fettered in iron. His family said, 'It has...'"],[1281,"We went on a military expedition with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and camped in a land with many dhabbs while we were low on provisions. We caught some, and the cooking pots were boiling with them. The Prophet ﷺ said: 'What is this?' We said: 'Dhabbs we caught.' He said: 'A nation from the Children of Israel was transformed, and I fear that these might be them.' So he ordered us, and we overturned the pots, while we were indeed hungry."],[1282,"I entered with Khalid b. al-Walid into the house of Maymunah bt. al-Harith with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and there was a roasted dhabb. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ reached for it with his hand. The women who were in Maymunah's house said: 'Tell the Messenger of Allah ﷺ what he is about to eat.' They told him, so he lifted his hand. I said: 'Is it forbidden, O Messenger of Allah?' He said: 'No, but it is not found in the land of my people, so I find myself averse to it.' Khalid said: So I pulled it over while the Messenger of Allah ﷺ was watching."],[1283,"Abū Burdah b. Niyār slaughtered before the Messenger of Allah ﷺ slaughtered on the day of sacrifice. He claimed that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ commanded him to repeat the sacrifice. Abū Burdah said, 'I have nothing but a jadhaʿ (one-year-old).' The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, 'Even if you have nothing but a jadhaʿ, slaughter it.'"],[1284,"He said on the day of Eid: \"The first thing we begin with on this day of ours is to pray, then to slaughter. Whoever does that has hit upon our Sunnah, and whoever hastens, it is only meat he has offered ahead to his family.\" He said: Abu Burdah b. Niyar had slaughtered before the prayer, so he said: \"O Messenger of Allah, I have a jadha'ah that is better than a musinnah.\" He said: \"Put it in its place, but it will not suffice, or be fulfilled, for anyone after you.\""],[1285,"We were at the pillar of the mosque, and if I were there I would tell you its location. He said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ addressed us and said: \"The first thing we begin with on this day of ours is to pray, then return and slaughter. Whoever does that has hit upon our Sunnah, and whoever slaughters before that, it is only meat he has offered ahead to his family, not part of the sacrifice in any way.\" He said: My maternal uncle Abu Burdah b. Niyar slaughtered, and said: \"O Messenger of Allah, I have slaughtered, and I have a jadha'ah that is better than a musinnah.\" He said: \"Put it in its place, but it will not suffice for anyone after you.\""],[1286,"\"Whoever faces our qiblah, prays our prayer, and performs our sacrifice, let him not slaughter until he prays.\" My maternal uncle Abu Burdah said: \"O Messenger of Allah, I have sacrificed on behalf of a son of mine.\" He said: \"That is something you hastened for your family.\" He said: \"I have a jadha'ah.\" He said: \"Sacrifice it on his behalf, for it is the best of his sacrifice.\""],[1287,"A man slaughtered before the Prophet ﷺ prayed, so the Prophet ﷺ said: \"It will not suffice for anyone after you to slaughter until he prays.\""],[1288,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ addressed us on the Day of Sacrifice after the prayer, then said: \"Whoever prays our prayer and performs our sacrifice has hit upon the sacrifice, and whoever sacrifices before the prayer, that is a meat sheep.\" Abu Burdah b. Niyar said: \"O Messenger of Allah, I sacrificed before I went out to the prayer, and I knew that today is a day of eating and drinking, so I hastened and ate and fed my family and neighbors.\" The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"That is a meat sheep.\" He said: \"I have a jadha'ah kid that is better than two meat sheep; will it suffice for me?\" He said: \"Yes, it will suffice for you, but it will not suffice for anyone after you.\""],[1289,"My maternal uncle slaughtered before the Prophet ﷺ prayed, so the Prophet ﷺ said: \"Your sheep is a meat sheep, not part of the sacrifice in any way.\" He said: \"O Messenger of Allah, I have a jadha'ah kid that is better than a musinnah.\" The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"It will be fulfilled for you, but it will not be fulfilled for anyone after you.\""],[1290,"He slaughtered a sacrificial animal before he went out on the Day of Sacrifice, and he mentioned that to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, so the Messenger of Allah ﷺ ordered him to repeat another sacrificial animal."],[1291,"We sacrificed with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and there were people who slaughtered their sacrificial animals before the prayer. When he finished, the Prophet ﷺ saw that they had slaughtered before the prayer, and said: \"Whoever slaughtered before the prayer, let him slaughter another in its place, and whoever has not slaughtered until we prayed, let him slaughter in the name of Allah.\""],[1292,"The Prophet ﷺ said to a man: \"I was commanded with the Day of Sacrifice as an Eid that Allah made for this community.\" The man said: \"What do you think if I find only a female manihah (lent milking animal); should I sacrifice it?\" He said: \"No, but you should take from your hair, trim your nails, shave your pubic area, and clip your moustache; that is the completion of your sacrifice with Allah.\""],[1293,"'Utbah b. Abi Waqqas had entrusted his brother Sa'd b. Abi Waqqas, saying, \"The son of Zam'ah's slave woman is from me; take him under your care.\" So when it was the year of the conquest, Sa'd b. Abi Waqqas took him and said, \"He is the son of my brother, who had entrusted him to me.\" 'Abd b. Zam'ah stood up and said, \"He is my brother and the son of my father's slave woman, born on his bed.\" They went to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. Sa'd said, \"O Messenger of Allah, my brother had entrusted him to me,\" and 'Abd b. Zam'ah said, \"He is my brother and the son of my father's slave woman, born on his bed.\" The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, \"He is yours, O 'Abd b. Zam'ah. The child belongs to the bed, and the adulterer gets the stone.\" Then the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to Sawdah bt. Zam'ah, \"Veil yourself from him,\" because of the resemblance he saw to 'Utbah. She never saw him until she met Allah."],[1294,"There came a person to the Prophet (may peace he upon him) ) from Banu Fazara and said: My wife has given birth to a child who is black, whereupon Allah's Apostle ﷺ said: Have you any camels? He said: Yes. He again said: What is this colour? He said: They are red. He said: Is there a dusky one among them? He said: Yes, there are dusky ones among them He said: How has it come about? He said: It is perhaps the strain to which it has reverted, whereupon he (the Holy Prophet) said: It is perhaps the strain to which he (the child) has reverted. (Using translation from Muslim 1500a)"],[1295,"\"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ left us, and there is no bird flying with its wings but that we have knowledge from him about it.\""],[1296,"When one of you prays, let him wear an izār and a ridā'."],[1297,"A man asked the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, 'May one of us pray in a single garment?' He said, 'When Allah has given you ample means, then be ample upon yourselves. A man gathered his garments upon him. A man prayed in an izār and a ridā', in an izār and a shirt, in an izār and a cloak, in trousers and a shirt, in trousers and a ridā', in trousers and a cloak, in short trousers and a shirt, in short trousers and a cloak.' He said, 'And I think he said, in short trousers and a ridā'.'"],[1298,"A man said: O Messenger of Allah, may a man pray in a single garment? He said: 'Let him wrap it over his shoulders, then pray in it.'"],[1299,"When one of you prays in a single garment, let him place its two ends oppositely on his shoulder."],[1300,"I went out with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ on one of his journeys. One night I came for some matter of mine and found him praying, while I had on a single garment with which I wrapped myself and prayed at his side. When he finished, he said: 'What is the night journey, O Jabir?' I told him, and he said: 'O Jabir, what is this wrapping that I saw?' I said: It was a single, narrow garment. He said: 'When you pray while wearing a single garment, if it is wide, envelop yourself with it; and if it is narrow, wrap it around your waist.'"],[1301,"That al-Ash'ari prayed with his companions, and when he sat in his prayer, a man from the people said: Has the prayer been joined with righteousness and zakah? When al-Ash'ari finished his prayer, he turned to the people and said: Which of you said such and such a word? The people fell silent. He said: Perhaps you, O Hittan, said it? He said: By Allah, I did not say it, and I feared you would rebuke me for it. A man from the people said: I said it, and I intended nothing but good by it. Al-Ash'ari said: Do you not know what you say in your prayer? The Messenger of Allah ﷺ addressed us and taught us our Sunnah and explained to us our prayer, saying: «When the prayer is established, straighten your rows and let one of you lead you. When he says the takbir, say the takbir, and when he says {nor of those who go astray}, say Amin, and Allah will answer you. Then when he says the takbir and bows, say the takbir and bow, for the imam bows before you and rises before you.» The Prophet of Allah ﷺ said: «That is for that. And when he says: Allah hears the one who praises Him, say: O Allah, our Lord, to You be praise, for Allah, majestic and exalted, said on the tongue of His Prophet ﷺ: Allah hears the one who praises Him. Then when he says the takbir and prostrates, say the takbir and prostrate, for the imam prostrates before you and rises before you.» The Prophet of Allah ﷺ said: «That is for that. And when it is at the sitting, let one of you say: The greetings, the prayers belong to Allah. Peace be upon you, O Prophet, and the mercy of Allah and His blessings. Peace be upon us and upon the righteous servants of Allah. I bear witness that there is no god but Allah and that Muhammad is His servant and Messenger.»"],[1302,"That when Umar extended the mosque, they neglected the piece of wood that was in the qiblah. Anas said: «Do you know for what reason that piece of wood was placed?» They said: No. He said: The Prophet ﷺ, when the prayer was established, took the piece of wood with his right hand, then turned and said: «Straighten your rows and stand evenly.» Then he took it with his left hand, then turned and said: «Straighten your rows.»"],[1303,"«Complete your rows, for straightening the row is part of the completeness of the prayer.»"],[1304,"'Straighten the rows well in prayer. The best rows of the men in prayer are the first ones and the worst are the last ones, and the best rows of the women in prayer are the last ones and the worst are the first ones.'"],[1305,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ went to relieve himself, then came. I poured water from the vessel for him, and he washed his face. Then he went to uncover his forearms, but the sleeve of the Messenger of Allah's ﷺ jubba—a Roman woolen one—was tight, so he inserted his hand through a slit at its waist and washed them up to the elbows. He wiped his head and wiped over his leather socks. Then he came forward while I was with him and found the people at prayer. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ stood in the row while 'Abd al-Rahman b. 'Awf was leading them. We caught up with them when he had already prayed one rak'ah, so we prayed with 'Abd al-Rahman the second one. When he said the salutation, the Messenger of Allah ﷺ stood up and completed his prayer. The people were startled at that. When the Messenger of Allah ﷺ finished his prayer, he said, \"You have done right and well. When your imam is detained and the prayer has arrived, put forward a man to lead you.\""],[1306,"Mu'adh b. Jabal came to us in Yemen; the Messenger of Allah ﷺ had sent him to us. I heard his takbir with the dawn: a man with a hoarse voice. I took a liking to him and did not part from him until I buried him in al-Sham. Then I looked for the most knowledgeable of people after him, so I went to Ibn Mas'ud and kept close to him until he died. He said to me: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, 'How will it be for you when rulers are placed over you who pray the prayer at other than its time?' I said, 'What do you command me to do if I live to see that, O Messenger of Allah?' He said, 'Pray the prayer at its time, and make your prayer with them a voluntary prayer.'"],[1307,"Abu al-Darda' asked me, 'Where do you live?' I said, 'In a village near Hims.' He said, 'I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: There are not three people in a village or desert among whom the prayer is not established except that Satan has gained mastery over them. So keep to the congregation, for the wolf eats only the stray sheep.'"],[1308,"He was in a gathering with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ while he prayed, then returned and Mihjan was still in his place. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to him, \"What prevented you from praying with the people? Are you not a Muslim man?\" He said, \"Yes, O Messenger of Allah, but I had already prayed with my family.\" The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, \"When you come, pray with the people even if you have already prayed.\""],[1309,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ led us in prayer. When he finished, he removed his sandals and placed them on his left side, so the people removed their sandals. When he completed his prayer, he said, 'Why did you remove your sandals?' They said, 'We saw you remove yours, so we removed ours.' He said, 'I did not remove them because of any harm, but Jibrīl...'"],[1310,"'When one of you prays, let him either wear his sandals or remove them and place them between his feet, and let him not harm others with them.'"],[1311,"When you come to prayer, do not come running; come calmly. Pray what you catch up with, and make up what you missed."],[1312,"When the prayer is established, come to it calmly. Pray what you catch up with, and complete what you were preceded in."],[1313,"While we were praying with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, he heard the noise of men. When he finished, he called them and said, 'What is the matter with you?' They said, 'O Messenger of Allah, we hurried to prayer.' He said, 'Do not hurry. When you come to prayer, be calm. Pray what you catch up with, and complete what you were preceded in.'"],[1314,"\"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: 'When the Iqamah for prayer is said, do not stand up until you see that I have come out.'\" (Using translation from Nasāʾī 687)"],[1315,"“Complete the front row; if there is any deficiency, let it be in the back row.”"],[1316,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ went to Banu Amr b. Awf to reconcile between them. The time for prayer came, so Bilal came to Abu Bakr al-Siddiq ؓ and said, 'Will you lead the people in prayer, so that the iqamah may be given?' He said, 'Yes.' So Abu Bakr prayed. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ came while the people were in prayer and made his way through until he stood in the row. The people clapped, but Abu Bakr would not turn around during his prayer. When the people clapped more, Abu Bakr turned and saw the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ gestured to him to stay in his place. Abu Bakr raised his hands and praised Allah Almighty for what the Messenger of Allah ﷺ had commanded him. Then Abu Bakr stepped back until he was in line with the row, and the Prophet ﷺ came forward and prayed. When he finished, he said, 'O Abu Bakr, what prevented you from remaining when I commanded you?' Abu Bakr said, 'It was not for the son of Abu Quhafah to pray in front of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ.' The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, 'Why did I see you clapping so much? Whoever is faced with something during his prayer should glorify Allah, for if he glorifies, attention will be turned to him. Clapping is only for women.'"],[1317,"There was fighting among Banu Amr b. Awf, so the Prophet ﷺ came to them to reconcile between them. He had already prayed Zuhr, so he said to Bilal, 'If the time for Asr prayer comes and I have not come, tell Abu Bakr to lead the people in prayer.' When the time for Asr came, Bilal gave the adhan and the iqamah and said, 'O Abu Bakr, come forward.' Abu Bakr came forward. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ came and made his way through the rows. When the people saw the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, they clapped. Abu Bakr used not to turn around once he had entered the prayer. When he saw the clapping not stopping, he turned and saw the Messenger of Allah ﷺ behind him. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ gestured to him, 'Continue.' Abu Bakr paused a little, praised Allah for the command of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, then Abu Bakr walked backwards on his heels. When the Prophet ﷺ saw that, he came forward and led the people in their prayer. When he finished the prayer, he said, 'O Abu Bakr, what prevented you from continuing when I gestured to you?' Abu Bakr said, 'It was not for the son of Abu Quhafah to lead the Messenger of Allah ﷺ in prayer.' Then he said to the people, 'If something befalls you during your prayer, let the men glorify and the women clap.'"],[1318,"We came to Jabir b. Abd Allah in his mosque while he was praying in a single garment, wrapping himself with it. I stepped over the people until I sat between him and the qiblah. I said, “May Allah have mercy on you! You pray in a single garment while your cloak is beside you?!” He said, gesturing with his hand to my chest, “I wanted a fool like you to come in to me and see how I do it, so he would do the same. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ came to us in this mosque of ours with a stalk of Ibn Tab dates in his hand. He saw spittle in the qiblah of the mosque, so he went to it and scraped it with the stalk. Then he turned to us and said, ‘Which of you would like Allah to turn away from him?’” He said, “We were humbled. Then he said, ‘Which of you would like Allah to turn away from him?’ We said, ‘None of us, O Messenger of Allah.’ He said, ‘When one of you stands to pray, Allah is before his face, so let him not spit before his face nor to his right, but let him spit to his left under his left foot. If he is overtaken by haste, let him do thus with his garment,’ and he folded part of it over another. ‘Show me some perfume.’ A young man from the clan got up and hurried to his family, then came with khaluq in his two palms. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ took it and put it on the tip of the stalk, then smeared it over the trace of the spittle.” Jabir said, “From that time you started putting khaluq in your mosques.”"],[1319,"“Be moderate in prostration, and let none of you spread his forearms like a dog spreads them.”"],[1320,"When you prostrate, place your palms, raise your elbows, and hold yourself upright."],[1321,"I was with Umm Salamah, the wife of the Prophet ﷺ, when a young boy relative of hers with long hair came to her and stood to pray. When he went to prostrate, he blew on the ground. She said: 'Do not do that, for the Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to say to a black slave boy of ours: \"O Rabah, put your face on the dust.\" '"],[1322,"When one of you prostrates, let him not spread out like a dog spreads out; let him join his thighs together."],[1323,"Do not spread your forearms when you pray like the spreading of a wild beast; support yourself on your palms and keep your upper arms away from your sides, for when you do that, every limb of you prostrates."],[1324,"Whoever catches a rak'ah before the sun rises, and then the sun rises, let him pray another rak'ah to it."],[1325,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: 'Whoever catches a rak'ah of Asr before the sun sets has caught it, and whoever catches a rak'ah of Fajr before the sun rises and a rak'ah after the sun rises has caught it.'"],[1326,"A woman came to the Prophet ﷺ and said, \"O Messenger of Allah, my husband Safwan b. al-Mu'attal beats me when I pray and makes me break my fast when I fast, and he does not pray the Fajr prayer until the sun has risen.\" He said, while Safwan was with him, and he asked him about what she said. He said, \"O Messenger of Allah, as for her saying 'he beats me when I pray,' she recites two surahs of mine, and I have forbidden her from them.\" The Prophet ﷺ said, \"If it were one surah, it would suffice the people.\" He said, \"As for her saying 'he makes me break my fast when I fast,' she goes and fasts, while I am a young man and cannot endure.\" The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said on that day, \"A woman may not fast except with her husband's permission.\" He said, \"As for her saying 'I do not pray until the sun rises,' we are a household who hardly wake up until the sun has risen.\" He ﷺ said, \"When you wake up, then pray.\""],[1327,"Whoever has not prayed the two rak'ahs of Fajr, let him pray them after sunrise."],[1328,"“When one of you prays the two rak'ahs of Fajr, let him lie down on his right side.” Marwan b. al-Hakam said to him, “Is it not enough for one of us to walk to the mosque until he lies down?” He said, “No.” That reached Ibn Umar, and he said, “Abu Hurayrah has gone too far.” It was said to Ibn Umar, “Do you reject anything of what he says?” He said, “No, but he has gone too far and we have been too timid.” That reached Abu Hurayrah, and he said, “What is my fault if I remembered something and they forgot?”"],[1329,"A man called out to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and said: \"How do you command us to pray at night?\" He said: \"One of you should pray two rak'ahs at a time, and if he fears dawn, he should pray one rak'ah, which will make odd for him what he has already prayed at night.\""],[1330,"A man called the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and I was between them, asked: \"How is the night prayer?\" He said, \"Two by two. When you fear the approaching dawn, then pray one rakah and make two prostrations before dawn.\""],[1332,"The night prayer is two rak'ahs at a time, and when you want to finish, pray one rak'ah, which will make odd for you what you have already prayed."],[1333,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ entered the mosque while a rope was stretched between two pillars. He said, \"What is this?\" They said, \"It is for Zaynab; she prays and when she becomes lazy or tired she holds onto it.\" He said, \"Untie it.\" Then he said, \"Let one of you pray as long as he is energetic, and when he becomes lazy or tired, let him sit.\""],[1334,"“The Messenger of Allah ﷺ commanded the people of Madinah to enter ihram from Dhu al-Hulayfah, the people of Syria from al-Juhfah, and the people of Najd from Qarn.” Ibn 'Umar said: “As for these, I heard them from the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and I was informed that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: ‘And the people of Yemen enter ihram from Yalamlam.’”"],[1335,"“The Messenger of Allah ﷺ commanded the people of Madinah to enter ihram from Dhu al-Hulayfah, the people of Syria from al-Juhfah, and the people of Najd from Qarn.” Ibn 'Umar said: “As for these, I heard them from the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and I was informed that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: ‘And the people of Yemen enter ihram from Yalamlam.’”"],[1336,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ entered upon Duba'ah while she was ill. She said, \"I intend to perform Hajj while I am ill.\" He said to her, \"Perform Hajj and stipulate, 'My place of exiting ihram is wherever You restrain me.'\""],[1337,"A man came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ having entered ihram for 'Umrah wearing a jubbah and perfumed with khaluq. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ ordered him to \"remove it by pulling it off and wash twice or three times,\" and said, \"Whatever you would do in your Hajj, do it in your 'Umrah.\""],[1338,"A man came to the Prophet ﷺ while he was at al-Ji'ranah wearing a jubbah with khaluq on it, or he said traces of yellow perfume. He said, \"How do you command me to proceed in my 'Umrah?\" He said, \"Revelation descended upon the Prophet ﷺ, and he was covered with a cloth.\" Ya'la used to say, \"I wished I could see the Prophet ﷺ while revelation descended upon him.\" He said, \"'Umar lifted the edge of the cloth.\" He said, \"I looked at him, and he was snoring.\" He said, \"When it was over, he said, 'Where is the one asking about 'Umrah? Wash off the traces of yellow perfume'—or he said 'the khaluq'—'and remove your jubbah, and do in your 'Umrah as you would do in your Hajj.'\""],[1339,"We, the Companions of the Prophet ﷺ, entered ihram for ḥajj purely, with nothing else accompanying it. We arrived in Makkah on the morning of the fourth day of Dhū al-Ḥijjah. The Prophet ﷺ commanded us to exit ihram. He said: \"Exit ihram and make it an ʿumrah.\" News reached him that we were saying, when there were only five days left between us and ʿArafah: \"He commanded us to exit ihram; shall we go to Minā while our private parts are dripping with semen?\" The Prophet ﷺ stood and gave a sermon, saying: \"I have heard what you said. I am the most dutiful and most God-fearing of you. Were it not for the sacrificial animal, I would have exited ihram. If I were to face what I have turned my back on from my matter, I would not have brought a sacrificial animal.\" He said: And ʿAlī arrived from Yemen, and he said: \"With what did you enter ihram?\" He said: \"With what the Prophet ﷺ entered ihram with.\" He said: \"Then offer a sacrifice and remain in ihram as you are.\" He said: And Surāqah said to him: \"O Messenger of Allah, is this ʿumrah of ours for this year or forever?\" He said: \"Rather, forever.\""],[1340,"We set out coinciding with the new moon of Dhū al-Ḥijjah. The Prophet ﷺ said: \"Whoever wishes to enter ihram for ḥajj, let him do so; and whoever wishes to enter ihram for ʿumrah, let him enter ihram for ʿumrah.\" She said: So among us were those who entered ihram for ḥajj and among us those who entered ihram for ʿumrah. She said: I was among those who entered ihram for ʿumrah, until when we were at Sarif, I mentioned the menstrual period. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ entered upon me while I was weeping. I said: I wish I had not gone out this year. And she mentioned her menstrual period. She said: The Prophet ﷺ said: \"Undo your hair, comb it, and do what the Muslims do in their ḥajj.\" She said: So I obeyed Allah and His Messenger. When it was the night of departure, he commanded ʿAbd al-Raḥmān b. Abī Bakr, and he took her out to al-Tanʿīm. She said: So I entered ihram from it for ʿumrah."],[1341,"We set out with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ proclaiming the ḥajj loudly. When we performed ṭawāf of the House, he said: \"Make it an ʿumrah, except for those who have a sacrificial animal with them.\" He said: So we exited ihram and made it an ʿumrah. When it was the morning of al-Tarwiyah, we proclaimed the ḥajj loudly, then we set off to Minā."],[1342,"We set out with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ entering ihram for ḥajj. He arrived on the fourth of Dhū al-Ḥijjah. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ prayed the morning prayer at al-Baṭḥāʾ. When he had prayed, he said: \"Whoever wishes to make it an ʿumrah, let him do so.\""],[1343,"We set out with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ in the months of ḥajj, the nights of ḥajj, and the sacred precinct of ḥajj, until we alighted at Sarif. She said: He went out to his Companions and said: \"Whoever does not have a sacrificial animal with him and would like to make it an ʿumrah, let him do so; but whoever has a sacrificial animal with him, no.\" She said: Some of his Companions accepted it and some left it. She said: As for the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and some men among his Companions, they were people of strength and had sacrificial animals with them, so they were not able to do the ʿumrah. She said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ entered upon me while I was weeping. He said: \"What makes you weep, O little one?\" I said: I heard what you said to your Companions, so I was prevented from the ʿumrah. He said: \"What is the matter with you?\" I said: I cannot pray. He said: \"That does not harm you. You are only a woman among the daughters of Adam. Allah has decreed for you what He has decreed for them. So remain in your ḥajj; perhaps you will attain it.\" She said: So we set out on his ḥajj until we arrived at Minā. Then I became pure. Then I left Minā and performed the ifāḍah ṭawāf of the House. She said: Then I went out with him in the last group of departures until he alighted at al-Muḥaṣṣab, and we alighted with him. He called ʿAbd al-Raḥmān b. Abī Bakr and said: \"Take your sister out of the ḥaram, and let her enter ihram for ʿumrah. Then finish and come here, for I will wait for you until you come to me.\" She said: So I went out for that until I finished, and I finished the ṭawāf. Then I came to him before dawn. He said: \"Have you finished?\" I said: Yes. He said: \"Then announce departure among his Companions.\" So the people departed, and he passed by the House before the morning prayer and performed ṭawāf of it. Then he went out, mounted, and turned away heading to Madinah."],[1344,"I said to ‘A’ishah, when I was then young in age: “Have you considered the saying of Allah, mighty and sublime: ‘Indeed, al-Safa and al-Marwa are among the rites of Allah; so whoever performs Hajj of the House or ‘Umrah, there is no blame upon him to go between them’? I do not see anything upon anyone if he does not go between them.” ‘A’ishah said: “No, if it were as you say, it would have been: ‘there is no blame upon him not to go between them.’ This verse was revealed concerning the Ansar. They used to declare the talbiyah for Manat, and Manat was opposite Qudayd, and they used to consider it sinful to go between al-Safa and al-Marwa. When Islam came, they asked the Messenger of Allah ﷺ about that, and Allah revealed: ‘Indeed, al-Safa and al-Marwa are among the rites of Allah; so whoever performs Hajj of the House or ‘Umrah, there is no blame upon him to go between them. And whoever does good voluntarily, then indeed Allah is Appreciative and Knowing.’”"],[1345,"He heard Jabir b. 'Abd Allah mention the Hajj of the Prophet ﷺ. He said: So he commanded us, after we had performed tamattu' and then exited ihram, so the Prophet ﷺ said, \"When you want to depart to Mina, enter ihram.\" He said: So we entered ihram from al-Batha'."],[1346,"He performed Hajj with his masters. He said: I came to Umm Salamah, the Mother of the Believers, and said: O Mother of the Believers, I have never performed Hajj. With which of the two should I begin, the Umrah or the Hajj? She said: Begin with whichever of them you wish. He said: Then I came to Safiyyah, the Mother of the Believers, and asked her, and she said to me the same as she said. He said: Then I came to Umm Salamah and informed her of what Safiyyah said. Umm Salamah said to me: I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: “O family of Muhammad, whoever of you performs Hajj, let him enter ihram for Umrah within a Hajj.”"],[1347,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to the people on the evening of ʿArafah and the morning of Jamʿ when he departed, “Keep to tranquility,” while he was reining in his she-camel until he quickened the pace in the valley of Muḥassir, which is part of Mina. He said, “Keep to the pebbles for khudhaf with which the Jamrah is stoned.” He said, “And the Messenger of Allah ﷺ did not cease saying the talbiyah until he stoned the Jamrah.”"],[1348,"“The Messenger of Allah ﷺ sent him with his sacrificial animal and commanded him to give its meat, hides, and coverings in charity.”"],[1349,"The Prophet ﷺ “commanded him to stay with his camels and commanded him to distribute all of them—their meat, hides, and covers—to the poor, and not to give anything from them for the butcher’s wages.”"],[1350,"I said, “O Messenger of Allah, what should I do with the sacrificial camels that become exhausted?” He said, “Slaughter it, then dip its sandal in its blood, then leave it and the people, so they may eat it.”"],[1351,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ sent me with a message. I said, 'O Messenger of Allah, you are sending me while I am a young boy of recent age, and I will be asked about judicial matters, and I do not know how to answer.' He said, 'There is no escape from this: either I go with it, or you go.' He said, 'I said, \"If it must be so, then I will go.\"' He said, 'Go and recite it to the people, for Allah, exalted is He, will steady your tongue and guide your heart.' Then he said, 'People will bring disputes to you. When two adversaries come to you, do not judge in favor of one until you hear the words of the other, for that is more likely to make clear to you to whom the right belongs.'"],[1353,"We returned with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ from Makkah to Madinah. When we were partway, some people hurried at the time of Asr and performed ablution hastily. He said: We reached them while their heels were gleaming, untouched by water. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: 'Woe to the heels from the Fire! Complete the ablution.'"],[1354,"When you perform wudu', then draw water into your nose and expel it, and when you cleanse yourself with stones, then make it an odd number."],[1355,"About the Prophet ﷺ said, \"When one of you wakes up, let him observe Witr prayer, for indeed Allah Mighty and Majestic is odd-numbered and He loves odd-numbered.\" He also mentioned the seven heavens, seven days, and the Tawaf (circumambulation of the Kaaba). And he mentioned some other things."],[1356,"Consult women about their intimate parts. It was said, \"The virgin is shy.\" He said, \"Her silence is her consent.\""],[1357,"She asked the Prophet ﷺ about a virgin being sought in marriage. She said: The Prophet ﷺ said, \"Women are to be consulted about their intimate parts.\" She said, \"O Messenger of God, the virgin is shy and remains silent.\" He said, \"Her silence is her consent.\""],[1358,"The virgin is shy. He ﷺ said, \"Her consent is her silence.\""],[1359,"The previously married woman has more right over herself than her guardian, and the virgin is asked for permission, and her permission is her silence."],[1361,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to remember Allah in all his states."],[1362,"In the pre-Islamic era, when they performed the 'aqiqah for a newborn boy, they would dye a piece of cotton with the blood of the sacrificial animal. Then, when they shaved the baby's head, they would place it on his head. The Prophet ﷺ said, \"Put perfume in place of the blood.\""],[1363,"\"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ performed the 'aqiqah for Hasan and Husayn with two rams.\""],[1364,"We entered upon Hafsah bt. 'Abd al-Rahman and asked her about the 'aqiqah. She told us that 'A'ishah informed her that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, \"For a boy, two sheep; for a girl, one sheep.\""],[1365,"\"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ performed the 'aqiqah for Hasan and Husayn on the seventh day, named them, and ordered that the filth be removed from his head.\""],[1366,"She heard the Prophet ﷺ say concerning the 'aqiqah, \"For a boy, two sheep; for a girl, one sheep. It does not matter whether they are male or female.\""],[1367,"I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say concerning the 'aqiqah, \"For a boy, two equivalent sheep; for a girl, one sheep.\""],[1368,"that he said regarding those killed at Uhud: They carried their slain, then the caller of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ called out: «Return the slain to their places of falling»"],[1369,"The Prophet ﷺ went out from Madinah to the polytheists to fight them, and my father 'Abd Allah said to me, \"O Jabir, it would not harm you to be among the onlookers of the people of Madinah until you know what becomes of our affair. For I, by Allah, were it not that I leave behind daughters after me, I would have loved to be killed before you.\" While I was among the onlookers, my paternal cousin came with my father and my maternal uncle, balancing them on a weak camel, and entered Madinah with them to bury them in our graveyard. Then a man caught up, calling out: \"Indeed the Prophet ﷺ commands you to return with the slain and bury them in their places of falling, where they were killed.\" He said: So we returned them with the slain to where they were killed."],[1370,"I was among those concerning whom Saʿd b. Muʿādh judged. They doubted whether I was a minor or a combatant. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, “Look: if he has grown pubic hair, then kill him; otherwise, do not kill him.”"],[1371,"“The Prophet ﷺ ordered that blights be waived.”"],[1372,"A woman entered upon the Prophet ﷺ and said, \"By my father and mother, I and my son bought something from so-and-so and we weighed it. By the One who honored you with what He honored you with, we did not take anything from it except what we ate in our stomachs or fed to a needy person, hoping for blessings. And we have been setting aside what we owe from it until we receive the complete amount.\" Then the Prophet ﷺ took an oath by Allah three times, saying, \"He who does not act with righteousness will not be successful.\" The news reached the owner of the merchandise, and he said, \"By my father and mother, if you wish, I will return what you are owed, and if you wish, I will donate from the capital.\""],[1373,"A man suffered in the time of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ regarding fruits he had bought, and his debt grew large. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, “Give charity to him.” So charity was given to him, but it did not reach the amount to cover his debt. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, “Take what you find, and you have nothing but that.”"],[1374,"“If you sell fruit to your brother and a blight strikes it, it is not lawful for you to take anything from him. Why would you take your brother’s wealth without right?”"],[1375,"On the authority of the Prophet ﷺ, he said: “Attach the wealth to the prescribed shares, and whatever the prescribed shares leave over is for the nearest male relative.”"],[1376,"“Attach the wealth to the prescribed shares, and whatever the prescribed shares leave over is for the nearest male relative.”"],[1377,"“Attach the wealth to the prescribed shares, and whatever the prescribed shares leave over is for the nearest male relative.”"],[1378,"ʿAlī b. Abī Ṭālib ordered him to ask the Messenger of Allah ﷺ about a man when he approaches his wife: what is upon him? For his daughter is with me, and I am too shy to ask him. Al-Miqdād said: So I asked the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and he said, “When he finds that, let him sprinkle his private part and perform ablution as he does for prayer.”"],[1379,"I was a man who emitted madhy frequently, so I asked the Prophet ﷺ. He said, “When you see madhy, wash your penis; and when you see water (mani), perform ritual bathing.”"],[1380,"I used to suffer greatly from madhy, so I would bathe frequently because of it. I asked the Messenger of Allah ﷺ about that, and he said, “Ablution suffices you for it.” I said, “What about what gets on my garment from it?” He said, “It is enough for you to take a handful of water and sprinkle it on your garment wherever you think it has touched.”"],[1381,"When you put on clothes and when you perform ablution, begin with your right sides."],[1382,"\"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ commanded that Zakat al-Fitr be given before the people go out, and ʿAbd Allah used to give it a day or two before that.\""],[1383,"ʿAmmār b. Yāsir addressed us and was brief yet eloquent. When he descended, we said, \"O Abu al-Yaqẓān, you have been eloquent and brief; if only you had paused for breath.\" He said, \"I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say, 'A man's lengthy prayer and short sermon are a sign of his understanding; so lengthen the prayer and shorten the sermon, for some eloquence is sorcery.'\""],[1384,"The evil eye is real; and if anything could outstrip divine decree, the evil eye would do so. And when you are asked to wash [for someone afflicted by the evil eye], then wash."],[1386,"“If one of you breaks wind during prayer, he should leave, then perform wudu, and repeat his prayer. And do not approach women in their anuses.”"],[1387,"“If one of you breaks his ablution while in prayer, he should hold his nose and then leave.”"],[1388,"“If one of you breaks his ablution while in prayer, he should hold his nose and then leave.”"],[1389,"He divorced his wife once while she was menstruating. 'Umar asked the Messenger of Allah ﷺ for a ruling, saying, \"'Abdullah divorced his wife while she was menstruating.\" He said, \"Command 'Abdullah to take her back, then keep her until she is pure from this menstruation. Then when she menstruates another menstrual period and becomes pure, if he wishes he may divorce her before having intercourse with her, and if he wishes he may keep her.\""],[1390,"She was married to Thabit b. Qais b. Shammas, and the Messenger of Allah ﷺ went out for the dawn prayer and found Habibah bint Sahl at his door in the darkness. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, 'What is the matter with you?' She said, 'Neither I nor Thabit b. Qais,' meaning her husband. When Thabit came, the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, 'This is Habibah bint Sahl; she has mentioned what Allah willed that she mention.' Habibah said, 'O Messenger of Allah, all that he gave me is with me.' The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to Thabit b. Qais, 'Take it from her.' So he took it from her, and she sat with her family."],[1391,"The Prophet ﷺ gave a sermon one day and mentioned a man among his companions who had died and was shrouded in a poor shroud and buried at night. The Prophet ﷺ forbade that a man be buried at night or prayed over unless compelled to do so, and he said, 'When one of you takes charge of his brother, let him make his shroud good.'"],[1392,"'When you perfume the deceased, do so an odd number of times.'"],[1393,"\"Delay in payment by a rich man is injustice, and if one of you is referred to a wealthy man for payment, let him follow up.\""],[1394,"A man was mentioned to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ as being deceived in transactions. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"When you sell, say: 'No cheating.'\" He said: The man would say, when buying, \"No cheating.\""],[1395,"She had a male slave and a female slave who were married. She wanted to free them, and the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to her: 'If you free them, begin with the male slave before the female slave.'"],[1396,"If a fly falls into the vessel of one of you, let him dip it in completely, for in one of its wings is disease and in the other is healing. It protects itself with the wing containing the disease, so let him dip it all the way in, then remove it."],[1397,"“When you travel in fertile land, give camels their due; when you travel in a year of drought, hasten the pace on them; and when you camp at night, avoid the road, for it is the shelter of creatures.”"],[1398,"Help your brother, whether he is an oppressor or oppressed. It was said: O Messenger of Allah, this one I help when he is oppressed, but how do I help him when he is an oppressor? He said: 'You restrain him from oppression; that is your help to him.'"],[1399,"Help your brother, whether he is an oppressor or oppressed. They said: O Messenger of Allah, this one we help when he is oppressed, but how do we help him when he is an oppressor? He said: 'You restrain him from oppression.'"],[1400,"“When one of you reaches a gathering, let him greet; and when he gets up, let him greet. The first is not more deserving than the last.”"],[1401,"“Let the rider greet the walker, the walker greet the sitter, and the few greet the many.”"],[1402,"A Jew greeted the Prophet ﷺ and his companions and said, \"May death be upon you (al-sām ʿalaykum).\" The Prophet ﷺ said, \"Do you know what he said?\" They said, \"Yes, he greeted us.\" He said, \"No, he only said, 'May death be upon you,' meaning 'may you be deprived of your religion.' So when a man from the People of the Book greets you, say, 'And upon you.'\""],[1403,"When one of you puts on sandals, let him begin with the right; and when he takes them off, let him begin with the left. The right should be the first to be put on and the last to be taken off."],[1404,"The Prophet ﷺ used to like starting from the right side in everything, even in combing his hair and wearing sandals."],[1405,"She brought to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ a son of hers who had not eaten food, and she had treated him with 'udhra (a throat ailment). The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: 'Why do you press your children's throats with this treatment? Use this Indian wood—meaning costus—for it contains seven cures, including pleurisy.'"],[1407,"“Come close, my dear son, mention Allah's name, eat with your right hand, and eat from what is near you.”"],[1408,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ was brought milk mixed with water, with a bedouin on his right and Abu Bakr on his left. He drank and then gave it to the bedouin, saying, \"The right, then the right.\""],[1409,"\"Overlook the slips of people of good standing.\""],[1410,"The Prophet ﷺ saw a woman, then he went in to Zaynab and fulfilled his need, then came out and said: “When a woman approaches, she approaches in the form of a devil. If one of you sees a woman who pleases him, let him go to his wife, for she has the like of what that woman has.”"],[1411,"When one of you looks at someone favored over him in wealth and physical build, let him look to one who is below him, over whom he has been favored."],[1412,"A man among the companions of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ manumitted a slave of his after his death, and he had no property other than him. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ ordered that he be sold, and he said: “You are more entitled to his price, and Allah has no need of him.”"],[1413,"«Whoever changes his religion, kill him.»"],[1414,"«Whoever abandons his religion — or he said: turns back from his religion — kill him, and do not punish anyone with the punishment of Allah.»"],[1415,"A man called Abu Madhkur arranged the manumission of a slave of his after his death, and he had no other property. The slave was called Ya'qub. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, \"Who will buy this?\" A man from Banu 'Adi b. Ka'b bought him for one hundred dirhams. The Prophet ﷺ said, \"If one of you is in need, let him begin with himself. If he has surplus, then for his family. If he has surplus, then for his relatives. If he has surplus, then here and here and here.\""],[1416,"\"There will be troubles and troubles. Whoever wants to divide the matter of this community while they are united, strike him with the sword, whoever he may be.\""],[1417,"\"After me there will be trials and more trials. Whoever you see separating from the community or wanting to divide the community of Muhammad ﷺ while their affair is united, kill him, no matter who he is, for the hand of Allah is with the community, and Satan runs with the one who separates from the community.\""],[1418,"When one of you sees someone favored over him in physical build or provision, let him look to one who is below him, over whom he has been favored."],[1419,"I memorized the Qur'an and recited it all in one night. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to him, 'Recite it in a month.' He said, 'O Messenger of Allah, let me enjoy my strength and youth.' He said, 'Recite it in ten days.' He said, 'O Messenger of Allah, let me enjoy my strength and youth.' He said, 'Recite it in seven days.' He said, 'O Messenger of Allah, let me enjoy my strength and youth.' He said, 'He refused.'"],[1420,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ came out to us one day while we were reciting [the Qur'an], and he said, \"Praise be to Allah. The Book of Allah is one, and among you are the red and among you are the black. Recite it before people recite it who will straighten it as arrows are straightened, hastening their reward and not delaying it.\""],[1421,"The Prophet ﷺ passed by him while he had uncovered his thigh, so he said, 'Cover it, for it is part of the private area.'"],[1422,"“If one of you becomes angry while standing, let him sit down. If the anger leaves him, then fine; otherwise let him lie down.”"],[1423,"I entered upon Abū Saʿīd al-Khudrī ؓ in his house. He said: I found him praying, so I sat waiting for him until he finished his prayer. Then I heard movement under the bed in his house, and it was a snake. I got up to kill it, but he gestured to me to sit down. When he finished, he pointed to a room in the house and said, “Do you see this room?” I said, “Yes.” He said, “There was a young man among us who had recently married, so we went out with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ to the trench. That young man used to ask his permission at midday and return to his wife. One day he asked the Prophet ﷺ for permission, and he said to him, ‘Take your weapon, for I fear for you from the Qurayẓah.' So he took his weapon and went, and there was his wife standing between the two doors. He aimed his spear at her to thrust it because of jealousy, but she said, ‘Hold back your spear until you see what is in your house.' He entered and found a huge snake coiled on his bed. He struck at it and pierced it with the spear, then went out and fixed the spear in the courtyard, and the snake writhed on the spearhead while the young man fell dead. We did not know which of them died first, the young man or the snake. We went to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and mentioned that to him, saying, ‘Call upon Allah to bring him back to life.' He said, ‘Ask forgiveness for your companion.' Then he said, ‘There are jinn in Madinah who have accepted Islam, so if you see any of them, give it notice for three days. If it appears to you after that, then kill it, for it is only a devil.'”"],[1424,"While the Prophet ﷺ was delivering a sermon, he saw a man standing in the sun. He asked about him, and they said, 'This is Abu Isra'il. He has vowed to stand in the sun, not to sit, not to seek shade, not to speak, and not to break his fast.' He said, 'Order him to sit, seek shade, speak, and fast, and break his fast (*).'"],[1425,"Whoever vows to obey Allah, let him obey Him; and whoever vows to disobey Allah, let him not disobey Him."],[1426,"Whoever vows to disobey Allah, let him not disobey Him."],[1427,"When you see it, fast, and when you see it, break the fast. If it is obscured for you, then estimate it."],[1428,"Fast at its sighting and break the fast at its sighting. If it is obscured for you, then estimate thirty."],[1429,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to be cautious about the crescent of Sha'ban more than he was about others, then he would fast upon sighting the crescent of Ramadan. If it was obscured for him, he would count thirty days, then fast."],[1430,"When you see the crescent, fast, and when you see it, break the fast. If it is obscured for you, then count thirty."],[1431,"«Some of his paternal uncles testified before the Prophet ﷺ to the sighting of the crescent, so the Prophet ﷺ ordered them to go out for their Eid on the following day.»"],[1432,"A bedouin came to the Prophet ﷺ and said, 'I sighted the crescent tonight.' He said, 'Do you testify that there is no god but Allah and that Muhammad is His servant and Messenger?' He said, 'Yes.' He said, 'Stand, O so-and-so, and call out among the people that they should fast tomorrow.'"],[1433,"The people looked for the crescent, and I saw it and informed the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, so he fasted and commanded the people to fast."],[1434,"Do not precede the fast of the month of Ramadan by fasting a day or two, except a man who was already observing a fast, then let him fast it."],[1435,"The month is only twenty-nine, so do not fast until you see it, and do not break your fast until you see it; and if it is obscured for you, then estimate it."],[1436,"«The month is thirty, and the month is twenty-nine. If it is obscured from you, then count thirty.»"],[1437,"Do not fast before Ramadan; fast upon seeing it and break your fast upon seeing it. And if a cloud covers it, then complete thirty (days)."],[1438,"'Ammar b. Yasir: 'Whoever fasts the day that is doubted has disobeyed Abu al-Qasim ﷺ.'"],[1439,"«Fast upon sighting it, and break the fast upon sighting it. If it is obscured from you, then fast thirty.»"],[1440,"«Do not anticipate the month until you see the crescent or complete the count. Then fast until you see the crescent or complete the count.»"],[1441,"«Fast upon sighting it, and break the fast upon sighting it. If it is obscured from you, then count thirty days, and then break the fast.»"],[1443,"If they drink it, flog them. Then if they drink it, flog them. Then if they drink it, flog them. Then if they drink it, kill them."],[1444,"“Learn the Qurʾān, for it will come on the Day of Resurrection as an intercessor for its companions. And adhere to the two bright ones, al-Baqarah and Āl ʿImrān, for they will come on the Day of Resurrection as if they were two clouds, or two canopies, or two flocks of birds, arguing on behalf of their companions. And adhere to Sūrat al-Baqarah, for taking it is a blessing and leaving it is a regret, and the false ones cannot withstand it.”"],[1445,"Indeed, a surah in the Quran with thirty verses intercedes for its reciter until he is forgiven: {Tabarak alladhi biyadihi al-mulk}."],[1446,"Publicize the marriage."],[1447,"\"Strive against the idolators with your wealth, your hands and your tongues.\" [1] [1] Its chain has defects while its meaning is supported by other chains. (Using translation from Nasāʾī 3096)"],[1448,"I went out with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ on a raid. He said: “Did you marry?” I said: “Yes.” He said: “A virgin or a previously married woman?” I said: “Rather, a previously married woman.” He said: “Why not a young girl whom you could play with and she could play with you?” I said: “I have sisters, so I preferred to marry a woman who would bring them together, comb their hair, and take care of them.” He said: “Indeed, you are arriving, so when you arrive, act wisely, act wisely.”"],[1449,"I married Umm Yahya bint Abi Ihab. A black woman came to us and claimed that she had breastfed us all. I went to the Prophet ﷺ and mentioned that to him. He said: \"How can you stay with her when she has said what she said? Leave her.\""],[1450,"He married the daughter of Abu Ihab. A black woman claimed that she had breastfed both of them. I came to the Prophet ﷺ and mentioned that to him, but he turned away from me. I came to him from the other side and said: \"O Messenger of Allah, she is lying.\" He said: \"How can you stay with her when she has claimed that she breastfed both of you?\" So he forbade him from her."],[1451,"He said, \"I breastfed Uqbah, who married me, and Uqbah said to me, 'I don't know that you breastfed me and didn't inform me.' So he sent a message to the family of Abi Ihab and asked them, and they said, 'We don't know that she breastfed our companion.' Uqbah then rode to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ in Medina and asked him. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, 'How is it possible when it has already been mentioned?' So Uqbah left her and married someone else.\""],[1452,"We were sitting with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ when the sun eclipsed. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ stood up alarmed, dragging his garment until he entered the mosque and prayed two rak‘ahs. He continued praying them until the sun cleared. That was at the death of Ibrahim, the son of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. The people said, “The sun eclipsed only because of Ibrahim’s death.” The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, “O people, the sun and the moon are two signs among the signs of Allah. They do not eclipse because of anyone’s death. So when you see that, supplicate until what is upon you is removed.”"],[1453,"We were with the Prophet ﷺ when the sun eclipsed. He ﷺ hurried to the mosque, dragging his lower garment or his robe, and people rushed to him. He prayed two rak‘ahs with them, similar to what you pray. Then it cleared. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ turned to the people and said, “The sun and the moon are two signs among the signs of Allah. He frightens His servants with them. They do not eclipse because of the death of anyone among people.” His son had died. “So when you see any of that, pray until it clears.”"],[1454,"“Throw dust in the mouths of the flatterers.”"],[1455,"They were with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ when they captured some domestic donkeys and slaughtered them. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, \"Overturn the cooking pots.\""],[1456,"She was married to Abu 'Amr b. Hafs b. al-Mughirah, who divorced her with the last of three divorces. She claimed that she came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and sought his ruling about leaving her house, and he commanded her to move to the house of Ibn Umm Maktum, the blind man."],[1457,"Abu 'Amr b. Hafs divorced her irrevocably while he was absent in Syria. He sent his agent to her with barley, and she was displeased with it. He said, 'By Allah, you have no claim on us for anything.' She came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and mentioned that to him. He said to her, 'You have no right to maintenance from him,' and commanded her to observe her waiting period in the house of Umm Sharik. Then he said, 'That is a woman whom my companions visit; observe your waiting period with Ibn Umm Maktum, for he is a blind man, and you can put off your garments wherever you wish. When you become lawful, inform me.' She said, 'When I became lawful, I mentioned to him that Mu'awiyah b. Abi Sufyan and Abu Jahm had proposed to me.' The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, 'As for Abu Jahm, he does not put down his stick from his shoulder; and as for Mu'awiyah, he is destitute with no property. Marry Usamah b. Zaid.' She said, 'I disliked that.' Then he said, 'Marry Usamah.' So I married him, and Allah placed good in him, and I was content with him."],[1458,"Her husband was in one of the villages of Madinah, and he pursued some non-Arab laborers, and they killed him. She came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and mentioned her feeling of loneliness and mentioned that she was in a house that did not belong to her, and she asked his permission to go to her brothers in Madinah. He granted her permission, then called her back and said to her, 'Stay in the house in which the news of his death came to you until the prescribed term reaches its end.'"],[1459,"She came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ asking him to allow her to return to her family among the Banu Khudrah, for her husband had gone out in pursuit of some slaves of his who had fled, and when they were at the edge of al-Qadum, they caught up with him and killed him. I asked the Messenger of Allah ﷺ to allow me to return to my family, for my husband had not left me in a house that he owned, nor any maintenance. She said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, 'Yes.' So I turned away, and when I was in the room or in the mosque, the Messenger of Allah ﷺ called me or ordered me to be called, so I was summoned to him. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, 'What did you say?' She said: I repeated to him the story I had mentioned about my husband's situation. He said, 'Stay in your house until the prescribed term reaches its end.' She said: So I observed the waiting period in it for four months and ten days."],[1460,"Abd Allah b. Abbas and Abu Salamah b. Abd al-Rahman differed about a woman who gave birth a few nights after her husband's death. Abd Allah said, 'The later of the two terms,' and Abu Salamah said, 'When she gives birth, she has become lawful.' He said: Abu Hurayrah came and said, 'I am with my nephew,' meaning Abu Salamah. So they sent Kurayb, the freed slave of Ibn Abbas, to Umm Salamah, the wife of the Prophet ﷺ, and he asked her about that. He came back to them and informed them that she said: Subay'ah al-Aslamiyyah gave birth a few nights after her husband's death, and she mentioned that to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and he said to her, 'You have become lawful, so marry.'"],[1461,"Abd Allah b. Abbas and Abu Hurayrah were asked about a woman whose husband died while she was pregnant. Ibn Abbas said, 'The later of the two terms,' and Abu Hurayrah said, 'When she gives birth, she has become lawful.' Then Abu Salamah entered upon Umm Salamah and asked her about that. She said: Subay'ah al-Aslamiyyah gave birth half a month after her husband's death. Two men proposed to her, one a young man and the other an older man, and she inclined to the young man. The older man said, 'You have not become lawful.' Her family was absent, and he hoped that when her family came, they would prefer him to her. She came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and he said, 'You have become lawful, so marry whomever you wish.'"],[1462,"We set out with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ intending only Hajj. When we were at Sarif, I menstruated. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ came to me while I was crying and said, \"What is the matter with you? Have you started your period?\" I said, \"Yes.\" He said, \"This is a matter which Allah has decreed for the daughters of Adam, so perform whatever the pilgrim performs except that you do not perform tawaf around the House.\" And the Messenger of Allah ﷺ sacrificed cows on behalf of his wives."],[1463,"Safiyyah bt. Huyayy menstruated after she had performed tawaf. A'ishah said: I mentioned her menstruation to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, \"Is she holding us back?\" She said: I said, \"O Messenger of Allah, she had performed the ifadah and circumambulated the House, then she menstruated after the ifadah.\" The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, \"Then let her depart.\""],[1464,"The brother of Abū Quʿays sought permission to enter upon me after the veil was imposed on us. I said: I will not permit you until the Prophet ﷺ comes. When the Prophet ﷺ came, I sought his permission and said: O Messenger of God, the brother of Abū Quʿays sought permission to enter upon me, but I refused to permit him until I seek your permission. It was only the wife of Abū Quʿays who suckled me; Abū Quʿays did not suckle me. He ﷺ said: \"Permit him, for he is your paternal uncle.\""],[1465,"\"My foster uncle came and asked permission to enter upon me, but I refused to permit him until I asked the Prophet ﷺ. She said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ came, and I asked him. He said: 'He is your uncle, so permit him.' She said: 'O Messenger of Allah, only the woman nursed me; the man did not nurse me.' The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: 'What is forbidden by birth is forbidden by suckling.'\""],[1466,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ would command one of us, when she was menstruating, to wear an izar, and then he would touch her."],[1467,"When the Messenger of Allah ﷺ wanted to lie with one of his wives while she was menstruating, he would command her, and she would wear an izar."],[1468,"Fatimah bt. Abi Hubaysh came to the Prophet ﷺ and said: \"O Messenger of Allah, I experience istihadah for a month or two months?\" He said: \"That is not menstruation, but rather it is a vein. When menstruation comes, abandon prayer for the number of days you used to menstruate in it. When it departs, perform ghusl and perform wudu for every prayer.\""],[1469,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ was asked about the mustahadah, and he said: \"She should abandon prayer for her [menstrual] days, then perform ghusl once, then perform wudu at every prayer.\""],[1470,"It is not lawful for a woman who believes in Allah and the Last Day to mourn for a deceased person more than three nights, except for a husband, four months and ten days."],[1471,"“If a man calls his wife to his need, she should respond to him even if she is at the oven.”"],[1472,"“Your affairs are among what concerns me after I am gone, and none will be patient with you after me except the patient.” He said: Then she says, “May God give your father to drink from the Salsabil of Paradise,” meaning ‘Abd al-Rahman b. ‘Awf. He had provided for the wives of the Prophet ﷺ with wealth sold for forty thousand."],[1473,"“If a foreleg were gifted to me, I would accept it, and if I were invited to it, I would respond.”"],[1474,"“If people knew what is in the call to prayer and the first row, and they found no way to it except by drawing lots, they would draw lots. If they knew what is in going early, they would race to it. And if they knew what is in the late evening prayer and the dawn prayer, they would come to them even crawling.”"],[1475,"\"How can a nation be sanctified when the rights of their weak are not taken from their strong?\""],[1477,"\"When you pass by our graves and the graves of the people of Jahiliyyah, tell them that they are in the Fire.\""],[1478,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ passed by a dead sheep and said: \"Why did you not make use of its skin?\" They said: \"O Messenger of Allah, it is dead.\" He said: \"Only its eating is forbidden.\""],[1479,"Maymunah, the wife of the Prophet ﷺ, narrated to me that a sheep of theirs [died], and the Prophet ﷺ said: \"Why did you not tan its hide and make use of it?\""],[1480,"I brought milk to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ while he was at al-Naqi', uncovered. He said, 'Why did you not cover it, even by placing a stick across it?'"],[1481,"The Prophet (peace be upon him) said, \"Indeed, the believer is to the believer like a building, each part supporting and strengthening the other.\""],[1482,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ came to us as a visitor in our home and saw a man with disheveled hair, so he said, \"Could this one not find something to settle his hair with?\" And he saw a man wearing dirty clothes, so he said, \"Could this one not find something to wash his garment with?\""],[1483,"The Prophet ﷺ gave a sermon on Friday and saw upon them garments of namirah (striped wool). The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, 'Why should one of you, if he finds the means, not take two garments for his Friday, other than his two working garments?'"],[1484,"I witnessed the Messenger of Allah ﷺ reciting in prayer and he omitted something he did not recite. A man said to him, “O Messenger of Allah, you omitted such-and-such a verse.” He said, “Why did you not remind me of it?”"],[1485,"I witnessed the Messenger of Allah ﷺ reciting in prayer and he faltered in a verse. A man said, “O Messenger of Allah, you omitted a verse.” He said, “Why did you not remind me of it?” He said, “I thought it had been abrogated.” He said, “It has not been abrogated.”"],[1486,"The Prophet ﷺ prayed a prayer and became confused in it. When he finished, he said to Ubayy, “Did you pray with us?” He said, “Yes.” He said, “What prevented you from prompting me?”"],[1487,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ entered the mosque and said, “Will you not form rows as the angels form rows before their Lord?” They said, “O Messenger of Allah, how do the angels form rows before their Lord?” He said, “They complete the first rows and stand close together in the row.”"],[1488,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ came to me (at night) and said, “Will you not pray?” I said, “O Messenger of Allah, our souls are in Allah’s hand; if He wills to raise us, He raises us.” The Messenger of Allah ﷺ left when I said that and did not reply to me with anything. Then I heard him striking his hand and saying, “{Man is the most disputatious of all things}” (18:54)."],[1489,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ entered the mosque, and a man entered and prayed. Then he came and sat down. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"Go back and pray, for you have not prayed.\" He did that three times. The man said: \"By the One who sent you with the truth, I do not know anything other than this, so teach me.\" He said: \"When you stand for prayer, say the takbir, then recite whatever is easy for you from the Quran, then bow until you are at ease in bowing, then rise until you are standing straight, then prostrate until you are at ease in prostration, then rise until you are sitting at ease. Do that throughout your prayer.\""],[1490,"Ammar b. Yasir prayed two rak'ahs and made them light. Abd al-Rahman b. al-Harith said to him: \"O Abu al-Yaqzan, I see that you have made them light.\" He said: \"I hastened through them to avoid distracting thoughts. I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: 'A man may pray a prayer and perhaps he gets only a tenth of it, or a ninth, or an eighth, or a seventh, or a sixth'\" until he counted all the fractions."],[1491,"«The Messenger of Allah ﷺ commanded us to scrutinize the eye and the ear.»"],[1492,"«Four are not permissible among sacrificial animals: the one-eyed whose defect is evident, the lame whose limp is evident, the sick whose illness is evident, and the emaciated that has no marrow.»"],[1493,"I asked Al-Bara' ibn 'Azib what the Messenger of Allah ﷺ disliked about sacrificial animals. He said, the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, \"There are four types that are not permissible in the sacrificial animals of Eid Al-Adha: a lame animal with a visible limp, a blind animal with visible blindness, a sick animal with evident sickness, and an animal that is emaciated and cannot be fattened.\""],[1494,"\"I heard the Prophet ﷺ saying, 'Recite the Quran from four people - Abdullah ibn Mas'ud, Salim, the freed slave of Abu Hudhaifa, Mu'adh ibn Jabal, and Ubay ibn Ka'b.'\""],[1495,"“Beware of the supplication of the wronged.”"],[1496,"“The supplication of the wronged is carried on the clouds, and the gates of the heavens are opened for it, and the Lord, Blessed and Exalted, says: By My might, I will surely help you, even after a while.”"],[1497,"That the Prophet ﷺ passed by a woman at a grave weeping and said, 'O woman, be patient.' She said, 'You do not know my affliction.' Then it was said to her afterwards, 'This is the Messenger of Allah ﷺ.' So she came to him and said, 'I did not recognize you.'"],[1498,"Bashir b. Sa'd came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and said: 'I have given this son of mine this slave.' The Prophet ﷺ said: 'Have you given all your children the like of this?' He said: 'No.' He said: 'Then take it back.'"],[1499,"My father took me to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ to have him witness a gift he was giving me. He said: 'Do you have any other children besides him?' I said: 'Yes.' He said: 'Treat them equally.'"],[1500,"\"My father took me to the Messenger of Allah to ask him to bear witness to a gift that he had given me. He said: 'Do you have any other children besides him?' He said: 'Yes.' He said: 'Treat them equally.'\" (Using translation from Nasāʾī 3686)"],[1501,"His father brought him to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and said: 'I have given this son of mine a slave that I owned.' The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: 'Have you given all your children the like of this?' He said: 'No.' The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: 'Then take it back.'"],[1502,"Bashir's wife said: 'Give this son of mine a slave as a gift, and have the Messenger of Allah ﷺ witness it.' The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: 'Does he have brothers?' He said: 'Yes.' He said: 'Did you give each of them the like of what you gave him?' He said: 'No.' He said: 'This is not right, and I do not bear witness except to what is true.'"],[1503,"That his father gave him a slave. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: 'What is this slave?' He said: 'A slave my father gave me.' He said: 'Did he give all your brothers as he gave you?' He said: 'No.' He said: 'Then return him.' And he said to his father: 'Do not call me as a witness to injustice.'"],[1504,"My mother asked my father for some gift from his wealth, and he put her off for a year. Then it occurred to him and he gave it to me. She said: 'I will not be satisfied until you have the Messenger of Allah ﷺ witness it.' He said: 'O Messenger of Allah, the mother of this one, the daughter of Rawaha, has disputed with me for a year over a gift for this son of mine. Now it has occurred to me to give it to him, and she would like you to witness it, O Messenger of Allah.' He said: 'O Bashir, do you have any child other than this one?' He said: 'Yes.' He said: 'Do not call me as a witness to injustice.'"],[1505,"\"To allow me to have a honey bee from his property, but he refused. Then after a while or two, he offered to give me a honey bee. I said to the person who had asked for it for my son, 'I had prevented you, but it has become clear to me that I should allow it for him.' She said, 'No, by Allah, I will not agree until you take him by the hand and present him to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ so that he may intercede for you.' So he took me by the hand and brought me to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and narrated the incident to him. The Prophet ﷺ said to him, 'Do you have any other offspring besides him?' He said, 'Yes.' The Prophet ﷺ asked, 'Have you given each of them the same as you have given this one?' He replied, 'No.' The Prophet ﷺ then said, 'I will not bear witness in favor of this action. This is an injustice. I only bear witness in favor of justice. Be fair to your children in regard to the bees as you would like them to be fair to you in righteousness and kindness.'\""],[1506,"Bashir b. Sa'd came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and said: 'O Messenger of Allah, 'Amra bt. Rawaha wanted me to give a charitable gift to her son and told me to have you witness it.' The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to him: 'Do you have sons other than him?' He said: 'Yes.' He said: 'Did you give all of them the like of what you gave this one?' He said: 'No.' He said: 'Then do not call me as a witness to injustice.'"],[1507,"My father gave me such-and-such, and he brought me to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ to have him witness it. He said: 'Did you give all your children the like of what you gave him?' He said: 'No.' The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: 'Have someone other than me witness this. This is injustice.' Then he said: 'Would you like them to be equal in dutifulness to you?' He said: 'Yes.' He said: 'Then not so.'"],[1508,"My father Bashir b. Sa'd came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and said: 'O Messenger of Allah, 'Amra bt. Rawaha gave birth to a boy, and I named him Nu'man. She refused to raise him unless I gave him a garden of mine, the best of my property. She said: 'Have the Prophet ﷺ witness that.' The Prophet ﷺ said to him: 'Do you have any child other than him?' He said: 'Yes.' He said: 'Do not call me as a witness except to justice, for I do not witness injustice.'"],[1510,"For every action there is a period of enthusiasm, and for every period of enthusiasm there is a period of slackening. Whoever's enthusiasm is toward my Sunnah has succeeded, and whoever's enthusiasm is toward other than that has perished."],[1511,"\"Soon the best wealth of a Muslim will be a small flock he follows to the mountain peaks and places of rainfall, fleeing with his religion from tribulations.\""],[1512,"\"A legal penalty carried out in the earth is better than forty mornings of rain.\""],[1513,"I came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ intending to ask him something, and I heard him delivering a sermon, saying: “Whoever seeks self-sufficiency, Allah will make him self-sufficient; whoever seeks chastity, Allah will keep him chaste; and whoever asks us, we will give him.” He said: So I turned back and did not ask him, and today I am the wealthiest of the Ansar."],[1514,"The example of a righteous companion and an evil companion is like that of a carrier of musk and a blower of the bellows. The carrier of musk either sells you some, or you find a pleasant scent from him; and the blower of the bellows either burns your clothes or you find a foul smell from him."],[1515,"Gentleness was never in anything but it adorned it, and obscenity was never in anything but it disfigured it."],[1516,"The woman is private; when she goes out, Satan seeks to seduce her, and the closest she is to her Lord is when she is in the innermost part of her house."],[1517,"\"The two parties to a sale have the option as long as they do not separate. If they are truthful and make things clear, they will be blessed in their sale; if they lie and conceal, the blessing of their sale will be erased.\""],[1518,"«The fitrah is five: circumcision, shaving the pubic hair, trimming the mustache, clipping the nails, and plucking the armpit hair.»"],[1519,"The Prophet ﷺ as saying: The inborn characteristics of man are five. Another version says: Five things are of the inborn characteristics of man: circumcision, shaving the pubes, plucking out hair under the armpit, paring the nails and clipping the moustaches. (Using translation from Abū Dāʾūd 4198)"],[1520,"Indeed, I am to you like a parent. When one of you goes to relieve himself, he should not face the qiblah nor turn his back to it, and he should not cleanse himself with his right hand.\" And he commanded using three stones and forbade using dung and bones."],[1521,"A Bedouin stood in the mosque and urinated. People grabbed him, but the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to them, \"Leave him, and pour a bucket of water over his urine, for you have been sent to make things easy, not to make them difficult.\""],[1522,"There is no amputation except for a quarter dinar or more."],[1523,"A young slave stole a small shoot from a walled garden. He was brought to Marwan, who ordered his hand to be cut off. Rafi' b. Khadij said: The Prophet ﷺ said: \"There is no amputation for fruit or palm pith.\""],[1524,"The conditions most deserving to be fulfilled are those by which you have made sexual intercourse lawful."],[1525,"Glorification is for men and clapping is for women."],[1526,"\"There is no obligatory prayer except that before it are two rak'ahs.\""],[1527,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ was brought milk mixed with water, with a bedouin on his right and Abu Bakr on his left. He drank and then gave it to the bedouin, saying, \"The right, then the right.\""],[1528,"“The oen who serves water to others should be the last one to drink from it.” (Using translation from Ibn Mājah 3434)"],[1531,"Every matter of importance not begun with praise of Allah is cut off."],[1532,"Al-Aqraʿ b. Ḥābis al-Tamīmī saw the Prophet ﷺ kissing Al-Ḥasan b. ʿAlī and said, “I have ten children and have never kissed any of them.” The Prophet of Allah ﷺ said: “Whoever does not show mercy will not be shown mercy.”"],[1533,"Seven [nights] for the virgin and three for the previously married."],[1534,"I have emphasized the siwak to you repeatedly."],[1535,"The Prophet ﷺ said: \"Witr is one rak'ah at the end of the night.\" (Using translation from Nasāʾī 1689)"],[1536,"The neighbor has more right to his adjacent property."],[1537,"I was with Saʿd b. Abī Waqqāṣ and al-Miswar b. Makhrama when Abū Rāfiʿ, the freedman of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, came and said to Saʿd b. Mālik: “Buy from me my two houses that are in your compound.” He said: “No, except for four thousand in installments” or he said “in portions.” He said: “By Allah, had I not heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say, ‘The neighbor has more right to his adjacent property,’ I would not have sold them to you. I was offered five hundred dinars for them.”"],[1538,"Preemption applies to what has not been divided. Once boundaries are set and roads are laid out, there is no preemption."],[1539,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ ruled for preemption in everything that has not been divided. Once boundaries are set and roads are laid out, there is no preemption."],[1540,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ ruled for preemption in everything that has not been divided. Once boundaries are set and roads are laid out, there is no preemption."],[1541,"Three things: whoever has them finds the sweetness of faith — for Allah and His Messenger to be more beloved to him than anything besides them; to love a person, loving him only for Allah's sake; and to hate returning to disbelief as much as he hates a fire being lit for him to be thrown into."],[1542,"\"Bilal was commanded to say the phrases of the Adhan twice and the phrases of the Iqamah once.\" (Using translation from Ibn Mājah 730)"],[1543,"\"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ commanded Bilal to say the phrases of the Adhan twice and the phrases of the Iqamah once.\" (Using translation from Nasāʾī 627)"],[1544,"«The adhan in the time of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ was in pairs, in pairs, and the iqamah single, except that he would say: The prayer has been established, twice.»"],[1545,"\"They looked for something by means of which they could call out informing of (the time of) the prayer. Then Bilal was commanded to say the phrases of the Adhan twice and the phrases of the Iqamah once.\" (Using translation from Ibn Mājah 729)"],[1546,"When the Prophet ﷺ commanded the bell to be struck to gather the people for prayer, a man wearing two green garments and carrying a bell in his hand came to me at night while I was sleeping. I said: O servant of Allah, will you sell the bell? He said: What will you do with it? I said: I will call the people to prayer with it. He said: Shall I not guide you to what is better than that? I said: Yes. He said: When you want to give the call, say: Allahu akbar, Allahu akbar, Allahu akbar, Allahu akbar; ashhadu an lā ilāha illā Allāh, ashhadu an lā ilāha illā Allāh; ashhadu anna Muḥammadan rasūlu Allāh, ashhadu anna Muḥammadan rasūlu Allāh; ḥayya ʿalā al-ṣalāh, ḥayya ʿalā al-ṣalāh; ḥayya ʿalā al-falāḥ, ḥayya ʿalā al-falāḥ; Allahu akbar, Allahu akbar; lā ilāha illā Allāh. Then he stepped back a little and said: When you establish the prayer, say: Allahu akbar, Allahu akbar; ashhadu an lā ilāha illā Allāh; ashhadu anna Muḥammadan rasūlu Allāh; ḥayya ʿalā al-ṣalāh; ḥayya ʿalā al-falāḥ; qad qāmat al-ṣalāh, qad qāmat al-ṣalāh; Allahu akbar, Allahu akbar; lā ilāha illā Allāh. When morning came, I went to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and told him. He said: «It is indeed a true vision, if Allah wills. Arise and cast upon Bilal what you saw, and let him give the call, for he has a louder voice.» So I stood with Bilal and began casting it upon him while he gave the call with it. Umar heard his voice while he was in his house on al-Zawrāʾ and stood up dragging his cloak, saying: By the One who sent Muhammad ﷺ with the truth, I saw the like of what he saw. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: «To Allah be praise.»"],[1547,"I said to Abu Mahdhurah: 'I intend to go to al-Sham, and I will ask about your adhan, so tell me.' He said: 'I set out with a group of people, and we were on part of the road to Hunayn as the Messenger of Allah ﷺ was returning from Hunayn. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ met us on part of the road, and the muezzin of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ called the adhan for prayer in the presence of the Prophet ﷺ. We heard the sound while we were off to the side of the road, so we shouted in mockery, imitating it. He heard the sound and said, \"Which of you recognizes this one whose sound I hear?\" He said: Then we were brought forward and stood before him. He said, \"Which of you is the owner of the sound?\" He said: The people all pointed to me. He said: He sent them away and kept me with him, and nothing was more hateful to me than what the Messenger of Allah ﷺ commanded me. He commanded me to give the adhan, and the Messenger of Allah ﷺ himself taught me the adhan, saying: \"Say: Allahu akbar, Allahu akbar, Allahu akbar, Allahu akbar; ashhadu an la ilaha illa Allah, ashhadu an la ilaha illa Allah; ashhadu anna Muhammadan rasul Allah, ashhadu anna Muhammadan rasul Allah.\" Then he said to me, \"Go back and stretch out your voice.\" He said: \"Ashhadu an la ilaha illa Allah, ashhadu an la ilaha illa Allah; ashhadu anna Muhammadan rasul Allah, ashhadu anna Muhammadan rasul Allah; hayya 'ala al-salah, hayya 'ala al-salah; hayya 'ala al-falah, hayya 'ala al-falah; Allahu akbar, Allahu akbar; la ilaha illa Allah.\" When he finished the adhan, he called me and gave me a purse containing some silver and said, \"O Allah, bless him and bless upon him.\" He said: I said, \"O Messenger of Allah, command me to give the adhan.\" He said, \"I have commanded you with it.\" He said: Then everything of dislike in my heart turned to love, and I came to 'Attab b. Usayd, the agent of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and I used to give the adhan in Makkah by the command of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ."],[1548,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ taught me the adhan with nineteen phrases and the iqamah with seventeen phrases. The adhan is: \"Allahu akbar, Allahu akbar, Allahu akbar, Allahu akbar; ashhadu an la ilaha illa Allah, ashhadu an la ilaha illa Allah; ashhadu anna Muhammadan rasul Allah, ashhadu anna Muhammadan rasul Allah; hayya 'ala al-salah, hayya 'ala al-salah; hayya 'ala al-falah, hayya 'ala al-falah; Allahu akbar, Allahu akbar; la ilaha illa Allah.\" And the iqamah is: \"Allahu akbar, Allahu akbar, Allahu akbar, Allahu akbar; ashhadu an la ilaha illa Allah, ashhadu an la ilaha illa Allah; ashhadu anna Muhammadan rasul Allah, ashhadu anna Muhammadan rasul Allah; hayya 'ala al-salah, hayya 'ala al-salah; hayya 'ala al-falah, hayya 'ala al-falah; qad qamat al-salah, qad qamat al-salah; Allahu akbar, Allahu akbar; la ilaha illa Allah.\""],[1549,"I said: \"O Messenger of Allah ﷺ, teach me the sunnah of the adhan.\" He said: He wiped the front of my head and said: \"You say: Allahu akbar, Allahu akbar, Allahu akbar, Allahu akbar,\" raising his voice with it. Then you say: \"Ashhadu an la ilaha illa Allah, ashhadu an la ilaha illa Allah; ashhadu anna Muhammadan rasul Allah, ashhadu anna Muhammadan rasul Allah,\" and lower your voice with it. Then you raise your voice with the testimony: \"Ashhadu an la ilaha illa Allah, ashhadu an la ilaha illa Allah; ashhadu anna Muhammadan rasul Allah,\" twice, and \"hayya 'ala al-salah, hayya 'ala al-salah; hayya 'ala al-falah, hayya 'ala al-falah.\" If it is the morning prayer, you say: \"Al-salahu khayrun min al-nawm, al-salahu khayrun min al-nawm; Allahu akbar, Allahu akbar; la ilaha illa Allah.\""],[1550,"Whoever says, 'Glory be to Allah and praise be to Him' one hundred times in a day, his sins are erased, even if they were like the foam of the sea."],[1551,"“Shall I not guide you to something that expiates sins and increases good deeds?” They said, “Yes, O Messenger of Allah.” He said: “Performing ablution thoroughly even in difficult circumstances, taking many steps to this mosque, and prayer after prayer. No one leaves his house purified, comes to the mosque and prays with the Muslims or with the imam, then waits for the next prayer, except that the angels say: O Allah, forgive him; O Allah, have mercy on him. So when you stand for prayer, straighten your rows and fill the gaps. When the imam says takbīr, say takbīr, for I see you from behind me. When he says ‘Allah hears the one who praises Him,’ say: ‘Our Lord, to You is praise.’ The best rows of men are the first, and the worst rows of men are the last. The best rows of women are the last, and the worst rows of women are the first. O assembly of women, when the men prostrate, guard your eyes from the nakedness of the men.”"],[1553,"The adoration of the tongue are due to Allah, and acts of worship, all good things. Peace be upon you, O Prophet, and Allah’s mercy and His blessings. Ibn ‘Umar said: I added: “And Allah’s blessings, peace be upon us, and upon Allah’s upright servants. I testify that there is not god but Allah. “Ibn ‘Umar said: I added to it: He is alone, no one is His associate, and I testify that Muhammad is His servant and His Apostle. (Using translation from Abū Dāʾūd 971)"],[1554,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to teach us the tashahhud as he would teach us a surah from the Quran: 'All compliments, blessed words, prayers, and good things are due to Allah. Peace be upon you, O Prophet, and the mercy of Allah and His blessings. Peace be upon us and upon the righteous servants of Allah. I bear witness that there is no god but Allah, and I bear witness that Muhammad is the Messenger of Allah.'"],[1555,"I said: “O Messenger of Allah ﷺ, how do we send blessings upon you?” He said: ʿSay: O Allah, send Your salah (grace, honour and mercy) upon Muhammad and upon the family of Muhammad, as You sent Your salah upon the family of Ibrahim, You are indeed Praiseworthy, Most Glorious. And send Your blessings upon Muhammad and the family of Muhammad, as You sent Your blessings upon the family of Ibrahim, You are indeed Praiseworthy, Most Glorious.” (Using translation from Aḥmad 1396)"],[1556,"\"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ came to us in the Majlis of Sa'd bin 'Ubadah and Bashir bin Sa'd said to him: 'Allah has commanded us to send Salah upon you, O Messenger of Allah; so how should we send salah upon you?' The Messenger of Allah ﷺ remained silent until we wished that he had not asked him. Then he said: 'Say: 'Alahumma salli 'ala Muhammad wa 'ala ali Muhammad, kama sallaita 'ala Ibrahima wa barik 'ala Muhammad kama barakta 'ala ali Ibrahim fil-'alamin, innaka hamidun majid (O Allah, send salah upon Muhammad and upon the family of Muhammad, as You sent salah upon the family of Ibrahim, and send blessings upon Muhammad and upon the family of Muhammad as You sent blessings upon the family of Ibrahim among the nations. You are indeed Worthy of praise, Full of glory.)\" And the salam is as you know.'\" (Using translation from Nasāʾī 1285)"],[1557,"“Indeed Satan has a touch and the angel has a touch. As for Satan’s touch, it is threatening evil and denying the truth. As for the angel’s touch, it is promising good and affirming the truth. Whoever finds that should praise Allah, and whoever finds the other should seek refuge from Satan.” Then he recited: {Satan threatens you with poverty} (the verse)."],[1558,"\"Satan will not cease to come to one of you and say, 'Who created the heavens and the earth?' So he says, 'Allah.' Then he says, 'And who created you?' So he says, 'Allah.' Then he says, 'Who created Allah?' So when any of you senses that, let him say, 'I believe in Allah and in His messengers.'\""],[1559,"When the heat is intense, delay the prayer until it is cooler, for intense heat is from the blaze of Hell."],[1560,"We were praying Zuhr with the Messenger of Allah at the time of intense heat (i.e., midday when the sun has just passed its zenith) and he said to us, \"Wait for it to cool down before you pray, for intense heat is from the flaring up of the Hell-fire.\" (Using translation from Ibn Mājah 680)"],[1561,"We were with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ on a journey, and the muezzin wanted to give the call for Zuhr. The Prophet ﷺ said to him: Delay until cooler. Then he wanted to give the call, and he said to him: Delay until cooler, two or three times, until we saw the shadows of the hillocks. He said: Intense heat is from the blaze of Hell, so when the heat is intense, delay the prayer until it is cooler."],[1562,"When it is hot, delay the prayer until it is cooler, for intense heat is from the blaze of Hell. It was mentioned that the Fire complained to its Lord, and He permitted it two breaths: one in winter and one in summer."],[1563,"When one of you leads the people in prayer, let him keep it short, for among the people are the weak, the sick, and those with needs."],[1564,"A man came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and said, 'O Messenger of Allah, I stay behind from the dawn prayer because so-and-so prolongs it for us.' The Messenger of Allah ﷺ stood up, and I never saw him angrier in any admonition than he was that day. He said, 'O people, some of you drive others away. Whoever leads the people in prayer, let him be brief, for among them are the weak, the elderly, and those with needs.'"],[1565,"When one of you leads the people in prayer, he should be brief, for among them are the weak, the sick, and the aged. But when one of you prays by himself, he may pray as long as he likes. (Using translation from Abū Dāʾūd 794)"],[1566,"He said: I asked Abu Dharr, and he struck my thigh as I struck your thigh, and said: I asked the Messenger of Allah ﷺ as you asked me, and he struck my thigh as I struck your thigh, and said: \"Pray the prayer at its time. If you catch it with them, then pray, and do not say, 'I have already prayed, so I will not pray.'\""],[1567,"'Let those of maturity and understanding stand nearest to me, then those who are next to them, then those who are next to them. Do not differ, lest your hearts differ. And beware of the clamor of the marketplaces.'"],[1568,"«Straighten your rows, for straightening the row is part of the completeness of the prayer.»"],[1569,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to straighten the row until he left it like the shaft of an arrow or a spear. Then he saw a man's chest protruding from the row and said, 'O servants of Allah! You will straighten your rows, or Allah will certainly cause discord between your faces.'"],[1570,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ turned his face toward us and said, 'Straighten your rows' — three times. 'By Allah, you will straighten your rows, or Allah will certainly cause discord between your hearts.' He said: Then I saw a man pressing his ankle to his companion's ankle and his shoulder to his companion's shoulder."],[1571,"\"My servant has denied Me, but it was not for him to do so, and he has reviled Me, but it was not for him to do so. His denial of Me is saying: How can He bring us back as He began us? And his reviling of Me is saying: Allah has taken a son. And I am the Self-Sufficient, I did not beget nor was I begotten, and there is none equal to Him.\""],[1572,"When one of you prays toward a sutra, let him draw close to it, for indeed the devil passes between him and it, and he should not let anyone pass in front of him."],[1573,"When one of you prays toward a sutra, let him draw close to it, so that the devil does not cut off his prayer."],[1574,"When one of you sleeps during his prayer, let him lie down until sleep leaves him, for when one of you stands praying while drowsy, perhaps he seeks forgiveness and curses himself."],[1575,"When a man becomes drowsy while praying, let him turn away; perhaps he supplicates in his prayer and supplicates against himself while he does not know."],[1576,"When one of you stands at night and the Quran becomes unclear on his tongue and he does not know what he is saying, let him lie down."],[1577,"That al-Hawla' bt. Tuwayt b. Habib b. 'Abd al-'Uzza passed by her while the Messenger of Allah ﷺ was with her. She said: I said, \"This is al-Hawla' bt. Tuwayt. They claim that she does not sleep at night.\" She said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, \"She does not sleep at night? Take from deeds what you are able to bear, for by Allah, Allah does not tire until you tire.\""],[1578,"Shut the doors, tie the waterskins, cover the vessels, and extinguish the lamps, for the devil does not open a locked door, nor untie a waterskin, nor uncover a vessel. And the little transgressor (the mouse) may set fire to people's houses."],[1579,"Shut your door and mention Allah's name, for the devil does not open a shut door. Extinguish your lamp and mention Allah's name. Tie your waterskin and mention Allah's name. Cover your vessel and mention Allah's name, even with a stick placed across it."],[1580,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ commanded us four things and forbade us five: When you go to sleep, shut your door, tie your waterskin, cover your vessel, and extinguish your lamp, for the devil does not open a door, nor untie a waterskin, nor uncover a cover. And the mouse, the little transgressor, may burn the people of a house in their house. And do not eat with your left hand, do not drink with your left hand, do not walk in a single sandal, do not wrap yourself in al-samma' (a way of wearing cloth that leaves no opening for the arms), and do not sit with your knees up while wrapped in a single garment, exposing your private parts."],[1581,"Tie the waterskins, shut the doors when you sleep at night, and cover food and drink, for the devil comes. If he does not find the door shut, he enters; if he does not find the waterskin tied, he drinks from it; but if he finds the door shut and the waterskin tied, he does not untie a waterskin and does not open a shut door. If one of you cannot find something to cover his vessel that contains his drink, let him place a stick across it."],[1582,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to us: Shut your doors, tie your waterskins, cover your vessels, extinguish your lamps, for the devil does not open a lock, does not untie a waterskin, and does not uncover a cover. The little transgressor (the mouse) may sometimes set fire to the people of a house in their house. And restrain your livestock and your family at sunset until the darkness of 'Isha' has passed."],[1583,"Restrain your livestock until the fright of 'Isha' passes, for it is an hour in which the devil penetrates."],[1584,"If you hear the barking of dogs or the braying of donkeys at night, seek refuge in Allah, for they see what you do not see. And reduce going out when feet are still, for Allah, Mighty and Exalted, sends forth of His creation in His night whatever He wills. And close the doors and mention the name of Allah over them, for Satan does not open a door that has been closed and over which the name of Allah has been mentioned. And cover the water skins, turn over the vessels, and tie the waterskins."],[1585,"A mouse came dragging a wick and dropped before the Messenger of Allah ﷺ on the mat on which he was sitting with the result that it burned a hole in it about the size of dirham. He (the prophet) said: When you go to sleep, extinguish your lamps, for the devil guides a creature like this to do thus and sets you on fire. (Using translation from Abū Dāʾūd 5247)"],[1586,"The example of the house in which Allah is remembered and the house in which Allah is not remembered is like the living and the dead."],[1587,"They said, \"O Messenger of Allah, we eat but we are not filled.\" He said, \"Do you gather together over your food or do you separate?\" They said, \"We separate.\" He said, \"Gather together over your food, and mention the name of Allah, and you will be blessed in it.\""],[1588,"We were invited to a meal, and with us were Sa'id b. Jubayr, Zadhan, Abu al-Bakhtari, and Miqsam. When the food was brought, Sa'id b. Jubayr said: \"I heard Ibn 'Abbas say: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: 'Blessing descends in the middle of the food, so eat from its sides.'\""],[1589,"“When one of you eats, let him eat with his right hand; and when he drinks, let him drink with his right hand, for Satan eats with his left hand and drinks with his left hand.”"],[1590,"The example of the house in which Allah is remembered and the house in which Allah is not remembered is like the living and the dead."],[1591,"A disbelieving guest came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, so the Messenger of Allah ﷺ ordered a sheep to be milked, and he drank its milk. Then another, and he drank its milk. Then another, and he drank its milk, until he had drunk the milk of seven sheep. Then the next morning he became Muslim, and the Messenger of Allah ﷺ ordered a sheep for him, so it was milked and he drank its milk. Then he ordered another for him, but he did not finish it. So the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, “The believer drinks in one intestine, and the disbeliever drinks in seven intestines.”"],[1592,"I have heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ saying, \"A human does not fill any vessel worse than his stomach. It is sufficient for the son of Adam to eat a few mouthfuls that will keep him upright. But if he must (eat more), then one third for his food, one third for his drink and one third for his breath.\""],[1593,"If a morsel of one of you falls, let him remove any dirt from it and eat it, and not leave it for Satan. And wipe your plates clean, for you do not know in which part of your food the blessing lies."],[1594,"When one of you eats and a morsel falls from his hand, let him remove whatever dirt is on it and eat it, and not leave it for Satan. And let him not wipe his hand with a napkin until he licks it, for a man does not know in which of his food blessing is placed. Satan lies in wait for people—or for a person—at everything, even at his eating or his food. And let him not lift the plate until he licks it or has it licked, for the last of the food has the blessing."],[1596,"If a fly falls into the vessel of one of you, then dip it, for in one of its wings there is a disease and in the other there is a cure."],[1597,"I said, 'O Messenger of Allah, tell me about ablution.' He said, 'Perform ablution thoroughly, comb between the fingers, and sniff water deeply into the nose, unless you are fasting.'"],[1598,"Abu Hurayrah used to come to the people while they were performing ablution at the place of purification and say to them, 'Perform ablution thoroughly, may Allah bless you, for I heard Abu al-Qasim ﷺ say, \"Woe to the heels from the Fire.\"'"],[1599,"When one of you touches a woman and then wants to return, let him perform ablution."],[1600,"When one of you has intercourse with his wife and then wants to return, let him perform ablution, for it makes him more energetic for returning."],[1601,"“Wear white from your clothes and shroud your dead in them, for they are among the best of your clothes. And among the best of your kohl is ithmid; it clears the vision and grows the hair.”"],[1602,"The best of your kohl is ithmid; when applied at bedtime, it makes the hair grow and clears the eyesight."],[1603,"Among the best of your kohl is ithmid, for it clears the eyesight and makes the hair grow."],[1604,"The Prophet ﷺ said to a man who passed by carrying arrows in the mosque: \"Hold their heads.\" He said: \"Yes.\""],[1605,"«He commanded a man who was giving arrows as charity in the mosque not to pass with them unless he was holding their heads.»"],[1606,"«When one of you passes through our markets or our mosque with arrows, let him hold their heads, lest he injure any of the Muslims.»"],[1608,"Messenger of Allah, I find a change in your mood today. Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: Gabriel had promised me that he would meet me tonight, but he did not meet me. By Allah, he never broke his promises, and Messenger of Allah ﷺ spent the day in this sad (mood). Then it occurred to him that there had been a puppy under their cot. He commanded and it was turned out. He then took some water in his hand and sprinkled it at that place. When it was evening Gabriel met him and he said to him: you promised me that you would meet me the previous night. He said: Yes, but we do not enter a house in which there is a dog or a picture. Then on that very morning he commanded the killing of the dogs until he announced that the dog kept for the orchards should also be killed, but he spared the dog meant for the protection of extensive fields (or big gardens). (Using translation from Muslim 2105)"],[1609,"Whoever keeps a dog that is not a hunting dog, nor a dog for livestock, nor a dog for farming, his reward is reduced every day by a qirat."],[1610,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ commanded us to kill dogs, to the point that a woman would come in from the desert with a dog and kill it. Then he forbade us from killing them and said: Keep to the black one with two spots, for it is a devil."],[1611,"The Prophet ﷺ visited the grave of his mother and wept, and made those around him weep. Then he said, \"I asked my Lord for permission to visit her grave, and He granted me permission. Then I asked Him for permission to seek forgiveness for her, but He did not grant me permission. So visit graves, for they remind you of death.\""],[1612,"«Hasten with your funerals, for if it is good you are advancing it toward it, and if it is evil you are removing it from your necks.»"],[1613,"\"Visit the sick and follow funerals; it will remind you of the Hereafter.\""],[1614,"\"Review the Qur'an, for it is more prone to escape from the hearts of men than camels from their hobbles. It is bad for one of you to say, 'I forgot such-and-such verse'; he did not forget, but he was made to forget.\""],[1615,"Al-Mughira b. Shuba proposed to a woman, and the Prophet ﷺ said to him, \"Go and look at her, for it is more likely to create affection between you two.\""],[1616,"A man came to the Prophet ﷺ and mentioned to him marriage to a woman from the Ansar. He said, \"Look at her, for there is something in the eyes of the Ansar.\""],[1617,"“Indeed, woman was created from a rib. If you try to straighten her, you will break her. So deal with her gently, and you will live with her.”"],[1618,"Wear sandals frequently, for a man remains a rider as long as he wears sandals."],[1619,"I heard the Prophet ﷺ say during a military expedition we undertook: 'Acquire many sandals, for a man remains a rider as long as he wears sandals.'"],[1620,"\"When one of you loves his brother, let him inform him.\""],[1621,"My father, Sahl b. Hunayf, bathed at al-Kharrar and took off a jubba he was wearing while 'Amir b. Rabi'a was looking on. Sahl was a fair-skinned man with beautiful skin. 'Amir b. Rabi'a said, 'I have never seen anything like today, nor the skin of a virgin.' Sahl fell ill on the spot and his illness became severe. So the Messenger of Allah ﷺ was informed that Sahl had fallen ill and that he would not be able to travel with you, O Messenger of Allah. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ came to him, and Sahl told him what had happened with 'Amir b. Rabi'a. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, 'For what reason would one of you kill his brother? Why did you not say, \"May Allah bless you\"? The evil eye is real. Perform wudu for him.' So 'Amir b. Rabi'a performed wudu for him, and Sahl went with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ with no harm."],[1622,"'Amir b. Rabi'a, the brother of Banu 'Adi b. Ka'b, saw Sahl b. Hunayf while he was with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ at al-Kharrar bathing. He said, 'By Allah, I have never seen anything like today, nor the skin of a hidden maiden.' Sahl was stricken and fell to the ground. The Prophet ﷺ was informed, and it was said, 'O Messenger of Allah, can you do anything for Sahl b. Hunayf? He cannot raise his head.' The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, 'Do you suspect anyone?' They said, 'Yes, 'Amir b. Rabi'a; he saw him bathing and said, \"By Allah, I have never seen anything like today, nor the skin of a hidden maiden.\"' So the Messenger of Allah ﷺ summoned 'Amir b. Rabi'a, and he was angry with him and said, 'For what reason would one of you kill his brother? Why did you not say, \"May Allah bless you\"? Bathe for him.' So 'Amir bathed for him, and Sahl went with the riding party with no harm."],[1623,"Yawning is from Satan. When one of you yawns, let him suppress it as much as he can."],[1624,"Yawning in prayer is from Satan. When one of you feels that, let him suppress it."],[1625,"When one of you yawns, let him place his hand over his mouth, for Satan enters."],[1626,"'When one of you prays, let him either wear his sandals or remove them and place them between his feet, and let him not harm others with them.'"],[1627,"\"We had some idols with us, and they were hanging on my door. When the Prophet ﷺ saw that, he said, 'Take them down, for they remind me of the worldly life.'\""],[1628,"\"You will be called on the Day of Resurrection by your names and the names of your fathers, so make your names good.\""],[1629,"“When one of you reaches a gathering, let him greet; and if he decides to sit, let him sit; then when he gets up, let him greet. The first is not more deserving than the last.”"],[1630,"“If one of you sees a woman who pleases him, let him return to his wife and have intercourse with her, for that is with her.”"],[1631,"None of you should be prevented by Bilal's call to prayer—or he said: Bilal's call—from having your pre-dawn meal, for he gives the call to prayer—or he said: he calls out—at night so that your standing [in prayer] may return and your sleeping may wake up. And he said: \"The dawn is not that it says thus and thus\"—and he struck his hand and raised it—\"until it says thus,\" and he spread his fingers apart."],[1632,"I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ inviting to the pre-dawn meal in the month of Ramadan, and he said, \"Come to the blessed meal.\""],[1633,"On the back of every camel there is a devil, so when you ride them, mention Allah’s name and do not neglect your needs."],[1634,"\"Allah has prescribed excellence in everything. So when you kill, kill well; and when you slaughter, slaughter well. Let each of you sharpen his blade and spare suffering to the animal he slaughters.\""],[1635,"\"I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: 'Measure your food, may you be blessed therein.\"' (Using translation from Ibn Mājah 2231)"],[1636,"Thumāmah al-Ḥanafī was taken captive. The Prophet ﷺ used to visit him and say: 'What do you have, O Thumāmah?' He would say: 'If you kill, you kill one with blood [i.e., a person of consequence]; if you show favor, you show favor to one who is grateful; and if you want wealth, you will be given whatever you wish.' He said: The companions of the Prophet ﷺ loved ransom and said: 'What do we gain by killing this man?' Then the Prophet ﷺ passed by him one day and he embraced Islam, so he sent him to the garden of Abū Ṭalḥah and ordered him to bathe, so he bathed and prayed two rakʿahs. Then the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: 'The Islam of your companion has become good.'"],[1637,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ sent a cavalry detachment toward Najd, and they brought a man from Banū Ḥanīfah called Thumāmah b. Uthāl, the chief of the people of al-Yamāmah. They tied him to one of the pillars of the mosque. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ came out to him and said: 'What do you have, O Thumāmah?' He replied: 'I have good, O Muḥammad. If you kill me, you kill one with blood; if you show favor, you show favor to one who is grateful; and if you want wealth, ask and you will be given whatever you wish.' The Messenger of Allah ﷺ left him until the next day, then said to him: 'What do you have, O Thumāmah?' He replied: 'What I told you: if you show favor, you show favor to one who is grateful; if you kill, you kill one with blood; and if you want wealth, ask and you will be given whatever you wish.' The Messenger of Allah ﷺ left him until the day after the next, then said to him: 'What do you have, O Thumāmah?' He replied: 'I have what I told you: if you show favor, you show favor to one who is grateful; if you kill, you kill one with blood; and if you want wealth, ask and you will be given whatever you wish.' Then the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: 'Release Thumāmah.' He went to some palm trees near the mosque, bathed, then entered the mosque and said: 'I bear witness that there is no god but Allah and that Muḥammad is the Messenger of Allah. O Muḥammad, by Allah, there was no face on earth more hateful to me than your face, but now your face has become the most beloved of all faces to me. By Allah, there was no religion more hateful to me than your religion, but now your religion has become the most beloved of all religions to me. By Allah, there was no town more hateful to me than your town, but now your town has become the most beloved of all towns to me. Your cavalry captured me while I was intending ʿUmrah, so what do you think?' The Messenger of Allah ﷺ gave him good news and ordered him to perform ʿUmrah. When he arrived in Makkah, someone said to him: 'Have you apostatized?' He replied: 'No, but I have embraced Islam with Muḥammad, the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. By Allah, not a grain of wheat will come to you from al-Yamāmah until the Messenger of Allah ﷺ permits it.'"],[1638,"That he embraced Islam, and the Prophet ﷺ ordered him to bathe with water and lote-tree leaves."],[1639,"I heard the Prophet ﷺ say three days before his death: “None of you should die except while thinking well of Allah.”"],[1640,"I went out to visit Yazid b. al-Aswad, and I met Wathilah b. al-Asqaʿ who also wanted to visit him. We entered upon him, and when he saw Wathilah, he stretched out his hand and gestured toward him. Wathilah came forward until he sat down. Yazid took Wathilah’s palms and placed them on his face. Wathilah said to him: “How do you think of Allah?” He said: “By Allah, my thought of Allah is good.” He said: “Then rejoice, for I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: ‘Allah, Mighty and Majestic, said: I am as My servant thinks of Me, whether he thinks good or thinks evil.’”"],[1641,"The Prophet ﷺ commanded the cutting of bells."],[1642,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ commanded that the bells be cut from the necks of the camels on the day of Badr."],[1643,"The angels do not accompany a group that has a dog or a bell."],[1644,"The bell is the musical instrument of the Satan. (Using translation from Muslim 2114)"],[1646,"When one of you wakes up from his sleep, let him not dip his hand into his vessel until he washes it three times, for he does not know where his hand spent the night."],[1647,"Whoever uses stones (for istijmar), let him use an odd number. Whoever does so has done well. Whoever goes to relieve himself should conceal himself, even if he finds only a mound of sand, for Satan plays with the backside of the children of Adam."],[1648,"We went out with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ in the Farewell Pilgrimage and pronounced the talbiyah for Umrah. Then the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, \"Whoever has a sacrificial animal with him should pronounce the talbiyah for Hajj and Umrah, then he should not exit ihram until he exits from both of them together.\" She said: Those who had pronounced the talbiyah for Umrah circumambulated the House and went between al-Safa and al-Marwah, then exited ihram. Then they performed another tawaf after returning from Mina for their Hajj. As for those who pronounced the talbiyah for Hajj and combined Hajj and Umrah, they performed only one tawaf. She said: I arrived in Makkah while I was menstruating, so I did not circumambulate the House nor go between al-Safa and al-Marwah. I complained about that to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and he said, \"Undo your hair, comb it, pronounce the talbiyah for Hajj, and leave the Umrah.\" She said: I did that. When we completed the Hajj, the Messenger of Allah ﷺ sent me with Abd al-Rahman b. Abi Bakr to al-Tan'im, and I performed Umrah. He said, \"This is in place of your Umrah.\""],[1649,"The Prophet ﷺ passed by a river of water while he was on his mule and the people were fasting, and there were many pedestrians. He said, “Drink.” They began looking at him. He said, “Drink, for I am commanding you.” They began looking at him, so he turned his hip, drank, and the people drank."],[1650,"A man praised another man in the presence of Ibn ʿUmar, and Ibn ʿUmar began raising dust toward him and said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “When you see the flatterers, throw dust in their faces.”"],[1651,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to me, “Recite to me.” I said, “Should I recite to you when the Qur’an was revealed to you?” He said, “I love to hear it from someone else.”"],[1652,"The Prophet ﷺ ordered that Ibn Zurara be cauterized."],[1653,"The Prophet ﷺ cauterized As'ad b. Zurara for a thorn wound."],[1654,"My family sent me with a milch-camel to the Prophet ﷺ. He said: I brought it to him, and he ordered me to milk it, so I milked it. The Prophet ﷺ said to me, \"Leave the one who draws the milk [i.e., do not milk it dry; leave some for the calf or the one who milks].\""],[1655,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ was told that he said—meaning himself—’I will certainly stand in prayer at night and fast during the day as long as I live.’ The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, “Are you the one who says that?” I said to him, “I have said it, O Messenger of Allah.” The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, “You will not be able to do that. Fast and break your fast, sleep and stand in prayer, and fast three days of the month, for a good deed is multiplied tenfold, and that is like fasting a lifetime.” He said, “I said, ‘I can do better than that.’” He said, “Fast one day and break your fast for two days.” He said, “I said, ‘I can do better than that.’” He said, “Fast one day and break your fast for one day. That is the fast of Dawud, and it is the most moderate fast.” He said, “I said, ‘I can do better than that.’” The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, “There is nothing better than that.” ‘Abdullah said, “If I had accepted the three days that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ mentioned, that would have been dearer to me than my family and my wealth.”"],[1656,"Take on of deeds what you are able to do, for Allah does not tire until you tire.” She said, “And the most beloved of deeds to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ were those done consistently, even if small. And when he prayed a prayer, he would be constant in it.”"],[1657,"We were with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ when a funeral passed by us, and the Messenger of Allah ﷺ stood up for it. When we went to carry it, it turned out to be the funeral of a Jew. He said: «Death has terror, so when you see a funeral, stand up.»"],[1658,"\"When you see the funeral, stand up until it passes you by or is set down.\""],[1659,"\"When you see the funeral, stand up for it until it passes you by.\""],[1660,"A man asked the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, saying: \"O Messenger of Allah, the funeral of a disbeliever passes by us; should we stand up for it?\" He said: \"Yes, stand up for it. Indeed, you are not standing for it; you are standing out of reverence for the One who seizes the souls.\""],[1661,"He ﷺ used to stand for the funeral, then he sat down."],[1662,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ stood for the funerals until they were set down, then he sat."],[1663,"I attended a funeral among the Banu Salimah, so I stood up. Nafiʿ b. Jubayr said to me: \"Sit down, for I will inform you about this with certainty.\""],[1664,"«When it was revealed, {And upon those who can afford it, a ransom of feeding a poor person}, whoever among us wanted to break the fast would break it and pay the ransom, until the verse after it was revealed and abrogated it.»"],[1665,"The day of Ashura was a day that the Quraysh used to fast in the pre-Islamic period. When the Messenger of Allah ﷺ came to Madinah, he fasted it and commanded fasting it. When Ramadan was made obligatory, that became the obligation, and the day of Ashura was left. So whoever wished fasted it, and whoever wished left it."],[1666,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said regarding fasting the day of Ashura after the fasting of Ramadan was revealed: Whoever wishes may fast it, and whoever wishes may break his fast."],[1667,"We were in Ramadan during the time of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ: whoever wished fasted, and whoever wished broke the fast and ransomed by feeding a poor person, until this verse was revealed: {So whoever among you witnesses the month, let him fast it}"],[1668,"His nose was cut on the day of al-Kilab, so he made a nose out of silver, but it began to stink, so the Prophet ﷺ ordered him to make a nose out of gold."],[1669,"While the people were in Qubā' during the morning prayer, a comer came to them and said, 'The Messenger of Allah ﷺ had Qur'an revealed to him tonight, and he has been commanded to face the Ka'bah, so face it.' Their faces had been toward Syria, so they turned around to the Ka'bah."],[1670,"When the Prophet ﷺ came to Madinah, he prayed toward Bayt al-Maqdis for sixteen or seventeen months, and he loved to be directed toward the Ka'bah. So Allah, Mighty and Exalted, revealed: 'We have seen the turning of your face toward the heaven, so We will surely turn you to a qiblah you will be pleased with. So turn your face toward the Sacred Mosque.' A man passed by a group of the Ansar while they were bowing and said, 'He bears witness that he has prayed with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and that he has faced toward the Ka'bah.'"],[1671,"«When the Prophet ﷺ was turned toward the Kaaba, they said, “What about those of our brothers who died while they prayed toward Bayt al-Maqdis?”» Then Allah, Mighty and Exalted, revealed: {And Allah would never let your faith be lost}"],[1672,"Some people from the companions of the Prophet ﷺ died while drinking wine. When it was forbidden, some people from the companions of the Prophet ﷺ said, 'What about our companions who died while drinking it?' Then this verse was revealed: {There is no sin on those who believe and do righteous deeds for what they ate.}"],[1673,"A man went out when wine was lawful and gifted the Messenger of Allah ﷺ a skin of wine. He brought it on a camel until he found the Messenger of Allah ﷺ sitting. He said, \"What is this with you?\" He said, \"A skin of wine which I gifted to you.\" He said, \"Did you know that Allah, Mighty and Majestic, has forbidden it?\" He said, \"No.\" He said, \"Indeed Allah has forbidden it.\" The man turned to the camel's driver and spoke to him about something between them. Then he stood up and the Prophet ﷺ said, \"What did you say to him?\" He said, \"I ordered him to sell it.\" He said, \"The One who forbade drinking it has forbidden selling it.\" He said, \"He then ordered the openings of the water skin to be opened, and it flowed out into the dirt. I looked at it in the wide valley and there was nothing in it.\""],[1674,"I was serving Abu Talha, Abu Ubayda, Ka'b, and Suhayl b. Bayda' nabidh of dates and unripe dates until it began to affect them. Then a caller announced: 'Verily, wine has been forbidden.' He said: By Allah, they did not wait to ascertain whether it was true or false. They said: 'Overturn it, O Anas.' So I overturned it. By Allah, it never returned to their heads until they met Allah. Their wine was unripe and ripe dates.”"],[1675,"Umar b. al-Khattab addressed us from the pulpit of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. He praised Allah and extolled Him, then said: “To proceed: the prohibition of wine was revealed on the day it was revealed, when it was from five things: grapes, dates, honey, wheat, and barley. And wine is what intoxicates the mind.”"],[1676,"Every intoxicant is unlawful."],[1677,"Every intoxicant is Khamr and every intoxicant is forbidden. He who drinks wine in this world and dies while he is addicted to it, not having repented, will not be given a drink in the Hereafter. (Using translation from Muslim 2003a)"],[1678,"\"Whatever intoxicates in large amounts, a small amount of it is unlawful.\""],[1679,"From the Messenger of Allah ﷺ that he used to say: «None of you should eat from the meat of his sacrificial animal beyond three days.»"],[1680,"I said to Abu Mahdhurah: 'I intend to go to al-Sham, and I will ask about your adhan, so tell me.' He said: 'I set out with a group of people, and we were on part of the road to Hunayn as the Messenger of Allah ﷺ was returning from Hunayn. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ met us on part of the road, and the muezzin of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ called the adhan for prayer in the presence of the Prophet ﷺ. We heard the sound while we were off to the side of the road, so we shouted in mockery, imitating it. He heard the sound and said, \"Which of you recognizes this one whose sound I hear?\" He said: Then we were brought forward and stood before him. He said, \"Which of you is the owner of the sound?\" He said: The people all pointed to me. He said: He sent them away and kept me with him, and nothing was more hateful to me than what the Messenger of Allah ﷺ commanded me. He commanded me to give the adhan, and the Messenger of Allah ﷺ himself taught me the adhan, saying: \"Say: Allahu akbar, Allahu akbar, Allahu akbar, Allahu akbar; ashhadu an la ilaha illa Allah, ashhadu an la ilaha illa Allah; ashhadu anna Muhammadan rasul Allah, ashhadu anna Muhammadan rasul Allah.\" Then he said to me, \"Go back and stretch out your voice.\" He said: \"Ashhadu an la ilaha illa Allah, ashhadu an la ilaha illa Allah; ashhadu anna Muhammadan rasul Allah, ashhadu anna Muhammadan rasul Allah; hayya 'ala al-salah, hayya 'ala al-salah; hayya 'ala al-falah, hayya 'ala al-falah; Allahu akbar, Allahu akbar; la ilaha illa Allah.\" When he finished the adhan, he called me and gave me a purse containing some silver and said, \"O Allah, bless him and bless upon him.\" He said: I said, \"O Messenger of Allah, command me to give the adhan.\" He said, \"I have commanded you with it.\" He said: Then everything of dislike in my heart turned to love, and I came to 'Attab b. Usayd, the agent of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and I used to give the adhan in Makkah by the command of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ."],[1681,"the Messenger of Allah forbade eating the meat of the sacrificial animals after three days then he said: \"Eat, take some with you (if traveling). And store some.\" ( Sahih) (Using translation from Nasāʾī 4426)"],[1682,"«He forbade the meat of sacrificial animals beyond three days; then he permitted that we eat and store.» Qatadah b. al-Nuʿman, the brother of Abu Saʿid al-Khudri, arrived, and they offered him some dried meat of the sacrifice. He said: Did the Messenger of Allah ﷺ not forbid it? Abu Saʿid said: «A matter occurred concerning it after you. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ had forbidden us to keep it beyond three days; then he permitted that we eat and store.»"],[1683,"«The Messenger of Allah ﷺ forbade eating the meat of sacrificial animals after three.»"],[1684,"«O people of Madinah, do not eat the meat of sacrificial animals beyond three days.» They complained to him that they had families and servants, so he said: «Eat, feed, and store.»"],[1685,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to me: «Preserve the meat of this sacrificial animal.» So I preserved it, and he kept eating from it until he reached Madinah."],[1686,"His wife Umm Sulaym asked ʿAʾishah about the meat of sacrificial animals. She said: ʿAli b. Abi Talib arrived from a military expedition and entered upon his family, and I offered him some meat from the sacrificial animals. He refused to eat it until he asked the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. The Prophet ﷺ said: «Eat it from Dhu al-Hijjah to Dhu al-Hijjah.»"],[1687,"I prayed beside my father and I placed my palms together (tatbiq) between my thighs, then I placed them between my thighs. He forbade me from that and said: \"We used to do this, but we were forbidden from it and were commanded to place our hands on the knees.\""],[1688,"I entered with 'Alqamah upon Ibn Mas'ud. He said to us, 'Stand and pray.' We went to stand behind him, and he placed one of us on his right and the other on his left. He prayed with us without adhan or iqamah. When he bowed, he clasped his fingers together and placed them between his knees.' When he finished, he said, 'Thus I saw the Messenger of Allah ﷺ do.'"],[1689,"When I prayed, I did tatbiq and placed my hands between my knees. My father Sa'd saw me and said: \"We used to do this, but we were forbidden from it and were commanded to place them on the knees.\""],[1690,"\"The Messenger of Allah commanded us to perform ablution after eating camel meat but not to perform ablution after eating the mutton.\" (Using translation from Ibn Mājah 495)"],[1691,"He was asked about praying in sheep folds, and he permitted it. He was asked about praying in camel resting places, and he forbade it. He was asked about wudu' from sheep meat, and he said: \"If you wish, perform wudu'; and if you wish, do not perform wudu'.\""],[1692,"He found Abu Hurayrah on the roof of the mosque performing wudu', so he asked him. Abu Hurayrah said, \"I am only performing wudu' because of pieces of dried curd that I ate. The Prophet ﷺ said, 'Perform wudu' from what fire has touched.'\""],[1693,"From the Prophet ﷺ , he said, \"Perform ablution with the water that touched the fire.\""],[1694,"The last of the two matters from the Messenger of Allah ﷺ was leaving wudu' after eating what the fire has touched."],[1696,"A woman from the Ansar invited the Messenger of Allah ﷺ to a sheep; the Prophet ﷺ and his companions ate. Then the prayer time came, so the Messenger of Allah ﷺ performed wudu', then returned to the remaining food and they ate. Then the 'Asr time came, and the Messenger of Allah ﷺ did not perform wudu'."],[1697,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ ate a shoulder and then prayed without performing wudu'."],[1698,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ ate the shoulder of a sheep, then prayed and did not perform wudu'."],[1699,"He saw the Prophet ﷺ perform wudu' after eating a piece of dried curd. Then he saw him eat the shoulder of a sheep and pray without performing wudu'."],[1700,"The Prophet ﷺ was asked: \"Should we pray in camel watering places?\" He replied: \"No.\" It was said: \"Should we pray in sheep folds?\" He replied: \"Yes.\" It was said: \"Should we perform wudu' from camel meat?\" He replied: \"Yes.\" It was said: \"Should we perform wudu' from sheep meat?\" He replied: \"No.\""],[1701,"A man asked the Prophet ﷺ, saying: 'O Messenger of Allah, should I perform ablution from the meat of sheep?' He said: 'If you wish, perform ablution, and if you wish, do not perform ablution.' He said: 'Should I perform ablution from the meat of camels?' He said: 'Yes, perform ablution from the meat of camels.' He said: 'May I pray in sheep enclosures?' He said: 'Yes.' He said: 'May I pray in camel resting places?' He said: 'No.'"],[1702,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ was asked about ablution from the meat of sheep, and he said: 'Perform ablution if you wish.'"],[1703,"\"Among what was revealed of the Qur'an was ten known sucklings that make [marriage] forbidden. Then they were abrogated by five known [sucklings]. The Messenger of God ﷺ passed away while they were part of what we recite of the Qur'an.\""],[1704,"I used to recite to ‘AbdurRahman bin ‘Awf, and he found me waiting for him. That was in Mina during the last Hajj performed by ʿUmar bin al-Khattab ؓ Abdur-Rahman bin ʿAwf said: A man came to ʿUmar bin al-Khattab and said: So and so is saying: If ʿUmar ؓ dies, I will swear allegiance to So and so. ʼUmar ؓ said: I will stand before the people today and warn them against these people who want to deprive them of their rights, ʿAbdur-Rahman said: I said: O Ameer al-Muʿmineen, do not do that, for the Hajj season brings together the riffraff and rabble among the people, and most of the people who gather around and listen to you will be of that type. Is you stand before the people, I am afraid that you will say something that they will spread and not understand it properly or interpret it properly. Rather wait until you come to Madinah, for it is the land of Hijrah and the Sunnah, and you will meet the most knowledgeable and noble people there, and you can say what you want to say with confidence; they wilt understand what you say and will interpret it correctly, ʿUmar ؓ said: If I reach Madinah safe and sound, I shall certainly talk to the people there in the first speech I deliver. When we came to Madinah at the end of Dhul-I-Iijah, it was a Friday. I set out early, ‘Umar did not care at what time he went out, because he did not pay attention to heat and cold and so on. I found Saʿeed bin Zaid at the right-hand corner of the minbar, he had got there before me. I sat down next to him, with my knee touching his knee, and it was not long before ʿUmar ؓ came. When I saw him, I said: He will certainly speak today on this minbar and say something that no one ever heard before. Saʿeed bin Zaid objected to that and said: What do you think he will say that no one said before? ʿUmar ؓ sat on the minbar, and when the muʿdhdhin fell silent, he stood up and praised and glorified Allah as He deserves, then he said: To proceed o people, I am going to tell you something that it has been decreed I should say. I do not know, perhaps it may signal my death. So whoever understands it and remembers it, let him narrate it to others wherever his mount takes him; whoever does not understand il, it is not permissible for him to tell lies about me. Allah, may He be blessed and exalted, sent Muhammad ﷺ with the truth and revealed the Book to him; among the things that were revealed to him was the verse of stoning [adulterers). We read it and understood it; the Messenger of Allah ﷺ stoned [adulterers] and we stoned adulterers] after him. But I fear that with the passage of time, some people will say: We do not find the verse of stoning in the Book of Allah, thus they will go astray by forsaking an obligation that Allah revealed. Stoning is the due punishment in the Book of Allah for those who commit zina, both men and women, if they have been married and if proof is established, or there is a pregnancy or a confession, And we used to recite: Do not claim to be the offspring of anyone other than your fathers, as it is disbelief (or ingratitude) on your part to claim to be the offspring of anyone other than your fathers, Verily the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: ʿDo not praise me excessively as ʿEesa, the son of Maryam, was praised; rather I am the slave of Allah, so say, the slave of Allah and His Messenger.ʿ I have heard that some among you are saying. If ʿUmar ؓ dies, I shall swear allegiance to So and so. No man should deceive himself by saying that the oath of allegiance to Abu Bakr was given suddenly and it was is successful. There is no doubt that this is the case, but Allah, may He be glorified and exalted, saved the to 2 people from its bad consequences and there is no one among you today who has the qualities of Abu Bakr ؓ What happened to us when the Messenger of Allah ﷺ died was that ‘Ali, az-Zubair and those who were with them stayed behind in the house of Fatimah, the daughter of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and all the Ansar stayed behind and gathered in Saqeefat Banu Saʿidah, whilst the Muhajireen gathered around Abu Bakr ؓ I said to him; O Abu Bakr, let us go to our brothers, the Ansar. So we set out, looking for them, then we were met by two righteous men who told us what the people had done, and said: where are you going, O Muhajireen? I said: We are looking for these brothers of ours, the Ansar, They said. You should not go near them; do whatever you have already decided, O Muhajireen. I said: By Allah, we will go to them. So we carried on until we came to them in Saqeefat Banu Saʿidah, where we found them gathered and among them was a man wrapped up [in a garment. I said: Who is this? They said: Saʿd bin ʿUbadah. ! said: What is the matter with him? They said: He is sick. After we sat down, their spokesman stood up and praised and glorified Allah, may He glorified and exalted, as He deserves, then he said: To proceed. We are the supporters (Ansar) of Allah and the majority of the Muslim army. You, O Muhajireen, are a small group among us. Some of you came to us, wanting to deny who we are and prevent us from attaining a position of authority. When he fell silent, I wanted to present a speech that I had prepared and that I liked in front of Abu Bakr ؓ I used to avoid provoking him and he was more forbearing and more dignified than me. But Abu Bakr ؓ said: Wait a while. I did not like to make him angry, and he was more knowledgeable and more dignified than me. By Allah, he did not omit any word that I liked in the speech I had prepared but he said something like it or better, speaking spontaneously, until he finished speaking. Then he said: To proceed. Whatever you have mentioned about your achievements and virtues, is correct. The Arabs would not acknowledge the leadership of anyone except someone from this tribe of Quraish, for they are the best of the Arabs in lineage and location. I am pleased to suggest to you one of these two men, whichever of them you want. Then he took hold of my hand and the hand of Abu ʿUbaidah bin al-Jarrah, and I disliked nothing of what he had said apart from this, for by Allah, I would rather have my neck struck for no sin on my part than to become the leader of people among whom was Abu Bakr ؓ unless my own self suggested something at the time of death. One of the Ansar said: I am the post on which the camel with a skin disease scratches itself and I am like a high class palm tree [i.e., a noble]. [I suggest] a ruler from among us and a ruler from among you, O Quraish. - I the narrator said to Malik; What does ‘I am the post on which the cainc! with a skin disease scratches itself and I am like a high class palm treeʿ mean? He said:It is as if he is saying, I am the smart one who has the answer. - Then there was a great deal of clamour and raised voices, to such an extent that I feared there would be a conflict, so I said: Hold out your hand, O Abu Bakr. So he held out his hand and I swore allegiance to him, and the Muhajireen swore allegiance to him, then the Ansar swore allegiance to him. Thus we surrounded Saʿd bin ‘Ubadah. One of them said: You have killed Saʿd i said: May Allah kill Sa’d! And ʿUmar ؓ said: By Allah, we never encountered any problem greater than the swearing of allegiance to Abu Bakr ؓ . We were afraid that if we left the people without having sworn allegiance to anyone, they might swear allegiance after we were gone, so we would either follow in their footsteps and swear allegiance to someone we were not pleased with, or we would disagree with them and that would cause trouble. If anyone swears allegiance to a leader without consulting the Muslims, there is no allegiance for him and no allegiance to the one who swore allegiance to him, lest both of them be killed. Malik said: Ibn Shihab told me, from ʿUrwah bin az-Zubair, that the men whom they met were ʿUwaim bin Saʿidah and Maʿn bin ʿAdiyy. Ibn Shihab said. Saʿeed bin al-Musayyab told me that the one who said, I am the post on which the camel with a skin disease scratches itself and I am like a high class palm tree, was al-lubab bin al-Mundhir. (Using translation from Aḥmad 391)"],[1705,"The Chapter of the Confederates used to be equal in length to the Chapter of the Cow, and in it was: \"The old man and the old woman, when they commit adultery, stone them both absolutely.\""],[1706,"I met Ubayy ibn Ka'b and said to him, \"Ibn Mas'ud used to erase the two protective surahs (Al-Mu'awwidhatayn) from the Qur'ans and say they are not part of the Qur'an, so do not include in it what is not part of it.\" Ubayy replied, \"It was said to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ , so he told us, and we say, 'How many verses do you consider in Surah Al-Ahzab?' I said, 'Seventy-three.' Ubayy then said, 'By Him in whose name oaths are taken, it was equivalent to Surah Al-Baqarah, and we used to read in it the verse of stoning: \"The older man and the older woman, stone them absolutely as a deterrent punishment from Allah. And Allah is Mighty, Wise.\"'\""],[1707,"\"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ supplicated against those who killed the companions of Bi'r Ma'unah for thirty mornings, supplicating against Ri'l, Lihyan, and 'Usayyah who disobeyed Allah and His Messenger.\" Anas said: \"Allah revealed concerning those killed at Bi'r Ma'unah a Quran [passage] that we recited until it was later abrogated: Inform our people that we have met our Lord, and He is pleased with us and we are pleased with Him.\""],[1708,"A man came to Umar asking him, and he began looking at his head once and at his feet another time because of the hardship he saw in him. Umar said to him, \"How much wealth do you have?\" He said, \"Forty camels.\" He said: Ibn Abbas said: I said, \"Allah and His Messenger have spoken the truth: 'If the son of Adam had two valleys of gold, he would seek a third, and nothing fills the belly of the son of Adam except dust, and Allah turns in mercy to whoever repents.'\" He said: Umar said to me, \"What are you saying?\" He said: I said, \"This is how Ubayy b. Ka'b taught me to recite it.\" He said: \"Let us go to him.\" He said: So he went to him and said, \"What does this one say?\" Ubayy said, \"This is how the Messenger of Allah ﷺ taught me to recite it.\""],[1709,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, \"Recite Surah Yasin upon your deceased.\""],[1710,"\"Instruct your dying to say: There is no god but Allah.\""],[1711,"\"Instruct your dying to say: There is no god but Allah. For whoever's last words are 'There is no god but Allah' at death will enter Paradise one day, even if he is afflicted before that with whatever afflicts him.\""],[1712,"When one of you is praying, let him not allow anyone to pass in front of him, and let him repel him as much as he can. If he insists, then let him fight him, for he is only a devil."],[1713,"Do not pray except facing a sutra, and do not let anyone pass in front of you. If he insists, then fight him, for he is only a devil."],[1714,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to wipe our shoulders in prayer and say: «Stand straight and do not differ, lest your hearts differ. Let those of you who possess maturity and intellect stand nearest to me, then those who are next to them, then those who are next to them.» Abu Mas'ud said: «Today you are even more divergent.»"],[1715,"By Allah, the Messenger of Allah ﷺ did not have 'A'ishah perform 'umrah in Dhu al-Hijjah except to thereby cut off the practice of the people of polytheism. For this tribe of Quraysh and those who followed their religion used to say, 'When the fur grows back, the sores heal, and Safar enters, then 'umrah is permitted for whoever wants to perform it.' They used to prohibit 'umrah until Dhu al-Hijjah had passed. So the Messenger of Allah ﷺ had 'A'ishah perform 'umrah only to counter that saying of theirs."],[1716,"Take the pre-dawn meal, for there is blessing in the pre-dawn meal."],[1717,"How excellent is the believer's pre-dawn meal of dates."],[1718,"Take the pre-dawn meal, even if it is with a gulp of water."],[1719,"The distinguishing factor between our fast and the fast of the People of the Book is eating the pre-dawn meal."],[1720,"The Jews used to take the day of Ashura as a festival, so the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, \"Differ from them: fast, you.\""],[1721,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ sent him to his people, saying: Command your people to fast this day. I said: What if I find that they have already eaten? He said: Then let them complete the rest of their day."],[1722,"«The Messenger of Allah ﷺ commanded trimming the mustaches and letting the beards grow.»"],[1723,"The Majus were mentioned in the presence of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and he said, «They leave their side whiskers and shave their beards, so differ from them.» Ibn 'Umar used to trim his side whiskers as a sheep or camel is sheared."],[1724,"«The Jews and the Christians do not dye, so differ from them.»"],[1725,"«Change gray hair and do not resemble the Jews and the Christians.»"],[1726,"«The best thing with which you change gray hair is henna and katam.»"],[1727,"'Act differently from the Jews and Christians, for they do not pray in their leather socks or their sandals.'"],[1728,"The Jews, when a woman among them menstruated, they would turn her out of the houses, and they would not eat with her, nor drink with her, nor have intercourse with her in the houses. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ was asked about that, and Allah, mighty and sublime, revealed: 'They ask you about menstruation. Say: It is harm, so keep away from wives during menstruation' [al-Baqarah 2:222]. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: 'Do everything except intercourse.' The Jews said: 'We do not see this man leaving anything of our affair but he contradicts us.' Usayd b. Hudayr and 'Abbad b. Bishr came and said: 'O Messenger of Allah, the Jews say such and such. Shall we not have intercourse with them during menstruation?' He said: The face of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ changed so much that I thought he had become angry with them. They left, and a gift of milk came to him. He sent after them, and we thought that he had not been angry with them, and he gave them to drink."],[1729,"“One of you should ask his Lord for all his needs, even the strap of his sandal when it breaks.”"],[1730,"Abu Bakr said: O Messenger of Allah, tell me what I should say when I reach morning and when I reach evening. He said: \"Say: O Allah, Knower of the unseen and the witnessed, Originator of the heavens and the earth, Lord of all things and their Sovereign, I bear witness that there is no god but You. I seek refuge in You from the evil of my soul and from the evil of Satan and his polytheism.\""],[1731,"\"These privies are attended by devils, so if one of you wants to enter, let him say: I seek refuge in Allah from the male and female devils.\""],[1732,"When one of you enters the mosque, let him greet and say: O Allah, open for me the gates of Your mercy. And when he leaves, let him say: O Allah, I ask You of Your bounty."],[1733,"When one of you comes to the mosque, let him say: O Allah, open for me the gates of Your mercy. And when he leaves, let him say: O Allah, I ask You of Your bounty."],[1734,"When one of you enters the mosque, let him greet the Prophet ﷺ and say: O Allah, open for me the gates of Your mercy. And when he leaves, let him greet the Prophet ﷺ and say: O Allah, protect me from the accursed Shayṭān."],[1735,"The sun eclipsed during the time of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. He stood up alarmed, and we feared it might be the Hour until he reached the mosque. He stood and prayed with the longest standing, bowing, and prostration I have ever seen him do in any prayer. Then he said, “These signs that Allah sends are not because of anyone’s death or life, but Allah sends them to frighten His servants. So when you see any of that, hasten to His remembrance, supplication, and seeking forgiveness.”"],[1736,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to me: “Sit down, O my dear son, mention Allah's name, eat with your right hand, and eat from what is near you.” He said: By Allah, my manner of eating has remained so ever since."],[1737,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ invited him to a meal and said: “Come, O my dear son, eat from what is near you, eat with your right hand, and mention Allah's name over it.”"],[1738,"“Whoever forgets to mention Allah at the beginning of his meal should say when he remembers: 'In the name of Allah at its beginning and its end,' for it starts his meal anew and prevents the evil one from having any share in it.”"],[1739,"“The Messenger of Allah ﷺ was eating food with six of his Companions when a Bedouin came and ate it all in two bites. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: ‘If he had said Bismillah, it would have sufficed you (all). When any one of you eats food, let him say Bismillah, and if he forgets to say Bismillah at the beginning, let him say Bismillah fi awwalihi wa akhirih (In the Name of Allah at the beginning and at the end).’” (Using translation from Ibn Mājah 3264)"],[1740,"“What brought you two out at this hour?” They said: By Allah, nothing brought us out except the pangs of hunger we feel in our bellies. He said: “By the One in whose hand is my soul, nothing brought me out either except that. So get up.” They went until they came to the door of Abu Ayyub al-Ansari. Abu Ayyub used to keep aside food or milk for the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, but that day he was late, and when he did not come at his usual time, he gave it to his family and went off to his palm grove to work. When they reached the door, his wife came out and said: Welcome to Allah's Prophet ﷺ and those with him. Allah's Prophet ﷺ said to her: “Where is Abu Ayyub?” He heard him while working in his palm grove and came running, saying: Welcome to Allah's Prophet ﷺ and those with him. O Prophet of Allah, this is not the usual time you come. The Prophet ﷺ said to him: “You are right.” He went and cut a bunch of dates from the palm tree, containing all kinds: dry dates, fresh ripe dates, and unripe dates. The Prophet ﷺ said: “I did not want this; could you not have picked only dry dates for us?” He said: O Prophet of Allah, I wanted you to eat from its dry dates, fresh dates, and unripe dates. And I will certainly slaughter something for you along with this. He said: “If you slaughter, do not slaughter a milk-giving animal.” So he took a young she-goat or a kid and slaughtered it, and said to his wife: Bake and knead for us; you know more about baking. He took the kid, cooked it, and roasted half of it. When the food was ready, it was placed before the Prophet ﷺ and his companions. He took some of the kid and placed it on a loaf, then said: “O Abu Ayyub, take this to Fatimah, for she has not had anything like this for days.” Abu Ayyub took it to Fatimah. When they had eaten and were satisfied, the Prophet ﷺ said: “Bread, meat, dry dates, unripe dates, and fresh dates.” His eyes filled with tears. “By the One in whose hand is my soul, this is the very bliss about which you will be questioned. Allah, Majestic and Exalted, said: 'Then you will surely be asked that Day about bliss' (Qur'an 102:8). This is the bliss about which you will be questioned on the Day of Resurrection.” This weighed heavily on his companions, so he said: “Rather, when you attain something like this and reach out your hands, say: 'In the name of Allah.' And when you are satisfied, say: 'Praise be to Allah who has satisfied us, blessed us, and favored us. This is enough for it.'” When he rose, he said to Abu Ayyub: “Come to us tomorrow.” He never received a favor from anyone but loved to repay it. Abu Ayyub did not hear that, so Umar said: The Prophet ﷺ ordered you to come to him tomorrow. So he went to him the next day, and the Prophet ﷺ gave him his slave girl, saying: “O Abu Ayyub, treat her well, for we have seen only good from her while she was with us.” When Abu Ayyub brought her from the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, he said: I find no better fulfillment of the Messenger of Allah's ﷺ instruction than to free her. So he freed her."],[1741,"\"When you hear the muezzin, say the like of what he says.\""],[1742,"\"When one of you intends a matter, let him say: O Allah, I seek Your guidance by Your knowledge, and I seek ability by Your power, and I ask You of Your great bounty. For You have power and I have none, and You know and I know not, and You are the Knower of hidden things. O Allah, if this matter is good for me in my religion, and good for me in my livelihood, and good for me in the outcome of my affair, then decree it for me and bless me in it. And if other than that is better for me, then decree for me the good wherever it may be, and make me content with Your decree.\""],[1743,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to teach us the istikharah supplication as he taught us a surah from the Quran, saying, \"When one of you intends a matter, let him pray two rak'ahs other than the obligatory, then let him say: O Allah, I seek Your guidance by Your knowledge, and I seek ability by Your power, and I ask You of Your great bounty. For You have power and I have none, and You know and I know not, and You are the Knower of hidden things. O Allah, if You know this matter, naming it specifically, to be good for me in my religion, my livelihood, and the outcome of my affair, then decree it for me, make it easy for me, and bless me in it. And if it is evil for me in my religion, my livelihood, and the outcome of my affair, then turn it away from me and turn me away from it, and decree for me the good wherever it may be, and make me content with it.\""],[1744,"Keep the proposal secret, then perform ablution and perfect your ablution, then pray what God has decreed for you, then praise your Lord and glorify Him, then say: O God, You have power and I have no power, You know and I do not know, and You are the Knower of the unseen. If You see in so-and-so (and you name her by her name) good for me in my religion, my worldly life, and my hereafter, then decree her for me; and if someone other than her is better for me than her in my religion, my worldly life, and my hereafter, then decree that for me.\""],[1745,"\"When you are present with a dying person, say good, for the angels say 'Amen' to what you say.\" She said: When Abu Salamah died, I said, \"O Messenger of Allah, what should I say?\" He said, \"Say: O Allah, forgive him and grant us a good successor.\" She said: And Allah gave me Muhammad ﷺ as a successor."],[1746,"The Prophet ﷺ entered the graveyard and said, \"Peace be upon you, O abode of a believing people. Indeed we, if Allah wills, shall join you.\""],[1747,"When they went out to the graveyards, the Messenger of Allah ﷺ taught them to say, \"Peace be upon the inhabitants of this abode from among the believers and Muslims. Indeed we, if Allah wills, shall join you. You are our predecessors and we are your followers. We ask Allah for well-being for us and for you.\""],[1748,"When you place your dead in the niche, say: 'In the name of Allah and upon the Sunnah of the Messenger of Allah.'"],[1749,"Allah loves sneezing and dislikes yawning. So if one of you yawns, let him suppress it as much as he can and not say 'haw,' for if he says 'haw,' Satan laughs at him. And if one of you sneezes and says, 'Praise be to Allah,' it is obligatory upon the one who hears him to say, 'May Allah have mercy on you.'"],[1750,"We were with Salim b. Ubayd on a military expedition, and a man from the people sneezed and said, 'Peace be upon you.' Salim said, 'Peace be upon you and upon your mother.' The man felt offended. Salim said to him, 'It seems you felt offended?' He said, 'I would not like you to mention my mother with good or evil.' Salim said, 'We were with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ on a journey, and a man sneezed and said, \"Peace be upon you.\" The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, \"Upon you and upon your mother. When one of you sneezes, let him say: 'Praise be to Allah in every situation,' or he said: 'Praise be to Allah, Lord of the worlds,' and let someone say to him: 'May Allah have mercy on you,' and let him say: 'May Allah forgive you.'\"'"],[1751,"How can I be at ease when the blower of the trumpet has put the horn to his mouth, bowed his forehead, and is waiting for the command to blow?' They said: 'O Messenger of Allah, what should we say that day?' He said: 'Say: Allah is sufficient for us, and He is the best disposer of affairs.'"],[1752,"Fatimah came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ asking him for a servant. He said to her, \"Say: O Allah, Lord of the seven heavens and Lord of the Mighty Throne, our Lord and Lord of everything, You are the Manifest, so there is nothing above You, and You are the Hidden, so there is nothing beneath You. Revealer of the Torah, the Gospel, and the Criterion, Splitter of the seed and the date-stone. I seek refuge in You from the evil of everything whose forelock You hold. You are the First, so there is nothing before You, and You are the Last, so there is nothing after You. Settle our debt and free us from poverty.\" *"],[1753,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ taught me these words and commanded me, if hardship or distress befell me, to say them: “There is no god but Allah, the Forbearing, the Generous. Glory be to Him, and blessed is Allah, Lord of the Mighty Throne, and praise be to Allah, Lord of the worlds.”"],[1754,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, \"No servant says when he is afflicted with sorrow or grief: 'O Allah, I am Your servant, the son of Your servant, the son of Your maidservant. My forelock is in Your hand, Your command over me is forever executed and Your decree over me is just. I ask You by every name belonging to You which You have named Yourself with, or revealed in Your Book, or You taught to any of Your creation, or You have preserved in the knowledge of the unseen with You, that You make the Quran the life of my heart and the light of my breast, and a departure for my sorrow and a release for my anxiety,' except that Allah will take away his distress and replace it with joy.\" They said, \"O Messenger of Allah, should we not learn these words?\" He said, \"Certainly, whoever hears them should learn them.\""],[1755,"\"Whoever is afflicted by a calamity, let him say: 'Indeed we belong to Allah and to Him we shall return. O Allah, with You I seek reward for my calamity, so reward me in it and replace it for me with something better than it.'\" When Abu Salama died, I said it, and every time I reached 'replace it for me with something better than it,' I said to myself: Who is better than Abu Salama? When her waiting period ended, Abu Bakr sent to propose to her, but she did not marry him. Then 'Umar sent to propose to her, but she did not marry him. Then the Messenger of Allah ﷺ sent 'Umar b. al-Khattab to her to propose on his behalf. She said, \"Inform the Messenger of Allah ﷺ that I am a jealous woman and that I have children, and none of my guardians is present.\" So 'Umar came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and mentioned that to him. He said, \"Return to her and say: As for your saying that you are a jealous woman, I will ask Allah to remove your jealousy. As for your saying that you have children, your children will be taken care of. As for your saying that none of your guardians is present, there is no guardian of yours, present or absent, who would dislike that.\" She said to her son, \"O 'Umar, stand up and marry the Messenger of Allah ﷺ.\" So he married her. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ would come to her to consummate the marriage, but when she saw him, she took her daughter Zaynab and placed her in her lap, so the Messenger of Allah ﷺ would leave. 'Ammar b. Yasir, who was her foster brother, learned of this, so he came to her and said, \"Where is this ugly one with whom you have harmed the Messenger of Allah ﷺ?\" He took her and went away. Then the Messenger of Allah ﷺ came and entered upon her, and he began looking around the house and said, \"What did Zaynab do?\" She said, \"'Ammar came and took her and went away.\" So the Messenger of Allah ﷺ consummated the marriage with her and said, \"I will not reduce you from what I gave so-and-so: two millstones, two jars, and a cushion stuffed with palm fiber.\" And he said, \"If I stay seven nights with you, I will stay seven nights with my wives.\""],[1756,"He used to teach them this supplication as he taught them a surah from the Quran: “O Allah, I seek refuge in You from the punishment of Hell, and I seek refuge in You from the punishment of the grave, and I seek refuge in You from the trial of life and death, and I seek refuge in You from the evil of the false messiah, the Dajjal.”"],[1757,"While we were in a garden belonging to Banu al-Najjar with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and he was on a mule, his mule shied, and there were graves in the garden. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Who knows these graves?” A man said: “I do, O Messenger of Allah.” He said: “What are they?” He said: “They died in polytheism.” He said: “Were it not that you would not bury your dead, I would have prayed to Allah to make you hear the punishment of the grave that I hear. This nation will be tested in their graves.” Then he turned to us and said: “Seek refuge in Allah from the punishment of the Fire and the punishment of the grave, and seek refuge in Allah from trials, both apparent and hidden, and seek refuge in Allah from the trial of the Dajjal.”"],[1758,"Umm Habibah said, \"O Allah, bless me in my husband, the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and my father Abu Sufyan, and my brother Mu'awiyah.\" The Prophet ﷺ said, \"You have asked Allah about fixed terms, attained ends, and apportioned provisions, none of which is hastened before its due time. If you had asked Allah to protect you from the punishment of the Fire or the punishment of the grave, it would have been better or more virtuous.\""],[1759,"“Seek refuge in Allah from poverty, humiliation, and from wronging or being wronged.”"],[1760,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to teach us these words as writing is taught: “O Allah, I seek refuge in You from miserliness, and I seek refuge in You from cowardice, and I seek refuge in You from being returned to the worst age, and I seek refuge in You from the trial of this world and the punishment of the grave.”"],[1761,"He complained to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ of a pain he felt in his body since he accepted Islam. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to him, \"Place your hand on the part of your body that hurts and say: In the name of Allah three times, then say seven times: I seek refuge in Allah and His power from the evil of what I find and fear.\""],[1762,"“The wind is from the mercy of Allah. It brings mercy and it brings punishment, so do not curse it. Ask Allah for its good and seek refuge from its evil.”"],[1763,"“When you hear the crowing of roosters, they have seen an angel, so ask Allah and desire from Him. When you hear the braying of donkeys, they have seen a devil, so seek refuge in Allah from the evil of what they saw.”"],[1764,"I swore by al-Lat and al-Uzza, and my companions said to me: You have spoken an evil word. So I went to the Prophet ﷺ and said: The covenant was recent, and I swore by al-Lat and al-Uzza. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to me: \"Say: There is no god but Allah alone, three times, and blow to your left three times, and seek refuge in Allah from Satan, and do not repeat it.\""],[1765,"A man came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and said, 'O Messenger of Allah, what I suffered from a scorpion that stung me last night!' He said, 'If you had said when evening came: Aʿūdhu bi-kalimāti llāhi t-tāmmāti min sharri mā khalaq (I seek refuge in the perfect words of Allah from the evil of what He has created), it would not have harmed you.'"],[1766,"Two men insulted each other in the presence of the Prophet ﷺ while we were sitting with him. One of them was insulting his companion in anger, and his face had turned red. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, “I know a word which, if he said it, what he feels would leave him: I seek refuge with Allah from the accursed Satan.” They said to the man, “Do you not hear what the Messenger of Allah ﷺ is saying?” He said, “I am not insane.”"],[1767,"\"These privies are attended by devils, so if one of you enters, let him say: O Allah, I seek refuge in You from the male and female devils.\""],[1768,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ drew back the curtain while the people were in rows behind Abu Bakr and said, “O people, nothing remains of the glad tidings of prophethood except the true dream a Muslim sees or is seen for him.” Then he said, “Verily, I have been forbidden from reciting while bowing or prostrating. As for bowing, magnify the Lord therein; and as for prostration, strive in supplication, for it is likely to be answered for you.”"],[1769,"When {So glorify the name of your Lord, the Magnificent} was revealed, he said, “Put it in your prostration.”"],[1770,"When one of you finishes the final tashahhud, let him seek refuge in Allah from four things: from the punishment of Hell, from the punishment of the grave, from the trial of life and death, and from the evil of the false messiah, the Dajjal."],[1771,"That he said to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ: Teach me a supplication to use in my prayer. He said: “Say: O Allah, I have wronged myself greatly, and none forgives sins but You, so forgive me with forgiveness from Yourself and have mercy on me. Indeed You are the Forgiving, the Merciful.”"],[1772,"Recite the mu‘awwidhat after every prayer."],[1773,"That the Messenger of Allah ﷺ took him by the hand one day and said: \"O Muʿādh, by Allah, I love you.\" Muʿādh said: \"May my father and mother be your ransom, O Messenger of Allah; by Allah, I love you.\" He said: \"I exhort you, O Muʿādh, never to fail, after every prayer, to say: O Allah, help me to remember You, thank You, and worship You well.\""],[1774,"Umm Sulaym came to the Prophet ﷺ and said: \"O Messenger of Allah, teach me words by which I may supplicate in my prayer.\" He said: \"Glorify Allah ten times, praise Him ten times, and magnify Him ten times, then ask Him your need.\""],[1775,"\"Two qualities no Muslim man keeps count of except that he enters Paradise. They are easy, but few are those who act upon them. He glorifies Allah after every prayer ten times, praises Him ten times, and magnifies Him ten times.\" He said: \"I saw the Prophet ﷺ counting them with his hand.\" He said: \"That is one hundred and fifty on the tongue, and one thousand five hundred in the Balance. When he retires to his bed, he glorifies, praises, and magnifies one hundred times, so that is one hundred on the tongue and one thousand in the Balance. Which of you would commit two thousand five hundred sins in a single day?\" He said: \"How can one not keep count of them?\" He said: \"Satan comes to one of you while he is in prayer and says: 'Remember such-and-such, remember such-and-such,' until he distracts him, and perhaps he will not comprehend. And he comes to him in his bed and keeps making him sleepy until he sleeps.\""],[1776,"\"Whoever glorifies Allah thirty-three times after his prayer, praises Him thirty-three times, magnifies Him thirty-three times, and completes one hundred with 'There is no god but Allah alone, with no partner. His is the dominion and His is the praise, and He is over all things competent,' his sins will be forgiven, even if they are like the foam of the sea.\""],[1777,"A man came to the Prophet ﷺ and said: \"I am not good at any of the Qur'an, so teach me something that will suffice me from it.\" He said: \"Say: 'Glory be to Allah, praise be to Allah, there is no god but Allah, and Allah is greatest.'\" He said: \"This is for my Lord; what is for me?\" He said: \"Say: 'O Allah, forgive me, have mercy on me, provide for me, and grant me well-being.'\""],[1778,"A man came to the Prophet ﷺ and said: \"O Messenger of Allah, I cannot learn the Qur'an, so teach me what will suffice me from the Qur'an.\" He said: \"Say: 'Glory be to Allah, praise be to Allah, there is no god but Allah, and Allah is greatest, and there is no might nor power except with Allah.'\" The man said: \"This is for Allah; what is for me?\" He said: \"Say: 'O Lord, forgive me, have mercy on me, guide me, grant me well-being, and provide for me.'\" Then the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"He has filled his hands with good.\""],[1779,"The most beloved speech to Allah is four phrases: 'Glory be to Allah, praise be to Allah, there is no god but Allah, and Allah is greatest.'"],[1780,"The best speech is four phrases; it does not harm you with whichever of them you begin: 'Glory be to Allah, praise be to Allah, there is no god but Allah, and Allah is greatest.'"],[1781,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ came upon me while I was glorifying Allah, then he went off for his need and returned after midday and said, 'Have you remained seated?' She said, 'Yes.' He said, 'Shall I not teach you words which, if weighed against them, would outweigh them, or if balanced against them, would balance them? Glory be to Allah by the number of His creation, three times; glory be to Allah by the weight of His Throne, three times; glory be to Allah by the contentment of Himself, three times; glory be to Allah by the ink of His words, three times.'"],[1782,"He entered with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ upon a woman who had date stones or pebbles in her hand with which she was glorifying Allah, and he said, 'Shall I not tell you what is easier for you than this and better? Glory be to Allah by the number of what He created in the heaven, and glory be to Allah by the number of what He created in the earth, and glory be to Allah by the number of what He is creating; and Allah is greatest the like of that, and praise be to Allah the like of that, and there is no god but Allah the like of that, and there is no might and no power except with Allah the like of that.'"],[1783,"\"Two words are light on the tongue, heavy on the scale: Subhan Allah wa bi-hamdihi (Glory be to Allah and with His praise), Subhan Allah al-`Azim (Glory be to Allah, the Magnificent).\""],[1784,"When the servant says, 'There is no god but Allah, and Allah is greatest,' his Lord affirms him as true, saying, 'My servant has spoken truth: there is no god but Me, and I am greatest.' When he says, 'There is no god but Allah alone,' his Lord affirms him as true, saying, 'My servant has spoken truth: there is no god but Me alone.' When he says, 'There is no god but Allah, with no partner,' his Lord affirms him as true, saying, 'My servant has spoken truth: there is no god but Me, with no partner.' When he says, 'There is no god but Allah; His is the dominion,' his Lord affirms him as true, saying, 'My servant has spoken truth: there is no god but Me; Mine is the dominion and Mine is the praise.' When he says, 'There is no god but Allah; there is no might and no power except with Allah,' his Lord affirms him as true and says, 'My servant has spoken truth: there is no god but Me, and there is no might and no power except with Me.'"],[1785,"I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say this day last year—then Abu Bakr, ؓ , was moved to tears and wept. Then he said, 'I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: You will never be given anything after the word of sincerity like well-being, so ask Allah for well-being.'"],[1786,"O Messenger of Allah, what should I ask Allah for? He said: \"Ask Allah for pardon and well-being.\" Then he said: What should I ask Allah for? He said: \"Ask Allah for pardon and well-being.\""],[1787,"I came to Madinah after the death of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and met Abu Bakr addressing the people. He said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ stood among us in the first year, and he was choked with tears three times, then said: \"O people, ask Allah for well-being, for no one has been given anything like certainty after well-being, nor anything more severe than doubt after disbelief. You must be truthful, for it leads to righteousness, and both are in Paradise. Beware of lying, for it leads to wickedness, and both are in the Fire.\" He meant by it the perpetrators of the two, not the two themselves."],[1788,"A man came intending to travel and said, “O Messenger of Allah, advise me.” The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to him, “I advise you to fear Allah and to say Allāhu akbar at every elevation.” When the man turned away, the Prophet ﷺ said, “O Allah, roll up the earth for him and make the journey easy for him.”"],[1789,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ taught her to say: “O Allah, I ask You for all good, the immediate and the deferred, what I know of it and what I do not know; and I seek refuge in You from all evil, the immediate and the deferred, what I know of it and what I do not know. O Allah, I ask You for the good that Your servant and Prophet asked You for, and I seek refuge in You from the evil from which Your servant and Prophet sought refuge. I ask You for Paradise and whatever word or deed brings one near to it, and I seek refuge in You from the Fire and whatever word or deed brings one near to it. I ask You to make every decree You decree for me good.”"],[1791,"The Prophet of Allah ﷺ used to teach us the tashahhud in prayer as he used to teach us a surah from the Quran, and he would teach us what he would not teach us as he taught us the tashahhud: “O Allah, unite our hearts, reconcile our differences, guide us to the paths of peace, deliver us from darkness to light, and keep us away from immoralities, both apparent and hidden. O Allah, protect us in our hearing, our sight, and our spouses, and make us grateful for Your blessing, praising You for it, accepting it, so complete it upon us.”"],[1792,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, \"None of you should wish for death because of harm that befalls him. But if he must wish, let him say: O Allah, keep me alive as long as life is better for me, and take me when death is better for me.\""],[1793,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, \"O Umm Harithah, verily, it (referring to Paradise) has gardens, and Umm Harithah is in the highest level of Paradise. So when you ask Allah, ask Him for Al-Firdaus.\""],[1794,"Umar b. al-Khattab suffered a misfortune, so he came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and complained to him about that, and asked him to order a wasq of dates for him. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to him: 'If you wish, I will order a wasq of dates for you, and if you wish, I will teach you words that are better for you?' He said: 'Teach them to me and order a wasq for me, for I am in need of it.' He said: 'Say: \"O Allah, preserve me with Islam while sitting, preserve me with Islam while standing, preserve me with Islam while lying down, and do not give power over me to a jealous enemy. I seek refuge in You from the evil of what You hold by its forelock, and I ask You for all the good that is in Your hand.\"'"],[1795,"A man came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and said: 'O Muhammad, 'Abd al-Muttalib was better for his people than you: he fed them liver and hump, while you slaughter them.' He said to him: 'Whatever Allah wills.' When he wanted to leave, he said: 'What should I say?' He said: 'Say: O Allah, protect me from the evil of my soul and resolve for me the most rightly-guided of my affairs.' The man left before he had accepted Islam, then said: 'O Messenger of Allah, I came to you and said: Teach me. You said: \"O Allah, protect me from the evil of my soul and resolve for me the most rightly-guided of my affairs.\" So what should I say now that I have accepted Islam?' He said: 'Say: O Allah, protect me from the evil of my soul and resolve for me the most rightly-guided of my affairs. O Allah, forgive me what I conceal and what I reveal, what I do mistakenly and what I do deliberately, and what I am ignorant of.'"],[1796,"I said to al-Hasan b. 'Ali, 'What do you remember from the Messenger of Allah ﷺ?' He said, 'I remember that I took a date from the dates of charity and put it in my mouth, and he removed it with its saliva and threw it among the dates. And he used to teach us this supplication: O Allah, guide me among those You have guided, grant me well-being among those You have granted well-being, take me under Your care among those You have taken under Your care, bless me in what You have given, and protect me from the evil of what You have decreed. Indeed, You decree and none decrees against You. Indeed, no one whom You befriend is humiliated.' Shu'bah said, 'And I think he also said, Blessed and Exalted are You.'"],[1797,"Bring me the platter so that we may play with it, but the people kept it away from me. So, he said, \"O my nephew, do not keep it away from me, but keep from me what I have heard from the Messenger of Allah, peace be upon him: 'When people hoard silver and gold coins, hoard these words: O Allah, I ask You for steadfastness in affairs, determination in righteousness. And I ask You for gratitude for Your blessings and excellence in worship. And I ask You for the best of what You know. And I seek refuge in You from the evil of what You know. And I seek Your forgiveness for what You know. Indeed, You are the All-Knower of the unseen.'\""],[1798,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ visited a sick man who had become like a chick. He said: 'What were you asking for or supplicating for?' He said: 'I used to say: \"O Allah, whatever punishment You would inflict on me in the Hereafter, hasten it in this world.\"' He said: 'Glory be to Allah! You cannot bear it, or you cannot endure it. Say: \"O Allah, grant us good in this world and good in the Hereafter, and protect us from the punishment of the Fire.\"'"],[1799,"He narrates that he heard the Prophet ﷺ saying, \"O people, repent to your Lord, for I repent to Him one hundred times every day.\""],[1800,"Indeed, a covering comes over my heart, and indeed I seek Allah's forgiveness every day a hundred times."],[1801,"The master of seeking forgiveness is for the servant to say: 'O Allah, You are my Lord, and I am Your servant. There is no god but You. You created me, and I am Your servant. I have entered the morning upon Your covenant and Your promise as much as I am able. I seek refuge in You from the evil of what I have done, and I acknowledge Your favor upon me, and I acknowledge my sins, so forgive me, for none forgives sins but You.'"],[1802,"When one of you retires to his bed, let him take the inner part of his lower garment and dust off his bed with it and mention Allah's name, for he does not know what has come upon it after him. And when he wants to lie down, let him lie down on his right side and say: 'Glory be to You, my Lord. By You I lay down my side and by You I raise it. If You withhold my soul, then forgive it; and if You release it, then protect it as You protect Your righteous servants.'"],[1803,"When one of you retires to his bed, let him take off his lower garment and dust off his bed with its inner side. Then let him use his right hand as a pillow and say: 'In Your name, O Allah, I lay down my side and by You I raise it. O Allah, if You withhold it (my soul), then have mercy on it; and if You release it, then protect it as You protect Your righteous servants.'"],[1804,"When you take to your bed, perform ablution as you would for prayer, then lie down on your right side, then say: 'O Allah, I have submitted my face to You and delegated my affair to You and entrusted my back to You, out of desire and fear of You. There is no refuge and no escape from You except to You. I believe in Your Book which You have sent down and in Your Prophet whom You have sent.' And make it the last thing you say. Then if you die, you die upon the fitrah. I said: 'Should I memorize them: and in Your Messenger whom You have sent?' He said: 'And in Your Prophet whom You have sent.'"],[1805,"Fāṭimah came to the Prophet ﷺ to complain about the marks on her hands from grinding flour. She heard that the Prophet ﷺ had received some captives, so she went to him to request a servant but did not find him. Instead, she met ʿĀʾishah and shared her request with her. When the Prophet ﷺ returned, ʿĀʾishah informed him about Fāṭimah's request. So the Messenger of Allah ﷺ came to us, and we had already taken our places in bed. We got up to greet him, and he said, \"Stay in your places.\" He then sat among us until I felt the coolness of his feet on my chest. He then said, \"I shall guide you to something better than having a servant: When you go to bed, say Allāhu akbar (Allah is the Greatest) thirty-four times, al-ḥamdu lillāh (Praise be to Allah) thirty-three times, and subḥān Allāh (Glory be to Allah) thirty-three times; This is better for you than having a servant.\""],[1806,"I entered upon the Prophet ﷺ and said, “O Prophet of Allah, teach me something to say when I retire to my bed.” He said, “Recite Qul ya ayyuha al-kafirun.”"],[1807,"He said, 'Would you like to take charge of a stepdaughter of ours, Zaynab, and look after her?' Then he came and the Prophet ﷺ asked him, and he said, 'I left her with her mother.' He said, 'Then what brings you? Has something new come?' He said, 'I have come so that you may teach me something to say at my bedtime.' He said, 'Recite: Qul ya ayyuha al-kafirun, then sleep upon its completion, for it is a declaration of freedom from shirk.'"],[1808,"Abu Salih used to command us, when one of us wanted to sleep, to lie down on his right side and then say: 'O Allah, Lord of the heavens and Lord of the earth and Lord of the Mighty Throne, our Lord and Lord of everything, Splitter of the grain and the date-stone, Revealer of the Torah, the Gospel, and the Criterion, I seek refuge in You from the evil of everything whose forelock You hold. You are the First, so there is nothing before You, and You are the Last, so there is nothing after You, and You are the Outward, so there is nothing above You. Settle our debt and free us from poverty.' And he would narrate that from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet ﷺ."],[1809,"I used to see dreams and they would make me ill, until I heard Abu Qatadah say, \"I used to see dreams and they would make me ill, until I heard the Prophet ﷺ say, 'The righteous dream is from Allah. If one of you sees what he loves, let him relate it to one he loves. If one of you sees what he dislikes, let him seek refuge with Allah from its evil and spit to his left three times.'\""],[1810,"The dream is from Allah and the bad dream is from Satan. If one of you sees something he dislikes, let him spit to his left three times when he wakes and seek refuge with Allah from its evil, for it will not harm him, if Allah wills."],[1811,"When one of you sees a dream he dislikes, let him spit to his left three times, seek refuge with Allah from Shaytan three times, and turn over from the side he was lying on."],[1812,"Do not initiate the greeting of salam with the People of the Book; and when you see them on a road, force them to its narrowest side."],[1813,"«When you pray over the deceased, make your supplication sincerely for him.»"],[1814,"«When you pray over the funeral, make your supplication sincerely for it.»"],[1815,"If one of you dozes in his sitting place on Friday, let him move from that spot to another."],[1816,"Umar b. al-Khattab appointed me over the sadaqah. When I finished with it and delivered it to him, he ordered for me an allowance. I said to him: I only worked for Allah, and my reward is with Allah. He said: Take what you are given, for I said to my worker at the time of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ the like of what you said, and the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “When you are given something without your asking, then eat it and give charity from it.”"],[1817,"The Prophet ﷺ said to his companions when they wanted to enter Makkah in his 'Umrah after al-Hudaybiyyah, \"Tomorrow your people will see you, so let them see you as sturdy.\" When they entered the mosque, they touched the Corner, then did ramal, and the Prophet ﷺ was with them, until when they reached the Corner, they walked to the Black Stone, then did ramal until they reached the Corner. He did that three times, then walked the four."],[1818,"Sulayk al-Ghaṭafānī entered the mosque on Friday while the Messenger of Allah ﷺ was delivering the sermon to the people. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to him, “Bow two rakʿahs and do not return to anything like this.” So he bowed them, then sat."],[1819,"Sulayk al-Ghaṭafānī came on Friday while the Messenger of Allah ﷺ was delivering the sermon and sat down. He said to him, “O Sulayk, stand up and bow two rakʿahs, and be brief in them.” Then he said, “When one of you comes on Friday while the imam is delivering the sermon, let him bow two rakʿahs and be brief in them.”"],[1820,"«Whoever seeks a right, let him seek it with chastity, whether he obtains it or not.»"],[1821,"When the Messenger of Allah ﷺ sent Mu'adh to Yemen, he said, «You will come to a people of the Book. When you come to them, call them to testify that there is no god but Allah and that Muhammad is the Messenger of Allah. If they obey you in that, then inform them that Allah has prescribed upon them five prayers every day and night. If they obey you in that, then inform them that Allah, Mighty and Exalted, has prescribed upon them a charity taken from their rich and returned to their poor. If they obey you in that, then beware of their finest properties and fear the supplication of the oppressed, for there is no veil between it and Allah.»"],[1822,"Abu Bakr brought Abu Quhafah to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ on the day of the conquest of Makkah. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to Abu Bakr, «If you had kept the old man in his house, we would have come to him, out of honor for Abu Bakr.» He said, 'Then he embraced Islam, and his head and beard were white like the thaghamah plant.' The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, «Change them both and keep him away from black.»"],[1823,"Barirah came to me and said: \"I have contracted with my owners for nine uqiyyahs, one uqiyyah each year, so help me.\" Aishah said: \"If your owners wish, I will pay them the full amount at once, and your wala' will be mine.\" Barirah went to her owners and told them that, but they refused. She came from her owners while the Messenger of Allah ﷺ was sitting, and she said: \"I offered that to them, but they refused unless the wala' is for them.\" The Messenger of Allah ﷺ heard it and asked her, and Aishah informed him. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"Take her and stipulate the wala' for them, for the wala' belongs only to the one who frees.\" Aishah said: Then the Messenger of Allah ﷺ stood up among the people and praised and extolled Allah, then said: \"Now then, what is the matter with men who impose conditions not in the Book of Allah? Whatever condition is not in the Book of Allah is void, even if it be a hundred conditions. The decree of Allah is more deserving and the condition of Allah is more binding, and the wala' belongs only to the one who frees.\""],[1824,"\"That I pour for them a drink from you, then I will free you.\" So, I did it and I said, \"And may I have your loyalty in return?\" Barirah mentioned that to her family and they said, \"We will not accept the loyalty unless it is for us.\" Yahya said, \"Ummrah claimed that Aishah mentioned that to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and he said, 'That should not prevent you. Buy her and free her, for loyalty is only for the one who frees.'\""],[1825,"Let me not find any man who, when a command of mine comes to him, whether I have commanded it or forbidden it, says, 'We do not know what this is; we have the Book of Allah, not this in it.'"],[1826,"I have been given the Book and what is equivalent to it. Soon a satiated man on his couch will say, 'Between us and you is this Book; whatever we find in it as lawful we will deem lawful, and whatever we find in it as unlawful we will deem unlawful.' Nay, it is not so."],[1827,"Those before you were destroyed only by their questioning and their disagreement with their prophets. So when I forbid you from something, avoid it, and when I command you with something, do of it what you are able."],[1828,"He halted his camel and a man held its nose-rein—or he said its halter—and he said: “Which day is this?” We remained silent until we thought he would call it by a name other than its own. Then he said: “Is it not the Day of Sacrifice?” We said: “Yes.” He said: “Which month is this?” We remained silent until we thought he would call it by a name other than its own. Then he said: “Is it not Dhu al-Hijjah?” We said: “Yes.” He said: “Which land is this?” We remained silent until we thought he would call it by a name other than its own. Then he said: “Is it not the Sacred Land?” We said: “Yes.” He said: “Your blood, your wealth, and your honor are sacred to one another, like the sanctity of this day of yours, in this month of yours, in this land of yours. Let those present among you convey to those absent, for the one present may convey to one who is more mindful than him.”"],[1829,"\"By the One besides whom there is no god, the blood of a man who bears witness that there is no god but Allah and that I am the Messenger of Allah is not lawful except for three persons: the one who abandons Islam and leaves the community, the previously married adulterer, and a life for a life.\""],[1830,"“The blood of a Muslim is not lawful except in one of three cases: a life for a life, the previously married adulterer, and the one who abandons his religion and separates from the community.”"],[1831,"“It is not lawful for anyone to take his brother’s staff without his willing consent.” He said that because of the severity with which Allah forbade the wealth of a Muslim to another Muslim."],[1832,"ʿAbd Allāh b. al-Zubayr said regarding a sale or a gift she had given, “By Allah, ʿĀʾishah will stop, or I will place her under interdiction.” When that reached her, ʿĀʾishah said, “I vow to Allah that I will never speak to Ibn al-Zubayr again.” When her desertion of him became prolonged, Ibn al-Zubayr sought intercession with her, but ʿĀʾishah said, “By Allah, I will not accept anyone’s intercession for him, and I will never break the vow I made.” When that became prolonged for Ibn al-Zubayr, he spoke to al-Miswar b. Makhramah and ʿAbd al-Raḥmān b. al-Aswad b. ʿAbd Yaghūth, both of Banū Zuhrah, and said to them, “I adjure you by Allah to bring me in to ʿĀʾishah, for it is not lawful for her to vow to cut me off.” So al-Miswar b. Makhramah and ʿAbd al-Raḥmān b. al-Aswad came with ʿAbd Allāh b. al-Zubayr, wrapping him in their cloaks, until they sought permission to enter upon ʿĀʾishah. They said, “Peace be upon the Prophet ﷺ. May we enter, O Mother of the Believers?” ʿĀʾishah said, “Enter.” They said, “All of us?” She said, “Yes, enter, all of you,” not knowing that Ibn al-Zubayr was with them. When they entered, Ibn al-Zubayr plunged through the curtain and entered upon ʿĀʾishah, embracing her, and began adjuring her and weeping. Al-Miswar and ʿAbd al-Raḥmān began adjuring ʿĀʾishah, saying to her, “The Messenger of Allah ﷺ forbade what you have done, and it is not lawful for a Muslim to desert his brother for more than three [days].” When they repeated the reminder to ʿĀʾishah, she began reminding them and weeping, saying, “I made a vow, and the vow is serious.” They did not cease until she spoke to Ibn al-Zubayr. Then she freed forty slaves to expiate her vow. And after she freed forty slaves, she would weep until her tears wetted her veil."],[1833,"Whoever vows to obey Allah, let him obey Him; and whoever vows to disobey Allah, let him not disobey Him."],[1834,"It is not lawful for a Muslim to boycott his brother for more than three nights. They meet, and this one turns away and that one turns away, and the better of them is the one who initiates the greeting of peace."],[1835,"The rich man's delay in payment is tyranny."],[1836,"\"Delay in payment by a rich man is injustice, and if one of you is referred to a wealthy man for payment, let him follow up.\""],[1837,"I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say on the day of the conquest of Makkah: \"Indeed Allah and His Messenger have forbidden the sale of pigs, the sale of carrion, and the sale of idols.\" A man said: \"O Messenger of Allah, what do you think about the fat of carrion, for we grease leather and ships with it, and we use it for lamps?\" He said: \"May Allah fight the Jews. Indeed Allah forbade them its fats, so they melted them down, then sold them and consumed their price.\""],[1838,"He asked Ibn 'Abbas about what is pressed from grapes. Ibn 'Abbas said: A man gifted the Messenger of Allah ﷺ a waterskin of wine, and the Prophet ﷺ said to him: \"Do you not know that Allah, Mighty and Exalted, has forbidden drinking it?\" So the man whispered to a person beside him, and the Prophet ﷺ said: \"What did you whisper to him?\" He said: \"I ordered him to sell it.\" The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to him: \"Indeed, the One who forbade drinking it forbade selling it.\" So he opened the two waterskins until what was in them drained away."],[1839,"\"When the verses at the end of Surat al-Baqarah concerning riba were revealed, the Messenger of Allah ﷺ went out and forbade trading in wine.\""],[1840,"Every intoxicant is wine, and every wine is forbidden.”"],[1841,"When wine was forbidden, Anas said, \"On that day I was serving eleven men. They ordered me, and I overturned it, and the people overturned their vessels with what was in them until the streets almost became impassable from its smell.\" Anas said, \"Their wine at that time was nothing but unripe dates and ripe dates mixed together. A man came to the Prophet ﷺ and said, 'I had the property of an orphan, and I bought wine with it. Do you think I may sell it and return the orphan's property to him?' The Prophet ﷺ said, 'May Allah destroy the Jews. Fat was forbidden to them, but they sold it and ate its price.' The Prophet ﷺ did not permit me to sell wine.\""],[1842,"Every intoxicant is forbidden. Allah has taken a pledge that whoever drinks an intoxicant, He will give him to drink from the mud of khabal on the Day of Resurrection.”"],[1843,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ was asked about al-bitʿ, and he said, 'Every drink that intoxicates is unlawful.'"],[1844,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ sent me to Yemen, and I said, 'O Messenger of Allah, there are drinks there called al-bitʿ and al-mizr.' He said, 'What is al-bitʿ?' I said, 'A drink made from honey, and al-mizr is a drink made from barley.' He ﷺ said, 'Every intoxicant is unlawful.'"],[1845,"Some people from Yemen came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and he taught them the prayer, the sunnas, and the obligatory duties. They said, 'O Messenger of Allah, we have a drink that we make from wheat and barley.' He ﷺ said, 'Al-ghubayrāʾ?' They said, 'Yes.' He said, 'Do not consume it.' Two days later, they mentioned it to him again, and he said, 'Al-ghubayrāʾ?' They said, 'Yes.' He said, 'Do not consume it.' When they intended to depart, they asked him about it, and he said, 'Al-ghubayrāʾ?' They said, 'Yes.' He said, 'Then do not consume it.'"],[1846,"He forbade a small amount of that which intoxicates in large amount."],[1847,"O people, the prohibition of wine was revealed when it was from five things: grapes, dates, honey, wheat, and barley. And whatever intoxicates the mind is wine.” Three things I wish the Messenger of Allah ﷺ had left us a definitive instruction that we could follow: the grandfather, the kalala, and some categories of riba."],[1848,"Eating any fanged predator is forbidden."],[1849,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ passed by a man lying on his belly and nudged him with his foot, saying: “This is a lying posture that Allah does not love.”"],[1850,"A mule was gifted to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and it pleased him. We said, 'O Messenger of Allah, if only we mated donkeys with our horses so they would produce something like this.' He said, 'Only those who do not know do that.'"],[1851,"Heﷺ said to us, the messenger of Allahﷺ led us in prayer in which he recited aloud. When he finished, he turned to the people and said, \"Did anyone among you recite before me?\" They said, \"Yes, O Messenger of Allah.\" He said, \"I would never argue with the Quran.\""],[1852,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ prayed with his companions, and when he finished his prayer he turned to face them and said: “Do you recite in your prayer behind the imam while the imam is reciting?” They remained silent. He said it three times. Then a man or men said: We do. He said: “Do not do so; let each of you recite the Fatihah of the Book silently to himself.”"],[1853,"Expectoration in the mosque is a sin, and its expiation is burying it."],[1854,"\"There is no obedience to any human in disobedience to Allah, Mighty and Majestic.\""],[1855,"“The gates of Paradise are opened every Monday and Thursday, and Allah, Mighty and Majestic, forgives every servant who does not associate anything with Allah, except a man between whom and his brother there is enmity. It is said, ‘Delay these two until they reconcile. Delay these two until they reconcile.’”"],[1856,"Whoever believes in Allah and the Last Day, let him not harm his neighbor. Whoever believes in Allah and the Last Day, let him honor his guest. Whoever believes in Allah and the Last Day, let him speak good or remain silent."],[1857,"A man from the polytheists joined the Prophet ﷺ to fight with him. The Prophet ﷺ said, \"Go back, for we do not seek help from a polytheist.\""],[1858,"“If I saw gazelles grazing in Madinah, I would not startle them.” The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Between its two lava tracts is sacred.”"],[1859,"It is not lawful for anyone to carry weapons in Makkah."],[1860,"I asked the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and he gave me. Then I asked him, and he gave me three times. Then the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “O Hakim, this wealth is sweet and green. Whoever takes it with a generous soul, it will be blessed for him in it; and whoever takes it with greed of the soul, it will not be blessed for him in it, and he will be like one who eats but does not become full. The upper hand is better than the lower hand.” Hakim said: I said: O Messenger of Allah, by the One who sent you with the truth, I will not ask anyone for anything after you until I leave this world."],[1861,"Allah does not accept the prayer of a menstruating woman except with a veil."],[1862,"That he sent a servant of his with a sa‘ of barley and said: Sell it, then buy barley with it. The servant went and took a sa‘ and an increase of part of a sa‘. When he came, Ma‘mar was informed of that, and Ma‘mar said to him: Why did you do that? Go and return it, and take only like for like, for I used to hear the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: “Food for food, like for like.” And our food in those days was barley."],[1864,"That he sought an exchange for one hundred dinars. He said: Talhah b. ‘Ubayd Allah called me, and we bargained until he exchanged with me and took the gold, turning it over in his hand, and said: Until my treasurer comes from al-Ghabah. ‘Umar b. al-Khattab was listening, so ‘Umar said: By Allah, you will not part with him until you take from him. Then ‘Umar said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Gold for silver is riba unless it is hand to hand; wheat for wheat is riba unless it is hand to hand; dates for dates is riba unless it is hand to hand; barley for barley is riba unless it is hand to hand.”"],[1865,"Whatever I forbid you from something, avoid it, and whatever I command you with the command, do of it what you are able."],[1866,"\"Avoid the seven destructive sins.\" They said, \"O Messenger of Allah, what are they?\" He said, \"Associating partners with Allah, sorcery, killing a soul which Allah has forbidden except by right, consuming riba, consuming the orphan's wealth, fleeing on the day of battle, and slandering chaste, heedless, believing women.\""],[1867,"A bedouin came to the Prophet ﷺ and said, \"O Messenger of Allah, what are the major sins?\" He said, \"Associating partners with Allah.\" He said, \"Then what?\" He said, \"Then disobedience to parents.\" He said, \"Then what?\" He said, \"Then the false oath.\" I said to 'Amir, \"What is the false oath?\" He said, \"That by which a man seizes the property of a Muslim with an oath of patience, while he is lying in it.\""],[1868,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to me: “O 'A'ishah, beware of the sins that are regarded as insignificant, for they have a pursuer from Allah.”"],[1869,"That the Messenger of Allah ﷺ recited the words of Allah: {He it is who sent down upon you the Book, in it are clear verses} to its end, and said: \"When you see those who follow what is ambiguous from it, know that they are the ones Allah meant, so beware of them.\""],[1870,"“Whatever Allah dislikes from you, do not do it when you are alone.”"],[1871,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ ascended this pulpit and called out with a loud voice, saying: “O assembly of those who have submitted with their tongues but faith has not entered their hearts: do not harm the Muslims, do not reproach them, and do not seek out their stumbles. For whoever seeks the private shame of a Muslim, Allah will seek his private shame, and whoever Allah seeks his private shame, He will expose him even in the depths of his house.” And one day Ibn ʿUmar looked at the House and said: “How great you are and how great your sanctity, yet the believer is greater in sanctity before Allah than you.”"],[1872,"We were sitting at the door of the Prophet ﷺ, and he came out to us and said: \"Listen.\" We said: \"We have heard.\" He said: \"Listen.\" We said: \"We have heard.\" He said: \"Listen.\" We said: \"We have heard.\" He said: \"Indeed, there will be after me rulers, so do not confirm them in their lies and do not aid them in their oppression. For whoever confirms them in their lies and aids them in their oppression will not come to me at the Basin.\""],[1873,"Do not revile my Companions. By Him in whose hand is my soul, if one of you were to spend the like of Uhud in gold, he would not attain a mudd of one of them, nor half of it."],[1874,"Do not revile my Companions. By Him in whose hand is my soul, if one of you were to spend the like of Uhud in gold, he would not attain a mudd of one of them, nor half of it."],[1875,"“The Messenger of Allah ﷺ forbade buying silver for silver and gold for gold except equal for equal, and he commanded buying silver for gold however one wishes and gold for silver however one wishes.”"],[1876,"Some people used to sell silver vessels from war spoils for payment to be given at the time of the stipend. ‘Ubadah said: “The Messenger of Allah ﷺ forbade selling gold for gold, silver for silver, wheat for wheat, barley for barley, dates for dates, and salt for salt, except like for like, hand to hand. Whoever gives more or asks for more has committed riba.”"],[1877,"“Do not sell gold for gold except like for like, and do not give some of it in excess over other. And do not sell silver for silver except like for like, and do not give some of it in excess over other. And do not sell anything of them that is absent for something present.”"],[1878,"That a man told Ibn ‘Umar that Abu Sa‘id al-Khudri narrated this hadith from the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. Nafi‘ said: Ibn ‘Umar, that man, and I set out until we entered upon Abu Sa‘id al-Khudri. Ibn ‘Umar said to Abu Sa‘id: What do you think of a hadith this man told me that you narrate from the Messenger of Allah ﷺ? Did you hear it? Abu Sa‘id said: What is it? Ibn ‘Umar said: Selling gold for gold and silver for silver. Abu Sa‘id pointed with his finger to his eyes and his ears and said: My eyes saw and my ears heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: “Do not sell gold for gold except like for like, and do not give some of it in excess over other. And do not sell silver for silver except like for like, and do not give some of it in excess over other. And do not sell anything of them that is absent for something present.”"],[1879,"“Gold for gold, silver for silver, wheat for wheat, and barley for barley are like for like, hand to hand. But when these kinds differ, then sell however you wish, as long as it is hand to hand.”"],[1880,"I set out with one hundred dinars and met Talhah b. ‘Ubayd Allah in the shade of a wall. He bargained with me for them until his servant came from al-Ghabah. ‘Umar heard that, so he asked Talhah about it. He said: Dinars I wanted to buy until my servant comes from al-Ghabah. ‘Umar said: Do not part with him, do not part with him until you pay him. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Gold for silver is riba unless it is hand to hand; wheat for wheat is riba unless it is hand to hand; barley for barley is riba unless it is hand to hand; dates for dates is riba unless it is hand to hand.”"],[1882,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ forbade the sale of fruit until its ripeness appears."],[1883,"He forbade the sale of fruits until they become ripe. It was said, \"And what is ripeness?\" He said, \"Until they turn red.\" The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, \"Do you not see that if Allah prevents the fruit, for what would one of you take his brother's wealth?\""],[1884,"He forbade the sale of fruits until their ripeness appears; he forbade both the seller and the buyer."],[1885,"He forbade muhaqala, muzabana, and mukhabara, and the sale of palm trees until they color. Coloring is that they turn red or yellow or some of it is eaten."],[1886,"He forbade the sale of palm trees until they become ripe, the sale of grains until they harden, and the sale of grapes until they turn black."],[1887,"He forbade the sale of ears of grain until they whiten and are safe from blight; he forbade both the seller and the buyer."],[1888,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ was brought fresh ripe dates, while the dates of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ were of the ba‘l kind that had dryness in them. He said: “Where did you get this?” They said: We bought it for a sa‘ of our dates for two sa‘s. He said: “Do not do that. This is not permissible. But sell your dates, then buy from this what you need.”"],[1889,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ appointed a man over Khaybar, and he came to him with dates of excellent quality. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Are all your dates like this?” He said: No, by Allah, O Messenger of Allah. We take one sa‘ of this for two sa‘s, and two sa‘s for three. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Do not do that. Sell the mixed dates for dirhams, then buy excellent dates with the dirhams.”"],[1890,"A man brought the Messenger of Allah ﷺ some barni dates, and he said: What is this? He said: I bought it for a sa‘ for two sa‘s. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Oh! That is the essence of riba. Do not do it.” *"],[1891,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ forbade the sale of wala' and its gifting."],[1892,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ forbade the sale of wala' and its gifting."],[1893,"Wala' is a kin relationship like the kin relationship of lineage. It is not sold nor gifted."],[1894,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ entered the mosque, and a man entered and prayed. Then he came and sat down. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"Go back and pray, for you have not prayed.\" He did that three times. The man said: \"By the One who sent you with the truth, I do not know anything other than this, so teach me.\" He said: \"When you stand for prayer, say the takbir, then recite whatever is easy for you from the Quran, then bow until you are at ease in bowing, then rise until you are standing straight, then prostrate until you are at ease in prostration, then rise until you are sitting at ease. Do that throughout your prayer.\""],[1895,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ drew back the curtain while the people were in rows behind Abu Bakr and said, “O people, nothing remains of the glad tidings of prophethood except the true dream a Muslim sees or is seen for him.” Then he said, “Verily, I have been forbidden from reciting while bowing or prostrating. As for bowing, magnify the Lord therein; and as for prostration, strive in supplication, for it is likely to be answered for you.”"],[1897,"Whoever makes two sales in one sale, he is entitled to the lower of the two or riba."],[1898,"“He forbade selling an animal for an animal on credit.”"],[1899,"When the imam says 'Allah hears the one who praises Him,' then say: 'O Allah, our Lord, and to You be praise,' for whoever's saying coincides with the saying of the angels, his previous sins are forgiven."],[1900,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ prohibited two sales: mulamasa and munabadha."],[1902,"“The Messenger of Allah ﷺ forbade selling an unmeasured heap of dates whose measure is unknown for a specified measure of dates.”"],[1903,"He forbade muzabana and muhaqala."],[1904,"Narrated by Al-Qa'nabi, from Malik, from Abdullah bin Yazid, the Mawla of Al-Aswad bin Sufyan, from Zaid bin Abi 'Ayyash, from Saad bin Abi Waqqas, that he was asked about selling white animals for silver coins. He replied, \"I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ being asked about selling ripe dates for dried dates, and he said, 'Doesn't the dried date decrease in value when it becomes dry?' They replied, 'Yes.' He said, 'Then no.'\""],[1905,"He forbade muzabana, and muzabana is selling dates for dates by measure, and selling vines for raisins by measure.\""],[1906,"\"He forbade selling the fruit of palm trees for dried dates by measure, selling grapes for raisins by measure, and selling crops for wheat by measure.\""],[1907,"\"He forbade muzabana, muhaqala, and mu'awama, and he permitted 'araya.\""],[1908,"\"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ permitted the owner of an 'ariyya to sell it for its estimated amount of dried dates.\""],[1909,"\"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ permitted the sale of 'araya for less than five wasqs or five wasqs.\""],[1910,"Whoever buys food should not sell it until he takes full possession of it."],[1911,"Whoever purchases food should not sell it until he takes possession of it."],[1913,"Do not sell fruit until its ripeness appears; and whoever purchases food should not sell it until he takes possession of it."],[1914,"\"We used to buy food from troops of riders (i.e., the caravans) without knowing the amount, but the Messenger of Allah ﷺ forbade us to sell it until it had been delivered to us.\" (Using translation from Ibn Mājah 2229)"],[1915,"I said, 'O Messenger of Allah, I am a man who buys merchandise. What is lawful for me from it and what is unlawful for me?' He said, 'O son of my brother, when you purchase something, do not sell it until you take possession of it.'"],[1916,"A man from Syria came with oil, and I bargained with him as other merchants bargained until I bought it from him. Then a man came to me and offered me a profit until he satisfied me. I took his hand to strike it, but a man grabbed my forearm from behind. I turned and it was Zayd b. Thabit. He said to me, 'Do not sell it until you transfer it to your camp, for the Messenger of Allah ﷺ prohibited that.' So I withheld my hands."],[1917,"He forbade the sale of habl al-habalah."],[1918,"He forbade the sale of habl al-habalah. It was a sale that the people of the pre-Islamic era used to conduct. A man would buy a she-camel to be delivered when the she-camel gives birth, then when the one in her belly gives birth."],[1920,"He forbade intercepting goods until they reach the markets."],[1921,"He forbade intercepting and that a settled muhajir sell on behalf of a desert Arab."],[1922,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ forbade a settled person from selling on behalf of a desert dweller, and he said: “Do not intercept the goods being brought for sale.”"],[1923,"A settled person should not sell on behalf of a desert dweller. Leave the people, so that some of them may provide for others."],[1924,"A settled person should not sell on behalf of a desert dweller. Leave the people, that Allah may provide for some of them through others."],[1925,"When the imam says 'Allah hears the one who praises Him,' then say: 'O Allah, our Lord, and to You be praise,' for whoever's saying coincides with the saying of the angels, his previous sins are forgiven."],[1926,"None of you should sell over the sale of his brother, except with his permission."],[1927,"A Jew came at the time of the Prophet ﷺ with thirty loads of barley and dates, and set the price of a mudd equal to the Prophet's mudd. There was no food among the people on that day except his, and the people had been struck by hunger before that, such that they could find no food. So the people came to the Prophet ﷺ complaining to him about the high prices. He ascended the pulpit, praised Allah, and extolled Him, then said: “I will never meet Allah having given anyone from another's wealth without his consent. Selling is only by mutual consent, but in your transactions there are traits which I will mention to you: do not bear grudges, do not bid up prices against one another, do not envy one another, a man should not haggle over the price haggled by his brother, a settled person should not sell on behalf of a desert dweller, and selling is only by mutual consent. Be, O servants of Allah, brothers.”"],[1929,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ prohibited the sale of gharar (uncertainty/risk)."],[1930,"Ibn ʿUmar saw me playing with pebbles in prayer. When he finished, he rebuked me and said: \"Do as the Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to do.\" He said: \"When he sat in prayer, he placed his right palm on his right thigh, clenched all his fingers, and pointed with the finger next to the thumb. And he placed his left palm on his left thigh.\""],[1931,"He forbade muhaqalah, muzabanah, and mukhabarah, and [he forbade] selling dates until they begin to ripen — ishqah means that they turn red or yellow or that some of them become edible."],[1932,"The Prophet ﷺ forbade the stud fee of a stallion camel."],[1933,"He forbade the stud fee of a male animal."],[1934,"When one of you sells a milch camel or a sheep, he should not withhold its milk in the udder."],[1935,"Do not tie up the udders of camels and sheep. Whoever buys them after that has the choice between two options after he milks them: if he approves of them, he keeps them, and if he dislikes them, he returns them along with a saa' of dates."],[1936,"I saw food merchants being beaten at the time of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ when they bought food in bulk and sold it before bringing it to their campsite."],[1937,"\"He prohibited the price of blood and the price of a dog.\""],[1938,"I asked Jabir about the price of dogs and cats, and he said: \"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ forbade that.\""],[1939,"\"Indeed the dowry of a prostitute, the price of a dog and a cat, and the earnings of a cupper are from illicit gain.\""],[1940,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ forbade the price of a dog, the dower of an adulteress, and the payment of a soothsayer."],[1941,"\"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ forbade the devil's slaughter.\""],[1942,"\"He forbade picking up the lost property of pilgrims.\" Ibn Wahb said: \"The lost property of pilgrims should be left until its owner finds it.\""],[1943,"He forbade the meat of domestic donkeys on the day of Khaybar and permitted horse meat."],[1944,"“Allah and His Messenger forbid you to eat the flesh of domesticated donkeys, for it is filthy.” (Using translation from Ibn Mājah 3196)"],[1945,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ forbade eating domestic donkey on the day of Khaybar, and the people were in need of it."],[1946,"On the day of Khaybar we slaughtered horses, mules, and assess. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ forbade us (to eat) mules and asses, but he did not forbid horse-flesh. (Using translation from Abū Dāʾūd 3789)"],[1947,"He forbade mixing dates and raisins together."],[1948,"He forbade making nabidh from raisins and dates together, and from unripe dates and ripe dates together.\""],[1949,"He forbade mixing dates with unripe dates then drinking it; that was the main source of their intoxicants on the day wine was forbidden.\""],[1950,"\"Do not make nabidh from dates and raisins together, nor from unripe dates and dates together; make nabidh from each of them separately.\""],[1951,"I asked Ibn Abbas about green jars, white jars, and red jars. He said: The first to ask the Prophet ﷺ about this was the delegation of Abd al-Qays. He said: “Do not drink from gourds, vessels smeared with pitch, or hantam, and do not drink from jars. Drink from waterskins.” They said: What if it becomes strong in the waterskins? He said: “Even if it becomes strong in the waterskins, pour water on it.” They said: What if it becomes strong again? He said: “Then pour it out.” Then he said: “Allah, Mighty and Exalted, has forbidden me—or has forbidden—wine, gambling, and the kubah, and every intoxicant is forbidden.”"],[1952,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ was asked about al-bitʿ, and he said, 'Every drink that intoxicates is unlawful.'"],[1953,"While I was standing over the clan, being the youngest of them in age, over my paternal uncles, a man came and said, 'Wine has been forbidden.' I was standing over them serving them from a fadikh (a beverage made from unripe and ripe dates) of theirs. They said, 'Spill it,' so I spilled it.\" I said to Anas, 'What is it?' He said, 'Unripe dates and ripe dates.' Abu Bakr b. Anas said, 'It was their wine that day,' and Anas b. Malik did not object to that."],[1954,"The Prophet ﷺ sent him and Muʿādh b. Jabal to Yemen, and he said to them, 'Give glad tidings and make things easy, teach and do not repel, and cooperate.' When Muʿādh turned away, Abū Mūsā returned and said, 'O Messenger of Allah, they have a drink made from grapes that is cooked until it thickens, and al-mizr made from barley.' The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, 'Everything that intoxicates and distracts from prayer is unlawful.'"],[1955,"“He forbade al-shamma’ (wrapping oneself in a single garment with no way to bring out the hands) and that a man sit with his legs drawn up wrapped in a single garment.”"],[1956,"“The Messenger of Allah ﷺ forbade two ways of dressing: al-shamma’, which is to wrap oneself in a single garment, placing its two ends on one shoulder, leaving one side exposed; and the other, that a man sit with his legs drawn up wrapped in a single garment with nothing else on him, exposing his private parts to the sky.”"],[1957,"“Do not kill your children secretly, for killing by ghīla overtakes the rider and throws him from his horse.”"],[1958,"“I am your forerunner at the Pool, and I shall vie with the nations through you, so do not fight one another after me.”"],[1959,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ forbade restraining an animal."],[1960,"We raided with Abd al-Rahman b. Khalid b. al-Walid, and four infidels from the enemy were brought, and he ordered them to be killed by restraining them with arrows. That reached Abu Ayyub, and he said: 'I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ forbid killing by restraint. By the One in whose hand is my soul, if it were a chicken, I would not restrain it.' That reached Abd al-Rahman b. Khalid, and he freed four slaves."],[1961,"Do not take anything that has a soul as a target."],[1962,"A man said to ʿImrān b. Ḥuṣayn, “One of my slaves has run away, and I have vowed that if I catch him, I will cut off his hand.” He said, “Do not cut off his hand, for the Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to stand among us and command us to give charity and forbid us from mutilation.”"],[1963,"I heard the caller of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ on the day of Hunayn prohibiting plunder."],[1964,"Ali was brought people who had apostatized from Islam—or he said heretics—who had books with them, so he ordered a fire to be kindled and threw them into it with their books. That reached Ibn Abbas, and he said: As for me, if it were I, I would not have burned them, because of the Messenger of Allah's ﷺ prohibition, but I would have killed them, because of the Messenger of Allah's ﷺ saying: 'Do not punish with Allah's punishment.' And the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: 'Whoever changes his religion, kill him.'"],[1965,"Beware of wrongdoing, for wrongdoing will be darknesses on the Day of Resurrection. Beware of obscenity, for Allah does not love obscenity or indecency. Beware of miserliness, for it destroyed those before you: it commanded them to sever ties, so they severed their kinship ties; it commanded them to wickedness, so they committed wickedness; and it commanded them to stinginess, so they were stingy.” A man said, “O Messenger of Allah, which Islam is best?” He said, “That the Muslims be safe from your tongue and your hand.” He said, “O Messenger of Allah, which emigration is best?” He said, “That you abandon what your Lord dislikes.” He said, and the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, “Emigration is of two kinds: the emigration of the settled person and the emigration of the Bedouin. As for the Bedouin, he answers when called and obeys when commanded. As for the settled person, he is the greater of the two in trial and the greater of the two in reward.”"],[1966,"“Do not hate one another, do not envy one another, do not turn your backs on one another, and be, O servants of Allah, brothers. It is not lawful for a Muslim to desert his brother for more than three [days].”"],[1967,"It is not lawful for a Muslim man to boycott his brother for more than three nights. They meet, and this one turns away and that one turns away, and the better of them is the one who initiates the greeting of peace."],[1968,"“Beware of suspicion, for suspicion is the most false of speech. Do not spy, do not pry, do not envy one another, do not compete with one another for worldly gain, do not hate one another, do not turn your backs on one another, and be, O servants of Allah, brothers.”"],[1969,"The gates of Paradise are opened on Monday and Thursday, and every Muslim servant who does not associate anything with Allah is forgiven, except a man between whom and his brother there is enmity. It is said: Delay these two until they make peace."],[1970,"“The best of you and the best of your leaders are those whom you love and who love you, and you pray for them and they pray for you. The worst of you and the worst of your leaders are those whom you hate and who hate you, and you curse them and they curse you.” It was said, “Shall we not oppose them, O Messenger of Allah?” He said, “No, as long as they establish the five prayers. Indeed, whoever has a ruler and sees him committing an act of disobedience to Allah, let him hate the act of disobedience to Allah he commits and not withdraw his hand from obedience to him.”"],[1971,"“Let not the fear of people prevent any of you from speaking the truth when he sees it or knows it.”"],[1972,"Hudhayfah asked a village chief in al-Mada'in for water, and he brought him a drink in a silver vessel. Hudhayfah threw it at him. We were afraid to speak to Hudhayfah, but when his anger subsided, he said, \"I apologize to you for this. I had told him beforehand not to give me drink in this.\" Then he said, \"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ stood among us as a preacher and said, 'Do not drink from vessels of silver or gold, and do not wear silk or brocade, for these are for them in this world and for you in the Hereafter.'\""],[1973,"Uthman b. Maz'un wanted to practice celibacy, and the Messenger of God ﷺ forbade him from that. Sa'd said: \"Had the Messenger of God ﷺ permitted him that, we would have castrated ourselves.\""],[1974,"The Messenger of God ﷺ used to enjoin marriage and strictly forbid celibacy, saying: \"Marry the affectionate and prolific, for I will outnumber the prophets on the Day of Resurrection.\""],[1975,"Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, \"The evil eye is a fact,\" and he forbade tattooing. (Using translation from Bukhārī 5944)"],[1976,"\"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ came to us in the Majlis of Sa'd bin 'Ubadah and Bashir bin Sa'd said to him: 'Allah has commanded us to send Salah upon you, O Messenger of Allah; so how should we send salah upon you?' The Messenger of Allah ﷺ remained silent until we wished that he had not asked him. Then he said: 'Say: 'Alahumma salli 'ala Muhammad wa 'ala ali Muhammad, kama sallaita 'ala Ibrahima wa barik 'ala Muhammad kama barakta 'ala ali Ibrahim fil-'alamin, innaka hamidun majid (O Allah, send salah upon Muhammad and upon the family of Muhammad, as You sent salah upon the family of Ibrahim, and send blessings upon Muhammad and upon the family of Muhammad as You sent blessings upon the family of Ibrahim among the nations. You are indeed Worthy of praise, Full of glory.)\" And the salam is as you know.'\" (Using translation from Nasāʾī 1285)"],[1977,"That 'Abbas b. 'Abd Allah b. 'Abbas gave his daughter in marriage to 'Abd al-Rahman b. al-Hakam, and 'Abd al-Rahman gave him his daughter in marriage, and they had made them the dower. Mu'awiyah b. Abi Sufyan, while he was caliph, wrote to Marwan ordering him to separate them, and he said in his letter: 'This is shighar, which the Messenger of Allah ﷺ forbade.'"],[1978,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ mentioned Ramadan and said, 'Do not fast until you see the crescent and do not break the fast until you see it. If it is obscured for you, then estimate it.'"],[1979,"We were with 'Ammar b. Yasir on the day that was doubted whether it was from Ramadan, and a sheep was brought. Some of the people moved aside, so 'Ammar b. Yasir said, 'Whoever fasts this day has disobeyed Abu al-Qasim ﷺ.'"],[1980,"Do not practice continuous fasting. They said: You practice continuous fasting. He said: I am not like any of you; I am fed and given drink."],[1981,"Abu Huraira (Allah be pleased with him) reported that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ forbade fasting on these two days. 'Id-ul-Adha and 'Id-ul-Fitr. (Using translation from Muslim 1138)"],[1982,"He forbade urinating in stagnant water."],[1983,"None of you should urinate in standing water and then perform wudu' from it."],[1984,"None of you should perform ghusl in standing water while he is junub.\" They said, \"How should we do it, O Abu Hurayrah?\" He said, \"He should take from it with a scoop.\""],[1985,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ was asked about water and what comes to it from animals and wild beasts. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, \"If the water is two qullahs, nothing makes it impure.\""],[1986,"“A man should not look at the nakedness of a man, nor a woman at the nakedness of a woman; a man should not lie with a man under one cloth, nor a woman with a woman under one cloth.”"],[1987,"Beware of the two things that provoke curses.\" They said: \"What are the two things that provoke curses?\" He said: \"The one who relieves himself in people's paths and their courtyards.\""],[1988,"\"Two men should not sit together to relieve themselves while conversing, each of them seeing the private part of his companion, for Allah abhors that.\""],[1989,"\"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ forbade using the right hand for istinja.\""],[1990,"\"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ forbade a man to touch his private part with his right hand.\""],[1991,"He heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ saying: \"When any one of you wakes up from sleep, let him not touch his private parts with his right hand, nor clean himself with his right hand.\""],[1992,"\"I am to you like a father, teaching you. When you go to relieve yourselves, do not face the qiblah or turn your backs to it, and none of you should cleanse himself with his right hand.\" He used to command using three stones and forbid using dung and bones."],[1993,"I asked 'Alqamah, \"Did Ibn Mas'ud attend the Night of the Jinn with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ?\" 'Alqamah said, \"I asked Ibn Mas'ud, 'Did any of you attend the Night of the Jinn with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ?' He said, 'No, but we were with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ one night and lost him. We searched for him in the valleys and mountain passes and said, \"He has been taken up or assassinated.\" He said, \"We spent the worst night any people ever spent.\" When morning came, he came from the direction of Hira'. We said, \"O Messenger of Allah, we lost you and searched for you but did not find you, so we spent the worst night any people ever spent.\" He said, \"A caller from the jinn came to me, and I went with him and recited the Qur'an to them.\" He said, \"He took us and showed us their fires. They asked him for provision, so he said, 'You will have every bone upon which the name of Allah has been mentioned, falling into your hands with as much meat as possible, and every piece of dung as fodder for your animals.'\" The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, \"So do not cleanse yourselves with bones or dung, for they are the provision of your brothers among the jinn.\"\""],[1994,"Do not precede me in bowing or in prostration, for I have grown heavy, and whatever I precede you with when I bow, you will catch me with when I rise, and what I precede you with when I prostrate, you will catch me with when I rise."],[1995,"O people, I have grown heavy—or I have become heavy—so do not race me in bowing and prostration, but I will precede you; you will catch up with what you missed."],[1996,"The people should be led in prayer by the one most learned in the Book of Allah. If they are equal in recitation, then the one earliest in emigration. If they are equal in emigration, then the eldest. And no man should lead another in his house or in his tent, nor sit on his cushion except with his permission."],[1997,"The people should be led in prayer by the one among them most versed in the Book of Allah. If they are equal in recitation, then the most knowledgeable of them in the Sunnah. If they are equal in the Sunnah, then the one of them who made hijrah first. If they are equal in hijrah, then the oldest of them in age. And a man must not lead another man in prayer in his domain of authority, nor sit in his place of honor in his house without his permission."],[1998,"He forbade praying between graves."],[1999,"He forbade praying toward graves."],[2000,"Do not sit on graves and do not pray toward them."],[2001,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ forbade plastering graves."],[2003,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ forbade plastering graves and building over them or sitting on them."],[2004,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ forbade plastering graves, writing on them, building over them, and sitting on them."],[2006,"She bought a cushion with images on it. When the Messenger of Allah ﷺ saw it, he stood at the door and did not enter. I recognized dislike in his face. She said, \"O Messenger of Allah, I repent to Allah and His Messenger. What sin have I committed?\" The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, \"What is the matter with this cushion?\" She said, \"I bought it for you to sit on and use as a pillow.\" He said, \"The makers of these images will be punished on the Day of Resurrection, and it will be said to them: Bring to life what you have created.\" Then he said, \"Angels do not enter a house in which there are images.\""],[2007,"\"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ forbade eating any fanged predator and any taloned bird."],[2008,"He forbade eating any fanged predator.\""],[2009,"\"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ forbade that a woman be married in addition to her paternal aunt or in addition to her maternal aunt.\""],[2010,"\"A woman is not to be combined in marriage with her paternal aunt, nor a woman with her maternal aunt.\""],[2011,"\"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ forbade marrying a woman in addition to the paternal aunt and the maternal aunt. He said: 'If you do that, you sever your ties of kinship.'\""],[2012,"\"A woman is not to be married in addition to her paternal aunt, nor the paternal aunt in addition to her brother's daughter; and a woman is not to be married in addition to her maternal aunt, nor the maternal aunt in addition to her sister's daughter.\""],[2013,"\"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ forbade that a woman be married in addition to her paternal aunt, her maternal aunt, her brother's daughter, and her sister's daughter; and he forbade that the elder be married in addition to the younger, and the younger in addition to the elder.\""],[2014,"The Prophet of Allah ﷺ recited this verse: {It is He who sent down upon you the Book, wherein are verses clear that are the Mother of the Book, and others ambiguous} up to His saying {those of understanding}. She said: Then the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, \"When you see those who dispute in it, they are those whom Allah meant, so beware of them.\""],[2015,"\"None of you should make a man rise from his seat and then sit in it.\""],[2016,"\"We used to not know what to say in prayer until the Prophet ﷺ taught us to say, 'Peace be upon Allah, peace be upon Jibril, peace be upon Mika'il.' Then he taught us to say, 'The greetings are for Allah, and the prayers and good deeds. Peace be upon you, O Prophet, and the mercy of Allah and His blessings. Peace be upon us and upon the righteous servants of Allah.' Abu Wail reported in his hadith from Abdullah that the Prophet ﷺ said, 'When you say it, it reaches every righteous servant in the heavens and on the earth.' And Abu Ishaq reported in his hadith from Abdullah that the Prophet ﷺ said, 'When you say it, it reaches every near and distant servant, prophetic messenger, or righteous servant. I bear witness that there is no god but Allah, and I bear witness that Muhammad is His servant and messenger.'\""],[2017,"Do not single out the night of Friday for night prayer from among the nights, and do not single out the day of Friday for fasting from among the days."],[2018,"He used to supplicate in the prayer: 'O Allah, I seek refuge in You from the punishment of the Fire, and I seek refuge in You from the punishment of the grave, and I seek refuge in You from the trial of the false messiah, the Dajjal, and I seek refuge in You from the trial of life and death. O Allah, I seek refuge in You from sin and debt.' She said: Someone said, 'O Messenger of Allah, how often you seek refuge from debt!' The Prophet ﷺ said, 'When a man is in debt, he speaks and lies, and he promises and breaks his promise.'"],[2019,"When one of you strikes, let him avoid the face, for Allah created Adam in His image."],[2020,"Answer the one who invites, do not refuse a gift, and do not strike the Muslims."],[2021,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ saw a donkey branded on its face and disapproved of it. The man said, “By Allah, I will only brand it on the furthest part of the face.” So he ordered a donkey of his to be cauterized on its jāʿiratayn, and he was the first to cauterize the jāʿiratayn."],[2022,"A donkey passed by the Messenger of Allah ﷺ that had been cauterized on its face, its nostrils bleeding. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, “May Allah curse the one who did this.” Then he forbade cauterizing on the face and striking on the face."],[2023,"Preemption applies to every dwelling or walled garden. It is not lawful for him to sell until he offers it to his partner; if he wishes, he may take it, and if he wishes, he may leave it."],[2024,"Whoever has a partner in a dwelling or palm trees, he has no right to sell until he notifies his partner. If he is pleased, he may take it; if he dislikes it, he may leave it."],[2025,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, \"None of you should prevent his neighbor from fixing a peg on his wall.\""],[2026,"I was with Marwan b. al-Hakam when Abu Sa'id al-Khudri entered upon him. Marwan said to him, \"Did you hear the Messenger of Allah ﷺ forbidding blowing into the drink?\" Abu Sa'id said, \"Yes.\" A man said to him, \"O Messenger of Allah, I do not quench my thirst from one breath.\" The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, \"Then move the cup away from your mouth, then breathe.\" He said, \"I see a speck in it.\" He said, \"Then pour it out.\""],[2027,"\"When one of you drinks, let him not breathe into the vessel.\""],[2028,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ forbade drinking from a crack in a cup and blowing into a drink."],[2029,"He forbade a man from drinking from the mouth of a waterskin and from breathing into a vessel."],[2030,"“The Messenger of Allah ﷺ forbade tipping up water skins in order to drink from their mouths.” (Using translation from Ibn Mājah 3418)"],[2031,"\"Let none of you eat with his left hand or drink with his left hand, for Satan eats with his left hand and drinks with his left hand.\""],[2032,"He forbade a man from giving something with his left hand or taking with it, and he forbade breathing into the vessel when drinking.”"],[2033,"“Let none of you eat with his left hand or drink with it, for Satan eats with it and drinks with it.”"],[2034,"He saw a man throwing pebbles and said, \"Do not throw pebbles, for the Messenger of Allah ﷺ forbade pebble-throwing,\" or he said, \"he disliked pebble-throwing,\" and he said, \"No game is hunted with it and no enemy is struck with it, but it may break a tooth and put out an eye.\" Then he saw him throwing pebbles again and said, \"I tell you from the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and you still throw pebbles? I will not speak to you for such-and-such a time.\""],[2035,"\"The Messenger of Allah forbade (eating) animals that had been taken as targets, the milk of Al-Jallalah (animals that eat dung), and drinking directly from water skins.\" (Using translation from Nasāʾī 4448)"],[2036,"Do not hasten to greet the People of the Book with salam; and when you meet them on a road, force them to its narrowest side."],[2037,"A man among the companions of the Prophet ﷺ saw in a dream that he met a group of Jews and their appearance pleased him. He said, 'You are a people, were it not that you say Ezra is the son of God.' They said, 'And you are a people, were it not that you say, \"What God wills and Muhammad wills.\"' He said, 'And he met a group of Christians and their appearance pleased him. He said, \"You are a people, were it not that you say the Messiah is the son of God.\" They said, \"And you are a people, were it not that you say, 'What God wills and Muhammad wills.'\"' When morning came, he related that to the Prophet ﷺ, and the Prophet ﷺ said, 'I kept hearing it from you and it hurt me, so do not say, \"What God wills and Muhammad wills.\"'"],[2038,"I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: The wind comes from Allah's mercy. Salamah's version has: It is Allah's mercy; it (sometimes) brings blessing and (sometimes) brings punishment. So when you see it, do not revile it, but ask Allah for some of its good, and seek refuge in Allah from its evil. (Using translation from Abū Dāʾūd 5097)"],[2039,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ forbade that people's livestock be milked except with the permission of their owners. And he said: 'Would any of you like his storeroom to be approached, its door broken, and the food in it taken out? Indeed, the udders of their livestock are the food of one of them. So let me not know of anyone who milks the livestock of another without his permission.'"],[2040,"A man came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and said, “O Messenger of Allah, I have found a woman of beauty, but she does not bear children. Should I marry her?” He forbade him. Then he came a second time, and he forbade him. Then he came a third time, and he forbade him, and said, “Marry the loving, the prolific, for I will boast of your numbers.”"],[2041,"Did you hear from the Messenger of Allah ﷺ about the plague? Usama b. Zayd said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, \"The plague is a punishment that was sent upon the Children of Israel or upon those before you. When you hear of it in a land, do not go forward to it; and if it occurs in a land while you are there, do not leave fleeing from it.\""],[2042,"I am only human, and you bring disputes to me. Perhaps some of you are more eloquent in presenting his argument than others. Whoever I judge in his favor with something from his brother's right, I am only cutting off for him a piece of the Fire."],[2043,"I am only human, and you bring disputes to me. Perhaps some of you are more eloquent in presenting his argument than others, and I judge in his favor according to what I hear from him. Whoever I judge in his favor with something from his brother's right, let him not take anything from it, for I am only cutting off for him a piece of the Fire."],[2044,"The judge must not judge between two parties while he is angry."],[2045,"Whoever vows to obey Allah, let him obey Him; and whoever vows to disobey Allah, let him not disobey Him."],[2046,"“If you sell fruit to your brother and a blight strikes it, it is not lawful for you to take anything from him. Why would you take your brother’s wealth without right?”"],[2047,"I bought food from the food of the charity, and I made a profit on it before taking possession of it. Then I wanted to sell it, so I asked the Prophet ﷺ. He said, \"Do not sell it until you take possession of it.\""],[2048,"He said: \"Whoever buys food should not sell it until he takes full possession of it.\" He also forbade selling it until he moves it from its place or transfers it."],[2049,"A man said, 'O Messenger of Allah, what clothing should we wear when we enter ihram?' He said, 'Do not wear shirts, trousers, turbans, hooded cloaks, or leather socks, except if someone does not have sandals; then let him wear leather socks cut below the ankles. And do not wear any clothing that has been touched by saffron or wars.'"],[2050,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ sent al-Aslamī with eighteen sacrificial camels. He said, “O Messenger of Allah, what do you think if one of them becomes too exhausted for me?” He said, “Slaughter it, then dip its sandal in its blood, then strike its side with it, and do not eat from it—neither you nor anyone of your companions.”"],[2051,"When one of you prays, let him not spit in front of him nor to his right, but let him spit to his left or under his left foot."],[2052,"His sister was married to a man who divorced her, then he left her alone until her waiting period ended, then he came to propose to her. Ma'qil became angry about that and said, \"He left her alone while he was capable of her,\" and he prevented him from her. Then Allah revealed: {When you divorce women and they reach their term, do not prevent them from marrying their husbands when they agree among themselves with what is fair}."],[2053,"He asked 'A'isha about the saying of Allah: {If you fear that you will not deal justly with the orphans, then marry what is good to you from the women, two, three, or four}. She said, \"O son of my sister, this is the orphan girl who is in the care of her guardian, sharing his wealth with him. Her wealth and beauty please him, so her guardian wants to marry her without dealing justly in her dower, giving her the like of what someone else would give her. They were forbidden to marry them unless they deal justly with them, giving them the highest dower of their kind. They were commanded to marry other women who were good to them.\" 'Urwa said: 'A'isha said: Then the people asked about them after this verse, so Allah revealed: {They ask you about women. Say: Allah gives you a ruling about them and what is recited to you in the Book concerning the orphan women to whom you do not give what is written for them and you desire to marry them}. She said, \"And what Allah mentioned that is recited to you in the Book is the first verse in which He said: {If you fear that you will not deal justly with the orphans, then marry what is good to you from the women}.\" 'A'isha said, \"And Allah said in the other verse about the desire of one of you for his orphan girl who is in his care when she has little wealth and beauty, so they were forbidden to marry those women whose wealth and beauty they desired except with justice, because of their desire for them.\""],[2054,"ʿAmr b. al-ʿĀṣ came to the house of ʿAlī b. Abī Ṭālib looking for him but could not find him. Then he returned and found him. When he entered, he spoke with Fāṭimah. ʿAlī said to him, 'I see your need is only with the woman.' He said, 'Yes, the Messenger of Allah ﷺ forbade us to enter upon women whose husbands are absent.'"],[2055,"A group of men from Banū Hāshim entered upon Asmāʾ bt. ʿUmays, and Abū Bakr al-Ṣiddīq came in while she was his wife that day. He saw them and disliked that, and mentioned it to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, saying, 'I saw nothing but good.' The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, 'Allah has declared her innocent of that.' Then the Messenger of Allah ﷺ stood on the pulpit and said, 'After this day of mine, no man should enter upon a woman whose husband is absent unless accompanied by a man.'"],[2056,"ʿUmar b. al-Khaṭṭāb addressed us at al-Jābiyah and said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ stood in a place like this of mine and said, 'Be good to my Companions, then those who follow them, then lying will spread until a man swears an oath before being asked to swear it, and bears witness before being asked to bear witness. Whoever of you wants to attain the best of Paradise, let him keep to the community, for Satan is with the one and is farther from the two. Indeed, no man should be alone with a woman, for the third of them is Satan. Indeed, whoever among you is grieved by his evil deed and pleased by his good deed is a believer.'"],[2057,"Do not strike the maidservants of Allah. He said: The women became defiant and their behavior toward their husbands worsened. Umar b. al-Khattab said: 'The women have become defiant and their behavior toward their husbands has worsened since you forbade striking them.' The Prophet ﷺ said: 'Then strike them.' So the people struck their wives that night. Many women came complaining of the beating. In the morning, the Prophet ﷺ said: 'Seventy women went around the family of Muhammad last night, all complaining of beating. By Allah, you will not find those among the best of you.'"],[2058,"\"Indeed, Allah is not shy of the truth. Do not come to women in their posteriors.\""],[2059,"A man said, \"O Messenger of Allah, one of us emits a slight wind.\" He said, \"If one of you breaks wind, let him perform ablution, and do not come to women in their posteriors.\""],[2060,"\"Indeed, Allah is not shy of the truth. Do not come to women in their anuses.\""],[2061,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “When any one of you’s wife asks his permission to go to the mosque, he should not prevent her.” Bilāl b. ʿAbd Allāh b. ʿUmar said: “By Allah, we shall prevent them.” He said: Then ʿAbd Allāh b. ʿUmar reviled him with the worst abuse I ever heard him use, and said: “You heard me say that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: ‘When any one of you’s wife asks his permission to go to the mosque, he should not prevent her,’ and you say, ‘By Allah, we shall prevent them’?!”"],[2062,"“Do not prevent the female slaves of Allah from the mosques of Allah, and let them go out unperfumed.”"],[2063,"“When any one of you women attends the ʿishāʾ, she should not touch perfume.”"],[2064,"In the year of Khaybar, he forbade having sexual intercourse with pregnant women among the captives until they had given birth."],[2065,"Indeed, a man should not spend the night with a woman in a house unless he is married to her or is a close relative."],[2066,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ forbade the gold ring."],[2067,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ saw a gold ring on a man’s hand, so he removed it and threw it aside and said, “Would one of you take a live ember from the Fire and place it in his hand?” Then, after the Messenger of Allah ﷺ had gone, it was said to the man, “Take your ring and benefit from it.” He replied, “No, by Allah, I will never take it, after the Messenger of Allah ﷺ has thrown it aside.”"],[2068,"“The Messenger of Allah ﷺ forbade gold rings, qassī (silk garment), and maythara (saddle cushion).”"],[2069,"ʿUmar b. al-Khaṭṭāb saw a striped silk robe at the door of the mosque and said: “O Messenger of Allah, if only you would buy this and wear it on Fridays and for delegations when they come to you.” The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Only those who have no share in the Hereafter wear this.” Then some robes of that kind came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and he gave ʿUmar b. al-Khaṭṭāb one of them. ʿUmar said: “O Messenger of Allah, you have clothed me with it, yet you said about the robe of ʿUṭārid what you said.” The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “I did not clothe you with it for you to wear it.” So ʿUmar gave it as clothing to a polytheist brother of his in Makkah."],[2070,"A woman should not have close contact with another woman such that she describes her to her husband, or describes her to a man as if he is looking at her."],[2071,"A woman should not have close contact with another woman and then describe her to her husband until it is as if he is looking at her."],[2073,"I heard Mu'awiya while he was on the pulpit and in his hand was a lock of hair, saying: 'What is wrong with women who put something like this on their heads? I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: \"There is no woman who puts hair from someone else on her head except that it is falsity.\"'"],[2074,"Mu'awiya came to Madinah and addressed us. He took out a bundle of hair and said: 'I did not think anyone would do this except the Jews. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ heard of it and called it falsity.'"],[2075,"He heard Mu'awiya in the year of the Hajj while he was on the pulpit. He took a lock of hair that was in the hand of a guard and said: 'O people of Madinah, where are your scholars? I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ forbidding the like of this, and he said: \"The Children of Israel perished only when their women adopted this.\"'"],[2076,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ cursed the one who attaches hair extensions and the one who has them attached, and the one who tattoos and the one who has herself tattooed."],[2077,"A slave girl was given in marriage, then she fell ill and her hair fell out, so they wanted to attach hair to her hair. They mentioned that to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and he said: \"May Allah curse the one who attaches hair extensions and the one who has them attached and the one who asks for that.\""],[2078,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ prohibited a woman from attaching anything to her head."],[2079,"When the news of the death of Ja'far b. Abi Talib, Zayd b. Harithah, and 'Abd Allah b. Rawahah came, the Messenger of Allah ﷺ sat down and sadness was recognizable on his face. 'A'ishah said: 'And I was peeking from the crack of the door.' A man came to him and said: 'O Messenger of Allah, the women of Ja'far's family have been weeping excessively.' The Messenger of Allah ﷺ ordered him to forbid them. 'A'ishah said: 'So the man went, then came back and said: I forbade them, but they did not obey me.' This happened until the third time. She claimed that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: 'Throw dust into their mouths.' 'A'ishah said: 'So I said: May Allah rub your nose in the dust! You are not going to do what the Messenger of Allah ﷺ mentioned.'"],[2080,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ cursed the woman who scratches her face, tears her garment, and calls for woe."],[2081,"When the Messenger of Allah ﷺ arrived in Medina, he gathered the women of the Ansar in a house. Umar bin Al-Khattab sent for us, and he stood at the door and greeted us with peace. We returned the greeting to him, and then he said, \"I am the Messenger of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ to you.\" We said, \"Welcome to the Messenger of Allah and the Messenger of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ.\" He said, \"Will you pledge allegiance to me that you will not associate anything with Allah, and that you will not commit adultery or steal?\" We said, \"Yes.\" He then extended his hand from outside the house, and we extended our hands from inside the house. Then he said, \"O Allah, bear witness.\" She said, \"He commanded us to celebrate Eid, and that we should go out during menstruation and post-natal bleeding, and that Jumu'ah prayer is not obligatory upon us. He also forbade us from following funeral processions.\""],[2082,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ went out on the day of Aḍḥa or ʿĪd to the prayer ground and performed the prayer, then he left and stood up to address the people and commanded them with charity. He said, \"O people, give charity.\" Then he left and passed by the women and said, \"O group of women, give charity, for I have seen that you are the majority of the people of Hellfire.\" They asked, \"Why is that, O Messenger of Allah?\" He said, \"You curse frequently and are ungrateful to your husbands. I have not seen anyone more deficient in intelligence and religious commitment than you. A cautious wise man may be led astray by some of you.\" They asked, \"O Messenger of Allah, what is deficient in our intelligence and religious commitment?\" He said, \"Is not the testimony of a woman equivalent to half of that of a man?\" They replied in the affirmative. He said, \"This is due to the deficiency in her intelligence. Is it not true that when a woman menstruates, she does not pray nor fast?\" They replied in the affirmative. He said, \"This is due to the deficiency in her religion.\" Then the Messenger of Allah ﷺ left and when he reached his house, Zainab, the wife of Abdullah ibn Mas'ud sought permission to see him. They said, \"O Messenger of Allah, here is Zainab seeking permission to see you.\" He asked, \"Which Zainab?\" They replied, \"The wife of Abdullah ibn Mas'ud.\" He said, \"Grant her permission.\" So they allowed her to enter and she said, \"O Prophet of Allah, you commanded us today to give charity and I had adornments with me that I wanted to give in charity. However, Abdullah ibn Mas'ud and his children claim that they have more right to receive my charity.\" The Prophet ﷺ said, \"Give charity to Abdullah ibn Mas'ud and his children.\""],[2083,"\"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ cursed women who visit graves and those who take them as places of worship and put lanterns on them.\""],[2084,"It is not lawful for a woman who believes in Allah and the Last Day to mourn for a deceased person more than three days, except for a husband."],[2085,"It is not lawful for a woman who believes in Allah and the Last Day to mourn for a deceased person more than three days, except for a husband, for she mourns for him four months and ten days."],[2087,"It is not lawful for a woman who believes in Allah and the Last Day to mourn for a deceased person more than three nights, except for a husband, four months and ten days."],[2088,"I swear to Allah, I have no need for perfume other than that I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say, \"It is not permissible for a woman who believes in Allah and the Last Day to mourn for a dead person for more than three nights, except for her husband for four months and ten days.\" Zainab said, \"I entered upon Zainab bint Jahsh when her brother Abdullah ibn Jahsh died, and she called for perfume and applied it. Then she said, \"I swear to Allah, I have no need for perfume other than that I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say on the pulpit, \"It is not permissible for a woman who believes in Allah and the Last Day to mourn for a dead person for more than three nights, except for her husband for four months and ten days.\""],[2089,"It is not lawful for a woman who believes in Allah and the Last Day to mourn for a deceased person more than three days, except for a husband, for she mourns for him four months and ten days. She should not apply kohl, nor wear a dyed garment except a garment of `asb, nor touch perfume except at the least of her purification when she has bathed from her menses, a little of costus and azfar."],[2090,"The woman whose husband has died should not wear saffron-dyed garments, nor those dyed with red earth, nor jewelry, nor apply henna, nor apply kohl."],[2091,"Umm Salamah, the wife of the Prophet ﷺ, said to the Messenger of Allah when the lower garment was mentioned, \"And the woman, O Messenger of Allah?\" He said, \"She may let it down a handspan.\" Umm Salamah said, \"Then she would be uncovered.\" He said, \"Then a forearm's length, and she should not add to that.\""],[2092,"When the Prophet ﷺ performed Hajj with his wives, he said, \"This is only this Hajj; then keep to the backs of the mats.\""],[2093,"When the Messenger of Allah ﷺ raised from the last rak'ah of the morning prayer, he said: “O Allah, save al-Walīd b. al-Walīd, Salamah b. Hishām, and ʿAyyāsh b. Abī Rabīʿah. O Allah, tighten Your grip on Muḍar and make it upon them like the years of Yūsuf.”"],[2094,"A woman must not fast a day other than the month of Ramadan while her husband is present except with his permission."],[2095,"“A woman should not permit anyone in her husband’s house while he is present except with his permission.”"],[2096,"“It is not lawful for a woman to fast while her husband is present except with his permission, nor to allow a man into his house when he dislikes it. And whatever charity she gives, half of its reward is his. She was created from a rib.”"],[2097,"One should not combine in marriage a woman with her father's sister, or her mother's sister. (Using translation from Muslim 1408e)"],[2098,"A woman should not ask for the divorce of her sister to empty her plate; rather she should marry, for she has what is decreed for her."],[2099,"A woman should not ask for the divorce of her sister to empty her plate, for the Muslim woman is the sister of the Muslim woman."],[2100,"“In the time of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, women were commanded during the prayer not to raise their heads until the men had taken their seats on the ground, because of the tightness of the garments.”"],[2101,"He forbade prayer after 'Asr until the sun sets, and prayer after Fajr until the sun rises.\""],[2102,"\"There are two prayers after which there is no prayer: 'Asr until the sun sets, and Fajr until the sun rises.\""],[2103,"A man came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and said: O Messenger of Allah, which hour of the night and day do you command me not to pray in? The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"When you have prayed Fajr, refrain from praying until the sun has risen, for it rises between the two horns of a devil. Then prayer is witnessed, attended, and accepted until midday. When midday comes, refrain from praying until the sun has declined, for at that time Hell is stoked, and the intense heat is from the blaze of Hell. When the sun has declined, prayer is attended, witnessed, and accepted until you pray 'Asr. When you have prayed 'Asr, refrain from praying until the sun has set, for it sets between the two horns of a devil. Then prayer is witnessed, attended, and accepted until you pray Fajr.\""],[2104,"There are three times in which the Messenger of Allah ﷺ forbade us to pray and to bury our dead: when the sun begins to rise until it is high; when the sun is at its zenith until it declines; and when the sun declines for setting.\""],[2105,"\"O Banu 'Abd al-Muttalib, if you have any authority, let me not find any one of you preventing a person from praying at the House at any hour he wishes, whether night or day.\""],[2106,"Whoever forgets a prayer or sleeps through it should pray it when he remembers."],[2107,"Whoever catches one rak'ah of the morning prayer before the sun rises has caught the prayer, and whoever catches one rak'ah of the afternoon prayer before the sun sets has caught the prayer."],[2108,"There will be rulers who make prayer deficient and delay it until the time of the death throes. Whoever of you lives to see that, let him pray the prayer at its proper time and make his prayer with them supererogatory."],[2109,"Between every two calls to prayer there is a prayer for one who wishes. Between every two calls to prayer there is a prayer for one who wishes. Ibn Buraydah would pray two rak'ahs before the sunset prayer."],[2110,"\"Do not pray after 'Asr unless you pray while the sun is still high.\""],[2111,"He prayed the morning prayer with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, but he had not prayed the two rak'ahs of dawn. When the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said the salam, he stood up to pray the two rak'ahs of dawn while the Messenger of Allah ﷺ was watching him, and he did not disapprove of that."],[2112,"The Prophet ﷺ prayed a prayer, and when he finished, he noticed two men at the back of the people. He ordered them to be brought forward, and they came trembling. He asked them, \"What prevented you from praying with us?\" They said, \"O Prophet of Allah, we had already prayed in our dwellings and then came.\" The Prophet ﷺ said, \"If you have already prayed in your dwellings and then come upon a prayer, pray it, for it will be supererogatory for you.\""],[2113,"I witnessed the Hajj of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ with him, and I prayed the Fajr prayer with him in the mosque of al-Khayf in Mina. When he finished his prayer, there were two men at the back of the people who had not prayed. They were brought to him, their sides trembling. He said, “What prevented you two from praying with us?” They said, “O Messenger of Allah, we had already prayed in our dwellings.” He said, “Do not do that. If you have prayed in your dwellings, then come to a mosque where there is a congregation, pray with them, for it will be a supererogatory prayer for you.”"],[2114,"\"None of you should intentionally pray at sunrise or sunset.\""],[2115,"“When the sun’s edge appears, withhold from prayer until it is fully risen; and when the sun’s edge disappears, withhold from prayer until it has fully set.”"],[2116,"I asked ‘A’ishah about prayer after ‘Asr. She said, “Pray. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ only prohibited prayer when the sun rose.”"],[2117,"“Do not deliberately aim your prayer at sunrise or sunset, for it sets between the two horns of the devil.”"],[2118,"“There was no day that passed the Messenger of Allah ﷺ except that he prayed two rak‘ahs after ‘Asr.”"],[2119,"\"I heard Masruq and Al-Aswad say: We bear witness that 'Aishah said: 'When the Messenger of Allah ﷺ was with me after 'Asr, he would pray them (these two Rak'ahs).'\" (Using translation from Nasāʾī 576)"],[2120,"“Should they be beaten for them? The Messenger of Allah ﷺ never came to me except that he prayed them.”"],[2121,"“The Messenger of Allah ﷺ never abandoned the two rak‘ahs after ‘Asr in my house until he departed this world.”"],[2122,"\"When the Messenger of Allah peace be upon him was busy with the two units after Dhuhr prayers, he performed them after Asr.\""],[2123,"The Prophet ﷺ was brought some wealth after Zuhr, and he distributed it until he prayed ‘Asr. Then he entered ‘A’ishah’s apartment and prayed the two rak‘ahs after ‘Asr, and he said, “This wealth preoccupied me from the two rak‘ahs after Zuhr, and I did not pray them until now.”"],[2124,"Ibn ‘Abbas, ‘Abd al-Rahman b. al-Azhar, and al-Miswar b. Makhramah sent him to ‘A’ishah, saying: “Convey our greetings to her all together, and ask her about the two rak‘ahs after ‘Asr, for we have been told that she prays them, and we have heard that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ forbade them.” Ibn ‘Abbas said: “I used to beat people with ‘Umar b. al-Khattab for them.” Kurayb said: “I entered upon her and conveyed to her what they had sent me with to ‘A’ishah.”"],[2125,"\"He used to pray them before 'Asr, but if he got distracted or forgot them, he would pray them after 'Asr, and if he did a prayer he would be constant in it.\" (Using translation from Nasāʾī 578)"],[2126,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ performed Qunut in the ʿatamah prayer for a month, saying in his Qunut: “O Allah, save al-Walid b. al-Walid. O Allah, deliver Salamah b. Hisham. O Allah, deliver ʿAyyash b. Abi Rabiʿah. O Allah, deliver the weak among the believers. O Allah, tighten Your grip on Muḍar. O Allah, make it years upon them like the years of Yusuf.” Abu Hurayrah said: And one day the Messenger of Allah ﷺ entered the morning and did not supplicate for them, so I mentioned that to him, and he ﷺ said: “Do you not see that they have arrived?”"],[2127,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ prayed Asr, then entered my house and prayed two rak'ahs. I said: \"O Messenger of Allah, you prayed a prayer you did not used to pray.\" He said: \"Some wealth came to me and distracted me from two rak'ahs I used to pray before Asr, so I prayed them now.\" I said: \"O Messenger of Allah, should we make them up if we miss them?\" He said: \"No.\""],[2128,"“When one of you enters at night, let him not come upon his family unannounced.”"],[2129,"We were with the Prophet ﷺ on a raid, and when we arrived, he said: “Wait until the disheveled woman combs her hair and the one whose husband is absent shaves her pubic hair.”"],[2130,"He forbade saffron dye."],[2131,"He forbade a man from dyeing with saffron."],[2132,"“When the prayer is called, do not stand up until you see me.”"],[2133,"“When the prayer is called, do not stand up until you see me come out to you.”"],[2134,"I asked 'Abd Allah b. Ma'qil about sharecropping, and he said:"],[2136,"Ibn 'Umar set out and we set out with him until we entered upon Rafi' b. Khadij. Ibn 'Umar said to him, “I have been informed that you narrate from the Prophet of Allah ﷺ that he forbade leasing farmland.” He said, “Yes.” After that, whenever Ibn 'Umar was asked, he would say:"],[2137,"“The Messenger of Allah ﷺ did not make sharecropping unlawful, but he commanded people to be kind to one another.”"],[2138,"“We used to lease land, and the landowner would stipulate for himself what was on the water channels and the mouths of the irrigation canals, so this would perish and that would remain safe. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ forbade that.” Rafi' said, “As for renting for something guaranteed and fixed, there is no harm in it.”"],[2139,"“Land used to be leased for [the produce of] the water channels and some straw that was stipulated as an exception for the landowner, so the Messenger of Allah ﷺ forbade them from leasing land.” Rafi' said, “As for gold and silver, there is no harm in it.”"],[2140,"When one of us no longer needed his land and someone else needed it, he would let him farm it for one-third, one-fourth, or one-half [of the produce], and he would stipulate three irrigation canals and what the spring watered. We used to work it with hard labor using oxen and iron tools and other things, and we would get a share from it. Then Rafi' b. Khadij came to us and said, “The Messenger of Allah ﷺ has forbidden you from something that was beneficial to you regarding the haql — and haql means [sharecropping for] one-third or one-fourth. Whoever has land and does not need it, let him grant it to his brother or let him cultivate it. And he forbade you from muzabanah.”"],[2141,"Whoever has land, let him cultivate it. If he cannot cultivate it, let him grant it to his brother and not lease it to him."],[2142,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ fought the people of Khaybar until he drove them into their fortress. He gained control over the land, the crops, and the palm trees. They made peace with him on the condition that they would leave it, taking what their mounts could carry, and that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ would have the gold and silver, and they would depart from it. He stipulated that they should not conceal or hide anything; if they did, they would have no protection or safeguard. They hid a leather bag containing wealth and jewelry belonging to Huyayy b. Akhtab, which he had carried with him to Khaybar when the Nadir were expelled. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to Huyayy's uncle, 'What happened to Huyayy's leather bag that he brought from the Nadir?' He said, 'Expenses and wars consumed it.' He ﷺ said, 'The pact is recent, and the wealth is more than that.' The Messenger of Allah ﷺ handed him over to al-Zubayr b. al-Awwam, who inflicted punishment on him. Huyayy had previously entered a ruin, and he said, 'I saw Huyayy going around in a ruin here.' They went and searched and found the leather bag in a ruin. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ killed the two sons of Abu Huqayq, one of whom was the husband of Safiyyah bt. Huyayy b. Akhtab. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ took their women and children captive and divided their wealth because of the breach they had committed. He wanted to expel them from it, but they said, 'O Muhammad, let us remain in this land to cultivate it and tend to it.' The Messenger of Allah ﷺ and his companions had no servants to tend to it, and they were not free to do so. So he gave them Khaybar on the condition that they would have half of every crop, palm produce, and anything else, as the Messenger of Allah ﷺ saw fit."],[2143,"Whoever does not abandon sharecropping, let him give notice of war from Allah and His Messenger."],[2144,"We used to lease land during the time of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ in exchange for what grew on the water channels and what was irrigated by water from it. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ forbade us from that and allowed us to lease it for gold and silver."],[2145,"I saw the Messenger of Allah ﷺ take hold of the waist-wrapper of Sufyān b. Abī Suhayl and say: “O Sufyān, do not let your izār hang low, for Allah does not look at those who let their garments hang low.”"],[2146,"“Whoever drags his garments out of arrogance, Allah will not look at him on the Day of Resurrection.”"],[2147,"Whoever drags his garment out of pride, Allah will not look at him on the Day of Resurrection. Abu Bakr said, \"O Messenger of Allah, one side of my lower garment hangs loose unless I keep adjusting it.\" The Prophet ﷺ said to him, \"You are not one of those who do that out of pride.\""],[2148,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ forbade the sale of water."],[2149,"He forbade the sale of surplus water, with which pasture is withheld."],[2150,"We entered upon 'Abd Allah b. al-Harith b. Jaz' al-Zubaydi on a Friday. He called for a basin and said to the slave girl: \"Veil me.\" She veiled him and he urinated in it. Then he said: \"I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ forbidding one of you to urinate facing the Qiblah.\""],[2151,"When one of you goes to relieve himself, he should not face the Qiblah nor turn his back to it for defecation or urination, but rather face east or west."],[2152,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to forbid us to face the Qiblah or turn our backs to it with our private parts when we urinated. Then I saw him a year before his death urinating while facing the Qiblah."],[2153,"Some people say: When you sit to relieve yourself, do not face the Qiblah or Bayt al-Maqdis. I climbed onto the roof of our house and saw the Messenger of Allah ﷺ sitting on two bricks, facing Bayt al-Maqdis for his need."],[2154,"None of you should propose over the proposal of his brother.\""],[2155,"He forbade that a man bargain over the bargain of his brother, or propose over the proposal of his brother.\""],[2156,"Abu Amr b. Hafs divorced her irrevocably while he was absent in Syria. He sent his agent to her with barley, and she was displeased with it. He said, \"By God, you have no claim on us.\" She went to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and mentioned that to him, and he said, \"You are not entitled to maintenance from him.\" He ordered her to observe her waiting period in the house of Umm Sharik. Then he said, \"That is a woman whom my Companions visit. Observe your waiting period with Ibn Umm Maktum, for he is a blind man. When you become lawful, notify me.\" She said: When I became lawful, I mentioned to him that Muawiya b. Abi Sufyan and Abu Jahm had proposed to me. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, \"As for Abu Jahm, he does not put down his stick from his shoulder; and as for Muawiya, he is destitute, with no wealth. Marry Usama b. Zayd.\" She said: I disliked him. Then he said, \"Marry Usama.\" So I married him, and God put good in him, and I was pleased with him."],[2157,"A man should not bargain over the bargain of his brother until he buys or leaves, and he should not propose over the proposal of his brother until he marries or gives up.\""],[2158,"A man should not propose over the proposal of his brother until the first suitor leaves or gives him permission, then he may propose.\""],[2159,"Hafsa bt. Umar was widowed from Khunays b. Hudhafa al-Sahmi, a man among the Companions of the Prophet ﷺ who had witnessed Badr and died in Madinah. Umar said: I met Uthman b. Affan and offered Hafsa to him, saying, \"If you wish, I will marry you to Hafsa bt. Umar.\" He said, \"I will consider that.\" He said: I waited some nights, and he met me and said, \"I do not want to marry this day of mine.\" Umar said: I met Abu Bakr and said, \"If you wish, I will marry you to Hafsa bt. Umar.\" He said: He did not give me any reply, and I was more upset with him than with Uthman. I waited some nights, and then the Messenger of Allah ﷺ proposed to her to me, and I married her to him. Abu Bakr met me and said, \"Perhaps you felt something in yourself when you offered Hafsa to me and I did not give you any reply.\" He said: I said, \"Yes.\" He said: \"Nothing prevented me from giving you any reply when you offered her to me except that I had heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ mention her, and I would not divulge the secret of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. Had he left her, I would have married her.\""],[2160,"The people used to disperse from every direction, so the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"No one should depart until his last act is the circumambulation of the House.\""],[2161,"He granted a concession to the menstruating woman to depart when she menstruates. He said: And I heard Ibn 'Umar say: \"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ granted them a concession.\""],[2162,"I said: O Messenger of Allah, I do not think Safiyyah will be anything but a source of delay for us. He said: \"What is the matter with her?\" I said: She has menstruated. He said: \"Had she not performed the circumambulation before that?\" I said: Yes, but she has menstruated. He said: \"Then there is no delay for her; let her depart.\""],[2163,"While I was lying with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ under a velvet cloth, I began to menstruate. I slipped away and took my menstrual garments. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to me: 'Have you started menstruating?' I said: 'Yes.' He called me, and I lay with him under the velvet cloth."],[2164,"We were with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ on a military expedition when he passed by a slain woman with people gathered around her. He said: 'This one was not one to fight. Catch up with Khalid and tell him: Do not kill children or laborers.'"],[2165,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ saw, on one of his journeys, a slain woman, and he forbade killing women and children."],[2166,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ was asked about the children of the polytheists' homes being raided at night while women and children were among them. He said: 'They are of them.'"],[2167,"I asked the Messenger of Allah ﷺ about the children of the polytheists, whether we should kill them along with them. He said: 'Yes, for they are of them.' Then he forbade it on the day of Hunayn."],[2168,"We were with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ on a military expedition, and Khalid b. al-Walid was at the head of the people. Suddenly, there was a slain woman on the road. They began to marvel at her appearance; the vanguard had struck her. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ came and stood over her and said: 'Ha! This one was not one to fight.' Then he said: 'Catch up with Khalid and tell him: Do not kill children or laborers.'"],[2169,"Whoever is killed defending his property is a martyr, and whoever wrongfully takes a span of land will be made to wear it as a collar from seven earths."],[2170,"He forbade wearing silk, wearing gold rings, and drinking from ḥanātim."],[2171,"I prohibited you from visiting graves, but now visit them; and I prohibited you from keeping the meat of sacrificial animals beyond three days, so keep what seems right to you; and I prohibited you from nabidh unless in a water-skin, so drink, but do not drink any intoxicant."],[2172,"He used to say on the pulpit: “I declare inviolable the wealth of the two weak ones: the orphan and the woman.”"],[2173,"“O Abu Dharr, indeed I see you as weak, and indeed I love for you what I love for myself: do not take charge of an orphan's wealth, and do not seek command over two people.”"],[2174,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ forbade the muhrim to wear a garment dyed with saffron or wars."],[2175,"“Let not the fear of people prevent any of you from speaking the truth when he sees it.”"],[2176,"I came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and said, 'O Messenger of Allah, we are people from the desert, so teach us something through which Allah may benefit us.' He said, 'Do not deem any good deed insignificant, even if it is pouring from your bucket into the vessel of one seeking water, or speaking to your brother with a cheerful face. Beware of letting your lower garment drag, for it is from arrogance, and Allah does not love it. If a man insults you with something he knows about you, do not insult him with something you know about him, for the reward is yours and the burden is upon the one who said it.'"],[2177,"The Prophet ﷺ took silk and placed it in his right hand, and gold and placed it in his left hand. Then he raised his hand and said: “These two are forbidden for the males of my community.”"],[2178,"A silk garment was gifted to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. He wore it, then prayed in it, then after finishing he removed it forcefully, as if disliking it, and said: “This is not appropriate for the righteous.”"],[2179,"Regarding silk, he said: “Whoever wears it in this world will not wear it in the Hereafter.”"],[2180,"“The Prophet of Allah ﷺ forbade wearing silk except for the area of two, three, or four fingers.”"],[2181,"“The Prophet ﷺ permitted ‘Abd al-Rahman b. ‘Awf and al-Zubayr b. al-‘Awwam to wear silk because of an itch that they had.”"],[2182,"O Banu Abd Manaf, do not prevent anyone from circumambulating this House and praying at whatever hour he wishes, whether night or day."],[2183,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ forbade me from reciting while bowing and prostrating."],[2184,"Jabir reported that Messenger of Allah ﷺ forbade that a man should eat with the left hand or walk with one sandal or wrap himself completely leaving no opening for the arms (to draw out) or support himself when sitting with a single garment wrapped round his knees which may expose his private parts. (Using translation from Muslim 2099a)"],[2185,"\"Whoever believes in Allah and the Last Day, let him honor his neighbor. Whoever believes in Allah and the Last Day, let him say good or remain silent. Whoever believes in Allah and the Last Day, let him honor his guest. His ja'izah is a day and a night, and hospitality is three days. Whatever is beyond that is charity. It is not lawful for him to stay with him until he causes him embarrassment.\""],[2186,"Abu Quhafah was brought on the day of the conquest of Makkah, and his head and beard were white like the thaghamah plant. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, «Change his head and avoid black.»"],[2187,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ passed while performing tawaf around the Kaaba and came upon a man leading another man by a nose ring in his nose; the Prophet ﷺ cut it with his hand and then ordered him to lead him by his hand."],[2188,"The Prophet ﷺ passed while performing tawaf around the Kaaba and came upon a man who had tied his hand to another man with a strap or a string or something else; the Prophet ﷺ cut it and said: \"Lead him by his hand.\""],[2189,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to him: “O 'Ali, you have a treasure, and you are the owner of its two horns. Do not follow a look with another look, for the first is yours but the second is not.”"],[2190,"“The Prophet of Allah ﷺ forbade me from qassi (a type of silk garment), from riding on mayathir (saddle cushions), and from wearing a ring on the index or middle finger.”"],[2191,"“The Messenger of Allah ﷺ forbade wearing qassī and safflower-dyed garments, wearing gold rings, and reciting while bowing.”"],[2192,"When the verse {When the believing women come to you to give you their pledge} up to His saying {and they do not disobey you in what is right} was revealed, she said, 'Part of that was wailing.' I said, 'O Messenger of Allah, except the family of so-and-so, for they helped me in wailing during Jahiliyyah, and I must help them in return.' He said, 'Except the family of so-and-so.'"],[2193,"The Prophet ﷺ took a pledge from the women when they gave him their allegiance that they would not wail. They said, 'O Messenger of Allah, there are women who helped us in wailing during Jahiliyyah; shall we help them in Islam?' The Prophet ﷺ said, 'There is no helping in wailing in Islam, and no shighar marriage in Islam, and no hamstringing of animals in Islam, and no jalab and no janab, and whoever plunders is not one of us.'"],[2194,"When Naiy is said to have come, Mayers and Abdullah bin Rawaha Allah's Messenger (saw) sat with sadness recognized in his face. Then a man came to him and said, \"These are the women of Mayer's, crying over him, and they have increased their weeping.\" He ordered him to stop them, so he stayed there for a while and then returned and mentioned that he ordered them to stop. They refused to obey him, so he ordered him for the second time to stop them. He mentioned that they had defeated him. He said, \"Scold them in their faces with dust.\""],[2195,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ came to visit me in the year of the Farewell Pilgrimage because of an illness that had become severe for me. I said: O Messenger of Allah, the illness has reached me to the extent you see, and I am a man of wealth, and no one will inherit from me except a daughter of mine. Should I give two-thirds of my wealth as charity? He said: No. I said: Then half? He said: No. Then he said: A third, and a third is much or great. If you leave your heirs rich, it is better than leaving them poor, begging from people. You will not spend any expenditure seeking thereby the face of Allah except that you will be rewarded for it, even what you put in your wife's mouth. I said: O Messenger of Allah, will I be left behind after my companions? He said: You will not be left behind and do a righteous deed seeking thereby the face of Allah except that you will increase in degree and elevation. Perhaps you will be left behind until some people benefit by you and others are harmed by you. O Allah, complete the emigration of my companions and do not turn them back on their heels. But the miserable one is Sa'd b. Khawlah. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ mourned for him that he died in Makkah."],[2196,"He used to turn away to his right."],[2197,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ forbade the delegation of Abd al-Qays from nabidh in gourds, green jars, pitch-coated vessels, hollowed stumps, and water-skins cut open at the mouth. And he said: 'Make nabidh in your water-skin, tie its mouth, and drink it sweet and pleasant.' A man said, 'O Messenger of Allah, permit me in the like of this,' and al-Nadr gestured with his palm. He said, 'Then you would make it like this,' and al-Nadr gestured with the length of his arm."],[2198,"Do not enter upon women. A man from the Anṣār said, 'What about the brother-in-law, O Messenger of Allah?' The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, 'The brother-in-law is death.'"],[2199,"\"Do not sit with the people of qadar (divine decree), nor engage them in discussion.\""],[2200,"The strong believer is more beloved to God than the weak believer, and in each there is good. Be eager for what benefits you, and do not be helpless. If something overwhelms you, then say, 'God's decree and what He wills.' Beware of 'if only,' for 'if only' opens the work of Satan."],[2201,"The strong believer is better and more beloved to God than the weak believer, and in each there is good. Be eager for what benefits you, and seek help from God, and do not be helpless. If something afflicts you, do not say, 'If only I had done such and such,' but say, 'God's decree and what He wills He does,' for 'if only' opens the work of Satan."],[2202,"Do not accompany anyone but a believer, and let no one eat your food but a pious person."],[2203,"He used to prevent his family from wearing ornaments and silk, saying: \"If you love the ornaments and silk of Paradise, do not wear them in this world.\""],[2204,"I said to al-Hasan b. 'Ali: Narrate to me something you memorized from the Messenger of Allah ﷺ that no one else narrated to you. He said: He said: I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: 'Leave what causes you doubt for what does not cause you doubt.' He said: 'Goodness is tranquility, and evil is doubt.'"],[2205,"“Ride these animals while they are sound, and do not take them as chairs.”"],[2206,"The men asked the Messenger of Allah ﷺ for permission to strike women, and he gave them permission. So they struck them. That night he heard a loud sound and said, 'What is this?' They said, 'You permitted men to strike women, so they struck them.' So he forbade them and said, 'The best of you are those who are best to their families, and I am the best of you to my family.'"],[2207,"Do not acquire estates, lest you become desirous of the world."],[2208,"I saw ‘Uthman sitting in the gathering place. He called for water for ablution and performed ablution, then said, “I saw the Messenger of Allah ﷺ in this seat of mine perform ablution like my ablution, then the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, ‘Whoever performs ablution like my ablution will have his past sins forgiven.’” Then the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, “And do not be deluded.”"],[2209,"Abū Hurayrah saw a man leaving the mosque after the muezzin had called the adhān, and he said, ‘As for this one, he has disobeyed Abu al-Qāsim ﷺ.’"],[2210,"The Prophet ﷺ saw a man supplicating with both fingers together, so he forbade him and said, \"With one of them, with the right one.\""],[2211,"Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, \"Do not withhold the superfluous water, for that will prevent people from grazing their cattle.\" (Using translation from Bukhārī 2353)"],[2213,"«It is not fitting for a servant to say: I am better than Jonah son of Matta.»"],[2214,"«Do not extol me as the Christians extolled Jesus son of Mary. Indeed I am only a servant, so say: The servant of Allah and His Messenger.»"],[2215,"A man said to the Prophet ﷺ, “O the best of us and the son of the best of us, O our master and the son of our master.” The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, “O people, speak with your normal words, and do not let Satan lead you astray. I am the servant of Allah and His Messenger.”"],[2216,"“It is not appropriate for a servant to say, ‘I am better than Yunus b. Matta.’” He attributed him to his father."],[2217,"“Allah chose Kinanah from the descendants of Isma'il, chose Quraysh from Kinanah, chose Banu Hashim from Quraysh, and chose me from Banu Hashim. Thus I am the master of the children of Adam, without boasting. I will be the first from whom the earth will split open, the first intercessor, and the first whose intercession will be accepted.”"],[2218,"Abu Bashir Al Ansari said that he was with the Apostle of Allaah ﷺ on one of his journeys. The Apostle of Allaah ﷺsent a messenger. The narrator ‘Abd Allah bin Abu Bakr said “I think he said while the people were sleeping. No necklace of bowstring or anything else must be left on a Camels’ neck, must be cut off. The narrator Malik said “I think this was due to evil eye.” (Using translation from Abū Dāʾūd 2552)"],[2219,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ commanded that the bells be cut from the necks of the camels on the day of Badr."],[2220,"The caravan that has a bell is not accompanied by the angels."],[2221,"Do not swear by your fathers, nor by your mothers, nor by the rivals [to Allah], and do not swear except by Allah, and do not swear unless you are truthful."],[2222,"None of you should urinate in standing water that does not flow and then perform ghusl from it."],[2223,"The Prophet of Allah ﷺ forbade us from naming our slaves with four names: Aflah, Rabah, Yasar, and Nafi'."],[2224,"Leave me with what I have left you, for those before you were destroyed only by their questioning and their disagreement with their prophets. So when I forbid you from something, avoid it, and when I command you with something, do of it what you are able."],[2225,"The Prophet ﷺ heard sounds and said: What are these sounds? They said: They are pollinating date palms. He said: If they did not do so, it would be fine. So they stopped and did not pollinate most of them, and it became stunted. That was mentioned to the Prophet ﷺ, and he said: If something pertains to your worldly affairs, it is your concern, and if something pertains to your religious affairs, then to me."],[2228,"A muhrim's camel threw him and broke his neck, killing him. He was brought to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, who said, 'Wash him and shroud him, but do not cover his head or bring perfume near him, for he will be raised reciting the talbiyah.'"],[2229,"A man's camel threw him and broke his neck while he was in ihram. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, 'Clothe him in two garments, wash him with water and lote-tree leaves, and do not cover his head, for Allah will raise him on the Day of Resurrection reciting the talbiyah.'"],[2230,"A man was in ihram with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ when his camel threw him and broke his neck, and he died. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, 'Wash him with water and lote-tree leaves, shroud him in his two garments, do not cover his head, and do not touch him with perfume, for he will be raised on the Day of Resurrection reciting the talbiyah.'"],[2231,"A man came on a camel while he was in ihram, and it threw him and broke his neck, and he died. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ ordered that he be washed with water and lote-tree leaves, shrouded in his two garments, not touched with perfume, and that his face and head not be covered."],[2232,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ prayed, and a man said, “Who will call for the red camel?” The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, “May you not find it! Mosques were built only for what they were built for.”"],[2233,"Ubayy saw a man consoling himself with the consolation of Jahiliyyah, so he cursed him with an explicit obscenity—though he did not (actually) do so—then said, 'I can see in yourselves, or in yourself, that I could not help but say it when I heard it. I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: Whoever consoles himself with the consolation of Jahiliyyah, curse him with an explicit obscenity and do not use a euphemism.'"],[2234,"I heard the Messenger of Allah (May peace be upon him) as saying; if anyone hears a man crying out in the mosque about something he has lost, he should say: May Allah not restore it to you, for the mosque were not built for this. (Using translation from Abū Dāʾūd 473)"],[2235,"«When you see a man buying and selling in the mosque, say: 'May Allah not make your trade profitable.'»"],[2236,"Whoever hangs an amulet, may Allah not fulfill for him, and whoever hangs a seashell, may Allah not leave him in peace."],[2237,"Do not practice continuous fasting. They said: But you practice continuous fasting, O Messenger of Allah. He said: I am not like any of you; my Lord feeds me and gives me drink."],[2238,"\"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ shunned* us after the late 'Isha prayer.\""],[2239,"“The Messenger of Allah ﷺ prohibited sleeping before it and talking after it.”"],[2240,"\"Usayd b. Hudayr and another man from the Ansar talked with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ one night until a period of the night passed, in a night of intense darkness. Then they left the Prophet ﷺ to return, each of them holding his staff. The staff of one of them lit up for them so that they walked in its light. When the road separated them, the staff of the other lit up, and each of them walked in its light until he reached his family.\""],[2241,"\"Abbad b. Bishr and Usayd b. Hudayr left the Messenger of Allah ﷺ on a dark, pitch-black night, each of them having a staff. The staff of one of them lit up as brightly as possible, and when they parted, the staff of each of them lit up.\""],[2242,"We waited for the Prophet ﷺ one night until the middle of the night came. He came and prayed with us, then gave us a sermon and said: \"Indeed, the people have prayed and slept, but you will continue to be in prayer as long as you have been waiting for the prayer.\""],[2243,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ would continue to converse at night in Abu Bakr's house about matters concerning the Muslims. One night he conversed with him while I was with him."],[2244,"Whoever fasts the entire time, Hell will be constricted for him like this, and he clasped ninety."],[2245,"\"The blood of a Muslim man who bears witness that there is no god but Allah and that I am the Messenger of Allah is not lawful except for one of three: the previously married adulterer, a life for a life, and the one who abandons his religion and leaves the community.\""],[2246,"The Prophet ﷺ said: \"The nations were presented to me, and I saw my nation, and I was amazed by their countless number and their appearance, as they filled the plains and mountains. Then Allah said, 'O Muhammad, are you pleased?' I said, 'Yes, my Lord.' Allah said, 'With them are also seventy thousand who will enter Paradise without being held accountable. They are those who do not seek omens, do not burn themselves with branding, and do not seek blessings through the performance of actions. Rather, they put their trust in their Lord.' Ukkashah said, 'O Allah, make me one of them.' Allah replied, 'You are one of them.' Then another man said, 'O Allah, make me one of them.' Allah said, 'Ukkashah has preceded you in asking for that.'\""],[2247,"\"I entered upon Al-Bara' bin 'Azib and I heard him say, 'The Messenger of Allah ﷺ forbade us from seven things: gold rings, precious stones, wearing fine striped silk, wearing silk, wearing garments dyed with saffron, drinking from silver vessels.'\""],[2248,"If you find only sheep pens and camel resting places, pray in the sheep pens and do not pray in the camel resting places."],[2249,"It was said to ʿUmar b. al-Khaṭṭāb, 'Tell us about the affair of the hardship.' He said, 'We went out to Tabūk in intense heat. We stopped at a place where we were struck by such thirst that we thought our necks would snap. A man would go looking for water and not return until we thought his neck would snap. A man would even slaughter his camel, squeeze its undigested stomach contents and drink it, and put what remained on his liver. Abū Bakr al-Ṣiddīq said, \"O Messenger of Allah, Allah has accustomed you to good in supplication, so supplicate for us.\" He said, \"Would you like that?\" He said, \"Yes.\" He said, so he raised his hands ﷺ and did not lower them until a cloud overshadowed us and poured down. They filled what they had with them, then we went to look and did not find it beyond the army.'"],[2250,"A group of Bedouins from 'Urayna came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and found the climate of Madinah unsuitable. So he ordered them to drink from the milk and urine of camels, and they drank until they became well. Then they killed the shepherds and drove off the camels. The Prophet of Allah ﷺ sent after them, and they were brought back. He cut off their hands and feet and branded their eyes."],[2251,"Eight men from 'Ukl came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and pledged allegiance to him upon Islam. They found the land unhealthy and their bodies became ill. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"Will you not go out with our shepherd among his camels and get some of their milk and urine?\" They said yes. So they went out, drank their milk and urine, and regained health. Then they killed the shepherd of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and drove away the livestock. That reached the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and he sent pursuers after them. They were brought back, and the Messenger of Allah ﷺ ordered them; he cut off their hands and feet, blinded their eyes with heated iron, and cast them into the sun until they died."],[2252,"Eight men from 'Ukl came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. They found the climate of Madinah unhealthy. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ ordered them to go to the camels of zakah and drink their milk and urine. They did so, then they killed the shepherd and drove away the camels. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ sent trackers in pursuit of them. They were brought back, and he cut off their hands and feet, blinded their eyes with heated iron, and left them without cauterizing."],[2253,"A group from 'Ukl—or he said 'Uraynah, and I do not think he said other than 'Ukl—arrived in Madinah. The Prophet ﷺ ordered milch camels for them and told them to go out and drink their urine and milk. They drank until they recovered, then they killed the shepherd and drove away the livestock. The Prophet ﷺ learned of it in the morning and sent pursuers after them. By the time the day had fully risen, they were brought back. He ordered them and cut off their hands and feet, blinded their eyes with heated iron, and threw them onto the harrah, asking for water but not given any. Abu Qilabah said: \"These are people who stole, killed, disbelieved after their faith, and waged war against Allah and His Messenger.\""],[2254,"People from 'Ukl and 'Uraynah came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and spoke words of Islam. They said: \"O Prophet of Allah, we were people of livestock, not of farmland,\" and they found Madinah unhealthy. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ ordered a small herd and a shepherd for them, and told them to go out and drink its urine and milk. They went until they were at the edge of the harrah, then they disbelieved after their Islam, killed the shepherd of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and drove away the small herd. That reached the Prophet ﷺ, and he sent pursuers after them. They were brought back, and he blinded their eyes with heated iron, cut off their hands and feet, then left them at the edge of the harrah until they died in that condition."],[2255,"Do not cut off his hand, for the Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to stand among us commanding charity and forbidding mutilation."],[2256,"The Prophet ﷺ blinded their eyes only because they had blinded the eyes of the shepherds."],[2257,"Suwayd b. Tariq asked the Messenger of Allah ﷺ about wine and said, \"We make it.\" The Messenger of Allah ﷺ forbade him from that. He said, \"O Messenger of Allah, it is a medicine.\" He ﷺ said, \"It is not a medicine, but a disease.\""],[2258,"A daughter of mine was ill, so I brewed for her in a jug. The Prophet ﷺ entered while it was boiling and asked, \"What is this?\" She said, \"My daughter is ill, so we brewed this for her.\" He ﷺ said, \"Allah has not placed your cure in what is unlawful.\""],[2259,"Pray in the sheep pens and do not pray in the camel resting places, for they were created from devils."],[2260,"On the back of every camel there is a devil, so when you ride them, mention Allah’s name and do not neglect your needs."],[2261,"Congregational prayer is superior to the prayer of one alone by twenty-seven degrees."],[2262,"He forbade a man from performing ablution with the leftover water of a woman's ablution."],[2263,"One of the Prophet's ﷺ wives bathed in a large bowl. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ wanted to perform ablution from it, so she said: \"O Messenger of Allah, I was in a state of major ritual impurity.\" He said: \"Water does not become impure.\""],[2264,"\"I heard Al-Qasim narrating that 'Aishah said: 'I used to perform Ghusl, the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and I from a single vessel, from Janabah.'\" (Using translation from Nasāʾī 233)"],[2265,"He saw the Prophet ﷺ and his Companions purifying themselves, men and women, from a single vessel, all of them purifying themselves from it."],[2266,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ rebuked against drinking while standing."],[2267,"If the one who drinks while standing knew what was in his stomach, he would vomit."],[2268,"We used to eat while walking and drink while standing in the time of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ."],[2269,"We prayed the noon prayer with 'Ali, then we went out to the open area. He called for a vessel containing a drink. He took it, rinsed his mouth, sniffed water, wiped his face, forearms, head, and feet, then drank what was left while standing. Then he said: “Some people dislike drinking while standing. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ did the same as I have done, and said: ‘This is the ablution of one who has not broken his wudu.’”"],[2270,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to Ka'b b. 'Ujra, 'When you perform ablution and enter the mosque, do not interlace your fingers.'"],[2271,"The Prophet ﷺ said to him, “O Ka'b b. 'Ujrah, when you perform ablution and do it well, then go out to the mosque, do not interlace your fingers, for you are in prayer.”"],[2272,"Ka'b b. 'Ujrah caught up with him while he was heading to the mosque. He said: He found me interlacing my fingers, one hand with the other. He said: He separated my hands and forbade me from that, saying: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"When one of you performs ablution and does it well, then goes out intending to go to the mosque, let him not interlace his fingers, for he is in prayer.\""],[2273,"When the Messenger of Allah ﷺ returned from the battle of Hunayn, he traveled through the night until sleepiness overtook him, and he halted for rest. He said to Bilāl, ‘Watch the night for us.’ Bilāl prayed as much as was decreed for him, and the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and his companions slept. When dawn approached, Bilāl leaned against his mount facing the dawn, but sleep overcame Bilāl as he leaned against his mount. Neither the Messenger of Allah ﷺ nor Bilāl nor any of his companions woke until the sun struck them. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ was the first to wake, and he was startled. He said, ‘O Bilāl!’ Bilāl said, ‘May my father be your ransom, O Messenger of Allah, the same thing seized me as seized you.’ He said, ‘Lead your mounts.’ Then the Messenger of Allah ﷺ performed ablution, ordered Bilāl, and he called the iqāmah. He said, ‘Whoever forgets a prayer or sleeps through it, let him pray it when he remembers it, for Allah, blessed and exalted, said: {Establish prayer for My remembrance}.’"],[2274,"The Prophet ﷺ was standing in al-Baqi' when a man called out to another, 'O Abu al-Qasim!' The Prophet ﷺ turned, and he said, 'I did not mean you, O Messenger of Allah; I only called so-and-so.' The Prophet ﷺ said, 'Name yourselves with my name, but do not use my kunya.'"],[2275,"Do not combine my name and my kunya."],[2276,"He forbade anyone to combine his name and his kunya, so that one is named Muhammad Abu al-Qasim."],[2277,"\"When you give kunyas, do not take my name, and when you take my name, do not take my kunya.\" *"],[2278,"\"Do not combine between my name and my kunya. I am Abu al-Qasim; Allah gives and I distribute.\""],[2279,"I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ forbidding three habits in prayer: pecking like a crow, spreading the arms like a beast of prey, and a man marking a fixed place in the mosque as a camel does."],[2280,"\"A man does not settle in the mosque for prayer or for the remembrance of Allah except that Allah rejoices in him, just as the family of an absent person rejoices when their absent one returns to them.\""],[2281,"A young slave stole a small shoot from a walled garden. He was brought to Marwan, who ordered his hand to be cut off. Rafi' b. Khadij said: The Prophet ﷺ said: \"There is no amputation for fruit or palm pith.\""],[2282,"“The hand of the thief is cut off for a quarter of a dinar or more.”"],[2283,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ was asked about a man who divorced his wife irrevocably, and she married another husband, then he divorced her before consummating the marriage: may she return to her first husband? He said: \"No, not until he tastes her sweetness as the other tasted it.\""],[2284,"Beware of sitting in the roadways.\" They said, \"O Messenger of Allah, we have no alternative to our gatherings; we talk in them.\" He said, \"If you insist on sitting, then give the road its right.\" They said, \"What is the right of the road?\" He said, \"Lowering the gaze, refraining from harm, returning the greeting, enjoining good, and forbidding evil.\""],[2285,"“The Messenger of Allah ﷺ forbade a man from praying with his hands on his waist.”"],[2286,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ forbade the exception (thunya) unless it is specified."],[2287,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ arrived in Madinah while the people were lending dates. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to them, 'Whoever lends, let him lend only in a known measure and a known weight.'"],[2288,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ forbade combing the hair except every other day."],[2289,"Ibn ʿUmar used to pass by us and say, “Do not pair dates together, for the Prophet ﷺ forbade pairing, unless a man asks his companion’s permission.”"],[2290,"\"Ibn Al-Musayyab told me that Umm Salamah, the wife of the Prophet told him that the Messenger of Allah said: 'Whoever wants to offer a sacrifice, let him not remove anything from his nails or cut his hair for the first ten days Dhul-Jijjah.\"' (Using translation from Nasāʾī 4362)"],[2291,"that Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"If anyone of you has seen the crescent of Dhū al-Ḥijjah and one of you want to offer a sacrifice [on the Day of Naḥr], then he should hold back [cutting] his hair and nails.\" (Using translation from Muslim 1977e)"],[2292,"He who has a sacrificial animal with him whom (he intends) to offer as sacrifice, and he enters the month of Dhu'I-Hijja, he should not get his hair cut or nails trimmed until he has sacrificed the animal. (Using translation from Muslim 1977g)"],[2293,"We were in the bathhouse shortly before Eid al-Adha, and there were people who had applied depilatory paste. Some of those in the bathhouse said: \"Sa'id b. al-Musayyib dislikes this and forbids it.\" He said: I met Sa'id b. al-Musayyib and mentioned that to him, and he said: \"O son of my brother, this is a hadith that has been forgotten. Umm Salamah told me that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: 'When the ten days enter, and one of you has a sacrificial animal that he intends to slaughter, let him refrain from his hair and nails.'\""],[2294,"Beware of obscenity, for Allah does not love the obscene or the indecent. Beware of wrongdoing, for wrongdoing will be darknesses on the Day of Resurrection. Beware of miserliness, for miserliness called those before you, so they shed their blood and severed their kinship ties. *"],[2295,"“The Messenger of Allah ﷺ forbade a man from praying with his hands on his waist.”"],[2296,"“Putting the hands on the waist in prayer is the rest of the people of Hell.”"],[2297,"None of you should urinate in stagnant water or bathe in it after major ritual impurity."],[2298,"When the Messenger of Allah ﷺ met a man from among his Companions, he would wipe over him and supplicate for him. He said: I saw him one day in the morning, so I turned away from him. Then I came to him after the day had risen, and he said: \"I saw you and you turned away from me.\" I said: \"I was in a state of major ritual impurity, and I feared that you would touch me.\" The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"A Muslim does not become impure.\""],[2299,"When one of you wakes up from his sleep, let him not put his hand into the vessel until he washes it three times, for one of you does not know where his hand spent the night."],[2301,"«Whoever eats of this plant — garlic, onion, and leek — should not come near us in our mosques, for the angels are harmed by what harms humans.»"],[2302,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to wipe our shoulders in prayer and say: «Stand straight and do not differ, lest your hearts differ. Let those of you who possess maturity and intellect stand nearest to me, then those who are next to them, then those who are next to them.» Abu Mas'ud said: «Today you are even more divergent.»"],[2303,"Do not race me in bowing and prostration, for however much I precede you when I bow, you will catch me when I prostrate, and however much I precede you when I prostrate, you will catch me when I rise. Indeed, I have grown heavy."],[2304,"\"When one of you prays, he should not place his sandal to his right or to his left, lest it be to the right of someone else, unless there is someone to his left; and he should place them between his feet.\""],[2305,"When one of you stands in prayer, let him not touch the pebbles, for mercy is facing him."],[2306,"When one of you stands in prayer, mercy is facing him, so let him not move the pebbles, or not touch the pebbles."],[2307,"\"I asked Messenger of Allah (S) about smoothening the pebbles during Salat. He said: 'If you must do so, then let it be only once.'\" (Using translation from Tirmidhī 380)"],[2308,"“The Messenger of Allah ﷺ forbade a man from praying with his hands on his waist.”"],[2309,"That the Prophet ﷺ said: “What is the matter with people who raise their eyes to the sky during their prayer?” until he said: “Let them stop that, or their sights will be snatched away.”"],[2310,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ saw spittle in the qiblah, so he took a pebble and scraped it, then said, “None of you should spit in the direction of the qiblah nor to his right, but let him spit to his left or under his left foot.”"],[2311,"When one of you prays in a single garment, let him place its two ends oppositely on his shoulder."],[2312,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ liked date-palm stalks and would hold them in his hand. One day he entered the mosque with one of them in his hand and saw spittle in the qiblah of the mosque. He scraped it with it until he cleaned it, then turned to the people angrily and said, “Would any of you like a man to face him and spit in his face? When one of you stands for prayer, he is facing his Lord, and the angel is on his right, so let him not spit in front of him nor to his right, but to his left under his left foot. If he is overtaken by haste, let him do thus,” and he spat into his garment and folded part of it over another."],[2315,"“Do not raise your eyes to the sky, lest your sight be snatched away.”"],[2316,"From the Messenger of Allah ﷺ that he said, \"Do not perform Witr (an odd number of units of prayer) with three (units of prayer), rather perform it with five or seven. And do not resemble the Maghrib prayer.\""],[2317,"“The Messenger of Allah ﷺ forbade a man from praying with his hands on his waist.”"],[2318,"“Putting the hands on the waist in prayer is the rest of the people of Hell.”"],[2319,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ entered the mosque and saw a rope stretched between two pillars. He said, \"What is this?\" They said, \"It belongs to so-and-so; she prays and when she becomes tired she hangs onto it.\" The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, \"Let her pray as long as she is in her right mind, and when she fears being overcome, let her sleep.\""],[2320,"\"The Bedouins must not prevail over you regarding the name of your 'Isha prayer; they call it 'Atamah because of the milking of camels at nightfall.\""],[2321,"\"None of you should say, 'I forgot such-and-such verse,' for he was not made to forget, but he was made to forget [by Allah].\""],[2322,"None of you should say, 'My soul has become wicked,' but let him say, 'My soul is averse.'"],[2323,"\"One of you is granted an answer (to his supplication) provided he does not say: 'I prayed but I was not granted an answer.'\" (Using translation from Abū Dāʾūd 1484)"],[2324,"The supplication of the servant is granted in case he does not supplicate for sin or for severing the ties of blood, or he does not become impatient. It was said: Messenger of Allah, what does:\" If he does not grow impatient\" imply? He said: That he should say like this: I supplicated and I supplicated but I did not find it being responded. and theu he becomes frustrated and abandons supplication. (Using translation from Muslim 2735c)"],[2325,"\"None of you should say: 'O Allah, forgive me if You will,' for He cannot be compelled, but let him be firm in asking.\""],[2326,"We came to Khabbab to visit him, and he had been cauterized in his belly seven times. He said, \"Were it not that the Prophet ﷺ forbade us to pray for death, I would have prayed for it.\" Then he mentioned those of his companions who had passed on, that they had gone without consuming any of their rewards, and that we remained after them until we attained of this world what none of us knows what to do with except to spend it on dust. And a Muslim is rewarded for everything except what he spends on dust."],[2327,"\"None of you should wish for death. If he is a doer of good, perhaps he may increase in good; and if he is an evildoer, perhaps he may seek to appease.\""],[2328,"The judge must not judge between two parties while he is angry."],[2329,"Do not deem provision slow, for a servant will never die until he reaches the last provision that is his. So be moderate in seeking: take the lawful and leave the unlawful."],[2330,"A beggar came to the Prophet ﷺ, and there was a fallen date, so he gave it to him. The Prophet ﷺ said, \"Take it; if you had not come to it, it would have come to you.\""],[2331,"\"Do not be importunate in asking. For by Allah, if any one of you asks me for something and his request brings out from me something while I am reluctant, it will not be blessed for him.\""],[2332,"A beggar came to her, and Aisha ordered that something be given to him. When the servant went out, she called her and looked at it. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to her, “You do not give anything except with your knowledge.” She said, “I indeed know.” He said to her, “Do not count it, lest Allah count it against you.”"],[2333,"I was with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ when a man came to him with something like an egg of gold that he had obtained from one of the expeditions. He said, “O Messenger of Allah, take this from me as charity, for by Allah, I have no wealth other than it this morning.” The Prophet ﷺ turned away from him. He came to him from his other side and said the same, and the Prophet ﷺ turned away from him. Then he came to him from in front of him, and he took it from him and threw it at him with a throw that, had it hit him, would have wounded or hurt him. Then he said, “One of you brings all that he owns and gives it in charity, then sits and begs from people. Charity is only from surplus wealth. Take your wealth from us; we have no need of it.”"],[2334,"She used to count what she spent. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to her: \"Spend and do not count, lest Allah count against you; and do not hoard, lest Allah withhold from you.\""],[2335,"“When you travel in fertile land, give camels their due; when you travel in a year of drought, hasten the pace on them; and when you camp at night, avoid the road, for it is the shelter of creatures.”"],[2336,"\"Indeed, the Prophet (PBUH) said, 'Dreams are one part of seventy parts of Prophethood, and dreams are tied to the leg of a bird unless reported by the dreamer, and if reported it becomes true. So, do not report them except to a scholar, advisor, or loved one.'\""],[2338,"When one of you prays in a single garment, let him place its two ends oppositely on his shoulder."],[2340,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"Two should not converse privately excluding the third.\""],[2341,"I and 'Abd Allah b. 'Umar were at the house of Khalid b. 'Uqbah, the one in the market. A man came wanting to converse privately with him, and there was no one with 'Abd Allah b. 'Umar except me and the man who wanted to converse privately with him. So 'Abd Allah b. 'Umar called a man until we were four. He said to me and to the man he called: Stand back, for I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: \"Two should not converse privately excluding one.\""],[2342,"\"When you are three, two should not converse privately excluding their companion until they mix with people, for that saddens him.\""],[2343,"\"Two should not converse privately excluding their companion, for that saddens him.\" Abu Salih said: I said to Ibn 'Umar: What about four? He said: It does not harm you."],[2344,"None of you should say, 'I have planted,' but let him say, 'I have plowed.'\" Abu Hurayrah said, \"Have you not heard the words of God, Blessed and Exalted: 'Have you considered what you till? Is it you who sow it, or are We the Sower?'"],[2345,"He forbade passing an unsheathed sword."],[2346,"\"Indeed, the angels curse one of you when he points a piece of iron at his brother, even if he be his brother by father and mother.\""],[2347,"\"None of you should point a weapon at his brother, for he does not know-perhaps Satan will snatch it from his hand and it will fall upon the one he is handing it to.\""],[2348,"None of you should say, “May Allah disfigure your face and the face of anyone who resembles your face,” for indeed Allah created Adam in His image."],[2349,"That the Prophet ﷺ said to him: «O 'Abd al-Rahman, do not ask for leadership, for if you are given it by asking, you will be left to it, and if you are given it without asking, you will be helped in it. And if you swear an oath and see something else better than it, then do what is better and expiate for your oath.»"],[2350,"Whoever is offered perfume should not refuse it, for it is light to carry and pleasant in scent."],[2351,"Two men from the east stood up as orators and spoke, then sat down. Then Thabit b. Qays, the orator of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, stood up and spoke, and they marveled at his speech. Then the Messenger of Allah ﷺ stood up and delivered a sermon, saying, “O people, speak according to your manner, for indeed the excessive elaboration of speech is from Satan. Indeed, some eloquence is sorcery.”"],[2352,"A settled person should not sell on behalf of a desert dweller. Leave the people, so that Allah may provide for some of them through others."],[2353,"There came to him (the Holy Prophet) a desert Arab and said: I saw in a dream that I had been beheaded and I had been following it (the severed head). Allah's Apostle ﷺ reprimanded him saying: Do not inform about the vain sporting of devil with you during the night. (Using translation from Muslim 2268c)"],[2354,"A drinker was brought to the Messenger of God ﷺ, and he said, 'Strike him.' Among us were those who struck with their hands and those who struck with their sandals. Some of the people said, 'May God disgrace you.' The Messenger of God ﷺ said, 'Do not say that. Do not help Satan against him.'"],[2355,"A man came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and said, “O Messenger of Allah, I have found a woman of noble lineage and beauty, but she does not bear children. Should I marry her?” He forbade him. Then he came a second time and said the like, and he forbade him. Then he came a third time and said the like. He ﷺ said, “Marry the loving, the prolific, for I will boast of your numbers.”"],[2356,"Do not insult the rooster, for it calls to prayer."],[2357,"A man cursed the wind in the presence of the Prophet ﷺ, so he ﷺ said: «Do not curse the wind, for it is commanded. No one curses something that does not deserve it except that the curse returns upon him.»"],[2358,"Do not look to those above you, but look to those below you, for that is more fitting lest you belittle Allah's blessing upon you."],[2359,"When one of you sees someone above him in wealth and lineage, let him look to one who is below him in wealth and lineage."],[2360,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ forbade a man from coming to his family at night, or seeking to betray them, or looking into their faults."],[2361,"Do not say al-karm (for grapes), but say al-habalah or al-'inab."],[2364,"None of you should ever say al-karm, for indeed al-karm is the heart of the believer."],[2365,"I used to recite to ‘AbdurRahman bin ‘Awf, and he found me waiting for him. That was in Mina during the last Hajj performed by ʿUmar bin al-Khattab ؓ Abdur-Rahman bin ʿAwf said: A man came to ʿUmar bin al-Khattab and said: So and so is saying: If ʿUmar ؓ dies, I will swear allegiance to So and so. ʼUmar ؓ said: I will stand before the people today and warn them against these people who want to deprive them of their rights, ʿAbdur-Rahman said: I said: O Ameer al-Muʿmineen, do not do that, for the Hajj season brings together the riffraff and rabble among the people, and most of the people who gather around and listen to you will be of that type. Is you stand before the people, I am afraid that you will say something that they will spread and not understand it properly or interpret it properly. Rather wait until you come to Madinah, for it is the land of Hijrah and the Sunnah, and you will meet the most knowledgeable and noble people there, and you can say what you want to say with confidence; they wilt understand what you say and will interpret it correctly, ʿUmar ؓ said: If I reach Madinah safe and sound, I shall certainly talk to the people there in the first speech I deliver. When we came to Madinah at the end of Dhul-I-Iijah, it was a Friday. I set out early, ‘Umar did not care at what time he went out, because he did not pay attention to heat and cold and so on. I found Saʿeed bin Zaid at the right-hand corner of the minbar, he had got there before me. I sat down next to him, with my knee touching his knee, and it was not long before ʿUmar ؓ came. When I saw him, I said: He will certainly speak today on this minbar and say something that no one ever heard before. Saʿeed bin Zaid objected to that and said: What do you think he will say that no one said before? ʿUmar ؓ sat on the minbar, and when the muʿdhdhin fell silent, he stood up and praised and glorified Allah as He deserves, then he said: To proceed o people, I am going to tell you something that it has been decreed I should say. I do not know, perhaps it may signal my death. So whoever understands it and remembers it, let him narrate it to others wherever his mount takes him; whoever does not understand il, it is not permissible for him to tell lies about me. Allah, may He be blessed and exalted, sent Muhammad ﷺ with the truth and revealed the Book to him; among the things that were revealed to him was the verse of stoning [adulterers). We read it and understood it; the Messenger of Allah ﷺ stoned [adulterers] and we stoned adulterers] after him. But I fear that with the passage of time, some people will say: We do not find the verse of stoning in the Book of Allah, thus they will go astray by forsaking an obligation that Allah revealed. Stoning is the due punishment in the Book of Allah for those who commit zina, both men and women, if they have been married and if proof is established, or there is a pregnancy or a confession, And we used to recite: Do not claim to be the offspring of anyone other than your fathers, as it is disbelief (or ingratitude) on your part to claim to be the offspring of anyone other than your fathers, Verily the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: ʿDo not praise me excessively as ʿEesa, the son of Maryam, was praised; rather I am the slave of Allah, so say, the slave of Allah and His Messenger.ʿ I have heard that some among you are saying. If ʿUmar ؓ dies, I shall swear allegiance to So and so. No man should deceive himself by saying that the oath of allegiance to Abu Bakr was given suddenly and it was is successful. There is no doubt that this is the case, but Allah, may He be glorified and exalted, saved the to 2 people from its bad consequences and there is no one among you today who has the qualities of Abu Bakr ؓ What happened to us when the Messenger of Allah ﷺ died was that ‘Ali, az-Zubair and those who were with them stayed behind in the house of Fatimah, the daughter of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and all the Ansar stayed behind and gathered in Saqeefat Banu Saʿidah, whilst the Muhajireen gathered around Abu Bakr ؓ I said to him; O Abu Bakr, let us go to our brothers, the Ansar. So we set out, looking for them, then we were met by two righteous men who told us what the people had done, and said: where are you going, O Muhajireen? I said: We are looking for these brothers of ours, the Ansar, They said. You should not go near them; do whatever you have already decided, O Muhajireen. I said: By Allah, we will go to them. So we carried on until we came to them in Saqeefat Banu Saʿidah, where we found them gathered and among them was a man wrapped up [in a garment. I said: Who is this? They said: Saʿd bin ʿUbadah. ! said: What is the matter with him? They said: He is sick. After we sat down, their spokesman stood up and praised and glorified Allah, may He glorified and exalted, as He deserves, then he said: To proceed. We are the supporters (Ansar) of Allah and the majority of the Muslim army. You, O Muhajireen, are a small group among us. Some of you came to us, wanting to deny who we are and prevent us from attaining a position of authority. When he fell silent, I wanted to present a speech that I had prepared and that I liked in front of Abu Bakr ؓ I used to avoid provoking him and he was more forbearing and more dignified than me. But Abu Bakr ؓ said: Wait a while. I did not like to make him angry, and he was more knowledgeable and more dignified than me. By Allah, he did not omit any word that I liked in the speech I had prepared but he said something like it or better, speaking spontaneously, until he finished speaking. Then he said: To proceed. Whatever you have mentioned about your achievements and virtues, is correct. The Arabs would not acknowledge the leadership of anyone except someone from this tribe of Quraish, for they are the best of the Arabs in lineage and location. I am pleased to suggest to you one of these two men, whichever of them you want. Then he took hold of my hand and the hand of Abu ʿUbaidah bin al-Jarrah, and I disliked nothing of what he had said apart from this, for by Allah, I would rather have my neck struck for no sin on my part than to become the leader of people among whom was Abu Bakr ؓ unless my own self suggested something at the time of death. One of the Ansar said: I am the post on which the camel with a skin disease scratches itself and I am like a high class palm tree [i.e., a noble]. [I suggest] a ruler from among us and a ruler from among you, O Quraish. - I the narrator said to Malik; What does ‘I am the post on which the cainc! with a skin disease scratches itself and I am like a high class palm treeʿ mean? He said:It is as if he is saying, I am the smart one who has the answer. - Then there was a great deal of clamour and raised voices, to such an extent that I feared there would be a conflict, so I said: Hold out your hand, O Abu Bakr. So he held out his hand and I swore allegiance to him, and the Muhajireen swore allegiance to him, then the Ansar swore allegiance to him. Thus we surrounded Saʿd bin ‘Ubadah. One of them said: You have killed Saʿd i said: May Allah kill Sa’d! And ʿUmar ؓ said: By Allah, we never encountered any problem greater than the swearing of allegiance to Abu Bakr ؓ . We were afraid that if we left the people without having sworn allegiance to anyone, they might swear allegiance after we were gone, so we would either follow in their footsteps and swear allegiance to someone we were not pleased with, or we would disagree with them and that would cause trouble. If anyone swears allegiance to a leader without consulting the Muslims, there is no allegiance for him and no allegiance to the one who swore allegiance to him, lest both of them be killed. Malik said: Ibn Shihab told me, from ʿUrwah bin az-Zubair, that the men whom they met were ʿUwaim bin Saʿidah and Maʿn bin ʿAdiyy. Ibn Shihab said. Saʿeed bin al-Musayyab told me that the one who said, I am the post on which the camel with a skin disease scratches itself and I am like a high class palm tree, was al-lubab bin al-Mundhir. (Using translation from Aḥmad 391)"],[2366,"He forbade the earnings of slave women."],[2367,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ forbade the earnings of slave women for fear that they would engage in prostitution."],[2368,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ prohibited blocking or preventing the flow of water from a well."],[2369,"I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ saying, \"Do not withhold the blessing of water, and do not withhold charity, for wealth will become worthless and families will go hungry.\""],[2370,"“I have had a ring made, so let no one engrave upon its inscription.”"],[2371,"“The inscription on the ring of the Prophet ﷺ was three lines: Muhammad one line, Messenger one line, Allah one line.”"],[2372,"None of you should walk in one sandal; he should either wear both or remove both."],[2373,"If the strap of one of your sandals breaks, he should not walk in one sandal or one leather sock; he should either wear both or remove both."],[2374,"Mu'awiyah wrote to al-Mughirah b. Shu'bah: 'Write to me a hadith you heard from the Messenger of Allah ﷺ.' He called his servant Warrad and said: 'Write: I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ prohibiting burying daughters alive, disobedience to mothers, withholding and demanding, and from 'it was said' and 'he said', excessive questioning, and wasting wealth.'\""],[2376,"We passed with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ by al-Hijr, and the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to us: \"Do not enter the dwellings of those who wronged themselves unless you are weeping, in caution that there may befall you the like of what befell them.\" Then he departed and hastened until he left it behind."],[2377,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to the companions of al-Hijr: \"Do not enter upon these punished people unless you are weeping, so do not enter upon them lest there befall you the like of what befell them.\""],[2378,"The people camped with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ at al-Hijr, the land of Thamud, and they drew water from its wells and kneaded dough with it. He ordered them to pour out what they had drawn and to feed the dough to the camels, and he ordered them to draw water from the well which the she-camel used to come to."],[2379,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ stayed in Tabuk near the houses of Thamud and the people drew water from the wells that Thamud used to drink from. They set up pots and kneaded dough. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, \"Fill the pots and feed the camels with the dough.\" Then he moved on until he reached the place where the camel used to drink from and said, \"Do not enter the dwellings of these people who were punished, lest the same punishment befall you.\""],[2380,"“When your companion dies, leave him be.”"],[2381,"“When your companion dies, leave him be.”"],[2382,"“Mention the good qualities of your dead and refrain from their faults.”"],[2383,"“What did Yazīd b. Qays do, upon him be the curse of Allah?” They said, “He has died.”"],[2384,"“Do not revile the dead, for you would hurt the living.”"],[2386,"“Snakes are among the transformed jinn, just as pigs and apes were transformed.”"],[2387,"I came to Abu Sa'id al-Khudri, and while I was sitting with him, I heard the movement of something under his bed. I looked and there was a snake, so I stood up."],[2388,"These are creeping creatures from among the jinn. So when one of you sees something in his house, let him command it three times. If he sees it after that, then let him kill it, for it is only a devil."],[2389,"Kill snakes and kill the one with two stripes and the short-tailed one, for they blind the sight and cause miscarriage."],[2390,"Kill snakes and kill the one with two stripes and the short-tailed one, for they blind the sight and cause miscarriage. Ibn Umar said: I did not leave a snake without killing it until Abu Lubabah b. Abd al-Mundhir and Zayd b. al-Khattab saw me chasing a snake from among the house snakes, and they forbade me from killing it. I said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ commanded killing them. They said: He forbade killing the house snakes."],[2391,"'Leave the birds in their nests.'"],[2392,"'Ammar b. Yasir: 'Whoever fasts the day that is doubted has disobeyed Abu al-Qasim ﷺ.'"],[2393,"Do not precede the fast of the month of Ramadan by fasting a day or two, except a man who was already observing a fast, then let him fast it."],[2394,"That the Prophet ﷺ said to him—or to a man—'Did you fast anything from the last part of this month?' He said, 'No.' He said, 'Then when you break your fast, fast a day or two.'"],[2395,"That the Prophet ﷺ said to him—or to a man—'Did you fast anything from the last part of this month?' He said, 'No.' He said, 'Then when you break your fast, fast a day or two.'"],[2396,"When the middle of Sha'ban comes, then refrain from fasting until Ramadan comes.[1]"],[2397,"I entered upon 'Ikrimah on the day that was doubted whether it was from Ramadan, and he was eating. He said, 'Come close and eat.' I said, 'I am fasting.' He said, 'By Allah, you will come close.' I said, 'Then tell me a hadith.' He said..."],[2398,"«Whoever eats of this tree should not annoy us in our gatherings.»"],[2399,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ forbade eating leek, but they did not desist, and then they found no alternative but to eat it. He noticed its smell and said: \"Did I not forbid you from this foul — or stinking — plant? Whoever eats it should not come near us in our mosques, for the angels are harmed by what harms humans.\""],[2400,"The Prophet ﷺ said, \"The most truthful part of a person's speech and the worst part of it are what is between his jaws.\" Wahb (may Allah be pleased with him) said, \"He means his tongue.\""],[2401,"A Bedouin came to the Prophet ﷺ and said, \"We are in a barren land, and one of us emits a slight wind, and water is scarce.\" The Prophet ﷺ said, \"If one of you breaks wind, let him perform ablution, and do not come to women in their posteriors, for indeed Allah is not shy of the truth.\""],[2402,"The Prophet ﷺ stood for prayer and we stood with him. A Bedouin said during the prayer, “O Allah, have mercy on me and Muhammad, and do not have mercy on anyone else with us.” When the Messenger of Allah ﷺ finished praying, he said to the Bedouin, “You have restricted something vast.”"],[2403,"The Prophet ﷺ saw a man following a pigeon and said: \"A devil following a she-devil.\""],[2404,"Many a person who stands (in prayer) gets from his standing only sleeplessness, and many a person who fasts gets from his fasting only hunger."],[2405,"I was sitting beside the pulpit on Friday when a man came stepping over people's necks while the Messenger of Allah ﷺ was addressing the people. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to him, \"Sit down, for you have caused harm and come late.\""],[2406,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, \"If one of you only knew the reward he has in walking to his brother, seeking to consult with him, while he is secluded in prayer with his Lord, he would have preferred to stand in that place for a hundred years rather than taking a single step.\""],[2407,"While Abū al-Dardāʾ was one day traveling alone from the army, he met two men who were alone from the army. He said, “O you two, whenever three are in a place like this they are given a commander, so let one of you take command.” They said, “You, O Abū al-Dardāʾ.” He said, “Rather you two. I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say, ‘There is no ruler of three except that he will meet Allah with his right hand fettered. His justice will release it, or his injustice will keep it fettered.’”"],[2408,"There was something between ʿĀʾishah and one of her nephews, so he entered upon her. When he sat down, food was brought, but he got up to go to the mosque. She said to him, “Sit down, you traitor, for I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say, ‘None of you should pray when food is present, nor while he is resisting the two impure things.’”"],[2409,"“When the call to prayer—the morning prayer—is given, and one of you is in a state of major impurity, he must not fast that day.”"],[2410,"That he heard Abu Hurayrah say, “Whoever wakes up in a state of major impurity must not fast.” He said: So Abu Bakr and his father went off until they entered upon Umm Salamah and ʿAʾishah, and both of them said, “The Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to wake up in a state of major impurity and then fast.” So Abu Bakr and his father went off until they came to Marwan and told him. He said, “I adjure you both: go to Abu Hurayrah and tell him.” So they went to Abu Hurayrah and told him, and he said, “They know better.”"],[2411,"He used to be overtaken by dawn while he was junub from his family, then he would perform ghusl and fast."],[2412,"That he came to ʿAʾishah and said, “Abu Hurayrah gives us the ruling that whoever wakes up in a state of major impurity has no fast. What do you say to him about that?” She said, “Bilal used to come to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and call him to prayer while he was in a state of major impurity, and he would get up and perform the ritual bath, and I would see the water running between his shoulders, and then he would remain fasting.”"],[2413,"“The Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to wake up in a state of major impurity, not from a wet dream, in Ramadan, and then fast.”"],[2414,"“The Prophet ﷺ would sometimes spend the night in a state of major impurity, then Bilal would come to him for the morning prayer, and he would get up and perform the ritual bath, and I would watch the water running down from his skin and his head, then I would hear his recitation in the morning prayer, and then he would remain fasting.” Mutarrif said: I said to him, “In Ramadan?” He said, “It was the same for him.”"],[2415,"“The Prophet ﷺ would sometimes spend the night in a state of major impurity, then Bilal would come to him and inform him of the prayer, and he would get up and perform the ritual bath, and I saw the water dripping from his hair, and then he would remain fasting that day.” Mutarrif said: I said to al-Shaʿbi, “In the month of Ramadan?” He said, “The month of Ramadan and others are the same.”"],[2416,"A man came to the Prophet ﷺ and said, “O Messenger of Allah, the morning comes upon me while I am in a state of major impurity—should I fast that day of mine?” I heard the Prophet ﷺ say, “Sometimes the morning comes upon me while I am in a state of major impurity, and I get up, perform the ritual bath, pray the morning prayer, and fast that day of mine.” The man said, “You are not like us: Allah has forgiven you your past and future sins.” The Prophet ﷺ said, “I hope that I am the most fearful of Allah among you and the most knowledgeable of what I avoid.”"],[2417,"A man delivered a sermon in the presence of the Prophet ﷺ and said, \"Whoever obeys Allah and His Messenger is guided, and whoever disobeys them both has gone astray.\" The Prophet ﷺ said, \"What a bad speaker! Say: 'And whoever disobeys Allah and His Messenger.'\""],[2418,"\"When one of you enters the mosque, he should not sit until he prays two rak'ahs.\""],[2419,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to me: \"Have I not been told that you fast all day and stand in prayer all night?\" I said: \"Yes, O Messenger of Allah.\" He said: \"Do not do that. Sleep and stand, fast and break your fast, for your body has a right over you, your visitor has a right over you, and your wife has a right over you. I give you the choice to fast three days of every month, for every good deed is multiplied tenfold, and that is like fasting the entire age.\" I said: \"O Messenger of Allah, I find strength.\" He said: \"Fast three days every week.\" He said: \"I insisted, and it was made strict on me.\" I said: \"O Messenger of Allah, I find strength.\" He said: \"Fast the fast of Allah's Prophet Dāwūd and do not add to it.\" I said: \"What is the fast of Allah's Prophet Dāwūd?\" He said: \"Half the age.\""],[2420,"Uyaynah and al-Aqra' asked the Messenger of Allah ﷺ for something, so he ordered Mu'awiyah to write it for them. He did so and the Messenger of Allah ﷺ sealed it and ordered him to give it to them. As for Uyaynah, he said, 'What is in it?' He said, 'In it is what I was ordered.' So he accepted it and tied it in his turban. As for al-Aqra', he said, 'I carry a document I do not know what is in it, like the document of al-Mutalammis?' Mu'awiyah informed the Messenger of Allah ﷺ of their words. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ went out for his need and passed by a camel kneeling at the door of the mosque from the beginning of the day. Then he passed by it at the end of the day and it was in the same state. He said, 'Where is the owner of this camel?' It was sought but not found. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, 'Fear Allah regarding these animals. Ride them while they are healthy and eat them while they are fat, like one who was displeased just now. Whoever asks while he has what suffices him is only increasing in the coals of Hell.' He said, 'O Messenger of Allah, what suffices him?' He said, 'That which gives him his morning and evening meals.'"],[2421,"When one of you follows a funeral, let him not sit until it is placed down."],[2422,"None of you should ever say, 'I fasted the whole of Ramadan and stood in prayer throughout it.'\" He said, \"I do not know whether he disliked self-praise or he said, 'There must be some sleep or heedlessness.'"],[2423,"The translation in English is: \"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to perform the Witr prayer with one unit (rak'ah).\""],[2424,"I divorced my wife while she was menstruating, so the Messenger of Allah ﷺ returned her to me until I divorced her while she was pure."],[2425,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ forbade killing four: the hoopoe, the shrike, the ant, and the bee."],[2426,"The Prophet ﷺ sent Saʿd b. ʿUbādah as a charity collector and said, “Beware, O Saʿd, lest you come on the Day of Resurrection with a camel that has a rumbling cry.” He said, “I shall not find it, nor shall I come with it.” So he excused him."],[2427,"A donkey passed by him that had been cauterized on its face or branded, and the Prophet ﷺ cursed the one who did that. Then he said, “Glory be to Allah! Do not strike them on their faces.”"],[2428,"We captured some captives on the day of Khaybar, and we wanted to ransom them. We asked the Prophet ﷺ about coitus interruptus, and he said: 'It does not matter if you do not do that, for it is only the decree.'"],[2429,"'You have a reward in having intercourse with your wife.' It was said: 'O Messenger of Allah, is there a reward even in satisfying desire?' He said: 'Yes. Do you think that if you had a son who reached maturity and then died, would you seek reward for him?' He said: 'Yes.' He said: 'Did you create him?' He said: 'No, Allah created him.' He said: 'Did you guide him?' He said: 'No, Allah guided him.' He said: 'Did you provide for him?' He said: 'No, Allah provided for him.' The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: 'Then place it in what is lawful for you and keep it away from what is forbidden, and keep it. If Allah wills, He will give it life, and if He wills, He will cause it to die, and you will have a reward.'"],[2430,"Some people asked the Messenger of Allah ﷺ about coitus interruptus during the expedition of Banu al-Mustaliq. They had captured female captives and disliked that they should bear children from them. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: 'It does not matter if you do not do that, for Allah has decreed what He will create until the Day of Resurrection.'"],[2431,"A man said to the Prophet ﷺ, “Tell me a saying and keep it brief.” He said, “Do not become angry.” He repeated it, and he said, “Do not become angry.”"],[2432,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ asked the people to be silent during the Farewell Pilgrimage, then said: “Do not return after me as disbelievers, striking one another’s necks.”"],[2433,"The translation in English is: \"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to perform the Witr prayer with one unit (rak'ah).\""],[2434,"Bashir b. al-Khasasiyyah—his name in the pre-Islamic era was Zahm b. Ma'bad—narrated to us. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to him, \"What is your name?\" He said, \"Zahm.\""],[2436,"It was narrated from ‘Ali ؓ that The Prophet ﷺ used to pray Witr with three raka’hs (Using translation from Aḥmad 685)"],[2437,"“The Messenger of Allah ﷺ forbade traveling with the Quran to the land of the enemy, fearing that the enemy might get hold of it.”"],[2438,"“Any man who says to his brother, ‘Unbeliever,’ then one of them has incurred it.”"],[2439,"He heard Ibn Umar say that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ was asked about the night prayer, and he replied, \"One of you should pray two units, two units, until he fears the dawn, then he should perform a prostration that prolongs what he has prayed.\""],[2440,"“No man ever calls another man an unbeliever except that one of them incurs it: if he is an unbeliever, then he incurs it; otherwise it returns upon the one who said it.”"],[2441,"'Perform the ʿAṣr prayer early on a cloudy day, for whoever abandons the ʿAṣr prayer has had his deeds nullified.'"],[2442,"I was with Ibn Umar when a man swore by the Ka'bah. Ibn Umar said: Woe to you, do not do that, for I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: \"Whoever swears by other than Allah has committed shirk.\""],[2443,"Verily the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: He who took an oath on a religion other than Islam as a liar would become so as he said, and he who slaughtered himself with a thing would be slaughtered with that on the Day of Resurrection. (Using translation from Muslim 110d)"],[2446,"He mentioned prayer one day and said, 'Whoever maintains it, it will be for him a light, a proof, and salvation on the Day of Resurrection. Whoever does not maintain it will have no proof, no light, and no salvation, and on the Day of Resurrection he will be with Korah, Haman, Pharaoh, and Ubayy b. Khalaf.'"],[2447,"\"I met my maternal uncle Abu Burdah, and he had the banner. I said: 'Where are you going?' He said: 'The Messenger of Allah ﷺ sent me to a man who married his father's wife, to kill him or strike his neck.'\""],[2448,"Three people Allah does not accept prayer from: an imam of a people who dislike him, a woman who spends the night while her husband is angry with her, and two brothers who are estranged."],[2449,"Three people whose prayer Allah does not accept and whose good deeds He does not raise to heaven: the runaway slave until he returns to his masters and places his hand in their hands, the woman with whom her husband is angry until he is pleased, and the drunkard until he sobers up.”"],[2450,"“Whoever drinks wine and gets drunk, his prayer will not be accepted for forty days, and if he dies he will enter Hell, but if he repents, Allah will accept his repentance. If he drinks wine again and gets drunk, his prayer will not be accepted for forty days, and if he dies he will enter Hell, but if he repents, Allah will accept his repentance. If he drinks wine again and gets drunk, his prayer will not be accepted for forty days, and if he dies he will enter Hell, but if he repents Allah will accept his repentance. But if he does it again, then Allah will most certainly make him drink of the mire of the puss or sweat on the Day of Resurrection.” They said: “O Messenger of Allah, what is the mire of the pus or sweat? He said: “The drippings of the people of Hell.” (Using translation from Ibn Mājah 3377)"],[2451,"Whoever meets Allah addicted to wine meets Him like a worshipper of an idol."],[2452,"\"That the Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to perform Witr prayer with five (rak'ahs) and also used to perform Witr prayer with seven (rak'ahs).\""],[2453,"“Every sin Allah may forgive except one who dies as a polytheist or one who kills a believer intentionally.”"],[2454,"“No soul is killed unjustly but that the first son of Adam bears a share of its blood, because he was the first to establish killing.”"],[2455,"“Whoever kills himself with an iron weapon, his iron will be in his hand, stabbing himself in his belly in the Fire of Hell, abiding therein forever, eternally. Whoever kills himself with poison, his poison will be in his hand, sipping it in the Fire of Hell, abiding therein forever, eternally. Whoever throws himself from a mountain intentionally and kills himself, he will be throwing himself down in the Fire of Hell, abiding therein forever, eternally.”"],[2456,"\"The Messenger [SAW] said: 'If two Muslims meet (and fight) with their swords and one of them kills the other, the killer and the slain will both be in Hell.'\" (Using translation from Nasāʾī 4121)"],[2457,"“Any man who grants security to another for his blood and then kills him, I am free of the killer even if the slain was a disbeliever.”"],[2458,"\"Indeed the treacherous person will have a banner set up for him on the Day of Resurrection at his anus, and it will be said: This is the treachery of so-and-so.\""],[2459,"When Abu Musa was on his deathbed, he said, 'When you carry my bier, walk quickly, and do not follow me with burning coals, and do not place anything over my grave that would come between me and the earth, and do not build a structure over my grave. I call you to witness that I am free of every woman who shaves her head, wails loudly, or tears her clothes.' They said, 'Did you hear something about this?' He said, 'Yes, from the Messenger of Allah ﷺ.'"],[2460,"Abu Musa became ill and kept losing consciousness, his head in the lap of a woman from his family. A woman cried out, and he could not respond to her. When he regained consciousness, he said, 'I am free of whoever the Messenger of Allah ﷺ freed himself from, and the Messenger of Allah ﷺ freed himself from the woman who shaves her head, wails loudly, and tears her clothes.'"],[2461,"«Whoever eats of this foul plant should not come near our mosque for three days.»"],[2462,"If the son of Adam had a valley of palm trees, he would wish for another like it, and nothing fills the belly of the son of Adam except dust."],[2464,"If the son of Adam had a valley of gold, he would love to have another valley, and nothing fills his mouth except dust, and Allah turns in mercy to whoever repents."],[2465,"If the son of Adam had two valleys of wealth, he would seek a third valley, and nothing fills the belly of the son of Adam except dust, then Allah turns in mercy to whoever repents."],[2466,"'If you knew what I know, you would laugh little and weep much.'"],[2467,"I stood at the gate of Paradise, and most of those who entered it were the poor, while people of good fortune were held back, and the people of the Fire had been ordered to the Fire. I looked at the Fire, and most of those who entered it were women."],[2468,"\"I have not left after me a tribulation more harmful to men than women.\""],[2469,"\"Woe to women from the two red things: gold and saffron-dyed garments.\""],[2470,"When the people camped at a place, they would scatter in the mountain passes and valleys. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Your scattering in these mountain passes and valleys is only from Satan.” He said: After that, they never camped at a place except that they gathered close to one another until if a cloth were spread over them, it would cover them all."],[2471,"\"Do not write from me anything except the Qur'an. Whoever has written from me anything else should erase it.\""],[2472,"It is not I who prohibited fasting on Friday. Muhammad ﷺ, by the Lord of the Kaaba, prohibited it."],[2473,"I was sitting with Abu Hurayrah when a man came to him and said, \"You have prohibited people from fasting on Friday.\" He said, \"I did not prohibit people from fasting on Friday, but I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: 'Do not fast on Friday, for it is a day of Eid, unless you connect it with other days.'\""],[2474,"None of you should fast on Friday unless he fasts a day before it or after it."],[2475,"Do you see this hand of mine? I pledged allegiance to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ with it, and I heard him say: Do not fast on Saturday except in what has been made obligatory upon you; and if one of you finds nothing but the bark of a tree, let him break his fast with it."],[2476,"Ibn Abbas and some of the companions of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ sent me to Umm Salamah to ask her about which days the Messenger of Allah ﷺ fasted most. She said: Saturday and Sunday. I returned to them and informed them, and they seemed to reject that. So they all went to her and said: We sent this one to you about such-and-such, and he mentioned that you said such-and-such. She said: He spoke the truth. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ most often fasted Saturday and Sunday, and he used to say: They are two festivals for the polytheists, and I want to differ from them."],[2477,"“Whoever eats dates with a group of people, let him not pair them; if he wants to do so, let him ask their permission, and if they give him permission, then let him do it.”"],[2478,"\"That the Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to perform Witr prayer with five (rak'ahs) and also used to perform Witr prayer with seven (rak'ahs).\""],[2479,"The people took a mountain pass or a hill, and whenever a man reached its top he said, 'There is no god but Allah, and Allah is greatest,' while the Prophet ﷺ was on a mule presenting it on the mountain. He said, 'O people, you are not calling upon one who is deaf or absent.' Then he said, 'O Abu Musa' - or 'O 'Abd Allah b. Qays - shall I not guide you to a treasure from the treasures of Paradise?' He said, 'Yes, O Messenger of Allah.' He said, 'There is no might and no power except with Allah.'"],[2480,"When Ja'far b. Abi Talib was struck (i.e., martyred), the Messenger of Allah ﷺ commanded me, saying, 'Observe three days (of mourning), then do whatever you wish after that.'"],[2481,"When Abu Musa was dying, they cried out over him. He said, 'The Prophet ﷺ said: He is not one of us who wails, tears his clothes, or shaves his head.'"],[2482,"He is not one of us who strikes the cheeks, tears the front openings of garments, or calls with the call of Jahiliyyah."],[2483,"When the son of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ passed away, Usama bin Zaid started crying. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, \"This is not from us, the one whose heart is filled with sadness and eyes are streaming with tears, and he does not say anything that angers the Lord.\""],[2484,"The Prophet passed by a heap of food and inserted his fingers into it, and found moisture. He said: \"What is this, O owner of the food?\" He said: \"It was affected by rain, O Messenger of Allah.\" He said: \"Why did you not put it on top of the food so that people could see it? Whoever deceives us is not of us.\""],[2486,"“There is no amputation for a snatcher, and whoever snatches a plunder is not from us.”"],[2487,"Whoever shoots at us with arrows is not one of us."],[2488,"“Whoever bears arms against us is not one of us.”"],[2489,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ came out to us while we were nine, and among us was a leather cushion, and he said: \"Indeed, there will be after me rulers. Whoever enters upon them and confirms them in their lies and aids them in their oppression is not of me, and I am not of him, and he will not come to me at the Basin. And whoever does not enter upon them, does not confirm them in their lies, and does not aid them in their oppression, he is of me and I am of him, and he will come to me at the Basin.\""],[2490,"“He is not one of us who does not honor the elder, show mercy to the young, enjoin what is right, and forbid what is wrong.”"],[2491,"He used to lighten the two rak'ahs of Fajr."],[2493,"\"Whoever corrupts a man's wife or his slave is not from us, and whoever swears by honesty (al-amānah) is not from us.\""],[2494,"We have not made peace with them since we fought them, meaning the snakes. Whoever leaves off killing anything of them out of fear is not from us."],[2495,"“Kill snakes, and kill the one with two white stripes on its back and the one with a short tail, for they cause blindness and cause miscarriage.”"],[2496,"«Whoever does not take from his mustache is not one of us.»"],[2497,"I will not marry women; someone among them said: I will not eat meat; and someone among them said: I will not lie down in bed. He (the Holy Prophet) praised Allah and glorified Him, and said: What has happened to these people that they say so and so, whereas I observe prayer and sleep too; I observe fast and suspend observing them; I marry women also? And he who turns away from my Sunnah, he has no relation with Me (Using translation from Muslim 1401)"],[2498,"“He is not one of us who does not beautify his voice with the Qurʾān.”"],[2499,"A man from the Muhajirun struck a man from the Ansar on the backside with his foot or hand. The Ansari said: \"O Ansar!\" and the Muhajir said: \"O Muhajirun!\" The Prophet ﷺ heard that and said: \"What is this call of Jahiliyyah?\" They said: \"O Messenger of Allah, a man from the Muhajirun struck a man from the Ansar on the backside.\" He said: \"Leave it, for it is stinking.\" Then 'Abdullah b. Ubayy b. Salul said: \"They have done it. If we return to Madinah, the more honorable will surely expel the more humble from it.\" 'Umar said: \"Let me, O Messenger of Allah, strike the neck of this hypocrite.\" He said: \"Leave him, lest people say that Muhammad kills his companions.\""],[2500,"Indeed, what I fear most for you is what Allah has brought forth from the plants of the earth and the splendor of the world. A man stood up to him and said: O Messenger of Allah, does good ever bring evil? The Prophet ﷺ was silent until we thought that revelation was descending upon him, and when it descended upon him, he would be covered with panting and sweat. When it was relieved from him, he said: 'Where is the questioner?' He said: Here I am, O Messenger of Allah, and I only intended good. He said: 'Good does not bring anything but good, but every spring-grown plant that the spring brings forth kills or nearly kills by bloating except the eater of green vegetation, for it eats until its flanks are distended, then it faces the sun, defecates and urinates, then returns and eats. Then it stands and chews the cud. So whoever takes wealth by its right, it is blessed for him and benefits him, and whoever takes wealth without its right, it is not blessed for him and he is like one who eats but is never satisfied.'"],[2501,"\"Indeed, a man among you may come to me to ask, and I give him, and he departs carrying in his lap nothing but Fire.\""],[2502,"\"And whoever asks people from their wealth, he is only asking for coals, so let him take little or much from them.\""],[2503,"“Whoever Allah intends good for, He grants him understanding of the religion.”"],[2504,"His family complained to him about need, so he went out to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ to ask him for something for them. He came upon him on the pulpit while he was saying: “O people, the time has come for you to be self-sufficient from begging. For whoever seeks chastity, Allah will keep him chaste; whoever seeks self-sufficiency, Allah will make him self-sufficient. By the One in whose hand is the soul of Muhammad, no servant has been granted anything more expansive than patience. And if you refuse except to ask me, I will give you whatever I find.”"],[2505,"\"Whoever asks people in order to increase his wealth, it is only a live coal from the Fire, so let him decrease it or let him increase it.\""],[2506,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ appointed a man from the Azd tribe called Ibn al-Utbiyya, in charge of Sadaqat to be received from Banu Sulaim. When he came (back), the Messenger of Allah ﷺ asked him to render his account. He said: This wealth is for you (i.e. for the public treasury) and this is a gift (presented to me). The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: You should have remained in the house of your father and your mother, until your gift came to you if you spoke the truth; then he addressed us. He praised God and extolled Him, and afterwards said: I appoint a man from you to a responsible post sharing with him authority that God has entrusted to me, and he comes to me saying: This wealth is for you (i.e. for the public treasury) and this is a gift presented to me. Why did he not remain in the house of his father and his mother and his gift came to him, if he was truthful? By God, any one of you will not take anything from (the public funds) without any justification, but will meet his Lord carrying it on himself on the Day of judgment. I will recognise any one of you meeting Allah and carrying a growling camel, or a cow bellowing or a goat bleating. Then he raised his hands so high that whiteness of his armpits could be seen. Then he said: O my Lord, I have conveyed (Thy Commandments). The narrator says: My eyes saw (the Prophet standing in that pose) and my ears heard (what he said). (Using translation from Muslim 1832c)"],[2507,"What is the matter with one of you, playing with the limits of Allah, saying, 'I have divorced, I have taken back'?!"],[2508,"They came to the Prophet ﷺ, and a man from Khath'am called Suwayd b. Tariq stood up to him and said: 'We make wine.' He forbade him from it. He said: 'We only use it as medicine.' The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: 'It is not a cure; it is a disease.'"],[2509,"A Bedouin entered the mosque while the Messenger of Allah ﷺ was sitting, and said, “O Allah, forgive me and Muhammad, but do not forgive anyone else with us.” The Messenger of Allah ﷺ laughed and said, “You have restricted something vast.” Then the Bedouin went away until he was at a corner of the mosque, and he spread his legs to urinate. The Bedouin said, after he had learned about Islam: “The Messenger of Allah ﷺ came to me and did not scold me or insult me. He said, 'This mosque was built for the remembrance of Allah and for prayer, and it should not be urinated in.' Then he called for a bucket of water and poured it over the urine.”"],[2510,"For one of you to have his belly filled with pus until it destroys him is better for him than to have it filled with poetry."],[2511,"\"Indeed, the greatest of people in slander are two: a poet who satirizes a whole tribe and a man who disowns his father.\""],[2512,"Zayd b. Khālid sent him to Abū Juhaym to ask him what he heard from the Messenger of Allah ﷺ about the one who passes in front of a praying person. Abū Juhaym said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: 'If the one who passes in front of a praying person knew what was upon him, it would be better for him to stand for forty than to pass in front of him.' I do not know whether he said forty years, months, days, or hours."],[2513,"When Abu Salamah died, I said, 'A stranger in a strange land—I will weep for him with such weeping that it will be talked about.' I had prepared to weep over him when a woman from the Mus'idat (women who assist in wailing) came wanting to join me in wailing. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ met her and said, 'Do you want to let the devil into a house from which Allah has expelled him?' She said, 'So I refrained from weeping and did not weep.'"],[2514,"\"Let me not find any one of you coming on the Day of Resurrection with a camel on his neck that bellows, saying, 'O Messenger of Allah!' I will say, 'I can do nothing for you against Allah; I had conveyed to you.' Let me not find any one of you coming on the Day of Resurrection with a sheep on his neck that bleats, saying, 'O Messenger of Allah!' I will say, 'I can do nothing for you against Allah; I had conveyed to you.' Let me not find any one of you coming on the Day of Resurrection with a horse on his neck that neighs, saying, 'O Messenger of Allah!' I will say, 'I can do nothing for you against Allah; I had conveyed to you.' Let me not find any one of you coming on the Day of Resurrection with a soul on his neck that cries out, saying, 'O Messenger of Allah!' I will say, 'I can do nothing for you against Allah; I had conveyed to you.' Let me not find any one of you coming on the Day of Resurrection with silent wealth on his neck, saying, 'O Messenger of Allah!' I will say, 'I can do nothing for you against Allah; I had conveyed to you.' Let me not find any one of you coming on the Day of Resurrection with fluttering patches on his neck, saying, 'O Messenger of Allah!' I will say, 'I can do nothing for you against Allah; I had conveyed to you.'\""],[2515,"I said to the Prophet ﷺ, \"I saw so-and-so praying and mentioning good, and he mentioned that you gave him two dinars.\" He said, \"But so-and-so — I gave him between such and such, and he neither praised nor said any good.\""],[2516,"The Prophet ﷺ said, \"The best of names near Allah is a man named 'Milk Al-Amalak,' which means 'The King of Kings.'\""],[2519,"The Prophet ﷺ said, \"Whoever misses the prayer, it is as if he has lost his family and wealth.\""],[2520,"The Messenger of Allah said: \"The one who misses the 'Asr prayer, it is as if he has been cheated out of his family and wealth.\" (Using translation from Ibn Mājah 685)"],[2521,"The Prophet ﷺ came out to his companions while they were sitting in circles in the mosque, and he said, “What is the matter with me that I see you in separate groups?”"],[2522,"“A people will not continue to hold back from the first row until Allah holds them back in the Fire.”"],[2523,"A bedouin came to the Prophet ﷺ and said: O Messenger of Allah, a sore appears on the lip of a camel or on its rump, and then all the camels become mangy. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: 'Then who infected the first one? Their lives, their afflictions, and their provision.'"],[2524,"I heard Jabir b. Abdullah say: I came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and knocked on the door. He said, \"Who is it?\" I said, \"Me.\" He said, \"Me, me,\" twice, as if he disliked it."],[2525,"That the Prophet ﷺ said: “What is the matter with people who raise their eyes to the sky during their prayer?” until he said: “Let them stop that, or their sights will be snatched away.”"],[2526,"Why would one of you flog his wife like a slave, then have intercourse with her at the end of the day?"],[2527,"He heard the Prophet ﷺ say in his sermon while mentioning the she-camel and the one who hamstrung her: “{When the most wretched of them was sent forth} (Qur'an 91:12) the one sent forth to her was a man, fierce, mighty, and protected among his people, like Abu Zam'ah.” Then he mentioned women and said, “Why does one of you flog his wife as he flogs a slave, and perhaps he will lie with her at the end of his day?” Then he admonished them about laughing at passing wind and said, “Why does one of you laugh at what he himself does?!”"],[2528,"\"Whoever recites the Qur'an in less than three days does not understand it.\""],[2529,"Food was brought to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ at Marr al-Ẓahrān. He said to Abū Bakr and ʿUmar, “Eat.” They said, “We are fasting.” He said, “Saddle up for your two companions, work for your two companions, come near and eat.”"],[2530,"The Prophet ﷺ passed by me while my mother and I were repairing a hut of ours. He said: «What is this, O ‘Abdullah?» He said: I said: A hut of ours we are repairing. He said: «The matter is faster than that.»"],[2531,"The Prophet ﷺ passed by us while we were repairing a hut of ours. He said: «What is this?» We said: A hut of ours that has become dilapidated, so we are repairing it. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: «I see the matter only as swifter than that.»"],[2532,"\"The son of Adam grows old, but two things remain young in him: greed for wealth and greed for life.\" *"],[2533,"Whoever believes in Allah and the Last Day should honor his neighbor. Whoever believes in Allah and the Last Day should not enter the bathhouse except with a waist wrapper. Whoever believes in Allah and the Last Day should say good or remain silent. And whoever of your women believes in Allah and the Last Day should not enter the bathhouse."],[2534,"Abd al-Rahman performed ablution in the presence of Aishah, and she said: 'O Abd al-Rahman, complete the ablution, for I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: \"Woe to the heels from the Fire.\"'\""],[2535,"An oath is only either a sin or a regret."],[2536,"He used to lighten the two rak'ahs of Fajr."],[2537,"The one who drinks from vessels of gold and silver only gurgles the fire of Hell into his inside."],[2538,"\"No one opens a door of begging for himself, except Allah opens a door of poverty upon him. If a man takes a rope to a mountain, gathers firewood on his back, and eats from it, it is better for him than asking people, whether they give or refuse.\""],[2539,"The likeness of one who helps his people in wrongdoing is like a camel that fell into a well and is being pulled out by its tail."],[2540,"For one of you to sit on a live coal that burns his clothes until it reaches his skin is better for him than sitting on a grave."],[2541,"'Umar b. al-Khattab went out to Syria until when he was at Sargh, the commanders of the armies met him: Abu 'Ubayda b. al-Jarrah and his companions. They informed him that the plague had occurred in Syria. Ibn 'Abbas said: 'Umar said, \"Call for me the earliest Muhajirun.\" So I called them, and he consulted them and informed them that the plague had occurred in Syria. They differed. Some of them said, \"You have set out for a matter, so we do not think you should turn back from it.\" Others said, \"With you are the rest of the people and the companions of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and we do not think you should bring them forward to this plague.\" He said, \"Leave me.\" Then he said, \"Call for me the Ansar.\" So I called them, and he consulted them. They followed the path of the Muhajirun and differed just as they had differed. He said, \"Leave me.\" Then he said, \"Call for me whoever is here from the elders of Quraysh who were among the Muhajirun of the conquest.\" So I called them, and no two of them differed. They said, \"We think you should return with the people and not bring them forward to this plague.\" 'Umar called out among the people, \"I am departing in the morning, so depart in the morning.\" Abu 'Ubayda b. al-Jarrah said, \"Fleeing from the decree of Allah?\" 'Umar said, \"If only someone else had said it, O Abu 'Ubayda!\" 'Umar disliked opposing him. \"We flee from the decree of Allah to the decree of Allah. Do you think if you had camels and they descended into a valley that had two sides, one fertile and the other barren: if you grazed them in the fertile side, you would graze them by the decree of Allah; and if you grazed them in the barren side, you would graze them by the decree of Allah?\" He said, \"Yes.\""],[2542,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ mentioned the plague and said, \"It is a remnant of punishment and torment that was sent upon a group of the Children of Israel. When it occurs in a land while you are there, do not flee from it; and when it is in a land, do not descend upon it.\""],[2543,"Insulting a Muslim is wickedness, and fighting him is disbelief."],[2544,"The adulterer does not commit adultery while he is a believer, nor does the thief steal while he is a believer, nor does he drink wine while he is a believer, nor does he plunder a plunder of noble worth upon which the Muslims raise their eyes while he is plundering it as a believer."],[2545,"Do not return after me to being disbelievers, striking one another's necks."],[2546,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ led us in the morning prayer at al-Hudaybiyyah following a rain that had fallen at night. When he finished, he turned to the people and said: 'Do you know what your Lord has said?' They said: Allah and His Messenger know best. He said: 'Some of My servants have become believers in Me and disbelievers this morning. As for the one who said: We were given rain by the grace and mercy of Allah, that one believes in Me and disbelieves in the star. As for the one who said: We were given rain by such-and-such a star, that one disbelieves in Me and believes in the stars.'"],[2547,"I said: O Messenger of Allah, my mother left a will that we free a slave on her behalf, and I have a black slave girl. He said: 'Call her.' She came, and he said: 'Who is your Lord?' She said: Allah. He said: 'Who am I?' She said: The Messenger of Allah. He said: 'Free her, for she is a believer.'"],[2548,"Faith is seventy-some branches, and modesty is part of faith."],[2549,"Faith has seventy-odd branches; the highest of them is the testimony that there is no god but Allah, and the lowest of them is removing harm from the road."],[2550,"A man entered the mosque on Friday while the Messenger of Allah ﷺ was on the pulpit. He called him and ordered him to pray two rakʿahs. Then he said, “Give charity.” So they gave charity. He ﷺ gave him two garments from what they had given. Then he said, “Give charity.” So the man threw one of his two garments aside. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ disliked what he did and said, “Look at this man: he entered the mosque in shabby appearance, and I hoped that you would notice him and give charity to him, but you did not. So I said, ‘Give charity,’ and they gave him two garments. Then I said, ‘Give charity,’ and he threw one of his two garments aside. Take your garment.” And he rebuked him."],[2551,"Wine is from these two trees: the date palm and the grapevine."],[2552,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ was asked about al-bitʿ, and he said, 'Every drink that intoxicates is unlawful.'"],[2553,"Every intoxicant is unlawful, and every intoxicant is wine."],[2554,"Every intoxicant is unlawful for every believer."],[2555,"\"Every intoxicant is unlawful, and whatever a farq of it intoxicates, a handful of it is unlawful.\""],[2556,"I heard Umar on the pulpit of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ saying: “To proceed, O people: the prohibition of wine was revealed, and it was from five things: grapes, dates, honey, wheat, and barley. And wine is what intoxicates the mind. Three things, O people, I wish the Messenger of Allah ﷺ had not departed from us until he had left us a definitive instruction about them that we could follow: al-kalala, al-jadd, and some categories of riba.”"],[2558,"“If I were invited to a foreleg, I would respond, and if it were gifted to me, I would accept.”"],[2559,"The Prophet ﷺ returned from a journey, and I had a curtain with images on it, which I placed over my shelf. She said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ took it and pulled it away, saying, \"Will you cover the wall?\" So I made it into two cushions, and I saw the Messenger of Allah ﷺ reclining on them."],[2560,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ sent us to al-Huraqah of Juhaynah. We raided the people in the morning and defeated them. He said: I and a man from the Ansar caught up with one of their men. When we overwhelmed him, he said, \"There is no god but Allah.\" The Ansari withheld from him, but I stabbed him with my spear and killed him. When we returned, that reached the Prophet ﷺ. He said, \"O Usamah, you killed him after he said 'There is no god but Allah'?\" He said: I said, \"O Messenger of Allah, he only said it to protect himself.\" He said, \"You stabbed him after he said 'There is no god but Allah'?\" He kept repeating it until I wished I had not become Muslim before that day."],[2561,"The morning prayer was announced, so I stood up to pray the two rak'ahs. The Prophet ﷺ took me by the hand and said, “Will you pray the morning prayer four times?”"],[2562,"When the prayer is established, there is no prayer except the obligatory one."],[2563,"I went on the expedition of hardship with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and it was the most reliable of my deeds in my own estimation. I had a hired man who fought with someone, and one of them bit the other, so he pulled out his finger, and his two front teeth fell out. He came to the Prophet ﷺ, and he declared his front teeth void. He said: I think Safwan said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"Would he leave his hand in your mouth so you can bite it as a stallion bites?\""],[2564,"\"My wife has given birth to a black boy.\" The Messenger of Allah said: \"Do you have camels?\" He said: \"Yes.\" He said: \"What color are they?\" He said: \"Red.\" He said: \"Are there any gray ones among them?\" He said: \"There are some gray ones among them.\" He said: \"Where do you think they come from?\" He said: \"Perhaps it is hereditary.\" He said: \"Likewise, perhaps this is hereditary.\" (Using translation from Nasāʾī 3478)"],[2565,"I and Maymunah were with the Prophet ﷺ when Ibn Umm Maktum came asking permission to enter, and that was after the hijab had been imposed. He said: “Get up.” We said, “He is blind and cannot see us.” He said: “Are you two blind, that you cannot see him?!” *"],[2566,"“A woman must not travel more than three days except with a dhu-mahram.”"],[2567,"“A woman must not travel a journey of three days or more except with her father, her son, her brother, her husband, or a dhu-mahram.”"],[2568,"“It is not lawful for a woman to travel three [days] unless she has with her a dhu-mahram who is forbidden to her.”"],[2569,"“It is not lawful for a woman to travel three [days] unless she has with her a dhu-mahram of hers.”"],[2570,"It is not lawful for a woman who believes in Allah and the Last Day to travel a distance of three nights unless she has a dhu-mahram with her."],[2571,"A woman may not travel two days and two nights except with a husband or a dhu-mahram."],[2572,"A woman may not travel two days of the entire time except with her husband or a dhu-mahram from her."],[2573,"It is not lawful for a woman who believes in Allah and the Last Day to travel a distance of a day and a night except with a dhu-mahram from her."],[2574,"It is not lawful for a woman who believes in Allah and the Last Day to travel a single day without a dhu-mahram with her."],[2575,"\"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ commanded us to pray four rak'ahs after Jumu'ah.\""],[2576,"It is not lawful for a Muslim woman to travel a distance of a night unless with her is a man with whom she has a forbidden degree."],[2577,"It is not lawful for a woman who believes in Allah and the Last Day to travel a distance of three nights unless she has a dhu-mahram with her."],[2578,"A man must not be alone with a woman, and she may not travel except with a dhu-mahram with her."],[2579,"“A man should not be alone with a woman unless there is a mahram with her.” A man stood up and said: “O Messenger of Allah, I have been enlisted in such-and-such a campaign, and my wife has set out for Hajj.” He said: “Go and perform Hajj with your wife.”"],[2580,"“It is not lawful for a woman to travel except with a mahram.”"],[2581,"His father asked the Messenger of Allah ﷺ for permission regarding the cupper's tax, but he refused to grant him permission, and he persisted until he said: \"Feed it to your slaves and give it as fodder to your water-carrying camel.\""],[2582,"Do not name your slave Aflah, Najih, Rabah, or Yasar, and make sure you do not add to it."],[2583,"Do not ever name your boy Rabah, Najih, Yasar, or Aflah. It is only four, so do not add to it."],[2584,"Women do not have the middle of the road."],[2585,"When one of you stands at night and the Quran becomes unclear on his tongue and he does not know what he is saying, let him lie down."],[2586,"Beware of continuous fasting, beware of continuous fasting. They said: But you practice continuous fasting, O Messenger of Allah. He said: I am not in that like you; I pass the night while my Lord feeds me and gives me drink, so take on of deeds what you have strength for."],[2587,"From the Prophet ﷺ, it is narrated that he forbade excessive socialization. It was said to him, \"But you maintain frequent communication with people.\" He replied, \"You are not like me. I have a sustainer who feeds me and gives me drink. So, whoever amongst you continues to maintain constant communication, it is from one magic spell to another.\""],[2588,"He prohibited vowing."],[2589,"\"Do not make vows, for a vow does not repel anything from destiny; it only extracts from the miser.\""],[2590,"\"A vow does not repel anything, but it extracts from the miser.\""],[2591,"“Do not reserve your properties as ruqba; whoever gives something as ruqba, it belongs to the one to whom he gave it.”"],[2592,"Do not give ruqba or give 'umra; whoever gives 'umra for something or gives ruqba, it belongs to [the recipient]."],[2594,"The 'umra belongs to the one to whom it is given."],[2595,"The 'umra is permissible."],[2596,"There is no 'umra; whoever gives 'umra for something, it belongs to him."],[2597,"The 'umra is to be treated like inheritance."],[2598,"The Prophet ﷺ ruled that the 'umra belongs to the heir."],[2599,"Whoever is given 'umra of land, it belongs to his heirs."],[2600,"The 'umra belongs to the one to whom it is given; it is his and for his descendants; those who inherit from him inherit it."],[2601,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to the Ansar: \"Do not give 'umra of your properties; whoever is given 'umra of something for his lifetime, it belongs to him and to his heirs when he dies.\""],[2602,"Any man who is given 'umra for himself and his descendants, it belongs to the one who was given it; it does not return to the one who gave it, because he gave a gift in which inheritance takes effect."],[2603,"Whoever gives a man 'umra for him and his descendants, his statement has cut off his own right to it, and it belongs to the one given 'umra and his descendants."],[2604,"When one of you stands at night and the Quran becomes unclear on his tongue and he does not know what he is saying, let him lie down."],[2606,"Hold onto your wealth and do not give it as 'umra, for whoever is given a thing as 'umra, it belongs to him during his life and to his heirs when he dies."],[2607,"While the Prophet ﷺ was sitting among the people, a man came to him asking permission to speak with him privately. He spoke privately with him about killing a man from the hypocrites. The Prophet ﷺ raised his voice with his words and said: \"Does he not testify that there is no god but Allah?\" He said: \"Yes, O Messenger of Allah, but his testimony is nothing.\" He said: \"Does he not testify that I am the Messenger of Allah?\" He said: \"Yes, O Messenger of Allah, but his testimony is nothing.\" He said: \"Does he not pray?\" He said: \"Yes, but his prayer is nothing.\" The Prophet ﷺ said: \"Those are the ones I was forbidden from.\""],[2608,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ drew back the curtain while the people were in rows behind Abu Bakr and said, “O people, nothing remains of the glad tidings of prophethood except the true dream a Muslim sees or is seen for him.” Then he said, “Verily, I have been forbidden from reciting while bowing or prostrating. As for bowing, magnify the Lord therein; and as for prostration, strive in supplication, for it is likely to be answered for you.”"],[2609,"'Three persons will not be asked about: a man who separated from the community and disobeyed his imam and died disobedient; a slave woman or slave who fled from his master and died; and a woman whose husband was absent after he had provided her with the means of the world, and she betrayed him after him. And three will not be asked about: a man who contends with Allah over His cloak, for His cloak is pride and His lower garment is might; a man in doubt about the affair of Allah; and one who despairs of the mercy of Allah.'"],[2610,"\"The worst of people is the two-faced one who comes to these with one face and to those with another.\""],[2611,"\"Among the worst of people is the two-faced one who comes to these with one face and to those with another.\""],[2612,"\"Whoever is two-faced in this world will have two tongues of fire on the Day of Resurrection.\""],[2613,"Every sermon that does not contain the testimony is like a maimed hand."],[2614,"The heaviest thing placed in the believer's scale on the Day of Resurrection is a good character. Indeed, Allah hates the obscene, foul-mouthed person."],[2615,"\"Allah will not look at a man who comes to a woman in her anus.\""],[2616,"\"Indeed Allah hates every arrogant, rude, loud-mouthed person in the markets, a corpse by night, a donkey by day, knowledgeable in worldly affairs, ignorant of the affairs of the Hereafter.\""],[2617,"I heard the Prophet ﷺ saying, \"Shall I tell you of the people of Paradise? They comprise every poor humble person, and if he swears by Allah to do something, Allah will fulfill it; while the people of the fire comprise every violent, cruel arrogant person.\" (Using translation from Bukhārī 6657)"],[2618,"ʿAʾidh b. ʿAmr, who was one of the companions of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, entered upon ʿUbayd Allah b. Ziyad and said, 'O my son, I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say, \"Indeed the worst of shepherds are the harsh ones, so beware of being one of them.\"' He said, 'Sit, for you are but from the chaff of the companions of Muhammad ﷺ.' He said, 'Was there any chaff among them? Chaff only came after them and among others.'"],[2619,"The worst thing in a man is an intense greed and a cowardice that flees."],[2620,"\"None hoards except a sinner.\""],[2621,"“It is enough sin for a man to neglect those whose maintenance is his duty.”"],[2622,"We were sitting with ʿAbd Allāh b. ʿAmr when his steward came to him and entered. He said: Have you given the slaves their sustenance? He said: No. He said: Go and give them, for the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “It is enough sin for a man to withhold sustenance from those he owns.”"],[2623,"Among the worst of people are those whom the Hour overtakes and those who take graves as mosques."],[2624,"May Allah destroy the Jews; they took the graves of their prophets as mosques."],[2625,"No people sit in a sitting where they do not mention Allah and send blessings upon the Prophet ﷺ except that it will be a regret for them on the Day of Resurrection, even if they enter Paradise."],[2626,"“Indeed, sadaqah is not lawful for a rich person, nor for one who is able-bodied and strong.”"],[2627,"I was with Qabisa b. al-Mukhariq when a group of his people sought his help for the marriage of a man of his people, but he refused to give them anything. So they went away from him. Kinanah said: I said to him: 'You are the chief of your people, and they came to you asking, yet you gave them nothing?' He said: 'As for this, I will not give anything, and I will tell you about that. I incurred a debt of reconciliation among my people, so I came to the Prophet ﷺ and informed him, and asked him to help me. He said: \"Rather, we will bear it on your behalf, O Qabisa, and we will pay it to them from the camels of zakah.\" Then he said: \"Indeed, asking is not lawful except for three: a man who has incurred a debt of reconciliation, so it becomes lawful for him until he pays it; or a man afflicted by a calamity that destroyed his wealth, until he obtains a means of livelihood or a sufficiency of livelihood; or a man stricken by poverty, and three men of sound judgment from his people testify that poverty has indeed befallen him, so asking becomes lawful for him until he obtains a means of livelihood or a sufficiency of livelihood. And asking in other than these cases is unlawful gain.\"\""],[2628,"A man recited behind the Prophet ﷺ during Zuhr or ‘Asr. He said: “Which of you recited ‘Glorify the name of your Lord, the Most High’?” A man from the people said: I did. He said: “I knew that some of you were contending with me over it.”"],[2629,"A man recited behind the Prophet ﷺ during Zuhr or ‘Asr—Abu ‘Awanah was uncertain—and he said: “Which of you recited ‘Glorify the name of your Lord, the Most High’?” A man from the people said: I did. He said: “I knew that some of you were contending with me over it.”"],[2630,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ prayed Zuhr, and a man began to recite behind him: “Glorify the name of your Lord, the Most High.” When he finished, he said: “Which of you recited? Or which of you is the reciter?” A man said: I, O Messenger of Allah. He said: “I knew that some of you were contending with me over it.”"],[2631,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ led us in the morning prayer, and the recitation became heavy upon him. When he finished, he said: “I see that you recite behind your imam.” We said: Yes, by Allah, O Messenger of Allah, quickly. He said: “Do not do so, except with the Mother of the Book, for there is no prayer for one who does not recite it.”"],[2632,"I was not commanded to build lofty mosques."],[2633,"A man came to the Messenger of Allahﷺ and said, \"I have married a woman.\" He asked, \"How much did you give as mahr (dowry)?\" The man replied, \"Four awqiya (a measurement of weight).\" The Prophetﷺ said, \"Four awqiya, it is as if you are carving silver from the width of this mountain.\""],[2634,"\"A false oath sells the goods but wipes out the profit.\""],[2635,"\"There are three whom Allah will not speak to, nor look at, on the Day of Resurrection, nor purify them, and they will have a painful punishment.\" I said, \"O Messenger of Allah, who are they? They have failed and lost.\" He repeated it, and I said, \"Who are they?\" He said, \"The one who lets his garment hang below his ankles, the one who reminds others of his gifts, and the one who sells his goods by swearing falsely.\""],[2636,"\"Whoever wakes up at night and says when he awakens: 'There is no god but Allah alone with no partner; His is the dominion and His is the praise, and He is able to do all things. Glory be to Allah, praise be to Allah, there is no god but Allah, and Allah is greatest. There is no might and no power except with Allah. My Lord, forgive me,' he will be forgiven. And if he stands, performs ablution, and prays, his prayer will be accepted.\""],[2637,"It was said to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ: So-and-so does not break his fast during the day all year except at night. He ﷺ said: He has neither fasted nor broken his fast."],[2638,"There is no contagion and no evil omen, but I like good omens."],[2639,"'There is no Tiyarah, and the best of Fa'l is a good word that one of you hears.'"],[2640,"I asked Sa'd b. Abi Waqqas about believing in omens in birds (tayarah)? He said: I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: 'There is no contagion, and no bird omen, and no hamah (death-owl). If there is any bird omen in anything, it is in the woman, the horse, and the house.'"],[2641,"'There is no contagion, no Safar, and no Hamah.' A bedouin said: O Messenger of Allah, what about camels that are in the sand like gazelles, then a mangy camel comes and enters among them and makes them mangy? He said: 'Then who infected the first one?'"],[2642,"'There is no Tiyarah, no Hamah, no contagion, and no Safar.' A man said: O Messenger of Allah, we take a mangy sheep and throw it among the flock, and the flock becomes mangy? The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: 'Then who infected the first one?'"],[2643,"'There is no contagion, no hamah (death-owl), no safar (month of Safar), and no naw' (rain star).'"],[2644,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: 'There is no contagion.' And he also related that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: 'A sick (animal) should not be brought to a healthy one.' Abu Salamah said: Abu Hurayrah used to narrate both of these from the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. Then afterwards Abu Hurayrah became silent about his saying 'There is no contagion,' and he maintained that 'a sick (animal) should not be brought to a healthy one.' Al-Harith b. Abi Dhi'ab, who was the cousin of Abu Hurayrah, said: I used to hear you, O Abu Hurayrah, narrate to us along with this hadith another hadith which you have now stopped narrating. You used to say: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: 'There is no contagion.' Abu Hurayrah refused to acknowledge that and said: 'A sick (animal) should not be brought to a healthy one.' Abu Salamah said: By my life, Abu Hurayrah used to narrate to us that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: 'There is no contagion.' I do not know whether Abu Hurayrah forgot or whether one of the two statements abrogated the other."],[2645,"'There is no contagion, and no safar (month of Safar), and no ghoul.'"],[2646,"A man should not bargain over the bargain of his brother, nor should a man propose over the proposal of his brother, nor should a woman ask for the divorce of her sister in order to overturn what is in her plate.\""],[2647,"\"A woman is not to be combined in marriage with her paternal aunt, nor a woman with her maternal aunt.\""],[2648,"When Allah, Mighty and Majestic, granted His Messenger ﷺ victory over Makkah, Hudhayl killed a man from Banu Layth in retaliation for a slain man of theirs in the pre-Islamic era. That reached the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, so he stood and said: \"Allah, Mighty and Majestic, withheld the elephant from Makkah and gave His Messenger and the believers authority over it. It was not lawful for anyone before me, nor will it be lawful for anyone after me. It was only made lawful for me for an hour of the day, and it is this hour of mine. Then it is sacred: its trees may not be cut, its thorns may not be uprooted, and its fallen items may not be picked up except by one who announces them. Whoever has a slain relative has the better of two options: either to kill or to accept blood money.\" A man from Yemen called Abu Shah stood and said, \"O Messenger of Allah, write it down for me.\" The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"Write it down for Abu Shah.\" Then al-'Abbas stood and said, \"O Messenger of Allah, except idhkhir (a kind of grass), for we use it in our graves and our houses.\" The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"Except idhkhir.\""],[2649,"He asked Jabir b. 'Abd Allah: “We have sheep and boys, and they beat down for their sheep this fruit, the hablah, which is the fruit of the samur tree.” Jabir said: “No.” Then he said: “Neither should it be beaten down nor cut within the sacred precinct of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, but shake it gently.” Then he said: “The Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to forbid us to cut the masad or the pulley-rod of the she-camel’s saddle.”"],[2650,"He mentioned sacrificial animals and said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ gestured with his hand, and my hand is shorter than his hand, and said: \"Four are not to be sacrificed: the one-eyed whose blindness is evident, the sick whose sickness is evident, the lame whose lameness is evident, and the emaciated one that has no marrow.\" They said to al-Bara': \"We only dislike defects in age, ear, and tail.\" He said: \"Dislike whatever you wish, but do not forbid it to the people.\""],[2651,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ bade farewell to a man and said, 'Where do you intend to go?' He said, 'I intend to go to the Holy House.' The Prophet ﷺ said, 'A prayer in this mosque is better than a hundred prayers in any other except the Sacred Mosque.'"],[2652,"I witnessed the Eid with Umar ibn al-Khattab. He came, prayed, then turned and addressed the people, saying, \"These are two days during which the Messenger of Allah ﷺ prohibited fasting: the day of your breaking the fast and the other day when you eat from your sacrifices.\" Abu Ubaid said, \"Then I witnessed the Eid with Uthman ibn Affan. He came, prayed, then turned and addressed the people, saying, 'Today, two Eids have coincided for you. Whoever from the residents of the higher areas wishes to wait for the Friday prayer, let him wait, and whoever wishes to return, let him return, for I have granted him permission.' Abu Ubaid said, \"Then I witnessed the Eid with Ali ibn Abi Talib while Uthman was present. He came, prayed, then turned and addressed the people.\""],[2653,"There is no continuous fasting in fasting."],[2654,"\"No far' and no 'atirah.\""],[2655,"Ibn ʿAbbās came to Ibn ʿUmar and greeted him. He said, “Do you accuse Usāmah?” He said, “Ibn ʿUmar said: No.” He said, “Then indeed he...”"],[2656,"The Prophet ﷺ took a pledge from the women when they gave him their allegiance that they would not wail. They said, 'O Messenger of Allah, there are women who helped us in wailing during Jahiliyyah; shall we help them in Islam?' The Prophet ﷺ said, 'There is no helping in wailing in Islam, and no shighar marriage in Islam, and no hamstringing of animals in Islam, and no jalab and no janab, and whoever plunders is not one of us.'"],[2657,"No driving of livestock from their pastures to the collector's place, no leading them away, no shighar marriage, and whoever plunders a raid is not one of us."],[2658,"Qays b. 'Asim asked the Prophet ﷺ about alliances, so he said: \"There is no alliance in Islam.\""],[2659,"\"There is no alliance in Islam, and whatever alliance existed in the pre-Islamic era, Islam only increases it in strength or intensity.\""],[2660,"\"There is no alliance in Islam, and whatever alliance existed in the pre-Islamic era, Islam only increases it in strength.\""],[2661,"\"There is no alliance in Islam, and whatever alliance existed in the pre-Islamic era, Islam only increases it in strength.\""],[2662,"\"I witnessed with my paternal uncles the alliance of the perfumed ones, and I would not love to have red camels in exchange for breaking it.\""],[2663,"\"I did not witness any alliance of Quraysh except the alliance of the perfumed ones, and I would not love to have red camels in exchange for having broken it.\" He said: \"And the perfumed ones are Hashim, Umayyah, Zuhrah, and Makhzum.\""],[2664,"We used to sell jamʿ dates, two ṣāʿs for one ṣāʿ of janīb dates. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “No two ṣāʿs of dates for one ṣāʿ of dates, nor two ṣāʿs of wheat for one ṣāʿ of wheat, nor two dirhams for one dirham.”"],[2665,"My father visited me one day in Ramadan, and he stayed with us and broke his fast. Then he prayed with us that night and performed the Witr prayer. After that, he went down to his mosque and prayed with his companions. Then a man came forward and said, \"Perform Witr with your companions, for I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ saying, 'There should not be two Witr prayers in one night.'\""],[2666,"We came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and prayed with him. He glanced from the corner of his eye at a man who did not make his back straight in bowing and prostration. He said: \"There is no prayer for one who does not make his back straight.\""],[2667,"There is no prayer for one who does not recite the Mother of the Qur'an and more."],[2668,"There is no marriage except with a guardian."],[2669,"“No one is flogged more than ten lashes except for a hadd among the hadd punishments of Allah.”"],[2670,"There is no protected grazing area except for Allah and His Messenger."],[2671,"There is no protected grazing area except for Allah and His Messenger."],[2672,"\"There is no obedience to a human in disobedience to Allah.\""],[2673,"There is no fulfillment of a vow in disobedience, and no fulfillment of a vow in what the slave—or the son of Adam—does not own."],[2674,"There is no fasting after the middle of Sha'ban until the month of Ramadan comes."],[2675,"The Messenger of God ﷺ stood and addressed the people, saying: \"No, by God, I do not fear for you, O people, except what God brings out for you of the splendor of this world.\" A man said, \"O Messenger of God, does good come with evil?\" The Messenger of God ﷺ remained silent for a while, then said, \"What did you say?\" He said, \"I said, O Messenger of God, does good come with evil?\" The Messenger of God ﷺ said to him: \"Good does not come except with good. But it is that everything the spring rain causes to grow kills by bloating or nearly kills, except for the eater of green plants: it eats until when its flanks are full, it faces the sun, then defecates and urinates, then chews the cud and returns to eat. Whoever takes wealth by his right will be blessed in it, and whoever takes wealth without his right, his example is like one who eats but is not satisfied.\""],[2676,"While the Messenger of God ﷺ was addressing the people, he said: \"Among what I fear for you is what will be opened for you of the splendor of this world and its adornment.\" A man stood and said, \"O Messenger of God, does good come with evil?\" Abu Sa'id said: We saw revelation descending upon the Messenger of God ﷺ, and we blamed the man for speaking to the Messenger of God ﷺ while he did not speak to him. When it was lifted from the Messenger of God ﷺ, he began wiping the sweat from his face, saying, \"Where is the questioner?\" It was as if he praised him, then he said: \"Good does not come with evil. Indeed, some of what the spring rain causes to grow kills by bloating or nearly kills, except for the eater of green plants: it eats until when its flanks are full, it faces the sun, then defecates and urinates. This wealth is an excellent companion for a Muslim who takes it by his right and gives from it to the orphan, the needy, and the beggar. Whoever takes it without his right is like one who eats but is not satisfied, then it will be a witness against him on the Day of Resurrection.\""],[2677,"I said, 'O Messenger of God, a man from my people insults me while he is inferior to me. Is there any blame on me if I defend myself against him?' He said, 'The two revilers are two devils who hurl abuse at each other and lie to each other.'"],[2678,"When one of you is praying, let him not allow anyone to pass in front of him, and let him repel him as much as he can. If he insists, then let him fight him, for he is only a devil."],[2679,"Indeed, the two revilers—whatever they say—it is upon the one who initiated it, as long as the wronged one does not transgress."],[2680,"The lower garment was mentioned, so I came to Abu Sa'id al-Khudri and said, \"Tell me about the lower garment.\" He said, \"Yes, with knowledge: I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say, 'The lower garment of the believer is to the middle of his shins, and there is no blame on him for what is between that and the ankles. Whatever is below that is in the Fire. Whoever drags his lower garment out of arrogance, Allah will not look at him.'\""],[2681,"\"Whoever deceives us is not of us, and plotting and deception are in the Fire.\""],[2682,"«Adhere to truthfulness, for it goes with righteousness, and they are both in Paradise. Beware of lying, for it goes with wickedness, and they are both in the Fire.»"],[2683,"Obscenity is from coarseness, and coarseness is in the Fire. Modesty is from faith, and faith is in Paradise."],[2684,"He gifted a wild donkey to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ at al-Abwāʾ or Waddān. He said: “The Messenger of Allah ﷺ returned it to me, and that distressed me. When he recognized that in my face, he said: ‘It is not that we are returning it to you, but we are in a state of iḥrām.’”"],[2685,"A man looked in from a hole into the Prophet's room, and the Prophet ﷺ had a comb with which he was scratching his head. The Prophet ﷺ saw him and said, \"If I knew that you were looking, I would have thrust it into your eye. Permission has been made only for the sake of sight.\""],[2686,"«Indeed, part of the excellence of a person's Islam is his leaving what does not concern him.»"],[2687,"I am only human, and perhaps some of you are more eloquent in presenting his argument than others. Whoever I judge in his favor with something from his brother's right, I am only cutting off for him a piece of the Fire."],[2688,"A man said, “O Allah, forgive me and Muhammad alone.” The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, “You have veiled it from many people.”"],[2689,"A man came to the Prophet ﷺ wearing an iron ring, so he said, \"Why do I see on you the ornament of the people of the Fire?\" So he threw it away. Then he came wearing a ring of brass, so he said, \"Why do I find on you the smell of idols?\" He said, \"O Messenger of Allah, from what should I make it?\" He replied, \"From silver, but do not make it a full mithqal.\""],[2690,"A man came from Najran to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ wearing a gold ring, so the Messenger of Allah ﷺ turned away from him and did not ask him about anything. The man returned to his wife and told her, and she said, \"There is something about you. Go back to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and throw away the ring.\" When he sought permission, he was granted it, and he greeted the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, who returned his greeting. He said, \"O Messenger of Allah, you turned away from me.\" The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, \"You came to me with a live coal from the Fire in your hand.\" He said, \"O Messenger of Allah, then I have brought many coals.\" He had brought ornaments from al-Bahrayn. The Prophet ﷺ said, \"What you have brought is not sufficient for us at all, except as the stones of the harrah are sufficient, but it is the goods of the life of this world.\" The man said, \"Excuse me before your companions so they do not think you are angry with me for some reason.\" So the Messenger of Allah ﷺ rose and excused him, and explained that what had happened had only been because of his ring."],[2691,"'Abd al-Malik used to send for Umm al-Darda', and sometimes she would stay overnight with him. He said: 'Abd al-Malik called a servant, and the servant was slow, so he said: «O Allah, curse him.» She said: «Do not curse him, for I heard Abu al-Darda' narrate from the Messenger of Allah ﷺ that he said: 'Those who curse excessively will not be witnesses or intercessors on the Day of Resurrection.'»"],[2692,"If a man says to his companion, 'Be quiet,' while the imam is delivering the sermon, he has engaged in idle talk."],[2693,"“The gates of Paradise are opened on Monday and Thursday, and forgiveness is granted to whoever does not associate anything with Allah, except the two who have deserted each other. He says, ‘Return these two until they reconcile.’”"],[2694,"Whoever kills a sparrow in vain, it will cry out to Allah on the Day of Resurrection, saying, 'O Lord, so-and-so killed me in vain and did not kill me for any benefit.'"],[2695,"'Al-iyafah (fortune-telling by birds), al-tiyarah (bird omens), and al-tarq (geomancy) are from al-jibt (devil worship).'"],[2696,"A man made bequests that he confirmed in his wealth, so I went to al-Qasim b. Muhammad to consult him. Al-Qasim said: I heard A'ishah say: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: Whoever introduces into this matter of ours what is not from it, it is rejected."],[2697,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, \"Two should not converse secretly without a third person.\""],[2698,"“The one who takes back his gift is like the one who goes back to his vomit.”"],[2699,"“The example of the one who gives charity then takes it back is like the dog that vomits then returns and eats its vomit.”"],[2700,"“It is not lawful for a man to give a gift or grant then take it back, except a father in what he gives his child. The example of the one who gives a gift or grant then takes it back is like the dog that eats until it is full, then vomits, then returns to its vomit.”"],[2701,"That Umar b. al-Khattab gave a horse of his to be ridden in the cause of Allah, then he found it being sold. He wanted to buy it, so he asked the Messenger of Allah ﷺ about that. He said, “Do not buy it, and do not take back your charity.”"],[2702,"I gave a horse to be ridden in the cause of Allah, and the one who had it neglected it. I wanted to buy it from him, and I thought that he would sell it cheaply. I asked the Messenger of Allah ﷺ about that, and he said, “Do not buy it, even if he gives it to you for a single dirham, for the one who takes back his charity is like the dog that returns to its vomit.”"],[2703,"The Prophet ﷺ once gave a sermon to women and advised them to fear Allah and obey their husbands. He said, \"Among you, some will enter Paradise while joining their fingers, and others will enter Hell while separating their fingers.\" The women asked, \"O Messenger of Allah, why is that?\" He replied, \"You curse frequently, and you are ungrateful and show ingratitude for the good done to you.\""],[2704,"“I return to my family and find a date fallen, then I pick it up to eat it. Then I fear that it might be sadaqah, so I throw it away.”"],[2705,"A man entered the mosque after the prayer had been commenced, and the Prophet ﷺ was praying. The man prayed two rakʿahs, then joined the row. When the Prophet ﷺ finished, he said: \"By which of them have you counted, or by which of them have you sought reward? The one you prayed with us, or the one you prayed alone?\""],[2706,"The Messenger of God ﷺ prayed the dawn prayer [fajr]. Then a man came and prayed two rakʿahs of the dawn prayer behind him, then joined the congregation. When the Messenger of God ﷺ finished his prayer, he said to the man: \"Which of them did you make your prayer: the one you prayed alone, or the one you prayed with us?\""],[2707,"\"When the obligatory prayer is commenced, there is no prayer except the obligatory prayer.\""],[2708,"\"When the muezzin begins the iqāmah, there is no prayer except the obligatory prayer.\""],[2709,"The Prophet ﷺ passed by some people passing an unsheathed sword among themselves and said: “Did I not forbid you from this? Let him sheathe it and then hand it to his brother.”"],[2710,"The Prophet ﷺ saw a donkey that had been branded on its face and said, “Did I not forbid this?! May Allah curse the one who did it.”"],[2711,"The earnings of the cupper are impure, the price of a dog is impure, and the dower of an adulteress is impure."],[2712,"The earnings of the cupper are impure, the dower of an adulteress is impure, and the price of a dog is impure."],[2713,"“Does not the one who raises his head before the imam fear that Allah will turn his head into the head of a donkey?”"],[2714,"“Does not the one who raises his head before the imam fear that Allah will turn his head into the head of a dog?”"],[2715,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ stood among us one day and mentioned ghulul (misappropriation of spoils), and he emphasized its gravity. Then he said, \"O people, let me not find any one of you coming on the Day of Resurrection with a camel on his neck that bellows, and he says, 'O Messenger of Allah, help me!' and I say, 'I can do nothing for you; I had conveyed to you.' Let me not find any one of you coming on the Day of Resurrection with a sheep on his neck that bleats, and he says, 'O Messenger of Allah, help me!' and I say, 'I can do nothing for you; I had conveyed to you.' Let me not find any one of you coming on the Day of Resurrection with a horse on his neck that neighs, and he says, 'O Messenger of Allah, help me!' and I say, 'I can do nothing for you; I had conveyed to you.' And let me not find any one of you coming on the Day of Resurrection with a soul on his neck that cries out, and he says, 'O Messenger of Allah, help me!' and I say, 'I can do nothing for you; I had conveyed to you.' Let me not find any one of you coming on the Day of Resurrection with fluttering patches on his neck, and he says, 'O Messenger of Allah, help me!' and I say, 'I can do nothing for you; I had conveyed to you.' Let me not find any one of you coming on the Day of Resurrection with silent wealth on his neck, and he says, 'O Messenger of Allah, help me!' and I say, 'I can do nothing for you; I had conveyed to you.'\""],[2716,"No prayer is valid for one who does not keep his backbone straight in bowing and prostration."],[2717,"\"The worst of people in theft is the one who steals from his prayer.\" It was said: \"How does he steal from his prayer?\" He said: \"He does not complete its bowing or its prostration.\""],[2718,"Hudhayfah saw a man at the gates of Kindah pecking [in prayer], so he said, “Since when have you been praying this prayer?” He said, “For forty years?” He said, “If you were to die, you would die upon other than the fiṭrah upon which Muhammad ﷺ was created. Indeed, a man may shorten [the prayer] and yet complete the bowing and prostration.”"],[2719,"I heard Anas b. Malik describe to us the prayer of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ: “He would stand and pray, and when he raised his head from bowing, we would think he had forgotten because of the length of standing.”"],[2720,"A prayer in which the Opening of the Book is not recited is not valid.' I said, 'Even if I am behind the imam?' He took my hand and said, 'Recite it to yourself.'"],[2721,"\"The one in ihram does not marry and does not marry off.\""],[2722,"He sent to Aban b. 'Uthman, while Aban was then the commander of the pilgrimage, and they were both in ihram: \"I want to marry Talhah b. 'Umar to the daughter of Shaybah b. Jubayr, and I would like you to attend that.\" Aban b. 'Uthman disapproved of that and said: \"I heard 'Uthman b. 'Affan say: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: 'The one in ihram does not marry, does not propose, and does not marry off.'\""],[2723,"\"The one in ihram does not marry, does not marry off, does not propose, and is not proposed to.\""],[2724,"\"The one in ihram does not marry, does not marry off, and does not propose.\""],[2725,"'Umar b. 'Ubayd Allah b. Ma'mar wanted to marry while in ihram, so he sent to Aban b. 'Uthman. Aban said: \"'Uthman narrated that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: 'The one in ihram does not marry, does not propose, and does not marry off.'\""],[2726,"\"The one in ihram does not marry and does not marry off.\""],[2728,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ \"married Maymunah while not in ihram, and consummated the marriage while not in ihram, and I was the messenger between them.\""],[2729,"When the call to prayer is given, do not come running; come calmly. Pray what you catch up with, and complete what you missed, for one of you is in prayer as long as he is heading to prayer."],[2730,"«By Allah, my heirs will not divide a single dinar. Whatever I leave behind after the expenses of my wives and the provision of my worker is charity.»"],[2731,"When you meet Habbar b. al-Aswad and Nafi b. Abd al-Qays, burn them both with fire. Then afterwards the Prophet ﷺ said: 'None punishes with fire except Allah, but if you meet them, kill them.'"],[2732,"So, I said to my father, \"What were you saying?\" He replied, \"We used to say, 'No one can perform Hajj after the designated year except if they are a polytheist. And no one can perform Tawaf around the Kaaba naked, nor enter Paradise except if they are a believer. And whoever has a gap between themselves and the Messenger of Allah ﷺ must make up for it, and the maximum duration for making up is four months. And once four months have passed, then Allah is free from the polytheists and their beliefs, as well as His Messenger.\" He added, \"The polytheists used to say, 'No, it's just a month,' and they would mockingly laugh about it.\""],[2733,"I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say on the day of the conquest of Makkah: \"No Qurayshi will be killed in restraint after this day until the Day of Resurrection.\" No Muslim encountered any of the disbelievers of Quraysh except Muti'. His name was al-'As, but the Messenger of Allah ﷺ named him Muti'."],[2734,"\"A person should not lie on his back and place one of his legs over the other.\""],[2735,"\"He saw the Messenger of Allah ﷺ lying on his back in the mosque, placing one of his legs over the other.\""],[2736,"He prohibited wrapping oneself in a single garment with no opening, sitting with legs drawn up wrapped in one cloth, and that a man raises one of his legs over the other while lying on his back.\""],[2737,"He prohibited that a man lies on his back and folds one of his legs over the other.\""],[2738,"“I prayed beside Anas b. Mālik between the pillars.” He said: “We used to avoid this in the time of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ.”"],[2739,"Regarding prayer, we stand between the rows and are not to be pushed out of them."],[2740,"I asked Bilāl: “Where did the Messenger of Allah ﷺ pray when he entered the Kaʿbah?” He said: “Between the two front pillars.” He said: And I forgot to ask him how many [rakʿahs] he prayed."],[2741,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ forbade us from cauterization, but we cauterized and were not successful nor did we succeed."],[2742,"\"On the Day of Al-Ahzab (the Confederates), Saad was hit and his eye was injured. It started bleeding and his hand swelled. The Prophet ﷺ cauterized it with fire, stopping the bleeding and reducing the swelling.\""],[2743,"He saw Ibn Umar sitting at al-Balat while the people were praying. I said, \"What keeps you sitting while the people are praying?\" He said, \"I have already prayed. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ forbade us from repeating a prayer twice in one day.\""],[2744,"A man entered the mosque after the Messenger of Allah ﷺ had prayed. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, \"Is there any man who will give charity to this man by praying with him?\""],[2745,"The Prophet ﷺ said: “Be moderate in prostration, and let none of you stretch out his forearms like a dog.”"],[2746,"The companions of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ complained to the Prophet ﷺ about the hardship of prostration upon them, so he said: “Seek help with the knees.”"],[2747,"Concerning a man who divorced his wife three times, then she married another husband, and he divorced her before consummating the marriage; then the first husband wanted to marry her. He said: \"No, until the other tastes her honey and she tastes his honey.\""],[2748,"Rifa'ah b. Samaw'al divorced his wife Tamimah bt. Wahb during the time of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ three times. Then 'Abd al-Rahman b. al-Zubayr married her, but he was unable to touch her, so he separated from her. Rifa'ah, her first husband who had divorced her, wanted to marry her, so he mentioned that to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. He forbade him from marrying her and said: \"She is not lawful for you until she tastes the honey.\""],[2749,"The days of Tashreeq are days of food and remembrance."],[2750,"The day of Arafah, the day of sacrifice, and the days of Tashreeq are our festival, O people of Islam - they are days of eating and drinking."],[2751,"We used to greet the Prophet ﷺ while he was praying, and he would respond to us before we went to the land of Abyssinia. When we returned from the Negus, I came to him while he was praying and greeted him, but he did not return the greeting. I was seized by what was near and what was far, so I sat waiting for him. When he finished the prayer, I said, “O Messenger of Allah, I greeted you while you were praying, but you did not return my greeting.” He said, “Allah brings about whatever He wills of His command, and He has brought about that we should not speak during prayer.”"],[2752,"\"I said: 'O Messenger of Allah ﷺ, we were recently in a state of ignorance, then Allah (SWT) brought Islam. Some men among us follow omens.' He said: 'That is something that they find in their own hearts; it should not deter them from going ahead.' I said: 'And some men among us go to fortune tellers.' He said: 'Do not go to them.' He said: 'Some men among us draw lines.' He said: 'One of the Prophets used to draw lines. So whoever is in accord with his drawing of lines, then so it is.'\" He said: \"While I was praying with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, a man sneezed and I said: 'Yarhamuk-Allah (May Allah have mercy on you).' The people glared at me and I said: 'May my mother be bereft of me, why are you looking at me?' The people struck their hands against their thighs, and when I saw that they were telling me to be quiet, I fell silent. When the Messenger of Allah ﷺ finished, he called me. May my father and mother be ransomed for him, he neither did hit me nor rebuke me nor revile me. I have never seen a better teacher than him, before or after. He said: 'This prayer of ours is not the place for ordinary human speech, rather it is glorification and magnification of Allah (SWT), and reciting Qur'an.' Then I went out to a flock of sheep of mine that was tended by a slave woman of mine beside Uhud and Al-Jawwaniyyah, and I found that the wolf had taken one of the sheep. I am a man from the sons of Adam and I get upset as they get upset. So I slapped her. Then I came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and told him what happened. He regarded that as a serious action on my part. I said: 'O Messenger of Allah ﷺ, should I set her free?' He said: 'Call her.' The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to her: 'Where is Allah (SWT), the Mighty and Sublime?' She said: 'Above the heavens.' He said: 'And who am I?' She said: 'The Messenger of Allah ﷺ.' He said: 'She is a believer, set her free.'\" (Using translation from Nasāʾī 1218)"],[2753,"The Prophet ﷺ said the salutation after two [units] of the afternoon prayer. Dhu al-Yadayn stood up to him and said, 'Has the prayer been shortened, or did you forget?' He said, 'None of that happened.' Then he turned to the people and said, 'Is it as Dhu al-Yadayn says?' They said, 'Yes.' So he completed what remained of the prayer, then said the salutation, then performed the two prostrations of forgetfulness."],[2754,"We used to speak during the prayer about our needs until this verse was revealed: 'Guard strictly the prayers, and the middle prayer, and stand before Allah devoutly obedient.' So we were commanded to remain silent."],[2755,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ prayed for us."],[2757,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ forbade sitting in the open areas of the roads. They said, \"O Messenger of Allah, we cannot avoid that and we cannot endure it.\" He said, \"If you must, then fulfill its right.\" They said, \"What is its right, O Messenger of Allah?\" He said, \"Returning the greeting, invoking mercy upon the one who sneezes when he praises Allah, lowering the gaze, and guiding the way.\""],[2760,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ prayed with us one of the two afternoon prayers. Ibn Sirin said, 'Abu Hurayrah named it for us, but I forgot.' He prayed two [units] with us, then said the salutation. Then he stood up to a wooden plank placed across the mosque, placed his right hand over his left, interlaced his fingers, and leaned on the plank as if he were angry. He said: The swift people left. Al-Nadr said, meaning the first of the people. They said, 'Has the prayer been shortened?' Among the people were Abu Bakr and Umar, but they were too in awe of him to speak to him. Among the people was a man with long hands called Dhu al-Yadayn. He said, 'Has the prayer been shortened, or did you forget?' The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, 'The prayer has not been shortened, and I have not forgotten.' Then he said to the people, 'Is it as Dhu al-Yadayn says?' They said, 'Yes.' So he prayed what he had left, then said the salutation. Then he said the takbir and prostrated similar to his prostration or longer. Then he raised his head and said the takbir. Then he said the takbir and prostrated similar to it or longer. Then he raised his head and then said the takbir."],[2761,"“The Prophet ﷺ prayed with them, then prostrated the two prostrations of forgetfulness, then recited the tashahhud and gave the salutation.”"],[2762,"I was standing over my uncles, serving them fadikh from their supply, and I was the youngest of them. A man came and said: 'Wine has been forbidden.' They said: 'O Anas, overturn it.' He said: So I overturned it.” Sulayman said: I asked, 'What was it?' He said: 'Unripe dates and ripe dates.'"],[2763,"I was serving Abu Ubayda b. al-Jarrah, Ubayy b. Ka'b, and Abu Talha al-Ansari a drink of fadikh. Then someone came and said: 'Wine has been forbidden.' Abu Talha said: 'Arise, O Anas, to these jars and break them.' He said: I went to a stone mortar of ours and struck them with its bottom until they were broken.”"],[2764,"The stray camel of a Muslim is the fuel of the Fire."],[2765,"A group from Banū ʿĀmir came to the Prophet ﷺ and said, \"O Messenger of Allah, we find stray camels on the road.\" He ﷺ said, \"The stray camel of a Muslim is the fuel of the Fire.\""],[2766,"\"Whoever shelters a stray animal is himself astray as long as he does not announce it.\""],[2767,"A man came to the Prophet ﷺ and asked him about found property. He said: \"Note its covering and its tie, then announce it for a year. If its owner comes, give it to him; otherwise, do as you wish with it.\" He asked about stray sheep, and he said: \"They are for you, or for your brother, or for the wolf.\" He asked about stray camels, and he said: \"What do you have to do with them? They have their own water-skins and shoes; they drink water and eat trees until their owner meets them.\""],[2768,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ forbade mut'a with women."],[2769,"He forbade mut'a with women on the day of Khaybar and the eating of the flesh of domesticated donkeys."],[2770,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ permitted mut'a with women. I came to him after three [days], and there he was forbidding it most severely and saying the harshest things about it."],[2771,"We set out with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. When we had completed our 'umrah, he said to us, 'Enjoy these women.' At that time, 'enjoyment' among us meant marriage. We presented to the women that we set a term between us and them. We mentioned that to the Prophet ﷺ and he said, 'Do that.' So I and a cousin of mine went out. I had a cloak and he had a cloak, and his cloak was better than mine, while I was more youthful than him. We came to a woman and presented that to her. My youth pleased her, and my cousin's cloak pleased her. She said, 'A cloak is as good as a cloak.' So I married her, and the term between me and her was ten [days]. I stayed with her that night, then in the morning I went to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ while he was standing between the [Black] Stone and the door, addressing the people. He was saying: 'O people, I had permitted you to enjoy these women. Verily, Allah has now forbidden that until the Day of Resurrection. Whoever has any of them, let him let her go, and do not take back anything of what you gave them.'"],[2773,"\"I heard 'Abdul-'Aziz - that is, bin Asid At-Tahi from Al-Basrah - say: 'Ibn Az-Zubair was asked about soaking (fruits) in earthenware jars and he said: \"The Messenger of Allah [SAW] forbade us from that.\" (Using translation from Nasāʾī 5618)"],[2774,"He prohibited nabidh in green jars."],[2775,"I was with Ibn Umar when a man asked him about nabidh in jars. He said, 'That is among what Allah and His Messenger ﷺ have forbidden.' He said: I went to Ibn Abbas and said to him, 'Ibn Umar was asked about nabidh in jars and said, \"That is among what Allah and His Messenger have forbidden.\"' Ibn Abbas said, 'He spoke the truth.' I said, 'And what is a jar?' He said, 'Anything made of clay.'"],[2776,"I used to spend the night with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and would bring him water for his ablution and his needs. When he stood at night, he would say, \"Glory be to my Lord and with His praise; glory be to my Lord and with His praise,\" for a long while. Then he would say, \"Glory be to the Lord of the worlds; glory be to the Lord of the worlds,\" for a long while."],[2777,"He said to the delegation of ‘Abd al-Qays: 'I forbid you the naqīr, the muqayyar, the ḥantam, the dubbā’, and the mazāda al-majbūba. Drink from your waterskin and tie its mouth.'"],[2778,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ forbade us the dubbā’, the ḥantam, the naqīr, and the muzaffat. As for the dubbā’, it was that the clusters of grapes used to be stripped and we would put them in the dubbā’, then bury it until they died. As for the ḥantam, they were jars in which wine used to be brought to us from Syria. As for the naqīr, the people of Madinah used to take the roots of the palm tree and hollow them out, putting fresh dates and unripe dates in them, then bury them in the ground until they died. As for the muzaffat, it is these skins coated with pitch."],[2779,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ forbade the muzaffat, the muqayyar, the ḥantama, the dubbā’, and the naqīr, and said: 'Every intoxicant is ḥarām.'"],[2780,"'I forbade you nabīdh in certain vessels. Indeed, no vessel makes anything ḥarām, and every intoxicant is ḥarām.'"],[2781,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ wrote to us one month before his death: 'Do not benefit from the dead animal's hide or sinew.'"],[2782,"The letter of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ was read to us while we were in the land of Juhaynah: 'Do not benefit from the dead animal's hide or sinew.'"],[2783,"The Prophet ﷺ wrote to them: 'Do not make use of anything from the dead animal.'"],[2784,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ found a dead sheep that had been given to a freed slave woman of Maymunah from the sadaqah. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"Why did you not benefit from its skin?\" They said: \"It is dead.\" He said: \"Only its eating is forbidden.\""],[2785,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ passed by a dead sheep from the sadaqah that had been given to a freed slave woman of Maymunah. He said: \"Would they not take its hide, tan it, and benefit from it?\" They said: \"O Messenger of Allah, it is dead.\" The Prophet ﷺ said: \"Only its eating is forbidden.\""],[2786,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ commanded that the skins of dead animals be used when they are tanned."],[2787,"Any hide that is tanned has become pure."],[2788,"Any hide that is tanned has become pure."],[2789,"The Prophet ﷺ saw a ring on a man's hand and said: \"What is this?\" He said: \"It is for the wahinah (a vein ailment).\" He said: \"It only increases you in weakness. Throw it away from you, for if you die while it is on you, you will be left to it.\""],[2790,"Whoever cauterizes or seeks incantation has disassociated himself from reliance on Allah."],[2791,"He entered upon the Messenger of Allah ﷺ while there was a ring of brass on his upper arm. He said: \"What is this?\" He said: \"For the wahinah?\" He said: \"Would it please you to be left to it? Throw it away from you.\""],[2793,"“He forbade letting one's garment hang down during prayer.”"],[2794,"He forbade letting one's garment hang down during prayer and that a man cover his mouth."],[2795,"Do not single out the night of Friday for night prayer from among the nights, and do not single out the day of Friday for fasting from among the days."],[2796,"“Do not boast about your forefathers of the pre-Islamic era. For by the One in whose hand is the soul of Muḥammad, what the dung beetle rolls with its nose is better than your forefathers who died in the pre-Islamic era.”"],[2797,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ caught up with Umar b. al-Khattab while he was swearing by his father. The Prophet ﷺ said: \"Allah forbids you from swearing by your fathers. Let the one who swears swear by Allah or be silent.\""],[2798,"\"Whoever swears, let him not swear except by Allah.\" Quraysh used to swear by their fathers, so he said: \"Do not swear by your fathers.\""],[2799,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ passed by me while I was sitting and had placed my left hand behind my back and was leaning on it. The Prophet ﷺ said: “Do you sit in the sitting of those who have incurred wrath?”"],[2800,"He forbade al-shtimāl al-ṣammā' (wrapping oneself in a garment with no opening for the arms)."],[2801,"\"Do not urinate standing.\""],[2802,"\"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ came to a people's rubbish dump and urinated standing, then performed ablution and wiped over his leather socks.\""],[2803,"“I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ forbidding qaza‘.”"],[2804,"\"Whoever learns knowledge by which the face of Allah is sought, but learns it only to attain some worldly gain, will not find the fragrance of Paradise on the Day of Resurrection.\""],[2805,"\"Whoever conceals knowledge will be bridled with a bridle of fire on the Day of Resurrection.\""],[2806,"\"Whoever conceals knowledge, Allah will bridle him on the Day of Resurrection with a bridle of fire.\""],[2807,"\"Do not learn knowledge to vie with the scholars, nor to argue with the foolish, nor to gain preeminence in gatherings. Whoever does that, then the Fire, the Fire!\""],[2808,"Whoever deliberately lies against me, let him take his seat in the Fire."],[2809,"Among the greatest of slanders are three: that a man invents against himself, saying he saw a dream when he saw nothing; or that a man fabricates against his parents, attributing himself to other than his father; or that he says he heard from me when he did not hear from me."],[2810,"\"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: 'Whoever attributes to me something that I have not said, let him take his place in Hell.\" (Using translation from Ibn Mājah 34)"],[2811,"Whoever narrates a hadith while considering it to be a lie, then he is one of the liars."],[2812,"It is enough of a sin for a man that he narrates everything he hears."],[2813,"Does Abu Hurayrah not amaze you? He came and sat by the side of my room narrating from the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, making me hear that while I was performing voluntary prayer. He left before I finished my voluntary prayer. Had I caught him, I would have responded to him: the Messenger of Allah ﷺ did not narrate hadith in a rapid sequence like your sequence."],[2814,"By the One in whose hand is my soul, no man hates us, the People of the House, but Allah will cause him to enter the Fire."],[2815,"Fear Allah, fear Allah regarding my Companions. Do not take my Companions as a target. Whoever loves them, loves them because of his love for me; whoever hates them, hates them because of his hatred for me. Whoever harms them has harmed me, and whoever harms me has harmed Allah, and whoever harms Allah, it is likely that He will seize him."],[2816,"When some men from the companions of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ were killed on the day of Khaybar, they said, 'So-and-so is a martyr, and so-and-so is a martyr,' until they mentioned a man and said, 'So-and-so is a martyr.' The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, 'No, indeed I saw him in the Fire in a cloak he had stolen or a striped garment he had stolen.' Then the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, 'O Ibn al-Khattab, go and announce among the people that none will enter Paradise except a believing soul.' He said, 'So I went out and announced among the people.'"],[2817,"He said in the year of Khaybar: 'Whoever believes in Allah and the Last Day, let him not water his own water (i.e., his semen) the child of another (i.e., let him not have intercourse with a pregnant captive). Whoever believes in Allah and the Last Day, let him not take a riding animal from the spoils and ride it until he has made it lean and then return it to the spoils. Whoever believes in Allah and the Last Day, let him not wear a garment from the spoils until he has worn it out and then return it to the spoils.'"],[2818,"We went out with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ in the year of Khaybar, and we did not gain gold or silver, but only goods, clothes, and baggage. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ headed towards Wadi al-Qura. Rifa'ah b. Zayd had given the Messenger of Allah ﷺ a black slave called Mid'am. We went on until we were at Wadi al-Qura. While Mid'am was unloading the saddle of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, a stray arrow came and struck him, killing him. The people said, 'Good for him, Paradise!' The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, 'No, by Him in whose hand is my soul, the cloak that he took on the day of Khaybar from the spoils, which the division had not reached, is burning upon him as fire.' When the people heard that, a man came with a shoe strap or two shoe straps to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, 'A shoe strap of fire or two shoe straps of fire.'"],[2819,"Rifa'ah gave the Messenger of Allah ﷺ a slave boy, and he took him with him to Khaybar. A stray arrow struck the boy and killed him. We said, 'Good for him, Paradise!' The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, 'By Him in whose hand is my soul, the cloak is burning upon him now in the Fire; he stole it from the Muslims on the day of Khaybar.' A man from the Ansar said, 'O Messenger of Allah, I got two shoe straps that day.' He said, 'The like of them will be counted for you in the fire of Hell.'"],[2820,"A man from the companions of the Prophet ﷺ died on the day of Khaybar, and they mentioned him to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. He said, 'Pray over your companion.' The faces of the people changed at that, and he said, 'Your companion committed ghulul in the way of Allah.' So we opened his baggage and found beads of the Jews' beads, not worth two dirhams."],[2821,"A dead man who owed a debt would be brought, and he would ask, 'Did he leave enough to pay his debt?' If he was told that he had left enough, he would pray over him; otherwise he would say, 'Pray over your companion.' When Allah, Mighty and Majestic, granted him the conquests, he said, 'I am closer to the believers than their own selves. Whoever dies owing a debt, its payment is upon me, and whoever leaves wealth, it belongs to his heirs.'"],[2822,"I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say while he was walking between two of the Jamarat and saying: 'Whoever takes a handspan of a Muslim man's property with a false oath, let him take his place in the Fire.'"],[2823,"\"Whoever swears on this pulpit of mine with a false oath has taken his seat in the Fire.\""],[2824,"Whoever takes a span of land unjustly will be made to wear it as a collar from seven earths."],[2825,"Whoever takes a span of land without right will be made to wear it as a collar from seven earths."],[2826,"“Whoever usurps a span of land, Allah will collar him on the Day of Resurrection with it from seven earths.”"],[2827,"Any man who wrongfully takes a handspan of land, Allah will charge him to dig it until he reaches seven earths, then it will be made a collar around his neck on the Day of Resurrection until judgment is passed between the people."],[2828,"«Whoever swears a false, binding oath to seize thereby the wealth of his brother will meet Allah while He is angry with him.» That is because Allah says: {Indeed, those who purchase a small gain at the cost of Allah's covenant and their oaths} – to the end of the verse."],[2829,"«Whoever swears an oath in which he is sinful will meet Allah while He is angry with him.» Al-Ash'ath said, \"By Allah, that was concerning me. There was a land between me and a Jewish man, and he denied me, so I brought him to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, 'Do you have clear proof?' I said, 'No.' He said to the Jew, 'Swear.' I said, 'O Messenger of Allah, then he will swear and take my wealth.' So Allah revealed: {Indeed, those who purchase a small gain at the cost of Allah's covenant and their oaths} – to the end of the verse.\""],[2830,"«Whoever swears a sinful oath to seize thereby the wealth of a Muslim without right, Allah has forbidden Paradise to him and made the Fire obligatory for him.» It was said, \"O Messenger of Allah, even if it is something small?\" He said, \"Even if it is a stick of arak.\""],[2831,"He who swears a false oath to deprive a Muslim of his property will meet Allah as a leper."],[2832,"\"Among the greatest of major sins are associating partners with Allah, disobedience to parents, and the false oath. By the One in whose hand is my soul, no man swears an oath about the like of a mosquito's wing except that it becomes a brand * on his heart on the Day of Resurrection.\""],[2833,"A man came to him and said, \"I have made these images.\" The Prophet ﷺ said, \"Allah punishes the image-makers for what they have made.\" The man went away, claiming that he had a family. Ibn Abbas said, \"Do not make an image of anything that has a soul.\""],[2834,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ entered upon her while she was screened by a curtain with figures on it. The face of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ changed color, and he reached for the curtain and tore it with his hand. Then he said, \"The people who will receive the severest punishment on the Day of Resurrection are those who imitate Allah's creation.\""],[2835,"I was with Ibn Abbas when a man came to him and said, \"I am a man whose livelihood comes from these images.\" Ibn Abbas said, \"I heard Muhammad ﷺ say: 'Whoever makes an image, Allah will punish him until he blows the soul into it, and he will never be able to do so.'\" His color turned pale. He said, \"If you must, then make trees and things that do not have a soul.\""],[2836,"Angels do not enter a house in which there are statues or an image."],[2837,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Indeed, the angels do not enter a house in which there is an image.” Busr said: Then he fell ill, so we visited him, and there was a curtain at his door, and on it there was an image. I said to ʿUbayd Allah al-Khawlānī: “Did he not inform us and yet leave the cloth?” ʿUbayd Allah said: “Did you not hear him?” He said: “Except for a pattern on a garment?”"],[2838,"He entered upon Abu Talhah al-Ansari to visit him. He said: We found Sahl b. Hunayf with him. Abu Talhah called someone and had him remove a carpet from beneath him. Sahl b. Hunayf said to him, \"Why do you remove it?\" He said, \"It has images on it, and the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said about it what you know.\" Sahl said, \"Did he not say: 'Except a marking on a garment'?\" He said, \"Yes, but it is more comforting to my soul.\""],[2839,"I saw my father buy a cupper, and he brought his cupping instruments, and they were broken."],[2840,"“Whoever makes an image, Allah will punish him until he blows into it, and he will not blow. Whoever listens to the talk of people who flee from him, molten lead will be poured into his ears on the Day of Resurrection. And whoever falsely claims to have seen a dream will be tasked with tying two grains of barley together, and he will not be able to do it.”"],[2841,"The one who sees with his eyes in sleep what he did not see will be charged on the Day of Resurrection to tie a knot between two grains of barley; and the one who listens to the talk of a people while they dislike it will have molten lead poured into his ear on the Day of Resurrection."],[2842,"Verily, the one who drinks from a silver vessel, he only gurgles the fire of Hell into his belly."],[2843,"Hudhayfah asked for water, and a servant brought him a silver-plated cup, so he returned it and said, 'I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say, \"It is for them in this world, and for us in the Hereafter.\"'"],[2845,"Ubaydullah b. Ziyad visited Ma'qil b. Yasar during the illness in which he died. Ma'qil said: I am going to tell you a hadith that I heard from the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. If I knew that I had any life left, I would not tell it to you. I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: «There is no servant whom Allah entrusts with a flock and who dies on the day he dies while being deceitful to his flock except that Allah forbids Paradise for him.»"],[2846,"I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: \"Whoever seeks refuge in Allah has sought a refuge.\" He said: Yes. He said: Then I seek refuge in Allah from being a judge. He said: What prevents you, when your father used to judge? He said: Because I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: \"Whoever is a judge and judges with ignorance will be among the people of the Fire, and whoever is a judge and judges with injustice will be among the people of the Fire, and whoever is a judge, knowledgeable, judging with truth or with justice, asks to slip away with nothing.\" So what hope do I have after that?"],[2847,"‘Urwa bin Al Zubair said “Hisham bin Halim bin Hizam found a man who was the governor of Hims making some Copts stand in the sun for the payment of jizyah. He said “What is this?” I heard the Apostle ﷺ as saying “Allaah Most High will punish those who punish the people in this world.” (Using translation from Abū Dāʾūd 3045)"],[2848,"Hakim b. Hizam passed by Umayr b. Sa'd while he was punishing people for the jizyah in the sun, and he said: O Umayr, I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: 'Allah will punish those who punish people in this world.' He said: Go and release them."],[2849,"I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: “Whoever does not show mercy to people, Allah will not show mercy to him.”"],[2850,"The Prophet (pbuh) said, \"Mercy is not taken away except from a wretched person.\""],[2851,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ came out to us while we were sitting on a leather cushion, and he said: \"There will be after me rulers. Whoever enters upon them and confirms them in their lies and aids them in their oppression is not of me, and I am not of him, and he will not come to me at the Basin. And whoever does not confirm them in their lies and does not aid them in their oppression, he is of me and I am of him, and he is one who will come to me at the Basin.\""],[2852,"There is no man who is among a people who commit sins while they are able to change them but they do not change them, except that Allah will strike them with punishment before they die."],[2853,"We were sitting with him in the marketplace when a man from the people of Madinah who had nobility passed by him, and he said to him: O son of my brother, you have a right (to be reminded), and indeed you enter upon these rulers and speak before them. Indeed, I heard Bilal b. al-Harith, the Companion of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, say: I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: \"Indeed, a servant speaks a word and does not see that it has reached where it has reached, and Allah writes for him thereby His pleasure until the Day of Resurrection; and indeed, a servant speaks a word and does not see that it has reached where it has reached, and Allah writes for him thereby His wrath until the day he meets Him.\" So consider, O son of my brother, what you say and what you speak. For much speech has been prevented from me by what I heard from Bilal b. al-Harith."],[2854,"I heard the Messenger of Allah (PBUH) say, \"Indeed, a person may utter a word, without seeing any harm in it, that causes them to fall into the Fire for seventy autumns.\""],[2855,"Indeed, a servant may speak a word by which he descends into the Fire farther than the distance between the east and the west."],[2856,"Indeed, a servant may speak a word about which he is not careful, and by it he descends into the Fire farther than the distance between the east and the west."],[2857,"Indeed, a man may speak a word to make his companions laugh, and by it he falls farther than the Pleiades."],[2858,"«Behold, lying blackens the face; and tale-bearing is from the torment of the grave.»"],[2859,"«There was no characteristic more hateful to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ than lying. A man would tell a lie in his presence, and it would remain in his mind until he knew that he had repented of it.»"],[2860,"Whoever has two wives and inclines toward one of them over the other will come on the Day of Resurrection with one of his sides sagging."],[2861,"There is no people among whom sins are committed while they are able to change them but they do not change them, except that Allah will strike them with punishment before they die."],[2862,"“Any man who calls his wife and she does not respond to him, and he spends the night angry with her until morning, the angels curse her until she wakes.”"],[2863,"“When one of you calls his wife to his bed and she refuses to come, the angels curse her until morning.”"],[2864,"“When a woman abandons her husband’s bed, the angels curse her until she returns.”"],[2865,"Any woman who asks her husband for divorce without any serious problem, the fragrance of Paradise is forbidden to her."],[2866,"Whoever keeps a dog, his deeds are reduced every day by a qirat, except a dog for farming or livestock."],[2867,"Whoever keeps a dog except a hunting dog or a dog for livestock, his reward is reduced by two qirats every day."],[2868,"We entered upon Anas b. Malik after Zuhr, and he stood to pray Asr. When he finished his prayer, we mentioned hastening the prayer or he mentioned it, and he said: 'I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: \"That is the prayer of the hypocrites, that is the prayer of the hypocrites, that is the prayer of the hypocrites—three times. One of them sits until when the sun turns yellow and is between the two horns of Satan or upon the two horns of Satan, then he stands and pecks four (units), not remembering Allah in them except a little.\"\""],[2869,"Whoever takes as patrons other than his patrons, let him take his seat in the Fire."],[2870,"\"Whoever claims a father in Islam while knowing that he is not his father, Paradise is forbidden for him.\" He said: I mentioned that to Abu Bakrah, and he said, \"My ears heard it and my heart retained it from the Prophet ﷺ.\""],[2871,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to pray thirteen rakʿahs at night."],[2872,"Jibril came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and said: “O Muhammad, Allah has cursed wine, its presser, the one who has it pressed, its carrier, the one to whom it is carried, its drinker, its seller, its buyer, its server, and the one to whom it is served.”"],[2873,"Three will not enter Paradise: the one addicted to wine, the one who severs ties of kinship, and the one who believes in sorcery. And whoever dies addicted to wine, Allah, Mighty and Majestic, will give him to drink from the river of al-Ghawta.\" It was said, \"And what is the river of al-Ghawta?\" He said, \"A river that flows from the private parts of prostitutes, whose stench harms the people of the Fire.\""],[2874,"\"Six are those whom I have cursed, and Allah and every prophet whose supplication is answered have cursed: the one who adds to the Book of Allah; the one who denies the decree of Allah; the one who rules with tyranny to thereby abase whom Allah has honored and to honor whom Allah has abased; the one who deems lawful what Allah has forbidden in His sanctuary; the one who deems lawful from my family what Allah has forbidden; and the one who abandons my Sunnah.\""],[2875,"A slave girl from the Ansar married, then she fell ill and her hair fell out, so they wanted to attach hair extensions for her. They asked the Messenger of Allah ﷺ about that, and he cursed the one who attaches hair extensions and the one who has them attached."],[2876,"\"It has reached me that you say the curse upon the tattooed woman, the one who tattoos, the one who plucks facial hair, and the one who alters the creation of Allah. I have read what is between the two tablets, but I did not find what you say.\" He said, \"Yes, I found it. However, you do not know.\" She asked, \"Where is it?\" He replied, \"Have you not read, 'Whatever the Messenger gives you, take it, and whatever he forbids you, abstain from it'?\" She said, \"Yes.\" He said, \"That is it.\" She said, \"Indeed, I see some of that on your family.\" He said, \"Enter and look.\" So she entered and looked but she did not see anything. Abdullah said to her, \"Did you see anything?\" She replied, \"No.\" Abdullah said, \"If you had seen anything from that, would you have followed me?\""],[2877,"What is this news that has reached me from you that you curse those women who tattooed and those women who have themselves tattooed, the women who pluck hair from their faces and who make spaces between their teeth for beautification changing what God has created? Thereupon 'Abdullah said: Should I not curse one upon whom Messenger of Allah ﷺ has invoked curse and that is in the Book also. Thereupon that woman said: I read the Qur'an from cover to cover, but I did not find that in it. whereupon he said: If you had read (thoroughly) you would have definitely found this in that (as) Allah, the Exalted and Glorious, has said:\" What Messenger of Allah brings for you accept that and what he has forbidden you, refrain from that.\" That woman said: I find this thing in your wife even now. Thereupon he said: Go and see her. She reported: I went to the wife of 'Abdullah but found nothing of this sort in her. She came back to him and said: I have not seen anything. whereupon he said: Had there been anything like it in her, I would have never slept with her in the bed. (Using translation from Muslim 2125a)"],[2878,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ \"cursed masculine women and effeminate men.\""],[2879,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ cursed the man who dressed like a woman and the woman who dressed like a man. (Using translation from Abū Dāʾūd 4098)"],[2880,"We have no book to read except the Book of Allah and a sheet in the sheath of my sword. He read it to us, and it contained something about the ages of camels and wound compensations, and it contained: whoever allies himself with a people without the permission of his masters, upon him is the curse of Allah, His angels, and all people. Allah will not accept from him on the Day of Resurrection any obligatory or supererogatory act. The protection of the Muslims is one; the lowest of them may extend it. Whoever violates a Muslim's covenant, upon him is the curse of Allah, the angels, and all people, and no obligatory or supererogatory act will be accepted from him on the Day of Resurrection. Madinah is sacred between its two lava fields. Whoever commits an offense in it or shelters an offender, upon him is the curse of Allah, the angels, and all people; no obligatory or supererogatory act will be accepted from him on the Day of Resurrection."],[2881,"We did not write from the Messenger of Allah ﷺ except the Qur'an and what is in this sheet. He said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"Madinah is sacred between 'Ayr and Thawr. Whoever commits an offense in it or shelters an offender, upon him is the curse of Allah, the angels, and all people; no obligatory or supererogatory act will be accepted from him. The protection of the Muslims is one; the lowest of them may extend it. Whoever violates a Muslim's covenant, upon him is the curse of Allah, the angels, and all people; no obligatory or supererogatory act will be accepted from him. Whoever allies himself with a people without the permission of his masters, upon him is the curse of Allah, the angels, and all people.\""],[2882,"\"May Allah curse the one who slaughters for other than Allah. May Allah curse the one who alters the landmarks of the land. May Allah curse the one who misleads a blind person from the path. May Allah curse the one who insults his parents. May Allah curse the one who turns to other than his patrons. May Allah curse the one who does the deed of the people of Lot.\" He said it three times regarding the deed of the people of Lot."],[2883,"Among the major sins is that a man reviles his parents.\" It was said, \"And how does a man revile his parents?\" He said, \"He reviles people, and then they revile his parents."],[2884,"Among the major sins is that a man reviles his parents.\" It was said, \"And how does a man revile his parents?\" He said, \"He reviles people, and then they revile his parents."],[2885,"\"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ cursed the man who wears women's clothing and the woman who wears men's clothing.\""],[2886,"The Prophet ﷺ passed by a donkey that had been branded on its face and said, “May Allah curse the one who branded it.”"],[2887,"“Two transactions in one transaction are not lawful.”"],[2888,"«May Allah curse the briber and the bribed in judgment.»"],[2889,"«May Allah curse the briber and the bribed.»"],[2890,"The consumer of riba, its agent, its scribe, and its two witnesses if they know about it, the woman who tattoos and the woman who asks to be tattooed for beauty, the one who withholds zakat, and the apostate who becomes a bedouin after his emigration are cursed on the tongue of Muhammad ﷺ on the Day of Resurrection."],[2891,"I said to ʿAlī b. Abī Ṭālib, 'Do you have anything besides the Book of Allah?' He said, 'No, except what is in the sheath of this sword: a small sheet.' He said, 'We found in it: \"May Allah curse whoever slaughters for other than Allah, and may Allah curse whoever gives allegiance to other than his patrons.\"'"],[2892,"Ali b. Abi Talib was asked: Did the Messenger of Allah ﷺ single you out for anything? He said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ did not single us out for anything that he did not make general for all people, except what is in the sheath of this sword of mine. Then he took out a sheet on which was written: \"May Allah curse whoever slaughters for other than Allah; may Allah curse whoever steals the boundary markers of the land; may Allah curse whoever curses his parents; may Allah curse whoever gives shelter to an innovator.\""],[2893,"“May Allah curse anyone who mutilates an animal.”"],[2894,"O Umm 'Abd Allah, shall I not tell you what the Messenger of Allah ﷺ cursed? She said, 'Yes.' He said, 'The Messenger of Allah ﷺ cursed the one who shaves her head, tears her clothes, or wails loudly.'"],[2895,"\"May Allah curse women who visit graves.\""],[2896,"\"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ cursed women who visit graves and those who take them as places of worship and put lanterns on them.\""],[2897,"We buried a deceased person with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ one day. When we finished, the Messenger of Allah ﷺ departed and we departed with him. When he was opposite his door and in the middle of the road, we saw a woman approaching. When she came near, it was Fatimah. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to her, \"What brought you out, O Fatimah, from your house?\" She said, \"I came, O Messenger of Allah, to the family of this house and consoled them for their deceased.\" The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to her, \"Perhaps you reached the graveyard with them?\" She said, \"I seek refuge in Allah! I heard you mention about it what you mention.\" He said, \"If you had reached the graveyard with them, you would not have seen Paradise until your grandfather, your father's father, sees it.\""],[2898,"\"Four types Allah hates: the trader who swears oaths constantly, the poor person who is arrogant, the elderly adulterer, and the oppressive leader.\""],[2899,"\"There are three whom Allah will not speak to, nor look at: a man who swears after the 'Asr prayer concerning the property of a Muslim man and thereby takes it unlawfully; a man who swears that he was given more for his goods than he actually was; and a man who withholds surplus water. Allah will say, 'Today I withhold My bounty from you as you withheld the surplus of what your hands did not produce.'\""],[2900,"A Bedouin passed by a sheep, and I said, \"Will you sell it to me for three dirhams?\" He said, \"No, by Allah,\" then he sold it to me. I mentioned that to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and he said, \"He sold his Hereafter for his worldly life.\""],[2901,"He went out with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ to al-Baqi' while people were trading. He called out, \"O company of merchants,\" and they responded to him and raised their eyes to him. He said, \"Indeed, merchants will be resurrected on the Day of Resurrection as wicked sinners, except those who fear Allah, act righteously, and speak the truth.\""],[2902,"Whoever abandons Friday three times out of negligence, Allah will seal his heart."],[2903,"the Messenger of Allah said: “Verily, when the slave (of Allah) commits a sin, a black spot appears on his heart. When he refrains from it, seeks forgiveness and repents, his heart is polished clean. But if he returns, it increases until it covers his entire heart. And that is the ‘Ran’ which Allah mentioned: ‘Nay, but on their hearts is the Ran which they used to earn.’” (Using translation from Tirmidhī 3334)"],[2904,"A man led some people in prayer and spat toward the qiblah while the Messenger of Allah ﷺ was watching him. When he finished, the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, 'He shall not lead you in prayer.' After that, the man wanted to lead them, but they prevented him and informed him of the Messenger of Allah's ﷺ statement. That was mentioned to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and he said, 'Yes,' and I think he said, 'You have offended Allah.'"],[2905,"The one who expectorates toward the qiblah will come on the Day of Resurrection with it on his face."],[2906,"«Whoever spits towards the qiblah will come on the Day of Resurrection with his spittle between his eyes.»"],[2907,"«My Ummah was presented to me with its deeds, good and evil, and I saw among the good deeds the removal of something harmful from the road, and I saw among the evil deeds the sputum in the mosque that is not buried.»"],[2908,"“No one who severs [kinship ties] will enter Paradise.”"],[2909,"“There is no sin more likely that Allah hasten its punishment for its perpetrator in this world, along with what He stores up for him in the Hereafter, than severing kinship ties and injustice.”"],[2910,"There was a man who carried tales to the ruler. We were sitting with Hudhayfah when that man passed by. It was said: It is he. Hudhayfah said: I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: “No talebearer enters Paradise.”"],[2911,"'Abd Allah b. 'Umar came to Ibn Muti' during the nights of al-Harrah and said, \"Place a cushion for Abu 'Abd al-Rahman.\" He said, \"I did not come to sit; I came to speak two words to you that I heard from the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: 'Whoever withdraws his hand from obedience will have no argument on the Day of Resurrection, and whoever dies separated from the community dies a death of ignorance.'\""],[2912,"The Messenger of Allah said, \"Whoever is killed under a blind banner, their killing is the killing of ignorant people.\""],[2913,"One who defected from obedience (to the Amir) and separated from the main body of the Muslims - if he died in that state-would die the death of one belonging to the days of Jahiliyya (i.e. would not die as a Muslim). One who fights under the banner of a people who are blind (to the cause for which they are fighting, i.e. do not know whether their cause is just or otherwise), who gets flared up with family pride, calls (people) to fight for their family honour, and supports his kith and kin (i.e. fights not for the cause of Allah but for the sake of this family or tribe) - if he is killed (in this fight), he dies as one belonging to the days of Jahiliyya. Whoso attacks my Ummah (indiscriminately) killing the righteous and the wicked of them, sparing not (even) those staunch in faith and fulfilling not his promise made with those who have been given a pledge of security - he has nothing to do with me and I have nothing to do with him. (Using translation from Muslim 1848a)"],[2914,"He heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say when the verse of mutual cursing (li'an) was revealed: \"Any woman who brings into a people someone who is not of them, she has nothing to do with Allah, and Allah will never admit her to His Paradise. And any man who denies his child while looking at him, Allah will veil Himself from him and disgrace him before the heads of the first and the last.\""],[2916,"\"Adultery and usury do not appear among a people except that they make lawful for themselves the punishment of Allah, mighty and majestic.\""],[2917,"\"Three people Allah will not look at on the Day of Resurrection: the old adulterer, the lying ruler, and the arrogant poor person.\""],[2918,"I said, \"O Messenger of Allah, which sin is greatest?\" He said, \"That you set up a rival to Allah while He created you.\" I said, \"Then which?\" He said, \"That you kill your child fearing he will eat with you.\" I said, \"Then which?\" He said, \"That you commit adultery with your neighbor's wife.\" Then Allah sent down confirmation of the statement of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ: {And those who do not call upon another god besides Allah, nor kill the soul that Allah has forbidden except by right, nor commit adultery}."],[2919,"\"Allah will not look at a man who comes to a woman in her anus.\""],[2920,"I heard one of them from the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and the other I say it myself."],[2921,"From the Messenger of Allah ﷺ , he said: \"Whoever suffocates himself in the world, he will suffocate himself in the Fire. And whoever stabs himself, he will be stabbed in the Fire. And whoever commits suicide, he will enter the Fire.\""],[2922,"Whoever kills a soul under covenant will not smell the fragrance of Paradise."],[2923,"My father ʿUthmān b. ʿAffān said to me: O my son, if you are given any authority over the affairs of the Muslims, honor Quraysh, for I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: Whoever humiliates Quraysh, Allah humiliates him."],[2924,"“Two categories of my nation I have not seen: a people with whips like the tails of cattle, striking people with them, and women who are clothed yet naked, swaying and causing others to sway, their heads like the leaning humps of bukht camels. They will not enter Paradise nor find its fragrance, even though its fragrance is found from such-and-such a distance.”"],[2925,"“Whoever wishes bad upon the people of Al-Madinah, Allah will cause him to melt as salt melts in water.” (Using translation from Ibn Mājah 3114)"],[2926,"“Whoever frightens the people of Madinah, Allah will frighten him.”"],[2927,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ came out to us with a staff in his hand while clusters of dates were hanging in the mosque, one of them containing inferior dry dates. He poked that cluster with the staff and said: “If the owner of this charity had wished, he could have given better than it. The owner of this charity will eat the inferior dates on the Day of Resurrection.” Then he turned to us and said: “By Allah, O people of Madinah, you will certainly leave it to the beasts. Do you know what the beasts are?” We said: “Allah and His Messenger know best.” He said: “The birds and the wild animals.”"],[2928,"Whoever plays with dice has disobeyed Allah and His Messenger."],[2929,"\"Three persons Allah will not look at on the Day of Resurrection: the lying leader, the adulterous old man, and the arrogant poor person.\""],[2930,"\"Three persons Allah will not look at on the Day of Resurrection: the one who is disobedient to his parents, the habitual drinker of wine, and the one who reminds others of what he has given.\""],[2931,"The Prophet ﷺ performed witr with one rak'ah."],[2932,"\"There are three whose opponent I will be on the Day of Resurrection, and whoever I oppose I will defeat: a man who gives a pledge in my name and then betrays; a man who sells a free person and consumes his price; and a man who hires a worker, receives full work from him, but does not give him his wages.\""],[2933,"\"The most beloved of you to me and the closest of you to me in the Hereafter are those of you with the best character. And the most hateful of you to me and the furthest of you from me in the Hereafter are those of you with the worst character: the garrulous, the arrogant boasters, and the verbose.\""],[2934,"I heard Maslama b. Makhlad while he was on the pulpit addressing the people, saying: “O people, do you not have in ʿaṣb (a type of cloth) and linen what suffices you from silk? Here is a man who will inform you from the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. Stand, O ʿUqba.” So ʿUqba b. ʿĀmir stood while I was listening and said: “I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: ‘Whoever deliberately lies about me, let him take his seat in the Fire.’ And I bear witness that I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: ‘Whoever wears silk will be deprived of wearing it in the Hereafter.’”"],[2935,"“Whoever wears silk in this world will not wear it in the Hereafter. Even if he enters Paradise, its people will wear it but he will not.”"],[2936,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ came to us while we were in the ṣuffah after sunset and said: “O so-and-so, go with so-and-so; and O so-and-so, go with so-and-so,” until he had sent five, I being the fifth of them. Then he said: “Get up with me.” We did so and entered upon ʿĀʾishah—that was before the hijab was revealed. He said: “O ʿĀʾishah, feed us.” She brought some jashīshah. Then he said: “O ʿĀʾishah, feed us.” She brought some ḥays. Then he said: “O ʿĀʾishah, give us something to drink.” She brought a large cup and he drank. Then he said: “O ʿĀʾishah, give us something to drink.” She brought a smaller cup. Then he said: “If you wish, sleep with us; and if you wish, go to the mosque and sleep there.” He said: “So we slept in the mosque. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ came to us at the end of the night and found me sleeping on my belly. He kicked me with his foot and said: “What is it with you and this sleep? This is a sleep that Allah hates—or that Allah detests.”"],[2937,"“Indeed, the one who drags his garment out of pride, Allah will not look at him on the Day of Resurrection.”"],[2938,"\"Whoever causes a Jew or a Christian to hear, will enter the Fire.\""],[2939,"Four things are in my Ummah from the customs of Jahiliyyah that they will not abandon: boasting about noble descent, defaming lineages, seeking rain by the stars, and wailing. And the wailing woman, if she does not repent before her death, will be made to stand on the Day of Resurrection wearing a garment of tar and a coat of mange."],[2940,"The most hateful of men to Allah is the quarrelsome, obstinate disputant."],[2941,"A man asked permission to enter upon the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. When he heard his voice, the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to 'A'isha, \"What an evil man,\" or \"what an evil son of the tribe.\" When he entered, the Messenger of Allah ﷺ was cheerful toward him. When he left, 'A'isha spoke to him and said, \"O Messenger of Allah, you said, 'What an evil man,' or 'what an evil son of the tribe,' but when he entered, you were cheerful toward him.\" He said, \"O 'A'isha, the worst of people is the one whom people avoid because of his obscenity.\""],[2942,"“Whoever makes an image will be punished until he blows the spirit into it, and he will not blow the spirit into it. Whoever falsely claims to have seen a dream will be tasked with tying two grains of barley together and will be punished for that. And whoever listens to a people while they dislike that, molten lead will be poured into his ears on the Day of Resurrection.”"],[2943,"The angels curse one of you when he points a piece of iron at his brother, even if he is his brother from the same father and mother."],[2944,"\"The Messenger [SAW] said: 'If two Muslims meet (and fight) with their swords and one of them kills the other, the killer and the slain will both be in Hell.'\" (Using translation from Nasāʾī 4121)"],[2945,"There is no servant who has wealth and does not pay its zakat except that Allah will gather it for him on the Day of Resurrection as heated plates of the fire of Hell with which his forehead and back will be branded, until Allah judges between His servants in a day whose measure is fifty thousand years of what you count. Then he will see his path, either to Paradise or to the Fire. And there is no owner of camels who does not pay their zakat except that he will be thrown down for them on a vast flat plain, as fat as they were, and they will tread on him. Every time the last of them passes over him, the first of them will be returned to him, until Allah judges between His servants in a day whose measure is fifty thousand years. Then he will see his path, either to Paradise or to the Fire. And there is no owner of sheep who does not pay their zakat except that he will be thrown down for them on a vast flat plain, as fat as they were, and they will trample him with their cloven hooves and gore him with their horns, none of them having twisted horns or being hornless. Every time the last of them passes over him, the first of them will be returned to him, until Allah judges between His servants in a day whose measure is fifty thousand years. Then he will see his path, either to Paradise or to the Fire."],[2946,"Whoever leaves behind a treasure, it will be made to appear to him on the Day of Resurrection as a bald-headed snake with two venomous fangs, pursuing him. He will say, 'Who are you?' It will say, 'I am your treasure that you left behind.' It will not cease pursuing him until it makes him swallow his hand, then it will bite it off, and then it will pursue the rest of his body."],[2947,"The treasure of any one of you will appear on the Day of Resurrection as a bald-headed snake that pursues its owner while he seeks refuge from it. It will not cease pursuing him until it makes him swallow his finger."],[2948,"I arrived in Madinah, and while I was sitting in a circle that included a group of Quraysh, a man came with rough clothes, rough body, and rough face. He stood before them and said, 'Give glad tidings to the hoarders of wealth of heated stones that will be placed on the nipples of their breasts until they come out from the shoulder joints, and placed on their shoulder joints until they come out from the nipples of their breasts.' They bowed their heads, and I did not see any of them respond to him. He turned away, and I followed him until he sat by a pillar. I said, 'I see these people only disliked what you said to them.' He said, 'These people do not understand. My close friend Abu al-Qasim ﷺ called me and said, \"O Abu Dharr,\" and I answered. He said, \"Do you see Uhud?\" I looked at the sun on me, thinking he would send me on an errand. He said, \"It would not please me to have its equivalent in gold and spend it all except three dinars. Then these people amass worldly wealth and understand nothing.\"' I said, 'What about you and your brothers of Quraysh?' He said, 'No, by your Lord, I will not ask them for worldly gain, nor seek their religious opinion, until I meet Allah and His Messenger ﷺ.'"],[2949,"I was among a group of Quraysh when Abu Dharr passed by saying, 'Give glad tidings to the hoarders of wealth of a branding on their backs that will come out from their sides, and a branding from the back of their necks that will come out from their foreheads.' Then he stepped aside and sat down. I asked, 'Who is this?' They said, 'Abu Dharr.' I went to him and said, 'What is this that I heard you saying a little while ago?' He said, 'I did not say anything except something I heard from their Prophet ﷺ.' I said, 'What do you say about this allowance?' He said, 'Take it, for today it is a means of support. But if it becomes a price for your religion, then leave it.'"],[2950,"The wealth from which its due right is not given will come, with the camels trampling their owner with their hooves, and the cows and sheep will come and trample their owner with their cloven hooves and gore him with their horns. The treasure will come as a bald-headed snake and will meet its owner, who will flee from it. Then it will confront him, and he will flee from it, saying, 'What do you have to do with me?' It will say, 'I am your treasure,' and it will make him swallow his hand."],[2951,"A man from the people of Najd came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ with disheveled hair; the murmur of his voice could be heard but what he was saying could not be understood until he came near to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and it turned out he was asking about Islam. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to him, “Five prayers in the day and night.” He said, “Are there any others due on me?” He said, “No, unless you do voluntary ones.” He said: And the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, “And fasting the month of Ramadan.” He said, “Is there any other due on me?” He said, “No, unless you do voluntary ones.” He said: And the Messenger of Allah ﷺ mentioned zakah to him. He said, “Is there any other due on me?” He said, “No, unless you do voluntary ones.” He said: The man turned away saying, “By Allah, I will not add to this nor subtract from it anything.” The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, “He will succeed if he is truthful.”"],[2952,"I saw Usama b. Zayd praying by the grave of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. Marwan b. al-Hakam came out and said, \"Do you pray toward his grave?\" He said, \"Indeed I love him.\" Then he said an ugly word to him and turned away. Usama left and said, \"O Marwan, you have harmed me. Indeed I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say, 'Indeed Allah hates the obscene, the one who is deliberately obscene, and you are obscene and deliberately obscene.'\""],[2953,"The heaviest thing placed in the believer's scale on the Day of Resurrection is a good character. Indeed, Allah hates the obscene, foul-mouthed person."],[2954,"When Allah gathers the first and the last on the Day of Resurrection, for a day about which there is no doubt, a caller will call out: 'Whoever associated anyone with Allah in his deed, let him seek his reward from that one, for Allah is the most self-sufficient of partners from association.'"],[2955,"Give glad tidings to this community of victory, loftiness, and empowerment. But whoever among them performs a deed of the Hereafter for the sake of this world, he will have no share in the Hereafter."],[2956,"Whoever seeks to be heard, Allah will make him heard; and whoever shows off, Allah will expose him."],[2957,"Whoever seeks to be heard, Allah will make him heard; and whoever shows off, Allah will expose him."],[2958,"\" Who is this?\" They said: \"Abu Hurairah.\" (He said):So I got close to him until I was sitting in front of him as he was narrating to the people. When he was silent and alone, I said to him: \" I ask youabsolute truth if you would narrate to me a Hadith which you heard from the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, That you understand and know.\" So Abu Hurairah said: \"You want me to narrate a Hadith to you which the Messenger of Allah ﷺ narrated to me that I understand and know.\" Then Abu Hurairah began sobbing profusely. We sat for a while, then he recovered and said: \"I shall narrate to you a Hadith which the Messenger of Allah ﷺ narrated in this House, while there was no one with us other than he and I.\" Then, again, Abu Hurairah began sobbing severely. Then he recovered, and wiped his face, and said: \"you want me to narrate to you a Hadith which the Messenger of Allah ﷺ narrated while he and I were sitting in this House, and no one was with us but he and I.\" Then Abu Hurairah began sobbing severely. Then he bent, falling on his face, so I supported him for a long time.Then he recovered and said: \"The Messenger of Allah narrated to me that on the Day of Judgement, Allah, Most High, will descend to His slaves t judge between them. Every nation shall be kneeling. The first of those who will be called before him will be a man who memorized the Qur'an, and a man who was killed in Allah's cause, and a wealthy man. Allah will say to the reciter: 'Did I not teach you what I revealed to My Messenger?\" He says: 'Of course O Lord!' He says: 'Then what did you do with what you learned?' He said: 'I would stand (in prayer reciting) with it during all hours of the night and all hours of the day.' Then Allah would say to him: 'You have lied.' And the angels will say: 'You have lied.'Allah will say to him: 'Rather, you wanted it to be said that so-and-so is a reciter. And that was said.' The person with the wealth will be brought, and Allah will say to him: 'Was I not so generous with you, such that I did not leave you having any need from anyone?' He will say: 'Of course O Lord!' He says: 'Then what did you do with what I gave to you?' He says: 'I would nurture the ties of kinship and give charity.' Then Allah will say to him: 'You have lied.' And the angels will say to him: 'You have lied.' Allah, Most High, will say: 'Rather, you wanted it to be said that so-and-so is so generous, and that was said.' Then the one who was killed in Allah's cause shall be brought, and Allah will say to him : 'For what were you killed?' So he says: 'I was commanded to fight in Your cause ,so I fought until I was killed.' Allah [Most High] will say to him: 'You have lied.' And the angels will say to him: 'You have lied.' Allah [Most High] will say: 'Rather, you wanted it be said that so-and-so is brave, and that was said.'\"Then the Messenger of Allah ﷺ hit me on my knees and said: 'O Abu Hurairah! These first three are the creatures of Allah with whom the fire will be enflamed on the Day of Judgement.'\"Al-Walid Abu 'Uthman Al-Mada'ini said: \"So 'Uqbah bin Muslim informed me that Shaufaiy, is the one who entered upon Mu'awiyah to inform him about this.\" Abu Uthman said: 'This has been done with these people, then how about with those who remain among the people?\" Then Mu'awiyah begin weeping so intensely, that we thought that he will kill himself with excessive weeping. We said: \"This man came to us to cause evil.\" Then Mu'awiyah recovered, wiped off his face and said: \"Allah and His Messenger told the truth: Whosoever desires the life of the world and its glitter, then we shall pay in full (the wages of) their deeds therein, and they shall have no diminution therein. They are those for whom there is nothing in the Hereafter Fire, and vain are the deeds they did therein. And of no effect is that which they used to do.\" (Using translation from Tirmidhī 2382)"],[2959,"Some people came and asked the Messenger of Allah ﷺ about a companion of theirs that they should cauterize him. He remained silent, then they asked him three times, and he remained silent and disliked that."],[2960,"'The Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to like good omens and dislike evil omens.'"],[2961,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ disliked a horse with a white mark on its right foreleg."],[2962,"\"Narrate on Friday once; if you refuse, then twice; if you refuse, then three times. And do not let me find you coming to a people while they are in their conversation, cutting it off. Rather, if they listen to your talk, then narrate to them. And avoid rhymed prose in supplication, for I knew the Prophet ﷺ and his Companions to dislike that.\""],[2963,"He used to dislike dragging the lower garment, displaying one’s adornment to those for whom it is not lawful, withholding water from its place, playing with dice, yellow dye, changing grey hair, tying amulets, and incantations except with the muʿawwidhāt."],[2964,"“The Messenger of Allah ﷺ disliked ten things: changing grey hair, a gold ring, playing with dice, incantations except with the muʿawwidhāt, amulets, dragging the lower garment, yellow dye, displaying one’s adornment in a place where it is not lawful, and withholding water from its place.”"],[2965,"The commencement of the Divine Inspiration to Messenger of Allah ﷺ was in the form of good righteous (true) dreams in his sleep. He never had a dream but that it came true like bright day light. He used to go in seclusion (the cave of) Hira where he used to worship(Allah Alone) continuously for many (days) nights. He used to take with him the journey food for that (stay) and then come back to (his wife) Khadija to take his food like-wise again for another period to stay, till suddenly the Truth descended upon him while he was in the cave of Hira. The angel came to him in it and asked him to read. The Prophet ﷺ replied, \"I do not know how to read.\" (The Prophet ﷺ added), \"The angel caught me (forcefully) and pressed me so hard that I could not bear it anymore. He then released me and again asked me to read, and I replied, \"I do not know how to read,\" whereupon he caught me again and pressed me a second time till I could not bear it anymore. He then released me and asked me again to read, but again I replied, \"I do not know how to read (or, what shall I read?).\" Thereupon he caught me for the third time and pressed me and then released me and said, \"Read: In the Name of your Lord, Who has created (all that exists). Has created man from a clot. Read and Your Lord is Most Generous...up to..... ..that which he knew not.\" (96.15) Then Messenger of Allah ﷺ returned with the Inspiration, his neck muscles twitching with terror till he entered upon Khadija and said, \"Cover me! Cover me!\" They covered him till his fear was over and then he said, \"O Khadija, what is wrong with me?\" Then he told her everything that had happened and said, 'I fear that something may happen to me.\" Khadija said, 'Never! But have the glad tidings, for by Allah, Allah will never disgrace you as you keep good reactions with your Kith and kin, speak the truth, help the poor and the destitute, serve your guest generously and assist the deserving, calamityafflicted ones.\" Khadija then accompanied him to (her cousin) Waraqa bin Naufal bin Asad bin ʿAbdul ʿUzza bin Qusai. Waraqa was the son of her paternal uncle, i.e., her father's brother, who during the Pre-Islamic Period became a Christian and used to write the Arabic writing and used to write of the Gospels in Arabic as much as Allah wished him to write. He was an old man and had lost his eyesight. Khadija said to him, \"O my cousin! Listen to the story of your nephew.\" Waraqa asked, \"O my nephew! What have you seen?\" The Prophet ﷺ described whatever he had seen. Waraqa said, \"This is the same Namus (i.e., Gabriel, the Angel who keeps the secrets) whom Allah had sent to Moses. I wish I were young and could live up to the time when your people would turn you out.\" Messenger of Allah ﷺ asked, \"Will they turn me out?\" Waraqa replied in the affirmative and said: \"Never did a man come with something similar to what you have brought but was treated with hostility. If I should remain alive till the day when you will be turned out then I would support you strongly.\" But after a few days Waraqa died and the Divine Inspiration was also paused for a while and the Prophet ﷺ became so sad as we have heard that he intended several times to throw himself from the tops of high mountains and every time he went up the top of a mountain in order to throw himself down, Gabriel would appear before him and say, \"O Muhammad! You are indeed Messenger of Allah ﷺ in truth\" whereupon his heart would become quiet and he would calm down and would return home. And whenever the period of the coming of the inspiration used to become long, he would do as before, but when he used to reach the top of a mountain, Gabriel would appear before him and say to him what he had said before. (Ibn ʿAbbas said regarding the meaning of: 'He it is that Cleaves the daybreak (from the darkness)' (6.96) that Al-Asbah. means the light of the sun during the day and the light of the moon at night). (Using translation from Bukhārī 6982)"],[2966,"I asked Abu Salamah which part of the Qur'an was revealed first. He said, \"{O you enveloped}.\" I said, \"I have been informed that the first surah revealed from the Qur'an was {Read in the name of your Lord who created}.\""],[2967,"I asked Abu Salama which chapter of the Quran was revealed first. He said, \"O you who wraps himself [in clothing]!\" I asked, \"Or was it 'Recite'?\" Then Abu Salama said, \"I asked Jabir ibn Abdullah about that, and he said, 'O you who wraps himself [in clothing]!' I asked, 'Or was it 'Recite'?' He said, 'I inform you of what the Messenger of Allah ﷺ informed us. He said, 'I was near the Mount Hira for a month, and when I finished my stay, I descended and hid myself in the valley. Then I heard a voice calling me. I looked ahead, behind me, to my right, and to my left, but I did not see anyone. Then the voice called again, and I looked up to the sky. And behold, it was above the throne in the air. I was seized with severe trembling. I went to Khadijah and said to her, 'Cover me! Cover me!' So they covered me until the fear subsided. Then Allah revealed to me, 'O you who wraps himself [in clothing], arise and warn! And your Lord, exalt [i.e., praise] and purify your garments.'\""],[2968,"When Allah decrees a matter in the heaven, the angels beat their wings in submission to His word, which is like a chain on a rock. Then when fear is removed from their hearts, they say, \"What did your Lord say?\" They say, \"The truth, and He is the Most High, the Most Great.\" Then the eavesdroppers hear it, and sometimes a meteor catches him before he can cast it down to the one below him, and sometimes the meteor does not catch him until he casts it down to the one below him."],[2969,"When Allah speaks the revelation, the inhabitants of the heaven hear from the heaven a sound like a chain being dragged on a rock, and they swoon. They remain like that until Jibril comes to them. When he comes, terror is removed from their hearts, and they say, \"O Jibril, what did your Lord say?\" He says, \"The truth,\" and they call out, \"The truth, the truth.\""],[2970,"Al-Harith b. Hisham asked the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, \"O Messenger of Allah, how does the revelation come to you?\" The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, \"Sometimes it comes to me like the ringing of a bell, and that is the severest upon me; then it leaves me and I have retained what he said. And sometimes the angel appears to me in the form of a man and speaks to me, and I retain what he says.\""],[2971,"The Prophet ﷺ used to treat the severity of the revelation by moving his lips. Ibn Abbas said, \"I move my lips like the Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to move his lips, and Allah revealed {Do not move your tongue to hasten it. Indeed, upon Us is its collection [in your heart] and [to make possible] its recitation.} He said, 'Its collection is in your heart, then recite it [from memory],' and He said, {So when We have recited it [through Gabriel], then follow its recitation.} He said, 'Listen to it and pay attention,' and He said, {Then indeed, upon Us is its clarification [to you].' Then it is upon Us [Allah] to make you recite it.\""],[2972,"I said to 'Uthman b. 'Affan, \"What led you to put al-Anfal and Bara'ah together, when Bara'ah is among the mi'in and al-Anfal is among the mathani, and you joined them?\" 'Uthman said, \"When a verse of the Qur'an was revealed, the Prophet ﷺ would call one of the scribes and say to him, 'Put it in the surah in which such-and-such is mentioned.' Al-Anfal was revealed in Madinah, and Bara'ah was revealed in Madinah, being among the last of the Qur'an. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ died without telling us where to put it, but I found its story similar to the story of al-Anfal, so I joined them together, and we did not write between them the line 'Bismillah al-Rahman al-Rahim.' I placed it among the seven long surahs.\""],[2973,"I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ saying, \"I have never desired anything ugly that the people of the pre-Islamic period desired except on two occasions, and both times Allah protected me from it.\""],[2974,"\"I was given four things none before us was given, and I asked my Lord for the fifth and He granted it to me: a prophet would be sent to his town and would not go beyond it, but I was sent to all people collectively; our enemy was made terrified of us for a month's journey; the earth was made for me a means of purification and mosques; and the fifth was made lawful for us and was not lawful for anyone before us. I asked my Lord for the fifth: I asked Him that no servant of my community who meets Him declaring His oneness but that He admits him to Paradise, and He granted it to me.\""],[2975,"I was favored over the prophets with six things: I was given comprehensive speech; I was aided with awe; spoils were made lawful for me; the earth was made pure and a mosque for me; I was sent to all creation; and the prophets were sealed with me."],[2976,"\"Indeed, with Allah I am written as the Seal of the Prophets, while Adam was still mixed in his clay. I shall inform you of the first of that: the supplication of my father Ibrahim, the glad tidings of Isa, and the dream of my mother which she saw when she gave birth to me—that a light came out of her which illuminated for her the palaces of Syria.\""],[2977,"I came to Hudhayfah and he said, \"Who are you, O bald one?\" I said, \"I am Zirr b. Hubaysh. Tell me about the prayer of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ in the Bayt al-Maqdis when he was taken on the Night Journey.\" He said, \"Who told you about it, O bald one?\" I said, \"The Qur'an.\" He said, \"The Qur'an?\" Then I recited, \"Exalted is He who took His servant by night,\" and thus is the recitation of 'Abdullah, up to His saying, {Indeed He is the Hearing, the Seeing}. He said, \"Do you think he prayed in it?\" I said, \"No.\" He said, \"He was brought a mount.\" Hammad said, \"'Asim described it, but I do not remember its description.\" He said, \"Jibril mounted him upon it, one of them riding behind the other, and he traveled with him that night until he came to the Bayt al-Maqdis. He was shown what is in the heavens and what is in the earth. Then they returned the same way they came, and he did not pray in it. Had he prayed, it would have become a sunnah.\""],[2978,"The Prophet ﷺ was brought al-Burāq on the night of his night journey, saddled and bridled, so that he could ride it. It proved difficult for him, so Jibrīl said to it, “What makes you do this? By Allah, no one more honored by Allah than him has ever ridden you.”"],[2979,"\"On the night I was taken on the night journey, I reached the Sacred House. Jibrīl split the rock with his finger and tied al-Burāq to it.” *"],[2980,"Whoever forgets a prayer, let him pray it when he remembers it; there is no expiation for it except that."],[2981,"\"On the night I was taken on the night journey, I passed by Mūsā ﷺ praying in his grave.\""],[2982,"\"On the night I was taken on the night journey, I passed by Mūsā while he was standing praying in his grave at the red sand dune.\""],[2983,"\"On the night I was taken on the night journey, I met Mūsā, who had a head of hair like a man of the Shanūʾah tribe, and I met ʿĪsā, who was a ruddy man as if he had just come out of a bath. I saw Ibrāhīm, and I am the most like his offspring among them to him. Two vessels were brought to me, one containing wine and the other milk. It was said to me, 'Take whichever you wish.' I took the milk, and it was said to me, 'You have been guided to the natural disposition. If you had taken the wine, your community would have gone astray.'\""],[2984,"\"On the night of the night journey, two cups were brought to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, one of wine and one of milk. He looked at them and then took the milk. Jibrīl ﷺ said to him, 'You have been guided to the natural disposition. If you had taken the wine, your community would have gone astray.'\""],[2985,"«The prophets were shown to me, and there was Moses ﷺ , a lean man, as if he were from the men of Shanūʾah. And I saw Jesus son of Mary ﷺ , and the closest of people to him and the one who most resembles him is ʿUrwah b. Masʿūd. And I saw Abraham, and the closest of people in resemblance to him is your companion—meaning himself. And I saw Gabriel, and the closest of people and the one who most resembles him is Diḥyah.»"],[2986,"\"On the night I was taken on the night journey, I saw men whose lips were being cut with scissors of fire. I said, 'Who are these, O Jibrīl?'\" He said, \"These are the preachers from your community who command people to do good but forget themselves, while they recite the Book. Do they not understand?\""],[2987,"\"I entered Paradise and saw a palace of gold. I said, 'Whose is this palace?' They said, 'For a young man of Quraysh.' I thought it was for me. I said, 'Who is he?' It was said, 'ʿUmar b. al-Khaṭṭāb.'\""],[2988,"I looked at Paradise, and most of its inhabitants were the poor. I looked at the Fire, and most of its inhabitants were women. And the people of fortune were being held back, and the disbelievers had been ordered to the Fire.\""],[2989,"I entered Paradise and found most of its inhabitants to be the poor. I looked into the Fire and found most of its inhabitants to be women. And I saw in it three being punished: a tall woman from Himyar who tied up a cat of hers, neither feeding it nor giving it drink, nor leaving it to eat from the vermin of the earth, so it was biting her front and back. And I saw in it the brother of Banu Da'da', the one who used to steal from the pilgrims with his hooked staff, and when he was noticed he would say, \"It only caught on my hooked staff.\" And the one who stole the two camels of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ."],[2990,"The Fire was shown to me, and I saw in it 'Amr b. Luhayy b. Qama'a b. Khindif dragging his intestines in the Fire. He was the first to change the covenant of Ibrahim and to let loose the sā'iba animals. He was the closest thing to Aktham b. Abi al-Jawn al-Khuza'i. Aktham said, \"O Messenger of Allah, will his resemblance harm me?\" He said, \"You are a Muslim and he is a disbeliever.\""],[2991,"\"I entered Paradise, and behold, I came upon a river whose two banks were of pearl. I struck with my hand the course of the water, and behold, it was fragrant musk. I said: O Gabriel, what is this? He said: This is al-Kawthar that Allah has granted you, or that your Lord has granted you.\""],[2992,"\"I entered Paradise, and behold, I came upon a river flowing, its whiteness like the whiteness of milk and sweeter than honey, and its two banks were tents of pearl. I struck with my hand, and behold, the soil was fragrant musk. I said to Gabriel: What is this? He said: This is al-Kawthar that Allah has granted you.\""],[2993,"\"While I was walking in Paradise, a river appeared before me, its two banks being domes of hollow pearl. The angel who was with him said: Do you know what this is? This is al-Kawthar that your Lord has granted you. And he struck with his hand to its ground and brought out musk from its clay.\""],[2994,"\"When Quraysh called me a liar, I stood in the Ḥijr, and Allah showed me the Sacred House. I began to inform them of its signs while I was looking at it.\""],[2995,"“That he saw the Prophet ﷺ and observed the seal that was between his shoulders.”"],[2996,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to me, “Come close to me and wipe my back.”"],[2997,"“I saw the seal between the shoulders of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, like a pigeon egg, its color like the color of his body.”"],[2998,"“The seal of prophethood was on the back of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, like a ball of flesh, on which was written, ‘Muhammad, Messenger of Allah.’”"],[2999,"Jibril came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ while he was playing with the boys. He took him, threw him down, split open his chest, and extracted a clot of blood from it, saying: “This is Satan’s share of you.” Then he washed it in a golden basin with Zamzam water, stitched him up, and returned him to his place. The boys came running to his mother—meaning his wet nurse—and said: “Muhammad has been killed.” They met him, and his color was pale. Anas said: “I used to see the trace of that stitching on his chest ﷺ.”"],[3000,"Umar b. al-Khattab ؓ was traveling with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ on one of his journeys. Umar asked him about something, but he did not answer him at all. Then he asked him again, but he did not answer. Then he asked him again, but he did not answer. Umar said, 'May your mother be bereaved of you, Umar! You have pestered the Messenger of Allah ﷺ three times, and each time he does not answer you.' Umar said, 'So I urged my camel on until I brought it ahead of the people, fearing that something concerning me had been revealed in the Quran. It was not long before I heard a crier calling to me. I came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, greeted him, and he said, \"A surah was revealed to me tonight that is more beloved to me than what the sun has risen upon.\" Then he recited: {Indeed, We have granted you a clear victory, so that Allah may forgive you your past and future sins.} (Quran 48:1–2)\""],[3001,"\"Indeed Allah chose Kinanah from the descendants of Isma'il, and chose Quraysh from Kinanah, and chose Banu Hashim from Quraysh, and chose me from Banu Hashim. So I am the master of the children of Adam, and no boast, and the first from whom the earth will split open, and the first intercessor and the first whose intercession is accepted.\""],[3002,"\"Yes, there was shown to me what will happen in the affairs of this world and the Hereafter. The first and the last were gathered on a single plain, until they went to Adam ﷺ while the sweat almost bridled them. They said, 'O Adam, you are the father of mankind. Allah chose you. Intercede for us with your Lord.' He said, 'I have encountered the like of what you have encountered. Go to your father after your father, to Nuh. Indeed Allah chose Adam and Nuh and the family of Ibrahim and the family of 'Imran above all the worlds.' So they go to Nuh and say, 'Intercede for us with your Lord, for Allah chose you and answered your supplication, and you did not leave on the earth any of the disbelievers.' He says, 'That is not with me. Go to Ibrahim, for Allah took him as an intimate friend.' So they come to Ibrahim and he says, 'That is not with me. Go to Musa, for Allah spoke to him directly.' Musa says, 'That is not with me, but go to 'Isa son of Maryam, for he heals the blind and the leper and brings the dead to life.' 'Isa says, 'That is not with me, but go to the master of the children of Adam, for he is the first from whom the earth will split open on the Day of Resurrection. Go to Muhammad, and let him intercede for you with your Lord.'\""],[3003,"I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ five nights before he passed away, addressing the people, saying: “O people, indeed there have been among you brothers and friends, and I declare my innocence before Allah from taking any of you as a close friend (khalīl). If I were to take from my community a close friend, I would have taken Abu Bakr as a close friend. Indeed Allah has taken me as a close friend, just as He took Ibrahim as a close friend. Indeed those before you took the graves of their prophets and righteous ones as places of worship, so do not take graves as places of worship, for I forbid you from that.”"],[3004,"“Indeed your companion is the close friend of Allah Almighty.”"],[3005,"“The distance between the two sides of my Pool is like [the distance] between Ayla and Sana‘a: a month’s journey; its width is like its length. In it are two spouts gushing from Paradise, of silver and gold. [Its water is] whiter than milk, sweeter than honey, and colder than snow. In it are pitchers [as numerous as] the number of the stars of the sky.”"],[3006,"Indeed, my Hawd is [as vast] as [the distance] between Ayla and San'a, and in it there are as many pitchers as the stars of the sky."],[3007,"\"My likeness and the likeness of the prophets before me is that of a man who built a structure, made it excellent and complete except for the place of one brick in a corner of its corners. People began to walk around it, marvel, and say, 'Why did you not place this brick?' He said, 'I am that brick, and I am the Seal of the Prophets, may Allah's blessings be upon them.'\""],[3009,"\"I was given five things no one before me was given: I was aided with awe for a month's journey; the earth was made for me a mosque and a means of purification, so any man of my community whom prayer overtakes should pray; war spoils were made lawful for me and were not lawful for anyone before me; I was given intercession; and a prophet would be sent to his people specifically, but I was sent to all people generally.\""],[3010,"\"I was sent with all-encompassing speech, and I was aided with terror, and while I was sleeping I was brought the keys of the treasures of the earth and they were placed in my hand.\""],[3011,"\"I was brought the keys of the world on a dappled horse, upon which was a velvet cloth of fine silk.\""],[3012,"“I was granted victory through the east wind, and ‘Ad was destroyed by the west wind.”"],[3013,"I was with Saʿīd b. Jubayr, and he said to us: Which of you saw the shooting star that fell last night? I said: I did. But I was not in prayer; rather I had been stung. He said: What did you do? I said: I sought a ruqyah (incantation). He said: What led you to that? I said: A hadith that al-Shaʿbī narrated to us. He said: What does al-Shaʿbī narrate to you? I said: He narrated to us from Buraydah b. al-Ḥuṣayb al-Aslamī that he said: “There is no ruqyah except for the evil eye or a sting.”"],[3014,"One day we prayed with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and he prolonged the standing. Normally when he prayed with us he would keep it light. We did not hear anything from him except that he kept saying: “My Lord, and I am among them.” Then I saw him reach out with his hand as if to take hold of something, then he bowed. After that he hastened. When the Messenger of Allah ﷺ finished with the salutation, he sat down and we sat around him. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “I knew that the length of my prayer and standing alarmed you.” We said: Yes, O Messenger of Allah, and we heard you saying: “My Lord, and I am among them.” The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “By the One in whose hand is my soul, there is nothing that you have been promised in the Hereafter except that it was presented to me in this place of mine, even Hell was presented to me. A part of it came towards me until it came close to this place of mine, and I feared that it would overwhelm you, so I said: My Lord, and I am among them; and He turned it away from you, and it retreated in pieces like carpets. I glanced at it and saw ʿAmr b. Ḥurthān, the brother of Banū Ghifār, leaning in Hell upon his bow, and in it was the Ḥimyarite woman, the owner of the cat that she had tied up: she neither fed it nor let it go.”"],[3015,"«The deeds of my Ummah, good and evil, were presented to me, and I found among their good deeds the removal of something harmful from the road, and I found among their evil deeds the sputum in the mosque that is not buried.»"],[3016,"While I was sleeping, two men came to me and took me by my upper arms and brought me to a rugged mountain. They said to me, \"Climb,\" until when I was on level ground of the mountain, I heard a loud sound. I said, \"What are these sounds?\" He said, \"This is the howling of the people of the Fire.\" Then he went with me, and I saw people hung by their Achilles tendons, their cheeks split, their cheeks streaming with blood. I said, \"Who are these?\" It was said, \"These are those who break their fast before the time of breaking it.\" Then he went with me, and I saw people with the worst swelling, the foulest odor, and the ugliest appearance. I said, \"Who are these?\" It was said, \"The male and female fornicators.\" Then he went with me, and I saw women whose breasts were being bitten by snakes. I said, \"What is the matter with these?\" It was said, \"These are those who deny their children their milk.\" Then he went with me, and I saw young boys playing between two rivers. I said, \"Who are these?\" It was said, \"These are the children of the believers.\" Then he ascended with me to a height, and I saw three people drinking from wine they had. I said, \"Who are these?\" They said, \"This is Ibrahim, Musa, and 'Isa, and they are waiting for you.\""],[3017,"The Prophet ﷺ was asked until they pressed him with questions, and he said: “Ask me, for by Allah, you will not ask me about anything except that I will make it clear to you.” Anas said: The people fell silent and feared that it might be before a great matter. We began to look right and left, and I saw every man burying his head in his garment, weeping, while the Messenger of Allah ﷺ kept saying: “Ask me, for by Allah, you will not ask me about anything except that I will make it clear to you.” Then a man stood up from the side of the mosque and said: O Prophet of Allah, who is my father? He said: “Your father is Ḥudhāfah.” Then Umar b. al-Khaṭṭāb ؓ stood up and said: O Prophet of Allah, we are content with Allah as Lord, with Islam as religion, and with Muhammad ﷺ as Messenger. We seek refuge in Allah from the evil of trials. The Prophet of Allah ﷺ said: “I have never seen good and evil like today; indeed Paradise and Hell were depicted for me, and I saw them beyond that wall.”"],[3018,"I asked Zirr b. Ḥubaysh about this verse: {Indeed he saw of the greatest signs of his Lord}. He said: Abdullah said: “He saw Gabriel in his true form, having six hundred wings.”"],[3019,"“I saw Gabriel at the Lote Tree of the Utmost Boundary, and upon him were six hundred wings, from whose feathers were scattered wonders of pearls and rubies.”"],[3020,"The Prophet ﷺ observed continuous fasting in Ramadan, and some of his companions also observed continuous fasting. He said, “If the month were extended for me, I would continue fasting such a continuous fast that would make those who go to extremes abandon their extremism. I remain in a state where my Lord feeds me and gives me drink.”"],[3021,"“There is none of you but has a devil.” They said, “Even you, O Messenger of Allah?” He said, “Even me, except that Allah helped me against him, so he became safe.”"],[3022,"There is none amongst you with whom is not an attache from amongst the jinn (devil). They (the Companions) said: Messenger of Allah, with you too? Thereupon he said: Yes, but Allah helps me against him and so I am safe from his hand and he does not command me but for good. (Using translation from Muslim 2814a)"],[3023,"I look at what is behind me just as I look at what is in front of me, so straighten your rows and perfect your bowing and prostration."],[3024,"Make your rows compact, bring them close together, and align your necks, for by the One in whose hand is my soul, I see Satan entering through the gaps in the rows as if they were small sheep."],[3026,"Uhud trembled while the Prophet ﷺ, Abu Bakr, Umar, and Uthman ؓ were on it. The Prophet ﷺ said, 'Be still, Uhud, for upon you are only a Prophet, a truthful one, and two martyrs.'"],[3027,"\"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ taught us to say when we sat following two rak'ahs: 'At-tahiyyatu lillahi was-salawatu wat-tayyibat, as-salamu 'alaika ayyuhan-Nabiyyu wa rahmatAllahi wa baraktuhu. As-salamu 'alaina wa 'ala 'ibad illahis-salihin, ashahdu an la illaha ill-Allah wa ashhadu anna Muhammadan 'abduhu wa rasuluhu (Allah compliments, prayers and pure words are due to Allah. Peace be upon you, O Prophet, and the mercy of Allah (SWT) and his blessings. Peace be upon us and upon the righteous slaves of Allah (SWT). I bear witness that none has the right to be worshipped except Allah and I bear witness that Muhammad is His slave and Messenger).'\" (Using translation from Nasāʾī 1162)"],[3028,"'Two visitors came to me last night and roused me. They said to me: \"Go,\" so I went with them until we came upon a man lying down, while another stood over him with a boulder, striking his head with it and splitting it. The boulder rolled away, so he went to the stone and picked it up. He did not return to him, I think he said, until his head healed as it was before, then he returned and did to him like the first time.' He said: 'I said: \"Glory be to Allah, what are these two?\" They said to me: \"Go, go.\"' He said: 'So I went with them and we came upon a man lying on his back, while another stood over him with an iron hook. He went to one side of his face and tore his mouth to the back of his neck, his nostril to the back of his neck, and his eye to the back of his neck. Then he turned to the other side and did to it like what he had done to the first side. He had not finished with that side before the first side healed as it was, then he returned and did to him like the first time.' He said: 'I said: \"Glory be to Allah, what are these two?\" They said: \"Go, go.\" So I went with them and we came upon something like a clay oven.' Awf said: 'I think he said: \"And in it were voices and clamor.\" We looked inside and there were naked men and women, and a river of flame beneath them. When the flame came to them, they cried out.' He said: 'I said: \"What are these?\" They said to me: \"Go, go.\"' He said: 'So we went on to a river, I think he said, red like blood, and in the river was a man swimming, and at the bank of the river was a man who had gathered many stones. Whenever the swimmer swam, he came to the man who had gathered the stones, opened his mouth for him, and the man placed a stone in it.' He said: 'I said: \"What are these?\" They said to me: \"Go, go.\"' He said: 'So we went on and came upon a man of hideous appearance, the ugliest man you could ever see, standing by a fire, stoking it and walking around it.' He said: 'I said to them: \"What is this?\" They said to me: \"Go, go.\" So we went on and came upon a garden containing every spring flower, and in the middle of the garden was a tall man, so tall I could hardly see his head in the sky, and around him were more children than I had ever seen, and the most beautiful.' He said: 'I said to them: \"What are these?\" They said to me: \"Go, go.\" So we went on and came to a huge tree, the largest and most beautiful I had ever seen. They said to me: \"Climb it.\" We climbed it and reached a city built of gold and silver bricks. We came to the gate of the city and asked for it to be opened, and it was opened for us. There we were met by men, half of whose bodies were the most beautiful you could see, and half the ugliest you could see.' He said: 'They said to them: \"Go and plunge into that river.\" There was a river flowing across, its water as white as pure milk. They went and plunged into it, then returned, and the ugliness had gone from them, and they were in the most beautiful form.' He said: 'They said to me: \"This is the Garden of Eden, and that is your dwelling.\"' He said: 'My sight rose upward, and there was a palace like a white cloud.' He said: 'They said to me: \"That is your dwelling.\"' He said: 'I said to them: \"May Allah bless you both, let me enter it.\" They said to me: \"Not now, but you shall enter it.\"' He said: 'I have seen wonders since tonight; what is this that I have seen?' He said: 'They said to me: \"We will now inform you. The first man you came upon whose head was being split with a stone is the one who learns the Quran but then abandons it and sleeps through the prescribed prayers. The man you came upon whose mouth, eye, and nostril were being torn to the back of his neck is the one who leaves his house in the morning and tells a lie that spreads to the horizons. The naked men and women in the clay oven are the adulterers and adulteresses. The man in the river swallowing stones is the one who consumes usury. The hideous man by the fire stoking it is Malik, the keeper of Hell. The tall man in the garden is Ibrahim ﷺ , and the children around him are every child born upon the fitrah.\"' He said: 'Some of the Muslims said: \"O Messenger of Allah, what about the children of the polytheists?\" The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"And the children of the polytheists.\" As for the people half of whom were beautiful and half ugly, they are a people who mixed righteous deeds with evil ones, and Allah pardoned them.'"],[3029,"\"When Allah created Adam, Iblis began to circle around him. When he saw that he was hollow, he said, 'I have overcome him; a creature that cannot control itself.'\""],[3030,"\"When Allah created Adam, he sneezed, and his Lord inspired him to say, 'Praise be to Allah.' His Lord said to him, 'May Allah have mercy on you.' Therefore, His mercy preceded His wrath.\""],[3031,"\"When He breathed into Adam and the soul reached his head, he sneezed and said, 'Praise be to Allah, Lord of the worlds.'\""],[3032,"Umar b. al-Khattab ؓ was asked about this verse: (And when your Lord took from the Children of Adam, from their backs, their descendants, and made them bear witness against themselves, \"Am I not your Lord?\" They said, \"Yes, we bear witness\") — the verse."],[3033,"When Allah created Adam and breathed into him the spirit, he sneezed and said, \"Praise be to Allah,\" so he praised Allah by Allah's permission. His Lord said to him, \"May your Lord have mercy on you, O Adam. Go to those angels, to a group of them sitting, and greet them.\" He said, \"Peace be upon you.\" They said, \"And upon you be peace and the mercy of Allah.\" Then he returned to his Lord, and He said, \"This is your greeting and the greeting of your descendants among one another.\" And Allah, Mighty and Exalted, said, with His two hands closed, \"Choose whichever of them you wish.\" He said, \"I choose the right hand of my Lord, and both hands of my Lord are blessed right hands.\" Then He spread them open, and there in them were Adam and his descendants. He said, \"My Lord, who are these?\" He said, \"These are your descendants.\" And every human among them had his lifespan written between his eyes, and among them was a man, the brightest of them or one of the brightest, for whom only forty years were written. He said, \"My Lord, what is this?\" He said, \"This is your son Dawud, and Allah has written his lifespan as forty years.\" He said, \"My Lord, increase his lifespan.\" He said, \"That is what I have written for him.\""],[3034,"«Allah created Adam from the surface of the entire earth, so his descendants came out according to that: among them are the black, the white, the red, and the yellow, and among them are those in between; and the easy-going and the harsh, and the wicked and the good.»"],[3035,"\"Indeed, Allah, Exalted is He, created Adam from a handful He took from the entire earth, so the children of Adam came according to the measure of the earth: among them the red, the black, the white, and the yellow, and between that; and the easy-going and the hard, and the evil and the good.\""],[3036,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ took me by the hand and said, \"Allah, Exalted is He, created the soil on Saturday, created the mountains in it on Sunday, created the trees on Monday, created the disliked things on Tuesday, created the light on Wednesday, spread the beasts in it on Thursday, and created Adam after the afternoon on Friday, the last of creation in the last hour of the hours of Friday.\""],[3037,"\"Allah created Adam in His image, and his height was sixty cubits. When He created him, He said, 'Go and greet those people—they were a group of angels sitting—and listen to how they greet you, for that is your greeting and the greeting of your descendants.'\""],[3038,"“Were it not for the Children of Israel, food would not spoil and meat would not become putrid. And were it not for Hawwa’, no female would ever betray her husband.”"],[3039,"\"Abraham was circumcised with an adze when he was one hundred and twenty years old, and he lived after that eighty years.\""],[3040,"\"Abraham the Prophet ﷺ was circumcised when he reached one hundred and twenty years, and he lived after that eighty years, and he was circumcised with an adze.\""],[3041,"Abu Hurayrah said: «Ibrahim never lied except on three occasions: two were for the sake of Allah — His saying, {Indeed, I am ill} and His saying, {Rather, the largest of them did it}.» He said: «He passed by one of the tyrants, and with him was his wife Sarah. It was said to the tyrant: 'There is a man here with a woman among the most beautiful of people.' So he sent for him, and he came to him and entered upon him. He asked him, and he said: 'She is my sister.'» He said: «He came to her and said: 'This man asked me about you, and I told him that you are my sister. You are my sister in the Book of Allah, so do not contradict me.'» He said: «When he saw her, he went to assault her, so she called upon Allah and he was seized. He said: 'Call upon Allah for me, and I will not return.' So she called upon him, and he was released. Then he went to assault her, so she called upon Allah, and he was seized with a seizure more severe than the first. He said: 'Call upon Allah for me, and I will not return.' So she called upon him, and he was released. Then he went to assault her, so she called upon Allah, and he was seized with a seizure more severe than the first two. He said: 'Call upon Allah for me, and I will not return.' So she called upon him, and he was released. He said to the closest of his chamberlains: 'You have not brought me a human being; you have brought me a devil.' And he made Hajar serve her. When Ibrahim saw her, he said: 'What is the matter?' She said: 'Allah sufficed against the plot of the disbelieving, wicked one, and He has made Hajar serve me.'» Abu Hurayrah said: «When he narrated this hadith, he would say: 'That is your mother, O Banu Ma' al-Sama'.'»"],[3042,"When Jibril struck Zamzam with his heel, the mother of Isma'il began to gather the pebbles.\" The Prophet ﷺ said: \"May Allah have mercy on Hajar; had she left it, it would have been a flowing spring."],[3043,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ went out to a group of Aslam who were competing in archery in the marketplace and said, “Shoot, O sons of Ismail, for your father was an archer, and I am with the sons of so-and-so,” meaning one of the two parties. They stopped and held their hands. He said, “What is the matter with you? Shoot.” They said, “How can we shoot when you are with the sons of so-and-so?” He said, “Shoot, and I am with all of you.”"],[3044,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ went out while Aslam were shooting. He said, “Shoot, O sons of Ismail, for your father was an archer. Shoot, and I am with Ibn al-Adra‘.” The people withheld their bows and said, “Whoever you are with wins.” He said, “Shoot, and I am with all of you.”"],[3045,"\"We are more entitled to doubt than Abraham when he said, 'My Lord, show me how You give life to the dead.' He said, 'Do you not believe?' He said, 'Yes, but to set my heart at rest.' And may Allah have mercy on Lot. He would indeed seek shelter in a strong support. And if I had remained in prison as long as Joseph remained, I would have answered the caller.\""],[3046,"\"If the caller who came to Joseph had come to me, I would have answered him, and He said to him: 'Return to your lord and ask him what was the matter with the women who cut their hands.' And may the mercy of Allah be upon Lot. He would indeed seek shelter in a strong support when he said to his people, 'If only I had strength against you or could seek shelter in a strong support.' And Allah sent no prophet after him except in a numerous clan of his people.\""],[3047,"\"May Allah have mercy on Joseph. Were it not for the word he said, 'Mention me to your lord,' he would not have remained in prison as long as he did. And may Allah have mercy on Lot. He would indeed seek shelter in a strong support when he said to his people, 'If only I had strength against you or could seek shelter in a strong support.'\" He said: \"And Allah sent no prophet after him except in a numerous clan of his people.\""],[3048,"“The noble one, son of the noble one, son of the noble one, son of the noble one: Yūsuf b. Yaʿqūb b. Isḥāq b. Ibrāhīm, may the blessings of Allah be upon them.”"],[3049,"\"The Children of Israel used to bathe naked, looking at one another's private parts, while Moses used to bathe alone. They said, 'By Allah, nothing prevents Moses from bathing with us except that he has a hernia.' He went once to bathe and placed his garment on a stone, and the stone fled with his garment. Moses ran after it, saying, 'My garment, stone! My garment, stone!' until the Children of Israel saw Moses' private parts and said, 'By Allah, there is no defect in Moses.' The stone stopped after the people had seen it, so he took his garment and began striking the stone.\""],[3050,"A man said about something the Prophet ﷺ distributed, 'There is no justice in this.' I said, 'By Allah, I will tell the Messenger of Allah.' So I told him, and he said, 'May Allah have mercy on Musa; he was afflicted with worse than this and was patient.'"],[3051,"\"Moses asked his Lord about six qualities which he thought were exclusively his, and a seventh which Moses did not like. He said: 'O Lord, which of Your servants is most pious?' He said: 'The one who remembers and does not forget.' He said: 'Which of Your servants is most guided?' He said: 'The one who follows guidance.' He said: 'Which of Your servants is most wise in judgment?' He said: 'The one who judges for people as he judges for himself.' He said: 'Which of Your servants is most knowledgeable?' He said: 'A scholar who is not satiated with knowledge, who gathers people's knowledge to his own.' He said: 'Which of Your servants is most honored?' He said: 'The one who, when he has power, forgives.' He said: 'Which of Your servants is most self-sufficient?' He said: 'The one who is content with what he is given.' He said: 'Which of Your servants is most poor?' He said: 'A person who is deprived.'\" The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"Self-sufficiency is not from abundance of goods; self-sufficiency is richness of the soul. If Allah wants good for a servant, He places his richness in his soul and his piety in his heart. If Allah wants evil for a servant, He places his poverty before his eyes.\""],[3052,"The Prophet ﷺ said, \"Moses asked his Lord, 'Which people of Paradise will have the lowest rank?' He said, 'A man who will come after all the people of Paradise have entered, and it will be said to him, \"Enter Paradise,\" and he will say, \"How can I enter Paradise when the people have taken their places and received their rewards?\" He will be told, \"Would you be content if you were given a kingdom equal to the kingdoms of the world?\" He will say, \"I am content, my Lord.\" He will be told, \"You will have that and ten times as much.\" He will say, \"I am content, my Lord.\" He will be told, \"You will have that and whatever your soul desires and your eye finds delight in.\" Moses asked his Lord, 'Which people of Paradise will have the highest rank?' He said, 'I will tell you about those whom I have created with My own hand and sealed with My own seal. No eye has seen, no ear has heard, and no human heart has ever imagined their reward.' The proof of that is in the Book of Allah the Exalted, where He says, \"No person knows what is kept hidden for them of joy as a reward for what they used to do.\" (Quran 32:17)\""],[3053,"\"Moses said, 'O Lord, teach me something by which I may remember You and supplicate You.' He said, 'Say, O Moses, \"There is no god but Allah.\"' He said, 'O Lord, all Your servants say this.' He said, 'Say, \"There is no god but Allah.\"' He said, 'I only want something that You single me out for.' He said, 'O Moses, if the people of the seven heavens and the seven earths were in one pan of a scale, and \"There is no god but Allah\" in the other, it would outweigh them: \"There is no god but Allah.\"'\""],[3054,"He and al-Ḥurr b. Qays b. Ḥiṣn al-Fazārī disputed about the companion of Mūsā. Ibn ʿAbbās said, “He is al-Khaḍir.” Ubayy b. Kaʿb passed by them, so Ibn ʿAbbās called him and said, “O Abū al-Ṭufayl, come to us, for I and this companion of mine have disputed about the companion of Mūsā, the one about whom Mūsā asked the way to meet him. Have you heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say anything about him?” He said, “I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: ‘While Mūsā was among a gathering of the Children of Israel, a man came to him and said to him, “Do you know anyone more knowledgeable than you?” Mūsā said, “No.” Then Allah revealed to Mūsā, “Rather, Our servant al-Khaḍir.” So Mūsā asked the way to meet him. Allah made the fish a sign for him and it was said to him, “When you miss the fish, turn back, for you will meet him.” Mūsā traveled as long as Allah willed him to travel, then he said to his servant, “Bring us our breakfast.” His servant said to Mūsā when he asked for breakfast, “Did you see when we took refuge at the rock? I forgot the fish, and none but Satan made me forget to mention it.” Mūsā said to his servant, “That is what we were seeking.” So they retraced their footsteps, and they found Khaḍir. Then what happened between them was as Allah related in His Book.’”"],[3055,"I said to Ibn 'Abbas: 'Nawf al-Bikali claims that Moses ﷺ is not the companion of al-Khidr, but it was another Moses.' He said: 'The enemy of Allah has lied. Ubayy b. Ka'b informed us from the Messenger of Allah ﷺ that he said: \"Moses stood up among the Children of Israel as a preacher, and it was said to him: 'Who is the most knowledgeable of people?' He said: 'I am.' Allah reproached him for not attributing knowledge to Him, so He said: 'A servant of Mine at the junction of the two seas is more knowledgeable than you.' He said: 'O Lord, how can I reach him?' He said: 'Take a fish and put it in a basket; wherever you lose the fish, he will be there.' So he took the fish and placed it in the basket and gave it to his servant. They set out until they came to the rock. Moses slept, and the fish stirred in the basket, came out, and fell into the sea. Allah held back the flow of water for it, making it like an arch, so that the sea became a path for the fish, and a wonder for Moses and his servant. They went on walking. When it was the next day, Moses felt fatigue and said: 'Bring us our meal; we have certainly met with fatigue from this journey of ours.'\""],[3056,"\"The boy whom al-Khidr killed was created as a disbeliever on the day he was created.\""],[3057,"When the Messenger of Allah ﷺ mentioned any of the prophets, he began with himself. One day he said, “May Allah's mercy be upon us and upon Musa. Had he been patient with his companion, he would have seen wonders beyond wonders. But he said, 'If I ask you about anything after this, do not accompany me.'”"],[3058,"\"Al-Khidr was named Khidr because he sat on a white fur, and it turned green and stirred beneath him.\""],[3059,"“It is as if I am looking at Musa b. 'Imran descending from the mountain pass of Harsha on foot.”"],[3060,"That the Messenger of Allah ﷺ came to the valley of al-Azraq and said: \"It is as if I can see Moses descending, raising his voice in supplication to his Lord with the talbiyah.\" And he passed by a mountain pass and said: \"What is this?\" It was said: \"Such-and-such a pass.\" He said: \"It is as if I can see Moses throwing stones at the jamrah on a red camel, its halter of palm fiber, and upon him a woolen cloak.\""],[3061,"We set out with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ from Makkah to Madinah. When we came to the valley of al-Azraq, he said, \"Which valley is this?\" They said, \"The valley of al-Azraq.\" He said, \"It is as if I am looking at Musa, describing his height, his hair, and his color, placing his two fingers in his two ears, with a fervent cry to Allah Almighty with the talbiyah, passing through this valley.\" Then we traversed the valley until we came to - Dawud said: I think it was Thaniyyat Harsha - he said, \"Which mountain pass is this?\" We said, \"Thaniyyat Harsha.\" He said, \"It is as if I am looking at Yunus on a red camel, with the camel's nose-rein of palm fiber, wearing a woolen jubbah, calling out in the daytime at this mountain pass with the talbiyah.\""],[3063,"\"The Angel of Death came to Moses to take his soul. He said to him: 'Answer your Lord.' Moses struck the eye of the Angel of Death and gouged it out. The Angel of Death returned to his Lord and said: 'O Lord, You sent me to a servant who does not want to die, and he has gouged out my eye.' Allah restored his eye and said to him: 'Go back to him and say: Do you want life? If you want life, place your hand on the back of a bull; for every hair covered by your hand, you will live a year.' He said: 'Then what?' He said: 'Death.' He said: 'Now, from near.' Then he said: 'Lord, bring me near the Holy Land within a stone's throw.'\" The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"If I were with him, I would show you his grave, beside the road, near the red sand hill.\""],[3064,"\"The report is not like seeing. Allah told Moses that his people had done such-and-such, but he did not care, until when he saw it with his own eyes, he cast down the tablets.\""],[3065,"\"The one who sees is not like the one who is told. Allah informed Moses that his people had been tempted, but he did not cast down the tablets; when he saw them, he cast down the tablets.\""],[3066,"\"Adam and Moses disputed, and Adam confuted Moses. Moses said: 'You are Adam who led people astray and brought them out of Paradise.' Adam said to him: 'Are you Moses whom Allah gave knowledge of everything and chose over people with His messages?' He said: 'Yes.' He said: 'Then do you blame me for a matter that was decreed upon me before I was created?'\""],[3067,"Adam and Musa argued. Musa said, 'You are Adam whom Allah created with His hand and breathed into you from His spirit, and you led people astray and expelled them from Paradise.' Adam said, 'You are Musa whom Allah chose with His speech. Do you blame me for a deed I did that Allah decreed for me before He created the heavens and the earth?' So Adam prevailed over Musa."],[3068,"«Adam and Musa had an argument. Musa said: 'O Adam, you are our father. You disappointed us and caused us to be expelled from the Garden.' Adam said to him: 'O Musa, Allah chose you for His speech and wrote for you with His hand. Do you blame me for a matter that was decreed upon me forty years before He created me?' He said: So Adam won the argument against Musa. So Adam won the argument against Musa. So Adam won the argument against Musa.»"],[3069,"«Recitation was made light for David, so he would order his mount to be saddled, and he would finish reciting the Psalms before his mount was saddled.»"],[3070,"\"Sulayman b. Dawud swore: 'I will go around to one hundred women, each of whom will bear a boy who will fight in the path of Allah.' The Prophet ﷺ said: 'If he had said: If Allah wills, it would have been as he said.'\""],[3071,"\"Sulayman b. Dawud swore: 'Tonight I will go around to ninety women, each of whom will give birth to a boy who will fight in the path of Allah.' His companion, or the angel, said to him: 'Say: If Allah wills.' But he forgot and went around that night to ninety women, and none of them brought anything except one woman who brought half a boy.\" The Prophet ﷺ said: \"If he had said: If Allah wills, he would not have broken his oath, and he would have attained his need.\""],[3072,"\"The most beloved prayer to Allah is the prayer of Dawud. He used to sleep half the night, stand for a third, and sleep a sixth. The most beloved fasting to Allah is the fasting of Dawud. He used to fast one day and break his fast one day.\""],[3073,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to me: «Have I not been told that you fast during the day and stand in prayer at night? If you do that, the eye will sink and the soul will become exhausted. No one who fasts forever has fasted. Fasting three days of every month is the fasting of a lifetime. Indeed, David used to fast one day and break his fast one day, and he did not flee when he met [the enemy].»"],[3074,"«David used not to eat except from the work of his own hands.»"],[3075,"“Satan appeared before me in this prayer place of mine, so I seized him and choked him until I felt the coldness of his tongue on the back of my hand. Were it not for the supplication of my brother Solomon, he would have been tied up for you to see.”"],[3076,"“An ifrit from the jinn came to me last night to interrupt my prayer, but Allah enabled me to overpower him. I wanted to seize him and tie him to one of the pillars of the mosque so that you could all wake up and look at him.” He said, “Then I remembered the saying of my brother Solomon: {My Lord, forgive me and grant me a kingdom that will not belong to anyone after me}. So Allah turned him back humiliated.”"],[3077,"Sulayman b. Dawud asked Allah, Blessed and Exalted, for three things, and He granted him two, and I hope He granted him the third. He asked Him for a kingdom that would not befit anyone after him, and He granted it to him. He asked Him for a judgment that would coincide with His judgment, and He granted it to him. He asked Him that whoever comes to this House—meaning the Holy House (Jerusalem)—intending only to pray in it, that he would come out of it as on the day his mother gave birth to him.' The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, 'And I hope that He granted him the third.'"],[3078,"Two women came to Dawud, each claiming the child as her own. He ruled in favor of the older one. When they went out, Sulayman said, 'How did he judge between you?' They told him. He said, 'Bring me a knife.'—The first person I heard say \"al-sikkin\" (knife) was the Messenger of Allah ﷺ; we used to call it \"al-mudya.\"—Then the younger woman said, 'What?' He said, 'I will split him between you.' She said, 'Give him to her.' The older woman said, 'Split him between us.' He said, 'So Sulayman ruled in favor of the younger one and said, \"If he were your son, you would not be pleased for us to split him.\"'"],[3079,"Ayyub, the Prophet of Allah ﷺ, remained in his affliction for eighteen years. The near and the far shunned him except two men from among his brothers, who were of his closest brothers. They would come to him morning and evening. One of them said to his companion, 'You know, by Allah, Ayyub committed a sin that no one in the worlds has committed.' His companion said, 'What is that?' He said, 'For eighteen years Allah has not shown him mercy and removed his affliction.' When they came to him in the evening, the man could not restrain himself until he mentioned that to him. Ayyub said, 'I do not know what you are saying, but Allah knows that I used to pass by two men disputing and mentioning Allah, and I would return to my house and make expiation for them, disliking that Allah be mentioned except in truth.' He said, 'He used to go out to relieve himself, and when he finished, his wife would take him by the hand. One day he was delayed. Allah revealed to Ayyub in his place, \"Strike with your foot; this is a cool bathing place and a drink.\" She found him late and reached him. He came to her, Allah having removed from him the affliction, and he was in the best condition. When she saw him, she said, 'May Allah bless you. Have you seen the Prophet of Allah, this afflicted one? By Allah, I have seen no one more resembling him than you when he was healthy.' He said, 'I am he.' He had two threshing floors: one for wheat and one for barley. Allah sent two clouds. When one of them was over the wheat floor, it poured gold into it until it overflowed, and the other poured silver onto the barley floor until it overflowed.'"],[3080,"«While Job was bathing naked, locusts of gold rained down upon him, and Job began to scoop them into his garment. His Lord called him: O Job, have I not made you rich enough to dispense with what you see? He said: Yes, but I have no richness without Your mercy.»"],[3081,"«Butterflies of gold rained down upon Job, and he began to take them. But Allah revealed to him: Have I not made you ample? He said: Yes, O Lord, but I have no richness without Your bounty.»"],[3083,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"Every child of Adam is touched by Shaytan on the day his mother gives birth to him, except for Maryam and her son 'Isa, peace be upon them.\""],[3084,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, \"Every newborn is touched by Satan, causing it to cry loudly, except for Mary, daughter of Imran, and her son. If you wish, recite: 'Indeed, I seek refuge for her and her offspring from Satan, the expelled.'\""],[3085,"«I saw myself tonight at the Kaʿbah, and I saw a brown man, the most handsome of brown men you could see, with a lock of hair, the most handsome lock you could see, which he had combed, and it was dripping water, leaning on two men or on the shoulders of two men, circumambulating the House. I asked: Who is this? They said: Jesus son of Mary. Then I saw a man with very curly hair, blind in the right eye, as if his eye were a floating grape. I asked: Who is this? They said: The false messiah, the Dajjal.»"],[3086,"«Allah took David from among his companions, and they were not tempted and did not change. And the companions of the Messiah remained upon his Sunnah and guidance for two hundred years.»"],[3087,"\"Isa b. Maryam saw a man stealing, so Isa said: 'Did you steal?' The man said: 'No, by the One besides whom there is no god.' So Isa said: 'I believe in Allah, and I disbelieve my own eyes.'\""],[3088,"And the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: 'I am the closest of people to Jesus, son of Mary, in this world and the Hereafter.' They said: 'How is that, O Messenger of Allah?' He said: 'The prophets are paternal half-brothers; their mothers are different, but their religion is one. And there is no prophet between us.'"],[3089,"The Prophet ﷺ said: 'I am the closest of people to Jesus. The prophets are sons of co-wives, and there is no prophet between me and Jesus.'"],[3090,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"My likeness and the likeness of the prophets is that of a palace whose construction was made excellent and from which the place of one brick was left. Onlookers walked around it and marveled at its excellent construction except for the place of that brick; they faulted nothing besides it. I was the place of that brick; the messengers were sealed with me.\""],[3091,"It is as if I am looking at the Messenger of Allah ﷺ relating about a prophet among the prophets whom his people struck until they made his face bleed. He began wiping the blood from his face and saying, 'O Lord, forgive my people, for they do not know.'"],[3092,"“No prophet was believed as I have been believed. Among the prophets were those whom only one man from his community believed.”"],[3093,"Abdullah b. Umar turned toward me while I was camped under a lote tree on the road to Makkah and said, “What made you camp under this tree?” I said, “I sought its shade.” He said, “Is there any other reason?” I said, “No, nothing else made me camp here.” Abdullah b. Umar said, “The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, ‘When you are between the two rugged hills of Mina’—and he gestured with his hand toward the east—‘there is a valley called al-Surar, in which there is a tree under which seventy prophets were given glad tidings.’”"],[3094,"\"There is no prophet but warned his nation against the Dajjal. I will make clear to you something that you will know to be true: he is one-eyed, and your Lord is not one-eyed. Between his eyes is written 'kafir' (disbeliever), which every believer, literate or illiterate, will read.\""],[3095,"We were with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ picking kabath, and he said, 'Take the black ones, for they are the best.' We said, 'Did you use to shepherd sheep?' He said, 'Yes, and there is no prophet but that he shepherded them.'"],[3096,"We were with the Prophet ﷺ and we were picking kabath, and the Prophet ﷺ said, 'Take the black ones from it, for they are the best. I used to eat them when I was a shepherd.' They said, 'O Messenger of Allah, were you a shepherd?' He said, 'And no prophet was sent except that he was a shepherd.'"],[3097,"An ant bit a prophet among the prophets, so he ordered the ant colony to be burned. Then Allah revealed to him: An ant bit you, and you destroyed a community among the communities that glorify Allah."],[3098,"A prophet from among the prophets camped under a tree, and an ant bit him. He ordered their dwelling to be burned upon those inside it. Then Allah revealed to him: Was it not one ant?"],[3099,"From the Prophet ﷺ , a prophet from among the prophets went on a military expedition with his companions. He said, \"No man should build a house without settling in it, or marry a woman without entering upon her, or have any need to return.\" He encountered the enemy when the sun was about to set. He prayed, \"O Allah, it is a command, and I am under command. Stop it from setting until I take revenge between me and them.\" Allah caused the sun to stop setting, and they fought against the enemy. They gathered spoils of war, but the fire did not consume it, for whenever they would gather war booty, Allah would send fire on it and consume it. Their prophet said to them, \"Among you, there are traitors. Let a man from every tribe come and pledge allegiance to me.\" They went to him and pledged allegiance. The hands of two men stuck to his hand, and they said, \"You are accusing us of treachery.\" He said, \"Indeed, there is a golden statue of a cow in the likeness of its head.\" So they brought it and threw it into the spoils of war. Allah sent fire, and it consumed it. At that moment, the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, \"Indeed, Allah provided us with spoils of war as a mercy. He showed mercy to us and stayed the hand of the enemy because of our weakness.\""],[3100,"'A prophet among the prophets went on a raid and said to his people: No man who has married a woman and wants to consummate with her should follow me; nor one who raised a building and has not raised its roof; nor one who bought sheep and awaits their birth. He raided and drew near to the monastery at the time of Asr prayer or close to that, then said to the sun: You are commanded, and I am commanded; O Allah, hold it back for me a while. So it was held back until Allah granted him victory. They gathered what they had taken as spoils, and the fire came to consume it, but the fire refused to eat it. He said: There is some stolen property among you, so let one man from every tribe pledge allegiance to me. They did, and the hand of a man stuck to his hand. He said: The stolen property is among you; let your tribe pledge allegiance to me. His tribe pledged allegiance to him, and the hand of two or three men stuck to his hand. He said: The stolen property is among you. So they brought out a piece of gold like the head of a cow and placed it in the wealth, and it was on the ground. The fire came and consumed it. Spoils were not lawful for anyone before us; and that is because Allah saw our weakness and made them good for us.'"],[3101,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ murmured something we did not understand. He said: “Did you notice me?” We said: Yes. He said: “I mentioned a prophet among the prophets who was given armies from his people. He said: ‘Who will stand against these?’ Allah revealed to him: ‘Choose for your people one of three: either I send upon them an enemy from other than them, or hunger, or death.’ He consulted his people about that. They said: ‘You are the prophet of Allah; we entrust that to you; choose for us.’ He stood for his prayer—and they, when they were frightened, resorted to prayer—and he prayed as long as Allah willed. Then he said: ‘O Lord, as for an enemy from other than them, and hunger, no; but death.’ So death was sent upon them for three days, and seventy thousand of them died. The murmuring you see from me is that I say: ‘O Allah, by You I fight, and by You I attack, and there is no might and no power except by Allah.’”"],[3102,"the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, 'There has not been a prophet except that he had disciples whom he would guide with his guidance and who would follow his Sunnah (way of life). Then after them, there would be generations who would say what they do not do and do what they disapprove of. So, whoever fights against them with his hands, he is a believer, and whoever fights against them with his tongue, he is a believer, and whoever fights against them with his heart, he is a believer. There is no faith beyond that even to the weight of a mustard seed.'"],[3103,"«There is no prophet except that he has two close advisors: one that commands him to do good and forbids him from evil, and one that spares no effort to harm him. Whoever is protected from its evil is indeed protected.»"],[3104,"«Allah did not send any prophet nor appoint any caliph except that he had two close advisors: one that commands him to do good and urges him to it, and one that commands him to do evil and urges him to it. The protected one is the one whom Allah protects.»"],[3105,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, \"Indeed, every prophet has a prayer that he made for his Ummah (community), and I have hidden my prayer as an intercession for my Ummah.\""],[3106,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, \"Every prophet has a prayer that he has made for his nation, and I have kept my prayer as an intercession for my nation on the Day of Judgment.\""],[3108,"“The Children of Israel were governed by prophets; whenever a prophet died, another prophet arose. There is no prophet after me.” They said, “What will there be after you?” He said, “Rulers, and they will be many.” They said, “What do you command us, O Messenger of Allah?” He said, “Fulfill the pledge of allegiance to the first, then the first, and give them their due, for Allah will ask them about what is due to you.”"],[3109,"A man asked, \"O Messenger of Allah, was Adam a prophet?\" He replied, \"Yes, he was spoken to by Allah.\" The man asked, \"So, how many generations were there between him and Noah?\" He replied, \"Ten generations.\""],[3110,"“Beware of oppression, for oppression will be darkness on the Day of Resurrection. Beware of obscenity, for Allah does not love the obscene and the one who uses obscene language. Beware of miserliness, for miserliness caused those before you to shed their blood, sever their kinship ties, and regard their sacred things as lawful.”"],[3111,"While a man was walking on a road, he found a thorny branch on the path, so he took it, and Allah thanked him and forgave him."],[3112,"A man from those before you was called to account and no good was found for him except a thorny branch that was on the path harming people, so he removed it, and he was forgiven."],[3113,"A man who took a thorny branch from people's path was forgiven his sin, the earlier of his sins and the later."],[3114,"“There was a man who used to lend people money, and when an insolvent person became insolvent, he would say to his servant, ‘Overlook it, perhaps Allah will overlook us.’ So he met Allah, and He overlooked him.”"],[3115,"“A man from those before you was called to account, and no good deed was found for him except that he was a wealthy man who used to mix with people, and he would say to his servant, ‘Overlook the insolvent.’ So Allah, glorified and exalted, said to His angels, ‘We are more entitled to that; overlook him.’”"],[3116,"A youth from Quraysh came to Abū Hurayrah and said, “O Abū Hurayrah, you narrate many hadiths from the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. Did you hear him say anything about this garment of mine?” He replied, “Were it not for what Allah has taken upon me in the Book, I would not have narrated anything to you. I heard him ﷺ say: ‘A man from those before you used to strut when his long hair and his two cloaks pleased him, so Allah caused the earth to swallow him, and he will be sinking in it until the Day of Resurrection.’”"],[3117,"\"While a man was driving a cow and wanted to ride it, it turned to him and said, 'We were not created for this; we were only created for plowing.' Those around him said, 'Glory be to Allah.' He ﷺ said, 'I believe in it, and Abu Bakr and 'Umar,' while they were not there. He said, 'And while a man was among his sheep, a wolf took a sheep. The shepherd followed it, and it spat it out and then said, \"How will you fare on the day of wild beasts, when there is no shepherd for them other than me?\"' Those around him said, 'Glory be to Allah.' He ﷺ said, 'I believe in it, and Abu Bakr and 'Umar,' while they were not there.\""],[3119,"“There was a man among those before you who never stored up any good with Allah. At death he said to his sons: ‘O my sons, what kind of father was I to you?’ They said: ‘The best of fathers.’ He said: ‘Then when I die, burn me and crush me, and when it is a day of violent wind, scatter me.’ He died, and that was done to him. Then He said to him: ‘Be,’ and he was, faster than the blink of an eye. Allah said: ‘O My servant, what made you do what you did?’ He said: ‘Fear of You, O Lord.’ He said: ‘He did not requite him except that he was forgiven.’”"],[3120,"A man who was a grave-digger died, and he said to his son: 'Burn me, then grind me, and scatter me in the wind.' He was asked: 'What have you done?' He said: 'Out of fear of You, my Lord.' He said: 'So He forgave him.'"],[3121,"A worshipper from the Children of Israel devoted himself to worship and worshipped Allah in his hermitage for sixty years. Then the land was rained upon and became green, and the monk looked out from his hermitage and said: If I were to go down and remember Allah, I would increase in good. So he went down, and with him was a loaf or two loaves. While he was on the land, a woman met him, and he kept talking to her and she kept talking to him until he had intercourse with her. Then he fainted, so he went down to the pool to bathe. A beggar came to him, and he gestured to him to take the two loaves or the loaf. Then he died. The worship of sixty years was weighed against that fornication, and the fornication outweighed his good deeds. Then the loaf or the two loaves were placed with his good deeds, and his good deeds outweighed, so he was forgiven."],[3122,"That the Messenger of Allah ﷺ during the night of Isra' passed by a pleasant fragrance, so he said, \"O Jibril, what is this fragrance?\" Jibril said, \"This is the fragrance of the comb of the daughter of Pharaoh and her children while she combs the hair of the daughter of Pharaoh. When the comb fell from her hand, she said, 'Bismillah (In the name of Allah),' and the daughter of Pharaoh said, 'My father,' she said, 'Rather, my Lord and your Lord is Allah.' She said, 'And do you have a Lord other than my father?' She said, 'Yes, Allah.' She said, 'And indeed, you have a Lord other than me?' She said, 'Yes, my Lord and your Lord is Allah.' She said, 'So shall I inform my father about this?' She said, 'Yes.' So she informed him, and he sent for her and said, 'Do you have a Lord other than me?' She said, 'Yes, my Lord and your Lord is Allah.' So he ordered a basin of copper to be heated, and it was heated for her. Then he ordered her children to be brought and started throwing them into it, one by one, until they came to the youngest child who was still breastfeeding. At that point she said, 'O my mothers, be firm, for you are upon the truth.'\""],[3123,"On the night I was taken on the night journey, I passed by a pleasant fragrance and said, 'What is this, O Jibril?' He said, 'This is the hairdresser of Pharaoh's daughter. She used to comb her hair, and the comb fell from her hand. She said, \"In the name of Allah.\" Pharaoh's daughter said, \"My father?\" She said, \"My Lord, your Lord, and the Lord of your father.\" She said, \"Should I tell him?\" She said, \"Tell him.\" So she told him. He said to her, \"Do you have a lord other than me?\" She said, \"My Lord and your Lord is the One in the heaven.\" So he heated a brass basin for her and said, \"I have a request of you.\" He said, \"What is your request?\" She said, \"My request is that you gather my bones with the bones of my child.\" He said, \"That is for you, due to the right you have over us.\" He threw her children into the basin one by one, and the last of them was an infant who said, \"O mother, be patient, for you are upon the truth.\""],[3124,"A man said, “By Allah, Allah will not forgive so-and-so.” Then Allah, Blessed and Exalted, said, “I have forgiven so-and-so and nullified your deeds.”"],[3125,"I entered the mosque of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and found an old man with a yellowish head and shining front teeth, accompanied by a handsome young man with dark wide eyes. The old man said, “O Yamami, come. Do not ever say to a man, ‘May Allah not forgive you’ or ‘By Allah, Allah will never admit you to Paradise.’” I said, “Who are you, may Allah have mercy on you?” He said, “I am Abu Hurayrah.” I said, “This is a word one of us says to some of his family or to his servant when he is angry with her.” He said, “Do not say it. I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: There were two men among the Children of Israel who were brothers. One of them was diligent in worship, and the other was a sinner. The diligent one saw the sinner committing a sin and said to him, ‘Refrain.’ He replied, ‘Leave me with my Lord.’ He repeated that to him, and he kept saying, ‘Leave me with my Lord,’ until one day he found him committing a sin, and he regarded it as grave. He said, ‘Woe to you, refrain.’ He said, ‘Leave me with my Lord. Have you been sent as a watcher over me?’ He said, ‘By Allah, Allah will never forgive you’ or ‘Allah will never admit you to Paradise.’ Then an angel was sent to them, and he took their souls, and they gathered before Him, Mighty and Majestic. Our Lord said to the diligent worshipper, ‘Did you have knowledge? Or were you capable over what is in My hand? Or do you withhold My mercy from My servant? Go to Paradise,’ meaning the sinner. And He said to the other, ‘Take him to the Fire.’” By the One in Whose hand is my soul, he spoke a word that destroyed his worldly life and his hereafter."],[3126,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ came out to us with something like a leather shield in his hand. He set it down and then urinated toward it. Some of the people said: Look at him, he urinates as a woman urinates. He said: The Prophet ﷺ heard him and said: “Woe to you! Do you not know what befell the man of the Children of Israel? When any of them was affected by urine, they would cut it off with scissors. He forbade them, and he was tormented in his grave.”"],[3127,"The Prophet ﷺ passed by two graves and said: “They are being tormented, and they are not tormented for something major.” Then he said: “Yes, one of them used to go about with tale-bearing, and the other did not guard himself from his urine.” Then he took a stalk, split it in two, and stuck each piece on a grave. Then he said: “Perhaps it will lighten their torment as long as they do not dry out.”"],[3128,"“Those before you were destroyed because of their excessive questioning and their disagreement with their prophets. Do not ask me about anything but I will tell you about it.” Abdullah b. Hudhafah b. Qays al-Sahmi stood up and said, “Who is my father, O Messenger of Allah?” He said, “Your father is Hudhafah.” He returned to his mother, and his mother said to him, “What made you do what you did? We were people of ignorance and evil deeds.” He said, “I would not stop until I knew who my father was among the people.” He was a playful man."],[3129,"Leave me with what I have left you, for those before you were destroyed only by their excessive questioning and their disagreement with their prophets. Whatever I forbid you, avoid it, and whatever I command you, do of it what you are able."],[3130,"“A woman entered the Fire because of a cat which she tied up. She neither fed it nor let it loose to eat from the vermin of the earth until it died.”"],[3131,"“The sun eclipsed during the time of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. He stood, and we stood with him, and he prayed. Then he turned to us and began narrating to us, saying, ‘Paradise was brought near to me, so much so that if I had wished, I could have plucked a bunch of its fruits. And the Fire was shown to me, and had I not warded it off from you, it would have overwhelmed you. In it I saw three people being punished: a tall, black Ḥimyarite woman being punished because of a cat she had tied up. She neither let it eat from the vermin of the earth nor fed it until it died. So whenever it comes toward her, it bites her, and whenever she turns away, it bites her. I saw the brother of Banū Daʿdaʿ, the owner of the two sāʾibahs, being pushed with two pillars in the Fire. The two sāʾibahs were two camels of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ which he stole. And I saw the owner of the hooked staff leaning on his staff. The owner of the hooked staff used to steal the belongings of pilgrims with his hooked staff. When it was unnoticed, he would take it away, and when it was discovered, he would say, “I did not steal; it merely got caught on my staff.”’”"],[3132,"While a man was walking on a road, thirst became severe upon him. He found a well, went down into it, drank, and then came out. There was a dog panting, eating moist earth from thirst. The man said, 'This dog has reached the same level of thirst as I have.' So he went down the well, filled his leather sock with water, held it with his mouth until he climbed up, and gave the dog water. Allah thanked him and forgave him.' They said, 'O Messenger of Allah, is there a reward for us in animals?' He ﷺ said, 'In every living, moist creature there is a reward.'"],[3133,"A prostitute woman saw a dog on a hot day circling a well, its tongue lolling from thirst. She drew water for it and gave it to drink, so she was forgiven."],[3134,"“There was among the Children of Israel a man who killed ninety-nine people. Then he went out asking, and he came to a monk and asked him, ‘Is there any repentance for me?’ He said, ‘No,’ so he killed him. He kept asking, and a man said to him, ‘Go to such-and-such a village.’ Death overtook him and he died. The angels of mercy and the angels of punishment disputed over him. Allah revealed to this one, ‘Draw near,’ and to that one, ‘Move away.’ He was found to be closer to this one by a span, and he was forgiven.”"],[3135,"During the illness of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, some of his wives mentioned a church they had seen in the land of Abyssinia. Umm Salamah and Umm Habibah had come to the land of Abyssinia, and they mentioned a church they had seen there called Maria, and they mentioned its beauty and the images in it. The Prophet ﷺ raised his head and said, \"Those people, when a righteous man among them dies, build a mosque over his grave and then make those images in it. Those are the worst of creation in the sight of Allah, Exalted is He.\""],[3136,"May Allah curse the people who took the graves of their prophets as mosques."],[3137,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ sent me to Najran. The people of Najran said to me, “Do you not recite this verse: ‘O sister of Harun, your father was not a man of evil, nor was your mother unchaste’? And you know how long the time was between Musa and Isa?” I did not know what to answer them until I came to Madinah to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and mentioned that to him. He said to me, “Why did you not tell them that they used to be named after the prophets and righteous people who came before them?”"],[3138,"Three men went out walking, and rain caught them. They entered a cave in a mountain, and a rock fell down and blocked the path over them. They said: 'Call upon Allah with the most trustworthy of your deeds.'"],[3139,"The Prophet ﷺ said: The Jews were split up into seventy-one or seventy-two sects; and the Christians were split up into seventy one or seventy-two sects; and my community will be split up into seventy-three sects. (Using translation from Abū Dāʾūd 4596)"],[3140,"We came to al-'Irbad b. Sariyah, who was among those about whom it was revealed: \"Nor upon those who, when they came to you for you to carry them, you said, 'I find nothing to carry you on.'\" We greeted and said, 'We have come to you as visitors and seekers of knowledge.' Al-'Irbad said: 'The Messenger of Allah ﷺ prayed the morning prayer with us one day, then turned to us and gave us an eloquent admonition that made eyes shed tears and hearts tremble. A man said, \"O Messenger of Allah, this seems like the admonition of one bidding farewell, so what do you enjoin upon us?\" He said, \"I enjoin you to fear Allah, to hear and obey, even if a slave, an Ethiopian with amputated limbs, is put over you. Whoever among you lives will see much disagreement, so hold to my Sunnah and the Sunnah of the rightly guided caliphs after me; cling to it firmly and bite onto it with the molar teeth. Beware of newly introduced matters, for every newly introduced matter is an innovation, and every innovation is misguidance.\"'"],[3141,"The Quraish were anxious about the Makhzumi woman who had committed theft, They said : Who will speak to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ about her ? Then they said: Who will be bold enough for it but Uasmah bin Zaid, the prophet’s ﷺ friend! So Usamah spoke to him, and the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said : Are you interceding regarding one of the punishments prescribed by Allah ? He then got up and gave an address, saying : What destroyed your predecessors was just that when a person of rank among them committed a theft, They left him alone , and when a weak one of them committed a theft, they inflicted the prescribed punishment on him . I swear by Allah that if Fatimah daughter of Muhammad should steal, I would have her hand cut off. (Using translation from Abū Dāʾūd 4373)"],[3142,"We came to the Prophet ﷺ while he was resting his head on a cloak in the shade of the Ka'bah. We had encountered severe hardship from the polytheists. I said, 'O Messenger of Allah, will you not supplicate to Allah for us?' He sat up angry, his face red, and said, 'Those before you would be asked to renounce their faith, and they would not do so. A saw would be placed on his head and he would be split into two, yet that would not turn him away from his religion. One of them would be combed with iron combs, tearing the flesh and sinews from his bones, yet that would not turn him away from his religion. But you are hasty. Allah will surely complete this matter until a rider travels from San'a' to Hadramawt fearing none but Allah and the wolf for his sheep.'"],[3143,"\"A man visited a brother of his in another village, so Allah sent an angel to wait for him on his path. When he came to him (the angel), he said: Where are you going? He said: I am visiting a brother of mine in this village. He said: Does he have any favor over you that you maintain? He said: No, except that I love him for the sake of Allah. He said: Then I am the messenger of Allah to you: Allah has loved you as you loved him for His sake.\""],[3144,"\"There was a man among the Children of Israel who used to lend money to people. A man came to him and said, 'O so-and-so, lend me six hundred dinars.' He said, 'Yes, if you bring me an agent.' He said, 'Allah is my agent.' He said, 'Glory be to Allah. Yes, I have accepted Allah as an agent.' So he gave him six hundred dinars and set a term for him. He traveled by sea with the money to trade with it. Allah decreed that the term arrived while the sea was stormy between them. The owner of the money kept coming to the shore asking about him. The one he asked about him said, 'We left him at such-and-such a place.' The owner of the money said, 'O Allah, compensate me for so-and-so for what I gave him for Your sake.' He said, 'And the one who owed the money went and carved out a piece of wood and placed the money inside it. Then he wrote a note: \"From so-and-so to so-and-so: I have delivered your money to my agent.\" Then he sealed the mouth of the wood and threw it into the sea. It kept carrying it until it cast it onto the shore. The owner of the money went to the shore and asked, and he found the wood. He carried it and took it to his family and said, 'Use this for fuel.' They broke it open, and the dinars and the note scattered out. He took the note and read it and recognized it. Then the other one came, and the owner of the money said to him, 'My money?' He said, 'I delivered my money to my agent, to the one entrusted with me.' He said to him, 'Your agent has paid me in full.'\" Abu Hurayrah said, \"Indeed we saw that our disputes and clamor increased in the presence of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, among us, as to which of them would be delivered.\""],[3145,"A man bought from another man a piece of real estate. The one who bought the real estate found in his real estate a jar of gold. The one who bought the real estate said to him: Take your gold from me. I only bought land from you and did not buy gold from you. The one who sold the land said: I sold you the land and whatever is in it. He said: They took their dispute to a man. The one to whom they took their dispute said: Do you have children? One of them said: A boy, and the other said: A girl. He said: Marry the boy to the girl, spend on them, and give charity."],[3146,"A Bedouin came to the Prophet ﷺ and he honored him. He said to him: 'Come to us.' So he came to him. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to him: 'Ask for your need.' He said: A she-camel that we ride, and goats that my family can milk. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: 'Have you become unable to be like the old woman of the Children of Israel?' They said: O Messenger of Allah, who is the old woman of the Children of Israel? He said: 'When Moses ﷺ traveled with the Children of Israel from Egypt, they lost the way. He said: What is this? Their scholars said: When death came to Joseph ﷺ , he took a covenant from us by Allah that we would not leave Egypt until we carry his bones with us. He said: Who knows the location of his grave? They said: An old woman of the Children of Israel. So he sent for her and she came to him. He said: Guide me to the grave of Joseph. She said: Not until you grant me my request. He said: What is your request? She said: To be with you in Paradise. He disliked granting her that, so Allah revealed to him: Grant her her request. She went with them to a lake, a place where water gathers. She said: Drain this water. So they drained it. She said: Dig. So they dug and extracted the bones of Joseph. When they lifted them to the land, behold, the road was like the light of day.'"],[3147,"When the Messenger of Allah ﷺ came to al-Hijr, he said: \"Do not ask your Prophet for signs. These are the people of Salih. They asked their Prophet for a sign, and the she-camel used to come to them from this mountain pass and leave from that mountain pass, and they would drink her milk on the day she came, as much as their water satisfied them. Then they hamstrung her, and they were promised three days, and it was a promise not to be belied. Then the Cry seized them, and there did not remain under the canopy of the sky a single man except that it destroyed him, except for one man in the Sanctuary whom the Sanctuary protected from the punishment of Allah.\" They said: \"O Messenger of Allah, who is he?\" He said: \"Abu Righal, the father of Thaqif.\""],[3148,"\"They were with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ on a journey, and they passed by the grave of Abu Righal, and he is the father of Thaqif, and he was a man from Thamud whose dwelling was in Harra'. When Allah destroyed his people with what He destroyed them, He protected him because of his location in the Sanctuary, and he went out until when he reached here, he died and was buried, and with him was a branch of gold, so we hastened and extracted it.\""],[3149,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to the companions of al-Hijr: \"Do not enter upon these punished people unless you are weeping, so do not enter upon them lest there befall you the like of what befell them.\""],[3150,"'A man said, \"I will certainly give charity.\" He went out with his charity and placed it in the hand of an adulteress. In the morning people were saying, \"Charity was given last night to an adulteress.\" He said, \"O Allah, to You be praise—to an adulteress! I will certainly give charity.\" He went out with his charity and placed it in the hand of a thief. In the morning people were saying, \"Charity was given last night to a thief.\" He said, \"O Allah, to You be praise—to a thief! I will certainly give charity tonight.\" He went out with his charity and placed it in the hand of a rich man. In the morning people were saying, \"Charity was given last night to a rich man.\" He said, \"O Allah, to You be praise—to a rich man!\" Then he was told, \"As for your charity, it has been accepted. As for the adulteress, perhaps she will become chaste by it and refrain from her adultery. As for the thief, perhaps he will refrain from his theft. And perhaps the rich man will take heed and spend from what Allah, Exalted is He, has given him.\""],[3151,"“A nation from the Children of Israel was lost, and it is not known what it did. I do not think it is anything but the mouse. Do you not see that when it finds camel milk it does not drink it, but when it finds sheep milk it drinks it.”"],[3152,"“I saw ʿAmr b. ʿAmir al-Khuzaʿi dragging his intestines in the Fire. He was the first to set free the Sa'ibah (a camel or other animal released in the name of idols).”"],[3153,"“It was said to the Children of Israel, ‘Enter the gate prostrating and say, “Relieve us of our sins,” and We will forgive you your sins.’ But they changed it, so they entered the gate dragging themselves on their backsides and said, ‘A grain in a hair.’”"],[3154,"Umar b. al-Khattab ؓ set out for Syria, and when he drew near, he learned that the plague was there. Abd al-Rahman b. Awf narrated to him from the Prophet ﷺ that he said, 'This disease is a punishment with which those before you were punished. If it occurs in a land where you are not, do not go down to it; and if it occurs in a land where you are, do not leave fleeing from it.' So Umar b. al-Khattab ؓ returned with the people that year."],[3155,"\"Gabriel was stuffing mud into Pharaoh's mouth for fear that he would say, 'There is no god but Allah.'\""],[3156,"\"Did you not see that your people when they built the Kaaba confined it to the foundations of Ibrahim?\" She said, \"So I said, 'O Messenger of Allah, will you not restore it to the foundations of Ibrahim?'\" He said, \"Were it not that your people are recent in disbelief.\" 'Abdullah b. 'Umar said, \"If 'A'ishah heard this from the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, I do not think that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ left off touching the two corners that are next to the Hijr except that the House was not completed upon the foundations of Ibrahim.\""],[3157,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to her, \"O 'A'ishah, were it not that your people are recent from ignorance, I would demolish the House and include in it what they left out of it in the Hijr, for they fell short of its expense, and I would attach it to the ground and place it upon the foundation of Ibrahim, and I would make for it two doors: an eastern door and a western door.\" He said, \"This is what prompted Ibn al-Zubayr to demolish it and rebuild it.\""],[3158,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, \"A nation entered Paradise by its Qada' (sustenance and resources) and Qideed (measuring utensils). They did not hoard or steal, and they relied on their Lord.\""],[3159,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ led us in ʿAṣr prayer. When he finished, he said, 'This prayer was presented to those before you, and they lost it and abandoned it. Whoever among you performs it will have its reward doubled, and there is no prayer after it until the witness appears.' The witness is the star."],[3160,"\"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: 'We are the last (to come) but will be the foremost on the Day of Resurrection, but they were given the Book before us and we were given it after them. They differed concerning this day which Allah, the Mighty and Sublime, had prescribed for them and Allah, the Mighty and Sublime, guided us to\"--meaning Friday--\"so the people follow us, the Jews the next day and the Christians the day after that.'\" (Using translation from Nasāʾī 1367)"],[3161,"A man among those before you developed an abscess. He took a knife and stabbed himself with it, and the blood did not stop flowing until he died. Allah, Blessed and Exalted, said: “My servant hastened his own death; I have forbidden Paradise to him.”"],[3162,"A man from those before you had an ulcer break out on him, and when it pained him, he drew an arrow from his quiver and lanced it, and his blood did not stop until he died. Then your Lord said: \"I have forbidden Paradise to him.\""],[3163,"While a woman was nursing her son, a rider passed by her while she was nursing him. She said, 'O Allah, do not let my son die until he becomes like this one.' He said, 'O Allah, do not make me like him.' Then he returned to the breast. Then she passed by a woman who was being cursed, and she said, 'O Allah, do not make my son like her.' He said, 'O Allah, make me like her.' As for the rider, he was a disbeliever, and as for the woman, they would say to her, 'She commits adultery,' and she would say, 'Allah is sufficient for me.' And they would say, 'She steals,' and she would say, 'Allah is sufficient for me.'"],[3164,"No one spoke in the cradle except three: Jesus son of Mary, and the companion of Jurayj. There was among the Children of Israel a man called Jurayj who built a hermitage and worshiped Allah in it. His mother came to him one day and called him, but he did not turn to her. Then she came to him a second day and called him, but he did not turn to her. Then she came to him a third day, and he said, 'My prayer or my mother?' She said, 'O Allah, do not let him die until he looks at the faces of prostitutes.' The Children of Israel one day mentioned Jurayj, and a prostitute of the prostitutes of the Children of Israel said, 'If you wish, I will tempt him.' They said, 'We wish it.' So she went and exposed herself to Jurayj, but he did not turn to her. She went to a shepherd who used to shelter his sheep in Jurayj's hermitage and offered herself to him, and he had intercourse with her. She became pregnant and gave birth to a boy. She said, 'He is from Jurayj.' Then a group of the Children of Israel attacked him, beat him, reviled him, and demolished his hermitage. He said to them, 'What is the matter with you?' They said, 'You committed adultery with this prostitute and she gave birth to a boy.' He said, 'Where is the boy?' They said, 'Here he is.'"],[3165,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ mentioned the world and said: 'The world is green and sweet, so be mindful of it and be mindful of women.' Then he mentioned three women from the Children of Israel: two tall women and a short woman who was not known. She made two legs of wood and fashioned a ring, filling it with the finest perfume. When she passed by the mosque or the assembly, she would say, 'With it,' and open it, and its fragrance would spread."],[3166,"A woman among the Children of Israel was short, so she made herself two sandals of wood and would walk between two tall women, making herself taller with them. She made a ring of gold and filled under its bezel with the finest perfume, musk. When she passed by a gathering, she would move it and its fragrance would spread."],[3167,"May Allah fight so-and-so who sells wine. By Allah, he has heard the saying of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ: “Fats were forbidden for them to eat, but they sold them.”"],[3168,"Samura sold wine. ʿUmar said, “May Allah fight Samura! Did he not know that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: ‘May Allah curse the Jews. Fat was forbidden for them, so they melted it and sold it.’”"],[3169,"The Prophet ﷺ looked at the sky and said: \"May Allah fight the Jews. Fats were forbidden to them, so they sold them and consumed their price. Indeed, when Allah forbids something, He forbids its price.\""],[3170,"\"I heard the Prophet ﷺ say more than twenty times, 'Dhul-Kifl, from the Children of Israel, did not hesitate about anything, so he desired a woman and fell into a sin with her. He gave her sixty dinars. When he left her, she cried and repented. Dhul-Kifl regretted his actions and died that same night. In the morning, they found a note on his door saying, 'Indeed, Allah has forgiven you.'\""],[3171,"Avoid the mother of all vices, for there was a man from those before you who worshipped and withdrew from people. A woman became attached to him, so she sent a servant to him, saying, 'We invite you to bear witness.' He entered, and every time he entered a door she locked it behind him until he reached a beautiful seated woman, and with her was a boy and a jug containing wine. She said, 'We did not invite you to bear witness, but I invited you to kill this boy, or to have intercourse with me, or to drink a cup of this wine. If you refuse, I will cry out and expose you.'\" He said, \"When he saw that he had no choice, he said, 'Give me a cup of this wine to drink.' She gave him a cup of wine to drink. He said, 'Give me more,' and he did not cease until he had intercourse with her and killed the soul. So avoid wine, for by Allah, faith and addiction to wine will never coexist in the chest of a man ever; one of them will soon expel the other.\""],[3172,"“There was a king among those before you who had a magician. When he grew old, he said to the king, ‘I have become old, so send me a boy to teach him magic.’ He sent him a boy to teach. On his way, when he passed by a monk, he would sit with him, listen to his words, and be impressed. When he went to the magician, he would beat him, and when he returned from the magician, he would sit with the monk and listen to his words. When he went to his family, they would beat him. He complained about that to the monk, who said, ‘If you fear the magician, say my family detained me, and if you fear your family, say the magician detained me.’ While he was like that, he came upon a great beast that had blocked the people’s way. He said, ‘Today I will know whether the monk is better or the magician.’ He took a stone and said, ‘O Allah, if the monk’s affair is more beloved to You than the magician’s, kill this beast so the people may pass.’ He threw it and killed it, and the people passed. He went to the monk and told him. The monk said, ‘My son, today you are better than me. You will be tested, and if you are tested, do not point to me.’ The boy used to heal the blind and the leper and treat other ailments. A courtier of the king who had gone blind heard of him. He came to the boy with many gifts and said, ‘All that is here is yours if you heal me.’ He said, ‘I do not heal anyone; it is Allah who heals. If you believe in Allah, I will supplicate Allah, and He will heal you.’ He believed in Allah, and Allah healed him. He came to the king walking, sitting with him as he used to. The king said, ‘So-and-so, who restored your sight?’ He said, ‘My Lord.’ He said, ‘Do you have a lord other than me?’ He said, ‘My Lord and your Lord is one.’ He kept torturing him until he pointed to the boy. The boy was brought, and the king said, ‘My son, has your magic reached such a level that you heal the blind and the leper and do all this?’ He said, ‘I do not heal anyone; it is Allah who heals.’ He seized him and kept torturing him until he pointed to the monk. The monk was brought and told, ‘Renounce your religion.’ He refused. He called for a saw, placed it on his head’s crown, and split him until his two halves fell. Then the king’s courtier was brought and told, ‘Renounce your religion.’ He refused. He placed the saw on his head’s crown and split him until his two halves fell. Then the boy was brought and told, ‘Renounce your religion.’ He refused. He handed him to a group of his companions and said, ‘Take him to such-and-such mountain, climb with him, and when you reach its summit, if he renounces his religion, spare him; otherwise, throw him off.’ They took him and climbed the mountain. He said, ‘O Allah, spare me from them however You will.’ The mountain shook with them, and they fell. He came walking to the king. The king said, ‘What happened to your companions?’ He said, ‘Allah spared me from them.’ He handed him to a group of his companions and said, ‘Take him and carry him in a boat, take him to the middle of the sea and set sail; if he renounces his religion, spare him; otherwise, throw him into the sea.’ They took him. He said, ‘O Allah, spare me from them however You will.’ The ship capsized with them. He came walking to the king. The king said, ‘What happened to your companions?’ He said, ‘Allah spared me from them.’ He said to the king, ‘You will not kill me until you do what I command you.’ He said, ‘What is it?’ He said, ‘Gather the people in one open space, crucify me on a trunk, then take an arrow from your quiver, place the arrow in the bow’s center, then say: In the name of Allah, the Lord of the boy, then shoot me. If you do that, you will kill me.’ He gathered the people in one open space, crucified him on a trunk, took an arrow from his quiver, placed the arrow in the center of his bow, said, ‘In the name of Allah, the Lord of the boy,’ and shot him. The arrow struck his temple. He placed his hand on the arrow’s spot and died. The people said, ‘We believe in the Lord of the boy, we believe in the Lord of the boy,’ three times. The king was approached and told, ‘Do you see what you feared? By Allah, your fear has befallen you. The people have believed.’ He ordered trenches at the mouths of the streets. They were dug, and fires were lit. He said, ‘Whoever does not renounce his religion, throw him into it.’ They did so until a woman came with her infant. She hesitated to fall into it. The boy said to her, ‘O mother, be patient, for you are upon the truth.’”"],[3173,"\"There were three among the Children of Israel: a leper, a bald man, and a blind man. Allah wanted to test them, so He sent an angel to them. He came to the leper and said: 'What thing is most beloved to you?' He said: 'A good color and good skin.' He said: 'So what wealth is most beloved to you?' He said: 'Camels.' So he wiped him and it went away. He said: 'And he was given a ten-month pregnant she-camel.' And he said: 'May Allah bless you in it.' He said: 'Then he came to the bald man and said: \"What thing is most beloved to you?\" He said: \"Good hair and that this which people abhor me for go away from me.\" He said: \"So he wiped him and it went away, and he was given good hair.\" He said: \"So what wealth is most beloved to you?\" He said: \"Cows.\" He said: \"So he was given a milch cow.\" he said: \"May Allah bless you in it.\" He said: \"Then he came to the blind man and said: 'What thing is most beloved to you?' He said: 'That Allah restore my sight so I can see people.' So he wiped him and Allah restored his sight. He said: 'So what wealth is most beloved to you?' He said: 'Sheep.' He said: 'So he was given a ewe.\" And these two produced offspring and this one gave birth, so this one had a valley of camels, this one a valley of cows, and this one a valley of sheep. He said: 'Then he came to the leper in his form and appearance and said: \"A poor man and a son of the road; my means have been cut off in my journey, so there is no way for me today except by Allah then by you. I ask you by the One who gave you the good color, the good skin, and the wealth, for a camel to help me along in my journey.\" He said: \"The rights are many.\" He said: \"It is as if I know you: were you not a leper whom people abhorred, poor, and Allah gave you wealth?\" He said: \"I inherited this wealth from a long line of ancestors.\" He said: \"If you are lying, may Allah return you to what you were.\" He said: 'Then he came to the bald man in his form and said to him the like of what he said to this one, and he replied with the like of what this one replied. He said: \"If you are lying, may Allah return you to what you were.\" Then he came to the blind man in his form and appearance and said: \"A poor man and a son of the road; my means have been cut off in my journey.\" He said: \"I was blind and Allah restored my sight, so take what you wish and leave what you wish. By Allah, I will not burden you today with anything you take for Allah.\" He said: \"Keep your wealth, for you all have only been tested. Verily, He is pleased with you and angry with your two companions.\"'"],[3174,"'While a man was in a desert area of the earth, he saw a cloud and heard a voice in it saying, \"Water the garden of so-and-so.\" That cloud came and emptied what was in it onto a rocky tract. He said, \"I followed it and found channels whose ends had captured the water, and one channel from among those channels had absorbed the water and carried it. I came to a man standing, directing the water with his shovel into a garden.\" I said to him, \"O servant of Allah, what is your name?\" He said, \"So-and-so,\" the name I had heard in the cloud. He said, \"Why do you ask me, O servant of Allah, about my name?\" I said, \"I heard in the cloud whose water this is saying, 'Water the garden of so-and-so,' with your name. Tell me what you do with it.\" He said, \"Since you say this, I look at what it produces and give a third of it in charity, I and my family eat a third, and I put a third back into it.\""],[3175,"I was commanded with a village that devours villages; they call it Yathrib, and it is al-Madinah. It expels people just as the bellows expel the dross of iron."],[3176,"When the Messenger of Allah ﷺ died, and Abu Bakr ؓ succeeded him, and those Arabs who disbelieved disbelieved, 'Umar said, \"O Abu Bakr, how can you fight the people when the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: 'I have been commanded to fight the people until they say: There is no god but Allah. Whoever says: There is no god but Allah has protected from me his wealth and his life except by its right, and his reckoning is upon Allah'?\" Abu Bakr ؓ said, \"By Allah, I will fight whoever separates prayer from zakat, for zakat is the right of wealth. By Allah, if they withheld from me a young female goat that they used to give to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, I would fight them for withholding it.\" 'Umar said, \"By Allah, it was only when I saw that Allah had opened Abu Bakr's chest to the fighting that I knew it was the truth.\""],[3177,"When the Messenger of Allah ﷺ died and Abu Bakr ؓ was made successor, and those Arabs who disbelieved disbelieved, 'Umar ؓ said to Abu Bakr, \"How can you fight the people when the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: 'I have been commanded to fight the people until they say: There is no god but Allah. Whoever says: There is no god but Allah has protected from me his wealth and his life except by its right, and his reckoning is upon Allah'?\" Abu Bakr ؓ said, \"By Allah, I will fight whoever separates prayer from zakat, for zakat is the right of wealth. By Allah, if they withheld from me a camel hobble that they used to give to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, I would fight them for withholding it.\" 'Umar said, \"By Allah, it was only when I saw that Allah had opened Abu Bakr's chest to the fighting that I knew it was the truth.\""],[3178,"«I have been commanded to fight the people until they say, \"There is no god but Allah.\" So whoever says, \"There is no god but Allah\" has protected from me his life and his property, except by its right, and his reckoning is with Allah. And Allah sent down in His Book than he mentioned a people who were arrogant, so He said: {Indeed they, when it was said to them, \"There is no god but Allah,\" were arrogant} and He said: {When those who disbelieved had put into their hearts the zealotry, the zealotry of ignorance, so Allah sent down His tranquility upon His Messenger and upon the believers and imposed on them the word of righteousness}, and it is \"There is no god but Allah, and Muhammad is the Messenger of Allah.\" The polytheists were arrogant against it on the day of Hudaybiyyah.»"],[3179,"I have been commanded to fight the people until they bear witness that there is no god but Allah and that I am the Messenger of Allah, and they establish prayer and give zakat. If they do that, they have protected their blood and their wealth from me, except by the right of Islam, and their reckoning is upon Allah."],[3180,"'I have been commanded to fight the people until they testify that there is no god but Allah and that Muhammad is the Messenger of Allah. If they testify that there is no god but Allah and that Muhammad is the Messenger of Allah, face our qiblah, eat our slaughtered animals, and pray our prayer, then their blood and wealth are forbidden to us. They have the rights of Muslims and bear the obligations that Muslims bear.'"],[3181,"«I have been commanded to fight the people until they say, \"There is no god but Allah,\" and believe in me and in what I have brought. So when they do that, they have protected from me their blood and their property, except by its right, and their reckoning is with Allah.»"],[3182,"“I was commanded to prostrate on seven (parts) and not to gather up hair or clothing.”"],[3183,"“I was commanded to prostrate on seven bones and not to gather up hair or clothing.”"],[3184,"“I was commanded to prostrate on seven bones: the forehead — and he pointed with his hand to his nose — the two hands, the two knees, and the two feet, and not to gather up clothing or hair.”"],[3185,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ stood up one night, put on his clothes, then went out."],[3186,"\"I saw as if I was given a large wooden bowl full of milk, and I drank from it until I was full. I saw it flowing in my veins between skin and flesh, and some of it was left over, so I gave it to Abu Bakr.\" They said: O Messenger of God, this is knowledge that God gave you, so that when you were full of it, some was left over and you gave it to Abu Bakr? The Prophet ﷺ said: \"You have spoken correctly.\""],[3187,"“If I were to take a close friend, I would have taken Abu Bakr as a close friend, but he is my brother and my companion, and Allah has taken your companion as a close friend.”"],[3188,"\"And the Prophet ﷺ commanded the closing of the doors of the streets in the mosque, except for the door of Abu Bakr.\""],[3189,"“No wealth has ever benefited me as much as the wealth of Abu Bakr.” Abu Bakr ؓ wept and said, “I and my wealth are only for you.”"],[3190,"“Abu Bakr ؓ spent forty thousand on the Messenger of Allah ﷺ.”"],[3191,"The Prophet ﷺ went out during the illness in which he passed away, with a band around his head. He then sat on the pulpit and praised Allah and praised Him. He then said, \"There is no one among the people who has not been entrusted with himself and his wealth except for Abu Bakr. If I were to take a close friend from the people, I would have taken Abu Bakr. But the companionship of Islam prevented me from anything other than the companionship of Abu Bakr in the mosque, except for the companionship of Abu Bakr.\""],[3192,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ sat on the pulpit and said, “Indeed, a servant whom Allah gave the choice between granting him the splendor of this world as much as He willed and what is with Him, and he chose what is with Him.” Abu Bakr wept and said, “May our fathers and mothers be your ransom.” The Messenger of Allah ﷺ was the one given the choice, and Abu Bakr was the most knowledgeable of us about it. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, “Indeed, the person most deserving of my companionship in his wealth and company is Abu Bakr. If I were to take a close friend, I would have taken Abu Bakr as a close friend, but it is the brotherhood of Islam. No small door should remain in the mosque except the small door of Abu Bakr.”"],[3193,"“Abu Bakr was the most beloved of us to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and he was our best and our master.”"],[3194,"“Am I not the most entitled of the people to this matter? Am I not the first one to accept Islam? Am I not the companion of such and such? Am I not the companion of such and such?”"],[3195,"Abu Bakr’s name was ʿAbd Allah b. ʿUthman. The Prophet ﷺ said to him, “You are ʿAtiq Allah, freed from the Fire,” so he was named ʿAtiq."],[3196,"The Prophet of Allah ﷺ climbed Uhud, and Abu Bakr, ʿUmar, and ʿUthman ؓ followed him. It shook with them, so the Prophet of Allah ﷺ struck it with his foot and said, “Be firm, Uhud, for upon you are only a prophet, a ṣiddīq, and two martyrs.”"],[3197,"\"Whoever spends a pair in the path of Allah will be called in Paradise: 'O servant of Allah, this is good.' So whoever was among the people of prayer will be called from the gate of prayer; whoever was among the people of jihad will be called from the gate of jihad; whoever was among the people of charity will be called from the gate of charity; whoever was among the people of fasting will be called from the gate of al-Rayyan.\" Abu Bakr said: 'O Messenger of Allah, what is upon the one called from these gates of necessity? Will anyone be called from all these gates?' He said: 'Yes, and I hope you will be among them.'"],[3198,"“A man will enter Paradise and no people of a house or a chamber will remain but they will say, ‘Welcome, welcome, to us, to us.’” Abu Bakr said, “O Messenger of Allah, what do you think will be upon this man on that day?” He said, “Indeed, and you are he, O Abu Bakr.”"],[3199,"I have never seen my parents without them practicing their faith, and not a day would pass without the messenger of Allah ﷺ visiting us at both ends of the day, in the morning and evening. When the Muslims were tested, Abu Bakr migrated before the Abyssinian land. When he reached Bark al-Ghimad, he was met by Ibn al-Daghinah, who was the ruler of the region. He asked, \"Where are you going, O Abu Bakr?\" Abu Bakr replied, \"My people have forced me out, and I intend to travel in the land and worship my Lord.\" Ibn al-Daghinah said, \"People like you, O Abu Bakr, do not leave nor are they forced to leave. You earn what is lost, maintain family ties, carry the load for others, honor guests, help those in need, and assist in matters of truth. I am your neighbor, so return and worship your Lord in your own land.\" Ibn al-Daghinah then left and Abu Bakr returned with him. Ibn al-Daghinah then went around the disbelievers of Quraish and said, \"Abu Bakr is not like anyone of you. You are expelling a man who earns what is lost, maintains family ties, carries the load for others, honors guests, and helps in matters of truth.\" The people of Quraish then surrounded Ibn al-Daghinah and granted protection to Abu Bakr. They told Ibn al-Daghinah, \"Tell Abu Bakr to worship his Lord in his own home as he pleases, to perform prayer as he pleases, to recite the Quran as he pleases, and to not harm us or cause disturbance by praying or reciting in a place other than his own home.\" And he did so."],[3200,"I said to the Prophet ﷺ, “If one of them looked under his foot, he would see us from under his foot.” The Prophet ﷺ said, “What do you think of two when Allah is their third?”"],[3201,"Abu Bakr bought a saddle from ‘Azib for thirteen dirhams, then Abu Bakr said to 'Azib. Tell al-Bara to carry it to my house. He said: No, not until you tell us what happened when the Messenger of Allah ﷺ went out and you were with him. Abu Bakr said: We started our journey at the beginning of the night and we hastened for one day and one night, until it was midday. I looked into the distance to see whether there was anywhere to seek shade, and I saw a rock, so I went to it and it had a little shade. I smoothed the ground for the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and spread a garment of camel hair for him, and said: Lie down and rest, O Messenger of Allah. So he lay down, and I went out to see if I could spot anyone looking for us. Then I saw a shepherd and I said: Who do you belong to, O boy? He said: To a man of Quraish. He mentioned his name and I recognised it. I said: Is there any milk in your sheep? He said: Yes | said: Will you milk some for me? He said: Yes. I told him to do that, so he caught a sheep, then I told him to brush the dust from its teat, then to brush the dust off his hands. I had a small vessel with me on the neck of which was a cloth. He milked a little bit of milk for me and I poured it into the vessel until it cooled down. Then I came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. When I reached him, he had already woken up. I said: Drink, O Messenger of Allah. He drank until I was pleased, then I said: Is it time to move on? So we moved on and the people were coming after us but none of them caught up with us except Suraqah bin Malik bin Ju'shum, who was riding a horse of his, I said: O Messenger of Allah, someone has caught up with us. He said: ʿDo not be afraid, for Allah is with us.ʿ When he got close to us, and there was no more between us and him then the length of a spear or two or three spears, I said: O Messenger of Allah, this pursuer has caught up with us, and I wept. He said: ʿWhy are you weeping?ʿ I said: I am not weeping for myself; rather I am weeping for you. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ prayed against him [the pursuer] and said: “O Allah, protect us from him by whatever means You will.” Then his horse's legs sank into the solid ground up to its belly, and he fell off it. He said: O Muhammad, I know that this is because of you; pray to Allah to save me from my predicament, and by Allah I shall divert away from you any one who is behind me of those who are seeking you. Here is my quiver, take one arrow. You are going to pass by some camels and sheep of mine in such and such a place, take whatever you need from thern. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: ʿI have no need of it.“ The Messenger of Allah ﷺ prayed for him and he was released, and he went back to his companions. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ and I continued on our way until we came to Madinah, where the people met him. They came out on the road and on the roofs, and a lot of servants and children crowded the road saying: Allahu Akbar, the Messenger of Allah ﷺ has come, Muhammad has come. The people disputed as to who he would stay with. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: ʿTonight I will stay with Banun-Najjar, the maternal uncles of 'Abdul-Muttalib, to honour them thereby.” The next morning, he went where he was instructed. Al-Bara' bin 'Azib said: The first of the Muhajireen to come to us was Mus'ab bin 'Umair, the brother of Banu 'Abdud-Dar. Then Ibn Umm Maktoom, the blind man and brother of Banu Fihr, came to us. Then 'Umar bin al-Khattab, came to us with twenty riders and we said: What happened to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ? He said: He is behind me. Then the Messenger of Allah ﷺ came and Abu Bakr was with him. Al-Bara said: the Messenger of Allah ﷺ did not come until I had read some soorahs from al-Mufassal [Al-Mufassal is that portion of the Qur'an which goes from Qaf to an-Nas]. Isra'eel said: al-Bara' was one of the Ansar from Banu Harithah. (Using translation from Aḥmad 3)"],[3202,"A woman came to the Prophet ﷺ asking him for something, and he said to her, \"Come back to me.\" She said to him, \"O Messenger of Allah, if I come back and do not find you\" — alluding to death. He ﷺ said, \"If you do not find me, then go to Abu Bakr.\""],[3203,"A woman came to the Prophet ﷺ and spoke to him about something, and he told her to come back to him. She said, \"O Messenger of Allah, what do you think if I come back and do not find you?\" as if she meant death. He said, \"If you do not find me, then go to Abu Bakr.\""],[3204,"When the Messenger of Allah ﷺ became gravely ill, Bilal came to tell him it was time for prayer. He said, \"Tell Abu Bakr to lead the people in prayer.\" I said, \"O Messenger of Allah, Abu Bakr is a tender-hearted man; whenever he stands in your place, he will not make the people hear [due to weeping]. If only you would order 'Umar.\" He said, \"Tell Abu Bakr to lead the people in prayer.\" I said to Hafsah, \"Tell him.\" She said, \"O Messenger of Allah, Abu Bakr is a tender-hearted man; whenever he stands in your place, he will not make the people hear.\" He said, \"You are indeed like the women around Yusuf. Tell Abu Bakr to lead the people in prayer.\" When he entered the prayer, the Messenger of Allah ﷺ found some relief, so he stood up, supported between two men, with his feet dragging on the ground, until he entered the mosque. When Abu Bakr heard his sound, he began to step back, but the Messenger of Allah ﷺ gestured to him, \"Stay as you are.\" Then the Messenger of Allah ﷺ sat down to the left of Abu Bakr. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ prayed with the people sitting, while Abu Bakr stood, following the prayer of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and the people followed the prayer of Abu Bakr."],[3205,"When the Messenger of Allah ﷺ became seriously ill, he said, \"Tell Abu Bakr to lead the people in prayer.\" 'A'ishah said to him, \"O Messenger of Allah, Abu Bakr is a soft-hearted man; if he stands in your place, he will not make the people hear due to weeping.\" He said, \"Tell Abu Bakr to lead the people in prayer.\" She repeated the same to him, and he said, \"You are indeed like the women around Yusuf. Tell Abu Bakr to lead the people in prayer.\""],[3206,"When it was Monday, the Messenger of Allah ﷺ drew back the curtain of the room and saw Abu Bakr al-Siddiq ؓ leading the people in prayer. He said, \"I looked at his face as if it were a page of a mushaf, and he was smiling. We almost became distracted in our prayer out of joy at seeing the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. Abu Bakr ؓ wanted to step back when the Messenger of Allah ﷺ came, but the Prophet ﷺ gestured to him, 'Stay as you are.' Then he let the curtain down and passed away on that day. 'Umar b. al-Khattab ؓ stood up and said, 'The Messenger of Allah ﷺ has not died, but he was sent for just as Musa was sent for, and he remained among his people for forty nights. By Allah, I hope that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ will live until he cuts off the hands and tongues of men among the hypocrites who claim that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ has died.'\""],[3207,"\"While I was sleeping, I saw a cup that was brought to me containing milk. I drank from it until I saw the moisture flowing in my nails, then I gave what was left to 'Umar b. al-Khattab.\" They said, \"How did you interpret that, O Messenger of Allah?\" He said, \"Knowledge.\""],[3208,"By Allah, no word was mentioned to him until he stood up intently towards the Mosque and called out the people of Quraysh. He said, \"O people of Quraysh, indeed the son of Al-Khattab has taken over.\" Umar said, \"He lied, but indeed I have embraced Islam, believed in Allah, and affirmed His Messenger.\" Then they confronted him and fought with him until the sun set on their heads. Umar got injured and sat down. They stood over his head, and Umar said, \"Do whatever seems best to you. By Allah, if we were three hundred men, you would not have escaped us, or we would have not left it to you.\" While they were in that situation, a man came wearing a silk robe and a Qumiss garment. He asked, \"What is happening?\" They said, \"Indeed the son of Al-Khattab has taken over.\" He said, \"It seems as if a garment has been removed from him.\" Then I said to him later in Medina, \"Father, who was the man who defended you that day?\" He said, \"O my son, that was Tha'alib bin Wail.\""],[3209,"\"We have been mighty since 'Umar embraced Islam.\""],[3210,"\"O Allah, strengthen the religion with the more beloved of these two men to You: Abu Jahl b. Hisham or 'Umar b. al-Khattab.\""],[3211,"\"O Allah, strengthen Islam with 'Umar b. al-Khattab in particular.\""],[3212,"When ʿUmar embraced Islam, Jibrīl ﷺ came to the Prophet ﷺ and said, “O Muhammad, the inhabitants of heaven rejoiced at ʿUmar’s Islam.”"],[3213,"ʿUmar b. al-Khaṭṭāb is among the people of Paradise."],[3214,"I said, “O Messenger of Allah, which people are most beloved to you?” He said, “ʿĀʾishah.” I said, “O Messenger of Allah, from among the men?” He said, “Her father, Abū Bakr.” I said, “Then who?” He said, “Then ʿUmar b. al-Khaṭṭāb.”"],[3215,"“I entered Paradise and saw therein a palace of gold or pearls. I said, ‘For whom is this palace?’ They said, ‘For ʿUmar b. al-Khaṭṭāb.’ Nothing prevented me from entering it except my knowledge of your jealousy.” He said, “May I be jealous for you, by my father and mother! I would be jealous for you.”"],[3216,"“I entered Paradise and there I was with a palace of gold. I said, ‘For whom is this palace?’ They said, ‘For a young man of Quraysh.’ I thought that I was he, so I said, ‘And who is he?’ They said, ‘ʿUmar b. al-Khaṭṭāb.’”"],[3217,"“While I was sleeping I saw myself in Paradise, and there was a woman performing ablution beside a palace. I said, ‘For whom is this?’ She said, ‘For ʿUmar b. al-Khaṭṭāb.’ Then I remembered ʿUmar’s jealousy and turned away.” Abū Hurayrah said: ʿUmar wept while we all were in that gathering, then he said, “May my father and mother be sacrificed for you, O Messenger of Allah! Would I be jealous of you?”"],[3218,"“Indeed Allah has placed the truth upon ʿUmar’s tongue and heart.”"],[3219,"“While I was sleeping, I saw the people being presented to me, wearing shirts, some of which reached the breasts and some of which were lower than that. ʿUmar was presented to me wearing a shirt that he was dragging.” Those around him said, “How did you interpret it, O Prophet of Allah?” He said, “The religion.”"],[3220,"He entered upon ʿUmar when he was stabbed and said, “Rejoice, O Commander of the Believers. You embraced Islam with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ when the people disbelieved, and you fought alongside the Messenger of Allah ﷺ when the people abandoned him. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ died while he was pleased with you, and no two men differed concerning your caliphate, and you will be killed as a martyr.” He said, “Repeat it.” So he repeated it, and he said, “The deceived is the one whom you deceive. If I had all that is on the earth of white and yellow, I would ransom myself with it from the terror of the rising.”"],[3221,"“I reckon that Satan flees from you, O ʿUmar.”"],[3222,"ʿUmar b. al-Khaṭṭāb ؓ entered upon the Messenger of Allah ﷺ while some women of Quraysh were with him, asking him and requesting more, raising their voices. When they heard ʿUmar’s voice, they shrank back and fell silent. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ laughed. ʿUmar said, “O enemies of your own selves, you fear me but you do not fear the Messenger of Allah ﷺ?” The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, “O ʿUmar, Satan does not meet you traveling on a path except that he travels on a path other than your path.”"],[3223,"“There were in the nations before you people who were inspired. If there is anyone in my nation, it is ʿUmar b. al-Khaṭṭāb.”"],[3224,"Verily Allah has placed the truth upon the tongue of 'Umar and his heart."],[3225,"I agreed with my Lord in three things, or my Lord agreed with me in three things. I said: 'O Messenger of Allah, if only you were to take the Station of Ibrahim as a place of prayer,' and Allah revealed: 'And take, [O believers], from the standing place of Abraham a place of prayer' (2:125). And I said: 'Righteous and wicked people enter upon you, so if only you were to screen the Mothers of the Believers,' and the verse of the veil was revealed. And I heard of some matter concerning the Mothers of the Believers, so I said to them: 'You must stop troubling the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, or Allah will surely replace him with wives better than you,' until I came to one of the Mothers of the Believers and she said: 'O 'Umar, is there not in the Messenger of Allah ﷺ enough to admonish his wives that you must admonish them?' So I refrained, and Allah revealed: 'Perhaps his Lord, if he divorces you [all], will substitute for him wives better than you' (66:5)."],[3226,"The Prophet ﷺ saw a white garment on 'Umar b. al-Khattab ؓ and said: \"Is your shirt new or washed?\" He replied: 'Rather, it is new.' The Prophet ﷺ said: \"Wear new clothes, live praiseworthy, and die a martyr.\""],[3227,"While I was sleeping, I saw myself over a well with a bucket on it. I drew from it as much as Allah willed, then Ibn Abi Quhafah took it from me and drew a bucket or two, and in his drawing there was weakness, and Allah will forgive his weakness. Then the bucket turned into a large bucket, and 'Umar b. al-Khattab took it, and I have never seen a chief among people draw as Ibn al-Khattab drew, until the people had watered their camels."],[3228,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"I am the first from whom the earth will split open, then Abu Bakr, then 'Umar. Then I will come to the people of al-Baqi' and they will be gathered with me. Then I will wait for the people of Makkah until they are gathered between the two sanctuaries.\""],[3229,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ sent him on the expedition of Dhat al-Salasil. He said: I came to him and asked: 'Which of the people is most beloved to you?' He said: \"'A'ishah.\" I said: 'Among men?' He said: \"Her father.\" I said: 'Then whom?' He said: \"Then 'Umar b. al-Khattab.\""],[3230,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, \"If people obey Abu Bakr and Umar, then they have indeed been guided.\""],[3231,"We were with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ when he said: \"I do not think I will remain among you but a little while, so follow the example of those after me,\" and he pointed to Abu Bakr and 'Umar, \"and be guided by the guidance of 'Ammar, and whatever Ibn Mas'ud tells you, accept it.\""],[3232,"While a man was driving a cow, he became weary and mounted it. It turned to him and said: 'We were not created for this; we were created for tilling the earth.' The people said: 'Glory be to Allah! Glory be to Allah!' The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"Indeed I believe in this, I, Abu Bakr, and 'Umar,\" though they were not among the people. Then the people said: 'We believe in what the Messenger of Allah ﷺ has believed in.'"],[3233,"Abu Bakr and 'Umar are the masters of the middle-aged men of Paradise, from the first and the last, except for the prophets and messengers."],[3234,"Abu Lu'lu'ah was a slave of al-Mughirah b. Shu'bah. He used to make millstones, and al-Mughirah exploited him for four dirhams daily. Abu Lu'lu'ah met 'Umar b. al-Khattab ؓ and said: 'O Commander of the Faithful, al-Mughirah has made my dues heavy; speak to him to lighten it for me.' 'Umar said to him: \"Fear Allah and be good to your master.\" The slave became angry and said: 'Your justice encompasses all people except me,' and he resolved to kill him. He fashioned a dagger with two heads and poisoned it, then brought it to al-Hurmuzan and said: 'What do you think of this?' He said: 'You will not strike anyone with this but that you will kill him.'"],[3235,"Abu Bakr ؓ asked permission to enter upon the Prophet ﷺ while I was with him under a single cloak. He gave him permission, and he fulfilled his need while he was in that state under the cloak, then left. Then 'Umar b. al-Khattab ؓ asked permission, and he gave him permission, and he fulfilled his need while I was in that state under the cloak, then left. Then 'Uthman b. 'Affan ؓ asked permission, and he adjusted his clothes and sat up, then fulfilled his need and left. 'A'ishah said: I said: 'O Messenger of Allah, Abu Bakr asked permission, and you fulfilled his need while you were in that state; then 'Umar asked permission, and you fulfilled his need while you were in that state; then 'Uthman asked permission, and you adjusted your clothes and composed yourself.' He said: \"O 'A'ishah, 'Uthman is a shy man, and if I had given him permission in that state, I feared he would not fulfill his need to me.\""],[3236,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ was lying in his house with his thighs uncovered. Abu Bakr asked permission, and he gave him permission while he was in that state, and he spoke. Then 'Umar asked permission, and he gave him permission while he was in that state, and he spoke. Then 'Uthman asked permission, and the Messenger of Allah ﷺ sat up and arranged his clothes, and he entered and spoke. When he left, 'A'ishah said: 'O Messenger of Allah, Abu Bakr entered and you did not stir for him nor mind him; then 'Umar entered and you did not stir for him nor mind him; then 'Uthman entered and you sat up and arranged your clothes.' The Prophet ﷺ said: \"Should I not feel shy before a man before whom the angels feel shy?\""],[3237,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ climbed Uhud, and Abu Bakr, Umar, and Uthman followed him. It trembled with them, so he said, 'Be firm, for upon you are a prophet, a truthful one, and two martyrs.'"],[3238,"A man asked Ibn Umar about Uthman: 'Did he witness Badr?' He said, 'No.' He said, 'Did he witness the Pledge of al-Ridwan?' He said, 'No.' He said, 'Was he among those who turned back on the day the two hosts met?' He said, 'Yes.' The man said, 'Allah is greatest,' then departed. It was said to Ibn Umar, 'What have you done? This man will go and tell people that you disparaged Uthman.' He said, 'Bring him back to me.' When he came, he said, 'Do you remember what you asked me about?' He said, 'I asked you about Uthman: did he witness Badr? You said no.' He said, 'Indeed, the Messenger of Allah ﷺ sent him on an errand of his on the day of Badr and allotted him a share.' He said, 'And I asked you: did he witness the Pledge of al-Ridwan? You said no.' He said, 'Indeed, the Messenger of Allah ﷺ sent him on an errand of his, then struck his own hand over Uthman's hand. Which of the two is better: the hand of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ or the hand of Uthman?' He said, 'And I asked you: was he among those who turned back on the day the two hosts met? You said yes.' He said, 'Indeed, Allah says, \"Satan only caused them to slip because of some of what they earned, but Allah has pardoned them. Indeed, Allah is Forgiving, Forbearing\" (3:155). Go and strive as hard as you can.'"],[3239,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ was in a garden, and I was with him. A man came and asked permission to enter. He said, 'Open for him and give him glad tidings of Paradise.' And it was Abu Bakr. Then another came and asked permission. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, 'Open for him and give him glad tidings of Paradise.' And it was Umar b. al-Khattab. Then another came and asked permission. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, 'Open for him and give him glad tidings of Paradise.' And it was Uthman b. Affan."],[3240,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to me, 'Guard the door.' A man came seeking permission. He said, 'Grant him permission and give him glad tidings of Paradise.' And it was Abu Bakr. Then a man came seeking permission. He said, 'Grant him permission and give him glad tidings of Paradise.' And it was Umar. Then a man came seeking permission. He said, and the Prophet ﷺ fell silent, then said, 'Grant him permission and give him glad tidings of Paradise along with a severe affliction that will befall him.' And it was Uthman."],[3241,"He was reclining in one of the gardens of Madinah, poking with a stick in the water and mud, when a man came and asked permission. He ﷺ said, 'Open for him and give him glad tidings of Paradise.' And it was Abu Bakr, so I opened for him and gave him glad tidings of Paradise. Then another asked permission. He said, 'Open for him and give him glad tidings of Paradise.' And it was Umar, so I opened for him and gave him glad tidings of Paradise. Then another asked permission. He sat for a while, then said, 'Open for him and give him glad tidings of Paradise along with an affliction.' He said, so I opened for him, and it was Uthman, and I gave him glad tidings of Paradise and told him what he had said. He said, 'O Allah, grant patience,' or he said, 'Allah is the one whose help is sought.'"],[3242,"The Prophet ﷺ said, 'I was shown tonight a righteous man: Abu Bakr was attached to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, Umar was attached to Abu Bakr, and Uthman was attached to Umar.' Jabir said: When we left the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, we said, 'As for the righteous man, he is the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and as for what he mentioned about their being attached to one another, they are the rulers of this affair with which Allah sent His Prophet ﷺ.'"],[3243,"While we were with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ on one of the roads of Madinah, he said, 'What will you do when a tribulation arises in the regions of the earth like the horns of cattle?' They said, 'What should we do, O Prophet of Allah?' He said, 'Stick to this man and his companions.' He said, so I hurried and turned to the man and said, 'This one, O Prophet of Allah?' He said, 'This one.' And it was Uthman b. Affan ؓ."],[3244,"Muawiya b. Abi Sufyan sent him with a letter to Aisha. He gave it to her, and she said, 'Shall I not tell you a hadith I heard from the Messenger of Allah ﷺ?' I said, 'Yes.' She said, 'I was with him one day, I and Hafsa, and the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, \"If only we had a man to talk to us.\" I said, \"O Messenger of Allah, shall I send for Abu Bakr to come and talk to us?\" She said, he remained silent. Hafsa said, \"O Messenger of Allah, shall I send for Umar to come and talk to us?\" She said, he ﷺ remained silent. Then he called a man and whispered something to him apart from us. The man went and brought Uthman. He turned to him and I heard him ﷺ say, \"O Uthman, perhaps Allah will clothe you with a shirt. If they want you to take it off, do not take it off\"—three times. I said, \"O Mother of the Believers, why did you not mention this hadith before?\" She said, \"O my son, I forgot it, as if I had never heard it.\""],[3245,"When Uthman was besieged and his house was surrounded, he looked out over the people and said, 'I adjure you by Allah: do you know that when Hira shook with us, the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, \"Be firm, Hira, for upon you are only a prophet, a truthful one, or a martyr\"?' They said, 'O Allah, yes.' He said, 'I adjure you by Allah: do you know that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said during the expedition of hardship, \"Whoever spends an accepted expenditure\"?' The people then were in straitened circumstances and exhausted, and I equipped a third of that army from my own wealth. They said, 'O Allah, yes.' Then he said, 'I adjure you by Allah: do you know that Ruma well was not drunk from except for a price, and I bought it with my own wealth and made it for the rich, the poor, and the wayfarer?' They said, 'O Allah, yes,' among other things he enumerated."],[3246,"Umar said, 'Do you two fear that you have loaded the earth with what it cannot bear?' They said, 'We have loaded it with a matter it is capable of, and there is not much surplus in it.' He said, 'Consider that you have not loaded the earth with what it cannot bear.' They said, 'No.' He said, 'If Allah grants me safety, I will leave the widows of Iraq not needing anyone after me.' He said, and only four nights passed before he was struck. Amr b. Maymun said: I was standing between him and nothing but Abdullah b. Abbas on the morning he was struck. When he passed between the two rows, he stood between them, and if he saw a gap, he said, 'Straighten up,' until he saw no gap among them, then he advanced and said the takbir. He said, sometimes he would recite Surah Yusuf or al-Nahl in the first rak'ah until the people gathered. He said, no sooner had he said the takbir than I heard him say, 'The dog has killed me,' or 'The dog has eaten me,' when the non-Arab struck him with a double-edged knife. He did not pass by anyone to the right or left without stabbing him, until he had stabbed thirteen men, of whom nine died. When a Muslim man saw that, he threw a burnous over him. When the non-Arab realized he was captured, he slit his own throat. Umar took the hand of Abd al-Rahman b. Awf and brought him forward. Those near Umar saw what I saw, but the people in the far parts of the mosque did not know what was happening, except that they missed Umar's voice, and they were saying, 'Glory be to Allah, glory be to Allah.' Abd al-Rahman led the people in a brief prayer. When they finished, Umar said, 'O Ibn Abbas, see who killed me.' He went around for a while, then said, 'The slave of al-Mughira b. Shu'ba.' He said, 'May Allah fight him! I had commanded him to do good.' Then he said, 'Praise be to Allah who did not make my death at the hand of a man who claims Islam. You and your father used to love that the non-Arabs increase in Madinah.' Al-Abbas had the most slaves among them. He was carried to his house. It was as if the people had never been afflicted with a calamity before that day. One said, 'We fear for him,' and another said, 'No harm.' Nabidh was brought to him, and he drank some, and it came out of his wound. Then milk was brought, and he drank some, and it came out of his wound. They knew he was dying. We entered upon him, and people came praising him. A young man came and said, 'Rejoice, O Commander of the Believers, with the good news of Allah. You have the companionship of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and precedence in Islam as you know. Then you were made caliph and you were just. Then martyrdom.' He said, 'O my nephew, I wish that this were just enough, neither against me nor for me.' When the man turned away, his waist-wrapper was touching the ground. He said, 'Bring the boy back to me.' He said, 'O my nephew, raise your garment, for it is cleaner for your garment and more fearful of your Lord. O Abdullah, see what debt I owe.' They calculated it and found it to be eighty-six thousand. He said, 'If the wealth of the family of Umar suffices, pay it from their wealth. Otherwise, ask among Banu Adi b. Ka'b. If their wealth does not suffice, ask among Quraysh, and do not go beyond them to others. Go to the Mother of the Believers Aisha and say to her: Umar b. al-Khattab sends you greetings of peace. Do not say Commander of the Believers, for I am not the commander of the believers. Say: Umar b. al-Khattab asks permission to be buried with his two companions.' Abdullah greeted and asked permission, and found her weeping. He said to her, 'Umar b. al-Khattab asks permission to be buried with his two companions.' She said, 'By Allah, I had wanted it for myself, but today I will prefer him over myself.' He came back. When he approached, it was said, 'This is Abdullah, he has come.' He said, 'Lift me up.' A man supported him, and he said, 'What did she say?' He said, 'What you love, O Commander of the Believers. She has permitted you.' He said, 'Praise be to Allah. Nothing was more important to me than that resting place. When I die, greet and say: Umar b. al-Khattab asks permission. If she permits me, bring me in; if she refuses, take me to the graveyard of the Muslims.' Then the Mother of the Believers Hafsa came with women, and they were veiling her. When we saw her, we stood up. She stayed with him for a while, then the men asked permission and she entered inside. Then we heard her weeping from inside. It was said to him, 'Give instructions, O Commander of the Believers. Appoint a successor.' He said, 'I see no one more entitled to this affair than these men with whom the Messenger of Allah ﷺ died while he was pleased with them.' He named Ali, Talha, Uthman, al-Zubayr, Abd al-Rahman b. Awf, and Sa'd ؓ. He said, 'Let Abdullah b. Umar be present, but he has no part in the affair, as a form of consolation for him. If Sa'd attains the affair, then that is it; otherwise, let whoever among you is appointed seek his help, for I have not removed him due to incapacity or treachery.' Then he said, 'I enjoin the caliph after me to fear Allah. I enjoin him concerning the early Muhajirun: to recognize their due and preserve their sanctity. I enjoin him concerning the Ansar, who had settled in the abode and embraced faith before them, to accept from their good-doers and overlook their wrongdoers. I enjoin him concerning the people of the garrison towns: they are the support of Islam, the collectors of wealth, and the vexation of the enemy. Let nothing be taken from them except their surplus with their consent. I enjoin him concerning the Bedouins: they are the origin of the Arabs and the substance of Islam. Let their wealth be taken from their surplus and returned to their poor. I enjoin him concerning the covenant of Allah and the covenant of His Messenger ﷺ: to fulfill their treaty, to fight for them, and not to burden them beyond their capacity.' When he died, ؓ , we went out with him walking. Abdullah b. Umar greeted and said, 'Umar asks permission.' She said, 'Bring him in.' He was brought in and placed there with his two companions. When the burial was finished and they returned, those men gathered. Abd al-Rahman b. Awf said, 'Entrust your affair to three of you.' Al-Zubayr said, 'I entrust my affair to Ali.' Sa'd said, 'I entrust my affair to Abd al-Rahman.' Talha said, 'I entrust my affair to Uthman.' So these three came: Ali, Uthman, and Abd al-Rahman b. Awf. Abd al-Rahman said to the other two, 'Which of you will withdraw from this affair and entrust it to him, with Allah and Islam as witness, that he will look for the best among them in his own judgment and strive for the welfare of the community?' He said, the two elders, Ali and Uthman, remained silent. Abd al-Rahman said, 'Entrust it to me, and Allah is my witness that I will not fail to choose the best of you.' They said, 'Yes.' He brought Ali and said, 'You have precedence, early Islam, and kinship as you know. By Allah, if I appoint you, will you be just, and if I appoint over you, will you listen and obey?' Then he brought Uthman and said the same to him. When he had taken the pledge, he said to Uthman, 'Raise your hand.' He gave him the oath of allegiance, then Ali gave him the oath of allegiance, then the people of the house entered and gave him the oath of allegiance."],[3247,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said during his illness, 'I wish some of my companions were with me.' She said, we said, 'O Messenger of Allah, shall we call Abu Bakr for you?' He remained silent. We said, 'Umar?' He remained silent. We said, 'Ali?' He remained silent. We said, 'Uthman?' He said, 'Yes.' She said, so we sent for Uthman. She said, the Prophet ﷺ began to speak to him, and his face changed. Qays said: Abu Sahla told me that Uthman said on the Day of the House, 'The Messenger of Allah ﷺ made a covenant with me, and I am patient with it.' Qays said: they used to think that that was the day."],[3249,"We came to Madinah. Uthman came, and it was said, 'This is Uthman,' and he was wearing a yellow cloak of his with which he had covered his head. He said, 'Is Ali here?' They said, 'Yes.' He said, 'Is Talha here?' They said, 'Yes.' He said, 'I adjure you by Allah, besides whom there is no god: do you know that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, \"Whoever buys the pen of Banu So-and-so, Allah will forgive him,\" and I bought it for twenty thousand or twenty-five thousand? Then I came to the Prophet ﷺ and said, \"I have bought it.\" He said, \"Make it part of our mosque and its reward is yours\"?' They said, 'O Allah, yes.' He said, 'I adjure you by Allah, besides whom there is no god: do you know that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, \"Whoever buys Ruma, Allah will forgive him,\" and I bought it for such and such? Then I came to him and said, \"I have bought it.\" He said, \"Make it a watering place for the Muslims and its reward is yours\"?' They said, 'O Allah, yes.' He said, 'I adjure you by Allah, besides whom there is no god: do you know that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ looked at the faces of the people and said, \"Whoever equips these men, Allah will forgive him,\" meaning the army of hardship, and I equipped them so that they did not lack even a rope or a halter?' They said, 'O Allah, yes.' He said, 'O Allah, bear witness,' three times."],[3250,"Fatima complained of the suffering caused to her by the hand mill. Some Captives were brought to the Prophet, she came to him but did not find him at home ʿAisha was present there to whom she told (of her desire for a servant). When the Prophet ﷺ came, Aisha informed him about Fatima's visit. ʿAli added \"So the Prophet ﷺ came to us, while we had gone to our bed I wanted to get up but the Prophet ﷺ said, \"Remain at your place\". Then he sat down between us till I found the coolness of his feet on my chest. Then he said, \"Shall I teach you a thing which is better than what you have asked me? When you go to bed, say, 'Allahu-Akbar' thirty-four times, and 'Subhan Allah thirty-three times, and 'Al hamdu-li l-lah thirty-three times for that is better for you both than a servant.\" (Using translation from Bukhārī 3705)"],[3251,"Fatimah complained to me about the flour, so I said, \"Why don't you go to your father and ask him for a servant?\" She went to the Prophet ﷺ to request a servant but did not find him. She returned to her place. When the Prophet ﷺ came, he was wearing a garment with a fringe at the bottom, and when we wore it lengthwise, our feet would extend beyond it, and when we wore it widthwise, our heads and feet would protrude.The Prophet ﷺ asked Fatimah, \"Did you come earlier with a need?\" She replied, \"No.\" I said, \"Yes, she complained to me about the flour, and I suggested she ask her father for a servant.\" The Prophet ﷺ said, \"Shall I guide you to something better for the two of you than having a servant? When you go to bed, say 'SubhanAllah' (Glory be to Allah) thirty-three times, 'Alhamdulillah' (Praise be to Allah) thirty-three times, and 'Allahu Akbar' (Allah is the Greatest) thirty-four times.\""],[3252,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to me: \"You have harmed me.\" I said: \"O Messenger of Allah, I would not love to harm you.\" He said: \"Whoever harms 'Ali has harmed me.\""],[3253,"\"By the One who split the grain and created the soul, it is the covenant of the unlettered Prophet ﷺ to me that none loves me but a believer, and none hates me but a hypocrite.\""],[3254,"A man came to him and said: \"This is so-and-so, an emir from the emirs of Madinah, who invites you to curse 'Ali on the pulpit.\" He said: \"What should I say?\" He said: \"You should call him Abu Turab (father of dust).\" So Sahl laughed and said: \"By Allah, no one named him that except the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. There was no name dearer to 'Ali than it. 'Ali entered upon Fatimah, then he left. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ came to Fatimah and said: 'Where is your cousin?' She said: 'There he is, lying in the mosque.' The Prophet ﷺ went out and found his cloak had fallen from his back. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ began wiping the dust from his back and saying: 'Sit up, Abu Turab.' By Allah, there was no name dearer to him than it. No one named him that except the Messenger of Allah ﷺ.\""],[3256,"Messenger of Allah, are you leaving me behind amongst women and children? Thereupon he (the Holy Prophet) said: Aren't you satisfied with being unto me what Aaron was unto Moses but with this exception that there would be no prophet after me? (Using translation from Muslim 2404b)"],[3257,"The Prophet ﷺ said to Ali, 'Are you not pleased that you are to me as Aaron was to Moses, except that there is no prophet after me?'"],[3258,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ sent Abu Bakr ؓ, and when he reached Dajnan, he heard the grumbling of Ali's ؓ camel, recognized it, and came to him. He said, \"What is my situation?\" He said, \"It is good. The Prophet ﷺ sent me with Bara'ah. When we returned, Abu Bakr ؓ went and said, 'O Messenger of Allah, what about me?' He said, 'It is good. You are my companion in the cave. However, none but me or a man from me may convey it'\""],[3259,"When they returned to Madinah from the Umrah of al-Ji'ranah, he sent Abu Bakr ؓ to lead the Hajj. We set out with him until, when we were at al-Arj, he called the iqamah for the dawn prayer. When he stood up for the takbir, he heard the rumble of a camel behind him, so he paused the takbir and said, \"This is the rumble of the camel of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, al-Jad'a'. Perhaps it is the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, so we may pray with him.\" But it was Ali on it. Abu Bakr said to him, \"Are you a commander or a messenger?\" He said, \"No, rather a messenger. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ sent me with Bara'ah to recite to the people at the stations of Hajj.\" We reached Makkah, and on the day before the Day of Tarwiyah, Abu Bakr stood and addressed the people. When he finished, Ali stood and recited Bara'ah until he completed it. Then we went out with him until the Day of Arafah. Abu Bakr stood and addressed the people, teaching them their rites. When he finished, Ali stood and recited Bara'ah to the people until he completed it. Then on the Day of Sacrifice, we departed. When Abu Bakr returned, he addressed the people and told them about their departure, their sacrifices, and their rites. When he finished, Ali stood and recited Bara'ah to the people until he completed it. On the first Day of Departure, Abu Bakr stood and addressed the people about how they should depart and how they should throw, teaching them their rites. When he finished, Ali stood and recited Bara'ah to the people until he completed it."],[3260,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to me: \"O 'Ali, shall I not teach you some words which, if you say them, you will be forgiven, even though you are already forgiven: There is no god but Allah, the Most High, the Magnificent. There is no god but Allah, the Forbearing, the Generous. Glory be to Allah, Lord of the seven heavens and Lord of the Mighty Throne. And praise be to Allah, Lord of the worlds.\""],[3261,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ dispatched a military expedition and appointed 'Ali over them. 'Ali went on the expedition and got a slave girl. The Companions of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ disapproved of that, and they said: \"When we meet the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, we will inform him of what 'Ali did.\" 'Imran said: When the Muslims returned from a journey, they would begin with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, greet him, and look at him, then they would go to their mounts. When the expedition returned, they greeted the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. One of the four stood up and said: \"O Messenger of Allah, did you not see that 'Ali did such-and-such?\" He turned away from him. Then another stood up and said: \"O Messenger of Allah, did you not see that 'Ali did such-and-such?\" He turned away from him. Then another stood up and said: \"O Messenger of Allah, did you not see that 'Ali did such-and-such?\" The Messenger of Allah ﷺ turned to him with anger recognizable on his face and said: \"What do you want from 'Ali?\" three times. \"Verily, 'Ali is from me and I am from him, and he is the ally of every believer after me.\""],[3262,"\"Whoever I am his ally, 'Ali is his ally.\""],[3263,"I adjure by Allah every person who heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say on the day of Ghadir Khumm when he stood up. So some people stood up and testified that they heard him say: \"Do you not know that I have more authority over the believers than their own selves?\" They said: \"Yes, O Messenger of Allah.\" He said: \"Whoever I am his mawla, this is his mawla. O Allah, befriend whoever befriends him, and be hostile to whoever is hostile to him.\" So I left with something in my soul about that. Then I met Zayd b. Arqam and mentioned that to him. He said: \"We heard it from the Messenger of Allah ﷺ saying that to him.\""],[3264,"\"I shall give the banner tomorrow to a man through whose hands Allah will grant victory.\" The people spent their night wondering which of them would be given it. When morning came, the people went early to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, each hoping to be given it. He said: \"Where is 'Ali b. Abi Talib?\" They said: \"He is complaining of his eyes, O Messenger of Allah.\" He said: \"Send for him.\" When he came, he spat in his eyes and supplicated for him, and he was cured as if he had no pain. He gave him the banner. 'Ali said: \"O Messenger of Allah, shall I fight them until they become like us?\" He said: \"Proceed at your ease until you alight in their courtyard, then call them to Islam and inform them of what is obligatory upon them of Allah's right therein. By Allah, for Allah to guide through you a single man is better for you than having red camels.\""],[3265,"\"I shall surely give the banner today to a man who loves Allah and His Messenger.\" The people stretched their necks. He said: \"Where is 'Ali?\" They said: \"He is complaining of his eye.\" He called him, spat into his palms, wiped them on 'Ali's eyes, then handed the banner to him, and Allah granted victory through him.\""],[3266,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said on the day of Khaybar: \"I shall surely give the banner today to a man who loves Allah and His Messenger, and Allah will grant victory through him.\" 'Umar said: \"I never desired command except on that day, and I stretched my neck for it.\" Then he said to 'Ali: \"Stand up.\" He handed the banner to him, then said: \"Go and do not turn around until Allah grants you victory.\" He walked a little, then stood without turning around because of the command. He said: \"On what basis shall I fight the people?\" The Prophet ﷺ said: \"Fight them until they testify that there is no god but Allah. If they say it, then they have protected their blood and their wealth from you except by its right, and their reckoning is with Allah.\""],[3267,"We went out to Khaybar, and my uncle 'Amir was reciting rajaz poetry to the people while saying:"],[3268,"\"O people, yesterday a man departed from you whom no one preceded and no later ones will reach. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to send him on expeditions and give him the banner, and he would not return until Allah granted him victory, with Jibril on his right and Mika'il on his left. He left neither white nor yellow except seven hundred dirhams remaining from his stipend; he wanted to buy a servant with it.\""],[3269,"«Indeed among you is one who will fight for the interpretation of the Qur'an just as I fought for its revelation.» Abu Bakr said, \"Is it I, O Messenger of Allah?\" He said, \"No.\" 'Umar said, \"Is it I, O Messenger of Allah?\" He said, \"No, but the one who is patching the sandal.\" He said, \"He had given 'Ali his sandal to patch.\""],[3270,"'Ali, ؓ , mentioned the Khawarij and said: \"Among them is a man with a deformed hand or a defective hand. Were it not that you would become exultant, I would inform you of what Allah has promised on the tongue of His Prophet ﷺ for those who kill them.\" So I said to 'Ali, \"Did you hear it from the Messenger of Allah ﷺ?\" He said, \"Yes, by the Lord of the Ka'bah, yes, by the Lord of the Ka'bah, yes, by the Lord of the Ka'bah.\""],[3271,"When the Haruriyyah rebelled, he was with 'Ali, and they said, \"No judgment except Allah's.\" 'Ali ؓ said, \"A word of truth by which falsehood is intended. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ described a people—I indeed recognize their description in these. They speak the truth with their tongues, but it does not pass this from them,\" and he pointed to his throat. \"Among the most hateful of Allah's creation to Him, among them is a black man, one of whose hands is [like] the teat of a breast.\" When 'Ali ؓ had killed them, he said, \"Look.\" They looked but did not find him. He said, \"Return, for by Allah, I have not lied nor been lied to,\" twice or three times. Then they found him in a ruin and brought him until they placed him before him."],[3272,"I was ill, and the Messenger of Allah ﷺ passed by me while I was saying, \"O Allah, if my appointed time has come, then give me rest; if it is delayed, then raise me; and if it is a trial, then grant me patience.\" The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to him, \"What did you say?\" So he repeated it to him. He said, \"Then he struck him with his foot and said, 'O Allah, cure him or heal him'—Shu'bah was the one who was unsure—\" He said, \"I never complained of that pain after that.\""],[3274,"«The caliphate after me is thirty years, then it becomes kingship.» He said: Count the caliphate of Abu Bakr ؓ as two years, 'Umar ؓ as ten, 'Uthman ؓ as twelve, and 'Ali ؓ as six. 'Ali b. al-Ja'd said: I said to Hammad b. Salamah, \"Was it Safinah who said 'Count'?\" He said, \"Yes.\""],[3275,"When Ibrahim, the son of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, died, the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, \"He has a wet-nurse in Paradise.\""],[3276,"I have never seen anyone more kind to one's family than Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and Ibrahim was sent to the suburb of Medina for suckling. He used to go there and we accompanied him. He entered the house, and it was filled with smoke as his foster-father was a bricksmith. He took him (his son Ibrihim) and kissed him and then came back. 'Amr said that when Ibrihim died. Allah's LMessenger ﷺ said: Ibrihim is my son and he dies as a suckling babe. He has now two foster-mothers who would complete his suckling period in Paradise. (Using translation from Muslim 2316)"],[3277,"\"The best women of the worlds are Maryam bint ʿImran, Khadijah bint Khuwaylid, Fatimah bint Muhammad ﷺ, and Asiyah the wife of Pharaoh.\""],[3278,"I said to Fatimah bint Rasulillah ﷺ, 'I saw you lean over the Prophet ﷺ during his illness and weep, then lean over him a second time and laugh.' She said, 'I leaned over him and he told me that he was going to die, so I wept. Then I leaned over him a second time and he told me that I would be the first of his family to join him and that I am the mistress of the women of the people of Paradise except Maryam bint ʿImran, so I laughed.'"],[3279,"Abu Bakr came to the Prophet ﷺ and sat before him, then said, \"O Messenger of Allah, you know my sincerity and my precedence in Islam, and I... and I...\" He said, \"And what is that?\" He said, \"Marry Fāṭimah to me.\" He said: He remained silent, so Abu Bakr returned to 'Umar and said to him, \"I have perished and caused ruin.\" He said, \"And what is that?\" He said, \"I proposed to Fāṭimah to the Prophet ﷺ, and he turned away from me.\" He said, \"Stay where you are until I go to the Prophet ﷺ and ask for the same as you did.\" So 'Umar came to the Prophet ﷺ and sat before him, then said, \"O Messenger of Allah, you know my sincerity and my precedence in Islam, and I... and I...\" He said, \"And what is that?\" He said, \"Marry Fāṭimah to me.\" He remained silent, so he returned to Abu Bakr and said to him, \"He is waiting for Allah's command regarding her. Come with us to 'Ali so that we may order him to ask for the same as we asked.\" 'Ali said: They came to me while I was tending a young palm of mine, and they said, \"We have come to you from your cousin's presence with a proposal.\" 'Ali said: They drew my attention to a matter, so I arose dragging my cloak until I came to the Prophet ﷺ and sat before him. I said, \"O Messenger of Allah, you know my precedence in Islam and my sincerity, and I... and I...\" He said, \"And what is that?\" I said, \"Marry Fāṭimah to me.\" He said, \"Do you have anything?\" I said, \"My horse and my body armor.\" He said, \"As for your horse, you cannot do without it; and as for your body armor, sell it.\" He said: I sold it for four hundred and eighty, and I brought the money and placed it in his lap. He took a handful from it and said, \"O Bilal, buy us perfume with this,\" and he ordered them to prepare her. He made for her a bed woven with palm leaves and a leather cushion stuffed with palm fiber. He said to 'Ali, \"When she comes to you, do not do anything until I come to you.\" She came with Umm Ayman and sat in one side of the house, and I in another side. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ came and said, \"Is my brother here?\" Umm Ayman said, \"He is your brother, and you have married your daughter to him?\" He said, \"Yes.\" The Messenger of Allah ﷺ entered the house and said to Fāṭimah, \"Bring me water.\" She went to a large wooden bowl in the house and brought water in it. He took it ﷺ and put some of his saliva in it, then said to her, \"Come forward.\" She came forward, and he sprinkled water between her breasts and on her head and said, \"O Allah, I seek refuge in You for her and her offspring from the accursed Satan.\" Then he ﷺ said to her, \"Turn around.\" She turned, and he poured water between her shoulders and said, \"O Allah, I seek refuge in You for her and her offspring from the accursed Satan.\" Then he ﷺ said, \"Bring me water.\" 'Ali said: I knew what he wanted, so I rose, filled the bowl with water, and brought it to him. He took it and put some of his saliva in it, then said to me, \"Come forward.\" He poured water on my head and between my breasts, then said, \"O Allah, I seek refuge in You for him and his offspring from the accursed Satan.\" Then he said, \"Turn around.\" I turned, and he poured it between my shoulders and said, \"O Allah, I seek refuge in You for him and his offspring from the accursed Satan.\" Then he said to 'Ali, \"Enter upon your wife in the name of Allah and with blessing.\""],[3280,"When 'Ali married Fāṭimah, the Prophet ﷺ said, \"Give her something.\" He said, \"I have nothing.\" He said, \"Where is your Huttamiyyah armor?\""],[3281,"«'Ali did not make Fāṭimah lawful except with an iron body armor.\""],[3282,"«The Messenger of Allah ﷺ prepared Fāṭimah with a velvet garment and a leather cushion stuffed with palm fiber.\""],[3283,"Abu Bakr and 'Umar proposed to Fāṭimah, and the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, \"She is young.\" Then 'Ali proposed to her, and he married her to him."],[3284,"\"I have never seen anyone whose speech and manner of speaking more closely resembled Rasulillah ﷺ than Fatimah. When she entered upon him, he would stand for her, kiss her, welcome her, take her hand, and seat her in his place. When he entered upon her, she would stand for him, kiss him, and take his hand. She entered upon him during the illness in which he died, and he confided something to her, so she wept. Then he confided something to her, so she laughed. I said, 'I used to think that this woman had some superiority over other people, but now she is just a woman among them: one moment she weeps and the next she laughs.' When Rasulillah ﷺ died, I asked her about that, and she said, 'He confided to me that he was going to die, so I wept. Then he confided to me and told me that I would be the first of his family to join him, so I laughed.'\""],[3285,"The Prophet ﷺ called Fatimah during his illness in which he passed away and whispered something to her, so she wept. Then he called her again and whispered something to her, so she laughed. ʿAʾishah said, 'I asked her about that afterwards, and she said, \"The Prophet ﷺ first whispered to me and told me that he would pass away during his illness, so I wept. Then he whispered to me and told me that I would be the first of his family to join him, so I laughed.\"'"],[3286,"I heard Rasulillah ﷺ on the minbar saying, \"The Banu Hisham b. al-Mughirah have asked my permission to marry their daughter to ʿAli in addition to my daughter. I will not permit it; then I will not permit it, unless ʿAli wishes to divorce my daughter and marry their daughter. For indeed my daughter is a part of me; what troubles her troubles me, and what hurts her hurts me.\""],[3287,"ʿAli b. Abi Talib ؓ proposed to the daughter of Abu Jahl in addition to Fatimah. He said, 'I heard the Prophet ﷺ while he was sermonizing about that on his minbar, and I was at that time on the verge of puberty. He said, \"Indeed Fatimah is from me, and I fear that she will be tempted in her religion.\" He mentioned a relative by marriage of his from the Banu ʿAbd Shams and praised him for his conduct as an in-law, and he spoke well. He said,'"],[3288,"ʿAli proposed to the daughter of Abu Jahl, and that reached Fatimah. She went to Rasulillah ﷺ and said, 'The people claim that you do not get angry for your daughters, and here is ʿAli marrying the daughter of Abu Jahl.' Al-Miswar said, 'I witnessed him ﷺ when he pronounced the testimony of faith, praised Allah, and extolled Him. Then he said, \"To proceed: I married my daughter to Abu al-ʿAs, and he spoke to me and was truthful to me. Indeed, Fatimah is a part of me, and by Allah, the daughter of Rasulillah ﷺ and the daughter of the enemy of Allah will never be united with one Muslim man.\" So ʿAli desisted from the proposal.'"],[3289,"When al-Hasan was born, I named him Harb. The Prophet ﷺ came and said, 'Show me my son; what have you named him?' We said, 'Harb.' He said, 'No, rather he is Hasan.' When al-Husayn was born, I named him Harb. The Prophet ﷺ came and said, 'Show me my son; what have you named him?' We said, 'Harb.' He said, 'Rather he is Husayn.' When the third was born to me, I named him Harb. The Prophet ﷺ came and said, 'Show me my son; what have you named him?' We said, 'We have named him Harb.' He said, 'Rather he is Muhsin.' Then he said, 'I have named them after the sons of Harun: Shabbar, Shabbir, and Mushabbir.'"],[3290,"\"Al-Hasan and al-Husayn are the masters of the youth of the people of Paradise, except for the two sons of the maternal aunt: ʿIsa b. Maryam and Yahya b. Zakariyya.\""],[3291,"I came to the Prophet ﷺ and prayed Maghrib with him. Then he stood to pray until he had prayed ʿIshaʾ. Then he left and I followed him. He said, 'An angel appeared to me, asked his Lord for permission to greet me, and gave me the glad tidings that al-Hasan and al-Husayn are the masters of the youth of the people of Paradise.'"],[3292,"“While the Prophet ﷺ was delivering a sermon, al-Hasan and al-Husayn came forward wearing two red shirts, walking and stumbling. The Prophet ﷺ descended to them, took them, and said: ‘Your wealth and your children are only a trial.’”"],[3293,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ was delivering a sermon to us when al-Hasan and al-Husayn came wearing two red shirts, walking and stumbling. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ descended from the pulpit, carried them, and placed them in front of him. Then he said: “Allah has spoken the truth: ‘Your wealth and your children are only a trial.’ I looked at these two boys walking and stumbling, and I could not be patient until I cut off my speech and lifted them up.”"],[3294,"Rasulillah ﷺ would take me and seat me on his thigh, and seat al-Hasan b. ʿAli on his other thigh, then say, 'O Allah, I have mercy on them, so have mercy on them.'"],[3295,"I saw the Prophet ﷺ carrying al-Hasan b. ʿAli on his shoulder, and he was saying, 'O Allah, I love him, so love him.'"],[3296,"I was with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ in one of the markets of Madinah. He departed and I departed with him. He said, \"Call al-Hasan b. Ali.\" Al-Hasan came walking with a rope around his neck. The Prophet ﷺ said, \"With his hand like this,\" and al-Hasan said, \"With his hand like this.\" He took hold of him and said, \"O Allah, I love him, so love him and love those who love him.\" Abu Hurayrah said, \"No one was more beloved to me than al-Hasan b. Ali after the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said what he said.\""],[3297,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ was leading us in prayer. Al-Hasan would come while he was small, and whenever the Messenger of Allah ﷺ prostrated, he would jump on his neck and back. The Prophet ﷺ would raise his head gently until he put him down. They said, \"O Messenger of Allah, you do something with this boy that we have never seen you do with anyone.\" He said, \"He is my sweet basil in this world. This son of mine is a master, and perhaps Allah will reconcile through him two factions of the Muslims.\""],[3298,"I was walking with al-Hasan b. Ali in the streets of Madinah, and we met Abu Hurayrah. He said to al-Hasan, \"Uncover your belly for me, may I be made your ransom, so that I may kiss where I saw the Messenger of Allah ﷺ kissing.\" He uncovered his belly and he kissed his navel."],[3299,"“I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: ‘The (funeral) prayer should be offered for a child.’” (Using translation from Ibn Mājah 1507)"],[3300,"I came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ one night for some need while he was covering something, and I did not know what it was. When I finished my need, I said, \"Who is this that you are covering?\" He uncovered ﷺ, and there were Hasan and Husayn on his thighs. He said, \"These are my two sons and the sons of my daughter. O Allah, You know that I love them, so love them.\""],[3302,"I heard Ibn Umar, and a man asked him about something. Shu'bah said: He asked him about a pilgrim in ihram killing a fly. Abdullah b. Umar said, \"They ask me about killing a fly when they have killed the son of the Messenger of Allah's daughter ﷺ. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, 'They are my sweet basil in this world.'\""],[3303,"The Prophet ﷺ was praying while al-Hasan and al-Husayn were jumping on his back, and people were pushing them away. He ﷺ said, \"Leave them, may my father and mother be their ransom. Whoever loves me, let him love these two.\""],[3305,"I was with Ibn Ziyad when the head of al-Husayn was brought. He began poking his nose with a stick and saying, \"I have never seen beauty like this.\" I said, \"Indeed, he was among those who most resembled the Messenger of Allah ﷺ.\""],[3306,"\"No one resembled the Messenger of Allah ﷺ more than al-Hasan b. Ali.\""],[3307,"\"Al-Hasan is the person most resembling the Messenger of Allah ﷺ from the chest to the head, and al-Husayn is the person most resembling the Messenger of Allah ﷺ below that.\""],[3308,"The Prophet ﷺ would stick out his tongue for al-Husayn, and the boy would see the redness of his tongue and be delighted. Uyaynah b. Badr said to him, \"Do I see him doing this to this one? By Allah, I have a son whose face has appeared and I have never kissed him.\" The Prophet ﷺ said, \"Whoever does not show mercy will not be shown mercy.\""],[3309,"I asked about Ali at his home and was told that he had gone to bring the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. Then he came, and the Messenger of Allah ﷺ entered, and I entered. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ sat on the bed, seated Fatimah on his right, Ali on his left, and Hasan and Husayn in front of him, and said, \"{Allah only desires to remove from you the impurity}, O people of the household, and to purify you thoroughly. O Allah, these are my family.\" Wathilah said, \"I said from the corner of the house, 'And I, O Messenger of Allah, am I from your family?' He said, 'And you are from my family.'\" Wathilah said, \"That is among the most hopeful things I hope for.\""],[3310,"The Prophet ﷺ said to Fatimah, al-Hasan, and al-Husayn, \"I am at war with those who fight you and at peace with those who make peace with you.\""],[3311,"We went out with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ ascending Uhud. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ went on his back to climb upon a rock, but he could not. So Talha b. Ubayd Allah knelt beneath him, and the Messenger of Allah ﷺ climbed on his back until he sat on the rock. Al-Zubayr said: I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say, “Talha has made [Paradise] incumbent.” Then the Messenger of Allah ﷺ commanded Ali b. Abi Talib ؓ, so he came to the Mihras and brought him water in his shield. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ wanted to drink from it, but he found it had a smell and disliked it, so he washed with it the blood that was on his face, saying, “Allah's wrath is severe upon the one who made the face of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ bleed.”"],[3312,"When the people were driven away from the Messenger of Allah ﷺ on the day of Uhud, I was the first to come to the Prophet ﷺ. He said: I began looking at a man in front of him fighting on his behalf and protecting him. I said: Be Talha, may my father and mother be your ransom — twice. Then I looked at a man behind me like a bird, and it was not long before he caught up with me, and it was Abu Ubayda b. al-Jarrah. We pushed on to the Prophet ﷺ, and there was Talha fallen before him. He ﷺ said, “Your brother is yours, for he has made [Paradise] incumbent.” He said: He had been struck in his forehead and his cheek, so I leaned toward the arrow in his forehead to pull it out, but Abu Ubayda said to me, “I adjure you by Allah, O Abu Bakr, to leave me.” He said: So I left him. Abu Ubayda took the arrow with his mouth and began wiggling it, disliking to hurt the Prophet ﷺ, then he extracted it with his mouth. Then I leaned toward the arrow in his cheek to pull it out, but Abu Ubayda said, “I adjure you by Allah, O Abu Bakr, to leave me.” So he took the arrow with his mouth and began wiggling it, disliking to hurt the Prophet ﷺ, then he extracted it. Talha was more severely wounded than the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and the Prophet of Allah ﷺ was more [severely wounded] than him. Talha had received thirty-some wounds, between stabs, strikes, and arrow shots."],[3313,"I saw the hand of Talha b. Ubayd Allah paralyzed, with which he shielded the Prophet ﷺ on the day of Uhud."],[3314,"Abd Allah b. al-Zubayr said to his father: O father, tell me about the Messenger of Allah ﷺ so that I may relate from you, for every son of a Companion relates from his father. He said: O my son, there is no one who accompanied the Messenger of Allah ﷺ with a companionship except that I accompanied him with the like of it or better. You know, O my son, that your mother Asma bt. Abi Bakr was my wife, and you know that A'isha bt. Abi Bakr is your maternal aunt, and you know that my mother is Safiyya bt. Abd al-Muttalib, and that my maternal uncles are Hamza b. Abd al-Muttalib, Abu Talib, and al-Abbas, and that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ is the son of my maternal uncle. You know that my paternal aunt is Khadija bt. Khuwaylid, and she was his wife, and that her daughter is Fatima bt. the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. You know that his mother ﷺ is Amina bt. Wahb b. Abd Manaf b. Zuhra, and that the mother of Safiyya and Hamza is Hala bt. Wahb b. Abd Manaf b. Zuhra. And I accompanied him with the best companionship, praise be to Allah. I heard him ﷺ say, “Whoever says about me what I did not say, let him take his seat in the Fire.”"],[3315,"The Prophet ﷺ climbed Hira with Abu Bakr, Umar, Uthman, Ali, Talha, and al-Zubayr. The mountain trembled with them, so the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, “Be still, Hira, for upon you is none but a prophet, a truthful one, or a martyr.”"],[3316,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ combined his parents for me on the day of Qurayza, saying, “May my father and mother be your ransom.”"],[3318,"One night the Messenger of Allah ﷺ was sleepless while she was beside him. She said: I said, “What is the matter with you, O Messenger of Allah?” He said, “Would that a righteous man from my Companions would guard me tonight.” She said: While we were thus, I heard the sound of weapons. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, “Who is this?” He said, “Sa'd b. Malik.” He said, “What brought you?” He said, “I came to guard you, O Messenger of Allah.” He said: Then I heard the snoring of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ in his sleep."],[3319,"I saw on the right of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and on his left on the day of Uhud two men wearing white garments, whom I had not seen before or after — meaning Gabriel and Michael."],[3320,"I did not hear the Prophet ﷺ combine his parents for anyone except Sa'd, for he said to him on the day of Uhud, “Shoot, may my father and mother be your ransom.”"],[3321,"By Allah, I am the first Arab who shot an arrow in the path of Allah. We used to raid with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ having no food to eat except leaves of the hubla and this samur tree, until one of us would defecate like a sheep defecates, with no mixture. Then the Banu Asad began disciplining me in religion. If so, I have lost and my deeds have gone astray."],[3322,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, \"O Allah, answer his prayer when he calls upon You, meaning Sa'd.\""],[3323,"We were sitting with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. He said, “A man from the people of Paradise will enter upon you from this gate.” He said: There was none of us but wished that he be from his own household. Then Sa'd b. Abi Waqqas appeared."],[3324,"Four verses were revealed concerning me. I obtained a sword and brought it to the Prophet ﷺ and said, “O Messenger of God, grant it to me as a gift.” He said, “Put it down.” Then I said, “O Messenger of God, grant it to me and consider me as one who has no need of it.” He said, “Put it back where you took it.” Then this verse was revealed: {They ask you about the spoils of war}. A man from the Ansar prepared food and invited us, and we drank wine until we became intoxicated. The Ansar and Quraysh boasted to one another. The Ansar said, “We are better than you,” and Quraysh said, “We are better.” A man from the Ansar took the jawbone of a slaughtered camel and struck Sa‘d’s nose, splitting it. Sa‘d’s nose remained split. He said: Then this verse was revealed: {Wine, gambling, stone altars, and divining arrows are only defilement from the work of Satan, so avoid it that you may succeed}. Sa‘d’s mother said, “Has God not commanded kindness? By God, I will not eat food or drink drink until I die or you disbelieve.” He said: When they wanted to feed her, they would pry open her mouth with a stick. Then this verse was revealed: {We have enjoined upon man goodness to his parents}—the verse. He said: The Messenger of God ﷺ entered upon me while I was ill, visiting me. I said, “O Messenger of God, shall I bequeath all my wealth?” He said, “No.” I said, “Then two-thirds?” He said, “No.” I said, “Then half?” He said, “No.” I said, “Then a third?” He said: Then he fell silent."],[3325,"He was in the mosque when someone mentioned ‘Ali and spoke ill of him. Sa‘id b. Zayd stood up and said, “I testify about the Messenger of God ﷺ that I heard him say: ‘Ten are in Paradise: the Prophet ﷺ is in Paradise, Abu Bakr is in Paradise, ‘Umar is in Paradise, ‘Uthman is in Paradise, ‘Ali is in Paradise, Talha b. ‘Ubayd Allah is in Paradise, al-Zubayr b. al-‘Awwam is in Paradise, Sa‘d b. Malik is in Paradise, and ‘Abd al-Rahman b. ‘Awf is in Paradise.’ If I wished, I would name the tenth.” They said, “Who is he?” He fell silent. They said, “Who is he?” He said, “Sa‘id b. Zayd.”"],[3326,"There was something between ‘Abd al-Rahman and Khalid b. al-Walid, and Khalid insulted him. The Messenger of God ﷺ said, “Do not insult any of my Companions. For if one of you were to spend the like of Mount Uhud in gold, he would not attain a mudd of one of them, nor even half of it.”"],[3327,"that Sa'eed bin Zaid bin 'Amr bin Nufail said: \"I bear witness for nine people, that they are in Paradise, and if I were to bear witness for a tenth, I would not be sinful.\" It was said: \"How is that?\" He said: \"We were with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ at (mount) Hira when he said, 'Be firm, Hira! There is not upon you any but a Prophet, or a Siddiq, or a martyr.\" It was said: \"And who were they?\" He said: \"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ, Abu Bakr, 'Umar, 'Uthman, 'Ali, Talhah, Az-Zubair, Sa'd, and 'Abdur-Rahman bin 'Awf.\" It was said: \"And who is the tenth?\" He said: \"Me.\" (Using translation from Tirmidhī 3757)"],[3328,"“Excellent man, Abu Bakr; excellent man, ‘Umar; excellent man, Abu ‘Ubayda b. al-Jarrah; excellent man, Usayd b. Hudayr; excellent man, Thabit b. Qays b. Shammas; excellent man, Mu‘adh b. ‘Amr b. al-Jamuh. Wretched man, so-and-so and so-and-so.”"],[3329,"It was said, “O Messenger of God, which of the people is most beloved to you?” He said, “‘A’isha.” It was said, “Among men?” He said, “Abu Bakr.” It was said, “Then who?” He said, “‘Umar.” It was said, “Then who?” He said, “Abu ‘Ubayda b. al-Jarrah.”"],[3330,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said to the people of Najran, “I will surely send over you a trustworthy man, truly trustworthy.” The people craned their necks for it, and he sent Abu ‘Ubayda b. al-Jarrah."],[3331,"The two bishops of Najran, al-‘Aqib and al-Sayyid, came to the Prophet ﷺ and said, “Send with us a trustworthy man, truly trustworthy.” The Messenger of God ﷺ said, “I will surely send with you a trustworthy man.” The Companions of the Messenger of God ﷺ craned their necks for it. The Messenger of God ﷺ said, “Arise, O Abu ‘Ubayda b. al-Jarrah,” and he sent him with them."],[3333,"The Prophet ﷺ said, \"Ten are in Paradise: Abu Bakr is in Paradise, Umar is in Paradise, Uthman is in Paradise, Ali is in Paradise, Zubayr is in Paradise, Talhah is in Paradise, Ibn Awf is in Paradise, Saad is in Paradise, Sa'id bin Zaid is in Paradise, and Abu Ubaidah bin al-Jarrah is in Paradise.\""],[3334,"“Sufficient for you among the women of the worlds are Maryam bt. ‘Imran, Khadija bt. Khuwaylid, Fatima bt. Muhammad, and Asiya the wife of Pharaoh.”"],[3335,"“The Messenger of God ﷺ gave Khadija glad tidings of a house in Paradise of hollow pearl, wherein there is no clamor or toil.”"],[3336,"“I was commanded to give Khadija glad tidings of a house in Paradise of hollow pearl, wherein there is no clamor or toil.”"],[3337,"When the Messenger of Allah ﷺ slaughtered a sheep, he would say: “Take this to the friends of Khadijah.” She said: One day I angered him, so he ﷺ said: “I have indeed been granted love for her.”"],[3338,"When the Prophet ﷺ was given something, he would say: “Take it to So-and-so, for she was a friend of Khadijah.”"],[3339,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to mention Khadijah frequently. I said: “Allah has replaced you with an old woman among the old women of Quraysh, red-cheeked.” His face ﷺ turned as red as I only ever saw it when revelation descended or when he saw rain clouds, until he knew whether it was mercy or punishment."],[3341,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ drew four lines on the ground and said: “Do you know what this is?” They said: “Allah and His Messenger know best.” The Messenger of Allah ﷺ then said: “The best women of Paradise are Khadijah bt. Khuwaylid, Fatimah bt. Muhammad, Maryam bt. ʿImran, and Asiyah bt. Muzahim, the wife of Pharaoh.”"],[3342,"They had promised the Messenger of Allah ﷺ to meet him the following year in Makkah, along with those of their people who followed them. The following year they set out, seventy men, among those of their people who left the land of polytheism. Kaʿb b. Malik said: When we were at the outskirts of al-Baydaʾ, al-Baraʾ b. Maʿrur b. Sakhr b. Khansaʾ, who was our elder and our chief, said: “I have formed an opinion. By Allah, I do not know whether you will agree with me or not. I have decided not to keep this structure behind me—meaning the Kaʿbah—and to pray toward it.” We said: “Do not do that. We have not heard that the Prophet of Allah ﷺ prays except toward Syria, and we would not pray toward any direction other than his.” We refused him that, and he refused us. We set out on our journey, and when prayer time came, he prayed toward the Kaʿbah while we prayed toward Syria until we arrived in Makkah. Kaʿb b. Malik said: Al-Baraʾ b. Maʿrur said to me: “By Allah, nephew, what I did on this journey has left me uneasy.” He said: We did not know the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, but we knew al-ʿAbbas b. ʿAbd al-Muttalib, who used to come to us for trade and we would see him. We went out asking about the Messenger of Allah ﷺ in Makkah until, when we were at al-Bathaʾ, we met a man and asked him about him. He said: “Do you two know him?” We said: “No, by Allah.” He said: “When you enter, look for the man sitting with al-ʿAbbas; it is he. I left him with him just now sitting.” He said: We went until we came to him ﷺ, and there he was with al-ʿAbbas. We greeted them and sat with them. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Do you know these two men, O ʿAbbas?” He said: “Yes. These are two men from the Khazraj. At that time the Ansar were called only the Aws and the Khazraj. This is al-Baraʾ b. Maʿrur, a man among the men of his people, and this is Kaʿb b. Malik.” By Allah, I will never forget the Messenger of Allah ﷺ saying: “The poet?” He said: “Yes.” Al-Baraʾ b. Maʿrur said: “O Messenger of Allah, I did something on this journey that I would like you to tell me about, for I am uneasy about it. I decided not to keep this structure behind me and prayed toward it. My companions rebuked me and opposed me, until it left me uneasy.” The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “You were upon a qiblah, had you remained steadfast upon it.” He said nothing more. He said: Then we went out to Mina and completed the pilgrimage. In the middle of the days of tashriq, we and the Messenger of Allah ﷺ agreed to meet at al-ʿAqabah. We went out in the depths of the night, slipping away from our camps and concealing it from the polytheists of our people. When we gathered at al-ʿAqabah, the Messenger of Allah ﷺ came with his uncle al-ʿAbbas b. ʿAbd al-Muttalib. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ recited the Quran to us, and we responded, believed him, trusted him, and were pleased with what he said. Then al-ʿAbbas b. ʿAbd al-Muttalib spoke and said: “O assembly of Khazraj, Muhammad is from us, as you know. We have protected him from those who are like us, and he is protected among his clan and his people.” Al-Baraʾ b. Maʿrur spoke, took the hand of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and said: “We pledge allegiance to you.” He said: “I accept your pledge that you will protect me from what you protect yourselves, your women, and your children.” He said: “Yes, by the One who sent you with the truth. By Allah, we are people of war; we have inherited it generation after generation.”"],[3343,"The Prophet ﷺ spent ten years following people in their homes during the pilgrimage season, at Majannah, ʿUkaz, and in their dwellings at Mina, saying: “Who will shelter me and support me so that I may convey the messages of my Lord, and for him is Paradise?” But he ﷺ found no one to support or shelter him, to the point that a man would travel from Egypt or Yemen to a relative, and his people would come to him and say: “Beware of the youth of Quraysh, lest he tempt you.” He would walk among their camps calling them to Allah, and they would point at him with their fingers. Until Allah sent us to him from Yathrib. A man would come to him, believe in him, and recite the Quran to him, then return to his family, and they would embrace Islam through his Islam, until there remained not a house among the houses of Yathrib but had a group of Muslims openly professing Islam. Then we consulted one another and gathered, saying: “How long will the Messenger of Allah ﷺ be driven away in the mountains of Makkah and live in fear?” So we traveled until we came to him during the pilgrimage season. He made an appointment with us at the mountain pass of al-ʿAqabah. His uncle al-ʿAbbas said: “O people of Yathrib,” so we gathered around him, one man and two. When he looked at our faces, he said: “These are people I do not know; these are young men.” We said: “O Messenger of Allah, upon what shall we pledge allegiance to you?” He said: “You pledge allegiance to me upon hearing and obedience in activity and in laziness, upon spending in hardship and ease, upon commanding good and forbidding evil, upon speaking for Allah without being deterred by any critic’s blame in Allah’s cause, and upon supporting me when I come to you and protecting me from what you protect yourselves, your wives, and your children. For you is Paradise.” We stood to pledge allegiance to him. Asʿad b. Zurarah, who was the youngest of the seventy except for me, took his hand and said: “Slowly, O people of Yathrib. We did not strike the livers of the camels to come to him except knowing that he is the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and that bringing him out today means separation from all Arabs, the killing of your best, and that the swords will bite you. If you are people who will endure it when it afflicts you, endure the killing of your best and separation from all Arabs, then take him, and your reward is with Allah. But if you fear for yourselves, then leave him, for that would be a clearer excuse before Allah.” They said: “O Asʿad, remove your hand from us. By Allah, we will not abandon this pledge nor seek to withdraw from it.” He said: We stood before him one by one. He took from us the pledge of al-ʿAbbas and guaranteed Paradise upon that."],[3344,"He informed me, saying, \"I was the leader of my father after he lost his eyesight, and he could not hear the call to Friday prayer except that he would say, 'May the mercy of Allah be upon As'ad ibn Zurarah.' I said, 'O Father, it amazes me your prayer for my father Ummamah every time you hear the call to Friday prayer.' He said, 'Oh my son, he was the first one to gather the people for Friday prayer in the city of Harrah of Bani Bayadah in a place called Al-Khadamat. I said, 'And how many were you that day?' He said, 'Forty men.'\""],[3345,"“I entered Paradise and heard a recitation. I said: ‘Who is this?’ It was said: ‘This is Harithah b. al-Nuʿman. Thus is piety, thus is piety.’”"],[3346,"“While I was walking around in Paradise, I heard the voice of a reciter. I said: ‘Who is this?’ They said: ‘Harithah b. al-Nuʿman. Thus is piety.’” He said: “He was the most dutiful of people to his mother.”"],[3347,"Umm Harithah came to the Prophet ﷺ after Harithah had perished at the Battle of Badr, struck by a stray arrow. She said, 'O Messenger of God, you know the place of Harithah in my heart. If he is in Paradise, I will not weep over him; otherwise you will see what I do.' He said to her ﷺ, 'Is it one garden? There are many gardens, and he is in the highest Firdaws.'"],[3348,"I went out with ʿUbayd Allah b. ʿAdi b. Nawfal b. ʿAbd Manaf during the time of Muʿawiyah, and we entered enemy territory with the people. When we returned, we came to Homs. Wahshi, the freedman of Jubayr b. Mutʿim, had settled and resided there. When we arrived, ʿUbayd Allah b. ʿAdi said to me: “Would you like us to go to Wahshi and ask him about Hamzah, how he killed him?” He said: We went out until we came to him. He was in the courtyard of his house on a rug, an old man. When we reached him, we greeted him. He raised his head toward ʿUbayd Allah b. ʿAdi and said: “A son of ʿAdi b. al-Khiyar?” He said: “Yes.” He said: “By Allah, I have not seen you since I handed you to your mother al-Saʿdiyyah, who nursed you, at Dhu Tuwa. I handed you to her while she was on her camel. She took you, and your feet gleamed when she lifted you up. By Allah, I only recognized her when she stood before me and I saw her.”"],[3349,"I went out with ʿUbayd Allah b. ʿAdi b. al-Khiyar to Syria. When we arrived in Homs, ʿUbayd Allah said to me: “Would you like to go to Wahshi and ask him about the killing of Hamzah?” I said: “Yes.” He said: Wahshi used to live in Homs. He said: We asked about him and were told: “He is over there in the shade of his palace, looking like a water skin.” He said: We went until we stood before him and greeted him. He returned the greeting. ʿUbayd Allah had covered his face with a turban, so Wahshi could see only his eyes and feet. ʿUbayd Allah said to him: “O Wahshi, do you recognize me?” He looked at him and said: “No, by Allah, except that I know that ʿAdi b. al-Khiyar married a woman called Umm al-Qital bt. Abi al-ʿIs, and she bore him a boy in Makkah. He sought a wet nurse for him, and I carried that boy with his mother and handed him to her. It is as if I am looking at your feet.” He said: ʿUbayd Allah uncovered his face and said: “Will you not tell us about the killing of Hamzah?” He said: “Yes. Hamzah killed Tuʿaymah b. ʿAdi b. al-Khiyar at Badr.” He said: My master Jubayr b. Mutʿim said to me: “If you kill Hamzah in revenge for my uncle, you are free.” He said: When the people set out in the year of ʿAynayn—ʿAynayn is a mountain below Uhud, with a valley between them—I went out with the people to fight. When they lined up for battle, Sibaʿ Abu Niyar came out. Hamzah b. ʿAbd al-Muttalib went out to him and said: “O Sibaʿ, O son of Umm Anmar, O son of the cutter of clitorises, do you oppose Allah and His Messenger?” He said: Then he attacked him, and he was like a bygone yesterday. He said: I hid from Hamzah until he passed by me. When he came near me, I threw my spear at him and planted it in his groin until it came out between his hips. He said: That was the last of him. When the people returned, I returned with them and stayed in Makkah until Islam spread there, then I went to al-Taʾif. He said: They sent messengers to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and it was said to him that he does not harm messengers. He said: I came with them until I reached the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. When the Messenger of Allah ﷺ saw me, he said: “Are you Wahshi?” I said: “Yes.” He said: “Are you the one who killed Hamzah?” He said: I said: “What happened has reached you.” The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Can you keep your face away from me?” He said: I left. When the Messenger of Allah ﷺ died, Musaylimah the Liar emerged. He said: I said: “I will go out against Musaylimah, perhaps I can kill him and thereby compensate for Hamzah.” He said: I went out with the people, and their affair happened as it happened. Then I saw a little man standing in a gap in a wall, looking like a dark camel; we could not see his head. He said: I threw my spear at him and planted it between his breasts until it came out between his shoulders. He said: A man from the Ansar rushed forward and struck him on the head with a sword. ʿAbd Allah b. al-Fadl said: Sulayman b. Yasar informed me that he heard ʿAbd Allah b. ʿUmar say: A slave girl on the roof said: “The Commander of the Faithful has been killed by the black slave.”"],[3350,"Food was brought to ʿAbd al-Rahman b. ʿAwf while he was fasting, and he began to weep. He said: “Hamzah was killed and only one garment could be found to shroud him. Musʿab b. ʿUmayr was killed and only one garment could be found to shroud him. I fear that the good things have been hastened for us in our worldly life.” He said: And he kept weeping."],[3351,"We came to visit Khabbab when he was ill. He said: “We emigrated with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ seeking the face of Allah, and our reward fell upon Allah. Among us are those who have passed on without consuming any of their reward. Among them is Musʿab b. ʿUmayr, who was killed on the day of Uhud and left behind a cloak. When we covered his head with it, his feet showed, and when we covered his feet, his head showed. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ ordered us to cover his head with it and put some idhkhir over his feet.”"],[3352,"My father ordered a khazira (a meat and bran dish), and it was made. Then he ordered me, and I carried it to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. I came to him while he was in his house. He said, “What is this, Jabir? Is it meat?” I said, “No, but it is khazira.” So he ordered it to be taken, and it was received. When I returned to my father, he said, “Did you see the Messenger of Allah ﷺ?” I said, “Yes.” He said, “Did he say anything?” I said, “Yes. He said, ‘What is this, Jabir? Is it meat?’” My father said, “Perhaps the Messenger of Allah ﷺ craved meat.” So he went to a domestic animal of his and slaughtered it. Then he ordered it, and it was roasted. Then he ordered me, and I carried it to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. I reached him while he was in that same gathering. He said, “What is this, Jabir?” I said, “O Messenger of Allah, I returned to my father and he said, ‘Did you see the Messenger of Allah ﷺ?’ I said, ‘Yes.’ He said, ‘Did he say anything?’ I said, ‘Yes. He said, “What is this? Is it meat?”’ My father said, ‘Perhaps the Messenger of Allah ﷺ craved meat.’ So he went to a domestic animal he had and slaughtered it. Then he ordered it, and it was roasted. Then he ordered me, and I carried it to you.” The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, “May Allah reward the Ansar well on our behalf, especially ‘Abd Allah b. ‘Amr b. Haram and Sa‘d b. ‘Ubadah.”"],[3354,"The Prophet ﷺ met me and said, “O Jabir, why do I see you broken-hearted?” I said, “O Messenger of Allah, my father was martyred and left behind dependents and debt.” He said, “Shall I give you glad tidings of how Allah met your father?” I said, “Yes, O Messenger of Allah.” He said, “Allah never spoke to anyone except from behind a veil, but Allah brought your father to life and spoke to him directly. He said, ‘O My servant, wish and I shall give you.’ He said, ‘Bring me back to life so that I may be killed a second time.’ Allah said, ‘I have decreed that they shall not return.’” And this verse was revealed: “Do not consider those who have been killed in the way of Allah as dead. Rather, they are alive with their Lord, receiving provision.”"],[3355,"My paternal uncle Anas b. al-Nadr, after whom I was named, was not present at Badr with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and this weighed heavily on him. He said, “The first battle the Messenger of Allah ﷺ witnessed, I was absent from it. By Allah, if Allah shows me a battle alongside the Messenger of Allah ﷺ in the future, Allah will see what I do.” He was afraid to say anything more. He was present with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ at Uhud the following year. Sa‘d b. Mu‘adh met him and said, “O Abu ‘Amr, where to?” He said, “Ah, the scent of Paradise! I find it before Uhud.” He fought until he was killed. More than eighty wounds were found on his body from sword strikes, spear thrusts, and arrow shots. My paternal aunt, his sister, said, “I recognized my brother only by his fingertips.” And this verse was revealed: “Among the believers are men who have been true to what they pledged to Allah. Among them are those who have fulfilled their vow, and among them are those who wait. They have not changed in the least.”"],[3356,"‘Amr b. al-Jamuh came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ on the day of Uhud and said, “O Messenger of Allah, whoever is killed today will enter Paradise?” He said, “Yes.” He said, “By the One in whose hand is my soul, I will not return to my family until I enter Paradise.” ‘Umar b. al-Khattab said to him, “O ‘Amr, do not make bold oaths regarding Allah.” The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, “Wait, O ‘Umar. Among them are those who, if they swore by Allah, He would fulfill their oath. Among them is ‘Amr b. al-Jamuh; he will wade through Paradise with his limp.”"],[3357,"I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say, while the people had fled from the Messenger of Allah ﷺ such that some of them reached beyond al-A‘rad, on a mountain near Madinah, and then returned to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ: Hanzala b. Abi ‘Amir met Abu Sufyan b. Harb. When Hanzala overpowered him, Shaddad b. al-Aswad saw him and struck Hanzala with his sword, killing him. He had almost killed Abu Sufyan. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, “Your companion Hanzala is being washed by the angels, so ask his wife.” She said, “He went out in a state of major ritual impurity when he heard the cry of battle.” The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, “That is why the angels washed him.”"],[3358,"Banu Qurayza surrendered to the judgment of Sa‘d b. Mu‘adh. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ sent for Sa‘d, and he came on a donkey. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, “Stand for your best one,” or “for your chief.” He said, “These people have surrendered to your judgment.” Sa‘d said, “I judge that their fighters be killed and their women and children taken captive.” The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, “You have judged among them with the judgment of Allah.” On another occasion he said, “You have judged with the judgment of the King.”"],[3359,"“I was the first concerning whom Saʿd judged. I was brought, and I thought he would kill me. They uncovered my pubic area and found I had not grown hair, so they put me among the captives.”"],[3360,"On the Day of the Confederates, Sa'd b. Mu'adh was shot, and they severed his median cubital vein. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ cauterized it with fire. His hand became swollen, so he left it, and the blood kept flowing. He cauterized it another time, and his hand became swollen. When he saw that, he said: 'O Allah, do not take my soul until my eye is cooled regarding Banu Qurayzah.' His vein then held fast, and not a drop fell until they surrendered to the judgment of Sa'd b. Mu'adh. He sent word concerning them, saying: 'Their men are to be killed, and their women and children are to be spared.' The Muslims took them as spoils. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: 'You have hit upon Allah's judgment concerning them.' They were four hundred. When he finished killing them, his vein burst open, and he died."],[3361,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ pitched a tent for Sa‘d b. Mu‘adh in the mosque so that he could visit him from nearby."],[3362,"I went out on the day of the Trench following the people’s traces. I heard the rumbling of the ground behind me, so I turned and saw Sa‘d b. Mu‘adh, with him his nephew al-Harith b. Aws, carrying his shield. I sat down on the ground. Sa‘d passed by wearing an armor whose edges were protruding. I feared for Sa‘d’s limbs, for he was among the greatest and tallest of people. He passed by reciting battle poetry and saying…"],[3363,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said while the funeral bier of Sa‘d b. Mu‘adh was before them, “The Throne of the Most Merciful shook for it.”"],[3364,"I heard the Prophet ﷺ saying, \"The Throne (of Allah) shook at the death of Saʿd bin Muʿadh.\" Through another group of narrators, Jabir added, \"I heard the Prophet ﷺ : saying, 'The Throne of the Beneficent shook because of the death of Saʿd bin Muʿadh.\" (Using translation from Bukhārī 3803)"],[3365,"“The Throne of the Most Merciful shook for the death of Sa‘d b. Mu‘adh.”"],[3366,"The Prophet ﷺ said while the funeral bier of Sa‘d was placed down, “The Throne of the Most Merciful shook for it.” The hypocrites began to talk about his funeral and said, “How light it is!” This reached the Prophet ﷺ, and he said, “The angels were carrying it along with them.”"],[3367,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said regarding Sa‘d, “This is the righteous man for whom the gates of heaven were opened. He was afflicted, and then relief was granted.”"],[3368,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ entered his grave—meaning Saʿd b. Muʿādh—and remained inside. When he came out, it was said, “O Messenger of Allah, what kept you?” He said, “Saʿd was squeezed in the grave with a squeeze, so I called upon Allah and He relieved him of it.”"],[3369,"The grave has a squeeze; if anyone were to escape it, Sa'd b. Mu'adh would have escaped it."],[3370,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ wore a garment of silk, and the people began touching it and marveling at it. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, “Do you marvel at it? The handkerchiefs of Saʿd b. Muʿādh in Paradise are better than it.”"],[3371,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ was brought a silk garment, and they began touching it and marveling at its softness. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, “The handkerchiefs of Saʿd b. Muʿādh in Paradise are softer than this, or better than this.”"],[3372,"I entered upon Anas b. Mālik, and he said to me, “Who are you?” I said, “I am Wāqid b. ʿAmr b. Saʿd b. Muʿādh.” He said, “You indeed resemble Saʿd.” Then he wept and wept profusely. He said, “May Allah have mercy on Saʿd. He was one of the greatest and tallest of people.” Then he said, “The Messenger of Allah ﷺ sent an army to Ukaydir of Dūmah, and he sent to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ a robe of brocade woven with gold. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ wore it, then stood on the pulpit—or sat—and did not speak. Then he descended, and the people began touching the robe and looking at it. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, ‘Do you marvel at it?’ They said, ‘We have never seen a garment more beautiful than it.’ The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, ‘The handkerchiefs of Saʿd b. Muʿādh in Paradise are more beautiful than what you see.’”"],[3373,"Ukaydir of Dūmah gifted the Messenger of Allah ﷺ a robe of fine silk, and he wore it—that was before silk was forbidden. The people marveled at its beauty, and the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, “The handkerchiefs of Saʿd b. Muʿādh in Paradise are more beautiful than it.”"],[3374,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ sent out a raiding party as scouts, appointing ʿĀṣim b. Thābit over them. They set out until, when they were partway along the route between ʿUsfān and Makkah, they halted. They were mentioned to a clan of Hudhayl called Banū Liḥyān, who pursued them with nearly a hundred archers, tracking their traces until they reached a place where they had stopped and found date stones from the dates of Madinah. It was said, “This is from the dates of the people of Yathrib,” and they followed their traces until they caught up with them. When ʿĀṣim b. Thābit and his companions sensed them, they took refuge on a high rocky hill, and the people came and surrounded them. They said, “You have a covenant and a solemn promise: if you come down to us, we will not kill any man among you.” ʿĀṣim said, “As for me, I will not descend under the protection of a disbelieving people. O Allah, inform Your Messenger about us.” They fought them from their positions until they killed ʿĀṣim along with seven men. Khubayb b. ʿAdī, Zayd b. al-Dathinah, and another man remained. They gave them a covenant and a solemn promise to come down to them. When they had them in their power, they untied the strings of their bows and bound them with them. The third man who was with them cried out, “This is the first treachery!” and refused to accompany them. They dragged him, but he refused to follow them and said, “I have an example in these,” so they struck his neck. They took Khubayb b. ʿAdī and Zayd b. al-Dathinah and sold them in Makkah. Khubayb was bought by the Banū al-Ḥārith b. ʿĀmir—and al-Ḥārith had been killed at Badr. He remained with them as a prisoner until, when they agreed to kill him, he borrowed a razor from one of the daughters of al-Ḥārith to shave his pubic hair, and she lent it to him. She said, “I was heedless of a young son of mine until he went to him and took him and laid him on his thigh while the razor was in his hand. When I saw him, I was terrified with a great terror. He said, ‘Did you fear that I would kill him? I would not do that, if Allah wills.’” She said, “I have never seen a prisoner better than Khubayb. I saw him eating from a bunch of grapes while Makkah had no fruit that day, and he was bound in iron. It was nothing but provision Allah granted him.” Then they brought him out of the sanctuary to kill him. He said, “Let me pray two rakʿahs,” and he prayed two rakʿahs. Then he said, “Were it not that you would think that what is in me is dread of death, I would have added more.” He was the first to establish the two rakʿahs at the time of execution. Then he said:"],[3375,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ entered upon Abū Salamah, whose eyes were fixed open. He closed them and said, “When the soul is taken, the eyesight follows it.” Some of his family cried out, and he said, “Do not supplicate against yourselves except for good, for the angels say āmīn to what you say.” Then he said, “O Allah, forgive Abū Salamah, raise his rank among those brought near, make his descendants successors among those who remain, and forgive him and us, O Lord of the worlds. O Allah, make his grave spacious for him and fill it with light for him.”"],[3376,"“We used to call him only Zayd b. Muḥammad until the Qurʾān came down: ‘Call them by their fathers; that is more just in the sight of Allah.’”"],[3377,"“ʿUmar allotted to Usāmah b. Zayd more than he allotted to me.” I said, “My emigration and Usāmah’s emigration are one and the same.” He said, “His father was dearer to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ than your father, and he was dearer to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ than you, and it was your parents who emigrated with you.”"],[3378,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ sent out a military expedition and appointed Usāmah b. Zayd over them. Some people criticized his leadership, so the Messenger of Allah ﷺ stood up and said, “If you criticize his leadership, you used to criticize his father’s leadership before. By Allah, he was indeed worthy of leadership, and he was one of the most beloved of people to me, and this one is one of the most beloved of people to me after him.”"],[3379,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to Ja'far: \"You resemble my physical appearance and my character.\""],[3380,"\"Ja'far was shown to me as an angel flying with his two wings in Paradise.\""],[3381,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ dispatched the army of commanders. He said: \"Zayd b. Harithah is over you. If Zayd is struck, then Ja'far; if Ja'far is struck, then 'Abdullah b. Rawahah.\" So Ja'far jumped up and said: \"May my father and mother be your ransom, O Messenger of Allah! I was not reluctant that you appoint Zayd over me.\" He said: \"Go, for you do not know in which of that is good.\" So they set off and remained as long as Allah willed. Then the Messenger of Allah ﷺ ascended the pulpit and ordered that it be announced: \"Prayer is to be performed in congregation.\" He said: \"Shall I not inform you about this expedition of yours that has gone forth? They set off and met the enemy. Zayd was struck as a martyr. Seek forgiveness for him.\" The people sought forgiveness for him. \"Then Ja'far b. Abi Talib took the banner and pressed upon the people until he was killed as a martyr. Seek forgiveness for him. Then 'Abdullah b. Rawahah took the banner, and his feet were firm until he was killed as a martyr. Seek forgiveness for him. Then Khalid b. al-Walid took the banner, and he was not one of the commanders; he appointed himself.\" Then the Messenger of Allah ﷺ raised his upper arms and said: \"O Allah, he is a sword among Your swords; give victory through him.\" From that day on, Khalid b. al-Walid was called the Sword of Allah."],[3382,"I witnessed with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ on the day of Hunayn, and indeed I saw the Messenger of Allah ﷺ while with him was only me and Abu Sufyan b. al-Harith b. 'Abd al-Muttalib. We stayed close to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and did not part from him. He was on a gray mule (and perhaps he said: white) that Farwah b. Nufathah al-Judhami had gifted to him. When the Muslims and the disbelievers met, the Muslims turned back in retreat, and the Messenger of Allah ﷺ began spurring his mule toward the disbelievers. Al-'Abbas said: I was holding the bridle of the mule of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, restraining it, while he did not slacken in hurrying toward the polytheists, and Abu Sufyan b. al-Harith was holding the stirrup strap of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"O 'Abbas, call: 'O companions of the samurah tree! (the tree under which the pledge of Ridwan was taken)'\" I was a man with a loud voice, and I said at the top of my voice: \"O companions of the samurah tree!\" By Allah, it was as if their turning when they heard my voice was the turning of a cow toward its calves, saying: \"Here we are, here we are.\" The Muslims came back and fought the disbelievers. The Ansar called out: \"O assembly of the Ansar!\" Then the call was restricted to the tribe of Banu al-Harith b. al-Khazraj, and they called: \"O Banu al-Harith b. al-Khazraj!\" He said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ looked while he was on his mule as if leaning over it toward their fighting. Then the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"This is the time when the battle has grown hot.\" Then the Messenger of Allah ﷺ took some pebbles and threw them at the faces of the disbelievers and said: \"They have been defeated, by the Lord of the Ka'bah! They have been defeated, by the Lord of the Ka'bah!\" He said: I went to look, and the fighting was as it had been as far as I could see. By Allah, it was only that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ threw his pebbles at them, and I saw their force only dwindling, and their affair only in retreat, until Allah defeated them. He said: It is as if I am looking at the Prophet ﷺ spurring after them on his mule."],[3383,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, \"Indeed, the greatest charity a person can give is to support his parents.\""],[3384,"When the Ka'bah was built, the Prophet ﷺ and al-'Abbas went to carry stones. Al-'Abbas said to the Prophet ﷺ: \"Put your izār on your neck.\" He did so, but he fell to the ground and his eyes turned toward the sky. Then he stood and said: \"My izār, my izār.\" So he tightened his izār on him."],[3385,"While the Messenger of Allah ﷺ was equipping an expedition in the place of today's suq al-nakhkhasin (slave market), al-'Abbas b. 'Abd al-Muttalib appeared. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"Al-'Abbas is the paternal uncle of your Prophet, the most generous of Quraysh in hand and the most mindful of kinship ties.\""],[3386,"The Prophet ﷺ went to relieve himself, and I placed water for his ablution. When he came out, he said: \"Who placed this?\" They said: Ibn 'Abbas. He said: \"O Allah, grant him understanding in religion.\""],[3387,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ embraced me and said: \"O Allah, teach him the wisdom.\""],[3388,"I was in the house of Maymunah bint al-Harith and placed for the Messenger of Allah ﷺ water for purification. He said: \"Who placed this?\" Maymunah said: 'Abdullah. He ﷺ said: \"O Allah, grant him understanding in religion and teach him the interpretation.\""],[3389,"Usamah b. Zayd stumbled at the threshold of the door and his face was wounded. The Prophet ﷺ said to 'A'ishah: \"Remove the harm from him.\" But she was disgusted by it. She said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ began to suck it out and say: \"If Usamah were a girl, I would have adorned him and clothed him until I made him desirable.\""],[3390,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ entered upon me happy and said: \"O 'A'ishah, did you not see that Mujazziz al-Mudliji entered upon me?\" He saw Usamah and Zayd with a velvet covering over them, their heads covered and their feet visible. He said: \"These feet are from one another.\""],[3391,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ wanted to wipe the mucus of Usamah b. Zayd, so 'A'ishah said: \"Let me be the one to do it.\" He said: \"O 'A'ishah, love him, for I love him.\""],[3392,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ appointed Usama b. Zayd over a people, and they criticized his command. So he ﷺ said: “If you criticize his command, you have criticized the command of his father before him. By Allah, he was indeed worthy of command, and he was among the most beloved of people to me, and this one is among the most beloved of people to me after him.”"],[3393,"Ali proposed to the daughter of Abu Jahl and arranged the marriage. Fatima came to the Prophet ﷺ and said: “Your people are saying that you do not get angry for your daughters, and Ali has proposed to the daughter of Abu Jahl.” The Prophet ﷺ said: “Fatima is a part of me, and I dislike what displeases her.” He mentioned Abu al-As b. al-Rabi and praised him well, and said: “The daughter of Allah’s Prophet and the daughter of Allah’s enemy shall not be joined together.”"],[3395,"“I saw myself as the sixth of six, when there was no Muslim on earth besides us.”"],[3396,"We said to Hudhayfa b. al-Yaman: “Tell us of a man close in guidance and manner to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ from whom we can take.” He said: “I do not know anyone closer in manner, guidance, and bearing to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ than Ibn Umm Abd, until the wall of his house hides him. And the preserved ones among the Companions of Muhammad ﷺ know that Ibn Umm Abd is among the closest of them to Allah as a means.”"],[3397,"I have read seventy or so surahs on the Messenger of Allah ﷺ , and indeed Zaid has two fosterings to play with the boys."],[3398,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to me: “Recite Surat al-Nisa to me.” I recited until I reached: {So how will it be when We bring from every nation a witness and bring you as a witness against these?} He said: either he nudged me or I turned, and behold his eyes were flowing with tears ﷺ."],[3399,"Abu Bakr and Umar, ؓ , gave him the good news that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Whoever would like to recite the Qur’an fresh as it was revealed, let him recite it according to the recitation of Ibn Umm Abd.”"],[3400,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ passed between Abu Bakr and Umar ؓ while Abdullah was praying, and he began with Surat al-Nisa and recited it fluently. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Whoever would like to recite the Qur’an fresh as it was revealed, let him recite it according to the recitation of Ibn Umm Abd.” Then he sat down and asked, and the Messenger of Allah ﷺ kept saying: “Ask and you will be given it. Ask and you will be given it.” Among what he said was: “O Allah, I ask You for faith that does not turn back, bliss that does not run out, and the companionship of our Prophet Muhammad in the highest Garden of Eternity.” Umar came to Abdullah to give him the good news and found that Abu Bakr had preceded him. He said: “If you did that, you are indeed foremost in good.”"],[3401,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to me: “Your permission with me is that the curtain be raised and that you hear my whispering until I forbid you.”"],[3402,"Abdullah b. Masud used to cut siwak for the Messenger of Allah ﷺ from arak trees, and his legs were thin. The people laughed, so the Prophet ﷺ said: “What makes you laugh at the thinness of his legs? By the One in whose hand is my soul, they are heavier in the Balance than Mount Uhud.”"],[3403,"During the life of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, when a man saw a dream he would relate it to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. I was a young unmarried boy and used to sleep in the mosque. I saw in my sleep as if two angels took me and went with me to the Fire, and behold it was folded like the folding of a well, and it had two horns, and in it were people whom I recognized. I began to say: “I seek refuge in Allah from the Fire,” twice. Then another angel met them and said to me: “You will not be frightened.” I related it to Hafsa, and Hafsa related it to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. He ﷺ said: “What a good man Abdullah b. Umar is, except that he does not pray at night except a little.”"],[3404,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ prayed Zuhr or 'Asr with us and said the salutation after two rak'ahs of one of them. Dhu al-Shimalayn b. 'Abd 'Amr b. Nadlah al-Khuza'i, the ally of Banu Zuhrah, said to him: 'Has the prayer been shortened or did you forget, O Messenger of Allah?' The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: 'I did not forget, nor has it been shortened.' Dhu al-Shimalayn said: 'Some of that happened, O Messenger of Allah.' The Messenger of Allah ﷺ turned to the people and said: 'Has Dhu al-Yadayn spoken the truth?' They said: 'Yes, O Messenger of Allah.' The Messenger of Allah ﷺ stood and completed the prayer."],[3405,"I saw in my sleep a piece of silk, and I did not desire with it any place in Paradise but it flew with me to it. I related it to Hafsa, and Hafsa related it to the Prophet ﷺ. He ﷺ said: “Indeed your brother is a righteous man,” or he said: “Indeed Abdullah is a righteous man.”"],[3406,"We were with the Prophet ﷺ on a journey, and I was on a difficult young camel belonging to Umar. It would overcome me and go ahead of the people, and Umar would shout at it and bring it back. Then it would go ahead, and Umar would shout at it and bring it back. The Prophet ﷺ said to Umar: “Sell it to me.” He said: “It is yours, O Messenger of Allah.” He said: “Sell it to me.” So he sold it to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. Then the Prophet ﷺ said: “It is yours, O Abdullah b. Umar, so do with it whatever you wish.” *"],[3407,"Ibn Umar used to follow the traces of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and every place where the Messenger of Allah ﷺ stopped, he would stop there too. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ once stopped under a samura tree, and Ibn Umar would bring water and pour it at the base of the samura tree so that it would not dry out."],[3408,"We were sitting with the Prophet ﷺ when Ammar came asking for permission. He ﷺ said: \"Give him permission; welcome to the good one, the purified one.\""],[3409,"Ammar sought permission to enter upon Ali, ؓ . He said: \"Welcome to the good one, the purified one. I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: 'Ammar is filled with faith up to his very bones'—meaning his innermost being.\""],[3410,"\"The transgressing party will kill Ammar.\""],[3411,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, \"Woe to Ibn Sumayyah, he will be killed by a rebellious group. He will invite them to Paradise while they invite him to the Fire.\""],[3412,"\"Rana came and took off his cloak, then sat down and started narrating to us until he mentioned the construction of the mosque. He said, 'We were carrying one brick each, while the builders carried two bricks each.' The Prophet ﷺ saw him and started shaking the dust off his head, saying, 'O Ammar, why don't you carry what your companions are carrying?' Ammar replied, 'I seek the reward from Allah.' The Prophet then shook the dust off him and said, 'Woe to Ammar! A rebellious group will kill him, inviting him to Paradise while he invites them to Hell.' Ammar said, 'I seek refuge with Allah from trials and tribulations.'\""],[3413,"I saw Ammar ibn Yasir on the day of Siffin: an old man, dark-skinned, tall, holding the spear in his hand while his hand trembled. He said: \"By the One in whose hand is my soul, I have fought with this banner alongside the Messenger of Allah ﷺ three times, and this is the fourth. By the One in whose hand is my soul, if they were to strike us until we reach the palm fronds of Hajar, we would know that our righteous ones are upon the truth and that they are upon falsehood.\""],[3414,"There was an exchange of words between me and Ammar ibn Yasir, so Ammar went to complain to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. Khalid kept increasing in harshness toward him while the Messenger of Allah ﷺ remained silent. Then Ammar wept and said: \"O Messenger of Allah, will you not listen to him?\" The Messenger of Allah ﷺ raised his head toward me and said: \"Whoever shows enmity to Ammar, Allah shows enmity to him; and whoever hates him, Allah hates him.\" So I went out, and nothing became dearer to me than the approval of Ammar. I met him and he was pleased."],[3416,"\"The first to openly profess Islam were seven: the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, Abu Bakr, Ammar and his mother Sumayya, Suhayb, Bilal, and al-Miqdad. As for the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, Allah protected him through his uncle Abu Talib. As for Abu Bakr, Allah protected him through his people. As for the rest, the polytheists seized them, put iron coats of mail on them, and exposed them to the heat of the sun. None of them gave in except Bilal, for his soul became insignificant to him for the sake of Allah, and he became insignificant to his people. They took him and handed him over to the children, who dragged him around the mountain passes of Makkah while he kept saying: 'One, One.'\""],[3417,"\"I was admitted into Paradise and heard a rustling sound ahead of me. I asked, 'Who is this?' He said: 'Jibril, ﷺ , said: This is Bilal.'\""],[3418,"I said to Abu Usamah, \"Shall I inform you about the most hopeful deed that Abu Hayyan narrated from Abu Zur'ah, from Abu Hurairah, who said that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to Bilal during the Fajr prayer: 'O Bilal, tell me of the most hopeful deed that you have done in Islam, for I heard a rustling of your sandals before me in front of Paradise tonight.' Bilal said, 'The most hopeful deed that I have done is that whenever I have performed ablution in a complete and perfect manner, at any hour of the day or night, I have prayed to my Lord as much as He has decreed for me to pray.'\""],[3419,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, \"I did not enter Paradise except that I heard a rustling sound. So I asked, 'Who is this?' They said, 'Bilal.' Then I passed by a beautifully constructed palace and asked, 'Whose is this?' They said, 'A man from the nation of Muhammad ﷺ .' So I asked, 'Am I Muhammad? Whose palace is this?' They said, 'It belongs to a man from the Arabs.' So I asked, 'Am I an Arab? Whose palace is this?' They said, 'It belongs to Umar ibn Al-Khattab.' Then Umar said to Bilal, 'By what did you surpass me to Paradise?' Bilal replied, 'I did not do anything except that I performed ablution and I did not perform ablution except that I prayed.' Umar said to the Messenger of Allah, 'If not for your jealousy, I would have entered the palace.' The Messenger of Allah said, 'O Umar, I could not bear to see you in a state of distress.'\""],[3420,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ heard a rustling sound ahead of him and said: \"Who is this?\" They said: \"Bilal.\" He informed him and said: \"By what have you preceded me to Paradise?\" Bilal said: \"O Messenger of Allah, I never perform ablution except that I pray two rak'ahs, and I never perform ablution except that I consider that Allah has a right over me to pray them.\" He ﷺ said: \"By that.\""],[3421,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ ordered the killing of the captives of Badr, so they were dragged to the well and thrown into it. Then he came and stood beside them, and said, \"O people of the well, have you found what your Lord promised you to be true? For I have found what my Lord promised me to be true.\" They said, \"O Messenger of Allah, are you speaking to dead people?\" He said, \"They have indeed known that what I promised them is true.\" When Abu Hudhayfah bin 'Utbah saw his father being dragged to the well, the Messenger of Allah ﷺ noticed the repulsion in his face, so he said, \"You seem to dislike what you see.\" Abu Hudhayfah said, \"O Messenger of Allah, my father was a noble and patient man, and I had hoped that Allah would guide him to Islam. When he was in the position he is now, it saddened me. So the Messenger of Allah ﷺ prayed for Abu Hudhayfah with goodness.\""],[3422,"\"Khalid bin Al-Walid had wielded in my hand on the day of Mu'tah nine swords, and there remained in my hand only a Yemeni metal plate.\""],[3423,"\"Fasting is a shield.\""],[3424,"Abdul Rahman ibn Auf complained to the Messenger of Allah PBUH about the harm caused by Khalid ibn Walid to a man from the people of Badr. The Messenger of Allah PBUH said, \"O Khalid, why do you harm a man from the people of Badr? If you were to spend the equivalent of Uhud in gold, you would not be able to attain his status.\" Khalid replied, \"O Messenger of Allah, they attack me and I respond to them.\" The Messenger of Allah PBUH said, \"Do not harm Khalid, for he is a sword from the swords of Allah whom Allah sends upon the disbelievers.\""],[3425,"I heard Amr ibn al-As say, \"The people panicked in Medina with the Prophet ﷺ, so they scattered. I saw Salim, the servant of Abu Hudhayfah, grab his sword and sit in the mosque. When I saw that, I did the same thing. Then the Messenger of Allah ﷺ came out and saw me and Salim as we were, and he came to the people and said, 'O people, wasn't your panic supposed to be towards Allah and His Messenger? Didn't you act like these two believers did?'\""],[3426,"Messenger of Allah ﷺ said (to me), \"You have been shown to me twice in (my) dreams. A man was carrying you in a silken cloth and said to me, 'This is your wife.' I uncovered it; and behold, it was you. I said to myself, 'If this dream is from Allah, He will cause it to come true.' \" (Using translation from Bukhārī 5078)"],[3427,"Gabriel ﷺ came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ wrapped in a silk garment and said, \"This is your wife in this life and the hereafter.\""],[3428,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ mentioned Fatimah and she said, \"I spoke and said, 'Would you not be pleased for me to be your wife in this life and the hereafter?' I said, 'Yes, by Allah.'\" He said, \"Then you are my wife in this life and the hereafter.\""],[3429,"She said, \"O Messenger of Allah, who are your wives in Paradise?\" He said, \"As for you, you are one of them.\" She then thought to herself that he had not married a virgin other than herself."],[3430,"\"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ married me when I was six years old, and he consummated the marriage with me when I was nine years old. He came to Madinah while I was ill, and my hair had grown long. Umm Ruman came to me while I was on a swing, and I had some friends with me. She called out to me, and I went to her, not knowing what she wanted. She took me by the hand and made me stand at the door. I said, 'Hah, hah,' like one out of breath. She brought me into a house where there were some women of the Ansar. They said: 'Upon goodness and blessing, and upon the best of fortune.' She handed me over to them, and they washed my head and prepared me. Nothing startled me except the Messenger of Allah ﷺ coming in the forenoon, and they handed me over to him.\""],[3431,"that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"O 'Aishah! Here is Jibril and he is giving Salam to you.\" She said: \"I said: 'And upon him be peace and the mercy of Allah, and His blessings. You see that which we do not.'\" (Using translation from Tirmidhī 3881)"],[3432,"(the wife of the Prophet) \"Whenever Messenger of Allah ﷺ intended to go on a journey, he would draw lots amongst his wives and would take with him the one upon whom the lot fell. During a Ghazwa of his, he drew lots amongst us and the lot fell upon me, and I proceeded with him after Allah had decreed the use of the veil by women. I was carried in a Howdah (on the camel) and dismounted while still in it. When Messenger of Allah ﷺ was through with his Ghazwa and returned home, and we approached the city of Medina, Messenger of Allah ﷺ ordered us to proceed at night. When the order of setting off was given, I walked till I was past the army to answer the call of nature. After finishing I returned (to the camp) to depart (with the others) and suddenly realized that my necklace over my chest was missing. So, I returned to look for it and was delayed because of that. The people who used to carry me on the camel, came to my Howdah and put it on the back of the camel, thinking that I was in it, as, at that time, women were light in weight, and thin and lean, and did not use to eat much. So, those people did not feel the difference in the heaviness of the Howdah while lifting it, and they put it over the camel. At that time I was a young lady. They set the camel moving and proceeded on. I found my necklace after the army had gone, and came to their camp to find nobody. So, I went to the place where I used to stay, thinking that they would discover my absence and come back in my search. While in that state, I felt sleepy and slept. Safwan bin Mu'attal As-Sulami Adh-Dhakwani was behind the army and reached my abode in the morning. When he saw a sleeping person, he came to me, and he used to see me before veiling. So, I got up when I heard him saying, \"Inna lil-lah-wa inn a ilaihi rajiun (We are for Allah, and we will return to Him).\" He made his camel knell down. He got down from his camel, and put his leg on the front legs of the camel and then I rode and sat over it. Safwan set out walking, leading the camel by the rope till we reached the army who had halted to take rest at midday. Then whoever was meant for destruction, fell into destruction, (some people accused me falsely) and the leader of the false accusers was ʿAbdullah bin Ubai bin Salul. After that we returned to Medina, and I became ill for one month while the people were spreading the forged statements of the false accusers. I was feeling during my ailment as if I were not receiving the usual kindness from the Prophet ﷺ which I used to receive from him when I got sick. But he would come, greet and say, 'How is that (girl)?' I did not know anything of what was going on till I recovered from my ailment and went out with Um Mistah to the Manasi where we used to answer the call of nature, and we used not to go to answer the call of nature except from night to night and that was before we had lavatories near to our houses. And this habit of ours was similar to the habit of the old 'Arabs in the open country (or away from houses). So. I and Um Mistah bint Ruhm went out walking. Um Mistah stumbled because of her long dress and on that she said, 'Let Mistah be ruined.' I said, 'You are saying a bad word. Why are you abusing a man who took part in (the battle of) Badr?' She said, 'O Hanata (you there) didn't you hear what they said?' Then she told me the rumors of the false accusers. My sickness was aggravated, and when I returned home, Messenger of Allah ﷺ came to me, and after greeting he said, 'How is that (girl)?' I requested him to allow me to go to my parents. I wanted then to be sure of the news through them I Messenger of Allah ﷺ allowed me, and I went to my parents and asked my mother, 'What are the people talking about?' She said, 'O my daughter! Don't worry much about this matter. By Allah, never is there a charming woman loved by her husband who has other wives, but the women would forge false news about her.' I said, 'Glorified be Allah! Are the people really taking of this matter?' That night I kept on weeping and could not sleep till morning. In the morning Messenger of Allah ﷺ called ʿAli bin Abu Talib and Usama bin Zaid when he saw the Divine Inspiration delayed, to consul them about divorcing his wife (i.e. ʿAisha). Usama bin Zaid said what he knew of the good reputation of his wives and added, 'O Messenger of Allah ﷺ! Keep you wife, for, by Allah, we know nothing about her but good.' ʿAli bin Abu Talib said, 'O Messenger of Allah ﷺ! Allah has no imposed restrictions on you, and there are many women other than she, yet you may ask the woman-servant who will tell you the truth.' On that Messenger of Allah ﷺ called Barirah and said, 'O Barirah. Did you ever see anything which roused your suspicions about her?' Barirah said, 'No, by Allah Who has sent you with the Truth, I have never seen in her anything faulty except that she is a girl of immature age, who sometimes sleeps and leaves the dough for the goats to eat.' On that day Messenger of Allah ﷺ ascended the pulpit and requested that somebody support him in punishing ʿAbdullah bin Ubai bin Salul. Allah's Apostle said, 'Who will support me to punish that person (ʿAbdullah bin Ubai bin Salul) who has hurt me by slandering the reputation of my family? By Allah, I know nothing about my family but good, and they have accused a person about whom I know nothing except good, and he never entered my house except in my company.' Saʿd bin Muʿadh got up and said, 'O Messenger of Allah ﷺ! by Allah, I will relieve you from him. If that man is from the tribe of the Aus, then we will chop his head off, and if he is from our brothers, the Khazraj, then order us, and we will fulfill your order.' On that Saʿd bin 'Ubada, the chief of the Khazraj and before this incident, he had been a pious man, got up, motivated by his zeal for his tribe and said, 'By Allah, you have told a lie; you cannot kill him, and you will never be able to kill him.' On that Usaid bin Al-Hadir got up and said (to Saʿd bin 'Ubada), 'By Allah! you are a liar. By Allah, we will kill him; and you are a hypocrite, defending the hypocrites.' On this the two tribes of Aus and Khazraj got excited and were about to fight each other, while Messenger of Allah ﷺ was standing on the pulpit. He got down and quieted them till they became silent and he kept quiet. On that day I kept on weeping so much so that neither did my tears stop, nor could I sleep. In the morning my parents were with me and I had wept for two nights and a day, till I thought my liver would burst from weeping. While they were sitting with me and I was weeping, an Ansari woman asked my permission to enter, and I allowed her to come in. She sat down and started weeping with me. While we were in this state, Messenger of Allah ﷺ came and sat down and he had never sat with me since the day they forged the accusation. No revelation regarding my case came to him for a month. He recited Tashah-hud (i.e. None has the right to be worshipped but Allah and Muhammad is His Apostle) and then said, 'O ʿAisha! I have been informed such-and-such about you; if you are innocent, then Allah will soon reveal your innocence, and if you have committed a sin, then repent to Allah and ask Him to forgive you, for when a person confesses his sin and asks Allah for forgiveness, Allah accepts his repentance.' When Messenger of Allah ﷺ finished his speech my tears ceased completely and there remained not even a single drop of it. I requested my father to reply to Messenger of Allah ﷺ on my behalf. My father said, By Allah, I do not know what to say to Messenger of Allah ﷺ.' I said to my mother, 'Talk to Messenger of Allah ﷺ on my behalf.' She said, 'By Allah, I do not know what to say to Allah's Apostle. I was a young girl and did not have much knowledge of the Qur'an. I said. 'I know, by Allah, that you have listened to what people are saying and that has been planted in your minds and you have taken it as a truth. Now, if I told you that I am innocent and Allah knows that I am innocent, you would not believe me and if I confessed to you falsely that I am guilty, and Allah knows that I am innocent you would believe me. By Allah, I don't compare my situation with you except to the situation of Joseph's father (i.e. Jacob) who said, 'So (for me) patience is most fitting against that which you assert and it is Allah (Alone) whose help can be sought.' Then I turned to the other side of my bed hoping that Allah would prove my innocence. By Allah I never thought that Allah would reveal Divine Inspiration in my case, as I considered myself too inferior to be talked of in the Holy Qur'an. I had hoped that Messenger of Allah ﷺ might have a dream in which Allah would prove my innocence. By Allah, Allah's Apostle had not got up and nobody had left the house before the Divine Inspiration came to Allah's Apostle. So, there overtook him the same state which used to overtake him, (when he used to have, on being inspired divinely). He was sweating so much so that the drops of the sweat were dropping like pearls though it was a (cold) wintry day. When that state of Messenger of Allah ﷺ was over, he was smiling and the first word he said, ʿAisha! Thank Allah, for Allah has declared your innocence.' My mother told me to go to Messenger of Allah ﷺ . I replied, 'By Allah I will not go to him and will not thank but Allah.' So Allah revealed: \"Verily! They who spread the slander are a gang among you . . .\" (24.11) When Allah gave the declaration of my Innocence, Abu Bakr, who used to provide for Mistah bin Uthatha for he was his relative, said, 'By Allah, I will never provide Mistah with anything because of what he said about Aisha.' But Allah later revealed: -- \"And let not those who are good and wealthy among you swear not to help their kinsmen, those in need and those who left their homes in Allah's Cause. Let them forgive and overlook. Do you not wish that Allah should forgive you? Verily! Allah is Oft-forgiving, Most Merciful.\" (24.22) After that Abu Bakr said, 'Yes ! By Allah! I like that Allah should forgive me,' and resumed helping Mistah whom he used to help before. Messenger of Allah ﷺ also asked Zainab bint Jahsh (i.e. the Prophet's wife about me saying, 'What do you know and what did you see?' She replied, 'O Messenger of Allah ﷺ! I refrain to claim hearing or seeing what I have not heard or seen. By Allah, I know nothing except goodness about Aisha.\" Aisha further added \"Zainab was competing with me (in her beauty and the Prophet's love), yet Allah protected her (from being malicious), for she had piety.\" (Using translation from Bukhārī 2661)"],[3433,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, \"Rejoice, for Allah has granted you an excuse.\" I said, \"Praise be to Allah, not to you.\""],[3434,"I asked Umm Romān, who is Umm Aisha, the mother of the believers, or it was said to her, \"What Allah has revealed as an excuse for her,\" meaning Aisha. She said, \"While I was with Aisha, a woman from the Ansar entered upon us and she was saying, 'Allah has done such and such with so and so.' Aisha said, 'Why did she say this?' I said, 'Because he was one of the people who narrated the Hadith.' Aisha said, 'Which Hadith?' So I informed her. She said, 'And the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and Abu Bakr heard it?' I said, 'Yes.' So she fainted and did not regain consciousness except with a high fever. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ came and said, 'What is this?' She said, 'We told him about the fever that took hold of her.' He said, 'Perhaps it is because of the Hadith that she narrated.' She said, 'She sat down and said, 'By Allah, if I swear to you, you will not believe me, and if I apologize, you will not accept my apology.' She said, 'My example and your example is like the example of Yaqub and his sons. And Allah is the one whose help is sought against what you describe.' She said, 'And Allah revealed what He revealed to him, so he informed her. She said, 'Praise be to Allah, not to anyone else.'\""],[3435,"My husband is a sort of the meat of a lean camel placed at the top of a hill, which it is difficult to climb up, nor (the meat) is good enough that one finds in oneself the urge to take it away (from the top of that mountain). The second one said: My husband (is so bad) that I am afraid I would not be able to describe his faults-both visible and invisible completely. The third one said: My husband is a long-statured fellow (i. e. he lacks intelligence). If I give vent to my feelings about him, he would divorce me, and if I keep quiet I would be made to live in a state of suspense (neither completely abandoned by him nor entertained as wife). The fourth one said: My husband is like the night of Tihama (the night of Hijaz and Mecca), neither too cold nor hot, neither there is any fear of him nor grief. The fifth one said: My husband is (like) a leopard as he enters the house, and behaves like a lion when he gets out, and he does not ask about that which he leaves in the house. The sixth one said: So far as my husband is concerned, he eats so much that nothing is left back and when he drinks he drinks that no drop is left behind. And when he lies down he wraps his body and does not touch me so that he may know my grief. The seventh one said: My husband is heavy in spirit, having no brightness in him, impotent, suffering from all kinds of conceivable diseases, heaving such rough manners that he may break my head or wound my body, or may do both. The eighth one said: My husband is as sweet as the sweet-smelling plant, and as soft as the softness of the hare. The ninth one said: My husband is the master of a lofty building, long-statured, having heaps of ashes (at his door) and his house is near the meeting place and the inn. The tenth one said: My husband is Malik, and how fine Malik is, much above appreciation and praise (of mine). He has many folds of his camel, more in number than the pastures for them. When they (the camels) hear the sound of music they become sure that they are going to be slaughtered. The eleventh one said: My husband is Abu Zara'. How fine Abu Zara' is! He has suspended in my ears heavy ornaments and (fed me liberally) that my sinews and bones are covered with fat. So he made me happy. He found me among the shepherds living in the side of the mountain, and he made me the owner of the horses, camels and lands and heaps of grain and he finds no fault with me. I sleep and get up in the morning (at my own sweet will) and drink to my heart's content. The mother of Abu Zara', how fine is the mother of Abu Zara'! Her bundles are heavily packed (or receptacles in her house are filled to the brim) and the house quite spacious. So far as the son of Abu Zara' is concerned, his bed is as soft as a green palm-stick drawn forth from its bark, or like a sword drawn forth from its scabbard, and whom just an arm of a lamb is enough to satiate. So far as the daughter of Abu Zara' is concerned, how fine is the daughter of Abu Zara', obedient to her father, obedient to her mother, wearing sufficient flesh and a source of jealousy for her co-wife. As for the slave-girl of Abu Zara', how fine is she; she does not disclose our affairs to others (outside the four walls of the house). She does not remove our wheat, or provision, or take it forth, or squander it, but she preserves it faithfully (as a sacred trust). And she does not let the house fill with rubbish. One day Abu Zara' went out (of his house) when the milk was churned in the vessels, that he met a woman, having two children like leopards playing with her pomegranates (chest) under her vest. He divorced me (Umm Zara') and married that woman (whom Abu Zara') met on the way. I (Umm Zara') later on married another person, a chief, who was an expert rider, and a fine archer: he bestowed upon me many gifts and gave me one pair of every kind of animal and said: Umm Zara', make use of everything (you need) and send forth to your parents (but the fact) is that even if I combine all the gifts that he bestowed upon me, they stand no comparison to the least gift of Abu Zara'. 'A'isha reported that Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to me: I am for you as Abu Zara' was for Umm Zara'. (Using translation from Muslim 2448a)"],[3436,"\"Fasting is a shield.\""],[3437,"I said, \"O Messenger of Allah, who do you love the most among the people?\" He said, \"Aisha.\" So I said, \"I do not mean women, but rather men.\" He said, \"Abu Bakr\" or he said, \"her father.\""],[3438,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ was asked, \"Who is the most beloved person to you?\" He said, \"Aisha.\" It was said to him, \"We are not asking you about your family.\" He said, \"Then her father.\""],[3439,"\"Oh mother, rejoice! By Allah, there is nothing between you and meeting Muhammad ﷺ and the beloved friends except for your soul leaving your body. You were the most beloved of the wives of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ to him, and the Messenger of Allah ﷺ did not love anyone except for kindness. She asked, \"Also?\" He said, \"Your necklace was destroyed by the fathers, so the Messenger of Allah ﷺ woke up without finding water, so they performed Tayammum with clean sand. This happened because of you and your blessings. Allah has revealed to this nation leniency and ease. It was due to a flat matter, so Allah revealed your innocence from above the seven heavens. There is no mosque where Allah is mentioned except that your issue is mentioned during the hours of night and day.\" She said, \"O Ibn Abbas, leave me and your praise. By Allah, I wish I were a forgotten and neglected person.\""],[3440,"\"To speak to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and ask him to command the people to give me their allegiance wherever he may be, for people seek his favor by giving him gifts on the day of Aisha. And indeed, we love goodness just as Aisha loves it.\" The Messenger of Allah ﷺ remained silent and did not respond to me. Then my companions came to me, and I told them that he did not speak to me. They replied, \"By Allah, we will not leave him.\" So, I spoke to him again, saying the same words two or three times. Still, the Messenger of Allah ﷺ remained silent. Then he said, 'O Umm Salamah, do not harm me with regards to Aisha. By Allah, revelation has not come to me while I am in the house of any of my wives except Aisha.'\" I said, \"I seek refuge in Allah from harming you in relation to Aisha.\""],[3441,"\"Aishah said: 'Shall I not tell you about me and about the Prophet?' We said: 'Yes.' She said: 'When it was my night when he was with me' - meaning the Prophet -'He came back (from 'Isha' prayer), put his sandals by his feet and spread the edge of his Izar on his bed. He stayed until he thought that I had gone to sleep. Then he put his sandals on slowly, picked up his cloak slowly, then opened the door slowly and went out slowly. I covered my head, put on my vie and tightened my waist wrapper, then I followed his steps until he came to Al-Baqi'. He raised his hands three times, and stood there for a long time, then he left and I left. He hastened and I also hastened; he ran and I also ran. He came (to the house) and I also came, but I got there first and entered, and as I lay down he came in. He said: \"Tell me, or the Subtle, the All-Aware will tell me.' I said: 'O Messenger of Allah, may my father and mother be ransomed for you,' and I told him (the whole story). He said: 'So you were the black shape that I saw in front of me?' I said, 'Yes.' He gave me a nudge on the chest which I felt, then he said: 'Did you think that Allah and His Messenger would deal unjustly with you?' I said: 'Whatever the people conceal, Allah knows it.' He said: Jibril came to me when I saw you, but he did not enter upon me because you where not fully dressed. He called me but he concealed that from you, and I answered him, but I concealed that from you too. I thought that you had gone to sleep and I did not want to wake you up, and I was afraid that you would be frightened. He told me to go to Al-Baqi' and pray for forgiveness for them.' I said: 'What should I say, O Messenger of Allah?' He said: 'Say\" Peace be upon the inhabitants of this place among the believers and Muslims. May Allah have mercy upon those who have gone on ahead of us and those who come later on, and we will join you, if Allah wills.\"' (Using translation from Nasāʾī 2037)"],[3442,"She said, \"When I saw the Prophet ﷺ in a good mood, I said, 'O Messenger of Allah, make du'a (supplication) for me.' He said, 'O Allah, forgive Aisha for her past sins and future sins, both those that she has kept hidden and those that she has made known.' Aisha laughed so much that her head fell into her lap from laughing. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to her, 'Does my du'a please you?' She replied, 'And why wouldn't your du'a please me?' He ﷺ said, 'By Allah, this du'a of mine is for my Ummah (nation) in every prayer.'"],[3443,"Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to me: I can well discern when you are pleased with me and when you are annoyed with me. I said: How do you discern it? Thereupon be said: When you are pleased with me you say;\" No, by the Lord of Muhammad,\" and when you are annoyed with me, you say:\" No, by the Lord of Ibrahim.\" I said: Messenger of Allah, by Allah, I in fact leave your name (when I am annoyed with you). (Using translation from Muslim 2439a)"],[3444,"“The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: ‘The superiority of ‘Aishah over other women is like the superiority of Tharid over all other foods.’” (Using translation from Ibn Mājah 3281)"],[3445,"“Many men have attained perfection but no women have attained perfection except Maryam bint ‘Imran (Mary) and Asiyah the wife of Fir’awn. And the superiority of ‘Aishah over other women is like the superiority of Tharid over all other foods.” (Using translation from Ibn Mājah 3280)"],[3446,"“The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: ‘The superiority of ‘Aishah over other women is like the superiority of Tharid over all other foods.’” (Using translation from Ibn Mājah 3281)"],[3447,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to me: \"It does not escape me when you are angry and when you are pleased. When you are angry, you say: No, by the Lord of Ibrahim; and when you are pleased, you say: No, by the Lord of Muhammad.\" I said: \"You have spoken the truth. I only abandon your name.\" She said: \"I said: O Messenger of Allah, consider if you descended into a valley in which there are many trees that have been grazed, and you found a tree that has not been grazed, in which of them would you leave your camel to graze?\" He said: \"In the one that has not been grazed.\""],[3448,"\"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ died in my house, on my day, and between my magic and sacrifice. Then Abdullah ibn Abu Bakr entered with a wet toothstick (miswak). The Messenger of Allah ﷺ looked at it, so I thought that he needed it. I took it, chewed on it, and perfumed it. Then I handed it to him, so he used it as beautifully as I had ever seen anyone using it before. Then he wanted to hand it back to me, but it fell from his hand. So I took it, and I sought assistance with a supplication that he used to make when he got sick, but he did not make that supplication during his sickness. Then he looked up to the sky and said, 'The Highest Companion, the Highest Companion.' Then his soul departed. Praise be to Allah who has brought my saliva and his saliva together on the last day of his life in this world.\""],[3449,"When Abdullah ibn Zubayr was born, I brought him to the Prophet ﷺ and he performed the tahneek (a custom of placing a piece of softened date in the newborn's mouth). The first thing that entered his (Abdullah's) stomach was this tahneek. The Prophet ﷺ said, \"He is Abdullah and you are the mother of Abdullah. I will always be attached to him and I have never had any other children.\""],[3450,"that the Prophet ﷺ married her when she was six years old and he consummated his marriage when she was nine years old, and then she remained with him for nine years (i.e., till his death). (Using translation from Bukhārī 5133)"],[3451,"Abu ʿAbdur-Rahman as-Sulami and Hibban bin ʿAtiyyah had a dispute. ʿAbdur-Rahman said to Hibban: I know what made your companion - meaning ʿAli ؓ - audacious. He said: What is it, may you be bereft of your father? He said. Something I heard ʿAli ؓ say. He said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ sent me, az-Zubair and Abu Marthad on a mission, and we were all horsemen. He said: ʿGo to Rawdat Khakh, for there you will find a woman who has a letter with her from Hatib bin Abi Baltaʿah to the mushrikeen; bring it to me.ʿ So we went on our horses until we caught up with her where the Messenger of Allah ﷺ had told us, travelling on a camel of hers. He [Hatib] had written to the people of Makkah, telling them about the march of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. We said to her. Where is the letter you have with you? She said: I do not have any letter. We made her camel kneel down and searched her luggage for it, but we did not find anything. My two companions said: We do not see any letter with her, I said: You know that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ did not tell a lie. Then I swore: By the One by whom oaths are sworn, you will give us the letter or we will remove your clothes. She stretched out her hand to her girdle, which was wrapped around her, and brought out the letter. I brought it to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and they said: O Messenger of Allah ﷺ, he has betrayed Allah and His Messenger and the believers; let me strike his neck. He said: ʿO Hatib, what made you do what you did?ʿ He said: O Messenger of Allah ﷺ, by Allah, it is not that I do not believe in Allah and His Messenger, but I wanted to do a favour for the people by means of which Allah might protect my family and my property, for every one of your Companions has some of his people there through whom Allah will protect his family and his property. He said: You have spoken the truth, do not say anything to him but good.ʿ ʻUmar said: O, Messenger of Allah, he betrayed Allah and His Messenger and the believers, let me strike his neck. He said. ʿls he not one of the people of Badr? How do you know? Perhaps Allah looked upon them and said. “Do what you like, for Paradise is guaranteed for you.ʻʼ ʻUmarʻs eyes filled with tears and he said: Allah, may He be exalted, and His Messenger know best. (Using translation from Aḥmad 827)"],[3452,"Hatib will definitely go to Hell. (But) Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: You tell a lie; he would not get into that for he had taken part in Badr and in (the expedition of) Hudaibiya. (Using translation from Muslim 2495)"],[3453,"'Utba b. Ghazwan delivered us a sermon and he praised Allah and lauded Him, then said: Now coming to the point, verily the world has been given the news of its end and that too quite early. Nothing would be left out of it but only water left in the utensil which its owner leaves, and you are going to shift to an abode which knows no end, and you should shift with the good before you, for we have been told that a stone would be thrown at one side of the Hell and it would go down even for seventy years but would not be able to reach its bottom. By Allah, it would be fully packed. Do you find it something strange, and it has been mentioned that there yawns a distance which one would be able to cover in forty years from one end to another of Paradise, and a day would come when it would be fully packed and you must be knowing that I was the seventh amongst seven who had been with Messenger of Allah ﷺ and we had nothing to eat but the leaves of the tree until the corners of the mouth were injured. We found a sheet which we tore in two and divided between myself and Sa'd b. Malik. I made the lower garment with halt of it and so did Sa'd make the lower garment with half of it and today there is none amongst us who has not become the governor of a city from amongst the cities (of the Islamic Commonwealth) and I seek refuge with Allah that I should consider myself great whereas I am insignificant in the eye of Allah. Prophethood does not remain for ever and its impact fades with the result that it changes eventually into kingship, and you would soon come to know and experience those rulers who would come after us and see (how far they are from religion). (Using translation from Muslim 2967a)"],[3454,"We used to go to Abdullah b. 'Amr and talk to him, Ibn Numair said: One day we made a mention of Abdullah b. Mas'ud, whereupon he said: You have made mention of a person whom I love more than anything else. I heard Messenger of Allah ﷺ as saying: Learn Qur'an from four persons: Ibn Umm 'Abd (i. e. 'Abdullah b. Mas'ud) he started from him-then Mu'adh b. Jabal and Ubayya b. Ka'b, then Salim the ally of Abu Hudhaifa. (Using translation from Muslim 2464a)"],[3455,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ recited this verse: \"And if you turn away, He will replace you with another people; then they will not be like you.\" They asked, \"O Messenger of Allah, who are those people that if we turn away, they will replace us and not be like us?\" He struck the thigh of Salman al-Farsi and said, \"This is him and his people. If faith were to be found at the Pleiades, men from Persia would attain it.\""],[3456,"We were sitting in the company of Hudhaifa. A man said: If I were in the time of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, I would have fought by his side and would have striven hard for his causes. Hudhaifa said: You might have done that, (but you should not make a flourish of your enthusiasm). I was with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ on the night of the Battle of Abzib and we were gripped by a violent wind and severe cold. The Messenger of Allah (may peace be him) said: Hark, the man who (goes reconnoitring and) brings me the news of the enemy shall be ranked with me on the Day of Judgment by Allah (the Glorious and Exalted). We all kept quiet and none of us responed to him. (Again) he said: Hark, a man who (goes reconnoitring and) brings me the news of the enemy shall be ranked with me on the Day of Judgment by Allah (the Glorious and Exalted). We kept quiet and none of us responded to him. He again said: Hark, a man who (goes reconnoitring and) brings me the news of the enemy shall be ranked with me on the Day of Judgtuent by Allah (the Glorious and Exalted) Then he said: Get up Hudhaifa, bring me the news of the enemy. When he called me by name I had no alternative but to get up. He said: Go and bring me information about the enemy, and do nothing that may provoke them against me. When I left him, I felt warm as if I were walking in a heated bath untill I reached them. I saw Abu Sufyan warming his back against fire I put an arrow in the middle of the bow. intending to shoot at him, when I recalled the words of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ\" Do not provoke them against me.\" Had I shot at him, I would have hit him. But I returned and (felt warm as if) I were walking in a heated bath (hammam). Presenting myself before him, I gave him information about the enemy. When I had done so, I began to feel cold, so the Messenger of Allah ﷺ wrapped me in a blanket that he had in excess to his own requirement and with which he used to cover himself while saying his prayers. So I continued to sleep until it was morning. When it was morning he said: Get up, O heavy sleeper. (Using translation from Muslim 1788)"],[3457,"My mother asked, \"When did you promise the Messenger of Allah ﷺ?\" I said, \"I didn't make any promise to him since such and such happened to me.\" So, my mother told me, \"Then go to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and pray with him, and seek forgiveness for you and me.\" So, I went to him and prayed with him the Maghrib prayer, and he ﷺ performed what was between the two prayers. Then, he left and I followed him. He asked me, \"Who is this?\" I said, \"Hudhayfah bin Al-Yaman.\" He asked, \"What brings you here?\" So, I informed him of what my mother had told me. He ﷺ said, \"May Allah forgive you and your mother.\""],[3458,"Al-Qama from Sham came and entered the mosque and performed prayer in it. Then he approached a group and sat among them. A man came and sat next to me, so I said, \"Praise be to Allah, I hope that Allah has answered my prayer.\" He said, \"And who is that?\" al-Qama said, \"I prayed to Allah to grant me a righteous companion, and I hope it is you.\" Abu Al-Darda' said, \"Who are you?\" I said, \"I am from the people of Kufa or from the people of Iraq, and then from the people of Kufa.\" Abu Al-Darda' said, \"Didn't you have the one who possesses the secret that no one else knows, meaning Hudhayfah?\" He said, \"Then he said, “Do you preserve it as Abdullah used to recite?’ I said, ‘Yes.’ He said, ‘{By the night when it covers, and [by] the day when it appears}.’ Al-Qama said, \"So I said, 'And the male and the female.' Abu Al-Darda' said, 'By Allah, whom there is no deity except Him, this is how the Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to recite it, from (fihi) to (fiiya).' They continued on like this until they almost turned me away from it.\""],[3459,"They made a mention of Ibn Mas'ud before 'Abdullah b. Amr, whereupon he said: He is a person whose love is always fresh in my heart after I heard Messenger of Allah ﷺ as saying: Learn the recita- tion of the Qur'an from four persons: from Ibn Mas'ud, Salim, the ally of Abu Hudhaifa, Ubayy b. Ka'b, Mu'adh b. Jabal. (Using translation from Muslim 2464e)"],[3460,"narrated that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"What an excellent man is Abu Bakr, what an excellent man is 'Umar, what an excellent man is Abu 'Ubaidah bin Al-Jarrah, what an excellent man is Usaid bin Hudair, what an excellent man is Thabit bin Qais bin Shammas, what an excellent man is Mua'dh bin Jabal, and what an excellent man is Mu'adh bin 'Amr bin Al-Jamuh.\" (Using translation from Tirmidhī 3795)"],[3461,"Four persons collected the Qur'an during the lifetime of Messenger of Allah ﷺ and all of them were Ansar: Mu'adh b. Jabal, Ubayy b. Ka'b, Zaid b. Thabit, Abu Zaid. Qatada said: Anas, who was Abu Zaid? He said: He was one of my uncles. (Using translation from Muslim 2465a)"],[3462,"The Messenger of Allah said: The most merciful of my Ummah towards my Ummah is Abu Bakr; the one who adheres most sternly to the religion of Allah is 'Umar; the most sincere of them in shyness and modesty is 'Uthman; the best judge is 'Ali bin Abu Talib; the best in reciting the Book of Allah is Ubayy bin Ka'b; the most knowledgeable of what is lawful and unlawful is Mu'adh bin Jabal; and the most knowledgeable of the rules of inheritance (Fara'id) is Zaid bin Thabit. And every nation has a trustworthy guardian, and the trustworthy guardian of this Ummah is Abu 'Ubaidah bin Jarrah.\" (Using translation from Ibn Mājah 154)"],[3464,"We set out from our people, the Ghifar, and they used to consider the sacred month lawful for fighting. I, my brother Unays, and our mother went out and stayed with a maternal uncle of ours. Our uncle honored us and treated us well, but his people envied us and said: 'When you leave your family, Unays will go to them against you.' Our uncle came and mentioned what had been said to him. I said: 'As for the good you have done in the past, you have spoiled it, and we have no need for anything after this.' So we brought our camels, loaded them, and set off until we halted near Makkah. He said: 'O son of my brother, I had prayed before I met the Messenger of Allah ﷺ.' I said: 'To whom?' He said: 'To Allah.' I said: 'In which direction did you face?' He said: 'I faced wherever my Lord directed me. I prayed in the evening until, near the end of the night, I would fall down, and the sun would rise over me.' Unays said: 'I have a need in Makkah.' So Unays went until he reached Makkah. Then he came back, and I said: 'What did you do?' He said: 'I met a man in Makkah who follows your religion, claiming that Allah has sent him.' I said: 'What do people say about him?' He said: 'They say: a poet, a soothsayer, a sorcerer.' Unays was one of the poets. He said: 'I have heard the words of the soothsayers, and his words are not like theirs. I compared his words with the various modes of poetry, and it does not fit on the tongue of anyone after me that it is poetry. By Allah, he is truthful, and they are liars.' I said: 'Then keep me covered until I go and see.' So I went to Makkah and sought hospitality from a man there. I said: 'Where is this man whom you call the Sabi'?' He pointed to me and said: 'The Sabi'.' Then the people of the valley rushed at me with every clod of earth and bone until I fell down unconscious. When I regained consciousness, I was like a red idol. I went to Zamzam, washed the blood off myself, and drank from its water. I stayed there between thirty nights and days with no food except Zamzam water, and I grew fat until the folds of my belly cracked, and I did not feel any weakness of hunger in my liver. While the people of Makkah were in a bright moonlit night, a deep sleep was cast over them, so no one was circumambulating the House except two women from among them who were calling upon Isaf and Na'ilah. They passed by me during their circumambulation, and I said: 'Marry one of them to the other.' They did not stop their invocation. Then they passed by me again, and I said: 'They are like the piece of wood.' They returned saying: 'If only someone were here.' Then the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and Abu Bakr met them as they were descending and said: 'What is the matter with you two?' They said: 'The Sabi' is between the Kaaba and its curtains.' They said: 'What did he say to you?' They said: 'He said a word to us that fills the mouth.' Then the Messenger of Allah ﷺ came until he touched the Black Stone, then he circumambulated the House with his companion and prayed. Abu Dharr said: 'I was the first to greet him with the greeting of Islam.' He said: 'And upon you and the mercy of Allah.' Then he said: 'From which people are you?' I said: 'From Ghifar.' He lowered his hand and placed his fingers on his forehead. I said to myself: 'He dislikes that I attributed myself to Ghifar.' Then he raised his head and said: 'Since when have you been here?' He said: 'I have been here for thirty days and nights.' He said: 'Who has been feeding you?' I said: 'I have had no food except Zamzam water, and I grew fat until the folds of my belly cracked.' The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: 'It is blessed; it is food that nourishes.' Abu Bakr said: 'O Messenger of Allah, permit me to feed him tonight.' So the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and Abu Bakr went, and I went with them. Abu Bakr opened a door and began taking out for us some raisins of Taif. That was the first food I ate there. Then I stayed for some time. Then I came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and he said: 'A land of palm trees has been shown to me, which I think is Yathrib. Can you convey a message from me to your people? Perhaps Allah will guide them through you and reward you among them.' So I set off and met Unays. He said: 'What did you do?' I said: 'I have embraced Islam and declared it true.' He said: 'I have no aversion to your religion, for I too have embraced Islam and declared it true.' Then we came to our mother, and she said: 'I have no aversion to your religion, for I too have embraced Islam and declared it true.' So we loaded up and went to our people, the Ghifar. Half of them embraced Islam, and Ima' ibn Rahada, who was their chief, led them in prayer. The other half said: 'When the Messenger of Allah ﷺ arrives in Madinah, we will embrace Islam.' When the Messenger of Allah ﷺ arrived in Madinah, the remaining half embraced Islam. The Aslam tribe came and said: 'O Messenger of Allah, our brothers, we submit to what they have submitted to.' The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: 'Ghifar—may Allah forgive her; Aslam—may Allah grant her peace.'\""],[3465,"\"I was the fourth to embrace Islam before me, three people had already accepted it. When I came to the Prophet ﷺ, I greeted him saying, 'peace be upon you, O Messenger of Allah. I bear witness that there is no god but Allah and I bear witness that Muhammad is His servant and Messenger.' I saw joy on the face of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, so he asked, 'Who are you?' I replied, 'I am Jundub, a man from the tribe of Ghifar.'\""],[3466,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to me: \"The dust-colored earth does not carry, nor does the green sky shade, anyone with a tongue more truthful and more loyal than Abu Dharr, resembling Isa ibn Maryam, peace be upon our Prophet and upon him.\" Then Umar ibn al-Khattab ؓ stood up and said: \"O Prophet of Allah, shall we acknowledge that for him?\" He said: \"Yes, acknowledge it for him.\""],[3467,"When death came to Abu Dharr, I wept, and he said, \"What makes you weep?\" I said, \"Why should I not weep, when you are dying in a desolate land, and I have no garment that can serve as your shroud, nor do I have the means to bury you?\" He said, \"Rejoice and do not weep, for I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: 'If two Muslim parents lose two or three children and remain patient and seek reward, they will never see the Fire.' And I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say to a group of people, among whom I was one: 'A man among you will surely die in a desolate land, witnessed by a band of believers.' And there was no one from that group except that he died in a village or among a gathering, so I am that man. By Allah, I have not lied, nor have I been lied to. So look out for the road.\" I said, \"How can I, when the pilgrims have gone and the routes are cut off?\" He said, \"Go and look.\" She said, \"So I would hurry to the mound, look out, then return and nurse him. While he and I were like that, suddenly I saw men on their mounts, like vultures, their riding camels speeding with them.\" She said, \"They hurried to me when they stopped beside me and said, 'O servant of Allah, what is the matter with you?' I said, 'A Muslim man is dying; will you shroud him?' They said, 'Who is he?' I said, 'Abu Dharr.' They said, 'The companion of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ?' I said, 'Yes.' Then they ransomed him with their fathers and mothers and hurried to him until they entered upon him. He said to them, 'Rejoice, for I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say to a group of people, among whom I was one: \"A man among you will surely die in a desolate land, witnessed by a band of believers.\" And there was no one from that group except that he died among a gathering. By Allah, I have not lied, nor have I been lied to. If I had a garment that could serve as a shroud for me or for my wife, I would not be shrouded except in a garment that is mine or hers. I adjure you by Allah that no one among you who has been an emir, a tax collector, a courier, or a chief should shroud me.' And there was no one from that group except that he had done some of what he said, except a young man from the Ansar. He said, 'I will shroud you, O uncle. I will shroud you in this cloak of mine and in two garments in my bag woven by my mother.' Abu Dharr said, 'You, then shroud me.' So the Ansari shrouded him among the group who attended, and they stood over him and buried him in a group, all of whom were from Yemen."],[3468,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to me: “Do you know Syriac well?” I said: “No.” He said: “Then learn it, for letters come to us.” He [Zayd] said: “So I learned it in seventeen days.”"],[3469,"The Messenger of Allah said: The most merciful of my Ummah towards my Ummah is Abu Bakr; the one who adheres most sternly to the religion of Allah is 'Umar; the most sincere of them in shyness and modesty is 'Uthman; the best judge is 'Ali bin Abu Talib; the best in reciting the Book of Allah is Ubayy bin Ka'b; the most knowledgeable of what is lawful and unlawful is Mu'adh bin Jabal; and the most knowledgeable of the rules of inheritance (Fara'id) is Zaid bin Thabit. And every nation has a trustworthy guardian, and the trustworthy guardian of this Ummah is Abu 'Ubaidah bin Jarrah.\" (Using translation from Ibn Mājah 154)"],[3470,"His father died leaving nine daughters or seven daughters. He said: So I came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and he said to me: “Did you marry, O Jabir?” I said: “Yes.” He said: “A virgin or a previously married woman?” I said: “Rather a previously married woman.” He said: “Why not a young girl so you could play with her and she play with you, and you make her laugh and she make you laugh?” I said: “Abdullah died leaving nine daughters or seven daughters, and I disliked bringing them one like them, so I wanted a woman who would take care of them.” He said to me: “May Allah bless you.”"],[3471,"My father died owing a debt. I offered his creditors to take the dates for what was owed, but they refused and did not think there was enough in them to cover it. So I came to the Prophet ﷺ and mentioned that to him. He said: “When you harvest it and place it, let me know.” When I harvested it and placed it in the mosque, I informed the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. He came with Abu Bakr and Umar, sat down, and supplicated for blessing in it, then said: “Call your creditors and pay them.” I did not leave anyone who had a debt on my father except I paid it, and thirteen wasqs of Ajwa dates remained extra for me. He said: Then I came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ at Maghrib prayer and mentioned that to him. He smiled ﷺ and said: “Go to Abu Bakr and Umar and tell them.” They said: “We knew when the Messenger of Allah ﷺ did what he did, it would be so.”"],[3472,"I was on a journey with the Prophet ﷺ, and I was on a weak camel that was at the rear of the people. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ struck it with something he had, and after that it began to advance ahead of the people, racing with me until I had to restrain it. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Will you sell it to me for such-and-such, and may Allah forgive you?” He said: I said: “It is yours, O Messenger of Allah.” He said: “Will you sell it to me for such-and-such, and may Allah forgive you?” He said: I said: “O Messenger of Allah, it is yours.”"],[3473,"We were with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ on a journey. He said: “Will you sell me your camel when we arrive in Madinah, if Allah wills, for a dinar? And may Allah forgive you.” He said: I said: “It is your camel, O Messenger of Allah.” He said: “Will you sell it to me when we arrive in Madinah, if Allah wills, for two dinars?” He said: I said: “It is your camel, O Messenger of Allah.” He kept increasing until it reached twenty dinars, each time saying: “And may Allah forgive you.” When we arrived in Madinah, I brought it leading it and said: “Here is your camel, O Messenger of Allah.” He said: “O Bilal, give him twenty dinars from the spoils and return with your camel to your family.”"],[3474,"“The Prophet ﷺ asked forgiveness for me on the night of the camel twenty-five times.”"],[3476,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to Ubayy b. Ka'b: “Allah has commanded me to recite the Quran to you.” Ubayy said: “Did Allah name me to you?” He said: “Allah named you to me.” He said: Then Ubayy began to weep."],[3477,"Hassan b. Thabit asked the Messenger of Allah ﷺ for permission to lampoon the polytheists. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “What about my lineage?” Hassan said: “I will draw you out from them as a hair is drawn from dough.”"],[3478,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to Hassan: “The Holy Spirit is with you as long as you lampoon them.”"],[3479,"I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say to Hassan b. Thabit: “The Holy Spirit will keep supporting you as long as you defend Allah and His Messenger.”"],[3480,"Umar passed by Hassan b. Thabit while he was reciting poetry in the mosque and looked at him. Hassan turned to Abu Hurayrah and said to him: “I ask you by Allah, did you hear the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: ‘Answer on my behalf, O Allah, support him with the Holy Spirit’?” He said: “Yes.”"],[3481,"Khuzaymah b. Thabit saw in a dream that he prostrated on the forehead of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. So Khuzaymah came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and told him. He said: Then the Messenger of Allah ﷺ lay down for him and said: “Confirm your dream.” So he prostrated on the forehead of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ."],[3482,"While I was traveling at night, there was a man saying takbir. I made my camel catch up with him and said, 'Who is this saying takbir?' He said, 'Abu Hurayrah.' I said, 'What is this takbir for?' He said, 'In gratitude.' I said, 'For what?' He said, 'For that I was a hired worker for Busrah bint Ghazwan in return for my food and the use of my feet [to serve her]. When the people rode, I drove their camels, and when they dismounted, I served them. Then Allah gave her to me in marriage, and now she is my wife. So now when the people ride, I ride, and when they dismount, I am served.'\""],[3483,"Severe hardship befell me. I met Umar b. al-Khattab ؓ and asked him to recite a verse from the Book of Allah to me. He entered his house and recited it to me. Then I walked a short distance and fell on my face from hunger. Suddenly the Messenger of Allah ﷺ was standing over my head, and he said, 'O Abu Hurayrah.' I said, 'At your service, O Messenger of Allah.' He took me by the hand and helped me stand, and he recognized what was wrong with me. He went to his mount and ordered a large bowl of milk for me, and I drank. Then he said, 'Drink again, O Abu Hurayrah.' I drank again until my stomach became full and like a cup. He said: I then saw Umar and mentioned what had happened to me, and I said to him, 'Who was more deserving of it than you, O Umar? By Allah, I asked you to recite the verse, and I can recite it better than you.' Umar said, 'By Allah, if I had let you in [to my house], that would be more beloved to me than having red camels.'"],[3484,"\"None of the companions of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ has more hadiths than I, except Abdullah b. Amr, for he used to write while I did not write.\""],[3485,"\"Doesn't Abu Hurayrah amaze you? He came and sat by the door of my room, narrating from the Prophet ﷺ so that I could hear, while I was glorifying Allah. He got up before I finished my glorification, and had I caught him I would have rebutted him. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ did not narrate hadiths in a rapid sequence like you do.\""],[3486,"\"By Allah, Allah has not created any believer who hears of me and sees me except that he loves me.\" I said, \"How do you know that, O Abu Hurayrah?\" He said, \"My mother was a polytheist woman, and I used to call her to Islam, but she refused. One day I called her, and she said about the Messenger of Allah ﷺ what I disliked. I came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ crying and said, 'O Messenger of Allah, I used to call my mother to Islam but she refuses, and when I called her she said about you what I disliked. Pray to Allah to guide the mother of Abu Hurayrah.' The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, 'O Allah, guide her.' When I reached the door, it was ajar, and I heard the splashing of water and the sound of a man's or men's footsteps. She said, 'O Abu Hurayrah, stay where you are,' and she opened the door, put on her garment, and hurried with her veil. She said, 'I bear witness that there is no god but Allah and I bear witness that Muhammad is the Messenger of Allah.' I returned to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ crying from joy as I had cried from sadness, and said, 'O Messenger of Allah, rejoice, for Allah has answered your supplication and guided the mother of Abu Hurayrah.' I said, 'O Messenger of Allah, pray to Allah to make me and my mother beloved to His believing servants and to make them beloved to us.' The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, 'O Allah, make Your servant and his mother beloved to Your believing servants and make them beloved to them.'\""],[3487,"\"Abu Hurayrah was bold with the Prophet ﷺ, asking him about things we would not ask him about.\""],[3488,"\"I came to Madinah while the Prophet ﷺ was at Khaybar, and a man from Banu Ghifar was leading them in the Fajr prayer. He recited in the first rak'ah 'Kaf Ha Ya Ayn Sad' and in the second 'Woe to those who give less [than due]'. We had a man with two measuring vessels, a large one and a small one; he would give with one and take with the other.\" So I said, \"Woe to so-and-so.\""],[3489,"We were with the Prophet ﷺ at the funeral of Abu Dahdah. After he prayed upon him, a horse was brought and he rode it while we were running behind him. He ﷺ said, \"How many splendid gardens (or rides) for Abu Dahdah in Paradise!\""],[3490,"\"The Prophet ﷺ prayed upon Abu Duhdah while we were present. The Prophet ﷺ was brought a horse and he rode it while we crowded around him. He said ﷺ, 'How many delights are there for Abu Duhdah hanging in Paradise!'\""],[3491,"A man came to the Prophet ﷺ and said, \"O Messenger of Allah, so-and-so has a date palm, and I am building a wall around my garden with it. Order him to give it to me so that I can complete my wall.\" The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, \"Give it to him in return for a date palm in Paradise.\" He refused. Abu al-Dahdah came to him and said, \"Sell me your date palm for my garden.\" He did so. Abu al-Dahdah came to the Prophet ﷺ and said, \"O Messenger of Allah, I have bought the date palm with my garden, and I give it to you; make it for him.\" The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, \"How many large clusters will Abu al-Dahdah have in Paradise!\" repeating it several times. Abu al-Dahdah went to his wife and said, \"O Umm al-Dahdah, leave the garden, for I have sold it for a date palm in Paradise.\" She said, \"You have profited from the transaction.\""],[3492,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ called him and said, \"I have been informed that Ibn Safwan ibn Nubayh al-Hudhali has gathered people to support me while he is near a date palm or a cluster of dates, so go to him.\" He said, \"O Messenger of Allah, describe him to me so that I may recognize him.\" He said, \"One of the signs between you and him is that when you see him, you will find a shiver down your spine.\" He said, \"So I set out with my sword wrapped around me until I came to him while he was in a shady place which he usually visited at the time of Asr prayer. When I saw him, I found exactly what the Messenger of Allah ﷺ had described to me. So I approached him and feared that there might be some attempt to distract me from the prayer, so I prayed while walking towards him and nodded with my head. When I finished the prayer, I went up to him and he said, \"Who is it?\" I said, \"A man from the Arabs who heard about you and your gathering for this man and came for that reason.\" He said, \"It is indeed me.\" So I walked with him for a while until it was possible for me to seize him with my sword, so I killed him. Then I came and left his belongings piled up around him. When I came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and he saw me, he said, \"The face has succeeded.\" I said, \"I killed him, O Messenger of Allah.\" He said, \"You have spoken the truth.\" Then the Messenger of Allah ﷺ stood up with me and took me to his house and gave me a stick and said, \"Keep this stick with you, O Abdullah ibn Unays.\" He said, \"So I went out with it among the people, and they said, \"What is this stick?\" I said, \"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ gave it to me and ordered me to keep it.\" They said, \"Why don't you return to the Messenger of Allah and ask him about it?\" He said, \"So I went back to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and said, \"O Messenger of Allah, why did you give me this stick?\" He said, \"It is a sign between you and me on the Day of Resurrection. Indeed, the least of people on that day will be those who are too short.\" So Abdullah linked it to his sword and it remained with him until his death. Then he (the Prophet) ordered that it be buried with him in his shroud, and so we were all buried together."],[3493,"Abdullah ibn Salam went to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ when he first arrived in Medina and said, \"I have three questions that only a prophet knows.\" The Prophet ﷺ said, \"Ask.\" Abdullah asked, \"What is the first sign of the Hour or the first thing that will happen at the Hour? What do the people of Paradise eat? And what causes a child to resemble his father or his mother?\" The Prophet ﷺ replied, \"Jibril informed me about them earlier.\" Jibril said, \"Yes.\" The Prophet ﷺ said, \"That is one of the enemies of the Jews from the angels.\" The Prophet ﷺ continued, \"As for the first sign of the Hour or the first thing that will happen at the Hour, it is a fire that will come out of the East and drive people to the West. As for what the people of Paradise eat, it is the additional lobe of the liver of a fish. And as for what causes a child to resemble his father or mother, when the water of the man precedes the water of the woman, the child resembles the father, and when the water of the woman precedes the water of the man, the child resembles the mother.\" Abdullah said, \"I bear witness that there is no god but Allah and that you are the Messenger of Allah.\" Abdullah said, \"O Messenger of Allah, the Jews are a confused people. If they come to know about my conversion to Islam before the others, a group of them will accompany me and ask them which one among them is Abdullah ibn Salam.\" They would respond, \"The best and most knowledgeable among us.\" Abdullah went back to them and said, \"I bear witness that there is no god but Allah.\" They said, \"Woe to us, he is the most evil among us.\" Abdullah said, \"This is the person I was afraid of them realizing.\""],[3494,"\"I never heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say to anyone walking on the earth, 'He is one of the people of Paradise,' except to Abdullah b. Salam.\""],[3495,"A bowl was brought to the Prophet ﷺ, and we ate from it. There was some leftover. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, \"A man from this mountain pass will appear and eat this bowl; he is one of the people of Paradise.\" Sa'd said, \"I had left my brother Umayr performing ablution, so I thought it was him.\" Then Abdullah b. Salam came and ate it."],[3496,"\"I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say, 'He is the tenth of ten in Paradise.'\""],[3497,"\"I was sitting in a circle in the mosque of Madinah, in which there was an old man of good appearance, who was Abdullah b. Salam. He narrated to them a good hadith. When he stood up, the people said, 'Whoever would like to look at a man from the people of Paradise, let him look at this man.' I said, 'By Allah, I will follow him and learn his house.' I followed him until he was about to leave Madinah, then entered his house. I asked permission and he allowed me. He said, 'What do you need, O son of my brother?' I said, 'I heard the people say when you stood up, \"Whoever would like to look at a man from the people of Paradise, let him look at this man,\" and I was pleased to be with you.' He said, 'Allah knows best who the people of Paradise are. I will tell you why they said that. While I was sleeping, a man came to me and said, \"Get up.\" He took me by the hand and I went with him. I saw a wide road on my left, and I wanted to take it, but he said, \"Do not take it, for it is the path of the people of the left.\" Then I saw a clear wide road on my right, and he said, \"Take this one.\" He brought me to a mountain and said, \"Climb this.\" When I tried to climb, I fell on my backside; I did that several times. Then he went on until he brought me to a pillar whose top was in the sky and bottom in the earth, and at its top was a ring. He said, \"Climb this.\" I said, \"How can I climb it when its top is in the sky?\" He took me by the hand and pushed me, and I found myself clinging to the ring. Then he struck the pillar and it fell, and I remained clinging to the ring until morning. I came to the Prophet ﷺ and told him the dream. He said, \"The road you saw on your left is the path of the people of the left; the road on your right is the path of the people of the right; the mountain is the stations of the martyrs, which you will not attain; the pillar is the pillar of Islam; the ring is the firm handhold of Islam, and you will keep holding to it until you die.\"'\""],[3498,"“O Messenger of Allah, by Allah, I have feared that I may have been ruined.” He said: “Why?” He said: “Allah has forbidden us to love being praised for what we have not done, and I find that I love praise. Allah has forbidden arrogance, and I find that I love beauty. And Allah has forbidden us to raise our voices above your voice, while I am a man with a loud voice.” So the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “O Thabit, would you not be pleased to live praiseworthy, be killed as a martyr, and enter Paradise?” He said: “Yes, O Messenger of Allah.” He said: So he lived praiseworthy, and he was killed as a martyr on the day of Musaylimah the Liar."],[3499,"When this verse was revealed: {O you who believe, do not raise your voices above the voice of the Prophet and do not be loud with him in speech}, Thabit b. Qays b. Shammas sat in his house and said: I am the one who used to raise my voice and be loud with him in speech, and I am among the people of the Fire. The Prophet ﷺ missed him, so they informed him, and he said: \"Rather, he is among the people of Paradise.\" Anas said: We used to see him walking among us while we knew that he was among the people of Paradise. Then on the day of al-Yamamah, when that rout occurred, he put on his clothes, perfumed himself with hanut, advanced, and fought until he was killed."],[3500,"When this verse was revealed: {O you who believe, do not raise your voices above the voice of the Prophet}, Thabit b. Qays said: By Allah, I am the one who used to raise my voice in the presence of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and I fear that Allah may have become angry with me. So he grieved and turned pale. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ missed him and asked about him. It was said: O Prophet of Allah, he says: I fear that I may be among the people of the Fire, for I used to raise my voice in the presence of the Prophet ﷺ. The Prophet ﷺ said: \"Rather, he is among the people of Paradise.\" So we used to see him walking among us as a man of the people of Paradise."],[3501,"That the Prophet ﷺ supplicated for him for beauty."],[3503,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ asked for water, so I brought him a vessel containing water with a hair in it. I removed the hair and handed it to him. He looked at me ﷺ and said: \"O Allah, make him beautiful.\" He said: I saw him when he was ninety-three years old, and there was not a white hair on his head or beard."],[3505,"I went on seven military expeditions with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and nine with Zayd b. Harithah, whom the Messenger of Allah ﷺ appointed as our commander."],[3506,"The companions of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, when a man was fasting and the time of breaking the fast came, if he slept before breaking his fast, he would not eat that night or that day until evening. Qays b. Ṣirmah was fasting, and when the time of breaking the fast came, he went to his wife and said, “Do you have any food?” She said, “No, but let me go and look for some.” That day he had been working, so sleep overcame him. His wife came and when she saw him, she said, “What a disappointment for you!” He woke up the next morning. When midday came, he fainted. That was mentioned to the Prophet ﷺ, and this verse was revealed: “It has been made lawful for you, on the night of the fast, to approach your wives; they are a garment for you.” They rejoiced greatly at it. “And eat and drink until the white thread becomes distinct to you from the black thread of dawn.”"],[3507,"Umm Sulaym came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, having wrapped me in part of her headcover and tied me with the rest. She said: O Messenger of Allah, this is Anas; I have brought him to serve you, so supplicate to Allah for him. He said: \"O Allah, increase his wealth and children.\" Anas said: By Allah, my wealth is abundant, and my children and grandchildren number around a hundred."],[3508,"She said to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ: Anas is your servant; supplicate to Allah for him. He said: \"O Allah, increase his wealth and children, and bless him in what You have given him.\""],[3509,"I served the Prophet ﷺ for ten years. He never sent me on an errand that did not turn out as intended except that he said: \"If it had been decreed, it would have happened,\" or \"If it had been destined, it would have happened.\""],[3510,"Drowsiness overcame us while we were in our ranks on the day of Badr. Abu Talhah said: I was among those whom drowsiness overcame that day. My sword kept falling from my hand, and I would pick it up, and it would fall, and I would pick it up. The other group, the hypocrites, had no concern except for themselves. They were the most cowardly people and the most abject regarding the truth, thinking of Allah other than the truth, the thought of ignorance, people of doubt and suspicion concerning the matter of Allah."],[3511,"Abu Talhah used to shoot in front of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. The Prophet ﷺ would raise his head from behind him to see where his arrow fell, and Abu Talhah would stretch his chest forward, shielding the Messenger of Allah ﷺ with it, and say: \"Like this, O Prophet of Allah, may Allah make me your ransom, my chest before your chest.\""],[3512,"Abu Talhah was the wealthiest of the Ansar in Madinah, and the most beloved of his properties to him was Bayruha', which faced the mosque. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to enter it and drink from its sweet water. Anas said: When this verse was revealed: {You will not attain righteousness until you spend from what you love}, Abu Talhah stood before the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and said, \"O Messenger of Allah, Allah says in His Book: {You will not attain righteousness until you spend from what you love}. The most beloved of my properties to me is Bayruha', so it is charity for Allah. I hope for its righteousness and its treasure with Allah. Place it, O Messenger of Allah, wherever you wish.\" The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, \"Excellent! That is profitable wealth. Excellent! That is profitable wealth. I have heard what you said about it, and I think you should make it for the nearest relatives.\" Abu Talhah said, \"I will do so, O Messenger of Allah.\" So Abu Talhah divided it among his relatives and his paternal cousins."],[3513,"When this verse was revealed, {You will never attain righteousness until you spend of what you love} (Qur'an 3:92), Abu Talhah said: \"O Messenger of Allah, Allah asks us of our wealth. I call you to witness that I have made my land an endowment.\" The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"Give it to your relatives.\" So he divided it between Hassan b. Thabit and Ubayy b. Ka'b."],[3514,"Abu Talhah recited Surat Bara'ah (Qur'an 9) and came upon this verse: {Go forth, light and heavy} (Qur'an 9:41). He said: \"I see that my Lord is calling me to go forth, young and old. Equip me.\" His sons said to him: \"You have gone on campaigns with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ until he passed away, and with Abu Bakr until he died, and with Umar. We will campaign on your behalf.\" He said: \"Equip me.\" So they equipped him, and he sailed on the sea and died. They could not find an island to bury him on until after seven days, and his body did not change."],[3515,"Umm Sulaym went out on the day of Hunayn with the Prophet ﷺ, and she had a dagger with her. Abu Talhah said to her: \"O Umm Sulaym, what is this?\" She said: \"I have taken it, by Allah, so that if any man comes near me, I will rip open his belly with it.\" Abu Talhah said: \"Do you not hear what Umm Sulaym is saying? She says such and such.\" She said: \"O Messenger of Allah, kill those after us from the released prisoners who fled with you.\" The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"O Umm Sulaym, Allah has sufficed and done well.\""],[3516,"The Prophet ﷺ entered upon Umm Sulaym, and she brought him dates and clarified butter. He said: \"Return your butter to its skin and your dates to their container, for I am fasting.\" Then he stood in a corner of the house and prayed a non-obligatory prayer, and supplicated for Umm Sulaym and her household. Umm Sulaym said: \"O Messenger of Allah, I have a little special request.\" He said: \"What is it?\" She said: \"Your little servant Anas.\" He left out no good of the Hereafter or this world but he supplicated for it for me. Then he said: \"O Allah, grant him wealth and children, and bless him in them.\" He (Anas) said: \"Indeed I am among the wealthiest of the Ansar.\" He said: \"And my daughter Umaynah told me: By the time al-Hajjaj came to Basra, one hundred and twenty-some of my loins had been buried.\""],[3517,"Abu Talhah proposed to Umm Sulaym. She said to him: \"Someone like you, O Abu Talhah, is not rejected, but I am a Muslim woman and you are a disbelieving man. It is not lawful for me to marry you. If you become Muslim, that will be my dowry; I ask you for nothing else.\" So he became Muslim, and she became his wife, and he consummated the marriage with her. She became pregnant and gave birth to a handsome boy. Abu Talhah loved him intensely. The boy lived until he began to move, then he fell ill, and Abu Talhah grieved over him with great sorrow until he became weak. Abu Talhah used to go to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ in the morning and return in the evening. He returned one evening and the boy had died. Umm Sulaym went to him, perfumed him, cleaned him, and placed him in our private room. Abu Talhah came and said: \"How is my little son this evening?\" She said: \"He is fine; he has never been calmer since he fell ill than tonight.\" He praised Allah and was pleased. She brought his dinner, and he ate. Then she touched some perfume and made herself available to him until he had intercourse with her. After he had eaten and been with his wife, she said: \"O Abu Talhah, what do you think if a neighbor of yours lent you a loan, and you enjoyed it, and then he wanted to take it back from you? Would you return it to him?\" He said: \"Yes, by Allah, I would return it to him.\" She said: \"May your soul be at ease with it?\" He said: \"May my soul be at ease with it.\" She said: \"Allah lent you your little son and let you enjoy him as long as He willed, then He took him back to Himself. So be patient and seek reward.\" Abu Talhah said: \"We belong to Allah and to Him we return,\" and he was patient. In the morning he went to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and told him what Umm Sulaym had done. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"May Allah bless you both in your night.\" She became pregnant from that intercourse and grew heavy. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to Abu Talhah: \"When Umm Sulaym gives birth, bring me her child.\" Abu Talhah carried him in a piece of cloth and brought him to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ chewed a date and put some of it into the child's mouth. The child began to move his tongue. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to Abu Talhah: \"The Ansar love dates.\" He performed tahnik on him, prayed for him, and named him Abdullah."],[3518,"Abu Talhah had a son whose kunyah was Abu Umayr. The Prophet ﷺ used to say: \"O Abu Umayr, what happened to the little bird?\" The boy fell ill while Abu Talhah was away in one of his gardens, and the child died. Umm Sulaym washed him, shrouded him, embalmed him, and covered him with a cloth. She said: \"Let no one tell Abu Talhah until I am the one who tells him.\" Abu Talhah came home tired and fasting. She perfumed herself for him and adorned herself, and brought his dinner. He said: \"What did Abu Umayr do?\" She said: \"He has eaten and is settled.\" He ate dinner and had intercourse with her as a man does with his wife. Then she said: \"O Abu Talhah, what do you think of a household that lent another household a loan, and the owners asked for it back? Should they return it or keep it?\" He said: \"They should return it.\" She said: \"Then seek reward for Abu Umayr.\" He became angry and went to the Prophet ﷺ and told him what Umm Sulaym had said. The Prophet ﷺ said: \"May Allah bless you both in the remainder of your night.\" She became pregnant with Abdullah b. Abu Talhah. When she gave birth, and it was the seventh day, Umm Sulaym said to me: \"O Anas, take this child and this basket, in which there are some pressed dates, to the Prophet ﷺ so that he may be the one to perform tahnik on him and name him.\" I brought him to the Prophet ﷺ. The Prophet ﷺ stretched out his legs, laid the child in his lap, took a date and chewed it, then put some of it into the child's mouth. The child began to move his tongue. The Prophet ﷺ said: \"The Ansar refuse anything but love of dates.\""],[3519,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ came to us and slept at our place. He woke up laughing. She (Umm Haram) said: \"I said: O Messenger of Allah, may my father and mother be your ransom, what made you laugh?\" He said: \"I saw people from my community riding this sea like kings on thrones.\" Then he slept and woke up laughing. She asked him, and he told her the same. She said: \"Supplicate Allah to make me one of them.\" He said: \"You are among the first.\" Ubadah b. al-Samit married her. He rode and she rode with him. When a mule was brought for her to ride, its neck broke and she died."],[3520,"\"I entered Paradise and heard a sound of footsteps. I said: 'Who is this?' They said: 'Al-Rumaysa bt. Milhan.'\""],[3521,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ appointed Abu Amir al-Ash'ari on the day of Hunayn over the cavalry of the pursuit. When Hawazin fled, he pursued them until he caught up with Durayd b. al-Simmah. His horse sped with him, and the son of Durayd killed Abu Amir. Abu Musa said: I attacked the son of Durayd and killed him, took the banner, and returned with the people to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. When he saw me with the banner in my hand, he said: \"Abu Musa, has Abu Amir been killed?\" I said: \"Yes, O Messenger of Allah.\" He raised his hands supplicating for him, saying: \"O Allah, as for Abu Amir, place him among the majority on the Day of Resurrection.\""],[3522,"\"People are coming who are the most tender-hearted.\" The Ash'aris came, among them Abu Musa, and they began chanting and saying."],[3523,"«People will come to you whose hearts are softer than yours.» Then the Ashʿaris arrived, among them Abū Mūsā, and they were the first to introduce shaking hands in Islam. When they drew near to Madinah, they began to chant in rajaz and say:"],[3524,"We set out to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ by sea until we came to Makkah, with my brothers and me among fifty* from the Ashʿaris and six from ʿAkk. Abū Mūsā said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to say, «The people have one migration, but you have two migrations.»"],[3525,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ heard Abū Mūsā's recitation and said, «This one has been given some of the melodious voices of the family of David.»"],[3526,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ heard Abū Mūsā al-Ashʿarī's recitation and said, «This one has been given some of the melodious voices of the family of David.»"],[3527,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ listened to my recitation at night, and when morning came he said, «O Abū Mūsā, I listened to your recitation last night; you have been given a flute from the flutes of the family of David.» I said, \"O Messenger of Allah, had I known where you were, I would have embellished it for you properly.\""],[3528,"When the Messenger of Allah ﷺ finished with Ḥunayn, he sent Abū ʿĀmir at the head of an army to Awṭās. He met Durayd ibn al-Ṣimmah and killed Durayd, and Allah routed his companions. Abū ʿĀmir was shot in his knee by a man from Banū Jusham with an arrow, which lodged in his knee. I came to him and said, \"O uncle, who shot you?\" He pointed and said, \"That is my killer,\" meaning the one who shot me. Abū Mūsā said: I made for him and caught up with him. When he saw me, he turned and fled, and I followed him, saying, \"Are you not ashamed? Will you not stand firm? Are you not ashamed? Are you not an Arab?\" He stopped, and we met and exchanged blows. I struck him with my sword and killed him. Then I returned and said, \"Allah has killed your companion.\" He said, \"Pull out this arrow.\" I pulled it out, and water flowed from the wound. He said, \"O son of my brother, go to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and convey my greetings to him, and tell him: he says to you, 'Ask forgiveness for me.'\" He said: Abū ʿĀmir appointed me as his deputy and remained a short while, then he died. When I returned to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, I entered upon him while he was in a house on a bed, and the bed had left marks on the back and sides of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. I informed him of our news and the news of Abū ʿĀmir, and I said to him, \"He said: tell him to ask forgiveness for me.\" He said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ called for water, performed ablution, raised his hands, and then said, \"O Allah, forgive ʿUbayd Abū ʿĀmir. O Allah, make him on the Day of Resurrection above many of Your creation.\" I said, \"And for me, O Messenger of Allah, ask forgiveness.\" The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, \"O Allah, forgive ʿAbd Allah ibn Qays his sin and admit him to a noble entrance.\""],[3529,"When I drew near to the city of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, I made my mount kneel, untied my saddlebag, put on my suit, and entered upon the Messenger of Allah ﷺ while he was delivering a sermon. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ greeted me, and the people stared at me. I said to my companion, \"O ʿAbd Allah, did the Messenger of Allah ﷺ mention anything about me?\" He said, \"Yes, he mentioned you in the best way. While he was delivering a sermon, it occurred to him in his sermon, and he said, 'There will enter upon you from this door, or from this mountain pass, one of the best of the people of Yemen, and upon his face is the touch of an angel.'\" So I praised Allah for what He had bestowed upon me."],[3530,"«The Messenger of Allah ﷺ never veiled himself from me since I became Muslim, and he never saw me except that he smiled in my face.»"],[3531,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to me, \"Will you not relieve me of Dhū al-Khalaṣah?\"—a house belonging to Khathʿam in the pre-Islamic era called the Yemeni Kaʿbah. He said: I said, \"O Messenger of Allah, I am a man who cannot keep steady on horseback.\" He wiped my chest and said, \"O Allah, make him a rightly-guided guide,\" until I felt its coolness."],[3532,"«O Jarīr, none of the idols of the pre-Islamic era remains except the house of Dhū al-Khalaṣah, so suffice me against it.» He said: I set out with one hundred and seventy men of my people, and we burned it. I sent a man to the Prophet ﷺ to give him the good news; he was called Abū Arṭāh. He said, \"By Allah, O Messenger of Allah, I did not come to you until I left it like a mangy camel.\" The Prophet ﷺ said, \"O Allah, bless the horses of Aḥmas and its men.\""],[3533,"He came to the Prophet ﷺ in a group from ʿAbd al-Qays to visit him. They approached, and when they arrived, the Prophet ﷺ was raised for them. They made their mounts kneel, and the people hurried off, wearing only their traveling clothes. Al-ʿAṣarī stayed behind, hobbled the mounts of his companions and his own camel, then took out his clothes from his saddlebag—all this under the eyes of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. Then he came to the Prophet ﷺ and greeted him. The Prophet ﷺ said to him, \"You have two qualities that Allah and His Messenger love.\" He said, \"What are they?\" He said, \"Deliberateness and forbearance.\" He said, \"Is it something I was created with, or something I have acquired?\" He said, \"No, rather you were created with it.\" He said, \"Praise be to Allah.\" Then the Prophet ﷺ said, \"O people of ʿAbd al-Qays, why do I see your faces have changed?\" They said, \"O Prophet of Allah, we live in a land with unhealthy climate, and we used to take some of these beverages that cut the meat in our stomachs. When we were forbidden from containers, that is what you see in our faces.\" The Prophet ﷺ said, \"Containers do not make things lawful or unlawful, but every intoxicant is unlawful. It is not that you should hold back and drink until your veins swell, then you fight one another, and a man jumps on his cousin and strikes him with a sword, leaving him crippled.\" He said: And on that day among the people was the crippled man who had suffered that."],[3534,"The Prophet ﷺ said to Ashajj ʿAbd al-Qays, \"You have two qualities that Allah loves: forbearance and deliberateness.\""],[3535,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ granted him a piece of land, and sent Mu'awiya with him, saying, 'Give it to him.' Mu'awiya said, 'Let me ride behind you.' He said, 'Do not be of those who ride behind kings.' Mu'awiya said, 'Give me your sandal.' He said, 'Shade yourself with the shadow of the she-camel.' When Mu'awiya became caliph, I came to him, and he seated me with him on the couch, and he mentioned the hadith to me, saying, 'I wish I had carried him in front of me.'"],[3536,"The cavalry of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, or the messengers of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, came and took my paternal aunt and some people. When they brought them to the Prophet ﷺ and lined them up before him, she said, 'O Messenger of Allah, the visitor has gone far away, and the offspring have been cut off. I am an old woman, of no use for service, so show favor to me, may Allah show favor to you.' He ﷺ said, 'And who is your visitor?' She said, ''Adi b. Hatim.' He said, 'The one who fled from Allah and His Messenger.' She said, 'So show favor to me.' When he returned—and a man beside him, whom we think was 'Ali—said, 'Ask him for a mount.' She said, 'So I asked him, and he ordered one for her.' She said, 'Then I came to him and said, \"You have done a deed your father would never have done. Come to him, whether desiring or fearing, for so-and-so came to him and obtained something from him, and so-and-so came to him and obtained something from him.\" So I came to him, and there was with him a woman and children—or a child—mentioned as being near the Prophet ﷺ, and I knew that he was not a king like Chosroes or Caesar. He said to me, \"O 'Adi b. Hatim, what makes you flee from saying 'There is no god but Allah'? Is there any god but Allah? What makes you flee from saying 'Allah is greater'? Is there anything greater than Allah?\" He said, 'So I embraced Islam, and I saw the face of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ bright with joy, and he said, \"Those upon whom is anger are the Jews, and those who go astray are the Christians.\"'"],[3537,"We were with the Prophet ﷺ in one of his expeditions. One night I went out and did not find the Messenger of Allah ﷺ in his place, and his companions were as if birds were on their heads, and the camels had laid down their necks. I looked, and behold, a figure appeared to me, and it was Mu'adh b. Jabal. I said, 'Where is the Messenger of Allah ﷺ?' He said, 'Behind me.' Then another figure appeared to me, and it was Abu Musa al-Ash'ari. I said, 'Where is the Messenger of Allah ﷺ?' He said, 'Behind me.'"],[3538,"When the Messenger of Allah ﷺ stopped at Dhu Tuwa, Abu Quhafa said to a daughter of his, one of his youngest children, 'O my little daughter, show me Abu Qubays.' She said—and his sight had failed—so she took him up to it. He said, 'O my little daughter, what do you see?' She said, 'I see a gathered black mass.' He said, 'That is the cavalry.' She said, 'And I see a man running before that black mass, coming and going.' He said, 'That, my little daughter, is the commander who directs the cavalry and goes ahead of it.' Then she said, 'By Allah, the black mass has spread out.' He said, 'By Allah, the cavalry has been let loose. Hurry with me to my house.' She descended with him, but the cavalry met him before he reached his house. On the girl's neck was a necklace of silver coins, and a man met her and snatched it from her neck. She said, 'When the Messenger of Allah ﷺ entered and entered the mosque, Abu Bakr ؓ brought his father, leading him. When the Messenger of Allah ﷺ saw him, he said, \"Why did you not leave the old man in his house so that I could come to him?\" Abu Bakr ؓ said, \"O Messenger of Allah, he has more right to walk to you than you to walk to him.\" He seated him before him, then wiped his chest, then said to him, \"Submit.\" So he submitted. She said, 'Abu Bakr ؓ brought him to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and his head was like a white flower. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, \"Change this hair of his.\" Then Abu Bakr stood up, took his sister by the hand, and said, \"I adjure you by Allah and Islam—my sister's necklace.\" No one answered him. He said, \"O my little sister, count your necklace as lost, for by Allah, trustworthiness among people today is scarce.\""],[3539,"The Muslims would not look at Abu Sufyan or sit with him. He said, 'O Messenger of Allah, three qualities I ask you to grant me.' He said, 'What are they?' He said, 'I have the most beautiful and finest of Arab women, Umm Habiba; I will marry her to you.' He said, 'Yes.' He said, 'And Mu'awiya, make him a scribe before you.' He said, 'Yes.' He said, 'And appoint me as a commander so that I may fight the polytheists as I used to fight the Muslims.' He said, 'Yes.'"],[3540,"I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ inviting to the pre-dawn meal in the month of Ramadan, and he said, \"Come to the blessed meal.\""],[3541,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, 'I am your share from among the prophets, and you are my share from among the nations.'"],[3542,"I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say while standing on the pulpit: «Your remaining among those who came before you is only like the time between the afternoon prayer and sunset. The people of the Torah were given the Torah and acted upon it until midday, then they were unable, so they were given a qirat each. The people of the Gospel were given the Gospel and acted upon it until the afternoon prayer, then they were unable, so they were given a qirat each. You were given the Quran and acted upon it until sunset, so you were given two qirats each. The people of the Torah and the Gospel said: Our Lord, these have done less work but have more reward. Allah, Blessed and Exalted, said: Have I wronged you in any of your reward? They said: No. He said: It is My bounty; I give it to whom I will.»"],[3543,"I saw seventy of the Companions of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ on the Bench, none of them had a cloak except a waist-wrapper or a garment wrapped over one shoulder, having tied it behind his back."],[3544,"«The best of people are my generation, then those who follow them, then those who follow them. Then will come a people whose one's testimony will precede his oath and his oath his testimony.»"],[3545,"«The best of my community is the generation that follows me, then those who follow them, then those who follow them. Then will come a people whose one's testimony will precede his oath and his oath his testimony.»"],[3546,"The Prophet ﷺ said, \"The best people are those of my generation, and then those who will come after them (the next generation), and then those who will come after them (i.e. the next generation), and then after them, there will come people whose witness will precede their oaths, and whose oaths will precede their witness.\" (Using translation from Bukhārī 6429)"],[3547,"«The best of people are my generation, then those who follow them, then those who follow them, then those who follow them.»"],[3548,"A man said to him: O Messenger of Allah, blessed is the one who saw you and believed in you. He said: «Blessed is the one who saw me and believed in me, and blessed, then blessed is the one who believed in me and did not see me.»"],[3549,"«Among the most intense of my community in love for me are a people who will be after me; one of them would wish that he had seen me, even with his family and wealth.»"],[3550,"\"Glad tidings to the one who saw me and believed in me, and glad tidings seven times to the one who believed in me and did not see me.\""],[3551,"\"Glad tidings to the one who saw me then believed in me, and glad tidings seven times to the one who believed in me and did not see me.\""],[3552,"A time will come upon people when a group of them goes on a military expedition, and it will be said: Is there among you anyone who accompanied the Messenger of Allah ﷺ? It will be said: Yes, and victory will be granted to them. Then a time will come upon people when a group of them goes on a military expedition, and it will be said: Is there among you anyone who accompanied the Companions of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ? It will be said: Yes, and victory will be granted to them. Then a time will come upon people when a group of them goes on a military expedition, and it will be said: Is there among you anyone who accompanied the companions of the Companions of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ? It will be said: Yes, and victory will be granted to them."],[3553,"That the Messenger of Allah ﷺ intended to attack them, so the Messenger of Allah ﷺ pointed to the woman who had the Book with her, so he sent to her and took her book from her head and said, \"O Hatib, what have you done?\" He said, \"Yes, I did it not out of deceit for the Messenger of Allah ﷺ nor hypocrisy, but I knew that Allah would expose His Messenger ﷺ and fulfill His command, except that I was a stranger among them, and my family was with them, so I wanted to make them feel comfortable. Then Umar ibn al-Khattab said, \"Shouldn't I strike the head of this man?\" The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, \"Would you kill a man from the people of Badr? And how do you know, perhaps Allah has looked upon the people of Badr?\" So he said, \"Do as you please.\""],[3554,"A man of the Ansar became blind, so he sent to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ: 'Come and mark out a mosque in my house that I may take as a place of prayer.' The Messenger of Allah ﷺ came, and his people gathered to him, but one man among them remained behind. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: 'Where is so-and-so?' Some of the people nudged him, meaning that he is such and such. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: 'Did he not witness Badr?' They said: 'Yes, O Messenger of Allah, but he is such and such.' The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: 'Perhaps Allah looked upon the people of Badr and said: Do what you will, for I have forgiven you.'"],[3555,"Jibril or an angel came to the Prophet ﷺ and said: How are the people of Badr among you? The Prophet ﷺ said: «They are, among us, the most excellent of people.» He said: And likewise those of the angels who were present at Badr are, among us, the most excellent."],[3556,"A slave of Hatib came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ complaining about Hatib. He said: 'O Messenger of Allah, Hatib will surely enter the Fire.' The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: 'You lie; he will not enter it, for he witnessed Badr and al-Hudaybiyyah.'"],[3557,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said while he was in Hafsa's house: 'No man who witnessed Badr and al-Hudaybiyyah will enter the Fire.' Hafsa said: 'O Messenger of Allah, did not Allah say: {And there is none of you but will come to it}?' The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: 'Then what about {Then We will save those who feared}?'"],[3558,"'You count the conquest as the conquest of Makkah; and the conquest of Makkah was indeed a conquest, but we count the conquest as the pledge of al-Ridwan on the day of al-Hudaybiyyah.' He said: 'We were with the Prophet ﷺ one hundred and fourteen; and al-Hudaybiyyah is a well, so we drew from it and did not leave a drop in it. That reached the Prophet ﷺ, so he came to it and sat on its edge, then called for a vessel of water, performed ablution and rinsed his mouth, and supplicated, then poured it into it. We left it not long before it gave us and our mounts to drink as much as we wished.'"],[3559,"'None of those who pledged allegiance under the tree will enter the Fire.'"],[3560,"I heard Abdullah ibn Abi Awfa saying, \"On the Day of the Tree (i.e. Hudaybiyyah), we were one thousand three hundred, and on that day, the tribe of Aslam was an eighth of the Muhajirun. May Allah have mercy on them.\""],[3561,"He said on the day of the conquest: “There is no hijrah, but rather jihad and intention. When you are called to mobilize, then mobilize.”"],[3562,"“Hijrah will not cease as long as the disbelievers are fought.”"],[3563,"I was with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ during the Farewell Pilgrimage, and I fell ill with an illness that brought me near death. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ visited me, and I said: O Messenger of Allah, I have much wealth and no one inherits from me except a daughter. Should I bequeath two-thirds of my wealth? He said: 'No.' I said: Then half of my wealth? He said: 'No.' I said: Then a third of it? He said: 'A third, and a third is much. Indeed, O Sa'd, to leave your heirs wealthy is better for you than to leave them poor, begging from people. You will never spend an expenditure seeking thereby the face of Allah except that you will be rewarded for it, even a morsel you put in your wife's mouth.' I said: O Messenger of Allah, will I be left behind after my companions? He said: 'You will never be left behind after me and perform a deed seeking thereby the face of Allah except that you will increase in degree and elevation by it. Perhaps you will be left behind after me, and Allah will benefit through you some people and harm others through you. O Allah, complete for my Companions their emigration and do not turn them back on their heels. But the unfortunate one is Sa'd b. Khawlah.' The Messenger of Allah ﷺ expressed grief for him, as he had died in Makkah."],[3564,"For the Emigrants there will be pulpits of gold on which they will sit on the Day of Resurrection, safe from the terror.” Abu Sa'id al-Khudri said: “By Allah, if I were to gift it to anyone, I would gift it to my people.”"],[3565,"I went with ʿUbayd b. ʿUmayr until we entered upon ʿĀʾishah. ʿUbayd b. ʿUmayr asked her about hijrah, and she said: “There is no hijrah after the conquest,” or she said, “after today. People used to flee with their religion to Allah and His Messenger from being tried, and Allah has now spread Islam, so wherever a servant wishes, he can worship his Lord.”"],[3566,"“Actions are but by intentions, and every person will have what he intended. Whoever’s hijrah was to Allah and His Messenger, his hijrah is to Allah and His Messenger. Whoever’s hijrah was for this world to attain it or for a woman to marry her, then his hijrah is to what he migrated for.”"],[3567,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to love that the Muhajirun and the Ansar be closest to him so that they might preserve from him."],[3568,"The Companions of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to say while they were digging the trench: [missing]"],[3569,"“When the call to prayer—the morning prayer—is given, and one of you is in a state of major impurity, he must not fast that day.”"],[3570,"The Prophet ﷺ came out one day with his head bandaged. The children and servants of the Helpers met him—not the men of the Helpers that day. He said, “By the One in whose hand is my soul, I love you,” two or three times. Then he said, “The Helpers have fulfilled what was upon them, and what is upon you remains, so be good to their good-doers and overlook their wrongdoers.”"],[3571,"“Whoever loves the Helpers, Allah and His Messenger love him. Whoever hates the Helpers, he hates Allah and His Messenger. None loves them but a believer, and none hates them but a hypocrite.”"],[3572,"There were young men from the Helpers called the reciters who would be in a corner of Madinah. Their families would think they were in the mosque, and the people of the mosque would think they were with their families. They would pray at night until near dawn, then they would gather firewood and draw water and place it at the doors of the rooms of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. He sent them all to the well of Ma'unah, and they were martyred, so the Prophet ﷺ supplicated against their killers for some days."],[3574,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ wanted to write for the Ansar regarding Bahrain. They said, \"No, not until you write for our companions from Quraysh the like of that.\" He said, \"You will encounter after me favoritism, so be patient until you meet me at the Pond.\""],[3575,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ once visited the Anṣār tribe of Bahrain or a group among them. They said, \"Do not cut off our brothers among the Muhājirīn (those who migrated from Mecca to Medina) like you cut off us.\" He said, \"Indeed, you will meet me after my departure, so be patient until you meet me.\""],[3576,"Usayd b. Hudayr al-Ashhalī, the Naqīb, came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and mentioned to him a household of the Ansar who were in need. He said—and he had already distributed some food—so the Prophet ﷺ said, \"You left us until what was in our hands was gone. So when you hear of something that has come to us, remind me of that household.\" He said: Then after that, food came to him from Khaybar: barley and dates. He said: And most of the people of that household were women. He said: So he distributed among the people and distributed among the Ansar, and he gave generously; and he distributed to the people of that household and gave generously. Usayd b. Hudayr said to him, thanking him: \"May Allah reward you, O Prophet of Allah, with the best reward on our behalf\"—or he said, \"with good.\" The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, \"And you, O assembly of the Ansar, may Allah reward you with the best reward\"—or he said, \"with good. I have known you to be chaste and patient, and you will see after me favoritism in command and livelihood, so be patient until you meet me at the Pond.\""],[3577,"Some people of the Ansar said on the day of Hunayn, when Allah gave His Messenger as spoils from the wealth of Hawazin what He gave, and the Messenger of Allah ﷺ began giving men of Quraysh one hundred camels each. They said, \"May Allah forgive His Messenger; he gives Quraysh and leaves us while our swords are dripping with their blood.\" Anas said: So I told the Messenger of Allah ﷺ of their saying. He sent for the Ansar and gathered them in a leather tent. When they had gathered, the Messenger of Allah ﷺ came to them and said, \"What is this report that has reached me from you?\" A group of the Ansar said to him, \"As for our elders, O Messenger of Allah, they said nothing; but some young men among us said, 'May Allah forgive His Messenger; he gives some people while our swords are dripping with their blood.'\" The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, \"I give men who are recent in disbelief, seeking to win their hearts. Are you not satisfied that the people go with wealth and you return to your dwellings with the Messenger of Allah? By Allah, what you return with is better than what they return with.\" They said, \"Yes, O Messenger of Allah, we are satisfied.\" He said, \"You will find severe favoritism, so be patient until you meet Allah and His Messenger at the Pond.\" They said, \"We will be patient.\""],[3578,"“No man who believes in Allah and the Last Day hates the Helpers.”"],[3579,"I saw al-Hajjaj beating ʿAbbas b. Sahl during the rule of Ibn al-Zubayr. Sahl b. Saʿd came to him—an old man with two braids, wearing two garments, an izār and a ridāʾ—and stood between the two rows and said, \"O Hajjaj, do you not preserve among us the testament of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ?\" He said, \"And what did the Messenger of Allah ﷺ enjoin regarding you?\" He said, \"He enjoined that good be done to the good-doer of the Ansar and that their wrongdoer be pardoned.\""],[3580,"“The Helpers are my bosom and my treasury. The people will increase and they will decrease, so accept from their good-doers and pardon their wrongdoers.”"],[3581,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ distributed the spoils of Hunayn and gave al-Aqra' b. Habis a hundred camels and 'Uyaynah b. Badr a hundred camels, and he mentioned a number of the Helpers. They said, “O Messenger of Allah, you give our spoils to people whose swords are dripping with our blood—or our blood is dripping from their swords.” That reached him, so he gathered the Helpers and said, “Are there among you other than you?” They said, “No, except the son of our sister.” He said, “The son of a people’s sister is one of them.” Then he said, “O assembly of Helpers, do you not wish that the people go with this world—or with sheep and camels—and you go with Muhammad to your homes?” They said, “Yes, O Messenger of Allah.” He said, “By the One in whose hand is the soul of Muhammad, if the people took a valley and the Helpers took a mountain pass, I would take the mountain pass of the Helpers. The Helpers are my bosom and my treasury. Were it not for the Hijrah, I would be a man of the Helpers.”"],[3582,"\"O Allah, forgive the Ansar, the sons of the Ansar, and the sons of the sons of the Ansar.\""],[3583,"The Prophet ﷺ came out one day with his head bandaged, and the Helpers met him with their men and youths. He said, “By the One in whose hand is the soul of Muhammad, I love you. The Helpers have fulfilled what was upon them, and what is upon you remains, so be good to their good-doers and overlook their wrongdoers.”"],[3585,"\"O Allah, forgive the Ansar, the offspring of the Ansar, the offspring of their offspring, and the freed slaves of the Ansar.\""],[3586,"\"O Allah, forgive the Ansar, the offspring of the Ansar, the offspring of their offspring, their freed slaves, and their neighbors.\""],[3587,"\"Shall I inform you of the best dwellings of the Ansar?\" They said, \"Yes, O Messenger of Allah.\" He said, \"The dwellings of Banu al-Najjar, then the dwellings of Banu ʿAbd al-Ashhal, then the dwellings of Banu al-Harith b. al-Khazraj, then the dwellings of Banu Saʿidah; and in every dwelling of the Ansar there is good.\""],[3588,"\"Shall I inform you of the best homes of the Ansar?\" They said, \"Yes, O Messenger of Allah.\" He said, \"The home of Banu al-Najjar, then the home of Banu ʿAbd al-Ashhal, then the home of Banu al-Harith b. al-Khazraj, then the home of Banu Saʿidah; and in every home of the Ansar there is good.\""],[3589,"\"Shall I inform you of the best homes of the Ansar?\" They said, \"Yes, O Messenger of Allah.\" He said, \"The home of Banu ʿAbd al-Ashhal, and they are the clan of Saʿd b. Muʿadh.\" They said, \"Then who, O Messenger of Allah?\" He said, \"Then Banu al-Najjar.\" They said, \"Then who, O Messenger of Allah?\" He said, \"Then Banu al-Harith b. al-Khazraj.\" They said, \"Then who, O Messenger of Allah?\" He said, \"Then Banu Saʿidah.\" They said, \"Then who, O Messenger of Allah?\" He said, \"In every home of the Ansar there is good.\" That reached Saʿd b. ʿUbadah, and he said, \"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ mentioned us last of four homes. I will certainly speak to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ about that.\" A man said to him, \"Are you not satisfied that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ mentioned you last of the four? By Allah, the Messenger of Allah ﷺ left out of the Ansar more than he mentioned.\" So Saʿd returned."],[3590,"\"Concerning us was revealed, 'When two parties among you were about to lose heart, but Allah was their protector' (Qur'an 3:122): Banu Salimah and Banu Harithah.\""],[3591,"The Muhajirun and the Ansar are allies of one another in this world and the Hereafter. And the Tulaqa' from Quraysh and the 'Utaqa' from Thaqif are allies of one another in this world and the Hereafter."],[3592,"“A woman who alights between two houses of the Helpers, or alights between her two parents, is not harmed.”"],[3593,"I went on the campaign to Tabuk with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. When he returned, we traveled one night, and I rode close to him. Drowsiness overcame me, and I kept waking up, but my mount had drawn near his mount, and its closeness frightened me, fearing I might strike his foot in the stirrup. So I kept pulling back my mount until my eyes overcame me in part of the night, and my mount jostled his mount while his foot was in the stirrup, and I struck his foot. I did not wake except at his saying 'Hass'. I raised my head and said: Seek forgiveness for me, O Messenger of Allah. He said: 'Proceed.' Then the Messenger of Allah ﷺ began asking me about those who stayed behind from Banu Ghifar, and I informed him. Then he said: 'What did the group of reddish men with sparse hair do?' I told him about their staying behind. He said: 'What did the group of black men with curly hair—or short hair—who have camels at Shabakat Sharkh do?' I tried to recall them among Banu Ghifar but could not remember them until I recalled a group from Aslam. I said: O Messenger of Allah, those are a group from Aslam and they stayed behind. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: 'What prevents those, when one of them stays behind, from carrying an energetic man on some of his camels in the path of Allah? The dearest of my people to me is that the Muhajirun and the Ansar, Aslam, and Ghifar should not stay behind from me.'"],[3594,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said concerning Ghifar: \"May Allah forgive her; and Aslam—may Allah keep them safe; and ʿUsayyah disobeyed Allah and His Messenger.\""],[3595,"Aslam, Ghifar, Juhaynah, and Muzaynah are better than Banu Tamim, Asad, Ghatfan, and Banu Amir b. Sa'sa'ah."],[3596,"Ghifar, Aslam, Muzaynah, and whoever is from Juhaynah are better than the two allies, Ghatfan and Asad, while Hawazin and Tamim are below them, for they are the people of horses and fur."],[3598,"The delegation of Banu Tamim came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and he said to them, \"Rejoice, O Banu Tamim.\" They said, \"You have given us glad tidings, so give us (something).\" The face of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ changed. Then the delegation of the people of Yemen came, and he said to them, \"Rejoice, O people of Yemen, since Banu Tamim did not accept the glad tidings.\""],[3599,"I entered upon the Prophet ﷺ with two men from Banu Amir, and he said, \"Who are you?\" We said, \"From Banu Amir.\" He ﷺ said, \"Welcome to you; you are from me.\""],[3600,"The people of Yemen have come to you. They have the softest hearts. Faith is Yemeni, understanding is Yemeni, and wisdom is Yemeni. Pride and arrogance are among the owners of camels, and composure is among the owners of sheep."],[3601,"While the Prophet ﷺ was in Madinah, he said, \"Allah is the Greatest, Allah is the Greatest! The help of Allah has come, and victory, and the people of Yemen have come—a people with pure hearts, soft obedience. Faith is Yemeni, understanding is Yemeni, and wisdom is Yemeni.\""],[3602,"The best of the people of the East are Abd al-Qays; the people accepted Islam unwillingly, but they accepted it willingly."],[3603,"The delegation of Abd al-Qays came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, \"Welcome to the delegation, not disgraced nor regretful.\" They said, \"O Messenger of Allah, between us and you are the polytheists of Mudar, and we can only reach you during the sacred months. So tell us of an action that, if we adopt it, we will enter Paradise, and we will call those behind us to it.\" He said, \"I command you with four and forbid you from four: faith in Allah.\" He said, \"Do you know what faith in Allah is?\" They said, \"Allah and His Messenger know best.\" He said, \"The testimony that there is no god but Allah, establishing prayer, giving zakat, fasting Ramadan, and giving the fifth of the spoils. And I forbid you from nabidh in gourds, hollowed stumps, green jars, and pitch-covered vessels.\""],[3604,"“People are followers of Quraysh in good and evil.”"],[3605,"“The Ansar are chaste and patient. And people follow Quraysh in this matter: their believer follows their believer, and their wicked follows their wicked.”"],[3606,"For a Qurashi there is the strength of two men from other than Quraysh."],[3607,"This affair will not cease to be in Quraysh as long as two people remain among mankind."],[3608,"The women of Quraysh are the best women who have ridden camels: the most tender to a child and the most attentive to a husband in what his hand possesses. Abu Hurayrah said, following that: And Maryam bt. ʿImrān never rode a camel at all."],[3609,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ proposed to Umm Hāniʾ bt. Abī Ṭālib, and she said: I have grown old and I have dependents. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: The best women who have ridden camels are the women of Quraysh: the most tender to her child in his infancy and the most attentive to a husband in what his hand possesses. And Maryam bt. ʿImrān never rode a camel at all."],[3610,"“No one endures its hardship and severity except that I will be an intercessor for him on the Day of Resurrection.”"],[3611,"Indeed, faith will retreat to al-Madinah just as a snake retreats to its hole."],[3612,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ bade farewell to a man and said, 'Where do you intend to go?' He said, 'I intend to go to the Holy House.' The Prophet ﷺ said, 'A prayer in this mosque is better than a hundred prayers in any other except the Sacred Mosque.'"],[3613,"A time will come upon people when a man will call his cousin and his relative: Come to ease, come to ease! Yet al-Madinah is better for them, if they only knew. By the One in whose hand is my soul, no one leaves it out of aversion for it except that Allah will leave behind in it one better than him. Indeed, al-Madinah is like a bellows: it expels the impurity. And the Hour will not occur until al-Madinah expels its wicked ones just as the bellows expel the dross of iron."],[3614,"A Bedouin gave allegiance to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ upon Islam. Then the Bedouin was afflicted with a fever in al-Madinah, so he left. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"Al-Madinah is only like a bellows: it expels its impurity and its goodness shines forth.\""],[3615,"The terror of al-Masih al-Dajjal will never enter al-Madinah. On that day it will have seven gates, at each gate two angels."],[3616,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said one day while we were with him, \"Blessings be upon the Sham (region).\" He said, \"Indeed, the angels of the Most Merciful spread their wings over it.\""],[3617,"A conquest was opened for the Messenger of God ﷺ, so I came to him and said, \"O Messenger of God, the horses have been let loose and they have laid down their weapons; war has laid down its burdens, and they say there is no fighting.\" The Messenger of God ﷺ said, \"They lie. Now fighting has come, now fighting has come. God, Mighty and Exalted, will cause the hearts of a people to deviate; they will fight them, and God will provide them from them until the command of God comes upon that. The main abode of the believers is Al-Sham.\""],[3618,"When the people of Sham become corrupt, there is no good in you."],[3619,"The Messenger of God ﷺ sent a man to a tribe among the Arab tribes for something—I do not know what he said—so they insulted him and beat him. He returned to the Prophet ﷺ and complained to him. He said, \"But the people of Oman, if my messenger came to them, they would not insult him or beat him.\""],[3620,"When we were with the Messenger of God ﷺ, it was revealed to him: {And others among them who have not yet joined them} (62:3). A man said, \"Who are these, O Messenger of God?\" He did not answer him. He repeated, and Salman passed by, so the Prophet ﷺ patted his shoulder and said, \"If faith were suspended from the Pleiades, men from the people of this one would attain it.\""],[3622,"From the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, who said, \"The poor believers will enter Paradise before the rich by half a day, five hundred years.\""],[3623,"While I was sitting in the mosque, a circle of poor Emigrants was sitting in the middle of the mosque. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ entered the mosque at midday and went to them and sat with them. When I saw that the Prophet ﷺ sat with them, I went to him and caught part of his speech: \"Give glad tidings to the poor Emigrants that they will enter Paradise before the rich by forty years.\""],[3624,"\"The poor Emigrants will outstrip the rich on the Day of Resurrection by seventy or forty autumns.\""],[3625,"Wealth is not from abundance of goods; wealth is only wealth of the soul."],[3626,"Zayd b. Thabit came out from Marwan's presence at midday. He said: I said, 'He did not send for him at this hour except for something he asked him about.' So I asked him, and he said: 'He asked us about things we heard from the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: \"May Allah brighten [the face of] a man who hears a hadith from us and conveys it to another, for perhaps a bearer of fiqh conveys it to one who has more fiqh than him, and perhaps a bearer of fiqh is not a faqih. Three things the heart of a Muslim never bears malice over: sincerity in action for Allah, giving good counsel to those in authority, and holding fast to the community, for their supplication surrounds what is behind them. Whoever has the world as his intention, Allah scatters his affairs for him and places his poverty before his eyes, and nothing of the world comes to him except what has been decreed for him. Whoever has the Hereafter as his intention, Allah gathers his affairs for him and places his wealth in his heart, and the world comes to him while it is compelled.\""],[3627,"While I was with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ in the mosque, he said, \"Look at the highest man in the mosque in your eyes.\" I looked, and there was a man in a fine garment sitting and talking to some people. I said, \"This one.\" He said, \"Look at the lowest man in the mosque in your eyes.\" He said, I looked, and there was a poor little man in a worn garment of his. I said, \"This one.\" The Prophet ﷺ said, \"This one is better with Allah on the Day of Resurrection than the whole earth full of the like of this one.\""],[3628,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, \"O Abu Dharr! Do you think that having a lot of wealth is wealth?\" I said, \"Yes, O Messenger of Allah.\" He said, \"Do you think that having little wealth is poverty?\" I said, \"Yes, O Messenger of Allah.\" He said, \"Indeed, true wealth is the richness of the heart, and true poverty is the poverty of the heart.\" Then he asked me about a man from the Quraysh and said, \"Do you know so and so?\" I said, \"Yes, O Messenger of Allah.\" He said, \"How do you see him and how does he see you?\" I said, \"When he asks, he is given, and when he comes, he is welcomed.\" Then he asked me about a man from the people of As-Suffah (the poor companions who stayed in the Prophet's Mosque) and said, \"Do you know so and so?\" I said, \"No, by Allah, I don't know him, O Messenger of Allah.\" He said, \"So he continued to praise him and mention his virtues until I recognized him.\" So I said, \"I have recognized him, O Messenger of Allah.\" He said, \"How do you see him or how do you perceive him?\" I said, \"He is a poor man from the people of As-Suffah.\" He said, \"He is better than the entire world and everything in it.\" I said, \"O Messenger of Allah! Shouldn't he be given some of what others are given?\" He said, \"If he is given something good, then he is deserving of it. And if it is withheld from him, then he has been given a reward for it.\""],[3629,"The sun has never risen except with two angels at its sides calling out: 'O Allah, whoever spends, give him a successor; whoever withholds, give him ruin.'"],[3630,"The one among you who will catch up with me soonest is the one with the longest hand.\" She said: So they would stretch out to see which of them had the longest hand. She said: The one with the longest hand among us was Zaynab, because she used to work with her hand and give charity."],[3631,"The likeness of the miser and the giver of charity is like two men upon whom are two coats of iron, or two gardens, from their nipples to their collarbones. As for the spender, every time he gives charity and intends it, it departs from his skin until it erases his trace and surpasses his fingertips. As for the miser, every time he spends something and intends it, it sticks to him and each ring of it bites into its place, and he tries to widen it but it does not widen."],[3632,"“Every act of kindness is charity.”"],[3633,"“Allah will surely remember a people in this world upon comfortable beds, whom He will admit to the highest degrees.”"],[3634,"“The Muslim is one from whose tongue and hand the Muslims are safe.”"],[3635,"A man said: “O Messenger of Allah, which of the Muslims is best?” He said: “The one from whose tongue and hand the Muslims are safe.”"],[3636,"\"Seven shall be shaded by Allah under his shade on a day in which there is no shade except His Shade: A just Imam, a young person raised upon worshiping Allah, a man whose heart is attached to the Masjid when he leaves from it until he returns from it, two men who love each other for Allah's sake, coming together upon that, and parting upon that, a man who remembers Allah in privacy and his eyes swell with tears, a man invited by a woman of status and beauty, but he says: 'I fear Allah, Mighty and Sublime is He,' and a man who conceals the charity he gives such that his left hand does not know what his right hand has spent.\" (Using translation from Tirmidhī 2391)"],[3637,"“Shall I inform you of the best of people? Indeed the best of people is a man who holds the rein of his horse in the cause of Allah. And shall I inform you of the one who follows him? A man who secludes himself with his sheep, fulfilling Allah’s right among them. And shall I inform you of the worst of people? A man who is asked by Allah and does not give by Him.”"],[3638,"A man came to the Prophet ﷺ and said: O Messenger of Allah, which deeds are most excellent? He said: “A man who strives in the cause of Allah with his wealth and his self.” He said: Then who? He said: “A believer in a mountain pass among the mountain passes who worships Allah and leaves people safe from his evil.”"],[3639,"The best of you are those with the softest shoulders in prayer."],[3640,"There was a man—I do not know anyone from the people of Madinah who prays toward the qiblah and attends prayer with the Prophet ﷺ who lived farther from the mosque than him. It was said: If only you bought a donkey to ride in the heat or the dark. He said: It would not please me that my house be adjacent to the mosque. That was mentioned to the Prophet ﷺ, and the Prophet ﷺ said: \"May Allah give you all of that, or may Allah give you what you hoped for.\""],[3641,"There was a man—I do not know any person from the people of Madinah who prays toward the qiblah who lived farther from the mosque than that man. He said: I said: If only you bought a donkey to ride in the dark or the heat? He said: So the matter reached the Prophet ﷺ, and he asked him. He said: O Prophet of Allah, I wanted my going to the mosque when I go, and my returning when I return, to be recorded for me. He said: The Prophet ﷺ said: \"May Allah give you all of that. May Allah give you all that you hoped for.\""],[3642,"A poor woman came to me along with her daughters. I gave her three dates. She gave a date to each of them and then she took up one date and brought that to her mouth in order to eat that, but her daughters expressed desire to eat it. She then divided the date that she intended to eat between them. This (kind) treatment of her impressed me and I mentioned that which she did to Messenger of Allah ﷺ. Thereupon he said: Verily Allah has assured Paradise for her, because of (this act) of her, or He has rescued her from Hell-Fire. (Using translation from Muslim 2630)"],[3643,"'If the believer knew what punishment Allah has, no one would hope for His Paradise; and if the disbeliever knew what mercy Allah has, no one would despair of His Paradise.'"],[3644,"Indeed, among the servants of Allah are those who, if they were to swear by Allah, He would fulfill their oath."],[3645,"The sister of al-Rabi', Umm Harithah, wounded a person. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, 'Retaliation, retaliation.' Umm al-Rabi' said, 'O Messenger of Allah, will you exact retaliation from so-and-so? No, by Allah, you will not exact retaliation from her.' They did not cease until they were satisfied with the blood money. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, 'Indeed, among the servants of Allah are those who, if they were to swear by Allah, He would fulfill their oath.'"],[3646,"\"If a fasting person eats or drinks forgetfully, let him complete his fast, for Allah has fed him and given him drink.\""],[3647,"«Indeed, Shaytan sat for the son of Adam on the path of Islam and said to him, ‘Will you submit and abandon your religion and the religion of your forefathers?’ But he disobeyed him and submitted, and he was forgiven. Then he sat for him on the path of emigration and said to him, ‘Will you emigrate and abandon your land and your sky?’ But he disobeyed him and emigrated. Then he sat for him on the path of jihad and said to him, ‘Will you fight, though it is the exertion of self and wealth? You will fight and kill, and then women will be married and wealth divided.’ But he disobeyed him and fought.’» The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: «So whoever does that and then dies, it is incumbent upon Allah to admit him to Paradise; or if he is killed, it is incumbent upon Allah to admit him to Paradise; and if he drowns, it is incumbent upon Allah to admit him to Paradise; or if a beast tramples him, it is incumbent upon Allah to admit him to Paradise.»"],[3648,"'Three Allah loves, and three Allah hates. As for those Allah loves: a man who came to a people and asked them by Allah, not asking them by kinship between them and him, and a man lagged behind them and gave him secretly, no one knowing of his gift except Allah and the one he gave; and a people who traveled through their night until sleep became dearer to them than anything they might equate with it, so they alighted, laid down their heads, and one stood appealing to Me and reciting My verses; and a man who was in a raiding party, met the enemy, and they were routed, and he advanced with his chest fighting or victory was opened for him. And three Allah hates: the adulterous old man, the arrogant poor man, and the oppressive rich man.'"],[3649,"That 'Itban b. Malik, who was one of the Companions of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and among those who witnessed Badr from the Ansar, came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and said, \"O Messenger of Allah, my eyesight has become weak, and I lead my people in prayer. When the rains come, the valley that is between me and them floods, and I am not able to come to their mosque to lead them in prayer. I wish that you, O Messenger of Allah, would come and pray in my house so that I may take it as a place of prayer.\" He said, so the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, «I will do so.» 'Itban said, so the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and Abu Bakr al-Siddiq went out in the morning when the day had risen, and the Messenger of Allah ﷺ asked permission, and I gave him permission. He did not sit until he entered the house, then he said, «Where would you like me to pray in your house?» He said, so I pointed to a corner of the house. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ stood and said the takbir, and we stood behind him, and he prayed two rak'ahs, then he said the salam. He said, and we detained him for a dish of khazirah that we had prepared for him. He said, then men from the people of the house gathered around him until a number of men had gathered in the house. One of them said, \"Where is Malik b. al-Dukhshun?\" Some of them said, \"That is a hypocrite, and he does not love Allah and His Messenger.\" The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to him, «Do not say that about him. Do you not see that he has said, \"There is no god but Allah,\" desiring thereby the face of Allah?» They said, \"Allah and His Messenger know best. We only see his face and his counsel for the hypocrites.\" The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, «Indeed Allah, Glorified and Exalted, has forbidden the Fire for one who says, \"There is no god but Allah,\" seeking thereby the face of Allah.»"],[3650,"When {And warn your nearest kindred} was revealed, the Messenger of Allah ﷺ stood up and said, 'O Fatimah bt. Muhammad, O Safiyyah bt. Abd al-Muttalib, O Banu Abd al-Muttalib, I cannot avail you anything before Allah. Ask me of my wealth whatever you wish.'"],[3651,"The people should be led in prayer by the one among them most versed in the Book of Allah. If they are equal in recitation, then the most knowledgeable of them in the Sunnah. If they are equal in the Sunnah, then the one of them who made hijrah first. If they are equal in hijrah, then the oldest of them in age. And a man must not lead another man in prayer in his domain of authority, nor sit in his place of honor except with his permission."],[3652,"Go out and announce among the people that there is no prayer except with the recitation of the Opening of the Book, and whatever is more [than that]."],[3653,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ led us in the dawn prayer, and the recitation became heavy upon him. When he had said the salam, he said, \"Do you recite behind me?\" We said, \"Yes.\" He said, \"Do not do so except with the Mother of the Book (Umm al-Kitab), for there is no prayer for one who does not recite it.\""],[3654,"\"Prayer during the night and day is two by two.\""],[3655,"The Prophet ﷺ said on the Day of the Trench, \"Occupying us from the middle prayer (Asr) has filled Allah's houses and their stomachs with fire.\""],[3656,"Glorification is for men and clapping is for women."],[3657,"\"A prayer is not valid if a man does not make his back straight in bowing and prostration.\""],[3658,"'If Allah were to hold me and the son of Mary accountable for what these two have committed—meaning the thumb and the one next to it—He would punish us, and He would not wrong us in anything.'"],[3659,"Paradise is surrounded by hardships, and Hellfire is surrounded by desires."],[3660,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ came to me with a distressed expression. She said: I thought that was due to some pain. I said: Why do I see you, may Allah bless you, with a distressed expression? He said: \"Because of the seven dinars that came to us yesterday and we did not distribute them.\""],[3661,"The Messenger of Allah, peace be upon him, drew a line for us and said, \"This is the path of Allah.\" Then he drew other lines to the right and left of it and said, \"These are paths, and there is a devil calling to each of them.\" Then he recited, \"{And indeed, this is My path, which is straight} until the end of the verse.\""],[3662,"Ali sent gold in tanned leather to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ from Yemen, and the Messenger of Allah ﷺ divided it among Zayd al-Khayl, al-Aqra' b. Habis, 'Uyaynah b. Hisn, and 'Alqamah b. 'Ulathah. Some people among the Muhajirun and Ansar said: We are more entitled to this. That reached the Prophet ﷺ and it distressed him. He said: Will you not trust me when I am the trustee of the One in heaven? The news of the One in heaven comes to me morning and evening. Then a man with protruding eyes, prominent cheekbones, a receding forehead, a thick beard, a shaved head, and a raised lower garment stood and said: O Messenger of Allah, fear Allah. The Prophet ﷺ said: Am I not the most entitled of the people of the earth to fear Allah? Then he turned away. Khalid, the sword of Allah, stood and said: O Messenger of Allah, shall I strike his neck? He said: No, perhaps he prays. Khalid said: How many a praying person says with his tongue what is not in his heart. He said: I have not been commanded to open people's hearts or split their bellies. He ﷺ looked at him while he was turning away and said: From the loins of this man will come a people who recite the Book of Allah but it does not pass their throats; they pass through the religion as an arrow passes through the target. 'Umarah said: I think he said: If I catch them, I will kill them as Thamud was killed."],[3663,"I sat with Abu Hanifah in Makkah, and a man came to him and said, \"I wore khuffs while in ihram\" or he said, \"I wore trousers while in ihram\"—Ibrahim was unsure. Abu Hanifah said to him, \"You owe a sacrifice.\" He said, \"I said to the man, 'Did you find sandals or find an izar?'\" He said, \"No.\" I said, \"O Abu Hanifah, this man claims he did not find them.\" He said, \"It is the same whether he found them or did not find them.\""],[3664,"A man asked the Prophet ﷺ what clothing the one in ihram may wear. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"He must not wear a shirt, turbans, trousers, hooded cloaks, or khuffs; except if someone cannot find sandals, then let him wear khuffs and cut them below the two ankles. And do not wear any clothing that wars or saffron has touched.\""],[3665,"I saw the Prophet ﷺ standing at Muzdalifah, and he said: \"Whoever prays this prayer of ours, then stays with us, and he had already stood at Arafat before that, by night or by day, his Hajj is complete.\""],[3666,"\"The Hajj is 'Arafat. Whoever reaches 'Arafat on the night of Jam' (Muzdalifah) before dawn breaks has caught (the Hajj). The days of Mina are three days. Whoever hastens in two days, there is no sin upon him, and whoever delays, there is no sin upon him.\""],[3667,"Safiyyah bt. Huyayy, the wife of the Prophet ﷺ, menstruated. This was mentioned to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and he said, \"Is she holding us back?\" It was said to him, \"She has already performed the ifadah.\" He said, \"Then no.\""],[3668,"He came with a letter from Quraysh to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. He said, 'When I saw the Prophet ﷺ, Islam was cast into my heart, and I said, \"O Messenger of Allah, by Allah, I will never return to them.\"' The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, 'I do not break treaties, and I do not detain messengers, but return to them. If what is in your heart now remains, then come back.' He said, 'I returned to them. Then I came back to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and embraced Islam.'"],[3669,"I came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ with my father and said, “O Messenger of Allah, my father has pledged allegiance for hijrah.” The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, “Rather, I will accept his pledge for jihad; hijrah has ceased.”"],[3670,"\"The injury caused by a beast is without liability, the well is without liability, and on treasure-trove one-fifth is due.\""],[3671,"\"The injury caused by a beast is without liability, the well is without liability, the mine is without liability, and on treasure-trove one-fifth is due.\""],[3672,"That she wanted to buy Barirah in order to manumit her, but they stipulated her wala'. That was mentioned to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, “Buy her and manumit her, for wala' belongs to the one who manumits.” And some meat was gifted to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. I said to the Prophet ﷺ, “This was given as charity to Barirah.” He said, “It is charity for her and a gift for us.”"],[3673,"Three Sunan were established because of Barirah. One of those Sunan was that she was set free and was given the choice concerning her husband; the Messenger of Allah said: 'Al Wala' is to the one who set the slave free;' and the Messenger of Allah entered when some meat was being cooked in a pot, but bread and some condiments were brought to him. He said: 'Do I not see a pot in which some meat is being cooked?' They said: 'Yes, O Messenger of Allah, that is meat that was given in charity to Barirah and you do not eat (food given in) charity.' The Messenger of Allah said: 'It is charity for her and a gift for us.' (Using translation from Nasāʾī 3447)"],[3674,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ passed by a dead sheep from the sadaqah that had been given to a freed slave woman of Maymunah. He said: \"Would they not take its hide, tan it, and benefit from it?\" They said: \"O Messenger of Allah, it is dead.\" The Prophet ﷺ said: \"Only its eating is forbidden.\""],[3675,"\"By the One besides whom there is no god, the blood of a man who bears witness that there is no god but Allah and that I am the Messenger of Allah is not lawful except for three persons: the one who abandons Islam and leaves the community, the previously married adulterer, and a life for a life.\""],[3676,"“There is nothing due on silver until it reaches five uqiyas; nothing is due on dates until they reach five wasqs; and nothing is due on camels until they reach five of the herd.”"],[3677,"“There is no sadaqah on less than five uqiyas; no sadaqah on less than five dhawd; and no sadaqah on less than five wasqs. And the wasq is sixty sa's.”"],[3678,"\"Whoever leaves wealth, it is for his heirs, and whoever leaves debt, it is to me and upon me.\""],[3679,"When the Messenger of Allah ﷺ died, the wives of the Prophet ﷺ wanted to send Uthman b. Affan to Abu Bakr al-Siddiq ؓ to ask him for their inheritance from the Prophet ﷺ. A'isha said to them: Did the Prophet ﷺ not say: \"We are not inherited from; what we leave is charity\"?"],[3680,"My heirs will not divide a single dinar after me. What I leave after the expenses of my dependents and the provision of my worker is charity."],[3681,"My heirs will not divide a single dinar. What I leave after the expenses of my wives and the provision of my worker is charity."],[3682,"\"O 'Amr, fasten your weapons and your clothes tightly.\" He said: I did so, then I came to him and found him performing ablution. He raised his head and gave me an upward and downward look. He said: \"O 'Amr, I intend to send you on an expedition, that Allah may keep you safe and grant you spoils, and I will assign you a good portion of wealth.\" I said: O Messenger of Allah, I did not accept Islam out of desire for wealth; I accepted Islam out of desire for jihad and to be with you. He said: \"O 'Amr, how excellent is righteous wealth with a righteous man.\""],[3683,"The servant says, 'My wealth,' but he has of his wealth only what he ate and consumed, or wore and wore out, or gave in charity and sent ahead. Whatever is besides that is departing and he leaves it to people."],[3684,"I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say, “If you follow the faults of people, you will corrupt them or risk corrupting them.”He said that Abū Dardāʾ said, “Muʿāwiyah heard [this] statement from the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and Allah benefited him by it.”"],[3685,"\"Whoever is granted a kindness and finds no reward for it except praise, has thanked for it; and whoever conceals it, has disbelieved in it. And whoever adorns himself with what is false is like one wearing two garments of falsehood.\""],[3686,"\"That the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) made a bond of brotherhood between Salman and Abu Darda. Salman visited Abu Darda and found Umm Darda in a bad state. Salman asked her: 'What is the matter with you?' She replied: 'Your brother (meaning Abu Darda) has no need in this world.' When Abu Darda returned, he welcomed Salman and presented food to him. Salman said: 'Eat.' Abu Darda said: 'I am fasting.' Salman said: 'I will not eat until you eat.' So, Abu Darda ate with him. Then when it was night, Abu Darda got up to offer the prayer, and Salman detained him. When the morning arrived, Abu Darda said: 'Stand up now.' Salman got up and they prayed together. When the Prophet (ﷺ) prayed Subh (morning prayer), he came to him and informed him of what Salman had said. The Prophet (ﷺ) said: 'He has spoken the truth.'\""],[3687,"«Each of you is a shepherd, and each of you is responsible. The ruler is a shepherd over the people and is responsible. A man is a shepherd over his household and is responsible. A woman is a shepherd over her husband's house and is responsible. A slave is a shepherd over his master's property and is responsible. Indeed, each of you is a shepherd, and each of you is responsible.»"],[3688,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ went out to Badr and met the enemy. When Allah defeated them, a group of the Muslims pursued them, killing them; another group surrounded the Messenger of Allah ﷺ; and another group took possession of the camp and the spoils. When Allah had sufficed against the enemy and those who had pursued them returned, they said, 'The extra share is ours: we pursued the enemy, and by us Allah expelled and defeated them.' The group that had surrounded the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, 'By Allah, you are not more entitled to it than we are; it is ours: we surrounded the Messenger of Allah ﷺ so that the enemy could not catch him off guard.' The group that had taken possession of the camp and the spoils said, 'By Allah, you are not more entitled to it than we are; it is ours.' Then Allah, Exalted, sent down: {They ask you about the spoils} (Qur'an 8:1), the verse. So the Messenger of Allah ﷺ divided it among them. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to give them an extra share of a fourth when they set out as raiders at the beginning of the expedition, and a third when they returned. He said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ took a piece of wool from the side of a camel on the day of Hunayn and said, 'O people, it is not lawful for me of what Allah has given you as booty even the amount of this, except the fifth, and the fifth is returned to you. So render the thread and the needle, and beware of ghulul, for it is a disgrace upon its owner on the Day of Resurrection. And upon you is jihad in the way of Allah, for it is a gate from the gates of Paradise by which Allah removes worry and grief.' He said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ disliked extra shares (anfal) and said, 'Let the strong of the believers return to their weak.'"],[3689,"«O people, whoever of you performs a task for us and conceals from us even a needle or anything above it, he is a misappropriator and will come with it on the Day of Resurrection.» Then a dark-skinned man stood up—I can almost see him, I think he was from the Ansar—and said, «Accept my work from me, O Messenger of Allah.» He said, «And what is that?» He said, «I heard you say what you said.» He said, «And I say it now: whoever we appoint to a task, let him bring its little and its much. Whatever he is given, he takes, and whatever he is forbidden, he refrains from.»"],[3690,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ took hold of the muscle of my calf and said, \"Here is the place of the lower garment; if you refuse, then here, and the lower garment has no right to the ankles.\""],[3691,"When the verse “And eat and drink until the white thread becomes distinct to you from the black thread” was revealed, the Prophet ﷺ said, “That is only the whiteness of day and the blackness of night.”"],[3692,"\"When the night approaches, the day departs, and the sun sets, the fasting person has broken his fast.\""],[3693,"\"Whoever finds dates, let him break his fast on them; whoever does not, let him break his fast on water, for it is purifying.\""],[3694,"\"The Messenger of Allah said: 'An orphan girl should be consulted with regard to marriage, and if she remains silent, that is her permission. If she refuses then she is not to be forced.'\" (Using translation from Nasāʾī 3270)"],[3695,"“When the infant cries out (at birth), funeral prayer is performed over him and he is inherited from.”"],[3696,"The Prophet ﷺ said, \"The boy is for (the owner of) the bed and the stone is for the person who commits illegal sexual intercourse.' (Using translation from Bukhārī 6818)"],[3697,"The fingers are equal. I said: Ten, ten? He said: Yes."],[3698,"The teeth are equal and the fingers are equal."],[3699,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ met me while I was in a state of major ritual impurity, and he reached out to me. I said: 'I am in a state of major ritual impurity.' He said: 'A Muslim does not become impure.'"],[3700,"When the Messenger of Allah ﷺ met a man from among his Companions, he would wipe over him and supplicate for him. He said: I saw him one day in the morning, so I turned away from him. Then I came to him after the day had risen, and he said: \"I saw you and you turned away from me.\" I said: \"I was in a state of major ritual impurity, and I feared that you would touch me.\" The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"A Muslim does not become impure.\""],[3701,"“The weight is the weight of Makkah, and the measuring vessel is the measuring vessel of the people of Madinah.”"],[3702,"'There is no contagion and no Tiyarah. A camel became mangy and made a hundred mangy; then who infected the first one?'"],[3703,"I met people from the Companions of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ who used to say, “Everything is by destiny.” Then I heard ʿAbd Allāh b. ʿUmar say: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, “Everything is by destiny, even inability and capability—or capability and inability.”"],[3704,"Subay'ah gave birth to her child twenty-three or twenty-five nights after her husband's death. When she gave birth, she adorned herself for suitors, and that was disapproved of for her. That was mentioned to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and he said, 'What prevents her? Her term has ended.'"],[3705,"\"O Messenger of Allah, would you like Durrah bint Abi Sufyan?\" He said: \"What would I do with her?\" She said: \"Marry her.\" He said: \"Is she lawful for me?\" She said: \"By Allah, I have been told that you are proposing to Zaynab bint Umm Salamah.\" The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"Zaynab is unlawful for me, for she is in my care, and Thuwaybah nursed both me and her. So do not offer me your daughters, nor your sisters, nor your paternal aunts, nor your maternal aunts, nor your mothers.\""],[3706,"A man looked in from a hole in the door of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and the Messenger of Allah had an iron comb with which he was scratching his head. When the Messenger of Allah ﷺ saw him, he said: \"If I knew that you were looking at me, I would have thrust it into your eye. Permission was ordained only for the sake of sight.\""],[3707,"\"If a person looked in upon you and you threw a pebble at his eye and gouged it out, there would be no sin upon you.\""],[3708,"\"A woman from the Muslims was captured by the polytheists, who had previously captured a camel belonging to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ . She found the people in a state of negligence and vowed that if Allah saved her, she would sacrifice the camel. He granted her safety and she arrived in the city, intending to sacrifice the camel. However, the people forbade her and the matter was brought to the attention of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ . He said, 'How bad is the way she intends to fulfill her vow!' Then he said, 'There is no fulfilling of a vow made by the son of Adam in disobedience to Allah or in something he does not possess.'\""],[3709,"Vineyards are assessed as date palms are assessed, then their zakāh is paid as raisins just as the zakāh of date palms is paid as dates."],[3710,"\"Hospitality is three days. Whatever is beyond that is charity.\""],[3712,"The Prophet ﷺ was brought dates from the dates of charity, and al-Hasan b. ʿAli took a date and chewed it in his mouth. The Prophet ﷺ said: \"Spit it out, spit it out! Indeed, charity is not lawful for us.\""],[3713,"Dates from the dates of charity were brought to Abu al-Qasim ﷺ. Al-Hasan b. ʿAli took a date and chewed it, so the Prophet ﷺ inserted his two fingers into his mouth and removed it, and said: \"Spit it out, O my little son. Did you not know that charity is not lawful for us?\""],[3714,"I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ saying, \"There is no punishment of more than ten lashes for anything below the prescribed limits of Allah's punishments.\""],[3715,"\"The wife of 'Uthman b. Maz'un came to the wives of the Prophet ﷺ and they saw her in a bad state. They said: 'What is with you? There is no man in Quraysh richer than your husband.' She said: 'We have nothing from him. As for his day, he is fasting, and as for his night, he is standing in prayer.' He said: 'Then the Prophet ﷺ entered and they mentioned that to him. So the Prophet ﷺ met him and said: \"O 'Uthman, do I not have an example for you?\" He said: \"And what is that, O Messenger of Allah, may my father and mother be your ransom?\" He said: \"As for you, you stand the night and fast the day, but your family has a right over you and your body has a right over you. Pray and sleep, fast and break your fast.\" He said: 'Then the woman came to them after that perfumed as if she were a bride, and they said to her: 'How [is it now]?' She said: 'We have been affected as the people have been affected.'\""],[3716,"A group of three men came to the houses of the wives of the Prophet ﷺ asking how the Prophet ﷺ worshipped (Allah), and when they were informed about that, they considered their worship insufficient and said, \"Where are we from the Prophet ﷺ as his past and future sins have been forgiven.\" Then one of them said, \"I will offer the prayer throughout the night forever.\" The other said, \"I will fast throughout the year and will not break my fast.\" The third said, \"I will keep away from the women and will not marry forever.\" Messenger of Allah ﷺ came to them and said, \"Are you the same people who said so-and-so? By Allah, I am more submissive to Allah and more afraid of Him than you; yet I fast and break my fast, I do sleep and I also marry women. So he who does not follow my tradition in religion, is not from me (not one of my followers). (Using translation from Bukhārī 5063)"],[3717,"We were with the Prophet ﷺ in the early part of the day when a group of people came, barefoot, naked, wearing striped cloaks, with swords, most of them from Mudar, indeed all of them from Mudar. I saw the face of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ change when he saw their poverty. He entered and ordered Bilal, who called the adhan and then the iqamah. He came out and prayed, then he said: 'O people, fear your Lord, who created you from one soul and created from it its mate and dispersed from both of them many men and women. And fear Allah, through whom you ask one another, and the wombs. Indeed Allah is ever, over you, an Observer. Fear Allah, and let every soul look to what it has put forth for tomorrow.' 'Let a man give charity from his dinar and from his dirham and from his garment and from a sa' of his wheat and from a sa' of his barley' until he mentioned half a date. Then a man from the Ansar came with a purse that his hands could hardly hold, indeed they could not. Then people followed one another until I saw before the Messenger of Allah ﷺ two heaps of clothes and food. I saw the face of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ brighten until it seemed gilded. Then he said: 'Whoever introduces a good practice in Islam and it is acted upon after him, he will have its reward and the reward of those who act upon it after him, without diminishing their rewards in any way. Whoever introduces an evil practice and it is acted upon after him, he will bear its burden and the burden of those who act upon it after him.'"],[3718,"“Whoever calls to guidance will have a reward like the rewards of those who follow him, without that diminishing their rewards in anything. And whoever calls to misguidance will bear a sin like the sins of those who follow him, without that diminishing their sins in anything.”"],[3719,"“The believer eats with one intestine and the disbeliever eats with seven intestines.’” (Using translation from Ibn Mājah 3256)"],[3720,"“A Muslim eats in one intestine, and a disbeliever eats in seven intestines.”"],[3721,"A disbelieving guest visited the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ ordered a sheep for him, and he drank its milk. Then another, and he drank its milk, until he drank the milk of seven sheep. Then he entered the morning and embraced Islam. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ ordered a sheep for him, it was milked, and he drank its milk. Then he ordered another for him, but he did not finish it. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, “The believer drinks in one intestine, and the disbeliever drinks in seven intestines.”"],[3722,"«The dead person is punished by the weeping of the living.»"],[3723,"«The dead person is punished by the weeping of his family over him.»"],[3724,"I attended the funeral of Abān b. ʿUthmān. Ibn ʿUmar came and sat down, and Ibn ʿAbbās came and sat down. Ibn ʿUmar said, \"Will you not prohibit these people from weeping? For I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say, 'Indeed, the dead person is punished by the weeping of his family over him.'\""],[3725,"He said to them, \"Do not weep, for the weeping of the living is punishment for the dead.\" ʿAmrah said, \"I asked ʿĀʾishah, and she said, 'May Allah have mercy on him. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ only said that about a Jewish woman whose family were weeping over her: \"Indeed, they are weeping, and she is being punished in her grave.\"'\""],[3726,"\"Muḥammad ﷺ saw his Lord.\""],[3727,"I said to Abu Dharr: If I had seen the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, I would have asked him about everything. He said: About what thing would you have asked him? He said: I would have asked him: Did you see your Lord? He said: I asked him, and he said: \"I saw light.\""],[3728,"\"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ saw Gabriel in a form of a ruby that filled the space between the heavens and the earth.\""],[3729,"\"The greatest fabrication against Allah is that one says that Muhammad ﷺ saw his Lord, and that Muhammad ﷺ concealed something of the revelation, and that Muhammad ﷺ knows what will be tomorrow.\" It was said: O Mother of the Believers, did he not see Him? She said: \"No, that was only Gabriel; he saw him twice in his true form: once when he filled the horizon, and once when he blocked the horizon of the sky.\""],[3730,"When he was buried, Umm Al-Ala said, \"May you have peace, Abu As-Saib, in Paradise.\" The Prophet of Allah ﷺ heard her and asked, \"Who is this?\" She replied, \"It is I, O Prophet of Allah.\" He asked, \"How do you know?\" She said, \"O Messenger of Allah, it is Uthman ibn Maz'un.\" The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, \"Indeed, Uthman ibn Maz'un—we have only seen good from him. Yet here I am, the Messenger of Allah ﷺ , and by Allah, I do not know what will happen to me.\""],[3731,"When the Prophet ﷺ married her, he stayed with her three [nights] and said: \"It is no dishonor to you among your family. If you wish, I will allocate seven [nights] for you; but if I allocate seven for you, I will allocate seven for my other wives.\""],[3732,"That when she arrived in Madinah, she informed them that she was the daughter of Abu Umayya b. al-Mughira, but they disbelieved her and began to say, \"How deceitful the strangers are!\" Then some of them decided to go on Hajj and said, \"Will you write to your family?\" So I wrote with them, and they returned to Madinah and believed her, and she increased in honor for them. She said: When I gave birth to Zaynab, the Prophet ﷺ came to me to propose. I said, \"A woman like me cannot be married. As for me, I have no child in me, and I am jealous, with dependents.\" He ﷺ said, \"I am older than you. As for jealousy, Allah will remove it. As for dependents, they are to Allah and His Messenger.\" So the Messenger of Allah ﷺ married her, and he said, \"I will come to you tonight.\" She said, \"So I brought out grains of barley that were in my jar and some fat, and I made 'asida for him.\" He spent the night, then morning came, and when he rose he said, \"You have honor with your family. If you wish, I will give you seven nights; but if I give you seven, I will give seven to my wives.\""],[3733,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to a man, “What do you say in prayer?” He said, “I recite the tashahhud, then I say: O Allah, I ask You for Paradise and I seek refuge in You from the Fire.”"],[3734,"\"I indeed know a stone in Makkah that used to greet me when I was sent as a prophet. I indeed know it now.\""],[3735,"While a shepherd was tending his sheep in the harrah, a wolf attacked one of his sheep. The shepherd came running and snatched it from him. The wolf said to the shepherd, 'Do you not fear Allah? You come between me and a provision that Allah has sent to me.' The shepherd said, 'How amazing! A wolf, sitting on its tail, speaking to me in human speech!' The wolf said to the shepherd, 'Shall I tell you something even more amazing? This is the Messenger of Allah ﷺ between the two harrahs, telling the people of the news of what has already happened.' The shepherd drove his sheep to Madinah, penned them in one of its corners, then entered upon the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and told him what the wolf had said. The Messenger of Allah came out and said to the shepherd, 'Stand and inform.' So he informed the people of what the wolf had said. And he ﷺ said, 'The shepherd has spoken the truth. Indeed, among the signs of the Hour is that wild animals will speak to humans. By the One in whose hand is my soul, the Hour will not come until wild animals speak to humans, a man speaks to his sandal and the strap of his whip, and his thigh tells him of what his family did after him.'"],[3736,"The moon split during the time of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ in Makkah."],[3737,"When the Messenger of Allah ﷺ arrived at Badr, he pointed to the ground and said, 'This is the place where so-and-so will fall, and this is the place where so-and-so will fall.' By Allah, none of them moved from the place where he fell. He left the dead of Badr for three days, then he came to them and stood over them and said, 'O Abu Jahl b. Hisham, O Umayyah b. Khalaf, O Utbah b. Rabi'ah, O Shaybah b. Rabi'ah, have you not found what your Lord promised you to be true? For I have found what my Lord promised me to be true.' Umar heard the words of the Prophet ﷺ and said, 'O Messenger of Allah, how can they hear you or respond when they have become corpses?' He said, 'By the One in whose hand is my soul, you are not more able to hear what I say than they are, but they cannot respond.' Then he ordered that they be dragged and thrown into the well of Badr."],[3738,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ sent me, al-Zubayr, Talhah, and al-Miqdad b. al-Aswad, saying, 'Go until you reach the garden of Khakh, for there is a woman with a letter. Take it from her.' We set off, our horses racing, until we reached the garden. There was the woman. We said to her, 'Bring out the letter.' She said, 'I have no letter.' We said, 'By Allah, you will bring out the letter or we will strip you of your clothes.' She took it out from her braids. We brought it to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and in it was from Hatib b. Abi Balta'ah to some of the polytheists of Makkah, informing them of some of the affairs of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, 'O Hatib, what is this?' He said, 'O Messenger of Allah, do not be hasty with me. I was a man allied to Quraysh, not one of them. The emigrants with you have relatives in Makkah who protect their relatives and families. I had no relative to protect my family, so I wanted, if I missed out on that kinship, to make a favor with them so they would protect my relatives and family. By Allah, O Messenger of Allah, I did not do this as apostasy from my religion or out of satisfaction with disbelief after Islam.' The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, 'This man has told you the truth.' Umar said, 'O Messenger of Allah, let me strike the neck of this hypocrite.' He ﷺ said, 'He witnessed Badr. What do you know? Perhaps Allah looked upon the people of Badr and said, \"Do what you wish, for I have forgiven you.\"' And He revealed concerning him: {O you who believe, do not take My enemy and your enemy as allies} the verse."],[3740,"We went out with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ to Tabuk until he came to Wadi al-Qura. There was a woman in her garden. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, 'Estimate the crop.' The people estimated ten wasqs. He said to the woman, 'Count what comes out of it until I return to you.' Then he traveled until he reached Tabuk. He said, 'A strong wind will come to you tonight, so no one should stand in it, and whoever has a camel should tie its hobble.' A strong wind blew, and no one stood in it except one man, and it threw him into the mountain of Tayy. The king of Aylah came to him and gifted him a white mule, and the Messenger of Allah ﷺ clothed him with his cloak. When the Messenger of Allah ﷺ returned, he came to Wadi al-Qura and said to the woman, 'How much did your garden produce?' She said, 'Ten wasqs, the estimate of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ.' Then the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, 'I am in a hurry. Whoever among you wishes to hasten with me, let him do so.' He traveled until he overlooked Madinah and said, 'This is Taybah, or Tabah.' When he saw Uhud, he said, 'This is a mountain that loves us and we love it.' Then he said, 'Shall I tell you of the best houses of the Ansar?' They said, 'Yes, O Messenger of Allah.' He said, 'The best houses of the Ansar are those of Banu al-Najjar. Shall I tell you of those who follow them?' They said, 'Yes, O Messenger of Allah.' He said, 'Banu Sa'idah and Banu al-Harith b. al-Khazraj.'"],[3741,"I slaughtered an animal for the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and he said, \"Hand me the foreleg.\" I handed it to him. Then he said, \"Hand me the foreleg.\" I handed it to him. Then he said, \"Hand me the foreleg.\" I said, \"O Messenger of Allah, a sheep has only two forelegs.\" He said, \"If you had looked for it, you would have found it.\""],[3742,"I incurred a debt of reconciliation, so I came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ to ask him for help with it. He ﷺ said: \"Stay, O Qabisa, until the zakah comes to us, and then we will order it for you.\" Then he said: \"O Qabisa, asking is not lawful except for one of three: a man who has incurred a debt of reconciliation, so asking is lawful for him until he obtains it, then he should refrain; or a man afflicted by a calamity that destroyed his wealth, so asking is lawful for him until he obtains a means of livelihood or a sufficiency of livelihood; or a man stricken by poverty such that three men of sound judgment from his people say: 'Poverty has indeed befallen so-and-so,' so asking is lawful for him until he obtains a means of livelihood or a sufficiency of livelihood. Whatever other asking is unlawful gain, and its owner consumes it as unlawful gain.\""],[3743,"“Every adult male must go to Jumu'ah, and whoever goes must bathe.”"],[3744,"\"The pen has been lifted from three: from the sleeper until he wakes, from the boy until he has a wet dream, and from the insane person until he regains his sanity.\""],[3745,"Ali b. Abi Talib ؓ passed by an insane woman of the Banu so-and-so who had committed adultery. Umar had ordered her stoning, but Ali turned her back and said to Umar, \"O Commander of the Believers, do you stone this one?\" He said, \"Yes.\" He said, \"Do you not remember that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, 'The pen has been lifted from three: from the insane person who is overcome in his mind, from the sleeper until he wakes, and from the child until he has a wet dream'?\" He said, \"You have spoken the truth,\" so he released her."],[3746,"The Prophet ﷺ set out from Makkah, and when he was at al-Rawha', a group of riders met him. He greeted them and said, \"Who are the people?\" They said, \"We are Muslims, so who are you?\" He said, \"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ.\" A woman among them became alarmed and lifted a small boy of hers from a litter, taking hold of his upper arm, and said, \"O Messenger of Allah, is there Hajj for this one?\" He said, \"Yes, and you will have a reward.\""],[3747,"«No one will enter Paradise in whose heart is a mustard seed's weight of arrogance, and no one will enter the Fire in whose heart is a mustard seed's weight of faith.»"],[3748,"'The one addicted to wine will not enter Paradise, nor the one who believes in sorcery, nor the one who severs kinship ties.'"],[3749,"“The child of fornication will not enter Paradise, nor the one who reminds others of his favors, nor the one who is disobedient to his parents, nor the one addicted to wine.”"],[3750,"“The one who is disobedient to his parents will not enter Paradise, nor the one who reminds others of his favors, nor the one addicted to wine.”"],[3751,"When Ziyad was claimed (as a son), I met Abu Bakrah and said, \"What is this that you have done? I heard Sa'd b. Abi Waqqas say: 'My ears heard and my heart retained that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"Whoever claims a father in Islam while knowing that he is not his father, Paradise is forbidden for him.\"'\". Abu Bakrah said, \"And I heard it from the Messenger of Allah ﷺ.\""],[3752,"Whoever kills a soul under covenant without its right, Allah has forbidden Paradise to him, that he should smell its fragrance."],[3753,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ ascended the pulpit, and when he reached the first step, he said, \"Ameen.\" Then he ascended another step and said, \"Ameen.\" Then he ascended a third step and said, \"Ameen.\" Then he said, \"Jibril came to me and said, 'O Muhammad, whoever reaches the month of Ramadan and is not forgiven, may Allah distance him.' I said, 'Ameen.' He said, 'Whoever reaches old age and both of his parents, or one of them, are not the reason for him to enter Paradise, may Allah distance him.' I said, 'Ameen.' He said, 'Whoever has your name mentioned in front of him and does not send blessings upon you, may Allah distance him.' I said, 'Ameen.' So I said, 'Ameen.'\""],[3754,"Jibril kept urging me to be good to the neighbor until I thought he would make him an heir."],[3755,"If I take away the two precious things of My servant and he is patient and seeks reward, I will not be satisfied with any reward for him less than Paradise.\""],[3756,"I said to Ubayy b. Ka'b, 'Ibn Mas'ud does not write the two Mu'awwidhat in his mushaf.' He said, 'The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to me, \"Jibril said to me, {Say: I seek refuge in the Lord of the daybreak}, and I said it, and he said to me, {Say: I seek refuge in the Lord of mankind}, and I said it.\" So we say what the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said.'"],[3757,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ came to Madinah, and Abdullah b. Salam was in his palm grove. Abdullah b. Salam came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and said: I will ask you about things that no one knows except a prophet. If you tell me them, I will believe in you. He asked him about resemblance, about the first thing that will gather the people, and about the first thing the people of Paradise will eat. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"Gabriel informed me about them just now.\" He said: That is the enemy of the Jews. So the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"As for resemblance, if the man's fluid precedes the woman's fluid, the child will resemble him, and if the woman's fluid precedes the man's fluid, the child will resemble her. The first thing that will gather the people is a fire that will come from the east and gather the people to the west. The first thing the people of Paradise will eat is the head of a bull and the liver of a whale.\" Then he said: O Messenger of Allah, the Jews are a slanderous people; if they hear of my belief in you, they will slander me and attack me. I would like you to send for them. So he sent for them and they came. He said: \"What do you say about Abdullah b. Salam?\" They said: He is our master and the son of our master, our scholar and the son of our scholar, our best and the son of our best. He ﷺ said: \"Do you think that if he accepts Islam, you will accept Islam?\" They said: May Allah protect him from saying that; he would never do it. He said: Come out, O Ibn Salam. So he came out to them and said: I bear witness that there is no god but Allah, and I bear witness that Muhammad is the Messenger of Allah. They said: Rather, he is our worst and the son of our worst, our ignoramus and the son of our ignoramus. He said: Did I not tell you, O Messenger of Allah, that they are a slanderous people?"],[3758,"Gabriel ﷺ came to the Prophet ﷺ, and in the house of the Prophet of Allah ﷺ there was a curtain with images on it, including statues. The Prophet of Allah ﷺ said, \"Enter.\" He said, \"We do not enter a house in which there are statues. If you must have something in your house, cut off their heads or cut them into cushions and make them rugs.\""],[3759,"Gabriel came to me and said, 'I came to you last night, and nothing prevented me from entering the house you were in except that there was a statue of a man in the house, and there was a curtain with images on it, and there was a dog in the house. So he ordered that the head of the statue be cut off, and he ordered that the curtain with the image be cut so that the head of the image was removed, and two cushions were made from it. He ordered that the dog be taken out. The dog was a puppy belonging to al-Hasan and al-Husayn, under a bed of theirs.' Then Gabriel came to me and kept advising me about the neighbor until I thought he would make him an heir."],[3760,"the Messenger of Allah ﷺ passed by a group of his Companions and they were laughing. Thereupon, he said, \"If you [only] knew what I know, you would laugh little and weep a lot.\" Then Jibrīl came to him and said, \"Allah says to you, 'Why are you putting my servants in despair?'\" He said that he returned back to them then said, \"Attempt moderation [in your actions as you] rejoice.\""],[3761,"\"Jibril recited a ruqyah over him while he was feverish, saying: In the name of Allah, I recite over you from every ailment that harms you, from every envious person when he envies, and from every eye, and [missing word] and Allah will heal you.\""],[3762,"One day the Messenger of Allah ﷺ put on a brocade outer garment that had been gifted to him, then he took it off and sent it to ‘Umar b. al-Khattab ؓ . It was said, “O Messenger of Allah, why did you take it off?” He said, “Gabriel came to me and forbade me from it.” He said, then ‘Umar b. al-Khattab ؓ came to him weeping and said, “O Messenger of Allah, you dislike it yet you give it to me?” He said, “I did not give it to you to wear; I gave it to you only to sell it.” So he sold it for two thousand dirhams."],[3763,"A man recited a verse, and I recited it differently from his recitation. I said, “Who taught you this?” He said, “The Messenger of Allah ﷺ taught it to me.” I went to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and said, “O Messenger of Allah, did you teach me such-and-such a verse?” He said, “Yes.” The man said, “Did you teach me such-and-such?” He said, “Yes. Gabriel and Michael came to me. Gabriel ﷺ sat on my right and Michael ﷺ on my left. Gabriel said, ‘O Muhammad, recite the Qur’an on one harf.’ Michael said, ‘Ask him for more.’ So I said, ‘Increase me.’ He said, ‘Recite it on two harf.’ Michael said, ‘Ask him for more,’ until he reached seven ahruf, and he said, ‘Recite it on seven ahruf, each one sufficient and healing.’”"],[3764,"Gabriel ﷺ came to the Prophet ﷺ while he was at the watering place of Banū Ghifār and said, “O Muhammad, Allah commands you to teach your Ummah this Qur’an on one harf.” The Prophet ﷺ said, “I ask Allah for His pardon and forgiveness, or His help and pardon; ask for them alleviation, for they will never bear that.” He left and then returned and said, “Allah commands you to teach your Ummah this Qur’an on two harf.” He said, “I ask Allah for His pardon and forgiveness, or His help and pardon; ask for them alleviation, for they will never bear that.” He left and then returned and said, “Allah commands you to teach your Ummah this Qur’an on three ahruf.” He said, “I ask Allah for His pardon and forgiveness, or His help and pardon; ask for them alleviation, for they will never bear that.” He left and then returned and said, “Allah commands you to recite this Qur’an on seven ahruf. Whoever recites one of them has recited it correctly.”"],[3765,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ met Gabriel ﷺ and said to him, “I was sent to an unlettered Ummah: among them are the boy, the girl, the old woman, and the elderly man.” He said, “Command them to recite the Qur’an on seven ahruf.”"],[3766,"\"I was sitting in the mosque when a man entered and recited a verse that I disliked. Then another man entered and recited a different verse than his companion. After completing the prayer, they both went to the Prophet Muhammad ﷺ. I said, 'O Messenger of Allah, this man recited a verse that I disliked, and the other one recited a different verse than his companion.' The Prophet ﷺ told them, 'Recite.' So they recited, and he said, 'You both did well, or he said, 'You both did correctly.' When the one whom the Prophet ﷺ had spoken to heard this, he felt proud, and when the Prophet ﷺ saw what happened to him, he hit his chest. It was as if I was seeing my Lord with a gap. The Prophet ﷺ then said, 'O Ubayy, my Lord has sent me with the command to recite the Quran in a certain way. I initially pleaded with Him to make it easier upon my Ummah, but He insisted that I recite it in seven different ways. For every recitation, I will be rewarded individually on the Day of Resurrection.' I said, 'O Allah, forgive my Ummah.' Then I postponed the second recitation until a day when creation will express their desire for it, even if it means delaying it until the Day of Judgment.\""],[3767,"I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say while he was at al-ʿAqīq: \"A messenger came to me from my Lord and said: 'Pray in this valley,' and he said: 'An ʿumrah in a ḥajj.'\""],[3768,"\"Gabriel came to me and commanded me to command my companions to raise their voices with the talbiyah.\""],[3769,"\"Gabriel ﷺ came to me and said: O Muhammad, command your companions to raise their voices with the talbiyah, for it is one of the rites of Hajj.\""],[3770,"O son of Adam, remember Me within yourself and I will remember you within Myself. Remember Me in an assembly of people and I will remember you in an assembly better than them."],[3771,"“He entrusted me with the speech, so we said, ‘O Abu Abdur-Rahman, some people have appeared among us who recite the Quran excessively and seek knowledge excessively. They claim that there is no predestination and that everything is a result of mere chance.’ He said, ‘If you meet them, inform them that I disassociate myself from them and they disassociate themselves from me.’ Ibn Umar swore an oath that if any of them were to spend gold equal to Uhud, it would not be accepted from him unless he believed in predestination. Then he said, ‘Umar ibn Al-Khattab narrated to us that one day the Messenger of Allah ﷺ was sitting when a man with extremely black hair and exceedingly white clothes came to him and placed his foot on the Prophet’s foot and said, ‘O Muhammad, what is Islam?’ He said, ‘To testify that there is no deity worthy of worship except Allah, to establish prayer, to give Zakah, to fast in Ramadan, and to perform Hajj if one is able.’ He said, ‘You have spoken the truth.’ We were amazed that he asked him and then confirmed the truth of his answers. He said, ‘Inform me about Iman.’ He said, ‘To believe in Allah, His angels, His books, His messengers, the Day of Resurrection, and in destiny, both its good and its evil.’ He said, ‘You have spoken the truth.’ We were amazed that he asked him and then confirmed the truth of his answers. He said, ‘Inform me about Ihsan.’ He said, ‘To worship Allah as if you see Him, for even though you do not see Him, He sees you.’ He said, ‘Inform me about the Hour.’ He said, ‘The one questioned about it knows no more than the questioner.’ He said, ‘Then tell me about its signs.’ He said, ‘The slave girl will give birth to her master, and you will see the barefooted, naked, destitute shepherds competing in constructing tall buildings.’ Then he went away. So I stayed there for a long time, and then he said, ‘O Umar, do you know who that questioner was?’ I said, ‘Allah and His Messenger know best.’ He said, ‘That was Jibril (Gabriel). He came to teach you your religion.’” Translation: He entrusts me with speech, so we said, \"O Abu Abdur-Rahman, some people have appeared among us who excessively recite the Quran and seek knowledge. They claim that there is no predestination and that everything is a result of mere chance.\" He said, \"If you meet them, inform them that I disassociate myself from them and they disassociate themselves from me.\" Ibn Umar swore an oath that if any of them were to spend gold equal to Uhud, it would not be accepted from him unless he believed in predestination. Then he said, \"Umar ibn Al-Khattab narrated to us that one day the Messenger of Allah ﷺ was sitting when a man with extremely black hair and exceedingly white clothes came to him and placed his foot on the Prophet's foot and said, 'O Muhammad, what is Islam?' He said, 'To testify that there is no deity worthy of worship except Allah, to establish prayer, to give Zakah, to fast in Ramadan, and to perform Hajj if one is able.' He said, 'You have spoken the truth.' We were amazed that he asked him and then confirmed the truth of his answers. He said, 'Inform me about Iman.' He said, 'To believe in Allah, His angels, His books, His messengers, the Day of Resurrection, and in destiny, both its good and its evil.' He said, 'You have spoken the truth.' We were amazed that he asked him and then confirmed the truth of his answers. He said, 'Inform me about Ihsan.' He said, 'To worship Allah as if you see Him, for even though you do not see Him, He sees you.' He said, 'Inform me about the Hour.' He said, 'The one questioned about it knows no more than the questioner.' He said, 'Then tell me about its signs.' He said, 'The slave girl will give birth to her master, and you will see the barefooted, naked, destitute shepherds competing in constructing tall buildings.' Then he went away. So I stayed there for a long time, and then he said, 'O Umar, do you know who that questioner was?' I said, 'Allah and His Messenger know best.' He said, 'That was Jibril (Gabriel). He came to teach you your religion.'\""],[3772,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ came one day in haste, ascended the pulpit, and it was announced among the people: 'Come together for prayer.' The people gathered, and he said, \"O people, I have not called you for desire or for fear that has come down, but Tamim al-Dari told me that people from Palestine rode the sea, and the wind cast them onto an island of the sea. There they saw a beast, and it was not known whether it was male or female because of the abundance of hair. They said, 'Who are you?' She said, 'I am the Jassasah.' They said, 'Tell us.' She said, 'I am not going to tell you or ask you, but here is someone who is in need of telling you and asking you.' So they went to the monastery, and there was a bitter man bound in iron. He said, 'Who are you?' They said, 'We are Arabs.' He said, 'Has the Prophet been sent?' They said, 'Yes.' He said, 'Have the Arabs followed him?' They said, 'Yes.' He said, 'That is better for them.' He said, 'What has Persia done?' They said, 'He has not prevailed over it.' He said, 'Indeed, he will prevail over it.' Then he said, 'What has the spring of Zughar done?' They said, 'It flows full.' He said, 'What have the date palms of Baysan done?' They said, 'Their first fruits have ripened.' He leapt at them with such a leap that we feared he would break free. We said, 'Who are you?' He said, 'I am the Dajjal. Indeed, I will tread the entire earth except Makkah and Taybah.'\" The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, \"Rejoice, O assembly of Muslims, for this is Taybah; he will not enter it.\""],[3773,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"What I fear for you the most is a man who has memorized the Quran, until his delight is seen on him and it becomes apparent that he is a supporter of Islam. Then he changes it to whatever Allah wills. He sheds it from himself and throws it behind his back, and he fights against his neighbor with the sword and accuses him of polytheism.\" I said, \"O Prophet of Allah, who is more deserving of being accused of polytheism, the thrower or the one thrown at?\" He said, \"Rather, it is the one who throws.\""],[3774,"\"I do not fear poverty for you after me, but I fear for you competition in wealth, and I do not fear error for you, but I fear for you deliberate actions.\""],[3775,"\"The Prophet of Allah ﷺ said, 'Verily, I do not fear for my nation except for the misguided leaders. And when the sword is brandished among my people, it will not be lifted from them until the Day of Resurrection.'\""],[3776,"\"Indeed Allah does not seize knowledge by forcibly removing it from people, but He seizes knowledge by taking the scholars, until when He leaves no scholar, people take ignorant leaders. They are asked and they give fatwas without knowledge, so they go astray and lead others astray.\" Then I met 'Abd Allah b. 'Amr a year later and he narrated it to me."],[3777,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ looked at the sky and said, \"This is the time when knowledge will be raised.\" A man from the Ansar named Labid b. Ziyad said, \"O Messenger of Allah, will knowledge be raised while it has been established and hearts have retained it?\" The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, \"I had considered you the most knowledgeable of the people of Madinah.\" Then he mentioned the straying of the Jews and Christians despite the Book of Allah in their hands. He said: Then I met Shaddad b. Aws and told him the hadith of 'Awf b. Malik, and he said, \"'Awf spoke the truth.\" Then he said, \"Shall I inform you of the first of that to be raised?\" I said, \"Yes.\" He said, \"Humility (khushu'), until you see no one humble.\""],[3778,"The Messenger of God ﷺ addressed us and said: \"The most fearful thing I fear for you is what God brings out of the adornment and splendor of this world.\" A man said to him, \"O Messenger of God, does good come with evil?\" The Messenger of God ﷺ remained silent. We saw that revelation was descending upon him. It was said to the man, \"What is the matter with you? You speak to the Messenger of God ﷺ while he does not speak to you.\" Then the Messenger of God ﷺ was relieved, and he began wiping away the sweat and said, \"Where is the questioner?\" And we saw that he praised him, then said: \"Good does not come with evil. Indeed, some of what the spring rain causes to grow kills or nearly kills by bloating, except for the eater of green plants: it eats until its flanks are full, faces the sun, then defecates and urinates, then grazes again. Wealth is sweet and green, and an excellent companion for a Muslim is the one who, from it, maintains kinship ties and spends in the way of God. The example of one who takes it without his right is like one who eats but is not satisfied, and it will be a witness against him on the Day of Resurrection.\""],[3779,"\"The thing I fear most for you is the argumentation of a hypocrite who is eloquent of tongue.\""],[3780,"His grandfather Sufyan b. 'Abd Allah al-Thaqafi said: O Messenger of Allah, tell me something I can hold fast to. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, \"Say: My Lord is Allah, then remain upright.\" He said, O Messenger of Allah, what do you fear most for me? He said, \"This,\" and pointed to his tongue."],[3781,"\"Any woman who perfumes herself and passes by a group of people so that they smell her fragrance is an adulteress, and every eye is an adulterer.\""],[3782,"\"The two eyes commit adultery, the tongue commits adultery, the two hands commit adultery, and the two legs commit adultery; the private part then confirms it or denies it.\""],[3783,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, \"Allah has decreed for the son of Adam his share of adultery which will inevitably happen to him; the adultery of the eyes is looking, the adultery of the tongue is speaking, and the soul desires and covets it, while the private parts either confirm or deny it.\""],[3784,"\"Every son of Adam has a share of adultery that has inevitably befallen him: the eye's adultery is the gaze; the tongue's adultery is speech; the heart's adultery is desire; and the private part either confirms it or denies it.\""],[3785,"\"Every son of Adam has inevitably committed some adultery: the eye's adultery is the gaze; the hand's adultery is the touch; the soul longs and desires; and the private part either confirms it or denies it.\""],[3786,"\"Upon every son of Adam his share of adultery has been written, which he will inevitably meet: the eye's adultery is the gaze; the ear's adultery is listening; the hand's adultery is seizing; the leg's adultery is walking; the tongue's adultery is speech; the heart longs and desires; and the private part either confirms it or denies it.\""],[3787,"from his father, from Abu Hurairah that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"Whoever performs a Salat in which he does not recite Umm Al-Qur'an in it, then it is aborted, it is aborted, not complete.\" He Said: \"I said: 'O Abu Hurairah! Sometimes I am behind an Imam.' He said: 'O Ibn Al-Farisi! Then recite it to yourself. For indeed I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ saying: Allah, the Most High said: \"I have divided the Salat between Myself and My slaves into two halves. Half of it is for Me, and half of it for My slave, and My slave shall have what he asks for. My slave stands and says: All praise is due to Allah, the Lord of All that exists.\" So Allah, Blessed is He and Most High says: \"My slave has expressed his gratitude to Me.\" He says: \"The Merciful, the Beneficent. So he says: \"My slave has praised Me.\" He says: Owner of the Day of Reckoning. He says: \"My slave has glorified Me. And this is for Me, and between Me and My slave is: It is You alone whom we worship and it is You alone from whom we seek aid\" until the end of the Surah \"This is for My slave and My slave shall have what he asks for.\" So he says: Guide us to the straight path. The path of those upon whom You have bestowed your favor, not those with whom is Your wrath, now those who are astray.\"' (Using translation from Tirmidhī 2953)"],[3788,"Concerning the saying of Allah, the Mighty and Sublime: \"And offer your salah (prayer) neither aloud nor in a low voice\"- It was revealed when the Messenger of Allah ﷺ was still (preaching) in secret in Makkah. When he led his companions in prayer, he would raise his voice\" -(One of the narrators) Ibn Mani' said: He would recite the Quran out loud\"- \"And when the idolators heard his voice they would insult the Quran, and the One Who revealed it, and the one who brought it. So Allah, the Mighty and Sublime, said to His Prophet ﷺ: And offer your salah (prayer) neither aloud that is, such that the idolators can hear your recitation and insult the Quran; nor in a low voice, so that your companions cannot hear; but follow a way between.\" (Using translation from Nasāʾī 1011)"],[3789,"A man said, \"O Messenger of Allah, what is faith?\" He said, \"When your good deeds please you and your evil deeds grieve you, then you are a believer.\" He said, \"O Messenger of Allah, what is sin?\" He said, \"When something stirs in your heart, leave it.\""],[3790,"Actions are by intentions, and every person will have what he intended. Whoever's migration is to Allah and His Messenger, his migration is to Allah and His Messenger. And whoever's migration is to a worldly gain he attains or a woman he marries, his migration is to what he migrated to."],[3791,"“There is nothing between the servant and disbelief except abandoning prayer.”"],[3792,"“The covenant that is between us and them is prayer, so whoever abandons it has disbelieved.”"],[3793,"Ibn ʿUmar was informed of his wife's illness during travel, so he delayed maghrib, and it was said: “The prayer!” but he remained silent and delayed it until after the twilight had disappeared, until a portion of the night had passed. Then he dismounted and prayed maghrib and ʿishāʾ, and then said: “This is what the Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to do when travel pressed him or a matter distressed him.”"],[3794,"The Prophet ﷺ, when he wanted to combine two prayers during travel, would delay ẓuhr until the first time of ʿaṣr entered, then combine them."],[3795,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ ordered a tent of hair, and it was pitched for him at Namirah. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ traveled, and Quraysh did not doubt that he would stand at al-Mashʿar al-Ḥarām as Quraysh used to do in the Jāhiliyyah. But the Messenger of Allah ﷺ passed on until he came to ʿArafah and found the tent pitched for him at Namirah, so he stopped there. When the sun declined, he ordered al-Qaṣwāʾ, and it was saddled for him. He came to the middle of the valley and addressed the people, then said: “Your blood and your wealth are forbidden to you like the sanctity of this day of yours, in this month of yours, in this land of yours. Indeed, every matter of the Jāhiliyyah is placed beneath my feet, and the blood of the Jāhiliyyah is abolished. The first blood I abolish from our own blood is the blood of Ibn Rabīʿah b. al-Ḥārith, who was being nursed among Banū Layth and was killed by Hudhayl. Fear Allah concerning women, for you have taken them by Allah's trust and made their private parts lawful by Allah's word. You owe it to them not to let anyone you dislike tread on your beds; if they do that, then strike them with a blow that is not severe. And they owe you their provision and clothing with kindness. I have left among you that which, if you hold fast to it, you will never go astray: the Book of Allah. You will be asked about me, so what will you say?” They said: “We bear witness that you have conveyed, fulfilled, and advised.” Then he raised his index finger to the sky and pointed it at the people, saying: “O Allah, bear witness,” three times. Then he called the adhān, then the iqāmah, and prayed ẓuhr; then he called the iqāmah and prayed ʿaṣr, and he did not pray anything between them."],[3796,"The Prophet ﷺ went out on the expedition of Tabūk. When he departed before the sun declined, he delayed ẓuhr until he combined it with ʿaṣr and prayed them together; and when he departed after the sun declined, he prayed ẓuhr and ʿaṣr together, then set out. And when he departed before maghrib, he delayed maghrib until he prayed it with ʿishāʾ; and when he departed after maghrib, he hastened ʿishāʾ and prayed it with maghrib."],[3797,"They went out with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ in the year of Tabuk, and the Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to combine Dhuhr and Asr, and Maghrib and Isha. He delayed the prayer one day, then came out and prayed Dhuhr and Asr together, then entered, then came out and prayed Maghrib and Isha together. Then he said, 'Tomorrow, if Allah wills, you will come to the spring of Tabuk, and you will not reach it until the forenoon. Whoever reaches it should not touch its water until I come.' He said: We reached it, and two men had gotten there before us, and the spring was like a shoelace, trickling with a little water. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ asked them, 'Did you touch any of its water?' They said, 'Yes.' He rebuked them and said to them what Allah willed him to say. Then they scooped water from the spring with their hands little by little until it collected in something. Then the Messenger of Allah ﷺ washed his face and hands in it and poured it back. The spring then flowed with abundant water, and the people drew water. Then the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, 'Soon, O Mu'adh, if your life lasts long, you will see this place filled with gardens.'"],[3798,"We stopped for rest with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ one night and did not wake up until the sun harmed us. The Prophet of Allah ﷺ said: “Let every man among you take his mount and move away from this place.” Then he called for water, performed ablution, prostrated twice, then the prayer was established."],[3799,"“There is no negligence in sleep; negligence is only on the one who does not pray a prayer until the time of another prayer comes.”"],[3800,"We traveled with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and at the end of the night we stopped for rest, and our eyes overpowered us, and nothing woke us except the heat of the sun. A man would rise to his ablution in confusion, so the Messenger of Allah ﷺ ordered them to perform ablution. Then he ordered Bilāl, who called the adhān, and they prayed the two rakʿahs of dawn; then he ordered him, and he called the iqāmah, and he prayed fajr. They said: “O Messenger of Allah, we were negligent; should we not repeat it at its time tomorrow?” He said: “Would your Lord forbid you from usury and accept it from you? Negligence is only in wakefulness.”"],[3801,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ called out among them on the day the confederates departed: 'Indeed, let no one pray Ẓuhr except among Banū Qurayẓah.' Some people delayed and feared missing the prayer time, so they prayed. Others said, 'We will not pray except where the Messenger of Allah ﷺ commanded us, even if the time elapses.' The Messenger of Allah ﷺ did not rebuke either of the two groups."],[3802,"'Perform prayer early on a cloudy day, for whoever abandons prayer has disbelieved.'"],[3804,"'Three are from disbelief in Allah: tearing one's garment (in grief), wailing, and defaming lineage.'"],[3805,"'Do not turn away from your fathers, for whoever turns away from his father has disbelieved.'"],[3806,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ sent me and said, “Call out among the people: whoever says ‘There is no god but Allah’ will enter Paradise.”"],[3807,"Whoever says, \"There is no god but Allah\" will enter Paradise.\" I said, \"Even if he commits adultery and even if he steals?\" He said, \"Even if he commits adultery and even if he steals.\""],[3808,"I was walking with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ on the ḥarrah of Madinah, and Uḥud faced us. He said, \"O Abū Dharr, it would not please me for Uḥud to be mine as gold, and evening comes upon me while I have a dinar of it except that I spend it toward a debt.\" Then he walked on and I walked with him, and he said, \"O Abū Dharr.\" I said, \"At your service, O Messenger of Allah, and at your call.\" He said, \"Those with the most are the ones with the least on the Day of Resurrection.\" Then he said, \"O Abū Dharr, do not leave until I come to you.\" Then he went off until he was hidden, and I heard a voice. I said, \"I will go.\" Then I remembered the Prophet's ﷺ words to me, so I remained until he came. I said, \"O Messenger of Allah, I heard a voice and wanted to catch up with you, but I remembered your words to me.\" He said, \"That was Jibrīl. He came to me and informed me that whoever of my community dies without associating anything with Allah will enter Paradise.\" I said, \"O Messenger of Allah, even if he commits adultery and even if he steals?\" He said, \"Even if he commits adultery and even if he steals.\""],[3809,"\"Do you know who the bankrupt is?\" They said, \"The bankrupt among us, O Messenger of Allah, is one who has no dirham and no possessions.\" The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, \"The bankrupt from my nation is one who comes on the Day of Resurrection with his prayer, fasting, and zakah, but he has insulted this one, consumed the wealth of this one, shed the blood of this one, and struck this one. So he will sit and this one will be given from his good deeds and this one from his good deeds. If his good deeds run out before he fulfills what he owes, some of their sins will be taken and cast upon him, and then he will be cast into the Fire.\""],[3810,"On the authority of the Prophet ﷺ, he said: “Indeed time has returned to its original state as it was on the day Allah created the heavens and the earth. The year is twelve months, of which four are sacred: three consecutive—Dhu al-Qa‘dah, Dhu al-Hijjah, and al-Muharram—and Rajab of Mudar, which is between Jumada and Sha‘ban.” Then he said, “Which month is this?” We said, “Allah and His Messenger know best.” He fell silent until we thought he would name it by a name other than its own. He said, “Is it not Dhu al-Hijjah?” We said, “Yes.” He said, “Which land is this?” We said, “Allah and His Messenger know best.” He fell silent until we thought he would name it by a name other than its own. He said, “Is it not this town?” We said, “Yes.” He said, “Which day is this?” We said, “Allah and His Messenger know best.” He said, “Is it not the Day of Sacrifice?” We said, “Yes.” He said, “Indeed your blood and your wealth”—Muhammad said, “and I think he said, ‘and your honor’”—“are sacred to you, like the sanctity of this day of yours in this land of yours. And you will meet your Lord, and He will ask you about your deeds. So do not return after me astray, striking the necks of one another. Let those of you who are present convey it to those who are absent, for perhaps some who receive it may understand it better than some who heard it.” He said: Muhammad would, whenever he mentioned it, say, “Allah and His Messenger have spoken the truth; it was indeed so.” Then he ﷺ said, “Have I conveyed (the message)? Have I conveyed (the message)?”"],[3811,"Whoever affirms the oneness of Allah and disbelieves in what is worshipped besides Him, his wealth and his blood become inviolable, and his reckoning is upon Allah."],[3812,"About the wine, the Prophet Muhammad ﷺ said, \"Indeed, the delegation of Abd al-Qais came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and he said, 'Who is the delegation or who are they?' They said, 'They are the Rabia'ah.' He ﷺ said, 'Welcome to the people or to the delegation, who are not deceitful or treacherous.' They said, 'O Messenger of Allah, we come to you from a distant, forbidding place. There are disbelievers between us and you, from the tribe of Mudar. And we can only come to you in the sacred month. So we have come with a matter that we will inform those who are behind us about, and we hope to enter Paradise with it.' He ﷺ gave them four commandments and prohibited them from four things. He commanded them to have faith in Allah alone and asked, 'Do you know what faith in Allah alone is?' They said, 'Allah and His Messenger know best.' He ﷺ said, 'It is to testify that there is no deity worthy of worship except Allah and that Muhammad is the Messenger of Allah, to establish prayer, to give charity, to observe the fast of Ramadan, and to give one-fifth of the war spoils. And he prohibited them from predatory hawks (du'ba'), the tame snake (hantam), and the muzaffat.'\" Note: Some of the mentioned terms may have different interpretations, as translating Old Arabic can be challenging due to language evolution and multiple possible meanings."],[3813,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ was once prominent among the people when a man came to him walking and said, \"O Muhammad, what is faith?\" He said, \"To believe in Allah, His angels, His messengers, and the Day of Judgement, and to believe in the resurrection after death.\" The man asked, \"O Messenger of Allah, what is Islam?\" He said, \"To worship Allah alone and not associate anything with Him, to establish the obligatory prayers, to pay the obligatory charity, and to fast during the month of Ramadan.\" The man then asked, \"O Muhammad, what is excellence (ihsan)?\" He said, \"To worship Allah as if you see Him, and if you cannot see Him, then know that He sees you.\" Finally, the man asked, \"O Muhammad, when will the Hour (the Day of Judgement) occur?\" He replied, \"The one being asked about it knows no more than the questioner, but I will inform you of its signs. When the servant girl gives birth to her master, and you see the barefooted, naked, destitute shepherds competing in the construction of tall buildings, that is among its signs. The knowledge of the Hour belongs only to Allah {Indeed, Allah [alone] has knowledge of the Hour} [Quran 31:34].\" Then the man left, and the Prophet ﷺ said, \"That was Gabriel who came to teach the people their religion.\""],[3814,"Faith is Yemeni, wisdom is Yemeni, and the head of disbelief is towards the East."],[3815,"The people of Yemen have come; they have the softest hearts. Faith is Yemeni, understanding is Yemeni, and wisdom is Yemeni."],[3817,"Al-Qaʿnabī narrated to us, ʿAbd al-ʿAzīz b. Muḥammad narrated to us, from al-ʿAlāʾ, from his father, from Abū Hurayrah, that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Faith is Yemeni, and disbelief is toward the east; tranquility is among the people of sheep, and pride and ostentation are among the loud-voiced owners of horses and camels. The Messiah will come until when he passes Uḥud, the angels will turn his face toward Syria, and there he will perish.”"],[3818,"Verily, my example and the example of what Allah has sent me with is like a man who came to his people and said, 'O my people, I have seen the army, and I am the warner, so a group of his people obeyed him and went at their own pace and were saved, but a group of them disbelieved him, so they remained in their places, and the army came upon them in the morning and destroyed them and annihilated them. That is the example of one who obeys me and follows what I have brought, and the example of one who disobeys me and disbelieves what I have brought of the truth.'"],[3819,"«The likeness of the believers among themselves is like a building; he inserted his fingers into the earth and said, \"They support one another.\"»"],[3820,"The likeness of the believer is that of a body: when one part of it hurts, the rest of the body rallies to it."],[3821,"that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"People are but like a hundred camels, a man can not find a mount (suitable to ride upon) among them.\" (Using translation from Tirmidhī 2872)"],[3822,"The likeness of the believer is like a plant: the wind keeps bending it, and the believer keeps being afflicted by calamity. And the likeness of the hypocrite is like the cedar tree: it does not shake until it is cut down."],[3823,"Your lifespan in comparison to the lifespans of the nations that have passed is like the time between the afternoon prayer and sunset. Your likeness and that of the Jews and Christians is that of a man who employed workers and said, 'Who will work for me until midday for a carat, a carat?' The Jews worked until midday for a carat, a carat. Then he said, 'Who will work for me from midday until the afternoon prayer for a carat, a carat?' The Christians worked from midday until the afternoon prayer. Then he said, 'Who will work from the afternoon prayer until sunset for two carats, two carats?' Then he said, 'You are the ones who work from the afternoon prayer until sunset for two carats, two carats.' The Jews and Christians became angry and said, 'We worked more and received less.' He said, 'Have I wronged you in anything of your work?' They said, 'No.' He said, 'That is My bounty; I give it to whom I will.'"],[3825,"\"My likeness and the likeness of people is that of a man who kindled a fire. When it illuminated what was around it, the small creatures of the earth and its moths approached, along with these beasts that rush into the fire and are thrust into it, while he drives them away from it. Today I am seizing the waists of people, [saying,] 'Come to Paradise! Come away from the Fire!' but they plunge into it.\""],[3826,"\"Indeed, my likeness and the likeness of the prophets before me is that of a man who built a structure, made it excellent, beautiful, and complete. People began to circle around it, saying, 'We have not seen anything more beautiful than this except the place of that brick.'\" He said: \"I was that brick.\""],[3827,"\"The parable of the companion of the Qur'an is like the parable of the owner of hobbled camels; if he keeps them hobbled, he holds them, and if he sets them free, they go away.\""],[3828,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ dispatched an expedition, and they were a group. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ called them and said, \"What do you have with you of the Quran?\" He examined them until he came to a man among them who was the youngest of them in age, and said, \"What do you have with you, O so-and-so?\" He said, \"I have such-and-such, and Surat al-Baqarah.\" He said, \"You have Surat al-Baqarah?\" He said, \"Yes.\" He said, \"Go, for you are their commander.\" A man who was the most noble of them said, \"By the One who such-and-such, O Messenger of Allah, nothing prevented me from learning the Quran except fear that I would not stand with it.\" The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, \"Learn the Quran and recite it and sleep, for the likeness of the Quran for one who learns it, recites it, and stands with it is like a bag stuffed with musk whose fragrance spreads everywhere; and one who learns it and sleeps while it is in his heart is like a bag tied over musk.\""],[3829,"That 'Abdullah b. 'Abbas saw 'Abdullah b. al-Harith while his hair was tied back behind him, so he stood behind him and began to untie it, and the other submitted to him. When he finished, he came to Ibn 'Abbas and said: “What do you have against my head?” He said: “I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: 'The likeness of this is only like the likeness of one who prays while he is bound.'”"],[3830,"\"The parable of the believer who recites the Qur'an is like the citron: its taste is good and its fragrance is good. The parable of the believer who does not recite the Qur'an is like the date: its taste is good but it has no fragrance. The parable of the hypocrite or the wicked person who recites the Qur'an is like the sweet basil: its fragrance is good but its taste is bitter. The parable of the hypocrite or the wicked person who does not recite the Qur'an is like the colocynth: its taste is bitter and it has no fragrance.\""],[3831,"“The likeness of the believer is the likeness of the palm tree: if it eats, it eats what is good; and if it gives, it gives what is good.”"],[3832,"They mentioned joy in the presence of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and they mentioned a lost animal that a man finds. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, “Allah is more intensely joyful at the repentance of one of you than the lost animal that a man finds in a desolate land.”"],[3833,"“The example of the believer and faith is like a horse at its tethering post: it roams, then returns to its tethering post. The believer slips, then returns to faith. So feed your food to the pious, and extend your kindness to the believers.”"],[3834,"\"The world compared to the Hereafter is only like one of you dipping his forefinger into the sea; let him see what he brings back.\""],[3835,"By Allah, the world compared to the Hereafter is only like one of you dipping his finger into the sea; let him see what it brings back."],[3836,"The likeness of the one who gives charity at death is the likeness of the one who gives a gift after he is full."],[3837,"Whoever plays with dice, it is as if he has dipped his hand in the flesh and blood of a pig."],[3838,"He used to tell stories in Makkah, and with him were 'Abd Allah b. 'Umar, 'Abd Allah b. Safwan, and some people from the Companions of the Prophet ﷺ. 'Ubayd b. 'Umayr said: 'The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"The likeness of the hypocrite is like that of a sheep between two flocks: if it leans to this side, it is butted; if it leans to this side, it is butted.\"' Ibn 'Umar said, 'It is not like that.' 'Ubayd b. 'Umayr became angry and said, 'Are you rejecting what I say?' He said, 'I did not reject what you said, except that I witnessed the Messenger of Allah ﷺ when he said it.' 'Abd Allah b. Safwan said, 'How did he say it, O Abu 'Abd al-Rahman?' He said, 'Between the two groups.' He said, 'O Abu 'Abd al-Rahman, between the two groups and between the two flocks are the same.' He said, 'Thus I heard, thus I heard, thus I heard.'"],[3839,"A woman came to the Prophet ﷺ and said: «O Messenger of Allah, I have a co-wife. Is there any sin upon me if I pretend from my husband that he gave me what he did not give me?» The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: «The one who pretends to have been given what he was not given is like the wearer of two garments of falsehood.»"],[3840,"That Hisham b. 'Abd al-Malik paid on behalf of al-Zuhri seven thousand dinars toward a debt he owed, then said to al-Zuhri, \"Do not return to incurring debt.\" Al-Zuhri said, \"How, O Commander of the Believers, when…\""],[3841,"And I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: 'The believers, in their mutual mercy and kindness to one another, are like a single body; if one part complains, the rest of the body aches.'"],[3842,"We were sitting with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ when some palm hearts were brought. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, \"Among trees there is a tree whose blessing is like that of a Muslim.\" I thought it was the date palm. Then I looked at the people, and I was the tenth of ten, the youngest of them, so I remained silent. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, \"It is the date palm.\""],[3843,"The lawful is clear and the unlawful is clear, and between that are matters that are dubious—and perhaps he said: ambiguous. I will strike for you an example of that: Allah has a protected pasture, and Allah's protected pasture is His sacred limits. Whoever grazes around the protected pasture will soon encroach upon it—and perhaps he said: Whoever grazes around the protected pasture will soon graze within it. And whoever gets involved in doubtful matters will soon become bold."],[3844,"We have been favored over people with three things: the whole earth has been made a mosque for us, its soil has been made a means of purification for us, our rows have been made like the rows of angels, and I have been given these verses from the end of Surah al-Baqarah from a treasure beneath the Throne that was not given to anyone before me nor will be given to anyone after me."],[3845,"He forbade praying between graves."],[3846,"The whole earth is a mosque except the bathhouse and the cemetery."],[3847,"If you find only sheep pens and camel resting places, pray in the sheep pens and do not pray in the camel resting places."],[3848,"'Allah ordained the measures (maqadir) fifty thousand years before He created the heavens and the earth.'"],[3849,"Sahl b. Sa'd reported it from Messenger of Allah ﷺ that a person performs deeds like the deeds of the people of Paradise apparently before people and he would be amongst the dwellers of Hell and a person acts apparently like the people of Hell, but (in fact) he would be among the dwellers of Paradise. (Using translation from Muslim 112b)"],[3851,"A man may perform the deeds of the people of Paradise for a long time, then Allah seals him with the deeds of the people of the Fire, and He makes him one of the people of the Fire. And a man may perform the deeds of the people of the Fire for a long time, then Allah seals him with the deeds of the people of Paradise, and He makes him one of the people of Paradise."],[3852,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ was brought a boy from the Ansar to pray over him. I said, \"O Messenger of Allah, a bird from the birds of Paradise.\" He said ﷺ: \"Do you not know that Allah created for Paradise a creation and made them its people while they were in the loins of their fathers, and created the Fire and created for it its people while they were in the loins of their fathers?\""],[3853,"The creation of one of you is gathered in his mother's womb for forty days and forty nights, then he becomes a clot for the like of that, then he becomes a lump for the like of that. Then Allah sends to him an angel and commands him with four words: he says, 'Write his deed, his term, his provision, and whether he is wretched or blessed.' And a man may perform the deeds of the people of Paradise until there is only a cubit between him and Paradise, then the decree that preceded overtakes him, and he is sealed with the deeds of the people of the Fire. And a man may perform the deeds of the people of the Fire until there is only a cubit between him and it, then the decree that preceded overtakes him, and he performs the deeds of the people of Paradise, and he enters Paradise.\""],[3854,"ʿUmar b. al-Khaṭṭāb ؓ said, “O Messenger of Allah, do we act upon something new or upon something already decreed?” He said, “Rather, upon something already decreed.” He said, “Then what is the point of action?” He said, “O ʿUmar, that is not attained except through action.” He said, “Then we will strive, O Messenger of Allah.”"],[3855,"He heard Ibn Mas'ud say, 'The wretched is one who was wretched in his mother's womb, and the blessed is one who is admonished by others.' Then a man from the companions of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ called Hudhayfa b. Asid al-Ghifari came and narrated that from the saying of Ibn Mas'ud. He said, 'I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: \"When the drop has passed forty-two nights, Allah sends to it an angel who shapes it and creates its hearing, sight, skin, flesh, and bones. Then he says, 'My Lord, male or female?' And your Lord decrees what He wills, and the angel writes it. Then he says, 'My Lord, its term?' And your Lord decrees what He wills, and the angel writes it. Then he says, 'My Lord, its provision?' And your Lord decrees what He wills, and the angel takes the scroll in his hand, and nothing is added to the matter or subtracted from it.\"'‭"],[3856,"When Allah wills to create a soul, the angel of the wombs says, turning aside, 'My Lord, male or female?' And Allah decrees His command. Then he says, 'My Lord, wretched or blessed?' And Allah decrees His command. Then he writes between his eyes what he will encounter, even the misfortune that will befall him."],[3857,"It was said, \"O Messenger of Allah, is it known who are the people of Paradise and who are the people of the Fire?\" He said, \"Yes.\" It was said, \"Then what do the workers do?\" He ﷺ said, \"Everyone is facilitated for what he was created.\""],[3858,"Suraqah b. Ju'shum said: O Messenger of Allah, inform us about our affair as if we were looking at it: is it by what the pens have recorded and the decrees have established, or by what is initiated anew? He said: “No, rather by what the pens have recorded and the decrees have established.” He said: Then what is the point of action? He said: “Act, for everyone is facilitated.”"],[3859,"“Allah created Adam, then took the creation from his back and said: These are in Paradise, and I do not care; and these are in the Fire, and I do not care.” A questioner said: O Messenger of Allah, then on what basis should we act? He said: “On the occasions of the decree.”"],[3860,"The Prophet ﷺ was at a funeral, and he took a stick and started making marks on the ground with it. He said: “There is none among you but has his seat written for him in the Fire and his seat in Paradise.” A man said: Should we not then rely (on that)? He said: “Act, for everyone is facilitated.” Then he recited: {As for him who gives and fears (Allah), and believes in the best (reward), We will make smooth for him the path of ease. But as for him who is miserly and considers himself self-sufficient, and denies the best (reward), We will make smooth for him the path of hardship} (Qur'an 92:5–10)."],[3861,"He was at a funeral, and he took a stick and made marks on the ground. He said: “There is none among you but has his seat written in Paradise or in the Fire.” They said: O Messenger of Allah, should we not then rely (on that)? He said: “Act, for everyone is facilitated. {As for him who gives and fears (Allah), and believes in the best (reward), We will make smooth for him the path of ease. But as for him who is miserly and considers himself self-sufficient, and denies the best (reward), We will make smooth for him the path of hardship} (Qur'an 92:5–10).”"],[3862,"I entered upon Abdullah b. Umar and said, \"They claim that you say the wretched is one who was wretched in his mother's womb.\" He said, \"I do not permit anyone to lie about me. I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: 'Indeed Allah created His creation in darkness and cast upon them from His light. Whoever was reached by that light is guided, and whoever missed it goes astray.' That is why I say the pen has dried concerning Allah's, Mighty and Exalted, knowledge.\""],[3863,"I said to Abdullah b. Amr, \"It has reached me that you say the pen has dried.\" He said, \"I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: 'Indeed Allah, Mighty and Exalted, created people in darkness, then took light from His light and cast it upon them. It reached whom He willed and missed whom He willed, and He knew whom it would miss and whom it would reach. Whoever was reached by something of His light is guided, and whoever it missed has gone astray.' That is why I say the pen has dried.\""],[3864,"\"The keys of the unseen are five: no one knows what the wombs will bring forth except Allah; no one knows what will be tomorrow except Allah; no one knows when the rain will come except Allah; no soul knows in which land it will die; and no one knows when the Hour will arise.\""],[3865,"\"The keys of the unseen are five, no one knows them except Allah: no one knows what the wombs will diminish except Allah; nor what will be tomorrow except Allah; nor when the rain will come except Allah; nor does any soul know in which land it will die; nor does anyone know when the Hour will arise except Allah.\""],[3866,"\"One suck or two sucks do not make [marriage] forbidden.\""],[3867,"\"One suck or two sucks, or one or two sips, do not make [marriage] forbidden.\""],[3868,"\"One suckling or two sucklings do not make [marriage] forbidden.\""],[3869,"\"Suckling does not make [marriage] forbidden except what opens the intestines.\""],[3870,"A man came to the Prophet ﷺ and said: O Messenger of God, I married a woman while I have another wife. The first one claimed that she suckled the new one a suckling or two. The Prophet ﷺ said: \"One sip or two sips do not make [marriage] forbidden.\""],[3871,"\"The Qur'an was revealed with ten known sucklings that make [marriage] forbidden. Then they were abrogated by five known sucklings. The Messenger of God ﷺ passed away while they were part of what we recite of the Qur'an.\""],[3872,"\"Suckling makes forbidden what birth makes forbidden.\""],[3873,"O Messenger of God, what removes from me the blame of suckling? He said: \"A slave boy or a slave girl.\""],[3874,"You said: O Messenger of Allah, what removes from me the reproach of suckling? He said: “A slave, male or female.”"],[3875,"«Three things are from the deeds of the Age of Ignorance that the people of Islam will not abandon: wailing, seeking rain by the stars, and reviling one another's lineage.»"],[3876,"Four things are from Jahiliyyah that the people will never abandon: wailing, boasting or defaming one another by lineage, saying, 'We were given rain by such and such a star,' and contagious disease. A camel had mange among a hundred camels; who infected the first one?"],[3877,"«Whom do you consider martyrs among you?» They said, \"Whoever is killed in the way of Allah is a martyr.\" He ﷺ said, «And whoever dies in the way of Allah is a martyr, and whoever dies in the plague is a martyr»"],[3878,"«The martyr is five: the one who dies of a stomach disease, the one who dies in the plague, the one who drowns, the one who dies under a collapsed building, and the martyr»"],[3879,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ came to visit 'Abd Allah b. Thabit and found that he had been overcome. He called out to him, but he did not answer. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, \"We belong to Allah and to Him we return,\" and said, «We have been overcome concerning you, O Abu al-Rabi'.» The women cried out and wept, and Ibn 'Atik began to silence them. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, «Leave them. When it becomes obligatory, no weeping woman should weep.» They said, \"What is the obligation, O Messenger of Allah?\" He said, «When he dies.» His daughter said, \"By Allah, I had hoped that you would be a martyr, for you had prepared your equipment.\" The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, «Indeed Allah has placed his reward according to his intention. What do you consider martyrdom?» They said, \"Being killed in the way of Allah.\" The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, «Martyrdom is seven besides being killed in the way of Allah: the one who dies of a stomach disease is a martyr, the one who drowns is a martyr, the one with pleurisy is a martyr, the one who dies in the plague is a martyr, the one who burns is a martyr, the one who dies under a collapsed building is a martyr, and a woman who dies in childbirth is a martyr»"],[3880,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ sent to Banu Lihyan, ordering that one man out of every two should go out. Then he said to the one who remained behind, \"Whichever of you takes the place of the one who has gone out in his family and property with good, he will have the like of half the reward of the one who went out.\""],[3881,"\"Whoever equips a warrior in the way of Allah or takes his place in his family will have written for him the like of his reward, such that nothing is diminished from the reward of the warrior.\""],[3882,"\"I was favored over people with three things: the entire earth was made for us a mosque; its dust was made for us a means of purification when we do not find water; our rows were made like the rows of the angels; and I was given these verses from the end of Surat al-Baqarah from a treasure beneath the Throne, the like of which was not given to anyone before me or after me.\""],[3883,"I was favored over the prophets with six things: I was given comprehensive speech; I was aided with awe; spoils were made lawful for me; the earth was made pure and a mosque for me; I was sent to all creation; and the prophets were sealed with me."],[3884,"Three things, all of them are obligations upon a Muslim: visiting the sick, attending funerals, and saying \"May Allah have mercy on you\" to one who sneezes if he praises Allah."],[3885,"A Muslim owes his fellow Muslim four duties: visiting him when he is sick, attending his funeral when he dies, responding with mercy when he sneezes, and accepting his invitation when he calls him."],[3886,"The right of a Muslim over a Muslim is five: returning the salam, visiting the sick, following funeral processions, accepting invitations, and responding with mercy to the one who sneezes."],[3887,"\"The right of a Muslim over a Muslim is six.\" They said, \"What are they, O Messenger of Allah?\" He said, \"When you meet him, greet him with salam; when he invites you, accept; when he seeks your counsel, give him sincere advice; when he sneezes and praises Allah, respond with mercy; when he is sick, visit him; and when he dies, accompany his funeral.\""],[3888,"It is not the right of a Muslim man who has something to bequeath to spend two nights except with his will written with him."],[3889,"It is not the right of a Muslim man that three nights pass except with his will with him."],[3890,"The best of what mounts are ridden to is this mosque of mine and the Ancient House."],[3891,"Saddles are not to be fastened except to three mosques: the Sacred Mosque, the Farthest Mosque, and this mosque of mine."],[3892,"He used to come to Quba riding and walking."],[3893,"He used to come to Quba every Saturday."],[3894,"Congregational prayer exceeds the prayer of one alone by twenty-five degrees."],[3895,"Congregational prayer is superior to the prayer of one alone by twenty-seven degrees."],[3896,"A man's prayer in congregation exceeds his prayer alone by twenty-five degrees; but if he prays it in an empty land (deserted area), perfecting its bowing and prostration, his prayer reaches fifty degrees."],[3897,"Whoever keeps a dog, except a dog for farming or livestock, a qīrāṭ is diminished from his deeds every day."],[3898,"Any people who take a dog that is not a dog for hunting, farming, or livestock, a qīrāṭ is diminished from their rewards every day."],[3899,"«The fitrah is trimming the mustache, clipping the nails, and shaving the pubic hair.»"],[3900,"«Five are from the fitrah: trimming the mustache, plucking the armpit hair, clipping the nails, shaving the pubic hair, and circumcision.»"],[3901,"The Prophet ﷺ held a race between horses, set a prize between them, and appointed a muḥallil between them. He said, 'There is no racing except in hoof or arrowhead.'"],[3902,"There is no racing except in camel hoof, horse hoof, or arrowhead."],[3903,"“There is no amputation for a pickpocket, nor for a betrayer.”"],[3904,"“There is no amputation for a snatcher, nor a pickpocket, nor a betrayer.”"],[3905,"“He used to cut off for a quarter of a dinar or more.”"],[3906,"\"Were it not that your people are recent from ignorance, I would demolish the Kaaba and make for it two doors.\" So Ibn al-Zubayr demolished it and made for it two doors."],[3907,"I heard Ibn al-Zubayr say while he was on the pulpit when he wanted to demolish the Kaaba and rebuild it: \"My maternal aunt 'A'ishah narrated to me that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to her, 'O 'A'ishah, were it not that your people are recent from polytheism, I would demolish the Kaaba, then add to it six cubits from the Hijr, for Quraysh reduced it when they built the House, and I would make for it two doors: an eastern door and a western door, and I would attach it to the ground.'\""],[3908,"\"Were it not that you are a messenger, I would have killed you.\""],[3909,"There is no enmity between me and any Arab. I passed by a mosque of Banu Hanifah, and they believed in Musaylimah. He sent 'Abdullah to them, and they were brought to him. He asked them to repent, except Ibn al-Nawwahah. He said to him, 'I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: \"Were it not that you are a messenger, I would have struck your neck, and today you are not a messenger.\"' He ordered Qurazah b. Ka'b, and he struck his neck in the market. Then he said, 'Whoever wants to look at Ibn al-Nawwahah, let him look at him dead in the market.'"],[3910,"If I live, God willing, I will forbid naming someone Barakah, Nafi', and Aflah. I do not know whether he said Aflah or not. Then the Prophet ﷺ passed away and did not forbid that. 'Umar intended to forbid that, then he left it."],[3911,"The Prophet ﷺ intended to forbid naming with Barakah, Aflah, Yasar, Nafi', and the like. Then I saw him remain silent about them afterwards, and he did not say anything, and he passed away ﷺ. Then 'Umar intended to forbid that, and he left it."],[3912,"If I live, I will certainly expel the Jews from the Arabian Peninsula."],[3913,"He heard Jabir Ibn Abdullah say: \"The Prophet ﷺ was worried about being called Ma'mun, Barakah, and Afalah, and this is how it was, then he left it.\""],[3914,"We were at the funeral of Abū Sufyān b. al-ʿAlāʾ, and Shuʿbah was with us. When he was buried, Shuʿbah said, “This one narrated to me,” and he pointed to the grave of Abū Sufyān b. al-ʿAlāʾ. He said, “I said to al-Ḥasan, ‘Who narrated to you that the Prophet ﷺ said, “Were it not that dogs are a community among the communities, I would have commanded that they be killed”?’ He said, ‘ʿAbd Allāh b. al-Mughaffal, by the One besides whom there is no god, narrated to me in this mosque,’ and he gestured toward the congregational mosque.”"],[3915,"By the One in Whose hand is my soul, I was about to order that firewood be gathered, then order the prayer and the call to prayer be made for it, then order a man to lead the people in prayer, and then go to some men [who did not attend] and burn their houses down upon them. By the One in Whose hand is my soul, if one of them knew that he would find a fat bone or two fine sheep's trotters, he would attend the Isha prayer."],[3916,"I was about to order a man to lead the people in prayer, then go to some people who stay behind from it and burn down upon them—meaning the two prayers, Isha and the morning prayer."],[3917,"The heaviest prayers upon the hypocrites are the Isha prayer and the Fajr prayer. If they knew what was in them, they would come to them even if they had to crawl. And I was about to order the prayer to be established, then order a man to lead the people in prayer, then go with men carrying bundles of firewood to some people who do not attend the prayer and burn their houses down upon them with fire."],[3918,"By the One in Whose hand is my soul, were it not that I would burden the Muslims, I would never stay behind any expedition that raids in the cause of Allah. But I do not find ample means to mount them, and they do not find ample means to go out, and it is hard for them to stay behind after me. By the One in Whose hand is the soul of Muhammad, I wish I could raid in the cause of Allah and be killed, then brought to life and killed. He said that three times."],[3919,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ came out to his companions one night while they were waiting for the Isha prayer and said, “The people have prayed and gone to sleep, while you are waiting for it. Indeed, you are in prayer as long as you are waiting for it.” Then he said, “Were it not for the weakness of the weak or the old age of the elderly, I would have delayed this prayer until half the night.”"],[3920,"I said to ʿAṭāʾ, “Which time do you prefer for me to pray the night prayer (al-ʿatamah), whether as an imam or alone?” He said, “I heard Ibn ʿAbbās say: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ delayed the night prayer until the people slept and woke, then slept and woke. Then ʿUmar ؓ said, ‘The prayer, the prayer.’ The Messenger of Allah ﷺ came out, and it is as if I am looking at him now, water dripping from his head, placing his hands on his head, and said, ‘Were it not that I would make it difficult for my community, I would have commanded them to pray like this.’”"],[3921,"The Prophet ﷺ was occupied one night from the night prayer until we slept in the mosque, then woke, then slept, then woke. Then he came out and said ﷺ, “No one on earth is waiting for the prayer except you.”"],[3922,"I came to Ṣafwān b. ʿAssāl al-Murādī, and he said to me, “What is your need?” I said, “Seeking knowledge.” He said, “Indeed, the angels lower their wings for the seeker of knowledge, pleased with what he seeks.” I said, “I have a doubt in myself about wiping over the leather socks after defecation and urination. I was one of the Companions of the Prophet ﷺ, so I came to ask you: Have you heard anything from him about that?” He said, “Yes. He used to command us, when we were traveling or on a journey, not to remove our leather socks for three days and their nights, except from major ritual impurity—but not from defecation, urination, or sleep.”"],[3923,"Were it not that I would burden my community, I would have commanded them to use the siwak at every prayer."],[3924,"Were it not that I would burden my community, I would have commanded them to use the siwak with the ablution at every prayer."],[3925,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: ʿThe siwak is purifying for the mouth and pleasing to the Lord.” (Using translation from Aḥmad 62)"],[3926,"«If it were not that you would not bury one another, I would have called upon Allah to make you hear the punishment of the grave.»"],[3927,"I had resolved not to accept a gift except from a Qurayshi, an Ansari, a Thaqafi, or a Dausi."],[3928,"“I declare myself quit of every close friend of his friendship. If I were to take a close friend, I would have taken Abu Bakr as a close friend, but it is the love of brotherhood and faith. Indeed, your companion is the close friend of Allah.”"],[3929,"On the authority of the Prophet ﷺ , he said, \"Every newborn is born upon the natural disposition, and then his parents make him Jewish, Christian or Magian.\""],[3930,"\"He used to kiss some of his wives while he was fasting.\""],[3931,"\"A woman may not fast while her husband is present except with his permission.\""],[3932,"Messenger of Allah ﷺ was asked about the offspring of the pagans. He said, \"Allah knows what they would have done (were they to live).\" (Using translation from Bukhārī 6598)"],[3933,"When they killed the children, the Prophet ﷺ was informed and he said, \"Are not your best among you the children of the polytheists? Every child is born upon the innate nature of Islam, and then his parents make him Jewish, Christian, or Magian.\""],[3934,"Abu Huraira (Allah be pleased with him) reported that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ forbade fasting on these two days. 'Id-ul-Adha and 'Id-ul-Fitr. (Using translation from Muslim 1138)"],[3936,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ saw, during one of his military expeditions, a woman who had been killed, and he disapproved of that and forbade killing women and children."],[3937,"I was among those concerning whom Sa'd b. Mu'adh gave judgment. They were uncertain about me, whether I was a child or a combatant. They looked at my pubic area and found that hair had not grown, so I was placed among the children and was not killed."],[3938,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ passed by me while I was at al-Abwāʾ or Waddān, and I gave him some wild donkey meat as a gift, but he returned it to me. When he saw the displeasure on my face, he said: “It is not that we are rejecting it from you, but we are in a state of iḥrām.”"],[3939,"“There is no protected pasture except for Allah and His Messenger.”"],[3940,"A boy died, so I said, \"Glad tidings for him—a sparrow among the sparrows of Paradise.\" The Prophet ﷺ said, \"Do you not know that Allah created Paradise and created the Fire, and He created for this one its people and for this one its people?\""],[3941,"Water is not made impure by anything."],[3942,"A woman from among the wives of the Prophet ﷺ performed ghusl from janabah. The Prophet ﷺ came to perform wudu' from her leftover water, and she told him about it, but he said, \"Water is not made impure by anything.\""],[3943,"One of the wives of the Prophet ﷺ performed ghusl from a large wooden bowl. The Prophet ﷺ came to perform ghusl or wudu' from it, and she said, \"O Messenger of Allah, I was junub.\" The Prophet ﷺ said, \"Water does not become junub.\""],[3944,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ was asked about water and what comes to it from animals and wild beasts. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, \"If the water is two qullahs, nothing makes it impure.\""],[3945,"Regarding this verse: {Indeed, Allah commands you to render trusts to their owners} up to His saying {Indeed, Allah is ever Hearing and Seeing}, I saw the Prophet ﷺ placing his thumb on his ear and his index finger on his eye."],[3946,"«The month is thus and thus» and he tucked in the thumb on the third time."],[3947,"«The month is thus, the month is thus» he fixed the first three with all his fingers, and the last three with all his fingers except the last one."],[3948,"Saad complained, so the Messenger of Allah ﷺ came to him accompanied by Abdurrahman ibn Awf, Saad ibn Abi Waqqas, and Abdullah ibn Masood. When they entered, they found him unconscious. So the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, \"Indeed, he has passed away!\" The Messenger of Allah ﷺ then wept, and when the Messenger of Allah ﷺ wept, they also wept. He said, \"Do you not hear? Indeed, Allah, the Almighty and Exalted, does not punish with the tears of the eyes or the sorrow of the heart, but He punishes with this,\" and he pointed to his tongue."],[3949,"I said: O Messenger of Allah, tell me something I can hold fast to. He said, \"Say: My Lord is Allah, then remain upright.\" He said: I said, O Messenger of Allah, what is the most severe thing you fear for me? The Messenger of Allah ﷺ took hold of his own tongue."],[3950,"Between every two calls to prayer there is a prayer for one who wishes—he said it three times."],[3951,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ prayed two rak'ahs before Maghrib, then said at the third, 'For whoever wishes,' fearing that people would consider it a sunnah."],[3952,"When the mu'adhdhin gave the adhan, some people from the companions of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ would stand and hasten to the pillars, until the Messenger of Allah ﷺ came out and they were still praying the two rak'ahs before Maghrib, and there was nothing between the adhan and the iqamah."],[3953,"None of you should fast on Friday unless he fasts a day before it or after it."],[3954,"Indeed, some poetry is wisdom."],[3955,"«The likeness of my community is that of rain: it is not known whether its beginning is better or its end.»"],[3956,"«The best of my community is the generation that follows me, then those who follow them, then those who follow them. Then will come a people whose one's testimony will precede his oath and his oath his testimony.»"],[3957,"«You ask me about the Hour. By the One in Whose hand is my soul, there is no soul breathing on the earth that one hundred years will come upon.»"],[3958,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ led us in the night prayer at the end of his life. When he said the salam, he stood and said: «Have you seen this night of yours? At the head of one hundred years, none of those who are on the surface of the earth today will remain.»"],[3959,"«There is none among you, no breathing soul, that one hundred years will come upon it while it is alive.»"],[3960,"“None of you should wish for death or pray for it before it comes, for when he dies his deeds cease, and the believer’s life only increases him in good.”"],[3961,"“When a person dies, his deeds cease except from three: ongoing charity, knowledge that is benefited from, or a righteous child who supplicates for him.”"],[3962,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said during the illness in which he died: \"O 'A'ishah, what did you do with the gold?\" She said: I said: It is with me. He said: \"Bring it to me.\" It was between seven and five. I brought it and placed it in his palm. Then he said: \"What does Muhammad think of Allah, if he meets Allah while this is with him? Spend it.\""],[3963,"If you had seen the Prophet of Allah ﷺ one day during an illness of his. He had with me six or seven dinars. She said: He ordered me to distribute them, but the pain of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ distracted me until Allah cured him. She said: Then he asked me about them. I said: No, by Allah, your pain had distracted me. She said: He called for them and placed them in his palm. Then he said: \"What does the Prophet of Allah think, if he meets Allah while it is with him?\""],[3964,"\"It would not please me to have gold equal to Uhud: three days pass while I have a dinar of it, except something I set aside for a debt I owe.\""],[3965,"The Prophet ﷺ did not store away anything for the next day."],[3966,"The neighbor of a house has more right to the house."],[3967,"I stood before Saʿd b. Abī Waqqāṣ, and al-Miswar b. Makhrama came and placed his hand on one of my shoulders when Abū Rāfiʿ, the freedman of the Prophet ﷺ, came and said: “O Saʿd, buy from me my houses in your compound.” Saʿd said: “No, by Allah, I will not buy them.” Al-Miswar said: “By Allah, you must buy them.” Saʿd said: “By Allah, I will not give you more than four thousand in installments” or “in portions.” Abū Rāfiʿ said: “By Allah, I was offered five hundred dinars for them. Had I not heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say, ‘A man has more right to his adjacent property,’ I would not have given them to you for four thousand dirhams while I was being offered five hundred dinars for them.”"],[3968,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ only established preemption in every property that has not been divided. Once boundaries are set and roads are laid out, there is no preemption."],[3969,"I said to Zaid ibn Arqam, \"Did you not know that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ was gifted a piece of game meat while he was in the state of Ihram, and he returned it?\" He said, \"Yes.\""],[3970,"He gifted a wild donkey to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ while he was at al-Abwāʾ or Waddān, and the Messenger of Allah ﷺ returned it to him. When the Messenger of Allah ﷺ saw what was in my face, he said: “We did not return it to you except that we are in a state of iḥrām.”"],[3971,"Al-Ṣaʿb b. Jaththāmah «gifted the hindquarter of a wild donkey to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ at Qudayd, and he was in a state of iḥrām, and the Messenger of Allah ﷺ returned it.»"],[3972,"«Land game is lawful as long as you did not hunt it or it was not hunted for you.»"],[3973,"We were with Ṭalḥah b. ʿUbayd Allāh, and game meat was gifted to him while they were in a state of iḥrām and he was sleeping. We refused to eat it until he woke up, then we said: “Game was gifted to you.” He said: “What is wrong with you that you did not eat?” They said: “We waited to see what you would say about it.” He said: “We ate the like of this with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. Eat.” So they ate, and he ate."],[3974,"We were with Ṭalḥah b. ʿUbayd Allāh on the Ḥajj while we were in a state of iḥrām, and a bird was gifted to us while Ṭalḥah was sleeping. Some of us ate, and some of us abstained and did not eat it. When Ṭalḥah woke up, we mentioned that to him, and he agreed with those who ate it and said: “We ate it with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ.”"],[3975,"Abū Qatādah was among people in a state of iḥrām, while Abū Qatādah himself was not in iḥrām. The people spotted a wild donkey, but they did not alert him to it until Abū Qatādah himself saw it. He mounted his horse, snatched a whip from one of them, charged at the donkey, and brought it down. He brought it to them, and they ate it and carried [the meat]. They met the Messenger of Allah and asked him about what Abū Qatādah had done. He ﷺ said: “Did any of you point to it or command him?” They said: “No.” He said: “Then eat it.”"],[3976,"The previously married woman has more right over herself than her guardian, and the virgin is asked permission regarding herself, and her permission is her silence."],[3977,"The previously married woman has more right over herself than her guardian, and the virgin's father asks her permission regarding herself, and her permission is her silence."],[3978,"The guardian has no authority over a previously married woman, and the orphan girl is consulted, and her silence is her consent."],[3980,"No marriage is valid without a guardian."],[3981,"We were with the Prophet ﷺ on a military expedition, and the people were afflicted with a severe famine. They asked the Messenger of Allah for permission to slaughter some of their riding camels. Umar said, \"O Messenger of Allah, what would happen to us if we met our enemy hungry and on foot? But if you see fit, O Messenger of Allah, call upon the people to bring the remainder of their provisions.\" So they came with them, each man bringing a handful of food or more, and the one who brought the most brought a sa' of dates. He gathered it on a leather mat, then called upon Allah as Allah willed him to call. Then he invited the people to bring their vessels, and there remained not a vessel in the army except that it was filled, and there remained the like of it. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ laughed until his molars showed, then he said: «I bear witness that there is no god but Allah, and I bear witness that I am the Messenger of Allah, and I bear witness before Allah that no believing servant meets Him with these two but that they will veil him from the Fire on the Day of Resurrection.»"],[3982,"«The people of Paradise will enter Paradise and the people of the Fire will enter the Fire. Then He, Glorified and Exalted, will say, \"Look for anyone in whose heart you find a mustard seed's weight of faith, and bring him out.\"» He said, «So they will be brought out of it as charcoal after they have been burned, and they will be thrown into the River of Life, and they will grow in it as a seed grows by the side of a torrent.» The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, «Have you not seen how it comes out yellow and twisted?»"],[3983,"\"And purify your clothes\" – he said: \"And your deeds, set them right.\""],[3984,"\"People will be gathered barefoot, naked, and uncircumcised.\""],[3985,"\"Every servant will be resurrected upon that which he died.\""],[3986,"A man from the people of the suffah died, and they found two dinars in his blanket. They mentioned that to the Prophet ﷺ, and he said, 'Two brands.'"],[3987,"I was with the Prophet ﷺ when a funeral was brought. They said, 'Pray over it, O Messenger of Allah.' He said, 'Did he leave behind any debt?' They said, 'No.' He said, 'Did he leave behind anything?' They said, 'Three dinars.' He said, 'Three brands.' Then a second funeral was brought. They said, 'O Prophet of Allah, pray over it.' He said, 'Did he leave behind any debt?' They said, 'Yes.' He said, 'Did he leave behind anything?' They said, 'No.' A man from the Ansar called Abu Qatadah said, 'O Messenger of Allah, I will be responsible for his debt.' Then the Messenger of Allah ﷺ prayed over him."],[3988,"While the Messenger of Allah ﷺ was distributing gold, a man came to him and said, 'O Messenger of Allah, give me.' He gave him. Then he said, 'Give me more,' and he gave him more three times. Then the man turned away. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, 'A man comes to me and asks me, and I give him, then he asks me again, and I give him three times, then he turns away, having placed fire in his garment to take back to his family.'"],[3989,"When the Messenger of Allah ﷺ returned from Tabuk, he was asked about the Hour, so he said: «One hundred years will not come upon people while on the surface of the earth there is a breathing soul.» *"],[3990,"«You ask me about the Hour. By the One in Whose hand is my soul, there is no soul breathing on the earth today that one hundred years will come upon it.»"],[3991,"The angels do not accompany a group that has a bell."],[3992,"The angels do not enter a house in which there is a dog or an image."],[3993,"Angels do not enter a house in which there is an image, a dog, or a person in a state of major ritual impurity."],[3994,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ woke up one day looking distressed. Maymunah said: O Messenger of Allah, I have noticed something strange about your appearance since today. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Jibril had promised me that he would meet me last night, but he did not meet me. By Allah, he did not break his promise to me.” He said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ remained like that the rest of his day. Then it occurred to him that there was a puppy under a tent of his, so he ordered that it be taken out. Then he took some water in his hand and sprinkled the place. When evening came, Jibril met him, and he said: “You had promised me that you would meet me last night.” He said: Yes, but we do not enter a house in which there is a dog or an image."],[3995,"The Prophet ﷺ ordered Umar b. al-Khattab ؓ at the time of the conquest, while he was at al-Batha', to go to the Ka'bah and erase every image in it, and the Prophet ﷺ did not enter it until every image in it had been erased."],[3996,"A prayer in the mosque of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ is better than a thousand prayers in any other mosque except the Sacred Mosque, for the Messenger of Allah ﷺ is the last of the prophets and his mosque is the last of the mosques."],[3997,"«Gabriel came to me and gave me glad tidings that whoever dies from my nation not associating anything with Allah will enter Paradise, even if he committed adultery and even if he stole.»"],[3998,"“It is not lawful for a Muslim to sever relations with a Muslim for more than three [days]. They are both deviating from the truth as long as they are severed. The first of them to return will have his precedence in returning as an expiation for him. If he greets him and he does not accept his greeting, the angels return it to him, and the devil returns it to the other. If they die while severed, they will not enter Paradise, nor will they be together in Paradise.”"],[3999,"From Abu al-Tayyah, Qatadah, and Hamzah al-Dabbi: They said, 'We heard Anas b. Malik say, from the Prophet ﷺ, \"I was sent and the Hour like this,\" and he gestured with his two fingers.' Qatadah would say, 'As the excess of one over the other.'"],[4000,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, 'I was sent and the Hour like these two,' and he joined his index finger and middle finger."],[4001,"I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say, pointing with his finger next to the thumb and the middle finger, 'I was sent and the Hour like this.'"],[4002,"I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say a month before he died: «You ask me about the Hour, but its knowledge is only with Allah. I swear by Allah, there is no breathing soul on the surface of the earth today that one hundred years will come upon.»"],[4003,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, \"Seventy thousand people from my Ummah (community) will enter Paradise without being held accountable.\" Ukasha bin Muhsin said, \"O Messenger of Allah, pray to Allah to make me one of them.\" The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, \"O Allah, make him one of them.\" Then another person said, \"Pray to Allah to make me one of them.\" The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, \"Ukasha has beaten you to it.\""],[4004,"Whoever fasts perpetually, he has neither fasted nor broken his fast."],[4005,"None of you should fast on Friday unless he fasts a day before it or after it."],[4006,"«The two months of Eid do not decrease: Ramadan and Dhu al-Hijjah.»"],[4007,"Indeed, faith will retreat to al-Madinah just as a snake retreats to its hole."],[4008,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ looked at Uhud and said: \"Indeed, Uhud is a mountain that loves us and we love it.\""],[4009,"An Arab man entered upon the Prophet ﷺ and the Prophet ﷺ said, \"Has Umm Milham taken hold of you?\" He said, \"And who is Umm Milham?\" He said, \"A blister that forms between the skin and the flesh.\" He said, \"I have never had this before.\""],[4010,"A man said: O Messenger of Allah, when will the Hour occur? The prayer was commenced. When the Messenger of Allah ﷺ finished his prayer, he said: \"Where is the one who asked about the Hour?\" He said: Here I am, O Messenger of Allah. He said: \"It is coming, so what have you prepared for it?\" He said: I have not prepared for it much action except that I love Allah and His Messenger. The Prophet ﷺ said: \"You are with the one you love.\" He said: And there was with him a man from the Ansar called Muhammad, so he said: \"If this one lives, old age will not overtake him until the Hour occurs.\""],[4011,"A man came to the Prophet Muhammad ﷺ arguing with his father about a debt owed to him. The Prophet ﷺ said, \"You and your wealth belong to your father.\""],[4012,"“A man is deprived of provision because of a sin he commits. Decree is not repelled except by supplication, and nothing increases one’s lifespan except righteousness.”"],[4013,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ as saying: If anyone becomes insolvent and the man (i.e. creditor) finds his very property with him, he is more entitled to it than anyone else. (Using translation from Abū Dāʾūd 3519)"],[4014,"When a man buys a commodity and then goes bankrupt while it is still with him in its original form, he has more right to it than the creditors."],[4015,"When a man goes bankrupt and the seller finds his goods themselves, he has more right to them than the creditors."],[4016,"When a man becomes insolvent and the seller finds his goods themselves, he has more right to them."],[4017,"Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, \"Whoever died and he ought to have fasted (the missed days of Ramadan) then his guardians must fast on his behalf.\" (Using translation from Bukhārī 1952)"],[4018,"When a dog laps from the vessel of one of you, then wash it seven times."],[4019,"The purification of the vessel of one of you, when a dog laps from it, is to wash it seven times."],[4020,"When a dog laps from the vessel of one of you, let him pour it out, then wash it seven times."],[4021,"The purification of the vessel of one of you, when a dog laps from it, is to wash it seven times, the first of them with dust."],[4022,"When a dog laps from the vessel, then wash it seven times and rub it the eighth time with dust."],[4023,"He who took an oath, but he found something else better than that, should do that which is better and break his oath. (Using translation from Muslim 1651b)"],[4024,"that a man came to him and asked him for provision. He said: I have nothing to give you except my coat of mail and my helmet, so I will write to my family to give it to you. He was not satisfied, so he swore that he would not give him anything. Then the man became satisfied, and 'Adi said: Were it not that I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say, «Whoever swears an oath and then sees something more God-fearing than it, let him do the God-fearing thing,» I would not have broken my oath."],[4025,"«Whoever swears an oath concerning his possession that he will strike it, its expiation is to leave it, and with the expiation there is a good deed.»"],[4026,"«Whoever swears an oath and then sees something better than it, let him do what is better and expiate his oath.»"],[4027,"«O 'Abd al-Rahman, do not ask for authority, for if it comes to you by asking, you will be left to it; and if it comes to you without asking, you will be helped with it. And when you swear an oath and then see something better than it, do what is better and expiate your oath.»"],[4028,"«Whoever swears an oath and then sees something better than it, let him expiate his oath and do what is better.»"],[4029,"\"Whoever swears an oath and says: If Allah wills, has made an exception.\""],[4030,"\"Whoever swears an oath and says: If Allah wills, will not break his oath.\""],[4031,"\"Whoever swears an oath and says: If Allah wills, has made an exception.\""],[4032,"\"Whoever swears an oath and makes an exception, he has the choice: if he wishes, he may proceed; and if he wishes, he may leave, without breaking his oath.\""],[4033,"«By Allah, I will surely raid Quraysh; by Allah, I will surely raid Quraysh; by Allah, I will surely raid Quraysh.» Then he fell silent and said, «If Allah wills.»"],[4034,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ caught up with Umar b. al-Khattab while he was swearing by his father, so he said: \"Allah forbids you from swearing by your fathers. Whoever swears, let him swear by Allah or remain silent.\""],[4035,"Any slave owned by partners, if one of them frees his share, then it is assessed at a fair value from the wealth of the one who freed, and the slave is freed if his wealth reaches that."],[4036,"Whoever frees his share in a slave and has wealth reaching the price of the slave, the slave is assessed at a fair value against him, and he gives his partners their shares and the slave is freed. Otherwise, he has freed what he freed."],[4037,"Whoever frees a slave in whom he has a partner, and he has sufficient means, the slave is free, and he guarantees his partners their shares at a fair value because he harmed their partnership, and the slave owes nothing."],[4038,"Any slave jointly owned by two people, if one of them frees his share, then if he is wealthy, the slave's value is assessed and he pays the other partner; and if he is poor, the slave is required to work to earn his freedom without being overburdened."],[4039,"Whoever frees a share in a slave, he is responsible for completing the freeing of the slave from his own wealth if he has wealth. If he has no wealth, the slave is assessed at a fair value, then the slave is required to work to earn the share of the one who did not free him, without being overburdened."],[4040,"\"The blood money for the hands and the feet is equal: ten camels for each finger.\""],[4041,"The fingers are equal, this and this."],[4042,"Whoever catches one rak'ah of the prayer has caught the prayer."],[4043,"Whoever prays one rak'ah of the morning prayer before the sun rises has not missed the prayer, and whoever prays one rak'ah of the afternoon prayer before the sun sets has not missed the prayer."],[4044,"Whoever catches one rak'ah of the prayer has caught the entire prayer."],[4045,"Whoever catches one rak'ah of a prayer has caught it, but let him complete what remains."],[4047,"Whoever catches a rak'ah of Subh before the sun rises has caught Subh, and whoever catches a rak'ah of Asr before the sun sets has caught Asr."],[4048,"Whoever catches a sajdah of Asr before the sun sets, or of Subh before the sun rises, has caught it."],[4049,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: 'Whoever catches a rak'ah of Asr before the sun sets has caught it, and whoever catches a rak'ah of Fajr before the sun rises * after the sun rises has caught it.'"],[4050,"When one of you catches the first sajdah of Subh before the sun rises, let him complete his prayer; and when he catches the first sajdah of Asr prayer before the sun sets, let him complete his prayer."],[4051,"Whoever forgets a prayer, let him pray it when he remembers it."],[4052,"Whoever forgets a prayer, let him pray it when he remembers it; there is no expiation for it except that."],[4053,"The translation of the given phrase from Arabic to English is as follows: \"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, 'Whoever experiences dawn and does not perform the Witr prayer, there is no Witr for him.'\""],[4054,"\"The two parties to a sale have the option as long as they do not separate.\""],[4055,"\"There is no sale between two parties to a transaction until they separate, except a sale with an option.\""],[4056,"\"Whoever buys something and it becomes his, he has the option over his counterpart as long as he does not part from him: if he wishes, he takes it, and if he wishes, he leaves it. If he parts from him, then there is no option for him.\""],[4057,"\"The two parties to a sale, each of them has the option against the other as long as they do not separate, except a sale with an option.\""],[4058,"\"When two men engage in a sale, each of them has the option as long as they do not separate and are together, or one of them gives the other the choice. If one of them gives the other the choice and they conclude the sale on that basis, then the sale is binding. If they separate after concluding the sale and neither of them has withdrawn from the sale, then the sale is binding.\""],[4059,"«Whoever buys palm trees after they have been pollinated and does not stipulate their fruit, then nothing of it belongs to him. And whoever buys a slave and does not stipulate his property, then nothing of it belongs to him.»"],[4060,"«Whoever buys palm trees after they have been pollinated, their fruit belongs to the seller, unless the buyer stipulates otherwise. And whoever sells a slave who has property, his property belongs to the seller, unless the buyer stipulates otherwise.»"],[4061,"«Whoever sells palm trees after they have been pollinated, their fruit belongs to the seller, unless the buyer stipulates otherwise. And whoever sells a slave who has property, his property belongs to the seller, unless the buyer stipulates otherwise.»"],[4062,"«Whoever buys a slave who has property, then the property belongs to him, and upon him is the slave's debt, unless the buyer stipulates otherwise. And whoever pollinates palm trees and then sells them after their pollination, the fruit belongs to him, unless the buyer stipulates otherwise.»"],[4063,"Whoever revives dead land, he has a reward in it, and whatever the grazing animals eat from it is charity for him."],[4064,"Whoever revives dead land, he has a reward for it, and whatever the grazing animals eat from it, he has a reward for it."],[4065,"Whoever revives dead land, it belongs to him, and whatever the grazing animals eat from it is charity for him."],[4066,"\"If someone looked into your house without your permission and you threw a pebble at him and gouged out his eye, there would be no sin upon you.\""],[4067,"\"Whoever looks into a people's house without their permission and they gouge out his eye, there is no blood money and no retaliation.\""],[4068,"I heard the Prophet ﷺ delivering a sermon at ʿArafāt: \"Whoever cannot find sandals, let him wear khuffs; and whoever cannot find an izar, let him wear trousers.\""],[4069,"\"The Messenger of Allah said: 'An orphan girl should be consulted with regard to marriage, and if she remains silent, that is her permission. If she refuses then she is not to be forced.'\" (Using translation from Nasāʾī 3270)"],[4071,"Any woman married without the permission of her guardian, her marriage is invalid, twice. She may keep what he gave her for what he obtained from her. If there is a dispute between them, then that is for the authority, and the authority is the guardian of one who has no guardian."],[4072,"There is no ṣadaqah upon the Muslim for his horse or his slave."],[4073,"There is no ṣadaqah upon a man for his horse and his slave except the zakāh of fiṭr."],[4074,"that two brothers from the Ansar had an inheritance between them. One of them asked his companion for the division, and he said: If you ask me again for the division, I will never speak to you, and all my wealth is for the door of the Ka'bah. 'Umar b. al-Khattab ؓ said: The Ka'bah is in no need of your wealth. Expiate your oath and speak to your brother, for I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: «There is no oath or vow in disobedience, or in severing ties of kinship, or in what you do not own.»"],[4075,"Umm Salamah made a mukataba contract with him (Nabhan), and there remained of his contract two thousand dirhams. Nabhan said: I used to withhold it so that Umm Salamah would not veil herself from me. He said: I performed the pilgrimage, and I saw her at al-Bayda'. She said to me: \"Who is this?\" I said: \"I am Abu Yahya.\" She said to me: \"O my son, call to me my brother's son Muhammad b. 'Abd Allah b. Abi Umayyah and give him what I am owed from you for his marriage, and I convey my greetings to you.\" He said: I wept and cried out and said: \"By Allah, I will never give it to him.\" She said: \"O my son, the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: 'When one of you has a mukatab who has enough to pay off his contract, then veil yourself from him. By Allah, you will not see me again except that you will see me in the Hereafter.'\""],[4076,"When the Messenger of Allah ﷺ conquered Makkah, he said: \"There is no god but Allah; He fulfilled His promise, aided His servant, and defeated the confederates alone. Indeed, every privilege of the pre-Islamic era is under these two feet of mine, except the custodianship of the Ka'bah and providing water for pilgrims. Indeed, the one killed by mistake, resembling intentional, killed by a whip or stick, requires a heavy blood money: forty camels, among them pregnant ones.\""],[4077,"\"If a fasting person eats or drinks forgetfully, let him complete his fast, for Allah has fed him and given him drink.\""],[4078,"\"Whoever breaks his fast in the month of Ramadan out of forgetfulness has no makeup or expiation due upon him.\""],[4079,"\"Whoever vomits involuntarily while fasting does not have to make it up, but whoever vomits deliberately must make it up.\""],[4080,"We were with the Prophet ﷺ on a journey. He said to a man, 'Dismount and prepare a drink for us by mixing.' The man said, 'The sun [has not set], O Messenger of Allah.' He said, 'Dismount and mix for us.' The man said, 'The sun, O Messenger of Allah.' He said, 'Dismount and mix for us.' So he dismounted and mixed, and he drank. Then he said, 'When you see the night approaching from here and the day departing from here, the fasting person has broken his fast.'"],[4081,"\"The injury caused by a beast is without liability, the well is without liability, the mine is without liability, and on treasure-trove one-fifth is due.\""],[4082,"That the Messenger of Allah ﷺ was asked about the slave woman if she committed adultery and was not muhsanah. He said: \"If she commits adultery, flog her. Then if she commits adultery, flog her. Then if she commits adultery, flog her. Then sell her, even for a rope of hair.\""],[4084,"\"Take from me: Allah has made a way for them. The previously married with the previously married: one hundred lashes, then stoning. The virgin with the virgin: one hundred lashes and both are exiled for a year.\""],[4085,"\"The Prophet ﷺ stoned two Jews who had been married.\""],[4086,"“When the two circumcised parts meet, bathing becomes obligatory.”"],[4087,"If you differ concerning roads, then leave seven cubits."],[4088,"There is no ṣadaqah in what is less than five ounces, no ṣadaqah in what is less than five wasqs, and no ṣadaqah in what is less than five camels."],[4089,"Two women were stitching, and there was no one else in the house with them. One of them came out having been stabbed in the palm of her hand with an awl that came out of the back of her hand. She said that her companion had stabbed her, but the other denied it. So she sent to Ibn 'Abbas about them and told him the story. He said, \"Do not give anything except with clear proof, for the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, 'If people were given according to their claims, men would claim the wealth and blood of other men, but the oath is upon the defendant.' So call her and recite to her the Qur'an, and recite: {Indeed, those who purchase a small gain at the cost of Allah's covenant and their oaths}.\" I did so, and she confessed."],[4090,"A pledge is not forfeited. Its benefit belongs to him and its liability is upon him."],[4091,"“A mount may be ridden when it is pawned, and its milk may be drunk when it is pawned, but the one who rides it or milks it must pay for its upkeep.' ” (Using translation from Ibn Mājah 2440)"],[4092,"Khaza'ah were allies of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and Banu Bakr, a clan of Banu Kinanah, were allies of Abu Sufyan. He said: There was a truce between them during the days of al-Hudaybiyyah. Banu Bakr raided Khaza'ah during that period, so they sent to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ seeking his aid. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ went out to aid them in the month of Ramadan. He fasted until he reached Qudayd, then he broke his fast and said: \"Let the people fast while traveling and break their fast. Whoever fasts, his fast suffices him, and whoever breaks his fast must make it up.\" Then Allah granted the conquest of Makkah. When he entered it, he leaned his back against the Ka'bah and said: \"Withhold weapons except Khaza'ah against Bakr,\" until a man came and said: \"O Messenger of Allah, a man was killed at al-Muzdalifah.\" He said: \"This sanctuary is sacred by the command of Allah. It was not lawful for anyone before me, nor will it be lawful for anyone after me. It was made lawful for me only for one hour. It is not lawful for a Muslim to brandish a weapon in it, nor to cut its fresh herbage, nor to cut its trees, nor to startle its game.\" A man said: \"O Messenger of Allah, except idhkhir, for it is for our houses and our graves.\" The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"Except idhkhir. The most insolent of people against Allah are three: one who kills in Allah's sanctuary, or kills other than his killer, or kills for a Jahiliyyah vendetta.\" A man stood up and said: \"O Prophet of Allah, I had intercourse with a slave girl of Banu so-and-so, and she bore me a child. Order that my child be returned to me.\" He ﷺ said: \"He is not your child. This is not permissible in Islam. The one against whom claim is made is more entitled to the oath unless clear evidence is established. The child belongs to the owner of the bed, and for the fornicator is the athlab.\" A man said: \"O Prophet of Allah, what is the athlab?\" He said: \"The stone. Whoever commits adultery with a woman he does not own or with the woman of another people and she gives birth, then the child is not his; he does not inherit nor is he inherited from. The believers are a hand against those besides them; their blood is equal. Their lowest may grant protection, and their farthest returns to them. A believer is not killed for a disbeliever, nor a person with a covenant while in his covenant. The people of two religions do not inherit from each other. A woman is not married to her paternal aunt or her maternal aunt. She does not travel three days without a mahram. Do not pray after dawn until the sun rises, and do not pray after 'asr until the sun sets.\""],[4093,"\"All of Arafat is a standing place, but keep away from Urana. All of Muzdalifah is a standing place, but keep away from Muhassir. All the passes of Mina are places of sacrifice, and on all the days of Tashriq, sacrifice is permitted.\""],[4094,"A man from the Ansar came to the Prophet ﷺ and said: \"O Messenger of Allah, there are some matters I want to ask you about.\" He said: \"Sit down.\" Then a man from Thaqif came and said: \"O Messenger of Allah, there are some matters I want to ask you about.\" The Prophet ﷺ said: \"The Ansari has preceded you.\" The Ansari said: \"He is a stranger, and a stranger has a right, so begin with him.\" So he turned to the Thaqafi and said: \"If you wish, I will answer you about what you were going to ask, and if you wish, you ask me and I will tell you.\" He said: \"O Messenger of Allah, rather answer me about what I was going to ask you.\" He said: \"You came to ask me about bowing, prostration, prayer, and fasting.\" He said: \"No, by the One who sent you with the truth, you did not miss anything that was in my mind.\" He said: \"When you bow, place your palms on your knees, then spread your fingers apart, then remain until every limb takes its position. When you prostrate, place your forehead firmly on the ground and do not peck quickly. Pray at the beginning of the day and at its end.\" He said: \"O Prophet of Allah, what if I pray between them?\" He said: \"Then you will be one who prays. Fast from every month the thirteenth, fourteenth, and fifteenth.\" Then the Thaqafi stood up. Then he turned to the Ansari and said: \"If you wish, I will tell you about what you came to ask, and if you wish, you ask me and I will tell you.\" He said: \"No, O Prophet of Allah.\""],[4095,"«When he sits between her four limbs and then exerts himself upon her, ghusl becomes obligatory.»"],[4096,"A man asked the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, 'What clothing should we wear when we enter ihram?' He replied, 'Do not wear the shirt, trousers, turbans, hooded cloaks, or leather socks, except a man who does not have sandals should cut the leather socks to below the ankles. And do not wear any garment that has been touched by saffron or wars.'"],[4097,"The tanning of the skins of dead animals is their purification."],[4098,"\"The slaughter of the fetus is the slaughter of its mother.\""],[4099,"There was a treaty between Mu'awiyah and the Romans, and he was marching towards their land, intending to raid them when the treaty expired. Then an old man said, 'Allahu Akbar, Allahu Akbar, no treachery!' It was 'Amr b. 'Abasah. I asked him, and he said, 'I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: \"If there is a treaty between a people, no knot may be untied until its term has elapsed or it is renounced to them equally.\"'"],[4100,"If a fly falls into the vessel of one of you, then indeed in one of its wings there is a disease and in the other there is a cure, and it protects itself with the wing that has the disease, so let him immerse it completely and then remove it."],[4101,"The Prophet ﷺ as saying: A Muslim may not inherit from an infidel nor an infidel from a Muslim. (Using translation from Abū Dāʾūd 2909)"],[4102,"O Messenger of Allah, stay in your house in Makkah. He said: 'And has 'Aqil left us any dwellings or houses?' 'Aqil and Talib inherited Abu Talib, but Ja'far and 'Ali did not inherit anything because they were Muslims, while 'Aqil and Talib were disbelievers. For that reason, 'Umar b. al-Khattab ؓ used to say: 'A believer does not inherit from a disbeliever.'"],[4103,"«The benefit is accompanied by liability.»"],[4104,"«If people were given according to their claims, people would claim the blood and wealth of other men, but the oath is upon the defendant.»"],[4105,"Whoever introduces into this matter of ours what is not from it, it is rejected."],[4106,"«The month is twenty-nine.»"],[4107,"None of you should fast on Friday unless he fasts a day before it or after it."],[4108,"The Prophet ﷺ secluded himself from his wives for a month. Then the Prophet ﷺ came out on the morning of the twenty-ninth, and some of the people said: O Messenger of Allah, we have reached the morning of the twenty-ninth. He ﷺ said: «The month may be twenty-nine.» Then the Prophet ﷺ clapped three times: twice with all the fingers of his hands, and the third with nine of them."],[4109,"«The month may be twenty-nine.»"],[4110,"A man praised another man in the presence of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, so the Prophet ﷺ said: “Woe to you, you have cut the neck of your companion” repeatedly. Then he said: “If one of you must praise his brother, let him say: I reckon so-and-so, and Allah is his reckoner—if he knows that to be such and such.”"],[4111,"A man praised another man in the presence of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, so the Prophet ﷺ said: “Woe to you—you have cut the neck of your companion” repeatedly. Then he said: “If one of you must praise his brother, then let him say: I reckon so-and-so, and I do not vouch for anyone before Allah.”"],[4112,"I had sheep at Uhud, and death fell upon them. I entered upon Maymunah and mentioned that to her, and Maymunah said to me: \"If you took their skins and benefited from them?\" I said: \"Is that lawful?\" She said: \"Yes. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ passed by some men of Quraysh who were dragging a sheep of theirs like a donkey, and the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to them: 'If you took its hide.' They said: 'It is dead.' The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: 'Water and qaraz (acacia pods) purify it.'\""],[4113,"«Whoever spends a pair in the path of Allah from his wealth, the keepers of Paradise call him: O so-and-so, come, this is good, several times.» Abu Bakr said: O Messenger of Allah, this is one who will have no loss. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: «Indeed, I hope that all the keepers will call you.»"],[4114,"«Do you have any difficulty in seeing the moon on the night of the full moon when there is no cloud?» They said: No, O Messenger of Allah. He said: «Do you have any difficulty in seeing the sun at midday when there is no cloud?» They said: No, O Messenger of Allah. He said: «By the One in whose hand is my soul, you will have no difficulty in seeing your Lord just as you have no difficulty in seeing them. Then the servant will be met, and He will say: O so-and-so, did I not honor you, did I not make you a chief, did I not marry you off, did I not subject for you horses and camels and let you lead and graze? He will say: Yes, O Lord. He will say: Did you think that you would meet Me? He will say: No, O Lord. He will say: Today I forget you as you forgot Me.» He said: «Then the second will be met, and He will say: Did I not honor you, did I not make you a chief, did I not marry you off, did I not subject for you horses and camels and let you lead and graze? He will say: Yes, O Lord. He will say: Did you think that you would meet Me? He will say: No, O Lord. He will say: Today I forget you as you forgot Me.» He said: «Then the third will be met, and He will say: What are you? He will say: I am Your servant; I believed in You and in Your Prophet and in Your Book, and I fasted, prayed, and gave charity, and he will praise with good as much as he can. He said: Then it will be said to him: Shall we not send Our witness against you? He said: Then he will think to himself who will testify against him. He said: Then his mouth will be sealed, and it will be said to his thigh: Speak. He said: Then his thigh, his flesh, and his bones will speak of what he used to do. That is the hypocrite, and that is to excuse Himself from him, and that is the one upon whom Allah is wrathful.» He said: «Then a caller will call out: Indeed, every nation has followed what it used to worship. He said: Then the allies of the devils will follow the devils. He said: And the Jews and Christians will follow their allies to Hell. Then he said: Then the believers will remain, then we will remain, O believers. Then our Lord will come to us, and He is our Lord, and He will say: What are these standing for? They will say: We are the servants of Allah, the believers; we worshipped Him, and He is our Lord, and He is coming to us and rewarding us, and this is our station. He said: Then He will say: I am your Lord, so proceed. He said: Then the bridge will be laid, and upon it are hooks of fire that snatch people. At that point, intercession will take place: O Allah, grant safety, O Allah, grant safety. When he crosses the bridge, then everyone who spent a pair of wealth from what he owns in the path of Allah, all the keepers of Paradise will call him: O servant of Allah, O Muslim, this is good. It will be said: O servant of Allah, O Muslim, this is good.» Abu Bakr said: O Messenger of Allah, that is for a servant who has no loss; he leaves one gate and enters from another. He said: Then the Prophet ﷺ struck his shoulders and said: «By the One in whose hand is my soul, I hope that you will be one of them.» 'Abd al-Jabbar said: Sufyan dictated it to me in full dictation."],[4115,"I arrived at the camp and met Abu Dhar. I said, \"O Abu Dhar, what is your wealth?\" He said, \"My wealth is my actions.\" I said, \"O Abu Dhar, won't you tell me a hadith that you heard from the Messenger of Allah ﷺ?\" He said, \"Yes, I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say, 'No Muslim couple has three children who do not reach the age of puberty, but Allah will admit them to Paradise by His mercy.'\" And I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say, 'No man spends on his two wives in the cause of Allah, but the two gates of Paradise will be opened for him.'\" I asked, \"And what are the two wives from his wealth?\" He said, \"Two servants from his slaves, two horsemen from his horses, and two camels from his camels.\""],[4116,"People will continue to be upon good as long as they hasten the breaking of the fast."],[4117,"The religion will continue to be manifest as long as people hasten the breaking of the fast, for the Jews and Christians delay it."],[4118,"I never saw the Messenger of Allah ﷺ pray the Maghrib prayer until he broke his fast, even if with a sip of water."],[4119,"\"My community will remain upon my sunnah as long as they do not wait for the stars to break their fast.\" He said: When the Prophet ﷺ was fasting, he would order a man to ascend to a high place, and when he said, 'The sun has set,' he would break his fast."],[4120,"«The Muslim is one from whose tongue and hand the Muslims are safe, and the emigrant is one who emigrates from what Allah has forbidden.»"],[4121,"The Muslim is one from whose tongue and hand the Muslims are safe, and the believer is one whom people trust with their blood and wealth."],[4122,"I had a small flock that a slave girl of mine pastured near Uḥud and al-Jawwāniyyah. One day I came upon her and the wolf had gone off with one of the sheep. I am one of the children of Adam; I feel regret as they feel regret, so I struck her a slap. That weighed heavily on me, so I went to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and said, \"Should I not set her free?\" He said, \"Bring her to me.\" I brought her to him, and he said, \"Where is Allah?\" She said, \"In the sky.\" He said, \"Who am I?\" She said, \"You are the Messenger of Allah ﷺ.\" He said, \"Set her free, for she is a believer.\""],[4123,"There will be rulers after me who say what they do not do and do what they are not commanded. Whoever strives against them with his hand is a believer, whoever strives against them with his tongue is a believer, and whoever strives against them with his heart is a believer; there is no faith beyond that."],[4124,"A servant does not believe until he believes in four things: he bears witness that there is no god but Allah and that I am the Messenger of Allah, he believes in the resurrection after death, and he believes in the divine decree."],[4125,"None of you believes until I am more beloved to him than his child, his parent, and all people."],[4126,"“Four traits: whoever has them is a pure hypocrite, and whoever has one of them has a trait of hypocrisy until he gives it up: when he speaks, he lies; when he makes a covenant, he betrays; when he promises, he breaks it; and when he quarrels, he acts wickedly.”"],[4127,"“Four traits: whoever has them is a pure hypocrite: when he speaks, he lies; when he promises, he breaks it; when he makes a covenant, he betrays; and when he quarrels, he acts wickedly. And whoever has one of them has a trait of hypocrisy.”"],[4128,"Three (traits): whoever has them is a hypocrite, even if he fasts, prays, and claims that he is a Muslim: one who, when he speaks, lies; when he promises, he breaks it; and when he is entrusted, he betrays."],[4129,"Whoever abandons Jumu'ah three times without an excuse is a hypocrite."],[4130,"I entered upon Anas b. Malik, I and a companion of mine, after Zuhr. He said, 'Have you two prayed Asr?' We said, 'No.' He said, 'Pray in the room at your place.' We finished, and he lengthened his prayer, then turned to us. The first thing he said to us was: 'The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"That is the prayer of the hypocrites: one of them delays until when the sun is between the two horns of Satan, then he stands and pecks four (units), not remembering Allah in them except a little.\"\""],[4131,"Shall I not inform you of the prayer of the hypocrites? He leaves Asr until when it is between the two horns of Satan or upon the two horns of Satan, then he stands and pecks like the pecking of a rooster, not remembering Allah in them except a little."],[4132,"Some people asked the Messenger of Allah ﷺ about the soothsayers (kuhhan). The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to them: 'They are nothing.' They said: 'O Messenger of Allah, sometimes they speak of something that comes true.' The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: 'That is a word from the jinn which he snatches and casts into the ear of his ally (walī), and they mix with it more than a hundred lies.'"],[4133,"“The thief does not steal when he steals while he is a believer, and he does not drink wine when he drinks it while he is a believer, but the doors of repentance are open.”"],[4134,"\"The thief does not steal when he steals while he is a believer, nor does the adulterer commit adultery when he commits adultery while he is a believer, nor does the wine drinker drink wine when he drinks it while he is a believer - and repentance is offered thereafter.\""],[4135,"The adulterer does not commit adultery while he is a believer, and the thief does not steal while he is a believer, and no one drinks wine while drinking it as a believer."],[4136,"The adulterer does not commit adultery while committing it as a believer, the thief does not steal while stealing as a believer, and no one drinks wine while drinking it as a believer, and no one plunders a plunder while plundering it as a believer."],[4137,"“The thief does not steal when he steals while he is a believer; the adulterer does not commit adultery when he commits it while he is a believer; the wine-drinker does not drink wine when he drinks it while he is a believer—by the One in whose hand is Muhammad’s soul—and no one snatches a prized plunder toward which the believers raise their eyes while he is a believer when he snatches it; and none of you kills when he kills while he is a believer. Beware, beware!”"],[4138,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ addressed us and said in the sermon: \"There is no faith for one who has no trustworthiness, and no religion for one who has no covenant.\""],[4139,"The Prophet ﷺ set out toward Baqi' al-Gharqad, and I set out behind him. He said, \"O Abu Dharr.\" I said, \"At your service, then at your service, and I am your ransom.\" He said, \"Those who have much wealth are the ones with little on the Day of Resurrection, except one who says of his wealth, 'Thus and thus,' to his right and to his left\"—he said it three times. Then Uhud appeared before us, and he said, \"O Abu Dharr, it would not please me that the family of Muhammad had gold and a dinar or mithqal remained with them overnight.\" I said, \"Allah and His Messenger know best.\" Then a valley appeared before us, and the Prophet ﷺ went into its interior and descended into it, while I sat at its edge. I thought he had some need, and he was slow in returning to me, and my thoughts became uneasy. Then I heard a whispered conversation. He said, \"That is Jibril informing me for my community: whoever of them bears witness that there is no god but Allah and that Muhammad is the Messenger of Allah will enter Paradise.\" I said, \"O Messenger of Allah, even if he commits adultery and steals?\" He said, \"Even if he commits adultery and steals.\""],[4140,"The believer is not one who defames, curses, speaks obscenely, or is shameless."],[4141,"There is no forbearing person but one who has stumbled, and no wise person but one with experience."],[4142,"The dust in the path of Allah and the smoke of Hellfire will never come together in the belly of a servant, and stinginess and faith will never come together in the heart of a servant, ever."],[4143,"ʿAbd Allāh b. Masʿūd entered the mosque while the Prophet ﷺ was delivering the sermon and sat beside Ubayy b. Kaʿb. He asked him about something or spoke to him about something, but Ubayy did not respond. Ibn Masʿūd thought it was because of some resentment. When the Prophet ﷺ finished his prayer, Ibn Masʿūd said, \"O Ubayy, what prevented you from responding to me?\" He said, \"You did not attend Friday with us.\" He said, \"Why?\" He said, \"You spoke while the Prophet ﷺ was delivering the sermon.\" Ibn Masʿūd got up, went to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and mentioned that to him. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to him, \"Ubayy spoke the truth; obey Ubayy.\""],[4145,"'If Allah were to withhold rain from the people for seven years, then send it down, a group of them would become disbelievers because of it, saying: We were given rain by the star of al-Mijdah.'"],[4146,"Three things are disbelief in Allah: wailing, tearing the garment, and defaming lineage."],[4147,"Abd Allah entered upon a woman, and on her neck was something that had an amulet, so he pulled it and cut it, then he said: The family of Abd Allah have become rich enough not to associate partners with Allah in that for which He has sent down no authority. Then he said: I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: 'Indeed, incantations, amulets, and love-charms are shirk.' They said: O Abu Abd al-Rahman, we know about incantations and amulets, but what is a love-charm? He said: 'Something that women make to endear themselves to their husbands.'"],[4148,"\"Whoever swears by a religion other than Islam falsely, he is as he said, and whoever kills himself with something in this world will be punished with it on the Day of Resurrection.\""],[4149,"From the Prophet ﷺ, he said: \"There will be after me rulers whom crowds of people will flock to. Whoever confirms them in their lies and aids them in their oppression, I am free from him and he is free from me. And whoever does not confirm them in their lies and does not aid them in their oppression, I am of him and he is of me.\""],[4150,"'Tiyarah (belief in evil omens) is Shirk (associating partners with Allah). There is none of us but has some of it, but Allah removes it by reliance on Him.'"],[4151,"«When the funeral is placed and the men carry it on their shoulders, if it was righteous it says: 'Send me forward,' and if it was not righteous it says: 'Woe to it! Where are they taking it?' Its voice is heard by everything except the human, and if the human heard it, he would faint.»"],[4152,"I said, 'O Prophet of God, a man from my people insults me while he is inferior to me. May I retaliate against him?' The Prophet ﷺ said, 'The two revilers are two devils who hurl abuse at each other and lie to each other.'"],[4153,"\"A bed for the man, a bed for his wife, the third for the guest, and the fourth for Satan.\""],[4154,"Two men came from the east and gave a speech, and the people were amazed at their eloquence. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, “Indeed, some eloquence is sorcery,” or “Indeed, some eloquence is sorcery.”"],[4155,"A Bedouin came to the Prophet ﷺ and spoke with eloquent speech, so the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"Indeed, some eloquence is sorcery, and some poetry is wisdom.\""],[4156,"“Eloquence is from Allah and inarticulateness is from Satan. Eloquence is not abundance of speech, but eloquence is decisiveness in the truth. Inarticulateness is not scarcity of speech, but it is the one who makes light of the truth.”"],[4157,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said one day to his companions: “Tell me about a tree whose likeness is the likeness of the believer.” He said: The people began mentioning trees from the trees of the valley. Abdullah said: And it was cast into my mind or my thought that it was the date-palm. He said: So I wanted to speak, but I saw some of the elders among the people, and I was afraid to say anything. Then when they had not identified it, the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “It is the date-palm.”"],[4158,"“Among the trees is a tree whose leaves do not fall, and it is like the Muslim. So tell me what it is?” The people fell to mentioning the trees of the deserts. Abdullah said: It occurred to me that it was the date-palm, but I felt shy. Then they said…"],[4159,"He asked, \"Which of you loves his own wealth more than the wealth of his heir?\" They said, \"O Messenger of Allah, there is none of us but loves his own wealth more than the wealth of his heir.\" He said, \"Know what you are saying.\" They said, \"We know nothing but that, O Messenger of Allah.\" He said, \"There is no man among you but loves the wealth of his heir more than his own wealth.\" They said, \"How so, O Messenger of Allah?\" He said, \"Indeed, a man's wealth is what he sends ahead, and the wealth of his heir is what he leaves behind.\""],[4160,"«Shall I not inform you of the best among you?» They said: \"Yes, O Messenger of Allah.\" He said: \"Those with the longest lives and the best character among you.\""],[4161,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said in a gathering, “Shall I not inform you of the most beloved of you to me and the nearest of you to me in seating on the Day of Resurrection?” three times, saying it. We said, “Yes, O Messenger of Allah.” He said, “The best of you in character.”"],[4162,"\"How will you be, O 'Abd Allah, when you remain among the dregs of people?\" He said, \"And what are they, O Messenger of Allah?\" He said, \"That is when their trusts and covenants become confused and they become like this,\" and he interlaced his fingers. He said, \"So what should I do, O Messenger of Allah?\" He said, \"Do what you know and leave what you disapprove of, attend to your own self and leave the common people.\""],[4163,"“What do you say about the wrestler?” I said, “The one whom men cannot throw down.” He said, “The wrestler is the one who controls himself at the time of anger.”"],[4164,"\"What do you consider a childless man among you?\" He said: We said, \"The one who has no children born to him.\" He said, \"That is not the childless one; rather it is the one who does not send ahead any of his children (i.e., none of his children die before him).\" He said, \"What do you consider a strong man among you?\" We said, \"The one whom men cannot throw down.\" He said, \"It is not that; rather it is the one who controls himself at times of anger.\""],[4165,"He said: 'Shall I not tell you of something that is better than the rank of fasting and praying?' They said: 'Yes, O Messenger of Allah.' He said: 'Reconciling between people, for the corruption of relations between people is the shaver.'"],[4166,"“The year of drought is not that you are not given rain, but the year of drought is that you are given rain and are given rain, but the earth does not grow anything.”"],[4167,"«Will you not form rows as the angels form rows in the presence of their Lord?» He said: We said: O Messenger of Allah, how do the angels form rows in the presence of their Lord? He said: «They complete the foremost rows and stand close together in the row.»"],[4168,"While they were sitting with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, a star was thrown (a meteor) and it lit up. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to them: 'What did you used to say in the pre-Islamic period (Jahiliyyah) when such a thing was thrown?' They said: 'We used to say: Tonight a great man is born, and tonight a great man has died.' The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: 'It is not thrown for the death of anyone or for his life. But our Lord, Blessed and Exalted, when He decrees a matter, the bearers of the Throne glorify Him, then the people of the heaven who are next to them glorify, until the glorification reaches the people of the lowest heaven. Then those next to the bearers of the Throne say: What did your Lord say? They inform them, and the people of the heavens inform one another until the news reaches the people of the lowest heaven. The jinn snatch (the word) and cast it to their allies, and they are pelted (with meteors). What they bring as it is, is true, but they add falsehood to it or they increase (in it).'"],[4169,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ led us in the morning prayer at al-Hudaybiyyah following a rain that had fallen at night. When he finished, he turned to the people and said: 'Do you know what your Lord has said?' They said: Allah and His Messenger know best. He said: 'Some of My servants have become believers in Me and disbelievers this morning. As for the one who said: We were given rain by the grace and mercy of Allah, that one believes in Me and disbelieves in the star. As for the one who said: We were given rain by such-and-such a star, that one disbelieves in Me and believes in the stars.'"],[4170,"'The keys of the unseen are five, none knows them but Allah: none knows what the wombs diminish except Allah, none knows what is in tomorrow except Allah, none knows when the rain comes except Allah, no soul knows in which land it will die except Allah, and none knows when the Hour will occur except Allah.'"],[4171,"«Whom do you consider martyrs among you?» They said, \"O Messenger of Allah, whoever is killed in the way of Allah is a martyr.\" He said, «Then the martyrs of my community would be few.» They said, \"Who then, O Messenger of Allah?\" He said, «Whoever is killed in the way of Allah is a martyr, whoever dies in the way of Allah is a martyr, whoever dies in the plague is a martyr, and whoever dies of a stomach disease is a martyr»"],[4172,"From the Prophet ﷺ who said, \"Do you know what backbiting is?\" They said, \"Allah and His Messenger know best.\" He said, \"It is mentioning your brother with something he dislikes.\" A man said, \"What if what I say about my brother is true?\" He said, \"If what you say about him is true, you have backbitten him; and if it is not true, you have slandered him.\""],[4173,"“While we were with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, he heard a thud. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, ‘Do you know what this is?’ We said, ‘Allah and His Messenger know best.’ He said, ‘This is a stone thrown into the Fire seventy autumns ago, and only now has it reached the bottom of the Fire.’”"],[4174,"I was with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ in the mosque at sunset, and he said, \"Do you know where the sun sets?\" I said, \"Allah and His Messenger know best.\""],[4175,"I was riding behind the Prophet ﷺ, and between me and him was only the rear part of the saddle. He said, \"O Mu'adh!\" I replied, \"At your service, O Messenger of Allah, and at your command.\" He said, then he traveled for a while, then he said, \"O Mu'adh!\" I replied, \"At your service, O Messenger of Allah, and at your command.\" He said, \"Do you know what Allah's right upon His servants is?\" I said, \"Allah and His Messenger know best.\" He said, \"That they worship Him and do not associate anything with Him.\" He said, then he traveled for a while, then he said, \"Do you know what the servants' right upon Allah is if they do that?\" I said, \"Allah and His Messenger know best.\" He said, \"Indeed, the servants' right upon Allah, if they do that, is that He will not punish them.\""],[4176,"I came to Abu Sa'id al-Khudri and said, \"Did you hear the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say anything about the lower garment?\" He said, \"Yes, I heard him say, 'The lower garment of the believer is to the middle of his shins, and there is no blame on him for what is between that and the ankles. Whatever is below that is in the Fire. Allah will not look at the one who drags his lower garment out of arrogance.'\""],[4177,"“Modesty is from faith, and faith is in Paradise; and obscenity is from harshness, and harshness is in the Fire.”"],[4178,"“Modesty is from faith, and faith is in Paradise; and obscenity is from harshness, and harshness is in the Fire.”"],[4179,"'Whoever obeys me has obeyed Allah, and whoever disobeys me has disobeyed Allah. Whoever obeys the amir has obeyed me, and whoever disobeys the amir has disobeyed me.'"],[4180,"“When we pledged allegiance to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ to hear and obey, he would say to us: ‘In what you are able.’”"],[4181,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ sent 'Alqamah b. Mujazziz al-Mudliji on an expedition, and I was among them. We set out until when we were at the start of our campaign or on part of the road, a group sought permission from him and he gave them permission, and he appointed over them 'Abd Allah b. Hudhafah al-Sahmi, who was one of the Companions of Badr and had a sense of humor. I was among those who returned with him. While we were on the road, we stopped at a place and the people kindled a fire to warm themselves by it or to prepare something for themselves. Then 'Abd Allah b. Hudhafah said to them: 'Do I not have over you the right of hearing and obedience?' They said: 'Yes.' He said: 'So I command you to something – will you not do it?' They said: 'Yes.' He said: 'Verily I adjure you by my right and your obedience that you leap into this fire.' He said: Some people stood up until he thought they were about to leap into it. Then he said: 'Restrain yourselves. I was only joking with you.' When they came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, they mentioned that to him. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: 'Whoever commands you to disobedience, do not obey him.'"],[4182,"“Whoever bears arms against us is not one of us.”"],[4183,"The parable of the one who is lenient with the limits of Allah, the one who commands them, and the one who forbids them is like a people who drew lots for a ship at sea. Some of them got the stern, farthest from the water, and some got the top. When they wanted water and were at the back of the ship, they annoyed their companions. Some of them said, 'We are closest to the water and farthest from it; let us bore a hole in the side of the ship and draw water, and when we no longer need it we will plug it.' The foolish among them said, 'Do it.' He took the axe and struck the side of the ship. A wise man among them said, 'What are you doing?' He said, 'We are closest to the water and farthest from it; we will break the side of the ship and draw water, and when we no longer need it we will plug it.' He said, 'Do not do it, for if you do, you will perish and we will perish.'"],[4184,"\"How will you be, O 'Abd Allah, when you remain among the dregs of people?\" He said, \"And what are they, O Messenger of Allah?\" He said, \"That is when their trusts and covenants become confused and they become like this,\" and he interlaced his fingers. He said, \"So what should I do, O Messenger of Allah?\" He said, \"Do what you know and leave what you disapprove of, attend to your own self and leave the common people.\""],[4185,"“Fasting while traveling is not part of righteousness.”"],[4186,"These people are the disobedient ones; these are the disobedient ones. (Using translation from Muslim 1114a)"],[4187,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to us at a river of rainwater—while he was on a mule of his and the people were fasting—“Drink.” They began looking at him. He said, “Drink, for I am riding, and I am the most at ease among you, while you are on foot.” They began looking at him, so he turned his hip, drank, and the people drank."],[4188,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ saw a man around whom people had gathered, and shade had been made for him. He asked, “What is this?” They said, “A man who is fasting.” The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, “It is not righteousness to fast while traveling.”"],[4189,"\"O Messenger of Allah, I find within myself strength to fast while traveling. Is there any sin upon me?\" The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"It is a concession from Allah. Whoever takes it has done well, and whoever loves to fast, there is no sin upon him.\""],[4190,"\"Allah loves that His concessions be taken, just as He loves that His strict commands be taken.\""],[4191,"A man came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and mentioned that he was burned. He asked him about his matter, and he mentioned that he had fallen upon his wife during Ramadan. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ was brought a basket called ʿaraq containing dates, and he said: \"Where is the burned one?\" The man stood up, and he said: \"Give this in charity.\""],[4192,"While we were sitting with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, a man came to him and said: O Messenger of Allah, I am destroyed. He said: \"What is the matter with you?\" He said: I fell upon my wife while I was fasting. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"Can you find a slave to free?\" He said: No. He said: \"Can you fast two consecutive months?\" He said: No, by Allah, O Messenger of Allah. He said: \"Can you find food to feed sixty poor people?\" He said: No, O Messenger of Allah. Then the Messenger of Allah ﷺ remained silent. Abu Hurayrah said: While we were in that state, the Messenger of Allah ﷺ was brought a basket containing dates, and ʿaraq is the miktal. He said: \"Where is the one who asked just now? Take this dates and give it in charity.\" The man said: On those poorer than my family, O Messenger of Allah? By Allah, there is no household between its two lava tracts — he meant the two ḥarrahs — poorer than my household. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ laughed until his canine teeth showed, then said: \"Feed it to your family.\""],[4193,"A man said: O Messenger of Allah, I am destroyed. He said: \"Woe to you, what is that?\" He said: I fell upon my wife on a day in the month of Ramadan. He said: \"Free a slave.\" He said: I cannot find. He said: \"Fast two consecutive months.\" He said: I cannot. He said: \"Feed sixty poor people.\" He said: I cannot find. Then the Messenger of Allah ﷺ was brought a basket containing fifteen saʿs of dates. He said to him: \"Give it in charity.\" He said: On those poorer than my family? There is no one between the two lava tracts of Madinah more in need than my family. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ laughed until his canine teeth showed and said: \"Take it, seek Allah's forgiveness, and feed it to your family.\""],[4194,"A woman came to the Prophet ﷺ and said: My sister died and owed two consecutive months of fasting. He said: \"Do you think if your sister had a debt, would you pay it?\" She said: Yes. He said: \"Then the right of Allah is more deserving.\""],[4195,"When ʿUmar was stabbed, Ḥafṣa began wailing over him. ʿUmar said to her, \"O Ḥafṣa, have you not heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say, 'The one over whom wailing is done is punished'?\" She said, \"Yes.\""],[4196,"«Indeed, the disbeliever is increased in punishment by some of the weeping of his family over him.»"],[4197,"We went out with the Prophet ﷺ one day until he passed by the house of a man from the Ansar. The Prophet ﷺ said: “Where is so-and-so?” He called him, and the man came out in a hurry, his head dripping water. The Prophet ﷺ said: “Perhaps we hurried you from your need.” The man said: Yes, by Allah, O Messenger of Allah, I was hurried. The Prophet ﷺ said: “When one of you is hurried or prevented from ejaculating, no bathing is due upon him; he only has to perform ablution.”"],[4198,"I said: O Messenger of Allah, a man has intercourse with a woman but does not ejaculate. He said: “He should wash what of him touched the woman, perform ablution, and pray.”"],[4200,"He asked ʿUthmān b. ʿAffān about a man who has sexual intercourse but does not ejaculate. He said: “Nothing is due from him.” Then ʿUthmān said: “I heard it from the Messenger of Allah ﷺ.” He said: “After that I asked ʿAlī b. Abī Ṭālib, al-Zubayr b. al-ʿAwwām, Ṭalḥa b. ʿUbayd Allāh, and Ubayy b. Kaʿb, and they said the same.”"],[4201,"“Water from water was only a dispensation in the early days of Islam, then it was forbidden.”"],[4202,"“When he sits between her four limbs and then exerts himself, bathing is obligatory upon him.”"],[4203,"She was asked about a man who has intercourse but does not ejaculate. She said: “I did that with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and we both bathed because of it.”"],[4204,"“When the two circumcised parts meet, bathing becomes obligatory. I did it with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and we bathed.”"],[4205,"Umm Sulaym asked the Messenger of Allah ﷺ about a woman who sees in her sleep what a man sees. He said: 'If the woman has a discharge, she should perform ghusl.'"],[4206,"Umm Sulaym, the wife of Abu Talhah, came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and said: 'O Messenger of Allah, Allah is not ashamed of the truth. Is a woman required to perform ghusl if she has a wet dream?' He said: 'Yes, if she sees water.'"],[4207,"«The man's fluid is thick and white, and the woman's fluid is thin and yellow. Whichever of the two prevails determines the resemblance.»"],[4208,"I was shown Laylat al-Qadr, then my family woke me and I forgot it, so seek it in the last ten nights."],[4209,"We were discussing Laylat al-Qadr, so I went to Abu Sa'id al-Khudri and said, \"Did you hear the Messenger of Allah ﷺ mention Laylat al-Qadr?\" He said, \"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ observed i'tikaf during the middle ten days of Ramadan, and we observed i'tikaf with him. When it was the morning of the twentieth, he returned and we returned with him. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ stood up and saw Laylat al-Qadr in a dream, then he was made to forget it.\""],[4210,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ observed iʿtikāf during the first ten days of Ramadan, then he observed iʿtikāf during the middle ten days in a Turkish tent, with a piece of matting over its doorway. He took the matting with his hand and moved it aside in the tent, then he put his head out and spoke to the people, and they drew near to him. He said: “I observed iʿtikāf during the first ten days seeking this night, then I observed iʿtikāf during the middle ten days. Then I was visited and told that it is in the last ten days. Whoever among you wishes to observe iʿtikāf, let him do so.” So the people observed iʿtikāf with him. He said: “I was shown it, and I was prostrating on its morning in mud and water.” On the morning of the twenty-first night, he got up for the dawn prayer, and the sky rained and the mosque leaked, and I saw the mud clearly when he came out after finishing the dawn prayer, with his forehead and nose in water and mud. And that was the twenty-first night of the last ten."],[4211,"I came to Abu Sa'eed Al-Khudri and said, \"O Abu Sa'eed, come out with us to the palm trees so that we can talk.\" He said, \"Yes.\" He called for a garment to wear, then he came out. I said, \"O Abu Sa'eed, have you heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ mention the Night of Decree?\" He said, \"Yes, we used to observe Itikaf with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ for the first ten days of Ramadan. When the twentieth day came, the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, 'Whoever was observing Itikaf should continue to do so, for I have been shown that Night (of Decree), but I have been made to forget which night it is, and I saw myself prostrating in water and mud. Seek it on the odd nights of the last ten nights of Ramadan.'\" Abu Sa'eed said, \"But we did not see any clouds in the sky.\" Then when the night came, the sky was covered with clouds like mountains, and it rained until the roof of the mosque started to leak. I looked at the Messenger of Allah ﷺ prostrating in water and mud until I saw the mud on the hair of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ .\""],[4212,"\"My father narrated to me: 'The Night of Al-Qadr was mentioned in the presence of Abu Bakrah, so he said: \"I do not search for it due to something that I heard from the Messenger of Allah, except for during the last ten (nights); for indeed I heard him say: 'Search for it when nine remain, or; when seven remain, or; when five remain, or; during the last three nights.'\" He (Uyainah) said: \"During the twenty (nights) of Ramadan, Abu Bakrah used to perform Salat just as he performed Salat during the rest of the year. But when the (last) ten began, he would struggle (performing more Salat during the night).\" (Using translation from Tirmidhī 794)"],[4213,"Some men among the companions of the Prophet ﷺ were shown Laylat al-Qadr in their dreams during the last seven nights. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, \"I see that your dreams have agreed on the last seven nights, so whoever seeks it, let him seek it in the last seven nights.\""],[4214,"The Messenger of Allahﷺ said, \"Seek out the Night of Qadr during the last ten nights of Ramadan, and if one of you weakens or becomes unable, let him not be overwhelmed by the remaining seven nights.\""],[4215,"“Laylat al-Qadr is the twenty-seventh night.”"],[4216,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ observed iʿtikāf during the middle ten days of Ramadan, seeking Laylat al-Qadr. When it ended, he ordered the structure to be dismantled, and it was dismantled. Then it was made clear to him that it was in the last ten days of Ramadan. He went out to the people and said: “O people, Laylat al-Qadr was made clear to me, and I came out to tell you about it, but two men came disputing, and the devil was with them, so I was made to forget it. Seek it in the seventh and seek it in the fifth.”"],[4217,"I sat with Abu Dharr near the middle Jamrah and drew close to him until my knee almost touched his knees. I said: Tell me about Laylat al-Qadr. He said: I was the one who asked people about it, and I asked the Messenger of Allah. I said: O Messenger of Allah, tell me about Laylat al-Qadr. Is it during the time of the prophets, when revelation descends upon them, and when they are taken, it is lifted? He said: “Rather, it remains until the Day of Resurrection.” I said: O Messenger of Allah, tell me in which month it is. He said: “If Allah willed, I would have informed you of it. Seek it in the last ten nights, in one of the two sets of seven, and do not ask me about it after this time.” He then turned to his companions and began speaking with them. When I saw the Messenger of Allah ﷺ become engrossed in conversation, I said: I adjure you by Allah, O Messenger of Allah, to tell me in which of the two sets of seven it is. He became angry with me in a way he had never been angry before and said: “May your mother be bereft of you! It occurs in the last seven.”"],[4218,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"Indeed, I saw the Night of Qadr (Decree/Power) and then I forgot it. It is in the last ten nights (of Ramadan), and it is calm, neither hot nor cold. It is as if there is a moon casting its light, not dimming its stars, and its evil spirits do not come out until its dawn comes.\""],[4219,"The Prophet of Allah ﷺ came out to inform us about Laylat al-Qadr, but two Muslim men were arguing. He said, \"I came out to inform you about Laylat al-Qadr, but so-and-so and so-and-so argued, and it was taken away. Perhaps that is better for you, so seek it in the ninth, the seventh, and the fifth.\""],[4220,"We said: O Abu al-Mundhir, how do you recognize that? He said: By the sign or the indication that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ told us: “The sun rises on that day with no rays.”"],[4221,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to spend the middle ten days of Ramadan in retirement and devotion (i'tikaf) in the mosque. One year he had retirement and devotion in the mosque (as usual); when the twenty-first night came, and this night when he used to come out his devotion in the mosque, he said: He who has engaged himself in devotion along with me should do so during the last ten days; I saw that night, that was caused to forget it, but I have seen myself prostrating in water and mud on the morning following (that night), so seek it in the last ten days and seek it every night with an odd number. Abu sa'id said: Rain fell that night, the mosque that was thatched building dripped, and my eyes saw the Messenger of Allah ﷺ with the traces of water and mud, on his forehead on the morning following the twenty-first night. (Using translation from Abū Dāʾūd 1382)"],[4222,"\"While the Prophet ﷺ was delivering a sermon, a caravan arrived in Madinah, and the Companions of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ rushed to it, so that only twelve men remained, among them Abu Bakr and 'Umar, and the verse was revealed.\""],[4223,"While the Prophet ﷺ was delivering the Friday sermon, a caravan arrived in Madinah, and the Companions of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ rushed to it, so that only twelve men remained with him ﷺ. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, \"By the One in whose hand is my soul, if you had all followed one another until none of you remained, the valley would have flowed with fire for you.\""],[4224,"\"A man from Banu Sulaym passed by a group of the companions of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ with some sheep. He greeted them with salam. They said, 'He did not greet you except to protect himself from you.' So they attacked him, killed him, and took his sheep. They brought them to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and Allah revealed: {O you who believe, when you go forth in the cause of Allah, investigate carefully} to the end of the verse.\" *"],[4225,"\"Idolaters from the Quraish came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ quarreling about Al-Qadar. So this Ayah was revealed: \"The day they will be dragged on their faces into the Fire (it will be said to them): \"Taste you the touch of Hell.\" Verily we have created all things with Qadar. (Using translation from Tirmidhī 2157)"],[4226,"A beautiful woman, one of the most beautiful of people, used to pray behind the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. Some of the people would come forward to the first row so as not to see her, and some would lag behind until they were in the last row; and when he bowed, he would look from under his armpit. So Allah revealed concerning her: “And We know those among you who come forward, and We know those who lag behind.” [Al-Hijr:24]"],[4227,"A Bedouin gave a gift to the Prophet ﷺ, and he rewarded him for it, then said, ‘Are you satisfied?’ He said, ‘No.’ So he increased it and said, ‘Are you satisfied?’ He said, ‘Yes.’ Then the Prophet ﷺ said, ‘I had resolved not to accept gifts except from a Qurayshi, an Ansari, or a Thaqafi.’"],[4228,"“Were it not that dogs are a community among the communities, I would have commanded that they be killed. So kill the pure-black one among them.” He said, “And any people who take a dog that is not a dog for farming, hunting, or livestock, a qīrāṭ is diminished from their reward every day.” He said, “And we were commanded to pray in the sheepfolds and not to pray in the camel resting places, for they were created from the devils.”"],[4229,"“Were it not that dogs are a community among the communities, I would have commanded that they be killed. But kill the black, pure-black dog, for it is a devil.”"],[4230,"\"I had intended to forbid al-ghīlah, until I remembered that the Byzantines and Persians do that and it does not harm their children.\""],[4231,"“Were it not that I would make things difficult for my Ummah, I would have commanded them to use the siwak with every wudu and would have delayed the Isha prayer until one-third of the night or half the night.”"],[4232,"Were it not that I would burden my Ummah, I would love not to stay behind any expedition that goes out in the cause of Allah. But I do not find what to mount them on, and they do not find anything to ride, and it is hard for them to stay behind after me. I wish I could fight in the cause of Allah and be killed, then brought to life and killed, then brought to life and killed."],[4233,"“If I live, if Allah wills, I will expel the Jews and the Christians from the Arabian Peninsula until only a Muslim remains in it.”"],[4234,"“The prayer is interrupted by the donkey, the woman, and the black dog.” He said: I said, “What about the black one as opposed to the red, the yellow, and the white?” He said, “O son of my brother, I asked the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and he said, ‘The black dog is a devil.’”"],[4235,"I asked Abu Dharr about what interrupts the prayer. He said: If there is not in front of you something like the back of a saddle, the woman, the donkey, and the black dog. I said: What about the black one as opposed to the yellow and the white? He said: O son of my brother, I asked the Messenger of Allah ﷺ just as you asked me, and he said, “The black dog is a devil.”"],[4236,"The prayer of a man is interrupted by the woman, the donkey, and the black dog if there is not in front of him something like the back of a saddle. He said: I said, “O Abu Dharr, what about the black one as opposed to the white and the red?” He said, “O son of my brother, I asked the Messenger of Allah ﷺ just as you asked me, and he said, ‘The black dog is a devil.’”"],[4237,"“The prayer of a man is interrupted if there is not in front of him something like the back of a saddle, by the donkey, the black dog, and the woman.” He said: I said, “What about the black one as opposed to the red and the yellow?” He said, “I asked the Messenger of Allah ﷺ just as you asked me, and he said, ‘The black one is a devil.’”"],[4238,"“The prayer is interrupted by the dog, the donkey, and the woman.”"],[4239,"“The prayer is interrupted by the dog and the menstruating woman.”"],[4240,"“The prayer is interrupted by the woman, the donkey, and the black dog.” I said, “O Abu Dharr, what about the black one as opposed to the red and the yellow?” He said, “I asked the Messenger of Allah ﷺ just as you asked me, and he said, ‘The black one is a devil.’”"],[4241,"“I saw myself lying in front of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, stretched out like a funeral bier, while he was praying.”"],[4242,"\"That the Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to pray during the night while I was asleep between him and the qibla, and when he reached Witr, he would awaken me.\""],[4243,"\"That the Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to pray and I would be positioned in front of him concerning the Qibla, so when he intended to perform Witr prayer, he would gesture to me with his leg.\""],[4244,"The translation of the given Arabic phrase into English is: \"The Prophet ﷺ used to pray at night, and I was between him and the qibla. When he wanted to perform the Witr prayer, he would wake me up, and I would also perform the Witr prayer.\""],[4245,"I used to stretch my legs toward the qiblah of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ while he was praying. When he prostrated he would poke me, so I raised them, and when he stood I returned them."],[4246,"“The prayer is repeated because of the passing of a donkey, a woman, and a black dog.” I said, “What about the black one as opposed to the yellow and the red?” He said, “I asked the Messenger of Allah ﷺ just as you asked me, and he said, ‘The black dog is a devil.’”"],[4247,"“If there is not in front of him something like the back of a saddle, then the woman, the donkey, and the black dog interrupt his prayer.” He said: I said, “O Abu Dharr, what about the black dog as opposed to the red dog and the yellow dog?” He said, “O son of my brother, I asked the Messenger of Allah ﷺ about what you asked me, and he said, ‘The black dog is a devil.’”"],[4248,"“I came riding on a female donkey, and at that time I had nearly reached puberty. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ was praying with the people at Mina, and I passed in front of part of the row. I dismounted, let the donkey graze, and entered the row, and no one objected to that.”"],[4249,"“I came to the Prophet ﷺ while he was at al-Abtah in a red leather tent of his.” He said: “Bilal came out with his ablution water, and it was partly used and partly fresh.” He said: “The Messenger of Allah ﷺ came out wearing a red suit, as if I were looking at the whiteness of his shins.” He said: “He performed ablution, and Bilal gave the call to prayer. He started following his mouth, here and there, saying right and left: ‘Come to prayer, come to success.’ Then a short spear was planted for him, and he stood and prayed the afternoon prayer as two rak‘ahs, while a donkey and a dog passed in front of him without being prevented. Then he continued to pray two rak‘ahs until he returned to Madinah.”"],[4250,"When one of you places before him something like the backrest of a saddle, let him pray and not care about whoever passes beyond that."],[4251,"Do not pray except facing a sutra, and do not let anyone pass in front of you. If he insists, then fight him, for he is only a devil."],[4252,"When one of you prays, let him place something before his face. Let him set up a stick. If he does not have a stick, let him draw a line. Then whatever passes in front of him will not harm him."],[4253,"A spear was planted for him and he prayed toward it."],[4254,"He used to come with Salamah b. al-Akwa' to the Duha prayer. He would head for a pillar and pray near it. I would say to him, “Do not pray here,” and point to another spot in the mosque, but he would say, “I saw the Messenger of Allah ﷺ seek out this place.”"],[4255,"I saw the Messenger of Allah ﷺ praying toward his riding mount."],[4256,"When one of you prays toward a sutra, let him draw close to it, for indeed the devil passes between him and it, and he should not let anyone pass in front of him."],[4257,"The fitrah is five: trimming the nails, clipping the moustache, shaving the pubic area, circumcision, and plucking the armpit hair."],[4258,"The most beloved of My servants to Me is the one who is quickest in breaking the fast."],[4259,"From the Prophet ﷺ, he said: “The best of companions are four, the best of raiding parties are four hundred, the best of armies are four thousand, and twelve thousand will never be defeated due to small numbers.”"],[4261,"The Messenger of Allah said: The most merciful of my Ummah towards my Ummah is Abu Bakr; the one who adheres most sternly to the religion of Allah is 'Umar; the most sincere of them in shyness and modesty is 'Uthman; the best judge is 'Ali bin Abu Talib; the best in reciting the Book of Allah is Ubayy bin Ka'b; the most knowledgeable of what is lawful and unlawful is Mu'adh bin Jabal; and the most knowledgeable of the rules of inheritance (Fara'id) is Zaid bin Thabit. And every nation has a trustworthy guardian, and the trustworthy guardian of this Ummah is Abu 'Ubaidah bin Jarrah.\" (Using translation from Ibn Mājah 154)"],[4262,"\"The most poetic word spoken by the Arabs is the saying of Labid.\""],[4263,"The most poetic verse uttered by the Arabs is the saying of Labid."],[4264,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ saw women and children of the Helpers coming from a wedding, and the Prophet ﷺ said to them, “You are the most beloved of people to me.”"],[4265,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ came to me, his face beaming, and said, \"Did you not see Mujazziz? He looked just now at Zayd b. Harithah and Usamah b. Zayd and said, 'Some of these feet are from the same.'\""],[4266,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ came to me happy and joyful because of what Mujazziz al-Mudliji said. He looked at Usamah b. Zayd lying with his father and said, 'These feet are from one another.' Mujazziz was a physiognomist."],[4267,"The Prophet ﷺ and I went together until we entered the synagogue of the Jews in the city on their holiday, but they did not like our entry. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to them, \"O assembly of Jews, show me twelve men who bear witness that there is no god but Allah and that I am the Messenger of Allah, and Allah will remove His anger from any Jew beneath the sky.\" None of them answered him, so he repeated his request three times, and no one answered him. Then he said, \"You have refused, so by Allah, I am the gatherer, the last to live, and the one who will strike with punishment. Have you believed or denied?\" Then he left and I was with him until he was about to leave, when a man from behind us said, \"As you are, O Muhammad.\" The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, \"Who are you, O Jews?\" They said, \"We do not know of any person among us who is more knowledgeable about the Book of Allah than you, nor more understanding than you or your father before you, or your grandfather before your father.\" He said, \"Then I bear witness for him with Allah that he is the Messenger of Allah whom you find written in the Torah.\" They said, \"You have lied.\" Then they rejected him and said evil things to him. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to them, \"You have lied, and your words will not be accepted. As for now, you praise him with good words when he does something good, but when he believes, you deny him and say what you do not say. Your words will not be accepted.\" Then we left, and we were three: the Messenger of Allah ﷺ , Abdullah ibn Salam, and I. Then Allah revealed in this regard the verse: \"Say, 'Have you considered: if it is from Allah and you disbelieved in it...?'\" (Surah Al-An'am, 6:35)."],[4268,"We were with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and we were six people. The polytheists said, 'Drive these away from you, for they are...' and I, Ibn Mas'ud, a man from Hudhayl, Bilal, and two men—one of whom I have forgotten—were present. He said: Then something entered the heart of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ as Allah willed, and he spoke to himself about it. Then Allah revealed: 'And do not send away those who call upon their Lord morning and evening, seeking His face' up to His saying: 'the wrongdoers' (Qur'an 6:52)."],[4269,"Jibrīl delayed coming to the Prophet ﷺ, and the polytheists said, 'He has been forsaken.' So Allah revealed: {Your Lord has not forsaken you, nor is He displeased}."],[4270,"The Prophet ﷺ became ill and did not stand for a night or two. A woman came to him and said, 'O Muhammad, I do not see your devil except that he has left you.' So Allah revealed: {By the morning brightness and by the night when it is still, your Lord has not forsaken you, nor is He displeased}."],[4271,"On the Day of Uhud, the Prophet ﷺ was wiping the blood from his face while saying, 'How can a people prosper who wounded their Prophet and broke his front tooth while he is calling them to Allah?' Then Allah revealed: 'Not for you, [O Muhammad], is the decision' (Qur'an 3:128)."],[4272,"When it was the day of Uhud, seventy-four of the Ansar were struck, and among them six, including Hamzah, and they mutilated them. The Ansar said, “If we ever get the better of them one day, we will do more to them.” When it was the day of the conquest of Makkah, Allah sent down, “And if you retaliate, then retaliate with the like of what you were afflicted with; but if you are patient, it is better for the patient.” A man said, “No Quraysh after today.” The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, “Restrain from the people except four.”"],[4273,"When the Prophet ﷺ left Makkah, Abu Bakr said, “They have expelled their Prophet. ‘Indeed we belong to Allah and indeed to Him we will return.’ They will surely be destroyed.” Then it was revealed: “Permission [to fight] has been given to those who are being fought, because they were wronged. And indeed, Allah is able to give them victory.” He said, “So I knew that it would happen.” Ibn Abbas said, “It is the first verse revealed concerning fighting.”"],[4274,"“We were in the city of the Byzantines, and they sent out against us a great rank of Byzantines, and a similar or larger one went out to them. Over the people of Egypt was Uqbah b. Amir, the companion of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. A man from the Muslims charged at the Byzantine rank until he entered among them. The people shouted at him and said, ‘Glory be to Allah! You are throwing yourself into destruction with your own hand.’ Abu Ayyub al-Ansari stood up and said, ‘O people, you are interpreting this verse in this way. This verse was only revealed concerning us, the Ansar. When Allah strengthened Islam and increased its supporters, we said to one another secretly from the Messenger of Allah ﷺ: “Our wealth has been lost, and Allah has strengthened Islam and increased its supporters. If only we stayed with our wealth and repaired what we had lost.” Then Allah revealed to His Prophet ﷺ, refuting what we had said: “And spend in the way of Allah and do not throw [yourselves] with your [own] hands into destruction. And do good; indeed, Allah loves the doers of good.” So destruction was staying with our wealth and repairing it and abandoning raiding.’”"],[4275,"Anas b. al-Nadr was absent from the fighting at Badr and said, “I was absent from the first battle the Prophet ﷺ witnessed. By Allah, if Allah shows me a fight, He will see what I do.” Then on the day of Uhud, the companions of the Prophet ﷺ were routed, and Saʿd b. Muʿādh came forward saying, “Where? Where? By the One in whose hand is my soul, I find the scent of Paradise before Uhud.” He said, so he charged and fought and was killed. Saʿd said, “By Allah, O Messenger of Allah, I could not do what he did.” His sister said, “By Allah, I did not recognize my brother except by the beauty of his fingertips.” They found in him eighty-some wounds, from sword strikes, arrow shots, and spear thrusts. Then Allah revealed: “Among the believers are men who have been true to what they pledged to Allah. Some of them have fulfilled their vow, and some are still waiting, and they have not changed in the least.” Ḥammād said, “And I read in Ubayy’s codex: ‘And among them are those who changed in the least.’”"],[4276,"'Spoils were not lawful for anyone of the black-haired before you; fire used to descend from heaven and consume them. When the day of Badr came, the people fell upon the spoils, so Allah revealed: {Had it not been for a decree from Allah that preceded, a great punishment would have touched you for what you took}.'"],[4277,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to Abū Ṭālib when death was present with him: Say: There is no god but Allah, and I will intercede for you with it on the Day of Resurrection. He said: O son of my brother, were it not that Quraysh would reproach me, I would have made your eyes cool with it. Then it was revealed: {Indeed, you do not guide whom you love}."],[4278,"I was near the pulpit of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and a man said, “I do not care if I do no deed after Islam except maintaining the Sacred Mosque.” Another said, “Jihad in the path of Allah is better than what you said.” Then Allah revealed: “Do you consider providing water to pilgrims and maintaining the Sacred Mosque like one who believes in Allah and the Last Day and strives in the path of Allah? They are not equal in the sight of Allah, and Allah does not guide the wrongdoing people.” *"],[4279,"\"Those before you used to kill the killer for the killed one, and blood money was not accepted from him.\" Then Allah revealed: {O you who believe, retaliation is prescribed for you in cases of murder} until the end of the verse: {That is a concession from your Lord and a mercy.} He said: \"So He lightened for you what was upon those before you, i.e., blood money was not accepted. The one who accepts blood money, that is pardoning, so follow up with kindness and payment to him by the one pardoned from his brother with goodness.\""],[4280,"He said: \"Whoever disbelieves in stoning has disbelieved in the Most Merciful. That is Allah's saying: 'O People of the Book, there has come to you Our Messenger, making clear to you much of what you used to conceal of the Book and overlooking much.' (5:15) Stoning was among what they concealed.\""],[4281,"I was a blacksmith, and al-ʿĀṣ b. Wāʾil owed me a debt. I went to him to demand payment, and he said, \"I will not pay you until you disbelieve in Muḥammad.\" I said, \"I will never disbelieve in him until you die and are resurrected.\" He said, \"Will I be resurrected after death? I will pay you when I return to my wealth and children.\" Then this verse was revealed: {Have you seen the one who disbelieved in Our verses and said, 'I will surely be given wealth and children'?}"],[4282,"The woman from the Ansar used to barely have a son to live for. She would vow that if she had a son who survived, she would make him Jewish. But when the Banu Nadir were expelled, among them were some people from the sons of the Ansar. So the Ansar said, \"O Messenger of Allah, these are our children.\" So Allah revealed this verse, \"There is no compulsion in religion.\" Sa'id bin Jubayr said, \"So whoever wanted to join them could do so, and whoever wanted to enter Islam could do so.\""],[4283,"\"I was a blacksmith in Makkah and I made a sword for al-'As b. Wa'il. I came to demand payment from him.\" He said, \"I will not give you until you disbelieve in Muhammad.\" I said, \"I will not disbelieve in Muhammad until Allah causes you to die and then brings you back to life.\" He said, \"When Allah causes me to die and then resurrects me, and I have wealth and children, I will give you.\" I said, \"That is for the Messenger of Allah ﷺ.\" So Allah revealed: {Have you seen the one who disbelieved in Our verses and said, 'I will surely be given wealth and children'} until the end of the verse."],[4284,"“When this verse was revealed: ‘Those who believe and do not mix their faith with injustice,’ the companions of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: ‘Which of us has not wronged himself?’ He said: Then it was revealed: ‘Indeed, associating partners with Allah is a great injustice.’”"],[4285,"When this verse was revealed: {If you disclose what is in your souls or conceal it, Allah will call you to account for it}, something entered their hearts that had never entered them before. The Prophet ﷺ said, 'Say: We hear and obey and we submit.' Then Allah cast faith into their hearts. So Allah revealed: {The Messenger believes in what was sent down to him from his Lord, and the believers} until the verse, and he said, 'Our Lord, do not take us to task if we forget or err.' He said, 'I have done so.' '{Our Lord, and do not lay upon us a burden as You laid upon those before us.' He said, 'I have done so.'"],[4286,"The Jews said: “If a man has intercourse with his wife while she is on her hands and knees, his child will be born cross-eyed.” Then it was revealed: “Your wives are a tilth for you, so come to your tilth as you wish” — if he wishes, on her hands and knees, and if he wishes, otherwise, as long as it is in the same orifice."],[4287,"Umar b. al-Khattab came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and said, \"I am ruined.\" He said, \"And what has ruined you?\" He said, \"I turned my mount around tonight.\" He said, and the Prophet ﷺ did not reply to him at all, then Allah revealed to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ this verse: {Your wives are a tilth for you, so come to your tilth as you will}."],[4288,"I was hiding behind the curtain of the Ka'bah, and in the mosque there was a man from Thaqif and his two sons-in-law from Quraysh. They said: Do you think that Allah hears our conversation? One of them said: He hears when we raise our voices. A man said: If He hears when we raise our voices, He will certainly hear when we conceal it. The other said: I think that Allah hears our conversation. Ibn Mas'ud said: I came to the Prophet of Allah ﷺ and told him what they said, so Allah revealed: {And you were not hiding yourselves, lest your hearing and your eyesight should bear witness against you} to the end of the verse."],[4289,"I was concealing myself with the coverings of the Kaʿbah when three men came: a Thaqafī and his two Qurashī in-laws, with abundant fat on their bellies and little understanding. They conversed among themselves. One of them said, “Do you think Allah hears what we say?” Another said, “When we raise our voices He hears, and when we lower them He does not hear.” The other said, “If He hears when we raise our voices, He hears when we lower them.” I came to the Prophet ﷺ and mentioned that to him, so Allah revealed: “And you were not concealing yourselves, lest your hearing, your eyes, or your skins testify against you.” [Fussilat:22]"],[4290,"The Prophet ﷺ said: 'Whoever goes to such and such a place or does such and such a thing,' and the young men rushed to it while the old men remained under the banners. When Allah granted them victory, they came seeking what the Prophet ﷺ had assigned to them. The old men said to them: 'Do not take it without us, for we were a support for you.' Then Allah revealed this verse: {So fear Allah and set things right among yourselves}."],[4291,"Among the hypocrites at the time of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, there were men who, when the Prophet ﷺ went out on a campaign and they stayed behind, rejoiced at their staying behind, contrary to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. When the Messenger of Allah ﷺ returned, they made excuses to him, swore oaths, and loved to be praised for what they did not do. Then {Do not think that those who rejoice in what they have brought} was revealed."],[4292,"Concerning me the prohibition of wine was revealed. I drank with a people before it was forbidden, and a man among them struck my nose with the jawbone of a camel. I came to the Prophet ﷺ and mentioned that to him, and Allah revealed the prohibition of wine.\" He said, \"And I obtained a sword on the day of Badr, so I asked the Prophet ﷺ about it, and it was revealed: {They ask you about the spoils of war. Say: The spoils of war belong to Allah and the Messenger.}\""],[4293,"Some people from the companions of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ died while drinking wine. When its prohibition was revealed, some people from the companions of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, 'What about our companions who died while drinking it?' Then it was revealed: {There is no sin on those who believe and do righteous deeds for what they ate, if they fear Allah and believe and do righteous deeds.}"],[4294,"\"A message came down to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ from Hudaybiyah, and indeed his companions were feeling sadness and distress. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, 'A verse has been revealed to me which is more beloved to me than the entire world and everything in it.' Then the Messenger of Allah ﷺ recited the verse to them: 'That He may admit the believing men and believing women to gardens beneath which rivers flow.'"],[4295,"\"It came down to the Prophet of Allah, upon him be peace, as a response from al-Hudaybiyah. His companions were overwhelmed with sadness and gloom, as there was a barrier between them and their demand. They had sacrificed their animals in al-Hudaybiyah. The Messenger of Allah, upon him be peace, said, 'Indeed, a verse has been revealed to me that is more beloved to me than the entire world.' He recited it to them until the end of the verse. Then, a man from the community said, 'Congratulations and glad tidings to you, O Messenger of Allah! Allah has made clear to you what He will do with you, so what will He do with us?' So Allah revealed, 'That He may admit the believing men and the believing women to gardens beneath which rivers flow...' until the end of the verse.\""],[4296,"When the Messenger of Allah ﷺ married Zaynab bt. Jaḥsh, he invited the people and they ate. Then they sat conversing. He made as if to get up, but they did not rise. When he saw that, he stood up, and when he stood, those who stood among the people stood, while three remained seated. The Prophet ﷺ came, and the people were still sitting, so he returned. Then they got up and left. I came and informed the Prophet ﷺ that they had left. He came and entered, and I went to enter, but he let down the screen between me and him, and Allah revealed: {O you who believe, do not enter the houses of the Prophet unless permission is given to you} up to His saying {that, in Allah's sight, is an enormity}."],[4297,"I heard Anas b. Malik say regarding this verse: {Do not enter the houses of the Prophet unless you are given permission for a meal}. He said, \"The Prophet of Allah ﷺ consummated marriage with one of his wives and prepared food. He sent me, and I invited some men. They ate, then he got up and went out to ʿAʾishah's house. I followed him, and he entered, finding two men in her house. When he saw them, he turned back without speaking to them. They got up and left, and the verse of the screen was revealed: {O you who believe, do not enter the houses of the Prophet unless you are given permission for a meal, not waiting for its preparation}.\""],[4298,"\"They had titles in the era of ignorance, so the messenger of Allah called a man by his title. It was said, 'O messenger of Allah, he dislikes being called by that title.' So Allah revealed, 'And do not insult one another by nicknames. Wretched is the name of disobedience after [one's] faith.'\" \"He (the Prophet) said, 'The Ansar used to give in charity and provide whatever Allah willed, until difficulties befell them. So they refrained from doing so. Then Allah revealed, 'And spend in the way of Allah and do not throw [yourselves] with your [own] hands into destruction [by refraining]. And do good; indeed, Allah loves the doers of good.'\""],[4299,"While the Prophet ﷺ was leaning against a wall in part of the city, the Jews approached him and asked him about the soul. He recited the verse, \"{And they ask you, [O Muhammad], about the soul. Say, 'The soul is of the affair of my Lord. And you have not been given of knowledge except a little}.\""],[4300,"I was walking with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ in a field in Madinah while he was leaning on a palm branch. He passed by a group of Jews, some of whom said to others, 'Would that you ask him.' Some of them said, 'Do not ask him, lest he makes you hear what you dislike.' They said, 'O Abu al-Qasim.'"],[4301,"Quraysh said to the Jews, 'Give us something we can ask this man about.' They said, 'Ask him about the spirit.' So they asked him, and it was revealed: \"{And they ask you about the spirit. Say: The spirit is of the command of my Lord, and you have not been given of knowledge except a little.}\" They said, 'We have not been given of knowledge except a little, yet we have been given the Torah, and whoever is given the Torah has been given abundant good?' So it was revealed: \"{Say: If the sea were ink for the words of my Lord...}\" the verse."],[4302,"'Ukaz and Dhu al-Majaz were markets they had in the Jahiliyyah. When Allah brought Islam, they felt sinful about trading during the Hajj, so they asked the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and it was revealed: {There is no blame on you for seeking bounty from your Lord} during the seasons of the Hajj."],[4303,"\"Quraysh used to be in charge of the Kaaba, and they used to overflow from Mina, while the people overflowed from Arafat. Then Allah revealed, 'Then depart from where [all] the people depart'.\""],[4304,"There were Qurayzah and al-Nadir, and al-Nadir was nobler than Qurayzah. He said: When a man of Qurayzah killed a man of al-Nadir, he was killed for him, and when a man of al-Nadir killed a man of Qurayzah, he paid a hundred wasq of dates as blood money. When the Prophet ﷺ was sent, a man of al-Nadir killed a man of Qurayzah. They said: Hand him over to us so we may kill him. They said: Between us and you is the Prophet ﷺ. So they came to him, and the verse was revealed: {And if you judge, judge between them with justice} and justice is life for life. Then it was revealed: {Is it the judgment of ignorance they seek?}"],[4305,"Abu Sufyan b. Harb came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and said, \"O Muhammad, I adjure you by Allah and the ties of kinship, for we have eaten 'ilhiz—that is, wool and blood.\" So Allah sent down: {And We had seized them with punishment, but they did not humble themselves before their Lord, nor did they supplicate} [23:76]."],[4306,"When this verse was sent down upon the Prophet ﷺ: {To Allah belongs whatever is in the heavens and whatever is in the earth; and whether you reveal what is in yourselves or conceal it, Allah will bring you to account for it. He forgives whom He wills and punishes whom He wills, and Allah is over all things competent}, they came to the Prophet ﷺ and knelt on their knees and said, \"We cannot bear it; we are not able. We have been charged with deeds we cannot bear and are not able to do.\" So Allah sent down: {The Messenger has believed in what was sent down to him from his Lord, and [so have] the believers} up to His saying: {[They say], 'Our Lord, grant us Your forgiveness, and to You is the [final] destination.'} Then the Prophet ﷺ said, \"Do not say as the People of the Book before you said: 'We hear and we disobey,' but say: 'We hear and we obey. [We seek] Your forgiveness, our Lord, and to You is the [final] destination.'\" So Allah sent down: {Allah does not charge a soul except [with that within] its capacity. It will have [the consequence of] what it has earned, and it will bear [the consequence of] what it has incurred. 'Our Lord, do not hold us accountable if we forget or make a mistake.'} He said, \"Yes.\" {Our Lord, and do not lay upon us a burden as You laid it upon those before us.} He said, \"Yes.\" {Our Lord, and do not make us bear what we have no strength for, and pardon us, and forgive us, and have mercy on us. You are our Protector, so help us against the disbelieving people.} He said, \"Yes.\""],[4307,"Regarding His saying, exalted is He, {And We did not make the vision which We showed you except as a trial for the people}, he said, \"It was a vision of the eye shown to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ on the night he was taken on the night journey.\""],[4310,"“Allah obligated them to fight one against ten, and that was heavy and hard for them, so He reduced it for them to one fighting two. Regarding that, Allah revealed: ‘If there are twenty patient ones among you’ to the end of the verse. Then He said: ‘Had it not been for a prior decree from Allah, a great punishment would have touched you for what you took’—meaning the spoils of Badr, ‘had it not been that I do not punish those who disobey Me until I have given them prior warning.’”"],[4311,"When it was revealed to the Prophet ﷺ: {Say: He is Able to send upon you a punishment from above you}, he said: «I seek refuge in Your Face»; {or from beneath your feet}, he said: «I seek refuge in Your Face»; {or to confound you into factions and make you taste the violence of one another}, he said: «These two are lighter or easier.»"],[4312,"We were with the Prophet ﷺ in the mosque of Madinah one night when a man said, 'What do you think: if a man finds another man with his wife, if he kills him you will kill him, and if he remains silent he remains silent in anger. By Allah, I will certainly ask the Messenger of Allah ﷺ about it.' When morning came, he went to him and asked him. He said, 'If a man finds another man with his wife, if he kills him you will kill him, and if he speaks you will flog him, and if he remains silent he remains silent in anger.' Then he said, 'O Allah, open (grant a ruling).' So it was revealed: {And those who accuse their wives}—these verses about li'an. Then the man came to the Prophet ﷺ with his wife, and they performed li'an. The man testified four times by Allah that he was truthful, and the fifth that the curse of Allah be upon him if he was lying. When his wife began to pronounce li'an, the Prophet ﷺ said to her, 'Stop.' Then she pronounced li'an. When she turned away, the Prophet ﷺ said, 'Perhaps she will bring forth a black, curly-haired child.' And she brought forth a black, curly-haired child."],[4313,"«Whoever swears an oath in which he is sinful in order to seize thereby wealth will meet Allah while He is angry with him.» The confirmation of that was revealed in the Book of Allah: {Indeed, those who purchase a small gain at the cost of Allah's covenant} – the verse. Al-Ash'ath b. Qays passed by while they were talking about this hadith in the mosque and said, \"What is Ibn Umm 'Abd saying?\" They told him, and he said, \"He has spoken the truth. This verse was revealed concerning me and my companion regarding a well that I claimed, and neither of us had clear proof, so he swore an oath about it.\" The Prophet of Allah ﷺ then mentioned this."],[4314,"“We used to carry loads, and a man would bring charity and it would be said, 'This is showing off,' and a man would bring half a ṣāʿ and it would be said, 'Indeed, Allah is in no need of this.' Then this verse was revealed: {Those who criticize the volunteers among the believers concerning charities.}”"],[4315,"The Quran was revealed to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ , and he recited it to them over a period of time. They said, \"O Messenger of Allah, if only you would narrate stories to us.\" So Allah revealed the verse {These are the verses of the clear Book}, until His saying, {We relate to you, O Muhammad, the best of stories}. So the Messenger of Allah ﷺ recited it to them over a period of time. They said, \"O Messenger of Allah, if only you would inform us.\" So Allah revealed the verse {Allah has sent down the best statement: a consistent Book}. They are being commanded with the Quran.\" Khallad added and further explained it: They said, \"O Messenger of Allah, remind us.\" So Allah revealed the verse {Has the time not come for those who have believed that their hearts should become humbly submissive at the remembrance of Allah}."],[4316,"«There was a man from the Ansar who accepted Islam, then apostatized and joined the polytheists. Then he regretted it and sent to his people, saying: Ask the Messenger of Allah ﷺ whether there is any repentance for me. He said: Then it was revealed: {How shall Allah guide a people who disbelieved after their belief and bore witness that the Messenger is true, and clear proofs came to them} up to His saying {except those who repent after that and make amends, for indeed Allah is Forgiving, Merciful}. So his people sent to him, and he accepted Islam.»"],[4317,"«When the Prophet ﷺ arrived in Madinah, they were among the worst of people in measuring. Then Allah ﷻ sent down {Woe to those who give less} [al-Mutaffifin 83:1], and after that they measured well.»"],[4318,"We were with the Prophet ﷺ when Allah sent down revelation upon him. When revelation came down upon him, his gaze remained fixed, his eyes open, and his hearing and heart were devoted to what came to him from Allah. He said: We recognized that from him. He said to the scribe, “Write: ‘Not equal are those who remain behind among the believers and those who strive in the way of Allah.’” The blind man stood up and said, “O Messenger of Allah, what is our sin?” Then revelation came down upon him. We said to the blind man, “Revelation is coming down upon the Prophet ﷺ.” He feared that something concerning his matter would be revealed, so he remained standing, saying, “I seek refuge from the anger of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ.” He said: Then the Prophet ﷺ said to the scribe, “Write: ‘Other than those with disabilities.’”"],[4319,"I was writing for the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and he said, “Write: ‘Not equal are those who remain behind among the believers and those who strive in the way of Allah.’” He said: Then Abdullah b. Umm Maktum came and said, “O Messenger of Allah, I love jihad in the way of Allah, but I have the disability you see; my sight has gone.” Zayd b. Thabit said: The thigh of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ grew heavy on my thigh until I feared it would crush it. When he was relieved, he said, “Write: ‘Not equal are those who remain behind among the believers, other than those with disabilities, and those who strive in the way of Allah.’”"],[4320,"While we were sitting in the mosque, a man entered on a camel. He made it kneel in the mosque, then hobbled it, then said to them, “Which of you is Muhammad?” The Messenger of Allah ﷺ was reclining among them. We said to him, “This white man who is reclining.” The man said to him, “O son of Abd al-Muttalib.” The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to him, “I have answered you.” The man said, “O Muhammad, I am going to ask you and be harsh in questioning, so do not find anything against me in yourself.” The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, “Ask whatever appears to you.” The man said, “I adjure you by your Lord and the Lord of those before you: did Allah send you to all the people?” The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, “O Allah, yes.” He said, “I adjure you by Allah: did Allah command you that we pray the five prayers in the day and night?” The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, “O Allah, yes.” He said, “I adjure you by Allah: did Allah command you that we fast this month of the year?” The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, “O Allah, yes.” He said, “I adjure you by Allah: did Allah command you to take this charity from our rich and distribute it among our poor?” The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, “O Allah, yes.” The man said, “I believe in what you have brought, and I am the messenger of those behind me from my people. I am Dimam b. Tha‘laba, the brother of the Banu Sa‘d b. Bakr.”"],[4321,"\"The religion is sincere advice.\" He said it three times. They said, \"To whom, O Messenger of Allah?\" He said, \"To Allah, His Book, His Messenger, the imams of the Muslims—or the believers—and the common people.\""],[4322,"They said: O Messenger of Allah, how will you recognize those of your community whom you have not seen? He said: They will have white blazes on their foreheads and white marks on their limbs from the traces of purification."],[4323,"A man asked the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, \"O Messenger of Allah, we ride the sea and carry with us a little water. If we perform wudu' with it, we will become thirsty. May we perform wudu' with seawater?\" He said, \"Its water is purifying and its dead animals are lawful.\""],[4324,"\"Its water is pure (and Purification) and its 'dead meat' is permissible (to eat).\" (Using translation from Nasāʾī 4350)"],[4325,"Umm Sulaym al-Ansariyya, the mother of Anas b. Malik, said: O Messenger of Allah, Allah is not shy of the truth. Is bathing obligatory upon a woman when she sees in her sleep what a man sees? Should she bathe or not? The Prophet ﷺ said: “She should bathe.” The wife of the Prophet ﷺ said: I turned to her and said: Uff to you! Does a woman see that? She said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ turned to her and said: “May your right hand be in the dust! How then does resemblance occur?”"],[4326,"Umm Sulaym asked the Prophet ﷺ about a woman who sees in a dream what a man sees. The Prophet ﷺ said to her: 'O Umm Sulaym, if a woman sees that, let her perform ghusl.' Umm Salamah said: 'I felt shy about that. Does that happen, O Messenger of Allah?' He said: 'Yes. The man's fluid is thick and white, and the woman's fluid is thin and yellow. Whichever of the two prevails or dominates determines the resemblance.'"],[4327,"Umm Sulaym, the wife of Abu Talha, came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and said: O Messenger of Allah, Allah is not shy of the truth. Is bathing obligatory upon a woman if she has a nocturnal emission? He said: “Yes, if she sees moisture.”"],[4328,"I was a man who emitted madhy frequently, so I asked the Prophet ﷺ. He said, “When you see water (madhy), wash your penis and perform ablution; and when you see mani, perform ritual bathing.”"],[4329,"ʿAlī ordered ʿAmmār to ask the Messenger of Allah ﷺ about madhy, and he said, “He should wash his private parts and perform ablution.”"],[4330,"ʿAlī b. Abī Ṭālib ordered him to ask the Messenger of Allah ﷺ about a man when he approaches his wife and madhy comes out from him: what is upon him? For his daughter is with me, and I am too shy to ask him. Al-Miqdād said: So I asked the Messenger of Allah ﷺ about that, and he said, “When one of you finds that, let him sprinkle his private part and perform ablution as he does for prayer.”"],[4331,"A man asked the Prophet ﷺ, saying: 'O Messenger of Allah, should I perform ablution from the meat of sheep?' He said: 'If you wish, perform ablution, and if you wish, do not perform ablution.' He said: 'Should I perform ablution from the meat of camels?' He said: 'Yes, perform ablution from the meat of camels.' He said: 'May I pray in sheep enclosures?' He said: 'Yes.' He said: 'May I pray in camel resting places?' He said: 'No.'"],[4332,"Umar came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and said, 'I become junub at night; what should I do?' He said, 'Wash your private part, then perform ablution, then sleep.'"],[4333,"I was the envoy of Banu al-Muntafiq to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. We arrived at the Messenger of Allah ﷺ but did not find him in his house; instead, we found Aishah. She ordered a khazirah (a kind of soup) for us, and it was prepared. She brought us a qina' - and the qina' is a tray - with dates on it. We ate. Then the Messenger of Allah ﷺ came and said: 'Have you had anything? Or shall I order something for you?' We said: 'Yes, O Messenger of Allah.'"],[4334,"I asked the Prophet ﷺ about tayammum, and he commanded me to do the face and the palms with one strike."],[4335,"Some sheep from the zakāt gathered with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. He said, “O Abū Dharr, go out to them.” I went out to them to al-Rabadha. I would become junub and remain for five or six days. I came to the Prophet ﷺ, and he said, “Abū Dharr.” I remained silent. Then he said, “Abū Dharr, may your mother be bereaved of you.” I told him. He called for a black slave girl who brought a vessel of water. She screened me and I screened myself with the riding camel, and I washed. It was as if a mountain had been lifted from me. He said ﷺ, “Clean earth is the ablution of a Muslim, even up to ten years. When you find water, apply it to your skin, for that is better.”"],[4336,"Fatimah bt. Abi Hubaysh said: \"O Messenger of Allah, I do not become pure; should I abandon prayer?\" She said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"That is only a vein, not menstruation. When menstruation comes, then abandon prayer, and when its extent passes from you, wash the blood from yourself and pray.\""],[4337,"Umm Habibah bt. Jahsh came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. She had been afflicted with istihadah for seven years, and she complained of that to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and sought his ruling. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to her: \"This is not menstruation, but rather it is a vein, so perform ghusl and then pray.\" Aishah said: \"Umm Habibah used to perform ghusl for every prayer. She would sit in a washtub, and the redness of the blood would rise above the water, then she would pray.\""],[4338,"Umm Habibah bt. Jahsh, the wife of Abd al-Rahman b. Awf, experienced istihadah for seven years. She sought the ruling of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ concerning that, and the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"This is not menstruation, but rather it is a vein, so perform ghusl and pray.\" Aishah said: \"She used to perform ghusl at every prayer in a washtub in the room of her sister Zaynab bt. Jahsh, until the redness of the blood rose above the water.\""],[4339,"Umm Habibah bt. Jahsh, the wife of Abd al-Rahman b. Awf, and her sister Zaynab bt. Jahsh, experienced istihadah for seven years. She complained of that to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and he said to her: \"It is not menstruation, but rather it is a vein, so perform ghusl and pray.\" \"She used to perform ghusl for every prayer, and she would sit in a washtub of her sister, and the redness of the blood would rise above the water.\""],[4340,"Fatimah bt. Abi Hubaysh experienced istihadah, so the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"Menstrual blood is black blood that is recognizable. When that occurs, withhold from prayer, but when the other occurs, perform wudu and pray.\""],[4341,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to the servant girl: \"Hand me the khumrah,\" intending to spread it out and pray on it. I said: \"She is menstruating.\" He said: \"Her menstruation is not in her hand.\""],[4342,"Safwan b. al-Mu'attal asked the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, saying: O Prophet of Allah, I ask you about something of which you are knowledgeable and I am ignorant. He said: \"What is it?\" He said: Is there any time among the hours of night and day in which prayer is disliked? He said: \"Yes. When you have prayed the morning prayer, then refrain from praying until the sun rises above the horn of Satan. Then pray, and prayer is witnessed and accepted until the sun is above your head like a spear. When it is above your head like a spear, then refrain from praying, for that is the hour in which Hell is kindled and its corners are covered until it declines. When it declines, then prayer is witnessed and accepted until you pray 'Asr. Then refrain from praying until the sun sets.\""],[4343,"Two men disagreed about the mosque founded on piety. One of them said it is the mosque of Madinah, and the other said it is the mosque of Quba. They came to the Prophet ﷺ, and he said, \"It is this mosque of mine.\""],[4344,"Two men argued about the mosque founded on piety. One man said it is the mosque of Quba, and another said it is the mosque of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, \"It is this mosque of mine.\""],[4345,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ was asked: \"How do you command us to pray at night?\" He said: \"One of you should pray two rak'ahs at a time, and if he fears dawn, he should pray one rak'ah as witr.\""],[4346,"A man said: \"O Messenger of Allah, teach me something that will suffice me instead of the Qur'an?\" He said: \"Say: 'Glory be to Allah, praise be to Allah, there is no god but Allah, and Allah is greatest.' Sufyan said: \"I think he also said: 'There is no might nor power except with Allah.'\""],[4347,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ was asked about turning around during prayer, so he said: “It is only a snatching that Satan snatches from the prayer of the servant.”"],[4348,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ was asked about a man who slept until morning. He said, “Satan urinated in his ear or in his ears.”"],[4349,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ was asked about praying in a single garment, and he said: 'Does every one of you find two garments?' When it was the time of Umar b. al-Khattab, he said: 'When Allah grants abundance, then be abundant. A man gathered his clothes upon him and prayed: a man in a waist-wrapper and a cloak, in a waist-wrapper and a shirt, in a waist-wrapper and a tunic, in trousers and a cloak, in trousers and a shirt, in trousers and a tunic.'"],[4350,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ was told about my fasting, so he entered upon me, and I threw a leather cushion stuffed with palm fiber for him, but he sat on the ground, and the cushion remained between me and him. Then he said, \"Is it not enough for you to fast three days from every month?\" I said, \"O Messenger of Allah.\" He said, \"Five.\" I said, \"O Messenger of Allah.\" He said, \"Seven.\" I said, \"O Messenger of Allah.\" He said, \"Nine.\" I said, \"O Messenger of Allah.\" He said, \"Eleven.\" I said, \"O Messenger of Allah.\" He said, \"There is no fast above the fast of Dāwūd: half of a lifetime - fasting one day and breaking the fast one day.\""],[4351,"A man came to the Prophet ﷺ and said, \"O Messenger of Allah, teach me to recite the Quran.\" He said, \"Recite three of the surahs that begin with alif-lam-ra.\" The man said, \"I have become old, my tongue is heavy, and my heart is coarse.\" The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, \"Recite three of the surahs that begin with ha-mim.\" The man said the same thing, \"But teach me, O Messenger of Allah, a comprehensive surah.\" So the Messenger of Allah ﷺ taught him: \"When the earth is shaken...\" until he reached: \"So whoever does an atom's weight of good will see it, and whoever does an atom's weight of evil will see it.\" The man said, \"By the One who sent you with the truth, I do not care if I never add to it until I meet Allah, but...\""],[4352,"\"May a fasting person kiss?\" The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to him, \"Ask this one, Umm Salamah.\" She informed him that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ did that. He said, \"O Messenger of Allah, Allah has forgiven you your past and future sins.\" The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to him, \"By Allah, I am the most God-fearing of you and the most reverent of Him.\""],[4353,"When this verse was revealed: {until the white thread becomes distinct to you} from the black thread, I took a white rope and a black rope and placed them under my pillow. I looked but could not distinguish, so I mentioned that to the Prophet ﷺ. He laughed and said, \"Your pillow is indeed wide and long! It is only the night.\""],[4354,"A man came to the Prophet ﷺ and said: My father has died and did not perform Hajj. Should I perform Hajj on his behalf? He said: \"Consider, if your father owed a debt, would you pay it?\" He said: Yes. He said: \"Perform Hajj on behalf of your father.\""],[4355,"A man came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and said: O Messenger of Allah, my father is an old man who is not able to perform Hajj. Should I perform Hajj on his behalf? He said: \"Yes, perform Hajj in place of your father.\""],[4356,"We entered ihram with the Prophet ﷺ for Hajj alone, not mixing anything else with it. We arrived in Makkah when four nights had passed of Dhu al-Hijjah. When we had circumambulated the House and gone between Safa and Marwah, the Messenger of Allah ﷺ commanded us to make it an Umrah and to come out of ihram to be with women. We said among ourselves: There are only five days between us and Arafah, and we will go out to it while our private parts drip semen. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “I am the most righteous and most truthful of you, and were it not for the sacrificial animal (hady), I would have come out of ihram.” Suraqah b. Malik stood up and said: O Messenger of Allah, is this tamattu' of ours for this year of ours or forever? The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Rather forever.”"],[4357,"We went out with the Prophet ﷺ entering ihram for Hajj. We arrived in Makkah and circumambulated the House and went between Safa and Marwah. Then the Prophet ﷺ stood among us and said: “Whoever of you has not brought a sacrificial animal (hady), let him come out of ihram and make it an Umrah.” We said: What kind of coming out of ihram, O Messenger of Allah? He said: “Complete coming out of ihram.” So we had intercourse with women, wore (ordinary clothes), and perfumed ourselves with fragrance. Some people said: What is this matter? We will go to Arafah while our private parts drip semen. That reached the Prophet ﷺ, and he stood among us as if angry and said: “By Allah, you know that I am the most God-fearing of you, and if I had known that you would say this, I would not have brought the sacrificial animal. So comply with what you are commanded.” Suraqah b. Malik b. Ju'shum stood up and said: O Messenger of Allah, is this Umrah of ours that you commanded us with for this year of ours or forever? The Prophet ﷺ said: “Rather forever.”"],[4358,"What is the matter with the people that they have exited ihram while you have not exited from your 'umrah?\" He said, \"I have matted my hair and garlanded my sacrificial animal, so I will not exit ihram until I slaughter.\""],[4359,"Sinān and I set out to perform ʿumrah. Sinān was driving a sacrificial camel, and it became exhausted on the way. He said, “If we reach the town, I will inquire about that.” He said: When morning came and we alighted at al-Baṭḥāʾ, he said, “Go to Ibn ʿAbbās.” So we went and he mentioned to him the matter of his sacrificial camel. He said, “You have come to the right person. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ sent sixteen sacrificial camels with a man and gave him instructions concerning them. He went, then returned and said, ‘O Messenger of Allah, what should I do with any of them that becomes disabled?’ He said, ‘Slaughter it, then dip its sandal in its blood, then place it on its side, and do not eat from it—neither you nor anyone of your company.’”"],[4360,"I came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ while he was at Muzdalifah, and I said: Is there any Hajj due upon me? He said: \"Whoever attends this standing place with us until he departs, and he had already departed from Arafat before that, by night or by day, his Hajj is complete and he has fulfilled his duties.\""],[4361,"I heard Umar b. Abd al-Aziz asking al-Sa'ib b. Yazid, \"What have you heard about residing in Makkah?\" He said,"],[4362,"\"The emigrant stays for three (nights) after completing his rites.\""],[4363,"\"Sawdah asked permission of the Prophet ﷺ to proceed ahead from Muzdalifah, and she was a heavy, slow woman, so he permitted her. And I wished that I had asked his permission.\""],[4364,"A man came to the Prophet ﷺ and said, 'My sister has obliged herself to perform Hajj on foot.' He said, 'Order her to ride and to offer expiation.'"],[4365,"I compiled the Qur'an and recited it all in one night. That reached the Prophet ﷺ, and he said, 'Recite it in a month.' I said, 'O Messenger of Allah, let me enjoy my strength and youth.' He said, 'Recite it in twenty days.' I said, 'O Messenger of Allah, let me enjoy my strength and youth.' He said, 'Recite it in ten days.' I said, 'O Messenger of Allah, let me enjoy my strength and youth.' He said, 'Recite it in seven days.' I said, 'O Messenger of Allah, let me enjoy my strength and youth.' He refused."],[4366,"When the Messenger of Allah ﷺ sent me and Muʿādh b. Jabal to Yemen, he commanded that each of us encamp near his companion. He said to us, 'Make things easy and do not make them difficult, give glad tidings and do not repel.' When we stood up, we said, 'O Messenger of Allah, give us a ruling about two drinks we used to make: al-bitʿ from honey, steeped until it becomes strong, and al-mizr from barley and corn, steeped until it becomes strong.' The Messenger of Allah ﷺ had been given comprehensive speech and its conclusions, so he ﷺ said, 'Unlawful for you is every intoxicant that intoxicates and distracts from prayer.' He said, 'One day Muʿādh came to me while I had a man who had been a Jew, then embraced Islam, then reverted to Judaism. He asked me about his situation, so I informed him, and I said to Muʿādh, \"Sit down.\" He said, \"I will not sit until I present Islam to him. If he accepts, then fine; otherwise, I will strike his neck.\" So he presented Islam to him, but he refused to embrace Islam, so he struck his neck. Muʿādh asked me one day, \"How do you recite the Qurʾān?\" I said, \"I recite it standing, sitting, and on my bed, taking it in portions.\" He said, \"I asked Muʿādh, 'How do you recite?' He said, 'I recite and sleep, then I get up and gain strength from my sleep for my standing, then I count my sleep as I count my standing.'\""],[4367,"\"He hunted two rabbits and slaughtered them with a sharp stone. He asked the Prophet ﷺ and he ordered him to eat them.\""],[4368,"I came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and said: \"O Messenger of Allah, we are in a land of the People of the Book, and we eat in their vessels. Our land is a land of game: I hunt with my bow, with a trained dog, and with a dog that is not trained. Tell me what is lawful for us from that which is forbidden to me?\" The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"As for what you mentioned that you are in a land of the People of the Book and you eat in their vessels, if you find vessels other than theirs, do not eat in them; but if you do not find vessels other than theirs, wash them and eat in them. As for what you mentioned about game, whatever you hunt with your bow, eat of it and mention the name of Allah over it. As for what your trained dog catches, eat of what it holds for you, and mention the name of Allah over it. As for what your untrained dog catches, if you reach it while it is still alive, slaughter it and eat; if you do not reach it while it is alive, do not eat.\""],[4369,"Adi b. Hatim asked the Prophet ﷺ: \"I shoot my arrow and hit [the game], but I cannot get to it except after a day or two.\" He said: \"If you find it with no mark or scratch except that of your arrow, eat it. If you find a mark other than that of your arrow, do not eat it. If you send your dog and mention the name of Allah over it, and you reach [the game] before it kills it, slaughter it. If you reach it after it has killed it and has not eaten any of it, eat it. If you reach it and it has eaten from it, do not eat, for it has held it only for itself.\" Adi said: \"I send my dogs and mention the name of Allah, and they mix with dogs of others, and they take the game and kill it.\" He said: \"Do not eat, for you do not know whether your dogs killed it or the dogs of others.\""],[4370,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ was asked about a mouse that dies in clarified butter. He said, \"If it is solid, throw away the mouse and what is around it, and eat the rest. If it is liquid, do not go near it.\""],[4371,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ was asked about a mouse that falls into clarified butter. He said, \"If it is solid, throw it away and what is around it; if it is liquid, do not go near it.\""],[4372,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ was asked about a mouse that falls into clarified butter and dies. He said, \"If it is solid, he should throw it away and what is around it and eat it; if it is liquid, he should not go near it.\""],[4373,"A man said, \"O Messenger of Allah, we find within ourselves things that we would not like to speak of, even if we had all that the sun rises upon.\" He ﷺ said, \"Have you found that?\" They said, \"Yes.\" He said, \"That is pure faith.\""],[4374,"They said, \"O Messenger of Allah, we find within ourselves something such that one of us would rather be a burnt cinder than to speak of it.\" He said, \"That is pure faith.\""],[4375,"They said, \"O Messenger of Allah, one of us speaks to himself about something that would be terrible for one of us to utter.\" He said, \"Have you found it? That is pure faith.\""],[4376,"We asked the Messenger of Allah ﷺ about a man who finds something such that if he fell from the sky and the birds snatched him away, it would be dearer to him than to speak of it. He said, \"That is pure faith.\""],[4377,"man came to the Prophet ﷺ and said, \"O Messenger of Allah, I find something in my heart that I prefer to be silent about rather than speak about it.\" The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, \"Allah is the Greatest, Allah is the Greatest. Praise be to Allah who has diverted His decree to whispering.\""],[4378,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ went out when the sun had declined, and he led them in the noon prayer. When he had said the salutation, he stood on the pulpit and mentioned the Hour and mentioned that before it there would be tremendous matters. Then he said, “Whoever wishes to ask me about anything, let him ask me about it. By Allah, you will not ask me about anything except that I will inform you of it as long as I remain in this place.” Anas b. Mālik said, “The people wept profusely when they heard that from the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and the Messenger of Allah ﷺ repeatedly said, ‘Ask me, ask me.’ ʿAbd Allāh b. Ḥudhāfah stood up and said, ‘Who is my father, O Messenger of Allah?’ He said, ‘Your father is Ḥudhāfah.’ When the Messenger of Allah ﷺ kept saying, ‘Ask me,’ ʿUmar b. al-Khaṭṭāb knelt on his knees and said, ‘O Messenger of Allah, we are content with Allah as Lord, Islam as religion, and Muḥammad ﷺ as Messenger.’ He said, ‘The Messenger of Allah ﷺ fell silent when ʿUmar said that.’ Then the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, ‘By the One in whose hand is my soul, Paradise and the Fire were shown to me just now in the side of this wall, and I have never seen good and evil as I have today.’”"],[4379,"I asked the Messenger of Allah ﷺ about righteousness and sin. He said: “Righteousness is good character, and sin is what wavers in your soul and you dislike that people should come to know it.”"],[4380,"A man said to the Prophet ﷺ: How can I know when I have done good and when I have done evil? He said: 'If you hear your neighbors saying, you have done good, then you have done good; and if you hear them saying, you have done evil, then you have done evil.'"],[4381,"The companions of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: When we are with the Prophet ﷺ, we see in ourselves what we love, but when we return to our families and mix with them, we disapprove of ourselves. They mentioned that to the Prophet ﷺ, and the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “If you were to persist in the state you are in with me, the angels would shake hands with you until they shaded you with their wings. But [it is] an hour and an hour.”"],[4382,"O Messenger of Allah, which people are most severely tested? He said, 'The prophets, then the next best, then the next best. A servant is tested according to his religion. If his religion is firm, his test is severe. Trials will keep afflicting the servant until they leave him walking on the earth with no sin upon him.'"],[4383,"I said, 'O Messenger of Allah, which people are most severely tested?' He said, 'The prophets, then the next best, then the next best. A man is tested according to his religion. If his religion is firm, his test is severe. If there is weakness in his religion, he is tested according to his religion. Trials will keep afflicting the servant until they leave him walking on the earth with no sin upon him.'"],[4384,"The Prophetﷺ was at her house with some of his companions when a man came to him and asked, \"O Messenger of Allah, how much charity for dates is so and so?\" The Prophet replied, \"Such and such.\" The man said, \"But so and so has wronged me and taken from me this and that.\" The Prophetﷺ then said, \"What will you do when someone who wrongs you does more harm than this?\" The people then discussed this matter, and a man among them asked, \"What should we do, O Messenger of Allah, when a person from among us is absent with his camels, cattle, crops, and palm trees, and he pays Zakah on his wealth, yet someone wrongs him? What should he do?\" The Prophetﷺ replied, \"Whoever pays his Zakah willingly, seeking the pleasure of Allah and the home of the Hereafter, and does not conceal anything from it, establishes prayer, and gives Zakah, then if someone transgresses against him, he should take his weapon and fight. If he is killed, he will be a martyr.\""],[4385,"That 'Umar consulted the Prophet ﷺ about his charity at Thamgh. He said: \"Withhold its origin and make its fruit available for charity.\" 'Abd Allah said: So 'Umar endowed it for the beggar, the deprived, the traveler, in the way of God, for slaves, and for the poor, and he appointed a custodian to eat from it and feed others without accumulating wealth."],[4386,"That 'Umar b. al-Khattab consulted the Messenger of Allah ﷺ about giving his property at Thamgh as charity. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"Give it as charity, dividing its fruit and withholding its origin; it is not to be sold, given as a gift, or inherited.\""],[4387,"'Umar acquired land at Khaybar and went to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ to consult him. He said: \"I have acquired land at Khaybar, and I have never acquired property more precious to me than it; what do you command regarding it?\" He said: \"If you wish, withhold its origin and give it as charity, on condition that it is not sold, given as a gift, or inherited.\" So he gave it as charity for the poor, the strangers, the slaves, in the way of God, the traveler, and the guest. There is no blame on the one who administers it to eat from it in a reasonable manner or to feed a friend without seeking to enrich himself from it."],[4388,"\"The best of what a man leaves after his death are three: a righteous child who prays for him, a continuous charity whose reward reaches him, and knowledge from which benefit is derived after him.\""],[4389,"A man came to the Prophet ﷺ and said, “O Messenger of Allah, who among people is most deserving of my good companionship?” He said, “Your mother.” He said, “Then who?” He said, “Your mother.” He said, “Then who?” He said, “Your father.”"],[4390,"A man asked the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, “What is the right of a wife upon her husband?” He said, “He should feed her when he eats and clothe her when he clothes himself. Then he should not strike the face, nor insult her, nor desert her except in the house.”"],[4391,"I was shown Laylat al-Qadr, then my family woke me and I forgot it, so seek it in the last ten nights."],[4392,"While the Messenger of Allah ﷺ was speaking to the people, a Bedouin came and said, “When is the Hour?” The Prophet ﷺ continued speaking. Some of the people said, “He heard what he said and disliked it,” and others said, “Rather, he did not hear,” until when he finished his speech he said, “Where is the one who asked about the Hour?” He said, “Here I am.” He said, “When trust is neglected, then await the Hour.” He said, “What is its neglect?” He said, “When authority is given to those unworthy of it, then await the Hour.”"],[4393,"A man came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and said, “O Muḥammad, do you see that a Paradise whose width is the heavens and the earth—where is the Fire?” The Prophet ﷺ said, “Do you see this night? It has come and then nothing is left of it. Where was it placed?” He said, “Allah knows best.” He said, “Indeed, Allah does whatever He wills.”"],[4394,"I said, \"O Messenger of God, if God sends down His might upon the people of the earth while the righteous are among them, will they perish with their destruction?\" He said, \"O Aisha, if God sends down His might upon the people of His vengeance while the righteous are among them, they will be struck with them, then they will be resurrected according to their intentions and deeds.\""],[4395,"'No one will enter the Fire who has an atom's weight of faith in his heart, and no one will enter Paradise who has an atom's weight of arrogance in his heart.' A man said: 'O Messenger of Allah, a man likes his garment to be nice and his sandals to be nice.' He said: 'Indeed Allah is beautiful and loves beauty. Arrogance is rejecting the truth and looking down on people.'"],[4396,"A Bedouin asked the Prophet ﷺ - and they (the Bedouins) were more entitled than his Companions to ask him - 'O Messenger of Allah, when is the Hour?' He said, 'What have you prepared for it?' He said, 'I have not prepared for it anything except that I love Allah and His Messenger.' He said, 'You will be with those whom you love.' Anas said: 'I never saw the Muslims rejoice at anything after Islam more than their rejoicing at his saying.'"],[4397,"O Messenger of Allah, what about a man who loves a people but cannot do deeds like theirs? He said, 'You, O Abū Dharr, are with the one you love.' He said, 'I love Allah and His Messenger.' He said, 'You, O Abū Dharr, are with the one you love.'"],[4398,"The Prophet ﷺ came and a man said, \"O Messenger of Allah, what do you think of a person who loves a group of people but is not able to join them?\" He ﷺ replied, \"A person will be with those whom he loves.\""],[4399,"It was said to Messenger of Allah ﷺ: What is your opinion about the person who has done good deeds and the people praise him? He said: It is glad tidings for a believer (which he has received in this mortal world). (Using translation from Muslim 2642a)"],[4400,"A man came to the Prophet ﷺ and said, “O Messenger of Allah, when is the Hour?” The Prophet ﷺ stood up for prayer, and when he finished the prayer he said, “Where is the one who asked about his Hour?” The man said, “Here I am, O Messenger of Allah.” He said, “What have you prepared for it?” He said, “I have not prepared much for it in terms of prayer or fasting,” or he said, “I have not prepared much in terms of deeds, except that I love Allah and His Messenger.” The Prophet ﷺ said, “A person will be with whom he loves,” or he said, “You will be with whom you love.” Anas said, “I have not seen the Muslims rejoice over anything after Islam as much as they rejoiced over this.”"],[4401,"He entered upon the Prophet ﷺ and said, \"O Messenger of Allah, I saw so-and-so thanking; he mentioned that you gave him two dinars.\" He ﷺ said, \"But so-and-so — I gave him between ten and a hundred, and he neither thanks for it nor mentions it. One of you leaves my presence with his need tucked under his arm, and it is nothing but the Fire.\" He said: I said, \"O Messenger of Allah, why do you give them?\" He said, \"They insist on asking me, and Allah refuses stinginess for me.\""],[4402,"We were with the Prophet ﷺ, as if on our heads were birds; none of us spoke when some people from the Bedouins came to him and said, “O Messenger of Allah, give us a ruling about such-and-such, give us a ruling about such-and-such.” He said, “O people, Allah has removed hardship from you, except a man who borrows from the honor of his brother; that is the one who is in hardship and has perished.” They said, “Shall we seek treatment, O Messenger of Allah?” He said, “Yes, for Allah has not sent down any disease except that He has sent down for it a cure, except one disease.” They said, “And what is it, O Messenger of Allah?” He said, “Old age.” They said, “Which of the people is most beloved to Allah, O Messenger of Allah?” He said, “The most beloved of people to Allah is the best of them in character.”"],[4403,"I said: O Messenger of Allah, I passed by a man and he did not offer me hospitality or entertain me; may I take recompense? The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, \"Rather, entertain him.\""],[4404,"I said: O Messenger of Allah, do we act for a matter that has already been settled, or for a matter that is initiated anew? He said: “For a matter that has already been settled.” He said: Then what is the point of action? The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Every doer is facilitated for his action.”"],[4405,"Imran b. Husayn said to me: 'O Abu al-Aswad, do you think that what people do today and strive in is something that was decreed for them and has passed, or is it in what they will face of what their Prophet ﷺ brought to them and by which the proof was established against them?' I said: 'Rather, it is something that was decreed for them and has passed upon them.'"],[4406,"Whoever is argued with in judgment will be destroyed. I said: 'O Messenger of Allah, Allah says: {As for him who is given his book in his right hand, he will be judged with a lenient judgment}.' He said: 'That is the presentation.'"],[4407,"Whoever is judged will be punished. I said: 'O Messenger of Allah, {As for him who is given his book in his right hand, he will be judged with a lenient judgment}.' He said: 'That is the presentation. There is no one who is judged on the Day of Resurrection except that he will be destroyed.'"],[4408,"O Allah, hold me to account with a lenient judgment. She said: 'O Messenger of Allah, what is the lenient judgment?' He said: 'That He looks at his sins and overlooks them. Whoever is argued with in judgment on that day will be destroyed. And whatever afflicts the believer, even a thorn that pricks him, atones for his sins.'"],[4409,"O Messenger of Allah, how can there be righteousness after this verse: {It is not by your desires nor the desires of the People of the Book; whoever does evil will be recompensed for it}? And everything we do we are recompensed for? He said, 'May Allah forgive you, O Abu Bakr. Do you not fall ill? Do you not grieve? Do you not suffer hardship?' I said, 'Yes.' He said, 'That is what you are recompensed with.'"],[4410,"He informed him that he said, \"O Messenger of Allah, what do you think about matters that I used to engage in during the period of ignorance, such as maintaining ties of kinship, freeing slaves, and giving charity? Is there any reward in them?\" The Prophet ﷺ said, \"You have embraced Islam upon what has preceded for you from reward.\""],[4411,"I said to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, \"Ibn Jud'an in the Jahiliyyah used to entertain guests, be good to neighbors, and maintain ties of kinship. Will that benefit him?\" He said, \"No, indeed he never said even one day: O Allah, forgive me my sin on the Day of Judgement.\""],[4412,"I said, \"O Messenger of Allah, my father used to maintain ties of kinship and used to do such and such.\" He said, \"Your father wanted something and attained it, meaning remembrance.\" He said, \"I said, 'O Messenger of Allah, I ask you about a food that I do not leave except out of scrupulousness.'\" He said, \"Do not leave anything in which you resemble Christianity.\" He said, \"I said, 'I send my dog and it seizes game, and I find nothing to slaughter with except a pebble or a stick?'\" He said, \"Let the blood flow with whatever you wish, and mention the name of Allah.\""],[4413,"I was shown Laylat al-Qadr, then my family woke me and I forgot it, so seek it in the last ten nights."],[4414,"When there was a day of wind or clouds, that could be recognized on the Prophet's face ﷺ, and he would turn and pace. When it rained, he rejoiced and that went away from him. He was asked, and he ﷺ said: 'I feared that it might be a punishment sent upon my nation.'"],[4415,"She was with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and Maymunah. She said: While we were with him, Ibn Umm Maktum approached and entered upon him, and that was after the command of hijab. She said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Veil yourselves from him.” They said: “O Messenger of Allah, is he not blind, so he cannot see us or know us?” The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Are you two not seeing him?”"],[4416,"I said, 'O Messenger of Allah, tell me a statement that I need not ask anyone about after you.' He said, 'Say, I believe in Allah; then remain upright.'"],[4417,"A man said: O Messenger of Allah, from what should I strike (i.e., spend on) my orphan? He said: \"From what you would have struck for your own child, without protecting your property with his property, and without accumulating wealth from his property.\""],[4418,"It was said: “O Messenger of Allah, who is the most noble of people?” He said: “The most God-fearing of them.” They said: “We are not asking you about this.” He said: “Then you are asking me about the origins of the Arabs? The best of you are the best of you in Islam when they gain understanding.”"],[4419,"No one asked the Prophet ﷺ about the Dajjal more than I did. He said, \"He will not harm you.\" I said, \"O Prophet of Allah, they claim that he will have rivers and food with him.\" He said, \"He is too insignificant in the sight of Allah for that.\""],[4420,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ returned from one of his expeditions, and a black slave girl came and said, 'O Messenger of Allah, I vowed that if Allah returned you safely, I would beat the duff on your head.' The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, 'If you made a vow, then fulfill it; otherwise, do not.' She said, 'I had vowed it.' So the Messenger of Allah ﷺ sat down, and she beat the duff."],[4421,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ was asked: \"Which people are best?\" He said: \"My generation, then those who follow them, then those who follow them. Then there will come a people whose testimony precedes their oath and whose oath precedes their testimony.\""],[4422,"A man said: O Messenger of Allah, a man wants to fight in the path of Allah while he seeks some of the fleeting worldly goods? The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: «He has no reward.» The people found that grave and said to the man: Go back to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, for perhaps you did not make him understand. So the man said: O Messenger of Allah, a man wants to fight in the path of Allah while he seeks some of the fleeting worldly goods? He said: «He has no reward.» The people found that grave and said to the man: Go back to the Messenger of Allah. Then he said to him the third time: A man wants to fight in the path of Allah while he seeks some of the fleeting worldly goods? He said: «He has no reward.»"],[4423,"A man came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and said: A man fights out of zeal, fights out of courage, and fights to be seen; which of that is in the path of Allah? He said, «Whoever fights so that the word of Allah is supreme is in the path of Allah.»"],[4424,"A man came to the Prophet ﷺ veiled in iron armor and said, ‘O Messenger of Allah, should I fight or submit?’ The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to him: «Submit, then fight.» So he submitted, then fought, and was killed. The Prophet ﷺ said: «This one did little and was rewarded much.»"],[4425,"It was said, \"O Messenger of God, will you not marry among the Ansar?\" He said, \"There is something in their eyes.\""],[4426,"I said: O Messenger of Allah, tell me something I can hold fast to. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, \"Say: My Lord is Allah, then remain upright.\" I said, O Messenger of Allah, what do you fear most for me? The Messenger of Allah ﷺ took hold of his own tongue and said, \"This.\""],[4427,"“O Messenger of Allah, tell me a saying that Allah will benefit me with, and keep it brief, for perhaps I will not forget it.” He said, “Do not become angry.” He repeated the request several times, and each time the Messenger of Allah ﷺ replied, “Do not become angry.”"],[4428,"That he divorced his wife irrevocably, and he came to the Prophet ﷺ, who said, \"What did you intend by it?\" He said, \"One.\" He said, \"By Allah?\" He said, \"By Allah.\" He said, \"It is according to what you intended.\""],[4429,"Hind bt. 'Utbah came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and said, \"O Messenger of Allah, by Allah, there was no household on the face of the earth more beloved to me that Allah should humiliate them than your household, and there is no household on the face of the earth today more beloved to me that Allah should honor them than your household.\" Then she said, \"O Messenger of Allah, Abu Sufyan is a withholding man. Is there any blame on me if I spend on his dependents from his wealth without his permission?\" The Prophet ﷺ said, \"There is no blame on you to spend in a reasonable manner on them.\""],[4430,"A woman came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and said: «O Messenger of Allah, I have a co-wife. Is there any sin upon me if I ask for more from my husband than what he has given me?» The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: «The one who pretends to have been given what he was not given is like the wearer of two garments of falsehood.»"],[4431,"There were three rulings concerning Barirah. Her owners wanted to sell her and stipulate the wala'. I mentioned that to the Prophet ﷺ, and he said, \"Buy her and manumit her, for the wala' belongs to the one who manumits.\" She was manumitted, and the Messenger of Allah ﷺ gave her the choice, and she chose herself. She used to be given charity, and she would give us a gift from it. I mentioned that to the Prophet ﷺ, and he said, \"Eat, for it is charity for her and a gift for you.\""],[4432,"I used to sell camels in al-Baqi'. I would sell for dinars and take dirhams, and sell for dirhams and take dinars. I came to the Prophet ﷺ while he was in Hafsah's house and said, 'O Messenger of Allah, I sell camels in al-Baqi'. I sell for dinars and take dirhams, and sell for dirhams and take dinars.' The Prophet ﷺ said, 'There is no harm if you take them at the exchange rate of that day, and you part while there is nothing outstanding between you.'"],[4433,"A man came to the Prophet ﷺ and said: 'O Messenger of Allah, I love beauty, and I do not like anyone to surpass me in it even by a shoelace. Is that arrogance?' He said: 'No, arrogance is rejecting the truth and looking down on people.'"],[4434,"Al-Hawla’ bt. Tuwayt b. Habib b. Asad b. ‘Abd al-‘Uzza passed by her while the Messenger of Allah ﷺ was with her. She said, “I said, ‘This is al-Hawla’ bt. Tuwayt, and they claim that she does not sleep at night.’” The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, “She does not sleep at night? Take on of deeds what you are able to do, for by Allah, Allah does not tire until you tire.”"],[4435,"the Messenger of Allah said: “Verily, when the slave (of Allah) commits a sin, a black spot appears on his heart. When he refrains from it, seeks forgiveness and repents, his heart is polished clean. But if he returns, it increases until it covers his entire heart. And that is the ‘Ran’ which Allah mentioned: ‘Nay, but on their hearts is the Ran which they used to earn.’” (Using translation from Tirmidhī 3334)"],[4436,"A funeral procession passed by the Prophet ﷺ, and the deceased was praised with good, so he ﷺ said, 'It has become incumbent.' Then another funeral procession passed by him, and the deceased was spoken of with evil, so the Prophet ﷺ said, 'It has become incumbent.' It was said, 'O Messenger of God, you said for this one, \"It has become incumbent,\" and you said for this one, \"It has become incumbent.\"' He said, 'The testimony of the people, and the believers are the witnesses of God on earth.'"],[4437,"I heard the Prophet ﷺ say in his sermon at al-Naba’ah or al-Nabawah near al-Ta’if: “You will soon know the people of Paradise from the people of the Fire, or your best from your worst.” And I think he said: “The people of Paradise from the people of the Fire.” A man among the Muslims said: “By what, O Messenger of Allah?” He said: “By good praise and evil praise. You are witnesses over one another.”"],[4438,"A scorpion stung a man among us while we were with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and a man said: O Messenger of Allah, should I perform ruqyah on him? He ﷺ said: 'Whoever of you is able to benefit his brother, let him do so.'"],[4439,"We set out, a delegation of six, to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ: five from Banu Hanifah and the sixth a man from Dubay'ah b. Rabi'ah, until we came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. We pledged allegiance to him, prayed with him, and told him that in our land we had a church, and we asked him for some of the leftover water of his purification. He called for water, performed ablution from it, rinsed his mouth, then poured it into a vessel for us. Then he said, 'Go with this water. When you reach your town, break your church, sprinkle its place with this water, and make it a mosque.' We said, 'O Messenger of Allah, the town is far and the water will dry up.' He said, 'Then add more water to it, for it will only increase it in goodness.' We departed and vied with one another over carrying the vessel. The Messenger of Allah assigned each of us to carry it for a day and a night. We traveled with it until we reached our town and did what he commanded. The monk of those people was a man from Tayy. We called him to prayer, and the monk said, 'A true call,' then fled and was not seen again."],[4440,"The Prophet ﷺ gave to some men and did not give one of them anything. I said, “O Messenger of Allah, you gave so-and-so and so-and-so, but you did not give so-and-so anything, though he is a believer.” The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, “Or a Muslim?” He said it three times."],[4441,"O Messenger of Allah, by the One who sent you with the truth, I did not come to you until I had sworn by the number of these fingers of mine that I would not come to you. What is it with which He sent you? He said, “Islam.” He said, “What is Islam?” He said, “That you submit your heart to Allah, direct your face to Allah, pray the prescribed prayer, and give the obligatory zakah. Two brothers, helpers: Allah does not accept repentance from a servant * who associates others after his Islam.”"],[4442,"O Messenger of Allah, what do you think if I meet a man from the disbelievers and he fights me and strikes one of my hands with a sword and cuts it off, then he takes refuge from me behind a tree and says, \"I have submitted to Allah\"—should I kill him after he has said it? The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, \"Do not kill him.\" I said, \"O Messenger of Allah, he has cut off my hand, and he said that after cutting it off—should I kill him?\" The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, \"Do not kill him, for if you kill him, he would be in the position you were in before you killed him, and you would be in the position he was in before he uttered the word he said.\""],[4443,"The brother of Abū Quʿays sought permission to enter upon me after the veil was imposed on us. I said: I will not permit you until the Prophet ﷺ comes. When the Prophet ﷺ came, I sought his permission and said: O Messenger of God, the brother of Abū Quʿays sought permission to enter upon me, but I refused to permit him until I seek your permission. It was only the wife of Abū Quʿays who suckled me; Abū Quʿays did not suckle me. He ﷺ said: \"Permit him, for he is your paternal uncle.\""],[4444,"She said, \"I sought permission from Abu Qais's brother to enter upon him after the veil descended, but I said: By Allah, I will not grant permission to him until I seek permission from the Messenger of Allah ﷺ . She added, \"So the Messenger of Allah ﷺ entered upon me and I said: O Messenger of Allah, Abu Qais's brother sought permission from me but I refused to grant him permission until I seek permission from you.\" The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"And what prevents you from granting permission to your uncle?\" She replied, \"O Messenger of Allah, it was not him who breastfed me, it was his wife who breastfed me.\" He ﷺ said: \"He is your uncle, grant him permission, for your right thigh is Haram to him.\" Urwah said: \"That is why Aisha used to say: 'Forbidding what is forbidden by lineage should also be applied to breastfeeding.'\""],[4445,"I was shown Laylat al-Qadr, then my family woke me and I forgot it, so seek it in the last ten nights."],[4446,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ was asked, \"Which sin is greatest in the sight of Allah?\" He said, \"That you set up a rival to Allah while He created you.\" He said, \"Then which?\" He said, \"That you commit adultery with your neighbor's wife.\" Then Allah sent down confirmation of it: {And those who do not call upon another god besides Allah, nor kill the soul that Allah has forbidden except by right, nor commit adultery - and whoever does that will meet a penalty}."],[4447,"I asked the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, \"Which sin is greatest?\" He said, \"That you set up a rival to Allah while He created you.\" I said, \"Indeed that is great. Then which?\" He said, \"That you kill your child fearing he will eat with you.\" I said, \"Then which?\" He said, \"That you commit adultery with your neighbor's wife.\""],[4448,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ was asked about a man who divorced his wife, and she married another husband, and he entered upon her, then he divorced her before having intercourse with her; is she lawful for the first? He said: \"No, until he tastes her honey and she tastes his honey.\""],[4449,"Abd Allah b. Utbah wrote to Umar b. Abd Allah b. al-Arqam al-Zuhri: Enter upon Subay'ah bt. al-Harith al-Aslamiyyah and ask her about the ruling the Messenger of Allah ﷺ gave her concerning her pregnancy. He said: Umar b. Abd Allah entered upon her and asked her, and she informed him that she had been married to Sa'd b. Khawlah, who was one of the Companions of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, one of those who witnessed Badr. He died leaving her during the Farewell Pilgrimage, and she gave birth before four months and ten days had elapsed since her husband's death. When she recovered from her post-natal bleeding, Abu al-Sanabil b. Ba'kak, a man from the Banu Abd al-Dar, entered upon her and saw her adorned, and said to her, 'Perhaps you want to marry before four months and ten days have passed over you.' She said: When I heard that from Abu al-Sanabil, I came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and told him and asked his ruling. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, 'You have become lawful when you gave birth to your child.'"],[4450,"On the day of Khaybar, my brother fought fiercely alongside the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and his sword recoiled upon him and killed him. The companions of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said about that, “A man died by his own weapon,” and they were doubtful about some of his affair. Salamah said: Then the Messenger of Allah ﷺ departed from Khaybar, and I said, “O Messenger of Allah, permit me to recite rajab verses for you.” The Messenger of Allah ﷺ permitted me, and Umar ibn al-Khattab said, “I know what you say.”"],[4451,"“Regarding a daughter, a son’s daughter, and a sister, he said: ‘For the daughter is half, for the son’s daughter is a sixth, and what remains is for the sister.’”"],[4452,"They said, \"O Messenger of Allah, we stay with people who do not offer us hospitality. What is your view about that?\" The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, \"If you stay with a people and they provide you with what is appropriate for a guest, accept it. If they do not, then take from them the right of the guest that is due to him.\""],[4453,"The Prophet ﷺ was asked what the muhrim may kill. He said, 'The mouse, the kite, the vicious dog, and the pied crow.'"],[4454,"«The Messenger of Allah ﷺ was asked about the hyena, and he said: “It is game, and in it is a ram.”»"],[4455,"I asked about the hyena: “Should I eat it?” He said: “Yes,” meaning [the Prophet ﷺ]. I said: “Is it game?” He said: “Yes.” I said: “On the authority of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ?” He said: “Yes.”"],[4456,"I said, \"O Messenger of Allah, is there any evil after the goodness that we are currently in, which we should beware of?\" He said, \"O Hudhayfah, rely on the Book of Allah, learn it, and follow what is good in it for you.\""],[4457,"A man said: “O Messenger of Allah, will Allah hold any of us accountable for what he did in the Jāhiliyyah?” He said: “Whoever does good in Islam will not be held accountable for what he did in the Jāhiliyyah, and whoever does evil in Islam will be held accountable for the first and the last.”"],[4458,"Hassan b. Thabit sought permission from the Messenger of Allah ﷺ to satirize the polytheists. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"What about my lineage?\" Hassan said: \"I will surely extract you from them as a hair is extracted from dough.\""],[4459,"I said: \"O Messenger of Allah, what has been revealed regarding poetry has been revealed.\" The Prophet ﷺ said: \"Indeed, the believer strives with his sword and his tongue. By the One in whose hand is my soul, it is as if you are pelting them with arrows.\""],[4460,"The servant says, 'My wealth, my wealth,' but he has only three things from his wealth: what he ate and consumed, or what he gave away and made remain, or what he wore and wore out. Anything else, he leaves behind for people."],[4461,"A man said: O Messenger of Allah, so-and-so is mentioned for her abundant prayer, yet she harms with her tongue. He said: “In the Fire.” He said: O Messenger of Allah, so-and-so is mentioned for her little prayer and fasting, and she gives charity with pieces of dried curd, yet she does not harm her neighbors. He said: “She is in Paradise.”"],[4462,"When Allah accepted the repentance of his grandfather Abu Lubabah for his staying behind from the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and for matters in which the Messenger of Allah ﷺ had been angry with him, he said, “O Messenger of Allah, I will abandon my house in which I committed the sin, and I will move to you and live with you. I will detach myself from all my wealth as charity to Allah and His Messenger.” The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to him, “A third of that will suffice you.”"],[4463,"A group of the companions of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ passed by a tribe among the Arab tribes, and among them was someone stung or bitten. They said, 'Is there any raqi among you?' A man from among them went and performed ruqyah on him for a flock of sheep, and he was cured. When he came to his companions, they disliked that and said, 'You took a fee for the Book of Allah.' When they came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, they told him about that. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ called the man and asked him, and he said, 'O Messenger of Allah, we passed by a tribe among the Arab tribes, and among them was someone stung or bitten. They said, \"Is there any raqi among you?\" So I performed ruqyah on him with the Opening of the Book, and he was cured.' The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: 'The most deserving thing for which you have taken a fee is the Book of Allah.'"],[4464,"In the care of an aunt of mine was an orphan son of hers. He used to earn, and she used to avoid eating from his earnings. She asked 'A'ishah about that, and she said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, \"The purest of what a man eats is from his earnings, and a man's child is from his earnings.\""],[4465,"The purest of what a man eats is from his earnings, and his child is from his earnings."],[4466,"The purest of what a man eats is from his earnings, and his child is from his earnings."],[4467,"While the Prophet ﷺ was dividing spoils at al-Ji'ranah, a man said to him, 'Be just.' The Prophet ﷺ said, \"Woe to me! I will be wretched if I am not just.\""],[4468,"A man said about something the Prophet ﷺ distributed, 'There is no justice in this.' I said, 'By Allah, I will tell the Messenger of Allah.' So I told him, and he said, 'May Allah have mercy on Musa; he was afflicted with worse than this and was patient.'"],[4470,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ stood to pray, and I heard him say: “I seek refuge in Allah from you.” Then he said: “I curse you with the curse of Allah,” three times. Then he stretched out his hand as if grabbing something. When he finished the prayer, he said: O Messenger of Allah, we heard you say something in your prayer we have not heard you say before, and we saw you stretch out your hand. He said: “Indeed the enemy of Allah, Iblīs, came with a flame of fire to put it in my face. I said: ‘I seek refuge in Allah from you,’ but he did not retreat. Then I said that again, but he did not retreat. Then I said it again, but he did not retreat. I wanted to strangle him, and were it not for the supplication of my brother Sulaymān, he would have been tied up in the morning for the children of Madinah to play with.”"],[4471,"A man said to the Prophet ﷺ, “Shall I send off my she-camel and rely [on Allah]?” He said, “Tether her and rely.”"],[4472,"A man came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and said: 'O Messenger of Allah, which charity is greatest?' He said: 'That you give charity while you are healthy and miserly, fearing poverty and hoping for wealth, and not delay until it reaches the throat and you say: For so-and-so is such and such, and for so-and-so is such and such, although it has already been for so-and-so.'"],[4473,"I was sitting with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ when a group from Banū Tamīm came to him and he said, “Receive the glad tidings, O Banū Tamīm.” They said, “You have given us glad tidings, O Messenger of Allah, so give us.” Then some people from the people of Yemen entered upon him and he said, “Receive the glad tidings, O people of Yemen, since Banū Tamīm did not accept it.” They said, “We have accepted, O Messenger of Allah. We have come to gain understanding in the religion and to ask you about the beginning of this matter: what was it?” He said, “Allah existed and there was nothing before Him, and His Throne was upon the water, then He created the heavens and the earth and wrote in the Remembrance everything.”"],[4474,"Actions are by intentions, and every person will have what he intended. Whoever's migration is to Allah and His Messenger, his migration is to Allah and His Messenger. And whoever's migration is to a worldly gain he attains or a woman he marries, his migration is to what he migrated to."],[4475,"From the Prophet ﷺ , he said, \"Migration is of two types: the migration of a person who responds when called and obeys when commanded, and the migration of a person who remains steadfast in the face of difficulties and adversities, which is considered the most challenging and rewarding.\""],[4476,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said during the Farewell Pilgrimage: “Shall I tell you who the believer is? It is the one whom people trust with their wealth and their lives. The Muslim is the one from whose tongue and hand people are safe. The mujāhid is the one who strives against his own self in obedience to Allah. The emigrant is the one who emigrates from sins and wrongdoings.”"],[4477,"A man said to 'Abd Allah b. 'Umar: Will you not go forth in battle? He said: I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: \"Islam is built on five: the testimony that there is no god but Allah, the establishment of prayer, the giving of zakat, fasting Ramadan, and the pilgrimage to the House.\""],[4478,"Then I met Suhayl and said to him, \"What do you think about a hadith that 'Amr used to narrate from al-Qa'qa' from your father—did you hear it from your father?\" He said, \"I heard it from the one whom my father heard it from. A friend of my father's used to come from Syria, called 'Ata' b. Yazid al-Laythi. I heard him narrate that from Tamim al-Dari, from the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, who said: 'Truly the religion is sincere advice. Truly the religion is sincere advice. Truly the religion is sincere advice.' They said, 'To whom, O Messenger?' He said, 'To Allah, His Book, His Messenger, the imams of the Muslims, and the common people.'\""],[4479,"Kabshah, daughter of Ka'b ibn Malik and wife of Ibn AbuQatadah, reported: AbuQatadah visited (me) and I poured out water for him for ablution. A cat came and drank some of it and he tilted the vessel for it until it drank some of it. Kabshah said: He saw me looking at him; he asked me: Are you surprised, my niece? I said: Yes. He then reported the Messenger of Allah ﷺ as saying: It is not unclean; it is one of those (males or females) who go round among you. (Using translation from Abū Dāʾūd 75)"],[4480,"\"If one of you steps in filth with his sandals, then dust is a purifier for them.\""],[4481,"\"If one of you steps in filth with his leather socks, then dust is their purifier.\""],[4482,"There will come people—or there will be people—who perform the prayer. If they complete it, then it is for you and for them. And if they fall short, then it is upon them and for you."],[4483,"“Whoever leads the people in prayer, and gets the time right and completes the prayer, then it belongs to him and to them. And whoever falls short of any of that, it is against him and not against them.”"],[4484,"When the call to prayer is made, Satan retreats, passing wind so that he will not hear the call. When the call is finished, he returns. When the iqamah for prayer is made, he retreats. When the iqamah is finished, he returns, until he whispers between a man and his soul, saying: 'Remember such-and-such, remember such-and-such,' which he had not been remembering, until the man prays and does not know how many he has prayed."],[4485,"“When a servant prostrates, seven parts prostrate with him: his face, his knees, his palms, and his feet.”"],[4486,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Angels of the night and angels of the day succeed one another among you, and they gather at the dawn prayer and the afternoon prayer. Then those who spent the night among you ascend, and their Lord asks them—though He is most knowing about them—‘How did you leave My servants?’ They say: ‘We left them while they were praying, and we came to them while they were praying.’”"],[4487,"Spitting in the mosque is a sin, and its expiation is burying it."],[4488,"“The Fire complained to its Lord, saying, ‘My Lord, parts of me are consuming one another, so give me relief.’ So He granted it two breaths every year, in winter and summer. Thus the severe cold you find is from its extreme frost, and the severe heat you find is from the heat of Hell.”"],[4489,"The prayer of travel, the prayer of Fitr, the prayer of Adha, and the Friday prayer are two rak'ahs, complete, not shortened, upon the tongue of your Prophet ﷺ."],[4490,"“The prayer of the signs is six rak‘ahs and four prostrations.”"],[4491,"If you say to your companion, 'Be quiet,' while the imam is delivering the sermon, you have engaged in idle talk."],[4492,"'Umar b. al-Khattab addressed us at al-Jabiyah and said, \"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ stood among us as I stand among you today and said: 'Be good to my companions, then those who follow them, then lying will spread until a man testifies without being asked and swears without being asked. Whoever of you wants the best part of Paradise, let him adhere to the community, for Satan is with the single person, and he is farther from two. None of you should be alone with a woman, for Satan is the third of them. Whoever is grieved by his evil deeds and pleased by his good deeds is a believer.'\""],[4493,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ drew lines for us from his right and his left and said, \"These are different paths, and along each path there is a devil calling to it.\" Then he recited the verse, \"And verily, this is My straight path, so follow it, and follow not (other) paths, for they will separate you away from His path.\" (Quran 6:153)"],[4494,"We returned from Makkah with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and people began asking permission of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and he began granting them. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, \"What is the matter that the side of the tree that is next to the Messenger of Allah is more hateful to you than the other side?\" He said: We saw none of the people except weeping. Abu Bakr said, \"The one who asks your permission after this is a fool in my estimation.\" The Messenger of Allah ﷺ stood up, praised Allah and extolled Him, and when he swore he would say, \"By the One in whose hand is my soul, I bear witness before Allah that there is not one of you who believes in Allah and then remains steadfast except that he will be led into Paradise. My Lord has promised me to admit seventy thousand of my nation into Paradise without reckoning or punishment. I hope they will not enter it until you and the righteous among your wives and descendants have taken up dwellings in Paradise.\" Then he said, \"When half the night or two-thirds of it has passed, Allah, Blessed and Exalted, descends to the lowest heaven and says: 'I will not ask about My servants other than Me. Who is there who asks Me that I may give him? Who is there who seeks My forgiveness that I may forgive him? Who is there who calls upon Me that I may answer him'—until the dawn breaks.\""],[4495,"O Messenger of Allah, we hear hadiths from you; will you permit us to write them down? He said: \"Yes.\""],[4496,"“You must be truthful, for truthfulness guides to righteousness, and righteousness guides to Paradise. A man will continue to be truthful until he is written with Allah as a truthful one (ṣiddīq). And indeed, lying guides to wickedness, and wickedness guides to the Fire. A man will continue to lie until he is written with Allah as a liar.”"],[4497,"“Deeds are but like a vessel: if its top is good, its bottom is good; and if its top is foul, its bottom is foul.”"],[4498,"“Actions are only [judged] by their outcomes, like a vessel: if its top is good, its bottom is good; and if its top is bad, its bottom is bad.”"],[4499,"When the Messenger of Allah ﷺ delivered a sermon, his eyes would redden, his voice would rise, and his anger would intensify, as if he were warning of an army saying, 'They will raid you in the morning and evening.' He would say, 'I and the Hour have been sent like these two,' and he would join his forefinger and middle finger. Then he would say, 'To proceed: the best speech is the Book of Allah, and the best guidance is the guidance of Muhammad. The worst of matters are newly introduced ones; every innovation is misguidance.' Then he would say, 'I am closer to every believer than his own self. Whoever leaves wealth, it is for his family; whoever leaves debt or dependents, they are to me and upon me.'"],[4500,"We prayed Maghrib with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, then we said, \"Would that we waited until we prayed 'Isha' with him.\" So we waited, and he came out to us and said, \"Have you been here all this time?\" We said, \"Yes, to pray 'Isha' with you.\" He said, \"You have done well,\" or \"You have done right.\" Then he raised his head to the sky and said, \"The stars are a trust for the sky; when the stars disappear, what is promised to the sky comes. I am a trust for my Companions; when I depart, what is promised to my Companions comes. My Companions are a trust for my ummah; when my Companions depart, what is promised to my ummah comes.\""],[4501,"The best of companions in the sight of Allah is the one who is best to his companion, and the best of neighbors in the sight of Allah is the one who is best to his neighbor."],[4503,"From the Messenger of Allah ﷺ , \"Whoever sees me in a dream, has indeed seen the truth, for the Satan does not assume my appearance.\""],[4504,"The Prophet ﷺ said, \"Whoever sees me in a dream, it is as if they have seen me while awake, for certainly Satan cannot imitate my form.\""],[4505,"When the Messenger of Allah ﷺ sent him to Yemen, the Messenger of Allah ﷺ went out with him advising him while Muʿādh was riding and the Messenger of Allah ﷺ was walking beneath his mount. When he finished, he said: “O Muʿādh, perhaps you may not meet me after this year of mine; perhaps you will pass by my mosque and my grave.” Muʿādh wept out of sorrow for parting from the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. Then the Messenger of Allah ﷺ turned toward Madinah and said: “These people of my household think they are the closest of people to me, but the closest of people to me are the God-fearing, whoever they are and wherever they are. O Allah, I do not permit for them the corruption of what You have set right. By Allah, they will turn my community away from its religion as a vessel is overturned in the valley.”"],[4506,"Ibn ʿAbbas was asked about this verse: “Say: I do not ask you any reward for it except love for the near kin.” Saʿid b. Jubayr said, “The near kin of Muhammad?” Ibn ʿAbbas said, “You are hasty. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ did not have any clan of Quraysh except that he had kinship among them. So he said: ‘Except that you maintain the kinship between me and you.’”"],[4507,"Abu Bakr al-Siddiq recited this verse: {O you who believe, upon you is [responsibility for] yourselves; those who have gone astray will not harm you when you have been guided.} He said: 'People place this verse in other than its proper place. Verily I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: \"When people see the wrongdoer and do not seize his hands\" or he said, \"the wrong\" and do not change it, Allah will soon overwhelm them all with His punishment.\"'"],[4508,"\"O people, you recite this verse and place it in other than the place Allah placed it: {O you who believe, upon you is [responsibility for] yourselves; those who have gone astray will not harm you when you have been guided.} Verily, when people see the wrong and do not change it, it is near that Allah will overwhelm them all with punishment.\""],[4509,"\"My intercession is for the people of major sins of my community.\""],[4510,"“Allah will surely support this religion with the wicked man.”"],[4511,"We were with the Prophet ﷺ at Ḥunayn, and he said about a man who was counted among the Muslims, “He is one of the people of the Fire.” When the fighting began, the man fought fiercely and was wounded. It was said, “O Messenger of Allah, the man whom you said was one of the people of the Fire fought fiercely today and died.” The Prophet ﷺ said, “To the Fire.” Some of the companions of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ were about to have doubts. While they were in that state, it was said that he had not died but had severe wounds. When night came, his wounds became severe and he killed himself. The Prophet ﷺ was informed of that, and he said, “Allah is greatest. I bear witness that I am the servant of Allah and His Messenger.” Then he ordered Bilāl, and he called out among the people, “None will enter Paradise except a believing soul, and Allah supports the religion with the wicked man.”"],[4512,"Indeed, Allah gives respite to the wrongdoer until, when He seizes him, He does not let him escape. Then he recited: {And thus is the seizure of your Lord when He seizes the towns while they are wrongdoing. Indeed, His seizure is painful and severe.}"],[4513,"«When Allah wants good for an amir, He gives him a truthful vizier: if he forgets, he reminds him, and if he remembers, he helps him. But when Allah wants otherwise for him, He gives him an evil vizier: if he forgets, he does not remind him, and if he remembers, he does not help him.»"],[4514,"«Every one of you is a shepherd and every one of you is responsible for his flock. The imam is a shepherd and is responsible for his flock. A man is a shepherd over his family and is responsible for his family. A woman is a shepherd over her husband's household and is responsible for her flock. A servant is a shepherd over his master's property and is responsible for his flock. Every one of you is a shepherd and is responsible for his flock.»"],[4515,"\"Indeed, the Prophet ﷺ said, 'Prophethood has ended, but glad tidings remain.'\""],[4516,"When he finished the morning prayer, he would say, \"Did any of you see a dream last night?\" And he would say, \"Nothing of prophethood will remain after me except the righteous dream.\""],[4517,"The good dream of a righteous man is one of forty-six parts of prophethood."],[4518,"“Dreams are of three types: Some are terrifying things from Satan, aimed at causing grief to the son of Adam; some are things that a person is concerned with when he is awake, so he sees them in his dreams; and some are a part of the forty-six parts of prophecy.” He said: “I said to him: ‘Did you hear this from the Messenger of Allah ﷺ?’ He said: ‘Yes, I heard it from the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, I heard it from the Messenger of Allah ﷺ.’” (Using translation from Ibn Mājah 3907)"],[4519,"The dream is one of seventy parts of prophethood."],[4520,"When time draws near, the dream of a believer will scarcely be false. The most truthful of them in dreams are the most truthful of them in speech. The dream is one of forty-five parts of prophethood."],[4521,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to be pleased with dreams. Sometimes a man would see a dream and he would ask about him if he did not know him. If he was commended as good, he was more pleased with his dream. A woman came to him and said, \"O Messenger of Allah, I saw as if I was taken out of Madinah and entered into Paradise. I heard a sound that Paradise made for it. I looked and saw so-and-so, so-and-so, and so-and-so,\" and she named twelve men whom the Messenger of Allah ﷺ had sent on an expedition before that. They were brought wearing worn-out garments, their jugular veins flowing. It was said, \"Take them to the river of al-Baydhakh.\" He said, \"They were immersed in it.\" He said, \"They came out with faces like the moon on the night of the full moon. A platter of gold was brought with a fresh date on it. They ate of its dates as much as they wished. They did not turn it from any side except that they ate of the fruit whatever they desired, and I ate with them.\" Then the bringer of good news from that expedition came and said, \"Our affair was such-and-such, and so-and-so, so-and-so, and so-and-so were struck,\" until he counted twelve men. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ called for the woman and said, \"Relate your dream.\" She related it and said, \"So-and-so and so-and-so were brought,\" as the man said."],[4522,"The dream of a Muslim is one of forty parts of prophethood, and it is on the foot of a bird as long as he does not relate it. When he relates it, it occurs."],[4523,"The Prophet ﷺ said, \"The (good) dreams of a faithful believer is a part of the forty-six parts of prophetism:' (Using translation from Bukhārī 6987)"],[4524,"There is no forbearing person but one who has stumbled, and no wise person but one with experience."],[4525,"While the Messenger of Allah ﷺ was walking, a man on a donkey said to him, 'Ride, O Messenger of Allah,' and moved back. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, 'The owner of the mount is more entitled to its front, unless you assign it to me.' He said, 'So he assigned it to him, and the Messenger of Allah ﷺ rode.'"],[4526,"A woman divorced three times has no right to housing or maintenance."],[4527,"“Tawaf around the House is a prayer, except that Allah has permitted speech in it. So whoever speaks, let him speak only good.”"],[4528,"I went with my father to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. When I saw him, my father said: \"Who is this?\" I said: \"I don't know.\" He said: \"This is the Messenger of Allah ﷺ.\" I shuddered when he said that. I had thought that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ did not resemble people, but he had a lock of hair with a trace of henna on it, and he wore two green garments. My father greeted him, then he began to talk to us for a while. He said: \"Is this your son?\" He said: \"Yes, by the Lord of the Ka'bah, I bear witness to it.\" He said: \"Indeed, this son of yours will not commit a crime against you, nor will you commit a crime against him.\" Then the Messenger of Allah ﷺ recited: {No bearer of burdens will bear the burden of another}. Then he looked at the swelling between his shoulders and said: \"O Messenger of Allah, I am like the best of physicians. Shall I treat it?\" He said: \"Its physician is the One who created it.\""],[4529,"“Those with whom Allah is angry are the Jews, and those who went astray are the Christians.”"],[4530,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ came out to us with truffles in his hand and said: 'These are from the manna, and their water is a cure for the eye.'"],[4531,"«In the human being there is a bone that the earth never consumes; from it he will be recomposed on the Day of Resurrection.» They said, \"Which bone is it, O Messenger of Allah?\" He said, \"The coccyx.\""],[4532,"«The earth consumes everything of the human being except his coccyx.» It was said, \"What is it, O Messenger of Allah?\" He said, \"Like a mustard seed; from it he will be created.\""],[4533,"\"Among the worst of people are those whom the Hour reaches while they are alive, and those who take graves as mosques.\""],[4534,"«The cry of the newborn when it falls [from the womb] is a touch from Shaytan.»"],[4535,"We were sitting with the Prophet ﷺ when a funeral procession passed by. The Prophet ﷺ said, \"The believer finds rest and is relieved from the afflictions, trials, and calamities of this world when they die. As for the disbeliever, the people, the land, the trees, and the animals find rest and relief from them.\""],[4536,"If there is ill omen in anything, it is in the house, the horse, and the woman."],[4537,"All the world is a provision, and the best provision of the world is a righteous wife."],[4538,"Four are from happiness: a righteous wife, a spacious dwelling, a good neighbor, and a comfortable mount. Four are from misery: a bad neighbor, a bad wife, a cramped dwelling, and a bad mount."],[4539,"The best of them is the one with the least dowry."],[4540,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to me, \"Part of a woman's blessing is the ease of her matter and the smallness of her dower.\" 'Urwah said: And I say on my own: Part of her misfortune is the difficulty of her matter and the largeness of her dower."],[4541,"“Indeed, woman was created from a rib, and she will never be straight for you in any way. If you enjoy her, you enjoy her while she has a crookedness. And if you try to straighten her, you will break her, and breaking her is divorcing her.”"],[4542,"“The likeness of a woman is like a rib. If you try to straighten it, it breaks. If you enjoy it, you enjoy it while it has a crookedness. So enjoy it despite the crookedness in it.”"],[4543,"Muadh b. Jabal wanted to travel, and said: O Prophet of Allah, advise me. He said: 'Worship Allah and do not associate anything with Him.' He said: O Prophet of Allah, give me more. He said: 'If you do evil, then do good.' He said: O Messenger of Allah, give me more. He said: 'Be upright, and let your character be good.'"],[4544,"A man said: O Messenger of Allah, when will I be a doer of good? He said: 'If your neighbors say, you are a doer of good, then you are a doer of good; and if they say, you are an evil-doer, then you are an evil-doer.'"],[4545,"The two revilers—whatever they say—the sin is upon the one who initiated it, as long as the wronged one does not transgress."],[4546,"The she-camel of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, al-Adba, was never outstripped. Whenever they raced her, she won. A Bedouin came on a young camel and raced her, and he beat her. That weighed heavily on the companions of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ until he saw it in their faces. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, 'It is incumbent upon Allah that nothing of this filthy world is raised but that Allah lowers it.'"],[4547,"I heard the Prophet ﷺ say, \"If the son of Adam had a valley of wealth, he would desire to have another similar to it. However, nothing can fill the soul of the son of Adam except dust. Allah accepts the repentance of those who repent.\""],[4548,"If the son of Adam had two valleys of palm trees, he would seek a third, and nothing fills the belly of the son of Adam except dust, and Allah turns in mercy to whoever repents."],[4549,"Every deed has a period of keenness, and every period of keenness is followed by a period of slackness. If someone is moderate and near-correct, hope for him, but if he is pointed at with fingers, do not count him as anything."],[4550,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said one night: \"Glory be to Allah! What trials have been sent down, and what treasures have been opened! Wake the women in the chambers, for perhaps a woman clothed in this world is naked on the Day of Resurrection.\""],[4551,"The status of the people of the world is wealth."],[4552,"Indeed, the status of the people of the world, to which they turn, is this wealth."],[4553,"“Indeed Allah does not look at your forms and your wealth, but He looks at your hearts and your deeds.”"],[4554,"\"When Allah loves a servant, He protects him from the world just as one of you keeps protecting his sick person from water.\""],[4555,"I came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ while he was reciting {Competition for more distracts you}. He said, 'The son of Adam says, \"My wealth, my wealth.\" But you have from your wealth only what you eat and consume, or wear and wear out, or give in charity and send ahead.'"],[4556,"I asked the Messenger of God ﷺ and he gave me, then I asked the Messenger of God ﷺ and he gave me, then I asked him and he gave me, then I asked and he gave me, then the Messenger of God ﷺ said: \"O Hakim b. Hizam, this wealth is sweet and green. Whoever takes it with a generous soul will be blessed in it, and whoever takes it with an avaricious soul will not be blessed in it, and will be like one who eats but is not satisfied. The upper hand is better than the lower hand.\" Hakim said: I said, \"O Messenger of God, by the One who sent you with the truth, I will not take anything from anyone after you until I leave this world.\" 'Urwah and Sa'id said: Abu Bakr would call Hakim and give him a gift, but he refused. Then 'Umar b. al-Khattab would give him, but he refused. 'Umar would say, \"I call you to witness, O assembly of Muslims, regarding Hakim b. Hizam, that I offer him his right which was apportioned for him from this booty, but he refuses to take it.\" He said: Hakim did not take anything from any of the people after the Messenger of God ﷺ until he died."],[4557,"\"The world is green and sweet, and God will make you successors in it to see how you act. So beware of the world and beware of women, for the first trial of the Children of Israel was women.\""],[4558,"\"The world is green and sweet. Whoever We give something from it with a good heart from Us and good enjoyment from it, without greed, is blessed in it. Whoever We give something from it without a good heart from Us, with good enjoyment and covetousness, is not blessed in it.\""],[4559,"Some of the Ansar asked the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and he gave them. Then they asked him again, and he gave them until what he had was exhausted. He said: “Whatever good I have, I will not withhold it from you. Whoever seeks chastity, Allah will keep him chaste; whoever seeks self-sufficiency, Allah will make him self-sufficient; and whoever tries to be patient, Allah will make him patient. No one has been given a gift better and more expansive than patience.”"],[4560,"The world is the believer's prison and the disbeliever's paradise."],[4561,"“Indeed, the world is sweet and green. Whoever takes it by its right will be blessed in it. Many a one who plunges into the wealth of Allah and the wealth of His Messenger will have the Fire on the Day of Resurrection.”"],[4562,"'If Allah were to hold me and Jesus accountable for our sins, He would punish us, and He would not wrong us in anything.' He said, and he gestured with his index finger and the one next to it."],[4563,"I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: “If you were to rely upon Allah with true reliance, Allah would provide for you as He provides for the birds: they go out in the morning hungry and return in the evening full.”"],[4564,"\"He has succeeded who submits and whose provision is sufficient, and he is content with it.\""],[4565,"\"Two hungry wolves sent among sheep are not more destructive to them than a man's greed for wealth and honor is to his religion.\""],[4566,"Whoever loves his worldly life harms his Hereafter, and whoever loves his Hereafter harms his worldly life. So prefer what lasts to what perishes."],[4567,"I came to Ubayy b. Ka'b and said to him: Something about divine decree has fallen into my soul. Narrate to me something that perhaps will remove it from my heart. He said: 'If Allah were to punish the inhabitants of His heavens and the inhabitants of His earth, He would punish them without being unjust to them. And if He were to have mercy on them, His mercy would be better for them than their deeds. And if you were to spend the like of Uhud in the path of Allah, Allah would not accept it from you until you believe in divine decree and know that what afflicted you would not have missed you, and that what missed you would not have afflicted you. And if you died on other than this, you would enter the Fire.'"],[4568,"“Allah has finished for every servant five things: his sustenance, his term, his deeds, his resting place, and his final abode.”"],[4569,"Provision surely seeks the servant just as his appointed term seeks him."],[4570,"\"The heart of an old man remains young in love of two things: love of life and love of wealth.\""],[4571,"\"Every nation has a trial, and the trial of my nation is wealth.\""],[4572,"«This is the son of Adam, and this is his appointed term.» He placed his hand at the back of his neck, then spread his hand and said: «And there is his hope, and there is his hope.»"],[4573,"\"Wretched is the slave of the dinar, the slave of the dirham, the slave of the velvet cloth, and the slave of the fine garment. If he is given, he is pleased; if he is denied, he is displeased.\""],[4574,"\"Whoever wakes up secure in his dwelling, healthy in his body, and has his day's food, it is as if the world has been gathered for him.\""],[4575,"The heart of the son of Adam remains young in love of two things: length of life and wealth."],[4576,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ took hold of my shoulder, or he said by my two shoulders, and said, 'Be in this world as though you were a stranger or a wayfarer.' Ibn Umar used to say, 'If you reach the morning, do not wait for the evening, and if you reach the evening, do not wait for the morning. Take from your health for your sickness, and from your life for your death.'"],[4577,"'Shall I inform you of the best of you from the worst of you?' A man said: Yes, O Messenger of Allah. He said: 'The best of you is the one whose good is hoped for and whose evil is safe, and the worst of you is the one whose good is not hoped for and whose evil is not safe.'"],[4578,"A man recited this verse: {Whoever does evil will be recompensed for it} and said, \"Indeed, if we are recompensed for everything we do, we will be ruined.\" When that reached the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, he said, \"Yes, he will be recompensed for it in this world through a calamity in his body that harms him.\""],[4579,"A man met a woman who had been a prostitute in the pre-Islamic era and started playing with her until he stretched his hand towards her. She said, 'Stop, for Allah has removed polytheism and brought Islam.' So he left her and turned away, then he kept looking back at her until his face hit a wall. Then he came to the Prophet ﷺ with blood flowing on his face and told him the story. The Prophet ﷺ said, 'You are a servant for whom Allah intends good.' Then he said, 'When Allah, Mighty and Majestic, intends good for a servant, He hastens the punishment for his sin, and when He intends evil for a servant, He withholds his sin until he meets the Day of Resurrection as if it were a stray.'"],[4580,"\"Calamity does not cease to afflict the believing man and woman in their body, wealth, and children until they meet Allah with no sin upon them.\""],[4581,"\"Indeed, Allah does not wrong the believer with a single good deed: he is rewarded for it with provision in this world and recompensed for it in the Hereafter. As for the disbeliever, he is fed for his good deeds in this world, and when he passes to the Hereafter, he has no good deed by which he may be given any good.\""],[4582,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ took a covenant from us as he took from the women among us, and said, \"Whoever among you commits a legal offense and his punishment is hastened for him, it is an expiation for him. Whoever is delayed, his affair is up to Allah; if He wills, He will have mercy on him, and if He wills, He will punish him.\""],[4583,"Then the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and Hamzah b. 'Abd al-Muttalib conversed about this world. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: 'This world is green and sweet. Whoever takes it with its right, he is blessed in it. But many a one plunges into whatever his soul desires of the wealth of Allah and the wealth of His Messenger ﷺ, and for him is the Fire on the Day of Resurrection.'"],[4584,"Do not deem provision slow, for there is no servant who will die until he reaches the last provision that is his. So be moderate in seeking, in the lawful and leaving the unlawful."],[4585,"“O Ka'b b. 'Ujrah, no flesh and blood that grew on unlawful sustenance will enter Paradise; the Fire is more fitting for it. O Ka'b b. 'Ujrah, people go out in the morning in two ways: one goes out to ransom his soul and sets it free, and another goes out to destroy it. O Ka'b b. 'Ujrah, prayer is a means of nearness, charity is a proof, fasting is a shield, and charity extinguishes sin just as ice disappears from a smooth rock.”"],[4586,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"There is no vessel that the son of Adam fills worse than his stomach. It is sufficient for the son of Adam to eat a few morsels that will keep his spine straight. However, if he must eat, then one-third for food, one-third for drink, and one-third for air.\""],[4587,"The food of the son of Adam has been made a parable for this world, even if he seasons and salts it. Look at what it becomes."],[4588,"“The food of one person is enough for two, the food of two is enough for four, and the food of four is enough for eight.”"],[4589,"The Muslim eats in one intestine, and the disbeliever eats in seven intestines."],[4590,"We came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ while he was doing a task, building a structure. When he finished, he called us and said, \"Do not compete with each other in provision as long as your heads shake, for a person is born of his mother red, with no shell on him, then Allah gives him and provides for him.\""],[4591,"We came to Khabbab to visit him, and he said, \"I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: 'A man is surely rewarded for all his spending except in this dust.'\""],[4592,"Indeed, those who have the most are the lowest, except one who says about wealth like this and like this, and earns it from what is good."],[4593,"the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, “One of you may see a splinter in your brother's eye, but forget the log in your own.”"],[4594,"\"The poor person is not the one who goes around and is turned away by a morsel or two, a bite or two, a date or two. Rather, the poor person is the one who does not find sufficiency to make him independent, does not beg people importunately, and is too shy to beg people importunately.\""],[4595,"\"Carrying out a legal penalty in a land is better for its people than forty mornings of rain.\""],[4597,"Whoever humbles himself before Allah by one degree, Allah will raise him by one degree until He places him in the highest of ʿIlliyyūn. And whoever is arrogant toward Allah by one degree, Allah will lower him by one degree until He places him in the lowest of the low. If one of you were to act upon a solid rock with no door or opening, what he conceals would still come out to the people, whatever it may be."],[4598,"The strong one is not the one who overcomes. The strong one is only the one who overcomes his own self."],[4599,"The most restrained of people in killing are the people of faith."],[4600,"The borrowed item is to be returned, the gift of a milch animal is to be returned, and whoever finds a milch camel kept unmilked for a long time, it is not lawful for him to keep it unmilked until he shows it."],[4601,"\"When you hear a man say, 'The people are ruined,' he is the most ruined of them.\""],[4602,"“When Allah intends good for a servant, He uses him.” It was said: How does He use him, O Messenger of Allah? He said: “He grants him success to do a righteous deed before death.”"],[4603,"“When Allah intends good for a servant, He sweetens him before his death.” It was said: And what is His sweetening him before his death? He said: “A righteous deed is opened for him before his death until He is pleased with him.”"],[4604,"“When Allah intends good for a servant, He sweetens him before his death.” It was said: And what is His sweetening him? He said: “A righteous deed is opened for him before his death until He is pleased with him.”"],[4605,"“Actions are only [judged] by their endings.”"],[4606,"Allah continues to plant in this religion with a planting, employing them in His obedience."],[4607,"When the emigrants to Abyssinia returned to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, he said: \"Will you not tell me the most amazing thing you saw in the land of Abyssinia?\" A group of young men among them said: O Messenger of Allah, while we were sitting, an old woman of their old women passed by us, carrying on her head a water skin. She passed by a young man of theirs, and he placed one of his hands between her shoulders, then pushed her onto her knees, and her water skin broke. When she got up, she turned to him and said: You will know, O treacherous one, when Allah places the Footstool and gathers the first and the last, and the hands and feet speak of what they used to earn. Then you will know my affair and your affair with Him tomorrow. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"She spoke the truth, then spoke the truth. How can Allah sanctify a people from whom the rights of their weak are not taken from their strong?\""],[4608,"“Whoever Allah grants sixty years of life, He has indeed left no excuse for him regarding his lifespan.”"],[4609,"\"Who will tell me about a tree whose likeness is that of the believer: its root is firm and its branches are in the sky, yielding its fruit at all times by the leave of its Lord?\" Abdullah said, \"I wanted to say it is the date palm, but the presence of my father kept me from speaking.\" The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, \"It is the date palm.\" I mentioned that to my father, and he said, \"If you had said it, it would have been dearer to me than such and such\" — I think he said — \"red camels.\""],[4610,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ was brought a bunch of dates, and he said: {A good word is like a good tree: its roots are firm and its branches are in the sky; it yields its fruit at all times by the permission of its Lord.} Then he said: \"It is the palm tree.\" And {the likeness of an evil word is that of an evil tree, which has been uprooted from the surface of the earth, having no stability.} He said: \"It is the colocynth.\""],[4611,"He came to the Prophet ﷺ and the Messenger of Allah ﷺ saw him disheveled and dusty in the appearance of a Bedouin. He said: 'What wealth do you have?' He said: 'Of every kind; Allah has given me.' He said: 'When Allah bestows a blessing on a servant, He loves to see its trace on him.'"],[4612,"Jabir b. 'Abd Allah visited al-Muqanna' and said: \"I will not leave until you have cupping done, for I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: 'Indeed, in it there is healing.'\""],[4613,"The Prophet Muhammadﷺ said, \"Indeed, Allah has not sent down a disease except that He has also sent down its cure. Some people may be aware of it while others may be unaware.\""],[4614,"Allah has not sent down any disease except that He has sent down a cure for it. So take to the milk of cows, for they graze upon every kind of tree."],[4615,"There is a remedy for every malady, and when the remedy is applied to the disease it is cured with the permission of Allah, the Exalted and Glorious. (Using translation from Muslim 2204)"],[4616,"Iblis has despaired of being worshipped by those who pray, but he is active in inciting discord among them."],[4617,"«The throne of Iblis is upon the water. Then he dispatches his raiding parties. The greatest of them in his sight is the greatest of them in temptation.»"],[4618,"Narrated by the Prophet ﷺ: \"When the morning comes, Satan sends out his troops and asks, 'Who has misguided a Muslim today and made him wear a crown?' One of them will come forward and say, 'I have been with him until he divorced his wife.' Satan will say, 'You have not done much.' Then another one will come forward and say, 'I have been with him until he intended to remarry.' Satan will exclaim, 'Yes, you have done well!' Then another one will come forward and say, 'I have been with him until he disobeyed his parents.' Again Satan will say, 'You have done well!' Then one more will come forward and say, 'I have been with him until he associated partners with Allah.' Satan will gleefully respond, 'Indeed, you are the one!' Finally, another one will come forward and say, 'I have been with him until he committed adultery.' Satan will proudly declare, 'Indeed, you are the one!' Then Satan will reward him by crowning him.\""],[4619,"I was shown Laylat al-Qadr, then my family woke me and I forgot it, so seek it in the last ten nights."],[4620,"I was with 'Abd Allah b. 'Umar b. al-Khattab when a man came to him and said: \"O Abu 'Abd al-Rahman, a son of mine was in the land of Persia when the plague struck there. I vowed that if Allah delivered my son to me, he would walk to the Ka'bah. My son has arrived, but he died.\" 'Abd Allah said to him: \"Fulfill your vow.\" The man said: \"I only vowed that my son would walk, but my son has died.\" 'Abd Allah became angry and said: \"Were you not forbidden from vowing? I heard the Prophet ﷺ say: 'A vow does not advance anything nor delay it, but Allah extracts from the miser by it.'\" When I saw that, I said to the man: \"Go to Sa'id b. al-Musayyab and ask him.\" He went to him and asked him, then returned. I said: \"What did he say to you?\" He said: \"Walk on behalf of your son.\" I said: \"Will that be sufficient for me?\" Sa'id b. al-Musayyab said: \"Consider if your son had a debt and you paid it, would it be sufficient for him?\" I said: \"Yes.\" He said: \"Then walk on behalf of your son.\""],[4621,"Every matter of importance not begun with praise of Allah is cut off."],[4622,"Every sermon that does not contain the testimony is like a maimed hand."],[4623,"Indeed, some jealousy Allah loves and some He hates. The jealousy Allah loves is jealousy for Allah's sake, and the jealousy Allah hates is jealousy for other than Allah. And indeed, some pride Allah loves and some He hates. The pride Allah loves is for a servant to show pride in himself at the time of fighting and to show pride at the time of charity. The pride Allah hates is pride for other than the religion."],[4624,"The one who is lenient with the limits of Allah, the one who transgresses the limits of Allah, the one who commands them, and the one who forbids them are like a people who drew lots for places on a ship at sea. One of them got the stern, the farthest from the water, and they were foolish. When they passed by the men of the people, they annoyed them. They said, 'We are the closest people on the ship to the water and the farthest from the water; come, let us bore a hole in the side of the ship, then we will repair it when we no longer need it.' The foolish among those who opposed him said, 'Do it.' He reached for an axe to strike the bottom of the ship. A wise man looked at him and said, 'What are you doing?' He said, 'We are the closest to the water and the farthest from it; I will bore a hole in the side of the ship, and when we no longer need it, we will plug it.' He said, 'Do not do it, for if you do, you will perish and we will perish.'"],[4625,"Nothing remains of the world except trial and tribulation."],[4626,"People are four types, and deeds are six: two that necessitate, a like for a like, a good deed with ten times its like, a good deed with seven hundred-fold, and people: one given expansiveness in this world and the Hereafter, one given expansiveness in this world but straitened in the Hereafter, one straitened in this world but given expansiveness in the Hereafter, one straitened in this world and the Hereafter, and wretched in this world and wretched in the Hereafter. The two that necessitate: whoever says 'There is no god but Allah' or says believing in Allah enters Paradise, and whoever dies associating partners with Allah enters the Fire. Whoever intends a good deed and does it, ten times its like is written for him; whoever intends a good deed but does not do it, one good deed is written for him; whoever intends an evil deed but does not do it, one good deed is written for him; whoever intends an evil deed and does it, one evil deed is written for him, not multiplied. Whoever spends a surplus expenditure in the way of Allah, it is seven hundred-fold.\""],[4627,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, \"A nation will not be successful if it is ruled by a woman.\""],[4628,"\"I have not left after me a tribulation more feared for men than women.\""],[4629,"The last time the Messenger of God ﷺ addressed us, he prayed over the martyrs of Uhud, then mounted the pulpit, praised God and extolled Him, then said: \"I am your forerunner and I am a witness over you. I am looking at my cistern now from this station of mine. By God, I do not fear that you will associate partners with God after me, but I was shown that I have been given the keys to the treasures of the earth, and I fear for you that you will compete over them.\""],[4630,"“Indeed, I will be your forerunner at the Basin, and I will vie with you against other nations, so do not fight one another after me.”"],[4631,"When Allah intends mercy for a nation of His servants, He takes its prophet before it, and makes him a forerunner and a predecessor for it. When He intends destruction for a nation, He punishes it while its prophet is alive, and lets him witness its destruction when they denied him and disobeyed his command."],[4632,"«If God sends down punishment upon a people, the punishment afflicts whoever is among them, then they are resurrected according to their deeds.»"],[4633,"About His saying {Every day He is in a matter}, he said: \"It is of His matter to forgive a sin, relieve a distress, raise a people, and abase others.\""],[4634,"{When the matter is decided and they are in heedlessness} He said: 'In this world.'"],[4635,"“No one is more patient with the harm he hears than Allah: they ascribe a rival to Him and ascribe a son to Him, yet He still provides for them, grants them well-being, and gives to them.”"],[4636,"A child was born into me this night and I named him after the name of my father Ibrihim. He then sent him to Umm Saif, the wife of a blacksmith who was called Abu Saif. He (the Holy Prophet) went to him and I followed him until we reached Abu Saif and he was blowing fire with the help of blacksmith's bellows and the house was filled with smoke. I hastened my step and went ahead of Messenger of Allah ﷺ and said: Abu Saif, stop it, as there comes Messenger of Allah (may peace he upon him). He stopped and Allah's Apostle ﷺ called for the child. He embraced him and said what Allah had desired. Anas said: I saw that the boy breathed his last in the presence of Messenger of Allah ﷺ. The eyes of Messenger of Allah ﷺ shed tears and he said: Ibrahim, our eyes shed tears and our hearts are filled with grief, but we do not say anything except that by which Allah is pleased. O Ibrahim, we are grieved for you. (Using translation from Muslim 2315)"],[4637,"He entered and saw a son of his with his forehead sweating, and he said, \"I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: 'The believer dies with sweat on his forehead.'\""],[4638,"I am amazed at the believer: Allah does not decree anything for him except that it is good for him."],[4639,"\"Many a disheveled one with two worn garments, if he swore by Allah, He would fulfill his oath.\""],[4640,"\"Good is a habit and evil is obstinacy. Whomever Allah wishes good for, He gives him understanding in the religion.\""],[4641,"'None of you will be saved by his deeds.' They said: 'Not even you, O Messenger of Allah?' He said: 'Not even me, unless Allah envelops me in forgiveness and grace.'"],[4642,"«When one of you perfects his Islam, every good deed he does is multiplied tenfold to seven hundred times, and every evil deed he does is recorded for him as the like of it until he meets Allah, Glorified and Exalted.»"],[4643,"“Shall I not guide you to something that expiates sins and increases good deeds?” They said, “Yes, O Messenger of Allah.” He said: “Performing ablution thoroughly even in difficult circumstances, taking many steps to this mosque, and prayer after prayer. No one leaves his house purified, comes to the mosque and prays with the Muslims or with the imam, then waits for the next prayer, except that the angels say: O Allah, forgive him; O Allah, have mercy on him. So when you stand for prayer, straighten your rows and fill the gaps. When the imam says takbīr, say takbīr, for I see you from behind me. When he says ‘Allah hears the one who praises Him,’ say: ‘Our Lord, to You is praise.’ The best rows of men are the first, and the worst rows of men are the last. The best rows of women are the last, and the worst rows of women are the first. O assembly of women, when the men prostrate, guard your eyes from the nakedness of the men.”"],[4644,"I saw in a dream that I was migrating from Makkah to a land with palm trees, and my mind went to its being al-Yamāmah and Hajar, but it was al-Madīnah, Yathrib. And I saw in this dream of mine that I shook a sword and it broke, and it was what befell the believers on the day of Uḥud. And I shook it another time and it returned to the best of what it was, and it was what Allah brought of conquest and the gathering of the believers."],[4645,"“There is no migration after the conquest, but only jihad and intention.”"],[4646,"\"Whoever fights seeking only an 'Iqal, then he will have what he intended.\" (Using translation from Nasāʾī 3139)"],[4647,"Indeed, the dinar and the dirham destroyed those before you, and they will destroy you."],[4648,"\"If you pay the zakah of your wealth, you have fulfilled what is due from it. Whoever gathers unlawful wealth and then gives charity from it will have no reward for it, and its burden will be upon him.\""],[4649,"\"We are the last and the first on the Day of Resurrection. The most numerous are the lowest, except for one who says thus and thus, to his right, to his left, behind him, and in front of him, and scoops with his garment.\""],[4650,"\"Do you know what backbiting is?\" They said, \"Allah and His Messenger know best.\" He said, \"It is mentioning your brother with something he dislikes.\" A man said, \"What if what I say about my brother is true?\" He said, \"If what you say about him is true, you have backbitten him; and if it is not true, you have slandered him.\""],[4651,"'Paradise is closer to any of you than his sandal strap, and the Fire is the same.'"],[4652,"He heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ saying, and his uncle Abu Talib was mentioned in his presence, so he said, \"Perhaps my intercession will reach him, so he will be placed in the shallowest part of Hellfire, where his brain will boil from it.\""],[4653,"“Indeed, the greatest sinner among the Muslims is one who asks about a matter that was not forbidden, and then it becomes forbidden for the Muslims because of his asking.”"],[4654,"Khawlah bt. Hakim, the wife of 'Uthman b. Maz'un, entered upon 'A'ishah in disheveled state. 'A'ishah asked her, 'What is the matter with you?' She said, 'My husband prays at night and fasts during the day.' Then the Prophet ﷺ entered, and 'A'ishah mentioned that to him. The Prophet ﷺ met 'Uthman b. Maz'un and said, 'O 'Uthman, monasticism has not been prescribed for us. Do you not have in me a good example? By Allah, I am the most fearful of Allah among you and the most mindful of His limits.' ﷺ"],[4655,"The plague occurred in Syria, and he said, \"It is a punishment.\" So they dispersed from it. Then Shurahbil b. Hasana said, \"I accompanied the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and 'Amr is more astray than the donkey of his family or the camel of his family.\" And he said, \"It is a mercy from your Lord, the supplication of your Prophet, and the death of the righteous before you. So gather together for it and do not disperse from it.\""],[4656,"Reconciliation is permissible among Muslims, except a reconciliation that makes lawful something unlawful or makes unlawful something lawful."],[4657,"The Prophet ﷺ said, \"A woman is a temptation, and when she goes out, the devil takes a closer look at her. And indeed, she is not closer to the face of Allah than when she is at the deepest part of her home.\""],[4658,"I came to Madinah and found the Messenger of Allah ﷺ standing, addressing the people, saying, \"The upper hand is the giving hand. Begin with those you support: your mother, your father, your sister, your brother, then the next nearest, and the next nearest.\""],[4659,"“The upper hand is better than the lower hand.”"],[4660,"“Hands are three: Allah's hand is the highest, the giver's hand is next to it, and the lower hand is the one that begs. So give from your surplus, and do not be incapable regarding yourself.”"],[4661,"Dates and fresh dates were brought near to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and they ate from them until none remained except a single stone. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: «Do you know what this is?» They said: Allah and His Messenger know best. He said: «The good will depart, then the good, until none of you remains except the like of this.»"],[4662,"The sun never rises without two angels at its sides calling out, making the inhabitants of the earth hear except the two heavy ones [humans and jinn]: 'O people, come to your Lord. What is little and sufficient is better than what is abundant and distracting.' And it never sets without two angels at its sides calling out: 'O Allah, give the spender a replacement and give the withholder destruction.'"],[4663,"\"The jinn are of three types: a type like dogs and snakes, a type that flies in the air, and a type that settles and moves about.\""],[4664,"\"The angels were created from light, the jinn were created from fire, and Adam was created from what has been described to you.\""],[4665,"\"When a man rises from his seat and then returns to it, he has more right to it.\""],[4666,"Whoever spends the night with grease on his hand and something happens to him, let him blame none but himself."],[4667,"“And prepare against them whatever you are able of power. Indeed, strength is archery. Indeed, strength is archery. Indeed, strength is archery.”"],[4668,"“When Allah wills to take a servant in a land, He makes for him a need in it.”"],[4669,"I spent the night reciting to the jinn, who were my companions at al-Hajun."],[4670,"We did not write from the Messenger of Allah ﷺ except the Qur'an and what is in this sheet. He said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"Madinah is sacred between 'Ayr and Thawr. Whoever commits an offense in it or shelters an offender, upon him is the curse of Allah, the angels, and all people; no obligatory or supererogatory act will be accepted from him. The protection of the Muslims is one; the lowest of them may extend it. Whoever violates a Muslim's covenant, upon him is the curse of Allah, the angels, and all people; no obligatory or supererogatory act will be accepted from him. Whoever allies himself with a people without the permission of his masters, upon him is the curse of Allah, the angels, and all people.\""],[4671,"Regarding His saying, 'Thus We have made you a middle nation,' he said, 'Just.'"],[4672,"\"Gatherings are of three kinds: safe, profitable, and harmful.\""],[4673,"\"When you hear a hadith from me that your hearts recognize, and your hair and skin soften to it, and you feel that it is close to you, then I am the closest of you to it. When you hear a hadith from me that your hearts reject, and your hair and skin recoil from it, and you feel that it is far from you, then I am the furthest of you from it.\""],[4674,"When the Messenger of Allah ﷺ entered the House, he found in it an image of Ibrahim and an image of Maryam. He said: “As for them, they have heard that the angels do not enter a house in which there is an image. This is Ibrahim depicted, so what is the matter with him that he is divining with arrows?”"],[4675,"The Prophet ﷺ entered the mosque, and around it were three hundred and sixty idols. He began striking them with a stick he had with him and saying: “The truth has come and falsehood has vanished. Indeed, falsehood is bound to vanish.”"],[4676,"The two months of Eid do not decrease: Ramadan and Dhu al-Hijjah."],[4677,"“Whoever leaves dependents, they are our responsibility. Whoever leaves wealth, it is for his heirs. I am the heir of the one who has no heir: I pay the blood money on his behalf and I inherit from him. The maternal uncle is the heir of the one who has no heir: he pays the blood money on his behalf and inherits from him.”"],[4678,"“Whoever leaves a debt or a destitute family, they are my responsibility. Whoever leaves wealth, it is for his heirs. I am the patron of the one who has no patron: I pay his ransom and inherit his wealth. The maternal uncle is the patron of the one who has no patron: he pays his ransom and inherits his wealth.”"],[4679,"Umar ؓ wrote to Abu Ubaydah: “Teach your children swimming and your fighters archery.” He said: They used to go back and forth among the targets. He said: A stray arrow came and struck a boy and killed him, and no family was known for the boy except his maternal uncle. Abu Ubaydah wrote to Umar and mentioned to him the affair of the boy—to whom should he pay his blood money? He wrote to him that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Allah and His Messenger are the patron of the one who has no patron, and the maternal uncle is the heir of the one who has no heir.”"],[4680,"From the Prophet ﷺ, who said: “Indeed, time has returned to its original state as it was on the day Allah created the heavens and the earth. The year is twelve months, of which four are sacred: three consecutive—Dhu al-Qa‘dah, Dhu al-Hijjah, and al-Muharram—and Rajab of (the tribe of) Mudar, which is between Jumada and Sha‘ban.” Then he said: “Which month is this?” We said, “Allah and His Messenger know best.” He remained silent until we thought he would call it by a name other than its own. He said: “Is it not Dhu al-Hijjah?” We said, “Yes.” He said: “Which land is this?” We said, “Allah and His Messenger know best.” He remained silent until we thought he would call it by a name other than its own. He said: “Is it not the Sacred Land?” We said, “Yes.” He said: “Which day is this?” We said, “Allah and His Messenger know best.” He remained silent until we thought he would call it by a name other than its own. He said: “Is it not the Day of Sacrifice?” We said, “Yes.” He said: “Indeed, your blood and your wealth”—Muhammad said: and I think he said, “and your honor”—“are sacred to you, like the sanctity of this day of yours, in this month of yours, in this land of yours. And you will meet your Lord, and He will ask you about your deeds. So do not return after me astray, striking the necks of one another. Let the one who is present convey to the one who is absent, for perhaps some to whom it reaches will understand it better than some who heard it. Have I conveyed (the message)?”"],[4681,"He and ʿUthman b. ʿAffan came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ to speak with him concerning what he had distributed of the khums of Khaybar to Banu Hashim and Banu al-Muttalib, the two sons of ʿAbd Manaf, saying: their kinship is like our kinship. They said: O Messenger of Allah, you distributed to our brothers Banu al-Muttalib and Banu Hashim, the two sons of ʿAbd Manaf, but you gave us nothing. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to them: \"Indeed, Hashim and al-Muttalib are one and the same.\" Jubayr b. Mutʿim said: And the Messenger of Allah ﷺ did not distribute any of that khums to Banu ʿAbd Shams or to Banu Nawfal, just as he distributed to Banu Hashim and Banu al-Muttalib."],[4682,"When the Messenger of Allah ﷺ prayed with the people, men would fall down from their standing in prayer because of the need they were in—they were the people of the Suffa—until the Bedouins would say: These are madmen. When the Messenger of Allah ﷺ finished his prayer, he said: 'If you knew what is stored for you with Allah, you would love to increase in poverty and need.'"],[4683,"'If you knew what I know, you would laugh little and weep much.'"],[4684,"the Messenger of Allah ﷺ passed by a group of his Companions and they were laughing. Thereupon, he said, \"If you [only] knew what I know, you would laugh little and weep a lot.\" Then Jibrīl came to him and said, \"Allah says to you, 'Why are you putting my servants in despair?'\" He said that he returned back to them then said, \"Attempt moderation [in your actions as you] rejoice.\""],[4685,"“Travel is a portion of torment; it prevents one of you from his sleep, food, and drink. When one of you fulfills his need from his journey, let him hasten to return to his family.”"],[4686,"I asked Ata about al-laghw (unintentional oaths) in oaths, and he said: Aishah said: \"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: 'It is a man's saying: No, by Allah, and Yes, by Allah.'\""],[4687,"We were in a gathering with Ubayy b. Ka'b when Abu Musa al-Ash'ari came with a stick until he stood and said, \"I adjure you by Allah, has any of you heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say, 'Seeking permission is three times; if permission is granted to you, then enter, otherwise return'?\" Ubayy said, \"What is that?\" He said, \"I sought permission upon Umar b. al-Khattab yesterday three times, but permission was not granted to me, so I returned. Then I came to him and entered upon him and told him that I had come yesterday and greeted three times and then left. He said, 'We heard you, and at that time we were busy. If only you had sought permission until permission was granted to you.' I said, 'I sought permission as I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ.' He said, 'By Allah, I will cause your back pain, or you will bring me someone who testifies for you about this.'\" Abu Musa said, \"Ubayy said, 'By Allah, none will stand with you except the youngest of us in age. Rise, O Abu Sa'id.' So I rose and went to Umar and said, 'I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say this.'\""],[4688,"Spirits are mustered troops; those that recognize one another come together, and those that reject one another part ways."],[4689,"Breaking the bone of a dead person is like breaking it when he is alive."],[4690,"“The middle prayer is the afternoon prayer.”"],[4691,"A house with no dates, its people are hungry."],[4692,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ entered on the day of the conquest of Makkah wearing a black turban."],[4694,"“The first Scripture would descend from one gate and on one harf, but the Qur’an descended from seven gates on seven ahruf: a restrainer, a command, what is lawful, what is unlawful, what is clear, what is ambiguous, and parables. So make lawful its lawful, make unlawful its unlawful, do what you are commanded, refrain from what you are forbidden, take heed of its parables, act by its clear verses, and believe in its ambiguous ones. Say: We believe in it; all is from our Lord.”"],[4695,"From the Prophet ﷺ regarding His saying: \"That is more likely to prevent you from doing injustice\" (Quran 4:3), he said: \"That you do not transgress.\""],[4696,"«Indeed Quraysh are recent in their Jahiliyya, so I wanted to win their hearts.» Then he said to them: «Is there anyone among you from other than yourselves?» They said: A son of our sister. He said: «The son of a people's sister is one of them.»"],[4697,"We were with the Prophet ﷺ in a cave when {By those sent forth in succession} was revealed to him. I took it from his mouth, and his mouth was still moist with it. I do not know with which verse he concluded—{Then in what statement after it will they believe?} or {And when it is said to them, \"Bow,\" they do not bow}. A snake darted ahead of us and entered a hole. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, \"You were protected from its evil as it was protected from your evil.\""],[4698,"\"Every letter in the Qur'an in which qunut is mentioned, it is obedience.\""],[4699,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ saw a man on a journey in the shade of a tree with water dripping on him. He said, “What is the matter with your companion?” They said, “He is fasting, O Messenger of Allah.” He said, “It is not righteousness to fast while traveling. Take Allah’s concession that He has granted you and accept it.”"],[4700,"Indeed, Allah does not sleep, nor is it befitting for Him to sleep. He lowers the scale and raises it. The deeds of the night are raised to Him before the day, and the deeds of the day before the night. His veil is light. If He were to remove it, the splendors of His Face would burn every creature that His sight reaches. He places His hand for the sinner of the night to repent during the day, and for the sinner of the day to repent during the night, until the sun rises from its west."],[4701,"Allah's right hand is full, spending does not diminish it, flowing generously night and day. Have you seen what He has spent since He created the heavens and the earth? Indeed, it has not diminished what is in His right hand. The other hand is the grasp; He raises and lowers, and His throne is upon the water."],[4702,"That the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said while he was on the pulpit, \"Allah will take His heavens and His earths in His hand, then say, 'I am Allah,' and He will close His fingers and open them, 'I am the Most Merciful, I am the King.'\" Until I looked at the pulpit moving from below him, until I even said, \"Is it going to fall with the Messenger of Allah?\""],[4703,"A man from the People of the Book came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and said, \"Indeed, Allah holds the heavens on a finger, the water and the earth on a finger, and all the creatures on a finger, then says, 'I am the King.'\" The Messenger of Allah laughed until his molar teeth appeared, then recited this verse: \"They have not appraised Allah with true appraisal, while the earth entirely will be His handful on the Day of Resurrection, and the heavens will be folded in His right hand. Exalted is He and high above what they associate with Him.\""],[4704,"A rabbi from the Jews came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and said, \"O Messenger of Allah, when the Day of Resurrection comes, Allah will place the heavens on a finger, the earths on a finger, the trees on a finger, and all the creatures on a finger, then shake them, then say, 'I am the King.'\" I saw the Messenger of Allah ﷺ laugh until his molar teeth appeared, in amazement at what the Jew said, confirming him, then he recited: \"They have not appraised Allah with true appraisal, while the earth entirely will be His handful on the Day of Resurrection.\""],[4705,"That the Messenger of Allah ﷺ recited these verses one day on the pulpit: \"They have not appraised Allah with true appraisal, while the earth entirely will be His handful on the Day of Resurrection, and the heavens will be folded in His right hand,\" and the Messenger of Allah was saying, \"Like this,\" with his finger, moving it, \"the Lord, Mighty and Exalted, glorifies Himself: I am the Compeller, I am the Proud, I am the King, I am the Mighty, I am the Generous.\" And the pulpit shook with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ until we said, \"It will surely throw him down.\""],[4706,"«The just ones are at the right hand of the Most Merciful — and both His hands are right: those who are just in their judgments, their families, and whatever they are given authority over.»"],[4707,"Verily, one of you gives charity with a date, if it is from good [earnings] — and Allah accepts only the good — and Allah places it in His palm and nurtures it as one of you nurtures his foal or his young camel, until it becomes, in His hand, Mighty and Exalted, like a mountain."],[4708,"Whoever gives charity equivalent to a date from good earnings — and nothing ascends to Allah except the good — Allah will accept it with His right hand and then nurture it for its owner as one of you nurtures his foal, until it becomes like a mountain."],[4709,"“No servant gives charity from pure earnings—and Allah accepts only what is pure, and nothing ascends to the sky except what is pure—except that it is as if he places it in the hand of the Most Merciful, who then nurtures it for him as one of you nurtures his colt or his young camel, until the morsel or the date arrives on the Day of Resurrection like a great mountain.”"],[4710,"There is no heart except that it is between two fingers of the fingers of the Most Merciful. If He wills, He keeps it straight, and if He wills, He turns it astray. He said, and the Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to say, 'O Turner of hearts, make our hearts firm upon Your religion.' He said, 'And the Scale is in the hand of the Most Merciful. He raises some people and lowers others until the Day of Resurrection.'"],[4711,"My servant is as he thinks of Me, and I am with him when he calls upon Me. If he remembers Me within himself, I remember him within Myself; and if he remembers Me in an assembly, I remember him in an assembly better than it and purer."],[4712,"Pride is My cloak and greatness is My lower garment. Whoever contends with Me for either of them, I will cast him into the Fire."],[4713,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said about Allah, Exalted and Majestic: \"Pride is my garment and greatness is my belt. Whoever disputes with me in any of them, I shall cast him into the Fire.\""],[4714,"Pride is My cloak and greatness My lower garment. Whoever contends with Me in either of them, I cast him into the Fire. Whoever draws near to Me by a span, I draw near to him by a cubit. Whoever draws near to Me by a cubit, I draw near to him by an arm's length. Whoever comes to Me walking, I come to him hurrying. Whoever comes to Me hurrying, I come to him running. Whoever mentions Me within himself, I mention him within Myself. Whoever mentions Me among a gathering, I mention him among a gathering greater than them and better."],[4715,"We returned from Makkah with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and people began asking permission of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and he began granting them. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, \"What is the matter that the side of the tree that is next to the Messenger of Allah is more hateful to you than the other side?\" He said: We saw none of the people except weeping. Abu Bakr said, \"The one who asks your permission after this is a fool in my estimation.\" The Messenger of Allah ﷺ stood up, praised Allah and extolled Him, and when he swore he would say, \"By the One in whose hand is my soul, I bear witness before Allah that there is not one of you who believes in Allah and then remains steadfast except that he will be led into Paradise. My Lord has promised me to admit seventy thousand of my nation into Paradise without reckoning or punishment. I hope they will not enter it until you and the righteous among your wives and descendants have taken up dwellings in Paradise.\" Then he said, \"When half the night or two-thirds of it has passed, Allah, Blessed and Exalted, descends to the lowest heaven and says: 'I will not ask about My servants other than Me. Who is there who asks Me that I may give him? Who is there who seeks My forgiveness that I may forgive him? Who is there who calls upon Me that I may answer him'—until the dawn breaks.\""],[4716,"“Our Lord, Mighty and Exalted, descends every night to the lowest heaven when the last third of the night remains, and says, ‘Who calls upon Me, that I may answer him? Who asks Me, that I may give him? Who seeks My forgiveness, that I may forgive him?’”"],[4717,"“Indeed, Allah gives respite until, when the first third of the night has passed, our Lord, Blessed and Exalted, descends to the lowest heaven and says, Mighty and Exalted, ‘Is there any seeker of forgiveness? Is there any repentant? Is there any asker? Is there any caller?’ until dawn breaks.”"],[4718,"She heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say while he was on the pulpit: \"Indeed, there is nothing more jealous than Allah, Mighty and Exalted.\""],[4719,"A time will come upon people when a man will call his cousin and his relative: Come to ease, come to ease! Yet al-Madinah is better for them, if they only knew. By the One in whose hand is my soul, no one leaves it out of aversion for it except that Allah will leave behind in it one better than him. Indeed, al-Madinah is like a bellows: it expels the impurity. And the Hour will not occur until al-Madinah expels its wicked ones just as the bellows expel the dross of iron."],[4720,"Allah is self-respecting and a believer is also self-respecting and the respect of Allah is injured if a believer does what He has forbidden him to do. (Using translation from Muslim 2761a)"],[4721,"No one loves praise more than Allah, so He praised Himself, and no one is more jealous than Allah, so He forbade indecencies."],[4722,"If I were to see a man with my wife, I would have struck him with the sword, and not with the flat part (side) of it. When Messenger of Allah ﷺ heard of that, he said: Are you surprised at Sa'd's jealousy of his honour? By Allah, I am more jealous of my honour than he, and Allah is more jealous than I. Because of His jealousy Allah has prohibited abomination, both open and secret And no person is more jealous of his honour than Allah, and no persons, is more fond of accepting an excuse than Allah, on account of which He has sent messengers, announcers of glad tidings and warners; and no one is more fond of praise than Allah on account of which Allah has promised Paradise. (Using translation from Muslim 1499a)"],[4723,"“Allah is more intensely joyful at the repentance of His servant than one of you who wakes to find his camel, which he had lost in a desolate land.”"],[4724,"“Allah is more joyful at the repentance of one of you than a man in a desolate, deadly land who has with him his mount carrying his provisions, food, and what sustains him. He loses it, so he goes out in search of it until death overtakes him. He says, ‘I will return to my place and die there.’ So he returns to the place where he lost it. While he is like that, sleep overcomes him, and he wakes to find his mount at his head, carrying his provisions and what sustains him. Allah is more joyful at the repentance of one of you than this man.”"],[4725,"“Our Lord wonders at two men: a man who rises from his bed and cover, from between his beloved and his family, to his prayer. Allah, Mighty and Exalted, says to His angels: ‘Look at My servant, he rises from his bed and cover, from between his beloved and his family, to his prayer, out of desire for what is with Me and fear of what is with Me.’ And a man who fights in the path of Allah, and his companions flee, but he knows what is upon him in fleeing and what is for him in returning, so he returns until his blood is shed. Allah says to His angels: ‘Look at My servant, he returned hoping for what is with Me and fearing what is with Me, until his blood was shed.’”"],[4726,"“Your Lord marvels at a shepherd of sheep on the top of a mountain crag who calls the adhan for prayer and prays. Allah says, ‘Look at this servant of Mine; he calls the adhan and establishes the prayer, fearing Me. I have forgiven My servant and admitted him to Paradise.’”"],[4727,"“It is not lawful for a woman to travel except with a mahram.”"],[4728,"\"Allah laughs at two men, one of whom killed the other but they both entered Paradise. The first one fought in the cause of Allah and was killed, then Allah accepted the repentance of the one who killed him, and he fought and was martyred.\" (Using translation from Nasāʾī 3166)"],[4729,"Prophet (saas) said: \"Your Lord is Kind and Most Generous, and is too kind to let His slave, if he raises his hands to Him, bring them back empty,\" or he said \"frustrated.\" (Using translation from Ibn Mājah 3865)"],[4730,"“Allah, glorified and exalted be He, will say to the servant on the Day of Resurrection: ‘O son of Adam, I fell ill and you did not visit Me.’ He will say: ‘O Lord, how can I visit You when You are the Lord of the worlds?’ He will say: ‘Did you not know that My servant so-and-so fell ill and you did not visit him? Did you not know that if you had visited him you would have found Me?’ And He will say: ‘O son of Adam, I asked you for water and you did not give Me to drink.’ He will say: ‘O Lord, how can I give You to drink when You are the Lord of the worlds?’ He will say: ‘Did you not know that if you had given him to drink you would have found that with Me? O son of Adam, I asked you for food and you did not feed Me.’ He will say: ‘O Lord, how can I feed You when You are the Lord of the worlds?’ He will say: ‘Did you not know that My servant so-and-so asked you for food and you did not feed him? Indeed, if you had fed him you would have found that with Me.’”"],[4731,"I said, “O Messenger of Allah, will we see our Lord on the Day of Resurrection?” He said, “Do you see the moon on the night of the full moon, or the sun, without clouds?” They said, “Yes.”"],[4732,"None of you should say, ‘What a disappointment time is!’ for indeed Allah is time."],[4733,"I heard Messenger of Allah ﷺ as saying: Allah, the Exalted and Glorious, said: The son of Adam abuses Dahr (the time), whereas I am Dahr since in My hand are the day and the night. (Using translation from Muslim 2246a)"],[4734,"The people of the pre-Islamic era used to say, ‘It is only the night and the day that destroy us; it is they that kill us and give us life.’ Allah said, {It is nothing but our life of this world} (the verse)."],[4735,"It will be cast into the Fire, and it will say, 'Is there any more?' until the Lord, Mighty and Exalted, places His foot in it, and it says, 'Enough, enough.'"],[4736,"I was sitting with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and my she-camel was hobbled at the door when a group from Banū Tamīm entered upon him and said, “O Messenger of Allah, we have come to you to gain understanding in the religion and to ask you about the beginning of this matter: what was it?” He ﷺ said, “Allah existed and there was nothing other than Him, and His Throne was upon the water, then He wrote in the Remembrance everything, then He created the heavens and the earth.”"],[4737,"“When Allah created the creation, He wrote in His Book, which He wrote upon Himself and it is raised above the Throne: ‘Verily, My mercy prevails over My wrath.’”"],[4738,"The Prophet ﷺ said, \"When Allah completed the creation, He wrote in a book near Him: 'My mercy prevails over My wrath.' \""],[4739,"“Verily, Allah when He created the creation, He wrote with His Hand concerning Himself, that: ‘My mercy prevails over My wrath.’” (Using translation from Tirmidhī 3543)"],[4740,"“Verily Allah created, on the day He created the heavens and the earth, one hundred mercies, each filling the space between the heavens and the earth. He placed in the earth one mercy from them, by which the mother shows compassion to her child and wild beasts show compassion to one another, and He deferred ninety-nine until the Day of Resurrection. So when it is the Day of Resurrection, He will complete them with this mercy to one hundred.”"],[4741,"“Verily, Allah has one hundred mercies. He sent down from them one mercy among the jinn, humans, and beasts. By it they show mutual affection and by it they show mutual compassion, and by it wild beasts show compassion to their young. He deferred ninety-nine mercies with which He will show mercy to His servants on the Day of Resurrection.”"],[4742,"“Allah, Majestic and Exalted, made mercy one hundred parts. He kept with Himself ninety-nine and sent down on the earth one part. From that part creatures show compassion to one another, so much so that an animal lifts her hoof from her young for fear of striking it.”"],[4743,"I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: “Allah, Blessed and Exalted, said: ‘I am with My servant’s thought of Me, so let him think of Me as he wishes.’”"],[4744,"I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ relate from Allah, Majestic and Exalted, who said: “I am with My servant’s thought of Me, so let him think of Me as he wishes.”"],[4745,"When My servant talks about doing a good deed, I write it for him as a good deed as long as he does not do it. When he does it, I write it as ten times its like. And when he talks about doing an evil deed, I forgive it as long as he does not do it. When he does it, I write it as its like."],[4746,"When My servant intends a good deed, write it as a good deed. When he does it, write it as ten times its like. And when My servant intends an evil deed, do not write it as its like. If he abandons it, write it as a good deed."],[4747,"When My servant wants to do an evil deed, do not write it against him until he does it. If he does it, write it as its like. If he abandons it for My sake, write it as a good deed. If he wants to do a good deed, write it for him as a good deed. If he does it, write it for him as ten times its like up to seven hundred fold."],[4748,"The Prophet (peace be upon him) said: \"Allah, the Blessed and Exalted, said: O son of Adam, if you come to Me with sins nearly as great as the earth and meet Me not associating anything with Me, I will come to you with forgiveness nearly as great as it.\""],[4749,"\"When My servant draws near to Me a span, I draw near to him a cubit. When he draws near to Me a cubit, I draw near to him a fathom. When he comes to Me walking, I come to him at speed. And if he runs, I hasten to him. And Allah is most capacious in forgiveness.\""],[4750,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Allah, Blessed and Exalted, says: I am the best of partners. Whoever does a deed in which he associates someone else with Me, I am free of it; it belongs to the one he associated.”"],[4751,"He heard the Prophet ﷺ say in his sermon: 'Allah commanded me to teach you what you did not know of what He taught me this day: every property I have granted to My servant is lawful. I created all My servants as hanifs, but the devils came to them and turned them away from their religion, forbade them what I had made lawful for them, and commanded them to associate with Me that for which I have sent down no authority. Allah looked upon the people of the earth and loathed them, Arabs and non-Arabs alike, except remnants of the People of the Book. He said: \"O Muhammad, I have sent you only to test you and to test others through you, and I have sent down to you a Book that water cannot wash away, which you recite awake and asleep.\" Allah, Mighty and Exalted, commanded me to warn Quraysh, so I said: \"Then they will split my head and leave it like a loaf of bread.\" He said: \"Drive them out as they drove you out, raid them and they will raid you, spend and it will be spent on you, send an army and We will send five times its like, and fight with those who obey you against those who disobey you.\" He said: \"The people of Paradise are three: a just imam who is truthful and granted success; a man who is merciful and tender-hearted toward every relative and Muslim; and a chaste poor man who gives charity.\" He said: \"The people of Hell are five: an unjust man whose greed does not conceal even the smallest thing; a man who does not enter evening or morning except that he is deceiving you regarding your family and wealth; and the weak who are followers among you, not seeking family or wealth.\" A man said to him: \"O Abu Abd Allah, is he one of the clients or one of the Arabs?\" He said: \"He is a follower who belongs to a man and commits illicit intercourse with his wife outside marriage; the shameless obscene one; and he mentioned miserliness and lying."],[4752,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ addressed us and said: 'Allah, Mighty and Exalted, commanded me to teach you some of what He taught me this day. He said to me: \"I created all My servants as hanifs, and everything I have granted to My servants is lawful for them. The devils came to them and turned them away from their religion, forbade them what I had made lawful, and commanded them to associate with Me that for which I sent down no authority. Allah examined the people of the earth before sending me and loathed them, Arabs and non-Arabs alike, except remnants of the People of the Book. He said to me: \"I have sent down a Book that water cannot wash away, so recite it asleep and awake. Allah commanded me to warn Quraysh, but I said: \"O Lord, then they will split my head and leave it like a loaf of bread.\" He said to me: \"Drive them out as they drove you out, raid them and they will raid you, spend and We will spend on you, send an army and We will send five times its like, and fight with those who obey you against those who disobey you.\""],[4753,"“It is not lawful for a woman to travel except with a mahram.”"],[4754,"When Allah loves a servant, He says to Jibril: \"I have loved so-and-so, so love him.\" Then Jibril loves him, then he announces among the inhabitants of heaven: \"Allah has loved so-and-so, so love him.\" Then the inhabitants of heaven love him, then acceptance is placed for him on earth. And when Allah hates a servant, Malik said: I do not think he said anything except in hatred, something similar to that."],[4755,"“Gabriel came to me and said: 'Indeed, my Lord and your Lord says to you: How have I raised your mention?' He said: 'Allah knows best.' He said: 'When I am mentioned, you are mentioned with Me.'”"],[4756,"«Indeed Allah has pardoned for my community error, forgetfulness, and what they are coerced to do.»"],[4757,"The Prophet ﷺ said: “Indeed Allah, Mighty and Exalted, says: ‘O son of Adam, devote yourself to My worship; I will fill your chest with richness and I will suffice your poverty. But if you do not, I will fill your hands with preoccupations and I will not suffice your poverty.’”"],[4758,"that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, \"Indeed, we, the prophets, were commanded to delay our suhur (pre-dawn meal), hasten our iftar (breaking of the fast), and hold our right hand upon the left hand during our prayers.\""],[4759,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ sent a small group to raid a tribe. One man from the tribe separated from the rest, and a man from the group followed him with his sword visible. The man said, \"I am a Muslim,\" but the other man did not pay attention to what he said and struck him, killing him. The news was conveyed to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ , who said something severe about the incident. The killer approached and said, \"O Messenger of Allah, I swear by Allah, he did not say anything except seeking protection from being killed.\" The Messenger of Allah ﷺ turned away from him and everyone around him. He continued his sermon and then turned back to the man and said, \"O Messenger of Allah, he did not say anything except seeking protection from being killed.\" The Messenger of Allah ﷺ turned away from him and everyone around him again. Unable to contain himself, the man said it a third time, and the anger on the Messenger's face became apparent. He said, \"Allah has made it forbidden for me to kill a believer,\" repeating it three times."],[4760,"Indeed, a servant whose body I have made healthy and whose livelihood I have made ample, yet five years pass without him coming to Me, is deprived.\""],[4761,"Leave me with what I have left you, for those before you were destroyed only by their questioning and their disagreement with their prophets. So when I forbid you from something, avoid it, and when I command you with something, do of it what you are able."],[4762,"The Prophet of Allah ﷺ came to Madinah while they were pollinating date palms, saying \"they were fertilizing them.\" He said: What are you doing? They said: Something they used to do. He said: If you did not do it, it would be better. So they left it, and it shed or decreased. They mentioned that to him, and he ﷺ said: I am only a human. If I tell you something regarding your religion, then take it, and if I tell you something regarding your worldly affairs, then I am only a human."],[4763,"Al-Qaʿnabī narrated to us, he said: ʿAbd al-ʿAzīz b. Muḥammad narrated to us, from al-ʿAlāʾ, from his father, from Abū Hurayrah, who said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, \"Allah, Blessed and Exalted, said: Every good deed the son of Adam performs, I reward him for it ten good deeds up to seven hundred times over, except fasting, for it is Mine and I reward it. Fasting is a shield. So whoever is fasting should not engage in obscene talk or act ignorantly. If someone insults him or harms him, let him say: 'I am fasting, I am fasting.'\""],[4764,"\"When My servant loves to meet Me, I love to meet him; and when he hates to meet Me, I hate to meet him.\""],[4765,"Allah loves that His concessions be taken, just as He loves that His strict commands be taken.”"],[4766,"\"My servant has denied Me, but it was not for him to do so, and he has reviled Me, but it was not for him to do so. His denial of Me is saying: How can He bring us back as He began us? And his reviling of Me is saying: Allah has taken a son. And I am the Self-Sufficient, I did not beget nor was I begotten, and there is none equal to Him.\""],[4767,"The Prophet ﷺ said: 'Allah, Blessed and Exalted, said: \"The son of Adam denies Me, though he has no right to deny Me. The son of Adam reviles Me, though he has no right to revile Me. As for his denying Me, it is his saying: 'He will not bring me back as He created me.' Is not the first creation easier for Me than bringing him back? As for his reviling Me, it is his saying: 'Allah has taken a son.' But I am Allah, the One, the Self-Sufficient. I do not beget, nor was I begotten, and there is none comparable to Me.\"\""],[4768,"I entered with Abu Hurayrah the house of Sa'id, or Marwan, and he saw a painter painting on the wall. He said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Allah, Blessed and Exalted, said: Who is more unjust than one who goes and creates like My creation? Let them create a grain, or let them create an ant.”"],[4769,"\"Indeed Allah has overlooked for my Ummah whatever their souls whisper to them, as long as they do not speak of it or act upon it.\""],[4770,"\"Indeed Allah has overlooked for my Ummah whatever their souls whisper to them, as long as they do not utter it or act upon it.\""],[4771,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ caught up with Umar b. al-Khattab while he was riding in a group and swearing by his father. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"Allah forbids you from swearing by your fathers. Whoever swears, let him swear by Allah or be quiet.\""],[4772,"“O My servants, I have forbidden oppression for Myself and made it forbidden among you, so do not oppress one another. O My servants, you err by night and day, and I am the One who forgives sins, and I do not care.”"],[4773,"Indeed Allah loves gentleness and gives for gentleness what He does not give for harshness, and what He does not give for anything else."],[4774,"\"Allah is pleased with three things for you and displeased with three things for you. He is pleased that you worship Him and do not associate anything with Him, that you hold fast to the rope of Allah all together, and that you give sincere counsel to those whom Allah has placed in authority over your affairs. And He is displeased for you with idle gossip, wasting wealth, and excessive asking.\""],[4775,"The Prophet ﷺ entered upon me, and I recognized in his face that something had come to him. He performed ablution and did not speak to anyone, then he went out, and I clung to the chamber to hear what he would say. He sat on the pulpit, praised Allah and extolled Him, then said: \"O people, indeed Allah, Blessed and Exalted, says to you: Enjoin good and forbid wrong before you call upon Me and I do not answer you, and you ask Me and I do not give you, and you seek My help and I do not help you.\" He added nothing more until he descended."],[4776,"Mu‘awiyah wrote to al-Mughirah, ‘Write to me something you heard from the Messenger of Allah ﷺ.’ He wrote to him, ‘I heard him say: Indeed, Allah dislikes three things for you: gossip (qil wa qal), wasting wealth, and asking too many questions.’"],[4777,"Indeed, Allah dislikes for you gossip (qil wa qal), asking too many questions, and wasting wealth."],[4778,"The Prophet ﷺ said, \"Allah has forbidden for you, (1) to be undutiful to your mothers, (2) to bury your daughters alive, (3) to not to pay the rights of the others (e.g. charity, etc.) and (4) to beg of men (begging). And Allah has hated for you (1) vain, useless talk, or that you talk too much about others, (2) to ask too many questions, (in disputed religious matters) and (3) to waste the wealth (by extravagance)."],[4779,"\"Take from me, take from me: Allah has made a way for them. The previously married with the previously married: one hundred lashes and stoning. The virgin with the virgin: one hundred lashes and exile for a year.\""],[4780,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ stood among us and did not leave anything that would happen from that moment until the Hour is established except that he spoke about it. Whoever memorized it, memorized it, and whoever forgot it, forgot it. These companions of mine knew it. One of them would forget something, but then I would see it and remind him, just as a man remembers the face of another man who had been absent; when he sees him, he recognizes him."],[4781,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ indeed stood and spoke to us about what will happen between us and the Hour. It is not that I am telling you I was alone; others were with me. Whoever memorized that, memorized it, and whoever forgot it, forgot it."],[4782,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ led us in the morning prayer, then ascended the pulpit and delivered a sermon until the noon prayer approached. Then he descended, prayed, ascended the pulpit and delivered a sermon to us until the afternoon prayer approached. Then he descended, prayed, ascended the pulpit and delivered a sermon to us until the sun set. He told us what had happened and what will happen, and the most knowledgeable of us is the one who memorized the most."],[4783,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ commanded the people of Madinah to enter ihram from Dhu al-Hulayfah, the people of Sham from al-Juhfah, and the people of Najd from Qarn. 'Abd Allah b. 'Umar said: And I was informed that he said, 'The people of Yemen enter ihram from Yalamlam.'"],[4784,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ came out to us and said, \"You think that I am the last of you to die, but I am the first of you to die. You will follow me in groups, striking one another's necks.\""],[4785,"\"When Allah wants mercy for a nation of His servants, He takes its Prophet before it, making him a forerunner and predecessor for it. When He wants destruction for a nation, He punishes it while its Prophet is alive, letting his eye be cooled by its destruction when they denied him and disobeyed his command.\""],[4786,"A woman came to the Prophet ﷺ and spoke with him. He told her to return. She said, 'O Messenger of God, do you think if I come and do not find you—meaning death?' He said: 'If you do not find me, then go to Abu Bakr.'"],[4787,"The Prophet ﷺ said, \"The caliphate will last for thirty years, and the rest of them will be kings. The caliphs and the kings will be twelve.\""],[4788,"There will be after me caliphs who act according to what they know and do what they are commanded. And after them there will be caliphs who act without knowledge and do what they are not commanded. Whoever disapproves is free, and whoever withholds is safe, but whoever is pleased and follows…"],[4789,"There will be after me caliphs who act according to what they know and do what they are commanded. Then after them there will be caliphs who act without knowledge and do what they are not commanded. Whoever disapproves of them is free, but whoever is pleased and follows…"],[4790,"I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ saying, \"There will be twelve caliphs after me, all of them from the Quraysh.\" When he returned to his house, people from the Quraysh came to him and asked, \"And then what will happen?\" He said, \"And then there will be strife.\""],[4791,"I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: Islam will continue to be triumphant until there have been twelve Caliphs. Then the Prophet ﷺ said something which I could not understand. I asked my father: What did he say? He said: He has said that all of them (twelve Caliphs) will be from the Quraish. (Using translation from Muslim 1821d)"],[4792,"This religion will remain mighty and protected; they will be helped against those who oppose them until there are twelve caliphs."],[4793,"\"Whoever cannot find sandals, let him wear khuffs and cut them below the two ankles.\""],[4794,"I saw the Messenger of Allah ﷺ pointing towards the east and saying, \"Indeed, the tribulation is here; indeed, the tribulation is here, from where the horn of Satan appears.\""],[4795,"\"Before the Hour there will be liars: among them the man of al-Yamamah, among them the man of San'a', al-Ansi, among them the man of Himyar, and among them the Dajjal, and he is the greatest of them in tribulation.\""],[4796,"\"The Hour will not be established until thirty Dajjals emerge, all of them claiming to be the Messenger of Allah, until wealth overflows, tribulations appear, and Harj increases.\" They said, \"What is Harj, O Messenger of Allah?\" He said, \"Killing, killing.\""],[4797,"The people spoke much about the affair of Musaylimah the Liar before the Prophet ﷺ said anything about him. Then the Messenger of Allah ﷺ stood among the people, praised Allah as He deserves, and said, \"Now then, regarding this man about whom you have spoken much, he is a liar among thirty liars who will emerge before the Dajjal. There is no town but the terror of the Masih will enter it, except Madinah. On every pass of its passes there are two angels defending it from the terror of the Masih.\""],[4798,"\"I saw in my hands two bracelets of gold. I blew on them and they flew away. I interpreted them as the two liars, Musaylimah and al-Ansi.\""],[4799,"Musaylimah came with a great army and stopped among the palm trees. It reached the Messenger of Allah ﷺ that he said, \"If Muhammad grants me the authority after him, I will follow him.\" The Messenger of Allah ﷺ approached with no one but Thabit b. Qays b. Shammas, holding a palm branch, until he stood before him. Then he said, \"If you asked me for this, I would not give it to you. If you turn back, Allah will destroy you. This is Thabit; he will answer you on my behalf. I think you are the one I saw in what I was shown.\""],[4800,"I asked Nafi' b. 'Utbah b. Abi Waqqas, \"Tell me, did you hear the Messenger of Allah ﷺ mention the Dajjal?\" He said, \"I came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ while there were people from the West with him who had come to him to submit to him, wearing wool. When I drew near to him, I heard him say: 'You will invade the Arabian Peninsula, and Allah will grant you victory over it. Then you will invade Persia, and Allah will grant you victory over it. Then you will invade Byzantium, and Allah will grant you victory over it. Then you will invade the Dajjal, and Allah will grant you victory over him.'\""],[4801,"\"Yemen will be conquered, and a people will come who urge others to move, and they will depart with their families and those who obey them, while Madinah is better for them, if they only knew. Syria will be conquered, and a people will come who urge others to move, and they will depart with their families and those who obey them, while Madinah is better for them, if they only knew. Iraq will be conquered, and a people will come who urge others to move, and they will depart with their families and those who obey them, while Madinah is better for them, if they only knew.\""],[4802,"\"Al-Hirah was shown to me like the fangs of dogs, and you will surely conquer it.\" A man stood up and said, \"Grant me, O Messenger of Allah, the daughter of Buqaylah.\" He said, \"She is yours.\" So they gave her to him. Then her father came and said, \"Will you sell her?\" He said, \"Yes.\" He said, \"For how much? Name your price as you wish.\" He said, \"For a thousand dirhams.\" He said, \"You have taken her.\" It was said to him, \"If only you had said thirty thousand?\" He said, \"Is there any number greater than a thousand?\""],[4803,"I came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ during the expedition of Tabuk while he was in a leather tent, and I sat at the entrance of the tent. I greeted him, and he returned the greeting and said, \"Enter, O 'Awf.\" I said, \"All of me?\" He said, \"All of you.\" So I entered and found him performing ablution slowly. Then he said, \"O 'Awf, remember six signs before the Hour: one of them is my death.\" 'Awf said, \"I was struck with deep grief at that.\" The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, \"Say: one.\" I said, \"One.\" Then he said, \"The conquest of Jerusalem. Then a disease will appear among you. Then wealth will overflow among you, so much so that a man among you will be given a hundred dinars and remain discontented. Then a tribulation will occur among you, so that no believing house will remain but it will enter it. Then a peace treaty will be made between you and the Banu al-Asfar (Byzantines), but they will betray you and march against you in eighty banners, under each banner twelve thousand.\""],[4804,"\"When the Messenger of Allah ﷺ arrived in Makkah, he did ramal ﷺ.\""],[4805,"I came to the Prophet ﷺ while he was in a dome of tanned leather containing forty men. He said: 'You will be given victory, and you will be helped, and you will take spoils. Whoever of you reaches that time, let him fear Allah, enjoin good, and forbid evil. And whoever lies about me deliberately, let him take his seat in the Fire.'"],[4806,"\"The Prophet ﷺ did ramal from the Stone to the Stone.\""],[4807,"The quickest of you to join me is the one with the longest hand. She said: They would compete over which of them had the longest. She said: The longest of us in hand was Zaynab, because she used to work with her hand and give charity."],[4808,"“Lands will be opened to you, and Allah will suffice you. Let none of you be unable to amuse himself with his arrows.”"],[4809,"“A band of Muslims will certainly conquer the white treasure of the family of Khosrow—or he said: in the white [palace].”"],[4810,"I used to ask about the hadith of 'Adi b. Hatim while he was beside me, but I did not go to him to ask him. Then I went to him and asked him. He said, \"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ was sent when he was sent, and I disliked him more than I have ever disliked anything. I set out until I was in the farthest land toward Byzantium and said: 'If I go to this man, then if he is a liar, it will not remain hidden from me; and if he is truthful, I will follow him.' So I returned. When I arrived in Madinah, the people looked eagerly at me and said, 'Adi b. Hatim has come, Adi b. Hatim has come.' The Prophet ﷺ said to me, 'O Adi b. Hatim, submit and you will be safe.' I said, 'I have a religion.' He said, 'I know your religion better than you do'—two or three times—'Are you not the chief of your people?' I said, 'Yes.' He said, 'Do you not take a quarter of the spoils?' I said, 'Yes.' He said, 'That is not lawful for you in your religion.' He said, 'I was humbled by that.' Then he said, 'O Adi b. Hatim, submit and you will be safe, for I think—or I see—or as the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said—that what prevents you from submitting is the poverty you see around me. But soon a woman will travel from al-Hirah without any protection until she circumambulates the House, and the treasures of Kisra b. Hurmuz will surely be conquered for us, and wealth will overflow—or will overflow—so much so that a man will be concerned about who will accept his wealth as charity.'\" 'Adi b. Hatim said, \"I have seen a woman travel from al-Hirah without any protection until she circumambulated the House, and I was among the first cavalry that raided al-Mada'in, the treasures of Kisra b. Hurmuz. And I swear by Allah that the third will surely come to pass, for it is the saying of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ to me.\""],[4811,"“When the treasures of Persia and Rome are opened for you, what kind of people will you be?” Abd al-Rahman b. Awf said, “We will be as Allah has commanded us.” The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, “You will vie with one another, then you will envy one another, then you will turn your backs on one another, then you will hate one another, then you will go to the poor among the Muhajirun and set some of them over others.”"],[4812,"ʿUmar b. al-Khaṭṭāb addressed us at al-Jābiyah and said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ stood in a place like this of mine and said, 'Be good to my Companions, then those who follow them, then lying will spread until a man swears an oath before being asked to swear it, and bears witness before being asked to bear witness. Whoever of you wants to attain the best of Paradise, let him keep to the community, for Satan is with the one and is farther from the two. Indeed, no man should be alone with a woman, for the third of them is Satan. Indeed, whoever among you is grieved by his evil deed and pleased by his good deed is a believer.'"],[4813,"“When Khosrow perishes, there will be no Khosrow after him, and when Caesar perishes, there will be no Caesar after him. By Him in whose hand is my soul, their treasures will certainly be spent in the cause of Allah, exalted is He.”"],[4814,"“When Khosrow perishes, there will be no Khosrow after him ever, and when Caesar perishes, there will be no Caesar after him ever. By Allah, their treasures will certainly be spent in the cause of Allah.”"],[4815,"The Prophet of God ﷺ came to me while I was sleeping in the mosque of Madinah. He struck me with his foot and said: 'Do I not see you sleeping in it?' I said: 'Yes, O Messenger of God, my eyes overcame me.' He said: 'Then what will you do when you are expelled from it?' I said: 'What should I do, O Prophet of God? Should I strike with my sword?' The Prophet ﷺ said: 'Shall I not guide you to what is better for you than that and closer to right guidance? You hear and obey, and you will be driven along with them wherever they drive you.'"],[4816,"The Messenger of God ﷺ began to recite this verse: {And whoever fears God—He will make for him a way out and provide for him from where he does not expect.} He kept repeating it to me until I became drowsy. Then he said: 'O Abū Dharr, if all the people took hold of it, it would suffice them.' Then he said: 'O Abū Dharr, how will you act when you are expelled from Madinah?' I said: 'To spaciousness and ease; I will be one of the pigeons of Makkah.' He said: 'How will you act when you are expelled from Makkah?' I said: 'To spaciousness and ease, to the land of Syria and the Holy Land.' He said: 'Then how will you act when you are expelled from it?' I said: 'Then, by the One who sent you with the truth, I will take my sword and place it on my shoulder.' He ﷺ said: 'Or better than that: you hear and obey, even an Ethiopian slave with mutilated limbs.'"],[4817,"When death approached Abū Dharr, I wept. He said: 'What makes you weep?' I said: 'Why should I not weep while you are dying in a desolate land and I have no garment that would suffice as a shroud for you?' He said: 'Do not weep, and rejoice, for I heard the Messenger of God ﷺ say to a group of which I was a member: \"A man from among you will surely die in a desolate land, witnessed by a band of believers.\" And none of that group remains except that he has died in a village among a community, and I am the one who will die in a desolate land. By God, I have not lied nor been lied to. So look out for the road.' She said: 'But how, when the pilgrims have gone and the roads are cut off?' He said: 'Go and keep watch.' She said: I would go to a sand hill and look out, then return to him and nurse him. While I was doing that, I saw men on their mounts as if they were vultures. They approached until they stopped by me and said: 'What is wrong with you, O slave girl of God?' I said: 'A Muslim man is dying; will you shroud him?' They said: 'Who is he?' I said: 'Abū Dharr.' They said: 'The companion of the Messenger of God ﷺ?' I said: 'Yes.' She said: They ransomed him with their fathers and mothers and hurried to him. They entered upon him and he welcomed them and said: 'I heard the Messenger of God ﷺ say to a group of which I was a member: \"A man from among you will surely die in a desolate land, witnessed by a band of believers.\" And none of that group remains except that he has died in a village and a community, and I am the one who will die in a desolate land. You hear: If I had a garment that would suffice as a shroud for me or for my wife, I would not be shrouded except in a garment of mine or hers. You hear: I call you to witness that one of you who was a commander or a headman or a courier or a leader should shroud me. And there is no one among the people except that he has been involved in some of that, except a young man from the Anṣār. He said: \"O uncle, I will shroud you. I have not committed anything of what you mentioned. I will shroud you in this cloak of mine and in two garments in my bag from my mother's spinning, which she wove for me.\" So the Anṣārī shrouded him among the group who witnessed it, among them Ḥujr b. al-Adbar and Mālik b. al-Ashtar, in a group all of whom were Yemeni.'"],[4818,"We complained to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ while he was leaning on a cloak of his in the shade of the Ka'bah. We said, 'Will you not seek victory for us? Will you not supplicate for us?' He said, 'Among those before you, a man would be seized, a pit would be dug for him in the ground, he would be placed in it, then a saw would be brought and placed on his head, cutting him into two halves, and his flesh would be combed with iron combs away from his bones and flesh, but that would not turn him away from his religion. By Allah, this matter will certainly be completed until a rider travels from Sana'a to Hadramawt fearing none but Allah, and the wolf for his sheep, but you are impatient.'"],[4819,"\"You will surely conquer a land in which the qirat is mentioned, so treat its people with kindness, for they have a covenant and a tie of kinship.\""],[4820,"\"You will surely come to a people with curly hair, so treat them well, for they will be a strength for you and a means to reach your enemy, by Allah's permission.\""],[4821,"\"The Prophet ﷺ did ramal from the Stone to the Stone.\""],[4822,"'Woe to the Arabs from an evil that has drawn near: a blind, deaf, and dumb tribulation. The one sitting in it is better than the one standing, the one standing is better than the one walking, and the one walking is better than the one running. Woe to the one running in it from Allah on the Day of Resurrection.'"],[4823,"We were with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ on a journey. Some of us were shooting arrows, some were in their camp, and some were repairing their tents when the call to prayer was announced. We gathered and found the Messenger of Allah ﷺ delivering a sermon, saying: \"There has been no prophet before me but it was incumbent upon Allah to guide his community to what is best for them and to warn them of what he knows is evil for them. Indeed, this community has been granted well-being at its beginning, and its later part will be afflicted with trials. A tribulation will come and the believer will say, 'This is my destruction.' Then it will come again and he will say, 'This is my destruction.' Then it will disperse. Whoever of you wishes to be kept away from the Fire and to enter Paradise, let his death come upon him while he believes in Allah and the Last Day, and let him bring to people what he loves to be brought to him. Whoever pledges allegiance to a leader, giving him his handshake and the fruit of his heart, let him obey him as much as he can.\" He (the narrator) said: I said: \"This is your cousin Mu'awiyah; he commands us to consume our wealth among ourselves in falsehood and to shed our blood, while Allah said: {O you who believe, do not consume your wealth among yourselves in falsehood} and said: {And do not kill yourselves}.\" He said: Then he was silent for a while and then said: \"Obey him in obedience to Allah and disobey him in disobedience to Allah.\""],[4824,"'The Children of Israel were governed by prophets; whenever a prophet died, another prophet arose. And there is no prophet after me.' A man said: What will be after you, O Messenger of Allah? He said: 'Caliphs, and they will be many.' He said: So what do you command us, O Messenger of Allah? He said: 'Fulfill the pledge of the first, then the first, and give them their due, for Allah will ask them about what is due to you.'"],[4825,"We came to al-Yashkuri in a group from Banu Layth. He said: \"From which people are you?\" We said: \"Banu Layth.\" We asked him and he asked us. They said: \"We have come to ask you about the hadith of Hudhayfah.\" He said: \"We returned with Abu Musa from one of his expeditions. The animals became expensive in Kufah. My companion and I asked Abu Musa for permission, and he granted it to us. We arrived in Kufah early in the day. I said to my companion: 'I am entering the mosque; when the market opens I will come out to you.' I entered the mosque and found a circle as if their heads had been cut off, listening to the talk of a man. I came and stood over them. A man came and stood beside me. I said to the man: 'Who is this?' He said: 'Are you from Basrah?' I said: 'Yes.' He said: 'I knew that if you were from Kufah you would not ask about this. This is Hudhayfah b. al-Yaman.' I drew near to him and heard him saying: 'People used to ask the Messenger of Allah ﷺ about good, but I used to ask him about evil, knowing that good would not overtake me. I said: \"O Messenger of Allah, will there be evil after this good?\" He said: \"O Hudhayfah, learn the Book of Allah and follow what is in it,\" saying it to me three times. I said: \"O Messenger of Allah, will there be evil after this good?\" He said: \"Tribulation and evil.\" I said: \"O Messenger of Allah, will there be good after this evil?\" He said: \"A truce upon smoke.\" I said: \"O Messenger of Allah, truce upon smoke, what is it?\" He said: \"The hearts of some people will not return to what they were upon.\" I said: \"O Messenger of Allah, will there be evil after this good?\" He said: \"O Hudhayfah, learn the Book of Allah and follow what is in it,\" three times. I said: \"O Messenger of Allah, will there be evil after this good?\" He said: \"A blind and deaf tribulation, upon which are callers at the gates of the Fire. If you die, O Hudhayfah, while biting upon the root of a dry tree, it is better for you than following any one of them.\"\""],[4826,"\"Indeed, before the Hour there will be tribulations like patches of dark night. In them a man will be a believer in the morning and a disbeliever in the evening, and a believer in the evening and a disbeliever in the morning. The one sitting in them is better than the one standing, the one standing is better than the one walking, and the one walking is better than the one running. Break your bows, cut your bowstrings, and strike your swords against stones. If someone's house is entered upon, let him be like the better of the two sons of Adam.\""],[4827,"'If you knew what I know, you would laugh little and weep much. Hypocrisy will appear, trust will be lifted, mercy will be withdrawn, the trustworthy will be suspected, and the untrustworthy will be trusted. The dark tribulations will camp with you.' They said, 'What are the dark tribulations, O Messenger of Allah?' He said, 'Tribulations like pieces of a dark night.'"],[4828,"\"Soon the best wealth of a Muslim will be sheep he follows to the mountain tops and places of rainfall, fleeing with his religion from tribulations.\""],[4829,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to him: \"O Abu Dharr, how will you act when people become so hungry that you cannot get up from your bed to go to your mosque?\" I said: \"Allah and His Messenger know best.\" He said: \"Keep yourself chaste.\" Then he said: \"How will you act when people die so much that a house is worth a servant?\" I said: \"Allah and His Messenger know best.\" He said: \"Be patient.\" Then he said: \"How will you act when people fight each other so much that the stone of oil is drowned?\" I said: \"Allah and His Messenger know best.\" He said: \"Go to the one you are with.\" I said: \"What do you think if it comes upon me?\" He said: \"Enter your house.\" I said: \"What do you think if it comes upon me?\" He said: \"If you fear that the flash of the sword will dazzle you, then throw a part of your cloak over your face; he will bear your sin and his sin.\" I said: \"Should I not carry a weapon?\" He said: \"Then you would share with him.\""],[4830,"An Arab man said, \"O Messenger of Allah, does Islam have any limit?\" He replied, \"Yes, whoever Allah intends good for, He guides them to Islam, whether they are Arabs or non-Arabs.\" The man asked, \"What then, O Messenger of Allah?\" He replied, \"Then there will be trials like layers of darkness.\" The man said, \"No, by Allah, O Messenger of Allah.\" The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, \"Indeed, and by the One in whose hand is my soul, you will return to that state, holding onto the reigns of ignorance, striking each other's necks. The best people on that day will be a believer who isolates himself in a mountain pass, fearing Allah and leaving people to their harm.\""],[4831,"\"Indeed, there will be tribulations in which the one lying down will be better than the one sitting, the one sitting better than the one standing, the one standing better than the one walking, and the one walking better than the one running.\" A man said: \"O Messenger of Allah, what do you command me?\" He said: \"Whoever has camels, let him join his camels; whoever has sheep, let him join his sheep; whoever has land, let him join his land; whoever has none of that, let him go to his sword and strike its edge against a rock, then let him escape if he can find a way of escape.\""],[4832,"“Indeed I have a right over Quraysh, and indeed Quraysh has a right over you: as long as they judge and act justly, and are entrusted and fulfill, and mercy is sought from them and they show mercy.”"],[4833,"We were sitting with Umar and he said: \"Which of you remembers the hadith of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ about tribulation?\" I said: \"I do.\" He said: \"You are indeed worthy, or bold. How did he say it?\" I said: \"I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: 'The tribulation of a man in himself, his family, his wealth, his child, and his neighbor is expiated by fasting, charity, prayer, enjoining good, and forbidding evil.'\" Umar said: \"This is not what I mean. I mean the one that surges like the waves of the sea.\" I said: \"What do you have to do with it, O Commander of the Believers? Between you and it is a closed door.\" He said: \"Will the door be broken or opened?\" I said: \"It will be broken.\" He said: \"That is more likely that it will never be closed again.\" We said to Hudhayfah: \"Did Umar know who the door was?\" He said: \"Yes, as he knows that before tomorrow is tonight.\""],[4834,"\"There will be tribulations like summer winds; the one sitting in them is better than the one standing, and the one standing is better than the one walking. Whoever seeks them out, they seek him out.\""],[4835,"Abu Dharr came to Uthman from Syria and said: \"O Commander of the Believers, open the door so that people may enter. Do you consider me among a people who recite the Quran but it does not go beyond their throats? They pass through the religion as an arrow passes through its target, then they do not return to it until the arrow returns to its notch. They are the worst of creation and creatures. By the One in Whose hand is my soul, if you commanded me to sit I would not stand, and if you commanded me to be standing I would stand as long as my legs could support me, and if you tied me to a camel I would not release myself until you are the one who releases me.\" Then he asked his permission to go to al-Rabadhah, and he granted it. He went there and found a slave leading them in prayer. They said: \"Abu Dharr.\" The slave stepped back. It was said to him: \"Come forward.\" He said: \"My close friend ﷺ advised me with three things: to hear and obey even if it is an Ethiopian slave with mutilated limbs; and when I make a broth, to increase its water, then look at your neighbors and give them from it in kindness; and to pray the prayer at its time, for if you come to the imam and he has already prayed, you have secured your prayer, otherwise it is supererogatory for you.\""],[4836,"When Aisha came, she passed by some waters of Banu Amir, she came to them at night and heard the barking of dogs. She said: What water is this? They said: The water of al-Haw'ab. She said: I think I should go back. They said: Wait, may Allah have mercy on you, go forward and the Muslims will see you and Allah will reconcile through you. She said: I think I should go back, for I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: “How will it be for one of you when the dogs of al-Haw'ab bark at her?”"],[4837,"Ali said, \"By Allah, the Messenger of Allah did indeed say this to me.\" Abu Al-Aswad said, \"I said to myself, 'I have never seen a warrior like him, addressing people with something like this today.'\""],[4838,"The Hour will not come until two great factions fight, and between them there is a great slaughter, while their claim is one."],[4839,"There will be two factions in my Ummah, and between them a group will deviate, and the faction closest to the truth will kill them."],[4840,"The transgressing faction will kill Ammar."],[4841,"«There will be before the Hour the harj.» They said, \"O Messenger of Allah, what is the harj?\" He said, \"Killing.\" They said, \"More than what we kill?\" He said, \"It is not your killing of the polytheists, but the killing of one another.\" He said, \"And will we have our minds with us?\" He said, \"Indeed, the minds of the people of that time will be taken away.\""],[4842,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ as saying: Allah, the Exalted, folded for me the earth, or he said (the narrator is doubtful): My Lord folded for me the earth, so much so that I saw its easts and wests (i.e. the extremities). The kingdom of my community will reach as far as the earth was floded for me. The two treasures, the red and the white, were bestowed on me. I prayed to my Lord that He may not destroy my community by prevailing famine, and not give their control to an enemy who annihilates then en masse except from among themselves. My Lord said to me: Muhammad, If I make a decision, it is not withdrawn ; and I shall not destroy them by prevailing famine, and I shall not give their control to an enemy, except from among themselves, who exterminates them en masse, even if they are stormed from all sides of the earth ; only a section of them will destroy another section, and a section will captive another section. I am afraid about my community of those leaders who will lead astray. When the sword is used among my people, it will not be withdrawn from them till the Day of Resurrection, and the Last Hour will not come before the tribes of my people attach themselves to the polytheists and tribes of my people worship idols. There will be among my people thirty great liars each of them asserting that he is (Allah's) prophet, where as I am the seal of the Prophet s after whom (me) there will be no prophet ; and a section of my people will continue to hold to the truth - (according to the Ibn Isa's version: (will continue to dominate) - the agreed version goes: \"and will not be injured by those who oppose them, till Allah's command comes.\" (Using translation from Abū Dāʾūd 4252)"],[4843,"\"A people will emerge among you whose prayer you will consider insignificant compared to their prayer, and your fasting compared to their fasting, and your deeds compared to their deeds. They recite the Qur'an, but it does not go beyond their throats. They pass through the religion as an arrow passes through the game. You look at the arrowhead and see nothing; you look at the shaft and see nothing; you look at the fletching and see nothing; and you are uncertain about the notch.\""],[4844,"\"Indeed, after me, from my nation — or there will be after me from my nation — a people who recite the Qur'an, but it does not go beyond their throats. They exit the religion as the arrow exits the game, then they do not return to it. They are the worst of creation and creatures.\""],[4845,"When I narrate to you from the Messenger of Allah ﷺ a hadith, falling from the sky is more beloved to me than lying about him. And when I narrate to you regarding what is between me and you, war is deception. I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: \"At the end of time there will come people young in age, foolish in intellect. They say the best of the speech of creation. They pass through Islam as the arrow passes through the game. Their faith does not go beyond their collarbones. Wherever you meet them, kill them, for killing them is a reward for the one who kills them on the Day of Resurrection.\""],[4846,"\"The Prophet of Allah ﷺ mentioned people who will be in his nation, emerging in a faction of people, their mark being shaving. They are among the worst of people, or they are among the worst of creation. The nearer of the two parties to the truth will kill them.\""],[4847,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ performed tawaf around the House on his mount, touching the Corner with a staff."],[4848,"The millstone of Islam will turn for thirty-five or thirty-six years. If they are destroyed, then that is the way of those who are destroyed, and if they remain, their religion will remain for them for seventy years."],[4850,"The Messenger of God ﷺ used to enter upon Umm Ḥarām bt. Milḥān and she would feed him. Umm Ḥarām was married to ʿUbāda b. al-Ṣāmit. One day the Messenger of God ﷺ entered upon her and she fed him, then she sat delousing his head. The Messenger of God ﷺ fell asleep, then woke up laughing. She said: I said, 'What makes you laugh, O Messenger of God?' He said: 'People of my community were shown to me, raiders in the path of God, riding the crest of this sea, kings on thrones'—or 'like kings on thrones' (he was unsure which). She said: I said, 'O Messenger of God, pray to God to make me one of them.' So he prayed for her. Then he laid his head down and slept, then woke up laughing. She said: I said, 'What makes you laugh, O Messenger of God?' He said: 'People of my community were shown to me, raiders in the path of God,' as he said the first time. She said: I said, 'O Messenger of God, pray to God to make me one of them.' He said: 'You are of the first ones.' So Umm Ḥarām rode the sea in the time of Muʿāwiya b. Abī Sufyān, and she fell from her mount when she came out of the sea and died."],[4851,"The angel of rain asked his Lord for permission to visit the Prophet ﷺ, and He granted him permission. It was Umm Salamah's day. The Prophet ﷺ said, \"Guard the door for us; no one should enter upon us.\" While she was at the door, al-Husayn b. Ali came, jumped, and burst in, opening the door and entering. He began leaping onto the Prophet's back, and the Prophet started kissing him and covering him. The angel said to him, \"Do you love him?\" He said, \"Yes.\" He said, \"Indeed, your nation will kill him. If you wish, I will show you the place where he will be killed.\" He said, \"Yes.\" He took a handful from the place where he would be killed and showed it to him. He brought him soft soil or red dust. Umm Salamah took it and placed it in her garment."],[4852,"«The destruction of my nation will be at the hands of foolish young boys from Quraysh.»"],[4853,"«Indeed, the corruption of my nation will be at the hands of foolish little boys from Quraysh.»"],[4854,"«Woe to the rulers! People will wish that they had been hung by their forelocks from the Pleiades and that they had never been given authority over anything at all.»"],[4855,"«The world will not come to an end until it belongs to Luka' b. Luka'.»"],[4856,"«O 'Abd al-Rahman, do not ask for leadership, for if you are given it by asking, you will be left to it, and if you are given it without asking, you will be helped in it. And if you swear an oath and see something else better, then do what is better and expiate for your oath.»"],[4857,"«You will be eager for leadership, and it will be regret and remorse on the Day of Resurrection. How good a wet-nurse, and how evil a weaner.»"],[4858,"“There will come upon you rulers who bring near the wicked of people and delay the prayer from its times. Whoever of you reaches that, let him not be a chief, nor a policeman, nor a tax collector, nor a treasurer.”"],[4859,"“Allah will surely support this religion with people who have no share of good.”"],[4860,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ came out while we were nine, and among us was a leather cushion, and he said: \"There will be after me rulers. Whoever enters upon them and confirms them in their lies and aids them in their oppression is not of me, and I am not of him, and he will not come to me at the Basin. And whoever does not enter upon them, does not confirm them in their lies, and does not aid them in their oppression, he is of me and I am of him, and he will come to me at the Basin.\""],[4861,"“Whoever pleases Allah by displeasing people, Allah will suffice him; and whoever displeases Allah by pleasing people, Allah will entrust him to the people.”"],[4862,"«The bonds of Islam will be undone, one by one. Each time a bond is undone, people cling to the one that follows it. The first of them to be undone is governance, and the last of them is prayer.»"],[4863,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to Kaʿb b. ʿUjrah: “O Kaʿb b. ʿUjrah, may Allah protect us from the rule of the foolish.” They said, “O Messenger of Allah, what is the rule of the foolish?” He said, “Rulers who will be after me who do not follow my guidance and do not practice my Sunnah. Whoever believes them in their lies and helps them in their wrongdoing, those are not from me and I am not from them, and they will not come to my basin. Whoever does not believe them in their lies and does not help them in their wrongdoing, they are from me and I am from them, and they will come to my basin. O Kaʿb b. ʿUjrah, fasting is a shield, charity extinguishes sin, and prayer is a proof”—or he said, “a means of nearness.”—“O Kaʿb b. ʿUjrah, people set out in the morning: one sells his soul and sets it free, and another sells his soul and destroys it.”"],[4864,"“There will be selfishness and matters you will disapprove of.” They said, “O Messenger of Allah, what do you command us?” He said, “Fulfill the right upon you, and ask Allah for what is yours.”"],[4865,"How will you be when you remain among people who delay the prayer beyond its time? He said, 'What should I do?' He said, 'Pray the prayer at its time. Then if you find them, they have not prayed, pray with them, and do not say, \"I have already prayed, so I will not pray.\"'"],[4866,"My dear friend enjoined upon me three things: “Listen and obey, even if a slave with amputated limbs; and when you make a broth, increase its water, then look to a household among your neighbors and give them some of it generously; and pray the prayer at its time, and if you find that the imam has already prayed, then you have secured your prayer, otherwise it is a supererogatory prayer.”"],[4867,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to me: “Pray the prayer at its time. If you come to the people and they have already prayed, you have secured your prayer, and if they have not prayed, you pray with them and it becomes a supererogatory prayer for you.”"],[4868,"«Time will draw together, knowledge will diminish, tribulations will appear, and harj will increase.» It was said, \"O Messenger of Allah, what is it?\" He said, \"Killing.\""],[4869,"«It is near that the Hour will not be established until knowledge is taken away, tribulations appear, lying becomes abundant, time draws together, markets draw close together, and harj increases.» It was said, \"What is harj?\" He said, \"Killing.\""],[4870,"«Indeed, Allah does not take away knowledge by snatching it away from people, but He takes away the scholars by [taking] their knowledge, until when no scholar remains, people take ignorant leaders. They are asked and they give fatwas without knowledge, so they go astray and lead others astray.\""],[4871,"Ibn ‘Umar said I have not seen the Apostle of Allaah ﷺ touching anything in the House (the Ka’bah) but the two Yamani corners. (Using translation from Abū Dāʾūd 1874)"],[4872,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ performed tawaf around the House on his mount, touching the Corner with a staff."],[4873,"Indeed, Allah does not take away knowledge by snatching it away from people after He has given it to them, but He takes it away by the death of the scholars. When no scholar remains, the people take ignorant leaders, they ask them for religious verdicts, and they give verdicts without knowledge, so they go astray and lead others astray."],[4874,"The affair of this Ummah will continue to be upright or close to upright as long as they do not speak about the children and the divine decree."],[4875,"“Soon a man will strike the livers of camels in pursuit of knowledge, and he will not find a scholar more knowledgeable than the scholar of the people of Madinah.”"],[4876,"The best of people are my generation, then those who follow them, then those who follow them. Then there will come a people whose oaths precede their testimony and whose testimony precedes their oaths."],[4877,"The best of my Ummah is the generation in which I was sent, then those who follow them—then Allah knows best whether he mentioned the third or not—then there will arise a people who give testimony but are not asked to testify, who make vows but do not fulfill them, who are treacherous and not entrusted, and among whom obesity will spread."],[4878,"“How will you be, O Abdullah b. Amr, if you remain among the worthless dregs of people?” He said: And what are they, O Messenger of Allah? He said: “That is when their covenants and trusts become confused and they become like this,” and he interlaced his fingers. He said: Then what should I do, O Messenger of Allah? He said: “Do what you know, leave what you disapprove of, attend to your own self, and leave the common people.”"],[4879,"\"By the One in whose hand is the soul of Muhammad, the Hour will not come until obscenity and miserliness appear, the trustworthy is betrayed, the treacherous is trusted, the wild goats perish, and the tahut appear.\" They said: O Messenger of God, what are the wild goats and the tahut? He said: \"The wild goats are the faces of people and their nobles, and the tahut are those who were under the feet of people, unknown.\""],[4880,"There will surely come a time when a man will not care whether he takes wealth from lawful or unlawful means."],[4881,"\"The Hour will not come until you kill a people small-eyed, as if their faces are layered shields.\""],[4882,"\"The Hour will not come until the Muslims fight the Turks, a people whose faces are like layered shields, who wear hair and walk in hair.\""],[4883,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ performed tawaf around the House on his mount, touching the Corner with a staff."],[4884,"\"The Hour will not come until you fight a people small-eyed, as if their eyes are locusts' eyes, broad-faced, as if their faces are layered shields, coming until they tie their horses to palm trees.\""],[4885,"\"Indeed, some people from my nation will settle at a walled garden they call al-Basrah, near which is a river called Dijlah. They will have a bridge over it, and its inhabitants will become numerous, and it will be among the cities of the emigrants. At the end of time, Banu Qantura' will come — peoples broad-faced — until they settle on the riverbank. Its people will divide into three factions. One faction will take to the tails of camels and the desert and perish. Another faction will take for themselves and disbelieve. Another faction will put their children behind their backs and fight them, and they are the martyrs.\""],[4886,"\"The Hour will not come until you fight Khuz and Kirman — a people among the non-Arabs, red-faced, snub-nosed, small-eyed, as if their faces are layered shields.\""],[4887,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, \"Indeed, the Jews have divided into seventy-one or seventy-two sects, and the Christians have done the same. This nation will also divide into seventy-three sects.\""],[4888,"From the Prophet ﷺ , he said, \"You hear and others hear from you, and others hear from those who hear from you.\""],[4889,"There will come upon people a time when a group of people goes on a military expedition, and it is said: Is there among you anyone who accompanied the Messenger of God ﷺ? It will be said: Yes. Then victory will be granted to them. Then there will come upon people a time when a group of people goes on a military expedition, and it is said: Is there among you anyone who accompanied the Companions of the Messenger of God ﷺ? It will be said: Yes. Then victory will be granted to them. Then there will come upon people a time when a group of people goes on a military expedition, and it is said: Is there among you anyone who accompanied those who accompanied them? It will be said: Yes. Then victory will be granted to them."],[4890,"“O Jabir, did you get married?” I said, “Yes.” He said, “Have you acquired carpets?” I said, “How could we have carpets?” He said, “Indeed, there will be.”"],[4891,"When a man would come to Madinah, if he had an acquaintance there, he would stay with his acquaintance. If he had no acquaintance, he would stay in the suffah. I was among those who stayed in the suffah. I shared with a man, and the Messenger of Allah ﷺ would give us every day a mudd of dates between two men. One day he said the salam at the end of the prayer, and a man among us called out, “O Messenger of Allah, the dates have burned our stomachs.” So the Prophet ﷺ went to his pulpit, ascended, praised Allah, and extolled Him. Then he mentioned what he had encountered from his people, saying, “Until I and my companion remained for over ten days with no food except berir, and berir is the fruit of the arak tree. Then we came to our brothers, the Ansar, and the bulk of their food was dates, and they shared them with us. By Allah, if I could find bread and meat for you, I would feed you, but perhaps you will live to see a time—or whoever of you lives to see it—when they will wear the like of the curtains of the Kaaba and will be served morning and evening with large bowls of food.”"],[4892,"\"Give charity, for a time will come when one of you will pass by with his charity and find no one to accept it. He will say: 'If only you had come before today; but today I have no need of it.'\""],[4893,"From the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, he said: \"The Hour will not come until wealth becomes abundant among you and overflows, so much so that the owner of wealth will be concerned about who will accept his charity from him, and he will offer it, but the one to whom it is offered will say: 'I have no need of it.'\""],[4894,"\"The Hour will not come until wealth becomes abundant and overflows, so much so that a man will bring out the zakat of his wealth and find no one to accept it from him.\""],[4895,"We were with Jabir b. 'Abd Allah, and he said, \"Soon the people of Iraq will not have a qafiz or a dirham collected for them.\" We said, \"From what cause?\" He said, \"From the non-Arabs; they will prevent that.\" Then he said, \"Soon the people of Syria will not have a dinar or a mudy collected for them.\" We said, \"From what cause?\" He said, \"From the Byzantines?\" Then he paused for a moment and said, \"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: 'In the last of my Ummah there will be a caliph who will pour out wealth without counting it.'\""],[4896,"When the Messenger of Allah ﷺ conquered Makkah, he went out with us toward Hawazin until we passed by the lote tree of the disbelievers, a tree around which they used to remain and which they called Dhat Anwat. We said, 'O Messenger of Allah, make for us a Dhat Anwat as they have a Dhat Anwat.' The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, 'Allah is greater! These are the ways. This is just as the Children of Israel said to Moses: \"Make for us a god as they have gods.\" He said, \"You are an ignorant people.\" Then the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, \"You will surely follow the ways of those before you.\"'"],[4897,"'You will certainly follow the ways of those before you, span by span and cubit by cubit, so much so that if they entered a lizard's hole, you would enter it.' We said, 'O Messenger of Allah, the Jews and the Christians?' The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, 'Who else?'"],[4899,"In the end of time there will be people whose talk in their mosques concerns worldly matters; Allah has no need of them."],[4900,"‘Abdullāh b. al-Mughaffal heard a son of his saying: “O Allah, I ask You for the white palace on the right side of Paradise.” He said: “O my son, when you ask, then ask Allah for Paradise and seek refuge in Him from the Fire, for I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: ‘There will be in the end of time a people who exceed the bounds in supplication and purification.’”"],[4901,"‘Abdullāh b. al-Mughaffal heard a son of his saying in his supplication: “O Allah, I ask You for the white palace on the right side of Paradise when I enter it.” He said: “O my son, ask Allah for Paradise and seek refuge in Him from the Fire, for I heard the Prophet ﷺ say: ‘There will be in this ummah a people who exceed the bounds in supplication and purification.’”"],[4902,"«They will keep asking for fatwas until one of them says, 'This Allah created the creation, so who created Allah?!'»"],[4903,"«When your raiding becomes extensive and the incursions multiply * and spoils are deemed lawful, then the best of your jihad is the ribat.»"],[4904,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ came out to us while we were reciting the Quran and said: “Praise be to Allah, the Book of Allah is one, and among you are the red, the white, and the black. Recite it before peoples recite it who will straighten it as an arrow is straightened.”"],[4905,"Umar b. al-Khattab delivered a sermon to us at al-Jabiyah and said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ stood among us as I am standing among you today and said: “Be good to my Companions, then those who follow them, then those who follow them. Then lying will spread until a man swears an oath without being asked to swear it. So whoever wants the luxuriant part of Paradise, let him adhere to the community, for Satan is with the one and he is farther from two. Let not one of you be alone with a woman, for Satan is the third of them. Whoever is pleased by his good deed and troubled by his evil deed is a believer.”"],[4906,"\"I have not left after me a tribulation more harmful to men than women.\""],[4907,"I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ saying, \"There will be in the latter part of my nation men who ride on saddles like skeletons of men; they will enter the doors of mosques. Their women will be clothed and yet naked, with their hair disheveled. Curse them, for they are cursed. If they die, do not offer the funeral prayer for them, nor bury them in Muslim graveyards, for they are disbelievers.\""],[4908,"'No house of mud-brick or hair tent will remain on the earth but Allah will cause Islam to enter it, either by the might of the mighty or by the humiliation of the humiliated.'"],[4909,"'No house of mud-brick or hair tent will remain on the face of the earth but Allah will cause the word of Islam to enter it, either by the might of the mighty or by the humiliation of the humiliated.'"],[4910,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"The Hour (Day of Judgment) will not come until there is much chaos and until the land of the Arabs returns to being pastures and rivers.\""],[4911,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ narrated two hadiths to us. I have seen one of them, and I am waiting for the other. He narrated to us: \"Trustworthiness descended in the roots of men's hearts, and the Quran descended, so they learned from the Quran and learned from the Sunnah.\""],[4912,"“By Him in Whose hand is my soul, a day will certainly come upon one of you when he will not see me; then seeing me will be dearer to him than his family and his wealth.”"],[4913,"“There will be in the end of time people from my ummah who will narrate to you what neither you nor your fathers have heard, so beware of them.”"],[4914,"Nothing remains of this world except trial and tribulation."],[4915,"“The Hour will not rise until you mount each other in the road like donkeys mount.” I said: “Will that really happen?” He said: “Yes, it will certainly happen.”"],[4916,"“The Hour will not rise” or “Among the signs of the Hour is that knowledge will be lifted, ignorance will abound, wine will be drunk, adultery will appear openly, men will become few and women many, until fifty women will have one guardian.”"],[4917,"“A time will certainly come when a man will go around with charity of gold and find no one to take it from him, and a man will be seen followed by forty women because of the scarcity of men and the abundance of women.”"],[4918,"«You will be enlisted as armies: an army in Al-Sham, an army in Iraq, and an army in Yemen.» He said: I said, \"O Messenger of God, choose for me?\" He said, \"You must go to Al-Sham. Whoever refuses, let him join his Yemen and drink from its waterholes, for God has guaranteed me Al-Sham and its people.\""],[4919,"The Last Hour would not come until a person would pass by a grave of another person and he would say: I wish it had been my abode. (Using translation from Muslim 157k)"],[4920,"The Hour will not come until the buttocks of the women of Daws wobble around Dhu al-Khalasah. It was an idol that Daws used to worship in the Jāhiliyyah at Tabālah."],[4922,"Narrated Abu 'Amir and Abu Malik Al-Ash'ari: We heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say, \"There will be people among my nation who will consider silk, alcohol, and musical instruments permissible.\""],[4923,"“The Hour will not rise until the sky rains such rain that houses of mud will not shelter from it, and nothing will shelter from it except houses of hair.”"],[4924,"“A time will come upon you when the Euphrates will recede from a mountain of gold, and people will fight over it. Of every hundred, ninety-nine will be killed.” He said, “O my son, if you witness that, do not be among those who fight over it.”"],[4925,"“The Hour will not be established until the Euphrates recedes from a mountain of gold, and people fight over it, and of every ten, nine are killed.”"],[4926,"“The Euphrates is about to recede from a treasure of gold. Whoever is present, let him not take anything from it.”"],[4927,"“The Euphrates is about to recede from a treasure of gold. Whoever is present, let him not take anything from it.”"],[4928,"'The Hour will not come until the Euphrates recedes from a hill of gold, and people will fight over it, and nine-tenths of them will be killed.'"],[4929,"'The earth will vomit the pieces of its liver, like columns of gold and silver. The thief will come and say, \"It was for this that I was cut.\" The killer will come and say, \"It was for this that I killed.\" The one who severed family ties will come and say, \"It was for this that I severed my womb.\" And they will leave it, taking nothing from it.'"],[4930,"“The Muslims are on the verge of being besieged in Madinah until their farthest outpost is Salāḥ.”"],[4931,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ performed tawaf around the House on his mount, touching the Corner with a staff."],[4932,"“Madinah will certainly be left in the best state it has ever been, until a dog enters and urinates on one of the pillars of the mosque or on the minbar.” They said: “O Messenger of Allah, to whom will the fruits belong at that time?” He said: “To the beasts, the birds, and the wild animals.”"],[4933,"\"The Hour will not come until Madinah expels its evil people as the blacksmith's bellows expel the dross of iron.\" He said, \"And there will come upon the people a time when a man will call his relative and his close friend to ease, while Madinah is better for them, if only they knew.\""],[4934,"\"The last town in Islam to fall into ruin is Madinah.\""],[4935,"We came to Anas b. Malik and complained to him about al-Hajjaj. He said, \"Be patient, for no day or time comes upon you except that what follows it is worse than it, until you meet your Lord. I heard this from your Prophet ﷺ.\""],[4936,"\"If only one night remained of this world, a man from the household of the Prophet ﷺ would rule during it.\""],[4937,"“The Hour will not come until the earth is filled with injustice and tyranny. Then a man from my family, or my household, will emerge and fill it with equity and justice, just as it was filled with injustice and tyranny.”"],[4938,"“The Hour will not come until a man from my household rules the people. His name will match my name, and his father’s name will match my father’s name. He will fill the earth with equity and justice.”"],[4939,"“A man from my nation will emerge whose name matches my name and whose character matches my character. He will fill the earth with equity and justice, just as it was filled with injustice and oppression.”"],[4940,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"The Hour will not be established until a man from my household rules over the people, filling the earth with justice as it was filled with oppression before him, ruling for seven years.\""],[4942,"An army will invade the Kaaba until, when they are in a desert of the land, the first of them and the last of them will be swallowed up. Aisha said, \"O Messenger of Allah, among them are those other than them and those who are not of them?\" He said, \"The first of them and the last of them will be swallowed up, then they will be resurrected according to their intentions.\""],[4943,"I went with Abdullah b. Safwan and al-Harith b. Rabi'ah until we entered upon Umm Salamah. They said, \"O Umm Salamah, will you not narrate to us about the sinking that will swallow the people?\" She said, \"Yes. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: 'A seeker of refuge will seek refuge at the House, and an expedition will be sent against him. When they are in a desert of the land, they will be swallowed up.'\" She said, \"I said, 'O Prophet of Allah, what about one who was unwilling?' He said, 'He will be swallowed up with them, but he will be resurrected on the Day of Resurrection according to what was in his heart.'\""],[4944,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"There will be disagreement upon the death of a Caliph, and a man from the Quraysh, from the people of Madinah, will come out to Makkah. People from Makkah will come to him and forcibly remove him, while he is reluctant. Then they will pledge allegiance to him between the corner of the Kaaba and the Station of Ibrahim. They will send an army from the people of Sham (Greater Syria) against him. When they reach the barren land, they will be swallowed by the earth. When the people learn about this, the people of Sham and a group from the people of Iraq will come to him and pledge allegiance to him. Then a man from the Quraysh, whose paternal relatives belong to the Kalb tribe, will send an army against them and defeat them. Then Islam will appear victorious and he will distribute among the people. He will remain for seven years.\""],[4945,"We were discussing the cooked grape juice (al-tila'), and Abd al-Rahman b. Ghanm entered upon us, so we discussed it. He said: Abu Malik al-Ash'ari narrated to me that he heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: \"People from my Ummah will drink wine, calling it by other than its name. Musical instruments and female singers will be played on their heads. Allah will cause the earth to swallow them, and He will turn some of them into apes and pigs.\""],[4946,"The Hour will not come until there is sinking, transformation, and stoning in my Ummah."],[4947,"\"A generation will come after sixty years who neglect the prayer and follow lusts; they will meet with ruin. Then there will be a generation who recite the Qur'an but it will not pass beyond their collarbones. The Qur'an is recited by three: a believer, a hypocrite, and a transgressor.\""],[4948,"The Kaaba will be destroyed by Dhu al-Suwayqatayn from Abyssinia."],[4949,"It is as if I am looking at him: a black man with bow legs, tearing it down stone by stone."],[4950,"Enjoy this House, for it has been demolished twice and will be raised up the third time."],[4951,"We were sitting with the Prophet ﷺ while revelation was being sent down to him, and he said, \"I will not remain among you long, and you will not remain after me except a little while. You will come to me in groups, destroying one another. Before the Hour there will be a severe death and after it years of earthquakes.\""],[4952,"The Messenger of God ﷺ looked upon us while we were discussing. He said: \"What were you discussing?\" We said: We were discussing the Hour. He said: \"It will not come until you see before it ten signs: the Dajjal, the smoke, Jesus son of Mary, Gog and Magog, the beast, the rising of the sun from its west, and three sinkings: a sinking in the east, a sinking in the west, and a sinking in the Arabian Peninsula; and the last of that is a fire that emerges from the depths of Aden, or from Aden, or from Yemen, driving the people to the gathering place.\""],[4953,"'You will make a secure peace with the Byzantines, until you and they together fight an enemy behind them, and you will be victorious and take spoils and return, until you camp in a meadow with mounds. Then a man from the Byzantines will say, \"The cross has prevailed,\" and a man from the Muslims will say, \"Rather, Allah has prevailed.\" Then a Muslim will rush to their cross, which is not far from him, and break it. The Byzantines will rush to the one who broke their cross and strike his neck. The Muslims will rush to their weapons, and they will fight. Allah will honor that group of Muslims with martyrdom. The Byzantines will say to their leader, \"We have spared you the Arabs.\" Then they will gather for the great battle, and they will come to you under eighty banners, under each banner twelve thousand.'"],[4954,"«You will make a secure peace treaty with the Romans, until you and they together raid an enemy behind them, and you will be victorious, safe, and gain spoils, until you camp in a meadow. Then a man from the Romans will say, 'The cross has prevailed,' and a man from the Muslims will say, 'Rather, Allah has prevailed.' They will exchange these words, and their cross will be not far from the Muslims. Then a man from the Muslims will rise to it and smash it. They will rise against the one who broke their cross and strike his neck. The Muslims will rise to their weapons and they will fight, and Allah will honor that band with martyrdom. Then they will come to their king and say, 'We have spared you [the burden of] the Arabian Peninsula.' Then they will gather for the great battle and come under eighty banners, under each banner twelve thousand [men].\""],[4955,"\"There was no prophet but warned his nation against the Dajjal, and I warn you against him. He will surely appear among you.\""],[4956,"I was walking with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and he passed by Ibn Sayyad. The Prophet ﷺ said, \"I have hidden something for you.\" Ibn Sayyad said, \"It is al-dukh.\" The Prophet ﷺ said, \"Be off! You will never exceed your measure.\" Umar ؓ said, \"Let me strike his neck.\" The Prophet said, \"No, if he is the one you fear, you will never be able to kill him.\""],[4957,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ performed tawaf around the House on his mount, touching the Corner with a staff."],[4958,"The Prophet of Allah ﷺ met Ibn Sayyad, and with him were Abu Bakr and Umar, while Ibn Sayyad was with some boys. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to him, \"Do you testify that I am the Messenger of Allah?\" He said, \"Do you testify that I am the Messenger of Allah?\" The Prophet of Allah said, \"I believe in Allah and His Messenger.\" Then the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, \"What do you see?\" He said, \"I see a throne on the water.\" He ﷺ said, \"You see the throne of Iblis on the sea.\" Then he said, \"Look, what do you see?\" He said, \"I see truthful ones and liars.\" The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, \"He is confused about himself.\" Then he called him."],[4959,"A wind blew while we were with 'Abd Allah, and Ibn Mas'ud became angry until we recognized anger in his face. He said, \"Woe to you! The Hour will not come until no inheritance is divided and no booty is rejoiced over.\" Then he struck his hand toward Syria and said, \"An enemy gathers against the Muslims from here, and they meet, and a death squad is chosen that does not return except victorious. They fight until the sun sets, then these and those withdraw, neither prevailing, and the squad is annihilated. Then the next day another death squad is chosen that does not return except victorious. They fight until the sun sets, then these and those withdraw, neither prevailing, and the squad is annihilated. Then the next day, on the third day, a death squad is chosen that does not return except victorious. They fight until the sun sets, then these and those withdraw, neither prevailing, and the squad is annihilated. Then they meet on the fourth day and fight them and defeat them until blood reaches the horses' chests. They fight until even brothers count themselves against a hundred, and they are killed until not one man of them remains. So what inheritance would be divided after this, and what booty would be rejoiced over? Then they conquer Constantinople. While they are dividing dinars with shields, a greater terror comes to them: the Dajjal has emerged among your families. So they abandon what is in their hands and turn back, and they send a vanguard of horsemen.\" The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, \"They are on that day the best horsemen on earth. I indeed know their names, their fathers' names, their tribes, and the colors of their horses.\""],[4960,"The call to prayer was made with the announcement 'Come together for prayer,' so the people gathered and were alarmed. She said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ ascended the pulpit, praised Allah and lauded Him, and said, \"I have not gathered you for desire or fear, but because of a report that Tamim al-Dari told me. He claimed that he rode the sea with thirty men from Lakhm and Judham. He said: The sea played with us—or perhaps he said: the waves played with us—for a month. Then the ship cast us onto an island in the sea. He said: We went out to it, and a girl met us dragging her hair; we did not know whether she was coming or going. We said, 'What are you?' She said, 'I am the Jassasah.' We said, 'Tell us.' She said, 'Go to the man in the monastery, for he will tell you and ask you.' He said: We entered upon him, and there was a man of such great size as Allah willed, bound with iron chains. We said, 'Who are you?' He said, 'Tell me about what I ask you.' They said, 'Ask us.' He said, 'What happened to the date palms of Baysan? Do they bear fruit?' We said, 'Yes.' He said, 'Soon they will not bear fruit.' Then he said, 'Tell me about the spring of Zughar. Does it have water?' We said, 'Yes.' He said, 'Soon it will have no water.' Then he said, 'Tell me about this man—has he emerged?' They said, 'Yes.' He said, 'He is truthful, so follow him.' We said, 'Who are you?' He said, 'I am the Dajjal.'\" Kahmas said: Ibn Buraydah mentioned something I did not memorize, except that he said, \"The earth will be folded for him, and he will come upon all of them in forty mornings.\""],[4961,"I heard Fatimah bint Qays saying: \"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ ascended the pulpit and praised Allah and glorified Him. Then he said, 'I warn you against the Dajjal (the Antichrist), for no prophet was sent before me who did not warn his nation against him. He is indeed among you, and indeed the sign of a restoration of a red hair, which she (the story-teller) mentioned. They added, 'Tell us'! She replied, 'I am not informing you about anything, neither am I asking you, but go to the monastery, for there is a man who yearns to meet you.' So they went to the monastery and there they found a man chained between two iron columns. The Prophet asked, 'Where are you from and who are you?' They replied, 'We are from the people of the Levant.' He asked, 'Who are you?' They replied, 'We are Arabs.' He asked, 'What are the Arabs doing?' They said, 'They have among them a Prophet in the land of Taimah.' He asked, 'What are the people doing?' They replied, 'Some of them believe him and some of them deny him.' He said, 'If they believe in him and follow him, it is good for them, if they only knew.' Then he asked, 'What are your houses made of?' They replied, 'They are made of hair and wool spun by our women.' He struck his thigh with his hand and said, 'Behold, what a pity! Then he asked, 'What has happened to Tabariyyah?' They replied, 'Its waters flow in all directions and whoever comes to it can take from it.' He struck his thigh with his hand and said, 'Behold, what a pity!' Then he asked, 'What has happened to your spring Zughar?' They replied, 'Its waters flow in all directions and whoever comes to it can take from it.' He struck his thigh with his hand and said, 'Behold, what a pity!' Then he asked, 'What has happened to the date-palm of Baysan?' They replied, 'Its fruit is taken.' He struck his thigh with his hand and said, 'Behold, what a pity! By Him in Whose Hand my soul is, if I have been released from these fetters, I would have destroyed every house of Baysan except the mosques of Makkah and Al-Madinah, as they hinder the Dajjal from entering them until the Day of Resurrection.'\""],[4962,"\"Hasten to do good deeds before six things: the Dajjal, the smoke, the Beast of the Earth, the rising of the sun from its west, the general affair, and the private affair of one of you.\""],[4963,"While the Messenger of Allah ﷺ was in an upper room and we were below it, the Messenger of Allah ﷺ looked down upon us and said, \"What are you discussing?\" We said, \"We are mentioning the Hour.\" He said, \"It will not come until there are ten signs before it: the rising of the sun from its west, the Dajjal, the smoke, 'Isa son of Maryam, the Beast, the emergence of Ya'juj and Ma'juj, a sinking in the east, a sinking in the west, a sinking in the Arabian Peninsula, and a fire that emerges from such-and-such a place.\" — I think he said — \"It will rest with them where they rest and descend with them where they descend.\""],[4964,"\"The Dajjal will emerge from here,\" and he pointed toward the east."],[4965,"Ibn 'Umar saw Ibn Sayyad in one of the streets of Madinah, so Ibn 'Umar cursed him and reviled him. Then he (Ibn Sayyad) swelled until he blocked the road. Ibn 'Umar struck him with a staff, and he subsided. Then he swelled again until he blocked the road. Ibn 'Umar struck him with a staff he had until he broke it on him. Hafsah said to him, \"What is between you and him? Why are you so persistent with him? Have you not heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say, 'The Dajjal will only emerge from a fit of anger that he gets'?\""],[4967,"\"The Dajjal's eye is green like glass. Seek refuge in Allah from the punishment of the grave.\""],[4968,"He mentioned the Dajjal and said, \"One-eyed, white-skinned, bright, as if his head is a snake. He is the most similar of people to 'Abd al-'Uzza b. Qatan. If the perished perish, then your Lord is not one-eyed.\""],[4969,"\"People will surely flee from the Dajjal into the mountains.\" Umm Sharik said, \"O Messenger of Allah, where will the Arabs be on that day?\" He said, \"They will be few.\""],[4970,"\"Seventy thousand Jews of Isfahan wearing tayalisah will follow the Dajjal.\""],[4971,"“Madinah: the Dajjal will come to it and find the angels guarding it. So neither the Dajjal nor the plague will enter it, if Allah Almighty wills.”"],[4972,"“The terror of the Masih will not enter Madinah. That day it will have seven gates, with two angels at each gate.”"],[4973,"“There is no town but the Dajjal will tread it, except Makkah and Madinah. There is no pass among their passes but the angels are upon it, standing in rows guarding them. He will alight at the salt marsh, and Madinah will quake with its people three tremors, and every disbeliever and hypocrite will go out to him.”"],[4974,"I know best what the Dajjal (Antichrist) will have with him. He will have with him a sea of water and a river of fire, and what you see as fire will be water and what you sea as water will be fire. If any of you who lives up to that time and desires water, he should drink from what he sees as fire, for he will find it water. Abu Mas’ud al-Badri said: I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say in this way. (Using translation from Abū Dāʾūd 4315)"],[4975,"I said, \"O Messenger of Allah, it has reached me that with the Dajjal there are mountains of bread and rivers of water.\" The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, \"He is more insignificant to Allah than that.\" Al-Mughirah said: I was among the people who asked most about him, and the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to me, \"He is not the one who will harm you.\""],[4976,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ prohibited two sales: mulamasa and munabadha."],[4977,"\"There was no prophet before me but warned his people against the Dajjal, and I warn you against him.\" He described him to us and said, \"Perhaps some of those who saw me or heard my speech will live to see him.\" They said, \"O Messenger of Allah, will our hearts then be like they are today?\" He said, \"Or better.\""],[4978,"“The Jews will fight you, and you will prevail over them, until the stone will say: O Muslim, here is a Jew behind me, so kill him.”"],[4979,"We were with the Prophet ﷺ when he mentioned the Dajjal and said: “The trial of some of you is more fearful to me than the trial of the Dajjal, for there is no trial, small or great, but it will be diminished before the trial of the Dajjal. Whoever is saved from the trial before it will be saved from it. Indeed, no Muslim will be harmed by it. Written between his eyes is ‘disbeliever,’ spelled out: K F R.”"],[4980,"“You will fight the Arabian Peninsula, and Allah will grant you victory over it. Then you will fight Persia, and Allah will grant you victory over it. Then you will fight the Dajjal, and Allah will grant you victory over him.”"],[4981,"“The Masih will come from the direction of the east, and his intention will be Madinah, until he alights near Uhud. Then he will depart toward Syria, and there he will perish.”"],[4982,"“The son of Mary will kill the Dajjal at the gate of Ludd.”"],[4983,"“The Hour will not rise until the Romans alight at al-A'maq or at Dabiq, and an army from the people of Madinah, the best people on earth that day, will go out to them. When they form ranks, the Romans will say: Leave us and those who were captured from us alone so we may fight them. The Muslims will say: No, by Allah, we will not leave you and our brothers. They will fight them, and one third will flee, and Allah will never forgive them. Then one third of them will be killed, and they are the best martyrs in the sight of Allah. And one third will conquer, and they will conquer Constantinople. While they are dividing the spoils, having hung their swords on olive trees, the devil will shout among them: The Masih has taken your place among your families. So they will go out, but it is false. When they come to Syria, he—meaning the Dajjal—will emerge. While they are preparing for battle and straightening the ranks, the prayer will be performed, and Jesus son of Mary will descend. When the enemy of Allah sees him, he will dissolve as salt dissolves. If they left him, he would dissolve until he perishes, but Allah will kill him by his hand, and He will show them his blood on his spear.”"],[4984,"“The son of Mary will certainly descend as a just judge. He will break the cross, kill the pig, and abolish the jizyah. Young she-camels will be left untended and no one will strive after them. Mutual hatred, envy, and enmity will disappear, and he will call people to wealth, but no one will accept it.”"],[4985,"Regarding His saying {And indeed, he is a sign of the Hour}, he said: “The descent of Jesus son of Mary before the Day of Resurrection.”"],[4986,"“By the One in whose hand is my soul, the son of Mary will soon descend among you as a just judge. He will break the cross, kill the pig, abolish the jizyah, and pour out wealth so abundantly that no one will accept it.”"],[4987,"“How will you be when the son of Mary descends among you while your imam is from among you?”"],[4988,"I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: A section of my people will not cease fighting for the Truth and will prevail till the Day of Resurrection. He said: Jesus son of Mary would then descend and their (Muslims') commander would invite him to come and lead them in prayer, but he would say: No, some amongst you are commanders over some (amongst you). This is the honour from Allah for this Ummah. (Using translation from Muslim 156)"],[4989,"“The prophets are brothers from different mothers; their mothers are diverse, and I am the closest of people to Jesus son of Mary. He will descend, so recognize him: he is a man of medium build, inclined to reddishness and whiteness, as if his head is dripping though no moisture touches it. He will break the cross, kill the pig, distribute wealth abundantly, and abolish the jizyah. Allah will destroy in his time all religions except Islam, and Allah will destroy the false messiah, the one-eyed liar. Allah will cast security upon the earth until the lion grazes with camels, the leopard with cattle, and the wolves with sheep; children will play with snakes and none will harm another.”"],[4990,"“Jesus son of Mary will come to a people whom Allah has protected from the Dajjal, and he will wipe their faces and inform them of their ranks in Paradise.”"],[4991,"“Indeed, the one-eyed Dajjal, the Masih of misguidance, will emerge from the direction of the east at a time of disagreement among the people and division. He will traverse whatever Allah wills of the earth in forty days—Allah knows best their length, Allah knows best their length, twice—and Allah will send down Jesus son of Mary, and he will lead them in prayer. When he raises his head from the bowing, he will say: Allah hears the one who praises Him. May Allah kill the Dajjal and grant victory to the believers.”"],[4992,"“The son of Mary will certainly raise his voice with the talbiyah at Fajj al-Rawha’, as a pilgrim for Hajj or ‘Umrah, or he will combine both.”"],[4993,"“The prophets are all brothers from different mothers; their mothers are diverse, but their religion is one. I am the closest of people to Jesus son of Mary, for there is no prophet between me and him. He will descend, and when you see him, recognize him: a man of medium build, inclined to reddishness and whiteness, wearing two garments dyed with wars, as if his head is dripping though no moisture touches it. He will fight the people for the sake of Islam; he will break the cross, kill the pig, abolish the jizyah, and Allah will destroy in his time all religions except Islam. Allah will destroy the false messiah, the Dajjal. Security will prevail on earth until lions graze with camels, leopards with cattle, and wolves with sheep; children will play with snakes and they will not harm them. He will remain on earth for forty years, then he will die and the Muslims will pray over him. May Allah’s blessings be upon him.”"],[4994,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ entered upon me while I was weeping. He said, “What makes you weep?” She said, “O Messenger of Allah, you mentioned the Dajjal.” He said, “Do not weep, for if he emerges while I am alive, I will suffice you against him. If I die, your Lord is not one-eyed. He will emerge with the Jews, and he will travel until he camps near Madinah, which on that day will have seven gates, with two angels on each gate. The wicked people of Madinah will go out to him, and he will proceed until he comes to Ludd. Then Jesus son of Mary will descend and kill him. Then Jesus will remain on earth for forty years, or close to forty years, as a just imam and an equitable judge.”"],[4995,"«The signs will appear one after another, following one another like beads on a string.»"],[4996,"“Gog and Magog: the least that one of them leaves from his loins is a thousand offspring. Behind them are three nations: Minsak, Ta’wil, and Taris, whose number no one knows except Allah.”"],[4997,"«They dig every day until they are about to see the rays of the sun. Then they say, \"We will return to it tomorrow.\" They return to it while it is even harder than it was, until when their time has come and God wants to send them against the people, they say, \"We will return to it tomorrow, God willing.\" Then they return to it as they had left it and dig through it and come out against the people.» The Messenger of God ﷺ said: «Then the people will flee from them to their fortresses.»"],[4998,"«Gog and Magog will be opened and they will come out upon the people, as God said: {They will descend from every height} [21:96]. The Muslims will withdraw from them to their cities and fortresses, gather their livestock to themselves, and drink up the water of the earth, until one of them passes by that river and says, \"There was once water here.\" When no one remains among the people except those in a fortress or a city, one of them will say, \"These are the people of the earth; we have finished with them. The people of heaven remain.\" Then one of them will shake his spear and throw it toward the sky, and it will return to them stained with blood, as a trial and a tribulation. While they are in that state, God will send worms in their necks like the worms of locusts that come out of their necks, and they will become dead, so that no sound is heard from them. Then the Muslims will say, \"Will not a man sell his life for us to see what has happened to this enemy?\" One of them will volunteer for that, expecting to be killed, and he will find them dead, one upon another. He will call out, \"O assembly of Muslims, rejoice, for God has sufficed you against your enemy!\" Then they will come out of their cities and fortresses and let their livestock roam.»"],[4999,"The Prophet ﷺ woke up saying: «There is no god but God. Woe to the Arabs from an evil that has drawn near. Today a breach has been opened in the barrier of Gog and Magog,» and he made a circle with his hand. I said, \"O Messenger of God, will we perish while there are righteous people among us?\" He said: «Yes, when wickedness becomes widespread.»"],[5000,"«This House will surely be performed Hajj and Umrah after the emergence of Gog and Magog.»"],[5001,"Narrated Abu Huraira: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"The Hour will not be established until the sun rises from its place of setting. When it rises and the people see it, all of them will believe. But on that day, faith will not benefit a soul that did not previously believe or earn good in its faith.\""],[5002,"I asked the Messenger of Allah ﷺ about the saying of Allah, Majestic and Exalted: “And the sun runs to its resting place” [Yā Sīn 36:38]. He said, “Its resting place is beneath the Throne.”"],[5003,"“Do you know where the sun goes?” They said, “Allah and His Messenger know best.”"],[5004,"«There will always be a group among my nation who are aided, not harmed by those who abandon them, until the Hour comes.»"],[5005,"«There will always be a group upon this matter, upon the truth, not harmed by the opposition of those who oppose them, until the command of God comes to them while they are upon that.»"],[5006,"He was with Maslama b. Mukhallad, and with him was ʿAbd Allah b. ʿAmr. ʿAbd Allah said, \"The Hour will not come except upon the worst of creation, who are worse than the people of the Jahiliyyah. They will not call upon God for anything but that He will refuse it to them.\" While they were in that state, ʿUqba b. ʿAmir came, and Maslama said to him, \"O ʿUqba, listen to what ʿAbd Allah says.\" ʿUqba said, \"He is more knowledgeable. As for me, I heard the Messenger of God ﷺ say: 'There will always be a group from my nation fighting for the command of God, overpowering their enemy, not harmed by those who oppose them, until the Hour comes to them while they are upon that.'\" ʿAbd Allah said, \"Then God will send a wind whose scent is the scent of musk and whose touch is the touch of silk. It will not leave any soul with a grain's weight of faith in his heart but that it will take it. Then the worst of people will remain, and upon them the Hour will be established.\""],[5007,"«This religion will always be fought for by a group of Muslims until the Hour comes.»"],[5008,"\"This authority will remain with Quraysh as long as two people remain among mankind.\""],[5009,"“Indeed I have a right over Quraysh, and indeed Quraysh has a right over you: as long as they judge and are just, and are entrusted and fulfill, and mercy is sought from them and they show mercy. Whoever of them does not do that, upon him is the curse of Allah.”"],[5010,"Two statements I heard, and I would not love to have the world and all it contains for either one of them. One was from the Negus and the other from the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. As for the one I heard from the Negus: we were with him when a son of his came from the scribes and showed him his tablet. I understood some of their words, and he came to a verse, and I laughed. He said, “What made you laugh? For by the One in whose hand is my soul, it was sent down from the One of the Throne: that Jesus son of Mary said, ‘The curse occurs in the earth when the rule of boys occurs.’” And what I heard from the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, I heard him say, “Listen to Quraysh and leave their deeds.”"],[5011,"«The Hour will not come until a fire emerges that illuminates the necks of camels in Busra.»"],[5012,"«A fire is about to emerge from a thicket, moving like slow-moving camels. It will travel by day and hide by night. It will be said, 'The fire has set out; O people, set out.' The fire will say, 'O people, take a midday rest.' It will be said, 'The fire has departed; O people, depart.' Whoever it catches it will consume.»"],[5013,"We came with the Messenger of God ﷺ and stopped at Dhu al-Hulayfa. Some men hurried to Madinah and spent the night there. When morning came, he asked about them and was told that they had hurried to Madinah. He said: «They hurried to Madinah and the women? Indeed, they will leave it in the best state it ever was.» And he said something good about those who stayed behind with him. Then he said: «Would that I knew when a fire will emerge from Yemen, from Mount Warraq, illuminating the necks of camels as it descends upon Busra like the light of day.»"],[5014,"\"The Hour will not come until a red wind is sent from the direction of Yemen, and God will with it take every soul that believes in God and the Last Day. People will not deny it due to the few who die from it: an old man died among Banu So-and-so, and an old woman died among Banu So-and-so. The Book of God will be taken by night and raised to heaven, so that no verse of it remains on earth. The earth will vomit up the pieces of its liver of gold and silver, and after that day no benefit will be gained from them. A man will pass by them and strike them with his foot and say: 'Over this those before us used to fight, and today it has become of no use.'\""],[5015,"\"The Hour will not come until a single prostration is better than the world and all that is in it.\""],[5018,"\"The Hour will not come until time contracts, so that a year will be like a month, a month like a week, a week like a day, a day like an hour, and an hour like the burning of a palm leaf or a reed.\""],[5020,"\"You will be selected as dates are selected from their dregs.\""],[5021,"\"The righteous will be taken in succession, and the righteous will perish one after another until only the likes of the dregs of dates and barley remain; God will not care about them.\""],[5022,"\"The Hour will surely come while two men have a garment between them, neither folding it nor completing its sale. The Hour will surely come when a man has turned away with the milk of his milch-camel and has not yet tasted it. The Hour will surely come while a man is plastering his cistern and has not yet watered from it. The Hour will surely come when a man has raised a morsel to his mouth and has not yet eaten it.\""],[5023,"\"The Hour will come upon two men between whom is a garment that they are bargaining over; neither of them spreads it out nor folds it. The Hour will come upon a man who has a morsel in his mouth; he neither swallows it nor spits it out.\""],[5024,"«Frequently remember the destroyer of pleasures.»"],[5025,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to frequently say: «Frequently remember the destroyer of pleasures.»"],[5026,"\"Whoever loves to meet Allah, Allah loves to meet him; and whoever does not love to meet Allah, Allah does not love to meet him.\""],[5027,"\"Whoever loves to meet Allah, Allah loves to meet him; and whoever hates to meet Allah, Allah hates to meet him.\" 'A'ishah said, \"We hate death, so is that hating to meet Allah?\" The Prophet ﷺ said, \"No, but when the believer is at the point of death and is given glad tidings of what lies ahead, he loves to meet Allah and Allah loves to meet him. And when the disbeliever is at the point of death and is given tidings of what lies ahead, he hates to meet Allah and Allah hates to meet him.\""],[5028,"\"Whoever loves to meet Allah, Allah loves to meet him; and whoever hates to meet Allah, Allah hates to meet him.\" She said: I said, \"O Prophet of Allah, is it hatred of death? For all of us hate death.\" He said, \"It is not that, but when the believer is given glad tidings of Allah's mercy, pleasure, and Paradise, he loves to meet Allah and Allah loves to meet him. And when the disbeliever is given tidings of Allah's punishment and wrath, he hates to meet Allah and Allah hates to meet him.\""],[5029,"“The lifespans of my nation are between sixty and seventy, and few of them exceed that.”"],[5030,"We used to be the ones who would inform the Messenger of Allah ﷺ when a deceased person was brought before him. He would then come and seek forgiveness for the deceased until they were buried. Once the burial was complete, the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and those with him would depart. Sometimes, the delay in the departure of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ was prolonged. When we became concerned about the burden of waiting, some people said to each other, \"By Allah, if we do not inform the Messenger of Allah ﷺ about someone's death until after the burial, it will not cause any hardship or inconvenience for him.\" They then proceeded to act upon this and began to inform him only after the burial had taken place. Thereafter, he would come, offer the prayer for the deceased, and seek forgiveness for them. Sometimes he would depart immediately afterwards, and sometimes he would stay until the deceased was buried.\" The narrator then added, \"We continued in this manner for some time. Then we said, 'By Allah, if we do not inform the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and carry our deceased to him until he offers the funeral prayer at their graveside, it would be even more compassionate and easier for the Messenger of Allah ﷺ .' We then began to do this. And this practice has continued to this day.\""],[5031,"\"When death comes to a believer, the angels of mercy attend him. When his soul is taken, it is placed in white silk and taken up to the gate of heaven. They say, 'We have never found a sweeter scent than this.' It is said, 'Leave him to rest, for he was in distress.' Then he is asked, 'What did so-and-so do? What did so-and-so do? What did so-and-so do?'\""],[5032,"“When the believer’s soul is taken, the angels of mercy come to it with white silk and say, ‘Come out to the mercy of Allah.’ It comes out with a scent like the finest musk, so that they pass it one to another, smelling it, until they bring it to the gate of heaven. They say, ‘What is this sweet fragrance that has come from the earth?’ And they do not come to any heaven but they say the like of that, until they bring it to the souls of the believers. They rejoice over it more than a family rejoices over its absent member when he returns. They say, ‘What did so-and-so do?’ They say, ‘Leave him until he rests, for he was in the distress of the world.’ He says, ‘Has he died? Did he not die?’ They say, ‘He was taken to his mother, the Pit (al-Hāwiya).’ As for the disbeliever, the angels of punishment come to him with coarse cloth and say, ‘Come out to the wrath of Allah.’ It comes out with the foulest stench of a corpse, and they take it to the gate of the earth.”"],[5033,"He prohibited mulamasa and munabadha."],[5034,"They passed by the Messenger of Allah ﷺ with a funeral and they spoke ill of it, so he ﷺ said, “It is affirmed.” They passed by another and they spoke well of it, so he ﷺ said, “It is affirmed.” ʿUmar said, “O Messenger of Allah, what is affirmed?” He said, “You spoke ill of that one, so the Fire is affirmed; you spoke well of this one, so Paradise is affirmed. You are Allah’s witnesses on the earth.”"],[5035,"Three things follow the deceased: two return, and one remains with him. His family, his wealth, and his deeds follow him; his family and wealth return, and his deeds remain."],[5036,"The son of Adam has three companions. One companion says: 'What you spent is yours, and what you kept is not yours' – that is his wealth. Another companion says: 'I am with you; but when you reach the king's door, I will leave you and return' – that is his family and relatives. The third companion says: 'I am with you wherever you enter and wherever you leave' – that is his deeds. He will say: 'You were the least of the three in my eyes.'"],[5037,"«When the funeral is placed and the men carry it on their shoulders, if it was righteous it says: 'Send me forward,' and if it was not righteous it says: 'Woe to it! Where are they taking it?' Its voice is heard by everything except the human, and if the human heard it, he would faint.»"],[5038,"Indeed the deceased hears the pattering of their sandals when they turn away departing."],[5039,"He forbade muzabana, and muzabana is selling dates for dates by measure, and selling vines for raisins by measure.\""],[5040,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ mentioned the two testers of the grave, and 'Umar b. al-Khattab said: 'Will our minds be restored to us, O Messenger of Allah?' He said: 'Yes, as you are today.' He said: 'Then he will be silenced.'"],[5041,"When the deceased enters the grave, the sun is shown to him at its setting, and he says: 'Leave me so that I may pray.'"],[5042,"“When the servant is placed in his grave and his companions turn away from him—so much so that he hears the knocking of their sandals—two angels come to him, make him sit up, and say: ‘What did you use to say about this man, about Muhammad?’ As for the believer, he says: ‘I bear witness that he is the servant of Allah and His Messenger.’ It is then said to him: ‘Look at your seat in the Fire; Allah has replaced it for you with a seat in Paradise.’” Qatadah said: “It was mentioned to us that his grave is widened for him by seventy cubits and filled with greenery until the day they are resurrected.” Then he returned to the hadith of Anas b. Malik; he said: “As for the disbeliever and the hypocrite, it is said to him: ‘What did you use to say about this man?’ He says: ‘I do not know; I used to say what the people say.’ It is said: ‘You neither knew nor followed.’ Then he is struck with an iron hammer with a blow between his ears, and he cries out with a cry heard by whoever is upon the earth except the two heavy ones (jinn and humans).”"],[5043,"When one of you—or the person—is buried, two black, blue-eyed angels come to him. One is called Munkar and the other Nakir. They say to him: 'What did you say about this man Muhammad?' He will say what he used to say. If he was a believer, he says: 'He is the servant of Allah and His Messenger. I bear witness that there is no god but Allah and that Muhammad is His servant and Messenger.' They say: 'We knew that you would say that.' Then his grave is widened for him seventy cubits by seventy cubits, and it is illuminated for him. Then it is said to him: 'Sleep.' He sleeps like the sleep of a bride whom no one wakes except the dearest of her family, until Allah raises him from that resting place. If he was a hypocrite, he says: 'I do not know. I heard people saying something, and I said it.' They say: 'We knew that you would say that.' Then it is said to the earth: 'Close in on him,' and it closes in on him until his ribs interlace. He remains punished until Allah raises him from that resting place."],[5044,"Regarding His saying, Mighty and Exalted, {then for him is a straitened livelihood}, he said: “The torment of the grave.”"],[5045,"The Prophet ﷺ heard a sound when the sun had set and said: “These are the voices of the Jews being tormented in their graves.”"],[5046,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ entered upon me while I was in one of the walled gardens of Banu al-Najjar, in which were graves of theirs, and he was saying: “Seek refuge in Allah from the torment of the grave.” I said: O Messenger of Allah, is there a torment for the grave? He said: “Yes, and they are being tormented in their graves; the beasts hear it.”"],[5047,"He entered a walled garden of Banu al-Najjar and heard a sound from a grave. He said: “When was the occupant of this grave buried?” They said: In the Jahiliyyah. He was pleased with that and said: “Were it not that you would not bury one another, I would have called upon Allah to make you hear the torment of the grave.”"],[5048,"The Prophet ﷺ passed by two graves and said: “These two are being tormented for something not major: tale-bearing and urine.” Then he called for a palm branch, split it, and placed it on them, and said: “Perhaps it will lighten their torment as long as they do not dry out.”"],[5049,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, \"Ninety-nine dragons will be set upon the disbeliever in his grave, tearing and biting him until the Day of Judgment. If one dragon were to breathe in the earth, it would not grow anything green.\""],[5050,"“The believer in his grave is in a green garden, his grave is widened for him to seventy cubits, and it is illuminated for him like the moon on the night of the full moon. Do you know about what this verse was revealed: {then for him is a straitened livelihood, and We will raise him on the Day of Resurrection blind}? Do you know what the straitened livelihood is?” They said: Allah and His Messenger know best. He said: “The torment of the disbeliever in his grave. By the One in whose hand is my soul, ninety-nine dragons are set upon him. Do you know what a dragon is? Seventy serpents, for each serpent seven heads, stinging him and scratching him until the Day of Resurrection.”"],[5051,"He forbade muzabana, and muzabana is selling dates for dates by measure, and selling vines for raisins by measure.\""],[5052,"«Every son of Adam is eaten by the earth except the coccyx; from it he was created, and in it he will be recomposed.»"],[5053,"She heard Aishah when it was mentioned to her that Abd Allah says that the deceased is tormented by the weeping of the living. Aishah said: May Allah forgive Abu Abd al-Rahman. Indeed he did not lie, but he forgot or erred. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ only passed by a Jewish woman who was being wept over and said: “They are weeping over her, and she is being tormented in her grave.”"],[5054,"When the deceased is placed in his grave, he hears the sound of their sandals as they turn away. If he is a believer, prayer is at his head, fasting is on his right, zakah is on his left, and deeds of goodness—charity, maintaining ties, kindness, and benevolence to people—are at his feet. He is approached from his head, and prayer says: 'There is no entrance from my side.' Then he is approached from his right, and fasting says: 'There is no entrance from my side.' Then from his left, and zakah says: 'There is no entrance from my side.' Then from his feet, and the deeds of goodness—charity, maintaining ties, kindness, and benevolence to people—say: 'There is no entrance from my side.' Then it is said to him: 'Sit up,' and he sits up. The sun is shown to him as if near setting. It is said to him: 'What do you say about this man who was among you? What do you say about him, and what testimony do you give against him?' He says: 'Leave me so that I may pray.' They say: 'You will do so.'"],[5055,"When a servant is placed on his bier, he says: 'Hasten me forward, hasten me forward.' And when a servant is placed on his bier, he says: 'Woe to me! Where are you taking me?' He means the Muslim and the disbeliever."],[5056,"A man from the Ansar heard a man from the Jews saying, \"By the One who chose Moses over all mankind.\" He raised his hand and slapped him. That was mentioned to the Prophet ﷺ, and the Ansari said, \"O Messenger of God, he said, 'By the One who chose Moses over all mankind,' while you are our Prophet.\" He ﷺ said, \"The trumpet will be blown, and whoever is in the heavens and whoever is on earth will be struck down, except whom God wills. Then it will be blown again, and I will be the first to raise my head. Then Moses will be holding onto one of the legs of the Throne. I do not know whether he was among those whom God exempted or whether he raised his head before me. Whoever says, 'I am better than Jonah son of Matta' has lied.\""],[5057,"A Bedouin asked the Prophet ﷺ, \"What is the trumpet?\" He said, \"A horn into which it is blown.\""],[5058,"\"People will be gathered upon a white, dusty earth, like a pure-white flatbread, with no landmark for anyone on it.\""],[5059,"\"People will be gathered barefoot, naked, and uncircumcised.\""],[5061,"That a man said, \"O Messenger of Allah, how will the disbeliever be gathered on his face?\" He said, \"Indeed, the One who made him walk on his two legs is able to make him walk on his face.\""],[5062,"\"Indeed, you will be gathered barefoot, naked, and uncircumcised, and the first of creatures to be clothed on the Day of Resurrection will be Ibrahim.\""],[5063,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ stood among us to deliver an admonition and said: \"O people, you will be gathered barefoot, naked, and uncircumcised. {As We began the first creation, We will repeat it, a promise upon Us. Indeed, We will do it.} [21:104] The first of creation to be clothed will be Abraham. Some men from my nation will be brought and taken to the left. I will say: 'O Lord, my companions, my companions!' It will be said: 'You do not know what they did after you.' Then I will say as the righteous servant said: {And I was a witness over them as long as I was among them, but when You took me up, You were the observer over them, and You are witness to all things.} [5:117] until His saying {the Mighty, the Wise} [5:118]. It will be said: 'They kept turning back on their heels.'\""],[5064,"«Every servant will be resurrected upon what he died: the believer upon his faith and the hypocrite upon his hypocrisy.»"],[5065,"\"On the Day when mankind will stand before the Lord of the worlds\" in a day whose measure is fifty thousand years, until a man will be immersed in his sweat up to the middle of his ears."],[5066,"He heard Uqbah ibn 'Amir saying, \"I saw the Messenger of Allah ﷺ saying, 'The sun comes close to the earth and people sweat. Among them are those whose sweat reaches their ankles, and among them are those whose sweat reaches halfway up their legs, and among them are those whose sweat reaches their knees, and among them are those whose sweat reaches their waists, and among them are those whose sweat reaches their necks, and among them are those whose sweat covers their entire body, and he gestured with his hand covering his mouth. He said, 'I saw the Messenger of Allah ﷺ gesturing in this way, and among them are those whose sweat is absorbed by their clothes,' and he struck his hand with a gesture.\""],[5067,"\"When the Day of Resurrection comes, the sun will be brought near to the servants until it is the distance of a mile or two miles.\" Sulaym said: I do not know which of the two miles he meant: the distance of the earth or the mile used for applying kohl to the eye? He said: \"The sun will melt them, and they will be in sweat according to the measure of their deeds. Among them is one whom it will reach to his heels, among them is one whom it will reach to his knees, among them is one whom it will reach to his waist, and among them is one whom it will bridle with a bridle.\" He said: I saw the Messenger of Allah ﷺ gesturing with his hand toward his mouth, saying, \"It will bridle them with a bridle.\""],[5068,"\"On the Day when mankind will stand before the Lord of the worlds\" until one of them will stand in his sweat up to the middle of his ears."],[5069,"Mankind will stand before the Lord of the worlds for the length of half a day of fifty thousand years; He will make that light upon the believers like the sinking of the sun until it sets."],[5070,"The Prophet ﷺ said, \"Indeed, on the Day of Judgment, the disbeliever will be restrained by sweat, and he will say, 'Let me breathe even if it is towards the Fire.'\""],[5071,"\"People will be gathered in three groups: hopeful and fearful; two on a camel, three on a camel, four on a camel, and ten on a camel. The rest of them will be gathered by the Fire which will rest with them wherever they rest at midday, spend the night with them wherever they spend the night, be with them in the morning wherever they are in the morning, and be with them in the evening wherever they are in the evening.\""],[5073,"About His saying {The Day We will call every people with their leader} [17:71], he said: \"One of them will be called and given his record in his right hand. His body will be extended sixty cubits, his face whitened, and a crown of shining pearls placed on his head.\" He said: \"He goes to his companions, who see him from afar and say: 'O Allah, bless us in this one,' until he reaches them and says: 'Rejoice, for each man among you will have the like of this.' As for the disbeliever, he will be given his record in his left hand, his face blackened, his body increased sixty cubits in the form of Adam, and he will wear a crown of fire. His companions see him and say: 'O Allah, disgrace him.' Then he says: 'May Allah distance you. Each one of you will have the like of this.'\""],[5074,"\"When Allah gathers the first and the last on a day about which there is no doubt, a caller will call out: Whoever associated someone in an action he did for Allah, let him seek his reward from other than Allah, for Allah is the most self-sufficient of partners from association.\""],[5075,"“People will be raised on the Day of Resurrection from their graves with their mouths blazing with fire.” It was said, “Who are they, O Messenger of Allah?” He said, “Have you not seen that Allah says: {Indeed, those who devour the property of orphans unjustly only consume fire into their bellies} (Qur'an 4:10) to the end of the verse.”"],[5076,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ recited this verse: {That Day it will declare its information} [99:4]. He said: \"Do you know what its information is?\" They said: \"Allah and His Messenger know best.\" He said: \"Its information is that it will testify about every male and female servant regarding what he did on its surface, saying: 'He did such and such on such and such a day.' That is its information.\""],[5077,"\"A banner will be set up for every treacherous person on the Day of Resurrection. It will be said: This is the treachery of so-and-so.\""],[5078,"\"Indeed the treacherous person will have a banner set up for him on the Day of Resurrection, and it will be said: Lo! This is the treachery of so-and-so.\""],[5079,"For the disbeliever on the Day of Resurrection will be set up a period of fifty thousand years. The disbeliever will see Hell and think it will fall upon him from a distance of forty years' travel.\""],[5080,"I heard a man say to Abdullah b. Amr: \"You claim that the Hour will come at such and such a time.\" He said: \"I had determined not to tell you anything. I only said that you will soon see a great event.\" Then Abdullah b. Amr said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"The Dajjal will appear among my nation and remain for forty—I do not know whether forty days, forty years, forty nights, or forty months. Allah will send Jesus son of Mary, who resembles Urwa b. Mas'ud al-Thaqafi. He will seek him and destroy him. Then people will remain for seven years with no enmity between two. Then Allah will send a wind from the direction of Syria that will take the soul of anyone with a mustard seed's weight of faith, even if one of you were inside a mountain, it would enter upon him.\" I heard it from the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. \"The worst of people will remain, in the lightness of birds and the minds of wild beasts. They will not recognize good or deny evil. Satan will appear to them and command them to worship idols, and they will worship them. In that time their provision will be abundant and their life pleasant. Then the trumpet will be blown. No one will hear it except he will listen. Then no one will remain except he will swoon. Then Allah will send rain like dew or shade—Nu'man was unsure—and the bodies of people will grow with it. Then it will be blown again, and suddenly they will be standing looking. Then it will be said: 'O people, come to your Lord. {And stop them; they are to be questioned.} [37:24]' Then it will be said: 'Bring out the share of the people of the Fire.' It will be said: 'How many?' It will be said: 'From every thousand, nine hundred and ninety-nine.' On that day children will be resurrected with gray hair, and on that day the shin will be uncovered.\""],[5081,"“If the believer knew what punishment is with Allah, no one would hope for Paradise; and if the disbeliever knew what mercy is with Allah, no one would despair of Paradise.”"],[5082,"We were talking with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ one night until we stayed late in conversation. Then we returned to our homes. In the morning we went to him, and the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"Tonight the prophets and their nations and those who followed them from their nations were presented to me. A prophet would pass with three of his nation, a prophet would pass with a group of his nation, a prophet with only one of his nation, and a prophet with no one from his nation, until Moses b. Imran passed in a great crowd of the Children of Israel. When I saw them, they impressed me.\" I said: \"O Lord, who are these?\" He said: \"Your brother Moses b. Imran and those who followed him from the Children of Israel.\" I said: \"O Lord, where is my nation?\" He said: \"Look to your right.\" I looked and saw the hills of Makkah black with the faces of men. I said: \"O Lord, who are these?\" He said: \"These are your nation. Are you pleased?\" I said: \"O Lord, I am pleased.\" He said: \"Look to your left.\" I looked and saw the horizon filled with the faces of men. I said: \"O Lord, who are these?\" He said: \"These are your nation. Are you pleased?\" I said: \"Lord, I am pleased.\" It was said: \"With these are seventy thousand who will enter without reckoning.\" Then Ukkasha b. Mihsan, one of the Banu Asad b. Khuzayma, stood up and said: \"O Messenger of Allah, supplicate Allah to make me one of them.\" He said: \"You are one of them.\" Then another stood up and said: \"O Messenger of Allah, supplicate Allah to make me one of them.\" He said: \"Ukkasha b. Mihsan got there before you.\""],[5084,"I said: “O Messenger of Allah, what do you think about the words of Allah, Mighty and Exalted: ‘On the Day when the earth will be changed to another earth, and the heavens [as well], and they will come forth before Allah, the One, the Irresistible’ (Ibrahim 14:48)? Where will the people be on that Day?” He said: “On the Sirat.”"],[5085,"She asked him about His saying: {On the Day the earth will be changed to other than the earth, and the heavens [as well], and they will come forth before Allah, the One, the Prevailing} (Quran 14:48). Where will the people be on that day? He said, \"On the bridge (al-sirat).\" She said, \"I said, 'O Messenger of Allah, Ibn Jud'an in the Jahiliyyah used to maintain ties of kinship and feed the poor. Will that benefit him?'\" He said, \"It will not benefit him. He never said even one day: My Lord, forgive me my sin on the Day of Judgement.\""],[5086,"“People will pass over the bridge of Hell, on which there are thorns, hooks, and claws that snatch people to the right and left. On its sides there are angels saying: ‘O Allah, grant safety, grant safety.’ Among the people, some will pass like the wind, some like a racing horse, some will run, some will walk, some will crawl on hands and knees, and some will drag themselves. As for the people of the Fire, those who are its people, they will neither die nor live. As for some people, they will be seized for their sins and errors and burned, becoming charcoal; then permission will be granted for intercession, and they will be taken in groups and cast into a river of the rivers of Paradise, and they will grow as a seed grows in the silt of a flood.” The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Have you not seen the wild rue, a plant that grows in open land? Among the last to be brought out of the Fire will be a man at its edge. He will say: ‘O Lord, turn my face away from it.’ Allah will say: ‘Your covenant and your protection: you will not ask Me for anything else.’” He said: “And on the Sirat there will be three trees. He will say: ‘O Lord, move me to this tree so that I may eat of its fruit and be in its shade.’ Allah will say: ‘Your covenant and your protection: you will not ask Me for anything else.’” He said: “Then he will see another tree better than it and say: ‘O Lord, move me to this one so that I may eat of its fruit and be in its shade.’ Allah will say: ‘Your covenant and your protection: you will not ask Me for anything else.’ Then he will see another better than it and say: ‘O Lord, move me to this one so that I may eat of its fruits and be in its shade.’” He said: “Then he will see the crowds of people and hear their voices and say: ‘O Lord, admit me to Paradise.’” Abu Nadrah said: Abu Sa’id and another man from the Companions of the Prophet ﷺ differed. One of them said: “He will admit him to Paradise and give him the world and the like of it,” and the other said: “He will enter Paradise and be given the world and ten times its like.”"],[5087,"It will be said to the disbeliever on the Day of Resurrection: 'Do you think that if you had the earth's full of gold, would you ransom yourself with it?' He will say: 'Yes.' It will be said: 'You were asked for something easier than that.'\""],[5088,"Whoever is judged will be punished. I said: 'O Messenger of Allah, {As for him who is given his book in his right hand, he will be judged with a lenient judgment}.' He said: 'That is the presentation. There is no one who is judged on the Day of Resurrection except that he will be destroyed.'"],[5089,"\"We were with 'Abdullah bin 'Umar when he was circumambulating the House; a man came up to him and said: 'O Ibn 'Umar, what did you hear the Messenger of Allah say about the Najwa?' He said: 'I heard the Messenger of Allah say: 'On the Day of Resurrection, the believer will be brought close to his Lord until He will cover him with His screen, then He will make him confess his sins. He will ask him: \"Do you confess?\" He will say: \"O Lord, I confess.\" This will continue as long as Allah wills, then He will say: \"I concealed them for you in the world, and I forgive you for them today.\" Then he will be given the scroll of his good deeds, or his record, in his right hand. But as for the disbeliever or the hypocrite, (his sins) will be announced before the witnesses.' \" (One of the narrators) Khalid said: \"At: 'before the witnesses' there is something missing.\" \"These are the ones who lied against their Lord!' No doubt! The curse of Allah is on the wrongdoers.\" (Using translation from Ibn Mājah 183)"],[5090,"I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ saying in a private conversation on the Day of Judgment, \"Indeed, Allah will bring the believer close to Him on the Day of Judgment until He places His shield over him, covering him from the people. Then He will say, 'Do you recognize this sin and that sin?' The believer will say, 'Yes, my Lord.' Then He will say, 'Do you recognize this sin and that sin?' The believer will say, 'Yes, my Lord.' Until when Allah has made him acknowledge his sins and he thinks within himself that he has deserved punishment, Allah will say, 'I concealed them for you from the people, and today I forgive them for you.' He will be given a book of good deeds. But as for the disbelievers and hypocrites, the witnesses will say, 'These are the ones who lied about their Lord. May the curse of Allah be upon the wrongdoers.'\""],[5091,"“A man from my nation will be called before all of creation on the Day of Resurrection, and ninety-nine scrolls will be spread out for him, each one extending as far as the eye can see. Then Allah will say: “Do you deny anything of this?” He will say: “No, O Lord.” He will say: “Have My recording scribes been unfair to you?” Then He will say: “Apart from that, do you have any good deeds?” The man will be terrified and will say: “No.” (Allah) will say: “Indeed, you have good deeds with Us, and you will not be treated unjustly this Day.” Then a card will be brought out on which is written Ash-hadu an la ilaha illallah wa anna Muhammadan ‘abduhu wa rasuluhu (I bear witness that none has the right to be worshipped but Allah, and that Muhammad is His slave and Messenger). He will say: “O Lord, what is this card compared with these scrolls?” He will say: “You will not be treated unjustly.” Then the scrolls will be placed in one side of the Balance and the card in the other. The scrolls will go up (i.e., be light) and the card will go down (i.e., will weigh heavily).” (Using translation from Ibn Mājah 4300)"],[5092,"“I know the last of the people of Paradise to enter Paradise and the last of the people of the Fire to come out of the Fire. A man will be brought and it will be said: ‘Ask him about his minor sins, and leave aside the major ones.’ It will be said to him: ‘You did such-and-such on such-and-such a day, and you did such-and-such on such-and-such a day.’ He will say: ‘O Lord, I did things that I do not see here.’” The narrator said: “I saw the Prophet ﷺ laugh until his molar teeth showed.” He said: “Then it will be said to him: ‘You will have a good deed in place of every evil deed.’”"],[5093,"We were with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ when he laughed and said: \"Do you know what I am laughing at?\" We said: \"Allah and His Messenger know best.\" He said: \"At the servant's conversation with his Lord. He will say: 'O Lord, did You not grant me refuge from injustice?' He will say: 'Yes.' He will say: 'I will not allow a witness against myself except from myself.' Then Allah will say: 'Your own self is sufficient today as a witness against you, and the noble recording angels as witnesses.' His mouth will be sealed, and it will be said to his limbs: 'Speak.' They will speak about his deeds. Then he will be released to speak, and he will say: 'Away with you! I was arguing only on your behalf.'\""],[5094,"Four will argue on the Day of Resurrection: a deaf man, a fool, a senile old man, and a man who died in the interval (between prophets). The deaf man will say: 'O Lord, Islam came but I could not hear anything.' The fool will say: 'Lord, Islam came, and the children were pelting me with dung.' The senile old man will say: 'Lord, Islam came and I had no understanding.' The one who died in the interval will say: 'Lord, no Messenger came to me from You.' Then He will take their covenant to obey Him and send a messenger to them, saying: 'Enter the Fire.' He said: 'By the One in whose hand is my soul, if they entered it, it would be coolness and peace.'\""],[5095,"From the Messenger of Allah, may ﷺ , that he said, \"There was a day whose duration was fifty thousand years.\" It was asked, \"What is the length of this day?\" The Prophet, may ﷺ , replied, \"By the One in whose hand is my life, it will be made easy for the believer until it becomes easier for him than performing an obligatory prayer in this worldly life.\""],[5096,"\"Do you know who the bankrupt is?\" They said, \"The bankrupt among us, O Messenger of Allah, is one who has no dirham and no possessions.\" The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, \"The bankrupt from my nation is one who comes on the Day of Resurrection with his prayer, fasting, and zakah, but he has insulted this one, consumed the wealth of this one, shed the blood of this one, and struck this one. So he will sit and this one will be given from his good deeds and this one from his good deeds. If his good deeds run out before he fulfills what he owes, some of their sins will be taken and cast upon him, and then he will be cast into the Fire.\""],[5097,"Whoever has an injustice against his brother, from his honor or his wealth, let him seek to be absolved today, before the day when there will be neither dinar nor dirham. If he has righteous deeds, an amount equal to his injustice will be taken from them. If he has no good deeds, some of the bad deeds of his companion will be taken and placed upon him."],[5098,"May Allah have mercy on a servant who has an injustice against his brother, in his person or his wealth, which he seeks to make right before the day when his good deeds are taken. If he has no good deeds, the bad deeds of his companion will be taken and placed upon him."],[5099,"«Indeed Allah will question every shepherd about that which He entrusted to him: did he preserve it or neglect it, even to the point that He will question the man about his household.»"],[5100,"“Whoever releases a Muslim from his stumble, Allah will release his stumble on the Day of Resurrection.”"],[5101,"Allah, Mighty and Majestic, will ask the servant on the Day of Resurrection, even to the point that He will say: 'What prevented you when you saw an evil from denouncing it?' If Allah grants a servant his argument, he will say: 'O Lord, I trusted in You and feared the people' or 'I feared the people and trusted in You.'"],[5102,"One of you will surely meet his Lord on the Day of Resurrection, and He will say to him: 'Did I not subjugate for you horses and camels? Did I not leave you to be a leader and to take a fourth? Did I not marry you to so-and-so, whom the suitors had proposed to and I kept them away and married you?'"],[5103,"\"Whoever leaves wealth, it is for his heirs, and whoever leaves debt, it is to me and upon me.\""],[5104,"“There is none among you but Allah will speak to him on the Day of Resurrection, with no interpreter between him and Allah. Then he will look to his right and see nothing but what he sent forth; then he will look to his left and see nothing but what he sent forth; then he will look in front of him and the Fire will face him.” The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “So whoever among you can shield his face from the Fire, even with half a date, let him do so.”"],[5105,"I was with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ when two men came to him, one complaining of poverty and the other of highway robbery. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “As for highway robbery, it will not be long before caravans travel from al-Hirah to Makkah without a guard. As for poverty, the Hour will not come until a man goes out with his charity and finds no one to accept it from him. Then one of you will surely stand before Allah with no barrier between him and Allah and no interpreter to translate for him. Allah will say to him: ‘Did I not give you wealth?’ He will say: ‘Yes.’ Allah will say: ‘Did I not send you a messenger?’ He will say: ‘Yes.’ Then he will look to his right and see nothing but the Fire; then he will look to his left and see nothing but the Fire. So let each of you guard against the Fire, even with half a date; and if he cannot find that, then with a good word.”"],[5106,"One of you will surely meet Allah, Mighty and Majestic, and He will say: 'Did I not make you able to hear and see? Did I not give you wealth and children? So what have you sent forth?' He will look in front, behind, to his right and to his left, but will find nothing. He will only find protection from the Fire with his face, so protect yourselves from the Fire, even with half a date. If you cannot find that, then with a good word."],[5107,"\"The just judge will be called on the Day of Resurrection and will meet such severity of reckoning that he will wish he had never judged between two people in his life.\""],[5108,"\"The first matter to be judged between people on the Day of Resurrection will be bloodshed.\""],[5109,"\"You will be gathered on the Day of Resurrection, and it will be said: Where are the poor of this nation and its destitute? He said: So they will stand, and it will be said to them: What did you do? They will say: Our Lord, You tested us and we were patient, while You gave wealth and authority to others besides us. Then Allah will say: You have spoken the truth. He said: So they will enter Paradise before the people, and the severity of the reckoning will remain upon those of wealth and authority.\" They said: Where are the believers on that day? He said: \"Chairs of light will be placed for them, and the clouds will shade them; that day will be shorter for the believers than an hour of the day.\""],[5110,"The wealth from which its due was not given will come, and the camels will trample their master with their pads, and the cattle and sheep will come and trample their owner with their cloven hooves and gore him with their horns. The treasure will come as a bald-headed snake and will meet its owner, who will flee from it. Then it will confront him and he will flee from it. It will say, 'What is between me and you?' He will say, 'I am your treasure, I am your treasure.' Then his owner will receive it with his hand, and it will swallow his hand."],[5111,"There is no owner of camels who does not do good in them except that they will come on the Day of Resurrection as numerous as they were, and he will be seated for them on a vast flat plain, and they will run over him with their legs and pads. And no owner of cattle except that they will come on the Day of Resurrection as numerous as they were, and he will be seated for them on a vast flat plain, and they will gore him with their horns and trample him with their cloven hooves, with none of them having broken horns or no horns. And no owner of treasure who does not fulfill its due except that his treasure will come on the Day of Resurrection as a bald-headed snake, pursuing him with its mouth open. When it comes to him, he will flee from it, and his Lord will call to him, 'This is your treasure that you hoarded.' When he sees that there is no escape from it, he will put his hand into its mouth, and it will chew it like a stallion."],[5112,"By the One in whose hand is my soul, no man dies and leaves behind camels, cows, or sheep without paying their zakah, except that they will be made to appear for him on the Day of Resurrection as large and fat as they ever were, goring him with their horns and trampling him with their hooves. Every time the last of them passes, the first of them returns, and so on, until Allah judges between mankind."],[5113,"You will surely return the rights to their owners, even to the point that the hornless sheep will be retaliated against by the horned sheep."],[5114,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “I will be your forerunner at the Basin.”"],[5115,"“Indeed, I will be your forerunner at the Basin, and I will vie with you against other nations, so do not fight one another after me.”"],[5116,"“The distance between the two sides of my Pool is like the distance between Sana‘a and al-Madina.”"],[5117,"I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: “I am your forerunner before you. If you do not find me, then I will be at the Pool, [whose distance is] as between Ayla and Makkah. Men and women will come with vessels and water-skins, but they will not taste anything from it.”"],[5118,"A bedouin stood up to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and said: “What is your Pool that you speak about?” He replied: “It is like [the distance] between Sana‘a and Busra. Then Allah will increase me in it with a watering-trough that no human knows from which of its two ends it was created.” He said: Then ʿUmar said, “Allahu Akbar.” Then he ﷺ said: “As for the Pool, the poor among the Emigrants who are killed in the path of Allah and die in the path of Allah will crowd to it. And I hope that Allah will bring me to the watering-trough and I will drink from it.”"],[5119,"“The distance between the two sides of my Pool is like the distance between al-Madina and Sana‘a, or like the distance between al-Madina and ʿAmman.”"],[5120,"“My Pool is a month’s journey [in extent]; its corners are equal; its water is whiter than snow and more fragrant than musk; its vessels are like the stars of the sky. Whoever drinks from it will never thirst afterwards.”"],[5121,"\"Whoever leaves wealth, it is for his heirs, and whoever leaves debt, it is to me and upon me.\""],[5122,"“Therein will be seen pitchers of gold and silver like the number of the stars of the sky, or more.”"],[5123,"The Prophet of Allah ﷺ said: “I shall be at the cistern of my Pool, driving people away from it. I shall strike them with my staff until it splinters.” He said: The Prophet of Allah ﷺ was asked about the width of the Pool, and he said: “Like this station of mine to ʿAmman; between them is a month or about that.” The Messenger of Allah ﷺ was asked about its drink, and he said: “More intensely white than milk and sweeter than honey. Two spouts will gush into it, their supply from Paradise: one of pearl and the other of gold.”"],[5124,"“I shall be at the cistern of my Pool, driving away from it for the people of Yemen, striking with my staff until it splinters.” He was asked about its width, and he said: “From this station of mine to ʿAmman.” He was asked about its drink, and he said: “More intensely white than milk and sweeter than honey. In it are two spouts extended from Paradise: one of gold and the other of silver.”"],[5125,"\"This ummah will certainly crowd around the Basin like camels crowding when they arrive at a watering place after five days.\""],[5126,"Yazid b. al-Akhnas al-Sulami said: “O Messenger of Allah, what is the width of your Pool?” He replied: “Like [the distance] between ʿAdan and ʿAmman. In it are two outlets of gold and silver.” He said: “What is your Pool, O Prophet of Allah?” He said: “More intensely white than milk, sweeter in taste than honey, and more fragrant in scent than musk. Whoever drinks from it will never thirst and his face will never be blackened.”"],[5127,"\"Delay in payment by a rich man is injustice, and if one of you is referred to a wealthy man for payment, let him follow up.\""],[5128,"\"My Basin is farther than the distance from Aylah to 'Adan. By the One in whose hand is my soul, its vessels are more numerous than the stars, and it is whiter than milk and sweeter than honey. By the One in whose hand is my soul, I will drive away men from it as a man drives away strange camels from his basin.\" It was said, \"O Messenger of Allah, will you recognize us?\" He said, \"Yes, you will come to me with radiant faces and limbs from the traces of ablution, which no one else will have.\""],[5129,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ halted with us for a night's rest. Each man of us spread out the forearm of his riding camel [as a pillow]. I woke up during part of the night, and behold, the she-camel of the Prophet ﷺ had no one before it. So I set off seeking the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and behold, Mu'adh b. Jabal and 'Abd Allah b. Qays were standing. He said: I said: Where is the Messenger of Allah? They said: We do not know, except that we heard a sound at the upper part of the valley, and it was like the rumbling of a mill. We waited but a little until the Messenger of Allah ﷺ came to us and said: \"A messenger from my Lord came to me tonight and gave me the choice between half of my community entering Paradise and intercession, and I chose intercession.\" We said: O Messenger of Allah, we adjure you by Allah and by companionship to make us among the people of your intercession. He said: \"You are among the people of my intercession.\" He said: So we went to the people, and behold, they were alarmed and had missed their Prophet ﷺ. The Prophet ﷺ said: \"A messenger came to me tonight and gave me the choice between half of my community entering Paradise and intercession, and I chose intercession.\" They said: O Messenger of Allah, we adjure you by Allah to make us among the people of your intercession. The Messenger of Allah said: \"I call to witness those present that my intercession is for whoever of my community dies not associating anything with Allah.\""],[5130,"\"My intercession is for the people of major sins of my community.\""],[5131,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, \"Every prophet has a supplication that he makes, and I have kept my supplication as an intercession for my nation in the hereafter.\""],[5132,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, \"I have been granted five things that no one before me was given: I was sent to both red and black people, the spoils of war were made lawful for me but not for anyone before me, I was given victory through fear, so that the enemy becomes terrified even from a month's distance, and the earth has been made a pure place of prayer and a means of purification for me. It was said to me, 'Ask and you shall be given.' And I have kept my intercession for my Ummah (nation) on the Day of Judgment, and it is a privilege that will be granted, Allah willing, to those who do not associate anything with Allah.\""],[5133,"I said: O Messenger of Allah, what has your Lord answered you regarding intercession? He said: \"By the One in whose hand is the soul of Muhammad, I thought that you would be the first of my community to ask me about that, because of what I saw of your keenness for knowledge. By the One in whose hand is the soul of Muhammad, their crowding at the gates of Paradise does not concern me more than the completion of my intercession for them. My intercession is for whoever bears witness that there is no god but Allah, sincerely, and that Muhammad is the Messenger of Allah, his tongue confirming his heart and his heart confirming his tongue.\""],[5134,"I sat with a group of people, I being the fourth of them, and one of them said: I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: “Through the intercession of a man from my Ummah, more people will enter Paradise than the tribe of Tamim.” The narrator said: “Someone other than you, O Messenger of Allah?” He said: “Other than me.”"],[5135,"We said, \"O Messenger of Allah, will we see our Lord?\" The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, \"Do you have difficulty in seeing the sun during a clear day?\" We said, \"No.\" He said, \"Do you have difficulty in seeing the moon on a full moon night?\" We said, \"No.\" He said, \"Indeed, you will not have difficulty in seeing your Lord, just as you have no difficulty in seeing the sun and the moon. He will call out in a loud voice, 'Everyone shall follow what they used to worship!' The people of the cross shall go with their cross, and the people of idols shall go with their idols, and the people of every deity shall go with their deity. Those who worshipped Allah alone, both the righteous and the wicked, will remain. Then Hell will be brought forth and presented as if it were a mirage. It will be said to the Jews, 'What were you worshipping?' They will say, 'We used to worship 'Uzair (Ezra), the son of Allah.' It will be said, 'You have lied. Allah did not take a son or companion. What do you want?' They will say, 'We want to drink.' It will be said, 'Drink,' and they will fall into Hell. Then it will be said to the Christians, 'What were you worshipping?' They will say, 'We used to worship the Messiah, the son of Allah.' It will be said, 'You have lied. Allah did not take a son or companion. What do you want?' They will say, 'We want to drink.' It will be said, 'Drink,' and they will fall into Hell. Only those who worshipped Allah alone, whether righteous or wicked, will remain. It will be said to them, 'What is stopping you from joining the people who have"],[5136,"We were sitting with the Prophet ﷺ, and he looked at the moon on the night when it is full, the night of the fourteenth. He said: “You will see your Lord just as you see this, without any doubt in seeing Him. If you are able not to be overcome and miss the prayer before sunrise and the prayer before sunset, then do so.” Then he recited this verse: {And glorify the praise of your Lord before the rising of the sun and before its setting}."],[5137,"We were sitting with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ when he looked at the moon on the night when it is full. He said: “Indeed, you will see your Lord just as you see this, without any doubt in seeing Him. If you are able not to be overcome and miss the prayer before sunrise and before sunset, then do so.” Then he recited: {And glorify the praise of your Lord before the rising of the sun and before its setting}."],[5138,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ came out to us on the night of the full moon and said: “You will see your Lord on the Day of Resurrection just as you see this, without any doubt in seeing Him.”"],[5139,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ recited this verse: {For those who have done good is the best and more}. He said: “When the people of Paradise enter Paradise and the people of the Fire enter the Fire, a caller will call out: ‘O people of Paradise, you have a promise with Allah which He wishes to fulfill for you.’ They will say: ‘What is it? Has He not made our scales heavy, whitened our faces, admitted us to Paradise, and saved us from the Fire?’ He said: ‘Then the veil will be removed, and they will look at Him. By Allah, Allah has not given them anything more beloved to them than looking at Him.’”"],[5140,"He said: \"Do you have any difficulty in seeing the sun on a clear day when the sky is free of clouds and there is no cloud in it?\" They said: No. He said: \"Do you have any difficulty in seeing the moon on the night of the full moon when the sky is clear and free of clouds, with no cloud in it?\" They said: No. He said: \"By Him in Whose hand is my soul, thus you will have no difficulty in seeing your Lord on the Day of Resurrection, just as you have no difficulty in seeing either of them. The servant will meet his Lord on the Day of Resurrection, and Allah, Mighty and Exalted, will say: 'O so-and-so, did I not create you? Did I not make you hearing and seeing? Did I not marry you? Did I not honor you? Did I not subjugate for you horses and camels? Did I not make you a leader and leave you to take the fourth part of the spoils?' He will say: 'Yes, O Lord.' Then He will say: 'Did you think that you would meet Me?' He will say: 'No, O Lord.' Then He will say: 'Today I forget you as you forgot Me.' He said: The other will meet Him, and He will say: 'O so-and-so, did I not create you? Did I not make you hearing and seeing? Did I not marry you? Did I not honor you? Did I not subjugate for you horses and camels? Did I not make you a leader and leave you to take the fourth part of the spoils?' He will say: 'Yes, O Lord.' Then He will say: 'What did you prepare for Me?' He will say: 'I believed in You, Your Book, and Your Messenger, and I affirmed, prayed, and fasted.' Then He will say: 'So here, then.' Then He will say: 'Shall We send against you?' He said: He will think to himself: Who is this who will testify against me? He said: That is the hypocrite with whom Allah is angry; that is to leave him no excuse. His mouth will be sealed, and his thigh will be told: 'Speak,' and his thigh, bones, and sinews will speak about what he used to do. Then a caller will proclaim: 'Let every nation follow what it used to worship.' The worshippers of the cross will follow the cross, the worshippers of fire will follow the fire, the worshippers of idols will follow the idols, the worshippers of Satan will follow Satan, and every tyrant will follow their tyrant to Hell. We, the believers, will remain, and we are the believers. Our Lord, Blessed and Exalted, will come to us while we are standing, and He will say: 'Why are these standing?' We will say: 'We are Allah's believing servants; we believed in Him and did not associate anything with Him. This is our station, and we will not leave until our Lord comes to us, and He is our Lord, and He will make us firm.' He will say: 'Do you recognize Him?' We will say: 'Glory be to Him; if He acknowledges Himself to us, we will recognize Him.'\" Sufyan said: \"And here there is a word I will not say to you.\" He said: \"We will proceed until we come to the bridge, and on it are hooks of fire that snatch people. At that place intercession takes place: O Allah, grant safety, grant safety; O Allah, grant safety, grant safety; O Allah, grant safety, grant safety. When he crosses the bridge, every person who spent a pair of wealth from what he owned in the cause of Allah, every keeper of Paradise will call him: 'O servant of Allah, O Muslim, this is better, come; O servant of Allah, O Muslim, this is better, come; O servant of Allah, O Muslim, this is better, come.'\" Abu Bakr, who was beside the Prophet ﷺ, said: \"That is a servant who will have no loss; he will leave one door and enter from another.\" The Prophet ﷺ said, wiping his shoulders: \"I hope that you will be among them.\""],[5141,"We were talking one night with the Prophet of Allah ﷺ until we talked long into the night, then we returned to our homes. When morning came, we went to the Prophet of Allah ﷺ and he said: “The prophets were presented to me last night with their followers from their communities. A prophet would come with three of his people, a prophet would come with a band of his people, a prophet would come with a small group of his people, and a prophet would come with no one from his people until Musa b. ʿImrān came to me in a large group of the Children of Israel. When I saw them, they impressed me, and I said: O Lord, who are these? He said: This is your brother Musa b. ʿImrān. And there were ridges of Makkah which blocked the faces of men. I said: Lord, who are these? He said: Your community. Then it was said to me: Are you satisfied? I said: My Lord, I am satisfied; my Lord, I am satisfied. Then it was said to me: Indeed with these are seventy thousand who will enter Paradise without reckoning.” Then ʿUkkāshah b. Miḥṣan, the brother of Banū Asad b. Khuzaymah, stood up and said: O Prophet of Allah, pray to your Lord to make me one of them. He said: “O Allah, make him one of them.” Then another man stood up and said: O Prophet of Allah, pray to your Lord to make me one of them."],[5142,"“Allah is with the judge so long as he is not unjust, but if he rules unjustly, He entrusts him to himself.” (Using translation from Ibn Mājah 2312)"],[5143,"That the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, \"I am the first to knock at the gate of Paradise.\""],[5144,"\"People will be resurrected on the Day of Resurrection, and I and my community will be on a hill. My Lord will clothe me with a green garment. I will say what Allah wills me to say. That is the Praised Station.\""],[5145,"\"Every prophet on the Day of Resurrection will have a pulpit of light. I will indeed be upon the longest and brightest of them. A caller will come and call out, 'Where is the unlettered prophet?' The prophets will say, 'All of us are unlettered prophets. To which of us was he sent?' He will return a second time and say, 'Where is the unlettered Arab prophet?' Muhammad will descend until he comes to the gate of Paradise and knocks on it. It will say, 'Who?' He will say, 'Muhammad' or 'Ahmad.' It will be said, 'Has he been sent to?' He will say, 'Yes.' It will be opened for him and he will enter. The Lord will manifest Himself to him, and He has not manifested Himself to any prophet before him. He will fall down prostrating before Allah and praise Him with praises that no one before him has praised Him with, and no one after him will praise Him with. It will be said to him, 'Muhammad, raise your head. Speak and you will be heard. Intercede and your intercession will be accepted. Ask and you will be given.' He will say, 'O Lord, my community, my community.' It will be said, 'Bring out those who had in their heart the weight of a barley grain.' Then he will return a second time and fall down prostrating before Allah and praise Him with praises that no one before him has praised Him with, and no one after him will praise Him with. It will be said to him, 'Muhammad, raise your head. Speak and you will be heard. Intercede and your intercession will be accepted. Ask and you will be given.' It will be said to him, 'Bring out those who had in their heart the weight of a wheat grain.' Then he will return a third time and fall down prostrating before Allah and praise Him with praises that no one before him has praised Him with, and no one after him will praise Him with. It will be said to him, 'Bring out of the Fire those who had in their heart the weight of a mustard seed.' Then he will return and fall down prostrating and praise Him with praises that no one before him has praised Him with, and no one after him will praise Him with. It will be said to him, 'Muhammad, raise your head. Speak and you will be heard. Intercede and your intercession will be accepted. Ask and you will be given.' He will say, 'O Lord, whoever said, \"There is no god but Allah.\"' It will be said to him, 'Muhammad, you are not there. That is for Me, and today I will reward it.'\""],[5146,"\"People will be gathered on the Day of Resurrection, and they will be inspired for that, and they will say: If only we could seek intercession with our Lord to relieve us from our place. He said: So they will come to Adam and say: You are Adam, whom Allah created with His own hand and breathed into you of His spirit, and He commanded the angels and they prostrated to you, so intercede for us with your Lord until He relieves us from this place of ours. He said: He will say: I am not the one for that. Then he will mention his sin that he committed and will feel shy before his Lord because of it. But go to Noah, the first messenger Allah sent. They will come to him, and he will say: I am not the one for that. He will mention his sin that he committed and will feel shy before his Lord because of it. But go to Abraham, whom Allah took as a close friend. He said: They will come to Abraham, and he will say: I am not the one for that. He will mention his sin that he committed and will feel shy before his Lord because of it. But go to Moses, whom Allah spoke to and gave the Torah. He said: They will come to Moses, and he will say: I am not the one for that. He will mention his sin and will feel shy before his Lord because of it. But go to Jesus. He will say: I am not the one for that. But go to Muhammad ﷺ, a servant whose past and future sins Allah has forgiven. He said: So they will come to me, and I will ask permission of my Lord, and He will give me permission. When I see Him, I will fall down prostrating, and He will leave me as long as Allah wills to leave me. Then it will be said: Raise your head, Muhammad, speak and you will be heard, ask and you will be given, intercede and your intercession will be accepted. He said: So I will raise my head and praise my Lord with praises that He will teach me. Then I will intercede, and He will set a limit for me, and I will bring them out of the Fire and admit them into Paradise. Then I will return and prostrate, and He will leave me as long as Allah wills to leave me. Then it will be said: Raise your head, Muhammad, speak and you will be heard, ask and you will be given, intercede and your intercession will be accepted. So I will raise my head and praise my Lord with praises that He will teach me. Then I will intercede, and He will set a limit for me, and I will bring them out of the Fire and admit them into Paradise. Then I will place my head [in prostration], and He will leave me as long as Allah wills to leave me. Then it will be said to me: Raise your head, speak and you will be heard, ask and you will be given, intercede and your intercession will be accepted. So I will raise my head and praise my Lord with praises that He will teach me. Then I will intercede, and He will set a limit for me, and I will bring them out of the Fire and admit them into Paradise.\""],[5147,"I placed before the Messenger of Allah ﷺ a bowl of tharid and meat. He took the foreleg, and it was the part of the sheep he liked most, and he took a bite and said: \"I am the master of mankind on the Day of Resurrection.\" Then he took another bite and said: \"I am the master of mankind on the Day of Resurrection.\" Then he took another bite and said: \"I am the master of mankind on the Day of Resurrection.\" When he saw that his companions were not asking him, he said: \"Will you not say: How?\" They said: How, O Messenger of Allah? He said: \"People will stand before the Lord of the worlds, and the caller will make them hear, and sight will pierce them, and the sun will draw near to their heads, and its heat will intensify upon them, and its nearness to them will become hard for them. So they will set off from the distress and vexation of what they are in, and they will come to Adam and say: O Adam, you are the father of mankind. Allah created you with His own hand and commanded the angels and they prostrated to you, so intercede for us with your Lord. Do you not see what we are in of evil? Adam will say: Indeed my Lord is angry today with an anger the like of which He has never been angry before and will never be angry after. He had commanded me with a command and I disobeyed Him, so I fear that He will cast me into the Fire. Go to someone other than me. Myself, myself.\""],[5148,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, \"Every Prophet has a supplication that he made for his nation, and I have saved my supplication as an intercession for my nation on the Day of Resurrection.\""],[5149,"\"Nuh will be called on the Day of Resurrection and he will say, 'At Your service and at Your command, O Lord.' He will say, 'Did you convey?' He will say, 'Yes, O Lord.' He will say to his community, 'Did he convey to you?' They will say, 'No warner came to us.' It will be said, 'Who will testify for you?' He will say, 'Muhammad ﷺ and his community.'\" He ﷺ said, \"So they will testify that he conveyed, and the Messenger will be a witness over them. That is His saying: 'And thus We have made you a middle community, that you will be witnesses over the people, and the Messenger will be a witness over you.' And the 'middle' means the just.\""],[5150,"That the Messenger of Allah ﷺ recited the words of Allah, Majestic and Exalted, concerning Ibrahim: {Indeed, they have led many people astray. So whoever follows me is of me, and whoever disobeys me—indeed, You are Forgiving and Merciful.} And 'Isa said: {If You punish them, they are Your servants.} Then he raised his hands and said, \"O Allah, my ummah, my ummah,\" and wept. So Allah said, \"O Jibril, go to Muhammad ﷺ—and your Lord knows best—and ask him what makes him weep.\" Jibril came to him and asked him, and he told him what he had said—and Allah knows best. Then Allah said, \"O Jibril, go to Muhammad and say: We will please you concerning your ummah and will not displease you.\""],[5151,"The Prophet ﷺ said one day to his Companions: “Is there anyone who will strive for Paradise? For Paradise has no equal. By the Lord of the Ka’bah, it is a shining light, a swaying sweet basil, a lofty palace, a flowing river, abundant ripe fruit, a beautiful fair wife, and many fine garments, in an eternal abode, in joy and radiance, in a high, secure, and splendid home.” They said: “We are the ones who will strive for it, O Messenger of Allah.” He said: “Say: ‘If Allah wills.’” Then he mentioned jihad and urged them to it."],[5152,"While he was one day in the treasury, he said: \"The Prophet of Allah ﷺ came out to us one day from a leather tent of his and said, 'Would you not be pleased to be a quarter of the people of Paradise?' They said, 'Yes.' He said, 'And a third of the people of Paradise?' They said, 'Yes.' He said, 'By the One in whose hand is my soul, I hope that you will be half of the people of Paradise. The likeness of the Muslims among the disbelievers is that of a white cow with a single black hair, or a black cow with a single white hair.'\""],[5153,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ addressed us, leaning his back against a leather tent, then said: \"Now then, would you be pleased to be a quarter of the people of Paradise?\" We said: 'Yes, O Messenger of Allah.' He said: \"By Him in Whose hand is my soul, I hope that you will be half of the people of Paradise. Indeed, none will enter Paradise except every Muslim soul. And the likeness of the Muslims on the Day of Resurrection in relation to the disbelievers in number is like a white hair on a black ox or a black hair on a white ox.\""],[5154,"On the Day of Resurrection, a man will surely take his father by the hand and want to enter him into Paradise, but it will be called out: ‘Paradise is not entered by a polytheist. Allah has forbidden Paradise to every polytheist.’ He will say: ‘O Lord, O Lord, my father!’ He said: Then he will be transformed into an ugly form and a foul smell, and he will leave him. Abu Said said: The companions of Muhammad ﷺ thought that he was Ibrahim, and the Messenger of Allah ﷺ did not add anything further to that."],[5155,"“The people of Paradise are one hundred twenty rows; this nation is eighty rows of them.” *"],[5156,"“The people of Paradise are one hundred twenty rows: eighty from this nation and forty from the rest of the nations.”"],[5157,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, \"Indeed, Allah has promised me that He will admit seventy thousand from my Ummah into Paradise without any reckoning.\" Yazid bin Al-Akhnas Al-Sulami said, \"By Allah, those are not but a small number within your Ummah, O Messenger of Allah, like the golden horseflies among other flies.\" The Messenger of Allah ﷺ replied, \"Verily, my Lord has promised me seventy thousand with each thousand being seventy thousand more, and He increased me with those who are like mountaintops.\""],[5158,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, \"Indeed, my Lord has promised me that He will admit seventy thousand members of my Ummah into Paradise without reckoning. Then, for every thousand, He will follow them with another seventy thousand, and He will clench His fist three times.\" Umar raised his voice and said, \"Indeed, the first seventy thousand will be interceded for by Allah on behalf of their fathers, mothers, and tribes, and I hope that my Ummah will be the last of those who clench their fists.\""],[5159,"“Whoever kills a person under a covenant without right will not smell the fragrance of Paradise, and the fragrance of Paradise can be found from a distance of a hundred years’ journey.”"],[5160,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Whoever kills a person under a covenant during his treaty will not smell the fragrance of Paradise, and its fragrance can be found from a distance of five hundred years’ journey.”"],[5161,"Paradise and the Fire boasted. The Fire said: 'The tyrants, kings, and nobles will enter me.' Paradise said: 'The poor and the needy will enter me.' Allah, Mighty and Exalted, said to the Fire: 'You are My punishment; with you I afflict whomever I will.' He said to Paradise: 'You are My mercy; you encompass everything, and for each of you there will be its fill.'\""],[5162,"I looked into the Fire, and I saw that most of its inhabitants were women. And I looked into Paradise, and I saw that most of its inhabitants were the poor.\""],[5163,"I stood at the gate of Paradise, and most of those who entered it were the poor, while people of good fortune were held back, and the people of the Fire had been ordered to the Fire. I looked at the Fire, and most of those who entered it were women."],[5164,"Indeed, the fewest inhabitants of Paradise will be women.\""],[5165,"The people of Paradise are three: a just, successful ruler; a merciful man with a tender heart toward every relative and Muslim; and a poor, chaste, charitable man.\""],[5166,"When God created Paradise, He said, 'O Gabriel, go and look at it.' He went and looked, then said, 'O Lord, by Your might, no one who hears of it will fail to enter it.' So He surrounded it with hardships. Then He said, 'Go and look at it.' He went and looked at it, then said, 'O Lord, I fear that no one will enter it.' When God created the Fire, He said, 'O Gabriel, go and look at it.' He went and looked at it, then said, 'O Lord, by Your might, no one who hears of it will enter it.' So He surrounded it with desires. Then He said, 'Go and look at it.' He went and looked at it, then said, 'O Lord, by Your might, I fear that no one will remain without entering it.'"],[5167,"\"Whoever spends a pair in the path of Allah will be called in Paradise: 'O servant of Allah, this is good.' So whoever was among the people of prayer will be called from the gate of prayer; whoever was among the people of jihad will be called from the gate of jihad; whoever was among the people of charity will be called from the gate of charity; whoever was among the people of fasting will be called from the gate of al-Rayyan.\" Abu Bakr said: 'O Messenger of Allah, what is upon the one called from these gates of necessity? Will anyone be called from all these gates?' He said: 'Yes, and I hope you will be among them.'"],[5168,"\"In Paradise there is a gate called al-Rayyan, prepared for those who fast. When the last of them enters, it is closed.\""],[5169,"I heard Muhammad say that the men and women argued about which of them would be more in Paradise. So they went to Abu Hurairah and asked him. He said, \"Abu al-Qasim ﷺ said: 'The first group to enter Paradise from my nation will have faces as bright as the full moon at night. Then those who follow them will have faces like the brightest star in the sky. Each man among them will have two wives, the marrow of whose legs can be seen behind the flesh, and there will be no unmarried person in Paradise.'\""],[5170,"\"Do you know who will be the first of Allah's creation to enter Paradise?\" They said: Allah and His Messenger know best. He said: \"The first of Allah's creation to enter Paradise are the poor emigrants, through whom the frontiers are secured and dangers are warded off. One of them dies while his need is in his chest, unable to fulfill it. Allah will say to whichever of His angels He wills: Go to them and greet them. The angels will say: Our Lord, we are the inhabitants of Your heavens and the choice of Your creation; would You command us to go to these and greet them? He will say: They were servants who worshipped Me, not associating anything with Me, and through them the frontiers are secured and dangers are warded off; one of them dies while his need is in his chest, unable to fulfill it. He said: So the angels will come to them at that time and enter upon them from every gate: {Peace be upon you for what you patiently endured; and excellent is the final home.}\""],[5171,"\"The first three to enter Paradise were shown to me: the martyr, a slave who perfected the worship of his Lord and gave sincere counsel to his master, and a chaste, self-restrained person of wealth or property.\""],[5172,"Between the two leaves of any of the gates of Paradise is a journey of seven years."],[5173,"By Him in whose hand is my soul, between the two leaves of any of the gates of Paradise is as the distance between Makkah and Hajar, or as between Makkah and Busra."],[5174,"I was standing near the Messenger of Allah ﷺ when a rabbi from the rabbis of the Jews came and said: Peace be upon you, O Muhammad. He said: I pushed him with a shove that nearly made him fall. He said: Why do you push me? I said: Why don't you say, O Messenger of Allah? The Jew said: I call him by the name his family gave him. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"My name is Muhammad, which my family gave me.\" The Jew said: I have come to ask you. The Messenger of Allah said: \"Will it benefit you if I inform you?\" He said: I will listen to what you say. So the Messenger of Allah tapped with a stick he had and said: \"Ask.\" The Jew said: Where will the people be on the day when the earth is changed to another earth and the heavens? The Messenger of Allah said: \"They will be in darkness, before the bridge.\" He said: Who will be the first of the people to cross? He said: \"The poor of the emigrants.\" The Jew said: What will be their gift when they enter Paradise? He said: \"The extra lobe of the whale's liver.\" He said: What will be their meal after it? He said: \"The bull of Paradise, which used to eat from its edges, will be slaughtered for them.\" He said: What will be their drink with it? He said: \"From a spring in it called Salsabil.\" He said: You have spoken the truth. He said: And I have come to ask you about something that no one on earth knows except a prophet. He said: \"Will it benefit you if I tell you?\" He said: I will listen with my ear. I have come to ask you about the child. He said: \"The fluid of the man is white and the fluid of the woman is yellow; when they meet, if the man's fluid prevails over the woman's, it will be male by Allah's permission, and if the woman's fluid prevails over the man's, it will be female by Allah's permission.\" The Jew said: Indeed you have spoken the truth, and you are a prophet. Then he left and went away. The Messenger of Allah said: \"He asked me about what he asked, and I had no knowledge of it until Allah brought it to me.\""],[5175,"“The supplication of the wronged is carried on the clouds, and the gates of the heavens are opened for it, and the Lord, Blessed and Exalted, says: By My might, I will surely help you, even after a while.”"],[5176,"A woman of the people of Paradise will have the whiteness of her shin visible through seventy robes of silk. That is because God says, {As if they were rubies and coral.} As for the ruby, it is a stone that, if you thread it with a wire and then look, you will see it from behind it."],[5177,"A man in Paradise will recline for seventy years before changing position. Then a woman will come to him and draw near, and he will look at her cheek, clearer than a mirror. She will greet him, and he will return the greeting and ask her, 'Who are you?' She will say, 'I am among the increase.' She will have seventy garments on, and his sight will penetrate them until he sees the marrow of her shin from behind that. Upon them will be crowns, and the lowest pearl on her will illuminate what is between the east and the west."],[5178,"A morning or an evening spent in the path of Allah is better than the world and what it contains. And the space of a bow of one of you, or the place of a foot in Paradise, is better than the world and what it contains. And if a woman from the women of the people of Paradise were to look upon the earth, she would illuminate what is between them and fill what is between them with fragrance. And her veil on her head is better than the world and what it contains."],[5179,"In Paradise there are pavilions of hollow pearl, sixty miles wide, in each corner of which are people who do not see the others, and the believer goes around among them."],[5180,"From the Messenger of Allah ﷺ who said, \"The lowest rank in Paradise is for a person who has eighty thousand servants, seventy-two wives, and is given a dome made of pearls, zabarjad (a green gem), and yaqoot (a red gem) that extends from Jabiya to Sana'a.\""],[5181,"By Him in Whose hand is my soul, if a woman from the women of the people of Paradise were to look upon the people of the earth, she would illuminate what is between them and fill what is between them with fragrance. And her veil on her head is better than the world and what it contains."],[5182,"A man will be given in Paradise such and such number of women. It was said, 'O Messenger of Allah, who can bear that?' He said, 'He will be given the strength of a hundred.'"],[5183,"It was said to him, 'Will we have intercourse in Paradise?' He said, 'Yes, by Him in Whose hand is my soul, with vigor, with vigor. And when he rises from her, she returns pure and virgin.'"],[5184,"that the Prophet ﷺ said: \"Indeed, when the believer desires a child in Paradise, its gestation, birth, and youth will be as he desires, in a single hour.\""],[5185,"The people of Paradise will see the chamber from the chambers of Paradise as you see the brilliant star sinking in the eastern or western horizon."],[5186,"The people of Paradise will see the people of the chambers above them as you see the brilliant star passing or sinking in the horizon from the east or west. They said, 'O Messenger of God, those are the dwellings of the prophets; none other can reach them.' He said, 'Yes, by Him in whose hand is my soul, men who believed in God and confirmed the messengers.'"],[5187,"The combs of the people of Paradise are of gold, and their censers are of aloeswood."],[5188,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"{And raised couches} By Him in Whose hand is my soul, its elevation is like the distance between heaven and earth, a journey of five hundred years.\""],[5189,"The roof of my house was opened while I was in Makkah, and Jibril descended and opened my chest, then washed it with Zamzam water. Then he brought a basin full of wisdom and faith and poured it into my chest, then closed it. Then he took my hand and ascended with me to the heaven. When we came to the lowest heaven, Jibril said to the keeper of the lowest heaven, 'Open.' He said, 'Who is this?' He said, 'This is Jibril.' He said, 'Is there anyone with you?' He said, 'Yes, Muhammad ﷺ is with me.' He said, 'Has he been sent for?' He said, 'Yes.' So it was opened. When we ascended to the lowest heaven, there was a man with dark masses to his right and dark masses to his left. When he looked to his right, he laughed, and when he looked to his left, he wept. He said, 'Welcome to the righteous prophet and the righteous son.' I said, 'O Jibril, who is this?' He said, 'This is Adam, and these dark masses to his right and left are the souls of his descendants. The people of the right among them are the people of Paradise, and the dark masses to his left are the people of the Fire. When he looks to his right, he laughs, and when he looks to his left, he weeps.' Then Jibril took me until he came to the second heaven and said to its keeper, 'Open.' Its keeper said to him the like of what the keeper of the lowest heaven had said, and he opened.\" Anas b. Malik said: He mentioned that he found in the heavens Adam, Idris, Isa, Musa, and Ibrahim, may Allah's blessings be upon Muhammad and upon them. He did not confirm how their stations were, except that he mentioned that he found Adam in the lowest heaven and Ibrahim in the sixth heaven."],[5190,"A bedouin stood up to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and said: Does it have grapes, meaning Paradise, O Messenger of Allah? He said: \"Yes.\" He said: What is the size of a bunch of them? He said: \"A month's journey for the piebald crow, neither turning aside nor tiring.\" He said: What is the size of a berry from it? He said: \"Has your father ever slaughtered a large goat from his flock?\" He said: Yes. He said: \"And he skinned its hide, gave it to your mother, and said: Tan this for us, then cut from it a bucket with which we water our livestock?\" He said: Yes. He said: \"Then that berry will satisfy me and my household.\" He said: \"Yes, and the majority of your clan.\""],[5191,"Indeed in Paradise there is a tree whose shade a rider travels for a hundred years.\" Abu Hurayrah said: And recite if you wish: {And extended shade}."],[5192,"In Paradise there is a tree whose shade a rider travels for a hundred years and does not cross it."],[5193,"He forbade leasing land."],[5194,"A bedouin stood up to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and said: What is the fruit of Paradise? He said: \"In it is a tree called Tuba.\" He said: Which of our trees does it resemble? He said: \"It does not resemble any tree of your land, but have you gone to Syria?\" He said: No, O Messenger of Allah. He said: \"It is a tree in Syria called the sycamore fig; it grows thick on a trunk, then its top is spread out.\" He said: What is the size of its root? He said: \"If you were to travel on a young camel of your family's camels, you would not encircle its root until its collarbones break from old age.\""],[5195,"There is no tree in Paradise but its trunk is of gold."],[5196,"“The people of Paradise eat and drink, but they do not urinate, defecate, blow their noses, or spit. They are inspired with praise and glorification just as they are inspired with breath. Their food produces belching, and their scent is musk.”"],[5197,"The rivers of Paradise emerge from beneath hills, or from beneath mountains of musk."],[5199,"Indeed in Paradise there is a sea of water, a sea of honey, a sea of wine, and a sea of milk. Then rivers split from them afterward."],[5200,"“The first group to enter Paradise will be in the form of the moon on the night when it is full, then those who follow them will be in the form of the brightest shining star in the sky. They will not urinate, defecate, spit, or blow their noses. Their combs will be of gold, their sweat will be musk, their censers will be aloeswood, and their wives will be the ḥūr al-ʿīn. Their character will be like that of a single man, in the form of their father, sixty cubits tall.”"],[5201,"“The first group to enter Paradise will have forms like the moon on the night when it is full. They will not spit therein, nor blow their noses, nor defecate. Their vessels and combs will be of gold and silver, and their censers will be of aloeswood. Each of them will have two wives, and the marrow of their shins will be visible from behind the flesh. There will be no disagreement among them and no mutual hatred; their hearts will be as one heart, glorifying Allah morning and evening.”"],[5202,"I have prepared for My righteous servants what no eye has seen, no ear has heard, and no human heart has imagined. And the confirmation of that is in the Book of Allah: {No soul knows what is hidden for them of comfort for the eyes as reward for what they used to do}."],[5203,"\"While he was on the Minbar, I heard Al-Mughirah bin Shu'bah saying - and he attributed it to the Prophet ﷺ - 'Indeed Musa [peace be upon him] asked his Lord: \"O Lord! Who is the lowest in rank among the people of Paradise?\" He said: \"A man who comes after the people of Paradise have been admitted to Paradise, and he is told to enter. He says: 'How can I enter when they have gotten all of their abodes, and all that is to be had?'\" He said: \"So it is said to him: 'Would you accept if you were to have what a king in the world?' He says: 'Yes, O Lord! I accept.' So it is said to him: 'Then for you is this and its like, and its like again, and its like again.' So he says: 'I accept, O Lord!' So it is said to him: 'Then for you is this and ten the like thereof.' So he says: 'I accept, O Lord!' So it is said: 'Indeed you shall have this, and whatever your soul desires, and whatever delights your eyes.'\" (Using translation from Tirmidhī 3198)"],[5204,"On the authority of the Prophet ﷺ who said, \"Indeed, I know the last person to come out of the Fire. It will be a man who crawls out and he will be told to enter Paradise, so he will enter, then he will come out and say, 'O Lord, everyone has taken their place in the ranks.' It will be said to him, 'Do you remember the time you were in the world?' He will say yes. Then he will be told, 'Wish for something.' So he will wish and it will be said to him, 'You will have something like it, and ten times as much.' He will be the lowest in status among the people of Paradise.\""],[5205,"\"There will be people in the Fire as long as Allah wills, then Allah will have mercy on them and bring them out. They will be in the lowest part of Paradise and will be washed in the spring of life. The people of Paradise will call them the Jahannamis. If one of them were to host the people of this world, he would feed them, give them drink, and furnish for them.\" He said: And I think he said: \"And marry them, without that diminishing what he has.\""],[5206,"\"In Paradise there is a market that they come to every Friday. In it are dunes of musk; a north wind stirs and blows musk into their faces. They return to their wives, who say to them: Allah has increased you in beauty and handsomeness after us, and they say: And you, Allah has increased you in beauty and handsomeness after us.\""],[5207,"Two gardens of silver, their vessels and all that is in them; and two gardens of gold, their vessels and all that is in them. And between the people and looking at their Lord is only the mantle of pride on His face in the Garden of Eden."],[5208,"That He may gather me and you in the market of Paradise. Saʿīd said: Is there a market in it? He said: Yes. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ informed me: “When the people of Paradise enter it, they will alight therein according to the excellence of their deeds. Then permission will be given to them for a period equal to Friday of the days of this world, and they will visit Allah, Mighty and Exalted. He will show them His Throne and appear to them in a garden of the gardens of Paradise. Pulpits of light will be set up for them, and pulpits of pearl, pulpits of ruby, pulpits of chrysolite, pulpits of gold, and pulpits of silver. The lowest of them—and there is no lowly one among them—will sit on mounds of musk and camphor. They will not think that the owners of the chairs are in a better position than them.” Abu Hurayrah said: I said: O Messenger of Allah, will we see our Lord? He said: “Yes. Do you doubt seeing the sun and the moon on the night when it is full?” We said: No. He said: “Likewise, you will not doubt seeing your Lord. No one will remain in that gathering except that Allah will confront him with a confrontation, until He says to a man among them: ‘O so-and-so, do you remember the day you did such and such?’ He will remind him of some of his treacherous acts in the world. He will say: ‘O Lord, did You not forgive me?’ He will say: ‘Yes, by the vastness of My forgiveness you have reached this station of yours.’” He said: “While they are thus, a cloud will cover them from above and rain down upon them a perfume whose like they have never smelled. Then He, Mighty and Exalted, will say: ‘Arise to what I have prepared for you of honor, and take whatever you desire.’” He said: “So we will come to a market surrounded by angels, the like of which eyes have not seen, ears have not heard, and hearts have not imagined. Whatever we desire will be carried to us. Nothing will be sold or bought in it. In that market the people of Paradise will meet one another. A man of high station will come forward and meet one who is below him—and there is no lowly one among them—and he will be amazed by the clothing he sees on him. Before his conversation ends, a better form will appear on him. That is because no one should grieve therein.” He said: “Then we will return to our dwellings, and our wives will meet us and say: ‘Welcome and greetings to our beloved. You have come, and you have more beauty and fragrance than when you left us.’ He will say: ‘We sat today with our Lord, the Compeller, and it is right that we return with the like of what we have returned with.’”"],[5210,"“Allah, Blessed and Exalted, will say: ‘O people of Paradise.’ They will say: ‘At Your service, our Lord, and at Your command, and all good is in Your hands.’ He will say: ‘Are you satisfied?’ They will say: ‘How could we not be satisfied when You have given us what You have not given anyone of Your creation?’ He will say: ‘Shall I not give you something better than that?’ They will say: ‘O Lord, what thing is better than that?’ He will say: ‘I bestow upon you My good pleasure, and I will never be angry with you after that, ever.’”"],[5211,"“In Paradise there are one hundred degrees which Allah has prepared for the mujāhidīn in His way. Between each two degrees is like what is between the heaven and the earth. So when you ask Allah, ask Him for al-Firdaws, for it is the middle of Paradise and the highest part of Paradise, and above it is the Throne, and from it the rivers of Paradise gush forth.”"],[5212,"Anas b. Malik recited: \"Indeed, We have granted you al-Kawthar\" (Qur'an 108:1). He said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"Al-Kawthar is a river in Paradise flowing on the surface of the earth; its two banks are domes of pearl.\" He ﷺ said: \"I struck with my hand, and behold, its clay is fragrant musk, and its pebbles are pearls.\""],[5214,"\"The space of a whip in Paradise is better than the world and all that is in it.\" Recite, if you wish: {And whoever is drawn away from the Fire and admitted to Paradise has indeed succeeded. And the life of this world is nothing but the enjoyment of deception.}"],[5215,"He forbade leasing land."],[5216,"By Allah, \"the length of a whip of one of you in Paradise is better for him than all that is between the heaven and the earth.\""],[5217,"“Musa said: ‘O Lord, who among the people of Paradise is highest in rank?’ Allah said: ‘I will tell you about them. I have prepared their honor with My own hand and sealed it. No eye has seen, no ear has heard, and it has never crossed the mind of any human.’ And the confirmation of that is in the Book of Allah: ‘And no soul knows what has been hidden for them of comfort for eyes’ (al-Sajdah 32:17).”"],[5218,"The offspring of the believers will be sponsored by Ibrahim in Paradise."],[5220,"“When one of you eats, let him eat with his right hand; and when he drinks, let him drink with his right hand, for Satan eats with his left hand and drinks with his left hand.”"],[5221,"There will remain of Paradise what Allah wills to remain, and Allah will create for it a creation as He wills."],[5223,"Death will be brought on the Day of Resurrection and made to stand on the bridge. It will be said: 'O people of Paradise,' and they will go forward, fearful and anxious, lest they be taken out of the place they are in. Then it will be said: 'O people of the Fire,' and they will go forward, rejoicing and hopeful, to be taken out of the place they are in. Then it will be said: 'Do you recognize this?' They will say: 'Yes, our Lord, this is death.' Then He will command it, and it will be slaughtered on the bridge. Then it will be said to both groups: 'Each of you will have eternal life, and there will be no death in it ever.'\""],[5224,"No one will enter Paradise without being shown his seat in the Fire had he done evil, so that he may increase in gratitude. And no one will enter the Fire without being shown his seat in Paradise had he done good, so that it may be a regret for him.\""],[5225,"“I warn you of the Fire, I warn you of the Fire, I warn you of the Fire,” until if he had been in this position of mine while he was in Kufah, the people of the market would have heard him, until the cloak that was on his shoulder fell to his feet."],[5226,"«Paradise and the Fire disputed. The Fire said, “The tyrannical and the arrogant will enter me.” Paradise said, “The weak among people and their lowly ones will enter me.” Allah said to the Fire, “You are My punishment; with you I afflict whomever I will.” And He said to Paradise, “You are My mercy; with you I bestow mercy upon whomever I will. And each of you will have its fill.”»"],[5227,"Paradise is surrounded by hardships, and the Fire is surrounded by desires."],[5228,"The Fire is surrounded by desires, and Paradise is surrounded by hardships."],[5229,"“Your fire which you kindle is one part of seventy parts of the fire of Hell.” They said, “O Messenger of Allah, it would have been sufficient.” He said, “It has been favored over it by sixty-nine parts.”"],[5230,"The Prophet ﷺ said, \"Your fire is only one part of seventy parts of the fire of Hell, which is as hot as the water of the sea. If it were not for that, Allah would not have made it beneficial for anyone.\""],[5231,"«The first three to enter the Fire were shown to me: a ruler who was given authority, a wealthy man who did not pay Allah’s due from his wealth, and a poor man who is boastful.»"],[5232,"«The people of the Fire are five: the weak one who is not paid any heed, and he is among you as a follower; they do not seek family or wealth.» I said, “Will that be the case, O Abu ʿAbd Allāh?” He said, “Yes, by Allah, I saw them in the pre-Islamic era. A man would graze for the tribe and have nothing except their servant girl whom he would have intercourse with. And a man who does not wake up in the morning or reach the evening except that he is deceiving you about your family and your wealth. And a man from whom nothing is hidden except that he betrays it, even if it is small. And he mentioned lying. And he mentioned miserliness.”"],[5233,"«As for the people of the Fire who are its rightful inhabitants, they will neither die nor live. But there are some people whom the Fire will afflict because of their sins, and it will cause them to die until they become like charcoal. Then permission will be given for intercession.»"],[5234,"The disbeliever's molar is like Uhud."],[5235,"«The molar of the disbeliever, or the canine tooth of the disbeliever, is like Mount Uḥud, and the thickness of his skin is a distance of three days’ travel.»"],[5236,"«{Water like molten metal} like the dregs of oil, and when it is brought near to him, the skin of his face falls into it.»"],[5237,"A man from the people of the Fire will be brought. He will be asked: 'O son of Adam, how do you find your abode?' He will say: 'O Lord, the worst abode.' He will say: 'Would you ransom yourself from it with the earth's full of gold?' He will say: 'Yes, O Lord.' He will say: 'You lie. You were asked for what is easier than that.' Then he will be returned to the Fire.\""],[5238,"“In the Fire are snakes like the necks of bukht camels; one of them bites a person with a single bite, and he feels its burning heat for forty autumns.”"],[5239,"“If a stone were thrown into Hell, it would fall for seventy autumns before reaching its bottom.”"],[5240,"“Wayl is a valley in Hell into which the disbeliever falls for forty autumns before reaching its bottom.”"],[5241,"“{O you who believe, fear Allah as He ought to be feared, and do not die except as Muslims} If a single drop of Zaqqum were to drip onto the earth, it would ruin the livelihood of the people of the earth. So how about one who has no food other than it?”"],[5242,"“The least punished of the people of the Fire is one for whom two sandals of fire are made, from which his brain boils.”"],[5243,"«The thickness of the disbeliever is forty-two cubits by the cubit of the All-Compelling, and his molar is like Mount Uḥud.»"],[5245,"‘Ubadah b. al-Samit was seen weeping on the eastern wall of Jerusalem, and it was said to him, so he said, “From here the Messenger of Allah ﷺ told that he saw Malik turning over coals like pickings.”"],[5246,"«No one will enter Paradise in whose heart is a mustard seed's weight of arrogance, and no one will enter the Fire in whose heart is a mustard seed's weight of faith.»"],[5247,"“A man will take his father by the hand on the Day of Resurrection, wanting to enter him into Paradise, but it will be called out: Indeed, no polytheist may enter Paradise. He will say: ‘O Lord, my father!’ Then he will be transformed into an ugly form and a foul odor, and he will leave him.”"],[5248,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ commanded the women to give charity and encouraged them to do so. He said, \"Give charity, for indeed you (women) are the majority of the inhabitants of Hell.\" A woman among them asked, \"Why is that, O Messenger of Allah?\" He replied, \"Because you (women) curse often, are ungrateful for kindness, and deny the good treatment of your husbands.\""],[5249,"«Paradise and the Fire argued. Paradise said, “What is the matter with me that the poor and the weak enter me?” The Fire said, “What is the matter with me that the tyrannical and the arrogant enter me?” Allah said, “You are My mercy; with you I have mercy upon whomever I will.” And He said to the Fire, “You are My punishment; with you I afflict whomever I will. And each of them will have its fill.”»"],[5250,"«When the people of Paradise have gone to Paradise and the people of the Fire have gone to the Fire, death will be brought until it is placed between Paradise and the Fire, then it will be slaughtered. Then a caller will call out: “O people of Paradise, there is no death; O people of the Fire, there is no death.” So the people of Paradise will increase in joy upon their joy, and the people of the Fire will increase in grief upon their grief.»"],[5251,"“I know the last of the people of Hell who will be brought forth from it, and the last of the people of Paradise to be admitted to Paradise. (It is) a man who will emerge from Hell crawling, and it will be said to him: ‘Go and enter Paradise.’ He will come to it and it will be made to appear to him as if it is full.’ Allah will say: ‘Go and enter Paradise.’ He will come to it and it will appear to him as if it is full. So he will say: ‘O Lord, I found it full.’ Allah will say: ‘Go and enter Paradise.’ He will come to it and it will be made to appear to him as if it is full. So he will say: ‘O Lord, I found it full.’ Allah will say: ‘Go and enter Paradise, for you will have the like of the world and ten times more, or you will have ten times the like of the world.’ He will say: ‘Are You mocking me, or are You laughing at me, when You are the Sovereign?’” He said: \"And I saw the Messenger of Allah ﷺ smiling so broadly that his molar teeth could be seen.\" And he used to say: \"This is the lowest of the people of Paradise in status.\" (Using translation from Ibn Mājah 4339)"],[5252,"«Allah will bring out people from the Fire and enter them into Paradise.» A man said to him in the narration of ʿAmr, “Allah says: {They will want to come out of the Fire, but they will not come out of it}.” Jābir b. ʿAbd Allāh said, “You are making the specific general. This is for the disbelievers. Read what is before it.” Then he recited: {Indeed, those who disbelieve—if they had all that is in the earth and the like of it with it to ransom themselves from the punishment of the Day of Resurrection, it would not be accepted from them, and for them is a painful punishment. They will want to come out of the Fire, but they will not come out of it}. “This is for the disbelievers.”"],[5253,"«Whoever says “There is no god but Allah” and has in his heart the weight of a speck of good will come out of the Fire.»"],[5254,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: 'Allah will admit the people of Paradise into Paradise; He admits whom He wills by His mercy, and He will admit the people of the Fire. Then He will say: Bring out whoever has in his heart a mustard seed of faith. They will be brought out of it as charcoal and cast into a river in Paradise, and they will grow as a seed grows in the side of a torrent. Have you not seen it yellow and twisted?'"],[5255,"When the people of Paradise and the people of the Fire are distinguished, the people of Paradise will enter Paradise and the people of the Fire will enter the Fire. The messengers will stand and intercede, and it will be said: Go and bring out whoever you know has in his heart a qirat's weight of faith. They will bring out many people. Then it will be said: Go and bring out whoever you know has in his heart a mustard seed of faith. They will bring out many people. Then He, Mighty and Exalted, will say: Now I will bring out by My grace and My mercy. He will bring out multiples of what they brought out, and they will have been scorched and become charcoal. They will be cast into a river—or into a river of the rivers of Paradise—and their burnt parts will fall off on the bank of that river, and they will return white like the thaarir. It will be written on their necks: 'The freed ones of Allah,' and they will be called therein 'the Jahannamis.'"],[5256,"As for the people of the Fire who are its inhabitants, they will neither die therein nor live. But people whom the Fire touched because of their sins—or he said: because of their errors—until when they become charcoal, permission will be given for intercession. They will be brought in groups and scattered over the people of Paradise. Then it will be said: O people of Paradise, pour water upon them. They will grow as the seed grows in the silt of the torrent. A man from the people said: It is as if the Messenger of Allah ﷺ was in the desert."],[5257,"“Ibrahim will say on the Day of Resurrection: ‘O my Lord!’ The Lord, Mighty and Exalted, will say: ‘Here I am, O Ibrahim.’ Ibrahim will say: ‘O Lord, You have burned my descendants.’ Allah will say: ‘Bring out of the Fire anyone who has a grain or a barleycorn of faith in his heart.’”"],[5258,"When he ate, he would lick his three fingers."],[5259,"I said to Abu Saʿīd al-Khudrī: Did you hear the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say about this verse: {Perhaps those who disbelieve will wish that they had been Muslims}? He said: Yes, I heard him say: “Allah will bring out some people from among the believers from the Fire after He has taken His vengeance upon them. He said: When Allah admitted them into the Fire along with the polytheists, the polytheists said: ‘Were you not claiming in the world that you were allies? So what is with you that you are with us in the Fire?’ When Allah heard that from them, He permitted intercession, and the angels and prophets interceded for them until they came out by Allah’s permission. When they were brought out, they said: ‘Would that we were like them, so that intercession might reach us and we might be brought out of the Fire.’ That is the saying of Allah, Mighty and Exalted: {Perhaps those who disbelieve will wish that they had been Muslims}. He said: So they are called in Paradise ‘the Jahannamīs’ because of blackness in their faces. They say: ‘Our Lord, remove this name from us.’ He said: So He commands them, and they bathe in a river in Paradise, and that goes away from them.”"],[5260,"“When the believers are saved from the Fire, they will be detained at a bridge between Paradise and the Fire, where they will settle the grievances that were between them in the world. When they are purified and cleansed, they will be permitted to enter Paradise. By the One in whose hand is the soul of Muḥammad, each of them will be more guided to his dwelling in Paradise than to his home in the world.”"],[5261,"When he ate, he would lick his three fingers."],[5262,"\"Do you have any difficulty in seeing the sun when there is no cloud over it?\" They said: No, O Messenger of Allah. He said: \"Do you have any difficulty in seeing the moon on the night of the full moon when there is no cloud over it?\" They said: No, O Messenger of Allah. He said: \"Then you will see Him on the Day of Resurrection just like that. Allah will gather the people on the Day of Resurrection and say: Whoever used to worship something, let him follow it. So those who worshipped the sun will follow the sun, those who worshipped the moon will follow the moon, and those who worshipped false gods will follow false gods. This nation will remain, including its hypocrites. Allah, Majestic and Exalted, will come to them in a form other than the one they know and say: I am your Lord. They will say: We seek refuge in Allah from you; this is our place until our Lord comes to us, and when our Lord comes, we will recognize Him. He said: Then He will come to them in the form they know and say: I am your Lord. They will say: You are our Lord. Then a bridge will be set up over Hell.\" The Prophet ﷺ said: \"I will be the first to cross it, and the call of the messengers on that day will be: O Allah, grant safety, grant safety. On it will be hooks like the thorns of the sa'dan; do you know the thorns of sa'dan?\" They said: Yes, O Messenger of Allah. He said: \"They are like the thorns of sa'dan, but no one knows their size except Allah. They will snatch people according to their deeds. Among them are those who will be destroyed by their deeds, and among them are those who will be torn apart, then saved. When Allah finishes judging between His servants and wishes to bring out of the Fire those He wishes among those who testified that there is no god but Allah, He will command the angels to bring them out, and they will recognize them by the mark of prostration. He said: Allah has forbidden the Fire to consume the trace of prostration on the son of Adam. He said: So they will bring them out, having been burned, and water called the water of life will be poured over them, and they will grow like the seed in the silt of a flood. He said: There will remain a man facing the Fire, and he will say: O Lord, its smell has poisoned me and its heat has burned me; turn my face away from the Fire. He will keep supplicating, and Allah, Majestic and Exalted, will say: Perhaps if I grant you that, you will ask Me for something else. He will say: No, by Your might, I will not ask You for anything else. So He will turn his face away from the Fire. Then he will say after that: O Lord, bring me near the gate of Paradise. Allah, Majestic and Exalted, will say: Did you not claim that you would not ask Me for anything else? Woe to you, O son of Adam, how treacherous you are! He will keep supplicating, and Allah, Majestic and Exalted, will say: Perhaps if I grant you that, you will ask Me for something else. He will say: No, by Your might, I will not ask You for anything else. He will make covenants and promises to Allah that he will not ask for anything else. So He will bring him near the gate of Paradise. When he is brought near it, Paradise will open up for him, and when he sees what is in it, he will remain silent as long as Allah wills, then say: O Lord, admit me into Paradise. Allah, Majestic and Exalted, will say: Did you not claim that you would not ask Me for anything else? Woe to you, O son of Adam, how treacherous you are! He will say: O Lord, do not make me the most wretched of Your creation. He said: He will keep supplicating until Allah, Majestic and Exalted, laughs, and when He laughs, He will permit him to enter Paradise. When he enters, it will be said to him: Wish for such and such, wish for such and such. He will wish until his wishes are exhausted. Then Allah, Majestic and Exalted, will say: That is for you, and the like of it with it.\" Abu Said said: I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: \"It is for you and ten times its like.\" Abu Hurairah said: I memorized, \"It is for you and the like of it with it.\" And that man will be the last of the people of Paradise to enter."],[5263,"On the authority of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ who said: \"The last person to enter Paradise will be a man walking on the Sirat (bridge to Paradise). He will stumble once and the fire will scorch him. Every time he passes by it, he will turn to it and say, 'Blessed is the One who saved me from you. By Allah, no one has been given anything like what I have been given among all the worlds.’ Then, a tree will be raised for him, and he will say, 'O Lord, draw me closer to it so that I may take shelter in its shade and drink from its water.’ Allah will say, 'O son of Adam, if I give you that, you will ask Me for something else.’ But the man will swear that he will not ask for anything else, even though he knows that he will. Then, Allah will bring him close to it, and he will take shelter in its shade and drink from its water. Then, another tree will be raised for him, which is even better than the first. He will say, 'O Lord, draw me closer to it so that I may take shelter in its shade and drink from its water.’ Allah will say, 'O son of Adam, if I give you that, you will ask Me for something else.’ But the man will swear that he will not ask for anything else, even though he knows that he will. Then, Allah will bring him close to it, and he will take shelter in its shade and drink from its water. Then, a third tree will be raised for him at the gate of Paradise, which is even better than the first two. He will say, 'O Lord, draw me closer to it so that I may take shelter in its shade and drink from its water.’ Allah will say, 'O son of Adam, if I give you that, you will ask Me for something else.’ But the man will swear that he will not ask for anything else, even though he knows that he will. Then, Allah will bring him close to it, and he will hear the voices of the people of Paradise. He will say, 'O Lord, admit me to Paradise.’ Allah will say, 'O son of Adam, what will make you content with Me and My favor? Would it please you if I give you the entire world and as much again?’ The man will reply, 'Are You making fun of me while You are the Lord of all creation?’ I said, 'Would you not like Me to give you that and as much again?’ The man will say, 'O Lord, I am not making fun of You, but I am asking You for something else.’ The Prophet ﷺ then smiled so broadly that his molars could be seen and he said, 'Do you not wonder at what made me laugh? They asked, 'O Prophet of Allah! What made you laugh?’ He said, 'I laughed because the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said the same as I have said (i.e., the man said the same as I said when he entered Paradise).' \""],[5264,"\"I know the last of the people of the Fire to depart from it. A man will exit it crawling, and he will say: 'O Lord! The people have taken all the places.'\" He said: \"So it will be said to him: 'Go to Paradise to enter Paradise.' So he will go to enter, but he will see that the people have taken all the places. He will return and say: 'O Lord! The people have taken all of the places.' So it will be said to him: 'Do you remember the times you used to live in?' And he will say: 'Yes.' So it will be said to him: 'Wish, He will wish for something, and it will be said to him: 'For you is whatever you wished for, and ten times the world.' He will say: 'Do you mock me while you are the King?'\" He (Ibn Masud) said: \"I saw the Messenger of Allah ﷺ laugh until his molars were visible.\" (Using translation from Tirmidhī 2595)"],[5265,"He used to urinate in a vessel of wood, then it would be placed under his bed.\""],[5266,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ rode his mule and seated me behind him. When the Messenger of Allah ﷺ went to relieve himself, the thing he most liked to use for concealment was a target or a palm-tree enclosure. He entered a garden belonging to a man of the Ansar."],[5267,"A sheep was gifted to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and its belly was roasted for him. He ate from it, then stood up to pray and did not perform wudu'."],[5268,"I saw the Messenger of Allah ﷺ eat a bone with meat on it from a sheep, then pray without rinsing his mouth and without touching water."],[5269,"\"The Prophet ﷺ passed by a cooking pot and extracted a bone from it and ate it, then prayed without performing wudu'.\""],[5270,"\"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ commanded us to perform wudu' from camel meat, and not to perform wudu' from sheep meat, and to pray in sheep folds, and not to pray in camel watering places.\""],[5271,"Then I witnessed 'Umar eat from a large bowl, then he stood and prayed without performing wudu'.\""],[5272,"The Prophet ﷺ came to a woman from the Ansar. She spread a mat for him in the shade of a palm tree and sprinkled water around it, and she slaughtered a sheep. He ate, and we ate with him. Then he lay down under the palm tree. When he woke up, he performed wudu' and prayed Zuhr. The woman said, \"O Messenger of Allah, we have some leftover food; would you like some?\" He said, \"Yes.\" He ate and we ate with him, then he prayed before performing wudu'."],[5273,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ drank milk, then called for a vessel and rinsed his mouth, and said: 'It has fat.'"],[5274,"The Prophet ﷺ performed ablution, wiped over his leather socks, and prayed all the prayers with one ablution."],[5275,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to perform ablution for every prayer, but on the day of the conquest of Makkah, he prayed all the prayers with one ablution."],[5276,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ prayed all the prayers on the day of the conquest of Makkah with one ablution and wiped over his leather socks. 'Umar said to him, 'I saw you today doing something you had not done before.' He said, 'I did it deliberately, O 'Umar.'"],[5277,"The Prophet ﷺ performed ablution twice each."],[5278,"I know best how the Messenger of Allah ﷺ performed ablution. He performed it once each."],[5279,"The Prophet ﷺ performed ablution once each (washing each part once) and combined rinsing the mouth and inhaling water into the nose."],[5280,"Abd Allah b. Umar used to perform ablution three times each, attributing that to the Prophet ﷺ."],[5281,"Allah does not accept prayer without purification, nor charity from ill-gotten gains."],[5282,"When the Kaaba was being built, the Prophet ﷺ and al-Abbas went to carry stones. Al-Abbas said to the Prophet ﷺ, 'Put your waist-wrapper on your shoulder to protect you from the stones.' He did so, but he fell to the ground and his eyes turned toward the sky. Then he stood up and said, 'My waist-wrapper, my waist-wrapper,' and he tied it on."],[5283,"I saw the Prophet ﷺ praying in a single garment, wrapping it around himself."],[5284,"He saw the Prophet ﷺ praying in a single garment in the house of Umm Salamah, placing its two ends on his shoulders."],[5285,"He entered upon the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and saw him praying in a single garment, having wrapped its two ends in opposite directions."],[5286,"He entered upon the Prophet ﷺ and saw him praying on a mat, prostrating on it."],[5287,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to mix with us until he would say to a young brother of mine: 'O Abu Umayr, what happened to the nughayr?' And a carpet of ours was sprinkled with water, and he prayed on it."],[5288,"“Allah and His Messenger forbid you to eat the flesh of domesticated donkeys, for it is filthy.” (Using translation from Ibn Mājah 3196)"],[5289,"There is no man who is among a people who commit sins while they are able to change them but they do not change them, except that Allah will strike them with punishment before they die."],[5290,"He used to pray on the khumrah."],[5291,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to mix with us a great deal, so much so that he would say to a young brother of mine, “O Abū ʿUmayr, what did the little bird do?” Then the prayer came, so we sprinkled water on a mat of ours, and he prayed on it, and we lined up behind him."],[5292,"I opened the door while the Messenger of Allah ﷺ was praying voluntary prayer and the door was in the direction of the qiblah. The Prophet ﷺ walked to his right or left until he opened the door, then he returned to the prayer."],[5293,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ was praying with the people when two slave girls from Banu 'Abd al-Muttalib came running and fighting each other. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ took hold of them and separated one from the other, and he did not mind that."],[5294,"“The Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to turn to the right and left during his prayer, and he did not twist his neck behind his back.”"],[5295,"The Prophet ﷺ saw a Satan while he was praying, so he seized him and choked him until he felt the coldness of his tongue on his hand. Then he ﷺ said: \"Had it not been for the supplication of my brother Sulayman, he would have been tied up for people to see.\""],[5296,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to carry Umamah while praying; when he wanted to bow, he would put her down, then he would prostrate; when he stood up, he would carry her; and when he wanted to bow, he would put her down."],[5297,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ went out to the prayer carrying Umamah bt. Abi al-'As on his shoulder. When he bowed he would place her down from his shoulder, and when he finished his prostrations he would carry her on his shoulder, and he continued doing so until he completed his prayer."],[5298,"While we were sitting at the door of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, the Messenger of Allah ﷺ came out to us carrying Umamah bt. Abi al-‘As b. al-Rabi‘, whose mother was Zaynab bt. the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and she was a young girl. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ prayed while she was on his shoulder: he would put her down when he bowed and put her back on his shoulder when he stood up, until he finished his prayer, doing that with her."],[5299,"There were no horsemen among us on the day of Badr apart from al-Miqdad. I could not see any of us who was not asleep, apart from the Messenger of Allah ﷺ who remained praying beneath a tree and weeping until morning. (Using translation from Aḥmad 1023)"],[5301,"The Prophet ﷺ entered the mosque of Banu Amr b. Awf, meaning the mosque of Quba. Men from the Ansar entered and greeted him. Ibn Umar said: I asked Suhayb, who was with him, 'How did the Prophet ﷺ respond when he was greeted while praying?' He said, 'He would gesture with his hand.'"],[5302,"He prayed with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, then spat and rubbed it with his left sandal."],[5303,"He saw the Prophet ﷺ praying while wearing patched sandals."],[5304,"The Prophet ﷺ prayed wearing a cloak belonging to one of his wives, and she was wearing part of it."],[5305,"The Prophet ﷺ used to pray in our sheets."],[5306,"Did the Prophet ﷺ pray in the garment in which he had intercourse with her? She said, \"Yes, if he did not see any harm in it.\""],[5307,"'A'ishah saw me washing the trace of janabah that had gotten on my garment. She said, \"What is this?\" I said, \"A trace of janabah that got on my garment.\" She said, \"I have certainly seen it get on the garment of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and he would do no more than say, 'Like this, we rub it.'\""],[5308,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ came out wearing a red suit, and a short spear was planted, and he prayed facing it, while a dog, a woman, and a donkey passed beyond it."],[5309,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ came out leaning on Usamah b. Zayd, wearing a Qatari striped cloak that he had wrapped around himself, and he led them in prayer."],[5310,"“If I were invited to a foreleg, I would respond, and if it were gifted to me, I would accept.”"],[5311,"He used to come with Salamah b. al-Akwaʿ to the forenoon prayer, and he would head to a pillar near the mushaf and pray close to it. I would say to him: “Why don’t you pray here?” and I would point to a part of the mosque, but he would say: “I saw the Messenger of Allah ﷺ seeking this spot.”"],[5312,"I used to sleep with my legs in front of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ when he would offer his prayer at night (i.e. tahajjud prayer offered towards the end of the night.). When he prostrated himself he struck my legs, and I drew them up and he then prostrated. (Using translation from Abū Dāʾūd 712)"],[5313,"A man came to Ibn Mas'ud and said: \"I recited the whole Mufassal tonight in one rak'ah.\" 'Abdullah said: \"This is like reciting poetry hastily. We have known the pairs which the Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to combine. He mentioned twenty surahs from the Mufassal, two surahs in each rak'ah.\""],[5314,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ prayed Fajr in Makkah and began Surah al-Mu'minun. When he reached the mention of Musa and Harun, or the mention of 'Isa (Muhammad b. 'Abbad was unsure), the Prophet ﷺ was seized by a cough and bowed."],[5315,"When the Messenger of Allah ﷺ raised from the last rak'ah of the morning prayer, he said: “O Allah, save al-Walīd b. al-Walīd, Salamah b. Hishām, and ʿAyyāsh b. Abī Rabīʿah. O Allah, tighten Your grip on Muḍar and make it upon them like the years of Yūsuf.”"],[5316,"\"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ prayed (saying the) Qunut after bowing for a month, supplicating against Ri'l, Dhakwan and 'Usayyah who had disobeyed Allah and His Messenger.\" (Sahih). (Using translation from Nasāʾī 1070)"],[5317,"Regarding the night prayer of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ , it was said, \"He used to pray eight rak'ahs, then perform Witr prayer. Then he would pray two rak'ahs while sitting, then he would stand and recite (the Quran). Then he would bow and perform two rak'ahs between the call to prayer (Adhan) and the start of the prayer (Iqamah) of Fajr (dawn prayer).\""],[5318,"“The Messenger of Allah ﷺ did not die until most of his prayer was performed while sitting, and the deed most beloved to him was that which a servant persists in, even if it is small.”"],[5319,"“I never saw the Prophet ﷺ pray sitting in his supererogatory prayer at all, until a year before his death. Then he would pray sitting in his supererogatory prayer, and he would recite a sūrah in such a slow measured way that it would become longer than a longer one.”"],[5320,"The Prophet ﷺ used to pray while sitting, after he had grown old. When thirty verses of a surah remained, he would stand, recite them, and then bow."],[5321,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to pray standing at night for a long time, and used to pray sitting at night for a long time. When he prayed standing, he bowed standing, and when he prayed sitting, he bowed sitting. (Using translation from Abū Dāʾūd 955)"],[5322,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to pray standing and sitting. When he began the prayer standing, he bowed standing; and when he began the prayer sitting, he bowed sitting."],[5323,"That the Prophet ﷺ prayed cross-legged."],[5324,"I saw the Prophet ﷺ when he finished his circumambulation go to the edge of the circumambulation area and pray two rak'ahs with no one between him and the circumambulators."],[5325,"I saw the Prophet ﷺ praying facing the Black Stone with men and women passing in front of him, and there was no sutra between him and them."],[5326,"I used to recognize the ending of the Messenger of Allah's ﷺ prayer by the takbir."],[5327,"“When one of you is invited to a wedding feast, let him attend it.”"],[5328,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ sent me on an errand. I caught up with him, greeted him with salām while he was praying, and he gestured to me. When he finished, he called me and said: 'You greeted me while I was praying,' and at that time he was facing toward the east."],[5329,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to pray on his riding camel in whatever direction it faced while traveling."],[5330,"We were with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ on a journey. He sent me on an errand, and I came to him while he was riding. I greeted him with salām, and he gestured with his hand. Then I greeted again, and he gestured, but he did not speak to me. Afterwards he called me and said: 'I was praying a voluntary prayer.'"],[5331,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ sent me on an errand. I found him riding, going east and west. I greeted him with salām, and he gestured with his hand. Then I greeted him again, and he gestured with his hand. I turned away, and he called me: 'O Jābir!' The people called me: 'O Jābir!' So I came to him and said: 'O Messenger of Allah, I greeted you with salām, but you did not respond to me.' He said: 'That is because I was praying.'"],[5332,"“The Messenger of Allah ﷺ forbade tipping up water skins in order to drink from their mouths.” (Using translation from Ibn Mājah 3418)"],[5333,"I saw the Prophet ﷺ praying on his riding beast during travel in the supererogatory prayer, gesturing with his head in a slight motion."],[5334,"I saw the Prophet ﷺ while he was praying on his mount, performing voluntary prayers in every direction, but he would lower the two prostrations lower than the two bowings, gesturing in a slight motion."],[5335,"Mu'adh, who is Ibn Jabal, used to pray with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, then return to his people and lead them."],[5336,"Mu'adh used to pray the last Isha prayer with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, then go to his people and pray that prayer with them."],[5337,"Mu'adh used to pray with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, then return and lead his people, praying that prayer with them."],[5338,"My father came while the Messenger of Allah ﷺ was delivering the sermon. He stood in the sun, so the Messenger of Allah ﷺ ordered him, and he moved to the shade."],[5339,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ addressed us and recited Ṣād. When he passed the prostration, he descended and prostrated, and we prostrated with him. He recited it another time, and when he reached the prostration, we prepared to prostrate. When he saw us, he said, \"It is only the repentance of a prophet, but I see you have readied yourselves for prostration.\" So he descended, prostrated, and we prostrated with him."],[5340,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ would descend from the pulpit, and the prayer would be established. A person would come and speak to him about a need, and he would stand with him until he fulfilled his need, then he would come forward and pray."],[5341,"That the Prophet ﷺ was praying when a sheep passed in front of him, so he moved it towards the direction of the qibla until his belly touched the qibla."],[5342,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to pray at night while I was lying across between him and the qiblah on the bed on which he and his family slept."],[5343,"I used to sleep in front of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ with my legs in the direction of his qiblah. When he prostrated he would poke me, so I would draw up my legs, and when he stood I would stretch them out. She said: And the houses at that time had no lamps."],[5344,"Ghudayf ibn al-Harith reported: I asked Aisha: Have you seen the Messenger of Allah ﷺ washing (because of defilement) at the beginning of the night or at the end? She replied: Sometimes he would take a bath at the beginning of the night and sometimes at the end. Thereupon I exclaimed: Allah is most Great. All Praise be to Allah Who made this matter accommodative. I again asked her: What do you think, did the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say the witr prayer (additional prayer after obligatory prayer at night) in the beginning of the night or at the end? She replied: Sometimes he would say the witr prayer at the beginning of the night and sometimes at the end. I exclaimed: Allah is most Great. All praise be to Allah Who made the matter accommodative. Again I asked her: What do you think, did the Messenger of Allah ﷺ recite the Qur'an (in the prayer) loudly or softly? She replied: Sometimes he would recite loudly and sometimes softly. I exclaimed: Allah is most Great. All praise be to Allah Who made the matter flexible. (Using translation from Abū Dāʾūd 226)"],[5345,"They distracted us on the day of al-Ahzab from ʿAsr prayer, until I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: ʿThey distracted us from the middle prayer, ‘Asr prayer. May Allah fill their graves and houses or stomachs with fire.” (Using translation from Aḥmad 1036)"],[5346,"The Prophet ﷺ \"recited aloud in the eclipse prayer.\""],[5347,"The Prophet ﷺ “prayed for rain, then prayed two rak‘ahs and recited aloud.”"],[5348,"The Prophet ﷺ appointed Ibn Umm Maktum as his deputy over Madinah to lead the people in prayer."],[5349,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ was asked about bitʿ (a beverage made from honey). He said, \"Every intoxicating drink is forbidden.\""],[5350,"The prayer was called one day, and a man approached the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and spoke to him about a need of his for a while into the night until some of the people dozed off."],[5351,"I asked Abu Sa'id al-Khudri about the prayer of the Prophet ﷺ. He said, 'There is no good for you in that.' [He said:] 'The prayer would be established for the Prophet ﷺ, and one of us would go out to al-Baqi' to relieve himself, then come back and perform ablution, and he would find the Messenger of Allah ﷺ still in the first rak'ah of Zuhr.'"],[5352,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to lengthen the first two rak'ahs of Fajr and Zuhr."],[5353,"The Prophet ﷺ was the lightest of people in prayer while still completing it."],[5354,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to recite with us in the first two rak'ahs of Zuhr, and he would lengthen the first and shorten the second."],[5355,"We used to estimate the standing of the Prophet ﷺ in Zuhr and Asr. We estimated his standing in the first two rak'ahs to be about thirty verses, and we estimated his standing in the last two to be half of that. We estimated his standing in the first two rak'ahs of Asr to be about the same as the last two of Zuhr, and we estimated his standing in the last two of Asr to be half of that."],[5356,"I was sitting with Umar b. al-Khattab when some people from the people of Kufah came to him complaining about Sa'd, to the point that they said to him, 'He does not pray well.' He said, 'My experience with him is that he prays well.' So he called him and informed him. Sa'd said, 'As for the prayer of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, I prayed with them, I was deliberate in the first two and quick in the last two.' Umar said, 'That is what was expected of you, Abu Ishaq.' Then he sent someone with him to ask about him in Kufah. He went around with him to the mosques of Kufah and nothing but good was said about him, until he came to the mosque of Banu Abs. There was a man called Abu Sa'dah. He said, 'O Allah, he did not go out on expeditions, did not divide equally, and did not judge justly.' Sa'd became angry and said, 'O Allah, if he is lying, then prolong his life, intensify his poverty, and expose him to trials.' Ibn Umayr claimed that he saw him with his eyebrows fallen over his eyes, impoverished and afflicted, and he would not find anything to ask about. 'How are you, Abu Sa'dah?' He would say, 'An old man, afflicted; the supplication of Sa'd has been answered against me.'"],[5357,"The Prophet ﷺ recited in the year of the conquest and made his voice quaver in his recitation."],[5358,"I prayed with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and he lengthened it until I thought of doing something bad. It was said, 'What did you think of?' He said, 'I thought of sitting down and leaving him.'"],[5359,"When he rose at night, he would sometimes raise his voice, and he mentioned that the Prophet ﷺ used to do that."],[5360,"I prayed with the Prophet ﷺ one night. He did not pass by a verse of mercy but that he paused at it and asked, nor did he pass by a verse of punishment but that he paused at it and sought refuge."],[5361,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to set up a mat as a screen at night and pray facing it, and spread it out during the day and sit on it. The people began to gather around the Prophet ﷺ and pray with his prayer until they became many. He turned to them and said, “O people, take on deeds you can bear, for Allah does not tire until you tire. The most beloved deeds to Allah are those that are consistent, even if little.”"],[5362,"We came with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ at the time of al-Hudaybiyah until we camped at al-Suqya. Mu'adh b. Jabal said: \"Who will give us water?\" He said: \"Jabir.\" So I went out with a group of young men from the Ansar until we came to the water at al-Uthayah, which was nearly twenty-three miles from there, and we drank and drew water. Then, after the night prayer, a man came on a camel that was pulling him toward the water trough. He said to him: \"Lead it to water.\" So he led it, and I took hold of the halter of his mount and made it kneel. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ stood up and prayed the night prayer, with Jabir beside him, and he prayed thirteen prostrations."],[5363,"“I prayed Ẓuhr with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ in Madinah as four [rakʿahs], and I prayed ʿAṣr with him at Dhū al-Ḥulayfah as two [rakʿahs], while he was traveling.”"],[5364,"“The Messenger of Allah ﷺ prayed Ẓuhr in Madinah as four [rakʿahs], and he prayed ʿAṣr at Dhū al-Ḥulayfah as two [rakʿahs].” He said."],[5365,"I asked Anas b. Mālik about shortening the prayer. He said: “When the Messenger of Allah ﷺ went out a distance of three miles or three farsakhs—Shuʿbah was the one who doubted—he would pray two rakʿahs.”"],[5366,"“I prayed Ẓuhr with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ in Madinah as four rakʿahs. Then he set out on one of his journeys, and he prayed for us at the tree as two rakʿahs.”"],[5367,"The Prophet ﷺ stayed at Tabūk for twenty days shortening the prayer."],[5368,"The Prophet ﷺ came to Makkah and stayed there seventeen nights shortening the prayer.” Ibn ʿAbbās said: “Whoever stays seventeen [days] shortens the prayer, and whoever stays more completes it.”"],[5369,"Anas bin Malik said: \" We went out with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ from Al-Madinah to Makkah and he used to lead us in praying two rak'ahs until we came back.\" I (Yahya) said: \"Did he stay in Makkah?\" He (Anas) said: \"Yes, we stayed there for ten days.\" (Using translation from Nasāʾī 1452)"],[5370,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to place his head in the lap of one of us and recite the Quran while she was menstruating."],[5371,"The Prophet ﷺ was not prevented from reciting the Quran by anything except major ritual impurity (janabah)."],[5372,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to remember Allah in all his states."],[5373,"He came to the Prophet ﷺ while he was performing ablution and greeted him, but the Messenger of Allah ﷺ did not return the greeting until he had finished ablution. Then he apologized to him and said, 'I disliked mentioning Allah except in a state of purity' - or he said, 'upon purification.'"],[5374,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ swore an oath of Ila' from his wives, and his foot was dislocated. He stayed in an upper room for twenty-nine days, then came down. They said, \"O Messenger of Allah, you swore an oath for a month.\" He said, \"The month is twenty-nine.\""],[5375,"While I was lying with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ under a velvet cloth, I began to menstruate. I slipped away and took my menstrual garments. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to me: 'Have you started menstruating?' I said: 'Yes.' He called me, and I lay with him under the velvet cloth."],[5376,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ would command one of us, when she was menstruating, to wear an izar, and then he would touch her."],[5377,"He would touch one of his wives while she was menstruating if she had an izar reaching midway down her thighs or to her knees, and she would wrap it around her waist."],[5378,"I used to place the vessel to my mouth while I was menstruating, then hand it to the Prophet ﷺ, and he would put his mouth on the place where my mouth had been. And I would take a bone with meat on it while I was menstruating, then hand it to him, and he would put his mouth on the place where my mouth had been."],[5379,"I was certainly brought a vessel while I was menstruating, and I would drink from it. Then he would take it and place his mouth on the spot where my mouth had been and drink. And I would gnaw on a bone while I was menstruating, and he would take it and place his mouth on the spot where my mouth had been."],[5380,"I would certainly bring the Prophet ﷺ a vessel, and he would take it and drink from it. Then he would take it and place his mouth on the spot where my mouth had been and drink. And I would certainly take a bone with meat on it and eat from it, and he would place his mouth on the spot where my mouth had been and eat from it, while I was menstruating."],[5381,"“He used to wake up in a state of major impurity from his wife, then fast.”"],[5382,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ went around to all his wives in one night with a single ghusl."],[5383,"He used to go around to all his wives in one night and then perform a single ghusl."],[5384,"He used to go around to his wives in an hour of the night or day, and they were eleven. I said to Anas b. Malik, 'Could he manage that?' He said, 'We used to say that he was given the strength of thirty men.'"],[5385,"Every intoxicant is unlawful, and every intoxicant is wine."],[5386,"\"I used to bathe, I and the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, from one vessel, both of us scooping from it together.\""],[5387,"Ayesha narrated, \"I and the Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to perform ablution from the same vessel, and it would overflow. He would then say, 'Leave some for me, leave some for me.'\""],[5388,"\"I heard Al-Qasim narrating that 'Aishah said: 'I used to perform Ghusl, the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and I from a single vessel, from Janabah.'\" (Using translation from Nasāʾī 233)"],[5389,"She said: I and the Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to bathe from a single vessel, our hands alternating in it and meeting."],[5390,"I asked A'ishah: Can a woman bathe with her husband from janabah from the same vessel together? She said: \"Yes, water is purifying and does not become junub. I used to bathe, I and the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, from the same vessel; I would start and pour over his hand before he dipped them into the water.\""],[5391,"Maymunah and the Messenger of Allah ﷺ performed ghusl from a large bowl that had traces of dough in it."],[5392,"She used to bathe, she and the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, from one vessel that held three mudds or close to that."],[5393,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to perform ablution with one mudd and perform ghusl with five mudds."],[5394,"The Prophet ﷺ and Abu Bakr and 'Umar used to «walk in front of the funeral.»"],[5395,"I saw the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and Abu Bakr and 'Umar «walking in front of the funeral.»"],[5396,"'Abd Allah b. 'Umar used to walk in front of the funeral. He said: «The Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to walk in front of it, as did Abu Bakr, 'Umar, and 'Uthman.»"],[5397,"Every drink that intoxicates is unlawful."],[5398,"“By Allah, the Messenger of Allah ﷺ did not pray over Sahl b. Bayda’ except in the mosque.”"],[5399,"When Sa'd died, 'A'ishah said, “Bring him into the mosque so that I may pray over him.” That was objected to, and she said, “By Allah, the Messenger of Allah ﷺ prayed over Ibn Bayda’ in the mosque.”"],[5400,"The Prophet ﷺ prayed over the grave of a woman who had been buried."],[5401,"The Prophet ﷺ prayed over a grave after it had been buried."],[5402,"A man used to cause harm in the mosque, and then he died. The Prophet ﷺ missed him and asked, \"What happened to so-and-so?\" They said, \"He died.\" The Prophet ﷺ replied, \"Why didn't you inform me?\" They seemed to have concealed his matter. He then said to his companions, \"Go and guide me to his grave.\" So, he went and prayed over him and said, \"Verily, these graves are filled with darkness for their inhabitants, but Allah illuminates them for them with my prayers.\""],[5403,"We went out with the Messenger of God ﷺ. When we reached al-Baqi', he came to a grave and asked about it. They said: So-and-so. He recognized her and said: «Would you not have informed me about her?» They said: You were taking a nap and fasting. He said: «Do not do that. Let me not find that any of you has died while I am among you except that you inform me, for my prayer over him is a mercy.» Then he came to the grave, and we lined up behind him, and he said the takbir over it four times."],[5404,"Someone who prayed with the Messenger of God ﷺ over a grave of an abandoned child informed me, and he lined them up behind him."],[5405,"The Prophet ﷺ came to the grave of an abandoned child and prayed over it, and we prayed with him."],[5406,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ prayed over the grave of a man after he had been buried for a night. He stood, he and his Companions, and he had asked about him. They said, 'So-and-so was buried last night,' so they prayed over him."],[5407,"When the Messenger of Allah ﷺ was with a funeral, he would not sit until it was placed in the niche or buried."],[5408,"\"He used to kiss her while he was fasting.\""],[5409,"She used to say, \"If the Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to kiss some of his wives while he was fasting,\" then she laughed."],[5410,"\"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to kiss me while he was fasting.\""],[5411,"\"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to kiss while he was fasting.\""],[5413,"\"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to kiss some of his wives while he was fasting.\" I said to 'A'ishah, \"In obligatory and voluntary fasting?\" 'A'ishah said, \"In all that, in obligatory and voluntary fasting.\""],[5414,"The Prophet ﷺ entered upon me one day and said, \"Do you have anything?\" I said, \"No.\" He said, \"Then I am fasting.\" She said: Then he came to us another day, and I said, \"O Messenger of Allah, some hays (a dish of dates and butter) was gifted to us, and we hid it for you.\" He said, \"Bring it near.\" He had begun the day fasting, then he broke the fast."],[5415,"“He used to wake up in a state of major impurity from his wife, then fast.”"],[5416,"He used to be overtaken by dawn while he was junub from his family, then he would perform ghusl and fast."],[5417,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ set out in the year of the conquest in the month of Ramadan and fasted until he reached al-Kadīd, then he broke his fast. He said, “The Companions of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to follow the most recent of his affairs, the most recent.”"],[5418,"\"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ traveled during Ramadan, and fasting became severe on a man among his companions, so his she-camel began to wander with him under the shade of trees. The Prophet ﷺ was informed, so he ordered him, and he broke his fast. Then the Messenger of Allah ﷺ called for a vessel with water in it and placed it on his hand. When the people saw him drink, they drank.\""],[5419,"\"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ set out from Madinah to Makkah and fasted until he reached ʿUsfān. Then he called for water and raised it to his hand so that the people could see him, and he broke his fast until he arrived in Makkah. That was in Ramadan.\""],[5420,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ set out in the year of the conquest, and he fasted until he reached Kurāʿ al-Ghamīm, and the people fasted. Then he called for a cup of water, raised it so the people saw it, and drank. After that, someone said to him, “Some of the people are still fasting.” He said, “Those are the disobedient ones.”"],[5421,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ would put his head out while he was observing i'tikaf, and I would wash it."],[5422,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ would put his head in to me while he was in the mosque observing i'tikaf, and I would comb it. He would not enter the house except for his need."],[5423,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ prohibited jars, gourds, and pitch-coated vessels."],[5424,"When the Messenger of Allah ﷺ was resident, he would observe i'tikaf during the last ten days of Ramadan. When he traveled, he observed i'tikaf for twenty days the following year."],[5425,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to send sacrificial animals from Madinah, and I would twist the garlands for his sacrificial animals. Then he would not avoid anything that a person in iḥrām avoids."],[5426,"I perfumed the Messenger of Allah ﷺ for his ihram when he intended to enter ihram, and for his exit from ihram before he circumambulated the House."],[5427,"\"I used to perfume the Messenger of Allah ﷺ for his ihram before he entered ihram, and for his exiting ihram before he performed tawaf al-ifadah.\""],[5428,"I perfumed the Messenger of Allah ﷺ when he entered ihram, and I saw the perfume in the parting of his hair after three days while he was in ihram."],[5429,"It is as if I am looking at the glisten of musk in the parting of the hair of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ while he was in iḥrām."],[5430,"It is as if I am looking at the glisten of musk in the parting of the hair of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ while he was reciting the talbiyah."],[5431,"Musk is the finest of perfumes."],[5432,"When Ibn Umar used istijmar (cleaned himself after relieving), he would use plain aloeswood without any added perfume and camphor which he would place with the aloeswood. Then he said: 'This is how the Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to perform istijmar.'"],[5433,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ underwent cupping while he was in ihram."],[5434,"The Prophet ﷺ underwent cupping and gave the cupper his wage."],[5435,"The Prophet ﷺ had cupping done on the two jugular veins and the upper back."],[5436,"The Prophet ﷺ underwent cupping while he was in ihram on the top of his foot due to a pain he had."],[5437,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ underwent cupping at Lahy Jamal on the road to Makkah while he was in ihram, in the middle of his head."],[5438,"Anas b. Malik performed Hajj on a pack-saddle and he was not miserly, and he reported that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ performed Hajj on a pack-saddle, and it was his riding camel."],[5439,"“The Messenger of Allah ﷺ forbade wearing qassī and safflower-dyed garments, wearing gold rings, and reciting while bowing.”"],[5440,"The Prophet ﷺ entered Makkah with a helmet on his head."],[5441,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ entered Makkah in the year of the conquest with a helmet on his head."],[5442,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ entered Makkah with a helmet on his head. When he took it off, it was said: \"This is Ibn Khatal clinging to the curtains of the Ka'bah.\" He said: \"Kill him.\""],[5443,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said on the day of the conquest of Makkah: \"This land is sacred; Allah has made it sacred until the Day of Resurrection. Its game may not be startled, its thorns may not be cut, its lost items may not be picked up except by one who announces them, and its fresh grass may not be uprooted.\" Al-'Abbas said: \"Except idhkhir, for it is used in their houses.\" He said: \"Except idhkhir. And there is no migration, but there is jihad and intention; and if you are called to march, march forth.\""],[5444,"The Prophet ﷺ entered Makkah on the day of the conquest with a helmet on his head. They said: \"O Messenger of Allah, Ibn Khatal is clinging to the curtains of the Ka'bah.\" He said: \"Kill him.\" So he was killed."],[5445,"The Prophet ﷺ entered in the year of the conquest with a white banner."],[5446,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ entered on the day of the conquest of Makkah wearing a black turban."],[5447,"“The Messenger of Allah ﷺ entered Makkah on the day of the conquest wearing a black turban.”"],[5448,"He heard al-Dahhak b. Qays during the Hajj of Mu'awiyah b. Abi Sufyan saying: “No one gives a legal opinion permitting tamattu' with Umrah to Hajj except one who is ignorant of the command of Allah, Mighty and Exalted.” Sa'd b. Abi Waqqas said to him: “What a bad thing you have said, O son of my brother! By Allah, the Messenger of Allah ﷺ did it, and we did it with him.”"],[5449,"We set out with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ when five nights remained of Dhul-Qa'dah. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ commanded that whoever had circumambulated the House should exit ihram, unless he had driven a sacrificial animal. She ('A'ishah) said, \"And beef was brought to us, so I said, 'What is this?' They said, 'The Messenger of Allah ﷺ slaughtered on behalf of his wives.'\""],[5450,"I used to twist the garlands of sheep for the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and he would send them and remain in a lawful state."],[5451,"«The Messenger of Allah ﷺ commanded trimming the mustaches and letting the beards grow.»"],[5452,"“He combined Hajj and Umrah, performed for them one seven-fold circumambulation (Tawaf), and one circuit (Sa'i) between Safa and Marwah, and said: ‘This is how I saw the Messenger of Allah ﷺ do.’”"],[5453,"\"When the Messenger of Allah ﷺ arrived in Makkah, he did ramal ﷺ.\""],[5454,"I entered upon Ibn 'Abbas and said, \"O Ibn 'Abbas, your people claim that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ did ramal and that it is a sunnah.\" He said, \"They have spoken truth and they have lied. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ did ramal, but it is not a sunnah.\" Then he said, \"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ arrived while the polytheists were on Qu'ayqi'an, and they had been saying that the companions of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ were weak and exhausted. So the Messenger of Allah ﷺ commanded them to do ramal to show them that they had strength.\""],[5455,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ performed tawaf around the House on his mount, touching the Corner with a staff."],[5456,"The Prophet ﷺ performed tawaf on his mount, and when we came to the Corner he pointed to it."],[5457,"That he touched the Stone, then kissed his hand and said, \"I have not left it since I saw the Messenger of Allah ﷺ kissing it.\""],[5458,"I complained to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ that I was ill. He said: \"Perform tawaf behind the people while riding.\" She said: So I did so."],[5459,"“The Prophet ﷺ drank water during Tawaf.”"],[5460,"“I gave the Messenger of Allah ﷺ water from Zamzam, and he drank it while standing.”"],[5461,"“When the Prophet ﷺ arrived in Makkah, he commanded them to exit the state of iḥrām except those who had sacrificial animals with them. He said: And the Messenger of Allah ﷺ slaughtered with his own hand seven camels while they were standing.”"],[5463,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ sent me with the heavy baggage from Jamʿ at night."],[5464,"I heard Ibn Abbas saying, \"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ sent me on a mission at night.\""],[5465,"“I performed the Farewell Ḥajj with the Prophet ﷺ, and I saw Usāmah and Bilāl, one of them holding the halter of the Prophet’s ﷺ she-camel and the other raising his garment to shade him from the heat until he threw the pebbles at Jamrat al-ʿAqabah.”"],[5466,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said on the morning of ʿAqabah, while he was standing on his mount, “Bring me some pebbles.” So I picked up pebbles for him, which were pebbles for khudhaf. When I placed them in his hand, he said, “Yes, with the likes of these, with the likes of these. Beware of extremism in religion, for those before you were destroyed only by extremism in religion.”"],[5467,"I saw the Messenger of Allah ﷺ addressing the people on the day of Eid on a she-camel of his with a slit ear, while an Abyssinian was holding its halter."],[5468,"When the Messenger of Allah ﷺ threw the pebbles and sacrificed his offering, he handed the barber the right side of his head, and he shaved it. Then he handed it to Abū Ṭalḥa al-Anṣārī and gave it to him. Then he handed him the left side and said, \"Shave it.\" He shaved it and gave it to Abū Ṭalḥa, and he said, \"Distribute it among the people.\""],[5469,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ slaughtered a cow on behalf of his wives."],[5470,"“The Prophet ﷺ drove with him one hundred camels. When he came to the place of sacrifice, he slaughtered sixty-three with his own hand, then he gave [the rest] to ʿAlī, who slaughtered what remained of them.”"],[5471,"“The Prophet ﷺ ordered that a piece be taken from each slaughtered camel, placed in a cooking pot. They ate from the meat and sipped from the broth.”"],[5472,"\"I perfumed the Messenger of Allah ﷺ at Minā before he visited the House.\""],[5473,"He used to depart on the Day of Sacrifice, then return and pray the noon prayer at Minā. It is mentioned that the Prophet ﷺ used to do that."],[5474,"\"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ departed on the Day of Sacrifice, then returned and prayed the noon prayer at Minā.\""],[5475,"\"That the Messenger of Allah ﷺ prayed the Dhuhr, Asr, Maghrib, and Isha prayers, then lay down to sleep in Mina. He then mounted his ride and headed towards the Kaaba, circumambulated it.\""],[5476,"The Prophet of Allah ﷺ performed four 'umrahs, all in Dhu al-Qa'dah: the 'Umrah of al-Hudaybiyah in Dhu al-Qa'dah, an 'Umrah the following year in Dhu al-Qa'dah, an 'Umrah from al-Ji'ranah when he distributed the spoils of Hunayn in Dhu al-Qa'dah, and an 'Umrah with his Hajj."],[5477,"“The Prophet ﷺ performed four ʿumrahs: the ʿumrah of al-Ḥudaybiyah, the ʿumrah of al-Qaḍāʾ in the following year, the ʿumrah of al-Jiʿrānah, and his ʿumrah that was with his ḥajj.”"],[5478,"Regarding His saying {A declaration of immunity from Allah and His Messenger}, he said, \"When the Messenger of Allah ﷺ returned from Hunayn, he performed Umrah from al-Ji'ranah, then he appointed Abu Bakr over that Hajj.\""],[5479,"«The Messenger of Allah ﷺ commanded trimming the mustaches and letting the beards grow.»"],[5480,"The Prophet ﷺ sought to excuse Abu Bakr regarding Aishah, and the Prophet ﷺ did not think that Abu Bakr would do to her what he did. Abu Bakr raised his hand and slapped her, and struck her chest. The Prophet ﷺ felt distressed at that and said, 'O Abu Bakr, I will never ask you to excuse her after this.'"],[5481,"\"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ divorced Hafsah then took her back.\""],[5482,"Umar entered upon Hafsah while she was weeping, and he said, \"What makes you weep? Perhaps the Messenger of Allah ﷺ has divorced you. He had divorced you once and taken you back because of me. By Allah, if he has divorced you, I will never speak to you again.\""],[5483,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ married her in Shawwal and consummated the marriage with her in Shawwal. So which of his wives was more favored with him?"],[5484,"The Prophet ﷺ was brought infants and he would perform taḥnīk on them. A baby boy was brought, and he urinated on him, so he followed it with water and did not wash it."],[5485,"I brought a son of mine who had not yet eaten solid food to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and he urinated on him. He called for water and sprinkled it on him."],[5486,"I brought a brother of mine to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ to have him chew on a date and rub it on the infant's palate, and I found him in the animal enclosure branding sheep—Shuʿbah said: My predominant thought is that he said: on their ears."],[5488,"Abu Hind performed cupping on the Prophet ﷺ on the fontanelle. The Prophet ﷺ said: \"O company of the Ansar, marry Abu Hind, and marry into his family.\" And he said: \"If there is any good in what you treat with, then it is cupping.\""],[5489,"«The Messenger of Allah ﷺ commanded trimming the mustaches and letting the beards grow.»"],[5490,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ raced the trained horses from al-Ḥafyāʾ to Thaniyyat al-Wadāʿ, and between them was six miles, and the untrained ones from Thaniyyat al-Wadāʿ to the mosque of Banū Zurayq, and between them was one mile. I was among those who raced."],[5491,"The Prophet ﷺ raced me and I beat him. We waited until, when I had gained weight, he raced me and beat me. The Prophet ﷺ said, 'This makes up for that.'"],[5492,"«The Prophet ﷺ sold a mudabbar slave.»"],[5493,"A man from the Ansar freed a slave of his, and he had no wealth other than him. This reached the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and he said, 'Who will buy him from me?' Nu'aym b. 'Abd Allah al-Nahham bought him for eight hundred dirhams and handed them to him. Jabir said, 'He was a Coptic slave who died in the first year.'"],[5494,"A man from the Ansar called Abu Madhkur made a slave of his a mudabbar. This reached the Prophet ﷺ, and he said, 'Does he have any other wealth?' They said, 'No.' He said, 'Who will buy him from me?' Nu'aym al-Nahham bought him for eight hundred dirhams. The Prophet ﷺ said, 'Spend it on yourself first; if there is any surplus, then on your relatives; if there is any surplus, then here and here.'"],[5495,"Abu Madhkur made a slave of his a mudabbar, then he fell into need, so the Prophet ﷺ sold him and said: \"When one of you is in need, let him begin with himself; if there is surplus, then for his family; if there is surplus, then for his relatives.\""],[5496,"A Persian man was a neighbor of the Prophet ﷺ, and his broth was the best smelling thing. He prepared food, then came to the Prophet ﷺ and gestured to him to come. 'A'ishah was beside him. He ﷺ said: “And this one with me,” and pointed to 'A'ishah. He said: No. He said: Then he gestured to him again, and he said: “And this one with me.” He said: No. Then he gestured to him a third time, and he said: “And this one with me,” and pointed to 'A'ishah. He said: Yes."],[5497,"A man prepared food and sent for the Prophet ﷺ, saying, \"Come to me, you and five others.\" He then sent to him, \"Will you permit a sixth?\""],[5498,"One of my paternal uncles prepared food for the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and said: I would love for you to eat in my house and pray in it. So the Messenger of Allah ﷺ came to him, and there was a stallion of those stallions in the house. He ordered a side of it, and it was swept, then sprinkled with water, and he prayed, and we prayed with him."],[5499,"We went on seven or six military expeditions with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ—Shu'bah was unsure—and we used to eat locusts with him."],[5500,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ fed us horse meat and forbade us donkey meat."],[5501,"I was with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ when he passed by a cooking pot belonging to some of his family, in which meat was being cooked. One of them handed him a shoulder from it, and he ate it while standing. Then he prayed and did not perform ablution."],[5502,"Bread and meat were brought to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and he ate it. Then he called for water for wudu' and prayed Zuhr. Then he called for the leftovers of his food and ate, then prayed 'Asr without performing wudu'."],[5503,"A woman from the Ansar invited us, slaughtered a sheep, prepared food, and spread a mat for us. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ called for water for purification and performed wudu', then prayed. Then we brought the leftover food, and he ate it, and the Messenger of Allah ﷺ prayed and did not perform wudu'."],[5504,"We were with Abu Musa al-Ash'ari, and he called for a table on which there was chicken meat, and he said, 'I saw the Messenger of Allah ﷺ eat from it.'"],[5505,"We were with Talhah b. 'Ubayd Allah while we were in ihram, and a bird was gifted to us while Talhah was asleep. Some of us ate and some of us refrained out of scrupulousness. When Talhah woke up, he agreed with those who ate it and said, 'We ate it with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ.'"],[5506,"A tailor in Madinah invited the Messenger of Allah ﷺ to barley bread and stale fat, and there was gourd in it. Anas said: I used to see the Prophet ﷺ liking gourd. He said: So I used to place it before him, and gourd has continued to please me since I saw him ﷺ liking it."],[5507,"Sahl said: \"We used to pray with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ on Friday, then there was the midday rest. There was a woman among us who had a farm where she grew chard. Every Friday, she would pull up the chard roots, put them in a pot, then add a handful of barley that she had ground. The chard became like a broth.\" Sahl said: \"After the Friday prayer we would go to her, greet her, and she would bring that food to us, and we would lap it up.\" He said: \"We used to look forward to Friday for that food of hers.\""],[5508,"The Prophet ﷺ was brought a cheese from Tabuk. He called for a knife, said \"Bismillah,\" and cut it."],[5509,"He met Zayd b. 'Amr b. Nufayl at the lower part of Baldah. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ offered him a leather mat with food on it, but he refused to eat and said: \"We do not eat from what you slaughter on your stone altars, and we eat only from that over which the name of Allah has been mentioned.\""],[5510,"We entered upon Abu Musa while a chicken was before him, and he was eating from it. We said: You are eating from it? He said: I ate it on the table of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ."],[5511,"Umm Hufayd, my maternal aunt bint al-Harith, gifted the Messenger of Allah ﷺ clarified butter, dried curd, and dabb lizards. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ called for them and ate on his table, but left them as if he found them repulsive. Had they been forbidden, they would not have been eaten on the table of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, nor would he have ordered them to be eaten."],[5512,"The Prophet ﷺ entered upon her and drank from the mouth of a water-skin while standing, so she got up and cut it, and kept it."],[5513,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ drank Zamzam water while standing."],[5514,"He hobbled the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and he hobbled a mouthful he spat from a bucket in a well in their home."],[5515,"I entered upon the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and saw him reclining on a cushion on his left."],[5516,"\"He used to breathe three times into the vessel.\""],[5517,"When the Messenger of Allah ﷺ drank, he would breathe three times, and he said, \"It is more wholesome, more healing, and more satisfying.\""],[5518,"\"Sweet water was sought for him from the houses of Suqya.\""],[5519,"\"We used to make nabidh for the Messenger of God ﷺ in a water skin tied at the top. We would make it in the morning and he would drink it in the evening, and we would make it in the evening and he would drink it in the morning.\""],[5520,"People came to him and asked him about nabidh. He said, \"The Prophet of God ﷺ went on a journey and returned from it, and some of his companions had made nabidh in green jars, hollowed-out stumps, and gourds. He ordered them to be poured out. Then he ordered a water skin, and raisins and water were put in it. Nabidh was made for him at night, and he would drink it that day and the coming night, and the next day until evening. When evening came, he drank and gave others to drink, and if any remained in the morning, he ordered it to be poured out.\""],[5521,"The Messenger of God ﷺ, when he did not find anything to make nabidh in, it was made for him in a stone trough."],[5522,"\"Now then, O people, the prohibition of wine has come down. It is from five things: grapes, dates, honey, wheat, and barley. Wine is what covers the mind.\""],[5523,"The Messenger of God ﷺ called a man from the Ansar to his side while water was in a well. He said, \"Do you have water that has spent the night in an old water skin? Otherwise we will drink directly from this.\" Water was brought and milk was milked into it, and he drank."],[5524,"The Prophet ﷺ entered upon a man of the Ansar, accompanied by a companion. The Prophet ﷺ and his companion greeted, and the man responded, saying: “May my father and mother be your ransom! At such a hot hour!” He said to him: “If you have water that has stood overnight in a waterskin, give it to us to drink; otherwise we will drink directly with our mouths.” The man was diverting water in his garden. He said: “By Allah, O Messenger of Allah, I do have water that has stood overnight. Come to the arbor.” He led them to an arbor, poured water into a cup, then milked over it from a domestic animal of his. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ drank, then he returned to it and the man who had come with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ drank."],[5525,"He used to combine watermelon with fresh dates."],[5526,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to eat watermelon with fresh dates."],[5527,"He used to eat cooked food or watermelon with fresh dates."],[5528,"The Prophet ﷺ took the hand of a leper and placed it with his own in the dish, and said: 'Eat in the name of Allah, with confidence in Allah and reliance upon Him.'"],[5529,"The Prophet of Allah ﷺ used to like sweets and honey."],[5531,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to eat with three fingers, then lick them."],[5532,"He forbade az-zur (false speech).”"],[5533,"They were eating dates on a shield, and the Prophet ﷺ passed by us. We said: 'Come.' He came forward and ate with us from the dates, and he did not touch water."],[5534,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ kissed al-Hasan b. Ali while al-Aqra' b. Habis al-Tamimi was sitting. Al-Aqra' said: 'I have ten children and I have never kissed any of them.' The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: 'Whoever does not show mercy will not be shown mercy.'"],[5535,"The Prophet ﷺ visited a sick Jewish boy."],[5536,"A Jewish boy used to serve the Prophet ﷺ, and he fell ill. The Prophet ﷺ came to visit him and said, \"Accept Islam.\" He looked at his father who was sitting near his head, and his father said, \"Obey Abū al-Qāsim.\" So he accepted Islam. The Prophet ﷺ then left, saying, \"Praise be to Allah who saved him from the Fire.\""],[5537,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to campaign with us, and with him were women from the Ansar. We provided water and treated the wounded."],[5538,"The Prophet ﷺ said to Abu Talhah, \"Find me a boy from your boys to serve me until I reach Khaybar.\" Abu Talhah went out with me riding behind him, and I was a boy nearing puberty. I served the Messenger of Allah ﷺ whenever he dismounted."],[5539,"“I indeed led the Prophet of Allah ﷺ, al-Ḥasan, and al-Ḥusayn on his gray mule until I brought them into the Prophet’s ﷺ room—this one in front of him and this one behind him.”"],[5540,"On the Day of Badr, they had one camel for every three men. The two companions of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ were 'Ali and Abu Lubabah. When the Prophet's ﷺ turn to ride came, they would say, 'Ride, and we will walk.' The Prophet ﷺ would say, 'You two are not stronger than me, and I am not less in need of the reward than you two.'"],[5541,"«We ate dried meat with the Prophet of Allah ﷺ on the way to Madinah.»"],[5542,"«We were with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, taking provisions of the meat of sacrificial animals to Madinah.»"],[5543,"The Prophet ﷺ used to love our food. He came to us one day and said, \"Do you have any of that?\" I said, \"No.\" He said, \"I am fasting.\""],[5544,"While the Messenger of Allah ﷺ was walking while fasting, he said to one of his companions, \"Go and prepare some food.\" The companion replied, \"O Messenger of Allah, if you wish, I can prepare it for you.\" The Prophet said, \"No, go and prepare it for me.\" So, the companion went and prepared some food and the Prophet drank it. Then he said, \"When you see the night coming from this direction (pointing towards the east), the fasting person should break their fast.\""],[5545,"While we were traveling with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ through parts of al-Rawha' in a state of ihram, there was a wounded donkey. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: 'Leave it, for its owner will soon come to it.' A man from Bahz, the one who had wounded the donkey, came and said: 'O Messenger of Allah, this donkey is yours to dispose of.' The Messenger of Allah ﷺ ordered Abu Bakr to divide it among the people."],[5546,"When the Messenger of Allah ﷺ married me, he said, “I had gifted to the Negus a garment and some ounces of musk, and I do not think he has died and the gift will be returned. If that is the case, then it is for you.” She said, “It happened as the Prophet ﷺ said: the Negus died and the gift was returned. The Prophet ﷺ gave to each of his wives an ounce of musk, and gave the garment and the rest of the musk to Umm Salamah.”"],[5547,"'Umar b. al-Khattab went out and saw a silk brocade suit being sold in the market. He came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and said: 'O Messenger of Allah, buy it and wear it on Friday and when delegations come to you.' The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: 'Only one who has no share in the Hereafter wears this.' Then the Messenger of Allah ﷺ was brought three suits from it, and he gave one to 'Umar, one to 'Ali, and one to Usama. 'Umar came to him and said: 'O Messenger of Allah, you said what you said about it, then you sent one to me.' He said: 'Sell it and meet your need with its price, or cut it into head covers for your women.'"],[5548,"Ubayd Allah b. Jahsh emigrated with Umm Habibah bt. Abi Sufyan—and she was his wife—to the land of Abyssinia. When he arrived in the land of Abyssinia, he fell ill. When death was near, he bequeathed to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ married Umm Habibah, and the Negus sent Shurahbil b. Hasanah with her."],[5549,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ came to us, and my wife called out to him, saying, “O Messenger of Allah, invoke blessings upon me and upon my husband.” He said, “May Allah bless you and your husband.”"],[5550,"A slave girl was given in marriage, then she fell ill and her hair fell out, so they wanted to attach hair to her hair. They mentioned that to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and he said: \"May Allah curse the one who attaches hair extensions and the one who has them attached and the one who asks for that.\""],[5551,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ would stick out his tongue for al-Husayn, and the boy would see the redness of his tongue and become excited toward it. Uyaynah b. Hisn b. Badr said to him: 'Do I see you doing this with this one? By Allah, I have a son whose face has grown hair and I have never kissed him.' The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: 'Whoever does not show mercy will not be shown mercy.'"],[5552,"A man stood up to the Prophet ﷺ and said: Where is my father? He said: \"In the Fire.\" When he turned away, he called him and said ﷺ: \"Indeed my father and your father are in the Fire.\""],[5553,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ ordered me, so I brought him the daughter of Zaynab while her soul was rattling as if it were in a waterskin. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: 'To Allah belongs what He takes, and to Him belongs what He gives, and everything has an appointed term.' He said: 'His eyes shed tears.' Sa'd b. 'Ubadah said to him: 'O Messenger of Allah, do you weep? Did you not forbid weeping?' The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: 'This is only a mercy that Allah has placed in the hearts of His servants. Allah has mercy on only the merciful among His servants.'"],[5554,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ seated me behind him and said: \"Do you have any poetry of Umayyah b. Abi al-Salt?\" I said: \"Yes.\" He said: \"Recite.\" So I recited a verse to him, and he said: \"Recite.\" Then I recited to him, and he kept saying \"Recite\" and I kept reciting until I completed a hundred verses."],[5555,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ sacrificed two salt-and-white rams with horns. He pronounced the name of Allah and said Allahu Akbar. I saw him slaughter them with his own hand, placing his foot on their sides."],[5556,"When he wanted to sleep while in a state of major impurity, he would perform ablution as he did for prayer before sleeping.”"],[5557,"“We were with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ compiling the Qur’an from parchments.”"],[5558,"I was with Abu Hurayrah, and he said to al-Hasan b. Ali: 'Show me the place where I saw the Messenger of Allah ﷺ kiss you.' So he uncovered his navel and he kissed it."],[5559,"I came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ with a group from Muzaynah and we pledged allegiance to him, and his buttons were undone. I put my hand into the opening of his shirt and touched the seal. I never saw Mu'awiyah or his father, in winter or summer, but that their lower garments were loose, never fastened."],[5560,"I saw Ibn 'Umar praying with his buttons unfastened. I asked him about that, and he said, \"I saw the Messenger of Allah ﷺ praying like that.\""],[5561,"\"I saw the Messenger of Allah ﷺ come to a people's rubbish dump and urinate standing, then he called for water, performed ablution and wiped over his leather socks.\""],[5562,"\"The Prophet ﷺ came to a people's rubbish dump and urinated standing. I approached him until I was at his heels and poured water for him, so he performed ablution and wiped over his leather socks.\""],[5563,"I was walking with the Prophet ﷺ when he stopped at a people's rubbish dump and urinated standing. I moved away, but he called me and said, \"Come closer.\" I came closer until I stood at his heels. Then he performed ablution and wiped over his leather socks.\""],[5564,"Abu Musa was strict about urine and said, \"When urine touched the skin of any of the Children of Israel, they would cut it off with scissors.\" Hudhayfah said, \"I wish your companion would not be so strict. I saw myself walking with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ when he came to a people's rubbish dump behind a wall and stood as one of you would stand and urinated. I hid from him, but he gestured to me, so I came and stood at his heels until he finished.\""],[5565,"«The Messenger of Allah ﷺ set a time limit for wiping over the two khuffs: three days and their nights for the traveler, and a day and a night for the resident.»"],[5566,"\"Whoever tells you that the Prophet of Allah ﷺ urinated standing, do not believe him. I saw him urinating sitting.\""],[5567,"The Prophet ﷺ prayed over the grave of so-and-so and said the takbir four times."],[5568,"\"We went with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ to Al-Baqi, and he saw a new grave, so we stood behind it and performed the funeral prayer four times.\""],[5569,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ came to an abandoned grave and prayed over it, and we prayed with him."],[5570,"Indeed, a brother of yours has died, so stand and pray over him. He said: So we lined up behind him in two rows."],[5571,"It was narrated from Ibn ‘Umar that the Prophet ﷺ offered the funeral prayer for Najashi and said four Takbir. (Using translation from Ibn Mājah 1538)"],[5572,"A man asked the Prophet ﷺ: \"Should I pray in the garment in which I have intercourse with my wife?\" He said, \"Yes, unless you see something on it, then wash it.\""],[5573,"Umar mentioned to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ that he becomes junub at night, so he ordered him to perform ablution and wash his private part, then sleep."],[5574,"I said: O Messenger of Allah, I am often out hunting and I pray with nothing on but a single shirt. He said: 'Fasten it, even with a thorn.'"],[5575,"That the Prophet ﷺ passed by a rope stretched between two pillars in the mosque and said, \"What is this rope?\" They said, \"So-and-so prays, and when she fears being overcome, she holds onto it.\" The Prophet ﷺ said, \"Let her pray as long as she is alert; when she is overcome, let her sleep.\""],[5576,"Hind came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and said, \"Abu Sufyan is tight-fisted with me and my child. May I take from his wealth without his knowledge?\" He said, \"Take from his wealth in a reasonable manner without his knowledge.\""],[5577,"We used to perform incantations in the pre-Islamic period, so we said: O Messenger of Allah, what do you say about that? He said: 'Show me your incantations. There is no harm in incantations as long as they do not involve shirk.'"],[5578,"When the Jews greet you, one of them merely says, \"May death be upon you (al-sām ʿalayk)\"; so say, \"And upon you.\""],[5579,"Abu Qatada belonged to a group of prohibited people while he himself was permissible. He offered his companions a wild donkey but they did not give permission to slaughter it until they had seen it. While he was sitting, he secretly took a whip from one of them and struck the animal with it until he killed it. Then he brought it to them and they ate from it and carried some with them. They went to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and asked him about it. He said, \"Did anyone of you indicate to it?\" They said, \"No.\" He said, \"Then eat it.\""],[5580,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ set out for Makkah. When he was at al-Rawha', there was a wounded wild donkey. It was mentioned to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and he said: 'Leave it, for its owner will soon come.' Its owner, a man from Bahz, came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and said: 'O Messenger of Allah, this donkey is yours to dispose of.' The Messenger of Allah ﷺ ordered Abu Bakr to divide it among the traveling companions. Then he continued until he was at al-Uthaya, between al-Ruwaytha and al-'Arj, where there was a gazelle crouching in the shade with an arrow in it. It is claimed that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ ordered a man to stand by it so that no one would disturb it until he passed it."],[5581,"Do not fast until you see the crescent, and do not break your fast until you see it, unless it is obscured for you; and if it is obscured, then estimate it."],[5582,"«Whoever swears an oath and then sees something better than it, let him do what is better and expiate his oath.»"],[5583,"that he said to ʿAbdullāh b. ʿUmar: \"Indeed, we find the prayer of the resident and the prayer of fear in the Quran, but we do not find the prayer of travel in the Quran?\" So ʿAbdullāh said to him: \"O son of my brother, indeed Allah sent Muhammad ﷺ to us and we do not know anything, so we only do as we have seen him do.\""],[5584,"The Prophet ﷺ stayed at Tabūk for twenty days shortening the prayer."],[5585,"The Prophet ﷺ prayed Zuhr in Madinah as four [rakʿahs] and prayed ʿAṣr at Dhū al-Ḥulayfah as two [rakʿahs]."],[5586,"«The Messenger of Allah ﷺ made wiping over the two khuffs three days for the traveler and a day and a night for the resident; and had the questioner continued his questioning, he would have made it five.»"],[5587,"A bedouin asked the Prophet ﷺ about wiping, and he said, «For the traveler, three days and their nights; and for the resident, a day and a night.»"],[5588,"Jarir b. Abdullah urinated, then performed wudu and wiped over his two khuffs. Someone said to him, “Do you do this?” He replied, “What prevents me when I have seen the Messenger of Allah ﷺ doing it?”"],[5589,"I came to Ṣafwān b. ʿAssāl al-Murādī and said, “There is something itching in my mind about wiping over the two khuffs. Have you heard the Prophet ﷺ mention anything about wiping over the two khuffs?” He said, “Yes. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ commanded us, when we were travelling or on a journey, not to remove or take off our khuffs for three days and their nights, except for janabah, whether from defecation or urination.”"],[5590,"While we were with the Prophet ﷺ in a cave, {By those sent forth in succession} was revealed to him. He was reciting it, and I was receiving it from his mouth while his mouth was still moist with it. Suddenly a snake leapt upon us. The Prophet ﷺ said, \"Kill it!\" We rushed at it, but it got away. The Prophet ﷺ said, \"It was protected from your evil as you were protected from its evil.\""],[5591,"A man became junub in winter and asked, and he was ordered to wash, and he died. That was mentioned to the Prophet ﷺ, and he said, “What is wrong with them? They killed him; may Allah kill them, three times. Allah has made clean earth, or tayammum, a purifier.”"],[5592,"\"Hand me the khumrah from the mosque.\" I said: \"I am menstruating.\" He said: \"Your menstruation is not in your hand.\""],[5593,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to me: \"Hand me the khumrah.\" She said: I said: \"I am menstruating.\" He said: \"It is not in your hand.\" So I handed it to him."],[5594,"A bedouin came to the Prophet ﷺ and said: 'Do you kiss children? We do not kiss them.' The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: 'What can I do for you if Allah has removed mercy from your heart?'"],[5595,"A man entered the mosque after the Messenger of Allah ﷺ had prayed. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, \"Is there any man who will give charity to this man by praying with him?\""],[5596,"The Prophet ﷺ prayed with his companions, then a man came. The Prophet of Allah ﷺ said, \"Who will give charity to this man and pray with him?\""],[5597,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to Fatima bt. Qays, \"Go to Umm Sharik, and do not let us miss out on you.\""],[5598,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ liked these date-palm stalks and would hold them in his hand. He entered the mosque with a stick from them in his hand and scraped with it, meaning some spittle in the qiblah of the mosque. He forbade a man from spitting in front of him or to his right and said, “Let him spit to his left or under his left foot. If he is overtaken by haste, let him put it into his garment and do thus with it.”"],[5599,"“The Messenger of Allah ﷺ prohibited sleeping before it and talking after it.”"],[5600,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to bring out the virgins, the secluded women, and the menstruating women on the day of Eid. As for the menstruating women, they kept away from the prayer place and witnessed the good and the supplication of the Muslims. One of them said, 'What if one of us has no jilbab?' He said, 'Let her lend her jilbab to her.'"],[5601,"When one of you is praying, he should not let anyone pass in front of him. If he refuses, then he should fight him, for indeed a qarin (companion devil) is with him."],[5602,"A man wanted to marry a woman from the Ansar, and the Prophet ﷺ said to him, \"Look at her, for there is something in the eyes of the Ansar.\""],[5603,"Kill snakes and the one with two stripes and the short-tailed one, for they efface the sight and cause miscarriage. Abdullah used to kill all snakes until Abu Lubabah saw him chasing a snake and said: He forbade the house snakes."],[5604,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ passed by a man lying on his belly and nudged him with his foot, saying: “This is a lying posture that Allah does not love.”"],[5605,"Sa'd b. 'Ubadah asked the Messenger of Allah ﷺ about a vow his mother had made, then she died before fulfilling it. He said, \"Fulfill it on her behalf.\""],[5606,"The Prophet ﷺ was with some of his companions, among them Sa'd, when the meat of a dhabb was brought. A woman from among the wives of the Prophet ﷺ said: 'It is the meat of a dhabb.' The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: 'Eat, for it is lawful, but it is not a food I eat.'"],[5607,"“Narrate from the Children of Israel, and there is no blame. And narrate from me, but do not lie about me.”"],[5608,"'Umar vowed to perform i'tikaf for one night in the Sacred Mosque during the pre-Islamic era, so the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to him: \"Fulfill your vow.\""],[5609,"\"O Messenger of Allah, may Allah's blessings be upon you, I vowed to perform i'tikaf for one night in the Sacred Mosque during the pre-Islamic era.\" The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"Then fulfill your vow.\""],[5610,"A woman should not have skin-to-skin contact with a woman, nor a man with a man, except a parent with a child."],[5611,"\"He forbade selling fruit for fruit, and he permitted an 'ariyya to be sold for its estimated amount. An 'ariyya is that which its owners eat fresh.\""],[5612,"I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ when he was asked about dry dates for fresh dates. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, \"Does fresh dates decrease when they dry?\" He said, \"Yes.\" So he forbade him from that."],[5613,"\"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ permitted 'araya for their estimated amount.\""],[5614,"He \"permitted the sale of 'araya for their estimated amount.\""],[5615,"\"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ permitted the sale of 'araya for less than five wasqs or five wasqs.\""],[5616,"I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ when he permitted 'araya to be sold for their estimated amount, saying, \"A wasq, two wasqs, three, and four.\""],[5617,"\"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ permitted the sale of 'araya and did not permit anything other than that.\""],[5618,"The heat is from the blaze of Hell, so delay the prayer until it is cooler."],[5619,"We were praying Zuhr with the Messenger of Allah at the time of intense heat (i.e., midday when the sun has just passed its zenith) and he said to us, \"Wait for it to cool down before you pray, for intense heat is from the flaring up of the Hell-fire.\" (Using translation from Ibn Mājah 680)"],[5620,"A woman should not have skin-to-skin contact with a woman, nor a man with a man, except a parent with a child."],[5621,"I said to Ata, “Which time do you prefer for me to pray the Atamah, whether as an imam or alone?” He said, “I heard Ibn Abbas say: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ delayed the Atamah until the people had slept, woken up, slept again, and woken up. Then Umar said, ‘The prayer!’ So the Messenger of Allah ﷺ came out, and it is as if I can see him now with water dripping from his head, placing his hands on his head. He said, ‘Were it not that I would make things difficult for my Ummah, I would have commanded them to pray like this.’”"],[5622,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ delayed the Isha prayer one night. Umar b. al-Khattab came and said, ‘O Messenger of Allah, the prayer! The women and children have fallen asleep.’ The Messenger of Allah ﷺ came out with water dripping from his head, saying, ‘Were it not that I would make things difficult for the believers, I would have commanded them to pray this prayer at this time.’"],[5623,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to delay the later Isha prayer."],[5624,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ delayed the Isha prayer—which is called the Atamah—one night. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ did not come out until Umar b. al-Khattab said, ‘The women and children have fallen asleep.’ Then the Messenger of Allah ﷺ came out and said to the people in the mosque when he came out to them, ‘No one on earth is waiting for it except you.’ And that was before Islam had spread widely among the people."],[5625,"We stayed one night waiting for the Messenger of Allah ﷺ for the Isha al-Akhirah. He came out to us when a third of the night had passed or after it. When he came out, he said, ‘You are waiting for a prayer that no people of any religion other than you are waiting for. Were it not that it would be burdensome for my Ummah, I would have prayed this prayer with them at this hour.’ Then he ordered the mu’adhdhin, who gave the iqamah, and then he prayed."],[5626,"They said to Anas b. Malik, ‘Did the Messenger of Allah ﷺ have a ring?’ He said, ‘The Messenger of Allah ﷺ delayed the Isha prayer one night until half the night had passed. Then he came and said, “The people have prayed, and you will continue to be in prayer as long as you are waiting for the prayer.”’ Anas said, ‘It is as if I can see the glint of his silver ring.’ He said, and Anas raised his left hand."],[5627,"“Were it not that I would make things difficult for my Ummah, I would have commanded them to use the siwak with every wudu and would have delayed the Isha prayer until one-third of the night or half the night.”"],[5628,"“Were it not that I would make things difficult for my Ummah, I would have commanded them to use the siwak with every wudu and would have delayed the Isha prayer until one-third of the night or half the night.”"],[5630,"I asked the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, 'Which deeds are best?' He said, 'Prayer at the beginning of its time.'"],[5631,"I said, 'O Messenger of Allah, which deeds are most beloved to Allah?' He said, 'Prayers at their times.' I said, 'Then which?' He said, 'Then dutifulness to parents.' I said, 'Then which?' He said, 'Then jihad.' Had I asked for more, he would have added more."],[5632,"A letter from 'Umar came to us while we were in Azerbaijan with 'Utbah b. Farqad: To proceed: Wear lower garments, cloaks, and sandals. Throw away the soft leather socks and cut the trousers short. You must wear the clothing of your father Isma'il. Beware of luxury and the dress of the non-Arabs. You must expose yourselves to the sun, for it is the bath of the Arabs. Be rough and shabby, shoot at targets, and jump. The Prophet ﷺ forbade us from silk except this much—his two fingers, the middle and the index.\" He said, \"We did not know that he meant anything except the stripes.\""],[5633,"“The Messenger of Allah ﷺ permitted ‘Abd al-Rahman b. ‘Awf and al-Zubayr b. al-‘Awwam to wear silk because of an itch that they had.”"],[5634,"Al-Zubayr b. al-ʿAwwām and ʿAbd al-Raḥmān b. ʿAwf complained to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ about lice during a campaign of theirs, so he permitted them to wear silk shirts. I saw a silk shirt on each one of them."],[5635,"“Whoever wears silk in this world will not wear it in the Hereafter.”"],[5636,"“I wish I had sought permission from the Messenger of Allah ﷺ as Sawdah sought permission, so that I could pray the morning prayer at Mina and throw the Jamrah before the people came.” I said to ʿĀʾishah, “Did Sawdah seek his permission?” She said, “Yes, indeed she was a heavy, slow-moving woman, so she sought permission from the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and he granted it to her.”"],[5637,"We were among those whom the Messenger of Allah ﷺ sent ahead among the weak members of his family on the night of Muzdalifah."],[5638,"\"Al-Abbas b. Abd al-Muttalib asked the Messenger of Allah ﷺ for permission to spend the nights of Mina in Mecca for the sake of his watering (duty), and he permitted him.\""],[5639,"\"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ granted a concession to al-Abbas to spend the nights of the days of Mina in Mecca for the sake of his watering (duty).\""],[5640,"\"Al-Abbas b. Abd al-Muttalib asked the Prophet ﷺ for permission to spend the nights of Mina in Mecca for the sake of his watering (duty), and he permitted him for the sake of the watering.\""],[5641,"Five creatures, if someone kills them while in ihram, there is no blame on him: the scorpion, the mouse, the vicious dog, the crow, and the kite."],[5642,"Al-Zubayr married me while he had no property on earth, no slave, nothing except a camel for drawing water and his horse. I used to feed his horse, take care of its upkeep, groom it, grind date pits for his camel, feed it, draw water, and stitch its leather bucket. Abu Usama said: meaning the bucket. I used to knead dough, but I was not good at baking, so some of my neighbors from the Ansar, who were truthful women, baked for me. I used to carry date pits from the land of al-Zubayr, which the Messenger of Allah ﷺ had granted to him, on my head. It was two-thirds of a farsakh away. One day I came with date pits on my head and the Messenger of Allah ﷺ met me with a group of his companions. He called me and then said: «Ikh, ikh,» to make me ride behind him. I felt shy to walk with the men, and I remembered al-Zubayr and his jealousy, for he was the most jealous of people. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ recognized that I felt shy, so he went on. I came to al-Zubayr and said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ met me while I had date pits on my head, and with him was a group of his companions. He made his camel kneel so that I could ride with him, but I felt shy and knew your jealousy. He said: By Allah, your carrying the date pits is more difficult for me than your riding with him. She said: Later Abu Bakr sent me a servant, and that servant took over the care of the horse, as if she had set me free."],[5643,"To call the Adhan (Islamic call to prayer) and the breast of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to be watched by a deer. So, I met a young boy who belonged to Abd al-Rahman ibn 'Awf and he said, \"The breast of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ has been taken.\" I asked, \"Who took it?\" He replied, \"Ghatafan.\" So, I shouted, \"O morning! (A way of attracting attention) and I heard the distance between Medina's Labti (a place outside Medina) and then I hurried until I caught up with the people as they were fetching water. I began throwing arrows at them, and I used to be a skilled archer, and I kept saying..."],[5644,"I came to the Prophet ﷺ with me two men from the Ash'aris, one on my right and the other on my left, while the Messenger of Allah ﷺ was using the siwak. Both of them asked for a position of authority. I said, 'By the One who sent you with the truth, they did not inform me of what was in their minds, and I did not realize that they were seeking a position of authority.' It is as if I can see his siwak under his lip, which had receded. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, 'We do not, or we will not, seek help in our work from someone who desires it. But you go.' So he sent him to Yemen, then he sent Mu'adh b. Jabal after him."],[5645,"We went out with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ in the year of Tabuk until we came to Wadi al-Qura, and there was a woman in her garden. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to his companions, 'Estimate.' The people estimated, and the Messenger of Allah ﷺ estimated ten wasqs. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to the woman, 'Count what comes out of it until I return to you, if Allah wills.' He said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ went out until he reached Tabuk. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, 'A strong wind will blow upon you tonight, so let no man stand in it, and whoever has a camel, let him tie its tether.' Abu Humayd said: So we tied them. When night came, a strong wind blew upon us, and a man stood in it, and it cast him into the mountain of Tayyiʾ. Then the king of Ayla came and presented to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ a white mule, and the Messenger of Allah ﷺ gave him a cloak and wrote for him. Then he returned and we returned with him until we came to Wadi al-Qura. He said to the woman, 'How much did your garden produce?' She said, 'Ten wasqs, the estimate of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ.' The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, 'I am hastening, so whoever of you wishes to hasten with me, let him do so.' He said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ went out and we went out with him until when he looked upon al-Madinah, he said, 'This is Tabah.' When he saw Uhud, he said, 'This is Uhud, a mountain that loves us and we love it. Shall I inform you of the best dwellings of the Ansar?' They said, 'Yes.' He said, 'The best dwellings of the Ansar are Banu al-Najjar, then the dwelling of Banu ʿAbd al-Ashhal, then the dwelling of Banu al-Harith, then the dwelling of Banu Saʿidah, and in every dwelling of the Ansar there is goodness.'"],[5646,"'Who will go with this letter of mine to Caesar, and for him is Paradise?' A man from the people said, 'Even if I am not killed?' He said, 'Even if you are not killed.' The man went with it and met Caesar while he was going to Jerusalem. A carpet had been placed for him that no one else walked upon, so he threw the letter onto the carpet and stepped aside. When Caesar reached the letter, he took it, then called the head of the jathiliq and read it to him, and he said, 'My knowledge of this letter is like your knowledge.' Caesar called out, 'Who is the bearer of the letter? He is safe.' The man came, and Caesar said, 'When I arrive, come to me.' When he arrived, he came to him, and Caesar ordered the doors of his palace to be closed, then ordered a caller to announce: 'Indeed Caesar has followed Muhammad ﷺ and abandoned Christianity.' His soldiers came armed and surrounded his palace. He said to the messenger of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, 'You see that I fear for my kingdom.' Then he ordered a caller to announce: 'Indeed Caesar is pleased with you, and he only tested you to see how patient you are upon your religion, so return.' They left, and Caesar wrote to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, 'I am a Muslim,' and sent dinars to him. When the Messenger of Allah ﷺ read the letter, he said, 'The enemy of Allah has lied; he is not a Muslim, and he is upon Christianity.' And he distributed the dinars."],[5647,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to visit Umm Sulaym, and she would spread for him a leather mat, and he would take a midday nap on it. She would take some of his sweat and put it in her perfume, and she would spread for him a small mat, and he would pray on it."],[5648,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to me, “When my messengers come to you, give them—or hand over to them—thirty camels or thirty coats of mail.” I said, “Is it a loan to be returned, O Messenger of Allah?” He said, “Yes.”"],[5649,"I witnessed Hunayn while I was a owned slave. I said, 'O Messenger of Allah, my share?' He gave me a sword and said, 'Wear it.' And he gave me some of the odds and ends of the goods."],[5650,"When the Messenger of Allah ﷺ came to the House, the people of Makkah made a treaty with him that he could enter it and stay for three days, and that he would not enter it except with the sheathed sword and its scabbard, and that no one who entered with him should leave with him, and that he would not prevent anyone who was with him from staying in it. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to 'Ali, 'Write the condition between us: This is what Muhammad, the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, has agreed upon.' The polytheists said, 'If we knew that you were the Messenger of Allah, we would have pledged allegiance to you, but write Muhammad b. 'Abdullah.' The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, 'Erase it and write Muhammad b. 'Abdullah.' 'Ali said, 'I will not erase it.' The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, 'Erase it and write Muhammad b. 'Abdullah.' 'Ali said, 'I will not erase it.' The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, 'Show me its place so that I may erase it,' and he erased it and wrote Muhammad b. 'Abdullah. He stayed there for three days. When it was the end of the third day, they said to 'Ali, 'The condition of your companion has elapsed, so order him to leave.' He informed him of that, and he said, 'Yes.'"],[5651,"When the Messenger of Allah ﷺ made a treaty with Quraysh on the day of al-Hudaybiyyah, he said to 'Ali, 'Write: In the name of Allah, the Most Gracious, the Most Merciful.' Suhayl b. 'Amr said, 'We do not recognize the Most Gracious, the Most Merciful. Write: In Your name, O Allah.' The Prophet ﷺ said to 'Ali, 'Write: This is what Muhammad, the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, has agreed upon.' Suhayl b. 'Amr said, 'If we knew that you were the Messenger of Allah, we would have followed you and not belied you. Write your lineage from your father.' The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to 'Ali, 'Write: Muhammad b. 'Abdullah.' He wrote: 'Whoever comes to you from us, we will return him to you, and whoever comes to us from you, we will leave him to you.' They said, 'O Messenger of Allah, should we grant them this?' The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, 'Whoever goes to them from us, may Allah distance him, and whoever comes to us from them and we return him, Allah will make for him a way out and an escape.'"],[5652,"The Prophet ﷺ sent me over the ṣadaqah of Baliyy and ʿUdhrah. I passed by a man from Baliyy who had thirty camels and said to him, “You owe for these camels of yours a bint makhāḍ.” He said, “That one has no riding strength and no milk, and I dislike lending Allah the worst of my wealth. Choose it.” Ubayy said to him, “I was not going to take more than what you owe, and this is the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, so bring it to him.” He brought it to him and said something similar to what he had said to Ubayy. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, “This is what you owe, and if you bring more than it, we shall accept it from you.” He said, “O Messenger of Allah, here is a fine fat she-camel. Who will receive it?” He ﷺ ordered someone to receive it and supplicated for blessing in his wealth. ʿUmārah said, “Then time struck a blow, and Marwān put me in charge of the ṣadaqah of Baliyy and ʿUdhrah in the time of Muʿāwiyah. I passed by this man and assessed his wealth as thirty ḥiqqahs, including their stallion, on one thousand five hundred camels.” Ibn Isḥāq said, “I said to ʿAbd Allāh b. Abī Bakr, ‘What is their stallion?’ He said, ‘In the Sunnah, when a man’s ṣadaqah reaches thirty ḥiqqahs, their stallion is taken with them.’”"],[5653,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ sent ʿUmar b. al-Khaṭṭāb over the ṣadaqah, and Ibn Jamīl, Khālid b. al-Walīd, and al-ʿAbbās refused to pay. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, “Ibn Jamīl finds nothing to resent except that he was poor and Allah enriched him. As for Khālid, you wrong Khālid, for he has kept his coats of mail and his equipment for the sake of Allah. As for al-ʿAbbās, he is the paternal uncle of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, so it is upon me, and the like of it.” Then he said, “Did you not know that a man’s paternal uncle is a man’s twin brother, or his father’s twin brother?”"],[5654,"A woman should not have skin-to-skin contact with a woman, nor a man with a man, except a parent with a child."],[5655,"The best marriage is the easiest. The Prophet ﷺ said to a man, \"Would you like me to marry you to so-and-so?\" He said, \"Yes.\" He said to her, \"Would you like me to marry you to so-and-so?\" She said, \"Yes.\" So the Messenger of Allah ﷺ married her to him, and he did not stipulate a dower, and he consummated the marriage without giving her anything. When death attended him, he said, \"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ married me to so-and-so, and I have not given her anything. I have given her my share of Khaybar.\" He had a share in Khaybar, so she took it and sold it, and it reached a hundred thousand."],[5656,"A woman should not have skin-to-skin contact with a woman, nor a man with a man, except a parent with a child."],[5657,"A woman should not have skin-to-skin contact with a woman, nor a man with a man, except a parent with a child."],[5658,"Ma'iz b. Malik came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and said, \"The far one has committed fornication.\" The Prophet ﷺ said to him, \"Woe to you, what makes you know what fornication is?\" Then he ordered that he be driven away and expelled. Then he came to him a second time and said, \"O Messenger of Allah, the far one has committed fornication.\" He said, \"Woe to you, what makes you know what fornication is?\" He was driven away and expelled. Then he came to him a third time and said, \"O Messenger of Allah, the far one has committed fornication.\" He said, \"Woe to you, what makes you know what fornication is?\" He said, \"I had unlawful intercourse with a woman, just as a man has intercourse with his wife.\" So he ordered that he be driven away and expelled. Then he came to him a fourth time and said, \"O Messenger of Allah, the far one has committed fornication.\" He said, \"Woe to you, what makes you know what fornication is?\" He said, \"Did you insert and withdraw?\" He said, \"Yes.\" So he ordered that he be stoned. When he felt the touch of the stones, he fled to a tree and was stoned at it until he died. Then the Messenger of Allah ﷺ passed by after that with a group of his companions. A man among them said to his companion, \"By your father, this one is indeed the loser. He came to the Prophet ﷺ several times, each time he turned him away, until he was killed as a dog is killed.\" The Prophet ﷺ remained silent about them until he passed by the carcass of a donkey with its leg raised. He said, \"Eat from this.\" They said, \"From a donkey's carcass, O Messenger of Allah?\" He said, \"What you attained from the honor of your brother is greater. By the One in whose hand is the soul of Muhammad ﷺ, he is surely in a river among the rivers of Paradise, plunging about.\""],[5659,"When the Prophet ﷺ stoned Ma'iz b. Malik, he said, \"I have seen him splashing about in the rivers of Paradise.\""],[5660,"When the Prophet ﷺ stoned Ma'iz b. Malik, he said, \"I have seen him splashing about in the rivers of Paradise.\""],[5661,"That he witnessed the Messenger of Allah ﷺ when a man with disheveled hair, short, with muscles, was brought to him who confessed to adultery. He turned him away twice, then ordered him to be stoned, and he said: \"Whenever we go out on a military expedition in the path of Allah, one of you stays behind with a bleating like the bleating of a he-goat, giving one of them the little mound. Indeed, I will not have anyone of them brought to me except that I will make him an example.\""],[5662,"That Ma'iz ibn Malik came to the Prophet ﷺ and said: \"I have committed a major sin.\" The Prophet ﷺ turned him away several times. Then he asked his people: \"Is there any defect in him?\" It was said: \"There is no defect in him, except that he did something which he thinks will not be removed from him except by having the punishment carried out on him.\" He said: \"So he ordered us, and we took him to Baqi' al-Gharqad. We did not dig a hole for him nor tie him up. We threw at him pieces of baked clay, bones, and stones. He complained and ran, so we ran after him. He came to the lava field and stood against us, and we threw its boulders at him until he became still. Then the Prophet ﷺ stood in the evening as a preacher, praised and extolled Allah, then said: 'Now then, what is the matter with people that when we go on a military expedition, one of them stays behind with our families, bleating like a he-goat? Indeed, it is incumbent upon me that no one is brought to me who did that except that I will make an example of him.'\" He said: \"And he did not revile him nor ask forgiveness for him.\""],[5663,"A woman should not have skin-to-skin contact with a woman, nor a man with a man, except a parent with a child."],[5664,"That a man from Aslam came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and told him that he had committed adultery and testified against himself four times. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ ordered him to be stoned, and he had been muhsan."],[5665,"A woman from Juhaynah came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and said: \"O Messenger of Allah, I have incurred a punishment, so carry it out on me.\" He said: \"So the Messenger of Allah ﷺ called for her guardian and said: 'Treat her well until she gives birth to what is in her womb. When she gives birth, bring her to me.'\" The Messenger of Allah ﷺ was brought to her, and he ordered that her clothes be fastened tightly around her, then he ordered her to be stoned. Then he prayed over her. Umar said: \"O Messenger of Allah, will you pray over her when she committed adultery?\" The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"She has repented with a repentance that if divided among seventy of the people of Madinah, it would suffice them. Have you found anything better than her giving herself to Allah?\""],[5666,"A woman came to the Prophet of Allah ﷺ and said: \"I have committed a sin while pregnant.\" The Prophet of Allah ﷺ ordered her to go away until she gave birth to what was in her womb. When she gave birth, she came, and he ordered her to go away and breastfeed it until she weaned it. She did so. Then she came, and he ordered her to give her child to some people, and she did so. Then she came, and he asked her to whom she had given it. She informed him that she gave it to so-and-so. He ordered her to take it and give it to the family of so-and-so, people from the Ansar. Then she came, and he ordered her to fasten her clothes tightly around her. Then he ordered her to be stoned. Then he shrouded her and prayed over her, then buried her. The people said: \"He stoned her, then shrouded her, prayed over her, then buried her.\" The Prophet ﷺ heard what the people were saying and said: \"She has repented with a repentance that if her repentance were divided among seventy men of the people of Madinah, it would suffice them.\""],[5667,"When revelation descended upon the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, he felt distress from it and his face became clouded. One day revelation descended upon him, and when it was lifted from him, he said ﷺ: \"Take from me. Allah has made a way for them: the previously married with the previously married, and the virgin with the virgin. The previously married with the previously married: one hundred lashes then stoning with stones. The virgin with the virgin: one hundred lashes then banishment for a year.\""],[5668,"It is not lawful for a woman who believes in Allah and the Last Day to mourn for a deceased person more than three days, except for a husband, for she mourns for him four months and ten days."],[5669,"A man must not spend the night with a woman in a house unless he is married to her or is a mahram."],[5670,"I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ while he was on the pulpit delivering a sermon: 'A woman must not travel except with a mahram, and a man must not be alone with a woman except with a mahram.'"],[5671,"A woman may not travel three days except with a dhu-mahram with her."],[5672,"It is not lawful for a woman to travel except with a dhu-mahram."],[5673,"That 'A'ishah was informed that Abu Sa'id al-Khudri said: \"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ forbade a woman to travel except with a dhu-mahram with her.\" 'Amrah said: 'A'ishah turned to some of the women and said: \"Do all of you not have a dhu-mahram?\""],[5674,"She narrated to him that she was with ʿĀʾishah, saying to ʿĀʾishah: “Abū Saʿīd al-Khudrī relates from the Messenger of Allah ﷺ that he said: ‘It is not lawful for a woman to travel more than three days except with a maḥram.’” ʿAmrah said: ʿĀʾishah turned to us and said: “Not all of them have a maḥram.”"],[5675,"I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ while he was on the pulpit delivering a sermon: 'A woman must not travel except with a mahram, and a man must not be alone with a woman except with a mahram.'"],[5676,"O Banu Abd Manaf, do not prevent anyone from circumambulating this House and praying at whatever hour he wishes, whether night or day."],[5677,"Whoever forgets a prayer should pray it when he remembers."],[5678,"He forbade prayer after 'Asr until the sun sets, and prayer after Fajr until the sun rises.\""],[5679,"\"When the edge of the sun rises, do not pray until it is fully visible. Then pray. When the edge of the sun disappears, do not pray until it has set. Then pray. Do not intentionally time your prayer at sunrise or sunset, for it rises between the two horns of a devil.\""],[5680,"\"There are three times in which the Messenger of Allah ﷺ forbade us to pray and to bury our dead: when the sun begins to rise until it is high; when the sun is at its zenith until it declines; and when the sun declines for setting.\""],[5681,"\"Do not pray after 'Asr unless you pray while the sun is still high.\""],[5682,"\"None of you should intentionally pray at sunrise or sunset.\""],[5683,"He forbade qaza‘, which is shaving part of a boy’s head and leaving part of his hair."],[5684,"The Prophet ﷺ saw a boy with part of his hair shaved and part left, so he forbade that and said, “Shave it all or leave it all.”"],[5685,"The day of Ashura is a day that the people of the pre-Islamic period used to fast. So whoever among you wishes to fast it, let him fast it, and whoever dislikes it, let him leave it."],[5686,"Ḥamzah al-Aslamī asked the Messenger of Allah ﷺ about fasting while traveling, and he said: \"You have the choice: if you wish, fast; and if you wish, break the fast.\""],[5687,"\"We traveled with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ in Ramadan. Those of us who fasted did so, and those of us who broke the fast did so. The one fasting did not criticize the one breaking the fast, nor did the one breaking the fast criticize the one fasting.\""],[5688,"\"We set out with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ on the seventeenth of Ramadan at the conquest of Makkah. Some fasted and some broke the fast. These did not criticize those, nor did those criticize these.\""],[5689,"We set out with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ on the expedition of Tabūk, which was called the Campaign of Hardship. While we were traveling after the forenoon had passed, he came upon a group under the shade of a tree. They said, “O Messenger of Allah, a man is fasting, and the fast has exhausted him.” He ﷺ said, “It is not righteousness to fast while traveling.”"],[5690,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said during one of his journeys, when he saw people gathered around a man. He asked, and they said, “A man exhausted by fasting.” The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, “Fasting while traveling is not part of righteousness.”"],[5691,"“We used to go on military expeditions with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ during Ramadan. Among us were those who fasted and those who broke their fast. The fasting one did not find fault with the one who broke his fast, nor did the one who broke his fast find fault with the fasting one. They considered that whoever found strength and fasted, it was good, and whoever found weakness and broke his fast, it was good.”"],[5692,"We were with the Prophet ﷺ on a journey. Among us were those who fasted and those who broke their fast. We stopped at a place on a very hot day. Some of us were shielding themselves from the sun with their hands, and most of us in the shade were those who had cloaks—the fasting ones sheltered with them. The ones who broke their fast stood up, set up the tents, and tended to the mounts. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, “Those who broke their fast have taken the reward today.”"],[5693,"A man came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and said: O Messenger of Allah, I have a dinar; what should I do with it? He said: “Spend it on yourself.” He said: I have another; what should I do with it? He said: “Spend it on your family.” He said: I have another. He said: “Spend it on your child.” He said: I have another; what should I do with it? He said: “Spend it on your servant.” He said: I have another; what should I do with it? He said: “You know best.”"],[5694,"“The best dinar is a dinar a man spends on his dependents, a dinar he spends on his mount in the way of Allah, and a dinar he spends on his companions in the way of Allah.”"],[5695,"\"If a fasting person eats forgetfully, let him complete his fast, for Allah has fed him and given him drink.\""],[5696,"'O son of my brother, may Allah not grieve you. This is a covenant from the Prophet ﷺ to us, that we should stand nearest to him.' Then he faced the qiblah and said, 'The people of the covenant have perished, by the Lord of the Kaʿbah' — three times. Then he said, 'By Allah, I do not grieve for them, but I grieve for those whom they have led astray.' He said: I said, 'Who does he mean by this?' He said, 'The rulers.'"],[5697,"\"O 'Amr, how excellent is righteous wealth with a righteous man.\""],[5698,"When the muhrim had a complaint in his eye, he would bandage it with aloe."],[5699,"I saw Muhammad ibn Muslimah chasing the daughter of Al-Dhahak on a running horse from the outskirts of the city, observing her. So I said to him, \"Are you doing this while you are the companion of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ ?\" He replied, \"Yes, I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ saying, 'When Allah places a speech of desire in the heart of a person towards a woman, it is not wrong for him to look at her.'\""],[5700,"War is deception."],[5701,"We were with the Messenger of God ﷺ on a journey, and he stopped with us while we were about a thousand riders. He prayed two rak'ahs with us, then turned to us with his face and his eyes were flowing with tears. Umar stood up to him, may his father and mother be ransomed for him, and said, \"What is wrong with you, O Messenger of God?\" He ﷺ said, \"I asked permission to seek forgiveness for my mother, but He did not permit me, so my eyes shed tears out of mercy for her from the Fire. I had forbidden you three things: visiting graves, so visit them, and let your visiting them increase you in good; I had forbidden you the meat of sacrificial animals after three days, so eat and keep what you wish; and I had forbidden you drinks in vessels, so drink in whatever vessel you wish, but do not drink any intoxicant.\""],[5702,"A man's messenger to another man is his permission."],[5703,"The companions of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, when a man was fasting and the time of breaking the fast came, if he slept before breaking his fast, he would not eat that night or that day until evening. Qays b. Ṣirmah was fasting, and when the time of breaking the fast came, he went to his wife and said, “Do you have any food?” She said, “No, but let me go and look for some.” That day he had been working, so sleep overcame him. His wife came and when she saw him, she said, “What a disappointment for you!” He woke up the next morning. When midday came, he fainted. That was mentioned to the Prophet ﷺ, and this verse was revealed: “It has been made lawful for you, on the night of the fast, to approach your wives; they are a garment for you.” They rejoiced greatly at it. “And eat and drink until the white thread becomes distinct to you from the black thread of dawn.”"],[5704,"I had forbidden you three things: visiting graves, keeping the meat of sacrificial animals beyond three days, and using certain vessels except what is in a waterskin. Permission has been given to Muhammad ﷺ to visit his mother's grave. I had forbidden you to keep the meat of sacrificial animals beyond three days so that those of you with abundance might distribute it to those who did not sacrifice. I had forbidden you certain vessels except what is made of waterskin, for no vessel makes anything lawful or unlawful."],[5705,"I prohibited you from visiting graves, but now visit them; and I prohibited you from the meat of sacrificial animals beyond three days, so keep what seems right to you; and I prohibited you from nabidh unless in a water-skin, so drink from all water-skins, but do not drink any intoxicant."],[5706,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said on the day of sacrifice: «Whoever among you sacrifices should not find after the third day anything of his sacrificial animal in his house.» When the next year came, on the day of sacrifice, they said: O Messenger of Allah, should we do as we did last year? He said: «No, the people were in hardship, so I wanted you to assist them. Eat, feed, and store.»"],[5707,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ forbade incantations. I have a maternal uncle who incants against scorpion stings, so he came to the Prophet ﷺ and mentioned that to him, and he said: 'Whoever of you can benefit his brother, let him do so.'"],[5708,"Ali b. al-Husayn took me by the hand, and we went to an old man from Quraysh called Ibn Abi Hathma, who was praying toward a pillar, so we sat with him. When he saw Ali, he turned to him, and Ali said to him—"],[5709,"'A scorpion stung me in the presence of the Prophet ﷺ, and he incanted over me and wiped it.'"],[5710,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to command her to seek ruqya against the evil eye."],[5711,"He passed by a people who had a madman fettered in iron. Some of them said to him, 'Do you have something with which you can treat this man? For your companion has come with good.' He said, 'I recited over him the Opening of the Book for three days, twice each day, and he recovered. They gave him one hundred sheep. He came to the Prophet ﷺ and mentioned that to him. He ﷺ said to him, 'Eat [of the sheep]. He who eats from a false ruqya has indeed eaten, but you have eaten from a true ruqya.'"],[5712,"It was said to him: Will you not appoint a successor? He said: «If I leave, then one better than me left — the Messenger of Allah ﷺ; and if I appoint a successor, then one better than me appointed a successor — Abu Bakr.» And he praised him and said: «I wish I could be free from it, with nothing against me or for me.»"],[5713,"The Prophet ﷺ ate a shoulder, then wiped his hand on a cloth that was beneath him, then stood and prayed."],[5714,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ ate the shoulder of a sheep, then prayed and did not perform wudu'."],[5715,"He saw the Messenger of Allah ﷺ cutting from a bone with meat on it and eating. Then the muezzin came for prayer, so he threw down the bone and the knife from his hand and did not perform wudu'."],[5716,"We set out with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ until we were at a resting place near Khaybar. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ called for food, but nothing was found except barley porridge. He said, so we ate it. Then he called for water, and the Messenger of Allah ﷺ rinsed his mouth and prayed without performing wudu'."],[5717,"He would not pray during travel before it or after it."],[5718,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ went out on the day of Fitr or Adha and prayed two rak'ahs with the people, then left, and he did not pray before or after it."],[5719,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ would not pray over a man who died while owing a debt. A deceased person was brought to him, and he said, “Does he owe a debt?” They said, “Yes, two dinars.”"],[5720,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ set out in the year of the conquest in the month of Ramadan and fasted until he reached al-Kadīd, then he broke his fast. He said, “The Companions of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to follow the most recent of his affairs, the most recent.”"],[5721,"The Prophet ﷺ never fasted a full month except Ramadan, and he never broke fast for a full month, and he did not fast in any month more than he fasted in Sha'ban."],[5722,"I never saw the Messenger of Allah ﷺ fast the ten days at all."],[5723,"\"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ and his companions did not go between al-Safa and al-Marwah except with one tawaf, his first tawaf.\""],[5724,"“Whoever combines Hajj and Umrah, one circumambulation (Tawaf) suffices him for both, and he does not come out of ihram until the Day of Sacrifice (Yawm al-Nahr), then he comes out of ihram from both together.”"],[5725,"Two men sneezed in the presence of the Prophet ﷺ, and he invoked mercy upon one of them and left the other. He said, 'This one praised Allah, and this one did not praise Him.'"],[5726,"“Storytelling was not done in the time of the Prophet ﷺ, nor of Abu Bakr, nor of ʿUmar, nor of ʿUthman. Storytelling only appeared in the time of the fitnah.”"],[5727,"The liar is not the one who reconciles between people, so he conveys good or says good."],[5728,"He used to pass by a fallen date, and nothing prevented him from taking it except fear that it might be from charity.\""],[5729,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ would stick out his tongue for al-Husayn, and the boy would see the redness of his tongue and become excited toward it. Uyaynah b. Hisn b. Badr said to him: 'Do I see you doing this with this one? By Allah, I have a son whose face has grown hair and I have never kissed him.' The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: 'Whoever does not show mercy will not be shown mercy.'"],[5730,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ, when he was brought food from other than his own household, would ask about it. If it was said, ‘A gift,’ he ate; and if it was said, ‘Charity,’ he said, ‘Eat,’ and he did not eat."],[5731,"The translation of the passage is: \"That the Messenger of Allah ﷺ injured his finger in some scenes, so he said ﷺ.\""],[5732,"A man from the desert people called Zahir b. Haram used to send gifts to the Prophet ﷺ, and the Messenger of Allah ﷺ would equip him when he wanted to depart. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, “Zahir is our bedouin and we are his townspeople.” He said: The Prophet ﷺ came to him while he was selling his goods and embraced him from behind while the man could not see him. He said, “Let me go, who is this?” He turned around, and when he recognized that it was the Prophet ﷺ, he began pressing his back against his chest. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, “Who will buy this slave?” Zahir said, “You will find me unsellable, O Messenger of Allah.” He said, “But you are not unsellable with Allah,” or he said ﷺ, “Rather, you are precious with Allah.”"],[5733,"The Prophet of Allah ﷺ saw an orphan girl with Umm Sulaym, who is the mother of Anas b. Malik, and the Prophet ﷺ said to her, “You have grown gray, may Allah not let your horn grow.” Umm Sulaym said, “You have supplicated, O Messenger of Allah, against my orphan girl that Allah should not let her horn grow. By Allah, she will never grow gray.” The Prophet of Allah ﷺ said, “O Umm Sulaym, do you not know that I made a covenant with my Lord that any one of my ummah against whom I supplicate when it is not deserved, He will make it a purification for him or a means of nearness by which He brings him near on the Day of Resurrection?”"],[5734,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to visit us, and I had a young brother called Abū ʿUmayr. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ entered upon us one day and said, “O Abū ʿUmayr, what happened to the little bird?”"],[5735,"“People are like a hundred camels, among which you can hardly find one suitable for riding.”"],[5736,"There was a fright in Madinah, and the Messenger of Allah ﷺ borrowed a horse from Abu Talhah called Mandub, rode it, and returned, saying, “We saw no fright, but we found it to be a sea.”"],[5737,"Umm Sulaym was with the wives of the Prophet ﷺ and a driver was driving. The Prophet ﷺ came upon him and said, “O Anjashah, drive slowly with the glass vessels.”"],[5738,"The Prophet ﷺ had a camel-driver named Anjashah, and he had a beautiful voice. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to him, “Gently, O Anjashah, do not break the glass vessels.”"],[5739,"Umm Sulaym was with the wives of the Prophet ﷺ on a journey, and a driver was driving them. He ﷺ said, “Drive slowly with the glass vessels.”"],[5740,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ was on one of his journeys, and with him was a black servant of his called Anjasha, who was driving the camels by singing. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to him, \"O Anjasha, drive gently with the glass vessels.\""],[5741,"I heard al-Barāʾ say when a man came to him and said: O Abū ʿUmārah, did you turn in flight on the day of Hunayn? He said: As for me, I bear witness that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ did not turn in flight; but the hasty ones of the people rushed ahead, and Hawāzin shot arrows at them while Abū Sufyān b. al-Ḥārith was holding the head of his white mule, and he was saying: “I am the Prophet, no lie; I am the son of ʿAbd al-Muṭṭalib.”"],[5743,"A man from the Ansar came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and said, \"I have a slave girl and I practice coitus interruptus with her.\" He ﷺ said, \"Indeed, what is decreed for her will come to her.\" Then he came to him after that and said, \"She has become pregnant.\" The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, \"Whatever soul Allah has decreed to come forth, it will surely come to be.\""],[5744,"He heard Ibn Umar say that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ was asked about the night prayer, and he replied, \"One of you should pray two units, two units, until he fears the dawn, then he should perform a prostration that prolongs what he has prayed.\""],[5745,"We were with Saʿīd b. al-ʿĀṣ in Ṭabaristān, and he said: “Which of you prayed with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ the prayer of fear?” Ḥudhayfah said: “I did.” He said: “Then Ḥudhayfah stood and arranged the people behind him in two rows—a row behind him and a row facing the enemy—and he prayed with those behind him one rakʿah, then these moved to the place of those, and those came, and he prayed with them one rakʿah, and they did not make up [the other].”"],[5746,"A man asked the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and said: O Messenger of Allah, I was fasting and I ate and drank forgetfully. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"May Allah feed you and give you drink; complete your fast.\""],[5747,"A woman came to the Prophet ﷺ and said: \"O Messenger of Allah, my sister died and she owed two consecutive months of fasting.\" The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"Tell me, if your sister had a debt, would you pay it?\" She said: \"Yes.\" He said: \"The right of Allah is more deserving.\""],[5748,"He heard Ibn Umar saying that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ was asked about Laylat al-Qadr (the Night of Power) and he said, \"Seek it in the last seven nights of Ramadan.\""],[5749,"\"Indeed, the Prophet ﷺ was asked about a man who shaved before slaughtering or slaughtered before throwing, so the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, 'There is no harm.'\""],[5750,"He was with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ until, when he was on part of the road to Makkah, he lagged behind with some companions of his who were in a state of iḥrām, while he was not in iḥrām. He saw a wild donkey, mounted his horse, and asked his companions to hand him his whip, but they refused. He asked them for his spear, and they refused, so he took it. Then he charged at the donkey and killed it. Some of the companions of the Prophet ﷺ ate from it, and some refused. When they caught up with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, they asked him about that, and the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “It is only a meal that Allah fed you.”"],[5751,"O Messenger of Allah, what do you think about poetry? He said, “The believer strives with his sword and his tongue. By the One in whose hand is my soul, it is as if you are showering them with arrows.”"],[5752,"\"Bring me the shoulder blade or the tablet.\" He wrote: {Not equal are those who sit among the believers}, while 'Amr b. Umm Maktum was behind his back. He said, \"Is there any concession for me?\" Then {other than those having a disability} was revealed."],[5753,"When {Not equal are those who sit among the believers} was revealed, the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, \"Call Zayd for me and let him come with the tablet and the inkwell, or with the shoulder blade and the inkwell.\" Then he said, \"Write: Not equal are those who sit among the believers and the mujahidun in the path of Allah.\" Behind the Prophet ﷺ was 'Amr b. Umm Maktum, the blind one. He said, \"O Messenger of Allah, what do you command me, for I am a man blind of sight?\" Al-Bara' said, \"Then it was revealed in its place: {other than those having a disability}.\""],[5754,"I heard Al-Bara' saying, when this verse was revealed \"Not equal are those believers who sit [at home] and those who strive and fight in the cause of Allah,\" the Messenger of Allah ﷺ called Zaid and he came with a shoulder on which it was written. Ibn Umm Maktum complained of his disability's harm, so the verse \"not [to be incurred] by those who have incurred [the obligation of] the discharge of a burden\" was revealed."],[5755,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ sent Abū Qatādah al-Anṣārī to collect zakāt, and the Messenger of Allah ﷺ set out with his companions in a state of iḥrām until they camped at ʿUsfān, at the pass of al-Ghazzāl. There they saw a wild donkey. Abū Qatādah came, and he was not in iḥrām. They lowered their heads, disliking to fix their gaze on it lest he notice it. He saw it, mounted his horse, took the spear, and the whip fell from him. He said: “Hand it to me.” We said: “We will not help you with it in any way.” He charged at it and hamstrung it. He said: Then they began to roast from it, then they said: “The Messenger of Allah ﷺ is among us,” and he had gone ahead of them. They came to him and asked him, and he saw no harm in it, and I think he said: “Do you have any of it with you?”"],[5756,"I went out with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. All the people entered ihram except me. We saw a wild donkey, so I saddled and bridled [my horse], then mounted, took the spear, and forgot the whip. I asked them to hand it to me, but they refused. So I dismounted, took my whip, then struck the donkey and hamstrung it. Some of the people ate from it and some left it. When the Messenger of Allah ﷺ came, he said, “Those who ate were correct. Do you have any of it with you?” He said: We said, “Yes, here is a leg.” The Messenger of Allah ﷺ ate from it."],[5757,"We landed at a place where a woman came to us and said: A scorpion has bitten the chief of the tribe. Is there any incantator amongst you? A person amongst us stood up (and went with her). We had no idea that he had been a good incantator but he practiced incantation with the help of Sura al-Fatiha and the (the chief) was all right. They gave him a flock of sheep and served us milk. We said (to him): Are you a good incantator. Thereupon he said: I did not do it but by the help of Sura al-Fatiha. He said: Do not drive (these goats) until we go to Messenger of Allah ﷺ and find out (whether it is permissible to accept (this reward of incantation). So we came to Allah's Apostle ﷺ and made a mention of that to him, whereupon he said: How did you come to know that this (Sura al-Fatiha) could be used as an incantation? So distribute them (amongst those who had been present there with him) and allocate a share of mine also. (Using translation from Muslim 2201c)"],[5758,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ sent us on a military expedition. We passed by the people of some dwellings and asked them for hospitality, but they refused to host us. They camped in the open. Their chief was stung, so they came to us and said, 'Is there anyone among you who can perform ruqya?' I said, 'Yes, I can perform ruqya.' They said, 'Perform ruqya on our companion.' I said, 'No, for we asked you for hospitality and you refused to host us.' They said, 'We will make a payment for you.' They set for me thirty sheep. I went to him and began to wipe him and recite the Opening of the Book until he recovered. We took the sheep and said, 'Should we take them while we do not know how to perform ruqya well? We will not eat them until we ask the Messenger of Allah ﷺ about them.' So we came to him and mentioned that to him. He began to say, 'What makes you know that it is a ruqya?' I said, 'O Messenger of Allah, I did not know that it was a ruqya; it was something Allah cast into my heart.' The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, 'Eat, and assign a share for me with you.'"],[5759,"“In the pre-Islamic era, when they entered iḥrām they would enter the House from its back, so Allah sent down: ‘It is not righteousness that you enter houses from their backs, but righteousness is [in] one who fears Allah.’”"],[5760,"Sawdah bt. Zam'ah was a corpulent woman. When she went out at night to relieve herself, she towered over the other women. 'Umar b. al-Khattab saw her and said: \"Watch how you go out, for by Allah, when you go out you are not hidden from us.\" Sawdah mentioned that to the Prophet ﷺ while a bone was in his hand. He did not put the bone down until the revelation finished, then he said: \"Allah has granted you a concession to go out for your needs.\""],[5761,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ delayed the Isha prayer, then came out to the mosque while the people were waiting for the prayer and said, “Indeed, there is no one from the people of the religions who remembers Allah at this hour except you.” Then it was revealed to him: {They are not all the same; among the People of the Scripture is a community standing [in obedience], reciting the verses of Allah...} up to {...they prostrate}."],[5762,"“They used to perform Hajj and not take provisions.” Then Allah revealed: {And take provisions, for indeed the best provision is taqwa}."],[5763,"\"We used to carry loads on our backs, and a man would bring something and give it in charity. A man came with half a sa', and someone came with a lot. They said, 'Allah has no need of this one's charity,' and they said, 'This one is showing off.' Then was revealed: {Those who criticize the voluntary givers among the believers concerning charities and those who find nothing but their effort}.\""],[5764,"The Jews said, \"Squint-eyedness only occurs when a man approaches his wife from behind her.\" So Allah revealed, {Your wives are a tilth for you, so come to your tilth as you will} from in front of her or from behind her, but he should not come to her except in the place of cultivation."],[5765,"He asked the Messenger of Allah ﷺ: We used to slaughter sacrifices and eat from them and feed whoever came to us. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"There is no harm in that.\""],[5766,"A servant of Ka'b b. Malik used to tend his sheep at Sal'. One of the sheep was about to die, so she could not find a knife to slaughter it with, so she slaughtered it with a sharp stone. The Prophet ﷺ was asked about that and he ordered that it be eaten."],[5767,"A slave girl of theirs was tending sheep at Mount Salʿ. She saw a sheep from their flock near death, so she broke a stone and slaughtered it with it. He said to his family, 'Do not eat from it until I go to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and ask him.' He came to the Prophet ﷺ and asked him about that. He said, 'O Messenger of Allah, a slave girl of ours was tending sheep at Salʿ. She saw a sheep from her flock near death, so she broke a stone and slaughtered it with it.' The Prophet ﷺ commanded him to eat it."],[5768,"I said: O Messenger of Allah, I send trained dogs and they catch game for me, and I mention Allah's name over it. He said: \"If you send your trained dog and mention Allah's name over it, then eat.\" I said: Even if they kill it? He said: \"Even if they kill it, as long as no other dog shares it with them.\" I said to him: I shoot game with a mi'rad and hit it. He said: \"If you shoot with a mi'rad and it pierces, then eat it; but if it is struck by its side, then do not eat it.\""],[5769,"My mother came from Makkah to Madinah during the truce of Quraysh, and she was a polytheist. I said, “O Prophet of Allah, my mother has come desiring [something].”"],[5770,"When the Messenger of Allah ﷺ arrived in Madinah, he fell ill, as did his Companions, Abu Bakr, Amir b. Fuhayrah the freed slave of Abu Bakr, and Bilal. Aishah asked the Messenger of Allah ﷺ for permission to visit them, and he permitted her. She said to Abu Bakr: 'How do you find yourself?' He said:"],[5771,"I saw the Messenger of Allah ﷺ perform ablution, washing his face and hands, then wiping over his two khuffs. I said, \"O Messenger of Allah, do you wipe over your two khuffs?\" He said, \"I put my feet in them while they were pure.\""],[5772,"\"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ was asked, and it was said, 'O Messenger of Allah, what do you think about a person who speaks, then performs ablution and wipes over his socks? Can he pray?' He replied, 'There is no problem with that.'\""],[5773,"Ubayy b. Kaʿb came to the Prophet ﷺ and said: “O Messenger of Allah, something happened from me tonight in Ramadan.” He said: “And what is that, O Ubayy?” He said: “Women in my house said: ‘We do not recite the Qur’an, so we will pray following your prayer.’” He said: “So I led them in eight rakʿahs, then I performed witr.” He said: “And it was as if he was pleased, and he did not say anything.”"],[5774,"She came to the Prophet ﷺ and said, 'O Prophet of Allah, I have nothing except what al-Zubayr brings to me. Is there any sin upon me if I give a little from what he brings to me?' He said, 'Give what you can, and do not hoard, lest Allah withhold from you.'"],[5775,"Hind, the wife of Abu Sufyan, came to the Prophet ﷺ and said, \"Abu Sufyan is a stingy man. Is it permissible for me to take from his wealth and spend it on myself and my children?\" The Prophet ﷺ said to her, \"There is no harm in you taking from Abu Sufyan's wealth and spending it on yourself and your children in a reasonable manner.\""],[5776,"That a man came to the Prophet ﷺ seeking his ruling while she was listening from behind the door, and he said, “O Messenger of Allah, the prayer comes upon me while I am in a state of major impurity—should I fast?” The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, “The prayer comes upon me too while I am in a state of major impurity, and I fast.” He said, “You are not like us, O Messenger of Allah: Allah has forgiven you your past and future sins.” He said, “By Allah, I hope that I am the most fearful of Allah among you and the most knowledgeable of what I avoid.”"],[5777,"A man came to the Prophet ﷺ and said: My sister has died and did not perform Hajj. Should I perform Hajj on her behalf? He ﷺ said: \"Consider, if she owed a debt and you paid it, Allah is more deserving of fulfillment.\""],[5778,"A man said, \"O Messenger of Allah, I slaughtered before I stoned.\" He said, \"Stone, and there is no harm.\" Another said, \"O Messenger of Allah, I shaved before I slaughtered.\" He said, \"Slaughter, and there is no harm.\" Another said, \"O Messenger of Allah, I circumambulated before I stoned.\" He said, \"Stone, and there is no harm.\""],[5779,"Sawdah was a large, slow-moving woman. She sought permission from the Messenger of Allah ﷺ to depart from Jamʿ at night, and the Messenger of Allah ﷺ granted it to her.” And ʿĀʾishah used to say, “I wish I had sought permission from the Messenger of Allah ﷺ as Sawdah sought permission from him.”"],[5780,"Guests came to stay with us, and my father was talking to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ during the night. He departed and said: O 'Abd al-Rahman, take care of your guests. When evening came, we brought them their hospitality, but they refused and said: Not until your father comes to his house and eats with us. I said: He is a stern man, and if you do not do so, I fear that some harm may befall me from him. They refused. When he came, he said: Have you finished with your guests? They said: No, by Allah. He said: Did I not command 'Abd al-Rahman? I moved aside, and he said: I adjure you, if you can hear my voice, come. So I came and said: By Allah, I have no fault; these are your guests, so ask them. I brought them their hospitality, but they refused to eat until you came. He said: What is wrong with you that you do not accept our hospitality from us? Abu Bakr said: By Allah, I will not eat it tonight. They said: By Allah, we will not eat it until you eat it. He said: I have not seen evil like tonight. Then he said: As for the first, it is from Satan, so bring your hospitality. The food was brought, and he invoked the name of Allah and ate, and they ate. When morning came, he went to the Prophet ﷺ and said: O Messenger of Allah, they were righteous and I broke my oath. He said: «Rather, you are the most righteous of them and the best of them.»"],[5781,"The Prophet ﷺ saw a man being supported by two others and said, 'What is the matter with him?' They replied, 'He vowed to perform Hajj on foot.' The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, 'Indeed Allah is in no need of this man's walking, so let him ride.'"],[5782,"Sa'd b. 'Ubadah came to the Prophet ﷺ and said, \"My mother died while she owed a vow she had not fulfilled.\" The Prophet ﷺ said to him, \"Fulfill it on her behalf.\""],[5783,"A woman came to the Prophet ﷺ and said, \"My mother died while she owed a fast from a vow.\" The Prophet ﷺ said to her, \"Would you pay a debt on behalf of your mother if she owed one?\" She said, \"Yes.\" He said, \"Then fast on behalf of your mother.\""],[5784,"Subay'ah gave birth a few days after her husband's death. She came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and asked his permission to marry, and he granted her permission."],[5785,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ came out of the privy and ate. It was said to him, 'Before you perform ablution?' He ﷺ said, 'I intend to pray, so I will perform ablution.'"],[5786,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ passed by me while I was kindling a fire under a pot of mine, and lice were falling from my head. He ﷺ said, “Are the vermin of your head harming you?” I said, “Yes.” He said, “Offer a sacrifice, or fast three days, or feed six poor persons.”"],[5787,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ passed by him while he was at al-Hudaybiyyah and said to him, “Are the vermin of your head harming you?” I said, “Yes.” So he ordered me to shave. He said: And he did not make clear to them that they would shave there while they were eager to enter Makkah. He said: Then the verse of ransom was revealed. “And the Messenger of Allah ﷺ ordered me to fast three days, or feed a faraq among six poor persons, or slaughter a sheep.”"],[5788,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ passed by me at al-Hudaybiyyah while I was kindling a fire under a pot of mine, or under an earthenware pot of mine, and lice were falling on my face. He said, “Are your vermin harming you, O Ka‘b?” I said, “Yes, O Messenger of Allah.” He said, “Then shave your head and offer a sacrifice, or fast three days, or feed a faraq among six poor persons.”"],[5789,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ called me and said, “O Ka‘b b. ‘Ujrah, are the vermin of your head harming you?” He said: I said, “Yes.” He said, “Then he ordered me to fast, or give charity, or offer a sacrifice, whichever is easy.”"],[5790,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ came to me at the time of al-Hudaybiyyah when I had a lot of hair. He said, “It seems the vermin of your head are harming you?” I said, “Yes.” He said, “Then shave it and slaughter a sheep as a sacrifice, or fast three days, or give in charity three sa‘s of dates among six poor persons.”"],[5791,"I sat with Ka‘b b. ‘Ujrah in the mosque and asked him about this verse: {A ransom of fasting, or charity, or sacrifice}. Ka‘b said: It was revealed concerning me. I had an affliction in my head, and I was carried to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ while lice were falling on my face. He ﷺ said, “I never thought that hardship had reached you to the extent I see. Can you find a sheep?” I said, “No.” He said: Then this verse was revealed: {A ransom of fasting, or charity, or sacrifice}. The fast is three days, the charity is half a sa‘ of food for each poor person, and the sacrifice is a sheep.”"],[5792,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ was told: “O Messenger of Allah, our sa' is the smallest of sa's and our mudd is the smallest of mudds.” The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “O Allah, bless us in our sa', and bless us in our little and our much, and grant us with the blessing two blessings.”"],[5793,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ was asked about the dhabb, and he ﷺ said: 'I neither eat it nor forbid it.'"],[5794,"A man came to the Prophet ﷺ and said, \"O Messenger of Allah, one of us finds within himself something such that he would rather be a burnt cinder than to speak of it.\" He ﷺ said, \"Allah is most great. Praise be to Allah who reduced his affair to whispering.\""],[5795,"Umar b. al-Khattab said, \"I became aroused and kissed while I was fasting. I came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and said, 'I have done a grave thing today.' He said, 'What is it?' I said, 'I kissed while fasting.' The Prophet ﷺ said, 'What do you think if you rinsed your mouth with water?' I said, 'Then it would not harm.' He said, 'So why worry?'\""],[5796,"«Indeed, Bilal gives the adhan at night, so eat and drink until you hear the adhan of Ibn Umm Maktum.»"],[5797,"Bilal gives the call to prayer at night, so eat and drink until Ibn Umm Maktum gives the call."],[5798,"Bilal gives the call to prayer at night so that he may awaken the sleeper among you and cause the one standing in prayer to return, and the dawn is not that one says thus—and he indicated with two forefingers—but the dawn is that one says thus—and he indicated with his palm."],[5799,"\"Ibn Umm Maktum gives the call to prayer at night, so eat and drink until Bilal gives the call to prayer.\" And Bilal used to give the call to prayer when he saw the dawn."],[5800,"When Ibn Umm Maktum gives the call to prayer, eat and drink. When Bilal gives the call to prayer, do not eat or drink. If any one of us had something left of her pre-dawn meal, she would say to Bilal, 'Wait until I finish my pre-dawn meal.'"],[5801,"He asked Uthman b. Affan about a man who has intercourse but does not ejaculate. He said: “No bathing is due upon him.” Then Uthman said: I heard it from the Messenger of Allah ﷺ."],[5802,"I said: What do you think if one of us has intercourse with a woman and is too weary to ejaculate? The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “He should wash his penis and testicles, perform ablution, then pray.”"],[5803,"That the legal opinion they used to give, «Water is due only from water,» was a dispensation that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ granted at the beginning of the era, or the start of Islam; then he commanded ghusl afterward."],[5804,"I asked ʿUrwah about the one who has intercourse but does not ejaculate. He said: People must follow the most recent practice, and the most recent is from the command of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. ʿĀʾishah told me: «The Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to do that and not perform ghusl, and that was before the conquest of Makkah. Then he performed ghusl after that and commanded the people to perform ghusl.»"],[5805,"«When he sits between her four limbs and then exerts himself, ghusl becomes obligatory.»"],[5806,"«When the two circumcised parts meet, ghusl becomes obligatory.»"],[5807,"«When the circumcised part passes the circumcised part, ghusl becomes obligatory.»"],[5808,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ dispatched us in a detachment of three hundred riders, with Abu 'Ubaydah b. al-Jarrah as our commander, to lie in wait for a caravan of Quraysh. We stayed on the coast for half a month, and severe hunger struck us until we ate the leaves of the mimosa flava tree. So that army was called the Army of the Leaves. Then the sea cast up a creature called the sperm whale, and we ate from it for half a month until our bodies recovered. We also used its fat as ointment. Abu 'Ubaydah b. al-Jarrah took one of its ribs, looked for the tallest camel in the army and the tallest man, and loaded him on it, and he passed under it. Sufyan said: Abu al-Zubayr said from Jabir: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ gave us a sack containing dates, and when it was exhausted, we felt its loss. A man would bring something. And we extracted from its eye sockets such-and-such amount of fat. When we came to the Prophet ﷺ, he asked us, 'Do you still have any of it with you?'"],[5809,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ dispatched us and appointed Abu 'Ubaydah b. al-Jarrah as our commander to meet a caravan of Quraysh. He provisioned us with a sack of dates, finding nothing else for us. Abu 'Ubaydah would feed us one date at a time. I said, 'How did you manage with it?' He said, 'We would suck it as a child sucks, then drink water over it, and it sufficed us for our day until night. And we would beat the leaves of the mimosa flava tree with our sticks, then moisten them with water and eat them.' Then we set out, and there appeared to us on the seashore something like a huge sand dune. We came to it and found it was a creature called the sperm whale. Abu 'Ubaydah said, 'It is carrion.' Then he said, 'No, we are the messengers of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, in the path of Allah, and you have been compelled by necessity, so eat.' We stayed with it for a month, and we were three hundred, until we grew fat. I saw us scooping fat from its eye socket with large vessels, and cutting pieces from it like an ox or the size of an ox. Abu 'Ubaydah took thirteen men from us and seated them in its eye socket. He took one of its ribs and stood it upright, then saddled the largest camel we had, and it passed under it. We provisioned ourselves with its meat and strips of dried meat. When we came to Madinah, we went to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and told him about that. He said, 'It is provision that Allah brought out for you. Do you have any of its meat with you to feed us?' So we sent some of it to him, and he ate it."],[5810,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ dispatched an expedition to the land of Juhaynah and appointed a man over them as commander. When their provisions ran out, their commander ordered that what remained of their provisions be collected, and he began rationing us one date at a time. I said, 'O Abu 'Abd Allah, what did a single date avail you?' He said, 'By Allah, when it was exhausted, we felt its loss. One of us would put it between his teeth and palate and suck it, and we would get leaves of trees and plants of the earth along with that, until we reached the seashore. Then Allah brought out for us a fish that the sea had cast up. We ate from it and cut strips of it. When we wanted to depart, our commander ordered that one of its ribs be taken, and its two ends were planted in the ground. Then he ordered a camel to be saddled, and it passed under it.'"],[5811,"He said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ dispatched an expedition towards the coast and appointed Abu 'Ubaydah b. al-Jarrah as our commander. They were three hundred, and I was among them. We set out until we were partway, and the provisions ran out. Abu 'Ubaydah ordered that the provisions of that army be collected all together, and it was a sack of dates. He rationed us little by little each day until it was exhausted, and none of us got more than one date at a time. I said, 'What does a single date avail?' He said, 'We felt its loss when it ran out.' Then we reached the sea, and there was a fish like a small hill. That army ate from it for eleven nights. Then Abu 'Ubaydah ordered that two of its ribs be taken, then ordered a mount to be saddled, and it passed under them without touching them."],[5812,"A man asked the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, \"O Messenger of Allah, we ride the sea and carry with us a little water. If we perform wudu' with it, we will become thirsty. May we perform wudu' with seawater?\" He said, \"Its water is purifying and its dead animals are lawful.\""],[5813,"I entered upon Abū Saʿīd al-Khudrī ؓ in his house. He said: I found him praying, so I sat waiting for him until he finished his prayer. Then I heard movement under the bed in his house, and it was a snake. I got up to kill it, but he gestured to me to sit down. When he finished, he pointed to a room in the house and said, “Do you see this room?” I said, “Yes.” He said, “There was a young man among us who had recently married, so we went out with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ to the trench. That young man used to ask his permission at midday and return to his wife. One day he asked the Prophet ﷺ for permission, and he said to him, ‘Take your weapon, for I fear for you from the Qurayẓah.' So he took his weapon and went, and there was his wife standing between the two doors. He aimed his spear at her to thrust it because of jealousy, but she said, ‘Hold back your spear until you see what is in your house.' He entered and found a huge snake coiled on his bed. He struck at it and pierced it with the spear, then went out and fixed the spear in the courtyard, and the snake writhed on the spearhead while the young man fell dead. We did not know which of them died first, the young man or the snake. We went to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and mentioned that to him, saying, ‘Call upon Allah to bring him back to life.' He said, ‘Ask forgiveness for your companion.' Then he said, ‘There are jinn in Madinah who have accepted Islam, so if you see any of them, give it notice for three days. If it appears to you after that, then kill it, for it is only a devil.'”"],[5814,"A man said: O Messenger of Allah, may one of us pray in a single garment? The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: 'Does every one of you find two garments?' Then Abu Hurayrah said to the one who asked him: 'Do you know Abu Hurayrah? He prays in a single garment while his clothes are placed on the rack.'"],[5815,"A man came to the Prophet ﷺ and said: What do you think about praying in a single garment? He said: 'Does every one of you find two garments?'"],[5816,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ was asked about praying in a single garment, and he said: 'Does every one of you find two garments?' Then when ʿUmar b. al-Khaṭṭāb became caliph, he said: 'If Allah grants you abundance, then be generous. A man should gather his clothes around him and pray in a waist-wrapper and a cloak, in a waist-wrapper and a shirt, in a waist-wrapper and an outer garment, in trousers and a cloak, in trousers and a shirt, in trousers and an outer garment.'"],[5817,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ commanded us to kill dogs, to the point that a woman would come in from the desert with a dog and kill it. Then he forbade us from killing them and said: Keep to the black one with two spots, for it is a devil."],[5818,"Jābir b. ʿAbd Allāh led us in prayer wearing a single garment, having wrapped its two ends in opposite directions. He said: 'The Messenger of Allah ﷺ prayed it like that.'"],[5819,"There was in my care a slave girl from the Ansar, and I married her off. She said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ entered upon me on the day of her wedding and did not hear any singing or playing. He said: \"O Aisha, did you not sing for her? Or do you not sing for her?\" Then he said: \"This tribe of the Ansar loves singing.\""],[5820,"Abu Bakr entered upon her, and with her were two slave girls singing with two duffs during their days. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ was covering himself with his garment. Abu Bakr scolded them, and the Messenger of Allah ﷺ uncovered his garment and said: \"Leave them, O Abu Bakr, for these are days of Eid.\""],[5821,"Abu Bakr entered upon me while I had two slave girls from the slave girls of the Ansar singing what the Ansar had said to one another on the day of Bu'ath. Abu Bakr said: \"A flute of Satan in the house of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ?\" That was on a day of Eid. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"O Abu Bakr, every people has a festival, and this is our festival.\""],[5822,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ came and entered upon me on the morning of my wedding, and sat on my bed as you are sitting from me. Some young slave girls of ours began beating a duff of theirs and lamenting those of my forefathers who were killed on the day of Badr, until one of them said: \"And among us is a Prophet who knows what will be tomorrow.\""],[5823,"\"Recite the Qur'an as long as your hearts are united upon it; when you differ about it, then depart from it.\""],[5824,"The Prophet ﷺ saw a man driving a sacrificial camel and said, “Ride it.” He said, “It is a sacrificial camel, O Messenger of Allah.” He said, “Ride it.” He said, “It is a sacrificial camel, O Messenger of Allah.” He said, “Ride it.” He said on the third or fourth time, “Ride it, woe to you.”"],[5825,"“Ride the sacrificial animals in a reasonable manner until you find another mount.”"],[5826,"Any town that disobeys Allah and His Messenger, its fifth belongs to Allah and His Messenger, then it is yours."],[5827,"I asked Anas b. Mālik about wiping over the two khuffs. He said, “The Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to wipe over them.”"],[5828,"Bilal and the Messenger of Allah ﷺ entered al-Aswaf*. He went to relieve himself, then came out. Usama said: I asked Bilal what the Messenger of Allah ﷺ had done, and Bilal said, «He went to relieve himself, then performed ablution, washing his face and hands, wiping his head, and wiping over the two khuffs, then he prayed.»"],[5829,"I asked 'Ali b. Abi Talib about wiping over the two khuffs, and he said, «The Messenger of Allah ﷺ granted us a concession to wipe over the two khuffs: for the resident, a day and a night; and for the traveler, three days and their nights.»"],[5830,"\"What's wrong with you?\" I said, \"I am seeking knowledge.\" He replied, \"For I have heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say, 'Verily, the angels lower their wings for the seeker of knowledge, pleased with what he does.' So I asked him about wiping over the two socks, and he said, 'The Messenger of Allah ﷺ commanded us to wipe over three (things) when we travel, and a day and a night when we stay, without removing them due to defecation, urination, or sleep, but rather due to sexual impurity.'\""],[5831,"«He granted a concession to the traveler for three days and their nights, and to the resident for a day and a night: if he purifies himself and puts on his two khuffs, he may wipe over them.»"],[5832,"The Messenger of Allah performed ablution and wiped over his socks and his sandals. (Using translation from Ibn Mājah 559)"],[5833,"that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ wiped over his forelock and over the turban, then wiped over his two khuffs."],[5834,"that he saw the Prophet ﷺ perform wudu and wipe over the turban and the two khuffs."],[5835,"I was with Salman al-Farisi when he saw a man who had broken his wudu and wanted to remove his two khuffs for wudu. Salman told him, “Wipe over them and over your turban, for I saw the Messenger of Allah ﷺ wiping over his khimar and over his two khuffs.”"],[5836,"I saw the Messenger of Allah ﷺ perform wudu and wipe over the two khuffs and the turban."],[5837,"that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ performed wudu and wiped over his forelock and over the turban."],[5838,"The Prophet ﷺ fell behind, and al-Mughirah b. Shubah fell behind with him. When he had relieved himself, he said, “Do you have any water?” I said yes, and brought him the water container. He washed his palms and face, then went to uncover his forearms, but the jubba was too tight. He brought his hand out from under the jubba and threw it over his shoulder, then washed his forearms and wiped over his two khuffs and his turban. Then he mounted, and I mounted with him. He reached the people when Abd al-Rahman b. Awf had already led them in one rakah. When he sensed the Prophet ﷺ arriving, he moved to step back, but the Prophet ﷺ gestured to him to continue praying. When Abd al-Rahman finished the prayer, the Prophet ﷺ and al-Mughirah stood up and completed what they had missed."],[5839,"Sa'd b. 'Ubadah said to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, 'O Messenger of Allah, what do you think: if I find a man with my wife, should I give him respite until I bring four witnesses?' The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, 'Yes.'"],[5840,"A man said to the Prophet ﷺ, 'My mother died suddenly, and I think if she had spoken she would have given charity. May I give charity on her behalf?' The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, 'Yes.'"],[5841,"Sa'd b. 'Ubadah set out with the Prophet ﷺ on one of his expeditions, and his mother was on the point of death in Madinah. Someone said to her, 'Make a bequest.' She said, 'In what should I make a bequest? The wealth belongs to Sa'd.' She died before Sa'd arrived. When Sa'd arrived, this was mentioned to him. Sa'd said, 'O Messenger of Allah, will it benefit her if I give charity on her behalf?' The Prophet ﷺ said, 'Yes.' Sa'd said, 'Such-and-such an orchard is charity on her behalf,' for an orchard he named."],[5842,"Umar b. al-Khattab asked the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, 'May one of us sleep while he is junub?' He ﷺ said, 'Yes, if he performs ablution.'"],[5843,"he asked the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, “May one of us sleep while he is in a state of major impurity?” He said, “Yes, and he may perform ablution if he wishes.”"],[5844,"A woman from Khathʿam said: O Messenger of Allah, Allah's obligation of Hajj has reached my father as an old man who cannot sit upright on his mount. Should I fulfill it on his behalf, or perform Hajj for him? The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to her: \"Yes.\""],[5845,"Al-Fadl b. ‘Abbas was riding behind the Messenger of Allah ﷺ when a woman from Khath‘am came to ask him for a ruling. Al-Fadl began looking at her and she at him. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ began turning al-Fadl’s face to the other side. She said, “O Messenger of Allah, Allah’s obligation upon His servants regarding Hajj has found my father an old man who cannot remain mounted on a riding beast. Should I perform Hajj on his behalf?” He said, “Yes.” That was during the Farewell Pilgrimage."],[5846,"A man came to the Prophet ﷺ and said: O Messenger of Allah, my father is an old man who is not able to perform Hajj. Should I perform Hajj on his behalf? The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"Yes, perform Hajj on behalf of your father.\""],[5847,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ passed by a woman and it was said to her, \"Is this the Messenger of Allah ﷺ?\" So she took the arm of a boy who was with her and said, \"Is there Hajj for this one, O Messenger of Allah ﷺ?\" He said, \"Yes, and for you is a reward.\""],[5848,"While the Prophet ﷺ was walking in the valley of al-Rawha', a delegation approached. A man among them said, \"Who are you?\" He said, \"We are the Muslims.\" Then a woman said, \"Who are you?\" He said, \"I am the Messenger of Allah.\" So she brought out a boy and said, \"O Messenger of Allah, is there Hajj for this one?\" He said, \"Yes, and for you is a reward.\""],[5849,"Asmāʾ asked the Prophet ﷺ about a mother of hers who was a polytheist. She said, “She came to me desiring and fearing [something]; should I maintain ties with her?” He said, “Yes.” *"],[5850,"Between every two calls to prayer there is a prayer for one who wishes."],[5851,"Between every two calls to prayer there is a prayer for one who wishes. Between every two calls to prayer there is a prayer for one who wishes. Ibn Buraydah would pray two rak'ahs before the sunset prayer."],[5853,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ came out and found the people in Ramadan praying in a corner of the mosque. He ﷺ said, \"Who are these?\" It was said, \"People who do not have the Qur'an with them, and Ubayy b. Ka'b is leading them in prayer, and they pray by his prayer.\" The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, \"They are correct, or what an excellent thing they have done.\""],[5854,"The Prophet ﷺ said to me, \"What did you do regarding touching the Stone?\" I said, \"I touched it and left it.\" He ﷺ said, \"You did right.\""],[5855,"The Prophet ﷺ said to Abu Bakr, \"When do you pray the Witr prayer?\" He said, \"I pray Witr and then sleep.\" The Prophet said, \"You have preferred determination.\" Then he asked Umar, \"When do you pray the Witr prayer?\" He said, \"I sleep and then get up at night to pray Witr.\" The Prophet said, \"You have chosen the action of the strong.\""],[5856,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ came to the watering place and asked for a drink. Al-Abbas said, 'O Fadl, go to your mother and bring the Messenger of Allah ﷺ a drink from what she has.' The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, 'Give me a drink.' He said, 'O Messenger of Allah, they put their hands in it.' He ﷺ said, 'Give me a drink.' So he drank from it. Then he came to Zamzam, where they were drawing water and working in it, and said, 'Work, for you are upon a righteous deed.' Then he said, 'Were it not that you might be overcome, I would descend and place the rope on this,' pointing to his shoulder."],[5857,"That the Prophet ﷺ was asked about Bit' so he said: \"All drinks that intoxicate are unlawful.\" (Using translation from Tirmidhī 1863)"],[5858,"I said, 'O Messenger of Allah, which mosque was established first?' He said, 'The Sacred Mosque, then the Aqsa Mosque.' I said, 'How long was between them?' He said, 'Forty years. Wherever the prayer finds you, pray, for that is a mosque.'"],[5859,"I said: O Messenger of Allah, which mosque was placed on the earth first? He said: «The Sacred Mosque.» I said: O Messenger of Allah, then which? He said: «The Farthest Mosque.» I said: How much was between them? He said: «Forty years. Then wherever the prayer overtakes you, pray, for it is a mosque for you.»"],[5860,"I was favored over the prophets with six things: I was given comprehensive speech; I was aided with awe; spoils were made lawful for me; the earth was made pure and a mosque for me; I was sent to all creation; and the prophets were sealed with me."],[5861,"If you find only sheep pens and camel resting places, pray in the sheep pens and do not pray in the camel resting places."],[5862,"If you find only sheep pens and camel resting places, pray in the sheep pens, and do not pray in the camel resting places."],[5863,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ forbade praying between graves."],[5864,"He forbade praying in the graveyard."],[5865,"Do not sit on graves and do not pray toward them."],[5866,"When the Messenger of Allah ﷺ came to Madinah, he stayed in the upper part of Madinah among a clan called Banu 'Amr b. 'Awf. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ stayed among them for fourteen nights, then he sent for the leaders of Banu al-Najjar, and they came wearing their swords. Anas said: It is as if I can see the Messenger of Allah ﷺ on his mount, with Abu Bakr riding behind him, and the leaders of Banu al-Najjar around him, until he dismounted in the courtyard of Abu Ayyub. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to pray wherever the time for prayer overtook him, and he would pray in sheepfolds. Then he ordered that the mosque be built, and he sent for the leaders of Banu al-Najjar, and they came. He said, \"O Banu al-Najjar, sell me this wall of yours.\" They said, \"No, by Allah, we do not seek its price; it is only for Allah.\" Anas said: There was in it what I am telling you: there were graves of the polytheists, date palms, and cultivated land. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ ordered that the graves of the polytheists be dug up, the cultivated land be leveled, and the date palms be cut down. They placed the date palms in the direction of the qiblah of the mosque and made its two side pillars of stone. He said: They began carrying that rock while reciting rajaz verses, with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ with them, and they were saying: \"O Allah, there is no good except the good of the Hereafter, so forgive the Ansar and the Muhajirun.\""],[5867,"\"The Messenger of Allah said: 'All the earth is a mosque, except for graveyards and Hammam.'\" (Using translation from Ibn Mājah 745)"],[5868,"The Prophet ﷺ ordered the 'Uranis to drink from the urine and milk of camels."],[5869,"The delegation from 'Urayna came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and found the climate of Madinah unsuitable. So the Messenger of Allah ﷺ sent them to his milch camels and said, \"Drink from their milk and urine.\" They drank until they were cured and gained weight. Then they killed the shepherd of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, drove off the herd, and apostatized. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ sent in their pursuit, and they were brought back. He cut off their hands and feet, branded their eyes, and left them in the hot sun."],[5870,"A group from 'Uraynah came to the Prophet ﷺ. He said to them: \"If only you would go out to our small herd of camels and stay with them, and drink their milk and urine.\" They did so. When they recovered, they went to the shepherd of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, killed him, returned as disbelievers, and drove away the small herd of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ sent in pursuit of them. They were brought back, and he cut off their hands and feet and gouged out their eyes."],[5871,"A group from Banu 'Ukl—or he said from 'Uraynah—arrived in Madinah and found its climate unhealthy. The Prophet ﷺ ordered milch camels for them and told them to drink their milk and urine. They drank their milk and urine until they recovered and their sickness was gone. Then they killed the shepherd of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and drove away the livestock. That reached the Prophet ﷺ, and he sent after them in the morning. By the time the day had fully risen, they were brought back. Their hands and feet were cut off, their eyes were gouged out, and they were thrown onto the harrah, asking for water but not given any. Abu Qilabah said: \"These are people who killed, stole, disbelieved after their faith, and waged war against Allah and His Messenger ﷺ.\""],[5872,"I said, \"O Messenger of Allah, our land has grapes that we press and drink from.\" He said, \"Do not drink.\" I said, \"Can we treat the sick with it?\" The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, \"That is only a disease, not a cure.\""],[5873,"\"Whoever cannot find an izar, let him wear trousers; and whoever cannot find sandals, let him wear khuffs.\""],[5874,"\"Whoever cannot find an izar, let him wear trousers; and whoever cannot find sandals, let him wear khuffs.\""],[5875,"\"Whoever cannot find sandals, let him wear khuffs and cut them below the two ankles.\""],[5876,"\"If the one in ihram cannot find sandals, let him wear khuffs and cut them until they are below the two ankles.\""],[5877,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ commanded us to kill dogs, to the point that a woman would come in from the desert with a dog and kill it. Then he forbade us from killing them and said: Keep to the black one with two spots, for it is a devil."],[5878,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ granted a concession for incantation against snakes and scorpions."],[5879,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ granted a concession for ruqya against the evil eye, the ant's sting, and the scorpion's sting."],[5880,"«The Messenger of Allah ﷺ granted us a concession to wipe for three days, and had we asked for more, he would have increased it.»"],[5881,"\"The Prophet ﷺ granted permission to the shepherds to stone one day and omit one day.\""],[5882,"“The Prophet ﷺ permitted a distinguishing mark on two fingers.”"],[5883,"“The Prophet ﷺ granted a concession regarding the dog of farming.”"],[5884,"\"Whoever performs the Hajj to the House, let his last act be at the House, except for the menstruating women; the Messenger of Allah ﷺ granted them a concession.\""],[5885,"\"O Messenger of Allah, I think Safiyyah will hold us back.\" He said, \"What is the matter with her?\" She said, \"She has menstruated.\" He said, \"Had she not performed the ifadah?\" I said, \"Yes, but she has menstruated.\" He said, \"Then there is no restriction on her; let her depart.\""],[5886,"Safiyyah bt. Huyayy menstruated after she had performed the ifadah. A'ishah said: I mentioned her menstruation to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, \"Is she holding us back?\" I said, \"O Messenger of Allah, she has performed the ifadah and circumambulated the House, then she menstruated after the ifadah.\" The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, \"Then let her depart.\""],[5887,"The companions of Muhammad ﷺ, when one of them was fasting and the time of breaking the fast came, if he slept before breaking his fast, he would not eat that night or day until evening. Qays b. Sirmah was fasting, and when the time of breaking the fast came, he went to his wife and said, \"Do you have any food?\" She said, \"No, but I will seek some.\" So she sought some for him while he had been working that day, and sleep overcame him. His wife came and said, \"Disappointment for you!\" Then he woke in the morning. When midday came, he fainted. He mentioned that to the Prophet ﷺ, and this verse was revealed: \"It has been made lawful for you, on the night of the fast, to go to your wives.\" They rejoiced greatly, and He said: \"And eat and drink until the white thread becomes distinct to you from the black thread of dawn.\""],[5888,"I arrived in Makkah while I was menstruating, and I had not performed Tawaf of the House or between al-Safa and al-Marwa. I complained about that to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and he said: “Do what the pilgrim does, except that you should not perform Tawaf of the House until you become pure.”"],[5889,"I complained to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ that I was in pain. He ﷺ said: \"Perform tawaf behind the people while riding.\" She said: I performed tawaf while the Messenger of Allah ﷺ was praying beside the House and reciting \"By Mount Sinai and a written Book.\""],[5890,"He heard Jabir ibn Abdullah saying, \"Indeed, the Prophet ﷺ delivered a sermon one day and mentioned a man from his companions who was wrapped in a non-perfumed shroud and buried at night. The Prophet ﷺ reprimanded that the man should not be buried at night, except if there is a necessity for it.\""],[5891,"I saw the Messenger of Allah ﷺ praying on a mount, facing toward the east, in the expedition of Anmār."],[5892,"A sheep belonging to the wife of the Prophet ﷺ died. The Prophet ﷺ came to her and she informed him, so he said: \"Would you not benefit from its skin?\" She said: \"O Messenger of Allah, the skin of a dead animal?\" He said: \"Then the Messenger of Allah ﷺ recited: 'Say: I do not find in what has been revealed to me anything forbidden to one who eats it, except that it be dead meat' to the end of the verse. You are not eating it.\" Ibn Abbas said: \"So she sent for it, and it was skinned, and she made a water-skin from its hide.\""],[5893,"A sheep belonging to Sawdah bt. Zam'ah died. She said: \"O Messenger of Allah, so-and-so died,\" meaning the sheep. He said: \"Why did you not take its skin?\" She said: \"Should we take the skin of a sheep that died?\" The Prophet ﷺ said: \"He only said: 'Say: I do not find in what has been revealed to me anything forbidden' to the end of the verse. There is no harm that you tan it and benefit from it.\" She said: \"So we sent for it, and she skinned its hide and made a water-skin from it until it wore out.\""],[5895,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ combined on a journey he made, during a military expedition, between Zuhr and Asr, and Maghrib and Isha. I said to him, 'What led him to do that?' He said, 'He wanted not to cause hardship for his ummah.'"],[5896,"When the Messenger of Allah ﷺ set out before the sun declined, he would delay Dhuhr until the time of Asr, then dismount and combine them; and when the sun declined before he set out, he would pray and then depart."],[5897,"The Prophet ﷺ went out on the expedition of Tabūk. When he departed before the sun declined, he delayed ẓuhr until he combined it with ʿaṣr and prayed them together; and when he departed after the sun declined, he prayed ẓuhr and ʿaṣr together, then set out. And when he departed before maghrib, he delayed maghrib until he prayed it with ʿishāʾ; and when he departed after maghrib, he hastened ʿishāʾ and prayed it with maghrib."],[5898,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ departed on the day of Arafah until, when he was at the mountain pass, he dismounted and urinated, then performed ablution but did not complete it thoroughly. I said to him, 'The prayer,' and he ﷺ replied, 'The prayer is ahead of you.' He mounted, and when he reached Muzdalifah he dismounted, performed ablution and completed it thoroughly. Then the prayer was announced, and he prayed Maghrib. Then every person made his camel kneel at his lodging. Then the prayer was announced for Isha and he prayed it, and he did not pray anything between them."],[5899,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ prayed Dhuhr and Asr together, and Maghrib and Isha together, without fear or travel."],[5900,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ prayed in Madinah seven and eight: Dhuhr and Asr, and Maghrib and Isha."],[5901,"\"that he prayed with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ during the Farewell Pilgrimage, Maghrib and Isha combined at Muzdalifah.\""],[5902,"\"Ibn Umar prayed the Maghrib prayer with us at Muzdalifah, three rak'ahs. When he said the salam, he stood and prayed Isha, two rak'ahs. And he narrated that the Prophet ﷺ prayed with them in that place the same as that.\""],[5903,"When this verse was revealed: {O you who believe, when you consult privately with the Messenger, then offer something in charity before your private consultation}, he said: The Prophet ﷺ said to 'Ali, \"O 'Ali, command them to give charity.\" He said, \"O Messenger of Allah, how much?\" He said, \"A dinar.\" He said, \"They cannot bear it.\" He said, \"Then half a dinar.\" He said, \"They cannot bear it.\" He said, \"Then how much?\" He said, \"A barley grain.\" He said: Then the Prophet ﷺ said to 'Ali, \"You are indeed abstemious.\" He said: Then Allah revealed: {Are you afraid to offer charity before your private consultation? Since you did not do so, and Allah has turned to you in mercy, then establish prayer and give zakah.} He said: 'Ali used to say, \"Through me the burden was lightened for this community.\""],[5904,"I witnessed the Hajj of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ with him, and I prayed the Fajr prayer with him in the mosque of al-Khayf in Mina. When he finished his prayer, there were two men at the back of the people who had not prayed. They were brought to him, their sides trembling. He said, “What prevented you two from praying with us?” They said, “O Messenger of Allah, we had already prayed in our dwellings.” He said, “Do not do that. If you have prayed in your dwellings, then come to a mosque where there is a congregation, pray with them, for it will be a supererogatory prayer for you.”"],[5905,"I was a man who emitted madhy frequently, so I used to bathe in winter until my back cracked. I mentioned that to the Prophet ﷺ, or it was mentioned to him, and he said, “Do not do that. When you see madhy, wash your penis and perform ablution as you do for prayer; and when you ejaculate water (mani), perform ritual bathing.”"],[5906,"We went out with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ on the expedition of Dhat al-Riqa'. A man among the Muslims had struck the wife of a man among the polytheists. When the Messenger of Allah ﷺ returned, her husband came, having been absent. When he was informed, he swore not to stop until he had shed blood among the companions of Muhammad ﷺ. He went out following the trail of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ encamped and said, 'Who is a man to guard us this night of ours?' A man from the Muhajirun and a man from the Ansar volunteered, saying, 'We are, O Messenger of Allah.' He ﷺ said, 'Then be at the mouth of the mountain pass.' He said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ and his companions had descended into a mountain pass of the valley. When the two men went out to the mouth of the pass, the Ansari said to the Muhajiri, 'Which part of the night would you like me to relieve you in, its beginning or its end?' He said, 'Relieve me in its beginning.' He said: So the Muhajiri lay down and slept, and the Ansari stood up to pray. The husband of the woman came, and when he saw the figure of the man, he knew that he was the watchman of the people, so he shot an arrow at him and lodged it in him. He pulled it out and remained standing in prayer. Then he shot another arrow and lodged it in him. He pulled it out and remained standing in prayer. Then he came back for the third time and lodged it in him. He pulled it out and put it down, then bowed and prostrated, then roused his companion and said, 'Sit up, for I have been struck.' He sprang up. When the man saw the two of them, he knew that he had been noticed and fled. When the Muhajiri saw the blood on the Ansari, he said, 'Glory be to Allah! Why did you not rouse me when he first shot you?' He said, 'I was in the middle of a surah that I was reciting and did not like to cut it off until I had completed it. When he continued shooting at me, I bowed and alerted you. By Allah, had I not feared neglecting a frontier that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ commanded me to guard, my soul would have departed before I cut it off or completed it.'"],[5907,"I said to Anas b. Malik, “Was shaking hands practiced in the time of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ?” He said, “Yes.”"],[5908,"She borrowed a necklace from Asma' and it was lost. The Prophet ﷺ sent some of his companions to search for it. The prayer time came upon them, so they prayed without ablution. When they came to the Prophet ﷺ, they complained to him about that. He said, 'Then the verse of dry ablution was revealed.' Usayd b. Hudayr said, 'May Allah reward you well. By Allah, no affair ever befell you except that Allah made for you a way out of it and made in it a blessing for the Muslims.'"],[5909,"Men and women used to perform ablution together during the time of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ."],[5910,"I saw the Messenger of Allah ﷺ in a red dome, and I saw Bilal bring out his ablution water, and I saw the people rushing to his ablution water, wiping themselves with it. He said: Then Bilal brought out a spear and planted it, then the Messenger of Allah ﷺ came out in a red striped garment and prayed facing it while people and animals were passing in front of him."],[5911,"One of the Prophet's ﷺ wives performed ghusl in a large bowl, then the Prophet ﷺ came to perform wudu or ghusl from the leftover water. She said, 'O Messenger of Allah, I was in a state of janabah.' The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, 'Water is not made impure by anything.'"],[5912,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ met me while I was in a state of major ritual impurity. I walked with him while he was holding my hand, but I slipped away from him, went and bathed, then returned to him and sat with him. He said: \"Where were you, O Abu Hurayrah?\" I said: \"You met me while I was in a state of major ritual impurity, and I disliked sitting with you.\" The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"The believer does not become impure.\""],[5913,"\"And indeed, a severe cold inflicted them that they had never seen before. So he went out to perform the morning prayer and said, 'By Allah, I had a wet dream last night, so I washed my private parts and performed ablution for prayer.' Then he led them in prayer. When he arrived to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ , the Messenger of Allah ﷺ asked his companions, 'How did you find 'Umar and his companions?' They praised him and said, 'O Messenger of Allah, he led us in prayer while he was in a state of sexual impurity.' So the Messenger of Allah ﷺ sent for 'Umar and asked him, and he informed him about that and the severe cold he had encountered. 'Umar said, 'O Messenger of Allah, indeed Allah says, \"And do not kill yourselves.\"' The Messenger of Allah ﷺ smiled at 'Umar.\""],[5914,"A woman asked Aishah: \"Does a menstruating woman make up the prayer?\" She replied: \"Are you a Haruriyyah? We used to menstruate in the presence of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and we did not make up [the prayers], nor were we commanded to make them up.\""],[5915,"\"I used to comb the head of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ while I was menstruating.\""],[5916,"A man stayed with ʿĀʾishah, Mother of the Believers, and in the morning he began washing his garment. ʿĀʾishah said, \"It would have sufficed you, if you saw it, to wash its place; and if you did not see it, to sprinkle around it. I used to rub it from the garment of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ with a vigorous rubbing, and he would pray in it.\""],[5917,"I used to wash janābah from the garment of the Prophet ﷺ, and he would go out to prayer while the spots of water were still in his garment."],[5918,"I used to wash semen from the garment of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and he would go out to prayer while the traces of the spots were still visible in his garment."],[5919,"One day we prayed with Umar b. Abd al-Aziz, then we entered upon Anas b. Malik and found him standing in prayer. When he finished, we said: O Abu Hamzah, which prayer did you pray? He said: Asr. We said: We have just finished Zuhr, which we prayed with Umar b. Abd al-Aziz. Anas said: I saw the Messenger of Allah ﷺ praying like this, so I will never abandon it."],[5920,"We used to pray Asr with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, then a she-camel would be slaughtered and divided into ten portions, then cooked, and we would eat well-cooked meat before the sun set. And we would pray Maghrib in the time of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and one of us would leave while he could still see the place where his arrow fell."],[5921,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ prayed Asr with us. When he finished, a man from Banu Salimah came to him and said, 'O Messenger of Allah, we want to slaughter a she-camel of ours, and we would like you to attend it.' He said, 'Yes.' So he went, and we went with him. We found the she-camel not yet slaughtered, so it was slaughtered, then cut up, then some of it was cooked, then we ate before the sun disappeared."],[5922,"Mu'adh b. Jabal used to pray Maghrib with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, then return to his people and lead them in prayer."],[5923,"A young woman from the Arabs was a slave, and they set her free. She was with them, and a little girl of theirs went out wearing a red scarf of leather straps. She said: She put it down, and a kite passed by it while it was lying there, and it thought it was meat, so it snatched it. She said: They looked for it but did not find it. She said: They accused me of it, so they set about searching me. They searched until they searched her private part. She said: By Allah, while I was standing with them, the kite passed by and dropped it, and it fell among them. She said: I said, “This is what you accused me of; you claimed I had it, and I am innocent of it, and here it is.” She said: She then went to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and embraced Islam. ʿĀʾishah said: “She had a tent in the mosque. She used to come to me and talk in my presence, and she would not sit with me except that she said…”"],[5924,"“I used to spend the night in the mosque of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and I was a young unmarried man. The dogs used to urinate and come and go in the mosque, and they would not sprinkle anything of that.”"],[5925,"“We used to eat bread and meat in the mosque during the time of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, then we would pray and not perform ablution.”"],[5926,"«The adhan in the time of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, Abu Bakr, and Umar was twice twice; when Uthman came and the people increased, he commanded a caller to call on al-Zawrāʾ.»"],[5927,"«The adhan in the time of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ was only twice, and the iqamah once, except that he would say: The prayer has been established, the prayer has been established. When we heard the iqamah we performed ablution, then came to the prayer.»"],[5928,"When they prayed with the Prophet ﷺ, they remained standing until they saw him prostrate, then they would prostrate."],[5929,"When we prayed behind the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, we did not cease standing until we saw him prostrate; then we would prostrate."],[5930,"Some men used to pray with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ tying their waist-wrappers around their necks like children, and it was said to the women: 'Do not raise your heads until the men have sat up straight.'"],[5931,"When we prayed with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and one of us could not press his forehead to the ground, he would spread his garment and prostrate on it."],[5932,"We used to pray while animals passed in front of us. We asked the Prophet ﷺ, and he said: 'Something like the backrest of a saddle placed before one of you will prevent harm from whatever passes in front of him.'"],[5933,"We were with Ibn Abbas, and we mentioned what cuts off prayer. They said: 'The donkey and the woman.' Ibn Abbas said: 'I came with a boy from the Banu Abd al-Muttalib, riding behind me on a donkey, while the Messenger of Allah ﷺ was praying with the people in an open space. We left the donkey in front of them, then we came and entered between them, and he did not mind that.'"],[5934,"I witnessed the Prophet ﷺ at al-Batha while he was in a red tent, and with him were some people. Bilal came and gave the call to prayer, then he started turning his mouth here and there. Sufyan said: meaning by saying 'Hayya ala al-salah, Hayya ala al-falah.' He said: And he brought out the leftover water of the Prophet's ﷺ ablution, and the people took from it, some getting it and some sprinkling it, until a child would insert his hand under the armpits of the people and reach it. Bilal planted a spear in front of him, and a donkey, a woman, and a dog passed and were not prevented. He prayed Zuhr as two rak'ahs, then he prayed two rak'ahs, two rak'ahs, until he arrived in Madinah."],[5935,"Mu'adh b. Jabal used to pray with the Prophet ﷺ, then return to his people and lead them in prayer. He said: One night the Prophet ﷺ delayed the Isha prayer. Mu'adh b. Jabal prayed with him, then returned to us and stepped forward to lead us. He began Surah al-Baqarah. When a man among the people saw that, he withdrew and prayed alone, then left. We said to him, \"What is the matter with you, O so-and-so? Have you become a hypocrite?\" He said, \"I have not become a hypocrite, but I will go to the Prophet ﷺ and inform him.\" He came to the Prophet ﷺ and said, \"O Messenger of Allah, Mu'adh prays with you, then returns and leads us. You delayed the Isha prayer last night, and he prayed with you, then returned to us and stepped forward to lead us. He began Surah al-Baqarah. When I saw that, I withdrew and prayed alone. O Messenger of Allah, we are workers who irrigate with camels, and we work with our hands.\" The Prophet ﷺ said, \"Are you a troublemaker, O Mu'adh? Are you a troublemaker, O Mu'adh? Recite such-and-such a surah and such-and-such a surah.\""],[5936,"Mu'adh b. Jabal used to pray the Isha prayer with the Prophet ﷺ, then go to his people and pray it with them, and he was their imam."],[5937,"He prayed the morning prayer with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ without having prayed the two rak'ahs of Fajr. When the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said the salam, he said the salam with him, then he stood up and prayed the two rak'ahs of Fajr while the Messenger of Allah ﷺ was looking at him and did not object to that."],[5938,"\"When the mu'adhdhin called the adhan, some people from among the companions of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ would get up and hasten to the pillars to pray, until the Messenger of Allah ﷺ came out to them while they were thus praying the two rak'ahs before Maghrib, and there was nothing between the adhan and the iqamah.\""],[5939,"Ubayy b. Kaʿb came to the Prophet ﷺ and said: “O Messenger of Allah, something happened from me tonight,” meaning in Ramadan. He said: “And what is that, O Ubayy? He said: Women in my house said: ‘We do not recite the Qur’an, so we will pray following your prayer.’ He said: So I led them in eight rakʿahs, then I performed witr. He said: And it was as if he was pleased, and he did not say anything.”"],[5940,"We used to pray the Friday prayer with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, then we would return and take a nap."],[5942,"I attended the funeral of 'Abd al-Rahman b. Samurah, and Ziyad came out walking in front of his bier, with men facing the bier and being trampled on their heels, saying: 'Slowly, slowly, may Allah bless you,' until when we were in part of the mirbad, Abu Bakrah caught up with us on a mule. When he saw those people and what they were doing, he charged his mule at them and aimed his whip at them and said: «Make way, for by the One in Whose hand is my soul, I saw us with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and we were almost running with it at a fast pace.» He said: Then the people came and hastened their walking, and Ziyad hastened his walking."],[5943,"When we missed a man at the Fajr and Isha prayers, we would think ill of him."],[5944,"I saw us, and no one stayed behind from the prayer except a hypocrite whose hypocrisy was known, or a sick person. A sick man would walk between two men to come to the prayer. He said: 'The Messenger of Allah ﷺ taught us the ways of guidance, and among the ways of guidance is praying in the mosque where the call to prayer is given.'"],[5945,"I came riding on a donkey, and at that time I had nearly reached puberty. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ was leading the people in prayer at Mina. I passed in front of part of the row, dismounted, let the donkey go to graze, and entered the row, and no one objected to that."],[5946,"In the time of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, when he said the salutation from the prescribed prayer, the women would rise, and the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and those men who prayed behind him would remain. When the Messenger of Allah ﷺ stood, the men would stand."],[5947,"We used to pray with the Prophet ﷺ in intense heat. One of us would take a handful of pebbles and put them in this palm of his, then in this palm of his, and when they cooled, he would prostrate on them."],[5948,"«I saw us, when I was with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, almost running with funerals at a fast pace.»"],[5949,"I was sitting with Ibn 'Umar when a funeral procession was brought, and women were weeping over it. Ibn 'Umar disapproved of that and rebuked them. Salamah b. al-Azraq said: 'I testify about Abu Hurayrah that I heard him say: A funeral procession passed by the Messenger of Allah ﷺ while I was with him, and 'Umar b. al-Khattab was with him, and women were weeping over it. He scolded them and rebuked them. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: Let them be, O 'Umar, for the eye sheds tears, the soul is afflicted, and the time of parting is near.'"],[5950,"We used to give for Zakat al-Fitr, when the Messenger of Allah ﷺ was among us, a sa' of food, or a sa' of dates, or a sa' of barley, or a sa' of aqt (dried curd). We continued doing that until Mu'awiya came to us from Syria to Madinah. Among what he said to the people was: 'I do not think that two mudds of Syrian wheat are equivalent to a sa' of this.' So people adopted that."],[5951,"Abu Sa'id al-Khudri said, when they mentioned to him the sadaqah of Ramadan: 'I will not give except what I used to give during the time of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ: a sa' of dates, or a sa' of wheat, or a sa' of barley, or a sa' of aqt.' A man from the people said to him: 'Or two mudds of wheat?' He said: 'No, those are the values of Mu'awiya. I do not accept them and I will not act upon them.'"],[5952,"\"I never used to give out anything except a saa' (a unit of measurement), as we used to give during the time of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ , a saa' of dates, or a saa' of barley, or a saa' of raisins, or a saa' of dry cottage cheese, which is for the obligatory charity of breaking the fast.\""],[5953,"\"One of us would have to make up fasts during the time of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and would not be able to make them up with the Prophet ﷺ until Sha'ban came. The Prophet ﷺ did not fast in any month as much as he fasted in Sha'ban; he used to fast it except for a little; rather, he used to fast all of it.\""],[5954,"'Ali came from Yemen, and the Prophet ﷺ said to him, \"With what did you enter ihram?\" He said, \"I entered ihram with what the Prophet of Allah ﷺ entered ihram.\" He said, \"If I did not have the sacrificial animal with me, I would exit ihram.\""],[5955,"\"That the Messenger of Allah ﷺ went out of Medina for Hajj, and I also went out from Yemen. I said, 'Labbaik Ihlaalan ka Ihlaal-in-Nabiyyi ﷺ .' So, Prophet ﷺ said, 'Indeed, I have combined Umrah and Hajj.'\""],[5956,"that he asked Anas b. Malik, while they were both going in the morning from Mina to Arafat: How did you use to act on this day with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ? He said: \"The one who uttered the talbiyah at Mina would do so, and he would not object to him; and the one who said Allahu Akbar would do so, and he would not object to him.\""],[5957,"They were present with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ in Madinah. He would send the sacrificial animal, and whoever of us wished would delay, and whoever wished would leave it."],[5958,"We slaughtered with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ at al-Ḥudaybiyyah a cow for seven people and a camel for seven people."],[5959,"We were with the Prophet ﷺ on a journey when the time of sacrifice came, and we shared in a cow among seven and in a camel among seven or ten."],[5960,"We sacrificed with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ a jadhaʿ (one-year-old) from sheep."],[5961,"The Prophet ﷺ met 'Abd al-Rahman b. 'Awf and on him was a trace of yellow perfume. The Prophet ﷺ said to him, \"What is this, 'Abd al-Rahman?\" He said, \"I married a woman from the Ansar.\" He said, \"How much did you give her as dower?\" He said, \"The weight of a date stone of gold.\" The Prophet ﷺ said, \"Hold a wedding feast, even with a sheep.\" Anas said: I saw him after his death divide among each of his wives one hundred thousand."],[5962,"\"The dowry, when the Messenger of Allah was among us, was ten Awaq.\" (Using translation from Nasāʾī 3348)"],[5963,"\"We used to practice coitus interruptus during the time of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and he did not forbid us from it.\""],[5964,"We used to sell our slave women who were mothers of children while the Prophet ﷺ was alive among us, and he saw no harm in that."],[5965,"We used to sell slave mothers during the time of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and Abu Bakr. When it was the time of Umar, he prohibited their sale."],[5966,"One day the Messenger of Allah ﷺ was met by boys and slave girls and slaves from the Ansar, and he said: \"By Allah, I love you.\""],[5967,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ sent him on the expedition of Dhat al-Salasil. His companions asked him to light a fire, but he forbade them. They spoke to Abu Bakr, who spoke to him about it. He said, \"None of them shall light a fire or I will throw him into it.\" He said, \"They met the enemy and defeated them. They wanted to pursue them, but he forbade them. When the army returned, they mentioned this to the Prophet ﷺ and complained about him. He said, 'O Messenger of Allah, I disliked allowing them to light a fire lest their enemy see how few they were, and I disliked that they pursue them lest reinforcements come to the enemy and they turn back against them.' The Messenger of Allah ﷺ praised his action. Then he said, 'O Messenger of Allah, who is the most beloved of people to you?' He said, 'Why?' He said, 'So that I may love whom you love.' He said, ''A'ishah.' He said, 'Among men?' He said, 'Abu Bakr.'\""],[5968,"The ʿishāʾ prayer was announced, and a man stood before the Prophet ﷺ and said: I have a need from you. He stood aside with him until the people dozed, or some of the people dozed. “Then he stood and prayed, and they prayed, and he did not mention that they performed ablution anew.”"],[5969,"Abu Talhah was shooting arrows in front of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ; the Prophet ﷺ would raise his head from behind him to see where his arrows fell, so Abu Talhah would stretch out his chest to shield the Messenger of Allah ﷺ with it, saying, “Thus, O Prophet of Allah, may Allah make me your ransom—my neck before your neck.”"],[5970,"“He was standing at the head of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ with his sword, his face veiled, while ʿUrwah was with him. ʿUrwah began to touch the beard of the Prophet ﷺ and speak with him, so al-Mughirah said to ʿUrwah, ‘Either stop your hand from his beard, or it will not come back to you.’” He said: ʿUrwah said, “Who is this?” He said, “This is your nephew, al-Mughirah b. Shuʿbah.” ʿUrwah said, “O traitor, you have not yet washed your head of your treachery.”"],[5971,"They used to pray Maghrib with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, then compete in archery."],[5972,"We went out with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ on an expedition while we were six men sharing one camel, taking turns riding it. Our feet became sore, and my feet became sore, and my toenails fell off. We used to wrap our feet with rags. The expedition was called Dhat al-Riqa' because of the rags we bound on our feet. Abu Burdah said: Abu Musa narrated this hadith, then he disliked that, saying, 'What need did I have to mention this hadith?' because he disliked disclosing any of his deeds."],[5973,"I raided with Abu Bakr when the Messenger of Allah ﷺ sent him over us. We attacked some polytheists at night and killed them. Our watchword was 'Amit! Amit!' I killed with my own hand seven people of the polytheist households."],[5974,"\"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ appointed Abu Bakr as commander over us. We raided some people from the polytheists, and we attacked them by night and killed them. Our war cry was 'Kill! Kill!'\" Salamah said: \"I killed with my own hand that night seven people of households.\""],[5975,"\"Our war cry on the night we attacked Hawazin with Abu Bakr, whom the Prophet ﷺ appointed over us, was 'Kill! Kill!'\" He said: \"I killed with my own hand that night seven people of households.\""],[5976,"“I was among those concerning whom Saʿd b. Muʿādh judged. They did not find that I had grown pubic hair, so I was spared. Here I am.”"],[5977,"I remember that I went out with the children to meet the Prophet ﷺ upon his return from Tabuk at Thaniyyat al-Wada'."],[5978,"A horse of his went astray and was taken by the enemy; then the Muslims prevailed over it, and it was returned to him in the time of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ."],[5979,"ʿAbdullāh ibn Shaddād and Abū Burdah sent me and said to me: “Go to ʿAbdullāh ibn Abī Awfā and say to him, ‘ʿAbdullāh ibn Shaddād and Abū Burdah send you greetings of peace,’ and ask, ‘Did you used to pay in advance for wheat, barley, and raisins?’” He said: “Yes. We used to obtain war-booty in the time of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and we would pay in advance for wheat, barley, dates, and raisins.” I said: “From someone who has crops, or from someone who does not have crops?” He said: “We did not used to ask them about that.”"],[5980,"Makhrafah al-'Abdi and I brought cloth from Hajar, and the Messenger of Allah ﷺ came to us and bargained with us for a pair of trousers. With him was a weigher who weighed for a fee. The Prophet ﷺ said to him: 'Weigh and give more.'"],[5981,"We used to drink at the time of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ while standing, and we would eat while walking."],[5982,"I entered with Khalid b. al-Walid b. al-Mughirah into the house of Maymunah bt. al-Harith with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. A roasted dhabb was brought, and the Messenger of Allah ﷺ reached for it. One of the women who were in Maymunah's house said: 'Tell the Messenger of Allah ﷺ what he is about to eat.' So the Messenger of Allah ﷺ lifted his hand. I said: 'Is it forbidden, O Messenger of Allah?' He said: 'No, but it is not found in the land of my people, so I find myself averse to it.' Khalid b. al-Walid said: So I pulled it over and ate it while the Messenger of Allah ﷺ was watching."],[5983,"We slaughtered a horse during the time of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and ate it."],[5984,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ gave us permission to eat horse meat and forbade us the meat of domestic donkeys."],[5985,"I served the Messenger of Allah ﷺ in this cup of mine milk, water, honey, and nabidh."],[5986,"When Abu Usayd al-Saidi gave a wedding feast, he invited the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and his companions. Then he made food for them, and only his wife, Umm Usayd, served it to them. She moistened some dates overnight in a stone vessel. When the Messenger of Allah ﷺ finished, she brought it to him and served him, singling him out for that."],[5987,"Nabidh used to be made for him in a stone vessel, and he would drink it on the first day, the second, and the third up to the middle of the day."],[5989,"Al-Nu'man b. Bashir addressed the people in Kufa and said: I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: 'Wine comes from juice, raisins, dates, wheat, barley, and corn. And I forbid you from every intoxicant.'"],[5990,"Every intoxicant is unlawful, and every intoxicant is wine."],[5991,"Abu Ubayda b. al-Jarrah, Suhayl b. Bayda', and Ubayy b. Ka'b were with Abu Talha, and I was serving them a drink until it nearly affected them. Then a Muslim passerby called out: 'Do you know that wine has been forbidden?' He said: By Allah, they did not wait; they told me to overturn the containers, and I did so. They never returned to any of that until they met Allah. And that drink was unripe and ripe dates, and it was our wine on that day.”"],[5992,"'When nothing was available for the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, nabīdh would be made for him in a stone trough.'"],[5993,"Nabīdh used to be made for him in a waterskin. If no waterskin was available, then in a stone trough."],[5994,"'A sheep belonging to Sawda died, so we tanned its skin and used to make nabīdh in it until it became a worn-out waterskin.'"],[5995,"A sheep belonging to Sawda bt. Zam‘a died. She said: 'O Messenger of Allah, so-and-so has died,' meaning the sheep. He said: 'Why did you not take its skin?' She said: 'Should we take the skin of a sheep that has died?' The Prophet ﷺ said: 'Allah only said: {Say, “I do not find in what has been revealed to me anything forbidden to one who eats it except carrion, or flowing blood”}. There is no harm in your tanning it and benefiting from it.' She said: 'So we sent for it, skinned it, and made it into a waterskin until it wore out.'"],[5996,"\"The Messenger of Allahﷺ arrived in Medina and his companion Abu Bakr was very dark-skinned. He covered himself with henna and dye until his skin became black. When I woke up in the morning, I said, 'His skin has become black.' He said, 'I did not say black.'\""],[5997,"“Al-ʿAbbās branded a camel or an animal on its face. The Prophet ﷺ saw it and became angry. ʿAbbās said, ‘I will only brand it on its rear,’ so he branded it on its jāʿiratayn (the two fleshy parts of the rump).”"],[5998,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ saw a donkey branded on its face and disapproved of it. The man said, “By Allah, I will only brand it on the furthest part of the face.” So he ordered a donkey of his to be cauterized on its jāʿiratayn, and he was the first to cauterize the jāʿiratayn."],[5999,"\"I sat with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ more than a hundred times, and his companions would recite poetry to one another and discuss things from the affairs of the Jahiliyyah while he remained silent, and sometimes he would smile with them ﷺ.\""],[6000,"“When the Messenger of Allah ﷺ prayed the dawn prayer, he would sit in his prayer place until the sun rose. They would sit and converse, and they would engage in matters of the Jahiliyyah, and they would laugh, and he ﷺ would smile.”"],[6001,"\"When the Messenger of Allah ﷺ entered Makkah, the people of Makkah stood in two rows.\" He said: \"And Abdullah b. Rawahah walked reciting.\""],[6002,"A man from the Companions of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ met me who had a heaviness in his tongue that prevented him from speaking clearly. He mentioned Uthman, and 'Abdullah said: By Allah, I do not know what he says, except that you know, O assembly of the Companions of the Prophet Muhammad, that during the lifetime of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ we used to say: Abu Bakr, then Umar, then Uthman. And it is only this wealth; if he gives it, you are pleased."],[6003,"During the lifetime of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ we used to rank them in excellence: Abu Bakr, then Umar, then Uthman, then we would remain silent."],[6004,"He ﷺ entered upon me while I was playing with toys. He lifted the curtain and said: “What is this, O A'ishah?” I said: Toys, O Messenger of Allah. He said: “What is this that I see among them?” I said: A horse, O Messenger of Allah. He said: “A horse made of patches with a wing?” She said: I said: Did not Sulayman b. Dawud have horses with wings? The Messenger of Allah ﷺ laughed."],[6006,"I used to play with dolls, and my friends would come and play with me. When they saw the Prophet ﷺ they would get up and leave him, so he would bring them in to me, and they would play with me."],[6007,"While the Abyssinians were playing with their spears, Umar entered and leaned on the stones, then the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, \"Leave them, O Umar.\""],[6008,"Abu Bakr entered upon her while she had two slave girls in the days of Mina, singing, and the Messenger of Allah ﷺ was covered with his garment. Abu Bakr scolded them. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ uncovered himself and said: “Leave them, O Abu Bakr, for these are days of Eid.” She said: I saw the Messenger of Allah ﷺ shielding me with his cloak while I looked at the Abyssinians playing, and I was a young girl. So estimate the age of a young Arab girl."],[6009,"Abu Bakr entered upon her during the days of Tashriq, and with her were two slave girls singing and beating the duff. He reviled them and tore their duffs. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"Leave them, for these are days of Eid.\""],[6010,"Indeed, the Abyssinians (Ethiopians) were presenting themselves in front of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and speaking in a language that he did not understand. So the Messenger of Allah ﷺ asked, \"What are they saying?\" They replied, \"Muhammad is a righteous servant.\""],[6011,"Abu Bakr entered upon her during the days of Eid, and with her were two slave girls singing, beating the duff, and striking [it]. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ was covered with his garment. Abu Bakr scolded them, and the Messenger of Allah ﷺ uncovered his face and said: \"Leave them, O Abu Bakr, for these are days of Eid, and those are the days of Mina.\" Aisha said: \"I saw the Messenger of Allah ﷺ shielding me with his cloak while I was looking at the Abyssinians playing in the mosque, and I was a young girl.\""],[6012,"About the night prayer of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, she said: “Do you not recite this surah: {O you wrapped in garments}?” I said: “Yes.” She said: “Indeed Allah, Mighty and Exalted, made the night prayer obligatory in the beginning of this surah, so the Prophet of Allah ﷺ and his companions stood for a year until their feet swelled. Then Allah, Mighty and Exalted, withheld its conclusion for twelve months in the heaven, then Allah, Mighty and Exalted, sent down the alleviation at the end of this surah, so the night prayer became voluntary after it had been obligatory.”"],[6013,"“When the Messenger of Allah ﷺ prayed a prayer, he loved to persist in it. And when sleep, illness, or pain kept him from the night prayer, he would pray twelve rakʿahs during the day.”"],[6014,"\"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to sleep until the middle of the night or a little before or after it. Then the Messenger of Allah ﷺ would wake up, wipe the sleep from his face with his hands, and recite the last ten verses of Surah Al-Imran. After that, he would go towards a hanging water container and perform ablution from it.\""],[6015,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ would sometimes pray in his voluntary prayer sitting, and he would recite a surah slowly, reciting it so deliberately that it would become longer than the longest of them."],[6016,"I asked Ibn Abbas, \"How was the prayer of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ at night?\" He said, \"He ﷺ would recite in some of his rooms, and those outside would hear him.\""],[6017,"I said to Aisha, \"Have you seen the Prophet ﷺ reciting aloud in his prayer or in a low voice?\" She said, \"Sometimes he recited aloud in his prayer, and sometimes in a low voice.\" I said, \"Praise be to Allah who has made the matter spacious.\""],[6019,"When he rose at night, he would clean his mouth with the siwak."],[6020,"That he spent the night at Maymunah's, the wife of the Prophet ﷺ, and she was his maternal aunt. He said: I lay down across the width of the cushion, and the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and his family lay along its length. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ slept until midnight, or a little before or after it. He woke up and began wiping sleep from his face with his hands, then recited the ten closing verses of Surah Al 'Imran. Then he went to a hanging water skin, performed ablution from it and did it well, then stood to pray.\" 'Abdullah said: I got up and did as he did, then went and stood at his side. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ placed his right hand on my head and took hold of my right ear, twisting it. He prayed two rak'ahs, then two rak'ahs, then two rak'ahs, then two rak'ahs, then prayed witr. Then he lay down until the mu'adhdhin came to him, then he stood and prayed two brief rak'ahs, then went out and prayed the morning prayer.\""],[6021,"“When the Messenger of Allah ﷺ prayed Tahajjud at night, he would say: “Allahumma lakal-hamd, Anta nurus-samawati wal-ard wa man fihinna. Wa lakal-hamd, Anta qayyamus-samawati wal-ard wa man fihinna. Wa lakal-hamd, Anta malikus- samawati wal-ard wa man fihinna. Wa lakal-hamd, Antal-haqq, wa waʿduka haqq, wa liqa’uka haqq, wa qawluka haqq, wal-jannatu haqq, wan-naru haqq, was-saʿatu haqq, wan-nabiyyuna haqq, wa Muhammadun haqq. Allahumma laka aslamtu, wa bika amantu, wa ʿalaika tawakkaltu wa ilaika anabtu, wa bika khasamtu, wa ilaika hakamtu, faghfirli ma qaddamtu wa ma akhkhartu, wa ma asrartu wa ma aʿlantu. Antal-muqaddimu wa Antal-muakhkhiru. La ilaha illa anta wa la ilaha ghairuka, wa la hawla wa la quwwata illa bika (O Allah, to you is praise, You are the Light of the heavens and the earth, and everyone therein. To You is praise, You are the Sustainer of the heavens and the earth, and everyone therein. To You is praise, You are the Sovereign of the heavens and the earth, and everyone therein. To You is praise, You are the Truth; Your promise is true, the meeting with You is true, Your saying is true, Paradise is true, the Fire is true, the Hour is true, the Prophets are true, and Muhammad ﷺ is true. O Allah, to You have I submitted, in You I believe, in You have I put my trust, to You I turn in repentance, by Your help I argue, to You I refer my case, so forgive me for my past and future sins, what I have done in secret and what I have done openly. You are the One Who brings forward and puts back. None has the right to be worshipped but You, and there is none who has the right to be worshipped other than You. And there is no power and no strength except with You.” Another chain that Ibn ʿAbbas narrated: “When the Messenger of Allah ﷺ stood during the night for Tahajjud,” and he mentioned something similar. (Using translation from Ibn Mājah 1355)"],[6022,"When he stood for prayer in the middle of the night, he would say, \"O Allah, to You belongs praise. You are the Light of the heavens and the earth, and to You belongs praise. You are the Sustainer of the heavens and the earth, and to You belongs praise. You are the Lord of the heavens and the earth and whoever is in them. You are the Truth, Your promise is true, meeting You is true, Paradise is true, Hellfire is true, and the Hour is true. O Allah, to You I have submitted, in You I have believed, upon You I have relied, to You I have turned, with You I have contended, and to You I have brought judgment. So forgive me for what I have sent ahead and what I have delayed, what I have concealed and what I have declared. You are my God; there is no god but You.\""],[6023,"When he got up at night, he said the takbir, then said, \"O Allah, to You belongs praise. You are the Sustainer of the heavens and the earth, and to You belongs praise. You are the Lord of the heavens and the earth and whoever is in them. You are the Truth, Your word is true, Your promise is true, meeting You is true, Paradise is true, Hellfire is true, and the Hour is true. O Allah, to You I have submitted, in You I have believed, upon You I have relied, to You I have turned, to You I have brought judgment, and to You is the return. O Allah, forgive me for what I have sent ahead and what I have delayed, what I have concealed and what I have declared. You are my God; there is no god but You.\""],[6024,"I asked ʿĀʾishah, Mother of the Believers: With what did the Messenger of Allah ﷺ open his prayer when he rose at night? She said: When he rose at night, he opened his prayer with: “O Allah, Lord of Gabriel, Michael, and Israfil, Originator of the heavens and the earth, Knower of the unseen and the witnessed, You judge between Your servants concerning that in which they used to differ. Guide me to the truth in what was disputed, for You guide whom You will to a straight path.”"],[6025,"I saw the Messenger of Allah ﷺ when he entered the prayer say: “Allah is most great, greatly; Allah is most great, greatly; Allah is most great, greatly. Praise be to Allah, abundantly; praise be to Allah, abundantly; praise be to Allah, abundantly. Glory be to Allah morning and evening; glory be to Allah morning and evening; glory be to Allah morning and evening. O Allah, I seek refuge in You from Satan—from his pricking, his spitting, and his blowing.”"],[6026,"He asked ʿĀʾishah, the wife of the Prophet ﷺ. He said: I said: With what did the Messenger of Allah ﷺ open when he rose at night? She said: You have asked me about something no one asked me before you. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to open when he rose at night to pray, beginning by saying Allahu akbar ten times, then saying subhan Allah ten times, saying al-hamdu lillah ten times, saying la ilaha illa Allah ten times, and seeking forgiveness ten times. He would say: “O Allah, forgive me, guide me, and provide for me” ten times, and he would seek refuge in Allah from the distress of the Day of Resurrection ten times."],[6027,"I prayed with the Prophet, the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, one night. He did not pass by a verse of mercy but that he paused at it and asked, nor did he pass by a verse of punishment but that he paused at it and sought refuge."],[6028,"I will certainly observe the prayer of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ tonight. He said: So I rested my head on his threshold or his tent. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ stood and prayed two light rakʿahs, then he prayed two long, long, long rakʿahs, then he prayed two rakʿahs shorter than the two before them, then he prayed two rakʿahs shorter than the two before them, then he prayed two rakʿahs shorter than the two before them, then he prayed two rakʿahs shorter than the two before them, then he prayed witr. That was thirteen rakʿahs."],[6029,"I prayed with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ one night. He began Surah al-Baqarah. I said: He will recite a hundred verses and then bow. But he continued. I said: He will finish it in two rakʿahs. But he continued. I said: He will finish it and then bow. But he continued until he recited Surah al-Nisāʾ, then Āl ʿImrān, then he bowed for about as long as his standing, saying: “Glory be to my Lord, the Magnificent.” Then he raised his head and said: “Allah hears the one who praises Him. O Allah, our Lord, to You belongs praise,” and he lengthened the standing. Then he prostrated and lengthened the prostration, saying in his prostration: “Glory be to my Lord, the Most High.” He did not pass by a verse of warning or glorification but that he mentioned it."],[6030,"\"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to remain in his prostration as long as a person recites fifty verses.\" You want to know about the night prayer."],[6031,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to pray thirteen rakʿahs at night."],[6032,"How did the Messenger of Allah ﷺ pray during Ramadhan ? She said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ did not pray more than eleven rak'ahs during Ramadhan and other than Ramadhan. He would pray four rak'ahs. Do not ask about their elegance and length. He then would pray for rak'ahs. Do not ask about their alegance and length. Then he would pray three rak'ahs. 'Aishah said: I asked: Messenger of Allah, do you sleep before observing witr ? He replied: 'Aishah, my eyes sleep, but my heart does not sleep. (Using translation from Abū Dāʾūd 1341)"],[6033,"He used to pray eleven rakʿahs at night. That was his prayer. He would prostrate in it for as long as one of you takes to recite fifty verses before raising his head, and he would pray two rakʿahs before the dawn prayer, then lie on his right side until the muʾadhdhin came to him for the prayer."],[6034,"The Prophet ﷺ used to pray nine rak'ahs at night."],[6035,"The translation of the given text into English is: \"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to pray eight units of voluntary prayers at night, then he would shorten it to odd numbers and perform two units of prayer while sitting.\""],[6036,"We never wished to see the Prophet ﷺ praying at night but we saw him praying, and we never wished to see him sleeping at night but we saw him sleeping."],[6037,"Anas b. Malik was asked about the fasting of the Prophet ﷺ. He said: \"He would fast during a month until we thought that he did not intend to break his fast at all during it, and he would refrain from fasting during a month until we thought that he did not intend to fast at all during it. And you would not wish to see him at night praying but you would see him praying, nor sleeping but you would see him.\""],[6038,"Al-Aswad ibn Yazid said that he entered upon Aisha and asked her about the prayer of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ during the night. She said: He used to pray thirteen rak'ahs during the night. Then he began to pray eleven rak'ahs and left two rak'ahs. When he died, he would pray nine rak'ahs during the night. His last prayer during the night was witr. (Using translation from Abū Dāʾūd 1363)"],[6039,"I spent the night at the house of my maternal aunt Maymunah, and the Messenger of Allah ﷺ was with her that night. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ performed ablution, then stood up to pray, so I stood on his left. He took me and placed me on his right. He prayed thirteen rak'ahs that night, then the Messenger of Allah ﷺ slept until he snored; when he slept, he would snore. Then the caller to prayer came to him, so he went out and prayed without performing ablution."],[6040,"He spent the night at the house of his maternal aunt Maymunah. The Prophet ﷺ got up to pray at night. He said: \"So I got up and performed ablution, then I stood on his left. He pulled me until he stood me on his right. Then he prayed thirteen rak'ahs, with equal standing in them.\""],[6041,"I saw the Messenger of Allah ﷺ make his mount kneel, then dismount, and pray ten rak'ahs, two at a time, then perform witr with one, then pray the two rak'ahs of dawn, then pray the morning prayer."],[6042,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to pray at night for a long time standing, and for a long time sitting. When he prayed standing, he bowed standing, and when he prayed sitting, he bowed sitting."],[6043,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ would not recite anything of the night prayer sitting down, until when he became old, he would recite sitting; and when thirty or forty verses remained, he would stand and recite them, then prostrate."],[6044,"I did not see the Messenger of Allah ﷺ pray any part of the night prayer sitting until he reached old age. Then he would recite while sitting, and when thirty or forty verses of the surah remained, he would stand and recite them, then bow."],[6045,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ would not recite in his prayer while sitting until he reached old age. Then he would recite while sitting, and when thirty or forty verses of the surah remained, he would stand and recite them, then bow."],[6046,"I spent the night with my maternal aunt Maymunah. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ got up at night, relieved himself, then washed his face and hands, then slept. Then he got up, went to the water skin, loosened its tie, and performed a moderate ablution between two ablutions, not excessive but complete. Then he stood and prayed. I got up and stretched, pretending that I had not been watching him. Then I got up and performed ablution. He stood to pray, and I stood on his left, so he took hold of my ear and turned me to his right. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ completed thirteen rak'ahs in his prayer. Then he lay down and slept until he snored, and when he slept he would snore. Then Bilal came and called him to prayer, so he got up and prayed without performing ablution. And in his supplication he said: \"O Allah, place light in my heart, light in my sight, light in my hearing, light on my right, light on my left, light above me, light below me, light in front of me, light behind me, and grant me abundant light.\""],[6047,"The pre-dawn time did not find him with me except sleeping."],[6048,"I asked A'ishah about the Messenger of Allah's ﷺ night prayer. She said: \"He would sleep at the beginning of the night, then get up. When it was the pre-dawn time, he would pray witr, then come to his bed. If he had a man's need for his wife, he would fulfill it. When he heard the call to prayer, he would spring up; if he was in a state of major ritual impurity, he would pour water over himself, otherwise he would perform ablution, then go out to prayer.\""],[6049,"He asked Umm Salamah, the wife of the Prophet ﷺ, about the Prophet's ﷺ night prayer. She said: \"The Prophet ﷺ would pray the later 'Isha', then glorify Allah, then pray after that as much as Allah willed of the night. Then he would leave and sleep for a similar length to what he had prayed. Then he would wake from that sleep and pray a similar length to what he had slept, and that last prayer of his would continue until morning.\""],[6050,"Regarding the night prayer of the Prophet (PBUH), it was reported that \"When the Messenger of Allah (PBUH) prayed Isha (night prayer), he would perform two extra rak'ahs (units of prayer) and then sleep. He would have his ablution and toothbrush next to his head. He would then wake up, use the toothbrush, perform ablution, pray, and perform two additional rak'ahs. Then he would stand and pray eight rak'ahs, reciting the Quran evenly among them. He would then perform the witr prayer with the ninth rak'ah and pray two rak'ahs while sitting. When the Prophet (PBUH) would shorten his recitation, he would decrease the number of rak'ahs in the eight rak'ah prayer to six. He would perform the witr prayer with the seventh rak'ah and pray two rak'ahs while sitting, reciting Surah Al-Kafirun in them and Surah Az-Zalzalah.\""],[6051,"How did the Messenger of Allah ﷺ pray during Ramadhan ? She said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ did not pray more than eleven rak'ahs during Ramadhan and other than Ramadhan. He would pray four rak'ahs. Do not ask about their elegance and length. He then would pray for rak'ahs. Do not ask about their alegance and length. Then he would pray three rak'ahs. 'Aishah said: I asked: Messenger of Allah, do you sleep before observing witr ? He replied: 'Aishah, my eyes sleep, but my heart does not sleep. (Using translation from Abū Dāʾūd 1341)"],[6052,"Between the time when the Messenger of Allah ﷺ finished the night prayer till the dawn broke, he used to pray eleven rak'ahs, uttering the salutation at the end of every two and observing the witr with a single one, and during that he would make a prostration about as long a one of you would take to recite fifty verses before raising his head. When the mu'adhdhin finished making the call for the dawn prayer, he stood up and prayed two short rak'ahs, then he lay down on his right side till the mu'adhdhin came to him (Using translation from Abū Dāʾūd 1336)"],[6053,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to pray thirteen rak'ahs during the night, observing a witr out of that with five, he did not sit during the five except the last and then gave the salutation. Abu Dawud said: Ibn Numair reported it from Hisham recently. (Using translation from Abū Dāʾūd 1338)"],[6054,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ, when he had not prayed during the night because sleep prevented him from that or his eyes overcame him, would pray twelve rak'ahs during the day."],[6055,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ, when he did a deed, he would make it constant. And when he slept during the night or was ill, he would pray twelve rak'ahs during the day. She said: \"I did not see the Messenger of Allah ﷺ stand in prayer a night until morning, nor fast a month consecutively except Ramadan.\""],[6056,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ went out one night in Ramadan and prayed in the mosque, and some men prayed behind him following his prayer. In the morning the people talked about it, and a larger number of them gathered. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ went out the second night and they prayed following his prayer. In the morning the people talked about it, and the people of the mosque gathered on the third night. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ went out and they prayed following his prayer. When it was the fourth night, the mosque could not contain its people, but the Messenger of Allah ﷺ did not come out to them until the dawn prayer. When the dawn prayer was completed, he turned to the people, pronounced the testimony of faith, and said, \"To proceed: your being here was not hidden from me, but I feared that it would be made obligatory upon you and you would fail to do it.\" And the Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to encourage them to stand in prayer during the month of Ramadan without commanding them to perform it as a duty, saying, \"Whoever stands in prayer during Ramadan out of faith and seeking reward, his previous sins will be forgiven.\" The Messenger of Allah ﷺ passed away while the matter was on that basis, then it remained so during the caliphate of Abu Bakr and the early part of the caliphate of Umar, ؓ ."],[6057,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ came out in the middle of the night and prayed in the mosque, and the people prayed. In the morning, the people talked about that, so the people increased. He came out to them the second night and prayed, and they prayed by his prayer. In the morning, they talked about that, so the people increased. He came out on the third night and prayed, and they prayed by his prayer. In the morning, the people talked about that, so the people increased until the mosque could not hold its people. He did not come out to them, and the people began saying, \"The prayer.\" He did not come out to them until he came out for the dawn prayer. When he finished the dawn prayer, he turned to the people, pronounced the testimony of faith, and said: \"To proceed: your affair was not hidden from me last night, but I feared that the night prayer would be made obligatory upon you and you would be unable to do that.\" He encouraged them to stand in Ramadan without commanding them with a firm command, saying, \"Whoever stands on Laylat al-Qadr out of faith and seeking reward, Allah will forgive him his previous sins.\" He said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ passed away while the matter was on that. Then likewise it was during the caliphate of Abu Bakr and the early period of the caliphate of 'Umar, until 'Umar b. al-Khattab gathered them behind Ubayy b. Ka'b, and he led them in Ramadan. That was the first gathering of the people behind one reciter in Ramadan."],[6058,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ came out in the middle of the night and prayed in the mosque, and some men prayed by his prayer. In the morning, the people talked about that, and more gathered than them. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ came out the second night and prayed, and they prayed by his prayer. In the morning, the people reminded one another of that, and the people of the mosque increased on the third night. He came out and prayed with them, and they prayed by his prayer. When it was the fourth night, the mosque could not hold its people, and the Messenger of Allah ﷺ did not come out. Some men began saying, \"The prayer,\" but the Messenger of Allah ﷺ did not come out to them until he came out for the dawn prayer. When he finished the dawn prayer, he turned to the people, then pronounced the testimony of faith and said: \"To proceed: your affair was not hidden from me last night, and I feared that the night prayer would be made obligatory upon you and you would be unable to do it.\""],[6059,"When the Messenger of Allah ﷺ stood for the night prayer, he would rub his mouth with the siwak."],[6060,"I entered upon the Messenger of Allah ﷺ while he was using the siwak, with the tip of the siwak on his tongue, and he was saying, 'A', 'A'."],[6061,"“I saw the Messenger of Allah ﷺ praying at night in a striped Ḥaḍramī cloak, wrapped in it, with nothing else on him.”"],[6062,"I asked Anas b. Malik about the recitation of the Prophet ﷺ, and he said, 'He used to prolong his voice greatly.'"],[6063,"The recitation of the Prophet ﷺ was prolonged: he would prolong 'Bismillah,' prolong 'al-Rahman,' and prolong 'al-Rahim.'"],[6064,"The Prophet ﷺ passed by Abū Bakr while he was praying, lowering his voice, and passed by ʿUmar while he was praying, raising his voice. When they came together at the Prophet ﷺ, he said to Abū Bakr, “O Abū Bakr, I passed by you while you were praying and lowering your voice.” He said, “I made the One with whom I was conversing hear.” He said, “And I passed by you, O ʿUmar, while you were raising your voice.” He said, “O Messenger of Allah, I wake the drowsy and seek reward for it.” He said: So the Prophet ﷺ said to Abū Bakr, “Raise your voice a little,” and said to ʿUmar, “Lower your voice a little.”"],[6065,"\"What prevented you, O so-and-so, from praying with the people?\" He said, \"O Messenger of Allah, I was afflicted by major ritual impurity and there is no water.\" The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, \"Use clean earth, for it suffices you.\" Then the Messenger of Allah ﷺ traveled on, and the people complained to him of thirst. He said: So he dismounted and summoned so-and-so—Abu Raja' used to name him but 'Awf forgot it—and summoned 'Ali, and said, \"Go and search for water for us.\" They met a woman between two water skins, or two flat leather water bags, full of water on a camel of hers. They said to her, \"Where is water?\" She said, \"My last sighting of water was yesterday at this hour, and our men have gone out to seek water.\" He said: So they said to her, \"Come with us, then.\" She said, \"To where?\" They said, \"To the Messenger of Allah ﷺ.\" She said, \"This one who is called the Sabian?\" They said, \"He is the one you mean; so come with us, then.\" They brought her to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and related the story to him. He said: So they made her dismount from her camel, and the Messenger of Allah ﷺ called for a vessel, into which he poured from the mouths of the two water skins, or the two flat leather water bags. He tied their mouths and loosened the spouts, and it was announced among the people: \"Draw water and give water.\" He said: So he gave drink to whom he wished, and drew water for whom he wished. The last of that was that the one who had been afflicted by major ritual impurity was given a vessel of water, and he said, \"Go and pour it over yourself.\" He said: And she was standing watching what was being done with her water. He said: By Allah, when it was lifted from her, it seemed to us that it was more full than when it was first started with. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, \"Gather food for her.\" He said: So they gathered for her from pressed dates, flour, and barley meal until they had gathered much food for her. They placed it in a cloth and mounted her on her camel, and put the cloth before her. He said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to her, \"Do you know that, by Allah, we did not diminish anything from your water? But it was Allah who gave us to drink.\" He said: So she came to her people, having been detained from them. They said, \"What detained you, O so-and-so?\" She said, \"The wonder: two men met me and took me to this one who is called the Sabian, and he did such and such with me. By Allah, he is either the greatest sorcerer between this and this, or he is truly the Messenger of Allah ﷺ.\" He said: After that, the Muslims used to raid the polytheists around her, but they would not strike the small group of tents in which she was. She said to her people, \"By Allah, these people are deliberately leaving you alone. Would you accept Islam?\" They obeyed her and entered Islam."],[6066,"Abu Musa said to 'Abdullah b. Mas'ud, \"If a person who is junub does not find water for a month, should he not pray?\" 'Abdullah said, \"No.\" Abu Musa said, \"Do you not remember when 'Ammar b. Yasir said to 'Umar, 'O Commander of the Believers, will you not fear Allah? Do you not remember when the Messenger of Allah ﷺ sent me and you on the camels, and I became junub, so I rolled in the dust? When I returned to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and told him, the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, 'It would have sufficed you to do like this,' and he struck the ground with his hand, then wiped his face and palms.\" 'Abdullah said, \"No indeed, I did not see 'Umar satisfied with that.\" Abu Musa said, \"Then what about this verse in Surat al-Nisa': {And if you do not find water, then perform tayammum} with clean earth?\" 'Abdullah said, \"Indeed, if we granted them this concession, it would soon happen that when the water is cold on one of their skin, he would perform tayammum.\""],[6067,"\"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ entered the privy, and I brought him water in a small vessel or a leather bucket. He performed istinja' with it, wiped his left hand on the ground, and washed it. Then I brought him a container and he performed wudu'.\""],[6068,"That he saw Uthman call for water for ablution and pour it over his hands from his vessel, washing them three times. Then he inserted his right hand into the water, rinsed his mouth, sniffed water, blew it out, washed his face three times, and his arms up to the elbows three times. Then he wiped his head, then washed each of his feet three times. Then he said: 'I saw the Messenger of Allah ﷺ perform ablution like my ablution here.' Then he said: 'Whoever performs ablution like my ablution here, then stands and prays two rak'ahs without letting his mind wander in them, his previous sins will be forgiven.'\""],[6069,"I witnessed ʿAmr b. Abī Ḥasan ask ʿAbd Allāh b. Zayd about the ablution of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. He called for a vessel of water and poured it over his hand, washing his hand three times. Then he inserted his hand into the vessel, rinsed his mouth and inhaled water into his nose three times from three handfuls. Then he inserted his hand into the vessel and washed his face three times. Then he inserted his hand into the vessel and washed his forearms twice up to the elbows. Then he inserted his hand into the vessel and wiped his head, passing his hands forward and backward. Then he inserted his hand into the vessel and washed his feet up to the ankles."],[6070,"I saw the Prophet ﷺ perform ablution. He scooped a handful of water and washed his right hand. Then he scooped a handful and washed his left hand. Then he scooped a handful and wiped his head and the inner and outer parts of his ears, inserting his two fingers into his ears. Then he scooped a handful and washed his right foot. Then he scooped a handful and washed his left foot."],[6071,"ʿAlī, ؓ , entered the open courtyard after praying the dawn prayer and sat down. Then he said to a servant, 'Bring me water for purification.' The servant brought him a vessel containing water and a basin. ʿAbd Khayr said: We were sitting and watching him. He took the vessel with his right hand and poured water over his left hand. All of that without inserting his hand into the vessel until he had washed both hands three times. Then he inserted his right hand and rinsed his mouth, inhaled water into his nose, and blew his nose with his left hand. He did this three times. Then he washed his face three times. Then he washed his right hand three times up to the elbow. Then he washed his left hand up to the elbow three times. Then he inserted his right hand into the vessel until it was submerged, then raised it with what it carried of water, then wiped it with his left hand. Then he wiped his head with both hands once. Then he poured with his right hand three times over his right foot and washed it with his left hand. Then he poured with his right hand over his left foot three times and washed it with his left hand. Then he inserted his hand into the vessel, scooped with his palm, and drank from it. Then he said, 'This is the purification of the Prophet of Allah ﷺ. Whoever wishes to look at the purification of the Prophet of Allah ﷺ, this is his purification.'"],[6072,"ʿAlī entered my house after he had urinated and called for water for ablution. We brought him a bowl that held a mudd until it was placed before him. He said, 'Shall I not perform for you the ablution of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ?' I said, 'May my father and mother be sacrificed for you.' He washed his hands, then rinsed his mouth, inhaled water into his nose, and blew his nose. Then he took water with his right hand and splashed his face with it until he completed his ablution."],[6073,"I saw ʿUthmān, ؓ , perform ablution and comb his beard with his fingers three times, and he said, 'Thus I saw the Messenger of Allah ﷺ do it.'"],[6074,"I saw the Prophet ﷺ performing ablution, and he began rubbing his forearms."],[6075,"The Prophet ﷺ was brought two-thirds of a mudd of water and performed ablution, rubbing his forearms."],[6076,"Can you show me how the Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to perform ablution? ʿAbd Allāh b. Zayd said, 'Yes.' He called for water for ablution and poured it over his right hand three times. Then he washed his face three times. Then he washed his hands twice up to the elbows. Then he wiped his head with both hands, passing them forward and backward, beginning from the front of his head, then going to the back of his neck, then returning them until he came back to the place where he had started. Then he washed his feet and said, 'Thus I saw the Messenger of Allah ﷺ perform ablution.'"],[6077,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ performed ablution: he rinsed his mouth and blew his nose, then washed his face three times and his right hand three times, and the other likewise, and wiped his head with fresh water, not the leftover water on his hand, and washed his feet until he cleansed them."],[6078,"That the Messenger of Allah ﷺ performed ablution: he took a handful of water and washed his face, then took a handful and washed his right hand, then took a handful and washed his left hand, then took a handful and wiped his head and his ears, their insides with his index fingers, and he crossed his thumbs to the outside of his ears and wiped their outside and inside, then took a handful and washed his right foot, then took a handful and washed his left foot."],[6079,"Ali b. Abi Talib, may Allah's pleasure be upon him, prayed Fajr, then entered the Rahbah, and we entered with him. He called for water for ablution, and the servant brought him a vessel containing water and a basin. He took the vessel with his right hand and poured it over his left hand, washing it three times, washing his palms before putting them into the vessel. Then he inserted his right hand into the vessel, scooped water, filled his mouth, and rinsed his mouth and sniffed water into his nostrils three times. Then he inserted his hand into the vessel and washed his face three times and his forearms three times. Then he wiped his head with both hands, front and back. Then he inserted his right hand, poured water over his right foot and washed it. Then he inserted his hand into the vessel, then took it out and washed the other foot. Then he said: 'Whoever loves to look at the ablution of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, this is his ablution.'"],[6080,"I prayed Zuhr with Ali b. Abi Talib, may Allah's pleasure be upon him; then he went to a gathering of his in the Rahbah and sat down, and we sat around him until Asr approached. A vessel of water was brought to him, and he took a handful from it, rinsed his mouth, sniffed water, wiped his face and forearms, wiped his head, and wiped his feet. Then he stood up and drank the leftover water from his vessel, then said: 'I have been told that some men dislike for one of them to drink while standing, but I saw the Messenger of Allah ﷺ do as I just did. This is the ablution of one who has not broken his wudu.'\""],[6081,"That Uthman b. Affan, may Allah's pleasure be upon him, called for water for ablution and performed ablution: he washed his palms three times, then rinsed his mouth and sniffed water, then washed his face three times, then washed his right arm up to the elbow three times, then washed his left arm likewise, then wiped his head, then washed his right foot up to the ankles three times, then washed his left foot likewise. Then he said: 'I saw the Messenger of Allah ﷺ perform ablution like my ablution here.' Then the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: 'Whoever performs ablution like my ablution here, then stands and prays two rak'ahs without letting his mind wander in them, his previous sins will be forgiven.'\""],[6082,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ was with us in the house, and he called for ablution water. We brought him a copper vessel containing water. He performed ablution, washing his face three times, washing his hands twice, wiping his head, passing his hands forward and backward, and washing his feet."],[6083,"I brought the Messenger of Allah ﷺ water for his ghusl from janābah. She said: He washed his hands twice or three times, then inserted his right hand into the vessel and poured with it over his private part, washing it with his left hand. Then he struck his left hand on the ground and rubbed it vigorously. Then he performed wuḍūʾ as for prayer, then poured over his head three handfuls, filling both hands. Then he moved away from that spot and washed his feet. Then I brought him a cloth, but he returned it."],[6084,"A'ishah described the ghusl of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ from janabah. She said: \"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to wash his hands three times, then pour with his right hand over his left, and wash his private part and what it touched, then rinse his mouth and sniff water three times, and wash his face and hands three times each, then pour over his head three times, then pour water over himself.\""],[6085,"\"I used to bathe, I and the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, from one vessel from janabah, both of us drawing from it together.\""],[6086,"When he bathed from janabah, he would begin by washing his hands, then perform wudu' as he would for prayer, then insert his fingers into the water and comb through the roots of his hair with them, then pour three handfuls of water over his head with his hand, then pour water over the rest of his body."],[6087,"\"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to bathe in a vessel like this\"—and Abu 'Asim gestured with his two hands—\"pouring on the right side, then taking with his two hands and pouring over the rest of his body.\""],[6088,"I am a woman who ties the braids of my hair tightly; should I undo it for the ghusl of janabah? He ﷺ said: \"It is sufficient for you to throw three handfuls of water on your head, then pour water over yourself, and then you will have become pure.\""],[6089,"That ʿUmar b. ʿAbd al-ʿAzīz delayed the prayer one day during his rule, so ʿUrwah b. al-Zubayr entered upon him and informed him that al-Mughīrah b. Shuʿbah delayed the prayer one day while he was in Kūfah, and Abū Masʿūd al-Anṣārī entered upon him and said: “O Mughīrah, what is this? Do you not know that Jibrīl, the blessings of Allah upon him, descended and prayed, and the Messenger of Allah ﷺ prayed, then he prayed and the Messenger of Allah ﷺ prayed, then he prayed and the Messenger of Allah ﷺ prayed, then he prayed and the Messenger of Allah ﷺ prayed, then he prayed and the Messenger of Allah ﷺ prayed,” then he said: “With this I have been commanded.” He said: “Do I not know what you are saying, O ʿUrwah, that Jibrīl established for the Messenger of Allah ﷺ the time of prayer?” He said: “That is how Bashīr b. Abī Masʿūd narrated from his father.”"],[6090,"'Gabriel came to the Prophet ﷺ when the sun declined and said, \"Rise, O Muhammad, and pray Ẓuhr.\" So he rose and prayed Ẓuhr. Then he came to him when the shadow of everything was equal to it and said, \"Rise and pray ʿAṣr.\" So he rose and prayed ʿAṣr. Then he came to him when the sun had set and said, \"Rise and pray Maghrib.\" So he rose and prayed Maghrib. Then he waited until the twilight disappeared and came to him and said, \"Rise and pray ʿIshāʾ.\" So he rose and prayed it. Then he came to him when dawn broke for the morning prayer and said, \"Rise, O Muhammad, and pray.\" So he rose and prayed the morning prayer. The next day he came to him when the shadow of everything was equal to it and said, \"Rise and pray Ẓuhr.\" So he rose and prayed Ẓuhr. Then he came to him when the shadow of everything was twice its length and said, \"Rise and pray ʿAṣr.\" So he rose and prayed ʿAṣr. Then he came to him at the same time as the previous day's sunset, without any change, and said, \"Rise and pray Maghrib.\" So he rose and prayed Maghrib. Then he came to him for ʿIshāʾ when a third of the night had passed and said, \"Rise and pray ʿIshāʾ.\" So he rose and prayed ʿIshāʾ. Then he came to him for the morning prayer when it was very bright and said, \"Rise and pray the morning prayer.\" So he rose and prayed the morning prayer. Then he said, \"All of the time between these two is a prayer time.\"'"],[6091,"Abu Humayd al-Sa'idi, Abu Usayd al-Sa'idi, Sahl ibn Sa'd, and Muhammad ibn Maslamah gathered and mentioned the prayer of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. Abu Humayd said, 'I am the most knowledgeable among you concerning the prayer of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. The Prophet ﷺ stood up and said takbir and raised his hands. Then he raised his hands when he said takbir for bowing. Then he bowed and placed his hands on his knees as if grasping them, and he braced his hands, keeping them away from his sides. He did not lower his head nor draw it in. Then he stood up and raised his hands and stood straight until every limb returned to its position. Then he prostrated, placing his nose and forehead on the ground, and kept his hands away from his sides, and placed his palms level with his shoulders. Then he raised his head until every limb returned to its position, until he finished. Then he sat and spread his left leg and directed the front of his right foot toward the qiblah, and placed his right palm on his right knee and his left palm on his left knee, and pointed with his index finger.'"],[6092,"I heard Abu Humayd al-Sa'idi among ten of the Companions of the Prophet ﷺ, one of them being Abu Qatadah. Abu Humayd said, 'I am the most knowledgeable among you concerning the prayer of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ.' They said to him, 'Why? By Allah, you were not the most frequent of us in following him, nor the earliest of us in his companionship.' He said, 'Yes, I was.' They said, 'Then describe it.' He said, 'When the Messenger of Allah ﷺ stood for prayer, he said takbir and raised his hands until they were level with his shoulders, and every bone settled in its position, straight. Then he recited. Then he said takbir and raised his hands until they were level with his shoulders, and bowed and placed his palms on his knees. Then he stood straight, not lowering his head nor raising it. Then he raised his head and said, \"Allah hears those who praise Him,\" and raised his hands until they were level with his shoulders, straight. Then he said, \"Allahu Akbar,\" then went down to the ground and kept his hands away from his sides. Then he raised his head and folded his left leg and sat on it, and spread the toes of his feet when he prostrated. Then he returned and prostrated, and raised his head and said, \"Allahu Akbar,\" and folded his left leg and sat on it until every bone returned to its position, straight. Then he did in the other rak'ah the same. When he stood up from the two rak'ahs, he said takbir and raised his hands until they were level with his shoulders, just as he did at the beginning of the prayer. Then he did the same in the rest of his prayer, until when it was the sitting of the prostration in which there is the taslim, he moved his left leg back and sat mutawarrikan on his left side.' They all said, 'This is how the Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to pray.'"],[6093,"“Bathe, wrap yourself with a cloth, and enter iḥrām.” The Messenger of Allah ﷺ prayed in the mosque, then mounted al-Qaṣwāʾ. When his she-camel stood him upright on the open desert, I looked as far as my sight could reach: in front of him were riders and walkers, on his right the like, on his left the like, and behind him the like, while the Messenger of Allah ﷺ was among us and the Qurʾān was being sent down upon him, and he knew its interpretation; whatever he did, we did. He assumed iḥrām with tawḥīd: “Labbayka allāhumma labbayka, labbayka lā sharīka laka labbayka, inna al-ḥamda wa al-niʿmata laka wa al-mulka lā sharīka laka.” The people assumed iḥrām with this same talbiyah, and the Messenger of Allah ﷺ did not correct them in any of it, and the Messenger of Allah ﷺ kept to his talbiyah. Jābir said: “We intended nothing but ḥajj; we did not know ʿumrah, until we came to the House with him. He touched the corner, then ramal in three rounds and walked four. Then he went forward to the Station of Ibrāhīm and recited: ‘And take the Station of Ibrāhīm as a place of prayer.’ He placed the Station between himself and the House. My father used to say—and I do not know but that he mentioned it only from the Prophet ﷺ—that he used to recite in the two rakʿahs: ‘Say: He is Allah, the One’ and ‘Say: O disbelievers.’ Then he returned to the corner and touched it, then he went out through the gate to al-Ṣafā. When he drew near al-Ṣafā, he recited: ‘Indeed, al-Ṣafā and al-Marwah are among the symbols of Allah.’ ‘We begin with what Allah began with,’ and he began with al-Ṣafā. He climbed it until he saw the House, then he faced the qiblah, declared Allah’s oneness, magnified Him, and said: ‘There is no god but Allah alone, with no partner; His is the dominion and His is the praise, and He has power over all things. There is no god but Allah alone; He fulfilled His promise, aided His servant, and defeated the confederates alone.’ Then he supplicated between that, saying the like three times. Then he descended to al-Marwah until his feet went down into the bottom of the valley, he hastened; when he climbed out, he walked until he came to al-Marwah, and he did on al-Marwah as he had done on al-Ṣafā. When it was the last circuit on al-Marwah, he said: ‘Had I known beforehand what came later, I would not have brought the sacrificial animal and would have made it an ʿumrah. Whoever of you does not have a sacrificial animal, let him exit iḥrām and make it an ʿumrah.’ Surāqah b. Juʿshum stood up and said: ‘O Messenger of Allah, is this for this year of ours or forever?’ He said—and the Messenger of Allah ﷺ interlaced his fingers one into the other: ‘The ʿumrah has entered into the ḥajj’ twice, ‘no, rather forever and ever; no, rather forever and ever.’ ʿAlī arrived from Yemen with the Prophet’s ﷺ camels, and he found Fāṭimah among those who had exited iḥrām; she had worn dyed clothes and applied kohl, and he disapproved of that. She said: ‘My father ordered me to do this.’ He said: ‘ʿAlī used to say in Iraq: I went to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, angry with Fāṭimah for what she had done, and I told him that I disapproved of it. He ﷺ said: “She has spoken truth. What did you say when you assumed iḥrām for ḥajj?” I said: “I said: O Allah, I assume iḥrām with what Your Messenger has assumed iḥrām.” He said: “I have the sacrificial animal, so do not exit iḥrām.”’” He said: “The total number of sacrificial animals that ʿAlī brought from Yemen and that the Prophet ﷺ brought was one hundred.” He said: “All the people exited iḥrām and shortened their hair, except the Prophet ﷺ and those who had sacrificial animals.”"],[6094,"“If you wish, you may rely on that.” He said, “So I went out until I came to my home, and I placed my sword, my quiver, my shield, and my sandals at my head, and I faced the horizon. Whenever I slept for a while, I woke up; when I saw that night was upon me, I slept until the first light of dawn. I wanted to set out when suddenly a man came running, calling, ‘O Bilāl, answer the Messenger of Allah ﷺ!’ So I went until I came to him, and there were four riding camels, kneeling, with their loads on them. I came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and asked permission. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to me, ‘Rejoice, for Allah has brought the means to pay your debt.’ I praised Allah. He said, ‘Did you not pass by the four kneeling camels?’ I said, ‘Yes.’ He said, ‘You have their necks and what is on them: clothing and food. The ruler of Fadak sent them as a gift to me. Take them and pay your debt.’” He said, “So I did. I unloaded their burdens, hobbled them, then went to give the call for the dawn prayer. When the Messenger of Allah ﷺ had prayed, I went out to al-Baqī‘, put my fingers in my ears, and called out: ‘Whoever is owed a debt by the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, let him come.’ I kept selling and paying, and offering and paying, until there remained in my hand two ūqiyyahs or an ūqiyyah and a half. I went to the mosque, and most of the day had passed. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ was sitting alone in the mosque. I greeted him, and he said, ‘What happened with what you had?’ I said, ‘Allah has paid everything that was owed by the Messenger of Allah ﷺ; nothing remains.’ The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, ‘Is there anything left over?’ I said, ‘Yes.’ He said, ‘See that you relieve me of it.’ When the Messenger of Allah ﷺ prayed the night prayer, he called me and said, ‘What happened with what you had?’ I said, ‘It is with me; no one has come to me.’ He spent the night in the mosque until morning, and remained in the mosque the second day. At the end of the day, two riders came. I went with them, clothed them and fed them. When he prayed the night prayer, he called me and said ﷺ, ‘What happened with what you had?’ I said, ‘Allah has relieved you of it, O Messenger of Allah.’ He said takbīr and praised Allah, fearing that death would overtake him while he still had it. Then I followed him until he came to his wives, greeting each one, until he reached his sleeping place. This is what you asked me about.”"],[6095,"«The Messenger of Allah ﷺ distributed dates among us, and I got five or four dates from it. He said: I saw that the dry, hard date was the harshest on my molar.»"],[6096,"A Bedouin asked the Prophet ﷺ, so he ordered that he be given sheep. Ibn ʿĀʾishah mentioned their abundance. The Bedouin went to his people and said, 'O my people, embrace Islam, for Muḥammad gives the gift of one who does not fear poverty.'"],[6097,"'Write it as al-tabut, for it is the tongue of Quraysh.'"],[6098,"I was in the delegation of Banu al-Muntafiq. While we were sitting with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, the shepherd brought his sheep to the fold, and there was a ewe lamb bleating. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, 'What did it give birth to?' The shepherd said, 'A lamb.' He said, 'Slaughter a sheep in its place.' Then the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, 'Do not think—and he did not say 'do not think' with nasb—that we slaughtered it for your sake. We have a hundred sheep, and when the shepherd has a lamb, we slaughter a sheep in its place.' I said, 'O Messenger of Allah, I have a wife, and there is something in her tongue, meaning obscenity.' He said, 'Divorce her then.' I said, 'She has companionship, and I have a child from her.' He said, 'Command her, admonish her, perhaps she will understand, and do not beat your wife as you beat your camel.' I said, 'O Messenger of Allah...'"],[6099,"“What I fear most for you is what the earth produces or the splendor of the world.” A man said, “O Messenger of Allah, does good come with evil?” He said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ fell silent until we thought that revelation was coming down upon him. He was seized by perspiration or breathlessness, then he recovered and said, “Where is the questioner?” He said, “Here I am, and I intended only good.” He said, “Good does not come except with good. Indeed, everything that spring causes to grow kills by bloating or nearly so, except the eater of green vegetation: it eats until its flanks are full, then it faces the sun and defecates, then urinates, then returns and eats again. Indeed, this wealth is sweet and green. Whoever takes it by its right will be blessed in it, and whoever takes it without its right will not be blessed in it, and he will be like one who eats but never is satisfied. The upper hand is better than the lower hand.”"],[6100,"I never saw the Messenger of Allah ﷺ pray the Maghrib prayer until he broke his fast, even if with a sip of water."],[6101,"Ibn ‘Umar said I have not seen the Apostle of Allaah ﷺ touching anything in the House (the Ka’bah) but the two Yamani corners. (Using translation from Abū Dāʾūd 1874)"],[6102,"“He made an alliance between Quraysh and the Anṣār in their houses in Madinah.”"],[6103,"Whenever it was the Messenger of Allah’s ﷺ night, he would go out at the end of the night to al-Baqīʿ and say, “Peace be upon you, abode of a believing people. What you are promised has come to us and to you, delayed until tomorrow, and we, if Allah wills, will join you. O Allah, forgive the people of Baqīʿ al-Gharqad.”"],[6104,"Rabīʿah b. al-Ḥārith and al-ʿAbbās b. ʿAbd al-Muṭṭalib met and said, “By Allah, if we sent these two boys”—meaning me and al-Faḍl b. al-ʿAbbās—“to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and he appointed them over these alms, they would pay what people pay and receive the benefit that people receive.” While they were discussing that, ʿAlī b. Abī Ṭālib came and said, “What do you two want?” They told him what they intended. He said, “Do not do it, for by Allah he will not do it.” They said, “Why do you say this? This from you is nothing but envy toward us. By Allah, you have accompanied the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and obtained his kinship by marriage, and we did not envy you that.” He said, “I am Abū Ḥasan. Send them.” Then he lay down. When the Messenger of Allah ﷺ had prayed ẓuhr, we preceded him to the room and stood at it until he passed by us ﷺ. He took hold of our ears and said, “Get out what you are hiding,” and entered. We entered with him, and that day he was in the house of Zaynab bt. Jaḥsh. We spoke to him and said, “O Messenger of Allah, we came to you so that you may appoint us over these alms, so that we may receive the benefit that people receive and pay to you what people pay.” He said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ fell silent and raised his head toward the ceiling of the house until we wanted to speak to him. Zaynab gestured to us from behind her screen as if she was telling us not to speak to him. Then he turned and said, “Indeed, alms are not appropriate for Muḥammad or the family of Muḥammad. They are only the impurities of people. Call for me Maḥmiyah b. Juzʾ”—he was in charge of the tithes—“and Abū Sufyān b. al-Ḥārith.” They came, and he said to Maḥmiyah, “Marry this boy to your daughter,” meaning al-Faḍl, and he married him. He said to Abū Sufyān, “Marry this boy to your daughter,” meaning me, and he married me. Then he said to Maḥmiyah, “Pay the dower for them from the fifth.”"],[6105,"A woman who had something wrong with her intellect said, \"O Messenger of Allah, I have a need to ask of you.\" The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, \"O mother of so-and-so, take whichever road you wish and stand there until I come and stand with you.\" So the Messenger of Allah ﷺ went aside with her and spoke privately with her until she had satisfied her need from the Prophet ﷺ."],[6106,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said on the day of Uhud when they pressed upon him while he was with seven of the Ansar and one man from Quraysh: “Who will repel them from us? He will be my companion in Paradise.” A man from the Ansar stood up and fought until he was killed. Then he said the same, and another stood up and fought until he was killed. He kept saying that until the seven were killed. Then the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, “We have not been fair to our companions. O Allah, if You will, You will not be worshipped on earth.”"],[6107,"The Prophet ﷺ went out on the day he marched to Badr and began consulting the people. Abu Bakr ؓ advised him. Then he consulted them and Umar ؓ advised him. He continued consulting ﷺ. The Ansar said, \"By Allah, he wants only us.\" A man from the Ansar said, \"I see that you consult and they advise you, but we will not say as the Children of Israel said: {Go, you and your Lord, and fight.} Rather, by the One who sent you with the truth, if you were to strike its flanks until you reach Birk al-Ghimad, we would be with you.\""],[6108,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ consulted the people during the days of Badr. Abu Bakr spoke and diverted from him. Then Umar spoke and diverted from him. Sa'd b. Ubadah said, \"O Messenger of Allah, do you mean us? If you commanded us to plunge into the sea, we would plunge, or to strike its flanks to Birk al-Ghimad, we would do it.\" The Messenger of Allah ﷺ summoned his companions and set off to Badr. They came upon water skins belonging to Quraysh, among which was a black slave of Banu al-Hajjaj. The companions of the Prophet ﷺ seized him and began asking him, \"Where is Abu Sufyan? Where did you leave him?\" He would say, \"By Allah, I have no knowledge of Abu Sufyan. This is Quraysh: Abu Jahl b. Hisham, Utbah b. Rabi'ah, Shaybah b. Rabi'ah, and Umayyah b. Khalaf.\" When he said that, they beat him. He said, \"Leave me, leave me, I will tell you.\" When they left him, he said, \"By Allah, I have no knowledge of Abu Sufyan, but this is Quraysh approaching. Among them are Abu Jahl, Utbah and Shaybah sons of Rabi'ah, and Umayyah b. Khalaf. They have come.\" The Prophet ﷺ was praying, then finished and said, \"By the One in whose hand is my soul, you strike him when he tells you the truth and leave him when he lies to you. This is Quraysh approaching to protect Abu Sufyan.\" He ﷺ pointed with his hand to the ground and said, \"This is the place where so-and-so will fall tomorrow, and this is the place where so-and-so will fall tomorrow.\" Anas said, \"By the One in whose hand is my soul, not one of them moved from his place of death.\""],[6109,"I was presented to the Prophet ﷺ on the day of Uhud when I was fourteen years old and had not reached puberty, and he did not accept me. Then I was presented to him on the day of the Trench when I was fifteen years old, and he accepted me."],[6110,"I was presented to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ when I was fourteen years old, and he did not permit me and did not consider me to have reached puberty. Then I was presented to him when I was fifteen years old, and he permitted me."],[6111,"On the Day of the Confederates—or the Day of Uhud—when we met the polytheists, the Messenger of Allah ﷺ seated a group of archers and appointed 'Abd Allah b. Jubayr over them, saying, 'Do not leave your place. If you see that we have prevailed over them, or if you see that they have prevailed over us, do not come to our aid.' When we met the enemy and the Muslims routed them, until you could see the women hurrying up the mountain, having lifted their garments so that their anklets showed, they began to turn back, saying, 'The spoils! The spoils!' 'Abd Allah said to them, 'Wait! Do you not know what the Messenger of Allah ﷺ instructed you?' But they went on. When they joined the enemy, Allah turned their faces, and ninety of the Muslims were killed. Then Abu Sufyan looked down upon us from an elevated place and said, 'Is Muhammad among the people?' The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, 'Do not answer him.' Then he said, 'Is Ibn Abi Quhafah among the people?' three times. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, 'Do not answer him.' Then he said, 'Is 'Umar b. al-Khattab among the people?' The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, 'Do not answer him.' Abu Sufyan turned to his companions and said, 'These have been killed; if they were alive, they would answer.' 'Umar could not control himself and said, 'You lie, O enemy of Allah! Allah has kept for you what will disgrace you.' Abu Sufyan said, 'Exalted be Hubal! Exalted be Hubal!' The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, 'Answer him.' They said, 'What should we say?' He said, 'Say: Allah is higher and more exalted.' Abu Sufyan said, 'We have al-'Uzza, and you have no 'Uzza.' The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, 'Answer him.' They said, 'What should we say?' He said, 'Say: Allah is our protector, and you have no protector.' Abu Sufyan said, 'A day for the day of Badr, and war has its ups and downs. You will find mutilation among the people that I did not command nor did it displease me.'"],[6112,"When the Messenger of Allah ﷺ sent an commander over an army or an expedition, he would instruct him personally to fear Allah and to treat the Muslims with him well. Then he would say, 'Raid in the name of Allah, in the cause of Allah. Fight those who disbelieve in Allah. Do not steal from the spoils, do not act treacherously, do not mutilate, and do not kill a child. When you meet your enemy among the polytheists, call them to one of three options. Whichever of them they accept, accept from them and refrain from them. Call them to Islam. If they accept that, accept from them and refrain from them. Then call them to move from their land to the land of the emigrants. If they refuse to move, inform them that if they do so, they will be like the Bedouin emigrants: the ruling of Allah that applies to the emigrants will apply to them. If they accept that, accept from them. If they refuse, seek help from Allah against them and then fight them. When you besiege the people of a fortress and they ask you to grant them the covenant of Allah and the covenant of His Messenger, do not grant them the covenant of Allah or the covenant of His Messenger, but grant them your covenant and the covenant of your fathers and the covenant of your companions. For you breaking your covenants and the covenants of your fathers is lighter for you than breaking the covenant of Allah and the covenant of His Messenger ﷺ. When you besiege the people of a fortress and they ask you to bring them down according to the judgment of Allah, do not bring them down according to the judgment of Allah, for you do not know whether you will attain the judgment of Allah regarding them or not.'"],[6113,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ sent an expedition and armed a man with a sword. When we returned, I never saw the Messenger of Allah ﷺ blame us as he did. He said, 'Were you unable, when I appointed a man over you and he did not carry out my command, whether I commanded or forbade, to put another in his place who would carry out my command?'"],[6114,"In the expedition of Mu'tah, the Messenger of Allah ﷺ appointed Zayd b. Harithah as commander and said, 'If Zayd is killed, then Ja'far; if Ja'far is killed, then 'Abd Allah b. Rawahah.' 'Abd Allah said: I was with them in that expedition. We looked for Ja'far b. Abi Talib and found him among the slain. We found on his body more than seventy wounds from strikes and thrusts."],[6115,"“Indeed, the one who drags his garment out of pride, Allah will not look at him on the Day of Resurrection.”"],[6116,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ went out to Khaybar at night. When he came upon a people at night, he would not attack until morning. He said: When morning came, the Jews came out with their shovels and baskets. When they saw him, they said, \"Muhammad and the army!\" The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, \"Allah is greatest! Khaybar is ruined. When we descend upon the courtyard of a people, evil is the morning of those warned.\""],[6117,"\"O Allah, bless my community in its early mornings.\" He said: When he dispatched a raiding party or an army, he would send them at the beginning of the day."],[6119,"\"I witnessed the Messenger of Allah ﷺ: when it was time for fighting, if he did not fight at the beginning of the day, he would delay it until the sun declined, the winds blew, and victory descended.\""],[6120,"I witnessed al-Yarmuk, and over it were five commanders: Abu Ubayda b. al-Jarrah, Yazid b. Abi Sufyan, Shurahbil b. Hasana, Khalid b. al-Walid, and Iyad—not the Iyad who is the companion of the hadith that Simak narrates from. Umar, ؓ , said: When there is fighting, Abu Ubayda is in charge of you. He (the narrator) said: So we wrote to him that death has surged upon us and we requested reinforcements. He wrote back: Your letter requesting reinforcements has come to me, and I direct you to what is greater in victory and more fortified in soldiers: Allah. So seek His help, for Muhammad ﷺ was granted victory with fewer than your number. When my letter reaches you, fight them and do not refer back to me. He (the narrator) said: So we fought them, routed them, and killed them for four farsakhs, and we seized wealth. They consulted, and Iyad suggested ten dirhams per head. Abu Ubayda said: Who will race me? A young man said: I will, if you do not get angry. He said: So he beat him, and I saw the two braids of Abu Ubayda bouncing while he was behind him on an Arab horse."],[6121,"On the day of Hunayn, Hawazin and Ghatafan came with their children and cattle, and with the Prophet ﷺ were ten thousand, and with him were the freed ones. They turned away from him until he remained alone. He said: That day he called out twice without mixing anything between them. He turned to his right and said: 'O assembly of the Ansar.' They said: At your service, O Messenger of Allah, rejoice, we are with you. Then he turned to his left and said: 'O assembly of the Ansar.' They said: At your service, O Messenger of Allah, rejoice, we are with you. He said: And he was on a white mule. He dismounted and said: I am the servant of Allah and His Messenger. Then the polytheists were defeated, and the Messenger of Allah ﷺ obtained much booty. He distributed it among the Muhajirun and the freed ones, and did not give the Ansar anything. The Ansar said: When there is hardship, we are there, but he gives the booty to others. That reached him, so he gathered them in a tent and said: 'O assembly of the Ansar, what is this talk that has reached me?' They remained silent. He said: 'O assembly of the Ansar, are you not pleased that the people go with sheep and you go with Muhammad ﷺ to your houses?' They said: We are pleased, O Messenger of Allah. He said: 'If the people were to go through a valley and the Ansar through a mountain pass, I would take the mountain pass of the Ansar.'"],[6122,"We set out with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, unaware of the people who had gathered an army against us. We faced the valley of Ḥunayn in the darkness of dawn—it is a hollow valley among the valleys of Tihāmah; they descend into it steeply. By Allah, the people were moving along, knowing nothing, when suddenly battalions came at them from every side. The people did not wait but fled, turning back. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ moved to the right and said, “Where are you, people? I am the Messenger of Allah, I am Muḥammad b. ʿAbd Allāh.” Before Hawāzin was a huge man on a red camel, holding a black banner: when he caught up with someone, he thrust it; when something escaped before him, he pushed it from behind. ʿAlī b. Abī Ṭālib, ؓ , and a man from the Anṣār lay in wait for him, both seeking him. ʿAlī struck the camel’s hamstrings, so it fell on its hindquarters, and the Anṣārī struck his shin, cutting off his foot with half his shin. He fell, and the people fought until the rout came. The maternal brother of Ṣafwān b. Umayyah said, “Indeed, magic is void today.” Ṣafwān b. Umayyah was then a polytheist, during the period the Messenger of Allah ﷺ had set for him. Ṣafwān said to him, “Be quiet, may Allah break your mouth! By Allah, a man of Quraysh ruling over me is dearer to me than a man of Hawāzin ruling over me.”"],[6123,"“When the Prophet ﷺ met the polytheists on the day of Ḥunayn, he dismounted from his mule and went on foot.”"],[6124,"A man had a wound, so he went to his quiver and took an arrowhead and slaughtered himself with it, and the Prophet ﷺ did not pray over him."],[6125,"“I was presented to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ on the day of Qurayẓah, and they doubted me. It was said to me, ‘Have you grown pubic hair?’ They examined me and found I had not, so I was set free.”"],[6126,"When the Messenger of Allah ﷺ acquired spoils, he would order Bilal to call out among the people, and the people would bring their spoils; he would take a fifth and divide it. Then a man came to him after that with a rope of hair and said: 'Did you not hear Bilal calling three times?' He said: 'Yes.' He said: 'What prevented you from bringing it?' He made an excuse to him. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: 'You yourself will bring it on the Day of Resurrection, and I will never accept it from you.'"],[6127,"For the horse are two shares, and for the man is one share."],[6128,"He allotted to the horseman three shares: two shares for his horse and one share for the man."],[6129,"When the Prophet ﷺ received the fay', he would divide it on the same day, giving the married man two portions and the unmarried man one portion."],[6130,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ divided some cloaks and did not give Makhramah anything. Makhramah said: 'O my son, take me to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ.' So I went with him. He said: 'Enter and call him for me.' He said: 'So I called him for him, and he came out to him wearing one of those cloaks as an outer garment, and said: \"I have kept this for you.\"' He said: 'He looked at it, and the Prophet ﷺ said: \"Makhramah is pleased.\"'"],[6131,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ divided some cloaks and did not give Makhramah anything. Makhramah said: 'O my son, take me to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ.' So I went with him. He said: 'Enter and call him for me.' He said: 'So I called him for him, and he came out to him wearing one of those cloaks as an outer garment, and said: \"I have kept this for you.\"' He said: 'He looked at it, and the Prophet ﷺ said: \"Makhramah is pleased.\"'"],[6132,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ was taking for the people in Bilal's garment on the day of Hunayn, giving them. A man among the people said, 'Be just, O Muhammad.' He ﷺ said, 'Woe to you! If I am not just, then who will be just? I would have failed and lost if I were not just.' He said: Umar, ؓ , said, 'Let me strike his neck, O Messenger of Allah.' He ﷺ said, 'I seek refuge with Allah that people should say that I kill my companions. This man and his companions recite the Qur'an, but it does not go beyond their throats.'"],[6133,"While he was traveling with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, with the people with him, on his return from Hunayn, the Bedouins clung to him asking him, and they forced him to a samura tree until his cloak was snatched away while he was on his mount. He stopped and said, 'Give me back my cloak. Do you fear stinginess from me? If these thorn trees were as numerous as livestock, I would distribute them among you, and then you would not find me stingy, cowardly, or a liar.'"],[6134,"\"When distributing the spoils of war, the Messenger of Allah used to make ten sheep equivalent to one camel.\" Shu'bah said: \"I know most if it from what I heard form Sa'eed bin Masruq, and Sufyan narrated it to me.\" (Sahih ) (Using translation from Nasāʾī 4391)"],[6135,"Safiyya was from the safi (selected share)."],[6136,"I was riding behind Abu Talha on the day of Khaybar, and my foot was touching the foot of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. We came to Khaybar when they had come out with their spades, axes, and baskets, and they said, 'Muhammad and the army!' The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, 'Allah is greater! Khaybar is ruined! When we descend upon the courtyard of a people, evil is the morning of those who were warned.' The Messenger of Allah ﷺ fought them and defeated them. When the spoils were divided, it was said to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ that a beautiful slave girl had fallen to the share of Dihya al-Kalbi. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ bought her for seven heads of cattle, then gave her to Umm Sulaym to prepare her. Umm Sulaym used to go on expeditions with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. He called for leather mats, and they were brought, and he spread the mats, and dates and ghee were brought, and he made them a generous portion of hais. The people ate until they were full. The people said, 'Did he marry her or take her as a mother of his child?' They said, 'If he veils her, she is his wife, and if he does not veil her, she is a mother of his child.' When she wanted to ride, he veiled her until she sat on the rear of the camel behind him, then she rode. When they approached Madinah, he hastened, and the people hastened, and the women looked out. His riding camel stumbled with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and he fell, and Safiyya fell. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ stood up and veiled her. The women said, 'May Allah distance the Jewess!' and they gloated over her. Thabit said, 'I said to Anas, \"O Abu Hamza, did the Messenger of Allah ﷺ fall from his riding camel?\" He said, \"Yes, by Allah, he fell from his riding camel, O Abu Muhammad.\"'"],[6137,"Fatima, daughter of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, sent to Abu Bakr asking for her inheritance from the Messenger of Allah ﷺ from what Allah bestowed upon His Messenger. At that time, Fatima, ؓ , was seeking the charity of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ that was in Madinah, Fadak, and what remained of the khums of Khaybar. A'isha said: Abu Bakr said, 'The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"We are not inherited; what we leave is charity. The family of Muhammad only eats from this wealth; it is not for them to increase beyond the food.\" And by Allah, I will not change anything of the charities of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ from the condition it was in during the time of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and I will act in it as the Messenger of Allah ﷺ acted in it.' Abu Bakr refused to give Fatima anything from it. Fatima became angry with Abu Bakr over that and shunned him, and did not speak to him until she died. She lived six months after the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. When she died, Ali b. Abi Talib, ؓ , buried her at night and did not inform Abu Bakr. Ali prayed over her. Ali had a standing among the people during Fatima's life, but when Fatima, ؓ , died, the people's faces turned away from Ali until he noticed their change. Then Ali inclined toward reconciliation with Abu Bakr and pledging allegiance to him, although he had not pledged allegiance during those months. He sent to Abu Bakr, 'Come to us, and let no one come with you,' for Ali disliked that Umar should attend, knowing Umar's harshness toward them. Umar said to Abu Bakr, 'By Allah, you will not enter upon them alone.' Abu Bakr said, 'What could they do to me? By Allah, I will go to them.' Abu Bakr entered. Ali recited the shahada, then said, 'We have recognized, O Abu Bakr, your virtue and what Allah has given you. We do not begrudge you any good that Allah has brought to you. But you have taken sole control of the affair, and we considered that we had a right, and he mentioned their kinship to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and their right.' He continued speaking until Abu Bakr's eyes overflowed. When Abu Bakr spoke, he said, 'By the One in whose hand is my soul, the kinship of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ is dearer to me to maintain than my own kinship. As for what arose between me and you regarding these charities, I have not failed to do good in them, and I would not leave any matter in them that I saw the Messenger of Allah ﷺ do except that I would do it.' Ali said, 'Your appointment is this evening for the pledge of allegiance.' When Abu Bakr prayed the noon prayer, he ascended the pulpit, recited the shahada, mentioned Ali's situation and his delay in pledging, and his excuse for what he had excused himself. Then he sought forgiveness. Ali recited the shahada, magnified Abu Bakr's right, and stated that what he had done was not out of envy toward Abu Bakr or denial of the virtue with which Allah had favored him, but we considered that we had a share in the affair, and he had taken sole control over us, so we found that within ourselves. The Muslims were pleased with that and said to Ali, 'You have done right.' The Muslims were close to Ali when he returned to the matter with good conduct."],[6138,"Najda al-Haruri went out during the fitna of Ibn al-Zubayr. He sent to Ibn Abbas asking about the share of the near of kin: for whom is it? He said, 'It is for the relatives of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ divided it for them. Umar had offered us something from it that we considered less than our right, so we rejected it and refused to accept it. He had offered to help their married ones, pay the debts of their indebted, and give to their poor, and he refused to give them more than that.'"],[6139,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ dispatched an army, and they took as spoils food and honey, and the Prophet ﷺ did not take the khums from it."],[6140,"On the day of Hunayn, the Prophet ﷺ gave Abu Sufyan b. al-Harith one hundred camels, gave Abu Sufyan b. Harb one hundred camels, gave al-Aqra' b. Habis al-Tamimi one hundred camels, gave Uyayna b. Hisn al-Fazari one hundred camels, and gave al-Abbas b. Mirdas less than that. He began reciting: 'You made my spoils and the spoils of the slaves between Uyayna and al-Aqra'.'"],[6141,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ gave me on the day of Hunayn, and he was among the most hateful of people to me. He kept giving me until he became the most beloved of creation to me."],[6142,"On the day of Hunayn, the Messenger of Allah ﷺ gave preference to some people in the division. He gave al-Aqra' b. Habis one hundred camels, gave Uyayna b. Hisn the like of that, and gave preference to some of the nobles of the Arabs. A man said, 'By Allah, this is a division in which justice was not observed, and the face of Allah was not intended by it.' I said, 'I will inform the Messenger of Allah ﷺ.' I came to him and informed him. The face of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ changed, then he said, 'Who will be just if Allah and His Messenger are not just?' Then he said, 'May Allah have mercy on Musa. He was harmed with more than this, and he was patient.' I said, 'No doubt, I will never raise a report to him after this.'"],[6143,"I undertook a blood-money responsibility for my people. I said, 'O Messenger of Allah, I have undertaken a blood-money responsibility for my people, so help me with it.' The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, 'Rather, we will bear it for you.' He said, 'It is yours among the charity camels when they come.' Then he said, 'O Qabisa b. Mukhariq, begging is not lawful except for one of three: a man who undertakes a blood-money responsibility for his people seeking reconciliation, and he begs until he reaches his aim, then he stops; a man who is stricken by poverty and three men of sound judgment from his people testify for him, and when he obtains what suffices or a covering, he stops; and a man who is stricken by a calamity and begs until he obtains what suffices or a covering, then he stops. Anything else, O Qabisa, of begging is unlawful earnings.' He said it three times."],[6144,"«The Messenger of Allah ﷺ sent a raiding party toward Najd, and ‘Abd Allah b. ‘Umar was in it. They captured many camels, and their shares were twelve camels each, and they were given as extra one camel each.»"],[6145,"«The Messenger of Allah ﷺ sent a raiding party toward Najd, and Ibn ‘Umar was among them. Their shares reached twelve camels each, and then they were given extra, in addition to that, one camel each. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ did not change it.»"],[6146,"I heard ‘Amr b. Shu‘ayb and Sulayman b. Musa mentioning the extra grant. ‘Amr said: «There is no extra grant after the Prophet ﷺ.» Sulayman b. Musa said to him: «You have been occupied with eating raisins in al-Ta’if.»"],[6147,"The Prophet ﷺ said on the day of Hunayn: «Whoever kills a disbeliever, his spoils belong to him.» Abu Talhah killed twenty men that day and took their spoils. Abu Qatadah said: “O Messenger of Allah, I struck a man on the shoulder strap, and he had a coat of mail. I was made to leave him, and a man said: ‘I took it, so satisfy him from it and give it to me.’” The Prophet ﷺ was not asked for anything except that he gave it or remained silent, so he remained silent ﷺ. ‘Umar b. al-Khattab, ؓ , said: “By Allah, Allah will not give it back to a lion of His lions and give it to you.” The Prophet ﷺ laughed and said: «‘Umar spoke the truth.»"],[6148,"We went out with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ in the year of Hunayn. When we met, the Muslims had a retreat. I saw a man from the polytheists over a man from the Muslims. I came behind him and struck him on the shoulder strap, cutting the coat of mail. He turned to me and squeezed me in an embrace in which I found the smell of death. Then death overtook him, and he released me. I caught up with ‘Umar b. al-Khattab and said: “What is the matter with the people?” He said: “The command of Allah.” Then the people returned, and the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: «Whoever kills a slain man, and he has evidence for it, his spoils belong to him.» Abu Qatadah said: I stood up and said: “Who will testify for me?” Then I sat down. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: «Whoever kills a slain man, and he has evidence for it, his spoils belong to him.» I stood up and said: “Who will testify for me?” Then I sat down. He said that the third time, and I stood up. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: «What is the matter with you, O Abu Qatadah?» I told him the story. A man from the people said: “He spoke the truth, O Messenger of Allah, and the spoils of that slain man are with me, so satisfy him from me.” Abu Bakr al-Siddiq, ؓ , said: “By Allah, no! He would intend a lion of Allah’s lions fighting for Allah and His Messenger, and you give you his spoils.” The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: «He spoke the truth, so give it to him.» Abu Qatadah said: He gave it to me. I sold the coat of mail and bought with it a garden among the Banu Salamah. It was the first property I acquired in Islam."],[6149,"The Hawazin came on the day of Hunayn with sheep, camels, and goats, and they arranged them in two rows to outnumber the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. The Muslims and the polytheists met, and the Muslims turned back in retreat, as Allah said. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: «I am the servant of Allah and His Messenger.» Then Allah defeated the polytheists, and we did not strike with a sword or thrust with a spear. The Prophet ﷺ said that day: «Whoever kills a disbeliever, his spoils belong to him.» Abu Talhah killed twenty men that day and took their spoils. Abu Qatadah said: “O Messenger of Allah, I struck a man on the shoulder strap, and he had a coat of mail. I was hurried away from him before taking it. Look with whom it is.” A man stood up and said: “O Messenger of Allah, I took it. Satisfy him from me and give it to me.” The Messenger of Allah ﷺ remained silent, and the Messenger of Allah ﷺ was not asked for anything except that he gave it or remained silent. ‘Umar said: “Allah will not give it back to a lion of His lions and give it to you.” The Messenger of Allah ﷺ laughed and said: «‘Umar spoke the truth.» Abu Talhah met Umm Sulaym, and she had a dagger. He said: “O Umm Sulaym, what is this with you?” She said: “I intended, if any of the polytheists came near me, to rip open his belly with it.” Abu Talhah said: “O Messenger of Allah, do you not hear what Umm Sulaym says?” She said: “O Messenger of Allah, I would kill with it the freed ones who fled from you.” He ﷺ said: «O Umm Sulaym, Allah has sufficed and done well.»"],[6150,"A man stood up near the Prophet ﷺ and was reported to be a spy for the polytheists. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: «Whoever kills him, his spoils belong to him.» I caught up with him and killed him, and the Messenger of Allah ﷺ gave me his spoils as extra."],[6151,"While I was standing between the ranks on the day of Badr, I looked to my right and left, and I was between two youths of the Ansar. While I was so, one of them nudged me and said: “O uncle, do you know Abu Jahl b. Hisham?” I said: “Yes, and what is your need with him, O son of my brother?” He said: “I was told that he reviles the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. By the One in whose hand is my soul, if I see him, my body will not leave his until the quicker of us dies.” I was pleased with his words. Then the other nudged me and said the like. It was not long before I saw Abu Jahl moving among the people. I said to them: “This is your companion whom you asked me about.” They rushed at him and struck him with their swords and killed him. Then they came to the Prophet ﷺ and told him what they had done. He said: «Which of you killed him?» Each of them said: “I killed him.” He said: «Did you wipe your swords?» We said: “No.” He looked at the two swords and the Prophet ﷺ said: «Both of you killed him.» Then he decreed his spoils to Mu‘adh b. ‘Amr b. al-Jamuh. The two men were Mu‘adh b. ‘Amr b. al-Jamuh and Mu‘adh b. ‘Afra’."],[6152,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said on the day of Hunayn: «Whoever is alone in shedding blood, his spoils belong to him.» Abu Talhah came with the spoils of twenty-one persons."],[6153,"A reinforcement fighter in the expedition of Tabuk accompanied them. A Roman was towering over the Muslims and inciting against them. The reinforcement fighter took a subtle position and sat under a rock. When the Roman passed by, he hamstrung his horse, and the Roman fell on the back of his neck. The reinforcement fighter attacked him with the sword and killed him, and came with his saddle, bridle, sword, belt, and weapons. They took the gold and jewels to Khalid b. al-Walid. Khalid took a portion from him and gave him the rest as extra. I said to him: “O Khalid, what is this? Do you not know that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ gave the entire spoils to the killer?” He said: “Yes, but I considered it too much.” I said: “By the life of Allah, I will make it known to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ.” When we came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, I told him his story. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ called him and ordered him to give the reinforcement fighter the rest of his spoils. Khalid turned to do it. I said to him: “How do you see, O Khalid, did I not fulfill for you what I promised you?” The Messenger of Allah became angry and said: «O Khalid, do not give it to him, and turn to me.» He said: «Will you leave my commanders alone? You have the best of their affairs, and upon them is its trouble.»"],[6154,"The Prophet ﷺ did not take the khums from the salb (spoils taken by a killer from the enemy he killed)."],[6155,"When the Messenger of Allah ﷺ acquired spoils, he would command Bilāl, who would call out among the people three times. Then the people would come with their spoils, and he would take a fifth and divide them. Later, a man came to him with a rein made of hair and said, “O Messenger of Allah, this was among what we seized as spoils.” He said, “Did you not hear Bilāl call out three times?” He said, “Yes.” He said, “Then what prevented you from bringing it?” He offered an excuse, so he said ﷺ, “You will be the one to bring it on the Day of Resurrection, and I will not accept it from you.”"],[6156,"When it was the day of Khaybar, a group of the Prophet’s ﷺ companions came and said, “So-and-so is a martyr, so-and-so is a martyr,” until they passed by a man and said, “So-and-so is a martyr.” The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, “No indeed, I saw him in the Fire in a cloak he embezzled or an abā’ah.” Then the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, “O b. al-Khaṭṭāb, go and call out among the people that only the believers will enter Paradise.” He said, “So I went out and called, ‘Indeed, only the believers will enter Paradise.’”"],[6158,"We were sitting with Abdullah while he was reclining among us. A man came to him and said: There is a storyteller telling stories at the gates of Kinda, claiming that the verse of the Smoke will come and seize the breaths of the disbelievers, and the believers will get from it something like a cold. Abdullah sat up, angry, and said: O people, fear Allah. Whoever among you knows something, let him say it; and whoever does not know, let him say: Allah knows best. For it is better for one of you to say about what he does not know: Allah knows best. Allah, Mighty and Exalted, said to His Prophet ﷺ: {Say: I do not ask you for any reward for it, and I am not of the pretentious} (Surah Sad 38:86). When the Messenger of Allah ﷺ saw people turning away, he said: 'O Allah, seven years like the seven of Joseph.' Then a year (of famine) seized them until they ate carrion and hides, and one of them would look at the sky and see something like smoke. Abu Sufyan came to him and said: O Muhammad, you have come commanding obedience to Allah and maintaining kinship, and your people have perished from hunger, so supplicate to Allah for them. Allah, Mighty and Exalted, said: {So watch for the day when the sky will bring a visible smoke} (Surah al-Dukhan 44:10), {The day We seize with the greatest seizure; indeed, We will take retribution} (Surah al-Dukhan 44:16). The seizure is the day of Badr, and the verse of the smoke, the seizure, the punishment, and the Romans have passed."],[6159,"I have not seen anyone more consultative with his companions than the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. Al-Zuhri said in his hadith from 'Urwah from al-Miswar and Marwan in their hadith: They departed until when they were on part of the road, the Prophet ﷺ said, 'Khalid b. al-Walid is at al-Ghamim with cavalry of Quraysh as a vanguard, so take the right path.' By Allah, Khalid b. al-Walid did not notice them until he saw the dust of the army, so he rushed back as a warner to Quraysh. The Prophet ﷺ proceeded until he was at the mountain pass from which he would descend upon them. When he reached it, his she-camel knelt down. The people said, 'Hal, hal!' She kept kneeling. They said, 'Al-Qaswa' has become stubborn.' The Prophet ﷺ said, 'Al-Qaswa' has not become stubborn, and that is not her nature, but she has been held back by the One who held back the elephant.' Then he said, 'By Him in whose hand is my soul, they will not ask me for any plan by which they honor the sanctities of Allah except that I grant it to them.' Then he urged her, and she leapt up with him. He turned away from them until he camped at the far side of al-Hudaybiyyah on a small water source that people were sipping from sparingly. The people did not linger before they exhausted it. Thirst was complained of to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, so he took out an arrow from his quiver and ordered them to put it in the water. It kept gushing for them with water until they all drank their fill. While they were thus, Budayl b. Warqa' al-Khuza'i came to him with a group of his people from Khuza'ah, who were the confidants of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ among the people of Tihamah. He said, 'I left Ka'b b. Lu'ayy and 'Amir b. Lu'ayy encamped at the water sources of al-Hudaybiyyah, with them were nursing camels and their young. They are fighting you and preventing you from the Sacred House.' The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, 'We have not come to fight anyone, but we have come to perform 'Umrah. Quraysh have been exhausted by war and harmed by it. If they wish, I will grant them a truce for a period, and they will leave me alone with the people. If we prevail and they wish to enter into what the people have entered, they may do so, and they have rested. But if they refuse, by Him in whose hand is my soul, I will fight them for this matter of mine until my neck is severed, or Allah will make His command prevail.' Budayl b. Warqa' said, 'I will convey to them what you say.' He went until he came to Quraysh and said, 'We have come to you from this man, and we heard him say something. If you wish, we will present it to you.' Their fools said, 'We have no need for you to tell us anything about him.' Those of sound judgment said, 'Give us what you heard him say.' He said, 'I heard him say such and such,' and he informed them of what the Prophet ﷺ said. At that, Abu Mas'ud 'Urwah b. Mas'ud al-Thaqafi stood up and said, 'O people, am I not the father?' They said, 'Yes.' He said, 'Am I not the son?' They said, 'Yes.' He said, 'Do you accuse me?' They said, 'No.' He said, 'Do you not know that I called upon the people of 'Ukaz, and when they refused me, I came to you with my family, children, and those who obeyed me?' They said, 'Yes.' He said, 'This man has offered you a plan of guidance, so accept it and let me go to him.' They said, 'Go to him.' He went and began to speak with the Prophet ﷺ, and the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said something similar to what he had said to Budayl b. Warqa'. 'Urwah b. Mas'ud said, 'O Muhammad, do you think that if you exterminate your people, have you heard of any Arab who destroyed his own root before you? And if it is the other way, by Allah, I see faces and a mixture of people who are likely to flee and abandon you.' Abu Bakr al-Siddiq, ؓ , said, 'Suck the clitoris of al-Lat! Would we flee and abandon him?' Abu Mas'ud said, 'Who is this?' They said, 'Abu Bakr b. Abi Quhafah.' He said, 'By Him in whose hand is my soul, were it not for a favor you did for me that I have not repaid, I would have answered you.' He continued speaking with the Prophet ﷺ, and whenever he spoke to him, he grabbed his beard. Al-Mughirah b. Shu'bah al-Thaqafi was standing at the head of the Prophet ﷺ, wearing a sword and helmet. Whenever 'Urwah reached his hand to the beard of the Prophet ﷺ, he struck his hand with the scabbard of the sword and said, 'Keep your hand away from the beard of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ.' 'Urwah raised his head and said, 'Who is this?' They said, 'Al-Mughirah b. Shu'bah al-Thaqafi.' He said, 'O treacherous one, am I not striving to rectify your treachery?' Al-Mughirah b. Shu'bah had accompanied a people in the Jahiliyyah, killed them, and taken their wealth, then he came and embraced Islam. The Prophet ﷺ said to him, 'As for Islam, I accept it, but as for the wealth, I have nothing to do with it.' Then 'Urwah began to observe the companions of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ with his eyes. By Allah, the Messenger of Allah ﷺ did not spit except that his spittle fell into the hand of one of them, and he would rub it on his face and skin. If he commanded them, they hastened to obey his command. If he performed ablution, they almost fought over his ablution water. If he spoke, they lowered their voices in his presence and did not stare at him out of reverence for him. 'Urwah b. Mas'ud returned to his companions and said, 'O people, by Allah, I have visited kings, I have visited Khosrau, Caesar, and the Negus, and by Allah, I have never seen a king whose companions honor him as the companions of Muhammad honor Muhammad. By Allah, he does not spit except that his spittle falls into the hand of one of them, and he rubs it on his face and skin. If he commands them, they rush to obey his command. If he performs ablution, they fight over his ablution water. When he speaks, they lower their voices in his presence and do not stare at him out of reverence for him. He has offered you a plan of guidance, so accept it.' A man from Banu Kinanah said, 'Let me go to him.' When he came in sight of the Prophet ﷺ, the Prophet ﷺ said, 'This is so-and-so from a people who venerate sacrificial camels, so send them to him.' So they were sent, and the people met him while reciting the talbiyah. When he saw that, he said, 'Glory be to Allah! It is not right for these people to be prevented from the House.' When he returned to his companions, he said, 'I saw the sacrificial camels garlanded and marked, so I do not think they should be prevented from the House.' A man from among them called Mikraz stood up and said, 'Let me go to him.' They said, 'Go to him.' When he came in sight of them, the Prophet ﷺ said, 'This is Mikraz, and he is a wicked man.' He began to speak with the Prophet ﷺ. While he was speaking with him, Suhayl b. 'Amr came. Ma'mar said: Ayyub al-Sakhtiyani informed me from 'Ikrimah: When Suhayl came, the Prophet ﷺ said, 'This is Suhayl; Allah has made your affair easy for you.' Ma'mar said in his hadith from al-Zuhri from 'Urwah from al-Miswar and Marwan: When Suhayl came, he said, 'Come, write a treaty between us and you.' The scribe was called, and he said, 'Write: In the name of Allah, the Most Gracious, the Most Merciful.' Suhayl said, 'As for the Most Gracious, I do not know, by Allah, what it is, but write: In Your name, O Allah.' Then the Prophet ﷺ said, 'Write: This is what Muhammad, the Messenger of Allah, has agreed upon.' Suhayl b. 'Amr said, 'If we knew that you were the Messenger of Allah, we would not have prevented you from the House nor fought you, but write Muhammad b. 'Abdullah.' The Prophet ﷺ said, 'By Allah, I am indeed the Messenger of Allah, even if you disbelieve me. Write Muhammad b. 'Abdullah.' Al-Zuhri said: That was because of his saying, 'They will not ask me for any plan by which they honor the sanctities of Allah except that I grant it to them.' He said in his hadith from 'Urwah from al-Miswar and Marwan: The Prophet ﷺ said, 'On condition that you leave us alone with the House so that we may circumambulate it.' Suhayl b. 'Amr said, 'The Arabs must not say that we were forced, but you will have it next year.' He wrote that. Suhayl b. 'Amr said, 'On condition that no man from us comes to you, even if he is on your religion or wants your religion, except that you return him to us.' The Muslims said, 'Glory be to Allah! How can a man be returned to the polytheists when he has come as a Muslim?' While they were thus, Abu Jandal b. Suhayl b. 'Amr came dragging his chains, having escaped from the lower part of Makkah until he threw himself among the Muslims. Suhayl b. 'Amr said, 'O Muhammad, this is the first one with whom I will settle the treaty: you must return him to me.' The Prophet ﷺ said, 'We have not yet concluded the treaty.' He said, 'By Allah, I will never make peace with you on anything.' The Prophet ﷺ said, 'Then grant him to me.' He said, 'I will not grant him to you.' He said, 'Do it.' He said, 'I will not do it.' Mikraz said, 'Rather, we have granted him to you.' Abu Jandal b. Suhayl b. 'Amr said, 'O assembly of Muslims, am I to be returned to the polytheists after I have come as a Muslim? Do you not see what I have suffered?' He had been severely tortured for the sake of Allah. 'Umar b. al-Khattab, ؓ , said, 'By Allah, I have not doubted since I embraced Islam except on that day. I came to the Prophet ﷺ and said, \"Are you not truly the Messenger of Allah?\" He said, \"Yes.\" I said, \"Are we not on the truth and our enemies on falsehood?\" He said, \"Yes.\" I said, \"Then why do we accept humiliation in our religion?\" He said, \"I am the Messenger of Allah, and I do not disobey my Lord, and He will help me.\" I said, \"Did you not tell us that we would come to the House and circumambulate it?\" He said, \"Yes, but did I tell you that you would come to it this year?\" I said, \"No.\" He said, \"Then you will come to it and circumambulate it.\" Then I came to Abu Bakr al-Siddiq, ؓ , and said, \"O Abu Bakr, is this not truly the Prophet of Allah?\" He said, \"Yes.\" I said, \"Are we not on the truth and our enemies on falsehood?\" He said, \"Yes.\" I said, \"Then why do we accept humiliation in our religion?\" He said, \"O man, he is the Messenger of Allah, and he does not disobey his Lord, and He will help him. Hold fast to his stirrup until you die, for by Allah, he is on the truth.\" I said, \"Did he not tell us that we would come to the House and circumambulate it?\" He said, \"Yes, but did he tell you that you would come to it this year?\" I said, \"No.\" He said, \"Then you will come to it and circumambulate it.\" 'Umar b. al-Khattab, ؓ , said, 'I did some deeds regarding that, meaning regarding the nullification of the document.' When the Messenger of Allah ﷺ finished the treaty, he ordered his companions, saying, 'Slaughter the sacrificial animals and shave your heads.' By Allah, not one of them stood up, hoping that Allah would bring about a change. When none of them stood, the Messenger of Allah ﷺ went to Umm Salamah and said, 'What I have encountered from the people!' Umm Salamah said, 'Do you want that? Go out and do not speak a word to any of them until you slaughter your sacrificial camel and call your barber.' The Prophet ﷺ stood up and went out, and did not speak to anyone until he slaughtered his sacrificial camel, then he called his barber and had his head shaved. When the people saw that, they began shaving one another until some of them almost killed others. Then some believing women came, and Allah revealed: \"O you who have believed, when the believing women come to you as emigrants...\" to the end of the verse. 'Umar, ؓ , divorced two wives he had in polytheism, one of whom Mu'awiyah b. Abi Sufyan married and the other Safwan b. Umayyah. The Prophet ﷺ returned to Madinah, and Abu Basir, a man from Quraysh who was a Muslim, came to him. They sent two men after him, saying, 'Remember the treaty you made with us.' He handed him over to the two men. They left with him until they reached Dhu al-Hulayfah, where they dismounted to eat some dates they had. Abu Basir said to one of the two men, 'By Allah, I see that your sword, O so-and-so, is excellent.' He said, 'Yes, by Allah, it is excellent. I have tried it and tried it again.' Abu Basir said, 'Show it to me, let me look at it.' He gave it to him, and Abu Basir struck him until he died. The other man fled until he reached Madinah and entered the mosque running. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, 'This man has seen something terrifying.' When he reached the Prophet ﷺ, he said, 'By Allah, my companion has been killed, and I am as good as dead.' Abu Basir came and said, 'O Prophet of Allah, by Allah, Allah has fulfilled your protection. You returned me to them, and then Allah saved me from them.' The Prophet ﷺ said, 'Woe to his mother, if only he had someone with him.' When Abu Basir heard that, he knew that he would return him to them again, so he left until he reached the coast. Abu Jandal b. Suhayl b. 'Amr escaped from them and joined Abu Basir. No man from Quraysh embraced Islam except that he joined Abu Basir, until a band of them gathered. By Allah, they did not hear of any caravan of Quraysh going to Syria except that they intercepted it, killed them, and took their wealth. Quraysh sent to the Prophet ﷺ, adjuring him by Allah and kinship to send word to those who came to him, and they would be safe. The Prophet ﷺ sent word to them, and Allah, Mighty and Sublime, revealed: \"And it is He who withheld their hands from you and your hands from them in the valley of Makkah...\" until \"the fervor of the Jahiliyyah.\" Their fervor was that they did not acknowledge that he was the Prophet of Allah and did not acknowledge \"In the name of Allah, the Most Gracious, the Most Merciful.\""],[6160,"The Prophet ﷺ performed 'Umrah in Dhu al-Qa'dah, and the people of Makkah refused to let him enter Makkah until he made a treaty with them that he would stay there for three days. When they wrote the document, they wrote, 'This is what Muhammad, the Messenger of Allah, has agreed upon.' They said, 'We do not acknowledge this. If we knew that you were the Messenger of Allah, we would not have prevented you from anything, but you are Muhammad b. 'Abdullah.' He said, 'I am the Messenger of Allah, and I am Muhammad b. 'Abdullah.' He said to 'Ali, 'Erase \"Messenger of Allah.\"' He said, 'By Allah, I will never erase you.' The Messenger of Allah ﷺ took the document, and he did not know how to write, so he ordered it to be written, and in place of \"Messenger of Allah\" he wrote \"Muhammad.\" So he wrote: 'This is what Muhammad b. 'Abdullah has agreed upon: that he will not enter Makkah with weapons except the sword in its sheath, and he will not take out anyone who follows him, and he will not prevent any of his companions if he wants to stay there.' When he entered it and the term elapsed, they came to 'Ali and said, 'Tell your companion to leave us, for the term has elapsed.' The Messenger of Allah ﷺ left, and the daughter of Hamzah followed them, calling, 'O uncle, O uncle!' 'Ali, ؓ , took her by the hand and said to Fatimah, 'Take care of your cousin's daughter,' and she carried her. 'Ali, Zayd, and Ja'far disputed about her. 'Ali said, 'I took her, and she is my cousin's daughter.' Ja'far said, 'She is my cousin's daughter, and her maternal aunt is my wife.' Zayd said, 'She is my brother's daughter.' The Messenger of Allah ﷺ ruled in favor of her maternal aunt and said, 'The maternal aunt is like the mother.' He said to 'Ali, 'You are from me and I am from you.' He said to Ja'far, 'You resemble me in appearance and character.' He said to Zayd, 'You are our brother and our client.'"],[6161,"He narrated to me that they were one thousand five hundred."],[6162,"He said, 'We were on the day of al-Hudaybiyyah one thousand four hundred, and we pledged allegiance to him while 'Umar was holding his hand under the tree, which was a samurah tree.' And he said, 'We pledged allegiance to him that we would not flee, and we did not pledge allegiance to him on death.'"],[6163,"The people pledged allegiance to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ at the time of al-Hudaybiyyah while he was under the tree, and I was lifting a branch from its branches from his face. We did not pledge allegiance to him on death, but we pledged allegiance to him that we would not flee. They were that day one thousand four hundred."],[6164,"Delegations came to Mu'awiya in Ramadan, I being among them along with Abu Hurayra. Some of us would prepare food for others, and Abu Hurayra would often invite us to his camp. I said: If I prepare food and then invite them to my camp. So I ordered food and it was prepared. Then I met Abu Hurayra in the evening and said: O Abu Hurayra, tonight the invitation is with me. He said: You have preceded me. He (the narrator) said: So I invited them to my camp, when Abu Hurayra said: Shall I not mount you (i.e., give you a ride) or talk to you? I will narrate to you a hadith from your own hadiths, O assembly of the Ansar, until the food is ready. Then he mentioned the conquest of Makkah and said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ approached and entered Makkah. He sent al-Zubayr to one of the two flanks and sent Khalid b. al-Walid to the left flank, and sent Abu Ubayda to the unarmored ones. They took the valley while the Messenger of Allah ﷺ was in his battalion. Quraysh had sent their rabble and their followers, and they said: We will put these forward; if they gain something, we will be with them, and if they are struck, we will give what they ask. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ looked and saw me, and said: 'O Abu Hurayra, call out to the Ansar; let no one come to me except an Ansari.' So he called out to them, and they came and surrounded the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: 'Do you not see the rabble of Quraysh and their followers?' He struck with his right hand, the one next to the little finger, on the middle of his left hand, and said: 'Reap them like harvest until you meet me at al-Safa.' Abu Hurayra said: We set out, and none of us wished to kill any of them whom he wished except that he killed him, and none of them directed anything at us. Abu Sufyan said: O Messenger of Allah, the green (youth) of Quraysh has been made lawful; there is no Quraysh after today. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: 'Whoever closes his door is safe, and whoever enters the house of Abu Sufyan is safe.' So they closed their doors. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ came until he touched the Stone and circumambulated the House, and in his hand was a bow; he was holding the bow. Beside the House there was an idol which they used to worship. The Prophet ﷺ began to stab it in its side with the bow and said: 'Truth has come and falsehood has vanished.' When he finished his circumambulation, he came to al-Safa and ascended to where he could see the House. He ﷺ began raising his hand and began praising Allah and mentioning what he wished to mention, while the Ansar were below him. Some of them said to others: As for the man, desire for his town and compassion for his clan have overtaken him. Then revelation descended upon the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. Abu Hurayra said: It was not hidden from us when revelation descended; none of us would look at the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, but rather he would lower his head until the revelation ended. When the revelation was finished, the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: 'O assembly of the Ansar, you said: As for the man, desire for his town and compassion for his clan have overtaken him.' They said: We said that, O Messenger of Allah. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: 'No, indeed I am the servant of Allah and His Messenger. I migrated to Allah and to you. My life is your life and my death is your death.' So they came forward weeping and said: By Allah, we did not say what we said except out of reluctance to part with Allah and His Messenger. He said: 'Indeed Allah and His Messenger believe you and excuse you.'"],[6165,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ announced departure in the year of the conquest when two nights of Ramadan had passed."],[6166,"A man from Qays said to al-Bara' b. Azib: Did you flee from the Messenger of Allah ﷺ on the day of Hunayn? Al-Bara' said: But the Messenger of Allah ﷺ did not flee. Hawazin were archers. I saw the Messenger of Allah ﷺ on a white mule, and Abu Sufyan b. al-Harith was holding its bridle, and he ﷺ was saying: 'I am the Prophet, no lie; I am the son of Abd al-Muttalib.'"],[6167,"The Prophet ﷺ called the female of the horses a faras."],[6168,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ, when he prayed during the days of Hunayn, murmured something [quietly]. It was said to him, \"You are doing something you did not used to do.\" He said, \"I say: O Allah, with You I attempt, with You I assault, and with You I fight.\""],[6169,"“When the Messenger of Allah ﷺ defeated a people, he liked to stay in their courtyard for three [days].”"],[6170,"«The Messenger of Allah ﷺ sent an expedition, and I was among them. We obtained spoils, and from the division I received twelve camels. Then the Messenger of Allah ﷺ gave us extra after that, one camel each.»"],[6171,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ ordered on the day of Badr that twenty-four men of the leading nobles of Quraysh be thrown into a dry well of Badr. When he gained victory over a people, he liked to stay in their courtyard for three nights. On the third day, he ordered his riding camel to be saddled; he mounted it, then walked, and his companions followed him. They said, “We think he is going only for some need of his,” until he stood at the edge of the well and began calling them by their names and their fathers’ names: “O so-and-so son of so-and-so, would it please you that you had obeyed Allah and His Messenger? We have found what our Lord promised us to be true; have you found what your Lord promised you to be true?” ʿUmar b. al-Khaṭṭāb, ؓ , said, “O Messenger of Allah, do you speak to bodies that have no spirits?” The Prophet ﷺ said, “By the One in whose hand is my soul, you are no better at hearing what I say than they are.” Qatādah said, “Allah revived them so that He could make them hear rebuke, belittlement, vengeance, regret, and remorse.”"],[6172,"that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"People are but like a hundred camels, a man can not find a mount (suitable to ride upon) among them.\" (Using translation from Tirmidhī 2872)"],[6173,"That the Prophet ﷺ would not attack except near the time of Fajr, so if he heard the Adhan he would refrain, and if not, then he would attack. So he listened one day and heard a man saying: \"Allahu Akbar, Allahu Akbar,\" so he said: \"Upon the Fitrah.\" Then he said: \"I bear witness that none has the right to be worshipped but Allah.\" So he said: \"You have departed from the Fire.\" (Using translation from Tirmidhī 1618)"],[6174,"“I pledged allegiance to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ to establish the prayer, give the zakāh, and give sincere advice to every Muslim.”"],[6175,"“I pledged allegiance to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ to hear and obey and give sincere advice to every Muslim.” Then whenever he bought or sold something, he would say to his companion: Know that what we take from you is dearer to us than what we give you, so choose."],[6176,"“We pledged allegiance to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ to hear and obey in ease and hardship, in what we like and dislike, and that we would not contend with those in authority, and that we would stand—or say—the truth wherever we are, not fearing in Allah the blame of any blamer.”"],[6177,"“When we pledged allegiance to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ to hear and obey, he would say to us: ‘In what you are able.’”"],[6178,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to the companions of al-Hijr: \"Do not enter upon these punished people unless you are weeping, so do not enter upon them lest there befall you the like of what befell them.\""],[6179,"A slave pledged allegiance to the Prophet ﷺ for emigration, and his master came to him wanting him. He said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ purchased him with two black slaves. Then he did not pledge allegiance from anyone for emigration until he asked him: “Is he a slave?”"],[6180,"I came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ among women who were pledging allegiance to him. They said: We pledge allegiance to you, O Messenger of Allah, that we will not associate anything with Allah, and will not steal, and will not commit adultery, and will not kill our children, and will not bring a slander that we fabricate between our hands and feet, and will not disobey you in what is right. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: 'In what you are able and can bear.' She said: I said: Allah and His Messenger are more merciful to us than we are to ourselves. Come, let us pledge allegiance to you, O Messenger of Allah. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: 'I do not shake hands with women. My word to one hundred women is like my word to one woman, or the like of my word to one woman.'"],[6181,"“We pledged allegiance to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ on the Day of al-Ḥudaybiyah while I was lifting the branch of the tree from his face. We pledged allegiance to him that we would not flee; we did not pledge allegiance to him for death.” We said to him: How many were you? He said: One thousand four hundred."],[6182,"We were sitting around the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and with us were Abū Bakr and ʿUmar, ؓ , in a group. The Prophet of Allah ﷺ got up from among us and was slow to return, so we feared he had been taken from us and became alarmed. I was the first to be alarmed, so I went out following the Messenger of Allah ﷺ until I came to a garden belonging to the Anṣār, to the Banū al-Najjār. I went around it looking for an entrance and found a stream entering the inside of the garden from its outside—al-rabīʿ means a water channel. I squeezed through and entered upon the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and he said: “Abū Hurayrah?” I said: Yes, O Messenger of Allah. He said: “What brought you?” I said: You got up from among us and were slow to return, so we feared you had been taken from us and became alarmed. I was the first to be alarmed, so I came to this garden and squeezed through as a fox squeezes through, and the people are behind me. He said: “O Abū Hurayrah,” and he gave me his two sandals and said: “Go with these two sandals of mine. Whomever you meet behind this wall who bears witness that there is no god but Allah with certainty in his heart, give him glad tidings of Paradise.” The first person I met was ʿUmar b. al-Khaṭṭāb, ؓ , and he said: What are these two sandals, O Abū Hurayrah? I said: These are the two sandals of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. He sent me with them: whomever I meet behind this wall who bears witness that there is no god but Allah with certainty in his heart, I am to give him glad tidings of Paradise. He said: ʿUmar, ؓ , struck me between my breasts with his hand and I fell on my backside. He said: Go back, O Abū Hurayrah. So I returned to the Prophet of Allah ﷺ and burst into tears, and ʿUmar caught up with me on my tracks. The Messenger of Allah said: “What is the matter with you, O Abū Hurayrah?” I said: I met ʿUmar and told him what you sent me with, and he struck me between my breasts such that I fell on my backside, and he said: Go back. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “O ʿUmar, what made you do that?” He said: O Messenger of Allah, may my father and mother be sacrificed for you, did you send Abū Hurayrah with your sandals to give glad tidings of Paradise to whomever he meets who bears witness that there is no god but Allah with certainty in his heart? He said: “Yes.” He said: Then do not do it, for I fear that people will rely upon it. Leave them to act. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Then leave them.”"],[6183,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ was delivering the Friday sermon when the people rose to him and shouted, “O Prophet of Allah, the rain has ceased, the trees have turned red, and the animals have died, so invoke Allah to send us rain.” He said, “O Allah, give us water.” He said, “By Allah, we did not see even a wisp of cloud in the sky.” He said, “Then a cloud arose and spread, and it rained. The Prophet of Allah ﷺ descended, prayed, and left. It kept raining until the next Friday. When the Prophet ﷺ stood to deliver the sermon, they shouted, ‘O Prophet of Allah, the houses have collapsed and the roads are cut off, so invoke Allah to withhold it from us.’” He said, “He ﷺ smiled and said, ‘O Allah, around us and not upon us.’” He said, “Then it cleared from Madinah and began to rain around it, and not a drop fell on Madinah.” He said, “I looked at Madinah, and it was like a crown.”"],[6184,"The rain was withheld for a year, so some Muslims rose to the Prophet ﷺ and said, “O Messenger of Allah, the rain has been withheld, the land has become barren, and the livestock have died.” He said, “He raised his hands, and we did not see any cloud in the sky. He extended his hands until I saw the whiteness of his armpits, seeking rain from Allah. We had not yet prayed Friday when a young man whose house was nearby was concerned to return to his family. It continued for a Friday. On the following Friday, a man said, ‘O Messenger of Allah, the houses have collapsed and travelers are held up.’” He said, “He ﷺ smiled at the quick boredom of the son of Adam and said with his hands, ‘O Allah, around us and not upon us.’” He said, “Then it cleared from Madinah.”"],[6185,"“When drought occurred in the time of the Prophet ﷺ, they sought rain through the Prophet ﷺ, and he would pray for rain for them and they were given water. After the death of the Prophet ﷺ, during the rule of Umar, drought occurred. Umar came out with al-Abbas to seek rain through him and said: ‘O Allah, we used to seek rain through Your Prophet ﷺ when drought befell us, and You gave us water. Today we seek intercession through the uncle of Your Prophet ﷺ, so give us water.’” He said: “And they were given water.”"],[6186,"When the people of a household gave charity to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, he invoked blessings upon them. He said: My father gave charity to him, so he said, “O Allah, bless the family of Abu Awfa.”"],[6187,"A man during the time of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to engage in trade, and there was weakness in his mental capacity. His family came to the Prophet of Allah ﷺ and said, 'O Prophet of Allah, place a restriction on so-and-so, for he engages in trade while there is weakness in his mental capacity.' The Prophet of Allah ﷺ called him and forbade him from selling. He said, 'O Prophet of Allah, I cannot be patient away from selling.' The Prophet of Allah said, 'If you will not abandon selling, then say, \"No cheating, no cheating.\"'"],[6188,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to campaign with us, and with him were women from the Ansar. We provided water and treated the wounded."],[6189,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ came, during the expedition of Tabūk, upon a house in whose courtyard hung a water-skin. He asked for water, and it was said to him, “It is from an animal that died.” He said, “Its tanning is its purification.”"],[6190,"When the Messenger of Allah ﷺ conquered Khaybar, al-Hajjaj b. 'Ilat said, \"O Messenger of Allah, I have property in Makkah and I have family there, and I want to go to them. Am I free to say something against you or about you?\" The Messenger of Allah ﷺ permitted him to say whatever he wished. He said, \"He went to his wife when he arrived and said, 'Collect for me what you have, for I want to buy from the spoils of Muhammad ﷺ and his companions, for they have been plundered and their property has been taken.'\" He said, \"This spread through Makkah and distressed the Muslims, while the polytheists showed joy and happiness. The news reached al-'Abbas b. 'Abd al-Muttalib, and he was struck with grief in his gathering and could not rise.\" Ma'mar said, \"Al-Jazari informed me from Miqsam, who said, 'Al-'Abbas took a son of his called Qutham, who resembled the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and lay down, placing him on his chest while saying...'\""],[6191,"I acquired an old she-camel from the spoils of Badr, and the Messenger of Allah ﷺ gave me another old she-camel. I made them kneel at the door of a man from the Ansar, intending to load on them idhkhir grass to sell and use the proceeds for Fatimah's wedding feast. With me was a man from Banu Qaynuqa', and Hamzah b. 'Abd al-Muttalib was in the house with a singing girl who was singing to him. She said..."],[6192,"Indeed, the Prophet ﷺ sent Abu Jahl bin Hudhayfah as a representative to collect charity. A man refused to give him charity, so Abu Jahl struck him and injured him. They all went to the Prophet ﷺ and said, \"O Messenger of Allah, seek justice!\" The Prophet ﷺ said, \"You have this and that.\" They were not satisfied, so he said again, \"You have this and that.\" They were still not satisfied, so he said, \"You have this and that.\" Finally, they agreed and said, \"Are you satisfied?\" They replied, \"Yes.\""],[6193,"The announcer of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ called out among us on the day he turned back from the Confederates: “No one should pray Zuhr except among Banu Qurayzah.” Some people feared missing the time, so they prayed before reaching Banu Qurayzah. Others said, “We will not pray except where the Messenger of Allah ﷺ commanded us, even if the time passes.” He said: “He did not rebuke any of the two groups.”"],[6194,"A man from the Anṣār freed six slaves at the time of his death, and he had no wealth besides them. He said: “That reached the Prophet ﷺ, and he spoke harshly to him. Then he summoned them, divided them into portions, and cast lots among them; then he freed two of them and left four as slaves.”"],[6195,"That Haytah used to enter the wives of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ without being counted among the family members. So the Messenger of Allah ﷺ entered upon him while he was being described as a woman, and he said: \"When she approaches, she approaches with four and when she turns away, she turns away with eight.\" So the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, \"Do I not see that he knows what is happening here? He should not enter upon you.\" So he expelled him, and he would come to the outskirts and enter every Friday, feeding them."],[6196,"He went on an expedition with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ before Najd. One day, the midday rest overtook them in a valley with many thorny trees. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ dismounted, and the people scattered among the trees to seek shade. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ dismounted under a tree and hung his sword on it. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to a man with him, \"This man drew my sword while I was sleeping. I woke up and it was in his hand. He said to me, 'Who will protect you from me?' I said to him, 'Allah.' He said, 'Who will protect you from me?' I said, 'Allah.' So he sheathed the sword and sat down. Here he is sitting.\" Then he did not punish him."],[6197,"I took 'Abdullah b. Abi Talha Ansari to Messenger of Allah ﷺ at the time of his birth. Messenger of Allah ﷺ was at that time wearing a woollen cloak and besmearing the camels with tar. He said: Have you got with you the dates? I said: Yes. He took hold of the dates and put them in his mouth and softened them, then opened the mouth of the infant and put that in it and the child began to lick it. Thereupon Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: The Ansar have a liking for the dates, and he (the Holy Prophet) gave him the name of 'Abdullah. (Using translation from Muslim 2144a)"],[6198,"When Umm Sulaym gave birth, she said, \"O Anas, look after this boy and make sure nothing happens to him until you take him early in the morning to the Prophet ﷺ so that he may perform tahnik on him.\" He said, \"So I went early with him, and there he ﷺ was in the walled garden, wearing a cloak and branding the camels that had been brought to him at the conquest.\""],[6199,"I brought 'Abd Allah b. Abi Talha to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ so that he might perform tahnik on him, and I found him with the branding iron in his hand, branding the camels of zakat."],[6200,"Umm Sulaim accompanied me with some dates in a clay pot to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, but I did not find him at his house. They said he had gone nearby. Suddenly, he was at a tailor's house, his servant, where he had a meal with meat and a type of wild game. I saw that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ liked the wild game, so I placed it in front of him. He returned to his house, and I placed the clay pot in front of him. He continued eating and distributing until nothing was left in the pot."],[6201,"A man used to give the Prophet ﷺ palm trees from his land until Qurayzah and al-Nadir were conquered for him, and after that he began to return to him what he had given him. Anas said: My family commanded me to go to the Prophet ﷺ and ask him for what he had given him, or part of it. The Prophet of Allah ﷺ had given it to Umm Ayman. I went to the Prophet ﷺ, and he gave them to me. Umm Ayman came and placed the garment around my neck and said, 'By Allah, he will not give them to you, for he gave them to me.' The Prophet of Allah ﷺ said, 'O Umm Ayman, leave him, and you shall have such and such.' She said, 'No, by the One besides whom there is no god,' until he gave her ten times its like, or close to ten times its like."],[6202,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ gave me sheep to distribute among his companions. I distributed them, and a young goat remained. I mentioned it to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and he said, 'Sacrifice it yourself.'"],[6203,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ distributed sheep for sacrifices among his companions and gave me a young goat. I brought it to him and said, 'O Messenger of Allah, it is a jadhaʿ (one-year-old).' He said, 'Sacrifice it.'"],[6204,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ passed by an onion field with his companions, and some people dismounted and ate from it, while others did not eat from it. We went to him, and he called those who had not eaten the onion and delayed the others until its smell went away."],[6205,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ, when he swore an oath, did not break it until the expiation for oaths was revealed. Then he ﷺ said: «I do not swear an oath and then see something better than it except that I do what is better and expiate my oath.»"],[6206,"We were on foot, so we came to the Prophet of Allah ﷺ asking him to provide us mounts. He said: «By Allah, I will not provide you mounts today,» or he said: «By Allah, I will not provide you mounts.» He said: When we returned to the camp—or he said: when we returned to the camp—a herd of camels came to him, and then he sent to us three with white spots on their humps. Some of us said to others: Shall we ride when the Messenger of Allah ﷺ has sworn an oath? We came to him and said: O Prophet of Allah, you have sworn an oath. He said: «By Allah, I do not provide you mounts; only Allah has provided you mounts. There is no oath on earth that I swear and then see something better than it except that I do it.»"],[6207,"A man asked permission to enter upon the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. He said, \"Let him in. What a bad son of his clan, or what a bad man of his clan.\" But when he entered, he spoke gently to him. When he left, I said, \"O Messenger of Allah, you said about him what you said, but when he entered you spoke gently to him.\" He ﷺ said, \"O 'A'ishah, the worst of people in station before Allah is one whom people leave or abandon to avoid his evil.\""],[6208,"I went, along with Al-Hasan, Al-Husayn, and Usama ibn Zaid, on the day of Eid. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ also went to the prayer place and prayed with us. Then he delivered a sermon and said, \"O people, this is a day of charity, so give in charity.\" A man started taking off his ring, and another man started taking off his garment. Bilal held on to them, waiting until he didn't see anyone giving anything. Then Bilal approached the women and said, \"O women, this is a day of charity, so give in charity.\" So the women started taking off their bracelets and rings. Bilal held on to them, waiting again until he didn't see anyone giving anything. Then Bilal approached and we all moved forward."],[6209,"\"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ spent the entire night alive when he reached Badr the next morning as a traveler.\""],[6210,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to the companions of al-Hijr: \"Do not enter upon these punished people unless you are weeping, so do not enter upon them lest there befall you the like of what befell them.\""],[6211,"He came as a delegate to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and asked him to grant him a piece of land. He granted him the salt land. When he turned away, a man said: O Messenger of Allah, do you know what you have granted him? You have granted him a perennial water source. So he took it back from him. He said: I asked him about what may be protected from the arak trees. He said: «What the feet of camels do not reach.»"],[6212,"I remember a mouthful of water that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ spat into my face from a bucket hanging in our house."],[6213,"A man used to make purchases during the time of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and there was weakness in his judgment. His family came to the Prophet ﷺ and said: O Messenger of Allah, place a restriction on so-and-so, for he buys while there is weakness in his judgment. The Prophet ﷺ called him and forbade him from selling. He said: O Prophet of Allah, I cannot refrain from selling. He ﷺ said: \"If you will not abandon selling, then say: 'There is no deception, and no cheating.'\""],[6214,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to the companions of al-Hijr: \"Do not enter upon these punished people unless you are weeping, so do not enter upon them lest there befall you the like of what befell them.\""],[6215,"My father used to send ahead the weak members of his family from Muzdalifah to Mina, and he would mention that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to do that."],[6216,"The Prophet ﷺ protected al-Naqīʿ as a grazing ground for the Muslims' horses."],[6217,"Prices became high during the time of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, so they said: \"O Messenger of Allah, prices have become high, so set prices for us.\" The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"Indeed Allah is the Creator, the Withholder, the Expander, the Provider, and I hope to not meet Allah with an injustice by which I wronged anyone of you regarding family or wealth.\""],[6218,"He used to send someone to the people to assess their vineyards and fruits."],[6219,"He used to remind the people every Thursday. A man said, “I wish you would remind us every day.” He said, “Indeed, what prevents me from that is only fear of boring you. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to space out admonition for us between days for fear of weariness upon us.”"],[6220,"A tailor invited the Messenger of Allah ﷺ to a meal he had prepared. Anas said, \"I went with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and he brought barley bread and broth with gourd and dried meat.\" Anas said, \"I saw the Messenger of Allah ﷺ picking out the gourd from around the bowl.\" He said, \"I have not ceased to love gourd since that day.\""],[6221,"The delegation of ʿAbd al-Qays, when they came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, said: O Messenger of Allah, we are a tribe from Rabīʿah, and between us and you are the disbelievers of Muḍar. We can only reach you during the sacred month, so command us with a matter to which we may call those of our people behind us, and by which we may enter Paradise if we take it up or act upon it. He said: “I command you with four things and forbid you from four: that you worship Allah and do not associate anything with Him, that you establish the prayer, give the zakāh, fast Ramaḍān, and give a fifth of the spoils. And I forbid you from four: from al-dubbāʾ, al-ḥantam, al-muzaffat, and al-naqīr.” They said: O Messenger of Allah, what do you know about al-naqīr? He said: “It is the trunk that you hollow out and cast into it small dates or dates, then pour water over them until it ferments; then when it settles you drink it, and it may lead one of you to strike his cousin with the sword.” He said: Among the people was a man who had such a wound. He said: I used to hide it out of shyness from the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. They said: In what do you command us to drink, O Prophet of Allah? He said: “Drink from waterskins of leather whose mouths are tied.” They said: O Messenger of Allah, our land has many rats, and no leather waterskins remain. He said: “Even if the rats eat them,” twice or three times. Then the Prophet of Allah ﷺ said to Ashajj ʿAbd al-Qays: “You have two qualities that Allah loves: forbearance and deliberateness.”"],[6222,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to carry earth with us on the Day of the Confederates, and the earth had covered the whiteness of his belly while he was saying..."],[6223,"I came to the Prophet ﷺ and spoke with him while he was in i'tikaf in the mosque. He got up with me one night to escort me to my house. Two men from the Ansar met him, and when they saw him, they felt shy and turned back. He said: «Come here, for she is Safiyya bt. Huyayy.» They said: We seek refuge in Allah. Glorified be Allah. He said: «I do not say this to you because you think ill, but I know that Satan runs through the son of Adam like blood.»"],[6224,"She came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ while he was in i'tikaf during the last ten nights of Ramadan. Then she got up to leave, and the Messenger of Allah ﷺ got up with her to escort her. When he reached near the door of the mosque, by the door of Umm Salama, the wife of the Prophet ﷺ, two men from the Ansar passed by and greeted the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, then they distanced themselves. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to them: «Slow down, she is only Safiyya bt. Huyayy.» They said: Glorified be Allah, O Messenger of Allah, and that weighed heavily on them. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: «Indeed Satan reaches in a person to the extent of blood, and I feared that he might cast something into your hearts.»"],[6225,"I heard him among ten of the Companions of the Prophet ﷺ, one of whom was Abu Qatadah, say: 'I am the most knowledgeable of you about the prayer of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ.' They said, 'You were not the earliest of us in companionship with him, nor the most frequent of us in following him!' He said, 'Yes, I was.' They said, 'Then present it.' He said: 'When the Messenger of Allah ﷺ stood for prayer, he faced the qiblah and raised his hands until they were level with his shoulders, then said Allahu Akbar. When he bowed, he said the takbir and raised his hands when bowing, then he straightened his back, neither raising his head nor lowering it. Then he raised his head and said, \"Allah hears the one who praises Him,\" and raised his hands until they were level with his shoulders, then he stood straight. Then he prostrated and pointed his toes toward the qiblah. Then he raised his head and said Allahu Akbar, then folded his left leg and sat, and straightened himself until every bone returned to its place. Then he said Allahu Akbar. When he stood from the two rak'ahs, he said the takbir, then stood. When it was the rak'ah in which the prayer would end, he moved his left leg back and sat on it, leaning on his left side, then he said the salam.'"],[6226,"He was in a gathering in which his father was present, and he was one of the Companions of the Prophet ﷺ, and in the gathering were Abu Hurayrah, Abu Usayd, and Abu Humayd al-Sa'idi from the Ansar. They mentioned prayer among themselves. Abu Humayd said, 'I am the most knowledgeable among you concerning the prayer of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ.' They said, 'Show us.' He said, 'He stood up to pray while they watched. He began by saying takbir and raised his hands level with his shoulders. Then he said takbir for bowing and raised his hands as well. Then he placed his hands on his knees, not drawing his head in and not lowering it. Then he raised his head and said, \"Allah hears those who praise Him. O Allah, our Lord, to You belongs praise.\" Then he raised his hands. Then he said, \"Allahu Akbar\" and prostrated, supporting himself on his palms, knees, and the front of his feet while prostrating. Then he said takbir and sat, placing one leg under him and standing the other foot upright. Then he said takbir and prostrated the second prostration, then said takbir and stood up without sitting for rest. Then he returned and bowed for the other rak'ah, and said takbir likewise. Then he sat after the two rak'ahs until he wanted to rise for standing, he said takbir, then he bowed for the last two rak'ahs. When he said the taslim, he turned to his right, saying, \"Peace be upon you and the mercy of Allah,\" and turned to his left, saying, \"Peace be upon you and the mercy of Allah.\"'"],[6227,"\"The Messenger of Allah ﷺturned to face us when he stood up to pray, before he said the Takbir and said: 'Make your rows straight and come close to one another, for I can see you behind my back.\"' (Using translation from Nasāʾī 814)"],[6228,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ began prayer with the takbir (Allah is most great) and with reciting “Praise be to Allah, the Lord of the Universe”. And when he bowed, he neither raised up nor lowered down his head, but kept it between the two (conditions). And when he raised his head after bowing, he did not prostrate himself until he stood up straight; and when he raised his head after prostration, he did not prostrate (the second time) until he sat down properly; and he recited al-tahiyyat after every pair of rak’ahs; and when he sat, he spread out his left foot and raised his right. He forbade to sit like the sitting of the devil, and to spread out to hands (on the ground in prostration) like animals. He used to finish prayer with uttering the salutation. (Using translation from Abū Dāʾūd 783)"],[6229,"He used to spread his fingers in prayer."],[6230,"When he began the obligatory prayer he would say: “I have turned my face to the One who created the heavens and the earth, as a ḥanīf, a Muslim, and I am not of the polytheists. My prayer, my sacrifice, my life, and my death belong to Allah, Lord of the worlds, who has no partner. With that I have been commanded, and I am of the Muslims. O Allah, You are the King, there is no god but You. Glory be to You and praise. You are my Lord and I am Your servant. I have wronged myself and I confess my sin, so forgive all my sins. None forgives sins but You. Guide me to the best of character; none guides to it but You, and turn away from me its evil; none turns away its evil but You. Here I am, at Your service. All good is in Your hands, and the guided one is the one You guide. I am through You and to You. Blessed and exalted are You. I seek Your forgiveness and I repent to You.”"],[6231,"Three practices the Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to do but people have abandoned: When the Messenger of Allah ﷺ stood for prayer, he raised his hands fully. He would pause briefly before recitation, asking Allah of His bounty. And he would say takbir in prayer whenever he bowed and prostrated."],[6232,"When the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said the takbir in prayer, he would pause briefly before reciting. I said, 'O Messenger of Allah, may my father and mother be ransomed for you, what do you say during your silence between the takbir and the recitation?' He said, 'I say: O Allah, distance me from my sins as You distanced between the east and the west. O Allah, purify me from sins as the white garment is purified from filth. O Allah, wash me from my sins with water, snow, and hail.'"],[6233,"I prayed behind Abu Hurayrah, and he said, \"In the name of Allah, the Most Merciful, the Most Compassionate (Bismillah al-Rahman al-Rahim),\" then he recited the Mother of the Book until, when he reached \"not of those who have incurred wrath nor of those who are astray,\" he said, \"Amin,\" and the people said, \"Amin.\" When he bowed, he said, \"Allah is Greatest (Allahu Akbar).\" When he raised his head, he said, \"Allah hears the one who praises Him (Sami'a Allahu liman hamidah).\" Then he said, \"Allah is Greatest,\" then he prostrated. When he raised, he said, \"Allah is Greatest.\" When he prostrated, he said, \"Allah is Greatest.\" When he raised, he said, \"Allah is Greatest.\" Then he stood up straight with the takbir. When he stood after the two [rak'ahs], he said, \"Allah is Greatest.\" When he said the salam, he said, \"By the One in whose hand is my soul, I am indeed the most like you in prayer to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ.\""],[6234,"He prayed with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. He said: \"He placed his right hand over his left hand. When he said: {nor of those who go astray} [Qur'an 1:7], he said 'Amin' and then he said the salam to his right and to his left.\""],[6235,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ, when he finished reciting the Opening of the Book, raised his voice and said 'Amin.'"],[6236,"Two pauses I memorized from the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. I mentioned that to 'Imran b. Husayn, and he said: \"We memorized one pause.\" So we wrote to Ubayy b. Ka'b in Madinah, and he wrote back to me that Samurah had indeed memorized correctly. Sa'id said: \"We said to Qatadah: 'What are these two pauses?' He said: 'When he entered his prayer and when he finished the recitation.'\""],[6237,"I said, 'I will certainly look at the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, how he prays.' So I looked at him when he stood up. He said the takbir and raised his hands until they were level with his ears, then he placed his right hand over the back of his left hand, wrist, and forearm. Then when he wanted to bow, he raised his hands similarly, then bowed and placed his hands on his knees. Then he raised his head and raised his hands similarly, then prostrated and placed his palms level with his ears. Then he sat and spread out his left thigh and placed the tip of his right elbow on his right thigh, and formed a circle with two of his fingers, then raised his finger. I saw him moving it, supplicating with it. Then I came after that in a time of cold, and I saw the people wearing heavy clothes, their hands moving under the clothes."],[6238,"I prayed behind the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. When he entered the row,* he raised his hands and said the takbir, then wrapped his garment around him and put his hand inside his garment, taking his left with his right. When he wanted to bow, he took out his hands, raised them, said the takbir, then bowed. When he raised his head from bowing, he raised his hands, said the takbir, then prostrated, and placed his face between his palms. Ibn Juhadah said: I mentioned that to al-Hasan b. Abi al-Hasan, and he said, 'That is the prayer of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. Whoever did it, did it, and whoever left it, left it.'"],[6239,"When he said the takbir, he raised his hands when he began the prayer until they were level with his ears; and when he bowed; and when he raised his head from bowing."],[6240,"I saw the Prophet ﷺ when he began the prayer, he raised his hands until they were level with his shoulders; and when he wanted to bow; and after he raised his head from bowing. He did not raise them between the two prostrations."],[6241,"We came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ while we were young men close in age, and we stayed with him for twenty nights. He thought that we had missed our families, so he asked us about whom we had left among our families, and we told him. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ was compassionate and gentle, so he said, “Return to your families, teach them, command them, and pray as you have seen me pray. When the prayer time arrives, let one of you call the adhan, and let the oldest of you lead you.”"],[6242,"Abu Qilaba reported that he saw Malik b. Huwairith raising his hands at the beginning of prayer and raising his hands before kneeling down, and raising his hands after lifting his head from the state of kneeling, and he narrated that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to do like this. (Using translation from Muslim 391a)"],[6243,"I entered with 'Alqamah upon Ibn Mas'ud. He said to us, 'Have these people prayed?' We said, 'No.' He said, 'Then stand and pray.' We went to stand behind him, and he placed one of us on his right and the other on his left. He prayed without adhan or iqamah. When he bowed, he interlaced his fingers in prayer and placed them between his knees.' When he finished, he said, 'Thus I saw the Messenger of Allah ﷺ praying.' And he said, 'O people, there will be rulers over you who kill the prayer, delaying it until the time of the dead. Whoever of you lives to see that, let him pray the prayer at its proper time, and let him make his prayer with them supererogatory.'"],[6244,"“When the Prophet ﷺ prostrated, he would spread his arms apart until the whiteness of his armpits appeared.”"],[6245,"I saw the Prophet ﷺ, when he prostrated, place his knees before his hands, and when he rose, he raised his hands before his knees."],[6246,"“When he bowed, he spread his fingers, and when he prostrated, he joined his fingers.”"],[6248,"I saw the Prophet ﷺ praying and in the odd rakʿat, he used to sit for a moment before getting up. (Using translation from Bukhārī 823)"],[6249,"He entered upon us in our mosque and said: \"Indeed I am praying, not intending (merely) the prayer, but I intend to teach you how the Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to pray.\" He said: \"Then he mentioned Allah, and when he raised his head from the prostration in the first rakʿah, he sat upright, then he stood up and leaned on the ground.\""],[6250,"«When the Messenger of Allah ﷺ rose from the second rakʿah, he began the recitation (immediately) and did not remain silent.»"],[6251,"The Prophet ﷺ used to raise his hands when he began to pray, when he wanted to bow, when he raised his head from bowing, and when he stood up after the first two rak'ahs, he would raise his hands likewise, level with his shoulders. (Using translation from Nasāʾī 1182)"],[6252,"When he would sit for tashahhud, he would place his left hand on his left thigh and place his right hand on his right thigh, and he would point with his index finger, his gaze not going beyond his pointing."],[6253,"We came to Madinah while they were shaking their hands from beneath their garments. I said, 'I will certainly look at the prayer of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ.' He said, 'He said the takbir until he opened the prayer, and he raised his hands until I saw his thumbs near his ears.' He said, 'Then he took his left hand with his right hand. When he bowed, he raised his hands. When he raised his head, he said, \"Allah hears the one who praises Him.\" Then he said the takbir and raised his hands. Then he prostrated and placed his head between his hands in the position relative to his face. When he sat, he spread his feet and placed his right elbow on his right thigh, and he grasped his little finger and the one next to it, joined his thumb and middle finger, and raised the one next to it, supplicating with it.'\""],[6254,"He saw the Messenger of Allah ﷺ in prayer with his right hand on his right thigh, raising his index finger, having bent it slightly, while supplicating."],[6255,"Ibn ʿUmar saw me playing with pebbles in prayer. When he finished, he rebuked me and said: \"Do as the Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to do.\" He said: \"When he sat in prayer, he placed his right palm on his right thigh, clenched all his fingers, and pointed with the finger next to the thumb. And he placed his left palm on his left thigh.\""],[6256,"«When the Messenger of Allah ﷺ sat in the two rakʿahs, he would spread out the left (foot) and erect the right, place his thumb on the middle finger, point with the index finger, place his left palm on his left thigh, and put his left palm against his knee.»"],[6257,"He saw a man moving pebbles with his hand while he was in prayer. When he finished, 'Abd Allah said to him, 'Do not move the pebbles while you are in prayer, for that is from Satan. But do as the Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to do.' He said, 'He placed his right hand on his thigh and pointed with the finger next to the thumb toward the qiblah, and he fixed his gaze upon it or toward it.' Then he said, 'Thus I saw the Messenger of Allah ﷺ do.'"],[6258,"I never prayed behind an imam whose prayer was lighter or more complete than the Messenger of Allah ﷺ."],[6259,"«The Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to turn to his right, saying: “Peace be upon you and the mercy of Allah,” until the whiteness of his cheek appeared, and to his left likewise.»"],[6260,"In the time of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, when the women had said the salutation from the prayer, they would rise, and the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and those men who prayed with him would remain as long as Allah willed. When the Messenger of Allah ﷺ stood, the men would stand."],[6261,"\"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ, when he prayed the dawn prayer, sat in his place of prayer until the sun rose.\""],[6262,"\"He used to pray two light rak'ahs when the muezzin called for the Fajr prayer, and it was a time when no one would enter upon him.\""],[6263,"He used to pray the two rak'ahs of Fajr when dawn broke."],[6264,"The Prophet ﷺ would pray the two rak'ahs of Fajr and lighten them so much that I would say, “Did he recite the Mother of the Qur'an in them?”"],[6265,"When the muadhdhin finished the first call of the Fajr prayer, the Messenger of Allah ﷺ would stand and pray two light rak'ahs before the Fajr prayer, after dawn had become clear to him, then he would lie on his right side until the muadhdhin came to him for the iqamah."],[6266,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to recite in the Subh prayer on Friday: Alif Lam Mim Tanzil and Hal Ata 'ala al-Insan."],[6267,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to recite in the Fajr prayer on Friday: Alif Lam Mim Tanzil al-Sajdah and Hal Ata 'ala al-Insan."],[6268,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to recite in the Maghrib prayer on the night of Friday: “Say: O disbelievers” and “Say: He is Allah, the One,” and he would recite in the late night prayer on Friday night: “Al-Jumu‘ah” and “Al-Munafiqun.”"],[6269,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ turned aside while I was with him during the expedition of Tabuk before dawn, so I turned aside with him. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ made his camel kneel and went to relieve himself, then came to me. I poured water from the vessel over his hands, and he washed his palms, then washed his face. Then he uncovered his forearms, but the sleeve of his jubba was tight, so he inserted his hands and brought them out from beneath the jubba and washed them up to the elbows. He wiped his head, then performed wiping over his leather socks. Then he mounted, and we set off until we came upon the people at prayer. They had put forward 'Abd al-Rahman b. 'Awf, and he led them in prayer when the time of prayer arrived. We found that 'Abd al-Rahman had already led them in one rak'ah of the dawn prayer. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ stood with the Muslims behind 'Abd al-Rahman b. 'Awf and prayed the second rak'ah of the dawn prayer. Then 'Abd al-Rahman said the salutation, and the Messenger of Allah ﷺ stood up to complete his prayer. The Muslims were startled and uttered much tasbih because they had preceded the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. When the Messenger of Allah ﷺ finished with the salutation, he said to them, \"You have done well,\" or \"You have done right.\""],[6270,"I am the most knowledgeable of people about the time of this prayer, meaning Isha. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to pray it when the moon set on the third night."],[6271,"\"That the Prophet ﷺ prayed witr with one rak'ah.\""],[6272,"\"That the Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to separate between the two prostrations in prayer and the odd units.\""],[6273,"“The Messenger of Allah ﷺ came out one day to pray for rain. He turned his back to the people, faced the qiblah, reversed his cloak, and prayed two rak‘ahs.”"],[6274,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ “did not raise his hands in any supplication except in the rain prayer, for he would raise his hands until the whiteness of his armpits could be seen.”"],[6275,"A governor sent me to Ibn Abbas to ask him about the rain prayer. He said: “The Messenger of Allah ﷺ came out humbly, submissively, imploringly, and modestly. He did not deliver a sermon like this sermon of yours. He prayed two rak‘ahs as he prayed on Eid.”"],[6276,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ went out to seek rainfall so he faced the Qibla, turned his back towards the people, flipped his cloak, and performed two loud Rak'ahs during which he recited out loud."],[6277,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ prayed for rain while wearing a black cloak. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ wanted to take hold of its lower part and make it its upper part, but when it became heavy on him he turned it over onto his shoulder."],[6278,"He saw the Prophet ﷺ and Abu Bakr and 'Umar, ؓ , «walking in front of the funeral.»"],[6279,"He used not to go out on the day of Fitr until he ate, and he would not eat on the day of sacrifice until he sacrificed."],[6280,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to break his fast with dates and then have his morning meal."],[6281,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ did not go out on the day of Fitr until he ate three, or five, or seven dates."],[6282,"When the Prophet ﷺ went out to the two Eids, he would return by a different route from the one he had taken."],[6283,"Ibn ʿAbbas was asked whether he had joined the Prophet ﷺ in the ʿId prayer. He said, \"Yes. And I could not have joined him had I not been young. (The Prophet ﷺ came out) till he reached the mark which was near the house of Kathir bin As-Salt, offered the prayer, delivered the Khutba and then went towards the women. Bilal was accompanying him. He preached to them and advised them and ordered them to give alms. I saw the women putting their ornaments with their outstretched hands into Bilal's garment. Then the Prophet ﷺ along with Bilal returned home. (Using translation from Bukhārī 977)"],[6284,"He used to pray Fitr and Adha, then deliver a sermon."],[6285,"I prayed with the Prophet ﷺ on Eid more than once or twice without adhan or iqamah."],[6286,"The Prophet of Allah ﷺ, when he reached Dhū al-Ḥulayfah, marked the sacrificial animal on the right side of its hump, then wiped away the blood and garlanded it with his two sandals. Then he mounted his riding camel, and when it stood upright with him at al-Baydāʾ, he entered iḥrām and pronounced the talbiyah for Hajj."],[6287,"that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ prayed Zuhr at Dhu al-Ḥulayfah, then called for a she-camel and marked it on the right side of its hump, then wiped the blood from it and put two sandals around its neck. Then his riding camel was brought, and when he sat on it and it stood up straight with him at al-Baydāʾ, he entered iḥrām."],[6288,"that the Prophet ﷺ marked the sacrificial camel."],[6289,"The Prophet ﷺ was at al-Jiʿrānah distributing meat, and I was then a boy carrying the limb of a camel. He said: Then a Bedouin woman approached. When she drew near to the Prophet ﷺ, he spread his cloak for her and she sat on it. I asked: Who is this? They said: His mother who suckled him."],[6290,"When he put on a shirt, he began with his right side.”"],[6291,"Zayd b. Ḥārithah came complaining to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ about Zaynab, so the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, “Keep your wife.” Then it was revealed: ‘And you hid in your soul what Allah was to bring to light.’"],[6292,"'He frowned and turned away' was revealed about Ibn Umm Maktum, the blind man. She said: He came to the Prophet ﷺ and began saying: O Prophet of Allah, guide me. She said: With the Prophet ﷺ was a man from the great ones of the polytheists, and the Prophet ﷺ began to turn away from him and face the other, and the Prophet ﷺ said: 'O so-and-so, do you see any harm in what I say?' He said: No. Then 'He frowned and turned away' was revealed."],[6293,"That he heard the Prophet ﷺ say in the Fajr prayer when he raised his head from bowing: “Our Lord, and to You is all praise,” in the last rakʿah, then he said: “O Allah, curse so-and-so and so-and-so,” supplicating against people among the hypocrites. Then Allah revealed: {Not for you is the decision whether He turns to them or punishes them, for they are wrongdoers}."],[6294,"The Prophet ﷺ used to stay with Zaynab bt. Jahsh and drink honey at her place. She said: Hafsah and I agreed that if the Prophet ﷺ entered upon either of us, she should say, 'I detect on you the smell of maghafir.' So he entered upon one of them and she said that to him. He said, 'Rather, I drank honey at Zaynab bt. Jahsh's place, and I will never do so again.' Then the verse was revealed: {O Prophet, why do you prohibit...}."],[6295,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ went out one day, and we went out with him until we reached the graveyard. He ordered us, and we sat down. Then he stepped over the graves until he came to one of them and sat by it. He spoke privately to it for a long time, then he returned weeping. We wept because of his weeping. Then he turned to us, and 'Umar ؓ met him and said, \"What made you weep, O Messenger of Allah? You have made us weep and alarmed us.\" He took 'Umar's hand, then turned to us and said, \"Did my weeping alarm you?\" We said, \"Yes.\" He said, \"The grave you saw me speaking privately to is the grave of Aminah bt. Wahb. I asked my Lord for permission to seek forgiveness for her, but He did not permit me. So it was sent down to me: {It is not for the Prophet and those who believe to seek forgiveness for the polytheists} [9:113]. Then I was seized by the tenderness that a child feels for his parent, and that is what made me weep. Indeed, I had forbidden you from visiting graves, so visit them, for they make one renounce this world and desire the Hereafter.\""],[6296,"When death approached Abu Talib, the Messenger of Allah ﷺ came and found Abu Jahl and 'Abd Allah b. Abi Umayyah b. al-Mughirah with him. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, \"O uncle, say: There is no god but Allah, and I will testify for you with it before Allah.\" Abu Jahl and 'Abd Allah b. Abi Umayyah said, \"O Abu Talib, will you turn away from the religion of 'Abd al-Muttalib?\" The Prophet ﷺ kept presenting it to him and repeating those words to him until Abu Talib said, as the last thing he spoke to them, that he was on the religion of 'Abd al-Muttalib, and he refused to say: There is no god but Allah. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, \"I will surely seek forgiveness for you as long as I am not forbidden from doing so.\" So Allah sent down: {It is not for the Prophet and those who believe to seek forgiveness for the polytheists, even if they were near relatives, after it has become clear to them that they are companions of the Blaze} [9:113]. And concerning Abu Talib was sent down: {Indeed, you do not guide whom you love, but Allah guides whom He wills, and He is most knowing of the guided} [28:56]."],[6297,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ came to the grave of 'Abd Allah b. Ubayy b. Salul after he had been placed in his burial pit. He ordered that he be brought out, then placed him on his knee, blew some of his saliva onto him, and clothed him with his shirt."],[6298,"When 'Abd Allah b. Ubayy died, his son came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and said, \"Give me your shirt so that I may shroud him in it, and pray over him, and seek forgiveness for him.\" So he gave him his shirt and said, \"When you are finished, inform me so that I may pray over him.\" When he had finished, he informed him. When he wanted to pray over him, 'Umar pulled him and said, \"Has Allah not forbidden you to pray over the hypocrites?\" The Prophet ﷺ said, \"I am between two choices. Allah said: 'Ask forgiveness for them or do not ask forgiveness for them' [Quran 9:80].\" Then the verse was revealed: \"And do not pray over any of them who has died, ever, nor stand at his grave\" [Quran 9:84]. So he abandoned praying over him."],[6299,"\"I heard Umar ibn Al-Khattab, may Allah be pleased with him, saying: When Abdullah ibn Ubay died, his son Abdullah ibn Abdullah ibn Ubay ibn Salul came to the Messenger of Allahﷺ and said: O Messenger of Allah, this is Abdullah ibn Ubay, we have buried him, so please pray for him. The Messenger of Allahﷺ stood up to pray for him. When he stood up to pray, I stood in front of the chest of the Messenger of Allahﷺ and I said: O Prophet of Allah, are you praying for the enemy of Allah who said such and such on such and such day, and the one who said such and such on such and such day, I number his evil days. The Messenger of Allahﷺ smiled and said: Leave me, O Umar. When I persisted, he said: Leave me, O Umar. I was given a choice, and I chose, for Allah says, 'Ask forgiveness for them, or do not ask forgiveness for them.' If I knew that by adding more than seventy, he would be forgiven, I would have added more.\" Umar said: I was amazed at my boldness to the Messenger of Allahﷺ but Allah and His Messenger know best. When he said that to me, I turned away from him and prayed for him, then I walked with him and stood by his grave until he was buried. Then he turned away, and by Allah, he did not stay except for a short while until Allah revealed, \"And never pray [the funeral prayer, O Muhammad], over any of them who has died - ever - or stand at his grave.\" So the Messenger of Allahﷺ did not pray for a hypocrite after that, nor did he stand at his grave.\""],[6300,"That the Prophet ﷺ freed Safiyyah and made her emancipation her dower."],[6301,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ freed Safiyyah and made her emancipation her dowry, and held a wedding feast for her with hays."],[6302,"The Prophet ﷺ gave a wedding feast for Safiyya with sawiq and dates."],[6303,"said: \"It reached Safiyyah that Hafsah said: 'The daughter of a Jew' so she wept. Then the Prophet ﷺ entered upon her while she was crying, so he said: 'What makes you cry?' She said: 'Hafsah said to me that I am the daughter of a Jew.' So the Prophet ﷺ said: 'And you are the daughter of a Prophet, and your uncle is a Prophet, and you are married to a Prophet, so what is she boasting to you about?' Then he said: 'Fear Allah, O Hafsah.'\" (Using translation from Tirmidhī 3894)"],[6304,"The Prophet ﷺ stayed between Khaybar and Madinah for three nights, consummating his marriage with Safiyya bint Huyayy. I invited the believers to his wedding feast, and there was no bread or meat in it. He ordered leather mats to be spread, and dates, dried curd, and ghee were placed on them, and that was his wedding feast. The Muslims said, 'Is she one of the Mothers of the Believers, or is she among those whom his right hand possesses?' They said, 'If he veils her, she is one of the Mothers of the Believers, and if he does not veil her, she is among those whom his right hand possesses.' When he departed, he made a cushion for her behind him and extended the veil between her and the people."],[6305,"Umar b. Abd al-Aziz was sitting on the pulpit and delayed the prayer a little. Urwa b. al-Zubayr said, \"Do you not know that Jibril informed Muhammad ﷺ of the time of prayer?\" Umar said to him, \"I know what you are saying, O Urwa.\" Urwa said, \"I heard Bashir b. Abi Mas'ud say: I heard Abu Mas'ud al-Ansari say: I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: 'Jibril descended and informed me of the time of prayer, and I prayed with him, then I prayed with him, then I prayed with him, then I prayed with him, then I prayed with him.' He counted with his fingers five prayers. 'And I saw the Messenger of Allah ﷺ praying Zuhr when the sun declines, and sometimes he delayed it when the heat was intense. And I saw him praying Asr while the sun was high and white before yellowness entered it, so that a man would leave from the prayer and reach Dhu al-Hulayfa before sunset. And he prayed Maghrib when the sun fell, and he prayed Isha when the horizon darkened, and sometimes he delayed it until people gathered. And he prayed Subh in darkness, then he prayed another time and made it bright. After that, his prayer was in darkness until he died ﷺ, and he did not return to making it bright.'\""],[6306,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ prayed Subh with us in darkness, then he prayed the morning prayer the next day and made it bright. Then he said, \"Where is the one who asked about the time of the morning prayer? It is between my prayer yesterday and today.\""],[6307,"\"The Prophet of Allah ﷺ and Zayd b. Thabit were brought a pre-dawn meal. When the Prophet of Allah ﷺ finished his pre-dawn meal, he stood up for the Subh prayer.\" We said to Anas b. Malik, \"How much was between his finishing his pre-dawn meal and when he entered his prayer?\" He said, \"The amount of time it takes a man to recite fifty verses.\""],[6308,"\"There were believing women who used to pray with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ wrapped in their cloaks in the Fajr prayer, then they would return to their homes, not being recognized from the darkness.\""],[6309,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to perform the Fajr prayer, and then the believing women would leave wrapped in their cloaks, unrecognizable due to the darkness."],[6310,"\"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to pray Subh, and the women would leave wrapped in their cloaks, not being recognized from the darkness.\""],[6311,"Abdullah b. al-Zubayr prayed the morning prayer with us in darkness. I turned to Ibn Umar and said, \"What is this prayer?\" He said, \"This is our prayer with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and Abu Bakr and Umar, ؓ . When Umar was killed, Uthman, ؓ , made it bright.\""],[6312,"\"Make the Subh prayer bright, for it is greater for the reward,\" or he said, \"greater for your rewards.\""],[6313,"'The time of Ẓuhr is when the sun declines and a man's shadow is equal to his height, as long as ʿAṣr has not arrived. The time of ʿAṣr is as long as the sun has not turned yellow. The time of ʿIshāʾ is up to half the night, or the middle of the night. The time of Fajr is as long as the sun has not risen.'"],[6314,"\"The Angel of Death came to Moses to take his soul. He said to him: 'Answer your Lord.' Moses struck the eye of the Angel of Death and gouged it out. The Angel of Death returned to his Lord and said: 'O Lord, You sent me to a servant who does not want to die, and he has gouged out my eye.' Allah restored his eye and said to him: 'Go back to him and say: Do you want life? If you want life, place your hand on the back of a bull; for every hair covered by your hand, you will live a year.' He said: 'Then what?' He said: 'Death.' He said: 'Now, from near.' Then he said: 'Lord, bring me near the Holy Land within a stone's throw.'\" The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"If I were with him, I would show you his grave, beside the road, near the red sand hill.\""],[6315,"I asked, \"What is this prayer of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ ?\" He replied, \"This is the prayer of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ that we used to pray with him.\""],[6316,"He used to pray Asr while the sun was white and alive, then a person would go to the highlands and reach them while the sun was still high."],[6317,"He used to pray Asr while the sun was high and alive, then a person would go to the highlands and reach the highlands while the sun was still high."],[6318,"He used to pray Asr while the sun was high and alive, then a person would go to the highlands and reach the highlands while the sun was still high."],[6319,"It was narrated from 'Aishah that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ prayed 'Asr when the sun was in her room and the shadow had not appeared on her wall. (Using translation from Nasāʾī 505)"],[6320,"He entered upon Anas b. Malik in his house in Basra when he had finished Zuhr. His house was beside the mosque. When we entered upon him, he said, 'Have you prayed Asr?' We said, 'We have just finished Zuhr now.' He said, 'Pray Asr.' So we stood and prayed Asr. When we finished, he said: 'I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: \"That is the prayer of the hypocrites: he sits watching the sun until when it is between the two horns of Satan, he stands and pecks it four (units), not remembering Allah in them except a little.\"\""],[6321,"I entered upon Anas b. Malik with a companion of mine after Zuhr. He said, 'Have you two prayed Asr?' We said, 'No.' He said, 'Pray with us in the room.' We finished, and he lengthened his prayer and then turned to us. The first thing he said to us was: 'The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"That is the prayer of the hypocrites: one of them sits until when it is upon the horn of Satan or between the two horns of Satan, then he stands and pecks four (units), not remembering Allah in them except a little.\"\""],[6322,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to pray Maghrib when the sun had set and disappeared behind the veil."],[6323,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to delay the later Isha prayer."],[6324,"We asked Jabir b. Abd Allah about the prayer of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. He said, 'He used to pray Zuhr when the sun declined, Asr while the sun was alive, Maghrib when the sun set, and Isha sometimes he would hasten it and sometimes delay it. When the people had gathered, he would hasten it, and when they had not come, he would delay it. And they used to pray Subh in the darkness before dawn.'"],[6325,"“Were it not that I would make things difficult for my Ummah, I would have commanded them to use the siwak with every wudu and would have delayed the Isha prayer until one-third of the night or half the night.”"],[6326,"We used to pray with the Prophet ﷺ on Fridays, and there was no shade available for the walls."],[6327,"We used to perform Jumu'ah with the Prophet ﷺ when the sun had passed its zenith, then we would return and trace the shadows."],[6328,"We used to pray Jumu'ah with the Prophet ﷺ, then we would return and let our camels rest. I asked: What time was that? He said: When the sun had passed its zenith."],[6329,"Command your husbands to cleanse themselves with water, for I am too shy to tell them. Indeed, the Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to do that."],[6330,"\"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to love what provided shelter or the fronds of palm trees.\""],[6331,"A Bedouin urinated in the mosque, and some people rushed to stop him, but the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, \"Leave him, and pour a bucket or a pail of water over his urine, for you have been sent to make things easy, not to make them difficult.\""],[6332,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ was sitting in the mosque when a Bedouin entered and squatted to urinate. The Companions of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, \"Stop, stop!\" but the Prophet ﷺ said, \"Do not interrupt him.\" Then he called him and said, \"These mosques are not suitable for any filth or relieving oneself. They are only for reciting the Qur'an or remembering Allah.\" Then he called for a bucket of water and poured it over the urine."],[6333,"A Bedouin entered the mosque while the Messenger of Allah ﷺ was sitting, and said, “O Allah, forgive me and Muhammad, but do not forgive anyone else with us.” The Messenger of Allah ﷺ laughed and said, “You have restricted something vast.” Then the Bedouin went away until he was at a corner of the mosque, and he spread his legs to urinate. The Bedouin said, after he had learned about Islam: “The Messenger of Allah ﷺ came to me and did not scold me or insult me. He said, 'This mosque was built for the remembrance of Allah and for prayer, and it should not be urinated in.' Then he called for a bucket of water and poured it over the urine.”"],[6334,"I came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ with a son of mine who had not yet eaten solid food. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ took him and seated him in his lap, and he urinated on the garment of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ took water and sprinkled it, and he did not wash it."],[6335,"The Prophet of Allah ﷺ said regarding the urine of a baby, \"The urine of a boy should be sprinkled, and the urine of a girl should be washed off.\""],[6336,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ threw the pebble at the Jamrah on the Day of Sacrifice, then he commanded that the sacrificial camels be slaughtered, and they were slaughtered. The barber was sitting with him. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ arranged his hair with his hand on that day, then he grasped the side of his right part on his hair. Then he said to the barber: 'Shave.' So he shaved. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ divided his hair that day among those present from the people: the hair and the two hairs. Then he grasped with his hand the side of his left part on his hair. Then he said to the barber: 'Shave.' So he shaved. He called Abu Talhah al-Ansari and gave it to him."],[6337,"The Prophet ﷺ came to visit me while I was ill and unconscious. He performed ablution and poured some of his ablution water over me, and I regained consciousness. I said: \"O Messenger of Allah, to whom does the inheritance go? For only distant relatives inherit from me.\" Then the verse of obligatory shares was revealed."],[6338,"A man asked 'Umar: \"I became junub and found no water.\" He said: \"Do not pray.\" 'Ammar said: \"Do you not remember when you and I were on an expedition during the time of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ?\" He mentioned that to him, and he ﷺ said: \"It would have been enough for you,\" and he struck the ground with his hand once, blew into his palms, and wiped his face and his palms."],[6339,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ passed by a boy skinning a sheep, and said to him: 'Move aside so I can show you, for I think you do not skin well.' He said: 'The Messenger of Allah ﷺ inserted his hand between the skin and the meat and pushed it until it disappeared up to the armpit, then said ﷺ: 'Like this, O boy, skin.' Then he went off and prayed, and he did not perform ablution and did not touch water."],[6340,"The Prophet ﷺ drank milk, then called for water and rinsed his mouth, and said: 'It has fat.'"],[6341,"When he entered the privy, he would remove his ring."],[6342,"The inscription on the Prophet's ﷺ ring was three lines: Muhammad (one line), Messenger (one line), Allah (one line)."],[6343,"I never saw the Prophet ﷺ fasting during the ten days, and he never came out from the privy except that he touched water."],[6344,"When the Messenger of Allah ﷺ came out from his need, I and a boy from the Ansar would bring a vessel of water, and he would cleanse himself with it."],[6345,"She was asked about a man who has intercourse but does not ejaculate. She said: “I did that with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and we both bathed because of it.”"],[6346,"I asked and was eager to find anyone among the people to tell me that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ prayed the Duha prayer, but I did not find anyone to tell me about that except Umm Hani' bt. Abi Talib. She told me, \"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ came after the sun had risen on the day of the conquest and ordered a garment to be used as a screen for him. He performed ghusl, then stood and prayed eight rak'ahs. I do not know whether his standing in them was longer, or his bowing, or his prostration—all of that was similar.\" She said, \"I did not see him pray it before or after.\""],[6347,"I went to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ in the year of the conquest, and I found him performing ghusl while Fāṭimah, his daughter, was screening him with a cloth. She said: I greeted him, and he said: «Who is this?» I said: Umm Hāniʾ bt. Abī Ṭālib. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: «Welcome, Umm Hāniʾ.» When he finished his ghusl, he stood and prayed eight rakʿahs wrapped in a single cloth, then he left. I said to him: O Messenger of Allah, the son of my mother ʿAlī b. Abī Ṭālib, ؓ , claims that he will kill a man whom I have granted protection, Fulān b. Hubayrah. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: «We have granted protection to the one you have granted protection, O Umm Hāniʾ.» And that was at mid-morning."],[6348,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ stayed in upper Makkah, and I went to him. Abū Dharr came to him with a bowl containing water. She said: I could see in it traces of dough. She said: Abū Dharr screened him, and he performed ghusl. Then the Prophet ﷺ screened Abū Dharr, and he performed ghusl. Then the Prophet ﷺ prayed eight rakʿahs, and that was at mid-morning."],[6349,"He used to bathe from a vessel, and it was the faraq, from janabah."],[6350,"\"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to perform wudu' with a makkuk and bathe with five makakik.\""],[6351,"“When the Messenger of Allah ﷺ wanted to sleep while in a state of major impurity, he would not sleep until he performed ablution; and when he wanted to eat, he would wash his hands and eat.”"],[6352,"I spent the night with my maternal aunt Maymunah, and I saw the Messenger of Allah ﷺ get up, urinate, then wash his face, then sleep."],[6353,"The Prophet ﷺ one day said the takbir in the dawn prayer, then gestured to them, then left and performed a full bath. He came back with his head dripping and led them in prayer."],[6354,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ came out after the prayer had been commenced and the rows had been straightened, until when he stood at his place of prayer and we waited for him to say the takbīr, he turned away and said, “Stay where you are.” He entered his house, and we remained as we were until he came out to us with his head dripping, having performed ghusl."],[6355,"\"We traveled with the Messenger of God ﷺ until, when we were in the evening and drew near the watering places of the Arabs, the Messenger of God ﷺ said: 'Who is a man who will go ahead of us, reach the pool, drink, and give us water?' Jābir said: So I stood up and said: 'Here is a man, O Messenger of God.' The Messenger of God ﷺ said: 'Which man is with Jābir?' Jabbār b. Ṣakhr stood up. We went to the well, drew a bucket or two into the pool, then plastered it, then drew water into it until we filled it. The first to appear to us was the Messenger of God ﷺ. He said: 'Do you two permit?' We said: 'Yes, O Messenger of God.' He let his she-camel drink, and she drank; then he held back the rope for her, and she urinated; then he turned her aside and made her kneel. Then the Messenger of God ﷺ came to the pool and performed ablution from it. Then I stood up and performed ablution from the place where the Messenger of God ﷺ had performed ablution. Jabbār b. Ṣakhr went to relieve himself. The Messenger of God ﷺ stood up to pray. I had on a burdah, and I tried to bring its two ends together, but it was not long enough for me. It had fringes, so I turned it down, then brought its two ends together, and came and stood to the left of the Messenger of God ﷺ. He took my hand, turned me around, and made me stand on his right. Then Jabbār b. Ṣakhr came, performed ablution, and came and stood to the left of the Messenger of God ﷺ. He took both of us by the hand, pushed us, and made us stand behind him. The Messenger of God ﷺ kept glancing at me while I was unaware; then I noticed. He said: 'Like this'—and he gestured with his hand—'tie it.' When the Messenger of God ﷺ finished, he said: 'O Jābir.' I said: 'At your service, O Messenger of God.' He said: 'When your garment is wide, bring its two ends together; and if it is narrow, tie it around your waist.'\""],[6356,"I have not prayed with anyone whose prayer was shorter or more complete than that of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ."],[6357,"Umar said to Sa'd, 'The people of Kufa have complained about you in everything, even in prayer.' Sa'd said, 'I lengthen the first two units and am brisk in the last two, and I do not fall short of the prayer of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ.' Umar said, 'That is what was thought of you.'"],[6358,"From the Prophet ﷺ: they would hear from him in Zuhr the soft tone of 'Sabbih isma Rabbika al-A'la' and 'Hal ataka hadithu al-Ghashiyah.'"],[6359,"We said to Khabbab, \"By what thing did you recognize the recitation of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ in Zuhr and 'Asr?\" He said, \"By the movement of his beard.\""],[6360,"\"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to recite Umm al-Qur'an and two surahs with it in the first two rak'ahs of the Zuhr and 'Asr prayers, and sometimes he would let us hear a verse, and he would lengthen the first rak'ah of the Zuhr prayer.\""],[6361,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ would recite the Quran and come upon a prostration verse, then prostrate, and we would prostrate with him due to his prostration."],[6362,"He recited to them “When the sky is split open” and prostrated in it. When he finished, he told them that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ prostrated in it."],[6363,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ prostrated in An-Najm, and the Muslims, the polytheists, the jinn, and humans prostrated with him."],[6364,"The Prophet ﷺ recited Surah An-Najm and prostrated. None of the people remained except that he prostrated, except one man who took a handful of pebbles and placed them on his forehead, and said, “This suffices me.”"],[6365,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ recited Sad while he was on the pulpit. When he reached the prostration, he descended and prostrated, and the people prostrated with him. On another day, he recited it, and when he reached the prostration, the people prepared themselves for prostration. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, “It is only the repentance of a prophet, but I saw you preparing yourselves for prostration.” So he descended and prostrated, and they prostrated."],[6366,"I said to Ibn Abbas, “The prostration of Sad—from where did you take it?” He said, “Then he recited to me, ‘And of his descendants, David and Solomon and Job’ until he reached His saying, ‘Those are they whom Allah has guided, so follow their guidance.’”"],[6367,"We prostrated with the Prophet ﷺ in “When the sky is split open” and “Recite in the name of your Lord who created.”"],[6368,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ prayed Zuhr in Madinah as four [rakʿahs] and prayed ʿAṣr at Dhū al-Ḥulayfah as two [rakʿahs]."],[6369,"\"I missed the prayer in congregation when I was in Al-Batha; how do you think I should pray?\" He said: \"Two rak'ahs, the sunnah of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ.\" (Using translation from Nasāʾī 1444)"],[6370,"I went out with the Prophet ﷺ from Madinah to Makkah, and he continued to shorten until he returned, and he stayed there ten [days]."],[6371,"We were with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ on a military expedition. He used to pray voluntary prayers on his riding camel, facing toward the east. When he intended to pray an obligatory prayer, he would dismount and face the qiblah."],[6372,"I saw the Prophet ﷺ praying voluntary prayers while on his mount, in every direction, but he would lower the two prostrations lower than the bowing, gesturing in a slight motion."],[6373,"\"I saw the Prophet ﷺ praying the voluntary prayers on his mount, lowering his head during the two prostrations of the two units of prayer.\""],[6374,"We traveled with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and some of the people said, “Would you stop for us to rest, O Messenger of Allah?” He said, “I fear that you will sleep through the prayer.” Bilal said, “I will wake you.” He leaned on his mount, and the Messenger of Allah ﷺ woke up when the sun’s edge had risen. He said, “O Bilal, where is what you said?” Bilal said, “A sleep was cast upon me the like of which I have never slept.” He said, “Stand and call the people to prayer.” When the sun rose and became bright, the Messenger of Allah ﷺ stood and led them in prayer."],[6375,"We traveled one night with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and we said, 'O Messenger of Allah, if only we could touch the ground and sleep, and let our mounts graze.' He said, 'Then who will guard us?' I said, 'I will.' But sleep overcame me, and nothing woke me until the sun had risen. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ did not wake except due to our talking. He then ordered Bilal, who gave the adhan, then the iqamah, and he led us in prayer."],[6376,"When the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and his companions slept past the prayer, the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"Pray it the next day at its time.\""],[6377,"We accompanied the Messenger of Allah ﷺ in a battle. When it was late at night, he got married. As soon as he woke up, he woke us up before the heat of the sun. The man stood up astonished and terrified. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, \"Mount (your horses).\" He mounted his horse and we mounted ours, and we set off until the sun rose. Then he stopped and ordered Bilal to call the Adhan. The people finished their needs, performed ablution, and prayed two Rak'ahs. Then he led us in prayer. We said, \"O Messenger of Allah, should we make up these prayers at their prescribed time tomorrow?\" He said, \"Does your Lord forbid you from praying at the time of their occurrence and accept it from you?\""],[6378,"We camped with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and did not wake up until the sun had risen. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"Let each person take hold of the head of his mount, for this is a place where Satan came to us.\" So we did that. Then he called for water, performed ablution, then prayed two prostrations, then the prayer was called."],[6379,"The Prophet ﷺ slept past the two rak'ahs of dawn and prayed them after the sun had risen."],[6380,"The Prophet ﷺ used to pray in sheepfolds."],[6381,"When dawn broke, the Messenger of Allah ﷺ would not pray except the two rak'ahs of Fajr."],[6382,"\"That the Prophet of Allah ﷺ was not more persistent in any of the supererogatory prayers than he was in the two rak'ahs before Fajr.\""],[6383,"He used to lighten the two rak'ahs of Fajr."],[6384,"\"The Prophet ﷺ would not pray the two rak'ahs after Maghrib nor the two rak'ahs after Jumu'ah except in his house.\""],[6385,"I came and sat down, and Muhammad b. Muslim b. Khabbab said: Anas b. Malik came and sat in this place of yours and said: Do you know what this piece of wood is? We said: No. He said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ, when he stood for prayer, took it with his right hand, then turned and said: «Stand straight and straighten your rows.» Then he took it with his left hand and said: «Stand straight and straighten your rows.» When the mosque was demolished, it was lost. Then Umar, ؓ , searched for it and found that the Banu 'Amr b. 'Awf had taken it and placed it in their mosque, so he seized it and returned it."],[6386,"«The Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to straighten the rows as if he were straightening arrow shafts with them.»"],[6387,"\"I spent the night at my maternal aunt Maymūnah's. The Prophet ﷺ got up to pray, so I got up to pray and stood to his left. He took hold of my head and made me stand on his right.\""],[6388,"I saw the Messenger of Allah ﷺ praying in a single garment, wrapping himself with it."],[6389,"\"I attended the Messenger of God ﷺ on the day of the conquest [of Makkah], and he prayed inside the Kaʿbah. He took off his sandals and placed them to his left, then began reciting Sūrat al-Muʾminūn. When he reached the mention of ʿĪsā or Mūsā, a cough seized him, so he bowed.\""],[6390,"Between the Prophet’s ﷺ prayer place and the wall there was room for a sheep to pass."],[6391,"Between the Prophet’s ﷺ prayer place and the wall there was room for a sheep to pass."],[6392,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ stood up to pray wearing a patterned cloak with markings; it is as if I can see its marking. When he finished his prayer, he said, \"Take this cloak to Abu Jahm b. Hudhayfah and bring me his plain garment, for it distracted me in my prayer.\""],[6393,"She said, \"Abu Jahl bin Huthaifah presented the Prophet ﷺ with a Syrian garment. She had a flag in it, so he prayed with it. When he finished, he said, 'Return this garment to Abu Jahl, for I looked at its flag during the prayer and it nearly distracted me'.\""],[6394,"\"The Messenger of Allah's ﷺ bowing, his raising his head after bowing, his prostration, and his sitting between the two prostrations were all close to equal in length.\""],[6395,"\"I strive to lead you in prayer as I saw the Messenger of Allah ﷺ lead us in prayer.\" Thabit said: \"I saw Anas b. Malik do something that I do not see you do: when he raised his head from bowing, he stood so long that one would say, 'He has forgotten,' and when he raised his head from the first prostration, he sat so long that one would say, 'He has forgotten.'\""],[6396,"\"I never prayed behind anyone whose prayer was lighter or more complete than the prayer of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. If the Messenger of Allah ﷺ heard the crying of a child behind him, he would shorten the prayer for fear that the child's mother would be distressed.\""],[6397,"I passed by the Messenger of Allah ﷺ while he was praying and greeted him. He returned my greeting with a gesture, and I believe he said, 'with his finger.'"],[6398,"Some men came to Sahl b. Sa'd, having disputed about the pulpit: of what wood was it? They asked him about that, and he said, 'By Allah, I know what it is made of, and I saw the first day the Messenger of Allah ﷺ sat on it. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ sent to a woman—Sahl named her—that she should order her carpenter servant to make me wooden planks to sit on when I speak to the people. She ordered him, and he made them from tamarisk of al-Ghaba. Then he brought them, and she sent to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and he ordered them to be placed here. Then I saw the Messenger of Allah ﷺ pray on it, say takbir while on it, bow while on it, rise while on it, then move backward and prostrate, and he ascended the pulpit. When he finished, he faced the people and said, 'O people, I did this only so that you may follow me and learn my prayer.'"],[6399,"Hudhayfa led us in prayer on a raised bench and prostrated on it. Abu Mas'ud pulled him, and Hudhayfa followed him. When the prayer was finished, Abu Mas'ud said, 'Was this not forbidden?' Hudhayfa said to him, 'Did you not see that I followed you?'"],[6400,"\"I saw the Messenger of Allah ﷺ while my father was riding behind him on a camel, and I was a young boy. I saw the Messenger of Allah ﷺ addressing the people on his she-camel al-ʿAḍbāʾ at Minā.\""],[6401,"I used to pray with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and his prayer was moderate, and his sermon was moderate."],[6402,"I asked Jābir b. Samurah: How did the Prophet ﷺ deliver the sermon? He said: 'He ﷺ would deliver the sermon, then sit for a short while, then stand and deliver the sermon.'"],[6403,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ would deliver the sermon on the pulpit, then sit, then stand and deliver the sermon. He would sit between the two sermons reciting from the Book of Allah and reminding the people."],[6404,"\"I bear witness that Muhammad is the Messenger of Allah, peace be upon him. Or Ata' said, 'I bear witness that Ibn Abbas narrated that the Prophetﷺ went out on the day of Eid with his companions, performed prayer, then gave a sermon. He then came to the women and commanded them to give charity, and they began to throw it.'\""],[6405,"“I prayed behind the Prophet ﷺ over a woman who died in her postpartum bleeding. He stood in prayer at her middle.”"],[6406,"I prayed behind Ibn 'Abbas over a funeral. He recited the Opening of the Book aloud until he made us hear it. When he finished, I took his hand and asked him about that. He said, “It is a sunnah and a truth.”"],[6407,"The Prophet ﷺ prayed over the Negus."],[6408,"The Prophet ﷺ prayed over the Negus when news of his death reached him, and I was in the second row."],[6409,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ announced the death of the Negus to the people on the day he died. He went out with them to the prayer ground, arranged them in rows, and said four takbirs."],[6410,"When the Messenger of Allah ﷺ was resident, he would observe i'tikaf during the last ten days of Ramadan. When he traveled, he observed i'tikaf for twenty days the following year."],[6411,"He used to observe i'tikaf during the last ten days of Ramadan, then he traveled and did not observe i'tikaf. The following year, he observed i'tikaf for twenty days."],[6412,"He used to observe i'tikaf during the last ten days of Ramadan until Allah took his soul."],[6413,"«David used not to eat except from the work of his own hands.»"],[6414,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ intended to observe i'tikaf, and Aisha asked his permission to observe i'tikaf with him, so he permitted her. She pitched her tent, then Hafsa asked her to seek permission for her to observe i'tikaf with her. When Zaynab saw that, she pitched a tent with her, and she was a jealous woman. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ saw their tents and said, ﷺ: \"What is this? Do you intend righteousness by this?\" So he abandoned i'tikaf until he broke his fast from Ramadan, then he observed i'tikaf for twenty days in Shawwal."],[6415,"\"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to observe I'tikaf during the middle ten days of the month, and after the twentieth (day of the month), he would come out on the twenty-first and go back to his home, and those who were observing I'tikaf with him would go back like him. Then he stayed one month on the night when he used to go back home, and he addressed the people and enjoined upon them whatever Allah (SWT) willed. Then he said: 'I used to observe I'tikaf during these ten days, then I decided to spend the last ten days in I'tikaf. So whoever was observing I'tikaf with me, let him stay in his place of I'tikaf, for I was shown this night (Lailatul Qadr), then I was caused to forget it, so seek it during the last ten nights on the odd-numbered nights. And I saw myself prostrating in water and mud.'\" Abu Sa'eed said: \"It rained on the night of the twenty-first, and the roof of the Masjid leaked over the place where the Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to pray. I looked at him when he had finished praying subh and his face was wet with water and mud.\" (Using translation from Nasāʾī 1356)"],[6416,"When the Messenger of Allah ﷺ wanted to observe i'tikaf, he would pray Fajr and then enter it."],[6418,"When the last ten days of Ramadan entered, the Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to wake his family, tighten his waist-wrapper, and keep the night alive."],[6419,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to send sacrificial animals from Madinah, and I would twist the garlands for his sacrificial animals. Then he would not avoid anything that a person in iḥrām avoids."],[6420,"I used to twist the garlands for the sacrificial animals of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. He would send them and then send the sacrificial animals while he was staying with us in Madinah. Then he would not enter iḥrām and would not avoid anything that a person in iḥrām avoids."],[6421,"This plain of yours, about which you attribute falsehood to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ: the Messenger of Allah ﷺ did not enter ihram except from near the mosque."],[6422,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ entered in the year of the conquest from Kuda', the upper part of Makkah."],[6423,"A man from the people of Iraq said: Ask for me 'Urwah b. al-Zubayr about a man who enters ihram for Hajj, and when he has circumambulated the House, has he exited ihram or not? 'Urwah said, \"The Prophet ﷺ performed Hajj, and 'A'ishah informed me that the first thing he began with when he arrived in Makkah was that he performed ablution and circumambulated the House.\""],[6424,"\"When the Messenger of Allah ﷺ arrived in Makkah, he circumambulated the House seven times, then prayed two rak'ahs behind the Station, then went out to al-Safa from the gate from which he exited, and went between al-Safa and al-Marwah.\""],[6425,"“Whoever combines Hajj and Umrah performs for them one circumambulation (Tawaf), then he does not come out of ihram until he comes out of it from his Hajj.”"],[6426,"“The Prophet ﷺ did not perform between Safa and Marwah except one circuit (Sa'i) for his Hajj and his Umrah.”"],[6427,"I know that you are only a stone. Were it not that I saw the Messenger of Allah ﷺ kiss you, I would not have kissed you. (Using translation from Aḥmad 226)"],[6428,"That [ʿUmar] came to the [Black] Stone and kissed it, and said: \"I know that you are a stone, you do not benefit nor harm, and were it not that I saw the Messenger of Allah ﷺ kissing you, I would not have kissed you.\""],[6429,"I prayed with the Prophet ﷺ in Makkah the prayers as two [rakʿahs] during the Farewell Pilgrimage when the people were most numerous and secure."],[6430,"I prayed with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, or he led us in prayer at Minā, while we were at our fullest number, as two [rakʿahs]."],[6431,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ performed tawaf on his she-camel al-Qaswa' on the Day of the Conquest, and touched the Corner with his staff, and he did not find a place for her to kneel in the mosque until she was taken out to the bottom of the valley and made to kneel. Then he praised Allah and extolled Him, then said: \"Now then, O people, Allah has removed from you the arrogance of the Jahiliyyah. O people, people are but two kinds: a righteous, God-fearing man, honored by his Lord, and a wicked, wretched man, insignificant to his Lord.\" Then he recited: \"O people, We created you from a male and a female and made you peoples and tribes that you may know one another\" until he read the verse, then said: \"I say this and I ask Allah's forgiveness for me and for you.\""],[6432,"I asked Anas b. Malik: “Inform me about something you observed from the Messenger of Allah ﷺ: Where did he pray Zuhr on the Day of Tarwiyah?” He said: “At Mina.” He said: “I said: ‘Where did he pray Zuhr on the Day of Nafr?’” He said: “At al-Abtah.”"],[6433,"that he was riding behind the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and he stood saying tahlil, takbir, and supplicating. When he departed, the people pressed forward, and he called out: \"Keep calm!\" When he reached the mountain pass, he urinated and performed wudu, then mounted. When he arrived at Muzdalifah, he combined Maghrib and Isha. When he prayed Fajr, he stood. When he departed, the people pressed forward, and he said as they moved: \"Keep calm!\" He was holding back his mount until he entered the interior of Mina, then he said: \"Use small pebbles like those thrown at the Jamrah.\" He was still reciting the talbiyah until he threw the pebbles at the Jamrah."],[6434,"Some people disputed in her presence on the day of Arafah regarding the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. Some of them said he was fasting, and some said he was not fasting. So Umm al-Fadl sent him a cup of milk while he was standing on his camel, and he drank."],[6435,"The people were uncertain about the affair of the Prophet ﷺ on the day of Arafah, so Maymunah sent him some milk while he was standing at the standing place, and he drank while the people were looking."],[6436,"\"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ threw the Jamrah on the Day of Sacrifice in the forenoon, then threw the rest of them at the time of the sun's decline.\""],[6437,"\"The Prophet ﷺ used to pray two rak'ahs in Mina, and Abu Bakr, 'Umar, and 'Uthman (did likewise). Then 'Uthman later prayed four. Ibn 'Umar used to pray with the imam according to his prayer, but when he prayed alone he prayed four.\""],[6438,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ prayed the traveler’s prayer at Minā as two [rakʿahs], and Abū Bakr and ʿUmar and ʿUthmān as two [rakʿahs] at the beginning of his caliphate, then he completed it as four [rakʿahs]."],[6439,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to sacrifice two salt-and-white rams with horns. He would pronounce the name of Allah and say Allahu Akbar. I saw him slaughter them with his own hand, placing his foot on their sides."],[6440,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ sacrificed a horned ram that was dark around the eyes, mouth, and feet, eating in blackness, looking in blackness, and drinking in blackness."],[6441,"I saw Ibn ʿUmar come upon a man who had made his camel kneel down in order to slaughter it. He said, 'Make it stand up with its leg tied; that is the Sunnah of Muhammad ﷺ.'"],[6442,"A horned ram was brought to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, which treads in blackness, looks in blackness, and kneels in blackness; he brought it to sacrifice it. He ﷺ said: \"O Aishah, bring the knife.\" Then he said: \"Sharpen it with a stone.\" So I did, and he took it and took the ram and laid it down, then slaughtered it and said: \"In the name of Allah. O Allah, in Your name, from Muhammad and the family of Muhammad and the community of Muhammad.\" Then he sacrificed it ﷺ."],[6443,"\"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ departed on the Day of Sacrifice, then returned and prayed the noon prayer at Minā.\""],[6444,"The Prophet ﷺ, Abu Bakr, 'Umar, and 'Uthman used to halt at al-Muhassab."],[6445,"Asma' and 'A'ishah did not stop at al-Muhassab. 'A'ishah said: \"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ only halted there because it was easier for his departure.\""],[6446,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ spent the night at Dhu Tuwa until he prayed the morning prayer, then he entered Makkah. Ibn Umar used to do that. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ entered Makkah from Kada' al-Thaniyyah al-Ulya, which is at al-Batha, and exited from the lower mountain pass."],[6447,"\"When the Messenger of Allah ﷺ left Makkah, he left by the road of al-Shajarah, and when he returned, he returned by the road of al-Mu'arras.\""],[6448,"He, when he arrived from a journey and looked at the walls of Madinah, made his riding camel go quickly, and if he was on a mount, he spurred it on, out of love for it."],[6449,"ʿAbd Allāh b. ʿUmar wanted to perform Hajj in the year al-Ḥajjāj besieged Ibn al-Zubayr. It was said to him: The people will be fighting, and we fear they may prevent you. He said: {Indeed, in the Messenger of Allah you have an excellent example.} Then I will do as the Messenger of Allah ﷺ did: \"I call you to witness that I have obligated ʿUmrah.\" Then he set out until he was at the outskirts of al-Baydāʾ, where he said: The matter of Hajj and ʿUmrah is but one matter. I call you to witness that I have obligated Hajj along with my ʿUmrah. And he sent forward a sacrificial animal that he had bought at Qudayd. He went on pronouncing the talbiyah for both together until he reached Makkah. He circumambulated the House and ran between al-Ṣafā and al-Marwah, and did not do more than that. He did not slaughter, did not shave, did not trim, and did not exit from any state of iḥrām he had entered until the Day of Sacrifice, when he slaughtered and shaved. He then considered that he had fulfilled the ṭawāf of both Hajj and ʿUmrah with the first ṭawāf. And he said: This is what the Messenger of Allah ﷺ did."],[6450,"I then tore it and prepared two cushions out of that. A person who was then in that company and whose name was Rabi'a b. 'Ata, the freed slave of Banu Zuhra, asked: Did you hear Abu Mabammad making a mention of A'isha having stated that Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to recline upon them? lbn al-Qasim said: No, but I heard Qasim b. Muhammad saying so. (Using translation from Muslim 2107m)"],[6451,"«Angels do not enter a house in which there is a dog or a statue.» I said, 'I will go to 'A'ishah and ask her about that.' So I came to her and said, 'O mother, this one narrated to me that the Prophet ﷺ said, \"Angels do not enter a house in which there is a statue or a dog.\" Did you hear the Messenger of Allah ﷺ mention that?' She said, 'No, but I will tell you what I saw him do. He went out on one of his military expeditions, and I was awaiting his return. I took a patterned cloth and hung it over a shelf. When he came, I met him at the door and said, \"Peace be upon you and the mercy of Allah. Praise be to Allah who honored you, supported you, and ennobled you.\" He looked at the house and saw the cloth, but he did not respond to me at all. I saw displeasure in his face. He pulled it until he tore it or cut it, then said, \"Allah has not commanded us, in what He has provided us, to clothe clay and stones.\"' She said, 'So I cut it into two pieces and stuffed them with palm fiber, and he did not criticize me for that.'"],[6452,"Whenever he went out on a military expedition, his last contact was with Fatimah, and whenever he returned from an expedition, his first contact was with Fatimah, ؓ . He set out for the expedition of Tabuk, and Ali, ؓ , was with him. Fatimah stood and spread a mat in her house, hung a curtain on her door, and dyed her head-covering with saffron. When her father ﷺ returned and saw what she had done, he turned back and sat in the mosque. She sent for Bilal and said, 'O Bilal, go to my father and ask him what is keeping him from my door.' He went to him and asked him. He ﷺ said, 'I saw that she made something new there.' He told her, so she tore down the curtain, picked up the mat, discarded what she was wearing, and put on her old clothes. Bilal came to him and told him, so he came to her and embraced her, saying, 'Be like this, may my father and mother be your ransom.'"],[6453,"Two men sneezed in the presence of the Prophet ﷺ, and he responded to one of them—or he said: and he said “Yarḥamuk Allāh” to one of them—and he did not respond to the other. So it was said to him: Two men sneezed, and you responded to one of them and left the other? He said: “This one praised Allah, and this one did not praise Him.”"],[6454,"Two men sat with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, one of them more noble than the other. The noble one sneezed but did not praise Allah, and the other sneezed and praised Allah. The Prophet ﷺ responded to him, so the noble one said: O Messenger of Allah, I sneezed and you did not respond to me, but this one sneezed and you responded to him? The Prophet ﷺ said: “This one remembered Allah, so I remembered him; and you forgot, so I forgot you.”"],[6455,"I was sitting with the Prophet ﷺ when a man sneezed, and the Prophet ﷺ said: “May Allah have mercy on you.” Then he sneezed again, and the Prophet ﷺ said: “The man has a cold.”"],[6456,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ would enter upon us and say, \"Do you have anything this morning?\" We would say, \"No,\" and he would say, \"I am fasting.\" She said: One day he entered upon us and said, \"Do you have anything?\" I said, \"Yes, some hays that was gifted to us.\" He ﷺ said, \"I began the day fasting,\" then he called for it and ate."],[6457,"That Juwayriyah, the wife of the Prophet ﷺ, informed him that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ entered upon her and said, “Is there any food?” She said, “No, by Allah, O Messenger of Allah, we have no food except a sheep’s bone that was given to my freedwoman from charity.” He said, “Bring it, for it has reached its destination.”"],[6458,"That the Prophet ﷺ entered upon her and said, “Is there any food?” She said, “No, O Messenger of Allah, except food that a freedwoman of ours was given from charity.” The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, “Bring it.”"],[6459,"That the Prophet ﷺ said to A’ishah, “Do you have anything to feed me?” She said, “No, except from the sheep that was sent to Nusaybah from charity.” He said, “Bring it, for it has reached its destination.”"],[6460,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ was in the house of Abu Ayyub. Food containing garlic was brought to him, but he did not eat from it. He sent it to Abu Ayyub, but Abu Ayyub did not eat from it because he did not see the Prophet's ﷺ trace in it. Then he came to him and asked him about it, saying: 'O Messenger of Allah, is it forbidden?' He said: 'No, but I disliked it because of the smell.' He said: 'I dislike what you dislike.'"],[6461,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ was brought a drink, with a boy on his right and elders on his left. He said to the boy, \"Will you permit me to give it to these?\" The boy said, \"No, by Allah, O Messenger of Allah, I will not prefer anyone over my share from you.\" So the Messenger of Allah ﷺ placed it in his hand."],[6462,"The Prophet ﷺ drank milk, with a bedouin on his right and Abu Bakr on his left, and he gave the bedouin the remainder of it, saying, \"The right, then the right.\""],[6463,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ was brought milk mixed with water, with a bedouin on his right and Abu Bakr on his left. The Prophet ﷺ drank and gave it to the bedouin, saying, \"The right, then the right.\""],[6464,"\"People came to him and asked him about selling, buying, and trading wine.\" Ibn Abbas said, \"Are you Muslims?\" They said, \"Yes.\" He said, \"It is not lawful for a Muslim to sell it, buy it, or trade in it. The example of those who do that among them is like the Children of Israel: fat was forbidden to them, but they did not eat it; they sold it and consumed its price.\" Then they asked him about tila'. Ibn Abbas said, \"What is this tila' of yours that you ask about?\" They said, \"It is grapes cooked then put into jars.\" He said, \"And what are jars?\" They said, \"Pitch-lined jars.\" He said, \"Does it intoxicate?\" They said, \"If one drinks a lot of it, it intoxicates.\" He said, \"Every intoxicant is unlawful.\" Then they asked him about nabidh. He said, \"The Prophet of God ﷺ went on a journey and returned, and some of his companions had made nabidh in hollowed-out stumps, green jars, and gourds. He ordered them to be poured out. He ordered a water skin, and raisins and water were put in it. Nabidh was made for him at night, and he would drink it that day and the coming night, and the next day until evening. When evening came, he drank and gave others to drink, and if any remained in the morning, he poured it out.\""],[6465,"There was a man of the Ansar called Abu Shu'ayb, and he had a slave who was a butcher. He saw the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and recognized hunger in his face. He said to his slave: Prepare for us food for five, for I intend to invite the Prophet ﷺ as the fifth of five. He said: So he prepared it. Then the Prophet ﷺ came as the fifth of five, and a man followed them. When he reached the door, the Prophet ﷺ said: “This man followed us, so if you wish, give him permission, and if you wish, he will return.” He said: Rather, I give him permission, O Messenger of Allah."],[6466,"A man came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and said, “O Messenger of Allah, the livestock have perished and the roads are cut off, so invoke Allah.” So the Messenger of Allah ﷺ supplicated. He said, “We were given rain from one Friday to the next.” He said, “Then a man came to the Prophet ﷺ and said, ‘O Messenger of Allah, the houses have collapsed and the livestock have perished.’ So the Messenger of Allah ﷺ stood and said, ‘O Allah, upon the tops of the mountains, the hillocks, the bottoms of the valleys, and the places where trees grow.’” He said, “Then the clouds parted from Madinah like the parting of a garment.”"],[6467,"We went out with Abū Bakr, ؓ , and the Messenger of Allah ﷺ appointed him as our commander. We raided Fazārah. When we drew near the water, Abū Bakr commanded us, and we halted for rest. When we prayed the morning prayer, Abū Bakr commanded us to launch the raid. We killed at the water whom we killed. Salamah said: I looked at a group of people among whom were children and women, and I ran in their tracks. I feared they would reach the mountain before me, so I shot an arrow, and it fell between them and the mountain. They stopped, and I brought them, driving them to Abū Bakr, until I came to the water. Among them was a woman from Fazārah wearing a piece of tanned leather, and with her was a daughter of hers, one of the most beautiful of the Arabs. Abū Bakr gave me her daughter as booty. I did not remove any garment from her until I arrived in Madinah. Then I spent the night and did not remove any garment from her. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ met me and said, “Give me the woman.” I said, “O Messenger of Allah, she has pleased me, and I have not removed any garment from her.” The Messenger of Allah ﷺ was silent and left me. Then he met me the next day in the market and said, “O Salamah, give me the woman, may your father be for Allah.” He said: I said, “O Messenger of Allah, I have not removed any garment from her. She is yours, O Messenger of Allah.” He said: So the Messenger of Allah ﷺ sent to the people of Makkah, who had Muslim captives in their hands, and he ransomed them with that woman, freeing them through her."],[6468,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ entered upon a bedouin to visit him and said, \"No harm, purification, if Allah wills.\" He said, \"No indeed, rather a boiling fever upon an old man that will bring him to the graves.\" The Prophet ﷺ said, \"Then yes, so be it.\""],[6469,"He placed his hand on the muscle of his calf and said, \"This is the place of the lower garment; if you refuse, then lower; if you refuse, then the lower garment has no right to the ankles.\""],[6470,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ took hold of the muscle of my calf and said, \"Here is the place of the lower garment; if you refuse, then here, and the lower garment has no right to the ankles.\""],[6471,"The Prophet ﷺ said, \"Do not prefer some prophets to others.\" (Using translation from Bukhārī 6916)"],[6472,"The Prophet ﷺ recited: {And take from the station of Ibrahim a place of prayer}."],[6473,"He used to write down copies of the Quran during the time of the wives of the Prophet ﷺ. He said: Hafsah asked me to write a copy for her and said, \"When you reach this verse in Surat al-Baqarah, do not write it until you bring it to me so I can dictate it to you as I memorized it from the Messenger of Allah ﷺ.\" He said: When I reached it, I brought her the paper on which I was writing, and she said, \"Write: {Guard strictly the prayers and the middle prayer} and the 'Asr prayer {and stand before Allah devoutly}.\""],[6474,"The believer, when he bears witness that there is no god but Allah and knows Muhammad ﷺ in his grave, that is His saying: {Allah keeps firm those who believe with the firm word in the life of this world and in the Hereafter}."],[6475,"“(If you wished, you could have taken for it a payment)” with a lightened (letter)."],[6476,"{If I ask you about anything after it, do not accompany me} — he said, 'I asked you' with a hamza — {You have already reached from me an excuse}."],[6477,"He used to recite {So is there any who will remember?}"],[6478,"I heard a man asking al-Aswad b. Yazid, while he was teaching the Quran to the people in the mosque, 'How is {So is there any who will remember?} recited — with a dal or a dhal?' He said, 'With a dal. I heard 'Abd Allah b. Mas'ud say: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ recited {So is there any who will remember?} with a dal.'"],[6479,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ taught me: 'Indeed, I am the Provider, possessor of strength, the Firm.'"],[6480,"I came to Syria, and Abu al-Darda' was informed, so he came to us and said, 'Which of you can recite to me the recitation of Ibn Umm 'Abd?' He said: We said, 'All of us can recite.' He said, 'Which of you is the best reciter?' He said: My companions pointed to me. Abu al-Darda' said, 'Have you memorized?' I said, 'Yes.' He said, 'How did he recite {By the night when it covers}?' I said, 'By the night when it covers, and the day when it appears, and the male and the female.' He said, 'Did you memorize it from 'Abd Allah?' He said: I said, 'Yes.' He said, 'And I, by the One besides whom there is no god, heard it from the Messenger of Allah ﷺ in this way, but these people want—by Allah, I will never follow them.'"],[6481,"ʿAlqama went to Syria. He came to the mosque and prayed two rakʿas, then said: “O Allah, grant me a righteous companion.” He sat with Abu al-Dardaʾ, who said: “From which people are you?” He replied: “From the people of Kufa.” He said: “Is there not among you the keeper of the secret which no one else knew—Hudhayfa? Is there not among you the one whom Allah protected through the tongue of His Prophet ﷺ from Satan—ʿAmmar b. Yasir? Is there not among you the keeper of the black standard—ʿAbd Allah b. Masʿud?” Then he said: “How do you recite this verse: {By the night when it covers, and the day when it shines}?” I said: “And by the male and the female.” He said: “These people kept almost making me doubt, but I heard it from the Messenger of Allah ﷺ.”"],[6482,"The Prophet ﷺ recited: {He thinks that his wealth will make him immortal}."],[6483,"I recited An-Najm before the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and he did not prostrate."],[6484,"She was asked about a man who has intercourse but does not ejaculate. She said: “I did that with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and we both bathed because of it.”"],[6485,"She was asked about a man who has intercourse with his wife but does not ejaculate. She said: «I and the Messenger of Allah ﷺ did that, and we both performed ghusl because of it.»"],[6486,"On the Day of Badr, the Messenger of Allah ﷺ looked at the polytheists—they were a thousand, while his companions were three hundred and some odd men. The Prophet of Allah ﷺ faced the qiblah, then stretched out his hands and began to call upon his Lord: 'O Allah, fulfill for me what You promised me. O Allah, give me what You promised me. O Allah, if this band of the people of Islam perishes, You will not be worshipped on earth.' He kept calling upon his Lord, mighty and exalted, with his hands extended, facing the qiblah, until his cloak fell from his shoulder ﷺ. Abu Bakr, ؓ , came to him, took his cloak, and placed it back on his shoulder. Then he embraced him from behind and said: 'O Prophet of Allah, enough of your supplication to your Lord, for He will surely fulfill what He promised you.' Then Allah revealed: 'When you sought help of your Lord and He answered you, \"Indeed, I will reinforce you with a thousand from the angels, following one another.\"' So Allah reinforced him with angels."],[6487,"Men from the Ansar asked permission of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, saying: 'Permit us, O Messenger of Allah, to leave the ransom for our nephew al-‘Abbas.' He ﷺ said: 'No, by Allah, you will not leave a single dirham.'"],[6488,"Jibril ﷺ descended upon him ﷺ and said to him: 'Give them a choice' meaning his Companions ﷺ regarding the captives: if they will, killing; and if they will, ransom, on condition that the same number of them be killed the coming year. They said: 'Ransom, and the same number of us will be killed.'"],[6489,"'We used to say that the people of Badr were three hundred and odd, the same number as the companions of Talut who crossed the river with him, and none but a believer crossed with him.'"],[6490,"When the Messenger of Allah ﷺ captured the captives of Banu al-Mustaliq, Juwayriyah bt. al-Harith fell to the share of Thabit b. Qays b. al-Shammas or to his cousin. She made a contract to purchase her freedom. She was a sweet, beautiful woman; hardly would anyone see her but that she captivated him. She came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ seeking his help in her contract. By Allah, no sooner had she stood at the door of the chamber but I saw her and disliked her, and I knew that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ would see from her what I saw. Juwayriyah said, “O Messenger of Allah, the matter has occurred as you know; I contracted for my freedom, and I have come to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ seeking his help.” The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, “Is there not something better than that?” She said, “What is it?” He said, “I marry you and pay your contract.” She said, “Yes.” He said, “I have done it.” She said, “That reached the Muslims, and they said, ‘In-laws of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ.’ So they sent what was in their hands of the captives of Banu al-Mustaliq.” She said, “By his marriage, one hundred households of Banu al-Mustaliq were freed. I do not know any woman who was a greater blessing upon her people than her.”"],[6491,"I have not seen a woman I would rather be in her place than Sawdah bint Zam'ah, a woman who had some sharpness. When she grew old, she gave her day with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ to 'A'ishah. She said: \"O Messenger of Allah, I have given my day with you to 'A'ishah.\" She said: \"And the Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to apportion for 'A'ishah two days: her day and Sawdah's day.\""],[6492,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to divide his time among his wives and be fair, then say, \"O Allah, this is my action in what I possess, so do not blame me for what I do not possess.\""],[6493,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to seek permission from us on the day of a woman among us after the revelation of: \"You may defer whom you will of them, and you may receive whom you will\" [33:51]. Mu'adhah said: \"What would you say to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ when he sought your permission?\" She said: \"I would say: 'If that is up to me, I would not prefer anyone over myself.'\""],[6494,"I asked al-Zuhri which of the Prophet's ﷺ wives sought refuge from him. He said: 'Urwah b. al-Zubayr informed me from 'A'ishah that when the daughter of al-Jawn entered upon the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and he approached her, she said, \"I seek refuge in Allah from you.\" The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, \"You have sought refuge in a great one; join your family.\""],[6495,"Regarding the two women among the Prophet's ﷺ wives to whom Allah said {If you two repent to Allah, your hearts have inclined}. This continued until he performed Hajj, and I performed Hajj with him. He turned aside, and I turned aside with him carrying a water-skin. He went to relieve himself, then came back, and I poured water over his hands from the water-skin, and he performed ablution. I said, 'O Commander of the Faithful, who are the two women among the Prophet's ﷺ wives to whom Allah said {If you two repent to Allah, your hearts have inclined}?' Umar said, 'How strange of you, O Ibn Abbas! They are Hafsah and Aishah.' Then Umar resumed his account and said: 'I and a neighbor of mine from the Ansar, in the Banu Umayyah b. Zayd, who lived in the upper part of Madinah, used to take turns going down to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. One day he would go down, and one day I would go down. When I went down, I would bring him the news of that day from the revelation and other matters; and when he went down, he did the same. We, the people of Quraysh, used to dominate our women. But when we came to the Ansar, we found a people whom their women dominated. So our women began to adopt the ways of the Ansari women. My wife raised her voice at me and talked back to me, and I disapproved of her talking back to me. She said, \"Why do you disapprove of me talking back to you? By Allah, the wives of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ talk back to him, and one of them may shun him from day until night.\" That alarmed me, and I said, \"Whoever among them does that will be in loss.\" Then I gathered my clothes and went down and entered upon Hafsah bt. Umar. I said to her, \"O Hafsah, does one of you anger the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and shun him from day until night?\" She said, \"Yes.\" I said, \"You have failed and lost. Do you feel secure that Allah will become angry for the anger of His Messenger ﷺ and you will perish? Do not ask the Messenger of Allah ﷺ for too much, do not talk back to him, do not shun him, and ask me for whatever you need. Do not be deluded because your neighbor is more radiant and more beloved to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ,\" meaning Aishah. Umar said: 'We had been told that Ghassan was shoeing horses to raid us. My Ansari companion went down on his day and returned to me in the evening. He knocked on my door violently, and I was alarmed and went out to him. He said, \"A great matter has occurred.\" I said, \"What is it? Has Ghassan come?\" He said, \"No, but something greater and more serious: the Messenger of Allah ﷺ has divorced his wives.\" Umar said: I said, \"Hafsah has failed and lost. I already thought this would happen soon.\" He said: So I gathered my clothes and prayed the dawn prayer with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. He said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ went into a small upper room of his and isolated himself there."],[6496,"When the Prophet of Allah ﷺ isolated himself from his wives, I entered the mosque and the people were striking pebbles and saying, 'The Messenger of Allah ﷺ has divorced his wives.' That was before the women were commanded to observe hijab. Umar said: 'I will certainly know about it today.' So I entered upon Aishah and said, 'O daughter of Abu Bakr, has your matter reached the point that you offend Allah and His Messenger?' She said, 'What is it to you, O son of al-Khattab? Look after your own family.' Then I entered upon Hafsah bt. Umar and said to her, 'O Hafsah, has your matter reached the point that you offend Allah and His Messenger? I know that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ does not love you, and were it not for me, he would have divorced you.' She wept bitterly. I said, 'Where is the Messenger of Allah ﷺ?' She said, 'He is in his storage room in the upper chamber.' So I went in, and there was Rabah, a servant of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, sitting on the threshold of the upper chamber, dangling his legs on a wooden notch—a trunk that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to climb up and descend on. I called, 'O Rabah, ask permission for me to see the Messenger of Allah ﷺ.' He looked at the room, then looked at me, but said nothing. I said, 'O Rabah, ask permission for me to see the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, for I think the Messenger of Allah ﷺ thought I came on behalf of Hafsah. By Allah, if the Messenger of Allah ﷺ commands me to strike her neck, I will strike her neck.' I raised my voice, and he gestured to me with his hand. So I entered upon the Messenger of Allah ﷺ while he was lying on a mat. He said: I sat down, and he had a waist-wrapper on, with nothing else, and the mat had left marks on his side. I looked around the storage room of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and saw a handful of barley, about a sa', and the like of it of qaraz in a corner of the room, and there was an untanned hide. Abu Hafs said: al-afiq is a hide whose hair has fallen off and has not been tanned. My eyes filled with tears, and he said, 'What makes you weep, O son of al-Khattab?' I said, 'O Prophet of Allah, why should I not weep? This mat has left marks on your side, and this is your storage room, and I see in it only what I see, while Caesar and Khosrau live amid fruits and rivers. You are the Messenger of Allah and His chosen one, and this is your storage room.' He said, 'O son of al-Khattab, are you not pleased that for us is the Hereafter and for them is this world?' I said, 'Yes.' I entered upon him and saw anger in his face. I said, 'O Messenger of Allah, what distresses you about the matter of women? If you have divorced them, then Allah and His angels, Jibril and Mikail, and I and Abu Bakr are with you. Seldom have I spoken—and I praise Allah—without hoping that Allah would confirm my words. And this verse, the verse of choice, was revealed: {Perhaps his Lord, if he divorces you, will give him in exchange wives better than you} and {If you two support one another against him, then Allah is his protector}—the verse. Aishah and Hafsah used to support one another against the rest of the Prophet's ﷺ wives. I said, 'O Messenger of Allah, have you divorced them?' He said, 'No.' I said, 'O Messenger of Allah, shall I go down and tell them that you have not divorced them?' He said, 'Yes, if you wish.' I kept talking to him until the anger left his face, and until he smiled and laughed. He had one of the most beautiful mouths of the people. Then the Prophet of Allah ﷺ descended, and I descended, holding onto the trunk. He came down as though walking on the ground, without touching it with his hand. I said, 'O Messenger of Allah, you were in the room for twenty-nine days.' Then I stood at the door of the mosque and called out at the top of my voice: 'The Prophet ﷺ has not divorced his wives.' And this verse was revealed: {When there comes to them a matter of security or fear, they spread it abroad} up to {those among them who could investigate it would have known it}. I was the one who investigated that matter. And Allah revealed the verse of choice."],[6497,"I was always eager to ask 'Umar b. al-Khattab about the two women among the wives of the Prophet ﷺ about whom Allah said, {If you two repent to Allah, then your hearts have deviated} until 'Umar performed Hajj and I performed Hajj with him. When we were on part of the road, he turned aside to perform ablution, and I turned aside with him with the water vessel. He went to relieve himself, then came to me, and I poured water on his hands, and he performed ablution. I said, \"O Commander of the Faithful, who are the two women among the wives of the Prophet ﷺ about whom Allah said, {If you two repent to Allah, then your hearts have deviated}?\" 'Umar said, \"How amazing you are, O Ibn 'Abbas!\" Then he said, \"They are 'A'ishah and Hafsah.\" Then he began to narrate the hadith, saying: We, the people of Quraysh, were a people who dominated women, but when we came to Madinah we found a people whose women dominated them, so our women began to learn from their women. My dwelling was among the Banu Umayyah b. Zayd in al-'Awali. He said: One day I became angry with my wife, and she talked back to me. I disapproved of her talking back to me, and she said, \"What do you disapprove of my talking back to you? By Allah, the wives of the Prophet ﷺ talk back to him, and one of them forsakes him for a day until night.\" He said: So I went and entered upon Hafsah and said, \"Do you talk back to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ?\" She said, \"Yes, and one of us forsakes him for a day until night.\" He said: I said, \"You have said it. Whoever does that among you is disappointed and loses. Does one of you feel secure that Allah will be angry with her because of the anger of His Messenger ﷺ? Then she is ruined. Do not talk back to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and do not ask him for anything, but ask me whatever you want. And let not your neighbor deceive you, if she is more beautiful and more beloved to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ than you,\" meaning 'A'ishah. He said: I had a neighbor from the Ansar, and we used to take turns going down to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. He would go down one day and I would go down one day, and he would bring me the news of revelation and other things, and I would go down and bring him the like of that. We used to talk that Ghassan was shoeing horses to raid us. He said: One day my companion went down, then he came to me and knocked on my door, then called me, and I went out to him. He said, \"A great matter has occurred.\" I said, \"What? Has Ghassan come?\" He said, \"No, but greater than that and longer. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ has divorced his wives.\" I said, \"Hafsah is disappointed and loses. I had thought this would happen.\" When I prayed the morning prayer, I tightened my clothes, then went down and entered upon Hafsah, and she was crying. I said, \"Has the Messenger of Allah ﷺ divorced you?\" She said, \"I do not know. He is there, secluded in this upper room.\" He said: So I went to a black slave of his and said, \"Ask permission for 'Umar.\" The slave entered, then came out to me and said, \"I mentioned you to him, but he said nothing.\" So I went until I came to the mosque, and there were people sitting around the pulpit, some of them crying to one another. He said: I sat for a little, then what I felt overcame me, so I went to the slave and said, \"Ask permission for 'Umar.\" He entered, then came out to me and said, \"I mentioned you to him, but he remained silent.\" So I returned and sat by the pulpit, then what I felt overcame me, so I went to the slave and said, \"Ask permission for 'Umar.\" He entered, then came out to me and said, \"I mentioned you to him, but he remained silent.\" So I turned to leave, and the slave called me and said, \"Enter, for he has given you permission.\" So I entered and greeted the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and he was reclining on a sand bed that had left marks on his side. I said, \"O Messenger of Allah, have you divorced your wives?\" He said: He raised his head to me and said, \"No.\" I said, \"Allah is Most Great. If you had seen us, O Messenger of Allah, we the people of Quraysh were a people who dominated women, but when we came to Madinah we found a people whose women dominated them, so our women began to learn from their women. One day I became angry with my wife, and she talked back to me. I disapproved of that from her, and she said, 'Do you disapprove of my talking back to you? By Allah, the wives of the Prophet ﷺ talk back to him, and one of them forsakes him for a day until night.'\" He said: I said, \"Whoever does that among them is disappointed and loses. Does one of them feel secure that Allah will be angry with her because of the anger of His Messenger ﷺ? Then she is ruined.\" He said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ smiled. I said, \"O Messenger of Allah, I entered upon Hafsah and said to her, 'Do not talk back to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and do not ask him for anything, but ask me whatever you want. And let not your neighbor deceive you, if she is more beautiful and more beloved to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ than you.'\" He said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ smiled again. I said, \"May I sit and be at ease, O Messenger of Allah?\" He said, \"Yes.\" So I sat down, and I raised my head in the house. By Allah, I saw nothing in it that would attract the eye except three hides. I said, \"O Messenger of Allah, supplicate Allah to expand for your ummah, for Allah has expanded for Persia and Rome, and they do not worship Him.\" He said: He sat up straight and said, \"Are you in doubt, O Ibn al-Khattab? Those are a people whose good things were hastened for them in the life of this world.\" I said, \"Ask forgiveness for me, O Messenger of Allah.\" And he had sworn not to enter upon them for a month because of his intense anger with them, until Allah admonished him."],[6498,"A’ishah bought Barirah from the Ansar to manumit her, and they stipulated that she make her wala' theirs. She stipulated that. When the Prophet of Allah ﷺ came, she informed him of that, and he ﷺ said, “Wala' belongs only to the one who manumits.” Then he ascended the minbar and said, “What is the matter with people who stipulate conditions that are not in the Book of Allah?” Barirah had a husband, and the Messenger of Allah ﷺ gave her the choice: if she wished, she could remain with her husband as she was, and if she wished, she could separate from him. She separated from him. The Prophet ﷺ entered the house, and in it was a sheep’s leg or foreleg. He ﷺ said to A’ishah, “Will you not cook this meat for us?” She said, “It was given as charity to Barirah, and she gifted it to us.” He said, “Cook it, for it is charity for her and a gift for us.”"],[6499,"She bought Barirah, and her owners stipulated their wala'. He ﷺ said, \"Manumit her, for the wala' belongs to the one who paid the silver and took charge of the favor.\" She said: So I manumitted her, and the Messenger of Allah ﷺ gave her the choice. She said, \"Even if I were given such and such, I would not be with him.\" Al-Aswad said: \"And her husband was a free man.\""],[6500,"Barirah contracted with herself for nine uqiyyas, one uqiyya each year. She came to Aisha seeking her help, and she said, \"No, unless they agree that I count it for them as a single payment and the wala' is mine.\" Barirah went and spoke to her owners about that, but they refused, insisting that the wala' be theirs. She came to Aisha, and the Messenger of Allah ﷺ came at that time, and she told her what her owners said. She said, \"No, by Allah, unless the wala' is mine.\" The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, \"What is this?\" I said, \"O Messenger of Allah, Barirah came to me seeking my help with her contract, and I said, 'No, unless they agree that I count it for them as a single payment and the wala' is mine.' She mentioned that to her owners, but they refused, insisting that the wala' be theirs.\" The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, \"Buy her and stipulate the wala' for them, then manumit her, for the wala' belongs to the one who manumits.\""],[6501,"That Barirah's husband was a slave called Mughith. It is as if I am looking at him following behind her, weeping with tears flowing onto his beard. The Prophet ﷺ said to al-Abbas, \"O Abbas, do you not marvel at the intensity of Mughith's love for Barirah and the intensity of Barirah's hatred for Mughith?\" He ﷺ said to her, \"Would you take him back, for he is the father of your child?\" She said, \"O Messenger of Allah, are you commanding me?\" He ﷺ said, \"I am only interceding.\" She said, \"I have no need of him.\""],[6502,"Julaybib was a man from the Ansar who used to enter upon women and converse with them. Abu Barzah said: I said to my wife, \"Julaybib must never enter upon you.\" When one of the companions of the Prophet ﷺ had an unmarried woman, he would not marry her off until he knew whether the Messenger of God ﷺ wanted her or not. One day the Messenger of God ﷺ said to a man from the Ansar, \"O so-and-so, marry your daughter to me.\" He said, \"Yes, with pleasure and delight.\" He said, \"I do not want her for myself.\" He said, \"For whom then?\" He said, \"For Julaybib.\" He said, \"O Messenger of God, let me consult her mother.\" He went to her and said, \"The Messenger of God ﷺ is proposing to your daughter.\" She said, \"Yes, with pleasure and delight.\" He said, \"He does not want her for himself.\" She said, \"For whom does he want her?\" He said, \"For Julaybib.\" She said, \"May she be shaven! For Julaybib? No, by the life of God, I will not marry Julaybib.\" When her father got up to go to the Prophet ﷺ, the girl said from behind her curtain to her mother, \"Who proposed to me?\" They said, \"The Messenger of God ﷺ.\" She said, \"Will you reject the command of the Messenger of God ﷺ? Give me to the Messenger of God ﷺ, for he will not waste me.\" Her father went to the Prophet ﷺ and said, \"She is yours to decide.\" So he married her to Julaybib. Hammad said: Ishaq b. 'Abd Allah b. Abi Talhah said, \"Do you know what he supplicated for her?\" He said, \"What did he supplicate for her?\" He said, \"O God, pour good upon them abundantly and do not make their livelihood difficult.\" Thabit said: So he married her to him. While the Messenger of God ﷺ was on a campaign, he said, \"Do you miss anyone?\" They said, \"No.\" He said, \"But I miss Julaybib. Look for him among the slain.\" They found him beside seven whom he had killed, and then they killed him. The Messenger of God ﷺ said, \"He killed seven and then they killed him? This man is from me and I am from him,\" saying it seven times. The Messenger of God ﷺ placed him on his forearms, for he had no bier except the forearms of the Messenger of God ﷺ, until he placed him in his grave."],[6503,"\"O Barirah, have you seen anything from 'A'ishah that makes you doubt her?\" Barirah said: \"O Messenger of Allah, by the One who sent you with the truth, I have never seen a matter in her that I would conceal from her. Nothing is more [trivial] than that she is a young girl who sleeps away from the dough of her family, and a tame animal comes and eats it.\" Then the Messenger of Allah ﷺ stood and sought to be excused from 'Abd Allah b. Ubayy b. Salul. He said while on the pulpit: \"O assembly of Muslims, who will excuse me from a man whose harm has reached my household? By Allah, I know nothing but good about my family. They have mentioned a man about whom I know nothing but good, and he never entered upon my family except with me.\" Sa'd b. Mu'adh al-Ansari stood and said: \"I will excuse you from him, O Messenger of Allah. If he is from Aws, we will strike his neck; and if he is from Khazraj, command us and we will do your command.\" Then Sa'd b. 'Ubadah stood—he was the chief of Khazraj and a righteous man, but zeal overcame him—and said: \"By Allah, you will not kill him, nor are you able to kill him.\" Usayd b. Hudayr, the cousin of Sa'd b. Mu'adh, stood and said: \"You lie, by the life of Allah, we will surely kill him. You are a hypocrite arguing on behalf of the hypocrites.\" The two tribes, Aws and Khazraj, became agitated until they were about to fight, while the Messenger of Allah ﷺ kept calming them until they fell silent. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ then became silent. I wept all day; my tears did not cease and I could not sleep. My parents thought that weeping would split my liver. While they were sitting with me, a woman from the Ansar asked permission to enter upon me. I gave her permission and she sat with me. While we were in that state, the Messenger of Allah ﷺ entered, greeted, and sat down. He had not sat with me since my affair began. He remained a month without receiving revelation. She said: He then testified and said: \"Now then, O 'A'ishah, such and such has reached me about you. If you are innocent, Allah will soon acquit you. If you have fallen into sin, then seek Allah's forgiveness and repent, for when a servant confesses a sin and then repents, Allah turns to him.\" When the Messenger of Allah ﷺ finished his speech, my tears stopped until I didn't feel even a drop. I said to my father: \"Answer the Messenger of Allah ﷺ on my behalf.\" He said: \"By Allah, I do not know what to say to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ.\" I said to my mother: \"Answer the Messenger of Allah ﷺ on my behalf.\" She said: \"By Allah, I do not know what to say to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ.\" I said, while I was a young girl who did not read much of the Qur'an: \"By Allah, I knew that you had heard this and it settled in your hearts and you believed it. If I say to you that I am innocent—and Allah knows I am innocent—you will not believe me. If I confess to you a matter—and Allah knows I am innocent—you will believe me. By Allah, I find for myself and you no example except as Abu Yusuf said: 'So patience is most fitting, and Allah is the one sought for help against what you describe' [12:18].\" Then I turned and lay down on my bed. At that time, by Allah, I knew I was innocent and that Allah, Mighty and Exalted, would acquit me. But I did not think that Allah, Mighty and Exalted, would send down revelation concerning my affair that would be recited. My affair was too insignificant in my own eyes for Allah, Mighty and Exalted, to speak about me with a matter to be recited. But I hoped that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ would see in his sleep a vision through which Allah would acquit me. She said: By Allah, the Messenger of Allah ﷺ did not leave his seat, nor did anyone leave the house, until Allah sent down [revelation] upon His Prophet ﷺ. He was seized by the same severity that would seize him at the time of revelation, from the weight of the words revealed to him. When the Messenger of Allah ﷺ was relieved, the first words he spoke were: \"O 'A'ishah, rejoice! By Allah, Allah has acquitted you.\" My mother said to me: \"Get up and go to him.\" I said: \"By Allah, I will not get up to him, and I praise none but Allah who sent down my acquittal.\" Then Allah sent down: \"Indeed, those who came with falsehood are a group among you\" [24:11], the ten verses. She said: So Allah sent down these verses concerning my acquittal. Abu Bakr, ؓ , used to spend on Mistah because of his kinship and his poverty. He said: \"By Allah, I will never spend on him again after what he said about 'A'ishah.\" Then Allah sent down: \"And let not those of virtue among you and wealth swear not to give [aid] to their relatives\" [24:22], until His saying: \"Would you not love that Allah should forgive you?\" [24:22]. Abu Bakr said: \"By Allah, I love that Allah should forgive me.\" He resumed spending on Mistah and said: \"By Allah, I will never withhold it from him.\" She said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ had asked Zaynab bint Jahsh about my affair: \"What do you know and what have you seen?\" She said: \"I protect my hearing and my sight. I know nothing but good.\" She said: She was the one among the wives of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ who vied with me, but Allah protected her through piety. Her sister Hamnah bint Jahsh began to fight on her behalf and was destroyed among those who were destroyed. Al-Zuhri said: \"This is what has reached me of the matter of these people.\""],[6504,"I used to play with dolls during the time of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. She said: My friends would come to me, and when they saw the Messenger of Allah ﷺ they would shrink away from him. He ﷺ would send them to me, and they would play with me."],[6505,"“I would bring the vessel to the Prophet ﷺ and take it and drink from it. The Prophet ﷺ would take it and place his mouth where my mouth had been. And I would take a piece of meat with bone and eat from it, and he would take it and place his mouth where my mouth had been and eat it, while I was menstruating.”"],[6506,"He saw the Messenger of Allah ﷺ wearing a silver ring one day, so the people made silver rings and wore them. Then the Prophet ﷺ threw away his ring, and the people threw away their rings."],[6507,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ took a gold ring and wore it, so the people took gold rings. Then the Messenger of Allah ﷺ stood up and said, \"I used to wear this ring, but I will never wear it again.\" Then he threw it away, and the people threw away their rings."],[6508,"He saw the Messenger of Allah ﷺ one day with a gold ring on his hand, and the people rushed to make rings, so he threw it away and said, \"I will never wear it again.\""],[6509,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ took a ring and wore it, then said, \"This has preoccupied me from you since today.\" Then he threw it away."],[6510,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ took a ring of gold, and the people took gold rings, so he threw it from his hand and said, “I will never wear it.” He then took a ring of silver and set its stone facing his palm, and engraved on it: Muhammad, Messenger of Allah. It remained on his hand until the Messenger of Allah ﷺ passed away."],[6511,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ took a ring of gold and used to set its stone facing the inside of his palm. The people took rings, so the Messenger of Allah ﷺ threw it away and said, “I will never wear it.” He then took a ring of silver, and it was on his hand, then on the hand of Abu Bakr, then on the hand of Umar, then on the hand of Uthman, until it fell from him into the well of Aris."],[6512,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ wanted to write to the non-Arabs, and they said to him, ‘They will not read a letter unless it has a signet ring with an engraving.’ So the Messenger of Allah ﷺ ordered a silver signet ring and engraved on it ‘Muhammad, Messenger of Allah.’"],[6513,"“The inscription on the ring of the Prophet ﷺ was three lines: Muhammad one line, Messenger one line, Allah one line.”"],[6514,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ had a ring made and said, “We have made a ring and inscribed on it an inscription, so let no one engrave upon it.”"],[6515,"The signet ring of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ was of silver, its stone from it."],[6516,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ wore a silver ring in which was an Abyssinian stone on his right hand, and he would place its stone inside his palm."],[6517,"“The Messenger of Allah ﷺ took a ring of gold and wore it on his right hand, placing its stone facing the inside of his palm. Then he threw it away and took a ring of silver.”"],[6518,"He used to wear his ring on his right hand.”"],[6519,"The Messenger of Allah [SAW] put on a ring of gold, and he used to wear its stone (Fass) next to his palm. Then the people started to wear rings of gold. Then the Messenger of Allah [SAW] discarded it, and the people discarded their rings. Then he acquired a ring of silver with which he used to seal letters, but he did not wear it. (Using translation from Nasāʾī 5218)"],[6520,"A man sat with the Prophet ﷺ wearing a gold ring. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ tapped his hand with a stick he had, then turned away from him. The man threw away his ring. Then the Messenger of Allah ﷺ looked at him and said, 'Where is your ring?' He said, 'I threw it away.' He said, 'I think we hurt you and caused you loss.'"],[6521,"Abu Musa al-Ash'ari came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ asking him to provide mounts for a group of his people. He said: By Allah, I will not provide them mounts. Then some camels were brought to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ as spoils, and he distributed them, leaving fifteen. He said: «Where is 'Abd Allah b. Qays?» He said: Here he is. He said: «Take these and mount your people on them.» He said: O Messenger of Allah, you had sworn an oath. He said: «And even if I swore?»"],[6522,"A Jewish boy used to serve the Prophet ﷺ, and he fell ill. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to his companions, \"Come with us to visit him.\" They came to him while his father was sitting at his head. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to him, \"Say: There is no god but Allah, so that I may intercede for you thereby on the Day of Resurrection.\" The boy began looking at his father, and his father said to him, \"See what Abul-Qasim says to you.\" He said, \"I bear witness that there is no god but Allah, and I bear witness that Muhammad is the Messenger of Allah.\" The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, \"Praise be to Allah who saved him from the Fire of Hell.\""],[6523,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ set out in the year of the conquest to Makkah in Ramadan until he reached Kurā‘ al-Ghamīm. The people were fasting, both on foot and mounted. He was told, “The people are suffering hardship from fasting; they are only watching what you do.” He called for a cup, raised it to his mouth so the people could see, then drank. Some people broke their fast and some continued fasting. The Prophet ﷺ was told that some of them were still fasting, and he said, “Those are the disobedient ones.” The foot soldiers among his companions gathered and said, “Let us seek the supplications of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, for the journey has become difficult and hardship has lengthened.” The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to them, “Seek help by moving briskly, for it cuts the distance and lightens the journey.” We did so and it became lighter for us."],[6524,"When the Prophet ﷺ saw the images in the House, meaning the Ka'bah, he did not enter, and he ordered that they be erased, and they were erased. He saw Ibrahim and Isma'il with divining arrows in their hands, and he said: “May Allah fight them! By Allah, they never sought divine judgment with arrows.”"],[6525,"“When the Prophet ﷺ defeated a people, he liked to stay in their courtyard for three, or he said three nights.”"],[6526,"We were with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and rain fell, and he bared part of his garment to the rain. We said: 'Why did you do this, O Messenger of Allah?' He said: 'Because it has recently been with its Lord.'"],[6527,"I was with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, stopping at al-Jiʿrānah between Makkah and Madinah, and with him was Bilāl. A Bedouin man came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and said, 'Will you not fulfill for me, O Muḥammad, what you promised me?' The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to him, 'Rejoice.' The Bedouin said to him, 'You have given me too much good news.' The narrator said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ turned to Abū Mūsā and Bilāl as if angry and said, 'This man has rejected the good news, so accept it yourselves.' They said, 'We accept, O Messenger of Allah.' The narrator said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ called for a bowl of water and then said to them, 'Drink from it and pour it over your faces or chests.' They took the bowl and did what the Messenger of Allah ﷺ commanded them. Then Umm Salamah called out to us from behind the curtain, 'Leave some for your mother in your vessel.' So they left a portion of it for her."],[6528,"We were walking with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and passed by two graves. He stood, and we stood with him. His complexion began to change until the sleeve of his shirt trembled. We said: 'What is wrong with you, O Prophet of Allah?' He said: 'Do you not hear what I hear?' We said: 'And what is that, O Prophet of Allah?' He said: 'These are two men being severely punished in their graves for a light sin.' We said: 'For what, O Prophet of Allah?' He said: 'One of them did not keep himself clean from urine, and the other used to harm people with his tongue and go among them with malicious gossip.' Then he called for two palm stalks and placed one in each grave. We said: 'Will that benefit them, O Messenger of Allah?' He said: 'Yes, it will lighten for them as long as they remain moist.'"],[6529,"The Prophet ﷺ vomited and broke his fast. I met Thawban in the mosque of Damascus and mentioned that to him. He said, 'He spoke the truth; I poured ablution water for him.'"],[6530,"Abu Bakr al-Siddiq, ؓ , sent for me after the killing of the people of al-Yamamah, and ʿUmar b. al-Khattab, ؓ , was with him. Abu Bakr said, 'ʿUmar came to me and said, \"The killing has been intense among the Muslims of al-Yamamah, and I fear that killing will be intense in the places and much of the Quran will be lost and not preserved. I want you to order the collection of the Quran.\" I said, \"How can you do something that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ did not do?\" ʿUmar said, \"By Allah, it is good.\" He kept reviewing this with me until Allah opened my chest for that, and I saw in it what ʿUmar b. al-Khattab, ؓ , saw.' ʿUmar was sitting with him, not speaking. Abu Bakr said, 'You are a young intelligent man, and we do not suspect you, and you used to write down the revelation for the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, so trace the Quran and collect it.' Zayd said: By Allah, if they had tasked me with moving a mountain among the mountains, it would not have been heavier upon me than what he ordered me to do of collecting the Quran. I said, 'How can you do something that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ did not do?' He said, 'By Allah, it is good.' Abu Bakr kept reviewing this with me until Allah opened my chest to what He had opened the chests of Abu Bakr and ʿUmar. He said: So I set out tracing the Quran, collecting it from palm stalks, shoulder blades, and the hearts of men, until I found the last part of Surah al-Tawbah with Khuzaymah al-Ansari; I did not find it with anyone else: 'There has certainly come to you a Messenger from among yourselves. Grievous to him is what you suffer.' The sheets in which I collected the Quran remained with Abu Bakr during his life until Allah took him, then with ʿUmar until Allah took him, then with Hafsah bint ʿUmar."],[6531,"He asked Sulayman b. Musa about a man looking at his wife's private parts. He said, 'I asked ʿAtaʾ about that, and he said, \"I asked ʿAʾishah about it, and she said, 'I and my beloved ﷺ used to perform ghusl from a single vessel, our hands alternating in it.'\"' And she pointed to a vessel in the house holding about six qists."],[6532,"She used to bathe with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ from a single vessel."],[6533,"He would recite the Quran while reclining against me, and I was menstruating."],[6534,"The Prophet ﷺ appointed Ibn Umm Maktum as his deputy over Madinah to lead the people in prayer."],[6536,"“The Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to say when he finished the recitation of the dawn prayer, and he said takbīr and raised his head: ‘Allah hears the one who praises Him; our Lord, to You be praise.’ He would say while standing: ‘O Allah, save al-Walīd b. al-Walīd, Salamah b. Hishām, ʿAyyāsh b. Abī Rabīʿah, and the weak among the believers. O Allah, tighten Your grip on Muḍar and make it upon them like the years of Yūsuf. O Allah, curse Liḥyān, Riʿl, Dhakwān, and ʿUṣayyah who disobeyed Allah and His Messenger.’ Then it reached us that he abandoned that when it was revealed: {Not for you is the decision whether He turns to them or punishes them, for they are wrongdoers}.”"],[6537,"Satan came across in my prayer place, so I seized him by his throat and choked him until I felt the coldness of his tongue on my palm. Had it not been for the supplication of my brother Sulayman, he would have been tied up and you would be looking at him."],[6538,"He used to pray while carrying Umāmah bt. Zaynab, his daughter. When he stood, he carried her; and when he prostrated, he put her down."],[6539,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ delivered a sermon on the day of Eid while standing on his feet."],[6540,"“The Messenger of Allah ﷺ was cupped while in iḥrām because of an ailment in his head.”"],[6541,"She used to say, \"If the Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to kiss some of his wives while he was fasting,\" then she laughed."],[6542,"\"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ set out for Makkah in the year of the conquest during Ramadan and fasted until he reached al-Kadīd, then he broke his fast, and the people broke their fast with him. They used to follow the most recent of the Messenger of Allah's ﷺ commands, the most recent.\""],[6543,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ besieged the people of al-Ṭāʾif and gained nothing from them. He said, “We are returning, if Allah wills.” His companions said, “We return without conquering?” The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, “Go out to fight in the morning.” They went out and were wounded. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to them, “We are returning tomorrow.” That pleased them, and the Messenger of Allah ﷺ laughed."],[6544,"His maternal aunt gifted the Messenger of Allah ﷺ clarified butter, dried curd, and dabb lizards. He ate from the clarified butter and dried curd but did not eat the dabb lizards, finding them repulsive. Ibn Abbas said: “It was eaten on the table of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. Had it been forbidden, it would not have been eaten on his table.”"],[6545,"The Prophet ﷺ had cupping done and gave the cupper his wage, and he used a nasal medicine."],[6546,"A slave came and pledged allegiance to the Prophet of Allah ﷺ for emigration, and he did not realize that he was a slave. His master came wanting him, so the Prophet ﷺ said, “Sell him to me.” He bought him for two black slaves. Then he did not accept allegiance from anyone until he asked him, “Are you a slave?”"],[6547,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ came from relieving himself, and a man met him at Biʾr Jamal and greeted him. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ did not return the greeting until he approached a wall. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ placed his hand on the wall, then wiped his face and his hands, then the Messenger of Allah ﷺ returned the greeting to the man."],[6548,"\"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ swore an oath of Ila' from his wives, and he made the forbidden lawful and made an expiation for the oath.\""],[6549,"We came from Makkah to Madinah and stopped at a place near Madinah. The Prophet ﷺ said, \"Sell me this camel of yours.\" I said, \"No, rather it is yours.\" He said, \"No, sell it to me.\" I said, \"No, rather it is yours, O Messenger of Allah.\" He said, \"No, sell it to me.\" I said, \"A man owed me an uqiyyah of gold, so it is yours for that.\" He ﷺ said, \"I have taken it; ride it to Madinah.\" When I arrived in Madinah, the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to Bilal, \"Give him an uqiyyah of gold and add more.\" He said, \"He gave me an uqiyyah of gold and added a qirat.\" I said, \"The addition of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ will never leave me,\" so it was in a pouch, and the people of Syria took it during the nights of al-Harrah."],[6550,"He was ten years old when the Prophet ﷺ came to Madinah. So my mothers used to urge me to serve the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. He said: 'So I served the Messenger of Allah ﷺ for ten years during his life in Madinah, and the Prophet ﷺ died when I was twenty years old.' He said: 'And I was the most knowledgeable of people about the matter of the hijab when it was revealed. Ubayy b. Ka'b used to ask me about it.' He said: 'And the first part of what was revealed concerning the wedding of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ to Zaynab bt. Jahsh was that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ became a bridegroom with her. He invited the people, and they ate the food and left. A group of them remained with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and they prolonged their stay. So the Messenger of Allah ﷺ got up and went out, and I went out with him so that they might leave. He walked, and I walked with him until he reached the threshold of 'A'ishah's room. Then the Messenger of Allah ﷺ thought that they had left, so he returned, and I returned with him until he entered upon Zaynab, and there they were sitting and had not gotten up. So the Messenger of Allah ﷺ returned, and I returned with him until he reached the threshold of 'A'ishah's room. He thought that they had left, so he returned, and I returned, and there they had left. So he put a screen between them and him, and the hijab was revealed.'"],[6551,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ held a wedding feast and provided the Muslims with ample bread and meat, as he used to do when he married. He went to the chambers of the Mothers of the Believers, greeted them, and they supplicated for him. Then he returned, and I was with him. When we reached the house, there were two men conversing in a corner of the house. When he saw them, he turned back. Then Allah revealed the verse of the veil."],[6552,"He heard the Prophet ﷺ saying, \"Labbayk, 'umrah and Hajj.\""],[6553,"\"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ combined Hajj and 'umrah, and the people combined with him.\""],[6554,"We were close to the calloused spots on the knees of the Messenger of Allah's ﷺ she-camel near the mosque. When it stood straight with him, he said, \"Labbayk with a Hajj and an 'umrah together.\" That was in the Farewell Pilgrimage."],[6555,"I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ saying, \"Labbayk with an 'umrah and a Hajj.\" Humayd said, \"Bakr b. 'Abd Allah al-Muzani narrated to me that he mentioned the hadith of Anas b. Malik to Ibn 'Umar, and he said, 'Did Anas make the Messenger of Allah ﷺ perform Hajj alone? ' He said, 'Then I mentioned the statement of Ibn 'Umar to Anas b. Malik, and he said, \"Ibn 'Umar only thinks that we were children.\"'\""],[6556,"\"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ performed Hajj alone.\""],[6557,"\"The Prophet ﷺ performed Hajj alone.\""],[6558,"\"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ performed Hajj alone.\""],[6559,"Muṭarrif visited ʿImrān b. Ḥuṣayn, and he said to him: “I shall relate to you a ḥadīth. If I recover from my illness, do not narrate it; but if I pass away to my fate, narrate it if it seems right to you: ‘We performed tamattuʿ with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and he did not forbid us from it until he died ﷺ. A man then voiced his own opinion about it.’”"],[6560,"ʿImrān b. Ḥuṣayn said to me: “Shall I not relate to you a ḥadīth, perhaps Allah will benefit you by it? ‘The Messenger of Allah ﷺ combined the ḥajj and the ʿumrah, and he did not forbid it, nor did any Qurʾān come down concerning it, nor did he declare it unlawful. And he used to greet me, but when I cauterized myself the greeting went away—or was lifted from me—and when I abandoned it, it returned to me.’”"],[6561,"He heard Saʿd b. Abī Waqqāṣ and al-Ḍaḥḥāk b. Qays in the year of Muʿāwiyah b. Abī Sufyān’s ḥajj, while they were discussing tamattuʿ with ʿumrah to ḥajj. Al-Ḍaḥḥāk said: “No one does that except one who is ignorant of Allah’s command.” Saʿd b. Abī Waqqāṣ said: “How bad is what you have said, O son of my brother.” Al-Ḍaḥḥāk said: “ʿUmar b. al-Khaṭṭāb forbade that.” Saʿd said: “The Messenger of Allah ﷺ did it, and we did it with him.”"],[6562,"Ibn ʿAbbās used to command us to do the mutʿah, while Ibn al-Zubayr forbade it. I mentioned that to Jābir, so he said: “The ḥadīth revolves around my hand. We performed tamattuʿ with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. When ʿUmar b. al-Khaṭṭāb came, he said: ‘Allah would make lawful for His Prophet ﷺ whatever He willed whenever He willed, but the Qurʾān has now been revealed in its proper stages, so complete the ḥajj and the ʿumrah for Allah as Allah has commanded you, and refrain from marrying these women for a fixed period. No man will be brought to me who marries a woman for a term except that I will stone him with rocks.’”"],[6563,"He pronounced the talbiyah for Hajj and Umrah. That was mentioned to Umar, and he said, \"You have been guided to the Sunnah of your Prophet ﷺ.\""],[6564,"I and Masruq often used to come to al-Subayy b. Ma'bad to ask him about this hadith. He said: I was a Christian man, and I embraced Islam. I pronounced the talbiyah for Hajj and Umrah. Salman b. Rabi'ah and Zayd b. Suhan heard me pronouncing the talbiyah for both of them at al-Qadisiyyah, and they said, \"This man is more astray than his family's camel.\" It was as if a mountain had been placed upon me by their words, until I reached Makkah. I came to Umar b. al-Khattab while he was at Mina and mentioned that to him. He turned to them and reprimanded them, then he turned to me and said, \"You have been guided to the Sunnah of your Prophet ﷺ,\" twice."],[6565,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ entered upon me for four or five nights of Dhu al-Hijjah during his Hajj, and he was angry. I said, \"O Messenger of Allah, whoever angers you, Allah will admit him into the Fire.\" He ﷺ said, \"Have you not felt that I commanded them with a matter and they hesitated in it? If it were not for the fact that I received guidance from my Lord, I would not have stoned the Jamrat nor sacrificed the animal until they did so.\""],[6566,"We set out to meet the new moon of Dhū al-Ḥijjah with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. The Prophet ﷺ said: “Whoever of you wishes to assume iḥrām for an ʿumrah, let him do so. Were it not that I have brought the sacrificial animal, I would assume iḥrām for an ʿumrah.” Some of his companions assumed iḥrām for ḥajj and some for ʿumrah. She said: “I was among those who assumed iḥrām for ʿumrah. The Day of ʿArafah overtook me while I was menstruating and I had not exited my ʿumrah. I complained about that to the Prophet ﷺ, and the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: ‘Leave your ʿumrah, undo your hair, comb it, and assume iḥrām for ḥajj.’” She said: “I did so, until when it was the night of al-Ḥaṣbah, ʿAbd al-Raḥmān b. Abī Bakr sent me with her, riding behind him, and she went out to al-Tanʿīm and assumed iḥrām for an ʿumrah in place of her ʿumrah, then she circumambulated the House and went between al-Ṣafā and al-Marwah. Thus Allah completed her ḥajj and her ʿumrah, and there was no fasting, no sacrificial animal, and no charity in any of that.”"],[6567,"He performed Hajj with his masters. He said: I came to Umm Salamah and said: O Mother of the Believers, I have never performed Hajj. With which of the two should I begin, the Hajj or the Umrah? She said: If you wish, perform Umrah before you perform Hajj, and if you wish, after you perform Hajj. I went to Safiyyah and she said to me the same. I returned to Umm Salamah and informed her of what Safiyyah said. Umm Salamah said: I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: “O family of Muhammad, whoever of you performs Hajj, let him enter ihram for Umrah within a Hajj.”"],[6568,"We set out with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ in the Farewell Pilgrimage. Among us were those who entered ihram for Hajj and those who entered ihram for 'umrah and drove a sacrificial animal. The Prophet ﷺ said, \"Whoever entered ihram for 'umrah and did not drive a sacrificial animal should exit ihram, and whoever entered ihram for 'umrah and drove a sacrificial animal should not exit ihram, and whoever entered ihram for Hajj should complete his Hajj.\" 'A'ishah said, \"And I was among those who entered ihram for 'umrah.\""],[6569,"We set out with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ in the Farewell Pilgrimage. I entered ihram for 'umrah and had not driven a sacrificial animal. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, \"Whoever of you has driven a sacrificial animal should enter ihram for Hajj along with his 'umrah, then not exit ihram until he exits from both of them together.\" She ('A'ishah) said, \"Then I menstruated on the night of 'Arafah, so I said, 'O Messenger of Allah, how should I proceed with my Hajj?' He said, 'Comb your hair, leave the 'umrah, and enter ihram for Hajj.'\" She said, \"So I performed Hajj, and the Messenger of Allah ﷺ sent 'Abd al-Rahman b. Abi Bakr with me, and he made me perform 'umrah in place of the 'umrah I had left.\""],[6570,"We went out with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ in the year of the Farewell Hajj and we entered ihram for Umrah. Then the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Whoever has with him a sacrificial animal (hady), let him enter ihram for Hajj along with Umrah, then he is not to come out of ihram until he comes out of it from both together.” She said: I came to Makkah while I was menstruating, so I did not circumambulate the House nor go between Safa and Marwah. I complained about that to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and he said: “Undo your hair, comb it, enter ihram for Hajj, and abandon the Umrah.” She said: So I did that. When we had finished the Hajj, the Messenger of Allah ﷺ sent me with Abd al-Rahman b. Abi Bakr to al-Tan'im, and I performed Umrah. He said: “This is in place of your Umrah.” She said: Those who had entered ihram for Umrah circumambulated the House and went between Safa and Marwah, then came out of ihram, then performed another circumambulation after returning from Mina for their Hajj. As for those who had entered ihram for Hajj and combined Hajj and Umrah, they performed only one circumambulation."],[6571,"We set out with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ in the months of ḥajj, the nights of ḥajj, and the sacred precinct of ḥajj, until we alighted at Sarif. She said: He went out to his Companions and said: \"Whoever does not have a sacrificial animal with him and would like to make it an ʿumrah, let him do so; but whoever has a sacrificial animal with him, no.\" She said: Some of his Companions accepted it and some left it. She said: As for the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and some men among his Companions, they were people of strength and had sacrificial animals with them, so they were not able to do the ʿumrah. She said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ entered upon me while I was weeping. He said: \"What makes you weep, O little one?\" I said: I heard what you said to your Companions, so I was prevented from the ʿumrah. He said: \"What is the matter with you?\" I said: I cannot pray. He said: \"That does not harm you. You are only a woman among the daughters of Adam. Allah has decreed for you what He has decreed for them. So remain in your ḥajj; perhaps you will attain it.\" She said: So we set out on his ḥajj until we arrived at Minā. Then I became pure. Then I left Minā and performed the ifāḍah ṭawāf of the House. She said: Then I went out with him in the last group of departures until he alighted at al-Muḥaṣṣab, and we alighted with him. He called ʿAbd al-Raḥmān b. Abī Bakr and said: \"Take your sister out of the ḥaram, and let her enter ihram for ʿumrah. Then finish and come here, for I will wait for you until you come to me.\" She said: So I went out for that until I finished, and I finished the ṭawāf. Then I came to him before dawn. He said: \"Have you finished?\" I said: Yes. He said: \"Then announce departure among his Companions.\" So the people departed, and he passed by the House before the morning prayer and performed ṭawāf of it. Then he went out, mounted, and turned away heading to Madinah."],[6572,"“Whoever does not have with him a sacrificial animal (hady), let him come out of ihram.” We said: What kind of coming out of ihram? He said: “Complete coming out of ihram.” When it was the Day of Tarwiyah, we entered ihram for Hajj. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to us: “Share in the camels and the cows; every seven (people) in one camel.” He said: Then Suraqah b. Malik b. Ju'shum came and said: O Messenger of Allah, do you think this Umrah of ours is for this year of ours or forever? He ﷺ said: “No, rather forever.” He said: O Messenger of Allah, explain to us our religion as if we were created just now. Do you think the deeds we perform, are they in what the pens have dried upon and the decrees have run with, or in what we face in the future? He ﷺ said: “No, rather in what the pens have dried upon and the decrees have run with.” I said: Then what is the point of deeds? The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Work, for everyone is facilitated (to that for which he was created).”"],[6573,"The Prophet ﷺ \"married Maymunah while he was in ihram.\""],[6574,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ married some of his wives while he was in a state of ihram, and he was cupped while in a state of ihram."],[6575,"The Prophet ﷺ married Maymunah while he was in a state of ihram during the Umrat al-Qada."],[6576,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ married her while he was not in a state of ihram, and consummated the marriage with her while not in a state of ihram. She died at Sarif, and we buried her in the shade structure where he had consummated the marriage with her. I and Ibn Abbas descended into her grave, and when we placed her in the niche, her head tilted, so I took my cloak and placed it under her head. Ibn Abbas pulled it and threw it aside. She had shaved her head during Hajj, and her hair was dyed with henna."],[6577,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ married Maymunah while he was not in a state of ihram, and consummated the marriage with her while not in a state of ihram. I was the messenger between them."],[6578,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ married her while he was not in a state of ihram."],[6579,"The Prophet ﷺ married her at Sarif while they were both not in a state of ihram."],[6580,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ married me at Sarif while we were both not in a state of ihram, after they had returned from Makkah."],[6581,"Umar b. Ubayd Allah sent to Aban b. Uthman, and Aban was at that time the commander of the pilgrimage, while both were in a state of ihram, saying: I intend to marry Talhah b. Umar to the daughter of Shaybah b. Jubayr, and I want you to attend that. Aban b. Uthman denied that and said: I heard Uthman b. Affan, ؓ , say: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: 'The one in ihram does not marry, nor does he propose, nor does he give in marriage.'"],[6582,"“The Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to like comprehensive supplications.”"],[6583,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to say when he reached morning: \"O Allah, by You we have reached morning, and by You we have reached evening, and by You we live, and by You we die, and to You is the return.\""],[6584,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to say when he reached morning: \"O Allah, by You we have reached morning, and by You we have reached evening, and by You we live, and by You we die, and to You is the return.\""],[6585,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ did not abandon these supplications when he reached evening and when he reached morning: \"O Allah, I ask You for well-being in this world and the Hereafter. O Allah, I ask You for pardon and well-being in my religion, my worldly affairs, my family, and my wealth. O Allah, cover my faults and calm my fears. O Allah, protect me from before me, from behind me, on my right, on my left, and from above me, and I seek refuge in Your greatness from being swallowed up from beneath me.\""],[6586,"The Prophet ﷺ used to say in the morning, \"We have entered the morning and the whole kingdom (of the earth) solely belongs to Allah, and all praises are due to Allah. I ask You for the goodness of this day and the goodness that follows it.\""],[6587,"When the Messenger of Allah ﷺ heard the muezzin, he said: \"And I, and I.\""],[6588,"We were with Mu'awiyah when he heard the caller saying: \"Allahu akbar, Allahu akbar,\" and Mu'awiyah said: \"Allahu akbar.\" When he said: \"Ashhadu an la ilaha illa Allah,\" Mu'awiyah said: \"And I bear witness.\" When he said: \"Ashhadu anna Muhammadan rasul Allah ﷺ,\" he said: \"And I bear witness.\" Then Mu'awiyah said: \"Thus I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say.\""],[6589,"I sat with Abu Umamah b. Sahl, and the muezzin came and said: \"Allahu akbar, Allahu akbar,\" and Abu Umamah said the like of that. Then he said: \"Ashhadu an la ilaha illa Allah,\" and Abu Umamah said the like of that. Then he said: \"Ashhadu anna Muhammadan rasul Allah,\" and Abu Umamah said the like of that. Then he turned to me and said: \"Thus.\""],[6590,"When he entered the privy, he would say, \"O Allah, I seek refuge in You from the male and female devils.\""],[6591,"When the Messenger of Allah ﷺ came out from the privy, he would say, \"Your forgiveness.\""],[6592,"When the Messenger of Allah ﷺ started to pray, he would say Takbir, then say: \"Wajahtu wajhi lilladhi fataras-samawatiwal-arda hanifan wa ma ana minal-mushrikin. Inna salati wa nusuki wa mahyaya wa mamati lillahi rabbil-alamin, la sharika lahu, wa bidhalika umirtu wa ana min al-muslimin. Allahumma! Antal-maliku la ilaha illa ant, ana abduka zalamtu nafsi wa'taraftu bidhanbi faghfirli dhunubi jami'an, la yaghfirudhunuba illa anta, wahdini lihasanil-ahklaqi, la yahdi li ahsaniha illa anta wasrif anni sayy'aha la yasrifu anni sayy'aha illa anta, labaika wa sa'daika, wal-khairu kulluhu fi yadaika wash-sharru laisa ilaika ana bika wa ilaika ana bika wa ilaika tabarkta wa ta'alaita astaghfiruka wa atubu ilaik. (Verily, I have turned my face toward Him who created the Heavens and the Earth hanifa (worhsipping none but Allah Alone), and I am not of the idolaters. Verily, my salah, my sacrifice, my living, and my dying are for Allah, the Lord of the all that exists. He has no partner. And of this I have been commanded, and I am one of the Muslims. O Allah, You are the Sovereign and there is none worthy of worship but You. I am Your slave, I have wronged myself and I acknowledge my sin. Forgive me all my sins for no one forgives sins but You. Guide me to the best of manners for none can guide to the best of them but You. Protect me from bad manners for none can protect against them but You. I am at Your service, all goodness is in Your hands, and evil is not attributed to You. I rely on You and turn to You, blessed and exalted are You, I seek Your forgiveness and repent to You.\" (Using translation from Nasāʾī 897)"],[6593,"When the Messenger of Allah ﷺ opened the prayer, he said takbir and then said: “I have turned my face to the One who created the heavens and the earth, as a ḥanīf, and I am not of the polytheists. My prayer, my sacrifice, my life, and my death belong to Allah, Lord of the worlds, who has no partner. With that I have been commanded, and I am the first of the Muslims. O Allah, You are the King, there is no god but You. You are my Lord and I am Your servant. I have wronged myself and I confess my sin, so forgive all my sins. None forgives sins but You. Here I am, at Your service. All good is in Your hands, and evil is not attributed to You. I am through You and to You. Blessed and exalted are You. I seek Your forgiveness and I repent to You.”"],[6594,"When the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said the takbir in prayer, he would pause briefly before reciting. I said, 'O Messenger of Allah, may my father and mother be ransomed for you, what do you say during your silence between the takbir and the recitation?' He said, 'I say: O Allah, distance me from my sins as You distanced between the east and the west. O Allah, purify me from sins as the white garment is purified from filth. O Allah, wash me from my sins with water, snow, and hail.'"],[6595,"I saw the Messenger of Allah ﷺ when he began the prayer, he said, 'O Allah, I seek refuge in You from Satan—from his madness and his arrogance.'"],[6596,"When the Messenger of Allah ﷺ entered prayer, he said, 'Allah is the Greatest, ever great; and abundant praise is due to Allah' three times. 'Glory be to Allah morning and evening' three times. 'I seek refuge in Allah from the accursed Satan—from his arrogance, his madness, and his spittle.'"],[6597,"A man came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and said, “O Messenger of Allah, I saw in this night, as a sleeper sees, as if I was praying behind a tree. I saw as if I recited a prostration, and I saw the tree as if it prostrated for my prostration. I heard it while prostrating, saying: O Allah, write for me with it a reward with You, and make it for me a treasure with You, and remove from me a burden by it, and accept it from me as You accepted it from Your servant David.” He said: Ibn Abbas said, “I saw the Messenger of Allah ﷺ recite the prostration, and I heard him while prostrating saying the like of what the man said from the speech of the tree.”"],[6598,"I prayed with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and when he bowed, he began saying, “Glory be to my Lord, the Magnificent.” Then he prostrated and said, “Glory be to my Lord, the Most High.”"],[6599,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to often say in his bowing and prostration: “Glory be to You, O Allah, our Lord, and with Your praise. O Allah, forgive me,” interpreting the Qur’an."],[6600,"He used to say in his bowing and prostration, “All-Glorious, All-Holy, Lord of the angels and the Spirit.”"],[6601,"When he bowed, he would say, “O Allah, to You I have bowed, in You I have believed, and to You I have submitted. You are my Lord. My hearing, sight, brain, bones, nerves, and what my feet carry have humbled themselves to Allah, Lord of the worlds.”"],[6602,"When the Messenger of Allah ﷺ bowed, he said, “O Allah, to You I have bowed, in You I have believed, and to You I have submitted. My hearing, sight, brain, bones, and nerves have humbled themselves to You.” And when he raised his head, he said, “Allah hears the one who praises Him. Our Lord, to You belongs all praise, filling the heavens and the earth, filling what is between them, and filling whatever else You will.”"],[6603,"When the Messenger of Allah ﷺ started to pray, he would say Takbir, then say: \"Wajahtu wajhi lilladhi fataras-samawatiwal-arda hanifan wa ma ana minal-mushrikin. Inna salati wa nusuki wa mahyaya wa mamati lillahi rabbil-alamin, la sharika lahu, wa bidhalika umirtu wa ana min al-muslimin. Allahumma! Antal-maliku la ilaha illa ant, ana abduka zalamtu nafsi wa'taraftu bidhanbi faghfirli dhunubi jami'an, la yaghfirudhunuba illa anta, wahdini lihasanil-ahklaqi, la yahdi li ahsaniha illa anta wasrif anni sayy'aha la yasrifu anni sayy'aha illa anta, labaika wa sa'daika, wal-khairu kulluhu fi yadaika wash-sharru laisa ilaika ana bika wa ilaika ana bika wa ilaika tabarkta wa ta'alaita astaghfiruka wa atubu ilaik. (Verily, I have turned my face toward Him who created the Heavens and the Earth hanifa (worhsipping none but Allah Alone), and I am not of the idolaters. Verily, my salah, my sacrifice, my living, and my dying are for Allah, the Lord of the all that exists. He has no partner. And of this I have been commanded, and I am one of the Muslims. O Allah, You are the Sovereign and there is none worthy of worship but You. I am Your slave, I have wronged myself and I acknowledge my sin. Forgive me all my sins for no one forgives sins but You. Guide me to the best of manners for none can guide to the best of them but You. Protect me from bad manners for none can protect against them but You. I am at Your service, all goodness is in Your hands, and evil is not attributed to You. I rely on You and turn to You, blessed and exalted are You, I seek Your forgiveness and repent to You.\" (Using translation from Nasāʾī 897)"],[6604,"When he said, “Allah hears the one who praises Him,” he would say, “Our Lord, to You belongs all praise, filling the heavens, filling the earth, filling whatever else You will. You are the most worthy of praise and glory, the truest thing a servant can say, and we are all Your servants. None can withhold what You give, none can give what You withhold, and the fortune of the fortunate cannot avail him against You.”"],[6605,"He would, when he raised his head from bowing, say: 'O Allah, our Lord, to You be praise, filling the heavens, filling the earth, and filling whatever else You will. Lord of praise and majesty, there is none to withhold what You give and none to give what You withhold, and the fortune of the fortunate avails nothing against You.'"],[6606,"«The Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to say frequently in his prostration: \"Glory be to You, our Lord, and with Your praise. O Allah, forgive me.\"» She said: \"And he would apply (the command of) the Quran.\""],[6607,"When the Messenger of Allah ﷺ prostrated, he said: “O Allah, to You I have prostrated, in You I have believed, and to You I have submitted. My face has prostrated to the One who created it, shaped it, and perfected its form, and split its hearing and sight. Blessed is Allah, the best of creators.”"],[6608,"When the Prophet ﷺ prostrated in the obligatory prayer, he said: “O Allah, to You I have prostrated, in You I have believed, and to You I have submitted. You are my Lord. My face has prostrated to the One who created it, split its hearing and sight. Blessed is Allah, the best of creators.”"],[6609,"He used to say in his prostration: \"O Allah, forgive me all my sins—the small and the great, the first and the last, the open and the secret.\""],[6610,"He used to say in his prayer: “O Allah, I ask You for steadfastness in the matter, resolve in right guidance, gratitude for Your favor, and excellence in worshipping You. I ask You for a sound heart, and I ask You for the good of what You know, and I seek refuge in You from the evil of what You know, and I ask Your forgiveness for what You know.”"],[6611,"I missed the Messenger of Allah ﷺ one night from the bed, so I searched for him and my hand fell upon the soles of his feet while he was in the mosque, with them (the feet) erect, and he was saying: \"O Allah, I seek refuge in Your pleasure from Your wrath, and in Your pardon from Your punishment, and I seek refuge in You from You. I cannot enumerate praise of You; You are as You have praised Yourself.\""],[6612,"I missed the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and he had been with me on my bed, then I found him prostrating, with his heels together, facing the qiblah with the tips of his toes. I heard him saying: \"O Allah, I seek refuge in Your pleasure from Your wrath, and in Your pardon from Your punishment, and in You from You. I praise You, but I cannot fully praise You as You deserve.\" When he finished, he ﷺ said: \"O ʿĀʾishah, has your devil incited you?\" I said: \"Do I have a devil?\" He said: \"There is no human being except that he has a devil.\" I said: \"And you, O Messenger of Allah?\" He said: \"And me, but I called upon Allah against him and he submitted (became a Muslim).\""],[6613,"“People are followers of Quraysh in good and evil.”"],[6614,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to teach us the tashahhud as he would teach us a surah from the Quran: 'All compliments, blessed words, prayers, and good things are due to Allah. Peace be upon you, O Prophet, and the mercy of Allah and His blessings. Peace be upon us and upon the righteous servants of Allah. I bear witness that there is no god but Allah, and I bear witness that Muhammad is the Messenger of Allah.'"],[6615,"When the Prophet ﷺ uttered salutation at the end of the prayer, he used to say: \"O Allah, forgive me my former and latter sins, what I have kept secret and what I have done openly, and what I have done extravagance; and what You know better than I do. You are the Advancer, the Delayer, there is no god but You.\" (Using translation from Abū Dāʾūd 1509)"],[6616,"He used to supplicate in the prayer: 'O Allah, I seek refuge in You from the punishment of the Fire, and I seek refuge in You from the punishment of the grave, and I seek refuge in You from the trial of the false messiah, the Dajjal, and I seek refuge in You from the trial of life and death. O Allah, I seek refuge in You from sin and debt.' She said: Someone said, 'O Messenger of Allah, how often you seek refuge from debt!' The Prophet ﷺ said, 'When a man is in debt, he speaks and lies, and he promises and breaks his promise.'"],[6617,"“Indeed I supplicated in it with a supplication that I heard from the Messenger of Allah ﷺ.”"],[6618,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ would not remain seated after the taslim except for as long as it takes to say: “O Allah, You are Peace, and from You is peace. Blessed are You, O Possessor of Majesty and Honor.”"],[6619,"When the Messenger of Allah ﷺ gave the salam, he would say: “O Allah, You are Peace, and from You is peace. Blessed are You, O Possessor of Majesty and Honor.”"],[6620,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ would not remain seated after the taslim except for as long as it takes to say: “O Allah, You are Peace, and from You is peace. Blessed are You, O Possessor of Majesty and Honor.”"],[6621,"When the Messenger of Allah ﷺ wanted to depart from the prayer, he would seek forgiveness three times, then say: “O Allah, You are Peace, and from You is peace. Blessed are You, O Possessor of Majesty and Honor.”"],[6622,"Mu‘awiyah wrote to al-Mughirah: “What did the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say when he departed from the prayer?” He said: “After every prayer he used to say: ‘There is no god but Allah alone, with no partner. To Him belongs dominion and to Him belongs praise, and He is over all things capable. O Allah, none can withhold what You give, and none can give what You withhold, and no possessor of fortune benefits from You, (for) fortune is Yours alone.’”"],[6623,"Mu‘awiyah wrote to al-Mughirah: “Write to me something you heard from the Messenger of Allah ﷺ.” So he wrote to him: “I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say when he finished his prayer: ‘There is no god but Allah alone, with no partner. To Him belongs dominion and to Him belongs praise, and He is over all things capable. O Allah, none can withhold what You give, and none can give what You withhold, and no possessor of fortune benefits from You, (for) fortune is Yours alone.’”"],[6624,"That al-Mughīrah b. Shuʿbah wrote to Muʿāwiyah that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, when he finished his prayer and said the salutation, would say: \"There is no god but Allah alone, with no partner. His is the dominion and His is the praise, and He is over all things competent. O Allah, none can withhold what You give, and none can give what You withhold, and no possessor of fortune can benefit from You his fortune.\""],[6625,"That ʿAbd Allāh b. al-Zubayr used to say after every prayer: \"There is no god but Allah alone, with no partner. His is the dominion and His is the praise, and He is over all things competent. There is no might and no power except with Allah. We worship none but Him. From Him is bounty, and from Him is grace, and from Him is excellence and good praise. There is no god but Allah, making the religion sincerely His, even if the disbelievers hate it.\" And he would say: \"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to say these words after every prayer.\""],[6626,"That ʿAbd Allāh b. al-Zubayr used to say after every prayer: \"There is no god but Allah alone, with no partner. His is the dominion and His is the praise, and He is over all things competent. There is no might and no power except with Allah. We worship none but Him. From Him is bounty, and from Him is grace, and from Him is excellence and good praise. There is no god but Allah, making the religion sincerely His, even if the disbelievers hate it.\" And he would say: \"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to say these words after every prayer.\""],[6627,"\"I heard Abdullah bin Az-Zubair speaking from the Minbar, saying: 'When the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said the taslim, he would say: \"La Ilaha Illallah wahdahu la sharika lah, lahul-mulk wa lahul-hamd wa huwa 'ala kulli shay'in qadir, la hawla wala quwwata illa billahil-'azim; la ilaha ill-Allahu wa la nabbed illa iyyah, ahlan-ni'mati wal-fadli wath-thana'il-has an; la ilaha ill-Allah, mukhlisina lahud-dina wa law karihal-kafirun (There is none worthy of worship except Allah (SWT) alone, with no partner or associate. His is the Dominion, to Him be all praise, and He is able to do all things; there is no power and no strength except with Allah (SWT) the Almighty. There is none worthy of worship except Allah (SWT), and we worship none but Him, the source of blessing and kindness and the One Who is deserving of all good praise. There is none worthy of worship except Allah (SWT), and we are sincere in faith and devotion to Him even though the disbelievers detest it. ) (Using translation from Nasāʾī 1339)"],[6628,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ, during the days of Khaybar, used to move his lips with something after the dawn prayer. It was said to him: \"O Messenger of Allah, you move your lips with something you did not use to do. What is this that you say?\" He ﷺ said: \"I say: O Allah, with You do I seek, with You do I fight, and with You do I charge.\""],[6629,"Ka'b swore to him by the One who split the sea for Musa that we find in the Book that Dawud the Prophet ﷺ , when he left the prayer, said: \"O Allah, set right for me my religion, which You made for me as the protection of my affair, and set right for me my worldly life, in which You placed my livelihood. O Allah, I seek refuge with You through Your pleasure from Your wrath, and with Your pardon from Your punishment, and I seek refuge with You from You. O Allah, none can withhold what You give, and none can give what You withhold, and the fortune of a person of fortune does not avail him against You.\" And Ka'b narrated to me that Suhayb narrated to him that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to say these when he left his prayer."],[6630,"Sa'd used to teach his sons these words just as a teacher teaches boys writing, saying: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to seek refuge with them after every prayer: \"O Allah, I seek refuge with You from miserliness, and I seek refuge with You from cowardice, and I seek refuge with You from being returned to the worst old age, and I seek refuge with You from the trial of this world, and I seek refuge with You from the punishment of the grave.\""],[6631,"\"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ, when he finished the prayer and said the taslim, said: 'O Allah, forgive me what I have sent ahead and what I have delayed, what I have concealed and what I have made public, and what I have exceeded, and what You know better than I. You are the One who brings forward and You are the One who delays; there is no god but You.'\""],[6632,"I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say upon finishing a meal: “Praise be to Allah, abundant, pure, blessed praise, unceasing, unforsaken, and never dispensed with, O our Lord.”"],[6633,"We attended a meal at the house of Abd al-A'la, and Abu Umamah was with us. Upon finishing the meal, Abu Umamah said: I would not like to be a preacher. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to say upon finishing a meal: “Praise be to Allah, abundant, pure, blessed praise, unforsaken, and never dispensed with.”"],[6634,"A man from the Ansar invited the Prophet ﷺ, and we went with him. When he had eaten and washed his hand, he said: “Praise be to Allah who feeds and is not fed. He bestowed favor upon us, guided us, fed us, gave us drink, and every good trial He tried us with. Praise be to Allah who fed us food, gave us drink, clothed our nakedness, guided us from error, gave us sight from blindness, and favored us over many of His creation with great favor. Praise be to Allah, Lord of the worlds.”"],[6635,"When he ate or drank, he would say: “Praise be to Allah who fed and gave drink, made it palatable, and made an exit for it.”"],[6636,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ came to my father and stayed with him. He brought him food, and hais, and sawiq, and dates. Then he brought him a drink, and he handed it to the one on his right. He said: He used to eat dates and put the pits on the back of his two fingers, the index and middle, then throw them away. Then he supplicated for them saying: “O Allah, bless them in what You have provided them, forgive them, and have mercy on them.”"],[6637,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ passed by my father while he was on a white mule. He took hold of its reins and said: Alight with me, O Messenger of Allah. So he alighted with him. He said: Then he brought them hais, and they ate it. Then he brought them dates. He said: The Prophet ﷺ began to eat and to say with the pits like this, turning them, and Shu'ba joined his two fingers. Then they brought him a drink, and he drank, then handed it to the one on his right. Then he said: “O Allah, bless them in what You have provided them, forgive them, and have mercy on them.”"],[6638,"My father said to my mother: If only you would prepare food for the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. So she prepared a tharidah, and he said with his hand like this, indicating it was small. My father went and invited the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. The Prophet ﷺ placed his hand on its top and then said: “Take in the name of Allah.” So they took from its sides. When they had eaten, he supplicated for them. The Prophet ﷺ said: “O Allah, forgive them, have mercy on them, and bless them in their provision.”"],[6639,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ broke his fast at Sa'd's. He said: “The fasting people have broken their fast with you, the angels have prayed for you, and the righteous have eaten your food.”"],[6640,"The Prophet ﷺ entered upon Umm Sulaym, and she brought him dates and clarified butter. He said: \"Return your butter to its skin and your dates to their container, for I am fasting.\" Then he stood in a corner of the house and prayed a non-obligatory prayer, and supplicated for Umm Sulaym and her household. Umm Sulaym said: \"O Messenger of Allah, I have a little special request.\" He said: \"What is it?\" She said: \"Your little servant Anas.\" He left out no good of the Hereafter or this world but he supplicated for it for me. Then he said: \"O Allah, grant him wealth and children, and bless him in them.\" He (Anas) said: \"Indeed I am among the wealthiest of the Ansar.\" He said: \"And my daughter Umaynah told me: By the time al-Hajjaj came to Basra, one hundred and twenty-some of my loins had been buried.\""],[6641,"When the Prophet ﷺ acquired a new garment, he would name it, saying: “O Allah, You have clothed me with this shirt, cloak, or turban. I ask You for its good and the good for which it was made, and I seek refuge with You from its evil and the evil for which it was made.”"],[6642,"When he acquired a new garment, he would name it by its name and say: “O Allah, You have clothed me with this, so to You belongs praise. I ask You for its good and the good for which it was made, and I seek refuge with You from its evil and the evil for which it was made.”"],[6643,"Some broth spilled on my hands and burned them. My mother took me to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and we came to him while he was in al-Rahbah. I remember that he said: “Remove the affliction, Lord of the people.” And most of my knowledge is that he said: “You are the Healer; there is no healer except You.”"],[6644,"“I brought you back from the land of Abyssinia until, when you were a night or two away from Madinah, I cooked a cooking for you and ran out of firewood. I went out to look for it, and you reached for the cooking pot, and it tipped over onto your forearm. I brought you to the Prophet ﷺ and said: ‘O Messenger of Allah, this is Muhammad b. Hatib, and he is the first to be named with your name.’” She said: “So the Messenger of Allah ﷺ spat into your mouth, wiped over your head, supplicated for you, and said: ‘Remove the affliction, Lord of the people. Heal, for You are the Healer. There is no healing except Your healing, a healing that leaves no sickness.’” She said: “I did not get up with you from his presence except that your hand was already healed.”"],[6645,"He entered upon him and said: 'Remove the affliction, Lord of mankind, from Thabit b. Qays b. al-Shammas.' Then he took some dust from Buthan, put it in a cup with water, and poured it over him."],[6646,"When the Prophet ﷺ came to a sick person or a sick person was brought to him, he would say, \"Remove the affliction, Lord of mankind; heal; You are the Healer; there is no healing but Your healing; a healing that leaves no sickness.\""],[6647,"When the Prophet ﷺ was brought a sick person, he would supplicate and say: “Remove the affliction, Lord of the people. Heal, for You are the Healer. There is no healing except Your healing, a healing that leaves no sickness.”"],[6648,"O son of my brother, shall I not incant over you with the incantation of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ? I said: Yes. She said: 'In the name of Allah I incant over you, and Allah will heal you from every disease in you. Remove the affliction, O Lord of mankind; heal, for You are the Healer; there is no healer except You.'"],[6649,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to incant: 'Remove the affliction, O Lord of mankind; in Your hand is healing; there is no remover except You.'"],[6650,"Among what he used to say for the sick person—he would say it with his saliva on his finger: “In the name of Allah, the dust of our earth with the saliva of some of us, our sick one is healed by the permission of our Lord.”"],[6651,"When he came to visit a sick man, he would say: “O Allah, heal Your servant so that he may wound an enemy for You or walk to prayer for You.”"],[6652,"When the Messenger of Allah ﷺ visited a sick person, he would sit at his head and then say seven times: “I ask Allah the Almighty, Lord of the Mighty Throne, to heal you.” If there was a delay in his appointed time, he would be cured of that pain of his."],[6653,"When he visited a sick person, he would wipe him with his right hand and say, \"Remove the affliction, Lord of mankind, and heal; You are the Healer; heal with a healing that leaves no sickness.\""],[6654,"When he complained of pain, he would recite over himself the mu'awwidhat and blow, and when his pain became severe, I would recite over him and wipe him with his own hand, hoping for its blessing."],[6655,"He complained to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ of a pain he had felt since he accepted Islam. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to him, \"Place your hand on the part of your body that hurts and say: In the name of Allah three times, then say: I seek refuge in Allah and His power from the evil of what I find and fear, seven times.\""],[6656,"The Prophet ﷺ used to seek protection for Ḥasan and Ḥusayn: “I seek protection for you both with the complete words of Allah, from every devil and harmful creature, and from every evil eye.” Then he ﷺ would say, “Ibrāhīm — may Allah’s blessings be upon him — used to seek protection with these words for his two sons Ismāʿīl and Isḥāq.”"],[6657,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to seek protection for Ḥasan and Ḥusayn: “I seek protection for you both with the complete words of Allah, from every devil and harmful creature, and from every evil eye.” And he ﷺ used to say, “Your forefather (Ibrāhīm) used to seek protection with them for Ismāʿīl and Isḥāq.”"],[6658,"\"None of you should ever wish for death due to harm that befalls him. If he must do so, let him say: 'Keep me alive as long as life is better for me, and take me when death is better for me.'\""],[6659,"\"None of you should ever wish for death due to harm that befalls him, but let him say: 'O Allah, keep me alive as long as life is better for me, and take me when death is better for me.'\""],[6660,"He used to say in the prayer over funerals: “O Allah, forgive our living and our dead, our present and our absent, our young and our old, our male and our female. O Allah, whomever of us You keep alive, keep him alive upon faith, and whomever of us You cause to die, cause him to die upon Islam.”"],[6661,"\"The complexion of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ was brownish.\""],[6662,"He prayed over a man and said: “O Allah, so-and-so the son of so-and-so is in Your protection and the rope of Your neighborhood, so protect him from the trial of the grave and the punishment of the Fire. You are worthy of faithfulness and truth. O Allah, forgive him and have mercy on him, for You are the Oft-Forgiving, the Most Merciful.”"],[6663,"I spent the night reciting to the jinn, who were my companions at al-Hajun."],[6664,"I witnessed Ibn 'Abbas praying over a funeral. He recited the Opening of the Book. When he finished, I said to him, “Do you recite the Opening of the Book?” He said, “Yes, O son of my brother, it is a sunnah and a truth.”"],[6665,"Whenever it was her night with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, he would go out at the end of the night to al-Baqi' and say, \"Peace be upon you, O abode of a believing people. What you were promised has come to you, and we, if Allah wills, shall join you. O Allah, forgive the people of Baqi' al-Gharqad.\""],[6666,"When he placed the deceased in the grave, he said: 'In the name of Allah and upon the religion of the Messenger of Allah.'"],[6667,"The people complained to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ about drought and lack of rain. He ordered a pulpit, and it was placed for him in the prayer area, and he promised the people a day to come out. Aisha said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ came out when the edge of the sun appeared and sat on the pulpit. He praised Allah and extolled Him, then said: “You have complained of the barrenness of your gardens and the withholding of rain from its usual time. Allah has commanded you to call upon Him and promised to answer you.” Then he said: “{All praise is due to Allah, Lord of the worlds, the Most Merciful, the Especially Merciful, Master of the Day of Judgment.} There is no deity but You; You do what You will. O Allah, You are Allah, there is no deity but You. You are the Self-Sufficient, and we are the needy. Send down upon us rain, and make what You send down a strength for us and a means to good.” Then he ﷺ raised his hands until we saw the whiteness of his armpits. Then he turned his back to the people and reversed or turned his cloak while still raising his hands. Then he faced the people, descended, and prayed two rak‘ahs. Allah brought forth clouds, thunder, lightning, and rain by Allah’s permission. We did not remain long in his mosque before the streams flowed. When the Messenger of Allah ﷺ saw the wetness of clothes on the people, he laughed until his premolars showed and said: “I bear witness that Allah is capable of all things and that I am the servant of Allah and His Messenger.”"],[6668,"A man entered the mosque on Friday through a door facing the pulpit while the Messenger of Allah ﷺ was delivering the sermon. He stood facing him and said, “O Messenger of Allah, the livestock have perished and the roads are cut off. Supplicate to Allah to send us rain.” The Messenger of Allah ﷺ raised his hand and said, “O Allah, give us rain. O Allah, give us rain.” Anas said, “By Allah, we saw no cloud in the sky, not even a small patch, between us and Sal' mountain, no house or dwelling. Then a cloud like a shield appeared from behind it. When it reached the middle of the sky, it spread and then rained. By Allah, we did not see the sun for six days.” Then on the following Friday, a man entered through the same door while the Messenger of Allah ﷺ was delivering the sermon. He stood facing him and said, “O Messenger of Allah, the wealth has been destroyed and the roads are cut off. Supplicate to Allah to hold it back from us.” The Messenger of Allah ﷺ raised his hands and said, “O Allah, around us and not upon us. O Allah, upon the hills, the rocky outcrops, the valleys, and the places where trees grow.” Anas said, “Then it stopped, and he ﷺ went out walking in the sunshine.” I asked Anas, “Was it the same man as the first time?” He said, “I do not know.”"],[6669,"When the Messenger of Allah ﷺ saw rain, he would say, “O Allah, make it a beneficial downpour.”"],[6670,"When the Messenger of Allah ﷺ saw rain, he would say, “O Allah, make it a beneficial downpour.”"],[6671,"When the wind intensified, he would say, “O Allah, (make it) a fertilizing (wind), not a barren (one).”"],[6672,"When the Messenger of Allah ﷺ saw dust or wind in the sky, he would seek refuge in Allah from its evil. When it rained, he would say: “O Allah, make it a beneficial downpour.”"],[6673,"When the wind blew, that would be known from his face ﷺ. *"],[6674,"He used to say: 'O Allah, to You I have submitted, in You I have believed, upon You I have relied, to You I have turned, and with You I have contended. I seek refuge in You—there is no god but You—from Your misguiding me. You are the Living Who does not die, while jinn and humans die.'"],[6675,"A man came to him while he was intending to travel and greeted him. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “I enjoin you to fear Allah and to say the takbir upon every elevation.” Then when the man turned away, he said: “O Allah, fold the earth for him and make the journey easy for him.”"],[6676,"When the Prophet ﷺ wanted to travel, when he mounted his riding camel, he would say the Takbir three times and say: Glory is to Him Who has subjected this to us, and we were not able to do it. And, surely, to our Lord are we returning (Subḥān alladhī sakh-khara lanā hādhā wa mā kunnā lahū muqrinīn. Wa innā ilā rabbinā lamunqalibūn). Then he would say: “O Allah, I ask You in this journey of mine from the righteousness and piety and actions that which you are pleased with. O Allah, ease for us the path, and make near for us the distance of the land. O Allah, You are the companion in the journey, and the caretaker for the family. O Allah, accompany us in our journey, and take care of our families (Allāhumma innī as’aluka fī safarī hādhā minal-birri wat-taqwā, wa minal-ʿamali mā tarḍā. Allāhumma hawwin ʿalainal-masīra, waṭwi ʿannā buʿdal-arḍ. Allāhumma antaṣ-ṣāḥibu fis safari wal-khalīfatu fil-ahli. Allāhumma aṣḥabnā fī safarinā wakhlufnā fī ahlinā).” And when he would return to his family, he would say: “(We are) Returning, if Allah wills, repenting, worshipping, and to our Lord directing the praise (Ā’ibūna in shā’ Allāh, tā’ibūna ʿābidūna lirabbinā hāmidūn).” (Using translation from Tirmidhī 3447)"],[6677,"Are you not in food and drink as you wish?"],[6678,"When he mounted his camel setting out on a journey, he would say the takbir three times and say: {Glory be to the One Who subjected this to us, for we were not capable of it}. “O Allah, we ask You in this journey of ours for righteousness, piety, and deeds that please You. O Allah, make this journey of ours easy for us and fold its distance for us. O Allah, You are the Companion in travel and the Deputy in the family. O Allah, I seek refuge in You from the hardship of travel, from a sorrowful sight, and from an evil return in family, wealth, and children.” When he returned, he would say these words and add: “Returning, repenting, worshiping, and praising our Lord.”"],[6679,"‘Alī mounted an animal and said, “In the name of Allah.” When he settled on it, he said, “Praise be to Allah who honored us and carried us on land and sea, provided us with good things, and favored us over many of those He created. Glory be to Him who subjected this to us, for we were not capable of it, and to our Lord we shall return.” Then he said Allāhu akbar three times, then said, “O Allah, forgive me, for none forgives sins but You.” Then he said, “The Messenger of Allah ﷺ did the same while I was riding behind him.”"],[6680,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ never saw a village he intended to enter without saying when he saw it: “O Allah, Lord of the seven heavens and what they shade, Lord of the seven earths and what they carry, Lord of the winds and what they scatter, Lord of the devils and what they mislead, we ask You for the good of this village and the good of its people, and we seek refuge in You from its evil, the evil of its people, and the evil of what is in it.”"],[6681,"When he traveled and came at dawn, he would say, “A hearer has heard with the praise of Allah and His good favor. Our Lord, accompany us and bestow favor upon us, seeking refuge in Allah from the Fire.”"],[6682,"Ibn ‘Umar said Talbiyah uttered by the Apostle of Allaah ﷺ was Labbaik(always ready to obey), O Allaah labbaik, labbaik; Thou hast no partner, praise and grace are Thine, and the Dominion, Thou hast no partner. The narrator said ‘Abd Allaah bin ‘Umar used to add to his talbiyah Labbaik, labbaik, labbaik wa sa’daik(give me blessing after blessing) and good is Thy hands, desire and actions are directed towards Thee. (Using translation from Abū Dāʾūd 1812)"],[6683,"The Prophet ﷺ said in his talbiyah, \"Labbayk, O God of truth, labbayk.\""],[6684,"I heard the Prophet ﷺ say between the Corner and the Stone: \"Our Lord, give us good in this world and good in the Hereafter, and protect us from the punishment of the Fire.\""],[6685,"“When he stood upon al-Safa, he would say the takbir three times and say: ‘There is no god but Allah alone, with no partner; His is the dominion and His is the praise, and He is over all things powerful.’ He would do that three times, then supplicate, and he would do the same upon al-Marwa.”"],[6686,"“The Messenger of Allah ﷺ performed ‘Umrah and did Tawaf of the House, then went out and did Sa‘i between al-Safa and al-Marwa, while we were shielding him from the people of Makkah lest anyone shoot him or strike him with something.” He said: “I heard him supplicating against the confederates, saying: ‘O Allah, defeat them and shake them, O Sender down of the Book, Swift in reckoning; defeat the confederates. O Allah, defeat them.’”"],[6687,"I heard the Prophet ﷺ say on the day of the confederates: “O Allah, Sender down of the Book, Swift in reckoning, defeat them and shake them.”"],[6688,"\"O Allah, have mercy on those who shave their heads.\" They said, \"And those who shorten, O Messenger of Allah.\" He said, \"O Allah, have mercy on those who shave their heads.\" They said, \"And those who shorten, O Messenger of Allah.\" He said, \"And those who shorten.\""],[6689,"‘Abd Allah bin ‘Umar said “When the Apostle of Allaah ﷺ returned from an expedition, Hajj or ‘Umrah on every rising piece of ground he would say three times “Allaah is Most Great” and he would say “There is no god bt Allaah alone who has no partner, to Whom the dominion belongs, to Whom praise is due, and Who is Omnipotent, serving, prostrating ourselves before our Lord and expressing praise. Allaah alone has kept his word, helped His servant and routed the confederate. (Using translation from Abū Dāʾūd 2770)"],[6690,"He, when he arrived from a journey, said: “Returning, repenting, worshiping, praising our Lord.”"],[6691,"The Prophet ﷺ, when he returned from a journey, said: “Returning, repenting, to our Lord, praising.”"],[6692,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ, when he wanted to set out on a journey, said: “O Allah, You are the companion in the journey and the successor over the family. O Allah, I seek refuge in You from hardship in the journey and sorrow upon return. O Allah, make the earth contracted for us and make the journey easy for us.” Then when he wanted to return, he said: “Returning, repenting, worshiping, prostrating to our Lord.” Then when he entered his house, he said: “Repentance, repentance, to our Lord, a return that leaves no sin upon us.”"],[6693,"“O Allah, bless them in their measure, and bless them in their ṣāʿ and their mudd.”"],[6694,"We went out with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ until when we were at al-Ḥarrah at al-Suqyā, the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, “Bring me water for ablution.” When he had performed ablution, he stood facing the qiblah, then said the takbīr, then said, “O Allah, indeed Ibrāhīm was Your servant and Your close friend; he supplicated to You for the people of Makkah for blessing, and I am Muḥammad, Your servant and Your Messenger; I supplicate to You for the people of Madinah that You bless for them in their mudd and their ṣāʿ the like of what You blessed for the people of Makkah, along with the blessing two blessings.”"],[6695,"When the people saw the first fruits, they would bring them to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. When the Messenger of Allah ﷺ took them, he would say, “O Allah, bless us in our fruits, bless us in our city, and bless us in our ṣāʿ and our mudd. O Allah, indeed Ibrāhīm was Your servant, Your close friend, and Your prophet, and I am Your servant and Your prophet. He supplicated to You for Makkah, and I supplicate to You for Madinah with the like of what he supplicated for Makkah, and the like of it along with it.” Then he would call the youngest child he saw and give him those fruits."],[6696,"It was said, “O Messenger of Allah, our ṣāʿ is the smallest of the ṣāʿs, and our mudd is the smallest of the mudds.” The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, “O Allah, bless us in our ṣāʿ and our mudd, our little and our much, and place with the blessing two blessings.”"],[6697,"\"O Allah, bless us in our Sham. O Allah, bless us in our Yemen.\" They said, \"And in our Najd?\" He said, \"O Allah, bless us in our Sham. O Allah, bless us in our Yemen.\" They said, \"And in our Najd?\" He said, \"There will be earthquakes and trials, and from there—or he said from it—the horn of Satan will emerge.\""],[6698,"Al-Tufayl b. 'Amr al-Dawsi came to the Prophet of Allah ﷺ and said, \"O Messenger of Allah, Daws has disobeyed and refused. Supplicate against them.\" He ﷺ said: \"O Allah, guide Daws and bring them.\""],[6699,"A man came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and mentioned Daws, saying, \"They have...\" Then he mentioned their men and women. The Prophet ﷺ raised his hands, and the man said, \"Indeed we belong to Allah, and indeed to Him we return. Daws has perished, by the Lord of the Ka'bah!\" The Prophet ﷺ raised his hands and said: \"O Allah, guide Daws.\""],[6700,"Al-Ṭufayl b. ʿAmr al-Dawsī came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ in Makkah and said, “O Messenger of Allah, come to a fortress, number, and equipment.” Abū al-Zubayr said: A fortress on the mountaintop that could only be reached by something like a sandal strap. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to him, “Do you have with you those behind you?” He said, “I do not know.” He turned away from him. When the Messenger of Allah ﷺ came to Madinah, al-Ṭufayl b. ʿAmr came as an emigrant to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and with him was a man from his tribe. That man fell ill with a severe fever and became impatient. He took a blade and cut his fingertips, and they bled until he died. He was buried. Then he appeared in a dream to al-Ṭufayl b. ʿAmr in a good appearance, covering his hand. Al-Ṭufayl said to him, “So-and-so?” He said, “Yes.” He said, “How did you fare?” He said, “My Lord did good to me: He forgave me because of my emigration to His Prophet ﷺ.” He said, “What happened to your hands?” He said, “My Lord said to me, ‘We will never set right what you corrupted of yourself.’” Al-Ṭufayl related his vision to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and the Messenger of Allah ﷺ raised his hands: “O Allah, forgive his hands. O Allah, forgive his hands. O Allah, forgive his hands.”"],[6701,"He used to, when a man wanted to marry, say to him, “May Allah bless you and bless upon you.”"],[6702,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, \"May Allah brighten the face of the individual who hears something from us and conveys it exactly as he heard it. There are times when the one who conveys something is more mindful of it than the one who hears it.\""],[6703,"When the Messenger of Allah ﷺ went on a military expedition, he would say: 'O Allah, You are my support and You are my helper, and by You I fight.'"],[6704,"We went on a campaign with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ in the expedition of Tabuk, and the mounts suffered severe hardship. They complained to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ about the hardship of their mounts. So the Messenger of Allah ﷺ waited for them at a narrow pass where the people marched, saying: 'Pass in the name of Allah.' He began to blow on their backs, saying: 'O Allah, carry them in Your way, for You carry on the strong and the weak, the moist and the dry, on land and at sea.'\" Fadalah said: \"When we reached Madinah, their reins began to pull us, so I said: 'This is the supplication of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ concerning the strong and the weak, but what about the moist and the dry?' When we reached Syria, we fought the campaign of Cyprus, and I saw the ships and what they carried, and I knew the supplication of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ."],[6705,"When he encountered a people, he would say: 'O Allah, we place You before their chests and seek refuge in You from their evils.'"],[6706,"\"O Allah, bless my community in its early mornings.\" He said: When the Prophet ﷺ dispatched a raiding party, he would send them at the beginning of the day."],[6707,"I came to the Prophet ﷺ seeking his help concerning a debt owed by my father. He said, “I will come to you.” I said to my wife, “The Messenger of Allah ﷺ is coming to us, so be careful not to speak to him or bother him.” He ﷺ came, and I slaughtered a domestic animal we had. He said, “O Jabir, it is as if you knew our love for meat!” When he left, my wife said to him, “O Messenger of Allah, pray for me and my husband.” He did so. Then I said to her, “Did I not tell you?” She replied, “The Messenger of Allah ﷺ would enter my house and leave without praying for us?!”"],[6708,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, \"O Allah, forgive my people for they do not know.\""],[6709,"When the Messenger of Allah ﷺ saw the crescent moon, he said, \"O Allah, let it appear over us with security, faith, safety, Islam, and success in what we love and what pleases You. Our Lord and your Lord is Allah.\""],[6710,"When the Messenger of Allah ﷺ lay down to sleep, he would place his right hand under his right cheek and then say: 'O Allah, protect me from Your punishment on the day You resurrect Your servants.'"],[6711,"When he lay down to sleep, he would place his right hand under his right cheek and say: 'O Allah, protect me from Your punishment on the day You resurrect Your servants.'"],[6712,"He used to say when he settled into his bed: 'Praise be to Allah who sufficed me and sheltered me and gave me drink. Praise be to Allah who bestowed favor upon me and was generous. Praise be to Allah who gave me and granted abundantly. Praise be to Allah in every situation. O Allah, Lord of everything, Owner of everything, and God of everything, to You belongs everything. I seek refuge in You from the Fire.' *"],[6713,"When the Prophet ﷺ retired to his bed, he would say: 'O Allah, in Your name I live and in Your name I die.' And when he woke up, he would say: 'Praise be to Allah who gave us life after He caused us to die, and to Him is the resurrection.'"],[6714,"When he retired to his bed, he would say: “Praise be to Allah who fed us, gave us drink, and sufficed us—how many are there who have no one to suffice them and no one to shelter them?”"],[6715,"Ibn ʿUmar, when he retired to his bed, would say: “O Allah, You created my soul and You take it. Yours is its death and its life. O Allah, if You take it, forgive it; and if You keep it alive, protect it. O Allah, I ask You for well-being.” A man from his children said to him: “Did ʿUmar used to say this?” He said: “Rather, one better than ʿUmar used to say it.” We thought he meant the Prophet ﷺ."],[6716,"When he lay down, he would say: “O Allah, I have submitted my soul to You, turned my face to You, and entrusted my affair to You, out of hope and fear of You. There is no refuge or escape from You except to You.”"],[6717,"“The Messenger of Allah ﷺ, when he wanted to sleep, would join his hands, blow into them, then recite: ‘Say: He is Allah, the One,’ ‘Say: I seek refuge in the Lord of the daybreak,’ and ‘Say: I seek refuge in the Lord of mankind.’ Then he would wipe with them his face, his head, and the rest of his body.” ʿAqīl said: “I saw Ibn Shihāb do that.”"],[6718,"“The Prophet ﷺ, when he retired to his bed, would join his palms, blow into them, and recite into them: ‘Say: He is Allah, the One,’ ‘Say: I seek refuge in the Lord of the daybreak,’ and ‘Say: I seek refuge in the Lord of mankind.’ Then he would wipe with them as much of his body as he could. He would do that three times.”"],[6719,"I used to spend the night with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and would bring him water for his ablution and his needs. When he stood at night, he would say, \"Glory be to my Lord and with His praise; glory be to my Lord and with His praise,\" for a long while. Then he would say, \"Glory be to the Lord of the worlds; glory be to the Lord of the worlds,\" for a long while."],[6720,"I used to spend the night by the chamber of the Prophet ﷺ, and I would hear him when he got up at night. He would say, \"Glory be to the Lord of the worlds,\" for a long while, then say, \"Glory be to Allah and with His praise,\" for a long while."],[6721,"When the Messenger of Allah ﷺ turned restlessly in the night, he would say: 'There is no god but Allah, the One, the Subduer, Lord of the heavens and the earth and whatever is between them, the Mighty, the Oft-Forgiving.'"],[6722,"When he woke in the night, he would say: 'There is no god but Allah. Glory be to You. O Allah, I ask Your forgiveness for my sin and I ask You for Your mercy. O Allah, increase me in knowledge and do not deviate my heart after You have guided me, and grant me mercy from Yourself. Indeed, You are the Bestower.'"],[6723,"When the Prophet ﷺ retired to his bed, he would say: 'O Allah, in Your name I live and in Your name I die.' And when he woke up, he would say: 'Praise be to Allah who gave us life after He caused us to die, and to Him is the resurrection.'"],[6724,"«O Allah, whoever believes in You and bears witness that I am Your Messenger, make the meeting with You beloved to him, make Your decree easy for him, and give him little of this world. And whoever does not believe in You and does not bear witness that I am Your Messenger, do not make the meeting with You beloved to him, do not make Your decree easy for him, and give him much of this world.»"],[6725,"O Allah, make the provision of the family of Muhammad sufficient."],[6726,"O Allah, make the provision of the family of Muhammad sufficient."],[6727,"The Prophet ﷺ used to say: \"O Allah, keep me away from reprehensible manners, desires, evils, and ailments.\""],[6728,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to say: \"O Allah, forgive me my serious sins and my jesting, my error and my intention, and all of that is with me.\""],[6729,"The Prophet ﷺ used to say: \"O Allah, purify me from sins with snow, hail, and water. O Allah, purify me from sins as a garment is purified from filth.\""],[6730,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to say: \"O Allah, to You is praise, filling the heavens and filling the earth and filling whatever You will after that. O Allah, purify me with snow, hail, and cold water. O Allah, purify me from my sins as a white garment is purified from filth.\""],[6731,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to supplicate with this supplication: \"My Lord, forgive me my error, my ignorance, and my extravagance in my affair, and what You know better than I. O Allah, forgive me my mistakes, my intention, my ignorance, my seriousness, and my jesting, and all of that is with me. O Allah, forgive me what I have done and what I have delayed, what I have concealed and what I have made public. Indeed, You are the Advancer and You are the Delayer, and You have power over all things.\""],[6732,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to say, \"O Allah, You have beautified my physical appearance, so beautify my character [as well].\""],[6733,"O Allah, make our well-being good in all matters, and deliver us from the disgrace of this world and the punishment of the Hereafter."],[6734,"the Prophet (saas) used to say: \"Allahumma inni as'alukal-huda wat-tuqa wal-'afaf wal-ghina (O Allah, I ask You for guidance, piety, chastity and affluence).\" (Using translation from Ibn Mājah 3832)"],[6735,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: allāhumma lā sahlan illā mā jaʿaltahū sahlan, wa-anta tajʿal al-ḥazna sahlan idhā shiʾta (O Allah, there is no ease except what You make easy, and You make the difficult easy if You Will.)"],[6736,"The Prophet ﷺ used to say, 'My Lord, help me and do not help against me, support me and do not support against me, devise for me and do not devise against me, guide me and make guidance easy for me, and support me against those who transgress against me. My Lord, make me grateful to You, remembering You, repentant to You, obedient to You, humble to You, devoted, returning in repentance. My Lord, accept my repentance, wash away my sin, answer my supplication, make firm my proof, guide my heart, direct my tongue, and remove the rancor from my heart.'"],[6737,"The Prophet ﷺ used to say, 'My Lord, help me and do not help against me, support me and do not support against me, devise for me and do not devise against me, guide me and make guidance easy for me, and support me against those who transgress against me. My Lord, make me grateful to You, remembering You, repentant to You, obedient to You, humble to You, devoted, returning in repentance. My Lord, accept my repentance, wash away my sin, answer my supplication, make firm my proof, guide my heart, direct my tongue, and remove the rancor from my heart.'"],[6738,"From 'Uthman b. Abi al-'As and a woman from Quraysh that they both heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: 'O Allah, forgive me my sins and my deliberate acts.' The other said: 'I heard him say: O Allah, I seek guidance from You for the most rightly-guided of my affairs, and I seek refuge in You from the evil of my soul.'"],[6739,"The hearts of the children of Adam are between two fingers of the fingers of the Most Merciful, like a single heart that He turns as He wills. Then the Messenger of Allah ﷺ says: 'O Allah, turn our hearts toward obedience to You.'"],[6740,"The oath of the Prophet ﷺ, by which he used to swear, was: \"No, by the Turner of the hearts.\""],[6741,"The Prophet ﷺ used to say: “O Allah, I ask You for guidance and right direction. By guidance, I mean Your guiding me to the right path; by right direction, I mean the straightness of an arrow.” And the Prophet of Allah ﷺ forbade me from wearing qassi (silk clothes), from using saddle cushions, and from wearing a ring on the index or middle finger."],[6742,"\"O Allah, I ask You for beneficial knowledge and I seek refuge in You from knowledge that does not benefit.\""],[6743,"He used to say: \"O Allah, I seek refuge in You from knowledge that does not benefit, from deeds that are not raised, from a heart that does not humble itself, and from words that are not heard.\""],[6744,"“O Allah, I seek refuge in You from a soul that is not satisfied, and I seek refuge in You from a prayer that does not benefit, and I seek refuge in You from a supplication that is not heard, and I seek refuge in You from a heart that does not humble itself.”"],[6745,"“I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ seeking refuge in Allah from the punishment of the grave.”"],[6746,"The Prophet of Allah ﷺ did not pray four rak'ahs or two except that I heard him supplicating: “O Allah, I seek refuge in You from the punishment of the Fire and from the punishment of the grave, and from the trial of the chest and the evil of life and death.”"],[6747,"“He used to seek refuge from the hardship of affliction, the attainment of misery, an evil decree, and the gloating of enemies.”"],[6748,"He used to say, “O Allah, I seek refuge in You from incapacity, laziness, old age, miserliness, cowardice, the punishment of the grave, and the evil of the false messiah (al-Masīḥ al-Dajjāl).”"],[6749,"He used to supplicate, “O Allah, I seek refuge in You from laziness, old age, incapacity, miserliness, the trial of the false messiah, and the punishment of the grave.”"],[6750,"He used to supplicate with these words: “I seek refuge in Allah from being returned to the worst part of life (aradhal al-ʿumur), and I seek refuge in Allah from miserliness and cowardice, and I seek refuge in Allah from the trial of the chest and the oppression of men.”"],[6751,"'I seek refuge in Allah from disbelief and debt.' A man said: 'O Messenger of Allah, is debt equated with disbelief?' He said: 'Yes.'"],[6752,"He used to supplicate: 'O Allah, forgive us our sins, our wrongdoing, our jesting and our seriousness, our intentional acts, and all of that is with us. O Allah, I seek refuge in You from being overcome by debt, from being overcome by enemies, and from the gloating of enemies.'"],[6753,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to say, 'O Allah, I seek refuge in You from disbelief, poverty, and the punishment of the grave.'"],[6754,"He used to say: 'O Allah, I seek refuge in You from disbelief and poverty.' A man said: 'O Messenger of Allah, are they equal?' He ﷺ said: 'Yes.'"],[6755,"He used to say, “O Allah, I seek refuge in You from leprosy, madness, and severe diseases.”"],[6756,"He used to seek refuge from the evil of life and death, the punishment of the grave, and the evil of the trial of the false messiah (al-Masīḥ al-Dajjāl)."],[6757,"O Allah, make the provision of the family of Muhammad sufficient."],[6758,"The Prophet ﷺ used to supplicate saying: 'O Allah, I seek refuge in You from incapacity, laziness, miserliness, senility, hardness of heart, heedlessness, humiliation, and poverty. And I seek refuge in You from poverty, disbelief, associating partners with You, hypocrisy, seeking reputation, and showing off. And I seek refuge in You from deafness, dumbness, insanity, leprosy, and evil diseases.'"],[6759,"\"I went for Hajj with 'Umar, and in Muzdalifah, I heard him say that the Prophet [SAW] used to seek refuge from five things: 'Allahumma inni a'udhu bika minal-bukhli, wal-jubni, wa a'udhu bika min su'il-'umuri, wa a'udhu bika min fitnatis-sadri, wa a'udhu bika min 'adhabil-qabr (O Allah, I seek refuge with You from miserliness and cowardice, and I seek refuge with You from reaching the age of second childhood, and I seek refuge in You from the ills of the heart, and I seek refuge in You from the torment of the grave.'\" (Using translation from Nasāʾī 5497)"],[6760,"Among the supplications of the Prophet ﷺ was: 'O Allah, I seek refuge in You from hunger, for it is an evil bedfellow, and I seek refuge in You from treachery, for it is an evil inner companion.'"],[6761,"The Prophet ﷺ used to say: \"O Allah, I seek refuge in Thee from poverty\", lack and abasement, and I seek refuge in Thee lest I cause or suffer wrong.\" (Using translation from Abū Dāʾūd 1544)"],[6762,"I asked the Mother of the Believers ʿĀʾishah about what the Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to supplicate. She said: He used to say: 'O Allah, I seek refuge in You from the evil of what I have done and from the evil of what I have not done.'"],[6763,"I asked ʿĀʾishah: 'Tell me something that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to supplicate with.' She said: He used to say ﷺ: 'O Allah, I seek refuge in You from the evil of what I have done and from the evil of what I have not done.'"],[6764,"He used to say: 'O Allah, I seek refuge in You from an evil neighbor in the abode of permanence, for the neighbor in the desert moves away.'"],[6765,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ came to us, and my wife called out to him, saying, “O Messenger of Allah, invoke blessings upon me and upon my husband.” He said, “May Allah bless you and your husband.”"],[6766,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ liked to supplicate three times and seek forgiveness three times."],[6767,"Indeed, I repent seventy times a day."],[6768,"Indeed, I seek Allah's forgiveness and repent to Him more than seventy times a day."],[6769,"I was a man with a sharp tongue against my family. I said: 'O Messenger of Allah, I fear that my tongue will cause me to enter the Fire.' He ﷺ said: 'Where are you with regard to seeking forgiveness? Indeed, I seek Allah's forgiveness a hundred times a day.'"],[6770,"I would sometimes count for the Messenger of Allah ﷺ in a single sitting a hundred times: 'My Lord, forgive me and turn to me; indeed You are the Accepting of repentance, the Merciful.'"],[6771,"I have never seen anyone say \"I seek forgiveness from Allah and repent to Him\" more than the Messenger of Allah ﷺ ."],[6772,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to say frequently before his death, “Glory be to Allah and with His praise; I seek Allah’s forgiveness and I turn to Him in repentance.” She said: I said, “O Messenger of Allah, you are making frequent a supplication that you did not make before this?” He said, “Indeed my Lord, mighty and exalted,”"],[6773,"When {When Allah’s help and victory comes} was revealed, to the end of it, I never saw the Messenger of Allah ﷺ pray any prayer except that he said, “Glory be to You, O Allah, and with Your praise; O Allah, forgive me.”"],[6774,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ would supplicate with this supplication: 'O Allah, grant us good in this world and good in the Hereafter, and protect us from the punishment of the Fire.'"],[6775,"They said to Anas b. Malik: \"Pray to Allah for us.\" He said: \"O Allah, give us good in this world and good in the Hereafter, and protect us from the punishment of the Fire.\" They said: \"Increase for us.\" So he repeated it. They said: \"Increase for us.\" So he repeated it. They said: \"Increase for us.\" He said: \"What do you want? I asked for you the best of this world and the Hereafter.\""],[6776,"I said to Anas b. Malik, 'Tell me about a supplication the Prophet ﷺ used to make.' He said, 'O Allah, give us good in this world and good in the Hereafter, and protect us from the punishment of the Fire.'"],[6777,"Qatadah asked Anas, 'Which supplication did the Prophet ﷺ make most often?' He said, 'The supplication the Prophet ﷺ made most often was: O Allah, our Lord, give us good in this world and good in the Hereafter, and protect us from the punishment of the Fire.'"],[6778,"The Prophet ﷺ visited a man who was so ill that he had become like a chick. He ﷺ said, 'Did you supplicate to Allah for anything?' He said, 'Yes. I used to say, O Allah, whatever punishment You would give me in the Hereafter, hasten it for me in this world.' The Prophet ﷺ said, 'You cannot bear it—or you cannot endure it. Why didn't you say, O Allah, give us good in this world and good in the Hereafter, and protect us from the punishment of the Fire?' He said, 'So he supplicated to Allah and He healed him.'"],[6779,"“The Prophet ﷺ used to raise his hands in supplication until the whiteness of his armpits was visible.”"],[6780,"He saw the Messenger of Allah ﷺ near the oil stones, close to al-Zawra', supplicating, raising his palms before his face, not raising them above his head."],[6781,"He saw the Messenger of Allah ﷺ praying for rain near the oil stones, close to al-Zawra', standing in supplication, praying for rain, raising his palms, not raising them above his head, with the inner sides of his palms facing his face."],[6782,"He saw Bishr b. Marwan raising his hands on the pulpit and said, \"May Allah make these two hands ugly. I have seen the Messenger of Allah ﷺ not going beyond saying with his hand like this, and he pointed with his index finger.\""],[6783,"\"I have not seen the Messenger of Allah ﷺ raising his hands in supplication on a pulpit or elsewhere, but I saw him saying like this.\" Abu Sa'id made a slight curve with his right index finger."],[6784,"The people complained to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ about drought and lack of rain. He ordered a pulpit, and it was placed for him in the prayer area, and he promised the people a day to come out. Aisha said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ came out when the edge of the sun appeared and sat on the pulpit. He praised Allah and extolled Him, then said: “You have complained of the barrenness of your gardens and the withholding of rain from its usual time. Allah has commanded you to call upon Him and promised to answer you.” Then he said: “{All praise is due to Allah, Lord of the worlds, the Most Merciful, the Especially Merciful, Master of the Day of Judgment.} There is no deity but You; You do what You will. O Allah, You are Allah, there is no deity but You. You are the Self-Sufficient, and we are the needy. Send down upon us rain, and make what You send down a strength for us and a means to good.” Then he ﷺ raised his hands until we saw the whiteness of his armpits. Then he turned his back to the people and reversed or turned his cloak while still raising his hands. Then he faced the people, descended, and prayed two rak‘ahs. Allah brought forth clouds, thunder, lightning, and rain by Allah’s permission. We did not remain long in his mosque before the streams flowed. When the Messenger of Allah ﷺ saw the wetness of clothes on the people, he laughed until his premolars showed and said: “I bear witness that Allah is capable of all things and that I am the servant of Allah and His Messenger.”"],[6785,"I came to ʿĀʾishah to ask her about something, and she said, 'I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say in this house of mine: O Allah, whoever is placed in charge of any affair of my ummah and makes it difficult for them, make it difficult for him; and whoever is placed in charge of any affair of my ummah and is gentle with them, be gentle with him.'"],[6786,"I watched the Messenger of Allah ﷺ in a prayer he performed until it was near dawn. When the Messenger of Allah ﷺ finished his prayer, Khabbab came to him and said, \"O Messenger of Allah, may my father and mother be your ransom, you prayed a prayer tonight the like of which I have not seen you pray.\" He said, \"Yes, it was a prayer of hope and fear. I asked my Lord for three things; He granted me two and withheld one. I asked Him not to destroy us with what He destroyed previous nations, and He granted me that. I asked Him not to let an enemy from outside us prevail over us, and He granted me that. I asked Him not to divide us into factions, and He withheld that from me.\""],[6787,"That the Messenger of Allah ﷺ came one day from al-'Aliyah until he passed by the mosque of Banu Mu'awiyah, entered it, prayed two rak'ahs, and we prayed with him. Then he supplicated his Lord for a long time and then turned to us and said, \"I asked my Lord not to destroy my ummah by famine, and He granted me that. I asked Him not to make their might turn against themselves, but He withheld that from me.\""],[6788,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ as saying: Allah, the Exalted, folded for me the earth, or he said (the narrator is doubtful): My Lord folded for me the earth, so much so that I saw its easts and wests (i.e. the extremities). The kingdom of my community will reach as far as the earth was floded for me. The two treasures, the red and the white, were bestowed on me. I prayed to my Lord that He may not destroy my community by prevailing famine, and not give their control to an enemy who annihilates then en masse except from among themselves. My Lord said to me: Muhammad, If I make a decision, it is not withdrawn ; and I shall not destroy them by prevailing famine, and I shall not give their control to an enemy, except from among themselves, who exterminates them en masse, even if they are stormed from all sides of the earth ; only a section of them will destroy another section, and a section will captive another section. I am afraid about my community of those leaders who will lead astray. When the sword is used among my people, it will not be withdrawn from them till the Day of Resurrection, and the Last Hour will not come before the tribes of my people attach themselves to the polytheists and tribes of my people worship idols. There will be among my people thirty great liars each of them asserting that he is (Allah's) prophet, where as I am the seal of the Prophet s after whom (me) there will be no prophet ; and a section of my people will continue to hold to the truth - (according to the Ibn Isa's version: (will continue to dominate) - the agreed version goes: \"and will not be injured by those who oppose them, till Allah's command comes.\" (Using translation from Abū Dāʾūd 4252)"],[6789,"“O Allah, any believing servant whom I have cursed, make that a means of nearness to You on the Day of Resurrection.”"],[6790,"O Allah, I make a covenant with You that You will never break. I am only human, so whichever believer I have harmed, reviled, flogged, or cursed, make that for him a prayer, a purification, and a nearness by which You bring him near on the Day of Resurrection."],[6791,"The Prophet ﷺ used to say: “O Allah, I ask You for guidance and right direction. By guidance, I mean Your guiding me to the right path; by right direction, I mean the straightness of an arrow.” And the Prophet of Allah ﷺ forbade me from wearing qassi (silk clothes), from using saddle cushions, and from wearing a ring on the index or middle finger."],[6792,"He used to let his hair hang down, and the polytheists used to part their hair, while the People of the Book used to let it hang down. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ loved to agree with the People of the Book in matters about which nothing had been revealed to him, so the Messenger of Allah ﷺ parted his hair."],[6793,"Ibn ʿAbbās and some people from the companions of the Prophet ﷺ sent me to Umm Salamah, the wife of the Prophet ﷺ, to ask her which days the Prophet ﷺ fasted most. She said, \"Saturday and Sunday.\" I returned to them and told them, but they rejected that from me and thought that I had not memorized correctly, so they sent me back. She said the same thing, and I told them. They all stood up and said, \"We sent you about such and such, and you claimed that she said such and such.\" She said, \"He spoke the truth: the Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to fast on Saturday and Sunday more than any other days, and he would say, 'They are two festivals for the polytheists, so I like to differ from them.'\""],[6794,"The religion will continue to be manifest as long as people hasten the breaking of the fast, for the Jews and Christians delay it."],[6795,"\"I lost my camel, so I went to search for it in Arafah. I saw the Messenger of Allah ﷺ standing with the people in Arafah, so I said, 'By Allah, this is from the blessings, so what is the reason for him standing here?'\""],[6796,"\"The people of the pre-Islamic era would not depart until they saw the sun on Thabir, but the Prophet ﷺ differed from them and departed before sunrise.\""],[6797,"That the Prophet ﷺ changed the name of 'Asiya and said, \"You are Jamila.\""],[6798,"That the Prophet ﷺ changed the name of 'Asiya and said, \"You are Jamila.\""],[6799,"That the Prophet ﷺ \"passed by a land called Ghadira and named it Khadira.\""],[6800,"That the Prophet ﷺ said to his grandfather, \"What is your name?\" He said, \"Hazn.\" The Prophet ﷺ said, \"Rather, you are Sahl.\" He said, \"I will not change a name my father gave me.\" Sa'id said, \"So harshness has remained among us ever since.\""],[6801,"That the Prophet ﷺ \"heard a man saying, 'O Shihab,' and said, 'You are Hisham.'\""],[6802,"\"Birds proceed by divine decree, and he liked a good omen.\""],[6803,"\"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to take good omens and liked a good name.\""],[6804,"\"There is no contagion and no evil omen, and I love a good omen.\""],[6805,"\"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ did not take evil omens from anything, except that when he intended to come to a land, he would ask about its name. If it was good, joy would be seen in his face, and if it was bad, that would be seen in his face.\""],[6806,"Abu had the name 'Aziz, and the Prophet ﷺ named him 'Abd al-Rahman."],[6807,"Juwayriyah bt. al-Harith had the name Barrah, and the Messenger of Allah ﷺ named her Juwayriyah."],[6808,"O Allah, make the provision of the family of Muhammad sufficient."],[6809,"'There is no Tiyarah, and Tiyarah is upon the one who practices it. And if it be in anything, it is in the house, the horse, and the woman.'"],[6810,"'There is no Tiyarah, and the best of it is Fa'l (a good omen).' It was said: O Messenger of Allah, what is Fa'l? He said: 'A good word that one of you hears.'"],[6811,"I said to Aisha: Did the Messenger of Allah ﷺ use to pray the Duha prayer? She said: No, except when he returned from a journey."],[6812,"I said to Aisha: Did the Messenger of Allah ﷺ use to pray the Duha prayer? She said: No, except when he returned from his absence. I said: Did the Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to pray sitting? She said: Yes, after old age had weakened him. I said: Did the Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to join between surahs? She said: Yes, from the Mufassal. I said: Did the Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to fast a specific month other than Ramadan? She said: By Allah, he did not fast a specific month other than Ramadan until he passed away ﷺ, nor did he break it until he passed away ﷺ."],[6813,"That the Prophet ﷺ would not pray the Duha prayer except when he returned from being away."],[6814,"I asked Aisha: Did the Messenger of Allah ﷺ use to pray the Duha prayer? She said: Yes, four rak'ahs, and he would add whatever Allah willed."],[6815,"I did not see the Messenger of Allah ﷺ praying his supererogatory prayer while sitting until he was ﷺ one year before his death. Then I saw him praying his supererogatory prayer while sitting, and he would recite the surah slowly until it became longer than the longest of them."],[6816,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ entered my house and prayed the Duha prayer, eight rak'ahs."],[6817,"\"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ did not perform the Duha prayer.\" And A'ishah used to perform it, and she used to say: 'The Messenger of Allah ﷺ abandoned many deeds fearing that the people would follow him and it would be made obligatory upon them.'"],[6818,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ recited (Qinata) a Surah after the Rukoo, supplicating against certain people from the Arabs, then he stopped."],[6819,"«I prayed behind the Prophet ﷺ and he did not perform Qunut; I prayed behind Abu Bakr and he did not perform Qunut; I prayed behind ʿUmar and he did not perform Qunut; I prayed behind ʿUthman and he did not perform Qunut; I prayed behind ʿAli and he did not perform Qunut.» Then he said: “O my son, it is an innovation.”"],[6820,"“The Messenger of Allah ﷺ prayed inside the House, and there will come someone who forbids that, while Ibn Abbas was sitting at his side.”"],[6821,"“The Messenger of Allah ﷺ prayed in the House between two pillars.”"],[6822,"On the day of the conquest, the Messenger of Allah ﷺ entered the Ka’bah, and with him were Bilal and Uthman ibn Talhah. They locked the door from inside. When they came out, I asked Bilal, “Where did the Messenger of Allah ﷺ pray?” He said, “I saw him pray facing forward when he entered, between the two pillars on his right.” Then I blamed myself for not asking him how many units the Messenger of Allah ﷺ prayed."],[6823,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ entered the House, and with him were Usamah ibn Zayd, Bilal, and Uthman ibn Talhah. They shut the door on themselves for a long time, then it was opened. I was the first to enter. I met Bilal and said, “Where did the Messenger of Allah ﷺ pray?” He said, “Between the two front pillars.” And I forgot to ask him how many units he prayed."],[6824,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ entered the Ka’bah, and with him were Usamah ibn Zayd, Uthman ibn Talhah, and Bilal ibn Rabah. He locked it and stayed inside. Ibn Umar said: I asked Bilal when he came out, “Where did the Messenger of Allah ﷺ pray?” He said, “He placed one pillar to his left and two pillars to his right, and three pillars behind him.” At that time the House had six pillars."],[6825,"I saw Ibn Umar entering the House, until when he was between the two pillars he prayed four units. I stood at his side, and when he finished I said, “Where did the Messenger of Allah ﷺ pray?” He said, “Here.”"],[6826,"The Prophet ﷺ would pray while between him and the qiblah there was a distance of three cubits."],[6827,"The Prophet ﷺ entered the Ka'bah, in which there were six pillars. He stood by each pillar and supplicated, but he did not pray."],[6828,"I said to 'Ata': Did you hear Ibn 'Abbas say: You have only been commanded to circumambulate, not to enter it? He said: He did not forbid entering it, but I heard him say:"],[6829,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ performed four 'Umrah, one of which was in the month of Rajab. We disliked discrediting him or arguing with him. We heard Aisha in her chamber and Urwah said to her, \"O Mother of the Believers, don't you listen to what Abu 'Abdur-Rahman is saying?\" She asked, \"What is he saying?\" Urwah replied, \"He is saying that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ performed four 'Umrah and one of them was in the month of Rajab.\" Aisha said, \"May Allah have mercy on Abu 'Abdur-Rahman! The Messenger of Allah ﷺ never performed an 'Umrah except that he was a witness, and he never performed 'Umrah in the month of Rajab at all.\""],[6830,"“That the Prophet ﷺ performed qunūt in the dawn and sunset prayers.”"],[6831,"“By Allah, I am the closest of you in prayer to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ.” And Abū Hurayrah “used to perform qunūt in the noon prayer, the night prayer, and the dawn prayer after saying ‘Allah hears the one who praises Him,’ then he would supplicate for the believers and curse the disbelievers.”"],[6832,"«The Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to say when he raised his head from bowing in the Fajr prayer in the second rakʿah after “Samiʿa Allahu liman hamidah”: “Our Lord, to You is all praise. O Allah, save al-Walid b. al-Walid, Salamah b. Hisham, ʿAyyash b. Abi Rabiʿah, and the weak among the believers. O Allah, tighten Your grip on Muḍar and make it years like the years of Yusuf.”»"],[6833,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ bowed in prayer, then raised his head and said: “Ghifar—may Allah forgive them—Aslam—may Allah grant them peace—and ʿUṣayyah disobeyed Allah and His Messenger. O Allah, curse Bani Liḥyan. O Allah, curse Riʿlan and Dhakwan.” Then he said the takbir and fell into prostration. He said: Thus the cursing of the disbelievers came to be for that reason."],[6834,"«The Messenger of Allah ﷺ performed Qunut for a month after bowing, supplicating against tribes among the tribes of the Arabs, then he abandoned it.»"],[6835,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ performed Qunut in the ʿatamah prayer for a month, saying in his Qunut: “O Allah, save al-Walid b. al-Walid. O Allah, deliver Salamah b. Hisham. O Allah, deliver ʿAyyash b. Abi Rabiʿah. O Allah, deliver the weak among the believers. O Allah, tighten Your grip on Muḍar. O Allah, make it years upon them like the years of Yusuf.” Abu Hurayrah said: And one day the Messenger of Allah ﷺ entered the morning and did not supplicate for them, so I mentioned that to him, and he ﷺ said: “Do you not see that they have arrived?”"],[6836,"That he heard the Prophet ﷺ say in the Fajr prayer when he raised his head from bowing: “Our Lord, and to You is all praise,” in the last rakʿah, then he said: “O Allah, curse so-and-so and so-and-so,” supplicating against people among the hypocrites. Then Allah revealed: {Not for you is the decision whether He turns to them or punishes them, for they are wrongdoers}."],[6837,"He used to supplicate against peoples in his Qunut.” Then Allah revealed: {Not for you is the decision whether He turns to them or punishes them, for they are wrongdoers}."],[6838,"«The Hour will not come until a fire emerges that illuminates the necks of camels in Busra.»"],[6839,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ prayed Zuhr or 'Asr and said the salutation after two rak'ahs. Dhu al-Shimalayn b. 'Abd 'Amr, who was an ally of Banu Zuhrah, said: 'Has the prayer been shortened or did you forget, O Messenger of Allah?' The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: 'What is Dhu al-Yadayn saying?' They said: 'He has spoken the truth, O Prophet of Allah.' He said: So he completed with them the two rak'ahs that he had missed, then he said the salutation."],[6840,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ left after two rak'ahs. Dhu al-Yadayn said to him: 'Has the prayer been shortened or did you forget, O Messenger of Allah?' The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: 'Has Dhu al-Yadayn spoken the truth?' The people said: 'Yes.' The Messenger of Allah ﷺ stood and prayed two more rak'ahs, then said the salutation, then said the takbir and prostrated like his prostration or longer, then raised his head, then said the takbir and prostrated like his prostration or longer, then raised his head."],[6841,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ prayed one of the two evening prayers with us, and he did not pray with us except two rak'ahs. A man called Dhu al-Yadayn from Khuza'ah said to him: 'O Messenger of Allah, has the prayer been shortened or did you forget?' He said: 'None of that happened.' He said: 'O Messenger of Allah, you only prayed two rak'ahs with us.' The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: 'What is Dhu al-Yadayn saying?' and he turned to the people. They said: 'O Messenger of Allah, you only prayed two rak'ahs with us.' The Prophet ﷺ stood and faced the qiblah and prayed the remaining two rak'ahs, then said the salutation, then prostrated two prostrations while sitting."],[6842,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ prayed one of the two evening prayers with us – either he said Zuhr or he said 'Asr. He said: My stronger assumption is that it was 'Asr. He prayed two rak'ahs with us then said the salutation and went to a piece of wood at the front of the mosque and placed his hands on it, one on top of the other. The swift among the people left, and they began to say: 'The prayer has been shortened.' Among the people were Abu Bakr and 'Umar ؓ , but they were too afraid to ask the Messenger of Allah ﷺ about that. A man called Dhu al-Yadayn said to him: 'Has the prayer been shortened, O Messenger of Allah, or did you forget?' He said: 'The prayer has not been shortened, and I did not forget.' He said: 'Rather, you forgot, O Messenger of Allah.' He said: 'Is it so?' They said: 'Yes.' He said: So he returned and prayed two rak'ahs with us, then said the salutation, then prostrated two prostrations and prolonged them for about as long as his prostration, then raised his head, then made the second prostration and prolonged it for about as long as his prostration, then raised his head."],[6843,"The Prophet ﷺ heard a man reciting in the mosque, and he said, “May Allah have mercy on him. He has reminded me of a verse I had been made to forget.”"],[6844,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said the salam in three rak'ahs of Asr. Al-Khirbaq said to him: \"O Messenger of Allah, did you forget or has the prayer been shortened?\" He ﷺ said: \"Did al-Khirbaq speak the truth?\" They said: \"Yes.\""],[6845,"The Prophet ﷺ named the two prostrations of forgetfulness \"the two humiliating ones.\""],[6846,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ led us in prayer and added or omitted. It was said, 'O Messenger of Allah, has something occurred in the prayer?' He ﷺ said, 'If something had occurred, I would have informed you of it, but I am only a human being; I forget as you forget. So whichever of you doubts in his prayer, let him consider what is most likely correct, complete it accordingly, then give the salutation, and prostrate two prostrations.'"],[6847,"Alqamah led us in Zuhr as five (rak'ahs). Ibrahim said to him, 'And you, O one-eyed?' He said, 'Yes.' He said, 'So he prostrated two prostrations.' Then Alqamah narrated from 'Abd Allah from the Prophet ﷺ the like of that."],[6848,"When one of you doubts in his prayer, let him cast aside the doubt and build upon certainty. If he becomes certain of completion, he prostrates two prostrations. If his prayer was complete, the rak'ah is voluntary and the two prostrations are voluntary; and if it was deficient, the rak'ah completes his prayer and the two prostrations humiliate Satan's nose."],[6849,"When one of you prays and does not know whether he prayed three or four (rak'ahs), let him pray one rak'ah and prostrate two prostrations before the salutation. If it was the fourth, the two prostrations are a humiliation for Satan; and if it was the fifth, the two prostrations make it even."],[6850,"When one of you doubts and does not know how many he prayed, three or four, let him stand and pray one rak'ah, completing its bowing and prostration, then prostrate two prostrations while he is sitting. If he had prayed five, the two prostrations make it even; and if he had prayed four, the two prostrations are a humiliation for Satan."],[6851,"“The Prophet ﷺ prayed with them, then prostrated the two prostrations of forgetfulness, then recited the tashahhud and gave the salutation.”"],[6852,"The Prophet ﷺ prayed Ẓuhr or ʿAṣr as three rakʿahs. Someone said that to him, and he said, “Is it so?” They said, “Yes.” So he prayed one rakʿah, then recited the tashahhud and gave the salutation, then prostrated the two prostrations of forgetfulness, then gave the salutation."],[6853,"“I prayed Maghrib with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and he forgot and gave the salutation after two rakʿahs, then turned away.” A man said to him, “O Messenger of Allah, you forgot and gave the salutation after two rakʿahs.” “He ordered Bilāl to announce the iqāmah for the prayer, then he completed that remaining rakʿah.” And I asked the people about the man who said, “O Messenger of Allah, you forgot,” and it was said to me, “Do you know him?” I said, “No, unless I see him.” A man passed by me, and I said, “It is he.” They said, “This is Ṭalḥah b. ʿUbayd Allāh.”"],[6854,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ prayed with us one of the two afternoon prayers, I think it was Ẓuhr, for two rakʿahs. Then he went to a piece of wood in the qiblah of the mosque, placed his hands on it, one over the other, and some people rushed out saying, “The prayer has been shortened.” Among the people were Abū Bakr and ʿUmar, ؓ , and they were too awed to speak to him. Among the people was a man with either short or long hands called Dhū al-Yadayn. He said, “Has the prayer been shortened, O Messenger of Allah, or did you forget?” The Prophet ﷺ said, “The prayer has not been shortened, and I have not forgotten.” He said, “Rather you forgot.” The Prophet said, “Is Dhū al-Yadayn telling the truth?” They said, “Yes.” So he prayed with us two rakʿahs, then gave the salutation, then said the takbīr and prostrated like his prostration or longer, then raised his head and said the takbīr, then said the takbīr and prostrated like his prostration or longer, then raised his head and said the takbīr."],[6855,"“The Messenger of Allah ﷺ prayed Ẓuhr with us and stood up while there was still sitting due. When he was at the end of his prayer, he prostrated twice while seated.”"],[6856,"“The Messenger of Allah ﷺ stood up after two rakʿahs, and the people stood up with him. When he sat after four, the people awaited his salutation. He said the takbīr and prostrated, then said the takbīr and prostrated before giving the salutation.”"],[6857,"«The Messenger of Allah ﷺ stood up from the noon prayer while he still had sitting (due). When he completed his prayer, he prostrated twice while sitting before saying the salam, and the people prostrated with him in place of the sitting he had forgotten.»"],[6858,"“The Messenger of Allah ﷺ stood up after two rakʿahs of Ẓuhr and did not sit. When he finished his prayer, he prostrated twice, then gave the salutation after that.”"],[6859,"“The Prophet ﷺ prayed and stood up in the even rakʿah in which he intended to sit. We said subḥān Allāh, but he continued. When he finished his prayer, he prostrated twice while seated.”"],[6860,"ʿUqbah b. ʿĀmir led us in prayer and stood up while he still had sitting (due). The people behind him said: \"Glory be to Allah,\" but he did not sit. When he finished his prayer, he prostrated twice while sitting and said: \"I heard you saying 'Glory be to Allah' so that I would sit, but that is not the sunnah; rather the sunnah is what I did.\""],[6861,"«The Messenger of Allah ﷺ stood up from the noon prayer while he still had sitting (due). When he completed his prayer, he prostrated twice while sitting before saying the salam, and the people prostrated with him in place of the sitting he had forgotten.»"],[6862,"“The Messenger of Allah ﷺ prayed five prayers with them. When he gave the salutation, that was said to him, so he faced the qiblah and prostrated twice while seated.”"],[6863,"From the Prophet ﷺ, it was narrated that he prayed Dhuhr prayer five units. It was asked, \"Was anything added in the prayer, O Messenger of Allah?\" He ﷺ said, \"What is that?\" It was said, \"Verily, you prayed five units, then you prostrated twice after making the salaam.\""],[6864,"“Satan comes to one of you while he is in his prayer to confuse him until he does not know how many he has prayed. When any of you experiences that, let him prostrate twice while seated.”"],[6865,"\"The Hour will not come until it is no longer said on earth: 'God, God.'\""],[6866,"We used to greet the Prophet ﷺ and he would respond to us, meaning during prayer. When we came from the land of Abyssinia, I greeted him and he did not respond to me. I was seized by what was near and what was far, so I sat down until he finished the prayer. I said to him, “You used to respond to us.” He ﷺ said, “Allah brings about whatever He wills, and He has brought about a decree that you should not speak during prayer.”"],[6867,"During the time of the Prophet ﷺ, one of us would talk to his companion during prayer about his need, until this verse was revealed: {Guard strictly the prayers, and the middle prayer, and stand before Allah devoutly obedient} [2:238]. Then we were commanded to be silent."],[6868,"“A man would talk to his companion during prayer about his need in the time of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, until {Guard strictly the prayers} was revealed” — the verse."],[6869,"I said, “O Messenger of Allah, we are recently from the pre-Islamic era, and Allah has brought Islam. Some of our men practice augury.” He said, “That is something they find in their hearts, but it does not harm them.”"],[6870,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ ate some meat, and with him were Abu Bakr and Umar ؓ, then they stood up for the 'Asr prayer and did not perform wudu'."],[6871,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ ate from a shoulder, or he said: \"He gnawed on a rib,\" then prayed without performing wudu'."],[6872,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ ate the shoulder of a sheep, then prayed, and did not perform wudu'."],[6873,"I saw the Messenger of Allah ﷺ cutting from the shoulder of a sheep and eating from it. Then he was called to prayer, so he stood up, threw down the knife, and prayed without performing wudu'."],[6874,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ ate the shoulder of a sheep, then stood up for prayer and prayed without performing wudu' and without rinsing his mouth."],[6875,"The Prophet ﷺ came to a woman of the Ansar. She spread a covering for him near a palm trunk, sprinkled water around it, slaughtered a sheep, and prepared food for him. He ﷺ ate, and we ate with him. Then he performed wudu' for the Zuhr prayer and prayed. The woman said, \"O Messenger of Allah, some of our sheep remains as leftovers. Would you like to have dinner?\" He said, \"Yes.\" So he ate, and we ate, then he prayed 'Asr without performing wudu'."],[6876,"Abu Hurayrah ate pieces of dried curd, then performed wudu', and then said, \"Do you know why I performed wudu'? I ate pieces of dried curd. I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say, 'Perform wudu' from what fire has touched.'\""],[6877,"A man asked the Prophet ﷺ, saying: 'O Messenger of Allah, should I perform ablution from the meat of sheep?' He said: 'If you wish, perform ablution, and if you wish, do not perform ablution.' He said: 'Should I perform ablution from the meat of camels?' He said: 'Yes, perform ablution from the meat of camels.' He said: 'May I pray in sheep enclosures?' He said: 'Yes.' He said: 'May I pray in camel resting places?' He said: 'No.'"],[6878,"He went out with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ in the year of Khaybar until when we were at al-Sahba', which is near Khaybar, the Messenger of Allah ﷺ dismounted and prayed 'Asr. Then he called for provisions, and nothing was brought except sawiq. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ ordered it to be moistened, and he ate and we ate with him. Then he stood for Maghrib and rinsed his mouth, and we rinsed our mouths, and he did not perform ablution."],[6879,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to wake up junub without having had a wet dream, then he would fast that day."],[6880,"He used to be overtaken by dawn while he was junub from his family, then he would perform ghusl and fast."],[6881,"I heard Abu Hurayrah say: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: 'Whoever is overtaken by morning while junub, there is no fast for him.' So I and my father went and entered upon Umm Salamah and Aishah, the two wives of the Prophet ﷺ, and asked them. They informed us that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to wake up junub without having had a wet dream, then he would fast. Then we entered upon Marwan b. al-Hakam and informed him of their statement and of the statement of Abu Hurayrah. Marwan said: 'I adjure you both to go to Abu Hurayrah and inform him.' So we met Abu Hurayrah while he was at the door of the mosque and said to him: 'The amir has adjured us concerning a matter we will mention to you.' He said: 'And what is it?' My father narrated it to him, and Abu Hurayrah's face changed color, and he said: 'Thus.'"],[6882,"\"That the Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to wake up in a state of sexual impurity, then he would observe fasting.\" Abu Hurairah responded with his youth."],[6883,"A man came to the Prophet ﷺ and said: 'O Messenger of Allah, morning overtakes me while I am junub, so may I fast that day of mine?' I heard the Prophet ﷺ say: 'Sometimes morning overtakes me while I am junub, so I get up, perform ghusl, pray the morning prayer, and fast that day of mine.' The man said: 'You are not like us; Allah has forgiven you your past and future sins.' The Prophet said: 'I hope that I am the most fearful of Allah among you and the most knowledgeable of you of what I avoid.'"],[6884,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ passed by Zamzam and asked for water. I brought him the bucket, and he drank while standing."],[6886,"We used to eat while walking and drink while standing in the time of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ."],[6887,"\"I used to be jealous of those who gave themselves to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and say, 'Does a woman give herself?' When Allah revealed {You may defer whom you wish of them, and receive to yourself whom you wish, and whoever you desire of those whom you had set aside}, she said, 'I said, By Allah, I see your Lord only hastens to your desire.'\""],[6888,"A woman came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and said to him, \"O Messenger of Allah, I have gifted myself to you.\" She stood for a long time, then a man stood up and said, \"O Messenger of Allah, marry her to me if you have no need of her.\" The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, \"Do you have anything to give her as dower?\" He replied, \"I have nothing except this lower garment of mine.\" The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, \"If you give it to her, you will sit with no lower garment. Look for something.\" He said, \"I cannot find anything.\" He said, \"Look for something, even an iron ring,\" but he could not find anything. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, \"Do you have any of the Quran with you?\" He said, \"Yes, Surah such-and-such and Surah such-and-such,\" naming some surahs. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, \"I have married her to you for what you have of the Quran.\""],[6889,"Jibril came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ while he was playing with the boys. He took him, threw him down, split open his chest, and extracted a clot of blood from it, saying: “This is Satan’s share of you.” Then he washed it in a golden basin with Zamzam water, stitched him up, and returned him to his place. The boys came running to his mother—meaning his wet nurse—and said: “Muhammad has been killed.” They met him, and his color was pale. Anas said: “I used to see the trace of that stitching on his chest ﷺ.”"],[6890,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Do you see my qibla here? By Allah, your humility and your bowing are not hidden from me, and I see you from behind my back.”"],[6891,"I said, \"O Messenger of Allah, is it recommended to sleep after Witr?\" He said, \"O Aisha, indeed, my eyes sleep but my heart does not sleep.\""],[6892,"“No wealth has ever benefited me as much as the wealth of Abu Bakr.” Abu Bakr ؓ wept and said, “I and my wealth are only for you.”"],[6893,"A funeral was brought to the Prophet ﷺ so that he might pray over it, and he said: \"Does he owe a debt?\" They said: \"Yes, two dinars.\""],[6894,"A funeral was brought to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ so that he might pray over it, and he said: \"Does he owe a debt?\" They said: \"He owes two dinars.\" He said: \"Pray over your companion.\" Abu Qatadah said: \"They are mine, O Messenger of Allah; they are upon me.\" Then the Messenger of Allah ﷺ advanced and prayed over him."],[6895,"A man was brought to the Prophet ﷺ so that he might pray over him, and he said: \"Pray over your companion, for he owes a debt.\" Abu Qatadah said: \"I will be responsible for it.\" He said: \"With fulfillment?\" He said: \"With fulfillment.\" So he ﷺ prayed over him, and he owed eighteen or seventeen dirhams."],[6896,"By Allah, no word was mentioned to him until he stood up intently towards the Mosque and called out the people of Quraysh. He said, \"O people of Quraysh, indeed the son of Al-Khattab has taken over.\" Umar said, \"He lied, but indeed I have embraced Islam, believed in Allah, and affirmed His Messenger.\" Then they confronted him and fought with him until the sun set on their heads. Umar got injured and sat down. They stood over his head, and Umar said, \"Do whatever seems best to you. By Allah, if we were three hundred men, you would not have escaped us, or we would have not left it to you.\" While they were in that situation, a man came wearing a silk robe and a Qumiss garment. He asked, \"What is happening?\" They said, \"Indeed the son of Al-Khattab has taken over.\" He said, \"It seems as if a garment has been removed from him.\" Then I said to him later in Medina, \"Father, who was the man who defended you that day?\" He said, \"O my son, that was Tha'alib bin Wail.\""],[6897,"\"When the Messenger of Allah ﷺ mentioned the Hour (Day of Judgment), his cheeks would turn red, his anger would intensify, and his voice would rise as if he were warning of an approaching army. He would say, 'You have experienced both morning and evening.' He would also say, 'I am more deserving of the believers than themselves. Whoever leaves behind wealth, it belongs to their family, and whoever leaves behind a debt or dependents, it is my responsibility and mine alone. I am more deserving of the believers.'\""],[6898,"In the time of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, when a man died owing a debt, he would ask: \"Does he have anything to fulfill it?\" If it was said: \"Yes,\" he would pray over him; and if it was said: \"No,\" he would say: \"Pray over your companion.\" When Allah granted His Messenger the conquests, he said: \"I am more entitled to the believers than their own selves. Whoever leaves a debt, it is upon me; and whoever leaves wealth, it is for the heirs.\""],[6899,"Umm Sulaym had an orphan girl. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ saw her and said: “Is it you? You have grown up; may your age not grow.” The orphan girl went back to Umm Sulaym weeping. Umm Sulaym said: “What is the matter with you, my little girl?” The girl said: “The Prophet of Allah ﷺ supplicated against me that my age should not grow. Now my age will never grow” or she said “my generation.” Umm Sulaym went out hastily, wrapping her headcover, until she met the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, who said to her: “O Umm Sulaym, what is the matter with you?” She said: “O Prophet of Allah, did you supplicate against my orphan girl?” He said: “And what is that, O Umm Sulaym?” She said: “She claims that you supplicated against her that her age should not grow.” He said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ laughed and said: “O Umm Sulaym, do you not know my condition with my Lord? I made a condition with my Lord and said: I am only a human; I am pleased as humans are pleased, and I become angry as humans become angry. For any one of my ummah against whom I supplicate with a supplication that he does not deserve, make it for him a purification, an increase, and a means of nearness by which You bring him near to You on the Day of Resurrection.” And he ﷺ was merciful."],[6900,"Ibn 'Umar used to lengthen the prayer before Jumu'ah and pray two rak'ahs after it in his house, and he reported that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to do that."],[6901,"«When one of you prays on Friday, let him pray four [rak'ahs] after it»"],[6902,"«The Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to pray two rak'ahs after Jumu'ah»"],[6903,"«Whoever among you prays after Jumu'ah, let him pray four [rak'ahs]»"],[6904,"«The prayer of night and day is two [rak'ahs] by two»"],[6905,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ came to Banu 'Amr b. 'Awf on Wednesday and said, \"If only, when you come to this 'Id of yours, you would stay until you hear my statement.\" They said, \"Yes, by our fathers and mothers, O Messenger of Allah.\" Then when they attended the Friday prayer, the Messenger of Allah ﷺ led them in Jumu'ah, then he prayed two rak'ahs after Jumu'ah in the mosque. He was not seen praying two rak'ahs in the mosque on Friday after Jumu'ah before that day, as he used to depart to his house."],[6906,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ was cupped while he was fasting."],[6907,"He went out with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ on the eighteenth of Ramadan to al-Baqiʿ. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ looked at a man being cupped and said: \"The cupper and the cupped have broken the fast.\""],[6908,"While I was walking with the Prophet ﷺ on the eighteenth of Ramadan, he happened to turn and saw a man being cupped, so he ﷺ said: \"The cupper and the cupped have broken the fast.\""],[6909,"I was with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ going to al-Baqi' at the time of the conquest, and he looked at a man performing cupping. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, \"The cupper and the one cupped have broken their fast.\""],[6910,"\"The cupper and the one cupped have broken their fast.\""],[6911,"The Prophet ﷺ commanded Abu Taybah to come to him at sunset, and he ordered him to apply the cupping glasses at the time of the fasting person's breaking the fast. So he cupped him, then he asked him, \"How much is your tax?\" He said, \"Two sa's.\" So the Prophet ﷺ reduced one sa' from him."],[6912,"He used to come to the Mosque of Quba riding and walking."],[6913,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to come to Quba walking and riding."],[6914,"Saddles are not to be fastened except to three mosques: the Sacred Mosque, this mosque of mine, and the Farthest Mosque."],[6915,"My father and I departed and entered upon Abu Barzah. My father said to him: Tell us how the Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to pray the prescribed prayers. He said: He would pray the midday prayer, which you call the first (Zuhr), when the sun had passed its zenith. He would pray Asr, then one of us would return to his home in the farthest part of Madinah. He said: I forgot what he said about Maghrib. He said: He preferred to delay Isha, which you call Atamah, and he disliked sleeping before it and talking after it. He would finish the Fajr prayer when a man could recognize his sitting companion, and he would recite between sixty and one hundred verses."],[6916,"He used to pray Asr while the sun was high and alive, then a person would go to the highlands and reach the highlands while the sun was still high."],[6917,"I said to Ibn ʿAbbas: “I am amazed at a shaykh who led us in the noon prayer and said twenty-two takbirs.” He said: “That is the Sunnah of Abu al-Qasim ﷺ.”"],[6918,"Abu Hurayrah, when praying with them, would say takbir at every lowering and raising, and when he finished he would say: “I am the one among you whose prayer most resembles that of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ.”"],[6919,"When Marwan appointed Abu Hurayrah in charge of Madinah, whenever he stood for the obligatory prayer he would say takbir, then say takbir when he bowed. When he raised his head from bowing he would say: “Allah hears the one who praises Him. Our Lord, to You belongs praise.” Then he would say takbir when going down to prostrate, then say takbir when rising from the two prostrations after the tashahhud. He would do the same until he completed his prayer. When he finished and gave the greeting, he turned to the people of the mosque and said: “By the One in whose hand is my soul, I am the one among you whose prayer most resembles that of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ.”"],[6920,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ would stand in the Zuhr prayer in the first two rak'ahs for the length of thirty verses in each rak'ah, and in the last two rak'ahs in each rak'ah for the length of fifteen verses. And he would stand in Asr in the first two rak'ahs in each rak'ah for the length of fifteen verses, and in the last two in each rak'ah for half of that."],[6921,"We said to Khabbab: Did the Messenger of Allah ﷺ recite in Zuhr and Asr? He said: Yes. We said: How did you know that? He said: By the movement of his beard."],[6922,"ʿUmar said to Saʿd: \"The people of Kufa have complained about you in everything, even in prayer.\" He said: \"I lengthen the first two (rakʿahs) and shorten the last two, and I do not fall short of the prayer of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ.\" He said: \"That is what is expected of you.\""],[6923,"When the Messenger of Allah ﷺ prayed the two rak'ahs of Fajr, he would lighten them so much that I would say to myself, “He did not recite the Opening of the Book.”"],[6924,"«The Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to turn to his right and to his left, saying: “Peace be upon you and the mercy of Allah; peace be upon you and the mercy of Allah,” until the whiteness of his cheek could be seen.»"],[6925,"He said to 'Abd Allah b. 'Umar, 'O Abu 'Abd al-Rahman, I have seen you do four things that I have not seen any of your companions do.' He said, 'What are they, O Ibn Jurayj?' He said, 'I have seen you not touching any of the corners except the two Yamani ones, I have seen you wearing hairless leather sandals, I have seen you dyeing with yellow, and I have seen you when you are in Makkah: the people enter ihram when they see the new moon, but you do not enter ihram until the Day of Tarwiyah.' 'Abd Allah b. 'Umar replied, 'As for the corners, I have never seen the Messenger of Allah ﷺ touch any except the two Yamani ones. As for the hairless leather sandals, I have seen the Messenger of Allah ﷺ wearing hairless leather sandals that had no hair on them and performing ablution while wearing them, so I like to wear them. As for yellow dye, I have seen the Messenger of Allah ﷺ dye with it. As for entering ihram, I have never seen the Messenger of Allah ﷺ enter ihram until his mount set off with him.'"],[6926,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ did not cease making talbiyah until he threw Jamrat al-'Aqabah."],[6927,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ departed from Arafat until when he was at the mountain pass, he dismounted and urinated, then performed wudu, but did not complete the wudu. I said to him: \"The prayer, O Messenger of Allah?\" He said: \"The prayer is ahead of you.\" He mounted, and when he came to Muzdalifah, he dismounted and performed wudu, completing the wudu. Then the iqamah was given, and he prayed Maghrib. Then each person made his camel kneel at his own campsite. Then the iqamah was given for Isha, and he prayed both, and he did not pray anything between them."],[6928,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ departed after he prayed Zuhr, then returned to Mina and stayed there during the three days of Tashrīq, stoning the Jamrahs after the sun had passed its zenith, with seven pebbles at each Jamrah, saying takbīr with each pebble. He would stand at the first Jamrah and at the middle one in the bottom of the valley, prolonging the stay, and he would depart when he threw at the largest one without standing at it. The Jamrahs were from the traces of Ibrāhīm ﷺ ."],[6929,"ʿAbd Allāh threw from the bottom of the valley. I said, “O Abū ʿAbd al-Raḥmān, the people throw it from above.” He said, “This, by the One besides whom there is no deity, is the standing place of the one upon whom Sūrat al-Baqarah was revealed.”"],[6930,"I heard al-Ḥajjāj ibn Yūsuf say while he was on the pulpit, “Arrange the Qurʾān as Jibrāʾīl arranged it: the surah in which the cow (al-Baqarah) is mentioned, the surah in which the family of ʿImrān (Āl ʿImrān) is mentioned, the surah in which the women (al-Nisāʾ) is mentioned.” Al-Aʿmash said: I met Ibrāhīm al-Nakhaʿī and told him, and he cursed him. Then Ibrāhīm said:"],[6931,"\"He used to throw the first Jamrah with seven pebbles, saying 'Allāhu Akbar' with each pebble. Then he would go forward and stand facing the qiblah for a long time, supplicating and raising his hands. Then he would throw the Jamrat al-ʿAqabah from the bottom of the valley and would not stop at it. Then he would leave and say: 'This is how I saw the Messenger of Allah ﷺ do it.'\""],[6932,"We set out with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ as pilgrims until we reached Sarif, and I menstruated. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ entered upon me while I was crying, and he said, \"What is the matter with you?\" I said, \"I wish I had not performed Hajj this year.\" He said, \"What is the matter with you?\" I said, \"I have menstruated.\" He said, \"This is something that Allah has decreed for the daughters of Adam. Do everything that a pilgrim does, except do not circumambulate the House.\" When we reached Makkah, the Prophet ﷺ said, \"Make it an ‘Umrah.\" So they did that. Those who had not brought a sacrificial animal came out of iḥrām, but the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, Abu Bakr, ‘Umar, and some of his companions who were well off had brought sacrificial animals, so they did not come out of iḥrām. On the Day of Sacrifice, the Prophet ﷺ slaughtered a cow on behalf of his wives. I became pure, so I circumambulated the House and performed sa‘y. Then I returned to the Prophet ﷺ at Mina. When we departed, he sent me with my brother ‘Abd al-Raḥmān b. Abī Bakr from al-Muḥaṣṣab and said, \"Take your sister behind you and have her perform ‘Umrah from al-Tan‘īm.\" So he took me behind him, and I entered iḥrām at al-Tan‘īm, circumambulated the House, and then returned to him, and we departed."],[6933,"The family of Muhammad ﷺ would see three months pass without kindling a fire in it—it was only water and dates. Around us were households of the Ansar who had domestic animals in their gardens. The people of each house would send to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ the milk of their best sheep, so the Messenger of Allah ﷺ had some of that milk."],[6934,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ came to Fāṭimah and saw a curtain on her door, so he did not enter upon her. He said, “It was rare for him to enter without beginning with her.” ‘Alī, ؓ , came and saw her distressed. He said, “What is with you?” She said, “The Messenger of Allah ﷺ came to me and did not enter.” ‘Alī went to him and said, “O Messenger of Allah, Fāṭimah is troubled that you came to her and did not enter upon her.” The Prophet ﷺ said, “What am I to the world and what am I to embroidered cloth?” So ‘Alī went to Fāṭimah and told her the words of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. She said, “Tell the Messenger of Allah ﷺ: what do you command me?” He said, “Tell her to send it to Banū so-and-so.”"],[6935,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ would not enter a house with embroidered curtains."],[6936,"A man came to the Prophet ﷺ to pledge allegiance to him for emigration and had already become Muslim. He said, “I left my parents weeping.” He said, “Return to them and make them laugh as you made them weep,” and he refused to let him go out with him."],[6937,"\"When the Messenger of Allahﷺ used to be with a funeral, he would not sit until it was placed in the grave or until it was buried.\" Abu Muawiyah doubted."],[6938,"ʿĀʾishah heard me talking after the latter ʿIshāʾ prayer and said: “O ʿUrayy, will you not give your scribe a rest? The Messenger of Allah ﷺ used not to sleep before it or talk after it.” *"],[6939,"The Prophet ﷺ used to sit holding his knees with his hands, and he would not recline."],[6940,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ prayed in the mosque one night, and some people prayed by his prayer. Then he prayed the following night, and the people increased. Then they gathered on the third or fourth night, but the Messenger of Allah ﷺ did not come out to them. When morning came, he said, \"I saw what you did, and nothing prevented me from coming out to you except that I feared it would be made obligatory upon you.\" That was in Ramadan."],[6941,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ came out in the middle of the night in the mosque, and some men prayed by his prayer. In the morning, the people talked about that, and more gathered. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ came out the second night, and they prayed by his prayer. In the morning, the people reminded one another of that, and the people of the mosque increased on the third night. He came out and prayed with them, and they prayed by his prayer. When it was the fourth night, the mosque could not hold its people, and the Messenger of Allah ﷺ did not come out until he came out for the dawn prayer. When he finished the dawn prayer, he turned to the people, then pronounced the testimony of faith and said: \"To proceed: your affair was not hidden from me last night, but I feared that the night prayer would be made obligatory upon you and you would be unable to do it.\""],[6942,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ prayed eight units and the Witr prayer with us in the month of Ramadan. When it was time for childbirth, we gathered in the mosque and hoped that he would come out to us. But he did not come out until we entered the mosque and said, \"O Messenger of Allah, we gathered in the mosque and hoped that you would pray with us.\" He said, \"I feared that the Witr prayer might be made obligatory upon you, or that it might become difficult for you.\""],[6943,"\"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ would leave a deed while he loved to do it, fearing that the people would do it and it would be made obligatory upon them.\""],[6944,"\"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ did not perform the Duha prayer.\" And A'ishah used to perform it, and she used to say: 'The Messenger of Allah ﷺ abandoned many deeds fearing that the people would follow him and it would be made obligatory upon them.'"],[6945,"\"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ did not fast a complete month since he arrived in Medina except for the month of Ramadan.\""],[6946,"I asked 'Abd Allah b. Abi Awfa: Did the Messenger of Allah ﷺ leave a will? He said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ did not leave anything to bequeath. I said: Then how can he command the people to make a will? He said: He bequeathed the Book of Allah."],[6947,"The Prophet ﷺ did not pray in our hair or our sheets."],[6948,"I recited An-Najm to the Prophet ﷺ and he did not prostrate."],[6949,"Ibn Umar was asked about fasting on the day of Arafah. He said, \"I performed Hajj with the Prophet ﷺ and he did not fast it; I performed Hajj with Abu Bakr and he did not fast it; I performed Hajj with Umar and he did not fast it; I performed Hajj with Uthman and he did not fast it. And I do not fast it, nor do I command it, nor do I forbid it.\""],[6950,"I used to twist the garlands for the sacrificial animals of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and he would send them and then would not avoid anything that a person in iḥrām avoids."],[6951,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ was not prevented from reciting the Quran by anything except being junub."],[6952,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to remember Allah in all his states."],[6953,"I came with 'Abd Allah b. Yasar, the freed slave of Maymunah, until we entered upon Abu al-Juhaym b. al-Harith b. al-Simmah. Abu al-Juhaym said, 'The Messenger of Allah ﷺ came from the direction of Bi'r al-Jamal, and a man met him and greeted him, but the Messenger of Allah ﷺ did not return the greeting until he faced a wall and wiped his face and hands with it, then he returned the greeting.'"],[6954,"He came to the Prophet ﷺ while he was urinating and greeted him, but he did not return the greeting until he had performed ablution. Then he apologized and said, 'I disliked mentioning Allah except in a state of purity' - or he said, 'upon purification.'"],[6955,"He used to pair together two of the slain of Uhud in a single cloth and say, “Which of them had taken more of the Qur’an?” When one of them was pointed to, he would place him first in the grave. He ﷺ said, “I am a witness over these on the Day of Resurrection.” He ordered that they be buried with their blood and did not pray over them, nor were they washed."],[6956,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ went out one day and prayed over the slain of Uhud as he prayed over the dead, then he went to the pulpit and said: “I am a forerunner for you, and I am a witness over you. By Allah, I am looking at my cistern now. Indeed, I have been given the keys of the treasures of the earth, or the keys of the earth.” By Allah, I do not fear that you will associate partners with Allah after me, but I fear that you will compete with one another over it.”"],[6957,"The Prophet ﷺ prayed over the slain of Uhud, then departed and sat on the pulpit, praised Allah and extolled Him, then said: “O people, I am before you as a forerunner, and I am a witness over you. By Allah, I do not fear that you will associate partners with Allah after me, but I have been given tonight the keys of the treasures of the earth and the heaven, and I fear that you will compete with one another over them.” Then he entered his house and did not come out until Allah, Mighty and Exalted, took his soul."],[6958,"\"The Prophet ﷺ would not touch any part of my face while I was fasting.\""],[6959,"“The Messenger of Allah ﷺ would kiss some of his wives while he was fasting.” Then she laughed."],[6960,"I entered upon the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, I and two men from my paternal cousins. One of the two men said: O Messenger of Allah, appoint us over some of what Allah has given you authority over. The other said the like of that. The Prophet ﷺ said: «By Allah, we do not appoint over this work anyone who asks for it, nor anyone who is eager for it.»"],[6961,"“When we pledged allegiance to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, he would instruct us: ‘On hearing and obedience in what we are able.’”"],[6962,"Fatimah bt. Utbah b. Rabi'ah came to pledge allegiance to the Prophet ﷺ. He took from her: 'that they should not steal nor commit adultery' – the verse. She said: She placed her hand on her head out of shyness. The Prophet ﷺ was pleased with what he saw from her. A'ishah said to her: 'Accept, O woman, for by Allah we did not pledge allegiance to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ except upon this.' So he accepted her pledge with the verse."],[6963,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ never shook hands with a woman."],[6964,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ never took the oath of allegiance from women except with what Allah, mighty and sublime, commanded him, and his hand never touched the hand of a woman. When he took their pledge, he would only say, 'I have accepted your pledge,' verbally."],[6965,"I asked Abu 'Amr al-Awza'i about the shares of those from the reinforcements who did not witness the conquest and the fighting. He said: 'They are not allotted shares. Do you not see that two parties enter by one mountain pass or two different passes, and one of them gains spoils while the other does not, and one of them is a support for the other? Neither of them shares with the other whether they both gain spoils or only one of them gains. Thus the matter has been settled concerning them.'"],[6966,"I set up my snares at al-Abwa', and a gazelle fell into one of my snares and escaped with it. I went out in its pursuit and found a man who had taken it. We disputed about it before the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and found him staying at al-Abwa' under a tree, shading himself with a leather mat. We brought our case to him, and the Messenger of Allah ﷺ judged between us that it be divided in halves. I said: O Messenger of Allah, we come across camels that are milked and are kept from their calves while their owners are in need. He said: \"Call the owner of the camels three times; if he comes, then fine; otherwise, untie their udder strings, then drink, then tie them again, and leave for the milk its natural draw.\" I said: O Messenger of Allah, lost animals come to us; is there a reward for us if we give them water? He said: \"Yes, in every living being there is a reward.\" Then the Messenger of Allah ﷺ began to tell us, saying: \"A time will come upon people when the best wealth will be sheep between the two mosques, eating from the trees and coming to water; their owner will eat from their milk, drink from their milk, and wear from their wool\" or he said \"from their hair, while trials will be churning among the masses of the Arabs, by Allah.\" I said: O Messenger of Allah, advise me. He said: \"Establish the prayer, give the zakat, fast Ramadan, perform Hajj to the House, perform 'umrah, be dutiful to your parents, maintain your kinship ties, honor the guest, enjoin what is right, forbid what is wrong, and move with the truth wherever it moves.\""],[6967,"\"My father was from the sons of Asawira, and I used to differ with him regarding the book. I had two young boys with me, and when they returned from the book, they entered upon a priest, and I entered with them. The priest said to them, 'Did I not forbid you from coming with anyone?' I said to him, 'I differ with him until he loves me more than them.' He said to me, 'O Salman, if your family asks you who detained you, say it was your teacher. And if your teacher asks you who detained you, say it was your family.' He also said to me, 'O Salman, I want to convert.' I said to him, 'I am with you.' So he converted and entered a village where a woman used to differ with him. When he arrived, he said to me, 'O Salman, dig.' So I dug and found a jar of money. He poured it on my chest and began hitting his own chest, saying, 'Woe to the priest!' Then he died, and I blew into his mouth. The priests and monks gathered and attended to him. He said to them, 'I had intended to keep the money, but Allah diverted my attention from it. When the priests and monks gathered, I said to them, 'He left some money behind.' So some young men from the village took it and buried him. I said to the priests, 'Show me a knowledgeable person whom I can join.' They said, 'We do not know anyone on earth who is more knowledgeable than a man who used to go to Bayt al-Maqdis. If you leave now, you will find his donkey at the door of Bayt al-Maqdis.' So I went and found the donkey. I sat beside it until he came out, and I told him my story. He said, 'Stay here until I return to you,' but I never saw him again. He used to go to Bayt al-Maqdis only once a year in that month. When he returned, I asked him, 'What did you do with me?' He said, 'Do you still have it?' I said, 'Yes.' He said, 'I do not know anyone on earth who is more knowledgeable than an orphan who left Tihama and whom you would meet if you leave now.' I left and found him. He raised me to a certain place and then lowered me to another place. I encountered a tribe of Arabs who rejected me and sold me until I arrived in Medina. I heard them mentioning the Prophet and that life there was good. So I asked my family to give me a gift for a day, and they did. I left and saved some money, and then I brought it to him and placed it in front of him. He asked, 'What is this?' I said, 'It is charity.' He said to his companions, 'Eat.' But he refused to eat. I said, 'This is only one, and I waited as Allah willed.' Then I asked my family for a gift for a day, and they gave it to me. I left and saved some money, and then I brought him something better than that. I cooked food and brought it to him. He placed it in front of him and asked, 'What is this?' I said, 'It is a gift.' He said, 'In the name of Allah.' Then he said to his companions, 'Take it and eat with me.' I stood behind him, and he placed his cloak in front of him. I saw the seal of prophethood on the back of his right shoulder, which resembled an egg with the color of his skin. I said, 'I bear witness that you are the Messenger of Allah.' He asked, 'What is that?' I told him, and then I asked him, 'O Messenger of Allah, will the priest enter Paradise? He claims that you are a prophet.' He said, 'No one will enter Paradise except a Muslim soul.' I said, 'O Messenger of Allah, he informed me that you are a prophet.' He said, 'No one will enter Paradise except a Muslim soul.'\""],[6968,"A man used to write for the Prophet ﷺ . He had read Al-Baqarah and Al 'Imran until he had become distinguished among us, and the Prophet ﷺ would dictate to him, \"Forgiving and Merciful.\" So he would write, \"Pardoning and Merciful.\" The Prophet ﷺ said, \"Write, for by the One in whose hand is my soul, whatever he (Gabriel) dictates to you.\" Then he dictated to him, \"Knowledgeable and Wise.\" So he wrote, \"All-Hearing and All-Seeing.\" The Prophet ﷺ said, \"Write, whichever of the two you wish.\" He (the scribe) narrated that he reverted from Islam and joined the pagans. He said, \"I know more about Muhammad than you all. If I wanted, I would write whatever I pleased.\" So he died in disbelief, and it reached the Prophet ﷺ . He said, \"Truly, the earth will not accept him.\" Then Abu Talhah said, \"So I went to the land where he died, and I found him rejected.\" I said, \"What happened to him?\" They said, \"We buried him, but the earth did not accept him.\""],[6969,"I said to Ibn Mas'ud, 'Did any of you accompany the Messenger of Allah ﷺ on the night of the jinn?' He said, 'None of us accompanied him, but we lost him one night in Makkah. We said, \"He has been assassinated or snatched away.\" So we spent the worst night any people have ever spent. When it was the last part of the night, or he said, in the morning, there he was coming from the direction of Hira'. We said, \"O Messenger of Allah,\" and mentioned to him what we had experienced. He ﷺ said, \"A caller from the jinn came to me, so I went to them and recited to them.\" Then the Messenger of Allah ﷺ went and showed us their traces and the traces of their fires.'"],[6970,"\"That the tree warned the Prophet ﷺ of the jinn on the night of the jinn.\""],[6971,"We were with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ on a journey, and he called for food, and the food was glorifying Allah."],[6972,"The moon split, and we were with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ at Mina, until a piece of it went behind the mountain. The Prophet ﷺ said, 'Bear witness.'"],[6973,"\"The moon split into two during the time of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ.\""],[6974,"The leaders of Quraysh gathered in al-Hijr and swore by al-Lat, al-'Uzza, and Manat, the third, the other, and by Na'ilah and Isaf: 'If we were to see Muhammad, we would rise against him as one man and not leave him until we kill him.' Then his daughter Fatimah came weeping until she entered upon the Prophet ﷺ and said: 'These leaders of your people have sworn against you that if they see you, they will rise against you and kill you; there is not a man among them but knows his share of your blood.' He said: 'O my little daughter, bring me water for ablution.' So he performed ablution, then entered the mosque. When they saw him, they said: 'Here he is! Here he is!' Then they lowered their eyes and their chins fell upon their chests; they did not raise their eyes to him, and no man among them rose against him. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ came forward until he stood over their heads, took a handful of dust, and said: 'May the faces be ugly!' Then he threw it at them. No man among them was struck by any of those pebbles except that he was killed on the Day of Badr."],[6975,"I was a youth tending sheep belonging to 'Uqbah b. Abi Mu'ayt. The Prophet ﷺ and Abu Bakr came to me and he said: “O boy, do you have any milk with you?” I said: “Yes, but I am entrusted.” He said: “Bring me a ewe that no male has mounted.” So I brought him a young she-goat. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ grasped it, then began to wipe its udder and supplicate until it let down milk. Abu Bakr, ؓ , came to him with something, and he milked into it, then said to Abu Bakr: “Drink.” Abu Bakr ؓ drank, then the Prophet ﷺ drank after him. Then he said to the udder: “Draw up,” and it drew up and returned as it was. He said: Then I came to the Prophet ﷺ and said: “O Messenger of Allah, teach me some of this speech, or some of this Qur'an.” He wiped my head and said ﷺ: “You are a taught boy.” He said: I took from his mouth seventy surahs, which no human ever disputed with me."],[6976,"We were with the Prophet ﷺ on a journey when a Bedouin came forward. When he drew near, the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Where do you intend to go?” He said: “To my family.” He said: “Would you like something good?” He said: “What is it?” He said: “That you bear witness that there is no god but Allah alone, with no partner, and that Muhammad is His servant and Messenger.” He said: “Is there any witness to what you say?” He ﷺ said: “This samurah tree.” The Messenger of Allah ﷺ called it while it was on the edge of the valley, and it came plowing through the ground until it stood before him. He asked it to testify three times, and it testified that he was as he said; then it returned to its place, and the Bedouin returned to his people, saying: “If they follow me, I will bring them to you; otherwise I will come back to you and be with you.”"],[6977,"He used to stand at a trunk and deliver the Friday sermon from it, and when the pulpit was made, he moved to it, and the trunk yearned. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ came to it and stroked it."],[6978,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to deliver his sermon on Fridays leaning against a wooden pillar. When the number of people increased, he said, \"Build a pulpit for me.\" So they built him a pulpit with two steps. When he stood on the pulpit to deliver the sermon, the wooden pillar longed for the Messenger of Allah ﷺ . Anas said, \"I was in the mosque and I heard the wooden pillar longing like a young child until the Messenger of Allah ﷺ came down to it and embraced it, and it became calm.\" Hasan used to cry when he narrated this Hadith and then say, \"O servants of Allah! The wooden pillar longs eagerly for the Messenger of Allah ﷺ out of its desire for his place near Allah. And you are the ones who are most deserving to long for meeting him.\""],[6979,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to stand beside a tree, or a trunk, or a piece of wood, or something he leaned against while delivering the sermon. Then he had a pulpit made and would stand on it, and that thing alongside which he used to stand yearned with a yearning heard by the people of the mosque. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ came to it—either he said he stroked it, or he said he held it—and it became still."],[6980,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ spat on the leg of 'Amr b. Mu'adh when his leg was severed, and it healed."],[6981,"I saw the mark of a wound on the shin of Salamah b. al-Akwa' and said: “O Abu Muslim, what is this wound?” He said: “This is a wound that struck me on the day of Hunayn. The people said: ‘Salamah is wounded! Salamah is wounded!’ He said: ‘I was brought to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and he blew on it three times. I have not complained of it until this very hour.’”"],[6982,"\"When the chapter {Perished be the hands of Abu Lahab} was revealed, the wife of Abu Lahab came to the Prophet Muhammad ﷺ with Abu Bakr. When Abu Bakr saw her, he said, \"O Messenger of Allah, she is a reprehensible woman, and I fear that she may harm you. If you allow me, I will leave.\" The Prophet replied, \"She will not see me.\" So she came and said to Abu Bakr, \"Your companion insults me.\" Abu Bakr said, \"No, he does not speak poetry.\" She said, \"You are known to be his supporter.\" Then she left. So I said, \"O Messenger of Allah, why did you not move away?\" He replied, \"No, for an angel has been shielding me from her with his wings.\""],[6983,"The Prophet ﷺ saw a man called Busr b. Ra'i al-'Ir eating with his left hand and said: “Eat with your right hand.” He said: “I cannot.” He said: “May you not be able.” He said: “After that, his hand never reached his mouth.”"],[6984,"A man was eating with his left hand in the presence of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and the Prophet ﷺ said to him: “Eat with your right hand.” He said: “I cannot.” The Prophet said: “May you not be able.” He never raised it to his mouth again."],[6985,"We returned from Makkah to Madinah with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. My camel became exhausted, so I lagged behind driving it. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ was behind attending to a need and caught up with me. He said to me, \"Why are you lagging behind?\" I said, \"Nothing, O Messenger of Allah, except that my camel is lame, and I wanted to catch up with the group.\" He took hold of its tail, struck it, then urged it on and said, \"Mount.\" I saw myself afterward holding it back from the group. We halted at a place short of Madinah, and I wanted to hurry to my family. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to me, \"Do not come to your family at night.\" I said, \"O Messenger of Allah, I am newly married.\" He said, \"To what did you marry?\" I said, \"A previously married woman.\" He said, \"Why not a virgin whom you could play with and she could play with you?\" I said, \"O Messenger of Allah, Abdullah died or was martyred and left young daughters, and I disliked marrying someone like them over them.\" The Messenger of Allah ﷺ fell silent and did not say whether I did well or badly. Then he said, \"Sell me this camel of yours.\" I said, \"No, rather it is yours, O Messenger of Allah.\" He said, \"No, sell it to me.\" I said, \"It is yours, O Messenger of Allah.\" He said, \"No, sell it to me.\" I said, \"Yes, for an ounce of gold; it is yours for that.\" He said, \"I have taken it, so ride it to Madinah.\" When I arrived in Madinah, the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to Bilal, \"Give him an ounce of gold and give him more.\" He gave me an ounce of gold and added a carat. I said, \"The increase of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ will never leave me.\" It was in a pouch of mine, and the people of Syria took it on the day of al-Harra."],[6986,"I went out with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ on a military expedition, and my camel held me back, so I fell behind. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ dismounted and prodded it with his staff, then said to me, \"Mount.\" I mounted it, and I saw myself holding it back from the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. He said, \"Did you marry?\" I said, \"Yes.\" He said, \"A virgin or a previously married woman?\" I said, \"Rather a previously married woman.\" He said, \"Why not a young girl whom you could play with and she could play with you?\" I said, \"I have sisters, so I wanted to marry a woman who could gather them together, comb their hair, and take care of them.\" He said, \"You will arrive soon, and when you arrive, act wisely, act wisely.\" Then he said, \"Will you sell your camel?\" I said, \"Yes.\" He bought it from me for an ounce. Then the Messenger of Allah ﷺ arrived before me, and I arrived in the morning. I came to the mosque and found him at the door of the mosque. He said, \"Now, when you arrived?\" I said, \"Yes.\" He said, \"Leave your camel, enter, and pray two rak'ahs.\" I entered and prayed, then returned, and he ordered Bilal to weigh for me an ounce. Bilal weighed for me and made the scale generous. I went away, and when I turned, he said, \"Call Jabir for me.\" I was called, and I said, \"Now he will return the camel to me, and nothing was more hateful to me than it.\" He said, \"Your camel and its price are yours.\""],[6987,"He was riding on a camel of his that had become exhausted and wanted to let it go. The Prophet ﷺ caught up with me and prayed for it and struck it, and it traveled as it had never traveled before. He said, \"Sell it to me for an ounce.\" I said, \"No.\" Then he said, \"Sell it to me for an ounce.\" I said, \"No.\" Then he said, \"Sell it to me for an ounce.\" So I sold it to him for an ounce and made an exception for its carrying me to my family. When I arrived, I went to him, and he said to me ﷺ, \"Do you think I haggled with you to take your camel and your dirhams? They are both yours.\""],[6988,"We raided with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ at Hunayn. When we faced the enemy, I advanced and climbed a hill. A man from the enemy confronted me, and I shot an arrow at him, but he hid from me, and I did not know what to do. Then I looked at the people, and they had appeared from another hill and met the companions of the Prophet ﷺ. The companions of the Prophet ﷺ fled, and I returned defeated, wearing two cloaks, wrapped in one and draped with the other. My cloak slipped, so I gathered it and passed by the Messenger of Allah ﷺ in flight while he was on his gray mule. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, \"Ibn al-Akwa' saw fright.\" When they surrounded the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, he dismounted from the mule, took a handful of dust from the ground, faced their faces with it, and said, \"May the faces be disfigured.\" Allah did not create any human among them but He filled his eyes with dust from that handful, and they turned back in retreat, and Allah defeated them, and the Messenger of Allah ﷺ divided their spoils among the Muslims."],[6989,"The fighting became intense on the day of Khaybar, and I was riding behind Abu Talhah. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, \"Allah is greatest; Khaybar is ruined. When we descend upon the courtyard of a people, evil is the morning of the warned ones.\""],[6990,"\"When the Messenger of Allah ﷺ entered Makkah, he found three hundred and sixty idols. He pointed at each idol with a stick and said, 'The truth has come and falsehood has vanished. Indeed, falsehood is bound to perish.' Then the idols fell down and were not touched.\""],[6991,"A man from Banu Amir came to the Prophet ﷺ as if he were a healer and a doctor. He said, \"O Muhammad, you say things; will you let me treat you?\" The Messenger of Allah ﷺ called him to Allah, then said, \"Will you let me show you a sign?\" Near him were palm trees and other trees. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ called a cluster of dates from one of them, and it came to him, prostrating and raising its head, prostrating and raising its head, until it reached him ﷺ. It stood before him, then he ﷺ said to it, \"Return to your place.\" The Amiri said, \"By Allah, I will never disbelieve you in anything you say ever.\" Then he said, \"O people of Amir b. Sa'sa'ah, by Allah, I will never disbelieve him in anything.\""],[6992,"\"Submit to me with the permission of Allah.\" It submitted with him like a camel with a nose ring that obeys its driver, until he came to the other tree. He took one of its branches and said, \"Submit to me with the permission of Allah.\" It submitted with him likewise, until when he was in the middle he joined them together and said, \"Join together over me with the permission of Allah.\" They joined together. Jabir said: I went out quickly for fear that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ would sense my nearness and move away. I sat down, and I happened to glance, and there was the Messenger of Allah ﷺ approaching, and the two trees had separated, each standing on its own trunk. I saw the Messenger of Allah ﷺ stop briefly and move his head like this to the right and left, then he came forward. When he reached me, he said, \"O Jabir, did you see my place?\" I said, \"Yes, O Messenger of Allah.\" He said, \"Go to the two trees and cut a branch from each of them, and come with them, and when you stand in my place, cast a branch on your right and a branch on your left.\" Jabir said: I took a stone and broke it, came to the two trees, cut a branch from each one, then came dragging them, and when I stood in the place of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, I cast a branch on my right and a branch on my left. Then I caught up with him and said, \"I have done it, O Messenger of Allah; what was that about?\" He said, \"I passed by two graves whose occupants are being punished, and I wanted by my intercession that relief be granted to them as long as the two branches remain fresh.\" We came to the camp, and the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, \"O Jabir, call for water for ablution.\" I said, \"Any water? Any water?\" I said, \"O Messenger of Allah, I did not find a drop among the riders.\" A man from the Ansar used to cool water for the Messenger of Allah ﷺ in his leather buckets. He said, \"Go to so-and-so the Ansari and see if there is anything in his buckets.\" I went to him and looked, and I found nothing but a drop in the spout of one of the buckets, which if I poured it out would not be a drink. I came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and said, \"O Messenger of Allah, I found nothing but a drop in the spout of one of them, which if I poured it out, its dryness would drink it.\""],[6993,"The Muslims heard the call of the Prophet ﷺ in the depths of the night while he was at the well of Badr, calling out, \"O Abu Jahl b. Hisham, O Utbah b. Rabi'ah, O Shaybah b. Rabi'ah, O Umayyah b. Khalaf, have you found what your Lord promised to be true?\" The Muslims said, \"O Messenger of Allah, do you call a people who have become corpses?\" He said, \"You are not more able to hear what I say than they are, except that they cannot respond to me.\""],[6994,"I came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ with a group of riders from Muzaynah. He said to Umar, \"Go and equip them.\" He said, \"O Messenger of Allah, it is only a few sa's of dates.\" He went and brought out a key from his belt and opened the door, and there was something like a crouching young camel of dates. We took from it what we needed. He said, \"I looked back at it, and I was one of the last of my companions, and it was as if we had not taken a single date from it.\""],[6995,"A large bowl of tharid was brought to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and placed before the people. They passed it around from morning until noon; some people would get up and others would sit. A man said to Samurah, \"Was it replenished?\" Samurah said, \"What are you surprised about? It was only replenished from here,\" and he pointed with his hand to the sky."],[6996,"During the campaign of Tabuk, the people were struck by hunger. They said, \"O Messenger of Allah ﷺ, if only you would permit us to slaughter our water-carrying camels and eat them.\" The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to them, \"Do so.\" ʿUmar, ؓ , came and said, \"O Messenger of Allah, if they do that, the riding camels will become few, but call them to bring the surplus of their provisions, then invoke blessing upon it; perhaps Allah will place (blessing) in that.\" He said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ called for a leather mat, and I spread it out. Then he called them to bring the surplus of their provisions. He said: One man came with a handful of millet, another with a handful of dates, another with a piece of bread, until a little of that gathered on the mat. He said: He ﷺ invoked blessing upon it, then said, \"Take into your vessels.\" So they took into their vessels until they left no vessel in the army but filled it. They ate until they were full, and some remained. He said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, \"I bear witness that there is no god but Allah and that I am the Messenger of Allah. No servant meets Allah with these two, not doubting, but he will be veiled from Paradise.\""],[6997,"When the Messenger of Allah ﷺ alighted at Marr al-Zahran at the time he made peace with Quraysh, it reached the Companions of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ that Quraysh were saying, \"The companions of Muhammad ﷺ are only pledging allegiance out of weakness and exhaustion.\" The Companions of the Prophet ﷺ said, \"O Prophet of Allah, if we slaughtered some of our riding camels and ate their meat and fat and sipped their broth, we would go to them tomorrow with strength.\" He said, \"No, but bring me what is left over from your provisions.\" So they spread leather mats, then poured upon them what was left over from their provisions. The Prophet ﷺ invoked blessing for them, and they ate until they were completely full. Then they poured back what was left of their provisions into their bags. Then they went to the people, and the Prophet ﷺ said to them, \"Let them not see any sign of weakness in you.\" So the Prophet ﷺ and his Companions uncovered their right arms and jogged in three circuits and walked in four, while the polytheists were in the Hijr and at Dar al-Nadwa. When the Companions of the Prophet ﷺ were hidden from them between the Yamani and Black corners, they walked. Then they appeared before them, and Quraysh said, \"By Allah, they are like gazelles.\" Thus it became a practice."],[6998,"I came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ with some dates that I had arranged in my hand and said, \"O Messenger of Allah, invoke blessing for me in them.\" He invoked blessing for me in them and said, \"When you want to take some, insert your hand and do not scatter them.\" Abu Hurayrah said: \"I carried from those dates such-and-such wasq in the way of Allah, and we used to eat from it and feed others. It was in my waist-wrapper until it was cut off from me during the nights of ʿUthman.\""],[6999,"Three days passed over me during which I did not eat any food. I came intending the Suffah and began to fall down. Children started shouting, \"Abu Hurayrah has gone mad.\" I began calling to them, \"Rather, you are the mad ones,\" until we reached the Suffah. I found the Messenger of Allah ﷺ being brought a bowl of tharid, and he called the People of the Suffah to it, and they ate from it. I kept stretching out hoping he would call me, until the people stood up and there was nothing left in the bowl except a little in its sides. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ gathered it and it became a single morsel. He placed it on his fingers, then said to me, \"Eat in the name of Allah.\" By the One in whose hand is my soul, I did not stop eating from it until I was full."],[7000,"Abu Talhah said to Umm Sulaym, \"I have heard the voice of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ weak, and I recognize hunger in it. Do you have anything?\" She said, \"Yes,\" and brought out some barley cakes. Then she took a headscarf of hers and wrapped the bread in part of it, then tucked it under my arm, and covered me with the rest. She sent me to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. He said: I went with it and found the Messenger of Allah ﷺ sitting in the mosque with the people around him. I stood over them, and the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, \"Did Abu Talhah send you?\" He said: I said, \"Yes.\" He said, \"For food?\" I said, \"Yes.\" The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to those with him, \"Arise.\" They went, and I went ahead of them until I came to Abu Talhah and told him. Abu Talhah said, \"O Umm Sulaym, the Messenger of Allah ﷺ has come with the people, and we do not have enough food for them.\" She said, \"Allah and His Messenger know best.\" Abu Talhah went until he met the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and the Messenger of Allah ﷺ came forward with him until they entered. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, \"Bring what you have, O Umm Sulaym.\" She brought that bread, and the Messenger of Allah ﷺ commanded it to be crumbled. Umm Sulaym squeezed a skin of ghee over it, making it a relish. Then the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said over it whatever Allah willed him to say. Then he said, \"Give permission to ten.\" He gave them permission, and they ate until satisfied, then left. Then he said, \"Give permission to ten.\" He gave them permission, and they ate until satisfied, then left. Then he said, \"Give permission to ten.\" He gave them permission, and they ate until satisfied, then left. Then he said, \"Give permission to ten,\" until all the people had eaten and were satisfied. The people were seventy or eighty men."],[7001,"By the One besides whom there is no god, I used to press my belly against the ground from hunger. One day I sat on their path where they would go out. Abu Bakr passed by me, and I asked him about a verse in the Book of Allah, only so that he might feed me; he passed by and did not do it. ʿUmar b. al-Khattab passed by me, and I asked him about a verse in the Book of Allah, only so that he might feed me; he passed by and did not do it. Then Abu al-Qasim ﷺ passed by me, and when he saw what was in my face and soul, he said, \"Abu Hirr.\" I said, \"At your service, O Messenger of Allah, and your pleasure.\" He said, \"Follow.\" I followed him. He entered upon his family and gave permission, so I entered. There was milk in a bowl. He said to his family, \"Where did you get this?\" They said, \"A gift from so-and-so,\" or he said, \"So-and-so.\" He said, \"Abu Hirr, go to the People of the Suffah and call them.\" The People of the Suffah were guests of the people of Islam; they did not have family or wealth. When charity came to him, he sent it to them and did not share with them in it; when a gift came to him, he sent it to them and shared with them in it, and he partook of it. By Allah, that saddened me. I said, \"Where will this milk be among the People of the Suffah, while I and the Messenger of Allah ﷺ are here?\" I went and called them. He gave them permission, and they entered and took their seats. He said, \"Abu Hirr.\" I said, \"At your service, O Messenger of Allah.\" He said, \"Take and pass it to them.\" I began passing it to one man, and he would drink. When he was satisfied, I took it and passed it to the next, until all the people were satisfied. Then I came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. He raised his head and smiled, and said, \"Abu Hirr, it is you and I.\" I said, \"You have spoken the truth, O Messenger of Allah.\" He said, \"Take and drink.\" He kept saying, \"Drink,\" until I said, \"By the One who sent you with the truth, I find no passage for it.\" He said, \"Show me the vessel.\" I gave him the vessel, and he drank the remainder and praised his Lord ﷺ."],[7002,"My father died owing a debt. I offered his creditors to take the dates for what was owed, but they refused and did not think there was enough in it. I came to the Prophet ﷺ and mentioned that to him. He said, \"When you have harvested it and placed it in the drying floor, inform me.\" When I harvested it and placed it in the drying floor, I came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. He came with Abu Bakr and ʿUmar, sat on it, and invoked blessing. Then he said, \"Call your creditors and pay them.\" He said: I did not leave anyone who had a debt owed by my father but I paid him. There remained thirteen wasq: seven of ʿajwa and six of other dates. I went to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ at Maghrib and mentioned that to him. He ﷺ laughed and said, \"Go to Abu Bakr and ʿUmar and inform them of that.\" I went to Abu Bakr and ʿUmar and informed them. They said, \"Since the Messenger of Allah ﷺ did what he did, we knew that this would happen.\""],[7003,"They went out with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ in the year of the Tabuk campaign. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to combine Zuhr and ʿAsr, and Maghrib and ʿIsha. He said: He delayed the prayer one day, then came out and prayed Zuhr and ʿAsr together. Then he entered, then came out and prayed Maghrib and ʿIsha together. Then he said, \"Tomorrow, if Allah wills, you will come to the spring of Tabuk. You will not reach it until the day is bright. Whoever comes to it, let him not touch any of its water until I come.\" He said: We came to it, and two men had preceded us to it. The spring was like a shoelace, oozing a little water. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ asked them, \"Did you touch any of its water?\" They said, \"Yes.\" He rebuked them and said to them whatever Allah willed. Then they scooped from the spring with their hands a little until it gathered in something. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ washed his face and hands in it, then returned it to the spring. The spring flowed with abundant water, and the people drew water. Then the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, \"It is near, O Muʿadh, if your life is prolonged, that you will see this place filled with gardens.\""],[7004,"I saw myself with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ when the afternoon prayer was due, and we had no water except a small leftover. It was put in a vessel and brought to the Prophet ﷺ. He inserted his hand and spread his fingers, and said, \"Come to ablution and blessing from Allah.\" He said: I saw water bursting from between his fingers ﷺ. People performed ablution and drank. I did not fail to take as much as I could into my belly, knowing it was a blessing. He said: I said to Jabir, \"How many were you that day?\" He said, \"One thousand four hundred.\""],[7005,"I saw the Messenger of Allah ﷺ when the afternoon prayer was due. The people sought water for ablution but could not find it. Some water for ablution was brought, and the Messenger of Allah ﷺ placed his hand in that vessel and ordered the people to perform ablution from it. I saw water springing from beneath his fingers ﷺ, and the people performed ablution until the last of them had done so."],[7006,"We were with the Prophet ﷺ on a journey, and they did not find water. A vessel of water was brought, and the Messenger of Allah ﷺ inserted his hand into it. I saw water bursting from between his fingers ﷺ, and he said, \"Come to the people of purification and blessing from Allah.\""],[7007,"The people became thirsty on the day of al-Hudaybiyyah, and they rushed to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. He placed his hand in water, and I saw the water like springs."],[7008,"The people became thirsty on the day of al-Hudaybiyah while the Messenger of Allah ﷺ had a small water-skin in front of him from which he performed ablution. When the people rushed toward him, he said, 'What is the matter with you?' They said, 'We have nothing to perform ablution with or drink except what is in front of you.' He said, 'He placed his hands in the water-skin and supplicated as Allah willed him to supplicate.' He said, 'The water began to gush from between his fingers ﷺ like springs.' He said, 'We drank and performed ablution.' He said, 'I said to Jabir, \"How many were you?\" He said, \"We were fifteen hundred, and had we been a hundred thousand it would have sufficed us.\"'"],[7009,"Some of the companions of the Prophet ﷺ sought water for ablution. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, 'Does any of you have water?' He placed his hand in the water and then said, 'Perform ablution in the name of Allah.' I saw water flowing from between his fingers ﷺ, and they performed ablution until the last of them had done so."],[7010,"'The prayer time arrived, and those whose houses were nearby went to their families and performed ablution, while a group remained. A stone basin containing water was brought to the Prophet ﷺ, but the basin was too small for him to put his whole palm in it, so he closed his fingers and placed them in the basin, and all the people performed ablution together.' We said, 'How many were they?' He said, 'Eighty men.'"],[7011,"'The Prophet ﷺ called for water, and a wide-topped, narrow-bottomed drinking vessel was brought. The people began to perform ablution, and I estimated them to be between sixty and eighty.'"],[7012,"'I witnessed the Prophet ﷺ with his companions in Madinah or at al-Zawra', and he wanted to perform ablution. A wooden bowl containing a little water was brought, and he placed his palm on the bowl. The water began to spring from between his fingers ﷺ until the people performed ablution.'"],[7013,"I said to Anas b. Malik, 'Tell me something of these wonders that we would not report from anyone but you.' He said, 'The Messenger of Allah ﷺ once prayed Zuhr in Madinah, then he came to the sitting places where Jibril used to come to him, and he sat upon them ﷺ. Bilal came and called the Adhan for Asr. Those who had families in Madinah stood up, performed ablution, and took care of their needs, while some men of the Muhajirun remained who had no families in Madinah. A cup containing water was brought to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and he placed his fingers in the cup, but it was not wide enough for all his fingers, so he placed these four and said, \"Come and perform ablution, all of you.\"' I said to Anas, 'How many do you estimate they were?' He said, 'Between seventy and eighty.'"],[7014,"When the Messenger of Allah ﷺ started to pray, he would say Takbir, then say: \"Wajahtu wajhi lilladhi fataras-samawatiwal-arda hanifan wa ma ana minal-mushrikin. Inna salati wa nusuki wa mahyaya wa mamati lillahi rabbil-alamin, la sharika lahu, wa bidhalika umirtu wa ana min al-muslimin. Allahumma! Antal-maliku la ilaha illa ant, ana abduka zalamtu nafsi wa'taraftu bidhanbi faghfirli dhunubi jami'an, la yaghfirudhunuba illa anta, wahdini lihasanil-ahklaqi, la yahdi li ahsaniha illa anta wasrif anni sayy'aha la yasrifu anni sayy'aha illa anta, labaika wa sa'daika, wal-khairu kulluhu fi yadaika wash-sharru laisa ilaika ana bika wa ilaika ana bika wa ilaika tabarkta wa ta'alaita astaghfiruka wa atubu ilaik. (Verily, I have turned my face toward Him who created the Heavens and the Earth hanifa (worhsipping none but Allah Alone), and I am not of the idolaters. Verily, my salah, my sacrifice, my living, and my dying are for Allah, the Lord of the all that exists. He has no partner. And of this I have been commanded, and I am one of the Muslims. O Allah, You are the Sovereign and there is none worthy of worship but You. I am Your slave, I have wronged myself and I acknowledge my sin. Forgive me all my sins for no one forgives sins but You. Guide me to the best of manners for none can guide to the best of them but You. Protect me from bad manners for none can protect against them but You. I am at Your service, all goodness is in Your hands, and evil is not attributed to You. I rely on You and turn to You, blessed and exalted are You, I seek Your forgiveness and repent to You.\" (Using translation from Nasāʾī 897)"],[7015,"“When the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said the takbir, he remained silent between the takbir and the recitation.” I said: “May my father and mother be your ransom, tell me about your silences between the takbir and the recitation.”"],[7016,"The Prophet ﷺ, Abu Bakr, 'Umar, and 'Uthman, ؓ , used to begin the recitation with \"Praise be to Allah, Lord of the worlds (al-hamdu lillahi rabbi l-'alamin).\""],[7017,"I prayed behind the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, Abu Bakr, 'Umar, and 'Uthman, ؓ , and I did not hear any of them recite aloud, \"In the name of Allah, the Most Merciful, the Most Compassionate.\""],[7018,"The Prophet ﷺ, Abu Bakr, 'Umar, and 'Uthman, ؓ , used to begin the recitation with \"Praise be to Allah, Lord of the worlds.\""],[7019,"I prayed behind Abu Hurayrah, and he recited, \"In the name of Allah, the Most Merciful, the Most Compassionate,\" then he recited the Mother of the Quran until, when he reached \"and not of those who are astray,\" he said, \"Amin,\" and the people said, \"Amin.\" And he would say, \"Allah is Greatest\" every time he prostrated, and when he stood from the sitting, he said, \"Allah is Greatest,\" and when he said the salam, he said, \"By the One in whose hand is my soul, I am indeed the most like you in prayer to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ.\""],[7020,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ, Abu Bakr, and 'Umar, ؓ , would not recite aloud, \"In the name of Allah, the Most Merciful, the Most Compassionate.\""],[7021,"The Prophet ﷺ, Abu Bakr, and 'Umar, ؓ , would not recite aloud, \"In the name of Allah, the Most Merciful, the Most Compassionate,\" but they would recite aloud, \"Praise be to Allah, Lord of the worlds.\""],[7022,"He used to recite in Fajr: {Qaf. By the glorious Qur'an} [Qur'an 50:1]. He said: \"And his prayer afterwards was light.\""],[7023,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ would lead us in Fajr [reciting] al-Saffat."],[7024,"The Prophet ﷺ led them in the two protective surahs (al-Mu'awwidhatayn) in the Subh prayer."],[7025,"I prayed Fajr behind the Prophet ﷺ and heard him recite: 'So I swear by the retreating stars, the running [stars] that disappear.' And none of us would bend his back until he was fully prostrate."],[7026,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to recite in the Ghada (Fajr) prayer between sixty and a hundred verses."],[7027,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ would pray approximately like your prayer; he would lighten the prayer, and he would recite in Fajr al-Waqi'ah and similar surahs."],[7028,"He prayed the Fajr prayer with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and heard him recite in one of the two rak'ahs of Fajr: {and tall date-palms with ranged clusters} [Qur'an 50:10]."],[7029,"The Prophet ﷺ used to recite in Zuhr and Asr: Al-Sama' wa al-Tariq and Al-Sama' dhat al-Buruj."],[7030,"We used to estimate the standing of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ in Zuhr in the first two rak'ahs as the length of thirty verses in each rak'ah, the length of Alif Lam Mim Tanzil al-Sajdah. And we estimated his recitation in the first two rak'ahs of Asr as the length of the last two rak'ahs of Zuhr. And we estimated his standing in the last two rak'ahs of Asr as half of that."],[7031,"\"He used to recite in the first two rak'ahs of Zuhr and 'Asr the Fatihah of the Book and a surah, and sometimes he would let us hear a verse, and he would recite in the latter two rak'ahs the Fatihah of the Book.\""],[7032,"Umm al-Fadl bt. al-Harith heard him reciting \"By those sent forth in succession\" (al-Mursalat), and she said, \"O 'Abd Allah, you have reminded me by this recitation of this surah. It was indeed the last thing I heard from the Messenger of Allah ﷺ; he recited it in Maghrib.\""],[7033,"He heard the Prophet ﷺ recite in Maghrib \"By the Mount\" (al-Tur)."],[7034,"I came for the ransom of the people of Badr, and I heard the Prophet ﷺ while he was leading the people in Maghrib prayer, reciting \"By the Mount and a Book inscribed\" (al-Tur)."],[7035,"The Prophet ﷺ recited to them in Maghrib \"Those who disbelieve and avert from the way of Allah\" (i.e., Surah Muhammad)."],[7036,"He heard Marwan recite \"Say: He is Allah, the One\" (al-Ikhlas) and \"Indeed, We have granted you al-Kawthar\" (al-Kawthar), and Zayd said, \"I swear by Allah, I saw the Messenger of Allah ﷺ recite in it the longest of the two long surahs.\""],[7037,"\"I have not seen anyone whose prayer more closely resembled that of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ than so-and-so, a governor in Madinah.\" Sulayman said, \"I prayed behind him, and he would lengthen the first two rak'ahs of Zuhr and lighten the latter two, lighten 'Asr, recite in the first two rak'ahs of Maghrib the short surahs of al-Mufassal, in 'Isha' the medium surahs of al-Mufassal, and in Subh the long surahs of al-Mufassal.\""],[7038,"\"He was on a journey and recited in 'Isha' in one of the two rak'ahs 'By the fig and the olive' (al-Tin).\""],[7039,"\"The Prophet ﷺ commanded Mu'adh to recite in the 'Isha' prayer 'By the sun and its brightness,' 'By the night when it covers,' 'Glorify the name of your Lord, the Most High,' 'By the morning brightness,' and similar surahs.\""],[7040,"Mu'adh used to pray with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, then return to his people and lead them in prayer. One night the Prophet ﷺ delayed the prayer, so Mu'adh returned and led them, reciting Surah al-Baqarah. When a man from the people saw that, he turned aside to a corner of the mosque and prayed alone. They said, \"You have become a hypocrite.\" He said, \"No, but I will go to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and inform him.\" He came to the Prophet ﷺ and said, \"Mu'adh prays with you, then returns and leads us. You delayed the prayer last night, so he came and led us, reciting Surah al-Baqarah. I fell behind him and prayed alone, O Messenger of Allah. We are owners of water-drawing camels and we work with our hands.\" The Prophet ﷺ said, \"O Mu'adh, are you a troublemaker? Recite with them 'By the night when it covers,' 'Glorify the name of your Lord, the Most High,' and 'By the sky with its constellations.'\""],[7041,"We did not know what to say in prayer, so we used to say \"Peace be upon Gabriel, peace be upon Michael.\" Then the Prophet ﷺ taught us and said, \"Verily, Allah is As-Salam (the Peace). So when you sit for the two prostrations, say: 'All compliments, prayers, and good words are due to Allah. Peace be upon you, O Prophet, and the mercy of Allah and His blessings. Peace be upon us and upon the righteous servants of Allah.' Abu Wail said in his narration that Abdullah said: \"When I said it, every close angel, sent prophet, and righteous servant was covered.\" I bear witness that there is no deity except Allah, and I bear witness that Muhammad is His slave and Messenger.\""],[7042,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to teach us the tashahhud as he would teach us a surah from the Quran. He used to say: 'All compliments, blessed words, prayers, and good things are due to Allah. Peace be upon you, O Prophet, and the mercy of Allah and His blessings. Peace be upon us and upon the righteous servants of Allah. I bear witness that there is no god but Allah, and I bear witness that Muhammad is the Messenger of Allah.'"],[7043,"«I saw the Messenger of Allah ﷺ turning to his right and to his left until the whiteness of his cheek could be seen.»"],[7044,"He used to turn to his right and to his left until the whiteness of his cheek could be seen: “Peace be upon you and the mercy of Allah; peace be upon you and the mercy of Allah and His blessings.”"],[7045,"Whatever I have forgotten of things, I have not forgotten “the salutation of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ in prayer, to his right and to his left: ‘Peace be upon you and the mercy of Allah; peace be upon you and the mercy of Allah.’” Then he said: It is as if I am looking at the whiteness of his cheeks ﷺ."],[7046,"He used to give one taslimah to his right, tilting his face toward the qiblah with it."],[7047,"He used to turn away to his right."],[7048,"‘Abdullah [said]: “Let none of you make a share for Shaytan from himself, thinking that it is obligatory upon him to turn away only to his right. For I saw the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and most of his turning away was to his left.”"],[7049,"He prayed with the Prophet ﷺ, and he used to turn away from both his sides."],[7050,"Most of his turning away was to his left, toward the apartments."],[7051,"“Witr is Haqq.* Whoever wishes let him pray Witr with five (Rak’ah), and whoever wishes let him pray Witr with three (Rak’ah), and whoever wishes let him pray Witr with one (Rak’ah).” (Using translation from Ibn Mājah 1190)"],[7052,"On the authority of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ , he said, \"Witr (an odd number of units of prayer) is a right (obligatory). So whoever wishes to perform Witr with five (units of prayer), let them do so. And whoever wishes to perform Witr with three (units), let them do so. And whoever wishes to perform Witr with one (unit), let them do so. And whoever finds it difficult, let them gesture with their head.\""],[7053,"Nafi' said: Ibn Umar used to lengthen his prayer before the Friday prayer and would offer two rak'ahs after it in his house. He used to say that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ would do that. (Using translation from Abū Dāʾūd 1128)"],[7054,"“I was with Ibn ‘Umar and I lagged behind and prayed Witr. He said: ‘What kept you?’ I said: ‘I was praying Witr.’ He said: ‘Do you not have the best of examples in the Messenger of Allah ﷺ?’ I said: ‘Of course.’ He said: ‘The Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to pray Witr while riding his camel.’” (Using translation from Ibn Mājah 1200)"],[7055,"The Prophet Muhammad ﷺ said, \"Whoever catches the morning prayer (Fajr) and does not offer the Witr prayer, there is no Witr prayer for them.\""],[7056,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ prayed with us eight units of prayer and performed the Witr prayer during the month of Ramadan. When the approaching night came, we gathered in the mosque and hoped that he would come out and pray with us. We waited there until morning and then said, \"O Messenger of Allah, we hoped that you would come out and pray with us.\" He said, \"I disliked or feared that the Witr prayer would be made obligatory on you.\""],[7057,"\"A man asked the Messenger of Allah ﷺ: 'O Messenger of Allah, how many prayers has Allah enjoined upon His slaves?' He said: 'Allah has enjoined upon His slaves (five) prayers.' He said: 'O Messenger of Allah, is there anything before them or after them?' He said: 'Allah has enjoined upon His salves (five) prayers.' The man swore that he would not do anything more or less than that. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: 'If he is speaking the truth he will most certainly enter Paradise.'\" (Using translation from Nasāʾī 459)"],[7058,"“I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: ‘Five prayers that Allah has enjoined upon His slaves, so whoever does them, and does not omit anything out of negligence, on the Day of Resurrection Allah will make a covenant with him that He will admit him to Paradise. But whoever does them but omits something from them out of negligence, will not have such a covenant with Allah; if He wills He will punish him, and if He wills, He will forgive him.’” (Using translation from Ibn Mājah 1401)"],[7059,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: Five prayers and from one Friday prayer to (the next) Friday prayer is an expiation (of the sins committed in between their intervals) if major sins are not committed. (Using translation from Muslim 233a)"],[7060,"When the Messenger of Allah ﷺ sent Mu‘adh to Yemen, he said, “You will come upon a people from the People of the Book. Let the first thing to which you call them be worship of Allah. When they acknowledge Allah, inform them that Allah has obligated upon them five prayers in their day and night. When they do them, inform them that Allah has obligated upon them charity taken from their wealth and returned to their poor. When they obey this, take from them and avoid the best properties of the people.”"],[7061,"It was narrated from ‘Ali ؓ that The Prophet ﷺ used to pray Witr with three raka’hs (Using translation from Aḥmad 685)"],[7062,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ was lying in his house with his thighs uncovered. Abu Bakr asked permission, and he gave him permission while he was in that state, and he spoke. Then 'Umar asked permission, and he gave him permission while he was in that state, and he spoke. Then 'Uthman asked permission, and the Messenger of Allah ﷺ sat up and arranged his clothes, and he entered and spoke. When he left, 'A'ishah said: 'O Messenger of Allah, Abu Bakr entered and you did not stir for him nor mind him; then 'Umar entered and you did not stir for him nor mind him; then 'Uthman entered and you sat up and arranged your clothes.' The Prophet ﷺ said: \"Should I not feel shy before a man before whom the angels feel shy?\""],[7063,"\"That the Prophet ﷺ prayed witr with one rak'ah.\""],[7065,"\"That the Prophet ﷺ prayed witr with one rak'ah.\""],[7066,"\"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to recite in the two Rak'ahs of Witr after which he would say, 'Glorify the name of your Lord, the Most High' and 'Say, O disbelievers' and in the Witr, he would recite 'Say: He is Allah, the One', and 'Say: I take refuge in the Lord of daybreak' and 'Say: I take refuge in the Lord of mankind'.\""],[7067,"\"That the Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to separate between the two prostrations in prayer and the odd units.\""],[7068,"The Prophetﷺ used to separate between the two units of prayer known as \"Shaf'a\" and \"Witr\" by uttering the \"tasleem\" out loud for us to hear."],[7069,"“The Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to perform Witr and recite: ‘Glorify the Name of your Lord the Most High.’, [Al-A’la (87)] ‘Say: O you disbelievers!” [Al-Kafirun (109)] and ‘Say: Allah is One.”. [Al-Ikhlas (112)] (Using translation from Ibn Mājah 1171)"],[7070,"\"That the Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to perform Witr prayer with five (rak'ahs) and also used to perform Witr prayer with seven (rak'ahs).\""],[7071,"\"That the Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to perform Sunnah prayers of five units and would not sit down except in the last one of them.\""],[7072,"The translation of the given Arabic sentence into English is: \"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to perform five Rak'ahs of voluntary prayer (Tahajjud) and would not sit down in any of the five units except in the last one, he would sit and then make the Salam (the final salutation).\""],[7073,"\"I said: 'O Mother of the believers! Tell me about the Witr of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ.' She said: 'We used to prepare his siwak and water for purification, then Allah (SWT) would wake him when He willed to wake him at night. He would use the siwak and perform wudu, then pray eith rak'ahs; not sitting until the eighth rak'ah, when he would sit and remember Allah (SWT) and call upon Him. Then he would say the taslim loud enough for us to hear.'\" (Using translation from Nasāʾī 1315)"],[7074,"The translation of the given text from Arabic to English is as follows: \"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to perform nine units of Taraweeh prayer. After completing the eighth unit, he would sit and praise and remember Allah, make supplications, then he would stand up without saying the final salutation, and he would pray the ninth unit, remembering Allah and making supplications, then he would complete the prayer in a way that we could hear it. After that, he would pray two units of prayer while sitting.\""],[7075,"Regarding the night prayer of the Prophet (PBUH), it was reported that \"When the Messenger of Allah (PBUH) prayed Isha (night prayer), he would perform two extra rak'ahs (units of prayer) and then sleep. He would have his ablution and toothbrush next to his head. He would then wake up, use the toothbrush, perform ablution, pray, and perform two additional rak'ahs. Then he would stand and pray eight rak'ahs, reciting the Quran evenly among them. He would then perform the witr prayer with the ninth rak'ah and pray two rak'ahs while sitting. When the Prophet (PBUH) would shorten his recitation, he would decrease the number of rak'ahs in the eight rak'ah prayer to six. He would perform the witr prayer with the seventh rak'ah and pray two rak'ahs while sitting, reciting Surah Al-Kafirun in them and Surah Az-Zalzalah.\""],[7076,"“I asked ‘Aishah about the Witr of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. She said: ‘He prayed Witr at every part of the night, at the beginning, in the middle and at the end, when he died (he would perform it) just before dawn.’” (Using translation from Ibn Mājah 1185)"],[7077,"\"In the first rak'ah of witr, the Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to recite: \"GLorify the Name of your Lord, the Most High;\" in the second; \"Say: O you disbelievers!\" and in the third; \"Say: He is Allah, (the) One.\" (Using translation from Nasāʾī 1700)"],[7078,"Ubayy bin Ka'b said: \"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to recite in Witr: \"Glorify the Name of your Lord, the Most High;\" and \"Say: O you disbelievers!;' and 'Say: He is Allah, (the) One.' And when he said the salam, he would say: Subhanal-Malikil-Quddus (Glory be to the Sovereign, the Most Holy) three times.\" (Using translation from Nasāʾī 1729)"],[7079,"«I memorized from the Messenger of Allah ﷺ two rak'ahs before Zuhr, two rak'ahs after it, two rak'ahs after Maghrib, and two rak'ahs after Isha»"],[7080,"I asked 'A'ishah about the prayer of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. She said, «He used to pray four [rak'ahs] before Zuhr, two after Maghrib, two after Isha, and nine at night.» I said, \"Standing or sitting?\" She said, «He used to pray long at night sitting, and long at night standing.» I said, \"What would he do when standing, and what would he do when sitting?\" She said, «When he recited standing, he bowed standing, and when he recited sitting, he bowed sitting.»"],[7081,"I asked 'A'ishah about the prayer of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. She said, «He used to pray four [rak'ahs] before Zuhr, then he would go out and pray, then he would return and pray two rak'ahs, then he would go out for Maghrib, then he would return and pray two rak'ahs, then he would go out for Isha, then he would return and pray two rak'ahs, then he would pray nine at night.» He said, \"I said, 'Sitting or standing?'\" She said, «He used to pray long at night standing.» I said, \"When he recited standing?\" She said, «When he recited standing, he bowed standing, and when he recited sitting, he bowed sitting, then he would pray two rak'ahs before Fajr.»"],[7082,"Abū Hurayrah: Thus did the Messenger of Allah ﷺ recite."],[7083,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to recite in the Friday prayer: \"Glorify the name of your Lord, the Most High (al-Aʿlā)\" and \"Has there come to you the narration of the Overwhelming (al-Ghāshiyah)?\""],[7084,"Al-Ḍaḥḥāk b. Qays asked al-Nuʿmān b. Bashīr: What did the Messenger of Allah ﷺ recite on Friday after Sūrat al-Jumuʿah? He said: 'He ﷺ used to recite \"Has there come to you the narration of the Overwhelming (al-Ghāshiyah)?\"'"],[7085,"Umar b. al-Khattab asked Abu Waqid al-Laythi what the Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to recite on Fitr and Adha. He said, 'The Prophet ﷺ used to recite Qaf. By the Glorious Quran, and The Hour has drawn near and the moon has split.'"],[7086,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to recite on the two Eids: Glorify the name of your Lord, the Most High and Has the story of the Overwhelming reached you?"],[7087,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to recite on Friday in the Friday prayer: Glorify the name of your Lord, the Most High and Has the story of the Overwhelming reached you? And when Eid and Friday coincided on one day, he recited them both together in the Friday prayer and the Eid."],[7088,"He prayed two rak‘ahs during the eclipse of the sun and moon like your prayer."],[7089,"The sun was eclipsed during the time of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ , so the Messenger of Allah ﷺ stood up to pray. He continued to pray until he almost couldn't perform the rukoo' (bowing position), then he performed rukoo' until he almost couldn't raise his head, and then he raised his head. He began to supplicate, cry, and say, \"O Lord, did You not promise me not to punish them while I am among them? Did You not promise me not to punish them while we seek Your forgiveness?\" After the Messenger of Allah ﷺ finished praying, the sun became visible again. He stood up, praised and glorified Allah, and said, \"Verily, the sun and the moon are two signs from the signs of Allah. So, when they are eclipsed, rush to the remembrance of Allah.\" Then he said, \"Paradise was shown to me, and if I wished, I could have plucked a cluster from it. Hellfire was shown to me, and I became so cautious of it that I feared it would envelop you. So, I would say, 'Didn't You promise me not to punish them while I am among them? O Lord, didn't You promise me not to punish them while they seek Your forgiveness?'\" He said, \"Then I saw a pitch-black female camel tied. She was neither fed nor watered, and she was not allowed to eat from the vegetation on the ground. So, every time she turned towards it, she was burned by fire. I also saw a man being pushed in the Fire with two staffs having hooks at the tips. I also saw a man reclining on his elbow in the Fire.\""],[7090,"On the day the sun eclipsed, the Messenger of Allah ﷺ prayed four rak‘ahs in two rak‘ahs and four prostrations."],[7091,"A Jewish woman came to her and said, 'May Allah protect you from the torment of the grave.' ʿĀʾishah said to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, 'Are people truly tried in the grave?' The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, 'I seek refuge in Allah.' ʿĀʾishah said: Then the Prophet ﷺ went out for some purpose, and the sun was eclipsed. We went out to the chamber, and the women gathered around us. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ came, and that was in the forenoon. He stood to pray and made a long standing. Then he bowed, then raised his head and stood but not as long as the first standing. Then he bowed but not as long as his previous bowing. Then he prostrated. Then he stood for the second rakʿah and did the same, except that his bowing was shorter than in the first rakʿah. Then he prostrated, and the sun became clear. When he finished, he sat on the pulpit and said among other things, 'People are truly tried in their graves like the trial of the Dajjāl.' ʿĀʾishah said: After that, we used to hear him seeking refuge from the trial of the grave."],[7092,"The sun was eclipsed during the time of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ stood for prayer and recited a long surah. Then he bowed for about as long as his standing. Then he raised his head and began another surah until he had finished it. Then he bowed a second time. Then he raised his head and prostrated. Then he stood for the second rakʿah, also reciting a surah, and he stood for a shorter time than the first recitation. Then he bowed, and his bowing was shorter than the first. Then he prostrated. When he raised his head from prostration, he said, 'There is nothing that you are promised but that I have seen it in this station of mine. I saw myself wanting to take a bunch from Paradise when you saw me moving forward. And I saw Hellfire, parts of it smashing into each other, when you saw me step back. And I saw ʿAmr b. Luḥayy, who is the one who set free the sāʾibah camels.'"],[7093,"\"There was an eclipse of the sun and the Messenger of Allah ﷺ ordered a man to call out: As-salatu jami'ah (prayer is about to begin in congregation). The people gathered and the Messenger of Allah ﷺ led them in prayer. He said the takbir, then he recited at length. Then he said the takbir and bowed for a long time, as long as he had recited or longer. Then he raised his head and said: Sami Allahu liman hamidah (Allah hears those who praise Him) Then he recited at length, but it was shorter than the first time, then he said the takbir and bowed for a long time, but it was shorter than the first time. Then he raised his head and said: 'Sami Allahu liman hamidah (Allah hears those who praise Him). Then he said the takbir and prostrated for a long time, as long as he had bowed or longer. Then he said the takbir and raised his head, then he said the takbir and prostrated. Then he said the takbir and stood up, and recited for a long time that was shorter than the first time. Then he said the takbir and bowed for a long time that was shorter than the first time. Then he raised his head and said: Sami' Allahu liman hamidah. (Allah hears those who praise Him). Then he recited for a long time that was shorter than the first recitation in the second standing. Then he said the takbir and bowed for a long time that was shorter than the first time. Then he raised his head and said: Sami Allahu liman hamidah (Allah hears those who praise Him). Then he said the takbir and prostrated for a long time that was shorter than the first time. Then he recited the tashahhud, then he said the taslim. Then he stood before them and praised and glorified Allah, then he said: 'The sun and the moon do not become eclipsed for the death or birth of anyone, but they are two of the signs of Allah (SWT). Whichever of them becomes eclipsed, turn to Allah (SWT), the Mighty and Sublime, and pray.'\" (Using translation from Nasāʾī 1497)"],[7094,"The sun was eclipsed during the time of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ prayed and prolonged the standing. Then he bowed, then raised his head and stood but not as long as his first standing. Then he bowed, then raised his head and stood but not as long as his first standing. Then he bowed—three bowings. Then he prostrated. Then he raised his head and stood and bowed three bowings, in which he stood for shorter periods than his first standing. Then he prostrated. Then he finished, and the sun had become clear. He said, 'The sun and the moon do not eclipse because of anyone's death or life. They are two signs among Allah's signs. When you see an eclipse, pray until it clears.'"],[7095,"The sun was eclipsed during the time of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and that was on the day in which Ibrāhīm died. The people said, 'The sun has only eclipsed because of the death of Ibrāhīm.' The Prophet of Allah ﷺ stood and prayed with the people six bowings and four prostrations. He said the takbir, then recited, and prolonged the recitation. Then he bowed for about as long as he had stood. Then he raised his head and recited, but for a shorter time than the first recitation. Then he bowed for about as long as his recitation. Then he raised his head and recited for a shorter time than the second recitation. Then he bowed for about as long as his recitation. Then he raised his head and prostrated twice. Then he stood and prayed three bowings before prostrating, in which each bowing was preceded by a standing, and the earlier standing was longer than the later one, except that his bowing was about as long as his standing. Then he moved back in his prayer, and the rows moved back with him. Then he moved forward, and the rows moved forward with him. Then he completed the prayer, and the sun had brightened. Then he said, 'O people, the sun and the moon are two signs among Allah's signs. They do not eclipse because of the death of any human. When you see any of that, pray until it clears.'"],[7096,"The sun was eclipsed during the time of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ prayed with the people. He stood and prolonged the standing. Then he bowed and prolonged the bowing. Then he stood and prolonged the standing, but it was shorter than the first standing. Then he bowed and prolonged the bowing, but it was shorter than the first bowing. Then he rose and prostrated. Then he did in the other rakʿah the same as he had done in the first. Then he finished, and the sun had become clear. He addressed the people, praised Allah and extolled Him, then said, 'The sun and the moon are two signs among Allah's signs. They do not eclipse because of anyone's death or life. When you see that, then call upon Allah, glorify Him, and give charity.' And he said, 'O ummah of Muḥammad ﷺ, by Allah, there is no one more jealous than Allah that His servant or His maidservant should commit adultery. O ummah of Muḥammad, by Allah, if you knew what I know, you would laugh little and weep much.'"],[7097,"\"There was an eclipse of the sun during the time of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. He stood and prayed, standing for a very long time, then he bowed for a very long time. Then he stood up and (remained standing) for a very long time, but shorter than the first time. Then he bowed for a very long time, but shorter than the first time. Then he prostrated, then he raised his head and stood for a long time, but it was shorter than the first time. The he stood up and (remained standing) for a long time, but it was shorter than the first time. Then he prostrated, and when he finished his prayer, the eclipse had ended. He addressed the people and praised and glorified Allah, then he said: 'The sun and the moon do not become eclipsed for the death or birth of anyone. If you see that then pray, give in charity, and remember Allah, the Mighty and Sublime.' And he said: 'O Ummah of Muhammad! There is no one who is more jealous than Allah (SWT) when His male or female slave commits Zina. O Ummah of Muhammad, if you knew what I know, you would laugh little and weep much.'\" (Using translation from Nasāʾī 1500)"],[7098,"The sun was eclipsed in the time of the Prophet ﷺ. He stood in alarm, then said, 'These signs that Allah sends do not occur because of anyone's death or life, but Allah sends them to frighten His servants thereby. When you see anything of them, hasten to His remembrance and His forgiveness.'"],[7099,"'I was shooting arrows in Madinah when an eclipse occurred, and I threw them down.' I said, 'By Allah, I shall certainly see what happens to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ during the eclipse of the sun.' He said: 'I came to him while he ﷺ was standing in prayer, raising his hands.' He said: 'He began to glorify Allah, praise Him, say takbir, say tahlil, and supplicate until it cleared. When it cleared, he recited two surahs and prayed two rakʿahs.'"],[7100,"\"The sun was eclipsed during the time of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and the Messenger of Allah ﷺ prayed four bowings in two rakʿahs and four prostrations, and he recited aloud.\""],[7101,"\"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ prayed the eclipse prayer with us, and we did not hear any sound from him.\""],[7102,"He attended a khutbah one day delivered by Samurah b. Jundub, and in his khutbah he mentioned a hadith from the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. Samurah said: While I and a boy from the Anṣār were one day shooting at a target of ours during the time of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, when the sun was about two or three spear-lengths above the horizon, in the eyes of an observer, it became dark. One of us said to his companion, 'Let us go to the mosque, for by Allah, this sun will surely bring about something new for the Messenger of Allah ﷺ in his ummah.' He said: So we hurried to the mosque and met the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and there he was, having just come out to the people. He said: He stepped forward and led us in prayer, and it was the longest standing he ever led us in, and we did not hear any sound from him. Then he prostrated, and it was the longest prostration we had ever made in any prayer, and we did not hear any sound from him. Then he sat in the second rakʿah, and it was likewise. He said: The clearing of the sun coincided with his sitting in the second rakʿah, and then he said the taslim."],[7103,"The sun was eclipsed during the time of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ prayed, and the people were with him. He stood for a long time, about the length of Surah al-Baqarah. Then he bowed for a long time. Then he raised and stood for a long time, but it was shorter than the first standing. Then he bowed for a long time, but it was shorter than the first bowing. Then he prostrated. Then he stood for a long time, but it was shorter than the first standing, and he bowed for a long time, but it was shorter than the first bowing. Then he prostrated. Then he finished, and the sun had become clear. He said, 'The sun and the moon are two signs among Allah's signs. They do not eclipse because of anyone's death or life. When you see that, then remember Allah.' They said, 'O Messenger of Allah, we saw you reach out for something in this station of yours, and then we saw you step back.' He said, 'I saw Paradise — or I was shown Paradise — and I reached out for a bunch of grapes from it. Had I taken it, you would have eaten from it as long as the world remains. And I saw the Fire, and I have never seen a sight like today at all. And I saw that most of its inhabitants are women.' They said, 'For what reason, O Messenger of Allah?' He said, 'Because of their ingratitude.' It was said, 'Are they ungrateful to Allah?' He said, 'They are ungrateful to their husbands and ungrateful for good treatment. If you treated one of them well for a long time and then she saw something from you, she would say, \"By Allah, I have never seen any good from you.\"'"],[7104,"“We used to regard the signs in the time of the Prophet ﷺ as blessings, while you regard them as a cause for fear.”"],[7106,"Allah, Mighty and Exalted, made prayer obligatory on the tongue of your Prophet ﷺ: while resident, four [rak'ahs]; while traveling, two rak'ahs; and during fear, one rak'ah."],[7107,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ led them in the prayer of fear. A row stood before him and a row behind him. He led them in one rak'ah and two prostrations. Then those [in front] came and stood [where the others had been] and those [behind] came forward, and the Messenger of Allah ﷺ led them in one rak'ah and two prostrations. Thus the Prophet ﷺ had two rak'ahs and they had one rak'ah each."],[7108,"I came to Zayd b. Thabit and asked him about the prayer of fear. He said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ prayed with a row behind him and a row facing the enemy. He led them in one rak'ah. Then they went to the positions of their brothers, and the others came, and he led them in one rak'ah. Then he said the taslim. So the Prophet ﷺ had two rak'ahs and each group had one rak'ah."],[7109,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ prayed at Dhu Qarad. The people formed two rows behind him: a row behind him and a row facing the enemy. He led the row nearest to him in one rak'ah. Then those [who had prayed] went back to the positions of those [who had not prayed], and those came to the positions of those, and he led them in one rak'ah, and they did not make [it] up."],[7110,"We were with Saʿīd b. al-ʿĀṣ in Ṭabaristān, and he said: “Which of you prayed with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ the prayer of fear?” Ḥudhayfah said: “I did.” He said: “Then Ḥudhayfah stood and arranged the people behind him in two rows—a row behind him and a row facing the enemy—and he prayed with those behind him one rakʿah, then these moved to the place of those, and those came, and he prayed with them one rakʿah, and they did not make up [the other].”"],[7111,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ camped between Dajnan and 'Usfan and besieged the polytheists. They said: These people have a prayer that is dearer to them than their sons and their virgins — meaning the 'Asr prayer. So make up your mind, then fall upon them with one single assault. Then Jibril came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and ordered him to divide his companions into two groups, to lead the first group in one rak'ah while the other group took their guard and their weapons, and when he had led them in one rak'ah they would move back and the others would come forward, and he would lead them in one rak'ah while those others took their guard and their weapons. Thus each group had one rak'ah with the Prophet ﷺ."],[7112,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ prayed the prayer of fear at Dhat al-Riqa'. She said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ split the people into two groups. One group formed a row behind him and one group stood facing the enemy. She said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said the takbir and the group that had formed a row behind him said the takbir. Then he bowed and they bowed. Then he prostrated and they prostrated. Then he raised his head and they raised [theirs]. Then the Messenger of Allah ﷺ remained sitting while they prostrated the second prostration by themselves. Then they stood and stepped backward on their heels, walking backwards until they stood behind them. Then the other group came and formed a row behind the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. They said the takbir, then bowed by themselves. Then the Messenger of Allah ﷺ prostrated the second prostration and they prostrated with him. Then the Messenger of Allah ﷺ stood up from his rak'ah and they prostrated the second prostration by themselves. Then both groups stood together and formed a row behind the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. He led them in one rak'ah and they all bowed. Then he prostrated and they all prostrated. Then he raised his head and they raised with him — all of that from the Messenger of Allah ﷺ was very quick, not failing to lighten as much as he could. Then the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said the taslim and they said the taslim. Then the Messenger of Allah ﷺ stood up and the people had shared with him in his entire prayer."],[7113,"The Prophet ﷺ led his companions in the prayer of fear. He bowed with both [groups] together. Then the Messenger of Allah ﷺ prostrated, and the row that was next to him [prostrated], while the others remained standing until he arose. Then those prostrated by themselves two prostrations. Then the front row moved back, and the Prophet ﷺ bowed and the row that was next to him [bowed]. When they raised their heads, those prostrated two prostrations. All of them had bowed with the Prophet ﷺ, and they prostrated by themselves two prostrations. The enemy was toward the qiblah."],[7114,"The Prophet ﷺ was in Usfan while the polytheists were in Dujnan. When the Prophet ﷺ performed the Dhuhr prayer, the polytheists saw him bowing and prostrating, so they decided to change their direction. When the Asr prayer approached, the people lined up behind him in two rows. The Prophet ﷺ then said \"Allahu Akbar\" and everyone following him said the same and they all bowed and prostrated. The row behind them, with their weapons in hand, stood facing the enemy. When the Prophet ﷺ raised his head from prostration, the second row also prostrated. When they raised their heads, they all bowed and prostrated. The row behind them, with their weapons in hand, stood facing the enemy. When the Prophet ﷺ raised his head from prostration, the second row also prostrated."],[7115,"We were with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ at 'Usfan, and Khalid b. al-Walid was in command of the polytheists. He said: We prayed Zuhr, and the polytheists said: They were in a state such that, had we wished, we could have caught them off guard, or caught them unaware. He said: Then the verse of shortening was revealed between Zuhr and 'Asr. The people took up their weapons and formed two rows behind the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, facing the enemy, and the polytheists were facing them. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said the takbir and they all said the takbir. Then he bowed and they all bowed. Then he raised his head and they all raised [theirs]. Then he prostrated and the row next to him prostrated, while the others remained standing guarding them. When those finished their prostration, the others prostrated. Then the row next to him stepped back and the others came forward and stood in their place. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ bowed and they all bowed. Then the Messenger of Allah ﷺ raised [his head] and they all raised [theirs]. Then he prostrated and the row next to him prostrated, while the others remained standing guarding them. When those finished their prostration, the others prostrated. Then they stood together with him and sat all together. Then he said the taslim to all of them. He prayed it at 'Usfan and he prayed it on the day of Banu Sulaym."],[7116,"He heard Jabir ibn Abdullah say, \"We went on expeditions with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ against a people from Juhaynah and fought them fiercely. After we prayed the Dhuhr prayer, they said, 'If we attacked them now, we would defeat them.' Jabir said that Jibril informed the Prophet ﷺ about that, and the Messenger of Allah ﷺ mentioned it to us. He said, The prayer between us and them is more beloved to them than the earlier prayer. When the time for prayer came, we formed two rows while the polytheists stood between us and the Qiblah (direction of prayer). The Messenger of Allah ﷺ then made the Takbir and we made the Takbir with him. He then performed the Ruku (bowing) and we performed the Ruku with him. He then performed the Sujud (prostration) and the first row performed the Sujud with him. When he stood up from Sujud, the first row performed the Sujud, and the second row advanced and stood in the place of the first row while the first row sat back. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ made the Takbir and we made the Takbir with him. He then performed the Ruku and we performed the Ruku with him. He then performed the Sujud and the first row performed the Sujud with him. He then sat down and the second row performed the Sujud. Then, they all gave Salam (peace)."],[7117,"I heard Abu Hurayrah while Marwan b. al-Hakam asked him about the prayer of fear. Abu Hurayrah said: I was with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ in that expedition. He said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ split the people into two groups. One group stood with him and the other group stood facing the enemy, with their backs to the qiblah. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said the takbir, and they all said the takbir — those with him and those fighting the enemy. Then the Messenger of Allah ﷺ bowed one rak'ah, and the group that was next to him bowed with him. Then he prostrated and the group that was next to him prostrated, while the others remained standing facing the enemy. Then the Messenger of Allah ﷺ stood up, and the group that had prayed with him took their weapons and walked backwards on their heels until they stood facing the enemy. Then the group that had been facing the enemy came forward and bowed and prostrated while the Messenger of Allah ﷺ remained standing as he was. Then they stood up, and the Messenger of Allah ﷺ bowed another rak'ah and they bowed with him, and he prostrated and they prostrated with him. Then the group that had been facing the enemy came forward and bowed and prostrated while the Messenger of Allah ﷺ was sitting, along with those with him. Then came the taslim, and the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said the taslim and they all said the taslim. Thus the people stood up and had shared with him in the prayer."],[7118,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ led us in the prayer of fear: with one of the two groups he prayed one rak'ah while the other group faced the enemy. Then they left and stood in the place of their companions, facing the enemy, and those came, and the Prophet ﷺ led them in one rak'ah. Then the Prophet ﷺ said the taslim with them, and those went and stood in the place of their companions, facing the enemy, and those came, and the Prophet ﷺ led them in one rak'ah. Then the Prophet ﷺ said the taslim with them, and these made up one rak'ah and those made up one rak'ah."],[7119,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ stood up and the people stood up with him. He said the takbir and they said the takbir with him. Then he bowed, and some people among them bowed with him. Then he prostrated and they prostrated. Then he stood up for the second rak'ah. Those who had prostrated with him stepped back guarding their brothers, and the other group came and bowed with the Prophet of Allah ﷺ and prostrated, while all the people were in prayer, saying the takbir, but some of them were guarding others."],[7120,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ arranged them in two rows and prayed two rak'ahs with the row that was closest to him, then he said the taslim. They moved back and the others came forward, and he prayed two rak'ahs with them, then he said the taslim. Thus the Messenger of Allah ﷺ had four rak'ahs and the Muslims had two rak'ahs each."],[7121,"He asked Jabir b. 'Abd Allah about the shortening of prayer in fear: where was it revealed and where is it? He said: We went out to meet a caravan of Quraysh that had come from Syria. When we were at Nakhl, a man came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ while his sword was placed down and said, 'Are you Muhammad?' He said, 'Yes.' He said, 'Are you not afraid of me?' He said, 'No.' He said, 'Then who will protect you from me?' He said, 'Allah protects me from you.' He said, so he drew his sword and threatened him, and the people threatened and intimidated him. Then the Messenger of Allah ﷺ ordered the people to depart and take up their weapons. Then he called for prayer, and one group prayed behind him while another group kept guard facing the enemy. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ prayed two rak'ahs with the group that was with him, then the other group came and stood in the rows of those who had prayed with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and the group that had prayed with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ kept guard facing the enemy. Then the Messenger of Allah ﷺ prayed two rak'ahs with them, so the Messenger of Allah ﷺ had four rak'ahs and his companions had two rak'ahs."],[7122,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ fought Muharib Khasafah at Nakhl, and they saw an opportunity against the Muslims. A man from them called 'Awf b. al-Harith or Ghawrath b. al-Harith came and stood over the head of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ with a sword and said, 'Who will protect you from me?' He said, 'Allah.' Then the sword fell from his hand, and the Messenger of Allah ﷺ took the sword and said to him, 'Who will protect you from me?' He said, 'Be better than me.' He said, 'Will you testify that there is no god but Allah?' He said, 'No, but I will make a pact with you that I will not fight you and will not be with a people who fight you.' So he let him go. He went back to his companions and said, 'I have come to you from the best of people.' When it was noon or afternoon—Abu 'Awanah was unsure—the Prophet ﷺ ordered the prayer of fear. The people were two groups: one group facing the enemy and one group praying with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. He prayed two rak'ahs with the group that was with him, then they left and took the place of the others, and the others came and prayed two rak'ahs with the Prophet ﷺ. Thus the Messenger of Allah ﷺ had four rak'ahs and the people had two rak'ahs."],[7123,"We advanced with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ until when we were at Dhat al-Riqa', the call 'prayer in congregation' was made. He prayed two rak'ahs with one group, then they moved back and he prayed two rak'ahs with the other group. Thus the Messenger of Allah ﷺ had four rak'ahs and the people had two rak'ahs."],[7124,"Regarding the prayer of fear, he said: 'One group stands behind the imam and another group behind them. He prays one rak'ah and two prostrations with those behind him, then he sits in his place until they complete one rak'ah and two prostrations. Then they move to the place of their companions, and their companions move to the place of these. He prays one rak'ah and two prostrations with them, then he sits in his place until they pray one rak'ah and two prostrations, then he says the taslim.'"],[7125,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: 'In the prayer of fear, the imam stands with a group of people and they prostrate one prostration, while another group is between them and the enemy. Then those who prostrated one prostration with the imam leave and take the place of those who have not prayed, and those come and pray one prostration with their imam. Then their imam leaves, and each group prays one prostration on its own. If fear is more intense than that, then on foot or riding.'"],[7127,"'Umar b. al-Khattab came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ on the night of the Trench and said, 'O Messenger of Allah, I could hardly pray 'asr until the sun was about to set, and that was after the fasting person had broken his fast.' He said, 'By Allah, we have not prayed it yet.' Then he went down to Buthan, and I was with him. He performed ablution and then prayed 'asr after the sun had set and after the fasting person had broken his fast."],[7128,"We were held back on the day of the Trench until after sunset, and that was before the revelation about fighting came down. When the fighting was over—and that is the saying of Allah, may He be majestic and exalted, {And Allah sufficed the believers in fighting, and Allah is Strong, Mighty}—the Messenger of Allah ﷺ ordered Bilal, and he called the iqamah for zuhr, and he prayed it as he used to pray it in its time. Then he called the iqamah for 'asr, and he prayed it as he used to pray it in its time. Then he called the iqamah for maghrib, and he prayed it as he used to pray it in its time."],[7129,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ announced the death of the Negus to the people on the day he died. He went out with them to the prayer ground, arranged them in rows, and said four takbirs."],[7130,"Zayd b. Arqam used to say four takbirs over our funerals, then he would say five. We asked him about that, and he said, “The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said them.”"],[7131,"I asked Abu al-Tufayl, \"What are the three corners that are supported by the Kaaba?\" Abu al-Tufayl said, \"I asked Ibn 'Abbas about that, and he said: When the Messenger of Allah ﷺ halted at Marr al-Zahran during the truce with Quraysh, word reached the companions of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ that Quraysh were saying, 'You are pledging allegiance to weak ones.' His companions said, 'O Messenger of Allah, if only we could eat from our camels, eat their fat and sip the broth, and rise tomorrow so that when we enter upon the people we have vigor.' He said, 'No, but bring me the surplus of your provisions.' They spread out their leather mats and gathered upon them all kinds of their food, and he prayed for blessing for them in it. They ate until they were full to the point of satiety, then they gathered the leftovers into their bags. When the Messenger of Allah ﷺ entered upon Quraysh and Quraysh gathered near the Stone, the Messenger of Allah ﷺ uncovered his right shoulder, then the Prophet ﷺ said to his companions, 'Let not the people see any weakness in you.' He touched the Yemeni Corner, and when Quraysh disappeared, he and his companions walked until they touched the Black Stone. He circumambulated three rounds, and that is why Quraysh said as they passed by them while they were doing ramal, 'It is as if they are gazelles.' Ibn 'Abbas said, 'And it became a sunnah.'\""],[7133,"I asked ‘A’ishah, the wife of the Prophet ﷺ, and said to her: “Have you considered the saying of Allah: ‘Indeed, al-Safa and al-Marwa are among the rites of Allah’ until the end of the verse? By Allah, there is no blame upon anyone not to go between al-Safa and al-Marwa.” ‘A’ishah said: “How bad is what you have said, O son of my sister! If this verse were as you have interpreted it, it would have been: ‘there is no blame upon him not to go between them.’ But it was revealed concerning the Ansar before they embraced Islam. They used to declare the talbiyah for Manat, the false deity whom they used to worship at al-Mushallal, and whoever declared the talbiyah for her used to consider it sinful to go between al-Safa and al-Marwa. When they embraced Islam, they asked the Messenger of Allah ﷺ about that and said: ‘O Messenger of Allah, we used to consider it sinful to go between al-Safa and al-Marwa.’ Then Allah revealed: ‘Indeed, al-Safa and al-Marwa are among the rites of Allah; so whoever performs Hajj of the House or ‘Umrah, there is no blame upon him to go between them.’” ‘A’ishah said: “Then the Messenger of Allah ﷺ established the Sunnah of going between them, so it is not for anyone to abandon going between them.”"],[7134,"I said to Ibn ‘Abbas: “Your people claim that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ did ramal and that it is a Sunnah.” He said: “They have lied and they have spoken truth. When the Messenger of Allah ﷺ entered Makkah, the polytheists were on Qu‘ayqi‘an, and they said that Muhammad ﷺ and his companions were weakened. So the Messenger of Allah ﷺ did ramal and commanded his companions, and they did ramal, but it is not a Sunnah.”"],[7135,"I said to Ibn ‘Abbas: “Have you considered this ramal at the House for three circuits and walking for four circuits? Is it a Sunnah? For your people claim that it is a Sunnah.” He said: “They have spoken truth and they have lied.” I said: “What do you mean by ‘They have spoken truth and they have lied’?” He said: “The Messenger of Allah ﷺ came to Makkah, and the polytheists said: ‘Muhammad and his companions are unable to circumambulate the House due to weakness.’” He said: “And they used to envy him.” He said: “So the Messenger of Allah ﷺ commanded them to do ramal for three circuits and walk for four.” He said: “So I said to him...”"],[7136,"A man came to the Prophet ﷺ and said, 'O Messenger of Allah, what do you think about a man who sees a man with his wife—should he kill him and you would kill him, or how should he act?' Then Allah, glorified and exalted, revealed what is mentioned in the Qur'an about the li'an spouses. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to him, 'A judgment has been given concerning you and your wife.' He (the narrator) said, 'So they performed li'an while I was present with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. Then he said, \"O Messenger of Allah, if I keep her, I will have lied about her.\" So he separated from her, and it became a sunnah thereafter that the li'an spouses be separated. She was pregnant, and he denied her pregnancy, and her son was attributed to her. Then the sunnah regarding inheritance was established: that she inherit from him and he inherit from her as Allah ordained for her.'"],[7137,"'Uwaimir al-'Ajlani came to 'Asim b. 'Adi al-Ansari and said to him, 'O 'Asim, what do you think: if a man finds a man with his wife, should he kill him and you would kill him, or how should he act? Ask the Messenger of Allah ﷺ about that for me.' So 'Asim asked the Messenger of Allah ﷺ about that, and the Messenger of Allah ﷺ disliked such questions and criticized them, so much so that it became burdensome for 'Asim what he heard from the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. When 'Asim returned to his family, 'Uwaimir came to him and said, 'O 'Asim, what did the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say to you?' 'Asim said to 'Uwaimir, 'You have not brought me any good. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ disliked the question I asked him about.' 'Uwaimir said, 'By Allah, I will not stop until I ask him about it.' So 'Uwaimir came while the Messenger of Allah ﷺ was among the people, and the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, 'Revelation has come concerning you and your wife, so go and bring her.' Sahl said, 'So they performed li'an while I was with the people near the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. When they finished their li'an, 'Uwaimir said, \"I lied about her, O Messenger of Allah, if I keep her.\" So he divorced her three times before the Messenger of Allah ﷺ commanded him.'"],[7138,"'Uwaimir al-'Ajlani came to 'Asim b. 'Adi, who was the chief of Banu 'Ajlan, and said, 'What do you say about a man who finds a man with his wife—should he kill him and you would kill him, or how should he act?' He said, 'Ask the Messenger of Allah ﷺ about that for me.' So 'Asim went to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and said, 'O Messenger of Allah, a man finds a man with his wife—should he kill him and you would kill him, or how should he act?' The Messenger of Allah ﷺ disliked such questions and criticized them. Then 'Asim came to 'Uwaimir and said to him, 'The Prophet ﷺ has disliked such questions and criticized them.' 'Uwaimir said, 'By Allah, I will not stop until I ask the Messenger of Allah ﷺ about that.' So 'Uwaimir went and asked him, and the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, 'Allah, glorified and exalted, has revealed (verses) concerning you and your wife.' The Messenger of Allah ﷺ commanded them, so they performed li'an using what Allah named in His Book. He said, 'So he pronounced li'an against her, then said, \"O Messenger of Allah, if I keep her, I will have wronged her.\" So he divorced her, and it became a sunnah for those after them among the li'an spouses. Then the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, \"Observe: if she gives birth to a child who is dark, with very black eyes, large buttocks, and thick legs, then I think 'Uwaimir has spoken truthfully about her; but if she gives birth to a reddish child as if he were a small lizard, then I think 'Uwaimir has lied about her.\" He said, 'So she gave birth to a child matching the description the Messenger of Allah ﷺ gave, confirming 'Uwaimir.' He said, 'Thereafter the child was attributed to his mother.'"],[7139,"What do you think: if one of us sees his wife committing lewdness, how should he act? If he speaks, he speaks about a grave matter, and if he remains silent, he remains silent about the like. The Prophet ﷺ did not answer him. Later, he came to the Prophet ﷺ and said, 'O Messenger of Allah, the matter I asked you about has befallen me.' Then Allah, glorified and exalted, revealed these verses. He called the man and recited them to him, admonished him, reminded him, and informed him that the punishment of this world is lighter than the punishment of the Hereafter. He said, 'No, by the One who sent you with the truth, I did not lie about her.' Then he called the woman, admonished her, reminded her, and informed her that the punishment of this world is lighter than the punishment of the Hereafter. She said, 'By the One who sent you with the truth, he is lying.' He began with the man, who testified four times by Allah that he was truthful, and the fifth that the curse of Allah be upon him if he was lying. Then he followed with the woman, who testified four times by Allah that he was lying, and the fifth that the wrath of Allah be upon her if he was truthful. Then he separated them."],[7140,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to the two li'an spouses, 'Your account is with Allah; one of you is lying. You have no way against her.' He said, 'O Messenger of Allah, what about my property?' He said, 'You have no property. If you were truthful about her, then it is what you made lawful of her private part; and if you were lying about her, then that is even further from you.'"],[7141,"A man pronounced li'an against his wife in the time of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and disowned her child. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ separated them and attached the child to the woman."],[7142,"Ibn Abbas was asked about a woman who gave birth forty nights after her husband's death. Ibn Abbas said, 'The later of the two terms.' Abu Salamah said: I said, 'But has not Allah said: \"And for those who are pregnant, their term is until they give birth\"?' Abu Hurayrah said, 'I am with my nephew,' meaning Abu Salamah. So Ibn Abbas sent Kurayb to the wives of the Prophet ﷺ to ask them whether they had heard any Sunnah from the Messenger of Allah ﷺ concerning that. They sent back to him: 'Subay'ah al-Aslamiyyah gave birth forty nights after her husband's death, and the Messenger of Allah ﷺ had her married.'"],[7143,"\"Do not impose upon us the practice of our Prophet's Sunnah, 'iddah for the mother of the child, the 'iddah of the deceased from her husband.\""],[7144,"A man had six slaves and freed them at his death, and he had no property besides them. The matter was brought to the Prophet ﷺ, and he disliked it. He divided them into three portions and cast lots among them; then he freed two and kept four as slaves."],[7145,"\"Take from me: Allah has made a way for them. The virgin with the virgin and the previously married with the previously married: the virgin is flogged and exiled, and the previously married is flogged and stoned.\""],[7146,"A man from the Bedouins came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and said: \"O Messenger of Allah, I adjure you by Allah to judge for me according to the Book of Allah.\" The other disputant, who was more knowledgeable than him, said: \"Yes, judge between us according to the Book of Allah and allow me to speak.\" The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"Speak.\" He said: \"My son was a hired worker for this man and he committed adultery with his wife. I was told that my son must be stoned, so I ransomed him with one hundred sheep and a slave girl. Then I asked the people of knowledge and they told me that my son must be flogged one hundred lashes and banished for a year, and that stoning is upon his wife.\" The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"By the One in Whose hand is my soul, I will judge between you according to the Book of Allah. The slave girl and the sheep are to be returned to you, and upon your son is one hundred lashes and banishment for a year. Go, O Unays, to the wife of this man, and if she confesses, stone her.\" He went to her the next morning and she confessed, so the Messenger of Allah ﷺ ordered her to be stoned."],[7147,"“The Prophet ﷺ flogged for the hadd with palm branches and sandals.” When Abu Bakr ؓ came, he flogged forty. When Umar came, the people approached the countryside and villages, so it was mentioned to his companions, and Abd al-Rahman said, “Make it like the lightest of the hadd punishments.”"],[7148,"\"That the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and Abu Bakr were lashed for alcohol with a whip and sandals. When Umar ibn al-Khattab became the caliph, people from the countryside and villages approached him. Umar consulted the people regarding the punishment for alcohol. Abdul Rahman ibn Awf said, 'O Amir al-Mu'minin (Commander of the Believers), whenever someone drinks it, they should be expelled. And whenever someone is expelled, they should be stoned. So we suggest that you make it the lightest of punishments.' The first person to be lashed for alcohol was Umar bin Khattab, may Allah be pleased with him, and there were eighty others after him.\""],[7149,"A man came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ having drunk wine. He ordered him and he was beaten with two sandals forty times. Then a man who had drunk wine was brought to Abu Bakr, and he did the same with him. Then a man who had drunk wine was brought to Umar, and he consulted the people about it. Abd al-Rahman b. Awf said, “The lightest of the hadd punishments is eighty.” So Umar ؓ beat him eighty."],[7150,"\"The first Li'an in Islam was when Hilal bin Umayyah accused Sharik bin As-Sahma' (of committing adultery) with his wife. He came to the Prophet and told him about that. The Prophet said: '(Bring) four witnesses, otherwise (you will feel) the Hadd punishment on your back.' And he repeated that several times. Hilal said to him: 'By Allah, O Messenger of Allah! Allah, the Mighty and Sublime, knows that I am telling the truth, and Allah, the Mighty and Sublime, will certainly reveal to you that which will spare my back from the whip.' While they were like that, the Verse of Li'an was revealed to him: 'As to those who accuse their wives.' He called Hilal and he bore witness four times by Allah that he was telling the truth, and the fifth time he invoked the curse of Allah upon him if he were lying. Then he called the woman and she bore witness four times by Allah that he was lying. When it came to the fourth or fifth time, the Messenger of Allah said: 'Stop her, for it will inevitably bring the punishment of Allah upon the liar.' She hesitated until we thought that she was going to confess, then she said: 'I will not dishonor my people today.' Then she went ahead with the oath. The Messenger of Allah said: 'Wait and see. If she produces a child who is white, with straight hair and Qadiy'a eyes, then he belongs to Hilal bin Umayyah, but if she produces a child who is dark with curly hair, of average size and with narrow calves, then he belongs to Sharik bin As-Sahma'.' She produced a child who was dark with curly hair, of average size and with narrow calves. The Messenger of Allah said: 'Had not the matter been settled by the Book of Allah, I would have punished her severely.'\" (Using translation from Nasāʾī 3469)"],[7151,"“The Messenger of Allah ﷺ cut off for a shield whose value was three dirhams.”"],[7152,"It did not pass long upon me, nor did I forget the amputation for a quarter dinar or more."],[7153,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ held a race between horses and gave preference to those with white blazes on their foreheads at the goal."],[7154,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ held a race between trained horses from al-Ḥafyāʾ to Thaniyyat al-Wadāʿ, and between untrained horses from al-Thaniyya to the mosque of Banū Zurayq. ʿAbd Allāh was among those who raced with them."],[7155,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ made for the horse two shares and for the man one share."],[7156,"«There was a slave jointly owned by me and some partners of mine. We took possession of him among ourselves, but one of the partners was absent. When he arrived, he refused to approve the division. We brought the dispute to Hisham, and he ruled that the slave and the gain he had produced should be returned. The gain had reached a thousand. I went to 'Urwah b. al-Zubayr and informed him.» He said, «'A'ishah informed me from the Messenger of Allah ﷺ that he ruled that the benefit is accompanied by liability.'» He said, «So I went to Hisham and informed him, and he returned the slave but did not return the gain.»"],[7157,"A man among the companions of the Prophet ﷺ manumitted a slave of his to be freed after his death, and he had no wealth other than him. So the Messenger of Allah ﷺ took him and sold him, and said: \"You are more in need of his price, and Allah is more independent of him.\""],[7158,"A man of the Ansar manumitted a slave of his to be freed after his death; the slave's name was Ya'qub, and the one who manumitted him was called Abu Madhkur, and he had no wealth other than him. The Prophet ﷺ called for him and said: \"Who will buy this from me?\" Nu'aym b. 'Abd Allah, the brother of Banu 'Adi b. Ka'b, bought him from him for eight hundred dirhams. Then he called for him and said: \"When you are poor, begin with yourself; if there is surplus, then for your dependents; if there is surplus, then for your relatives; if there is surplus, then here and there.\" When he related this hadith, he said: \"He was a Coptic slave who died last year.\""],[7159,"He demanded from Ibn Abi Hadrad a debt that he owed him during the time of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ in the mosque. Their voices rose until the Messenger of Allah ﷺ heard them while he was in his house. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ came out to them, lifted the curtain of his chamber, and called out, 'O Ka'b b. Malik!' He said, 'At your service, O Messenger of Allah.' He gestured with his hand, meaning, 'Remit half of your debt.' Ka'b said, 'I have done so, O Messenger of Allah.' He said, 'Arise and settle it.'"],[7160,"\"That two men claimed ownership of a camel, so each of them presented two witnesses. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ then judged between them, dividing the camel into two halves.\""],[7162,"A man from Hadramawt and a man from Kindah came to the Prophet ﷺ. The Hadrami said, 'O Messenger of Allah, this man has overpowered me regarding a land of mine that belonged to my father.' The Kindi said, 'It is my land, in my possession; I have cultivated it. He has no right in it.' The Prophet ﷺ said to the Hadrami, 'Do you have evidence?' He said, 'No.' He said, 'Then you have his oath.' He said, 'O Messenger of Allah, the man is wicked; he does not care what he swears to, and he does not refrain from anything.' He said, 'You have nothing from him except that.' He said, 'So he went to make him swear. When he turned away, the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, 'Indeed, if he swears about his property to consume it unjustly, he will meet Allah, majestic and exalted is He, while He is turning away from him.'"],[7163,"A man freed six slaves of his upon his death, and he had no property besides them. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ drew lots among them, freed two, and returned four to slavery."],[7164,"A Jew killed a girl for her ornaments, so the Messenger of Allah ﷺ killed him."],[7165,"A Jew killed a girl for ornaments she had, killing her with a stone. He said: She was brought while still breathing. He said to her: \"Did so-and-so kill you?\" She gestured with her head: No. Then he asked her a second time, and she gestured with her head: No. Then he asked her a third time, and she said: Yes, and gestured with her head. So the Messenger of Allah ﷺ killed him between two stones."],[7166,"A girl was found with her head crushed between two stones. They said to her: \"Who did this to you? So-and-so? So-and-so?\" until a Jewish man was mentioned, and she nodded with her head. The Jew was seized and he confessed. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ commanded that his head be crushed with stones."],[7167,"A man fought with another man and bit his hand, and his front tooth fell out. The Prophet ﷺ said: \"Would one of you bite as a stallion bites?\" and he invalidated it."],[7168,"A man bit another man's hand, and he pulled his hand away like this, drawing it from his mouth, and his two front teeth fell out. They brought their dispute to the Prophet ﷺ, and he ﷺ said: \"Would one of you bite his brother as a stallion bites? There is no blood money for you.\""],[7169,"A man came to the Prophet ﷺ who had bitten another man's hand and pulled his hand away from him, and the two front teeth of the one who bit him fell out. He said: The Prophet ﷺ invalidated it and said: \"Did you want to bite him as a stallion bites?\""],[7170,"A she-camel belonging to al-Bara' b. 'Azib entered a garden and caused damage in it. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ ruled that the owners of land are responsible for protecting it during the day, and the owners of livestock are responsible for protecting them at night."],[7171,"'Abd Allah b. Sahl and Muhayyisa b. Mas'ud went to Khaybar for some need of theirs. They separated, and 'Abd Allah b. Sahl was killed. His brother 'Abd al-Rahman b. Sahl and his cousin Huwayyisa came to the Prophet ﷺ. He said: 'Abd al-Rahman spoke, and the Prophet ﷺ said: \"The elder, the elder.\" So they both spoke about the matter of their companion. The Prophet ﷺ said: \"You may establish your claim to your companion—or he said: your slain man—by fifty oaths from among you.\" They said: O Messenger of Allah, we did not witness it; how can we swear about it? He said: \"Then the Jews will clear themselves with fifty oaths from among them.\" They said: O Messenger of Allah, they are a disbelieving people. He said: So the Prophet ﷺ paid his blood money from his own resources. Sahl said: One day I entered an enclosure of theirs, and a she-camel from those camels kicked me."],[7172,"There was a man from these people who had two wives. One of them became jealous of the other and threw her with a stone or a stick of chaff, causing her to miscarry. This matter was brought to the attention of the Prophet ﷺ , who made a sudden judgment in it and said, \"Should the child bear the consequences of one who neither shouted, nor pleaded, nor drank, nor ate?\" He said ﷺ , \"Is this not a crime like the crimes of the pre-Islamic era?\" And he placed it upon the guardians of the woman"],[7173,"Two women of Hudhayl threw at each other, and one of them miscarried her fetus, and the Messenger of Allah ﷺ ruled for it with a ghurrah: a male or female slave."],[7174,"A woman of Banu Lihyan struck another who was pregnant, and she miscarried. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ ruled for the woman's miscarriage with a ghurrah: a male or female slave. He said: The woman on whom the blood money was due died, and the Messenger of Allah ﷺ ruled that the blood money was upon her male relatives and that her inheritance was for her husband and her son."],[7175,"There were two co-wives. One of them threw a stone at the other, and the woman died. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ ruled the blood money upon the 'aqilah. Her paternal aunt said: She miscarried, O Messenger of Allah, a boy whose hair had grown. The father of the killer said: She is lying. By Allah, he did not cry out, nor drink, nor eat, so should one like him be left unavenged? The Prophet ﷺ said: The rhymed prose of the Jahiliyyah - a ghurrah. Ibn 'Abbas said: The name of one of them was Mulaykah and the other Umm Ghutayf."],[7176,"Two women from Hudhail fought with each other and one of them hit the other with a stone that killed her and what was in her womb. The relatives of the killer and the relatives of the victim submitted their case to the Prophet ﷺ who judged that the Diya for the fetus was a male or female slave, and the Diya for the killed woman was to be paid by the 'Asaba (near relatives) of the killer. (Using translation from Bukhārī 6910)"],[7177,"Umar, ؓ , adjured the people about the fetus. Hamal b. Malik b. al-Nabighah stood and said: I was between two of my wives, and one of them struck the other and killed her and her fetus. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ ruled for it with a ghurrah: a male or female slave, and that she be executed for her."],[7178,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ ruled for the fetus with a ghurrah: a male or female slave, or a horse, or a mule. The one against whom it was ruled said: Should we pay blood money for one who did not eat, nor drink, nor cry out, nor make a sound? Should one like him be left unavenged? The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: This one speaks with the speech of a poet. For it is a ghurrah: a male or female slave, or a horse, or a mule."],[7179,"A grandmother came to Abu Bakr al-Siddiq asking him about her inheritance. He said, “There is nothing for you in the Book of Allah, and I do not know of anything for you in the Sunnah of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. Return until I ask the people.” He asked the people, and al-Mughirah b. Shu‘bah said, “I was present when the Messenger of Allah ﷺ gave her a sixth.” He said, “Is there anyone else with you?” Muhammad b. Maslamah al-Ansari stood up and said the like of what al-Mughirah said. So Abu Bakr carried out for her the sixth. Then another grandmother came to Umar b. al-Khattab asking him about her inheritance. He said, “There is nothing for you in the Book of Allah, and the ruling that was given was only for someone other than you. I am not one to add anything to the prescribed shares, but it is that sixth. If you two are together in it, it is between you, and whichever of you is alone with it, it is hers.”"],[7180,"Regarding a man who married but had not consummated the marriage and had not stipulated a dower, he said: She is entitled to the full dower, she must observe the waiting period, and she inherits. Ma'qil b. Sinan said, \"I witnessed the Messenger of Allah ﷺ rule this in the case of Birwa' bt. Washiq.\""],[7181,"That a man came to him and asked him about a man who married a woman and then died before consummating the marriage and before stipulating a dower. He did not say anything and turned them away for a month, then he said, \"I will speak according to my own opinion. If it is correct, it is from Allah; if it is wrong, it is from me. I think she should have a dower like that of her peers, without reduction or excess, she must observe the waiting period, and she inherits.\" So-and-so al-Ashja'i stood up and said, \"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ ruled in the case of Birwa' bt. Washiq exactly like that.\" He said: 'Abdullah rejoiced at that and said, \"Allahu Akbar.\""],[7182,"Some people came to 'Abdullah b. Mas'ud and said, \"We have come to ask you about a man among us who married but did not stipulate a dower, and Allah did not bring them together before he died.\" 'Abdullah said, \"I have not been asked about anything since I parted from the Messenger of Allah ﷺ that is harder on me than this. Go to someone else.\" They kept coming to him for a month, then at the end they said to him, \"Whom should we ask if we do not ask you? You are the most senior of the companions of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ in this region, and we find no one else.\" Ibn Mas'ud said, \"I will speak about it according to the best of my opinion. If it is correct, it is from Allah; if it is wrong, it is from me, and Allah and His Messenger are free of it. I think she should be assigned a dower like that of her peers, without reduction or excess, she inherits, and she must observe the waiting period of four months and ten days.\" That was in the presence of some people from Ashja'. A man called Ma'qil b. Sinan al-Ashja'i stood up and said, \"I bear witness that you have ruled exactly as the Messenger of Allah ﷺ ruled in the case of a woman of ours called Birwa' bt. Washiq.\" 'Abdullah was never seen to rejoice at anything after Islam as he rejoiced at this story."],[7183,"A woman accepted Islam during the time of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, then her husband came and said: O Messenger of Allah, she had accepted Islam along with me, so he returned her to him."],[7184,"\"That her husband divorced her three times, and the Prophet ﷺ did not assign her any maintenance or housing.\" He said: I mentioned that to Ibrahim al-Nakha'i, and he said: 'Umar b. al-Khattab said: \"We will not abandon the Book of our Lord and the Sunnah of our Prophet for the statement of a woman. She is entitled to maintenance and housing.\""],[7185,"My husband divorced me during the time of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"There is no housing for you and no maintenance.\""],[7186,"I entered upon Fatimah bt. Qays and asked her about the judgment of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. She said: Her husband divorced her irrevocably. She said: \"I disputed with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ regarding housing and maintenance, but he did not assign me any housing or maintenance, and he ordered me to observe my waiting period in the house of Ibn Umm Maktum.\""],[7187,"That Abu 'Amr b. Hafs divorced her three times and sent her maintenance, but she deemed it insufficient. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ had sent him toward Yemen. Khalid b. al-Walid went with a group from Banu Makhzum to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ while he was in the house of Maymunah and said: O Messenger of Allah, Abu 'Amr b. Hafs has divorced Fatimah three times, so does she have any maintenance? The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"She has no maintenance and no housing.\" So the Messenger of Allah ﷺ sent to her that she should move to Umm Sharik. Then he sent to her that Umm Sharik is visited by the early emigrants, so move to the house of Ibn Umm Maktum, for if you remove your headcover he will not see you. And he sent to her: Do not precede me with yourself. Then the Messenger of Allah ﷺ married her to Usamah b. Zayd."],[7188,"I fastened my clothes and went to the Prophet ﷺ and mentioned that to him. He said: \"How many times did he divorce you?\" I said: Three. He said: \"He spoke the truth. You have no maintenance. Observe your waiting period in the house of your cousin Ibn Umm Maktum, for he is blind; you can put down your garment in his presence. When your waiting period ends, inform me.\" She said: Suitors proposed to me, among them Mu'awiyah and Abu Jahm. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"Mu'awiyah is light of means, and Abu Jahm has severity with women—or he beats women or something like this—but you should choose Usamah b. Zayd.\""],[7189,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ gave us a choice, and we chose him, so was that divorce?"],[7190,"\"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ gave Barirah the choice, and she chose herself.\""],[7191,"Concerning 'By Allah' and concerning Aws b. al-Samit, Allah, Mighty and Exalted, revealed the beginning of Surat al-Mujadilah. She said: I was with him, and he was a very old man, ill-tempered and irritable. One day he came in to me, and I argued with him about something, and he became angry and said, \"You are to me like my mother's back.\" Then he went out and sat in the gathering place of his people for a while, then came back to me and wanted me for himself. I said, \"No, by the One in whose hand is the soul of Khuwaylah, you will not reach me after what you have said until Allah and His Messenger judge between us.\" She said: Then he pounced on me, and I resisted him, overpowering him as a woman overpowers a weak old man, and I threw him beneath me. Then I went out to one of my neighbors and borrowed clothes from her, then I went out until I came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and sat before him. I mentioned to him what I had encountered from him, complaining about his ill temper. She said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ began saying, \"O Khuwaylah, your cousin is a very old man, so fear Allah concerning him.\" She said: By Allah, I did not leave until the Quran was revealed, and the Messenger of Allah ﷺ was overcome by what used to overcome him, then it was lifted from him, and he said, \"O Khuwaylah, Allah, Mighty and Exalted, has revealed concerning you and your companion.\" She said: Then he recited to me: {Allah has heard the words of the one who argues with you concerning her husband and complains to Allah} up to His saying {and for the disbelievers is a painful punishment}. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, \"Tell him to free a slave.\" I said, \"O Messenger of Allah, he has nothing to free.\" He said, \"Then let him fast two consecutive months.\" I said, \"By Allah, O Messenger of Allah, he is a very old man, not capable of fasting.\" He said, \"Then let him feed sixty poor people a wasq of dates.\" I said, \"By Allah, O Messenger of Allah, he does not have that.\" She said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, \"Then we will help him with an araq of dates.\" She said: I said, \"And I, O Messenger of Allah, will help him with another araq.\" He said, \"You have done well and excelled; go and give charity on his behalf, then advise your cousin well.\" She said: So I did."],[7192,"“The Messenger of Allah ﷺ made obligatory a tenth on what the sky, rivers, and springs water, or what is athari; and half a tenth on what is irrigated by nadih.”"],[7193,"“What is ba'l, or is watered by a river, or is athari, one is taken from every ten.”"],[7194,"A man from the Ansar disputed with al-Zubayr before the Messenger of Allah ﷺ about the channels of the Harrah through which they irrigated date palms. The Ansari said: Let the water flow. Al-Zubayr refused. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: Irrigate, O Zubayr, then release to your neighbor. The Ansari became angry and said: O Messenger of Allah, is it because he is your cousin? The face of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ changed color, then he said: Irrigate, O Zubayr, then hold back the water until it returns to the wall. Al-Zubayr said: By Allah, I think this verse was revealed about that: \"But no, by your Lord, they will not believe until they make you judge concerning what arises between them...\""],[7195,"'The Messenger of Allah ﷺ wrote to Kisra, Caesar, and Ukaydir of Dumat, inviting them to Allah Almighty.'"],[7196,"'The Messenger of Allah ﷺ wrote to Kisra, Caesar, and Ukaydir of Dumat, inviting them to Allah, Mighty and Exalted.'"],[7197,"In the name of Allah, the Most Gracious, the Most Merciful. From Muhammad, the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, to Heraclius, the Great One of the Romans. Peace be upon him who follows guidance. To proceed: I call you with the call of Islam. Submit and you will be safe; submit and Allah will give you your reward twice. But if you turn away, upon you will be the sin of the Arīsiyyīn. {O People of the Scripture, come to a word that is equitable between us and you – that we worship none but Allah} up to His saying {and bear witness that we are Muslims.} When he finished reading the letter, voices were raised in his presence and clamor increased, so he ordered that we be taken out. When we went out, I said to my companions, 'The matter of Ibn Abī Kabsha has become great; indeed the king of the Banū al-Aṣfar fears him.' He said, 'I remained certain about the matter of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, that it would prevail, until Allah brought me to Islam.'"],[7198,"The Prophet ﷺ wrote to the Jewish scholar of Taymā’ and greeted him."],[7199,"We were at al-Mirbad when I saw a man with disheveled hair, in his hand a piece of leather. We said to him, \"You seem to be a man from the desert.\" He said, \"Yes.\" We said to him, \"Hand us that piece of leather that is in your hand.\" We took it and read what was in it, and there was in it: \"From Muhammad, the Messenger of Allah, to Banū Zuhayr: Give the fifth of the spoils, the Prophet's share, and the ṣafī. You are secure with the protection of Allah and the protection of His Messenger.\" He said, we said, \"Who wrote this for you?\" He said, \"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ.\" He said, we said, \"Did you hear anything from him?\" He said, \"Yes, I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: 'Fasting the month of patience and three days of every month remove the rancor of the chest.'\" We said to him, \"Did you hear from the Messenger of Allah ﷺ?\" He said, \"Do I see you suspecting me? By Allah, I will not tell you anything.\" Then he left."],[7200,"The Prophet ﷺ wrote to Bakr b. Wā’il: \"From Muhammad, the Messenger of Allah, to Bakr b. Wā’il: Submit and you will be safe.\" He said, \"None read it except a man among them from Banū Ḍubayʿa, so they are called Banū al-Kātib.\""],[7201,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ wrote to the people of Yemen a letter containing the obligatory shares, the Sunnahs, and the blood monies, and sent it with ʿAmr b. Ḥazm. It was read to the people of Yemen, and this is its copy."],[7203,"some jews came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and mentioned to him that a man and a women of their number had committed fornication. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ asked them: What do you find in the Torah about stoning? They replied: We disgrace them and they should be flogged. ‘Abd Allah b. Salam said: You lie; it contains (instruction for) stoning. So they brought the Torah and spread it out, and one of them put his hand over the verse of stoning and read what preceded it and what followed it. ‘Abd Allah b. Salam said to him: Lift your hand. When he did so, the verse of stoning was seen to be in it. They then said: He has spoken the truth, Muhammad, the verse of stoning is in it. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ then gave command regarding them, and they were stoned to death. ‘Abd Allah b. ‘Umar said: I saw the man leaning on the woman protecting her from the stones. (Using translation from Abū Dāʾūd 4446)"],[7204,"some jews came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and mentioned to him that a man and a women of their number had committed fornication. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ asked them: What do you find in the Torah about stoning? They replied: We disgrace them and they should be flogged. ‘Abd Allah b. Salam said: You lie; it contains (instruction for) stoning. So they brought the Torah and spread it out, and one of them put his hand over the verse of stoning and read what preceded it and what followed it. ‘Abd Allah b. Salam said to him: Lift your hand. When he did so, the verse of stoning was seen to be in it. They then said: He has spoken the truth, Muhammad, the verse of stoning is in it. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ then gave command regarding them, and they were stoned to death. ‘Abd Allah b. ‘Umar said: I saw the man leaning on the woman protecting her from the stones. (Using translation from Abū Dāʾūd 4446)"],[7205,"\"The Prophet ﷺ stoned two Jews who had been married.\""],[7206,"We went out to Khaybar, and my uncle 'Amir was reciting rajaz poetry to the people while saying:"],[7207,"We came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ three days after Khaybar was conquered, and he allotted to us, but he did not allot to anyone who had not witnessed the conquest besides us."],[7208,"I asked Abu 'Amr about allotting shares to one who did not witness the conquest and the fighting. He said: 'They are not allotted shares. Do you not see that two parties enter by one mountain pass or two different passes, and one of them gains spoils while the other does not, and one of them is a support for the other? Neither of them shares with the other whether they both gain spoils or only one of them gains. Thus the matter has been settled concerning them.'"],[7209,"When the Messenger of Allah ﷺ was invited to a funeral, he would ask about it. If [the deceased] was praised with good, he would stand and pray; and if [the deceased] was mentioned with evil, he would say to its family: \"It is your affair,\" and he would not pray over it."],[7210,"A man had a wound, so he went to his quiver and took an arrowhead and slaughtered himself with it, and the Prophet ﷺ did not pray over him."],[7211,"\"No one resembled the Messenger of Allah ﷺ more than al-Hasan b. Ali.\""],[7212,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ informed us that your brother the Negus has died, so stand and pray over him. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ stood and they lined up behind him, and he said four takbirs while they did not think except that his bier was before him."],[7213,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ announced the death of the Negus on the day he died and said, 'Seek forgiveness for your brother.' Then he went out with the people to the prayer place, they lined up behind him, and he said four takbirs."],[7214,"A man came to 'Umar b. al-Khattab and said, \"I became junub and did not find water.\" 'Umar said, \"Do not pray.\" 'Ammar said, \"Do you not remember, O Commander of the Believers, when I and you were in a military detachment, and we became junub and did not find water? As for you, you did not pray; as for me, I rolled in the dust and prayed. When we came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, I mentioned that to him, and he said, 'It would have sufficed you,' and the Prophet ﷺ struck the ground with his hand, then blew into them, and wiped his face and palms with them.\""],[7215,"I was with ʿAbd Allāh and Abū Mūsā. Abū Mūsā said, “O Abū ʿAbd al-Raḥmān, a man becomes junub and does not find water—does he pray?” He said, “Do you hear what ʿAmmār b. Yāsir said to ʿUmar: ‘The Messenger of Allah ﷺ sent us, me and you. I became junub and rolled in the dust, then I came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and told him. He said, “This is enough for you,” and he wiped his face and his palms once.’” He said, “I did not see ʿUmar accept that.” He said, “How do you apply this verse? ‘If you do not find water, then perform tayammum with clean earth.’” He said, “If we made it easy for them in this matter, one of them, when he found cold water, would wipe with dust.” Al-Aʿmash said: I said to Shaqīq, “He disliked it only for this reason.”"],[7216,"A man came to the Prophet ﷺ and asked him about the time of prayer. He said, 'Pray with us these two times.' When the sun declined, he prayed Zuhr. He said: And he prayed Asr while the sun was high, white, and alive. And he prayed Maghrib when the sun had set. And he prayed Isha when the twilight had disappeared. And he prayed Fajr in the darkness before dawn. He said: The next day, he ordered Bilal, and he gave the call for Zuhr, and he delayed it until it was cooler. He ordered him, and he performed the Iqamah for Asr while the sun was alive, delaying it beyond what it had been the first time. He ordered him, and he performed the Iqamah for Maghrib before the twilight disappeared. He ordered him, and he performed the Iqamah for Isha after a third of the night had passed. He ordered him, and he performed the Iqamah for Fajr, and he made it bright. Then he said, 'Where is the one who asked about the time of prayer?' He said, 'I am he, O Messenger of Allah.' He said, 'The time of your prayer is between what you have seen.'"],[7217,"I saw my father perform wudu and wipe over his two shoes. I objected to that and said, “Do you wipe over the two shoes?” He replied, “I saw the Messenger of Allah ﷺ wiping over them.”"],[7218,"I prayed Zhuhr with Ali, ؓ . Then he went to a gathering he used to hold in al-Rahbah and sat down, and we sat around him until Asr approached. A vessel containing water was brought to him. He took a handful, rinsed his mouth, sniffed water into his nose, wiped his face and forearms, wiped his head and his feet, then stood and drank the leftover water. Then he said, “I have been told that some men dislike one drinking while standing. Indeed, I saw the Messenger of Allah ﷺ do as I have done, and this is the wudu of one who has not broken his wudu.”"],[7219,"We prayed Zhuhr with Ali, ؓ , then we went out to al-Rahbah. He called for a vessel containing a drink. He took it, rinsed his mouth, sniffed water into his nose, wiped his face, forearms, head and feet, then drank the leftover while standing. Then he said, “Some people dislike drinking while standing. Indeed, the Messenger of Allah ﷺ did the same as I have done, and this is the wudu of one who has not broken his wudu.”"],[7220,"When he began the prayer, he raised his hands level with his shoulders; and when he said the takbir for bowing; and when he raised his head from bowing, he raised them likewise, and said, 'Allah hears the one who praises Him. Our Lord, and to You be praise.' He did not do that in prostration."],[7221,"When he entered into prayer, he raised his hands, and when he bowed, and when he said, \"Allah hears those who praise Him,\" and when he stood up from the two rak'ahs, he raised them to his shoulders.\""],[7222,"He was sitting with a group of the Companions of the Prophet ﷺ. Abu Humayd al-Sa'idi said, 'I am the most knowledgeable among you concerning the prayer of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. I saw him when he said takbir, he placed his hands level with his shoulders. When he bowed, he placed his hands on his knees, then bent his back. When he raised his head, he stood straight. When he prostrated, he placed his hands, not spreading them on the ground and not clenching them, and he faced the tips of his feet toward the qiblah. When he sat in the last rak'ah, he put forward his left leg and sat on his buttocks.'"],[7223,"When the Messenger of Allah ﷺ stood for prayer, he faced the qiblah and raised his hands until they were level with his shoulders, then said, \"Allahu Akbar.\" When he bowed, he said takbir and raised his hands as he bowed. Then he straightened his back, without lowering his head or drawing it in. Then he said, \"Allah hears those who praise Him,\" and raised his hands until they were level with his shoulders. Then he stood straight until every bone returned to its position, straight. Then he went down to the ground, saying, \"Allahu Akbar,\" and prostrated, keeping his upper arms away from his sides and facing the tips of his toes toward the qiblah. Then he raised his head and said, \"Allahu Akbar,\" and folded his left leg and sat on it, straight until every bone returned to its position, straight. Then he said, \"Allahu Akbar,\" then returned and prostrated. Then he raised his head and said, \"Allahu Akbar.\" Then he folded his left leg and sat on it until every bone returned to its position. Then he stood up and did the same in the other rak'ah. When he stood up from the two rak'ahs, he said takbir and did as he did at the start of the prayer. When it was the prostration that is the end of the prayer, he raised his head from them, moved his leg back, and sat mutawarrikan on his leg ﷺ."],[7224,"When {And warn your nearest kindred} was revealed to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, he said, 'O assembly of Quraysh, ransom yourselves from Allah, for I cannot avail you anything before Allah. O Banu Abd al-Muttalib, I cannot avail you anything before Allah. O Abbas b. Abd al-Muttalib, I cannot avail you anything before Allah. O Safiyyah, paternal aunt of the Messenger of Allah, I cannot avail you anything before Allah. O Fatimah bt. Muhammad, ask me whatever you wish, but I cannot avail you anything before Allah.'"],[7225,"When this verse was revealed: {And warn your nearest kindred} and your chosen clan among them—he said, and in the recitation of Abd Allah it is: \"and your chosen clan among them\"—the Messenger of Allah ﷺ went out until he came to al-Safa and climbed it. Then he called out, 'O calamity of the morning!' The people gathered to him, some coming themselves and some sending a messenger. He ﷺ said, 'O Banu Abd al-Muttalib, O Banu Fihr, O Banu Abd Manaf, O Banu—tell me, if I informed you that cavalry were at the foot of this mountain wanting to raid you, would you believe me?' They said, 'Yes.' He said, 'Then indeed I am a warner to you before a severe punishment.' Abu Lahab said, 'May you perish for the rest of the day! Did you call us only for this?' Then he stood up, and {May the hands of Abu Lahab perish} was revealed, and he has indeed perished. They said, 'We have never known you to lie.'"],[7226,"'When {And warn your nearest kindred} was revealed to the Prophet ﷺ, he put his two fingers in his ears, raised his voice, and said: O Banu Abd Manaf.'"],[7227,"When this verse was revealed: “And warn your closest kindred” (26:214), the Messenger of Allah ﷺ gathered Quraysh and said: “O assembly of Quraysh, save yourselves from the Fire, for I do not possess for you any harm or benefit.” And to the Banū ʿAbd Manāf he said the like, and to the Banū ʿAbd al-Muṭṭalib he said the like. Then he said: “O Fāṭimah bint Muḥammad ﷺ, save yourself from the Fire, for I do not possess for you any harm or benefit, except that you have a kinship tie which I will maintain with its due.”"],[7228,"\"Blessed are these eyes that have seen the Messenger of Allah ﷺ . By Allah, we wish we had seen what you saw and witnessed what you witnessed. May anger befall whosoever claims anything extraordinary other than good, then he approached the Messenger ﷺ and said, 'What motivates a person to resemble someone he has never seen, not knowing how he would have been in his presence? By Allah, the Messenger of Allah ﷺ appeared to people, but they turned away from him and disbelieved him. Should you not praise Allah when He brought you out, recognizing your Lord and confirming what your Prophet ﷺ brought? Indeed, you were spared from affliction through means other than yourselves. By Allah, the Prophet ﷺ was sent in the most difficult circumstances that no prophet before him had ever experienced during a period of ignorance. They did not perceive any religion better than idol worship until he brought a clear distinction between truth and falsehood, and between a parent and his child. To the extent that a person might see his child, parent, or brother as a disbeliever, while Allah has opened the lock of his heart to faith, knowing that if he perishes, he would enter Hell, yet his eyes do not shed a tear, and he is aware that his beloved is in Hell, and that is the one to whom Allah has said: \"Those who say, 'Our Lord, grant us from among our wives and offspring comfort to our eyes' –\" (Quran 25:74)."],[7229,"I have been harmed for the sake of Allah in a way no one has been harmed. I have been frightened for the sake of Allah in a way no one has been frightened. Three [periods] between a day and a night came upon me when I had no food except what Bilāl’s armpit concealed."],[7230,"\"No one resembled the Messenger of Allah ﷺ more than al-Hasan b. Ali.\""],[7231,"I saw the Messenger of Allah ﷺ in the marketplace of Dhi Al-Majaz wearing a red robe, and he was saying, \"O people, say there is no deity but Allah, and you will be successful.\" A man was following him, throwing stones at him, causing his back and heels to bleed, while saying, \"O people, do not obey him, for he is a liar.\" I asked, \"Who is this?\" It was said, \"He is the son of Abd Al-Muttalib.\" I then asked, \"Who is the one who follows him and throws stones at him?\" It was said, \"He is Abd Al-Uzza, the father of Lahab.\" When Islam emerged, we left until we reached a place near Madinah, and we had with us a container of dates. While we were sitting, a man approached us wearing two white garments and greeted us, asking, \"Where are the people coming from?\" We said, \"From Rabdah.\" He asked, \"Do you sell this camel?\" We said, \"Yes.\" He asked, \"For how much?\" We replied, \"For such and such amount of dates.\" He said, \"I will take it.\" He took the camel and did not haggle with us. Then, he disappeared within the walls of Madinah, and we whispered to each other, wondering if he knew the value of our camel. The man with the container said, \"Do not whisper among yourselves, for I saw the face of a man whom none of you could belittle. I have never seen anything resembling the moon on the night of a full moon as his face.\" Later that evening, a man approached us and greeted us, saying, \"I am the Messenger of the Messenger of Allah, and he says, 'You may eat until you are satiated, and trade until you are content.'\" We ate until we were full and traded until we were content. The next morning, we arrived at Madinah, and there stood the Messenger of Allah, delivering a sermon from the pulpit, saying, \"The hand that gives is higher than the one that receives, and start with those you are responsible for, your mother and father, then your sister and brother, and then the closest ones.\" A man stood up and said, \"O Messenger of Allah, these are the sons of Tha'laba ibn Yarbua who killed so and so in the age of ignorance. Take our revenge from him.\" The Messenger of Allah ﷺ raised his hands up, and I saw the whiteness of his armpits as he said, \"No, a mother cannot seek revenge for her child, no, a mother cannot seek revenge for her child.\""],[7232,"The word of (Allah) Great and Glorious: 'And utter not thy prayer loudly, nor be low in it\" (xvii. 110) was revealed as the Messenger of Allah (may peace beupon him) was hiding himself in Mecca. When he led his Companions in prayer he raised his voice (while reciting the) Qur'an. And when the polytheists heard that, they reviled the Qur'an and Him Who revealed it and him who brought it. Upon this Allah, the Exalted, said to His Apostle ﷺ: Utter not thy prayer so loudly that the polytheists may hear thy recitation and (recite it) not so low that it may be inaudible to your Companions. Make them hear the Qur'an, but do not recite it loudly and seek a (middle) way between these. Recite between loud and low tone. (Using translation from Muslim 446)"],[7233,"An army of the Muslims went out with me as their commander until we camped at Alexandria. A great man among their great ones said, 'Bring out to me a man who will speak with me and I will speak with him.' I said, 'No one will go out to him except me.' So I went out with my interpreter and he had his interpreter until a pulpit was placed for us. He said, 'What are you?' I said, 'We are the Arabs, the people of thorns and qaraẓ. We are the people of the House of Allah. We were the people with the most constricted land and the harshest life. We used to eat carrion and blood, and some of us would raid others with the harshest life people lived. Until there emerged among us a man, not the greatest of us that day in nobility nor the most of us in wealth. He said, \"I am the Messenger of Allah to you,\" commanding us what we did not know and forbidding us what we and our fathers were upon. We denied him and rejected his words until people from other than us went out to him and said, \"We believe you and have faith in you and follow you and fight those who fight you.\" He went out to them, and we went out to him. We fought him, and he killed us and prevailed over us and defeated us. He went on to take the Arabs who followed him and fought them until he prevailed over them. If those behind me among the Arabs knew the life you are in, none would remain except that he would come to you and share with you in the life you are in.' He laughed then said, 'Your messenger has spoken truth. Our messengers came to us with the like of what your messenger brought. We remained upon it until kings appeared among us and acted upon their whims and abandoned the affair of the prophets. If you take the affair of your prophet, no one will fight you except that you overcome him, and no one will oppose you except that you prevail over him. But if you do like what we did and abandon the affair of your prophet and act according to their whims, then He will leave us and you. You are not more in number than us nor stronger in power than us.' ʿAmr b. al-ʿĀṣ said, 'I have never spoken to a man more cunning than him.'\""],[7234,"I said, \"I have never seen anything that afflicted the Quraysh as much as the Messenger of Allah, ﷺ , in terms of the enmity they showed towards him.\" He replied, \"I was there when their nobles gathered in the Hijr and they mentioned the Messenger of Allah, ﷺ . They said, 'We have never seen anyone like this man who has tested our patience. He has mocked our dreams, insulted our fathers, criticized our religion, divided our community, and cursed our idols. We have endured great hardships because of him, or so they claim.' As they were talking, the Messenger of Allah, ﷺ , appeared and started walking until he reached the corner of the Kaaba. He passed by them and they made mocking gestures and whispered some remarks. I could see that on his face. Then he continued and when he passed by them for the second time, they made the same gestures and I noticed it on his face. Peace be upon him. Then he passed by them for the third time and they made the same gestures. Then he said, 'O people of Quraysh, do you hear me? By the One in whose hand is the soul of Muhammad, I have come to you for slaughtering.' His words silenced them, and every one of them looked as if a bird had struck their heads. Even the harshest of them trembled in his presence and answered him with the best of manners. Finally, he said, 'Go on, O Abu al-Qasim, go on with your business. By Allah, you are not ignorant.' So the Messenger of Allah, ﷺ , continued until the next morning. When they gathered in the Hijr and I was with them, some of them said to others, 'Do you remember what he told us and what we told him about their criticism of their gods and their religion?' He replied, 'Yes, I am the one who said that.' Then I saw one of them grabbing his garment and saying, while Abu Bakr al-Siddiq was standing beside him, crying, 'Do you kill a man just because he says his Lord is Allah?' Then they turned away from him. That was the most severe thing I have ever seen the Quraysh do to him.\""],[7235,"Ḍimād came to Makkah from Azd Shanū’a, and he used to treat possession by wind. He heard the foolish ones of the people of Makkah saying that Muhammad was insane. He said, 'If I were to see this man, perhaps Allah would cure him at my hands.' He met him and said, 'O Muhammad, I treat possession by wind, and Allah cures at my hands whom He wills. Will you?' The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, 'Indeed, praise belongs to Allah. We praise Him and seek His help. Whoever Allah guides, none can lead astray, and whoever He leads astray, none can guide. I bear witness that there is no god but Allah alone, with no partner, and that Muhammad is His servant and His messenger. To proceed.' He said, 'Repeat to me these words of yours.' The Messenger of Allah ﷺ repeated them to him three times. He said, 'I have heard the words of soothsayers, the words of sorcerers, and the words of poets, but I have never heard the like of these words of yours. Give me your hand that I may pledge allegiance to you upon Islam.' The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, 'And upon your people?' He said, 'And upon my people.' He pledged allegiance to him. Then the Messenger of Allah ﷺ sent a raiding party, and they passed by his people. The leader of the raiding party said to the army, 'Did you take anything from these people?' A man from the people said, 'I took from them a water container.' He said, 'Return it, for these are the people of Ḍimād.'\""],[7236,"I never saw Quraysh wanting to kill the Messenger of Allah ﷺ except on a day I saw them while they were sitting in the shade of the Kaʿba and the Messenger of Allah ﷺ was praying near the Maqām. ʿUqba b. Abī Muʿayṭ stood up to him and put his cloak around his neck and pulled it until he fell to his knees ﷺ. People shouted, thinking he was killed. Abū Bakr ؓ came hurrying until he grabbed the upper arms of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ from behind, saying, 'Would you kill a man for saying my Lord is Allah?' Then they turned away from the Prophet ﷺ. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ stood up, and when he finished his prayer, he passed by them while they were sitting in the shade of the Kaʿba and said, 'O assembly of Quraysh, by the One in whose hand is my soul, I was not sent to you except with slaughter.' He gestured with his hand to his throat. Abū Jahl said to him, 'O Muhammad, you were not ignorant.' The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, 'You are one of them.'"],[7237,"While the Messenger of Allah ﷺ was prostrating, with people around him, 'Uqbah b. Abi Mu'ayt came with the afterbirth of a slaughtered camel and threw it onto the back of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. He did not lift his head. Then Fatimah came, removed it from his back, and supplicated against the one who did that. He said, 'O Allah, take the chiefs of Quraysh: Abu Jahl b. Hisham, 'Utbah b. Rabi'ah, Shaybah b. Rabi'ah, 'Uqbah b. Abi Mu'ayt, and Umayyah b. Khalaf or Ubayy b. Khalaf'—Shu'bah was uncertain. He said, 'I saw them on the Day of Badr when they were thrown into a well, except that Umayyah's limbs were torn apart, so he was not thrown into the well.'"],[7238,"Abu Jahl said, \"Does Muhammad humble his face behind your backs? By the one he swears by, if I see him do that, I will step on his neck.\" So he came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ while he was praying, intending to step on his neck. But suddenly he was unable to move; it was as if his hands were being restrained and his heels were being pulled back. They came to him and said, \"What's wrong with you, O Abu Al-Hakam?\" He replied, \"Between him and me is a trench of fire and terror with wings.\" Abu Al-Mu'tamir said, \"So Allah revealed 'Have you seen the one who forbids a servant when he prays' until the end of the verse, 'So let him call his band of supporters.' His people said, 'We shall summon the executioners.' But the angels said, 'Do not obey him.' Then Allah commanded him to perform the prostration as He had commanded him in the end of the Surah.\" He also narrated to me in this Hadith that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, \"If he came near me, the angels would seize him limb by limb.\""],[7239,"When Ka'b b. al-Ashraf came to Makkah, they came to him and said, 'We are the people of the watering and the custodianship of the Ka'bah, and you are the master of the people of Yathrib. Are we better or this little contemptible one, cut off from his people, who claims that he is better than us?' He said, 'You are better than him.' Then it was revealed regarding the Messenger of Allah ﷺ: 'Indeed, your enemy is the one cut off' (Qur'an 108:3), and it was revealed: 'Have you not seen those who were given a portion of the Scripture, believing in jibt and taghut and saying to those who disbelieve, \"These are better guided than those who believe as to the way\"?' (Qur'an 4:51)."],[7240,"We were sitting with the Prophet ﷺ in the mosque when his gaze fixed upon a man walking in the mosque. He said, “O so-and-so, do you bear witness that I am the Messenger of Allah?” He replied, “No.” He said, “Do you read the Torah?” He replied, “Yes.” He said, “And the Gospel?” He replied, “Yes.” He said, “And the Quran?” He replied, “By Him in whose hand is my soul, if I wished I could recite it.” He then called out to him and said, “Do you find me in the Torah and the Gospel?” He replied, “We find one like you, and the likeness of your community, and the likeness of the one who will bring you forth. We had hoped that you would be among us, but when you emerged we feared that it was you, so we looked, and it was not you.” He said, “And why is that?” He replied, “Because with him from his community are seventy thousand for whom there will be neither reckoning nor punishment, whereas with you there are only a few.” He said, “By Him in whose hand is my soul, I am indeed he, and it is indeed my community, and they are indeed more than seventy thousand, and seventy thousand, and seventy thousand.”"],[7241,"We were with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and he said: Count every person who has professed Islam. He said: I said: O Messenger of Allah, do you fear for us while we are between six hundred and seven hundred? He ﷺ said: You do not know; perhaps you will be tested. He said: Then we were tested until a man among us would not pray except secretly."],[7242,"The Prophet ﷺ spent ten years following people in their homes during the pilgrimage season, at Majannah, ʿUkaz, and in their dwellings at Mina, saying: “Who will shelter me and support me so that I may convey the messages of my Lord, and for him is Paradise?” But he ﷺ found no one to support or shelter him, to the point that a man would travel from Egypt or Yemen to a relative, and his people would come to him and say: “Beware of the youth of Quraysh, lest he tempt you.” He would walk among their camps calling them to Allah, and they would point at him with their fingers. Until Allah sent us to him from Yathrib. A man would come to him, believe in him, and recite the Quran to him, then return to his family, and they would embrace Islam through his Islam, until there remained not a house among the houses of Yathrib but had a group of Muslims openly professing Islam. Then we consulted one another and gathered, saying: “How long will the Messenger of Allah ﷺ be driven away in the mountains of Makkah and live in fear?” So we traveled until we came to him during the pilgrimage season. He made an appointment with us at the mountain pass of al-ʿAqabah. His uncle al-ʿAbbas said: “O people of Yathrib,” so we gathered around him, one man and two. When he looked at our faces, he said: “These are people I do not know; these are young men.” We said: “O Messenger of Allah, upon what shall we pledge allegiance to you?” He said: “You pledge allegiance to me upon hearing and obedience in activity and in laziness, upon spending in hardship and ease, upon commanding good and forbidding evil, upon speaking for Allah without being deterred by any critic’s blame in Allah’s cause, and upon supporting me when I come to you and protecting me from what you protect yourselves, your wives, and your children. For you is Paradise.” We stood to pledge allegiance to him. Asʿad b. Zurarah, who was the youngest of the seventy except for me, took his hand and said: “Slowly, O people of Yathrib. We did not strike the livers of the camels to come to him except knowing that he is the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and that bringing him out today means separation from all Arabs, the killing of your best, and that the swords will bite you. If you are people who will endure it when it afflicts you, endure the killing of your best and separation from all Arabs, then take him, and your reward is with Allah. But if you fear for yourselves, then leave him, for that would be a clearer excuse before Allah.” They said: “O Asʿad, remove your hand from us. By Allah, we will not abandon this pledge nor seek to withdraw from it.” He said: We stood before him one by one. He took from us the pledge of al-ʿAbbas and guaranteed Paradise upon that."],[7243,"“O servants of Allah, see how Allah turns away from me their insults and their curses,” meaning Quraysh. They said: “How is that, O Messenger of Allah?” He said: “They insult Mudhammam and curse Mudhammam, but I am Muhammad ﷺ.”"],[7244,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ neither recited the Qur'an to the Jinn nor did he see them. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ went out with some of his Companions with the intention of going to the bazaar of 'Ukaz And there had been (at that time) obstructions between satans and the news from the Heaven, and there were flung flames upon them. So satan went back to their people and they said: What has happened to you? They said: There have been created obstructions between us and the news from the Heaven. And there have been flung upon us flames. They said: It cannot happen but for some (important) event. So traverse the eastern parts of the earth and the western parts and find out why is it that there have been created obstructions between us and the news from the Heaven. So they went forth and traversed the easts of the earth and its wests. Some of them proceeded towards Tihama and that is a nakhl towards the bazaar of 'Ukaz and he (the Holy Prophet) was leading his Companions in the morning prayer. So when they heard the Qur'an. they listened to it attentively and said: It is this which has caused obstruction between us and news from the Heaven. They went back to their people and said: O our people, we have heard a strange Qur'an which directs us to the right path; so we affirm our faith in it and we would never associate anyone with our Lord. And Allah, the Exalted and Glorious, revealed to His Apostle Muhammad ﷺ:\" It has been revealed to me that a party of Jinn listened to it\" (Qur'an, lxxii. 1). (Using translation from Muslim 449)"],[7245,"I asked Alqamah b. Qays whether Ibn Mas'ud was present with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ on the night of the jinn. He said: I asked Abdullah b. Mas'ud whether any of you was present with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ on the night of the jinn. He said, \"No, but we were with him one night, and we missed him. We spent the worst night ever. When morning came, he came from the direction of Hira'. He said, 'A caller from the jinn came to me, and I went with him and recited the Qur'an to them.' He went and showed us their fires and their traces. They asked him about provisions, and he said, 'Every bone of food over which the name of Allah is mentioned and that falls into your hands will be as full of meat as possible, and every piece of dung is fodder for your animals.' The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, 'Do not clean yourselves with them, for they are the food of your brothers from the jinn.'\""],[7246,"I saw in a dream that I was migrating from Makkah to a land of palm trees, and my mind went to its being al-Yamāmah or Hajar, but it was al-Madīnah, Yathrib. And I saw in this dream of mine that I shook a sword and it broke, and it was what befell the believers on the day of Uḥud. Then I shook another and it returned to the best of what it was, and it is what Allah brought anew of booty and the gathering of the believers."],[7247,"I never knew my parents except that they followed the religion. No day passed over us but that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ came to us at the two ends of the day, morning and evening. When the Muslims were tested, Abū Bakr, ؓ , went out as an emigrant toward the land of Abyssinia, and Ibn al-Daghinnah, the chief of al-Qārah, met him and said: Where are you going, O Abū Bakr? He said: My people have expelled me, so I will roam in the land and worship my Lord. Ibn al-Daghinnah said to him: A man like you, O Abū Bakr, should not go out nor be expelled. You earn for the destitute, maintain ties of kinship, entertain the guest, bear the burden of others, and help in the calamities of truth. And I am your protector. So Ibn al-Daghinnah set out and Abū Bakr returned with him. He said to them and went about among the disbelievers of Quraysh: Abū Bakr should not go out nor be expelled. A man like him earns for the destitute, maintains ties of kinship, bears the burden of others, entertains the guest, and helps in the calamities of truth. So Quraysh honored the protection of Ibn al-Daghinnah and gave safety to Abū Bakr, and they said to Ibn al-Daghinnah: Tell Abū Bakr to worship his Lord in his house and pray as much as he wishes and recite as much as he wishes, and not to harm us nor to make public the prayer and recitation outside his house. So Abū Bakr ؓ did that. Then it occurred to Abū Bakr, and he built a mosque in the courtyard of his house, and he used to pray in it and recite the Qurʾān, and the women of the polytheists and their children would stand by him, wondering at him and looking at him. And Abū Bakr ؓ was a man who wept much and could not control his tears when he recited the Qurʾān. So they sent to Ibn al-Daghinnah, and he came to them. They said: We granted Abū Bakr safety only on condition that he worship his Lord in his house, but he has built a mosque and has made public the prayer and recitation, and we fear that he will tempt our women and children. So go to him and tell him to confine himself to worshiping his Lord in his house, and if he refuses except to make that public, then let him return to us your protection, for we dislike breaking your protection and we will not acknowledge for Abū Bakr making it public. So Ibn al-Daghinnah came to Abū Bakr and said: You know what I stipulated for you, so either confine yourself to that or return my protection to me, for I do not like the Arabs to hear that I was treacherous in the pact of a man for whom I made a pact."],[7248,"I said to the Prophet ﷺ while we were in the cave: If one of them wanted to look at his feet, he would see us beneath his foot. He ﷺ said: What do you think of two, Allah is their third?"],[7249,"Abu Bakr ؓ sought permission from the Prophet ﷺ to leave Makkah when the situation became difficult for him, and the Prophet ﷺ said to him: \"Be patient.\" He said: \"O Messenger of Allah, do you hope that permission will be granted to you?\" The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"I certainly hope so.\" Abu Bakr waited for him, and one day the Messenger of Allah ﷺ came to him at noon and called out to him, saying: \"Send out whoever is with you.\" Abu Bakr said: \"They are only my two daughters, O Messenger of Allah.\""],[7251,"Abu Bakr bought a saddle from ‘Azib for thirteen dirhams, then Abu Bakr said to 'Azib. Tell al-Bara to carry it to my house. He said: No, not until you tell us what happened when the Messenger of Allah ﷺ went out and you were with him. Abu Bakr said: We started our journey at the beginning of the night and we hastened for one day and one night, until it was midday. I looked into the distance to see whether there was anywhere to seek shade, and I saw a rock, so I went to it and it had a little shade. I smoothed the ground for the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and spread a garment of camel hair for him, and said: Lie down and rest, O Messenger of Allah. So he lay down, and I went out to see if I could spot anyone looking for us. Then I saw a shepherd and I said: Who do you belong to, O boy? He said: To a man of Quraish. He mentioned his name and I recognised it. I said: Is there any milk in your sheep? He said: Yes | said: Will you milk some for me? He said: Yes. I told him to do that, so he caught a sheep, then I told him to brush the dust from its teat, then to brush the dust off his hands. I had a small vessel with me on the neck of which was a cloth. He milked a little bit of milk for me and I poured it into the vessel until it cooled down. Then I came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. When I reached him, he had already woken up. I said: Drink, O Messenger of Allah. He drank until I was pleased, then I said: Is it time to move on? So we moved on and the people were coming after us but none of them caught up with us except Suraqah bin Malik bin Ju'shum, who was riding a horse of his, I said: O Messenger of Allah, someone has caught up with us. He said: ʿDo not be afraid, for Allah is with us.ʿ When he got close to us, and there was no more between us and him then the length of a spear or two or three spears, I said: O Messenger of Allah, this pursuer has caught up with us, and I wept. He said: ʿWhy are you weeping?ʿ I said: I am not weeping for myself; rather I am weeping for you. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ prayed against him [the pursuer] and said: “O Allah, protect us from him by whatever means You will.” Then his horse's legs sank into the solid ground up to its belly, and he fell off it. He said: O Muhammad, I know that this is because of you; pray to Allah to save me from my predicament, and by Allah I shall divert away from you any one who is behind me of those who are seeking you. Here is my quiver, take one arrow. You are going to pass by some camels and sheep of mine in such and such a place, take whatever you need from thern. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: ʿI have no need of it.“ The Messenger of Allah ﷺ prayed for him and he was released, and he went back to his companions. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ and I continued on our way until we came to Madinah, where the people met him. They came out on the road and on the roofs, and a lot of servants and children crowded the road saying: Allahu Akbar, the Messenger of Allah ﷺ has come, Muhammad has come. The people disputed as to who he would stay with. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: ʿTonight I will stay with Banun-Najjar, the maternal uncles of 'Abdul-Muttalib, to honour them thereby.” The next morning, he went where he was instructed. Al-Bara' bin 'Azib said: The first of the Muhajireen to come to us was Mus'ab bin 'Umair, the brother of Banu 'Abdud-Dar. Then Ibn Umm Maktoom, the blind man and brother of Banu Fihr, came to us. Then 'Umar bin al-Khattab, came to us with twenty riders and we said: What happened to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ? He said: He is behind me. Then the Messenger of Allah ﷺ came and Abu Bakr was with him. Al-Bara said: the Messenger of Allah ﷺ did not come until I had read some soorahs from al-Mufassal [Al-Mufassal is that portion of the Qur'an which goes from Qaf to an-Nas]. Isra'eel said: al-Bara' was one of the Ansar from Banu Harithah. (Using translation from Aḥmad 3)"],[7252,"\"When the emigrants arrived from Makkah to Madinah, they came with nothing in their hands, while the Ansar were the people of land and property. He said: The Ansar made an agreement with them to give them half the fruits of their properties every year, and the emigrants would suffice them the labor. He said: Anas b. Malik's mother gave the Messenger of Allah ﷺ some date palms of hers, and the Messenger of Allah ﷺ gave them to Umm Ayman, his freedwoman, the mother of Usamah b. Zayd. When the Messenger of Allah ﷺ finished with the people of Khaybar and returned to Madinah, the emigrants returned to the Ansar the gifts they had given them of their fruits. He said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ returned to my mother her date palms and gave Umm Ayman in their place some from his own orchard.\""],[7253,"The verse {that Allah may forgive for you what preceded of your sin and what will follow} was revealed to the Prophet ﷺ upon his return from al-Hudaybiyyah. The Prophet ﷺ said, “A verse has been revealed to me that is dearer to me than everything on the face of the earth.” Then he recited it to them, and they said, “May it be pleasant and wholesome, O Prophet of Allah! Allah has made clear to you what He will do with you, but what will He do with us?” Then it was revealed to him: {that He may admit the believing men and believing women into gardens beneath which rivers flow} up to {a great attainment}."],[7254,"The Prophet ﷺ had his front tooth broken on the Day of Uhud, and his face was wounded until blood flowed on his face. He said, 'How can a people prosper who did this to their Prophet ﷺ while he is calling them to their Lord?' Then it was revealed: 'Not for you, [O Muhammad], is the decision whether He should [cut them down] or forgive them or punish them, for indeed, they are wrongdoers' (Qur'an 3:128)."],[7255,"They asked Sahl b. Sa'd, 'With what was the wound of the Prophet ﷺ treated?' He said, 'No one among the people knows better than I. 'Ali ؓ would bring water in a waterskin, and Fatimah would wash the blood. Then a mat was taken, burned, and he ﷺ was treated with it.'"],[7256,"A man asked him about the wound of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. He said, 'The face of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ was wounded, his front tooth was broken, and the helmet was smashed on his head ﷺ. Fatimah bt. Muhammad ﷺ was washing the blood, and 'Ali ؓ was pouring water on it with a shield. When Fatimah ؓ saw that the water only increased the blood, she took a piece of mat, burned it until it became ash, and applied it to the wound, and the blood stopped.'"],[7257,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ rode a donkey with a packsaddle and a velvet cloth beneath it. He rode and mounted Usamah b. Zayd behind him while he was visiting Sa'd b. Mu'adh among the Banu al-Harith in al-Khazraj, and that was before the Battle of Badr. He passed by a gathering in which there was a mixture of Muslims, polytheists, idol worshippers, and Jews. Among them was 'Abd Allah b. Ubayy b. Salul, and in the gathering was 'Abd Allah b. Rawahah. When the dust of the animal settled over the gathering, 'Abd Allah covered his nose with his cloak and said, 'Do not raise dust upon us.' The Prophet ﷺ greeted them, stopped before them, called them to Allah, and recited the Qur'an to them. Then 'Abd Allah b. Ubayy b. Salul said, 'O man, none is better than this if what you say is true. Do not annoy us in our gatherings, return to your own place, and if any of us comes to you, narrate to him.'"],[7258,"A Jew from Banu Zurayq, called Labid b. al-A'sam, bewitched the Prophet ﷺ until the Prophet ﷺ would imagine that he had done something when he had not done it. Then one day or one night, the Prophet ﷺ supplicated, then supplicated again, then said, 'O 'A'ishah, do you know that Allah, Mighty and Majestic, has answered me in what I asked Him? Two men came to me: one sat at my head and the other at my feet. The one at my feet said to the one at my head, \"What is the man's ailment?\" He said, \"He is bewitched.\" He said, \"Who bewitched him?\" He said, \"Labid b. al-A'sam.\" He said, \"In what?\" He said, \"In a comb and hair combings and the spathe of a male date palm.\" He said, \"Where is it?\" He said, \"In the well of Dhi Arwan.\"' He said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ went to it with a group of his companions, then came back and said, 'O 'A'ishah, its water was as if it were the infusion of henna, and its palm trees were as if they were the heads of devils.' I said, 'O Messenger of Allah, why did you not burn it or take it out?' He said, 'As for me, Allah has healed me, and I disliked to stir up any evil among the people because of it.' So he ordered it, and it was buried."],[7259,"“A Jew from among the Jews of Bani Zuraiq, whose name was Labid bin A’sam, cast a spell on the Prophet ﷺ, and the Prophet ﷺ began to imagine that he had done something when he had not. One day, or one night, the Messenger of Allah ﷺ supplicated, and then supplicated again. Then he said: ‘O ‘Aishah, do you know that Allah has instructed me concerning the matter I asked Him about? Two men came to me, and one of them sat at my head and the other at my feet. The one at my head said to the one at my feet, or the one at my feet said to the one at my head \"what is ailing this man ?\" He said: “He has been affected by a spell.” He said: “Who cast the spell on him?” He said: “Labid bin A’sam.” He said: “With what?” He said: “With a comb and the hairs stuck to it, and the spathe of a male date palm.” He said: “Where is that?” He said: “In the well of Dhu Arwan.” She said: “So the Prophet ﷺ went to it, with a group of his Companions, then he came and said: ‘By Allah. O ‘Aishah. It was as if its water was infused with henna and its date palms were like the heads of devils.’” She said: “I said: ‘O Messenger of Allah, why don’t you burn them?’ He said: ‘As for me, Allah has healed me, and I do not like to let evil spread among the people.’ Then he issued orders that the well be filled up with earth.” (Using translation from Ibn Mājah 3545)"],[7260,"While a man was narrating in Kindah, he said, 'A smoke will come on the Day of Resurrection and will seize the hearing and sight of the hypocrites, and it will seize the believer like a cold.' He said: We were alarmed, so I went to Ibn Mas'ud. He said: He was reclining, but he became angry, sat up, and said, 'O people, whoever knows something should speak from it, and whoever does not know should say, \"Allah knows best.\" For it is part of knowledge that a man says, when he does not know, \"I do not know.\" Allah, Mighty and Majestic, said to His Prophet ﷺ: \"Say, I do not ask you for any reward for it, and I am not of the pretentious\" (Qur'an 38:86). Quraysh—the Prophet ﷺ supplicated against them and said, \"O Allah, help me against them with seven years like the years of Yusuf.\" Then a year of famine seized them until they perished, eating carrion and bones. A man would see something like smoke between the sky and the earth. Abu Sufyan b. Harb came to him and said, \"O Muhammad, you came to command the maintaining of kinship ties, and your people have perished. So supplicate to Allah.\" Then he recited this verse: \"So watch for the Day when the sky will bring a visible smoke covering the people; this is a painful punishment\" up to His saying: \"Indeed, We will remove the punishment a little; indeed, you will return [to disbelief]\" (Qur'an 44:10–15). He will remove the punishment from them when it comes, but then they will return to their disbelief. That is His saying: \"The Day We will strike with the greatest assault\" (Qur'an 44:16), that is the Day of Badr, and \"Indeed, it will be a perpetual punishment\" (Qur'an 44:16). And \"Alif Lam Mim. The Romans have been defeated in the nearest land, but they, after their defeat, will overcome\" (Qur'an 30:1–3). The Romans have passed, and the four have passed.'"],[7261,"A Jew said to Umar: If we, the Jewish people, knew when this verse was revealed, we would have taken it as a festival: {Today I have perfected for you your religion}. And if we knew the day on which it was revealed, we would have taken it as a festival. Umar ؓ said: 'I know the day on which it was revealed and the night in which it was revealed: the day of Friday, while we were with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ at Arafat.'"],[7262,"The mosque in the time of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ was built of mud bricks, its roof was of palm branches, and its pillars were of palm trunks. Abu Bakr ؓ did not add to it. Umar ؓ added to it and rebuilt it on its original structure from the time of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ with mud bricks and palm branches, and replaced its pillars with wood. Then Uthman ؓ changed it, made a large addition, built its walls with carved stones, made its pillars of carved stones, and roofed it with teak."],[7263,"\"Qais bin Sa'd used to be, to the Prophet ﷺ, in the position of the head of police for a ruler.\" (One of the narrators) Al-Ansari said: \"That is: Due to his affairs that he takes charge of.\" (Using translation from Tirmidhī 3850)"],[7264,"Gabriel sat down with the Prophet ﷺ and looked at the sky, and behold an angel was descending. Gabriel said to him, \"This angel has not descended since he was created before this hour.\" When he descended, he said, \"O Muhammad, your Lord sent me to you: has He made you a king for them or a servant messenger?\" Gabriel said to him, \"Humble yourself to your Lord, O Muhammad.\" He ﷺ said, \"No, rather a servant messenger.\""],[7265,"He was the best of people, the most generous of people, and the bravest of people. The people of Madinah were alarmed, so they went toward the sound, and the Messenger of Allah ﷺ met them, having preceded them to the sound, mounted on a bare horse belonging to Abu Talhah with no saddle, and a sword around his neck, saying to the people, “Do not be alarmed,” turning them back. Then he said of the horse, “We found it to be a sea, and it is indeed a sea.”"],[7266,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ was the most generous of people, and he was most generous during the month of Ramadan and when Jibril met him. Jibril used to meet him every night of Ramadan and study the Quran with him. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ was more generous with good than the sent wind when Jibril met him."],[7267,"The Prophet ﷺ did not eat his fill twice in a single day until he died."],[7268,"A month would pass over Muhammad’s ﷺ family without bread being baked in it. I said, “O Mother of the Believers, what did the Messenger of Allah ﷺ eat?” She said, “We had neighbors among the Ansar, may Allah reward them well, who had milk and would gift some of it to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ.”"],[7269,"A man came to the Prophet ﷺ, and he gave him sheep between two mountains. The man went to his people and said, “O my people, submit, for by Allah, Muhammad ﷺ gives the gift of a man who does not fear poverty. A man would come to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ desiring only worldly gain, and by evening his religion had become dearer to him than the world and all it contains.”"],[7270,"A man came to the Prophet ﷺ, and he ordered for him sheep between two mountains. He returned to his people and said, “Submit, for Muhammad ﷺ gives the gift of a man who does not fear poverty.”"],[7271,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ entered the mosque one day wearing a thick Najrani cloak. A bedouin came up behind him, grabbed the edge of his cloak, and pulled it so hard that the border left a mark on the side of the Messenger of Allah’s ﷺ neck. He said, “O Muhammad, give me from Allah’s wealth that is with you.” He turned to him, smiled ﷺ, and said, “Give orders for him.”"],[7272,"The Prophet ﷺ was never asked for anything and refused."],[7273,"The Prophet ﷺ was never asked about anything and said no."],[7274,"We said to Anas b. Malik, 'Which clothing was most beloved to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ?' He said, 'The hibara.'"],[7275,"\"That the Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to let his turban hang between his shoulders, and that Ibn Umar used to do the same.\""],[7276,"“Four things the Messenger of Allah ﷺ never abandoned: fasting the day of Ashura, the ten days, three days of every month, and the two rak‘ahs before the dawn prayer.”"],[7277,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to remember Allah a great deal, speak little nonsense, lengthen the prayer, shorten the sermon, and not disdain to walk with a widow or a poor person in order to fulfill his need."],[7278,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to remember Allah a great deal, speak little nonsense, lengthen the prayer, shorten the sermon, and not disdain or deem it too much to walk with a widow or a poor person in order to fulfill his need."],[7279,"“When we came to the Prophet ﷺ, one of us would sit wherever the gathering ended.”"],[7280,"While the Messenger of Allah ﷺ was distributing something, a man approached and leaned over him, so the Messenger of Allah ﷺ poked him with a palm stalk he had, and it wounded his face. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to him: “Come and obtain retribution.” The man said: I have forgiven you, O Messenger of Allah."],[7281,"I never saw a man take the hand of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and let go of his hand until the man himself would let go of his hand."],[7282,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ never criticized any food. If he desired it, he ate it, and if not, he left it."],[7283,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ never criticized any food. If he desired it, he ate it; if he disliked it, he left it."],[7284,"When he halted at night, he would recline on his right side. When he halted after dawn, he would set his forearm upright and place his head on his palm."],[7285,"When something concerned him, he would take hold of his beard like this."],[7286,"A group of Jews entered upon the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and said, “Death be upon you.” The Prophet ﷺ said, “And upon you.” ʿAʾishah said: I understood it, so I said, “And upon you be death and the curse.” The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, “Take it easy, O ʿAʾishah. Indeed Allah loves gentleness in every matter.” I said, “O Messenger of Allah, did you not hear what they said?” He said, “I said, ‘And upon you.’”"],[7287,"Indeed the Messenger of Allah ﷺ was not obscene nor one who made others obscene, and he used to say: “The best of you are those with the best character.”"],[7288,"I said to ʿAʾishah: How was the character of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ with his family? She said: “He was the best of people in character. He was not obscene, nor one who made others obscene, nor one who shouted in the markets. He did not repay evil with evil, but he pardoned and overlooked.”"],[7289,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ never struck anything with his hand, except when fighting in the path of Allah, and he never struck a woman or a servant."],[7290,"“The Messenger of Allah ﷺ stood (in prayer) until his feet became swollen. It was said: ‘O Messenger of Allah, Allah has forgiven you your past and future sins.’ He said: ‘Should I not be a thankful slave?’” (Using translation from Ibn Mājah 1419)"],[7291,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ was in pain (or found in pain). When morning came, it was said, \"O Messenger of Allah, the trace of pain is evident on you.\" He said, \"Indeed, as you see, I recited last night the seven long surahs.\""],[7292,"He informed them that while he was walking with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ after the Battle of Hunayn, the Bedouins came and started asking the Messenger of Allah ﷺ questions until they forced him to stop at Samurah. Then the robe of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ was snatched, so the Messenger of Allah ﷺ stopped and said, \"Give me my robe. If I had the same number of camels as the number of hairs on this robe, I would distribute them among you. Then you would not find me a liar or a coward.\""],[7293,"“When the last ten days of Ramadan began, the Prophet ﷺ used to stay up at night, tighten his waist- wrap, and wake up his family (to pray).” (Using translation from Ibn Mājah 1768)"],[7294,"I asked A'ishah about the work of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. She said, \"His work ﷺ was continuous.\""],[7295,"“The Prophet ﷺ used to visit the Anṣār, greet their children, and wipe their heads.”"],[7296,"I never saw the Messenger of Allah ﷺ strike a servant ever, nor strike a woman of his ever, nor strike with his hand anything ever, except when he was fighting in the path of Allah. And never was anything taken from him that he would take revenge for it from its owner, unless it was for Allah; and if it was for Allah, he would take revenge for it. And never were two matters presented to him except that he took the one that was easier, until it was a sin; and if it was a sin, he was the farthest of people from it."],[7297,"I, along with Ubayd ibn Umair, visited Aisha. She said to Ubayd ibn Umair, \"It's time for you to visit us.\" He replied, \"I say, O mother, as the first one said: 'Visit occasionally, and you will increase in affection.'\" She said, \"Leave us with your rhetoric.\" Ibn Umair said, \"Tell us about the most wondrous thing you have seen from the Messenger of Allah ﷺ.\"She fell silent for a while and then said, \"One night, he said, 'O Aisha, let me worship my Lord tonight.' I said, 'By Allah, I love your nearness, and I love what makes you happy.' She said, 'So he got up, purified himself, and stood to pray. He continued weeping until his lap became wet. Then he wept, and he did not stop weeping until his beard became wet. Then he wept, and he did not stop weeping until the ground became wet. Bilal came to announce the prayer to him, and when he saw him weeping, he said, 'O Messenger of Allah, why do you weep when Allah has forgiven all your past and future sins?' He said, 'Shall I not be a grateful servant? Tonight a verse has been revealed to me, woe to one who recites it and does not reflect on it: {Indeed, in the creation of the heavens and the earth} [and what follows] the entire verse.'\""],[7298,"\"I entered the mosque and found the Prophet ﷺ standing and praying. There was a buzzing sound coming from his chest, like the sound of a boiling pot.\""],[7299,"Our food during the time of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ was nothing but the two black things: dates and water."],[7300,"Whoever tells you that we used to eat our fill of dates has lied to you. When ﷺ conquered Qurayzah, we obtained some dates and fat."],[7301,"Ibn Umar heard the sound of a shepherd's pipe. He put his fingers in his ears, turned away from the road, and kept saying, 'O Nafi, do you hear it?' I would say, 'Yes.' When I said, 'No,' he returned to the road and said, 'This is how I saw the Messenger of Allah ﷺ do.'"],[7302,"Umm Sulaym sent a basket of fresh dates to the Prophet ﷺ, and he would take a handful and send it to one of his wives, then take a handful and send it to another of his wives, then send it, while he desired it. He did that more than once, while he desired it."],[7303,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ had a bed frame woven with palm leaves, over which was a black blanket stuffed with palm leaves. Abu Bakr and Umar entered upon him, and the Prophet ﷺ was sleeping on it. When he saw them, he sat up. They looked and saw the marks of the bed frame on the side of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. Abu Bakr and Umar wept and said, 'O Messenger of Allah, does the hardness of what we see of your bed and mattress not hurt you? Yet Chosroes and Caesar are on beds of silk and brocade.' He said, 'Do not say that. The beds of Chosroes and Caesar are in the Fire, while my bed and this bed frame of mine will end in Paradise.'"],[7304,"When he entered his house, he would begin with the siwak."],[7305,"When he rose at night, he would clean his mouth with the siwak."],[7306,"He used to like starting with the right side as much as he could in his purification, putting on his sandals, and combing his hair."],[7307,"\"When the Messenger of Allah ﷺ prayed fajr, he would sit in the place where he had prayed until the sun rose.\" (Using translation from Nasāʾī 1357)"],[7308,"\"When the Prophet ﷺ would fall ill and could not perform the night prayer, he would pray twelve units of prayer during the day.\""],[7309,"I asked Aisha when the Prophet ﷺ used to perform the Sunnah prayer after Isha. She said, \"When he heard the rooster crowing, and he used to persistently perform it even if it was little.\""],[7310,"I said to her: 'With what would the Messenger of Allah ﷺ begin when he entered upon you and when he left you?' She said: 'He would begin with the toothstick when he entered, and when he left he would pray two rak'ahs.'"],[7311,"I asked 'A'ishah about the Prophet's ﷺ prayer at night. She said, \"He used to sleep at the beginning of the night, then get up and pray. When it was the time before dawn, he prayed witr. If he had need of his family, he would go to them; otherwise he slept. When he heard the adhan, he leapt up—she did not say 'he got up'—and if he was in a state of major impurity, he poured water over himself—she did not say 'he performed ghusl'—otherwise he performed ablution and went out to the prayer.\""],[7312,"We went to ʿAbd Allah b. Masʿūd one day after we had prayed the dawn prayer. We greeted at the door and he gave us permission, so we waited a little while. A servant came out and said: “Will you not enter?” So we entered and found him sitting and glorifying Allah. He said: “What prevented you from entering when permission had been given to you?” They said: “Nothing, except that we thought some of the household were asleep.” He said: “You thought the family of Umm ʿAbd were negligent?” Then he resumed glorifying Allah until he thought the sun had risen. He said: “O girl, look and see whether it has risen.” She looked and it had risen. He said: “Praise be to Allah who has granted us this day”—Mahdī said: I think he said—“and did not destroy us for our sins.” A man from the group said: “I recited all the mufaṣṣal last night.” ʿAbd Allah said: “Rapidly, like the recitation of poetry? I know the pairs which the Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to recite: eighteen surahs from the mufaṣṣal and two surahs from the family of Ḥā Mīm.”"],[7313,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to pray eleven rak'ahs between the completion of 'Isha prayer, which is when people are called to the darkness of dawn, and the dawn prayer. In each set of two rak'ahs, he would recite the salaam. Additionally, he would perform one witr rak'ah. When the muezzin finished calling for the dawn prayer and the dawn appeared to him, and the muezzin came to him, he would stand and perform two light rak'ahs, then lie down on his right side until the muezzin came to him with the call to establish the prayer."],[7314,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ, when he did a deed, he would make it a habit. She said: \"When he slept through the night or was ill, he would pray twelve rak'ahs during the day. And I did not see the Messenger of Allah ﷺ stand in prayer for an entire night until morning, nor fast a whole month consecutively except Ramadan.\""],[7315,"I served the Messenger of Allah ﷺ for ten years, and he never said to me, 'Why did you do such-and-such?' or 'Why did you not do such-and-such?'"],[7316,"I served the Messenger of Allah ﷺ for ten years, and he never said to me 'Uff' at all, nor did he say to me, 'Why did you not do such-and-such?' or 'Why did you do such-and-such?'"],[7317,"He used to fast three days from the beginning of every month.\""],[7318,"He asked ʿĀʾishah about the fasting of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and she said, \"He used to fast all of Shaʿbān until he connected it with Ramadan, and he used to seek to fast on Mondays and Thursdays.\""],[7319,"\"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to fast three days from the beginning of every month, and he rarely broke his fast on Friday.\""],[7320,"I asked the Mother of the Believers, ʿĀʾishah: \"O Mother of the Believers, how was the practice of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ? Did he single out any days?\" She said, \"No, his practice was continuous, and which of you can bear what the Messenger of Allah ﷺ could bear?\""],[7321,"Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to fast till one would say that he would never stop fasting, and he would abandon fasting till one would say that he would never fast. I never saw Messenger of Allah ﷺ fasting for a whole month except the month of Ramadan, and did not see him fasting in any month more than in the month of Sha'ban. (Using translation from Bukhārī 1969)"],[7322,"\"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to fast three days of every month.\" I said, \"In which part of it?\" She said, \"He did not mind in which part of it.\""],[7323,"He used to use his right hand for his food, and he used his left hand for what was other than that.”"],[7324,"She was asked: What was the work of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ in his house? She said: “He was only a human being among human beings. He would delouse his garment, milk his sheep, and serve himself.”"],[7325,"I said to ʿĀʾishah: O Mother of the Believers, what would the Messenger of Allah ﷺ do when he was with you? She said: “What one of you does in serving his family: he would mend his sandal, sew his garment, and patch his bucket.”"],[7326,"She was asked: What did the Prophet ﷺ do in his house? She said: “He would sew his garment, mend his sandal, and do what men do in their houses.”"],[7327,"A man asked her: Did the Messenger of Allah ﷺ work in his house? She said: Yes. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to mend his sandal, sew his garment, and work in his house just as one of you works in his house."],[7328,"The people went out to pray for rain, and among them was Zayd b. Arqam, with only one man between him and me. He said: I said: \"How many expeditions did he go on?\" Ibn Kathir said: \"O Abu 'Amr, how many expeditions did the Messenger of Allah ﷺ go on?\" He said: \"Nineteen.\" I said: \"How many did you go on with him?\" He said: \"Seventeen.\" I said: \"What was his first expedition?\" He said: \"Dhu al-'Ushayrah or al-'Usayrah.\" Then 'Abd Allah b. Zayd led the people in two rak'ahs."],[7329,"\"When the Prophet walked, his Companions would walk in front of him, and he would leave his back for the angels.\" (Using translation from Ibn Mājah 246)"],[7330,"I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ reciting, and I never heard anything more beautiful in recitation than him."],[7331,"Are you not in food and drink as you wish?"],[7332,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ would not find even low-quality dates to fill his stomach, and he was hungry."],[7333,"ʿUmar said, mentioning what had befallen the people of worldly things: “I saw the Messenger of Allah ﷺ writhing, not finding even low-quality dates to fill his stomach.”"],[7334,"The family of Muhammad ﷺ never ate their fill of one food for three days until he ﷺ passed away, except the two black things: dates and water."],[7335,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ never filled his family for three consecutive days with wheat bread until he departed this world."],[7336,"I asked Sahl b. Sa‘d al-Sā‘idī, “Did the Messenger of Allah ﷺ eat refined flour?” Sahl said, “The Messenger of Allah ﷺ never saw refined flour from the time Allah sent him until He took him.” He said, “Did you have sieves during the time of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ?” He said, “The Messenger of Allah ﷺ never saw a sieve from the time He sent him until He took him.” I said, “How did you eat unsifted barley?” He said, “We would grind it, then blow on it, so whatever flew away flew away, and what remained we moistened and ate.”"],[7337,"We used to look at the new moon, then the new moon, then the new moon: three new moons in two months, and no fire was kindled in the houses of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. I said, “O maternal aunt, what did you live on?” She said, “The two black things: dates and water, except that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ had neighbors among the Ansar—excellent neighbors—who had milch animals, and they would give the Messenger of Allah ﷺ some of their milk, and he would give us to drink of it.”"],[7338,"There was not in the family of Muhammad a sā‘ of wheat or a sā‘ of dates."],[7339,"By the One in whose hand is the soul of Muhammad, if I had Mount Uhud in gold, I would love that three nights would not pass over me while I had a dinar of it, unless I found someone to accept it from me, not anything I was keeping for a debt I owed."],[7340,"‘Umar b. al-Khaṭṭāb entered upon the Prophet ﷺ while he was on a mat that had left marks on his side. He said, “O Messenger of Allah, if only you would take a bed softer than this?” He said, “O ‘Umar, what have I to do with the world, and what has the world to do with me? By the One in whose hand is my soul, my likeness and the likeness of the world is only that of a rider who travels on a hot day and takes shade under a tree for an hour of the day, then moves on and leaves it.”"],[7341,"We used to come to Anas b. Mālik while his baker was standing. He said, “Eat, for I do not know that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ ever saw a thin flat loaf or a roasted sheep with his own eyes until he met Allah.”"],[7342,"He used not to store away anything for tomorrow.\""],[7343,"The wealth of Banu an-­Nadeer was among the fai' that Allah bestowed upon His Messenger ﷺ, for which the Muslims made no expedition with either cavalry or camelry (cf. al-Hashr 59:6). It was only for the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and he used to spend from it on his family's annual expenses-and on one occasion he said: his annual food supply ­-and what was left he spent on horses and weapons in preparation for jihad for the sake of Allah, may He be glorified and exalted, (Using translation from Aḥmad 171)"],[7344,"\"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ died and never had his fill of bread and oil twice in one day.\""],[7345,"\"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ never had lunch and dinner together of bread and meat except with guests.\""],[7346,"I asked Sahl b. Saʿd al-Sāʿidī, 'Did the Messenger of Allah ﷺ eat refined white bread?' Sahl said, 'The Messenger of Allah ﷺ never saw refined white bread from the time Allah sent him until He took him.' I said, 'Did you have sieves at the time of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ?' He said, 'The Messenger of Allah ﷺ never saw a sieve from the time Allah sent him until He took him.' I said, 'Then how did you eat barley un-sieved?' He said, 'Yes, we would blow on it, and whatever flew off from it flew away, and what remained we moistened and ate.'"],[7347,"\"The bedding of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ was of tanned leather stuffed with palm fiber.\" She said, \"A month would pass on us and we would not light a fire; it was only the two black things: dates and water, until some neighbors of ours sent us a milking ewe.\""],[7348,"The Prophet ﷺ was on a bedstead, and it was woven with a rope. He said: Then some of his companions entered upon him, and ʿUmar entered. The Prophet ﷺ turned, and the rope had left marks on his side. ʿUmar wept and said, \"By Allah, we know that you are more honored before Allah than Kisrā and Caesar, and they wallow in what they wallow in.\" He ﷺ said, \"Are you not content that theirs is this world and ours is the Hereafter?\" He said, \"Yes.\" He said, \"Then be silent.\""],[7349,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ returned to me one day from a funeral in Al-Baqi' while I had a headache. I said, \"O Rasulullah, my head is hurting.\" He replied, \"Rather, it is my head that is hurting.\" Then he said, \"What harm would it do to you if you were to die before me, then I would wash you, shroud you, pray over you, and bury you?\" I said, \"Because I fear that if you did that, you would return to my house and marry one of your other wives.\" The Messenger of Allah ﷺ smiled, then he began to experience the pain in which he eventually passed away."],[7350,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ first fell ill in the house of Maymunah. His illness became severe until he lost consciousness. He said: They consulted about giving him ladud (a medicine poured into the side of the mouth), so they gave it to him. When he regained consciousness, he said: \"What is this? Is this the action of women who have come from here?\" and he pointed to the land of Abyssinia. Asma' bt. Umays was among them. They said: \"We suspected you had pleurisy, O Messenger of Allah.\" He said: \"If that were a disease, Allah would not afflict me with it. No one in the house shall remain but that he is given ladud, except the uncle of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ,\" meaning Abbas. He said: Indeed Maymunah was given ladud that day while she was fasting, due to the command of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ."],[7351,"“I asked ‘Aishah: ‘O mother! Tell me about the sickness of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ.’ She said: ‘He felt pain and started to spit (over his body), and we began to compare his spittle to the spittle of a person eating raisins. Like a person eating raisins and spitting out the seeds. He used to go around among his wives, but when he became ill, he asked them permission to stay in the house of ‘Aishah and that they should come to him in turns.’ She said: ‘The Messenger of Allah ﷺ entered upon me, (supported) between two men, with his feet making lines along the ground. One of them was ‘Abbas.’ I told Ibn ‘Abbas this Hadith and he said: ‘Do you know who the other man was whom ‘Aishah did not name? He was ‘Ali bin Abu Talib.’” (Using translation from Ibn Mājah 1618)"],[7352,"We gave the Messenger of Allah ﷺ ladud during his illness, and he began gesturing to us: \"Do not give me ladud.\" We said: \"It is the patient's dislike of medicine.\" When he regained consciousness, he said: \"Did I not forbid you to give me ladud?\" We said: \"It is the patient's dislike of medicine.\" He said: \"No one shall remain in the house but that he is given ladud,\" and I was looking at Abbas, for he had not been present with them."],[7353,"Whenever he fell ill, he would blow over himself with the mu'awwidhat and wipe over himself with his hand. She said: \"When the Prophet ﷺ fell ill with the illness in which he died, I began to blow over him with the mu'awwidhat that he used to blow over himself with, and I would wipe with the hand of the Prophet ﷺ over him.\""],[7354,"I used to treat the Messenger of Allah ﷺ with a ruqya that Jibril used to treat him with when he fell ill: \"Remove the affliction, Lord of mankind; send down healing, for there is no healer but You; heal with a healing that leaves no sickness.\" When he was in the illness in which he died, I began supplicating with this supplication, and he ﷺ said, \"Lift your hand, for it used to benefit me during the period.\""],[7355,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ lost consciousness while his head was in my lap. I began to wipe him and supplicate for his healing. When he regained consciousness, he ﷺ said: \"Rather, I ask Allah for the highest companion, with Jibril, Mika'il, and Israfil.\""],[7356,"I used to hear that no prophet dies until he is given a choice between this world and the Hereafter. She said: I heard the Prophet ﷺ during his illness in which he died, and he had developed hoarseness, and he began to say: \"{with those upon whom Allah has bestowed favor of the prophets, the truthful, the martyrs, and the righteous; and excellent are those as companions}.\" She said: Then I thought that he had been given the choice at that time."],[7357,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ came out to us during his illness in which he died, with his head bandaged. I followed him until he stood on the minbar and said: \"Indeed I am at this moment standing at the Hawd.\" Then he said: \"Indeed a servant was offered the world and its adornment, and he chose the Hereafter.\" None of the people understood it except Abu Bakr, who said: \"May my father and mother be your ransom; rather we ransom you with our wealth, our selves, and our children.\" He said: Then he descended from the minbar, and he was not seen on it again until this hour."],[7358,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ gave a sermon and said: \"Indeed Allah has given a servant a choice between granting him as much of the splendor of this world as He wills and meeting Him, and he chose meeting his Lord.\" Abu Bakr wept and said: \"Rather we ransom you with our fathers and our sons.\" The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"Be quiet, O Abu Bakr.\" Then he said: \"Indeed the most gracious of people to me in his companionship and his wealth is Abu Bakr. If I were to take a bosom friend from among people, I would have taken Abu Bakr, but there is the brotherhood of Islam and its affection. Indeed no small door shall remain in the mosque but that it is closed, except the small door of Abu Bakr.\" Abu Sa'id said: I said: \"How strange! The Messenger of Allah ﷺ tells us that a servant was given a choice by Allah between this world and the Hereafter, and this one is weeping! And behold, the one given the choice was the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and the one weeping was Abu Bakr, and Abu Bakr was the most knowledgeable of us about the Messenger of Allah ﷺ.\""],[7359,"The Prophet ﷺ prayed over the slain of Uhud, then departed and sat on the pulpit, praised Allah and extolled Him, then said: “O people, I am before you as a forerunner, and I am a witness over you. By Allah, I do not fear that you will associate partners with Allah after me, but I have been given tonight the keys of the treasures of the earth and the heaven, and I fear that you will compete with one another over them.” Then he entered his house and did not come out until Allah, Mighty and Exalted, took his soul."],[7360,"\"Pour over me from seven waterskins whose ties have not been untied, perhaps I may find relief and give instructions to the people.\" Aisha said: We seated him in a copper basin belonging to Hafsa and poured water over him until he began gesturing to us: \"You have done it.\" Then he came out, praised Allah and extolled Him, and sought forgiveness for the martyrs who were killed on the day of Uhud."],[7361,"When the Prophet ﷺ was near death and there were men in the house, among them Umar b. al-Khattab, the Prophet ﷺ said: \"I will write for you a book, after which you will never go astray.\" Umar said: \"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ is overcome by pain, and you have the Quran; sufficient for us is the Book of Allah.\" So the people of the house differed and argued. When the noise and talk increased in the presence of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"Get up.\" Ibn Abbas used to say: \"The calamity, the whole calamity, is what prevented the Messenger of Allah ﷺ from writing that book for them because of their disagreement and noise.\""],[7362,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said during his illness: \"Call for me Abu Bakr, your father, so that I may write, for I fear that someone will wish and say: 'I am more entitled,' but Allah and the believers refuse except Abu Bakr.\""],[7363,"The Prophet ﷺ said during his illness in which he was taken: \"Pour over me from seven waterskins whose ties have not been untied, perhaps I may give instructions to the people.\" She said: We seated him in a basin belonging to Hafsa, and we kept pouring over him until he began gesturing to us: \"You have done it.\""],[7364,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said during the illness in which he died: \"Pour over me from seven waterskins whose openings have not been untied, so that I may find relief and then give my covenant to the people.\" A'isha said: So we seated him in a copper tub belonging to Hafsa bt. Umar, and we poured water over him until he began to gesture to us that we had done enough. Then he went out to the mosque."],[7365,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ fell ill and said: \"Command Abu Bakr to lead the people in prayer.\" I said: O Messenger of Allah, when Abu Bakr stands in your place, the people will not be able to hear him due to weeping, so command Umar to lead the people in prayer. He said: \"Command Abu Bakr to lead the people in prayer.\" I said the same thing again, and he ﷺ said: \"Command Abu Bakr to lead the people in prayer.\" I said to Hafsa: Say to him that Abu Bakr, when he..."],[7366,"I entered upon A'isha and said to her: Will you not tell me about the illness of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ? She said: Yes, the Messenger of Allah ﷺ became gravely ill and said: \"Have the people prayed?\" I said: No, O Messenger of Allah, they are waiting for you. He said: \"Put water for me in the tub.\" We did so, and he ﷺ performed ghusl. Then he tried to rise but fainted. Then he regained consciousness and said: \"Have the people prayed?\" We said: No, O Messenger of Allah, and they are waiting for you. She said: The people were gathered in the mosque waiting for the Messenger of Allah ﷺ for the last evening prayer. She said: So the Messenger of Allah ﷺ sent a man to Abu Bakr to lead the people in prayer. The messenger came to him and said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ commands you to lead the people in prayer. Abu Bakr, who was a tender-hearted man, said: O Umar, lead the people in prayer. Umar said: You are more entitled to that. So Abu Bakr led them in prayer during those days. Then the Messenger of Allah ﷺ felt some relief and went out supported by two men, one of whom was al-Abbas b. Abd al-Muttalib, while Abu Bakr was leading the people in prayer. When Abu Bakr saw him, he moved to step back, but he gestured to him not to step back. He said to them: \"Seat me beside Abu Bakr.\" So they seated him beside Abu Bakr. She said: Abu Bakr prayed while following the prayer of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, standing, and the people prayed following the prayer of Abu Bakr, while the Messenger of Allah ﷺ was seated. Ubayd Allah said: I entered upon Ibn Abbas and said to him: Shall I present to you what A'isha narrated to me about the illness of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ? He said: Yes. So I narrated her hadith about the illness of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. He did not object to anything of it except that he said: Did she not name for you the man who was with al-Abbas? I said: No. He said: It was Ali."],[7367,"The last bequest of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, while he was gurgling in his chest and his tongue could not utter it clearly, was: \"The prayer, the prayer; fear Allah regarding those your right hands possess.\""],[7368,"When death approached the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, he began to place the edge of a cloak over his face, and when he felt distressed by it, he uncovered his face and said, \"Allah's curse be upon the Jews and Christians who took the graves of their prophets as mosques.\""],[7369,"A man came to him while I was listening and said, \"O Abu Bakr, how long was the revelation cut off from the Prophet of Allah ﷺ before his death?\" He said, \"No one has asked me about this since I heard it from Anas b. Malik.\" Anas b. Malik said, \"He was taken from this world while it was more frequent than it had been.\""],[7370,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said during his illness, 'Your kinship ties, your kinship ties.'"],[7371,"I heard the Prophet ﷺ say three days before his death: “None of you should die except while having a good opinion of Allah, Mighty and Majestic.”"],[7372,"The pain of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ intensified, and he had seven dinars or nine with him. He said, \"O ʿĀʾishah, what has happened to that gold?\" I said, \"It is with me.\" He said, \"Give it in charity.\" She said, \"I was occupied with him.\" Then he said, \"O ʿĀʾishah, what has happened to that gold?\" I said, \"It is with me.\" He said, \"Bring it to me.\" She said, \"So I brought it, and he placed it in his palm and said, 'What does Muhammad think if he meets Allah while this is with him? What does Muhammad think if he meets Allah while this is with him?'\""],[7373,"I have not seen pain more severe on anyone than on the Messenger of Allah ﷺ."],[7374,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ died while his shield was pawned with a Jew for thirty sāʿs of barley."],[7375,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ pawned a shield of his with a Jew for a dinar, and he did not find what to redeem it with until he died."],[7376,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ bought food from a Jew on credit for a year and pawned him a shield of his made of iron."],[7377,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ drew aside the curtain during the illness in which he died, while the people were in rows behind Abu Bakr, and he said, \"Nothing remains of the glad tidings of prophethood except the righteous dream, which a believer sees or is seen for him. Verily, I have been forbidden to recite while bowing or prostrating. As for bowing, magnify the Lord therein; and as for prostration, strive in supplication, for it is likely to be answered for you.\""],[7378,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ drew aside the curtain, his head bandaged, during the illness in which he died, and said, \"O Allah, have I conveyed?\" three times. \"Nothing remains of the glad tidings of prophethood except the dream that a righteous servant sees or is seen for him.\""],[7379,"\"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ did not die until it became lawful for him from women whatever he wished.\""],[7380,"When death descended upon the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, Fatimah said, \"O what grief!\" The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, \"No grief upon your father after this day.\""],[7381,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ fell ill, so his wives said, \"Choose where you would like to be, and we will come to you.\" He ﷺ said, \"Will all of you agree to that?\" She said, \"Yes.\" So he moved to the house of Aisha and died in it ﷺ."],[7382,"Abu Bakr said to me, \"On which day did the Messenger of Allah ﷺ die?\" I said, \"Monday.\" He said, \"I hope to die on that day.\" And he died on Monday in the evening and was buried at night."],[7384,"\"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ died in my house, on my day, and between my magic and sacrifice. Then Abdullah ibn Abu Bakr entered with a wet toothstick (miswak). The Messenger of Allah ﷺ looked at it, so I thought that he needed it. I took it, chewed on it, and perfumed it. Then I handed it to him, so he used it as beautifully as I had ever seen anyone using it before. Then he wanted to hand it back to me, but it fell from his hand. So I took it, and I sought assistance with a supplication that he used to make when he got sick, but he did not make that supplication during his sickness. Then he looked up to the sky and said, 'The Highest Companion, the Highest Companion.' Then his soul departed. Praise be to Allah who has brought my saliva and his saliva together on the last day of his life in this world.\""],[7385,"She heard the Prophet ﷺ before he died, while she was leaning him against her chest, say: \"O Allah, forgive me, have mercy on me, and join me with the highest companion.\""],[7386,"While the Muslims were in the dawn prayer on Monday, with Abu Bakr leading them, the Messenger of Allah ﷺ suddenly appeared to them, having drawn back the curtain of Aisha's chamber. He looked at them while they were in rows in their prayer, then he smiled and laughed. Abu Bakr stepped back on his heels to join the row, thinking that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ wanted to come out for the prayer."],[7387,"It was narrated from Ibn ‘Abbas and ‘Aishah that Abu Bakr kissed the Prophet ﷺ when he died. (Using translation from Ibn Mājah 1457)"],[7388,"Abu Bakr entered the mosque while Umar was speaking to the people, when he entered the house of the Prophet ﷺ in which he had died, which is the house of Aisha, the wife of the Prophet ﷺ. He uncovered his face from a striped Yemeni cloak that was covering him, looked at his face, then bent over him and kissed him, and said, 'May my father be your ransom, by God, God will not combine two deaths upon you. You have died the death after which you will not die.'"],[7389,"Fatimah wept for the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and said: \"O father, how near he is to his Lord! O father, to Jibril we announce his death. O father, the Garden of Firdaws is his abode.\""],[7390,"When the distress overcame the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, his head was in Fatimah's lap. Fatimah said, \"What distress for your distress today, O father!\" He ﷺ raised his head and said, \"No distress upon your father after today, O Fatimah.\" When he died, Fatimah said, \"O father, he answered a Lord who called him. O father, how near he is to his Lord! O father, to the Garden of Firdaws is his abode. O father, to Jibril we announce his death.\" Anas said, \"When we buried him, I passed by Fatimah's dwelling and she said, 'O Anas, did your souls find it easy to heap dust upon the Messenger of Allah ﷺ?!'\""],[7391,"I entered upon A'ishah, and she brought out to us a thick lower garment of the kind made in Yemen and a cloak of what they call mulabbadah. She swore by Allah that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ died in these two garments."],[7392,"A'ishah brought out to us a felted lower garment and a thick cloak, and said, \"In this the Messenger of Allah ﷺ passed away.\""],[7393,"“While I was walking around in Paradise, I heard the voice of a reciter. I said: ‘Who is this?’ They said: ‘Harithah b. al-Nuʿman. Thus is piety.’” He said: “He was the most dutiful of people to his mother.”"],[7394,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ was wrapped in a hibarah garment, then it was removed from him."],[7395,"When the Messenger of Allah ﷺ died, his Companions surrounded him and were uncertain about washing him. They said, \"Should we strip the Messenger of Allah ﷺ as we strip our dead, or how should we do?\" Allah, Mighty and Majestic, sent upon them a slumber, and none of them raised his head. Then a caller called from the house—they did not know who it was—\"Wash the Messenger of Allah ﷺ with his clothes on.\" She said, \"So they washed the Messenger of Allah ﷺ with his shirt on.\" A'ishah said, \"If I had known then what I know now, none but his wives would have washed him.\""],[7396,"When they gathered to wash the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, they differed among themselves. They said, \"By Allah, we do not know whether to strip the Messenger of Allah ﷺ as we strip our dead, or to wash him with his clothes on.\" She said, \"Allah sent sleep upon them until every man's chin was on his chest. Then a caller called from the side of the house—they did not know what it was—'Wash the Messenger of Allah ﷺ with his shirt on.'\" He said, \"They sprang to him like one man and washed the Messenger of Allah ﷺ with his shirt on, pouring water over him and rubbing him from behind the shirt. The one who sat him in his lap was Ali b. Abi Talib, leaning him against his chest.\" She said, \"Nothing was seen of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ of what is seen of a dead person.\""],[7397,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ was covered with a Yemeni suit that belonged to Abdullah b. Abi Bakr. Then it was removed from him, and he was shrouded in three white Yemeni cotton garments, with no turban and no shirt. Abdullah took the suit and said, 'I will be shrouded in it.' Then he said, 'The Messenger of Allah ﷺ was not shrouded in it, so should I be shrouded in it?' And he gave it away as charity."],[7398,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ was shrouded in a Najrani garment and two soft white cloths."],[7399,"The Prophet ﷺ was shrouded in two Suhuli garments."],[7400,"I was with Abu Bakr when death came to him, and I recited this line of poetry."],[7401,"The Messenger of God ﷺ was shrouded in three white Suhuli garments, with no shirt and no turban among them."],[7402,"A red velvet cloth was placed in the grave of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ."],[7403,"The Prophet ﷺ was shrouded in three Sahuli garments, a niche (lahd) was dug for him, and unbaked bricks were set up over him."],[7404,"Al-Abbas, Ali, and Al-Fadl entered the grave of the Prophet ﷺ, and a man from the Ansar leveled his niche; he was the one who leveled the niches of the martyrs on the day of Badr."],[7405,"On the day the Messenger of Allah ﷺ entered Madinah, everything in it was illuminated, and on the day he died, everything in it became dark. We had not yet dusted off our hands from burying the Prophet ﷺ when we already felt estranged in our hearts."],[7406,"\"That the Prophet ﷺ was slandered and they poured milk over him, and his grave was raised from the ground by about a handspan.\""],[7407,"They claim that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ made a bequest to Ali. Indeed, he called for a basin and urinated in it while it was on my chest, and then he became limp and died, and I was not aware of it."],[7408,"\"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ was a man of medium height, broad-shouldered, with hair reaching his earlobes. I saw him in a red hullah, and I have never seen anyone more handsome than him ﷺ.\""],[7409,"\"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ had the most beautiful face of all people, and the finest physique and character. He was neither tall and lanky nor short.\""],[7410,"\"The complexion of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ was brownish.\""],[7411,"A man said to al-Bara': \"Was the face of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ like a sword?\" He said: \"No, but like the moon.\""],[7412,"I asked Jabir b. Samurah about the description of the Prophet ﷺ, and he said: \"He had eyes with a reddish tinge, a wide mouth, and lean heels.\""],[7413,"\"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ had a wide mouth, eyes with a reddish tinge, and lean ankles or feet.\""],[7414,"\"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ laughed, and he had the most beautiful front teeth of all people.\""],[7415,"I said to Anas b. Malik: \"What was the hair of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ like?\" He said: \"It was wavy hair, neither curly nor straight, hanging between his ears and his shoulders.\""],[7416,"That they said to Anas b. Malik, “Did the Messenger of Allah ﷺ have gray hair?” He said, “Allah did not disfigure him with gray hair. There were only seventeen or eighteen hairs in his head and beard.”"],[7417,"“I did not count in the head and beard of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ except fourteen white hairs.”"],[7418,"“The white hair of the Prophet ﷺ numbered approximately twenty.” (Using translation from Ibn Mājah 3630)"],[7419,"“I saw the gray hairs of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, about twenty white hairs on the front of his head.”"],[7420,"“That the Messenger of Allah ﷺ did not dye; there was only a little gray at the anfaqah (hair just below the lower lip), a little on the head, and a little at the temples.”"],[7421,"“The front of the head and beard of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ had become gray, but when he oiled and combed them, it did not show; only when his hair was disheveled could I see it. He had abundant hair and beard.” A man said, “Was his face like a sword?” He said, “No, it was like the sun and the moon, round.” He said, “And I saw his seal near his shoulder, like an ostrich egg, resembling his body.”"],[7422,"“I looked at the seal that was on the Prophet ﷺ. He said, ‘It was as if it were a pigeon egg.’”"],[7423,"“I never touched silk or brocade softer than the palm of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and I never smelled a fragrance or sweat more pleasant than the scent of the sweat of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ.”"],[7424,"“I never smelled musk or ambergris more pleasant than the scent of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ.”"],[7425,"He used to come to Umm Sulaym and take a midday nap at her place on a leather mat. He sweated profusely, so she would collect the sweat from the mat and put it into bottles along with perfume. And he used to pray on a khumrah."],[7426,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ was more bashful than a virgin in her private chamber."],[7427,"I asked 'Abd al-Rahman b. Mahdi, saying, 'O Abu Sa'id, was the Messenger of Allah ﷺ more bashful than a virgin in her private chamber?' He said, 'Yes. About something like this, ask; about something like this, ask.'"],[7428,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ was more bashful than a virgin in her private chamber. When he saw something he disliked, we would recognize it in his face."],[7429,"I have never seen anything more beautiful than the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. It was as if the sun were running across his face. And I have never seen anyone swifter in his gait than the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. It was as if the earth were folded up for him. We would exhaust ourselves, while he would be unconcerned."],[7430,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ was fair in complexion, as if his sweat were pearls. When he walked, he walked with a slight sway (takaffu)."],[7431,"When he described the Prophet ﷺ, he said: 'He had a large head, was fair with a reddish tinge, had a thick beard, a long line of hair from chest to navel, and coarse palms and feet. When he walked, it was as if he were descending a slope. I have never seen anyone like him before him or after him.'"],[7432,"\"Prophet Muhammad ﷺ performed 'Umrah al-Qadha' while Abdullah ibn Rawaha was gripping his mount and saying\""],[7433,"I have several names: I am Muhammad, I am Ahmad, I am al-Mahi through whom Allah erases disbelief, I am al-Hashir at whose feet mankind will be gathered, and I am al-'Aqib after whom there is no prophet. And Allah has named him Ra'uf (compassionate) and Rahim (merciful)."],[7434,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to name himself to us with several names, saying, 'I am Muhammad, and Ahmad, and al-Muqaffi, and al-Hashir, and the Prophet of Mercy, and the Prophet of Battles.'"],[7435,"I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say in one of the alleys of Madinah, 'I am Muhammad, and Ahmad, and al-Hashir, and al-Muqaffi, and the Prophet of Mercy.'"],[7436,"Allah chose Kinana from the descendants of Ismaʿil, chose Quraysh from Kinana, chose Banu Hashim from Quraysh, and chose me from Banu Hashim."],[7437,"A man asked her about the inheritance of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. She said, \"Are you asking me about the inheritance of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, may you have no father? By Allah, the Messenger of Allah ﷺ did not inherit a dinar, nor a dirham, nor a slave, nor a slave girl, nor a sheep, nor a camel.\""],[7438,"O people, your Prophet ﷺ was the most ascetic of people regarding the world, while you have become the most desirous of it."],[7439,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ was neither excessively tall nor short, nor was he very white nor dark, nor did he have very curly hair nor very straight hair. Allah, mighty and exalted, sent him at the age of forty, and he stayed in Makkah for ten years and in Madinah for ten years, and Allah, mighty and exalted, took him at the age of sixty, and there were not twenty white hairs in his head and beard ﷺ."],[7440,"\"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ passed away when he was sixty-three years old.\""],[7441,"The Prophet ﷺ passed away at sixty-three, Abu Bakr passed away at sixty-three, and ‘Umar passed away at sixty-three."],[7442,"The Prophet ﷺ was sent at forty, called people to Islam, and was not permitted to fight for thirteen years. The Hijrah was after ten years, and the Messenger of Allah ﷺ passed away at sixty-three."],[7443,"The Prophet ﷺ wore a black cloak, and ‘A’ishah said, ‘How beautiful it is on you, O Messenger of Allah; your whiteness blends with its blackness and its blackness blends with your whiteness.’ Then an odor emanated from it, so he threw it off. Pleasant fragrance used to please him."],[7444,"“The Messenger of Allah ﷺ died and left with us some barley, and we kept eating from it until the slave girl measured it, and it did not take long before it was exhausted. Had she not measured it, I would have hoped that it would have lasted longer.”"],[7445,"I asked A'isha about the inheritance of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and she said: You ask me about the inheritance of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ left neither a dinar nor a dirham, nor a sheep nor a camel, and he made no bequest of anything."],[7446,"Fatima bt. the Messenger of Allah ﷺ sent to Abu Bakr asking for her inheritance from the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, from what Allah had granted him as spoils in Madinah, Fadak, and what remained of the fifth of Khaybar. Abu Bakr said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"We are not inherited from; what we leave is charity. The family of Muhammad ﷺ only eats from this wealth.\" By Allah, I will not change anything of the charity of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ from the state it was in during the lifetime of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and I will act in it as the Messenger of Allah ﷺ acted. Abu Bakr refused to give Fatima anything from it, so Fatima became angry with Abu Bakr over that and shunned him, and did not speak to him until she died six months after the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. When she died, her husband Ali b. Abi Talib ؓ buried her at night and did not inform Abu Bakr of her death, and he prayed over her. Ali had a certain standing among the people during Fatima's lifetime, but when Fatima died, he noticed the people's faces turning away from him, so he sought reconciliation with Abu Bakr and to pledge allegiance to him, although he had not pledged allegiance during those months. He sent to Abu Bakr: Come to us, but let no one come with you, disliking that Umar b. al-Khattab should be present. Umar b. al-Khattab said to Abu Bakr: By Allah, do not enter upon them alone. Abu Bakr said: What could they possibly do to me? By Allah, I will go to them. So Abu Bakr entered upon them. Ali b. Abi Talib then bore witness and said: We have recognized, O Abu Bakr, your excellence and what Allah has given you, and we do not grudge you any good that Allah has brought to you, but you have acted autocratically toward us in this matter, and we saw that we had a right due to our kinship with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. He continued to speak to Abu Bakr until Abu Bakr's eyes overflowed. When Abu Bakr spoke, he said: By Him in whose hand is my soul, kinship with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ is more beloved to me than maintaining ties with my own family and kin. As for the dispute between me and you over these properties, I have not fallen short in them regarding what is right, and I have not left anything that I saw the Messenger of Allah ﷺ do with them except that I have done it. Ali b. Abi Talib ؓ said to Abu Bakr: Your appointment is this evening for the pledge of allegiance. When Abu Bakr had prayed the noon prayer, he ascended the pulpit, bore witness, then mentioned the affair of Ali b. Abi Talib and his delay from pledging allegiance and the excuse he had given to him. Then he sought forgiveness. Ali b. Abi Talib bore witness, magnifying the right and sanctity of Abu Bakr, and stating that what he had done was not out of envy of Abu Bakr nor denial of what Allah had favored him with, but we saw that we had a share in this matter, and he acted autocratically toward us, so we felt something in ourselves. The Muslims were pleased with that and said: You have done right. The Muslims became close to Ali once more when he returned to the matter with what is proper."],[7447,"Umar b. al-Khattab sent for me and said: Some families of your people have arrived in Madinah, and we have ordered a small share for them, so distribute it among them. I said: O Commander of the Believers, order someone else to do that. He said: Take it, O man. While I was in that situation, his freedman Yarfa' came and said: Here are Uthman, Abd al-Rahman b. Awf, Sa'd b. Abi Waqqas, and al-Zubayr b. al-Awwam - and I do not know whether he mentioned Talha or not - asking permission to enter upon you. He said: Give them permission. Then he waited a while, then came and said: Al-Abbas and Ali are asking permission to enter upon you. He said: Give them permission. When al-Abbas entered, he said: O Commander of the Believers, judge between me and this one - at that time they were disputing over what Allah had granted His Messenger as spoils from the wealth of Banu al-Nadir. The people said: Judge between them, O Commander of the Believers, and relieve each of them from the other, for their dispute has gone on too long. Umar said: I adjure you by Allah, by whose permission the heavens and the earth stand, do you know that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"We are not inherited from; what we leave is charity\"? They said: He did say that. Then he said to the two of them the same thing, and they said: Yes. He said: I will inform you about this fay'. Allah, mighty and sublime, singled out His Prophet ﷺ with something He did not give to anyone else, as He said: {And what Allah restored to His Messenger from them, you did not spur any horses or camels for it} [Quran 59:6]. So this was exclusively for the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. By Allah, he did not keep it from you or hoard it over you; he distributed it among you and spread it among you until what remained of the wealth remained. He would spend on his family for a year - and perhaps Ma'mar said: he would withhold from it the provision of his family for a year - then he would place what remained in the place of Allah's wealth. When Allah took His Messenger ﷺ, Abu Bakr said: I am the one most entitled to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ after him; I will act in it as he used to act. Then he turned to Ali and al-Abbas and said: And you two claim that he was unjust and sinful in it, but Allah knows that he was truthful, righteous, and followed the truth. Then I was given charge of it after Abu Bakr for two years of my rule, and I acted in it like the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and Abu Bakr acted. And you two claim that I am unjust and sinful in it, while Allah knows that I am truthful, righteous, and follow the truth. Then you came to me - this one, meaning al-Abbas, seeking his inheritance from his nephew, and this one, meaning Ali, asking me for the inheritance of his wife. I said to you both: I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: \"We are not inherited from; what we leave is charity.\" Then it occurred to me to hand it over to you two, so I took from you both the covenant of Allah and His pledge that you would act in it as the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and Abu Bakr acted, and as I have acted during my charge. You said: Hand it over to us on that condition. Do you want from me a judgment other than this? By Him by whose permission the heavens and the earth stand, I will not judge between you two in it with any judgment other than this. If you are unable to manage it, then hand it back to me. He said: Then Ali gained control over it, and it was in Ali's hand, then in the hand of Hasan b. Ali, then in the hand of Husayn b. Ali, then in the hand of Ali b. Husayn, then in the hand of Hasan b. Hasan, then in the hand of Zayd b. Hasan. Ma'mar said: Then it was in the hand of Abd Allah b. al-Hasan."]]);
